COLLDATA("mujamkabir","en",[[14590,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Roughness, harshness, and hardness of hearts are among the camel-herding bedouins at the roots of the camels' tails, of the tribes of Rabi‘a and Mudar.”"],[14591,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gestured toward Yemen and said, “Faith is here, but harshness and hardness of hearts are among the camel-herding bedouins, where the horn of Satan rises, among Rabi‘a and Mudar.”"],[14592,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gestured toward Yemen and said, “Faith is here, faith is here. Indeed, harshness and hardness of hearts are among the camel-herding bedouins, where the horn of Satan rises, among Rabi‘a and Mudar.”"],[14593,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Faith is here,” and he gestured with his hand toward Yemen, “and roughness and hardness of hearts are among the camel-herding bedouins at the roots of the camels' tails, where the horn of Satan rises, among Rabi‘a and Mudar.”"],[14594,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gestured toward Yemen and said, “Faith is here. Harshness and hardness of hearts are among the camel-herding bedouins at the roots of the camels' tails, where the horn of Satan rises, among Rabi‘a and Mudar.”"],[14595,"I heard Abu Mas‘ud say: The sun eclipsed on the day Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of God ﷺ, died. The people said, “It eclipsed because of the death of Ibrahim.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of God. They do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone. So when you see that, hasten to the remembrance of God and to prayer.”"],[14596,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of God. They do not eclipse for the death of anyone. So when you see them, pray until they clear.”"],[14597,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and that coincided with the death of Ibrahim. He said, “The sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone, but when you see them, pray.”"],[14598,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Some people said, “The sun eclipsed only because of the death of Ibrahim ﷺ .” The Prophet ﷺ said, “The sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone, but they are two signs among the signs of God. So when you see them, pray.”"],[14599,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death of anyone among people, but they are two signs among the signs of God. So when you see them, rise to prayer.”"],[14600,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked toward Yemen and said, “Faith is Yemeni, and harshness and coarseness of hearts are among the owners of camels' tails, the clamorous ones, in Rabīʿah and Muḍar, where the two horns of Satan rise.”"],[14601,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A prayer is not sufficient in which a man does not straighten his backbone in bowing and prostration.”"],[14602,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The prayer of any one—or he said: of a man—is not sufficient if he does not straighten his back in bowing and prostration.”"],[14603,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “A prayer is not hoped for in which a man does not straighten his backbone in bowing and prostration.”"],[14604,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A prayer is not sufficient in which a man does not straighten his backbone in bowing and prostration,” or he said, “when he bows and when he prostrates.” Abū ʿAwānah was uncertain."],[14605,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A prayer is not hoped for in which a man does not straighten his backbone in bowing and prostration.” Sufyān said: Thus al-Aʿmash said: “not hoped for” [meaning] “not sufficient.”"],[14606,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A prayer is not sufficient in which a man does not straighten his backbone in bowing and prostration.”"],[14607,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, “The prayer of a man is not accepted if he does not straighten his backbone for bowing and prostration.”"],[14608,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe our shoulders during prayer and say, “Do not differ, lest your hearts differ.”"],[14609,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to straighten our shoulders during prayer and say, “Do not differ, lest your hearts differ.”"],[14610,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to straighten our shoulders during prayer and say, “Do not differ, lest your hearts differ.”"],[14611,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe our shoulders and say, “Stand straight and do not differ, lest your hearts differ.”"],[14612,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe our shoulders during the prayer and say, “Stand straight and do not differ, lest your hearts differ.”"],[14613,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say, “Let those of you with maturity and understanding stand closest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them.”"],[14614,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, “Let those of you with maturity and understanding stand closest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them.”"],[14615,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, “Let those of you with maturity and understanding stand closest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them.”"],[14616,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, “Let those of you with maturity and understanding stand closest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them.”"],[14617,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, “Let those of you with maturity and understanding stand closest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them.”"],[14618,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe our shoulders during the prayer and say, “Stand straight and do not differ, lest your hearts differ.”"],[14619,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Let those who take from me stand closest to me, meaning in the prayer.”"],[14620,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe our shoulders during the prayer and say, “Make the shoulders level and straighten the rows, and do not differ, lest your hearts differ.”"],[14621,"“Whoever recites the last two verses of al-Baqarah in a night, they will suffice him.”"],[14622,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “The most entitled of a people to lead them in prayer is the one most versed in the Book of Allah. If they are equal in recitation, then the most knowledgeable of the Sunnah. If they are equal in the Sunnah, then the earliest in migration. If they are equal in migration, then the eldest in age. And no man should lead another in his place of authority, nor sit on his seat of honor in his house except with his permission.”"],[14623,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one who should lead a people in prayer is the best reciter among them; if they are equal in recitation, then the earliest of them in emigration; if they are equal in emigration, then the most knowledgeable of them in the Sunnah; if they are equal in knowledge, then the eldest of them. No man should lead in the domain of another man's authority, and do not sit on his place of honor in his house unless he gives you permission.\""],[14624,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The one who should lead a people in prayer is the best reciter of the Book of God among them; if they are equal in recitation, then the most knowledgeable of them in the Sunnah; if they are equal in the Sunnah, then the earliest of them in emigration; if they are equal in emigration, then the eldest of them. No man should lead in the domain of another man's authority, and do not sit on his place of honor in his house unless he gives you permission.\" Za'idah said: I said to Sulayman, \"His place of honor is the head of his bed?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[14625,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one who should lead a people in prayer is the best reciter of the Book of God among them; if they are equal in recitation, then the most knowledgeable of them in the Sunnah; if they are equal in the Sunnah, then the eldest of them. No one should lead in another man's domain of authority, and no one should sit on his place of honor except with his permission.\""],[14626,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one who should lead a people in prayer is the best reciter of the Book of God among them; if they are equal in recitation, then the eldest of them. No man should lead in the domain of another man's authority, and do not sit on his place of honor in his house unless he gives you permission.\""],[14627,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one who should lead you in prayer is the best reciter of the Qur'an among you; if your recitation is equal, then the earliest of you in emigration; if your emigration is equal, then the eldest of you. No man should lead another man in his domain of authority or among his family, and do not sit on his place of honor unless he gives you permission.\""],[14628,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one who should lead a people in prayer is the one with the most Qur'anic recitation among them; if the recitation is equal, then the earliest of them in emigration; if the emigration is equal, then the most understanding of them in jurisprudence; if the jurisprudence is equal, then the eldest of them. No man should lead in the domain of another man's authority, and no one should sit on his place of honor in his house except with his permission.\""],[14629,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The one who should lead a people in prayer is the best reciter of the Book of God among them; if they are equal in emigration, then the most knowledgeable of them in the Sunnah; if they are equal in it, then the earliest of them in Islam. Do not lead a man in his domain of authority, and do not sit on his place of honor in his house unless he gives you permission.\""],[14630,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one who should lead a people in prayer is the best reciter of the Book of God among them and the earliest of them in emigration; if they are equal, then the most knowledgeable of them in the Sunnah; if they are equal in it, then the eldest of them. No one should lead in another man's domain of authority, and no one should sit on his place of honor in his house except with his permission.\""],[14631,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one who should lead a people in prayer is the best reciter of the Book of God among them; if they are equal in recitation, then the most knowledgeable of them in the Sunnah; if they are equal in the Sunnah, then the earliest of them in emigration; if they are equal in emigration, then the eldest of them. No man should lead in the domain of another man's authority, and no one should sit on his place of honor except with his permission.\""],[14632,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"The one who should lead a people in prayer is the best reciter of the Book of God among them; if they are equal in recitation, then the most knowledgeable of them in the Sunnah; if they are equal in knowledge of the Sunnah, then the earliest of them in emigration; if they are equal in emigration, then the eldest of them. Do not lead anyone in his command, and do not sit on his place of honor in his house unless he gives you permission.\""],[14633,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one who should lead a people in prayer is the best reciter of the Book of God among them; if they are equal in recitation, then the earliest of them in emigration; if they are equal in emigration, then the most knowledgeable of them in the Sunnah; if they are equal in the Sunnah, then the eldest of them. Do not lead anyone in his domain of authority, and do not sit on his place of honor in his house unless he gives you permission.\""],[14634,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The one who should lead a people in prayer is the best reciter of the Book of God among them; if their recitation is equal, then the earliest of them in emigration; if their emigration is equal, then the eldest of them. A man should not lead in his own family or in his domain of authority, and no one should sit on his place of honor except with his permission, unless he gives you permission.\" Shu'bah said: I said to him, \"What is his place of honor?\" He said, \"His bed.\" The wording is that of the hadith of Hajjaj."],[14635,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The people should be led by the one who is most versed in the Book of Allah. If they are equal in recitation, then the one who emigrated earliest. If they are equal in emigration, then the oldest of them. And no man should lead another in his domain or among his family, nor should one sit in his place of honor unless he permits him.\""],[14636,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people should be led by the one who emigrated earliest. If their emigration is equal, then the oldest of them. If they are equal in age, then the one most versed in recitation.\""],[14637,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people should be led by the one who is most versed in the Book of Allah. If they are equal in recitation, then the one who emigrated earliest. If they are equal in emigration, then the oldest of them. And do not lead a man of authority in his authority, and do not sit in his place of honor except with his permission.\""],[14638,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people should be led by the one who emigrated earliest. If they are equal in emigration, then the one most knowledgeable in the religion. If they are equal in knowledge, then the one most versed in the Qur'an. And no man should lead in another's domain, and no one should sit in his place of honor except with his permission.\""],[14639,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let the one most versed in the Book of Allah lead you. If the recitation is equal, then the one most knowledgeable of the Sunnah. If the Sunnah is equal, then the one who emigrated earliest. If the emigration is equal, then the oldest of you.\""],[14640,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people should be led by the one who is most versed in the Book of Allah. If they are equal in recitation, then the one most knowledgeable of the Sunnah. If they are equal in knowledge, then the one who emigrated earliest. If they are equal in emigration, then the oldest of them. And no man should lead another in his domain, nor should he sit in his place of honor in his house except with his permission.\""],[14641,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Whoever guides to a good deed will have the like of the reward of the one who does it.\""],[14642,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I have been left stranded, so give me a mount.\" He said, \"I do not find anything to mount you on, but go to so-and-so; perhaps he will mount you.\" So he went to him and he mounted him. Then he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever guides to a good deed will have the like of the reward of its doer.\""],[14643,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I have been left stranded, so give me a mount.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I have nothing, but go to so-and-so and ask him; perhaps he will mount you.\" So he went to him and he mounted him. Then he passed by the Prophet ﷺ and told him that he had mounted him, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever guides to a good deed will have the like of the reward of its doer.\""],[14644,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"Give me a mount.\" He said, \"I do not find anything to mount you on, but go to so-and-so; perhaps he will mount you.\" So he went to him and he mounted him. Then he mentioned that to him, and he said: \"Whoever guides to a good deed will have the like of the reward of its doer.\""],[14645,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have been left stranded, so give me a mount\"—meaning my journey has been cut short, so give me a mount. He said, \"I have nothing.\" A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I will guide him to someone who will mount him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever guides to a good deed will have the like of the reward of its doer.\""],[14646,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Give me a mount.\" He said, \"I have nothing to mount you on, but go to so-and-so, for he has something to mount you on.\" So he went to him and he mounted him. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever guides to a good deed is like its doer.\""],[14647,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “The one who guides to good is like the doer of it.”"],[14648,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The one who guides to good is like the doer of it.”"],[14649,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever guides to good has the like of the reward of its doer.”"],[14650,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The one who guides to good is like the doer of it.”"],[14651,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have been left stranded, so give me a mount.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “I do not find anything to mount you on, but go to so-and-so and he will mount you.” So he went to him and he mounted him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The one who guides to good is like the doer of it, or like the one who performs it.”"],[14652,"A man brought the Prophet ﷺ a bridled she-camel and said, “O Messenger of Allah, this is for the sake of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You will have for it seven hundred she-camels on the Day of Resurrection, all bridled.”"],[14653,"The Prophet ﷺ [said], “You will have for it seven hundred she-camels, all of them bridled.”"],[14654,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ with a bridled she-camel and said, “O Messenger of Allah, [this is] for the sake of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “You will have for it on the Day of Resurrection seven hundred bridled she-camels.”"],[14655,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ with a bridled she-camel and said, “This is for the sake of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed, you will have for it a hundred she-camels in Paradise.”"],[14656,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The one whose counsel is sought is entrusted.”"],[14657,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The one whose counsel is sought is entrusted.”"],[14658,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Indeed, among what people have retained from the earlier prophethood is the saying of a man: 'If you feel no shame, then do as you wish.'\""],[14659,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"A man died and it was said to him: 'What did you do?' He said: 'I used to trade with people, and I would be lenient in the currency, and I would give respite to the one in difficulty.' Then he died and entered Paradise.\" Abu Mas'ud al-Badri said: \"I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[14660,"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say it? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed with the Dajjal, when he emerges, there will be fire and water. As for what people see as fire, it is water; and as for what people see as water, it is fire. So whoever of you reaches that, let him fall into what he sees as fire, for it is sweet, cold water.\" And Hudhayfah said: I heard him say: \"A man from those before you was visited by the angel to take his soul. It was said to him: 'Have you done any good?' He said: 'I do not know.' It was said: 'Look.' He said: 'I do not know of anything, except that I used to trade with people in the world, and I would be generous with them, give respite to the one in difficulty, and overlook the one who was well-off.' So Allah admitted him to Paradise.\" And I heard him say: \"A man was approached by death. When he despaired of life, he instructed his family: 'When I die, gather for me a large amount of firewood around me, then wait for a windy day and scatter me in the sea.' They did so, and Allah gathered him and said: 'Why did you do that?' He said: 'Out of fear of You.' So Allah forgave him.\" 'Uqbah said: I heard him say that, and he was..."],[14661,"Did you hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: I heard him say: \"Indeed with the Dajjal, when he emerges, there will be water and fire. As for what people see as fire, it is cold water. Whoever of you reaches that, let him fall into what people see as fire, for it is sweet, cold water.\" 'Uqbah b. 'Amr said: I heard him say that."],[14662,"I sat with Hudhayfah and Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari. One of them said to his companion: 'Narrate what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' The other said: 'Rather, you narrate and I will confirm you.' So one of them narrated and the other confirmed him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: 'Look at his deeds.' He will say: 'My Lord, I did not do any good, except that I had wealth and I used to mix with people. Whoever was well-off, I made things easy for him; and whoever was in difficulty, I gave him respite until his ease.' Then Allah Almighty said: 'I am more deserving of making things easy,' and He forgave him.\" And the other said: You have spoken the truth. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that."],[14663,"I sat with Hudhayfah and Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari. One of them said to his companion: 'Narrate what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' The other said: 'Rather, you narrate and I will confirm you.' So one of them narrated and the other confirmed him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: 'Look at his deeds.' He will say: 'My Lord, I did not do any good, except that I had wealth and I used to mix with people. Whoever was well-off, I made things easy for him; and whoever was in difficulty, I gave him respite until his ease.' Then Allah Almighty said: 'I am more deserving of making things easy,' and He forgave him.\" And the other said: You have spoken the truth. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that."],[14664,"Hudhayfah said: I know better than him what is with the Dajjal: \"Indeed with him is a river of fire and a river of water. What they see as fire is water, and what they see as water is fire. Whoever of you reaches that, let him drink from what he sees as fire, for he will find it water.\" Abu Mas'ud said: Thus I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say."],[14665,"A man from those before you commanded that when he died, his corpse be burned, then ground, then raised. When there was a violent wind, it would be scattered in it. Then he was gathered to his Lord, and He said: 'Woe to you! What prompted you to do this?' He said: 'My Lord, there was no servant more daring against You than I, nor more disobedient to You than I, so I hoped that I might escape.' So He forgave him. Abu Mas'ud said: Thus I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[14666,"That they should burn him, then crush him, then scatter him on a windy, violent day. They did so, and he was gathered to his Lord, Mighty and Majestic. He said: 'What prompted you to do what you did?' He said: 'My Lord, there was no servant more disobedient to You than I, so I hoped that I might escape.' He said: 'Overlook My servant,' and He forgave him. Abu Mas'ud said: Thus I heard it from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[14667,"A man was brought by his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and He said: \"What did you do for Me in the world?\" He said: 'I did not do for You even an atom's weight of good that I might hope for, except that I was a man whom You had given wealth. I used to trade with people, and it was my character to overlook, and I would make things easy for the well-off and give respite to the one in difficulty.' Then Allah, Exalted is He, said: \"We are more deserving of that. So overlook My servant,\" and He forgave him. Abu Mas'ud said: Thus I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say."],[14668,"Allah, Exalted is He, will bring a servant from His servants and say: \"What did you do?\" He will say: 'I did not do anything I hope for You with, much of prayer and fasting, except that You gave me surplus wealth, and I used to mix with people, make things easy for the well-off, and give respite to the one in difficulty.' Then He will say: \"We are more deserving of that. So overlook My servant,\" and Allah forgave him."],[14669,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i b. Hirash, from Abu Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, among what people have retained from the speech of the earlier prophethood is: 'If you feel no shame, then do as you wish.'\""],[14670,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, among what the people have attained from the speech of the earlier prophethood is: If you feel no shame, then do as you wish.'"],[14671,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, among what the people have attained from the speech of the earlier prophethood is: If you feel no shame, then act as you wish.'"],[14672,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Indeed, among what the people have attained from the speech of the earlier prophethood is: If you feel no shame, then do as you wish.'"],[14673,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, among what the people have attained from the speech of the earlier prophethood is: If you feel no shame, then do as you wish.'"],[14674,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, among what the people have attained from the speech of the earlier prophethood is: If you feel no shame, then do as you wish.'"],[14675,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The last of what remained from the speech of the earlier prophethood is: If you feel no shame, then do as you wish.'"],[14676,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Indeed, among what the people have attained from the speech of the earlier prophethood is: If you feel no shame, then do as you wish.'"],[14677,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Among what has been attained from the speech of the earlier prophethood is: If you feel no shame, then do as you wish.'"],[14678,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, among what the people have attained from the speech of the earlier prophethood is: If you feel no shame, then do as you wish.'"],[14679,"From a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'We woke up fasting for the completion of thirty days in the month of Ramadan. Then two bedouin men came and testified before the Messenger of God ﷺ that they had sighted the new moon yesterday evening. So the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded them, and they broke their fast.' And the wording is that of the hadith of Abu Hudhayfah."],[14680,"'The people woke up fasting for the completion of thirty days. Then two men came and testified that they had seen the new moon yesterday. So the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded the people, and they broke their fast.' No one said in this hadith, on the authority of Ibn ʿUyaynah or anyone else, on the authority of Abu Masʿud, except Ishaq b. Ismaʿil al-Talaqani."],[14681,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The angels received the soul of a man who was before you. They said to him, \"Have you ever done any good?\" He said, \"No, except that I used to lend money to people, and I would instruct my servants to give respite to the wealthy and to overlook the one in hardship.\" God, glorified and exalted be He, said, \"Overlook [his shortcomings].\"'"],[14682,"I saw Abu Masʿūd when ʿAlī was killed, so I followed him and said: I adjure you by God, what did you hear from the Prophet ﷺ about the trials (fitan)? He said: \"We do not conceal anything. You must observe taqwā of God and adhere to the jamaʿah (community). Beware of splitting, for it is deviation. Indeed, God ﷻ would never gather the ummah of Muhammad ﷺ upon misguidance.\""],[14683,"Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, when Uthman was killed, he secluded himself in his house. I entered upon him and asked him about the situation of the people. He said, \"Adhere to the congregation, for Allah has not gathered the nation of Muhammad on misguidance. Be patient until a righteous person emerges or a corrupt one is removed.\""],[14684,"Abu Masʿūd al-Anṣārī set out in this direction, and I went out with him until when we were at al-Saylaḥīn, he dismounted and I dismounted with him. When I saw that he was alone, I went to him and said: O Abā Masʿūd, among us there were three Companions of Muhammad ﷺ. As for Ḥudhayfah, he died; as for Abū Mūsā, he went to Syria; and you have taken this direction. Of the trials, there has occurred what you see. He said to me: \"O Yasīr, I am giving sincere advice: adhere to the jamaʿah, for God would not gather the ummah of Muhammad ﷺ upon misguidance until the righteous one finds rest or people are relieved of the wicked one.\""],[14685,"Sālim al-Barrād narrated to me—and he was more trustworthy in my view than myself—he said: Abū Masʿūd al-Badrī said to us: \"Shall I not pray for you the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" Then when he bowed (rakʿah), he placed his palms on his knees, spread his fingers, and kept his upper arms away from his sides until every part of him settled. Then he said takbīr, prostrated, and kept his upper arms away from his sides until every part of him settled. Then he said takbīr and sat up straight until every part of him settled. He led us in four rakʿahs like this, then said: \"Thus I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pray—or thus was the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[14686,"\"Shall I not show you how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?\" We said: \"Yes.\" So he stood up and when he bowed, he placed his palms on his knees and put his fingers behind his knees, and held his arms out from his sides, until every part of him settled. Then he raised his head and stood up until every part of him settled. Then he prostrated and held his arms out from his sides, until every part of him settled. Then he sat up until every part of him settled. Then he prostrated again until every part of him settled. Then he did four rak'ahs like that. Then he said: \"This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray, and this is how he used to lead us in prayer.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1037)"],[14687,"\"Shall I pray with you the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" We said: Yes. He stood up and said takbīr, then bowed, placing his palms on his knees and making his fingers below his knees, and kept his upper arms away from his sides until every part of him settled in its place. Then he raised until every part of him settled. He prostrated, placing his palms on the ground and keeping his upper arms away from his sides, and raised his head until every part of him settled. He returned and did the same for four rakʿahs, then said: \"Thus I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pray with us.\""],[14688,"\"When the Prophet ﷺ raised (from bowing), he straightened his back such that if water were poured on his back, it would stay still.\""],[14689,"The Prophet ﷺ became thirsty around the Kaʿbah and asked for a drink. He was brought nabīdh from the siqāyah (drinking place), and he brought it close to his mouth, but he grimaced. A man said: Is it forbidden? He said: \"No.\""],[14690,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"No sacrifice is to be made of an animal with its front or back part of its ears cut off (muqābalah or mudābarah), nor one with a split ear (sharqāʾ), nor one with a pierced ear (khirqāʾ). And the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to examine the eye and the ear.\""],[14691,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The sister-in-law is like a mother.\""],[14692,"Concerning grabbing things at a wedding feast.\""],[14693,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed witr at the beginning of the night, in its middle, and at its end.\""],[14694,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , used to perform the Witr prayer at the beginning, end, and middle of the night."],[14695,"On the authority of Uqbah ibn 'Amr and Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari, they said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform voluntary prayers occasionally at the beginning and middle of the night to make it easy for the Muslims.\""],[14696,"It was narrated that the Prophet ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer at the beginning, middle, and end of the night."],[14697,"While I was beating a slave boy of mine, I heard a voice behind me: \"Know, Abā Masʿūd! Know, Abā Masʿūd!\"—three times. I turned and it was the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: \"By God, God has more power over you than you have over this slave.\" I swore that I would never beat a slave of mine again."],[14698,"While I was beating a slave boy of mine with a whip, I heard a voice from behind me: \"Know, Abā Masʿūd!\" I was so angry that I could not understand, until the Messenger of God ﷺ came close to me. When I saw him, the whip fell from my hand. He said: \"Know, Abā Masʿūd, that God has more power over you than you do.\" I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never strike a slave again."],[14699,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said, “Indeed there are hypocrites among you, so whoever I name, let him stand up.” Thirty-six men stood up. Then he said, “Indeed there are among you or from you – so ask Allah for well-being.” Then Umar passed by a man whom he knew and said, “What is your matter?” He told him what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said, and Umar said, “May you be far from good for the rest of the day.”"],[14700,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him as a tax collector, he said, “Look, Abu Mas‘ud, let me not find you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a camel on your back that has a bray, from the camels of zakat, which you have embezzled.” He said, “I am not going in this direction of mine.” The Prophet said, “Then I will not compel you.”"],[14701,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed me to collect sadaqah and then said: Go, AbuMas'ud, I should not find you on the Day of Judgment carrying a camel of sadaqah on your back, which rumbles, the one you have taken by unfaithful dealing in sadaqah. He said: If it is so, I will not go. He said: Then I do not force you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2947)"],[14702,"“We have been granted a dispensation for weddings and for weeping over the dead as long as there is no wailing.”"],[14703,"We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we know how to say salaam to you, but how do we send blessings upon you?\" He said, \"Say: \"O Allah, send prayers upon Muhammad as You sent prayers upon Ibrahim. O Allah, bless Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim.\""],[14704,"He informed him, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and sat with us in the gathering of Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah. Bashir ibn Sa'd, also known as Abu Nu'man ibn Bashir, said to him: Allah has commanded us to send blessings upon you, so how should we send blessings upon you? The Messenger of Allah remained silent until we wished that he had not been asked. Then he said: Say, \"Allahumma salli 'ala Muhammadin wa 'ala ali Muhammadin kama salayta 'ala Ibrahim wa barik 'ala Muhammadin kama barakta 'ala Ibrahim fi al-'alamayn, innaka hamidun majid (O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim, and bestow blessings upon Muhammad as You bestowed blessings upon Ibrahim in the two worlds. You are indeed praiseworthy, glorious)\"."],[14705,"We discussed standing at the funeral in the presence of Ali. Abu Mas‘ud said, “We have continued to do it.” Ali said, “He spoke the truth, and you are witnesses.”"],[14706,"“Yes, I remembered.”"],[14707,"Hudhayfah prayed with his companions on a bench in al-Mada’in, so Abu Mas‘ud made him come down. When he finished his prayer, he said, “Did you not know that we were forbidden from this?” He said, “Yes, I remembered when you brought me down.”"],[14708,"I was brought to Hudhayfah and Abu Mas'ud in the mosque, and Abu Mas'ud was saying: By Allah, I never thought that it would increase beyond its heel, and not a cupping glass of blood was spilled in it. Hudhayfah said: \"But I knew that it would increase beyond its heel, and not a cupping glass of blood was spilled in it. A man will enter the morning as a believer and enter the evening as a disbeliever, and enter the evening as a believer and enter the morning as a disbeliever, and his heart will be turned upside down and his buttocks will rise above him. He fights the fitnah today, and Allah kills him tomorrow.\" Abu Mas'ud said: \"This is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to us about the fitnah.\""],[14709,"On the authority of Abu Thawr al-Hudayani, who said: I was sent to Hudhayfa and Abu Mas'ud while they were in the Mosque of Kufa during the days of the Jarā'ah (a plague or epidemic) when the people did to Sa'id ibn al-Aas what they did, and Abu Mas'ud was teaching the people and he said, \"By Allah, I do not see that it should be retaliated until there is bloodshed in it.\" Hudhayfa said, \"By Allah, it will be retaliated and there will be no bloodshed in it, and I do not know anything in it today except that I have learned it, and Muhammad ﷺ is alive.\" Harun ibn Saad was not mentioned in his narration, nor was Abu al-Bakhtari mentioned."],[14710,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Is one of you unable to recite a third of the Qur'an?\" That seemed great to them, so he said: \"Allah, the One, the Eternal Refuge is a third of the Qur'an.\""],[14711,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Is one of you overcome from reciting a third of the Qur'an every night?\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, which of us can bear that? He said: \"Qul huwa Allahu ahad.\""],[14712,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Is one of you unable, or is one of you overcome, from reciting a third of the Qur'an?\" We said to him about that, so he said: \"Qul huwa Allahu ahad.\""],[14713,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made an appointment with us at the foot of al-'Aqabah on the day of al-Adha, and we were seventy men. 'Uqbah said: Indeed, I am the youngest of them in age. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and said: \"Be brief in the sermon, for I fear for you the disbelievers of Quraysh.\" We said: O Messenger of Allah, ask for us from your Lord, and ask for us for yourself, and ask for us for your companions, and tell us what reward we have from Allah ﷻ and from you. He said: \"As for what I ask for my Lord, that you believe in Him and not associate anything with Him. As for what I ask for myself, I ask you to obey me, and I will guide you to the path of right guidance. And I ask you for me and for my companions that you share with us from what you possess and that you protect us from what you protect yourselves. If you do that, then you will have Paradise from Allah and from me.\" He said: So we stretched out our hands and pledged allegiance to him."],[14714,"Abu Mas'ud said to him: \"By Allah, O Mughirah, you know that Jibril ﷺ descended and prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, and the people prayed with him. Then he descended and prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, and the people prayed with him, until he counted five prayers.\" 'Umar said to him: Watch what you say, O 'Urwah. Indeed, Jibril is the one who established the time of the prayer. 'Urwah said to him: This is how Bashir b. Abi Mas'ud narrated to me. He said: 'Umar continued to know the time of the prayer by a sign until he departed from this world."],[14715,"'Urwah said: Al-Mughirah delayed the 'Asr prayer while he was over Kufah, and Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari entered upon him and said: What is this, O Mughirah? By Allah, you know that Jibril descended and prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, and the people prayed five prayers, saying it. Then he said: \"This is what I was commanded.\" 'Umar said to 'Urwah: Know what you are saying, for Jibril is the one who established the time of the prayer. 'Urwah said: This is how Bashir b. Abi Mas'ud narrated from his father."],[14716,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, he said: I recited to Malik b. Anas. And Bakr b. Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, 'Abdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed us. And 'Ali b. al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il b. Abi Uways narrated to us, Malik narrated to me from Ibn Shihab that 'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Aziz delayed the prayer one day, and 'Urwah b. al-Zubayr entered upon him and informed him that al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah delayed the prayer one day while he was in Kufah, and Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari entered upon him and said: O Mughirah, do you not know that Jibril ﷺ descended and prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, then he said: \"With this I was commanded.\" 'Umar said to 'Urwah: Know what you narrate, O 'Urwah. Or was it Jibril who established for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the time of the prayer? 'Urwah said: This is how Bashir b. Abi Mas'ud narrated from his father."],[14717,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us. And 'Ubayd b. Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: 'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Aziz delayed the prayer one day, and 'Urwah b. al-Zubayr said to him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Jibril ﷺ descended and led me in prayer, and I prayed with him. Then he descended and led me in prayer, and I prayed with him. Then he descended and led me in prayer, and I prayed with him, until he counted the five prayers.\" 'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Aziz said to him: Fear Allah, O 'Urwah, and watch what you say. 'Urwah said: Bashir b. Abi Mas'ud informed me from his father from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. And the wording is that of al-Humaydi."],[14718,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Jibril ﷺ descended and led me in prayer, and I prayed with him. Then I prayed with him. Then I prayed with him. Then I prayed with him. Then I prayed with him.\" And he counted with his fingers five prayers."],[14719,"Jibril ﷺ descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and prayed with him, and informed him of the time of the prayer. 'Umar said: What do you say, O 'Abdullah? 'Urwah said at that: Bashir b. Abi Mas'ud al-Ansari informed me from Abu Mas'ud that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Jibril ﷺ descended upon me, and I prayed with him. Then I prayed with him. Then I prayed with him. Then I prayed with him. Then I prayed with him. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying the noonday prayer when the sun begins to decline, and sometimes he would delay it in intense heat. And the 'Asr prayer while the sun was white and high, a man could travel from it until he returned from it to Dhu al-Hulayfah, six miles before sunset. And he would pray Maghrib when the sun had set, and pray 'Isha' when the horizon had become dark, and pray Subh in the darkness before dawn. Then one day he prayed it and it became bright, then he did not return to brightness until Allah took him. And the wording is that of Abu Salih."],[14720,"Jibril ﷺ descended and prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, then he prayed and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, then he said, \"Thus have I been commanded.\""],[14721,"I was before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hajj, and the foam of his camel was falling on my back, and I heard him say, \"Give to every possessor of a right his right. The child belongs to the bed, and for the fornicator is the stone. Whoever allies himself with other than his patrons or claims descent from other than his father, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all the people. Neither will any obligatory duty nor supererogatory act be accepted from him.\""],[14722,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Quraysh, \"This affair will continue to be among you, and you will be its guardians, as long as you do not introduce innovations. If you do that, Allah will set upon you the worst of His creation, and they will strip you as a branch is stripped.\""],[14723,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Quraysh, \"This affair will continue to be among you, and you will be its guardians.\""],[14724,"We were sitting in the company of Sa'id b. 'Ubida when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us. Bashir b. S'ad said: Allah has commanded us to bless you. Messenger of Allah! But how should we bless you? He (the narrator) said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept quiet (and we were so much perturbed over his silence) that we wished we had not asked him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: (For blessing me) say:\" 0 Allah, bless Muhammad and the members of his household as Thou didst bless the mernbers of Ibrahim's household. Grant favours to Muhammad and the members of his household as Thou didst grant favours to the members of the household of Ibrahim in the world. Thou art indeed Praiseworthy and Glorious\" ; and salutation as you know. (Using translation from Muslim 405)"],[14725,"The Prophet ﷺ \"forbade the price of a dog, the earnings of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer.\""],[14726,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the price of a dog, the earnings of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer.\""],[14727,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"forbade the price of a dog, the earnings of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer.\""],[14728,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade the price paid for a dog, the hire paid to a prostitute, and the gift given to a soothsayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3428)"],[14729,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he \"forbade the price of a dog, the earnings of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer.\""],[14730,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he \"forbade the price of a dog, the earnings of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer.\""],[14731,"He informed him, saying: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from the price of a dog, the earnings of a soothsayer, and the dowry of a prostitute.” Ibn Shihab said: “The earnings of a soothsayer is his wage.”"],[14732,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “A Muslim owes his brother four courtesies: to answer him when he invites him, to attend his funeral when he dies, to visit him when he is ill, and to say ‘yarhamuk Allah’ to him when he sneezes.”"],[14733,"My grandfather and my father narrated to me that they saw ʿUqbah b. ʿĀmir al-Juhanī dyeing his hair black."],[14734,"And he was a poet."],[14735,"About three things, so hold fast to them: do not accept a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except from a trustworthy person; do not incur debt even if you have to wear coarse woolen cloaks; and do not write poetry so that it distracts your hearts from the Qur’an."],[14736,"He said to me: “O ʿUqbah, when did you put these two on?” I said: “On Friday.” He said: “And today is Friday?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “You have done right.”"],[14737,"One day I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I hastened to him and took his hand, or he hastened to me and took my hand. Then he said: “O ʿUqbah, shall I not tell you of the best traits of the people of this world and the Hereafter? You maintain ties with those who cut you off, you give to those who deprive you, and you pardon those who wrong you. Whoever desires that his provision be expanded and his lifespan extended, let him fear Allah and maintain ties of kinship.” The wording is that of the hadith of Ibn Abī Maryam."],[14738,"I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me what the most virtuous deeds are.” He said: “To give to those who deprive you, to maintain ties with those who cut you off, and to pardon those who wrong you.”"],[14739,"One day I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked: “What is salvation?” He said: “O ʿUqbah, restrain your tongue, let your house suffice you, and weep over your sins.”"],[14740,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Shall I not tell you of the best three surahs revealed in the Torah, the Gospel, the Psalms, and the Criterion?” I said: “Teach me, O Messenger of Allah, from what Allah has taught you.” Then he recited: “Say: He is Allah, the One,” “Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the dawn,” and “Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.” He said: “If you can, do not let a night pass without reciting them, and do not let a day pass without reciting them.”"],[14741,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the salvation of the believer?” He said: “Guard your tongue, let your house suffice you, and weep over your sins.”"],[14742,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, shall I perform Hajj on behalf of my mother who has died?” He said, “Do you not think that if your mother owed a debt and you paid it, it would be accepted from you?” She said, “Yes.” So he commanded her to perform Hajj on her behalf. Then a woman came and said, “Shall I take my infant son with me for Hajj?” He said, “Yes.”"],[14743,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about his sister who had vowed to walk to the Kaʿbah. He said, “Allah is in no need of your sister’s vow. Let her ride and sacrifice a camel.”"],[14744,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The expiation for a vow is the expiation for an oath.”"],[14745,"The expiation of the (breach of) a vow is the same as that of the (breach of an oath). (Using translation from Muslim 1645)"],[14746,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “The expiation for a vow is the expiation for an oath.”"],[14747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The expiation for a vow is the expiation for an oath.”"],[14748,"That she asked me to seek a ruling for her, so I asked the Prophet ﷺ for her, and he said, “Let her walk and let her ride.” Abu al-Khayr never parted from ʿUqbah."],[14749,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ [said], “Let her walk and let her ride.”"],[14750,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Indeed, the conditions most deserving to be fulfilled are those by which you have made private parts lawful.”"],[14751,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The conditions most deserving to be fulfilled are those by which you have made private parts lawful.”"],[14752,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed, the most deserving of conditions for you to fulfill are those by which you have made women’s private parts lawful,” or he said, “by which private parts have been made lawful.”"],[14753,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us, ʿAbdullah b. Lahiʿah narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from ʿUqbah b. ʿAmir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Indeed, the conditions most deserving to be fulfilled are those by which you have made private parts lawful.”"],[14754,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Indeed, the conditions most deserving to be fulfilled are those by which you have made private parts lawful.”"],[14755,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The conditions most deserving to be fulfilled are those by which you have made the private parts lawful.”"],[14756,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed in a silk garment, then took it off. I said: “O Messenger of God, you prayed in it and then took it off?” He said: “This is not the clothing of the pious.”"],[14757,"He said: A silk garment was gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ, he wore it, then prayed in it, then left and took it off forcefully, as if disliking it, then said: “This is not befitting for the pious.”"],[14758,"A silk garment was gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ, he wore it and prayed. When he said the salam, he took it off harshly, then threw it aside. They said: “O Messenger of God, you wore it and prayed in it?” He said: “This is not befitting for the pious.”"],[14759,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave him some sheep, and he divided them among his companions as sacrificial animals. A young goat remained, and he mentioned it to the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said: “Sacrifice it yourself.”"],[14760,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Beware of entering upon women.” A man from the Ansar said: “O Messenger of God, what about the brother-in-law?” He said: “The brother-in-law is death.”"],[14761,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not enter upon women.” A man from the Ansar said: “O Messenger of God, what about the brother-in-law?” He said: “The brother-in-law is death.”"],[14762,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not converse with women.”"],[14763,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Do not enter upon women.” It was said: “The brother-in-law?” He said: “The brother-in-law is death.”"],[14764,"We said, \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! You send us out and it happens that we have to stay with such people as do not entertain us. What do you think about it?\" Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, \"If you stay with some people and they entertain you as they should for a guest, accept is; but if they do not do then you should take from them the right of the guest, which they ought to give.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6137)"],[14765,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out one day and prayed over the martyrs of Uhud as he prayed over the dead, then went to the pulpit and said: “I am your forerunner, and I am a witness over you. By God, I can see my cistern right now. I have been given the keys of the earth, and by God, I do not fear that you will associate partners after me, but I fear that you will compete with each other over it.”"],[14766,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered funeral prayers for the martyrs of Uhud after eight years, as if bidding farewell to the living and the dead. Then he ascended the pulpit and said, \"Indeed, I am going ahead of you, and I am a witness over you. Indeed, your meeting place is at the pond (in Paradise), and I am looking at it from this position of mine. Indeed, I am not afraid that you will associate others with Allah, but I am afraid that you will compete with each other for worldly benefits.\" Ubay ibn Ka'b said, \"This was the last gaze I cast at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One of them directed towards his conversation companion and the other did not mention Al-Laith ibn Sa'd after eight years.\""],[14767,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed over the slain of Uhud, then ascended the pulpit, as if bidding farewell to the living and the dead, and said: “I am your forerunner at the cistern. Its width is between Ayla and al-Juhfa. I do not fear that you will associate partners after me, but I fear for you the world, that you will compete with each other over it, and thus falter, and thus perish, as those before you perished.” That was the last time I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ in the mosque."],[14768,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed over the slain of Uhud, then left and sat on the pulpit. He praised God and extolled Him, then said: “O people, I am a forerunner before you, and I am a witness over you. By God, I can see my cistern from where I stand. Its expanse is between al-Juhfa and Ayla. By God, I do not fear that you will associate partners after me, but I have been given the keys to the treasures of the world and the treasures of the earth. I only fear that you will compete with each other over them.” Then he entered and did not come out of his house until God ﷻ took him."],[14769,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every person is in the shade of his charity until judgment is passed among the people.” Or he said: “until judgment is rendered among the people.” Yazid said: Abu al-Khayr never let a day pass without giving charity, whether a cake, a bean, or something else he named."],[14770,"He said to the Prophet ﷺ: “My mother left behind jewelry; should I give it in charity on her behalf?” He said: “Did she instruct you to do that?” He said: “No.” He said: “Then keep it for yourself.”"],[14771,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “My mother has died and left behind jewelry, and she did not make a will. Will it benefit her if I give it in charity on her behalf?” He said: “Keep your wealth for yourself.”"],[14772,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “You must use this blessed tree, the oil of olives, and treat yourselves with it, for it is a cure for hemorrhoids.”"],[14773,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Our Lord is All-Hearing, All-Seeing,” and he pointed with his hand to his eyes."],[14774,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite this verse at the end of Surah An-Nur, while placing his two fingers under his eyes and saying, \"With Him are the keys of all things; He sees everything.\""],[14775,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The mu'adhdhins will have the longest necks of all people on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[14776,"The Prophet ﷺ took a handful of dates and said: “What an excellent suhur for the Muslim.”"],[14777,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Recite these two verses at the end of Surat al-Baqarah, for my Lord gave them to me from beneath the Throne.”"],[14778,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Recite these two verses at the conclusion of Surat al-Baqarah, for I was given them from beneath the Throne.”"],[14779,"He said: “Repeat the two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah: {The Messenger believes in what was revealed to him from his Lord} to its conclusion, for Allah chose Muhammad ﷺ by means of them.”"],[14780,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “There is no day’s deeds but they are sealed upon it. When the believer falls ill, the angels say: ‘O our Lord, Your servant so-and-so You have detained.’ He says: ‘Continue recording for him the like of his deeds until he recovers or dies.’”"],[14781,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The likeness of one who does evil deeds then does good deeds is like a man who had on a tight coat of mail that was choking him. Then he did a good deed, and one ring loosened. Then he did another, and another ring loosened, until it came off onto the ground.”"],[14782,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The example of one who commits evil deeds then does good deeds is like a man wearing a tight coat of mail that has choked him; each time he performs a good deed, a ring is loosened, then another, until he comes out to the ground.\""],[14783,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When I was taken up to the heavens, I entered the Garden of Eden, and an apple fell into my hand. When I held it in my hand, it split open revealing a wide-eyed, pleasing houri whose eyelashes were like the leading edges of eagles' wings. I said to her, 'For whom are you?' She said, 'I am for the successor after you.'\""],[14784,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever has a man embrace Islam at his hands, Paradise is assured for him.\""],[14785,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Charity extinguishes the heat of the graves.\""],[14786,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Charity extinguishes for its giver the heat of the graves, and the believer will only seek shade on the Day of Resurrection in the shade of his charity.\""],[14787,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was riding his white mule. I placed my hand on his foot and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, teach me [something to recite].\" He said, \"You will never recite anything more effective before Allah than 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak.'\""],[14788,"\"O Messenger of Allah, you have grown gray.\" He said, \"Hud and its sisters have made me gray.\""],[14789,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, one of us commits a sin?\" He said, \"It is recorded against him.\" Then he said, \"Then he seeks forgiveness for it and repents?\" He said, \"He is forgiven and rewarded for it, and Allah does not tire until you tire.\""],[14790,"\"This is a prayer we used to perform in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[14791,"He reported: I heard Abu al-Khayr say, \"I saw Abu Tamim al-Jayshani pray two rak'ahs when he heard the call to Maghrib before the prayer. I came intending to stop him, but 'Uqbah b. 'Amir said, 'We used to do this in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'\""],[14792,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Three things—whoever is saved from them is saved: whoever is saved from killing a believer is saved; whoever is saved from killing a caliph who was killed unjustly while he was patient, giving the truth of himself, is saved; and whoever is saved from the trial of the Dajjal is saved.\""],[14793,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"No man sees a private part of his brother and conceals it except that Allah will conceal him and admit him to Paradise.\""],[14794,"that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If there is healing in anything, it is in the stroke of a cupper, a drink of honey, or a cauterization that hits pain; but I dislike cauterization and do not love it.”"],[14795,"I heard ʿUqbah b. ʿĀmir al-Juhanī say: “Three times the Messenger of God ﷺ used to forbid us to pray in them, or to bury our dead in them: when the sun rises appearing until it is high, when the midday heat stands until the sun declines, and when the sun turns to setting until it sets.”"],[14796,"I heard ʿUqbah b. ʿĀmir say: The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us while we were in the veranda and said: “Which of you would like to go out every morning to Buṭḥān or al-ʿAqīq and bring two camel mares, large-humped and fine, and take them?” We said: “O Messenger of God, all of us would love that.” He said: “Would not one of you go out to the mosque and learn two verses of the Book of God, which is better for him than two camels; and three, better for him than three; and four, better for him than four; and their numbers like the days of Minā from camels.”"],[14797,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out while we were studying the Qur’an and said: “Learn the Book of God, spread it, and chant it. For by the One in whose hand is my soul, it slips away faster than a pregnant camel from its rope.”"],[14798,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Learn the Qur’an, chant it, and acquire it. For by the One in whose hand is my soul, it slips away faster than a pregnant camel from its rope.”"],[14799,"that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The day of ʿArafah, the day of sacrifice, and the days of tashrīq are our festival, the people of Islam, and they are days of eating and drinking.”"],[14800,"that the Prophet ﷺ divorced Ḥafṣah. This reached ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb, so he placed dust on his head and said: “God will not care about you, O son of al-Khaṭṭāb, after this.” Then Jibrīl ﷺ came down and said: “God Almighty commands you to take back Ḥafṣah as a mercy to ʿUmar.”"],[14801,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Who will inform us where our milch-camels are?” A man stood and said: “I will.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “What is your name?” He said: “Ṣakhr” or “Jandal.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “Sit.” Then he said: “Who will inform us where our milch-camels are?” A man stood and said: “I will.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “What is your name?” He said: “Yaʿīsh.” He said: “Inform us where our milch-camels are.”"],[14802,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of God. They do not eclipse for the death of anyone or for his life. So when you see that, hasten to prayer.”"],[14803,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not force your sick ones to eat, for God feeds them and gives them drink.”"],[14804,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Shall I inform you of the best of your governors and the worst of them?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “The best of them for you are those whom you love and who love you, and you pray to God for them and they pray to God for you. And the worst of them for you are those whom you hate and who hate you, and you pray to God against them and they pray to God against you.” They said: “Shall we not fight them, O Messenger of God?” He said: “No, leave them as long as they fast and pray.”"],[14805,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When you want to go on a raid, buy a horse that is white on the forehead and legs, with the right foreleg marked white, for you will be safe and gain booty.”"],[14806,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, I seek refuge with You from an evil day, from an evil night, from an evil hour, from an evil companion, and from an evil neighbour in the eternal abode.”"],[14807,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to recite the Muʿawwidhat after every prayer.”"],[14808,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Recite the Muʿawwidhat after every prayer.”"],[14809,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said of a man called Dhu al-Bijadayn: “He is one who turns to Allah often (awwah).” That was because he used to remember Allah much through the Qur'an and supplication."],[14810,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “These lineages of yours are not a cause for reviling anyone. You are all children of Adam, like the fill of a saʿ; if you fill it, no one has superiority over another except through religion or righteous deeds. It is enough for a man to be obscene, vulgar, miserly, and given to oaths.”"],[14811,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What I fear most for my community is the Book and milk. As for milk, it will be opened up for some people who will abandon Friday prayer and Friday prayers. As for the Book, it will be opened up for some people who will argue with it against the believers.”"],[14812,"I heard Uqbah bin Amir say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Verily, the thing that I fear the most for my Ummah is milk and the Book.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the matter with milk?\" He said, \"They leave gatherings and abandon congregations.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the matter with the Book?\" He said, \"It will be opened for certain people, and they will recite it and engage in argumentation with it.\""],[14813,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Some of my community will be destroyed because of the Book and milk.” ʿUqbah b. ʿAmir said: I said, “What are the people of the Book?” He said, “People who learn the Book of Allah and argue with it against the believers.” I said, “And what are the people of milk, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “People who pursue desires and neglect prayers.”"],[14814,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever hangs a seashell, may Allah not grant him peace; whoever hangs an amulet, may Allah not complete things for him.”"],[14815,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Some people from my Ummah will emerge who will drink the Quran just as they drink milk.\""],[14816,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If there were to be a prophet after me, it would be ʿUmar.”"],[14817,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The people of Yemen have the softest and most tender hearts and are the most obedient.”"],[14818,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I not inform you of the borrowed billy-goat?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “He is the one who makes a woman lawful [for her former husband]. May Allah curse the one who makes a woman lawful and the one for whom she is made lawful.”"],[14819,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Whoever has three daughters and is patient with them, feeds them, gives them drink, and clothes them, they will be a screen for him from the Fire.”"],[14820,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Whoever has three daughters and is patient with them, feeds them, gives them drink, and clothes them, they will be a screen for him from the Fire.”"],[14821,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever loses three children from his own loins and expects reward for them from Allah.” Abu ʿUshana said once, “in the path of Allah,” but did not say it another time – “Paradise becomes obligatory for him.”"],[14822,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said: “Whoever has three daughters and is patient with them, they will be a covering for him from the Fire.”"],[14823,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ he said: “Whoever performs ablution, gathers his clothes, then goes out to the mosque, his scribe writes ten good deeds for him with every step. A person remains in prayer as long as he is waiting for the prayer, and he is recorded among those who pray from the time he leaves his house until he returns.”"],[14824,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in Hell.”"],[14825,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Your Lord marvels at a shepherd of sheep on the top of a mountain crag who calls the adhan for prayer and prays. Allah, may He be glorified, says, ‘Look at this servant of Mine: he calls the adhan and establishes the prayer out of fear of Me. I have forgiven My servant and admitted him to Paradise.’”"],[14826,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The sun will come close to the earth on the Day of Judgment, and people will sweat. Among them are those whose sweat reaches their ankles, and others whose sweat reaches their knees, and some whose sweat reaches their hips, and others whose sweat reaches their shoulders, and others whose sweat reaches their ears, and others whose sweat covers them completely.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then pointed to his fingers and held them between his lips, and said, \"And among them are those who are submerged in their sweat.\""],[14827,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid his family from ornaments and silk, and he would say: “If you love the ornaments of Paradise and its silk, then do not touch them in this world.”"],[14828,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The first two adversaries on the Day of Resurrection will be two neighbors.”"],[14829,"I heard ʿUqbah b. ʿĀmir saying on the pulpit: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah while I was tending sheep. I left them and went to him and said, 'Will you accept my pledge, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'From whom are you?' I told him. He said, 'Which is dearer to you: a pledge of emigration or a Bedouin pledge?' I said, 'A pledge of emigration.' So he accepted my pledge. Then he said, 'Whoever here is from Maʿadd, let him stand.' I stood. He said, 'Sit.' Then he said, 'Whoever here is from Maʿadd, let him stand.' I stood. He said, 'Sit.' Then he said it a third time. I stood. He said, 'Sit.' I said, 'From whom are we, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'You are from Quḍāʿah, then from Mālik b. Ḥimyar.'"],[14830,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The greatest hypocrites of my community are its reciters.'"],[14831,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: 'When a servant performs ablution and then comes to the mosque to observe the prayer, for every step he takes to the mosque ten good deeds are recorded for him. The one sitting in it awaiting the prayer is like the one in constant devotion, and he is recorded among those who pray from the time he leaves his house until he returns to it.'"],[14832,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever attributes to me something I did not say, let him take his seat in Hellfire.'"],[14833,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever attributes to me something I did not say, let him take his seat in Hellfire.'"],[14834,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"On the Day of Resurrection, the sun will come close to the earth and people will sweat. Among the people, there will be those whose sweat reaches their knees, and among them are those whose sweat reaches their ankles, and among them are those whose sweat reaches their shoulders, and among them are those whose sweat reaches their necks, and among them are those whose sweat covers their entire body.\" And he gestured with his hand to demonstrate. He said, \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spreading his sweat in this way, and some of them will have their sweat covering them.\" And he struck his head with his hand."],[14835,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The people submitted (became Muslim), and ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ believed.'"],[14836,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is the Hajj favored with two prostrations?' He said: 'Yes, so whoever does not prostrate in them, let him not recite them.'"],[14837,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, are there two prostrations in Sūrat al-Ḥajj?' He said: 'Yes, so if he does not prostrate for them, let him not recite them.'"],[14838,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Every deceased person has his deeds sealed at death, except the one stationed in the path of Allah, for his deeds continue to accrue for him until he is resurrected.'"],[14839,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'Recite the Muʿawwidhatān (the two chapters of seeking refuge), for you will never recite anything like them.'"],[14840,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If the Qurʾan were placed in a hide, the fire would not consume it.'"],[14841,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Faith is Yemeni, and harshness and coarseness of hearts are in Rabīʿah and Muḍar, near the tails of camels.'"],[14842,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The first two disputants on the Day of Resurrection will be two neighbors.\""],[14843,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ marvels at a young man who has no youthful indiscretion.\""],[14844,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever has three daughters and is patient with them, they will be a screen for him from the Fire.\""],[14845,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Your Lord marvels at a shepherd of sheep on a mountain peak who calls the adhan for prayer and gives the iqamah.\""],[14846,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not dislike daughters, for they are the comforting, precious ones.\""],[14847,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If there were a prophet after me, it would be ʿUmar b. al-Khattab ؓ.\""],[14848,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever acts deliberately, hits the mark or nearly does; and whoever acts hastily, errs or nearly does.\""],[14849,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever Allah has blessed with a favor and wants it to remain, let him frequently say: 'There is no might nor power except with Allah.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {If only, when you entered your garden, you had said, 'What Allah wills [will be]; there is no power except with Allah'}\""],[14850,"I followed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was riding, and I placed my hand on his foot and said: \"Teach me from Surah Hud or Surah Yusuf.\" He said: \"You will never recite anything more efficacious with Allah than 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak.'\""],[14851,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day while he was riding, and I placed my hand on his foot and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, teach me from Surah Hud or from Surah Yusuf.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O ʿUqbah b. ʿAmir, you will never recite a surah more beloved to Allah and more efficacious with Him than reciting 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak.' So if you can ensure it never escapes you in any prayer, do so.\""],[14852,"He heard ʿUqbah b. ʿAmir say: \"I clung to the foot of the Messenger of Allah and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, teach me Surah Hud and Surah Yusuf.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'O ʿUqbah, you will never recite a surah more beloved to Allah nor more efficacious than \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak.\"'\""],[14853,"I am Abu Hammad. I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: \"Whoever finds a Muslim upon a private part and conceals it, it is as if he revived a buried alive girl from her grave.\""],[14854,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The expiation of a vow is the expiation of an oath.\""],[14855,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A vow is an oath, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.\""],[14856,"The people said: 'Glory be to God, glory be to God.' And he realized what they intended. When he completed his prayer, he prostrated two prostrations while sitting. Then he said: \"Indeed I heard your words. This is the Sunnah.\""],[14857,"The people behind him said: 'Glory be to God,' but he did not sit. When he finished, he prostrated two prostrations while sitting. Then he said: \"I heard you saying 'Glory be to God' so that I sit, but that is not the Sunnah. Rather, the Sunnah is what I have done.\""],[14858,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"A band of my community will continue fighting upon the truth, dominant over their enemy. The enmity of those who oppose them will not harm them until the Hour comes to them while they are upon that.\""],[14859,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I saw the Fire, and in it I saw ʿImrān b. Ḥurthān leaning on his bow. He used to steal from the pilgrims. And I saw the woman of the cat from Ḥimyar.\""],[14860,"He heard ʿUqbah b. ʿĀmir al-Juhanī saying: I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ one day, and he prolonged the standing, though when he prayed with us he usually kept it light. I saw him reach out with his hand to take something. Then he bowed after that. When the Messenger of God ﷺ said the salutation, he sat and we sat around him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I knew that the length of my prayer and my standing alarmed you.\" We said: Yes, O Messenger of God, and we heard you say: \"O Lord, and I am among them?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, there is nothing you have been promised in the Hereafter but that it has been shown to me in this place of mine, until even the Fire was shown to me. Sparks from it came toward me until they were level with this tent of mine, and I feared that they would overwhelm you. So I said: 'O Lord, and I am among them?' Then God turned it away from you, and it retreated in pieces like carpets. I took a glance and saw ʿImrān b. Ḥurthān b. al-Ḥārith, one of the Banū Ghifār, leaning in Hell upon his bow. And I saw in it the Ḥimyarī woman, the owner of the cat who tied it up and neither fed it nor gave it water.\" Aḥmad b. Ṣāliḥ said: the correct form is Ḥurthān."],[14861,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The believer is the brother of the believer. It is not lawful for a believer to purchase against the purchase of his brother until he leaves it, nor to propose against his proposal until he leaves it.\""],[14862,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"None of you may purchase against the purchase of his brother, nor propose against his proposal.\""],[14863,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim.\""],[14864,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim. It is not lawful for a Muslim, if he sells something to his brother that has a defect, unless he makes it clear to him.\""],[14865,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “No collector of unjust taxes will enter Paradise.”"],[14866,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “No collector of unjust taxes will enter Paradise.”"],[14867,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “No collector of unjust taxes will enter Paradise.”"],[14868,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “One who dies of pleurisy is a martyr.”"],[14869,"ʿUqbah, were it not for words I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would not have cared: “Whoever learns archery then abandons it is not one of us.”"],[14870,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Whoever sees the private shame of a Muslim and conceals it, it is as if he revived a girl buried alive from her grave.”"],[14871,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever sees a private shame and conceals it is like one who revives a girl buried alive from her grave.”"],[14872,"Ten men came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance. He accepted the pledge of nine and withheld from one. They said, “O Messenger of Allah, you accepted the pledge of nine and withheld from this one?” He said, “This one has an amulet on him.” So he put his hand in and cut it off, then he pledged allegiance to him."],[14873,"That she walk to the House of Allah barefoot and unveiled. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by her and said, “What is the matter with her?” They said, “She vowed to walk to the House of Allah barefoot and unveiled.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Tell her to cover her head, ride, and perform the pilgrimage.”"],[14874,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When Allah gathers the first and the last, and judges between them, and finishes judging between them, the believers will say, “Our Lord has judged between us. Who will intercede for us with our Lord? Let us go to Adam, for he is our father, and Allah created him with His hand and spoke to him.” They will come to him and ask him to intercede for them, but he will say, “You should go to Nuh.” So they will come to Nuh, and he will direct them to Ibrahim. They will come to Ibrahim, and he will direct them to Musa. They will come to Musa, and he will direct them to ʿIsa. Then they will come to ʿIsa, and he will say, “I will direct you to the unlettered Prophet.” So they will come to me, and Allah will permit me to stand, and my place will send forth the most fragrant scent anyone has ever smelled, until I come to my Lord, Blessed and Exalted. He will grant me intercession and place for me a light from the hair of my head to the nail of my foot. Then the disbelievers will say, “The believers have found someone to intercede for them, so who will intercede for us?” They will say, “No one but Iblis; he is the one who led us astray.” So they will come to him and say, “The believers have found someone to intercede for them, so you stand and intercede for us, for you are the one who led us astray.” He will stand, and his place will send forth the foulest stench anyone has ever smelled. Then he will drive them into Hell, and at that point he will say: {And Satan will say when the matter is decided: “Indeed, Allah promised you a true promise, and I promised you, but I broke it.”}"],[14875,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Subayʿah al-Aslamiyyah eating with her left hand and said, “What is wrong with her that she eats with her left hand? Do I find her wicked?” She said, “O Messenger of Allah, there is a sore on my right hand.” He said, “Even so.”"],[14876,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, “Place it in your prostrations.”"],[14877,"When this verse was revealed: {So glorify the name of your Lord, the Most Great} (Quran 56:96), the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Place it in your bowing.” And when “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High” (Quran 87:1) was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Place it in your prostration.” And when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed, he said: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most Great” three times, and when he prostrated, he said: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High” three times."],[14878,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is thrown from his mount is a martyr.”"],[14879,"To walk barefoot without being menstruating, Uqbah asked the Prophet ﷺ about this matter. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, \"Indeed, Allah is self-sufficient from your sister's distress. Therefore, instruct her to become menstruating, perform Ghusl (ritual bath), and fast for three days.\""],[14880,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Men will recite the Quran but it will not go beyond their collarbones; they will pass out of the religion as an arrow passes through its game.”"],[14881,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Before the Hour, a black cloud will appear to you from the west, like a shield. It will keep rising in the sky and spreading until it fills the sky. Then a caller will call out: ‘O people!’ They will turn to one another: ‘Did you hear?’ Some will say: ‘Yes.’ Then he will call a second time: ‘O people, the command of Allah has come, so do not seek to hasten it.’” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, two men will be spreading out a garment and will not fold it up, and a man will leave his watering trough and never drink from it again, and a man will be milking his she-camel and never drink it again.”"],[14882,"\"There are five things, whoever dies of any of them is a martyr. The one who is killed in the cause of Allah is a martyr; the one who dies of an abdominal complaint in the cause of Allah is a martyr; the one who dies of the plague in the cause of Allah is a martyr; and the woman who dies in childbirth in the cause of Allah is a martyr.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3163)"],[14883,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would wake up in a state of major ritual impurity, then bathe and fast."],[14884,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then prays without being heedless, his past sins of the previous year will be expiated.”"],[14885,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then prays without being heedless or distracted, his past sins will be expiated.”"],[14886,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Stand up, O ʿUqbah.” So ʿUqbah b. ʿAmir stood up while I was listening and said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.’ And I bear witness that I heard him say: ‘Whoever wears silk in this world will be deprived of wearing it in the Hereafter.’”"],[14887,"He heard ʿUqba b. ʿĀmir saying: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do not frighten the souls after they have been at ease.” They said, “O Messenger of God, and what is that?” He said, “Debt.”"],[14888,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “No servant leads a people in prayer but that he undertakes whatever is upon them in their prayer. If he does well, it is for him; and if he errs, it is for them and against him.”"],[14889,"And he said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “No servant leads a people in prayer but that he undertakes what is upon them in their prayer. If he does well, it is for him and for them; and if he errs, it is against him and not against them.”"],[14890,"Abū ʿAlī al-Hamdānī, whose residence was in Alexandria for a year, narrated to me. He said: We went out on a journey, and ʿUqba b. ʿĀmir was with us. We said to him, “Lead us in prayer.” He said, “I will not do so. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘Whoever leads the people and gets the time right and completes the prayer, it is for him and for them; and whoever falls short of any of that, it is against him and not against them.’”"],[14891,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say on the pulpit: {And prepare against them whatever you are able of power.} “Verily, power is archery. Verily, power is archery.”"],[14892,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “When you see God giving a servant what he loves while he persists in his disobedience, that is only a gradual leading of him from Himself.” Then he recited this verse: {So when they forgot what they had been reminded of, We opened for them the doors of everything, until, when they rejoiced in what they had been given, We seized them suddenly, and at once they were in despair. So the last remnant of the people who had done wrong was cut off. And praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.}"],[14893,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the campaign of Tabūk. I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was talking to his companions, and he said, “Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then prays two rakʿas, his sins fall away like the day his mother gave birth to him.” So I said, “Praise be to God who granted me to hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[14894,"He was a camel herder. My turn came to pasture them, so I brought them back in the evening and caught up with the Messenger of God ﷺ standing and speaking to the people. I caught from his words: “There is none of you who performs ablution and does it well, then stands and prays two rakʿas, facing them with his face and his heart, but that Paradise becomes assured for him.”"],[14895,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever frees a believing slave, it is his ransom from the Fire.”"],[14896,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he said, “Whoever frees a believing slave, it will be his ransom.”"],[14897,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he said, “Whoever frees a believing slave, it will be his ransom from the Fire—for each limb, a limb.”"],[14898,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “The first part of a person to speak, when the mouths are sealed, will be his thigh from the left leg.”"],[14899,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Certainly, when a man is satisfied with the generosity and actions of another man, he is like him.\""],[14900,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he said, “The one who recites the Qur’an quietly is like the one who gives charity secretly, and the one who recites the Qur’an aloud is like the one who gives charity openly.”"],[14901,"The Prophet of God, may God’s blessings be upon him, said, “The one who recites the Qur’an quietly is like the one who gives charity secretly, and the one who recites the Qur’an aloud is like the one who gives charity openly.”"],[14902,"I was leading the Messenger of God ﷺ’s she-camel during a journey, and he said, “O ʿUqbah, shall I not teach you the best two surahs ever recited?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of God, teach me.” He then taught me “Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind” and “Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak.” He did not see me pleased with them. When he dismounted, he led the people in the dawn prayer with them. After finishing his prayer, he turned to me and said, “O ʿUqbah, how did you find it?”"],[14903,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ : \"Whoever fasts for a day in the cause of Allah, Allah will keep Hellfire away from him a distance of a hundred years of travel.\""],[14904,"From ʿUqbah b. ʿAmir, who was the keeper of the Messenger of God ﷺ’s gray mule and led it during journeys, he said: I led the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was on his mount for part of the night. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Make the camel kneel.” I made it kneel, and he dismounted. Then he said, “Mount, O ʿUqbah.” I said, “Glory be to God! On your mount?” He ordered me, saying, “Mount.” I said the same again and repeated that several times until I feared I would disobey the Messenger of God ﷺ. So I mounted his riding camel. Then he urged his she-camel and it rose. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ called me at one of the mountain passes and said, “O ʿUqbah, shall I not teach you two surahs from the Qur’an that are the best of the Qur’an, or among the best of it?” I said, “Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom.” He taught me the two protective surahs (al-Muʿawwidhatayn). Then he said, “O ʿUqbah, when you see dawn, inform me.” When I saw dawn, I said, “O Messenger of God, this is dawn.” He made his camel kneel, performed ablution, stood for prayer, then took my hand and placed me on his right. He recited those two surahs in the dawn prayer, then turned to me and said, “O ʿUqbah, recite them whenever you rise and whenever you sleep.”"],[14905,"I came with twelve riders, and we shaded the Messenger of God ﷺ. My companions said, “You graze our camels while we go and acquire knowledge from the Messenger of God ﷺ; when we return, we will share with you what we heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ.” I did that for days. Then I thought to myself, “Perhaps I am being cheated: my companions hear what I do not hear and learn what I do not learn from the Prophet of God ﷺ.” So I attended one day, and the Prophet of God ﷺ said, “Whoever performs ablution completely and then stands for prayer, his sins become as on the day his mother gave birth to him.”"],[14906,"A gray mule was gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He mounted it and took ʿUqbah to lead it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Recite.” He said, “What should I recite, O Messenger of God?” He said, “Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak.” Then he said, “You will never stand to pray with anything like it.”"],[14907,"He asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the two protective surahs (al-Muʿawwidhatayn). ʿUqbah said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ led us with them in the dawn prayer.”"],[14908,"He heard ʿUqbah b. ʿAmir say, “The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade cauterization, disliked drinking hot water, and when he applied kohl, he applied it an odd number of times; and when he used stones for cleansing, he used an odd number.”"],[14909,"ʿUqbah b. ʿAmir reported that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “When one of you applies kohl, let him apply it an odd number of times; and when he uses stones for cleansing, let him use an odd number.”"],[14910,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the women who seek divorce by khulʿ and the women who forcibly separate themselves are the female hypocrites.\""],[14911,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever meets Allah not associating anything with Allah, and not having shed forbidden blood, will enter Paradise.\""],[14912,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Pray in the sheep pens, but do not pray in the watering places of camels—or the resting places of camels.\""],[14913,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"There are two kinds of jealousy, one of which Allah loves and the other Allah hates; and two kinds of pride, one of which Allah loves and the other Allah hates. Jealousy in relation to a doubtful matter—Allah, may He be exalted, loves it; and jealousy in other than that—Allah hates it. Pride when a man gives charity—Allah loves it; and pride in arrogance—Allah hates it.\" And he said: \"Three people's supplications are answered: the parent, the traveler, and the wronged.\" And he said: \"Indeed, Allah will admit three people to Paradise because of a single arrow: its maker, the one who gifts it, and the one who shoots it in the cause of Allah.\""],[14914,"That he went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk, and the herding was assigned to me and a companion of mine. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ alone while people had gathered around him, so I said to my companion, 'Take care of it for me until I sit with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and listen to him.' I went to him and heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever performs ablution and perfects his ablution, then prays two rakʿahs in which he focuses on them and nothing distracts him, he will emerge from his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him.\""],[14915,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed sacrificial animals among his companions, and a young sheep fell to my lot. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, a young sheep fell to my lot.' He said, 'Sacrifice it.'"],[14916,"That the Prophet ﷺ distributed sacrificial animals among his companions, and a young sheep fell to my lot, so he said, 'Sacrifice it.'"],[14917,"From ʿUqba b. ʿĀmir Abū ʿĀbis al-Juhanī: I was with the Messenger of Allah in an army. I sent out the riding animals of my companions to pasture. When I returned to him, my companions came rushing to me, saying: While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the muezzin gave the call to prayer, and he said: \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.\" Then he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[14918,"While I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said to me: \"Say, O ʿUqba.\" I said to him: What shall I say? Then he fell silent. He said: I said to myself, if he repeats it to me, I will say as he said. Then he said to me: \"Say,\" and he recited, \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak\" until he finished it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one has asked and no one has sought refuge with the like of it.\""],[14919,"\"We sacrificed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ jadhaʿa sheep.\""],[14920,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the jadhaʿa of sheep, and he said: \"Sacrifice it.\""],[14921,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿUqba: \"Recite them in your prayer when you pray, for you will never recite the like of them,\" meaning the two refuge-seeking surahs."],[14922,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set for us a warranty period for slaves of three days.\""],[14923,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When two guardians contract a marriage, it belongs to the first.”"],[14924,"“I did not come to you as a visitor, but rather a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ when you were with me that day.” He said: “Whoever knows a fault of his brother and conceals it, God will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[14925,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Verses were revealed to me that I have never heard of anything like them, or I have never seen anything like them in terms of effectiveness.\""],[14926,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Verses were sent down to me the like of which have not been sent down to me: ‘Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of people’ and ‘Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak.’”"],[14927,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Verses were sent down to me the like of which I have not seen—meaning the two refuge-seeking chapters.”"],[14928,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever meets God not associating anything with Him and has not shed forbidden blood will enter Paradise.”"],[14929,"He informed him, or he heard it from him if he did not single him out, that he married Umm Yahya bt. Abi Ihab. A black slave woman said to him, “I breastfed both of you.” He said: I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him, but he turned away. I came to him a second time and mentioned that to him, and he said: “How, when she claims that she breastfed both of you?” and he prohibited it."],[14930,"He married Umm Yahya, the daughter of Abi Ihab, and a black slave girl came and said, \"I have breastfed both of you.\" He then went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him about it. The Prophet ﷺ turned away from him. He mentioned it to him again, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"How can she claim that she breastfed both of you? She is prohibited from doing so.\""],[14931,"That he married a woman, then a black slave woman came and claimed that she had breastfed both of them. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, but he turned away from him. Then he mentioned it a second time and said, “She is lying.” The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled and said: “How, when it has already been said?”"],[14932,"I married the daughter of Abi Ihab al-Taymi. On the morning after taking possession of her, a freedwoman of my family in Makkah came and said, “I breastfed both of you.” So I rode to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in Madinah and mentioned that to him. I said, “I asked the girl’s family, and they denied it.” He said, “How, when it has already been said?” He said: So I separated from her and married another."],[14933,"A companion of mine narrated to me—and I am mindful of my companion’s hadith—he said: I married Umm Yahya bt. Abi Ihab. A black woman entered upon us and claimed that she had breastfed both of them together. So I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, but he turned away from me. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, but he turned away from me. I mentioned that to him, but he turned away from me. So I said, “She is lying.” He said, “What makes you know she is lying, when she has said what she said? Leave her.”"],[14934,"That Umm Yahya was his wife. A black woman came and said, “I breastfed both of you.” So he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, a black woman claims that she breastfed me and my wife, and she is lying.” He turned away from him. Then he repeated it to him, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “Then leave her.”"],[14935,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'I married the daughter of Abu Ihab, then a black woman came and claimed that she had suckled us.' He turned away from me, so I approached from the other side and he turned away from me. I faced him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, she is a black woman' — making light of her claim. He said, 'How [can that be] when it has been said?'"],[14936,"Al-Nuʿayman, or the son of al-Nuʿayman, was brought while drunk, and this weighed heavily on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with severe heaviness. He commanded those in the house to beat him, so they beat him with sandals and palm branches. 'Uqbah said, 'I was among those who beat him.'"],[14937,"Al-Nuʿayman, or the son of al-Nuʿayman, was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as a drinker. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded those in the house to beat him. I was among those who beat him, and we beat him with sandals and palm branches."],[14938,"I prayed ʿAsr behind the Prophet ﷺ in Madinah. When he said salam, he stood up quickly, stepping over people's necks towards one of the rooms of his wives. The people were alarmed by his haste. Then he came out to them and saw that they were surprised by his haste, so he said, 'I remembered some bits of gold that I had, and I disliked that it should detain me, so I ordered it to be distributed.'"],[14939,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us; and al-Miqdam b. Dawud narrated to us; Asad b. Musa narrated to us; they said: Sulayman b. al-Mughirah narrated to us from Humayd b. Hilal, who said: Abu al-ʿAliyah came to me and a companion of mine, and said, 'Come, for you two are younger than me and more retentive of hadith than me.' He went with us until he brought us to Bishr b. ʿAsim al-Laythi and said, 'Narrate your hadith to these two.' Bishr said: ʿUqbah b. Malik narrated to us — and he was of his clan — saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a raiding party. They raided a people, and a man from the people fled. A man from the raiding party pursued him with his sword drawn. The fleeing man said, 'I am a Muslim,' but he paid no heed to what he said and struck him and killed him. News of this reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said harsh words about it, which reached the killer. While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a sermon, the killer said, 'By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he only said what he said seeking protection from death.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him and from the people in front of him and continued his sermon. Then he said it a second time: 'By Allah, he only said what he said seeking protection from death.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him and from the people in front of him and continued his sermon. Then he could not restrain himself and said a third time: 'By Allah, he only said what he said seeking protection from death.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to him, with displeasure visible on his face, and said three times: 'Allah has refused to [forgive] me concerning one who kills a believer.'"],[14940,"A group from the army of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided the people of a water source in the morning. A man from the people of the water rose up and a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ attacked him. He said, \"I am a Muslim!\" and the companion killed him. When they came to the Prophet ﷺ, they informed him of what happened. He stood up to deliver a sermon, praised Allah and glorified Him, then he said, \"As for what follows, what is the matter with a Muslim killing another Muslim while he says, 'I am a Muslim?'\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he said it seeking refuge.\" So he turned his face away from him and said, \"Indeed, Allah has prohibited me from taking the life of a Muslim.\" He said this three times."],[14941,"On the authority of his father ʿUqbah — who was struck by an arrow alongside the Prophet ﷺ — he said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say three times: 'No Muslim who has seen me, nor one who has seen one who saw me, nor one who has seen one who saw one who saw me, will enter the Fire.'"],[14942,"'Iyad b. Himar b. ʿArfajah b. Najiyah b. Sufyan b. Mujashiʿ.'"],[14943,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about found property. He said, 'Make it known and do not hide it or conceal it. If its owner comes, [return it]; otherwise, it is the wealth of Allah, which He gives to whomever He wills.'"],[14944,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Whoever finds a stray animal should call two just witnesses and not conceal it. If he does not find its owner, it is the wealth of Allah, which He gives to whomever He wills.'"],[14945,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah commanded me to teach you what you did not know from what He taught me this day. He said: Every wealth that I have granted My servants is lawful for them. I created all My servants as hanifs, but the devils came to them and turned them away from their religion, forbade them what I had made lawful, and commanded them to associate with Me that for which I sent down no authority. Allah looked at the people of the earth and despised them, Arab and non-Arab, except for remnants of the People of the Book. Allah commanded me to raid Quraysh. I said, \"My Lord, they will then smash my head until they leave it like a loaf of bread.\" He said, \"I have only sent you to test you and to test through you. I have sent down to you a Book that water will not wash away; you will recite it in sleep and wakefulness. So raid them; Allah will honor you. Spend, and it will be spent on you. Send an army, and We will reinforce you with five times their number. Fight with those who obey you against those who disobey you. The people of Paradise are three: a just ruler, a merciful man tender-hearted toward every relative and Muslim, and a rich man who is chaste and charitable. The people of the Fire are five: the weak man without restraint, those among you who are followers not seeking family or wealth; a man who, when morning comes, would deceive you concerning your family and wealth; a man who has no desire, however small, but pursues it; the vulgar and obscene.\" He mentioned miserliness and lying.'"],[14946,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Whoever finds a stray animal should call two just witnesses and not conceal it. If he does not find its owner, it is the wealth of Allah, which He gives to whomever He wills.'"],[14947,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, 'Whoever finds lost property should call a just witness, then not conceal it or hide it, and announce it for a year. If its owner comes, [return it]; otherwise, it is the wealth of Allah, which He gives to whomever He wills.'"],[14948,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about a found item, and he said, \"Announce it; if you find its owner [return it], otherwise it is the wealth of Allah, which He gives to whom He wills.\" Ayyub did not mention in his hadith the report of Mutarrif."],[14949,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say in his sermon: \"Allah, mighty and sublime, commanded me to teach you what you do not know from what He taught me this day. Every wealth I have bestowed upon My servant is lawful. I created My servants all as upright monotheists, but the devils came to them and turned them away from their religion, forbade them what I had made lawful for them, and commanded them to associate with Me that for which I sent down no authority. Allah, mighty and sublime, looked upon the people of the earth and despised them, their Arabs and non-Arabs, except remnants of the People of the Book. He said: 'O Muhammad, I have sent you to test you and to test by you. I have sent down to you a Book that water will not wash away, which you will recite while awake and asleep.' Allah revealed to me to raid Quraysh. I said: 'My Lord, they will split my head and leave it like a piece of bread.' He said: 'Expel them as they expelled you; raid them and We will grant you victory. Spend and it will be spent on you. Send an army and We will send five times their number. Fight with those who obey you against those who disobey you.'\" He said: \"The people of Paradise are three: a just and successful ruler, a merciful man tender-hearted toward every relative and Muslim, and a chaste poor person who gives charity. The people of Hell are five: a man who does not conceal his greed, even if it is as small as a speck, but takes it; a man who does not spend evening or morning except deceiving you regarding your family and property; the weak one who has no restraint, those among you who are followers and do not seek family or wealth.\" A man said: \"O Abu ʿAbd Allah, are they from the clients or from the Arabs?\" He said: \"He is a follower who belongs to a man and commits adultery with his wife outside marriage, 'the shameless vulgar one.'\" He said: And he mentioned lying and miserliness. The wording is that of Abu Muslim."],[14950,"The Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon and said in it: \"Allah commanded me to teach you what you do not know from what He taught me this day. Every wealth I have bestowed upon My servants is lawful. I created My servants all as upright monotheists. The devils came to them, turned them away from their religion, forbade them what I had made lawful for them, and commanded them to associate with Me that for which I sent down no authority. Then Allah, mighty and sublime, looked upon the people of the earth and despised them, their Arabs and non-Arabs, except remnants of the People of the Book. He said: 'I have only sent you to test you and to test by you. I have sent down to you a Book that water will not wash away, which you will recite asleep and awake.' Allah commanded me to come to Quraysh. I said: 'My Lord, they will split my head and leave it like a piece of bread.' He said: 'Expel them as they expelled you; raid them and We will raid for you. Spend and it will be spent on you. Send an army and I will send with it five times its like.'\" And he mentioned the hadith."],[14951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in a sermon he delivered: \"Allah, mighty and sublime, commanded me to teach you what you do not know from what He taught me this day. Verily, every wealth I have bestowed upon My servants is lawful for them. I created My servants all as upright monotheists. The devils came to them, turned them away from their religion, forbade them what I had made lawful for them, and commanded them to associate with Me that for which I sent down no authority. Allah looked upon the people of the earth before He sent me and despised them all, their Arabs and non-Arabs, except remnants of the People of the Book. Allah said: 'I have only sent you to test you and to test by you. I have sent down to you a Book that water will not wash away, which you will recite asleep and awake.' Allah revealed to me to raid Quraysh. I said: 'My Lord, they will split my head and leave it like a piece of bread.' He said: 'Expel them as they expelled you; raid them and We will grant you victory. Send an army and We will send five times its like. Spend and it will be spent on you. Fight with those who obey you against those who disobey you.' He said: 'The people of Paradise are three: a just leader, a merciful man tender-hearted toward every relative and Muslim, and a wealthy, chaste man who gives charity. The people of Hell are five: the weak one who has no restraint; those who are followers among you and do not seek family or wealth; a man who, when morning comes, deceives you regarding your family and property; a man who does not conceal his greed, even if it is small, but takes it; and the shameless vulgar one.' And he mentioned miserliness and lying."],[14952,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day: \"Shall I not tell you what Allah, mighty and sublime, told me in the Book? Allah, mighty and sublime, created Adam and his descendants as upright Muslims. He gave them wealth as lawful, with no prohibition in it. They worshipped the false deities. He commanded me to come to them and clarify for them what He had created them upon. I addressed my Lord: 'If I come to them, Quraysh will split my head as a loaf of bread is split.' He said to me: 'Go, and I will make you succeed. Spend, and I will spend on you. Fight those who disobey you with those who obey you. I will give with every army you send ten times its like from the angels, and I will cast terror into the hearts of your enemy. I will give you a Book that water will not erase, which I will remind you of asleep and awake. Look at me and Quraysh, this Quraysh: they wounded my face and robbed me of my family, and I will initiate against them. If I overcome them, they will come to what I called them to, willingly or unwillingly. If they overcome me, then I am upon something to which I call you.'\""],[14953,"Iyaḍ b. Himar came with a she-camel and a riding camel to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as a gift. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Lead it.\" He led it. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ called him: \"O Iyaḍ b. Himar, have you embraced Islam?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Take your she-camel, for Allah has forbidden to us the gifts of the polytheists.\""],[14954,"I gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a she-camel or a sacrificial camel as a gift. He said, \"Have you embraced Islam?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"I have been forbidden the gifts of the polytheists.\""],[14955,"The Prophet ﷺ said in his sermon: \"Allah, mighty and sublime, revealed to me: Be humble, so that no one boasts over another and no one oppresses another.\""],[14956,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, a man from my people insults me; is there any harm in my defending myself against him?\" He said, \"The two who insult each other are two devils who trade insults and lies.\""],[14957,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The two who insult each other are two devils who trade lies and insults.\""],[14958,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whatever the two who insult each other say is upon the one who started, unless the wronged one transgresses.\""],[14959,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whatever the two who insult each other say is upon the one who started, as long as the wronged one does not transgress.\""],[14960,"Iyad b. Ghanm b. Zuhayr b. Abi Shaddad b. Rabi'a b. Hilal b. Dabba b. al-Harith b. Fihr accepted Islam early, before al-Hudaybiyyah, and witnessed al-Hudaybiyyah. He was in Syria with Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah. When death came to Abu 'Ubaydah, he appointed 'Iyad b. Ghanm over the office he had held. 'Umar b. al-Khattab confirmed him in that office until he died. 'Iyad was a righteous, generous man. He died without wealth and without debt to anyone. He died in Syria in the year 20 AH at the age of sixty."],[14961,"Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah died and appointed as his successor his cousin 'Iyad b. Ghanm al-Fihri."],[14962,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection will be those who were the most severe in punishing people in this world.\" 'Iyad said to him: \"O Hisham, we have heard what you heard, seen what you saw, and accompanied those you accompanied. Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever has sincere advice for a ruler, let him not speak it to him publicly, but let him take him by the hand and be alone with him. If he accepts it, he accepts it; otherwise he has fulfilled what was owed by him and upon him.' And you, O Hisham, are the very one who dares to challenge the authority of Allah. Why did you not fear that the authority of Allah might kill you, and you would become a victim of the authority of Allah?\""],[14963,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me one day: \"O 'Iyad, do not marry an old woman or a barren one, for I will boast of your numbers before the nations.\""],[14964,"Regarding the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, he said, \"Whoever drinks alcohol and becomes intoxicated, his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights. And if he dies in that state, he will enter the Fire. But if he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. However, if he drinks again, it will be the same. And if he drinks a third time, it will be the same. But if he drinks a fourth time, it becomes the right of Allah to make him drink from the sludge of impurity.\" It was asked, \"What is the sludge of impurity?\" He replied, \"It is the juice of the people of the Fire.\""],[14965,"The Prophet ﷺ came to Hawazin with twelve thousand. On the day of Hunayn, from our people of al-Ta'if, there were killed as many as were killed of Quraysh on the day of Badr. The Prophet ﷺ took a handful of pebbles and threw it in our faces, and we were defeated."],[14966,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about a deed that would admit him into Paradise. He said: \"Is either of your parents alive?\" He said: \"No.\" He asked him three times. He said: \"Give water to drink; carry it to them when they are absent, and suffice them with it when they are present.\""],[14967,"When this verse was revealed: {Allah will bring a people whom He loves and who love Him}, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They are the people of this one, meaning Abu Musa al-Ash'ari.\""],[14968,"\"Why do I see them not clapping in rhythm as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to clap in rhythm?\""],[14969,"By the One who saved me on the day of Badr. He would take the mushaf and place it on his face and say: \"The speech of my Lord, the speech of my Lord.\""],[14970,"\"What is this?\" It was said: \"A place where none but God can benefit.\" ʿIkrimah said: \"Then this is the God of Muḥammad to whom he calls us. Return with us to him.\" So he returned and became Muslim. His wife had become Muslim before him, and they remained married."],[14971,"ʿIkrimah b. Abī Jahl fled, heading for Yemen, while Umm al-Ḥakīm bt. al-Ḥārith b. Hishām—who was then a Muslim and was married to ʿIkrimah b. Abī Jahl—came and asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for permission to seek her husband. He permitted her and granted him safe-conduct. She set out with a Byzantine slave of hers, who tried to seduce her. She kept giving him hope and drawing him on until she reached some people of ʿAkk and sought their help against him, so they detained him. She caught up with her husband in part of Tihāmah; he had boarded a ship. When he sat in it, he called upon al-Lāt and al-ʿUzzā. The people of the ship said: \"No one may pass here who calls upon anything except God alone, sincerely.\" ʿIkrimah said: \"By God, if He is in the sea, He is certainly also on land alone.\" So he swore by God that he would return to Muḥammad ﷺ. ʿIkrimah returned with his wife and entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ to give him allegiance, and he accepted it from him. A man from Hudhayl entered upon his wife fleeing when Banū Bakr were defeated, and she blamed him, deemed him weak, and reproached him for fleeing. He said:"],[14972,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ relieved himself, if we spoke to him he would not speak to us, and if we greeted him he would not return our greeting, until he came to his dwelling and performed the ablution he performed for prayer. We said: \"O Messenger of God, we speak to you and you do not speak to us, and we greet you and you do not return our greeting?\" He said: \"Until the verse of concession was revealed: {O you who believe, when you rise to pray…}\""],[14973,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent al-Walīd b. ʿUqbah b. Abī Muʿayṭ to us to collect the zakah on our wealth. He traveled until he was near us—that was after the battle of al-Muraysīʿ—then he turned back. We mounted and followed him. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, I came to a people still in their paganism; they took up arms and refused the zakah.\" That did not trouble the Prophet ﷺ until it was revealed: {O you who believe, if a wicked person comes to you…} Then the people of al-Muṣṭaliq came to the Prophet ﷺ following al-Walīd with a portion of their zakah, driving it, and with provisions they were carrying. They mentioned to him that they had gone out seeking al-Walīd with their zakah but did not find him. They handed over to the Messenger of God ﷺ what they had and said: \"O Messenger of God, we heard of your messenger's departure and were glad, and we said we would go to meet him. Then we heard of his return and feared it was from his displeasure with us.\" They offered the Prophet ﷺ to buy from them what was left. He accepted the obligatory portion from them and said: \"Go back with your provisions. We do not sell any of the zakah until we have taken possession of it.\" So they returned to their families, and he sent someone to collect the remainder of their zakah."],[14974,"That he was among the delegation of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq to the Messenger of God ﷺ regarding the matter of al-Walīd b. ʿUqbah, and that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Depart, neither detained nor summoned.\""],[14975,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received a people bringing their zakat, he would say, “O Allah, bless them.” Then my father came to him with some zakat, and he said, “O Allah, bless the family of Abu Awfa.”"],[14976,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received a people bringing their zakat, he would say, “O Allah, bless them.” Then my father came to him with some zakat, and he said, “O Allah, bless the family of Abu Awfa.”"],[14977,"It is called al-tarhīḥ. They said to us, “Here there is a man who saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” So we came to a very old man. He said: We said, “Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said, “Yes, and he wrote for me concerning this water.” He brought out to us a skin in which was a writing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We said, “What is your name?” He said, “Al-ʿAddāʾ b. Khālid.” We said, “What did you hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said, “I was beneath his she-camel on the day of ʿArafah while it was chewing its cud, and he said, ‘O people, what day is this? What month is this? What land is this?’ We said, ‘Allah and His Messenger know best.’ He said, ‘Is this not a sacred month, a sacred land, and a sacred day?’ We said, ‘Allah and His Messenger know best.’ He said, ‘Indeed your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to one another like the sacredness of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours, until the day you meet your Lord. O Allah, have I conveyed? O Allah, bear witness.’”"],[14978,"I heard al-ʿAddāʾ b. Khālid b. Hawdhah say, “We fought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but Allah did not grant us victory or make us prevail.”"],[14979,"Al-ʿAddāʾ b. Khālid b. Hawdhah said, “Shall I read to you a document that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote for me?” We said, “Yes.” And in it was written: “In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. This is what al-ʿAddāʾ b. Khālid b. Hawdhah purchased from Muhammad the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He purchased from him a male slave—or a female slave (ʿUthmān was uncertain)—a sale of a Muslim: no disease, no defect, and no deceit.” Al-Aṣmaʿī said: I asked Saʿīd b. Abī ʿArūbah about al-ghāʾilah, and he said, “Running away, theft, and fornication.” I asked him about al-khibthah, and he said, “The sale of the people under covenant of the Muslims.”"],[14980,"I set out for Makkah. When I reached al-Ḍariyyah, one of my companions said to me, “Would you like to meet a man who was a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “The owner of the tent pitched in such-and-such a place.” I said to my companions, “Let us go to him.” We went, and when we reached the owner of the tent, we greeted him, and he returned the greeting and said, “Who are the people?” We said, “A group from the people of Basrah. We have heard that you were a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said, “Yes, I accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sat beneath his pulpit on the day of the Farewell Pilgrimage. He ascended the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Allah ﷻ says, {O mankind, indeed We created you from a male and a female and made you peoples and tribes that you may know one another. Indeed, the most noble of you in the sight of Allah is the most righteous of you.} There is no virtue of an Arab over a non-Arab, nor of a non-Arab over an Arab, nor of a black over a white, nor of a white over a black, except by piety. O company of Quraysh, do not come to me with the world carrying it on your necks while the people come with the Hereafter, for I cannot avail you against Allah in anything.” We said, “What should we call you? What is your name?” He said, “I am al-ʿAddāʾ b. ʿAmr b. ʿĀmir, the rider of al-Ḍaḥyāʾ in the Jāhiliyyah.”"],[14981,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “The Hour will not be established until a man greets only those he knows, until mosques are taken as thoroughfares, until a woman and her husband trade together, and until women and horses become cheap and do not rise in price until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[14982,"We performed Hajj and passed by the road of al-Munkadir, where people used to take it, but we lost the way. While we were thus, suddenly a bedouin appeared as if he had sprung from the earth. He said to me, “O old man, do you know where you are?” I said, “No.” He said, “You are at al-Dhawāʾib, by this white hill that you see—the bones of Bakr b. Wāʾil and Taghlib—and this is the grave of Kulayb, the brother of Muhalhil.” Then he said to me, “Would you like to meet a man who was a companion of the Prophet ﷺ, whose words you may hear?” I said, “Yes.” He took me to a dark tent, and there I saw a man with his eyebrows bound with a bandage. I said, “Who is this?” He said, “Al-ʿAddāʾ b. Khālid b. ʿAmr b. ʿĀmir, the rider of al-Ḍaḥyāʾ in the Jāhiliyyah.” I said to him, “May Allah have mercy on you, narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said, “We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he stood up suddenly as if alarmed. Ibn Masʿūd said to him, ‘O Messenger of Allah, you stood up as if alarmed.’ He said, ‘Beware of the three deceivers.’ Ibn Masʿūd said, ‘May my father and mother be ransomed for you, you have told us about the one-eyed Dajjāl and about the most lying of the liars, so who is the third deceiver?’ He said, ‘A man who emerges among a people whose first are afflicted and whose last are cut off, upon them is a perpetual curse, in a tribulation called al-Ḥāriqah, and he is the bald Dajjāl, who devours the servants of Allah.’”"],[14983,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I said, “Describe him to me.” He said, “He had a fine sabilah—the Arabs called the beard sabilah.”"],[14984,"He gifted to the Prophet ﷺ a silk brocade garment that Kisrā had given him. His companions entered and said, “Has it been sent down upon you from heaven?” He said, “Why do you marvel at this? A handkerchief from among the handkerchiefs of Saʿd b. Muʿādh in Paradise is better than this.” Then he said, “O boy, take it to Abū Jahm b. Ḥudhayfah and tell him to send me the khamīṣah.”"],[14985,"From ʿAʾidh b. ʿAmr, who was among those who gave the pledge to the Messenger of God ﷺ under the tree, and he said: His wife gave birth and saw purity after twenty days, so she performed ghusl, then came to enter with him in his blanket, and he felt her touch and said, \"Who is this?\" She said, \"So-and-so.\" He said, \"What is the matter with you?\" She said, \"I saw purity, so I performed ghusl.\" He struck her with his foot and made her get up from his bed, and said, \"Do not lead me astray from my religion until forty days have passed.\""],[14986,"That he used to ride on leopard-skin saddles and wear khazz silk, and he saw no harm in that."],[14987,"That Abū Barzah should pray over him, so he mounted his riding beast and returned."],[14988,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Among the worst of shepherds is the harsh one.\" He said: Beware lest you be one of them. Ziyād said to him: \"Sit down, for you are only of the bran of the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ.\" ʿAʾidh said to him: \"And was there bran among them? Bran came only after them and in others besides them.\""],[14989,"That Abū Sufyān passed by Salmān, Ṣuhayb and Bilāl, and they said: \"The swords of God have not yet taken from the neck of this one what they have taken.\" Abū Bakr said: \"Do you say this of the elder of Quraysh and its master?\" Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him what they said. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Abū Bakr, perhaps you have angered them. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you have angered them, you have angered your Lord.\" So he returned to them and said: \"O my brothers, perhaps I have angered you?\" They said: \"No, O Abū Bakr, may God forgive you.\""],[14990,"That Abū Sufyān passed by Salmān, Ṣuhayb and Bilāl, and they said: \"The swords of God have not yet taken from the neck of this one what they have taken.\" Abū Bakr said: \"Do you say this of the elder of Quraysh and its master?\" Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him what they said. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Abū Bakr, perhaps you have angered them. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you have angered them, you have angered your Lord.\" So he returned to them and said: \"O my brothers, perhaps I have angered you?\" They said: \"No, O Abū Bakr, may God forgive you.\""],[14991,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever is offered something of this provision without asking for it or craving it, let him expand his provision through it. And whoever is wealthy, let him direct it to one who is more in need of it than him.\""],[14992,"\"Milk for them, O boy.\" The boy went to a milch camel and milked it, then came to them. He said to the one on his right: \"Drink.\" He said: \"I am fasting.\" He said: \"May God accept from you and from us.\" Then he said to the second, and he said: \"I am fasting.\" He said the like of that. Then he said to the third, and he said the like of that. He said: \"Are all of you fasting? It is near that you will take this day as the like of Ramaḍān. We used to fast this day before Ramaḍān was made obligatory upon us. When Ramaḍān was made obligatory upon us, the fast of Ramaḍān abrogated the fast of this day, and this day is voluntary, not obligatory. So whoever wishes, let him fast, and whoever wishes, let him break his fast.\" When the people heard that from him, they all broke their fast. The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Zayd b. al-Ḥarīsh."],[14993,"ʿAʾidh b. ʿAmr said: \"I was struck by an arrow while I was fighting before the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Ḥunayn, in my face. When the blood flowed over my face, my beard and my chest, the Messenger of God ﷺ took my hand and wiped the blood from my face and chest down to my nipples, then supplicated for me.\" Ḥashraj said: ʿAʾidh used to tell us that during his lifetime. When he died and we washed him, we looked at what he had described to us of the trace of the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ to the extent he had told us of his chest, and there was a flowing white mark like the blaze of a horse."],[14994,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a cup or a large wooden bowl, and there was little water in it. He performed ablution with it, then ordered it, and he sprinkled it on them – or he said: he sprinkled it on them. He said: The fortunate among us was the one whom it reached. He said: I think it reached all of them. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ stood and prayed the forenoon prayer with them."],[14995,"We came as a delegation to the Prophet ﷺ, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father be your ransom and may you be the one to wipe my face and supplicate for blessing for me. So he wiped my face and supplicated for blessing for me. Umm al-Banin, who was his wife, said: I never saw him awaken from sleep but that his face was shining, and he used to be content with a few dates."],[14996,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays a prayer and does not complete it, it will be increased for him from his supererogatory prayers until it is complete.\""],[14997,"Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated to us: \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr: 'Ukkashah b. Mihsan b. Harthan b. Kabir b. Ghanm b. Dudan b. Asad b. Khuzaymah, an ally of Banu 'Abd Shams.\""],[14998,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The nations were displayed before me, and the Prophet and the prophets would pass with a small band.\" — the hadith."],[14999,"\"That we may consider lawful what is lawful for him except women, and when evening comes and we have not completed the rites, we become in ihram as we were before throwing. So we left from your presence wearing our shirts, and when evening came and we had not completed the rites, we returned with our shirts on our hands as you saw.\""],[15000,"From 'Urwah: \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Salim b. 'Awf b. al-Khazraj, then from Banu al-'Ajlan b. Zayd b. Ghanim b. Salim: 'Itban b. Malik b. 'Amr b. 'Ajlan b. Zayd b. Ghanm b. Salim b. 'Awf b. 'Amr b. 'Awf b. al-Khazraj.\""],[15001,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Awf b. al-Khazraj: 'Itban b. Malik b. 'Amr b. 'Ajlan.\""],[15002,"Something affected my eyesight, so I sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I would like you to come to me and pray in my house so that I may take it as a place of prayer. The Prophet ﷺ came to me with whom Allah willed of his Companions. He entered while he was praying in my house, and his Companions were talking among themselves and mentioning the hypocrites. Then they attributed the most severe and greatest of that to Malik b. al-Dukhshum, wishing that he would supplicate against him and he would perish, wishing that evil would befall him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer and said: \"Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" They said: He says that, but it is not in his heart. He said: \"No one testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah and then enters the Fire, or the Fire consumes him.\""],[15003,"When 'Utban ibn Malik was injured in his eye, he sent a message to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"I would like for you to come to me and pray in my house and ask for blessings for us.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up among a group of his companions and they went to him. They spoke amongst themselves and mentioned Malik ibn Dukhshum, and some of them said, \"O Messenger of Allah, that is the cave of the hypocrites and their dwelling place. They frequent it a lot.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Doesn't he pray?\" They replied, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but it is a prayer that has no good in it.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I have forbidden the killing of those who pray,\" repeating it twice."],[15004,"He narrated to me that his eyesight went away during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would come to my house and designate a mosque for me in it and pray in it, so that I may take it as a mosque, for my eyesight has gone and I am too weak to go out to the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ promised him a day to come to him. On that day, he gathered his companions for him, and they assembled in my house. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and heard them mentioning the most severe of the people of Madinah against the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the greatest in enmity toward him. They attributed that to Malik b. al-Dukhshum. The Prophet ﷺ asked them what they were mentioning. He said: \"Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, he is a man of that. He said: \"Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" They said: Yes. He said: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, if he says it sincerely from his heart, the Fire will never consume him.\" Anas said to me: \"Memorize this hadith, for it is among the treasures of knowledge.\" When we came to Madinah, we found 'Itban b. Malik alive, so I said to my father: Would you like to go to 'Itban and ask him about the hadith that Mahmud narrated to us from him? So we went and asked him about it, and he narrated it to us."],[15005,"'Itban b. Malik's eyesight was afflicted during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, I am unable to pray with you in your mosque, and I would like you to pray with me in my mosque so that I may follow your prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him, and they mentioned Malik b. al-Dukhshum. They said: That is the cave of the hypocrites, their refuge to which they resort, and their stronghold. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger?\" They said: Yes, but there is no good in his testimony. He said: \"No servant testifies to it sincerely from his heart and then dies except that Allah forbids him from the Fire.\""],[15006,"I went to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My eyesight has become weak, and the floods come between me and the mosque of my people. I wish you would come and pray in my house in a place that I may take as a mosque. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I will do so, if Allah wills.\" The Prophet ﷺ passed by Abu Bakr and asked him to follow, so he went with him. He asked permission and entered, and while standing he said: \"Where do you want me to pray?\" I pointed to him where I wanted. He said: Then we detained him for a dish of kharizah that we made for him. The people of the valley, meaning the people of the house, heard of him and came to him until the house was full. A man said: Where is Malik b. al-Dukhshun or Ibn al-Dukhaysh? A man said: That is a hypocrite who does not love Allah or His Messenger. The Prophet ﷺ said again: \"Do not say that, for he says there is no god but Allah, seeking thereby the countenance of Allah.\" He said: O Messenger of Allah, as for us, we see his face and his talk among the hypocrites. The Prophet ﷺ said again: \"Do not say that, for he says there is no god but Allah, seeking thereby the countenance of Allah.\" They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"No one will meet the Day of Resurrection saying there is no god but Allah, seeking thereby the countenance of Allah, except that Allah will forbid him from the Fire.\" Mahmud said: I narrated this hadith to a group including Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, and he said: I do not think the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said what you said. I vowed that if I returned to 'Itban b. Malik, I would ask him. So I returned to him and found him a very old man whose eyesight had gone, and he was the imam of his people. I sat beside him and asked him about this hadith, and he narrated it to me just as he had narrated it the first time. Ma'mar said: When al-Zuhri narrated this hadith, he would say: \"Then after that, religious obligations and matters were revealed which we consider to be the final authority, so whoever is able not to change should not change.\""],[15007,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Saʿd narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Mahmud b. al-Rabiʿ, from ʿItban b. Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Fire is forbidden for whoever says ‘There is no god but Allah,’ seeking thereby the Face of Allah.”"],[15008,"And he said: “O Messenger of Allah, there is darkness, rain, and flood, and I am a man with weak eyesight. So pray, O Messenger of Allah, in my house in a place I will take as a prayer place.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him and said: “Where would you like me to pray for you?” He pointed to a corner of the house, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed there."],[15009,"ʿItban b. Malik, one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and among those from the Ansar who witnessed Badr, narrated to him that he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have noticed a decline in my eyesight, and I lead my people in prayer. When the rains come, the valley between me and them floods, and I cannot reach their mosque to lead them in prayer. I would love, O Messenger of Allah, for you to come and pray in a place that I will take as a prayer place.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “I will do so, if Allah wills.” ʿItban said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr set out early the next day, when the day had risen. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked permission, and I gave him permission. He did not sit down until he entered the house. Then he said: “Where would you like me to pray in your house?” I pointed to a corner of the house. He stood, said the takbir, and we stood behind him. He prayed two rakʿahs, then said the salam. We detained him over a khazirah that we had prepared. Men from the household around us came, until a number of men gathered in the house. One of them said: “Where is Malik b. al-Dukhshun?” Some of them said: “He is a hypocrite; he does not love Allah and His Messenger.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not say that. Do you not see that he has said ‘There is no god but Allah,’ seeking thereby the Face of Allah?” They said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “His face and his counsel are toward the hypocrites.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah has forbidden the Fire for whoever says ‘There is no god but Allah,’ seeking thereby the Face of Allah, may He be glorified and exalted.” Ibn Shihab said: Then I asked al-Husayn b. Muhammad al-Ansari, one of the Banu Salim, about the hadith of Mahmud b. al-Rabiʿ, and he confirmed it. Ahmad b. Salih said: “Or you say al-Dukhshum, and that is correct.”"],[15010,"He was the imam of his people and had witnessed Badr. He said to the Prophet ﷺ: “When my eyesight deteriorated, crossing the valley when it flooded between me and the mosque of my people became hard for me.” On a Friday he said to the Prophet ﷺ: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me: if you came to me and prayed in a place in my house that I would take as a prayer place?” The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “I will do it.” The Prophet ﷺ set out early on Saturday, with Abu Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ. He entered and did not sit until he said: “Where would you like me to pray in your house?” I pointed to the corner that I wanted, and he prayed there in the forenoon. We detained him over a khazirah that was being made for him."],[15011,"He informed him that ʿItban b. Malik, one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and among those from the Ansar who witnessed Badr, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have noticed a decline in my eyesight, and I lead my people in prayer. When the rains come, the valley between me and them floods, and I cannot reach their mosque to lead them in prayer. I would love, O Messenger of Allah, for you to pray in a place that I will take as a prayer place.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I will do so, if Allah wills.” ʿItban said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and ʿUmar set out early the next day, when the day had risen. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked permission, and I gave him permission. He did not sit down until he entered the house. He said: “Where would you like me to pray in your house?” I pointed to a corner of the house. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood, said the takbir, and we stood and formed rows behind him. We prayed two rakʿahs. Then a number of people gathered in the house. Someone said: “Where is Malik b. al-Dukhaykhin?” Some of them said: “He is a hypocrite; he does not love Allah and His Messenger.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not say that. Do you not see that he has said ‘There is no god but Allah,’ seeking thereby the Face of Allah?” They said: “Allah knows best. We see his face and his counsel toward the hypocrites.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah has forbidden the Fire for whoever says ‘There is no god but Allah,’ seeking thereby the Face of Allah.” Muhammad said: “Then I asked al-Husayn b. Muhammad, one of the Banu Salim among their leaders, about the hadith of Mahmud, and he confirmed it.”"],[15012,"Mahmud b. al-Rabiʿ narrated to me: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when he was five years old, and he remembered a spray of water that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sprayed on his face from a hanging bucket in the Darahim.”"],[15013,"Mahmud b. al-Rabiʿ narrated to me: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when he was five years old, and he remembered a spray of water that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sprayed on his face from a hanging bucket in the Darahim.”"],[15014,"“And I remembered a spray of water that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sprayed on my face from a hanging bucket in our house.”"],[15015,"“And I remembered a spray of water that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sprayed on my face from a hanging bucket in our house.”"],[15016,"He remembered the Messenger of Allah when he was five years old, and he claimed that he remembered a spray of water that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sprayed on his face from a hanging bucket in their house.”"],[15017,"He remembered the Messenger of Allah when he was five years old, and he claimed that he remembered a spray of water that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sprayed on his face from a hanging bucket in their house.”"],[15018,"From ʿAbis al-Ghifari, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he was on a rooftop and saw the people departing. He asked: “What is the matter with the people?” They said: “They are departing because of the plague.” He said: “O plague, take me! O plague, take me! O plague, take me!” His nephew said to him: “Do you wish for death when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Do not wish for death, for it cuts off deeds and does not return a man so that he may be shown mercy’?”"],[15019,"From ʿĀbis al-Ghifārī, a companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he was on a rooftop and saw people departing. He said, 'What is the matter with the people?' They replied, 'They are departing because of the plague.' He said, 'O plague, take me! O plague, take me! O plague, take me!' His nephew said to him, 'You wish for death, although the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do not wish for death, for it cuts off deeds and does not return a man so that he may be asked to repent.'"],[15020,"I was with ʿĀbis al-Ghifārī on the roof of a house in Basra, and he saw people loading up to flee from the plague. He said, 'O plague, take me to you! O plague, take me to you! O plague, take me to you!' A cousin of his, who was a companion, said, 'Why does he wish for death? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Let none of you wish for death, for at that point his term is cut off.'"],[15021,"I was with ʿĀbis al-Ghifārī on the roof of a house in Basra, and he saw people loading up to flee from the plague. He said, 'O plague, take me to you! O plague, take me to you! O plague, take me to you!' A cousin of his, who was a companion, said, 'Why does he wish for death? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Let none of you wish for death, for at that point his term is cut off.'"],[15022,"We were with him on a rooftop of his, and some people passed by loading up. He asked, 'Who are these?' It was said, 'They are fleeing from the plague.' He said, 'O plague, take me! O plague, take me! O plague, take me!' A nephew of his, who was a companion, said to him, 'You wish for death, although I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Let none of you wish for death, for death is the last deed of a believer; he does not return to be asked to repent.' He replied, 'O nephew, I am hastening toward certain traits that I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, which will occur in the last days and which he feared for his ummah: the rule of fools, the proliferation of police, the cheapening of blood, the severing of family ties, and a generation that takes the Qur'an as musical instruments, putting forward a man who is not the most knowledgeable among them in religion nor the most learned, even though among them are those more knowledgeable and more learned than him, so that he may sing to them.'"],[15023,"We were with ʿĀbis al-Ghifārī on a rooftop, and he saw people loading up. He asked, 'What is the matter with these?' It was said, 'They are fleeing from the plague.' He said, 'O plague, take me to you!' A cousin of his, who was a companion, said, 'He wishes for death, although I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Let none of you wish for death.' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Hasten to do good deeds before six things: the rule of fools, the proliferation of police, the selling of judgment, the cheapening of blood, the severing of family ties, and a generation that takes the Qur'an as musical instruments, putting forward one of them to sing to them even if he is the least knowledgeable among them in jurisprudence.'"],[15024,"What is the matter with them? They said, 'They are fleeing from the plague.' He said, 'O plague, take me to you!' A cousin of his said to him, 'Do you wish for death?' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Wish for death when six traits appear: the rule of fools, the selling of judgment, the cheapening of blood, the proliferation of police, the severing of family ties, and a generation that takes the Qur'an as musical instruments, putting forward a man to sing to them even though he is not the most knowledgeable among them.' Sharīk added in the chain: 'Ulaym al-Kindī."],[15025,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, nine or eight or seven of us, and he said: 'Will you not give allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ?' He repeated it three times. We said, 'O Messenger of God, we have already given you allegiance. On what should we give you allegiance?' He said: 'That you worship God and do not associate anything with Him, and [perform] the five prayers—and he whispered a hidden word—and that you do not ask people for anything.'"],[15026,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to his companions: 'Will you not give me allegiance?' They said, 'O Messenger of God, we have already given you allegiance once. On what should we give you allegiance?' He said that three times. Then he said: 'You give me allegiance on that you do not associate anything with God, that you establish prayer, give zakat, listen and obey.' Then he followed that with a hidden word: 'And that you do not ask people for anything.'"],[15027,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to wipe over the leather socks during the expedition of Tabuk: for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."],[15028,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in a tent of tanned leather. He performed ablution thoroughly and then said, \"O 'Awf, count six things before the Hour.\" I said, \"And what are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"My death.\" He said, so I was struck silent by it. He said, \"Say one.\" I said, \"One.\" \"And the second is the conquest of Jerusalem, and the third is a death among you like the quivering of sheep, and the fourth is the abundance of wealth to the point that a man is given one hundred dinars and remains displeased with them. Then there is a tribulation that will not leave any house of the Arabs except that it enters it, and a truce that will be between you and the Banu al-Asfar. Then they will betray, and they will come against you under eighty banners, each banner having twelve thousand.\""],[15029,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in a tent of his made of tanned leather. I greeted him and said, \"May I enter?\" He said, \"Enter.\" So I put my head inside and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing ablution thoroughly. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, may I enter fully?\" He said, \"All of you.\" When I sat down, he said to me, \"Count six things before the Hour: the death of your Prophet.\" 'Awf said, \"I was struck by such grief as I had never felt before.\" He said, \"Say one.\" I said, \"One.\" He said, \"And the conquest of Jerusalem, and a tribulation in which there will be a death among the Arabs—a disease that will seize you like the quivering of sheep—and wealth will become widespread among you to the point that a man is given one hundred dinars and remains angry. And a truce will be between you and the Banu al-Asfar, then they will betray, and they will come against you with eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand.\""],[15030,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in a structure of his. I greeted him and he said, \"'Awf b. Malik?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Enter.\" I said, \"All of me or part of me?\" He said, \"Rather all of you.\" Then he said to me, \"O 'Awf, count six things before the Hour. The first of them is my death,\" and I wept until he kept calming me. Then he said, \"Say one.\" I said, \"One.\" He said, \"And the second is the conquest of Jerusalem. Say two.\" I said, \"Two.\" He said, \"And the third is a death that will occur in my community, seizing them like the quivering of sheep. Say three.\" I said, \"Three.\" He said, \"And the fourth is a tribulation that will occur in my community,\" and he magnified it. Then he said, \"Say four.\" I said, \"Four.\" He said, \"And the fifth is that wealth will overflow among you, so much that a man will be given one hundred dinars and will be displeased with them. Say five.\" I said, \"Five.\" He said, \"And the sixth is that there will be a truce between you and the Banu al-Asfar, then they will march against you under eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand. The camp of the Muslims on that day will be in a land called al-Ghutah, in a city called Damascus.\""],[15031,"\"There is no sin except that I know its repentance.\" It was said, \"And what is its repentance?\" He said, \"That one leaves it and does not return to it.\""],[15032,"\"The hour of Friday is in one of the three hours: when the muezzin gives the call, when the imam heads to the pulpit, and at the time of the iqamah.\""],[15033,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at the sky one day and said, \"This is a time when knowledge will be lifted.\" A man from the Ansar called Ziyad b. Labid said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, will knowledge be lifted while you have come and hearts have preserved it?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I had thought you were one of the most understanding of the people of Madinah.\" Then he mentioned to him the misguidance of the Jews and Christians despite the Book of Allah in their hands. So I met Shaddad b. Aws and told him the hadith of 'Awf, and he said, \"'Awf spoke the truth. Shall I tell you of the first of that to be lifted?\" He said, \"It is humility; you will not see a humble person.\""],[15034,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying over a funeral, saying: \"O Allah, forgive him, have mercy on him, pardon him, grant him well-being, honor his lodging, widen his entrance, wash him with water, snow, and hail, and cleanse him of sins as a white garment is cleansed of dirt. And grant him a home better than his home, a family better than his family, and a spouse better than his spouse. Protect him from the trial of the grave and the punishment of the Fire.\" 'Awf b. Malik said, \"I wished that I were the deceased because of the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[15035,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over a funeral, and I memorized from his supplication while he was saying: \"O Allah, forgive him, have mercy on him, grant him well-being, pardon him, honor his lodging, widen his entrance, wash him with water, snow, and hail, and cleanse him of sins as a white garment is cleansed of dirt. And replace his home with a home better than his, a family better than his, and a spouse better than his. Admit him to Paradise and protect him from the punishment of the grave and the punishment of the Fire.\" So much that I wished I were that deceased."],[15036,"\"When the Prophet ﷺ received booty, he would distribute it the same day, giving the married man two shares and the unmarried man one share.\""],[15037,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received booty, he would distribute it the same day, giving the married man two shares and the unmarried man one share. We were called, and I was called before 'Ammar b. Yasir, and I was given one share. He became displeased until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and those present noticed. A piece of gold remained, and the Prophet ﷺ began lifting it with the tip of his staff, and it would fall; then he would lift it and it would fall, saying, \"How will you be on the day when this is hoarded for you?\" No one answered him. Then 'Ammar b. Yasir said, \"By Allah, we would love it to be hoarded for us, so that those who are patient remain patient and those who are tempted are tempted.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Perhaps you will be in it an evil, one who is tempted.\""],[15038,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ lifted with his staff a piece of a gold chain that remained from the booty, saying, \"How will you be on the day when this is hoarded for you?\" No one answered him. Then a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"By Allah, we would love it to be hoarded for us, so that those who are patient remain patient and those who are tempted are tempted.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Perhaps you will be an evil, one who is tempted.\""],[15039,"The Prophet ﷺ set out one day with me accompanying him until we entered the synagogue of the Jews on the day of their festival, and they disliked his entering upon them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O company of Jews, show me twelve men among you who will testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; Allah will remove from every Jew under the canopy of the sky the wrath that is upon him.” They fell silent; no one answered him. Then he repeated it to them, and no one answered him. Then he said it a third time, and no one answered him. So he said: “You refuse. By Allah, I am the Hasher, and I am the Aqib, and I am the Muqaffi, whether you believe or you deny.” Then he departed with me, and when we were about to leave, a man called out from behind him and said: “Stay where you are, O Muhammad.” So he turned, and that man said: “Which man do you know among you, O company of Jews?” They said: “By Allah, we do not know any man among us more knowledgeable of the Book of Allah, nor more understanding, than you, nor than your father before you, nor than your grandfather before your father.” He said: “Then I testify to him by Allah that he is the Prophet of Allah whom you find in the Torah.” They said: “You have lied.” Then they replied to him and said evil things about him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You have lied. We will never accept your word.” He said: Then we went out, and we were three: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, myself, and Ibn Sallam. And Allah, exalted be He, revealed: {Say, “Have you considered: if it is from Allah and you disbelieve in it, while a witness from the Children of Israel has testified to something similar and believed, and you are arrogant?” Indeed, Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people.}"],[15040,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not levy the fifth on spoils, and that a man from the reinforcements was his companion in the campaign of Mu’tah, on the border of Syria. They met the enemy, and a Byzantine among them began to press hard upon the Muslims, mounted on a chestnut horse with a gilded saddle, a belt smeared with gold, and a sword adorned with gold. He would raid them, and that reinforcement man sought an opportunity against him until he passed by him, so he hamstrung his horse, and he fell. Then he fell upon him with the sword and killed him. When Allah defeated the Byzantines, clear testimony was established for the reinforcement man that he had killed him, so Khalid gave him his sword and a fifth of his property. Awf said: I spoke to Khalid b. al-Walid and said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled the spoils belong to the killer? He said: Yes, but I considered it too much. Awf said: And there was an exchange of words between me and him, so I said: By Allah, I will inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of what you have done. Awf said: When we gathered before the Prophet ﷺ, Awf mentioned what had happened from him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What prevented you from giving it to him?” Khalid said: I considered it too much. He said: “Give it to him.” Awf said: Then I said: How do you see it now, O Khalid? Have I not fulfilled for you what I promised you? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry and said to Khalid: “Do not give it to him,” and said: “Will you not leave my commanders to me?”"],[15041,"“That the Prophet ﷺ assigned the spoils to the fighter and did not levy the fifth on it.”"],[15042,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Will you not leave my commanders to me? Indeed, my likeness and their likeness is that of a man who bought camels and cattle, pastured them, then brought them to a watering trough, and they lowered their heads into it and drank its clear water and left its dregs. Its clear water is for you, and its dregs are upon them.”"],[15043,"We used to perform incantations in the pre-Islamic era, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, how do you regard that? He said: “Present your incantations to me. There is no harm in incantations as long as there is no polytheism in them.”"],[15044,"A man from Himyar killed a man from the enemy and wanted his spoils, but Khalid b. al-Walid prevented him, as he was the governor over them. Awf came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him, and he said: “O Khalid, what prevented you from giving him his spoils?” He said: I considered them too much, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “Give them to him.” Then Khalid passed by Awf, pulled his cloak, and said: Have I fulfilled for you what I mentioned to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? So he became angry and said: “Do not give them to him, O Khalid. Will you not leave my commanders to me? Indeed, your likeness and their likeness is that of a man who bought camels, pastured them, then waited for the time of their watering and brought them to a trough, and they lowered their heads into it and drank its clear water and left its dregs. Its clear water is for you, and its dregs are upon them.”"],[15045,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “My community will split into seventy-some sects; the greatest of them in trial upon my community is a people who measure matters by their own opinions, thereby making lawful what is forbidden and making forbidden what is lawful.”"],[15046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “How will you be, O Awf, when this community splits into seventy-three sects, one of which is in Paradise and the rest are in the Fire?” I said: And when will that be, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “When the police are many, slave women become rulers, the lowly sit upon pulpits, the Quran is taken as flutes, mosques are adorned, pulpits are raised, the fay’ is taken as spoils of war, zakah is treated as a fine, trust is treated as booty, religious understanding is sought for other than Allah, a man obeys his wife, is undutiful to his mother, and drives away his father, the last of this community curses its first, the wicked of a tribe becomes its leader, and the chief of a people is their most despicable, and a man is honored out of fear of his evil. On that day that will be, and on that day people will flee to Syria, and it will protect them from their enemy.” I said: Will Syria be conquered? He said: “Yes, soon. Then trials will occur after its conquest, then a dusty, dark trial will come, then trials will follow one another until a man from my household emerges, called the Mahdi. If you reach him, follow him and be among the rightly guided.”"],[15047,"“That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled the spoils belong to the killer.”"],[15048,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among his companions and said: “Do you fear poverty or destitution, or are you preoccupied with this world? For Allah will open Persia and Byzantium to you, and the world will be poured upon you abundantly, until if you go astray afterwards, nothing will cause you to deviate but it.”"],[15049,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands you to seek refuge from three things: from greed where there is no greed, from greed that returns to a natural disposition, and from greed toward something that is not a proper object of greed."],[15050,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ during the expedition of Tabuk in the last part of the night while he was in his tent. I greeted him and said, “May I enter?” He said: “Enter.” I said, “All of me?” He said: “All of you.” Then he said: “There are six things before the Hour. The first is the death of your Prophet ﷺ—say one.” I said, “One.” “The second is the conquest of Jerusalem—say two.” I said, “Two.” He said: “The third is a pestilence that will seize you like the quʿāṣ of sheep—say three.” I said, “Three.” He said: “The fourth is that wealth will overflow among you, so much that a man will be given a hundred dinars and remain displeased with them—say four.” “And the fifth is a tribulation that will occur among you, and no house of mud or hair will remain among you but it will enter it—say five.” I said, “Five.” “And the sixth is a truce between you and the Banu al-Asfar. They will gather against you with the force of a pregnant woman, then they will betray you and advance in eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand.”"],[15051,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque with a staff in his hand. He saw clusters of dates hanging, struck one of them, and found in it a withered, poor-quality date. He said: “Who does this belong to? If only he had given in charity something better than this. The owner of this will eat such poor dates on the Day of Resurrection.” Then he said: “O people of Madinah, you will surely leave it to the scavengers for forty years.” It was said, “What are the scavengers?” He said: “The birds and the beasts of prey.”"],[15052,"ʿAwf, what is this?” They said, “Kaʿb is telling stories.” He said, “Woe to him! Has he not heard the hadith of the Messenger of God ﷺ: ‘No one tells stories to the people except a ruler, one commanded, or a show-off.’”"],[15053,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever stands in a position of showing off, God will expose him; and whoever stands in a position of seeking reputation, God will make him heard of.”"],[15054,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no Muslim who has three daughters and spends on them until they marry or die, but they will be a screen for him from the Fire.” A woman said, “Or two?” He said: “And two.”"],[15055,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I and a woman with sunken, dark cheeks will be like these two—a woman who is left without a husband and restrains herself for her daughters until they part or die.”"],[15056,"Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whenever the life of a Muslim is prolonged, it is good for him?” He said, “Yes.”"],[15057,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “I fear for you six things: the rule of fools, shedding of blood, selling of judgments, severing of kinship, a generation who take the Qurʾan as pipes, and the proliferation of police.”"],[15058,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “My Lord, Exalted is He, gave me the choice between two options: that half of my community enter Paradise, or intercession.”"],[15059,"We traveled with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey and stopped. When night came, my eyes grew restless and sleep did not come to me. I got up, and there was no beast in the camp but had its cheek on the ground—and the highest thing in my mind was the place of the rear of the saddle. I said, “I will certainly go to the Messenger of God ﷺ, for I cannot sleep at all tonight until morning.” I went out, threading my way through the saddles, until I reached the saddle of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He was not at his saddle, so I went out threading my way through the saddles until I left the camp. Then I saw a dark shape and made for it. It was Abu ʿUbaydah b. al-Jarrah and Muʿadh b. Jabal. They said to me, “What brought you out?” I said, “The same as brought you out.” Then we found ourselves near a thicket not far from us. We walked to the thicket, and we heard in it something like the hum of bees or the rustling of winds. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Is Abu ʿUbaydah b. al-Jarrah here?” We said, “Yes.” He said: “And Muʿadh b. Jabal?” We said, “Yes.” He said: “And ʿAwf b. Malik?” We said, “Yes.” The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us. We stood without asking him about anything, and he did not ask us about anything. Then he returned to his saddle and said: “Shall I tell you what my Lord offered me just now?” We said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “He gave me the choice between a third of my community entering Paradise without reckoning or punishment, and intercession.” We said, “O Messenger of God, what did you choose?” He said: “I chose intercession.” We all said, “O Messenger of God, make us among the people of your intercession.” He said to us: “My intercession is for every Muslim.”"],[15060,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us over the funeral of a man from the Ansar, and I heard him say: “O Allah, send blessings upon him, forgive him, have mercy on him, grant him well-being, pardon him, honor his lodging and his final abode, wash him with water, snow, and hail, and purify him of sins as a white garment is purified of dirt. Give him in exchange a home better than his home and a family better than his family, and protect him from the trial of the grave and the punishment of the Fire.” ʿAwf said: I saw myself wishing in my sleep for that—that I might be the deceased in place of that Ansari—because of what I saw of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[15061,"O people, beware of sins for which there is no expiation. A man may commit usury and then repent, and Allah will turn to him, yet Allah, exalted is He, says: “It is not for a prophet to be treacherous, and whoever is treacherous will bring what he treacherously took on the Day of Resurrection.” Indeed, Allah will raise the consumer of usury on the Day of Resurrection insane, choking."],[15062,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Storytellers are three: a ruler, one commanded, or a conceited boaster.”"],[15063,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of you and the best of your leaders are those whom you love and who love you, and upon whom you invoke blessings and who invoke blessings upon you. The worst of you and the worst of your leaders are those whom you hate and who hate you, and whom you curse and who curse you.” They said: Should we not then oppose them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “No, as long as they establish the five prayers. Indeed, if someone is appointed a ruler over a man and sees him commit something of disobedience to Allah, let him hate what he does of disobedience to Allah. Indeed, do not withdraw your hand from obedience.”"],[15064,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The best of your leaders are those whom you love and who love you, and for whom you supplicate to Allah and who supplicate to Allah for you. The worst of your leaders are those whom you hate and who hate you, and whom you curse and who curse you.” It was said: O Messenger of Allah, should we not then oppose them? He said: “No, as long as they establish the prayer among you. If you see from your ruler something you dislike, then hate his action, but do not withdraw your hand from obedience.”"],[15065,"I set out for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the expedition of Tabuk while he was in a tent. He heard the scuff of my feet and said: \"Who is this?\" I said: \"ʿAwf b. Malik.\" He said: \"Enter, O ʿAwf.\" I said: \"All of me, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Yes.\" So I entered, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was performing wudu in a thorough manner. He said: \"O ʿAwf, six things are before the Hour. Do you count the first of them? The death of your Prophet ﷺ. Say 'one.'\" I said: \"One.\" And at that I grieved with a severe grief. Then he said: \"The conquest of Iliya. Say 'two.'\" I said: \"Two.\" \"Then wealth will pour upon you until a man is given a hundred dinars and he is displeased with it. Say 'three.'\" I said: \"Three.\" \"Then a plague will be sent upon you like the scab of sheep. Say 'four.'\" I said: \"Four.\" \"Then a tribulation will emerge from among you that will hardly leave a Muslim household without entering it. Say 'five.'\" I said: \"Five.\" \"Then there will be a truce between you and the Romans, and they will betray it at its end, and they will gather against you as a woman carries a child. Then they will come to you in eighty banners, under each banner eighty thousand.\""],[15066,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Before the Hour there will be years of deception, in which the trustworthy will be suspected, the treacherous will be trusted, the truthful will be disbelieved, the liar will be believed, and the ruwaybidah will speak in the affairs of the people.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the ruwaybidah?\" He said: \"The insignificant fool who speaks in the affairs of the common people.\""],[15067,"I heard ʿAwf b. Malik al-Ashjaʿi say: We encamped with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at a place. I woke up during the night and saw nothing in the camp taller than the back of a saddle; every person and his camel were flattened to the ground. I got up and walked among the people until I reached the Prophet's resting place, and he was not there. I placed my hand on the bed, and it was cold. I got up and went out walking among the people, saying: \"Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we shall return. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been taken away.\" I went out of the whole camp and saw a dark shape, so I went toward it and threw a stone. I continued to the dark shape, and there were Muʿadh b. Jabal and Abu ʿUbaydah b. al-Jarrah. And before us there was a sound like the rumbling of a mill and like the sound of a staff stirred by the winds. Some of us said to others: \"O people, stand firm until you are healthy or your Messenger of Allah ﷺ comes to you.\" We waited as long as Allah willed. Then he called out: \"Are Muʿadh b. Jabal, Abu ʿUbaydah b. al-Jarrah, and ʿAwf b. Malik there?\" We said: \"Yes.\" He came toward us until we were with him, and we did not ask him anything nor did he tell us anything until he sat on his bed. Then he said: \"Do you know what my Lord offered me tonight?\" We said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"He offered me the choice between half of my ummah entering Paradise and intercession, and I chose intercession.\" We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make us among its people.\" He said: \"It is for every Muslim.\""],[15068,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Seek refuge in Allah from greed that leads to avarice, and from greed that leads to what is not desired.\""],[15069,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you wish, I will tell you about authority and what it is: its beginning is blame, its second is remorse, and its third is punishment on the Day of Resurrection, except for one who is just.\""],[15070,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in one of his military expeditions. One night I woke up and did not find the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in his place, while his companions were as if rocks were on their heads, and the camels had put down their necks. Then I saw a figure approaching me, and I approached it, and it was Muadh b. Jabal. I said, 'Where is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said, 'Behind me.' Then I saw a figure approaching me, and I approached it, and it was Abu Musa al-Ashari. He said: Humayd b. Hilal narrated to me, from Abu Burdah b. Abi Musa, from Awf b. Malik al-Ashjai, who said: I heard behind Abu Musa a sound like the sound of a millstone. I said, 'Where is the Prophet ﷺ?' He said, 'Behind me, he has come.' Then I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, when a prophet is in enemy territory, he should have a guard.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'A messenger came to me from my Lord, may He be exalted, and gave me the choice between half of my nation entering Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession.' Muadh said, 'May my father and mother be sacrificed for you. You have known my kinship and my status, so make me among them.' He said, 'You are among them.' Awf and Abu Musa said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you know that we left our families, preferring Allah and His Messenger, so make us among them.' He said, 'It is for every Muslim; you two are among them.' Then we reached the people when they called out. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Sit down,' so they sat down as if no one had stood up. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: 'A messenger came to me from my Lord and gave me the choice between half of my nation entering Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession.' The people said, 'O Messenger of Allah, make us among them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Listen attentively,' so they listened as if no one had spoken. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'My intercession is for whoever dies without associating anything with Allah.'"],[15071,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'My intercession is for whoever of my nation dies without associating anything with Allah.'"],[15072,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during a journey, and we stopped for the night. I got up to look for the Prophet ﷺ , but I couldn't find him. Instead, I found Mu'adh ibn Jabal and Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari, so I asked, \"Where is the Messenger of Allah?\" They replied, \"We don't know.\" While we were in this situation, we heard a sound coming from the top of the valley, like the sound of a grinding mill. Soon after, the Prophet ﷺ came, and we said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we lost you tonight.\" He said, \"I was visited by a caller from my Lord who gave me the choice between having half of my Ummah enter Paradise and having the power of intercession. So I chose intercession.\" We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah to make us among the people of your intercession.\" He said, \"O Allah, make them among the people of intercession.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, my intercession will be for those who die without associating anything with Allah.\""],[15073,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'No one should relate stories except a commander, one commanded to do so, or one who pretends.' So he refrained from storytelling until Muawiyah commanded him to do it."],[15074,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever recites a letter of the Quran has a good deed written for him.' I do not say to you, 'Alif Lam Mim. That is the Book,' but rather the alif, the lam, the mim, the dhal, and the kaf."],[15075,"One day the Prophet ﷺ went out and a man from the Anṣār met him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. I am distressed by what I see on your face—what is it?” He said, and the Prophet ﷺ looked at the man’s face for a moment then said, “Hunger.” The man went off running, or nearly running, until he reached his house and searched for food but found nothing. Then he went to the Banū Qurayẓa and hired himself out for a date for every bucket he drew, until he gathered a handful or a cupped hand of dates. Then he returned with the dates and found the Prophet ﷺ still sitting in the same gathering. He placed them before him and said, “Eat, O Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Where did you get these dates?” He told him the story, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “I think you love Allah and His Messenger.” He said, “Yes, by the One who sent you with the truth, you are dearer to me than myself, my children, my family, and my wealth.” He said, “Then be patient with poverty and prepare for affliction with protective covering. By the One who sent me with the truth, they are swifter to the one who loves me than water descending from the top of a mountain to its foot.”"],[15076,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The Hour will not come except upon the dregs of mankind.”"],[15077,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whom do you count as a martyr among you?” We said, “O Messenger of Allah, the one who is killed in the path of Allah.” He said, “Then the martyrs of my community would be few. Whoever is killed in the path of Allah is a martyr; the one who dies of a stomach ailment is a martyr; the one who falls from a height is a martyr; the woman who dies in childbirth is a martyr; and the one who drowns is a martyr.” Al-Ḥulwānī added in his narration: “And the one who dies of tuberculosis is a martyr, the one who dies in a fire is a martyr, and the stranger is a martyr.”"],[15078,"Al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Ḥaḍramī wrote to the Prophet ﷺ and began with himself."],[15079,"Because he came from the land of Hadramaut."],[15080,"Al-Ḥaḍramī, Abū al-ʿAlāʾ, his name is ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbbād b. Akbar b. Rabīʿah b. Mālik b. ʿArīf b. Mālik b. al-Khazraj b. al-Ṣadaf. Al-ʿAlāʾ was governor for the Prophet ﷺ over al-Baḥrayn. The Prophet ﷺ died while he was over it. Al-ʿAlāʾ died in al-Baḥrayn or returning from it in the year twenty-one, and it is said in the year fourteen, and it is said \"in the year fifteen.\""],[15082,"Abū Shuʿayb ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us:"],[15083,"Abū Shuʿayb ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us:"],[15084,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent Al-Ala' bin Al-Hadrami to Bahrain, I followed him and observed three qualities in him that I don't know which one was more amazing. We reached the seaside, and they said, \"Name and invade!\" So we named and invaded, and we crossed over. The water barely reached the ankles of our camels. When we stopped, we found ourselves surrounded by sandy hills with no water. We complained to him, so he performed two Rak'ahs (units) of prayer, then supplicated. Suddenly, a cloud resembling a shield appeared and it poured rain. We drank and filled our containers. Abu Bakr sent him to Bahrain again, but he passed away after that. When Rabi'ah tribe turned back, Allah granted them victory and they gave what they had withheld from Zakah (alms). After he died, we buried him in the sand. When we were not far away, we said, \"Seven people will come and eat him.\" So we returned, but we did not see them."],[15085,"And Abū Bakr sent al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Ḥaḍramī in an army of the Muslims toward the people of al-Baḥrayn. They had withheld the jizyah. Abū Bakr sent against them when they withheld the right of Allah in their wealth. He marched to them, and between him and them was the sea, until they walked in it with their feet. Thus they crossed at a place where ships had sailed before that, and they sail in it today. He fought them, and Allah gave him victory over them, so they surrendered, after having refused the right of Allah in their wealth."],[15086,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The emigrant may stay in Makkah after completing his rites for three (days).\""],[15087,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The emigrant may stay after completing his rites for three (days).\""],[15088,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The emigrant may stay after completing his rites for three (days).\""],[15089,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"For the emigrant, three (days).\""],[15090,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"For the emigrant, three (days) after the departure.\""],[15091,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me and wrote regarding two partners, one of them a Muslim and the other a polytheist: \"Take from the Muslim the tithe and from the polytheist the jizyah.\""],[15092,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no community that innovates a heresy in its religion after its prophet except that it loses an equivalent amount of the Sunnah.\""],[15093,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Imru' al-Qays was mentioned, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"That is a man renowned in this world, forgotten in the Hereafter; noble in this world, obscure in the Hereafter. On the Day of Resurrection he will come holding the banner of the poets, leading them to the Fire.\""],[15094,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a delegation from Yemen came, and they mentioned Imru' al-Qays b. Hujr al-Kindi and quoted two lines of his poetry in which there is mention of Sarikh, one of the watering-places of the Arabs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"That is a man renowned in this world, forgotten in the Hereafter; noble in this world, obscure in the Hereafter. On the Day of Resurrection he will come with the banner of the poets, leading them to the Fire.\""],[15095,"I was a merchant. By Allah, I was with him when a man came out from near him and looked at the sun. When he saw that it had declined, he stood and prayed. Then a woman came out from that tent from which the man had come out, and she stood behind him praying. Then a boy who had reached puberty came out from that tent praying. I said to al-Abbas: \"Who is this?\" He said: \"This is Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Abd al-Muttalib, my nephew.\" I said: \"Who is this woman?\" He said: \"His wife, Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid.\" I said: \"Who is the youth?\" He said: \"Ali b. Abi Talib, his cousin.\" I said: \"What is this that he is doing?\" He said: \"He prays, and he claims that he is a prophet. No one has followed him in his affair except his wife and this youth, his cousin. He claims that the treasures of Kisra and Caesar will be opened for him.\" Afif later became a Muslim — he was the cousin of al-Ash'ath b. Qays — and he used to regret what he had missed of Islam on that day."],[15096,"I brought my son to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"What is his name?\" I said: \"So-and-so.\" He said: \"Rather, Abd al-Rahman.\""],[15097,"I brought my son to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"What is his name?\" I said: \"So-and-so.\" He said: \"Rather, Abd al-Rahman.\""],[15098,"When Husayn embraced Islam, the Prophet ﷺ taught him a supplication to invoke."],[15099,"I came to Basra, and there was Abu Nujayd Imran b. al-Husayn — Umar b. al-Khattab had sent him to teach the jurisprudence to the people of Basra."],[15100,"Imran b. al-Husayn died in the year fifty-two."],[15101,"I came to Basra and entered the mosque, and there was an old man with a white head and beard, leaning against a pillar, with a circle of people around him whom he was narrating to. I said: \"Who is this?\" They said: \"Imran b. al-Husayn.\""],[15102,"No one came to Basra among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who surpassed ʿImrān b. al-Ḥuṣayn."],[15103,"Sufyan ibn Uyaynah said, \"Basra has never witnessed anyone like Imran ibn Husain.\""],[15104,"I have not touched my private part with my right hand since I pledged allegiance with it to the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[15105,"One of those who came to him said: He almost prevented us from what we see. He said: \"Do not do that, for by God, the one most beloved to me is the one most beloved to my Lord.\""],[15106,"That I should sacrifice an aged animal: God is more deserving of self-sufficiency and generosity.\""],[15107,"\"I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ hadiths that I heard and memorized. Nothing prevents me from narrating them except that my companions contradict me in them.\""],[15108,"\"That I be a black Abyssinian slave tending pebbles in the eyes on the top of a mountain until my appointed time overtakes me is dearer to me than that I shoot an arrow in one of the two ranks, whether I miss or hit.\""],[15109,"Al-Ḥasan said: \"By God, if ʿImrān were alive today, he would have more to say.\""],[15110,"\"Those who remembered are gone, and those who are forgotten remain; those who fed are gone, and those who seek food remain.\""],[15111,"\"When I die, wrap a turban tightly over my belly, and when you return, slaughter and feed.\" Khālid said: Then Ḥafṣ said to me: \"It is not as your sons, the people of the family of al-Muhallab, and Thaqīf do.\""],[15112,"\"I saw ʿImrān b. al-Ḥuṣayn wearing silk brocade.\""],[15113,"We accompanied ʿImrān from Kufa to Basra, and no day passed except that he recited poetry to us, and he said to us regarding that: \"In indirect allusion there is ample scope to avoid lying.\""],[15114,"ʿImrān b. al-Ḥuṣayn had a brother killed in the pre-Islamic era, and he killed seventy for him."],[15115,"\"The angels used to shake hands with 'Imran b. Husayn until he was cauterized.\""],[15116,"that a man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ entered ihram from one of the garrison cities.\""],[15117,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Looking at 'Ali ؓ is an act of worship.\""],[15118,"When it was the Day of the Conquest, Khuza'ah killed a man from Quraysh called al-Harith. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said, \"Did they kill him before the prohibition or after it?\" They said, \"Rather after it.\" He said: Then we came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and we paid his blood money. It was the first blood money in Islam."],[15119,"A man from Hudhayl killed a man from Khuza'ah in the Jahiliyyah. The Hudhali went into hiding. When it was the Day of the Conquest and the call became public, he appeared. A man from Khuza'ah met him and slaughtered him like a sheep is slaughtered. That was raised to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"Did he kill him before the call or after the call?\" They said, \"He killed him after the call.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"If I were to kill a believer for a disbeliever, I would have killed him for him, but bring out his blood money.\" They brought out his blood money, and the first blood money in Islam began."],[15120,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants were the weak, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants were women.\""],[15121,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'umrah for a group of his family during the ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prohibit it, and no verse abrogating it was revealed until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A group of the people of Islam will continue fighting for Islam, triumphant over those who oppose them, until they fight the Dajjal.\""],[15122,"\"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'umrah for some of his family during the ten days,\" and Ibn Kathir and al-Firyabi did not mention Mutarrif b. 'Abdullah in their narration, and Waki' made it well."],[15123,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had performed 'umrah for a group of his family during the ten days. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prohibit it, and no Qur'an was revealed concerning it. A man said according to his own opinion whatever he wished."],[15124,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had performed 'umrah for a group of his family during the ten days, and no verse abrogating that was revealed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prohibit it.\""],[15125,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had already performed ʿumrah for a group of his family in the first ten days of Dhū al-Ḥijjah, and he did not prohibit it, nor did a revelation come down [against it]."],[15126,"It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so does not break his fast all year.” He said, “He neither fasted nor broke his fast.”"],[15127,"It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so does not break his fast by day.” He said, “He neither fasted nor broke his fast.”"],[15128,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said to him, or to a man, “Did you fast anything during the month of Shaʿbān?” He said, “No.” He said, “Then when you break your fast, fast two days.”"],[15129,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Did you fast during the middle days of this month?” I said, “No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Then when you break your fast from Ramaḍān, fast two days in place of that day.”"],[15130,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said to him or to someone else, “Did you fast the last nights of this month?” He said, “No.” He said, “When the people break their fast, or when you break your fast, then fast two days.”"],[15131,"A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have embraced Islam, so what do you command me?” He said, “Say: O Allah, I seek Your guidance in my affair, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of my own self.”"],[15132,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Most of the people of the Fire are women.”"],[15133,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man, “Did you fast the middle days of this month?” He said, “No.” He said, “Then when you break your fast, fast two days in its place.” Then I asked a man from his family about who narrated this: “Abū al-ʿAlāʾ?” He said, “ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn from the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[15134,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say regarding cauterization.”"],[15135,"It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so fasts all year.” He said, “He neither fasted nor broke his fast.”"],[15136,"The Prophet ﷺ said: A section of my community will continue to fight for the right and overcome their opponents till the last of them fights with the Antichrist. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2484)"],[15137,"ʿImrān said to me, “I have not prayed since a while, or since such and such, a prayer more resembling the prayer of the Messenger of Allah than this prayer.”"],[15138,"ʿImrān said: “This is a prayer the like of which I have not prayed after the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[15139,"“We performed the tamattuʿ of Hajj with the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[15140,"The Messenger of God ﷺ combined a Hajj and an ʿUmrah, then no scripture was revealed concerning it and the Messenger of God ﷺ did not prohibit it. A man said regarding it what he wished by his own opinion.”"],[15141,"“We performed tamattuʿ with the Messenger of God ﷺ and the Quran was revealed during that. Let a man say by his own opinion what he wishes.”"],[15142,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ combined a Hajj and an ʿUmrah.”"],[15143,"“We performed tamattuʿ of Hajj with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and it is a verse in the Book of God that nothing has abrogated.”"],[15144,"The Messenger of God ﷺ combined a Hajj and an ʿUmrah, then no scripture was revealed concerning it and the Messenger of God ﷺ did not prohibit it. A man said regarding it what he wished by his own opinion.”"],[15145,"About cauterization: he suffered from a stomach ailment for thirty years and did not cauterize.”"],[15146,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Modesty brings nothing but good.”"],[15147,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The fewest inhabitants of Paradise are women.”"],[15148,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, on two consecutive days; then he became slower to me about some of that, or out of dislike for it: that men among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ—I witnessed as they witnessed and I heard as they heard—related to us hadiths that are not as they say. I know that they do not fall short of the truth—or he said, of the good—but I fear that it may be confused for me as it was confused for them. Sometimes he would say: If I were to say that I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ such-and-such, I would think that I have spoken truthfully. And sometimes he would stand and say: The Messenger of God ﷺ said such-and-such.”"],[15149,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from cauterization, but we cauterized ourselves and neither succeeded nor prospered.”"],[15150,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to him, or to a man: “Have you fasted any of the middle days of Shaʿbān?” He said: “No.” He said: “When you have broken your fast, then fast two days.”"],[15151,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade cauterization, but we cauterized ourselves and neither succeeded nor prospered.”"],[15152,"ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn said to me: “Shall I not narrate to you a hadith that perhaps Allah will benefit you by? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Ḥajj and ʿUmrah, and no Qurʾān was revealed prohibiting it, nor did he forbid it until he died.” He said: “A man expressed his opinion as he wished.”"],[15153,"“The Prophet ﷺ performed ʿUmrah for a group of his family during the ten days.”"],[15154,"We used to count the false oath (al-yamīn al-ghamūs) among the major sins."],[15155,"ʿImran and I prayed behind ʿAli bin Abi Talib and he said Takbir on prostrating, on rising and on getting up after the two rakʿat (i.e. after the second rakʿa). When the prayer was finished, ʿImran took me by the hand and said, \"He (ʿAli) has prayed the prayer of Muhammad\" (or said, \"He made us remember the prayer of Muhammad). (Using translation from Bukhārī 826)"],[15156,"ʿImrān, holding my hand, said: “This man led us in prayer with the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[15157,"ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn: “He led us in the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[15158,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him, or to a man: “Did you fast the ‘white days’ of this month?” He said: “No.” He said: “Then when you break your fast, fast two days.”"],[15159,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade cauterization, so I had myself cauterized, and it did not benefit me or succeed for me."],[15160,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The fewest inhabitants of Paradise are women.”"],[15161,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The inhabitants of Paradise least in number are women.\""],[15162,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The fewest inhabitants of Paradise are women.”"],[15163,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched a military expedition and appointed ʿAlī as commander over them. ʿAlī proceeded with the expedition and obtained a slave girl. They disapproved of that. Four men from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a pact, saying: “When we meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we will inform him of what ʿAlī did.” ʿImrān said: “The Muslims, when they arrived from travel, would begin with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, greet him, then depart.” When the expedition arrived, they greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One of the four stood and said: “O Messenger of Allah, did you not see that ʿAlī did such-and-such?” He turned away from him. Then another stood and said: “O Messenger of Allah, did you not see that ʿAlī did such-and-such?” He turned away from him. Then another of them stood and said: “O Messenger of Allah, did you not see that ʿAlī did such-and-such?” He turned away from him. Then the fourth stood and said: “O Messenger of Allah, did you not see that ʿAlī did such-and-such?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to him, anger recognizable in his face, and said three times: “What do you want from ʿAlī? Indeed ʿAlī is from me and I am from him, and he is the ally of every believer after me.”"],[15164,"“O Messenger of Allah, are the people of Paradise known from the people of the Fire?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Then for what do the workers work?” He said: “Each is facilitated for what he was created.”"],[15165,"“O Messenger of Allah, are the people of Paradise known from the people of the Fire?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Then for what do the workers work?” He said: “Work, for each is facilitated for what he was created.”"],[15166,"A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, are the people of Paradise known from the people of the Fire?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Then for what do the workers work?” He said: “Each is facilitated for what he was created.”"],[15167,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “O Messenger of Allah, are the people of Paradise known from the people of the Fire?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Then for what do the workers work?” He said: “Each is facilitated for what he was created.”"],[15168,"A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, are the people of Paradise known from the people of the Fire?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Then what is the point of action?” He said, “Act, for everyone is facilitated toward that for which he was created.”"],[15169,"About a man who divorced his wife once and did not have witnesses, then took her back and did not have witnesses? ʿImran said, “You divorced contrary to the Sunnah and took her back contrary to the Sunnah. Have witnesses for her divorce and for her return.”"],[15170,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked, “Are the people of Paradise known from the people of the Fire?” He said, “Yes.” It was said to him, “Then for what do the workers act?” He said, “Each acts for that for which he was created, or for that which has been facilitated for him.”"],[15171,"They said, “O Messenger of Allah, for what do the workers act—for what has already passed or for what is to come?” He said, “For what has already passed.” He said, “Then for what do they act?” He said, “Each is facilitated.”"],[15172,"Imran ibn Husain came to his wife from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and she said, \"Tell us what you heard from the Prophet ﷺ.\" He said, \"There was no opportunity for conversation, so I left him.\" She insisted, and he said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were the poor, and I looked into Hell and saw that most of its people were women.'\""],[15173,"We were on a journey with the Prophet ﷺ and traveled one night until, in the last part of the night just before dawn, we fell into that sleep—and no sleep is sweeter for a traveler. Nothing woke us but the heat of the sun. The first to wake was Bilal, then so-and-so and so-and-so (and he named them), then ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept, no one would wake him until he woke on his own, because we did not know what might happen to him in his sleep. When ʿUmar woke and saw what had befallen the people—and he was a strong man—he said takbīr and raised his voice with takbīr, and kept saying takbīr and raising his voice until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke at his voice. The people complained to him about what had happened to them. He said, “No harm; move on.” So he departed and traveled a short distance, then stopped and called for water for ablution and performed ablution. Then the call to prayer was given, and he led the people in prayer. When he finished his prayer, there was a man who had kept apart and had not prayed with the people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “What prevented you, O so-and-so, from praying with the people?” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I became junub and there is no water.” He said, “Use the earth, for it suffices you.” Then he traveled on, and the people complained to him of thirst. He stopped and called so-and-so—Abu Raja' named him—and called ʿAlī, and said to them, “Go and seek water.” They set off and met a woman between two waterskins—or two leather water bags—of water on a camel of hers. They went to her and said, “Where is the water?” She said, “My last contact with it was yesterday at this hour.” They said to her, “Then come with us.” She said, “To where?” They said, “To the Prophet ﷺ.” She said, “The one called the Ṣābi'?” They said, “The one you mean; come along.” So they brought her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him the story. They made her dismount from her camel, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a vessel and put in it the mouths of the two waterskins—or the two water bags—then rinsed his mouth and returned it to the vessel, then returned it to the mouths of the two waterskins—or the two water bags—then tied their mouths and released the spouts, and it was announced among the people: “Drink and fill your containers.” So whoever wished drank, and whoever wished filled his container. The last of that was that he gave to the one who had become junub and said, “Go and pour it over yourself.” She stood watching what was being done with her water. By Allah, he mounted her when he had finished, and it seemed to us that they were fuller than they had been before. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Collect for her from dates, barley meal, and flour,” until they collected food for her in a cloth, loaded her on her camel, and placed it in front of her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, “Know, by Allah, that we have not taken anything from your water; rather it is Allah who gave us to drink.” She came to her people after having been delayed from them, and they said, “O so-and-so, what delayed you?” She said, “The wonder: two men met me and took me to this one called the Ṣābi', and he did such-and-such. By Allah, he is either the greatest sorcerer between this and that, or he is truly the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” The Muslims used to raid the polytheists around her, but they would not touch the small group of camels near her. One day she said to her people, “By Allah, I think these people are calling us; would you accept Islam?” So they agreed with her, and they all entered Islam."],[15174,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants were women, and I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants were the poor.”"],[15175,"“We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey.” A man of the people became junub and found no water, so he performed tayammum and prayed. Then he came to water at the time of that prayer and bathed, and the Prophet ﷺ did not order him to repeat it."],[15176,"ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn said, “The verse of mutʿah was revealed in the Book of Allah—meaning the mutʿah of Hajj—and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded it, and no verse was revealed abrogating the verse of the mutʿah of Hajj, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not forbid it until he died. A man said, by his own opinion, whatever he wished.”"],[15177,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling weapons during times of civil strife."],[15178,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A people will come out of the Fire by the intercession of Muhammad ﷺ and enter Paradise; they will be called the Jahannamiyyun.\""],[15179,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, his sins and misdeeds are expiated. When he begins walking, twenty good deeds are recorded for him for every step. When he finishes the prayer, he is rewarded with the work of two hundred years.\""],[15180,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"What do you say about the adulterer, the thief, and the wine drinker?\" They said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"They are immoral acts, and in them is punishment. Shall I not tell you of the greatest of major sins? It is associating partners with Allah.\" Then he recited: \"And whoever associates others with Allah has certainly fabricated a tremendous sin.\" And undutifulness to parents. Then he said: \"Be grateful to Me and to your parents; to Me is the final destination.\" He was reclining, so he sat up and said: \"Indeed, and false speech.\" Ibn ʿAbbas said: \"Everything Allah has forbidden is a major sin.\""],[15181,"Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ stoned."],[15182,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Indeed, the son of my son has died. What is my portion of his inheritance?\" He said, \"You have the sixth.\" When he turned to leave, the Prophet called him back and said, \"Indeed, the remaining sixth is a provision.\""],[15183,"\"About the topic of the kayy\""],[15184,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade cauterization, but we insisted and cauterized, and we did not succeed or prosper."],[15185,"Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ used to recite: \"And you will see the people drunk, yet they are not drunk, but the punishment of Allah is severe.\""],[15186,"Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no marriage except with a guardian and two just witnesses.\""],[15187,"Concerning a man who divorced his wife without calling witnesses and took her back without calling witnesses, he said: \"If he divorced outside the waiting period and took her back not according to the Sunnah, let him call witnesses now.\""],[15188,"That a man emancipated six slaves on his deathbed while he had no property other than them, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cast lots among them, freed two, and kept four enslaved."],[15189,"That a man emancipated six slaves, and the Prophet ﷺ was informed of it, so he cast lots among them, freed two, and kept four enslaved."],[15190,"That a man emancipated slaves on his deathbed while he had no property other than them, so the matter was referred to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he cast lots among them, freed two of them, and returned the rest to slavery."],[15191,"That a man from the Ansar emancipated six slaves on his deathbed while he had no property other than them, and that reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he summoned them and cast lots among them, and two were freed while four were returned to slavery."],[15192,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and he had drawn close to his companions when he raised his voice with these two verses: 'O mankind, fear your Lord. Indeed, the quaking of the Hour is a tremendous thing. On the Day you see it, every nursing mother will be distracted from what she nurses, and every pregnant woman will deliver her burden, and you will see people appearing drunk while they are not drunk; but the punishment of Allah is severe.' When the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard that, they urged on their mounts, knowing that he was about to say something. He said: 'Do you know which day that is?' They said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'That is a day when Adam will be called, and his Lord will call him and say: O Adam, send forth the delegation of the Fire. He will say: O Lord, from how many? He said: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one to the Garden.' The people despaired until they did not even smile. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw what had befallen his companions, he said: 'Work and rejoice, for by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are with two creations that, whenever they are in anything, they increase it greatly: Gog and Magog, and those among the children of Adam who have perished.' Then some of the distress the people were feeling was relieved. Then he said: 'Work and rejoice, for by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are among mankind only like a mole on the side of a camel, or like a mark on the foreleg of a beast.'"],[15193,"When these two verses were revealed to the Prophet ﷺ while he was on a journey and his companions were getting closer to him, we restrained the camels and knew that this was an indication of something important. When we gathered around him, he said, \"Do you know what day it is?\" We replied, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"This is the day when Allah will say to Adam, 'Send forth an army to the Fire.'\" Adam will say, 'O Lord, how many?' Allah will reply, 'From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine will go to the Fire.' When his companions heard this, they became saddened and no one among them spoke clearly. When the Prophet saw what his companions were feeling, he said, 'Know and be glad! By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are two nations that no people before you have ever equalled in number: Gog and Magog. I think it is because of the offspring of Iblis that has perished, and you are like a black hair on the side of a white camel or like a speck on the foreleg of a donkey.'\""],[15194,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Three sons were born to Noah: Shem, the father of the Arabs; Ham, the father of the Abyssinians; and Japheth, the father of the Byzantines.\""],[15195,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: two pauses, a pause when he said the takbīr and a pause when he finished reciting 'not of those who incur wrath nor of those who go astray.' 'Imrān disapproved, so they wrote about that to Ubayy b. Kaʿb, and in his reply to them he wrote that Samurah had remembered correctly."],[15196,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had one pause.' Samurah said: 'Two pauses.' So they wrote to Ubayy b. Kaʿb, and he wrote: 'You have remembered correctly, O Samurah, and the people forgot.'"],[15197,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I do not ride purple saddles, nor do I wear safflower-dyed garments or silk-bordered garments.\""],[15198,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Garments hemmed with silk are not to be worn.\""],[15199,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The beauty of men lies in their scent, with no color, and the beauty of women lies in their color, with no scent.\""],[15200,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no shighār in Islam, nor janab, nor jalab.\" Shighār is when a man marries this one's sister and this one marries that one's sister with no dower. Jalab and janab were in horse racing."],[15201,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"There is no shighār in Islam, and no janab, and no jalab.\" Shighār is when a man marries off the sister of this one and this one marries off the sister of that one without any dower. Jalab and janab pertain to horse racing."],[15202,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"No jalab, no janab, and no shighār in Islam.\""],[15203,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Beware of red clothing, for it is the most beloved adornment to Satan.\""],[15204,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at a man wearing red clothes and said: \"This is the adornment of Satan.\""],[15205,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever swears a false oath in order to seize thereby the property of his brother, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[15206,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever swears an oath deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[15207,"The Prophet of God ﷺ said: \"The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support: your mother, your father, then the next nearest, and the next nearest.\""],[15208,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade cauterization. So we cauterized ourselves, and we neither prospered nor succeeded."],[15209,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from cauterization. So we cauterized ourselves, and we neither prospered nor succeeded."],[15210,"Do you know why I have come to you? Do you not remember that when the Messenger of God ﷺ learned what his commander had said to a man — \"Stand and throw yourself into the fire\" — the man stood up to throw himself in, but he was caught and restrained. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Had he thrown himself into it, both of them would have entered the Fire. There is no obedience in disobedience to God.\" He said: [another chain], meaning he said: I only wanted [to narrate] this hadith."],[15211,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us and forbade us from mutilation."],[15212,"\"My slave has run away, and I have vowed that if God returns him, I will cut off his hand.\" He said: \"Do not cut off his hand, for the Messenger of God ﷺ used to command charity and forbid mutilation.\""],[15213,"Indeed, my servant has remained (steadfast) and indeed I swore that if I find him, I will cut off his hand, but he said, \"Do not cut off his hand. For indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to stand among us and prohibit us from amputation and command us to give charity.\""],[15214,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey when Surah al-Hajj was revealed. He raised his voice reciting it while the people were dozing and their mounts had dispersed: “O mankind, fear your Lord. Indeed, the quaking of the Hour is a tremendous thing” up to “but the punishment of Allah is severe.” So they gathered around the Prophet ﷺ, thinking that the Hour had come. He said, “Do you know which day that is?” They said, “Which day is it?” He said, “It is the day on which Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, says: ‘O Adam, send forth the delegation of the Fire.’ He says, ‘What is the delegation of the Fire?’ He says, ‘From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise.’” The people were struck silent, until none of them showed even a tooth. He then said, “Work and rejoice, for there was no prophethood except that a period of ignorance preceded it, so the count is completed from the people of that ignorance; and whatever remains is completed from the hypocrites.” And he said, “Work and rejoice, for you are among mankind but like a black mark on a camel’s flank, or like a spot on a beast’s foreleg. And you are alongside two creations that never enter anything without multiplying it: Yaʾjuj and Maʾjuj, along with those of Adam’s children who perished, and Iblis.”"],[15215,"About a man who divorced his wife without making witnesses and took her back without making witnesses, he said: “He divorced outside the prescribed period and took her back contrary to the Sunnah, so let him make witnesses from now on.”"],[15216,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade cauterization, but I cauterized myself and it neither succeeded nor prospered.”"],[15217,"“The Prophet ﷺ forbade cauterization.”"],[15218,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a march, and they overslept and missed the Fajr prayer, waking up with the heat of the sun. They moved a little until the sun had risen high, then he ordered a muʾadhdhin who gave the call to prayer, and he prayed two rakʿahs before Fajr, then the iqamah was given and he prayed Fajr.”"],[15219,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ with his brother, whose stomach had been afflicted with dropsy. He said, “O Messenger of God, my brother’s belly has become swollen, and I took him to the physicians and they instructed me to cauterize him. Should I cauterize him?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “Do not cauterize him,” and he sent him back to his family. Then a camel passed by him and struck his belly, and his belly shrank. He brought him to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Had you taken him to the physicians, they would have said: The fire cured him.”"],[15220,"A man had six slaves and freed them at his death, having no other property. The matter was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he disliked it and divided them into three shares, casting lots among them; he freed two and kept four in slavery."],[15221,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled concerning a man who freed six slaves at his death, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided them and freed one third.”"],[15222,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever goes on a military expedition at sea in the path of Allah—and Allah knows best who is truly in His path—has fulfilled all his obedience to Allah, sought Paradise in every way, and fled from the Fire in every way.”"],[15223,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever supports his brother in his absence, Allah will support him in this world and the Hereafter.”"],[15224,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mutilation. Among mutilation is that a man pierces his nose [to wear a ring], and among mutilation is that a man vows to perform Hajj on foot. If he does that, let him offer a sacrificial animal and ride."],[15225,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ask him for mounts, along with a group from my people. He said, “By Allah, I will not give you mounts; by Allah, I have nothing to mount you on,” twice. Then the Prophet ﷺ received three loads from the white-topped camels, so he sent for us and mounted us. When we had gone on with it, I said to my companions, “I do not think we will be blessed in this, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ swore that he would not mount us, then he mounted us.” So we returned to him and told him about his oath. He said, “I did not forget my oath, but when I swear an oath and then see something better than it, I do what is better and expiate for my oath.”"],[15226,"He entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while there was a ring of brass on his upper arm. He said, “What is this?” He replied, “For the pain in my shoulder vein.” He said, “Would it please you to be left to it? Throw it away from you.”"],[15227,"The Prophet ﷺ used to command charity in his sermon and forbid mutilation."],[15228,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mutilation."],[15229,"A man freed six of his slaves at the time of his death, and he had no property other than them. The Prophet ﷺ drew lots among them and freed two and re-enslaved four."],[15230,"The Prophet ﷺ gathered the Banū Hāshim one day and said to them, \"O Banū Hāshim, I cannot avail you in any way against Allah. O Banū Hāshim, my allies among you are the God-fearing. O Banū Hāshim, guard against the Fire, even with half a date. O Banū Hāshim, let me not find you coming with this world, carrying it on your backs, and bringing the Hereafter, carrying it.\""],[15231,"He saw a man with a brass ring on his upper arm, so he said to him, \"What is this?\" He said, \"It was prescribed for me for the wāhina.\" He said, \"Indeed, if you die while it is on you, you will be left to it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He is not one of us who practices augury or has it done for him, or who practices divination or has it done for him.\" I think he said, \"Or who practices magic or has it done for him.\""],[15232,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The request of a wealthy person is a blemish on his face; if it is little, then little, and if it is much, then much.\""],[15233,"A man freed six of his slaves at his death, so the Prophet ﷺ drew lots among them, freed two, and returned four to slavery."],[15234,"A man freed six of his slaves at his death, so the Prophet ﷺ drew lots among them, freed two, and returned four to slavery."],[15235,"A man freed six of his slaves at his death, so the Prophet ﷺ drew lots among them, freed two, and returned four to slavery."],[15236,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The request of a wealthy person is a blemish on his face.\""],[15237,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no vow in disobedience or in anger, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.\""],[15238,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no vow in disobedience or in anger, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.\""],[15239,"A man freed six slaves he owned at his death. The Prophet ﷺ cast lots among them, freed two, and kept four in bondage."],[15240,"The Prophet of God ﷺ said: \"There is no shighar in Islam.\""],[15241,"Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"There is no obedience to a creature in disobedience to God\"? He said: Yes."],[15242,"From our Prophet ﷺ, when a man said to him: O Abu Nujayd, tell us about the Qur’an. Imran said to him: \"Do you and your companions recite the Qur’an? Would you tell me how much zakah is due on gold, camels, cattle, and types of wealth, even if you witnessed and you were absent?\" Then he said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ prescribed in zakah such and such.\" The man said: O Abu Nujayd, you have revived me, may God revive you. Then al-Hasan said: \"That man did not die until he became one of the jurists of the Muslims.\""],[15243,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever recites the Qur’an, let him ask God by it, for after you there will come a people who recite the Qur’an and ask people by it.\""],[15244,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever recites the Qur’an, let him ask God by it, for there will come peoples who recite the Qur’an and ask people by it.\""],[15245,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Recite the Qur’an and ask God by it before a people come who ask people by it.\""],[15246,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Acquire many sandals, for one of you remains a rider as long as he is wearing sandals.\""],[15247,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade accepting the food of the wicked."],[15248,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A man’s standing in the ranks in the way of God is better than the worship of sixty years.\""],[15249,"We traveled by night with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then the Prophet ﷺ made camp with us at the end of the night. He woke after the sun had risen, and one of our men began to rush to his purification in alarm. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Mount up.\" So we mounted and traveled until the sun had risen high, then we dismounted, took care of our needs, and performed ablution. Then he ordered Bilal to give the call to prayer, and we prayed two rakʿahs. Then Bilal gave the iqamah, and the Prophet ﷺ led us in prayer. We said, \"O Messenger of God, shall we make it up at its proper time tomorrow?\" He said, \"Your Lord forbids you from riba yet accepts it from you?\""],[15250,"The Messenger of God ﷺ died while he disliked three tribes: Banu Umayyah, Banu Hanifah, and Thaqif."],[15251,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Seventy thousand of my Ummah (followers) will enter Paradise without being held accountable. They do not seek Ruqyah (protection through recitation), nor do they believe in the influence of evil omens, and they put their trust in their Lord.\" Upon hearing this, 'Ukkasha bin Mihsan stood up and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah to make me one of them.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Allah, make him one of them.\" Then, another man stood up and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah to make me one of them.\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Ukkasha has preceded you in that.\""],[15252,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"There is no obedience to a creature in disobedience to the Creator.\""],[15253,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"There is no jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam. Whoever plunders spoils is not one of us.\""],[15254,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"There is no jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam. Whoever plunders spoils is not one of us.\""],[15255,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"There is no shighar in Islam.\""],[15256,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"There is no obedience in disobedience to God.\""],[15257,"The Messenger of God ﷺ never gave us a sermon without commanding us to give charity and forbidding mutilation."],[15258,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Modesty is all good.\""],[15259,"The Messenger of God ﷺ never gave us a sermon without commanding us to give charity and forbidding us from mutilation."],[15260,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"There is no jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam.\""],[15261,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a ring on a man's upper arm and said, “What is this?” He said, “For the wahinah (a pain in the shoulder).” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “It will only increase you in weakness. Cast it away from you, for if you die while it is upon you, you will be left to it.”"],[15262,"“Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from cauterization, so we cauterized, and we neither succeeded nor prospered.”"],[15263,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The station of a man in a rank in the path of Allah is better than the world and all that is in it. And whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah and it reaches its target, whether it misses or hits, it is like the freeing of a slave. And whoever grows a grey hair in the path of Allah, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[15264,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to my father, “How many gods do you worship today?” He said, “Seven: six in the earth and one in the heaven.” He said, “So which of them do you count for your desire and your fear?” He said, “The one in the heaven.” He said, “O Aba Husayn, indeed if you were to embrace Islam, I would teach you two words that would benefit you.” So when Husayn embraced Islam, he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, teach me the two words you promised me.” He said, “Say: O Allah, inspire me with my right guidance, and protect me from the evil of my own soul.”"],[15265,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Is not one of you able to do every day the equivalent of Uhud in deeds?” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, who is able to do every day the equivalent of Uhud in deeds?” He said, “All of you are able to do it.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is it?” He said, “Subhan Allah is greater than Uhud, and La ilaha illa Allah is greater than Uhud, and Alhamdu lillah is greater than Uhud, and Allahu akbar is greater than Uhud.”"],[15266,"About the prayer: we woke up and said, “O Messenger of Allah, should we not pray such-and-such a prayer?” He said, “Does our Lord forbid us from usury yet accept it from us? Indeed, negligence is only in wakefulness.”"],[15267,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “The asking of the rich is a disgrace on his face on the Day of Resurrection, and the asking of the rich is fire; if he is given little, then it is little, and if he is given much, then it is much.”"],[15268,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There is no jalab (bringing livestock to market), no janab (withholding livestock from market), and no shighar (a type of marriage exchange) in Islam.”"],[15269,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never addressed us except that he commanded us to give charity and forbade us from mutilation.”"],[15270,"A man owned six slaves and freed them at his death. The Prophet ﷺ drew lots among them and freed two and returned four to slavery."],[15271,"A man freed six slaves. His heirs came and found nothing, so they went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him. He said, 'If I had known that, if Allah wills, I would not have prayed over him.' He drew lots among them and freed two and re-enslaved four."],[15272,"A man freed six slaves of his at his death. His heirs from the Bedouins came and told the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he had done. He said, 'And why did he do that?' He drew lots among them, and two were freed and four were returned to slavery."],[15273,"A man freed six of his slave boys at his death. The Prophet ﷺ was brought concerning them. He cast lots among them, and two of them won. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed the two who won and re-enslaved four."],[15274,"A man freed six of his slaves at his death, having no property other than them. The Prophet ﷺ drew lots among them and freed two and re-enslaved four."],[15275,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Modesty is from faith, and faith is in Paradise. Obscenity is from harshness, and harshness is in the Fire.'"],[15276,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us, commanding us to give charity and forbidding us from mutilation."],[15277,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed Allah ﷻ punishes the deceased because of the wailing of his family over him.' A man said, 'He dies in Khurasan and wailing is made over him here, and he is punished?' Imran said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke the truth and you have lied.'"],[15278,"A man from the Ansar freed six of his slaves at his death, having no property other than them. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he became angry about it and said, 'I have thought about not praying over him.' Then he called his slaves, divided them into three portions, drew lots among them, and freed two and re-enslaved four."],[15279,"A Muslim woman was taken captive by the enemy. They had earlier captured a she-camel belonging to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She saw negligence among the people and mounted the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ she-camel. She vowed to slaughter the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ she-camel. He said, 'How badly you have rewarded her. There is no vow for the son of Adam concerning what he does not own, nor in disobedience to Allah.'"],[15280,"He saw on a man's hand a ring of brass. He said, 'What is this?' He said, 'For the weakening pain.' He said, 'Indeed, it does not increase you except in weakness. If you were to die while thinking that it benefits you, you would die upon other than the natural disposition.'"],[15281,"I heard Abu al-Qasim ﷺ say: “When Allah, the Exalted, bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves to see its trace on him.”"],[15282,"A man divorced without making witnesses, and took back without making witnesses? He said: “Evil is what he did. He divorced in an innovation, and took back contrary to the Sunnah. Let him make witnesses to what he did.”"],[15283,"About a man who divorced without witnesses and took back without witnesses, he said: “He divorced outside the waiting period and took back contrary to the Sunnah. Let him make witnesses to his divorce and to his taking back, and seek Allah’s forgiveness.”"],[15284,"A man divorced without making witnesses, and took back without making witnesses? He said: “Evil is what he did. He divorced in an innovation, and took back contrary to the Sunnah. Let him make witnesses to what he did.”"],[15285,"About a man who divorced without witnesses and took back without witnesses? He said: “He divorced contrary to the Sunnah and took back outside the waiting period. Let him make witnesses now.”"],[15286,"He is the one who says: “Seventy thousand will enter Paradise without reckoning. They do not practice augury, nor seek cauterization, and upon their Lord they rely.”"],[15287,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Seventy thousand from my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment.” It was said: “Who are they?” He said: “Those who do not seek cauterization, nor seek ruqya, nor practice augury, and upon their Lord they rely.”"],[15288,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Seventy thousand from my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning. They do not seek cauterization, nor seek ruqya, nor practice augury, and upon their Lord they rely.” Imran said: “We sought cauterization, and we neither prospered nor succeeded.”"],[15289,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Seventy thousand from my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment.” It was said: “Who are they?” He said: “They are those who do not seek cauterization, nor seek ruqya, nor practice augury, and upon their Lord they rely.”"],[15290,"A man had six slaves and freed them upon his death. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cast lots among them, and freed two and returned four to slavery."],[15291,"A man freed six slaves during his illness. The Prophet ﷺ drew lots among them, freed two, and kept four in bondage."],[15292,"A man from the Ansar died leaving six slaves with no other property. He freed all of them at his death. The matter was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, who divided them into three portions, then drew lots among them. He freed one third and kept two thirds in bondage. Muhammad b. Sirin said: 'Had this not reached me from the Prophet ﷺ, it would have been my own opinion.'"],[15293,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah.' The other said: 'Allahu akbar' three times, or as he said."],[15294,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah.'"],[15295,"I have been seeking you since today. You have been sent with a great matter. Do you remember the day when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah'? He said: 'Yes.' Imran said: 'Allahu akbar. I thought you had forgotten.'"],[15296,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no obedience to anyone in disobedience to Allah.' He said: 'Allahu akbar.'"],[15297,"And he said: 'We did it with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[15298,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no obedience to a creature in disobedience to Allah.'"],[15299,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah.'"],[15300,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Imran, say: O Allah, I seek guidance from You for the most upright of my affairs, and I seek Your protection from the evil of my self.'"],[15301,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:"],[15302,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah loves the believer who is poor and abstinent.'"],[15303,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[15304,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Your brother the Negus has died, so pray over him.\""],[15305,"The Prophet ﷺ said: A man fought another man and bit his hand, so he pulled it away and his front tooth fell out. He brought the dispute to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Would he leave his hand in your mouth for you to bite it as a stallion bites?\" So the Prophet ﷺ declared it void."],[15306,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to us: \"Whoever swears a binding oath to wrongfully take the property of a Muslim man, lying in it, let him take his place in the Fire with his face.\""],[15307,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Your brother the Negus has died, so stand and pray over him.\" So we lined up as we line up for the dead, and we prayed over him as we pray over the dead."],[15308,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"She is cursed, so leave her alone.\" He said: \"I saw her follow the camps; no one approached her—a dark gray camel.\""],[15309,"While I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, he heard a curse and said: \"What is this?\" They said: \"A woman cursed a camel of hers.\" He said: \"Take the load off her, for she is cursed.\" So they unloaded her, and there was a dark gray camel."],[15310,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was on a journey when a woman cursed a camel of hers. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Throw off her load.\" It is as if I see her: a dark gray camel."],[15311,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was on one of his journeys, a woman of the Ansar was on a camel and became irritated, so she cursed it. The Messenger of God ﷺ heard that and said: \"Take what is on her and leave her, for she is cursed.\" Imran said: \"It is as if I see her wandering in the market; no one approaches her.\" And sometimes he said: \"the market of Madinah.\""],[15312,"Banu Amir had captured two men from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ captured a man from Thaqif and took his camel, on which he used to outrun the pilgrims. The Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he was bound, and he said: \"O Muhammad, O Muhammad.\" So he turned to him, and he said: \"Why am I detained and the leading pilgrim camel taken?\" He said: \"Because of the crime of your allies.\" Banu Amir were allies of Thaqif. Then the Prophet ﷺ moved on, and he called him again: \"O Muhammad.\" He answered him: \"I am a Muslim.\" He said: \"If you had said that while you were in control of your affair, you would have succeeded utterly.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ moved on, and he called him again, so he returned to him, and he said: \"Feed me, for I am hungry.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"This is your need.\" So he ordered food for him. Then the Prophet ﷺ ransomed the man for the two men who had been captured from his Companions. Some polytheists raided the outskirts of Madinah and took that camel, and among what they took they also took a woman. They took her to their camps. The woman got up during part of the night among their camels—they used to make them kneel at their courtyards—and whenever she approached a camel to ride it, it bellowed, so she left it, until she came to the camel of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and it was a docile camel; it did not bellow until she sat on its hindquarters, then she shouted at it and startled the people, so they rode in pursuit of her. While she was going and they were on her trail, she vowed that if God saved her on it, she would slaughter it. So she escaped. When she arrived in Madinah, the Prophet ﷺ was told: \"This is your camel; so-and-so came on it; God saved her on it from the polytheists.\" The Prophet ﷺ was brought the woman and the camel, and he asked her: \"What did you do?\" She told him and said: \"I vowed while they were pursuing me on it that I would slaughter it.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"What a bad reward you gave it. Indeed, there is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience, nor in what the son of Adam does not own.\""],[15313,"The polytheists raided the grazing camels of Madinah and drove them off. Al-ʿAdbaʾ was among what they took, and they captured a woman from the Muslims. When night came, they would let their camels rest in their courtyards. In the middle of the night, the woman got up one night after they had fallen asleep, and she began to place her hand on no camel except that it brayed, until she came to al-ʿAdbaʾ. She came upon a docile, guarded she-camel and mounted it, and she vowed: ‘If Allah ﷻ saves her by means of it, I will certainly slaughter it.’ When she arrived, the she-camel was recognized, and it was said, ‘The she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.’ The Prophet ﷺ was brought the she-camel, and he was told of her vow, so he said: ‘What an evil reward you would have given it! If Allah saves her by means of it, you will certainly slaughter it. There is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience, nor in what a son of Adam does not own.’”"],[15314,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ransomed two Muslim men with a man from the polytheists of Banu ʿUqayl whom Thaqif had captured. Banu ʿUqayl had been allies of Thaqif in the pre-Islamic era, and Thaqif had captured two Muslim men, so the Muslims captured a man from Banu ʿUqayl. They also took a she-camel of his that had outstripped the pilgrims' mounts in the pre-Islamic era. In the pre-Islamic era, when a she-camel won a race, it was not prevented from any watering place it wished to drink from, nor from any pasture it wished to graze in. The man sat in a place and the Prophet ﷺ passed by him, and he said: ‘O Muhammad, why am I being detained, along with the winner of the pilgrims' race?’ He replied: ‘We detained you because of the crime of your allies, Thaqif.’ And he mentioned the hadith."],[15315,"A man freed six slaves at the time of his death, having no property other than them. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he spoke harshly to the man. Then he called them, divided them into three portions, cast lots among them, freed two, and kept four enslaved."],[15316,"A man from the Ansar died leaving six slaves, with no property other than them, and he freed them all at his death. That was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, so he divided them into three portions, then cast lots among them, and freed one-third and kept two-thirds enslaved."],[15317,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Your brother has died, so stand and pray over him.’"],[15318,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: ‘Your brother has died, so stand and pray over him’—meaning the Najashi."],[15319,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Your brother has died, so stand and pray over him.’ So we stood and prayed over him."],[15320,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: ‘When a man says to his brother, “O disbeliever,” it is like killing him, and cursing a believer is like killing him.’"],[15321,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ concluded the prayer with salam after three rakʿahs of ʿAsr, then entered his room. A man called al-Khirbaq, who had long arms, stood up to him and said: ‘Did you shorten the prayer, O Messenger of Allah?’ He came out angry, dragging his cloak, and said: ‘Is he telling the truth?’ They said: ‘Yes.’ So he stood and prayed that rakʿah."],[15322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr or ʿAsr as three rakʿahs. A man called al-Khirbaq said to him: ‘O Messenger of Allah, you prayed only three rakʿahs.’ He said: ‘Is it so?’ They said: ‘Yes.’ So he prayed one rakʿah, then recited the tashahhud and said salam, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness."],[15323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a mistake in prayer and prostrated two prostrations in which he said salam."],[15324,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said salam after three rakʿahs of ʿAsr, then stood and entered the room. Al-Khirbaq, a man with long arms, stood and said: ‘Did you shorten the prayer, O Messenger of Allah, or did you forget?’ He came out angry, dragging his garment, asked about it, and was informed. Then he prayed the rakʿah he had omitted, then said salam, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then said salam."],[15325,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the salam during the two prostrations of forgetfulness."],[15326,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in prayer and forgot something in his prayer, so he prostrated twice for forgetfulness, then recited the tashahhud, then said the salam."],[15327,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed ʿAsr with three rakʿahs, then entered [his house]. A man called al-Khirbāq stood up and said, “O Messenger of Allah,” mentioning to him what he had done. He came out angry, dragging his cloak, until he reached the people and said, “Is this man telling the truth?” They said, “Yes.” So he prayed that rakʿah, then said the salam, then prostrated twice, then said the salam."],[15328,"That the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was lost, and there was a woman who wanted to slaughter it. They told the Prophet ﷺ, and she said, “I had vowed to slaughter it.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “No one is bound by a vow concerning what he does not own.”"],[15329,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Your brother the Negus has died, so pray over him.” He stood and we prayed behind him, and I was in the second row, and he prayed over him."],[15330,"That a woman from Juhaynah confessed adultery before the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I am pregnant.” The Prophet ﷺ called her guardian and said, “Treat her well, and when she gives birth inform me.” He did so, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered that her clothes be fastened around her, then ordered that she be stoned, and she was stoned. Then he prayed over her. ʿUmar said, “O Messenger of Allah, you stone her and then pray over her?” He said, “She has repented with such a repentance that if it were divided among seventy of the people of Madinah it would suffice them. Have you found anything better than her offering her own self to Allah, Mighty and Exalted?”"],[15331,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a prescribed punishment, so carry it out on me.” The Prophet ﷺ said to her guardian, “Take good care of her, and when she delivers what is in her womb bring her to me.” When she delivered, he brought her to the Prophet ﷺ. Her clothes were fastened around her, and he ordered that she be stoned, and she was stoned. Then he prayed over her. ʿUmar said, “O Messenger of Allah, you stoned her and then prayed over her?” He said, “She has repented with such a repentance that if it were divided among seventy of the people of Madinah it would suffice them. Have you found anything better than her offering her own self to Allah, Mighty and Exalted?”"],[15332,"That a woman from Juhaynah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while she was pregnant from adultery and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have committed a sin, so carry out [the punishment] on me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called her guardian and said, “Treat her well, and when she delivers what is in her womb bring her to me.” He did so, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that her clothes be fastened around her, then ordered that she be stoned, and she was stoned. Then he prayed over her. ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb said, “You pray over her when she has committed adultery?” He said, “She has repented with such a repentance that if it were divided among ninety of the people of Madinah it would suffice them. Have you found anything better than her offering her own self to Allah, Mighty and Exalted?”"],[15333,"That a woman from Juhaynah committed adultery, and she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after she had become pregnant from the adultery and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a prescribed punishment, so carry it out on me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called her guardian and said, “Treat her well, and when she delivers what is in her womb bring her to me.” He did so, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that her clothes be held fast around her, then ordered that she be stoned, and she was stoned. Then he prayed over her. ʿUmar said to him, “You pray over her when she has committed adultery?” He said, “She has repented with such a repentance that if it were divided among seventy of the people of Madinah it would suffice them. Have you found anything better than her offering her own self to Allah, Mighty and Exalted?”"],[15334,"That a woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I have incurred a prescribed punishment, so carry it out on me,” and she was pregnant. He ordered her guardian to treat her well until she gave birth. When she gave birth, he ordered that her clothes be fastened around her, then he stoned her and prayed over her. ʿUmar said, “O Prophet of Allah, do you pray over her when she has committed adultery?” He said, “By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad, she has repented with such a repentance that if it were divided among seventy of the people of Madinah it would suffice them. Have you found anything better than her offering her own self to Allah, Mighty and Exalted?”"],[15335,"That he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he heard a woman curse a she-camel. He said, “Take your belongings [off it], for it has become binding on her.” ʿImrān said, “It is as if I am looking at it, a dark ash-colored she-camel.”"],[15336,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, a woman was on a she-camel and it brayed, so she cursed it. He said, “Take your belongings off it, for it has become due upon it.”"],[15337,"A woman was on a she-camel and it brayed, so she cursed it. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Remove its load from it, for it is cursed.”"],[15338,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There is no vow in anger, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.”"],[15339,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is an oath.”"],[15340,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.”"],[15341,"That he should not attend the prayer in the mosque of his people. ʿImran said to him, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.’”"],[15342,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is an oath.”"],[15343,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade hantam jars, wearing silk, and wearing gold rings."],[15344,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Modesty is all good.” Bushayr b. Kaʿb said, “Some of it is weakness.” ʿImran said, “Hujayr, who is this?” I said, “This is a man from among us; there is nothing wrong with him.” He said, “He hears me narrating from the Messenger of God ﷺ and says, ‘Some of it is weakness, and some of it is dignity for God.’ By God, I will not narrate a single hadith to you today.”"],[15345,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Seventy thousand of my community will enter Paradise without reckoning—those who do not cauterize, do not seek ruqya, do not practice divination by birds, and upon their Lord they rely.” Then affliction kept befalling us until we cauterized, and we neither succeeded nor prospered."],[15346,"Imran b. Husayn: “I have not touched my private part with my right hand since I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[15347,"A group from Banu Tamim came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said, “Accept the good news, O Banu Tamim.” They said, “You have given us good news, so give us [something].” That was visible on his face. Then a group from the people of Yemen came and he said, “Accept the good news, since Banu Tamim did not accept it.” They said, “We accept, O Messenger of God.”"],[15348,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God, Exalted is He, was, and there was nothing other than Him. His Throne was upon the water, and He wrote in the Reminder everything that is to be. Then He created the heavens.” A speaker said, “Catch up with your she-camel,” so I got up, and there was the mirage cutting off before it. Would that it had gone and I had fully grasped the hadith of the Prophet ﷺ."],[15349,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ on a she-camel; I hobbled it at the door, then entered. Some people from Banu Tamim came to him and he said, “Accept the good news.” They said, “We have accepted, so give us.” He turned away from them. Then some people from Yemen came to him and he said, “Accept the good news, and do not say as Banu Tamim said.” They said, “We accept; so tell us about the beginning of this matter.” He said, “God was, and there was nothing other than Him. His Throne was upon the water.” Then a man came and said, “O Ibn Husayn, catch up with your she-camel.” So I went and caught up with it at the mirage. By God, I wish I had left it."],[15350,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and hobbled my she-camel at the door, then entered. Some people from Banu Tamim came to him and he said, “Accept the good news, O Banu Tamim.” They said, “You have given us good news, so give us.” Then a group from the people of Yemen came to him and he said, “Accept the good news, O people of Yemen, since Banu Tamim did not accept it.” They said, “We will seek understanding in the religion and ask you about the beginning of this matter: how was it?” He said, “God, Exalted is He, was, and there was nothing other than Him. His Throne was upon the water, and He wrote in the Reminder everything. Then He created the heavens and the earth.” Then a man came to me and said, “Catch up with your she-camel, for it has gone.” So I went out and found that the mirage was cutting off before it. By God, I wish I had left it."],[15351,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Modesty is all good.”"],[15352,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Modesty is all good.”"],[15353,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Modesty is all good.”"],[15354,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Modesty is all good.” Then Bushayr b. Kaʿb said, “Part of it is weakness and part of it is dignity for God.” Imran said to Bashir, “You hear me narrating from the Messenger of God ﷺ and you say, ‘Part of it is weakness and part of it is dignity’?” And he became angry and said, “I will not narrate any hadith to you today.”"],[15355,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Modesty brings only good.”"],[15356,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Modesty brings only good.”"],[15357,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ was more modest than a virgin in her private quarters, and when he disliked something it was recognized on his face.”"],[15358,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was more bashful than a virgin in her seclusion; and when he disliked something, it was known from his face."],[15359,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade cauterization, but we cauterized ourselves, and it had neither healing from illness nor acquittal from sin."],[15360,"A slave belonging to poor people cut off the ear of a slave belonging to wealthy people, so his family came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, we are poor.\" He did not impose anything upon them."],[15361,"The Messenger of God ﷺ never traveled except that he prayed two rak'ahs until he returned. He stayed in Makkah for twelve days praying two rak'ahs, then he would say: \"O people of Makkah, stand and pray two rak'ahs, for we are travelers.\" He raided al-Ta'if and Hunayn and prayed two rak'ahs. Then he came to al-Ji'irranah and performed 'umrah from there."],[15362,"About the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ during military expeditions, Hajj, and 'Umrah. He came and stood among us and said: \"This man asked me about a matter, and I wanted you to hear it. I raided with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he did not pray except two rak'ahs until he returned to Madinah. I witnessed the conquest with him; he stayed in Makkah for eighteen nights not praying except two rak'ahs. I performed Hajj with Abu Bakr and raided, and he did not pray except two rak'ahs until he returned to Madinah. I performed Hajj with 'Uthman for seven years of his rule, and he did not pray except two rak'ahs, then he prayed four at Mina.\""],[15363,"I raided with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he did not pray except two rak'ahs until he returned to Madinah. I performed Hajj with him, and he did not pray except two rak'ahs until he returned. He stayed in Makkah for eighteen nights praying two rak'ahs and saying: \"Complete the prayer, O people of Makkah, for we are travelers.\""],[15364,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"It is enough evil for a man that he be pointed at with fingers.\""],[15365,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr with his companions, and when he finished his prayer, he said: \"Which of you recited 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High'?\" Some of the people said: \"I did, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"I knew that one of you contended with me for it.\""],[15366,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr with his companions, and he said: \"Which of you recited 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High'?\" A man said: \"I did.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I knew that a man contended with me for it.\""],[15367,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in one of the two evening prayers, either Zuhr or Asr, and said, “Which of you recited ‘Exalt the name of your Lord, the Most High’?” A man said, “I did.” He said, “I knew that a man was contending with me over it.”"],[15368,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr, and when he said the salam, he said, “Which of you recited ‘Exalt the name of your Lord, the Most High’?” A man said, “I did, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “I knew that some of you were contending with me over it.”"],[15369,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr, and when he turned away, he said, “Which of you contended with me over the surah?” A man said, “I did, O Messenger of Allah, and I intended only good.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I thought that a man was contending with me over it.”"],[15370,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the Zuhr prayer, and when he said the salam, he said, “Which of you recited ‘Exalt the name of your Lord, the Most High’?” A man from the people said, “I did,” so he said, “I thought that some of you were contending with me over it.”"],[15371,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them.”"],[15372,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The best of my ummah is the generation in which I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them – and Allah knows best whether he mentioned the third or not – then there will arise a people who testify without being asked to testify, make vows but do not fulfill them, betray trusts and are not trusted, and obesity will spread among them.”"],[15373,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The best of this ummah is the generation in which I was sent, then those who follow them” – three times, and Allah knows best whether he mentioned the third or not – “then there will arise a people who testify without being asked to testify, make vows but do not fulfill them, betray trusts and are not trusted, and obesity will spread among them.”"],[15374,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “The best of this ummah is the generation in which I was sent, then those who follow them, then there will arise peoples who make vows but do not fulfill them, swear oaths without being asked to swear, and obesity will spread among them.”"],[15375,"A man bit the hand of another man, and he pulled out his front tooth. They brought their dispute to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “One of you bites his brother as a stallion bites? There is no blood money for you.”"],[15376,"A man bit the hand of another man, and the one bitten pulled out the biter’s front tooth. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned it to him, so he declared it void."],[15377,"A man bit another on the forearm, and he pulled it away and pulled out his front tooth. He raised the matter to the Prophet ﷺ, and he declared it void and said, “You wanted to bite your brother’s flesh as a stallion bites.”"],[15378,"A man bit the hand of another man, and he withdrew his hand from his mouth, and his front tooth fell out. The Prophet ﷺ declared it void, or he said, “The Prophet ﷺ nullified it.”"],[15379,"A man bit the hand of another man, so the latter pulled his hand away, and the biter’s front teeth fell out. He came to the Prophet ﷺ, who ruled it void. Then he said, “Would one of you eat the flesh of his brother like a stallion eats—or rather, like a stallion bites?”"],[15380,"A man bit the forearm of another man, and his front tooth was pulled out. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ declared it void."],[15381,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform the voluntary prayer of Witr by reciting \"Subhan Rabbi al-A'la\", which means \"Glory be to your Lord, the Most High.\""],[15382,"\"From the Prophet ﷺ that he used to recite in Witr prayer: 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' and 'Say: O disbelievers' and 'Say: He is Allah, [who is] One'.\""],[15383,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “My community is excused for what their minds whisper, so long as they do not speak it or act upon it.”"],[15384,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Allah, bless my community in its early morning.” Whenever he intended to dispatch a raiding party, he would send it at dawn."],[15385,"A slave belonging to his father ran away, so he made a vow that if he caught him, he would cut off one of his fingers. When he did catch him, he sent me to ʿImran b. al-Husayn, so I asked him. ʿImran said, “Tell your father to free his slave or expiate for his oath, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to urge us to give charity and forbid us from mutilation.” Then I came to Samurah and asked him, and he said the same as ʿImran. This is how Maʿmar, Hammam, and Qatadah narrated it from al-Hasan from Hayyaj. Saʿid b. Abi ʿArubah and Hammam b. Yahya disagreed with him."],[15386,"Regarding a slave of his who ran away—he had sworn, ‘If I catch him, I will cut off a part of him or his hand’—he did catch him, so Hayyaj went to ʿImran and asked him about that, informing him of his father’s statement. ʿImran said, “Tell your father to expiate for his oath or free his slave, and not cut off any part of him, for the Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to urge charity in his sermon and forbid mutilation.” Then he mentioned that he came to Samurah b. Jundub, and he said the same as ʿImran."],[15387,"A slave of his father ran away, so he made a vow to Allah ﷻ that if he caught him, he would cut off his hand. When he came to him—meaning to ʿImran b. Husayn—he said, “Tell your father not to do it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urging charity in his sermon and forbidding mutilation. Tell your father to expiate for his oath and overlook his slave.”"],[15388,"A man divorced his wife without witnesses and took her back without witnesses. He said, “He divorced outside the waiting period and took her back contrary to the Sunnah. Let him call witnesses to his divorce and to his taking her back.”"],[15389,"A man said to him, “I divorced my wife publicly and took her back secretly.” ʿImran replied, “You divorced outside the waiting period and took her back contrary to the Sunnah. Fear Allah and call witnesses.”"],[15390,"When this mosque, the Congregational Mosque, was built—and ʿImran b. Husayn was sitting there—they mentioned intercession in his presence. A man from the group said, “O Abu Nujayd, you relate to us hadiths for which we find no basis in the Qur’an.” ʿImran b. Husayn became angry and said to a man, “Have you read the Qur’an?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Did you find in it that the sunset prayer is three rakʿahs, the night prayer four, the dawn prayer two, the noon prayer four, and the afternoon prayer four?” He said, “No.” He said, “Then from whom did you take this matter? Did you not take it from us, and we took it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Did you find in the Qur’an that for every forty dirhams one dirham is due, and for every such-and-such number of sheep one sheep, and for every such-and-such number of camels such-and-such?” He said, “No.” He said, “Then from whom did you take this? We took it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and you took it from us.” He said, “Did you find in the Qur’an: ‘and let them circumambulate the Ancient House’? Did you find that you should circumambulate seven times and pray two rakʿahs behind the Station? Did you find this in the Qur’an? From whom did you take it? Did you not take it from us, and we took it from the Prophet of Allah ﷺ? Did you find in the Qur’an: no jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam?” He said, “No.” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘No jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam.’ Did you hear Allah say to some people in His Book: ‘What brought you into Saqar? They said, We were not among those who prayed, and we did not feed the poor’ until He reached ‘so the intercession of intercessors will not benefit them’?” Habib said, “I heard him say ‘intercession.’”"],[15391,"Abu Husayn b. ʿUbayd came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Do you think a man who entertains guests, maintains kinship ties, and does such-and-such—that is your father?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Your father and my father are both in the Fire.” He did not remain after that except twenty nights until he died."],[15392,"From ʿImrān b. al-Ḥuṣayn: His father Ḥuṣayn came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “What do you think about a man who used to host guests and maintain family ties, who died before you, and he is your father?” He said, “Indeed my father, your father, and you are in the Fire.” He said, “Then Ḥuṣayn died as a polytheist.”"],[15393,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever hears of the Dajjal (the false messiah) should stay away from him. By Allah, a man will come to him thinking he is a believer, but will then follow him because of what he sees of doubts.\""],[15394,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever among you hears of the Dajjāl, let him flee from him, for a man will come to him thinking that he is a believer, then he will follow him because of the specious matters he sees.”"],[15395,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever hears of the Dajjāl, let him keep far away from him” — twice or three times — “for a man will come to him thinking that he is a believer, then he will see with him specious matters and follow him.”"],[15396,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Modesty is all goodness.\" Bishr bin Ka’b said, \"O Abu Nujayd, we find in some books that it includes tranquility and dignity, while others say it weakens it.\" Imran repeated the statement, and then Bashir repeated it again, which made Imran angry until his cheeks turned red. He said, \"I am telling you about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and you contradict me with books.\" We said, \"O Abu Nujayd, he is a man from the Ahlul-Bayt.\""],[15397,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “No servant sells inherited wealth except that Allah, Exalted is He, sets over him something that causes loss.”"],[15398,"I argued with the people of qadar until they exhausted me. Do you have any knowledge that you can narrate to me? They said, “If Allah ﷻ were to punish the people of the heavens and the earth, He would punish them without being unjust; and if He were to admit them into His mercy, His mercy would be more expansive than their sins. But as He has decreed, He punishes whom He wills and has mercy on whom He wills. So whoever is punished, that is the truth, and whoever is shown mercy, that is the truth. If you had the like of Uḥud to spend in the way of Allah, it would not be accepted from you until you believe in qadar entirely, its good and its evil.” Then ʿImrān said to Abū al-Aswad when he narrated the ḥadīth to him, “I heard that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and ʿAbdullāh and Ubayy b. Kaʿb heard it with me.” Abū al-Aswad then asked them and they narrated it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[15399,"Did you send me the money? We took it as we used to take it during the time of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ and we placed it as we used to place it."],[15400,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Wear white and shroud your dead in it.”"],[15401,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a military expedition. A man attacked a man from the polytheists, and when he overtook him with the spear, the man said, “I am a Muslim,” but he killed him. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I have sinned, so seek forgiveness for me.” He said, “What is that?” He said, “I attacked a man from the polytheists, and when I overtook him with the spear, he said, ‘I am a Muslim,’ but I thought he was seeking protection, so I killed him.” He said, “Why did you not split open his heart so that it would become clear to you?” He said, “Would it become clear to me, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “He told you with his tongue, but you did not believe him regarding what was in his heart.” He said, “Then the man died, and we buried him, but in the morning he was on the surface of the earth. We ordered our servants to guard him, but in the morning he was on the surface of the earth. We said they had been negligent, so we guarded him ourselves, but in the morning he was on the surface of the earth. We came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him. He said, “Indeed, it accepts one who is worse than him, but Allah wanted to teach you the sanctity of blood.” Then he said, “Take him to the foot of this mountain and pile stones upon him.” So we did."],[15402,"When ʿAlī prevailed over the people of Baṣra, he led them in prayer like the prayer of our Prophet ﷺ: the takbīr when he bowed, when he raised his head, and when he prostrated, and he stood up from the two rakʿahs."],[15403,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever hears of the Dajjal, let him keep far away from him.”"],[15404,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “All of modesty is good.”"],[15405,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “It is enough sin for a man that fingers be pointed at him.” It was said: O Messenger of God, even if he is good? He said: “Even if he is good, it is evil for him, except for one on whom God has mercy; and if he is evil, then it is evil.”"],[15406,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Undertake of deeds what you are able to bear, for God does not weary until you weary.”"],[15407,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, she has committed adultery. She said that several times. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Which of you will take charge of this woman?” A man from the people said: I, O Messenger of God. He said: “Go with her, and let her be given respite; when she has given birth, bring her to me.” So he brought her to the Prophet ﷺ after she had given birth, and he ordered that she be stoned. Then he said to his companions: “Come forward and pray over her.” ʿUmar said: O Messenger of God, will you pray over her? He said: “She has repented with a repentance that, if seventy of the people of Madinah were to repent with it, it would be accepted from them.”"],[15408,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no obedience in disobedience to God.”"],[15409,"Should you pray as Sukbah prays? He only says that as if he means him by it. He said: ʿImrān remained silent and we moved on. Then ʿImrān said: I was walking with the Messenger of God ﷺ when we came to Uḥud, and we climbed it. He looked over Madinah and said: “Woe to its mother, a town whose people will leave it when it is at its best. The Dajjal will come to it and will not be able to enter it; he will find at each of its gates an angel with a drawn sword.” Then we descended."],[15410,"Should you pray as Sukbah prays? He only says that as if he means him by it. He said: ʿImrān remained silent and we moved on. Then ʿImrān said: I was walking with the Messenger of God ﷺ when we came to Uḥud, and we climbed it. He looked over Madinah and said: “Woe to its mother, a town whose people will leave it when it is at its best. The Dajjal will come to it and will not be able to enter it; he will find at each of its gates an angel with a drawn sword.” Then we descended."],[15411,"The Prophet ﷺ died while he hated these three Arab tribes: Thaqīf, Banū Umayyah, and Banū Ḥanīfah."],[15412,"He witnessed Uthman b. Affan during the days of the Tabuk expedition, in the army of hardship. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded charity, strength, and mutual consolation. The Christians of the Arabs had written to Heraclius: 'This man who has come forth claiming prophethood has perished, and years of drought have afflicted them and destroyed their wealth. If you want to restore your religion, now is the time.' So he sent a man from their nobles called al-Danad, and equipped with him forty thousand. When that reached the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, he wrote among the Arabs, and he would sit every day on the minbar, supplicating Allah and saying: 'O Allah, if this band perishes, You will not be worshipped on earth.' The people had no strength. Uthman b. Affan had equipped a caravan to Syria, intending to provision it. He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, here are two hundred camels with their saddles and blankets, and two hundred uqiyyahs.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ praised Allah and the people said takbir. Then he stood in another position and commanded charity. Uthman b. Affan stood up and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, and these two hundred and two hundred uqiyyahs.' He said takbir and the people said takbir. Uthman brought the camels and brought the wealth and poured it before him. I heard him say: 'Nothing Uthman does after today will harm him.'"],[15413,"\"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the shafa'ah (intercession) and the witr (odd-numbered prayer), so he said, 'It is the prayer, some of which is shafa'ah and some of which is witr.'\""],[15414,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding the prayers of Shaf' and Witr: 'It is prayer, from which some are Shaf' (even in number) and some are Witr (odd in number).\""],[15415,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: 'The best of my Ummah is the generation in which I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will arise people who testify but are not asked to testify, who swear oaths but are not asked to swear, who betray trust and are not entrusted, and obesity will spread among them.'"],[15416,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The best of you are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them.' Imran said: 'I do not know whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned after his generation two generations or three. Then after them will come a people who testify but are not asked to testify, who betray trust and are not entrusted, who speak but do not fulfill, and obesity will appear among them.' The wording is that of Amr b. Hakkam."],[15417,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The best of my Ummah is the generation in which I am, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people who fatten and love obesity, and who give testimony without being asked for it.'"],[15418,"I was in Basra and entered the mosque. There was an old man with people gathering around him, and he was narrating to them. I heard him say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then after them will come a people who fatten and love obesity, and who give testimony before they are asked for it.' I asked: 'Who is this?' They said: 'Imran b. al-Husayn.'"],[15419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people who fatten and love obesity, and who give testimony before they are asked for it.'"],[15420,"There is no ruqyah except for the evil eye or a sting."],[15421,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no ruqyah except for the evil eye or a sting.'"],[15422,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was a wealthy man, about a man's prayer standing and sitting. He said: 'His prayer sitting is half of his prayer standing.'"],[15423,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing, and the prayer of one lying down is half of the prayer of one sitting.'"],[15424,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was a wealthy man, about the prayer of one sitting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing, and the prayer of one lying down is half of the prayer of one sitting.'"],[15425,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the prayer of a man while sitting, so he said: \"His prayer while standing is better, and his prayer while sitting is equivalent to half of his prayer while standing, and his prayer while lying down is equivalent to half of his prayer while sitting.\""],[15426,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, the most fearful thing I fear for you after me is every hypocrite with a learned tongue.”"],[15427,"Muhammad — and if I were to say that I heard it from Ribʿi, I would be truthful — from ʿImran b. Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I will surely give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love.” Then he gave it to ʿAli."],[15428,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I will give the banner to a man whom Allah and His Messenger love, and he also loves Allah and His Messenger.\" Then he gave it to Ali."],[15429,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I will surely give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love.” Then he called ʿAli ؓ and gave it to him."],[15430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Khaybar: “I will surely give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love.” Then he called ʿAli and gave it to him."],[15431,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “I will surely give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love.” Then he gave it to ʿAli."],[15432,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Fatimah, arise and witness your sacrificial animal, for with the first drop of its blood, every sin you have committed will be forgiven. And say: 'Indeed, my prayer, my rites of sacrifice, my living and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds. No partner has He. And this I have been commanded, and I am the first [among you] of the Muslims.'” ʿImran said: “O Messenger of Allah, is this for you and your household specifically — you are the people of that — or for the Muslims generally?” He said: “Rather, for the Muslims generally.”"],[15433,"From ʿImran b. Husayn and Abu Barzah, that they said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a funeral procession, and he saw a people who had thrown off their cloaks and were walking in sandals. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Is it by the practice of Jahiliyyah or by a custom that you take this? I had resolved to invoke against you an invocation that would make you return in forms other than your own.” So they took their cloaks and did not return to that."],[15434,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “There is no judge among the judges of the Muslims but that with him are two angels guiding him to the truth as long as he does not desire other than it. When he desires other than it and deviates deliberately, the two angels disown him and leave him to himself.”"],[15435,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade bringing animals from the outskirts to the market before reaching the town and buying from a mount before it reaches the market."],[15436,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade bringing animals from the outskirts to the market before reaching the town and buying from a mount before it reaches the market."],[15437,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade bringing animals from the outskirts to the market before reaching the town and buying from a mount before it reaches the market."],[15438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ loves His servant, the believer who is poor, abstaining from begging, and has dependents.\""],[15439,"\"The Prophet ﷺ died when he was sixty-three years old.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3654)"],[15440,"I heard Abu Raja' al-Utaridi say, \"The Prophet ﷺ was sent while I was a small boy, calling to Paradise.\""],[15441,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out until he entered an orchard belonging to one of the Ansar, and he was drawing water in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"What will you give me if I water your orchard?\" He said, \"I strive to water it, but I cannot do that.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Will you give me one hundred dates that I choose from your dates?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the bucket, and it was not long before he watered it, until the man said, \"My orchard has been flooded.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ chose one hundred dates from his dates, and he and his companions ate until they were full, then he returned to him one hundred dates as he had taken from him."],[15442,"I witnessed Mu'awiya give al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad a donkey. A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ called al-'Irbad b. Sariya stood up and said, \"What is it to you that you take it, and what is it to Mu'awiya that he gives it to you? It is as if I can see you on the Day of Resurrection carrying it on your neck with its head downwards.\""],[15443,"From al-'Irbad b. Sariya, who was a very old man among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he loved to be taken in death. He used to supplicate, \"O Allah, my age has grown old and my bones have become weak, so take me to You.\" He said: While I was one day in the mosque of Damascus, there was a young man, one of the most handsome of men, wearing a green cloak, and he said, \"What is this that you supplicate with?\" I said, \"How should I supplicate, O son of my brother?\" He said, \"Say: O Allah, make my deeds good and let me reach my appointed term.\" I said, \"Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you?\" He said, \"I am Riba'il, the one who removes sorrow from the hearts of the believers.\""],[15444,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us an exhortation that made the eyes shed tears and the hearts tremble. We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this is the exhortation of one bidding farewell, so advise us.\" He said, \"I advise you to fear Allah, and to hear and obey, even if a black slave is placed over you. For whoever lives after me will see much difference. So hold firmly to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs after me, and bite onto it with the molar teeth. Beware of newly invented matters, for every innovation is misguidance.\""],[15445,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ exhorted them one day after the dawn prayer, and the eyes shed tears and the hearts trembled. A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this is the exhortation of one bidding farewell, so what do you enjoin upon us?\" He said, \"I advise you to fear Allah, and to hear and obey, even if a black slave is placed over you. For whoever of you lives after me will see much difference. Beware of newly invented matters, for they are misguidance. Hold firmly to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs after me, biting onto it with the molar teeth.\""],[15446,"That he heard ʿIrbaḍ b. Sāriya al-Sulamī saying: The Messenger of God ﷺ admonished us with an exhortation that made the eyes weep and the hearts tremble. We said, “O Messenger of God, this is the admonition of one bidding farewell, so what do you enjoin upon us?” He said, “I have left you upon the clear white path; its night is like its day. None deviates from it after me but is destroyed. Whoever of you lives will see much disagreement. So hold fast to what you know of my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs. And you must obey, even if it is an Abyssinian slave. Bite onto it with the molar teeth. Indeed, the believer is like a compliant camel: wherever it is led, it follows.”"],[15447,"The Messenger of God ﷺ admonished us after the morning prayer with a profound exhortation that made the eyes weep and the hearts tremble. A man from among his Companions said, “O Messenger of God, this is the admonition of one bidding farewell.” He said: “I enjoin upon you fear of God, listening and obedience, even if it is an Abyssinian slave. Whoever of you lives will see much disagreement, so beware of newly invented matters, for they are innovation. Whoever of you reaches that, let him hold fast to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided, divinely guided caliphs; bite onto it with the molar teeth.”"],[15448,"The Messenger of God ﷺ admonished us with an exhortation that made the hearts tremble and the eyes shed tears. We said, “O Messenger of God, it is as if it is the admonition of one bidding farewell, so give us a covenant.” He said: “I enjoin upon you fear of God, listening and obedience, even if it is an Abyssinian slave. Whoever of you lives after me will see much disagreement. So hold fast to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided, divinely guided caliphs; bite onto it with the molar teeth. And beware of newly invented matters, for every newly invented matter is misguidance.”"],[15449,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite the musabbiḥāt before he slept, and he said: “In them there is a verse that is better than a thousand verses.”"],[15450,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ invited him to the pre-dawn meal in Ramadan and said: “Come to the blessed meal.” And I heard him say: “O God, teach Muʿāwiya the Book and reckoning, and protect him from the punishment.”"],[15451,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “I am the servant of God and the Seal of the Prophets, while Adam ﷺ was still clay in his form. I will inform you about that: the supplication of my father Abraham, the glad tidings of Jesus, and the vision of my mother that she saw. In the same way the mothers of the prophets see visions. Indeed, the mother of the Messenger of God ﷺ, when she gave birth to me, saw a light that illuminated for her the palaces of Syria.”"],[15452,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “I am the servant of God and the Seal of the Prophets, while Adam ﷺ was still clay in his form. I will tell you about that: the supplication of my father Abraham, the glad tidings of Jesus, and the vision of my mother that she saw. In the same way the mothers of the prophets see visions.” And the mother of the Messenger of God ﷺ saw, when she gave birth, a light that illuminated from it the palaces of Syria."],[15453,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I am, with God in the Mother of the Book, the Seal of the Prophets, while Adam was still clay in his form. I will tell you its interpretation: the supplication of Abraham—the call, ‘And raise among them a Messenger from among themselves’—and the glad tidings of Jesus son of Mary, ‘And bringing good news of a Messenger who will come after me, whose name is Aḥmad,’ and the vision of my mother: she saw in her sleep that she gave birth to a light that illuminated from it the palaces of Syria.”"],[15454,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “This community will certainly crowd at the Basin like camels crowding when they come to drink for five.”"],[15455,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “If I take from a servant his two precious ones while he is patient with them, I will not be satisfied for him with any reward less than Paradise if he praises Me for them.”"],[15456,"The Lord ﷻ [said]: “If I seize from My servant his two precious ones while he is attached to them, I will not be satisfied for him with any reward less than Paradise.”"],[15457,"I sold the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a young camel. I came to demand payment and said, “Pay me for my young camel.” He said, “Yes, I will certainly pay you.” He paid me and paid me well. Then a Bedouin came and said, “Pay me,” and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ paid him with an older camel. The Bedouin said, “This is better than my young camel, O Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “The best of people are those who are best in repayment.”"],[15458,"He heard ʿIrbad b. Sariyah say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray for the first row three times and for the one after it once.”"],[15459,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek forgiveness for the first row three times and for the second once.” Maʿmar and ʿIkrimah did not mention Jubayr b. Nufayr in their hadith."],[15460,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to seek forgiveness for the first row three times and for the second once.” Hisham did not mention Jubayr b. Nufayr in the chain."],[15461,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for the first row three times and for the second once.”"],[15462,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every deed is cut off from its doer when he dies, except the one stationed in the way of Allah. His deeds will be increased for him and his provision will continue to be sent to him until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[15463,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever performs an obligatory prayer, he has an answered supplication; and whoever completes the Qur'an, he has an answered supplication.'"],[15464,"That the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Khaybar forbade every fanged beast of prey, and every bird with talons, and he forbade al-mujaththama (animals tied up and used as targets), and that pregnant women be taken as concubines until they give birth to what is in their wombs."],[15465,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a hair from the booty and said: 'I have nothing of this except what one of you has, except the fifth, and it is returned to you. So return the needle and the thread. And beware of ghulūl (embezzlement from booty), for it is a disgrace and a shame.'"],[15466,"the Messenger of Allah forbade (the flesh of) domesticated donkeys on the Day of Khaibar. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4336)"],[15467,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Khaybar forbade al-khulsa (snatching something quickly)."],[15468,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the slaughtered animals of the Christians and their festivals. He said: 'If you do not eat it, then feed me.'"],[15469,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever licks the plate and licks his fingers, Allah will satisfy him in this world and the Hereafter.'"],[15470,"He is called al-Mandaqūn. He invited him to Islam, and the Christian mentioned the Prophet ﷺ and reviled him. So that was brought to ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ, and he sent for him and said: 'We have given them the covenant.' Ghurfah said: 'I seek refuge with Allah that we would give them covenants and pledges on condition that they harm us concerning Allah and His Messenger. We only gave them on condition that we leave them and their churches, that they say in them what they wish, and that we do not burden them beyond their capacity, and that we fight on their behalf, and that they be left to their own judgments—unless they come to us, and we judge between them by what Allah has revealed.' ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ said: 'You have spoken the truth.'"],[15471,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and the sacrificial camels were brought. He said: 'Call Abu Ḥasan for me.' So he called ʿAlī, and he said: 'Take the lower end of the spear,' and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took its upper end, and we slaughtered the sacrificial camels with it. When he finished, he mounted the mule and seated ʿAlī behind him."],[15472,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'There is no emigration after the conquest. It is only three: jihad, intention, and the gathering (on the Day of Resurrection).'"],[15473,"That they wanted to emigrate to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but their fathers prevented them. They mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no emigration after the conquest. It is only jihad and intention.'"],[15474,"He is called Ghaylan b. Salama. He embraced Islam while he had ten wives. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to choose four of them and leave six."],[15475,"Nafi' was a slave belonging to Ghaylan b. Salama, and he fled to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and embraced Islam while Ghaylan was a polytheist. Then Ghaylan embraced Islam, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned his wala' to him."],[15476,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and he said: \"If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the wife to prostrate to her husband.\""],[15477,"From Ghudayf or Abu Ghusayf, a companion of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever introduces satire in Islam, cut off his tongue.\""],[15478,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, a drought has befallen us, and the fattest of our wealth are donkeys.\" He said: \"Eat from the fattest of your wealth; I only found repugnant the village-roving ones.\""],[15479,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"If a man drinks wine, flog him; then if he repeats it, flog him; then if he repeats it, flog him; then if he repeats it, flog him; then if he repeats it, kill him.\""],[15480,"I mentioned Qays in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"May Allah have mercy on Qays; may Allah have mercy on Qays.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you invoke mercy on Qays?\" He said: \"Yes, for he followed the religion of my forefather Isma'il b. Ibrahim, the close friend of Allah. O Qays, protect Yemen! O Yemen, protect Qays! Qays are the horsemen of Allah on earth. By Him in whose hand is my soul, a time will come upon people when this religion has no helper other than Qays. Allah, exalted is He, has horsemen from the people of heaven who are marked, and horsemen from the people of earth who are taught. The horsemen of Allah from the people of earth are Qays. Qays is but an egg that split from us, the people of the House. Qays is the harm of Allah on earth—meaning the lion of Allah.\""],[15481,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: \"O Messenger of Allah, nothing remains of the food of my family except some donkeys I have.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Feed your family from the fat of your wealth, for I only found repugnant the village-roving ones.\""],[15482,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: \"Nothing remains of my wealth except donkeys.\" He said: \"Feed your family from the fat of your wealth; I only disliked for you the village-roving ones.\""],[15483,"Mis'ar said, and I think Ghalib is the one who asked the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, nothing remains of my wealth to feed my family except donkeys.\" He said: \"Feed your family from the fat of your wealth, for I only forbid for you the village-roving ones.\""],[15484,"Abjar or the son of Abjar asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: \"O Messenger of Allah, nothing remains of my wealth except donkeys.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Feed your family from the fat of your wealth; I only disliked for you the village-roving ones.\""],[15485,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, a famine has befallen us, and the fattest of our wealth are donkeys.\" He said: \"Eat from the fattest of your wealth,\" and he said: \"I only found repugnant for you—or disliked for you—the village-grazing ones.\""],[15486,"Some of the people were martyred in Syria on the day of Ajnadayn, and it is said on the day of Marj al-Suffar; both days were together in the year eighteen. He died when he was twenty-one years old."],[15487,"The Prophet ﷺ did not cease saying the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah, throwing seven pebbles while saying takbir with each pebble."],[15488,"The Prophet ﷺ mounted him behind him on the morning of Jam' (Muzdalifah), and he did not cease saying the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah. He said: He threw it from below with seven pebbles, saying takbir with each pebble: one takbir. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered and said: \"I have slaughtered here, and all of Mina is a place of slaughter, so slaughter in your dwellings.\""],[15489,"The Prophet ﷺ slaughtered near Jamrat al-Aqabah and said: \"I have slaughtered here, and all of Mina is a place of slaughter, so slaughter in your dwellings.\""],[15490,"From al-Fadl b. Abbas: \"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I did not stop hearing him say the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah. When he threw it, he stopped the talbiyah.\" The wording is from the hadith of al-Hasan b. al-Rabi'."],[15491,"The Prophet ﷺ said the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah."],[15492,"\"And by Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued to walk with me the next morning after the gathering. A man from the Bedouins accompanied us, and he had his young daughter with him. While walking with the Prophet ﷺ , I became distracted and turned my face away from her. He continued to call me until he threw the pebble at the Jamarat.\""],[15493,"From al-Fadl b. Abbas, who was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ on the morning of Muzdalifah: \"I did not stop hearing him say the tahlil (ihlal) until he reached the Jamrah. When he threw it, he stopped.\""],[15494,"That I should pray inside the Ka'bah? Whoever prays in it has left something behind him. But my brother told me that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered it, he fell prostrate between the two pillars, then sat down, and did not pray."],[15495,"The Prophet ﷺ mounted him behind him from Muzdalifah, and he did not cease saying the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah."],[15496,"He was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he departed from Muzdalifah. A Bedouin came alongside him with a beautiful daughter of his. I began looking at her, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept turning my face away from her. He did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-‘Aqabah."],[15497,"Al-Fadl b. al-‘Abbas was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ. The young man began glancing at the women and looking at them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept turning his face away with his hand from behind him. The young man kept glancing at the women, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “O son of my brother, this is a day on which whoever controls his hearing, his sight, and his tongue will be forgiven.”"],[15498,"“He entered the Ka‘bah with the Prophet ﷺ while Bilal was at the door.” He said: “He did not pray,” while Bilal said: “He prayed.”"],[15499,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: “Whoever wakes up in a state of major ritual impurity must not fast that day.” So my father sent to ‘A’ishah to ask her, and I went with him to her, and he asked her, and she said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wake up in a state of major ritual impurity without a wet dream, then he would wake up fasting.” So he returned to Marwan and told him, and he said: “Meet Abu Hurayrah and tell him.” He said: “He is my neighbor, and I dislike to confront him with what he dislikes.” He said: “I adjure you to go to him.” So he went to him and said: “O Abu Hurayrah, I disliked to confront you with what you dislike, but the governor adjured me.” So he told him, and he said: “Al-Fadl b. ‘Abbas narrated it to me.”"],[15500,"Al-Fadl b. ‘Abbas was asked: Did the Prophet ﷺ pray inside the House? He said: “No.”"],[15501,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us in a desert and he performed the Asr prayer, and in front of him was a dog or a donkey belonging to us, and he did not forbid it or make us delay it.\""],[15502,"It was said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who cannot perform Hajj or ‘Umrah or travel. He said: “Perform Hajj and ‘Umrah on behalf of your father.”"],[15503,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not stand for any night prayer except that he used the siwak."],[15504,"That he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Muzdalifah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-‘Aqabah, and his mount did not lift a foot moving onward until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-‘Aqabah."],[15505,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ stopped at a place during a journey or entered his house, he would not sit until he prayed two rakʿahs."],[15506,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went on the expedition of Tabuk, and the riding beasts became severely exhausted. They complained to him about that, and he saw that they were men who did not give their mounts rest. The Messenger of God ﷺ looked at a narrow pass through which the people were passing and stood at it while the people passed by, and he blew upon it and said, \"O God, make them carry in Your cause, for You carry the strong and the weak, the fresh and the dry, in sea and on land.\" So they remained strong, and we did not enter Madinah except while they were pulling at their reins."],[15507,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God is more attentive to a man with a beautiful voice reciting the Quran than the owner of a singing slave-girl is to his singing slave-girl.\""],[15508,"From Fadalah b. 'Ubayd that they were with the Prophet ﷺ on a military expedition of theirs, and they acquired a necklace containing gold and jewels. They sold it for dinars. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do not sell it like that,\" and he forbade them from that, and said: \"The jewels separately and the gold separately.\""],[15509,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever abandons his brother for more than three days, he will be in the Fire, unless Allah rescues him by His generosity.\""],[15510,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for food. It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, were you not fasting this day?' He said, 'Yes, but I vomited.'"],[15511,"He entered upon A'ishah and she brought out some hairs from the hair of the Prophet ﷺ, and it was red, dyed."],[15512,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Islam consists of three levels: a lower one, an upper one, and a chamber. The lower one is Islam, which the common Muslims have entered; none of them is asked but that he says, \"I am a Muslim.\" The upper one is the superiority of their deeds, some Muslims being better than others. As for the highest chamber, it is striving in the path of Allah; none attains it except the best of them.'"],[15513,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The earth is Allah's earth and the servants are Allah's servants. Whoever revives dead land, it is his.'"],[15514,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Three are the barren ones: a leader who, if you do good, does not thank, and if you do wrong, does not forgive; a neighbor who, if he sees good, buries it, and if he sees evil, spreads it; and a wife who, if she is present with you, harms you, and if you are absent from her, betrays you.'"],[15515,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and whoever had an 'arif would stay with his 'arif, and whoever did not have an 'arif would stay in the Suffah. I stayed in the Suffah. A man called out to him on Friday, saying, 'O Messenger of Allah, dates have burned our stomachs.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Soon, or whoever of you lives, will be given platters in the morning and evening, and you will clothe the walls as the Ka'bah is veiled.'"],[15516,"That he asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about Sabaʾ, saying, \"O Messenger of God, what is Sabaʾ? Is it a man, a mountain, or a valley?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"No; rather, it is a man who fathered ten. Four went north and six went south. Those who went north: Lakhm, Judhām, ʿĀmila, and Ghassān. Those who went south: Ḥimyar, Madhḥij, al-Azd, Kinda, al-Ashʿariyyūn, and Anmār, from whom is Bajīla.\""],[15517,"\"I came to the Prophet ﷺ in winter and found them praying in hooded cloaks and wraps, with their hands inside them.\""],[15518,"His grandfather Fudayk came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Establish the prayer, give the zakāh, abandon evil, and dwell among the land of your people wherever you wish.\""],[15519,"Al-Fadl b. Abbas narrated to me, and he was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ that day, so he heard the Prophet ﷺ saying the tahlil (ihlal) until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah."],[15520,"I rode behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the morning of Jam' (Muzdalifah), and I did not stop hearing him say the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah."],[15521,"The Prophet ﷺ mounted him behind him on the morning of Jam' (Muzdalifah), and he did not cease saying the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah."],[15522,"I rode behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the morning of Jamʿ (Muzdalifah), and he did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrat al-ʿAqabah."],[15523,"He informed him, saying: I was with the Prophet ﷺ until he came to ʿArafah during the Farewell Pilgrimage. When the people departed, he said to the people: \"O people, proceed gently with tranquility, for righteousness is not in hastening.\""],[15524,"From al-Faḍl b. ʿAbbās, who was the riding companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said to the people on the evening of ʿArafah and the morning of Jamʿ when they stood: \"Upon you is tranquility,\" while he was holding back his she-camel. Then when he entered Muḥassir, which is part of Minā, he said: \"Upon you are the pebbles of khadhf, with which the jamrah is thrown.\" He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw the jamrah."],[15525,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said on the evening of ʿArafah and the morning of Jamʿ to the people when they departed: \"Upon you is tranquility,\" while he was holding back the she-camel. Then when he entered Minā, when he descended into Muḥassir, he said: \"Upon you are the pebbles of khadhf, with which the jamarāt are thrown,\" and the Prophet ﷺ was moving as a person moves."],[15526,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Throw pebbles like the pebbles of khadhf.\""],[15527,"That when it was the day of ʿArafah, al-Faḍl b. ʿAbbās was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿAbbās said: When the people said the takbīr, I said: Al-Faḍl will tell me what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did. He said: When he departed on the evening of ʿArafah, the people departed with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began pulling the head of his camel, restraining it, and he kept calling out: \"O people, upon you is tranquility,\" until when he reached Muḥassir he hastened a little and began saying: \"Upon you are the pebbles of khadhf.\""],[15528,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said on the evening of ʿArafah and the morning of Jamʿ when they departed: \"Upon you is tranquility,\" while he was holding back his she-camel, until he reached Muḥassir, and he said: \"Upon you are the pebbles of khadhf, with which the jamarāt are thrown.\""],[15529,"That the Prophet ﷺ on the evening of ʿArafah would say takbīr, tahlīl, and supplicate. When the people departed, he said: \"Upon you is tranquility.\" When he reached the mountain pass, he turned aside to it, wanting water, then performed ablution, and the people mounted. When he arrived at Muzdalifah, he combined Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ. When he prayed the morning prayer, he stood. When he departed, the people departed. He said, while he was restraining his mount: \"Upon you is tranquility,\" until when he came to Minā, he said: \"Upon you are the pebbles of khadhf, with which the jamarāt are thrown.\" And he did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrat al-ʿAqabah."],[15530,"ʿAbdullāh said: \"Do not fast, for a milking vessel containing milk was brought near to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of ʿArafah, and he drank it. So do not fast, for the people are being tested by you.\""],[15531,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drinking from a worn waterskin on the day of ʿArafah."],[15532,"That the Prophet ﷺ commanded the weak among Banū Hāshim and their children to depart from Jamʿ at night."],[15533,"That the Prophet ﷺ was shrouded in two white Suḥūlī garments."],[15534,"“I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ from Jam‘ (Muzdalifah), and he departed while tranquility was upon him.”"],[15535,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from ‘Arafāt while Usāma b. Zayd was riding behind him. The she-camel swerved with him while he was standing at ‘Arafāt before departing, and he was raising his hands, not letting them go above his head. When he departed, he traveled at his easy pace until he came to Jam‘. And he departed from ‘Arafah while al-Faḍl b. ‘Abbās was riding behind him.”"],[15536,"“That he was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw the pebble at the Jamrah near al-‘Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice.”"],[15537,"From ‘Āmir al-Aḥwal, Jābir al-Ju‘fī, and Ibn ‘Aṭā’, from ‘Aṭā’, from Ibn ‘Abbās, from al-Faḍl b. ‘Abbās: “That he was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he recited the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrah of al-‘Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice.”"],[15538,"“That the Prophet ﷺ recited the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrah of al-‘Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice.”"],[15539,"“That he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting the talbiyah on the Day of Sacrifice until he threw the Jamrah of al-‘Aqabah.”"],[15540,"“Usāma was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from ‘Arafah to al-Muzdalifah, and I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from al-Muzdalifah to Minā. I did not cease hearing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrah of al-‘Aqabah.”"],[15541,"“That he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he kept reciting the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrah of al-‘Aqabah.”"],[15542,"“That he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he kept reciting the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrah of al-‘Aqabah.”"],[15543,"“I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrah.”"],[15544,"“That the Prophet ﷺ did not abandon the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrah of al-Quṣwā (the farthest one) on the Day of Sacrifice.”"],[15545,"He narrated to him that the Prophet ﷺ seated al-Faḍl b. ‘Abbās behind him from Jam‘. Al-Faḍl said: “He did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrah of al-‘Aqabah.”"],[15546,"That the Prophet ﷺ continued to recite the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah."],[15547,"He informed him that the Prophet ﷺ did not cease reciting the talbiyah, with him hearing it, until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah."],[15548,"That the Prophet ﷺ continued to recite the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah."],[15549,"About Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, he was a companion of Prophet Muhammad ﷺ and remained by his side until he threw the pebbles at the Jamrah."],[15550,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from ʿArafāt with Usāmah b. Zayd riding behind him. His she-camel turned aside while he was standing, and he struck her before departing, while raising his hands, not letting them go beyond his head. When he departed, he traveled at an easy pace until he came to Jamʿ; then he departed from Jamʿ, and then he recited the talbiyah from Jamʿ with al-Faḍl riding behind him. Al-Faḍl said: \"He did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah.\""],[15551,"\"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah on the Day of Sacrifice.\""],[15552,"That the Prophet ﷺ continued to recite the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah on the Day of Sacrifice."],[15553,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered into the state of ihrām until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah."],[15554,"That the Prophet ﷺ continued to recite the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah."],[15555,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me, so I went out to him and found him suffering from a fever, having bandaged his head. He said: \"Take my hand, O Faḍl.\" So I took his hand until he reached the pulpit and sat on it. Then he said: \"Call out among the people.\" So I called out among the people, and a group of people gathered to him. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \"O people, indeed rights have drawn near to me from among your midst. Whoever I have lashed his back, here is my back, let him take retribution from it. Indeed, whoever I have insulted his honor, here is my honor, let him take retribution from it. Indeed, let no man say, 'I fear ill will from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Indeed, ill will is not of my nature nor of my concern. Indeed, the most beloved of you to me is the one who takes a right if he has one against me, or who absolves me, so that I meet Allah with a sound soul. Indeed, I do not see that as sufficient for me until I stand among you repeatedly.\" Then he descended and prayed the noon prayer, then returned to the pulpit and repeated his speech about ill will and other matters. Then he said: \"O people, whoever has anything with him, let him return it, and let him not say 'the disgraces of this world.' Indeed, the disgraces of this world are easier than the disgraces of the Hereafter.\" A man stood up to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have three dirhams owed by you.\" He said: \"Indeed, we do not call a claimant a liar, nor do we make him swear. How did they come to be owed by me to you?\" He said: \"Do you remember the day a poor man passed by you, and you ordered me to give them to him?\" He said: \"Give them to him, O Faḍl.\" Then another man stood up to him and said: \"I have three dirhams that I pilfered in the cause of Allah.\" He said: \"Why did you pilfer them?\" He said: \"I was in need of them.\" He said: \"Take them, O Faḍl.\" Then he said: \"O people, whoever fears something within himself, let him stand, and I will pray for him.\" A man stood up to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I am indeed a liar, and I am indeed a hypocrite, and I am indeed prone to sleeping.\" He said: \"O Allah, grant him truthfulness and faith, and remove sleep from him when he desires.\" Then another man stood up to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I am indeed a liar, and I am indeed a hypocrite, and there is nothing of things except that I have committed it.\" ʿUmar said to him: \"O this one, you have exposed yourself.\" He said: \"Enough, O Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, the disgraces of this world are easier than the disgraces of the Hereafter.\" Then he said: \"O Allah, grant him truthfulness and faith, and turn his affair to good.\" Then ʿUmar spoke a word to them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"ʿUmar is with me, and I am with him, and the truth after me is with ʿUmar wherever he is.\""],[15556,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Bind my head so that I may go out to the mosque.\" So I bound his head with a yellow bandage. Then he went out to the mosque, being supported between two men."],[15557,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"My father has reached the time of Hajj, but he is a very old man who cannot ride a camel. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" He said: \"Perform Hajj on his behalf.\""],[15558,"A woman from Khathʿam asked the Prophet ﷺ while al-Faḍl was riding behind him. She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the obligation of Allah upon His servants concerning Hajj has overtaken my father, an old man. If they bind him on his mount, he cannot hold himself upright. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" He said: \"Yes, perform Hajj on his behalf.\""],[15559,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik; ḥ, and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us; Mālik reported to us from Ibn Shihāb, from Sulaymān b. Yasār, from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbbās, who said: Al-Faḍl b. al-ʿAbbās was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a woman of Khathʿam came to ask him for a ruling. Al-Faḍl began looking at her and she looked at him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began turning al-Faḍl's face to the other side. She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation upon His servants regarding Hajj has found my father an old man who cannot remain upright on the saddle; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf?' He said, 'Yes.' That was during the Farewell Pilgrimage."],[15560,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted al-Faḍl b. ʿAbbās behind him on his camel on the Day of Sacrifice. Al-Faḍl was a handsome man. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped to give rulings to the people, and a beautiful woman from Khathʿam came asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a ruling. Al-Faḍl began looking at her, and her beauty pleased him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned and saw al-Faḍl looking at her, so he reached back with his hand, took hold of al-Faḍl's chin, and turned his face away from looking at her. She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation regarding Hajj upon His servants has found my father an old man who cannot sit upright on the camel; can I fulfill it by performing Hajj on his behalf?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, 'Yes, perform Hajj on his behalf.'"],[15561,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who cannot hold himself steady on the camel; should I fulfill it for him by performing Hajj on his behalf?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Yes.'"],[15562,"a woman from Khath'am asked the Messenger of Allah a question during the Farewell Pilgrimage, when Al-Fadl bin 'Abbas was riding behing the Messenger of Allah She said: \"O Messenger of Allah! The command of Allah has come for His slaves to perform Hajj, but my father is an old man and cannot sit upright in the saddle. Will it be paid off on his behalf if I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" The Messenger of Allah said to her: \"Yes.\" And Al-Fadl started to turn toward her, as she was a beautiful woman, but the Messenger of Allah took hold of Al-Fadl's face and turned it to the other side. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2642)"],[15563,"A woman of Khathʿam came to ask the Prophet ﷺ for a ruling in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage and said, 'O Prophet of Allah, Allah's obligation upon His servants regarding Hajj has found my father an old man who cannot sit upright on the camel; will it suffice him if I perform Hajj on his behalf?' The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, 'Yes.'"],[15564,"A woman asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about her father who had died without performing Hajj. He said, 'Perform Hajj on behalf of your father.'"],[15565,"A woman of Khathʿam asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a ruling: 'Allah's obligation regarding Hajj upon His servants has found my father an old man who cannot sit upright on the camel; will it suffice him if I perform Hajj on his behalf?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Yes.'"],[15566,"From the Prophet ﷺ: A woman of Khathʿam asked him for a ruling during the Farewell Pilgrimage and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation regarding Hajj upon His servants has found my father an old man who cannot sit upright on the camel; can I fulfill it for him by performing Hajj on his behalf?' He said to her, 'Yes.'"],[15567,"A woman of Khathʿam asked the Prophet ﷺ for a ruling during the Farewell Pilgrimage and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation regarding Hajj upon His servants has found my father an old man who cannot sit upright on the camel; can I fulfill it for him by performing Hajj on his behalf?' He said to her, 'Yes.'"],[15568,"'O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation regarding Hajj upon His servants has found my father an old man who cannot sit upright on the camel; can I fulfill it for him by performing Hajj on his behalf?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, 'Yes.'"],[15569,"'O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation regarding Hajj has found my father an old man who cannot hold himself steady on the camel; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf?' He said, 'Yes, perform Hajj on behalf of your father.'"],[15570,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted al-Faḍl b. ʿAbbās behind him on the rear of his camel on the Day of Sacrifice. Al-Faḍl was a handsome man. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped to give rulings to the people, and a beautiful woman from Khathʿam came asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a ruling. Al-Faḍl began looking at her, and her beauty pleased him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned and saw al-Faḍl looking at her, so he reached back with his hand, took hold of al-Faḍl's chin, and turned his face away from looking at her. That Khathʿamī woman said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation regarding Hajj has found my father an old man who cannot sit upright on the camel; can I fulfill it for him by performing Hajj on his behalf?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, 'Yes, perform Hajj on his behalf.'"],[15571,"'I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-ʿAqabah.'"],[15572,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever intends to perform Hajj, let him hasten, for the sick may fall ill, the stray animal may wander off, and a need may arise.”"],[15573,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever among you intends to perform Hajj, let him hasten, for the sick may fall ill, the stray animal may go astray, and a need may arise.”"],[15574,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me on the morning of ‘Aqabah: “Bring me—pick up for me.” So I picked up for him seven pebbles, the size of pebbles for throwing. When he placed them in his palm, he said: “With the likes of these, with the likes of these. Beware of extremism, beware of extremism, for those before you were destroyed only by extremism in religion.” A group narrated this hadith from ‘Awf, among them Sufyan al-Thawri, but no one said “from Ibn ‘Abbas, from his brother” except Ja‘far b. Sulayman, and no one narrated it from Ja‘far except ‘Abd al-Razzaq."],[15575,"He informed him that he entered the House with the Prophet ﷺ, and that the Prophet ﷺ did not pray inside the House when he entered it; but when he came out, he prayed two rak‘ahs at the door of the House."],[15576,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in the Ka‘bah glorifying Allah, proclaiming His greatness, supplicating, and seeking forgiveness, and he did not bow or prostrate.”"],[15577,"“I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Sacrifice, and he did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-‘Aqabah.”"],[15578,"I woke up in a state of janabah, so I came to Abu Hurayrah and asked him. He said to me: “Break your fast.” I said: “Should I not fast it and make it up?” He said: “No, rather break your fast.” So I came to Marwan b. al-Hakam, asked him, and informed him of Abu Hurayrah’s statement. He sent ‘Abd al-Rahman b. al-Harith b. Hisham to ‘A’ishah, and he asked her. She said: “The Prophet ﷺ would go out for the Fajr prayer with his head dripping from intercourse, then he would fast that day.” He returned to Marwan and informed him of that. Marwan said: “Go to Abu Hurayrah and inform him.” Abu Hurayrah said: “Indeed, I did not hear it from the Prophet ﷺ; it was only narrated to me by al-Fadl b. al-‘Abbas from the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[15579,"I became junub in Madinah during the month of Ramadan and woke up in a state of janabah. I came to Abu Hurayrah and mentioned that to him. He said: “Break your fast.” I said: “I fast my day and make up a day in its place?” He said: “No, break your fast.” So I came to Marwan b. al-Hakam, who was the governor of Madinah, and mentioned that. He sent Abu Bakr b. ‘Abd al-Rahman b. al-Hakam to ‘A’ishah, and he asked her about that. ‘A’ishah said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would wake up in the month of Ramadan in a state of janabah without a wet dream, and he would continue his fast.” Abu Bakr came to Marwan and informed him of ‘A’ishah’s statement. Marwan said to him: “I adjure you to meet Abu Hurayrah and inform him of ‘A’ishah’s statement.” So I met him and informed him of ‘A’ishah’s statement. He said: “Indeed, I did not hear it from the Prophet ﷺ; it was only informed to me by al-Fadl b. al-‘Abbas.” Ibn ‘Awn said: I said to Raja’ b. Haywah: “Who narrated this hadith to you from Ya‘la?” He said: “Ya‘la narrated this hadith to me directly.”"],[15580,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is overtaken by dawn, there is no fast for him.” So I and my father went and entered upon ‘A’ishah and Umm Salamah, and we asked them about that. They informed us that “the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would wake up in a state of janabah without a wet dream, then he would fast.” He said: We then entered upon Marwan and informed him of their statement and the statement of Abu Hurayrah. Marwan said: “I adjure you both to go to Abu Hurayrah and inform him.” He said: I met Abu Hurayrah at the gate of the mosque, and my father said to him: “The governor has adjured us concerning a matter that we should mention to you.” He said: “And what is it?” My father narrated it to him, and Abu Hurayrah’s face changed color. Then he said: “This is what al-Fadl b. al-‘Abbas said, and he is more knowledgeable.” Al-Zuhri said: “So he shifted the hadith to someone else.”"],[15581,"That he heard Abu Hurayrah say: “Whoever wakes up in a state of major ritual impurity, there is no fasting for him.” So Abu Bakr and his father ‘Abd al-Rahman went until they entered upon Umm Salamah and ‘A’ishah, and both of them said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wake up in a state of major ritual impurity without a wet dream, then he would fast.” So Abu Bakr and his father ‘Abd al-Rahman went to Marwan and told him, and he said: “I adjure you both to go to Abu Hurayrah and tell him.” So Abu Bakr and ‘Abd al-Rahman went until they came to Abu Hurayrah and informed him. He said: “Did they both say that to you?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “They know better. It was only al-Fadl b. ‘Abbas who narrated it to me.”"],[15582,"That he informed him that he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-‘Aqabah."],[15583,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited al-‘Abbas in a desert land of ours, and we had a gazelle and a female donkey grazing. The Prophet ﷺ prayed while they were in front of him, and they were not moved back or driven away."],[15584,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"The prayer is performed in pairs, with a testimony in each two units of prayer, and with supplication, humility, and devotion. You should hold firmly and submit with your hands, raising them towards your Lord, facing Him. You should say, 'O Lord, O Lord.' Whoever does not do that, he is deceiving.\""],[15585,"He was a companion of the Prophet ﷺ , and a man came to him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my mother is elderly and she cannot hold on to me, and if I tie her up, I fear that I will kill her. Should I perform Hajj on her behalf?\" He (the companion) said, \"Have you considered that if your mother was in debt, would you pay it off on her behalf?\" The man said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then perform Hajj on behalf of your mother.\""],[15586,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever intends to perform Hajj should hasten, for there may occur in it a stray animal or some other matter.”"],[15587,"I spent a night with the Prophet ﷺ to observe how he prayed. He stood at a water skin hung on a peg in the wall, performed ablution, then prayed two rak‘ahs, his standing being like his bowing and his bowing like his prostration. Then he slept, then woke up, performed ablution and sniffed water into his nose, then recited about fifty verses from Al ‘Imran: “Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of the night and the day…” He continued doing this until he had prayed ten rak‘ahs. Then he stood praying a single rak‘ah and made it witr. At that point the muezzin called, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood after the muezzin fell silent and prayed two light rak‘ahs, then sat until he performed the Fajr prayer."],[15588,"Nabidh would be prepared for the Prophet ﷺ at night, and he would drink it the next day and the night of the next day until the third day, then he would stop."],[15589,"About my religion, and that will not happen until I meet Muhammad ﷺ and his companions. “Whoever sells food or fodder from what was captured in the land of the Romans for gold or silver, the khums of Allah and the shares of the Muslims are due on it.”"],[15590,"Study together, receive glad tidings, and increase. May God increase you in good and love you and love those who love you. Return matters to us, for the reward of the last of them is like the reward of the first of them, and intermix your speech with seeking forgiveness."],[15591,"I accompanied Fadalah b. Ubayd, the Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and said, “Counsel me, may God have mercy on you.” He said, “Preserve from me three traits by which God will benefit you: if you are able to know but not be known, then do so; if you are able to listen but not speak, then do so; and if you are able to sit but not have people sit with you, then do so.”"],[15592,"I accompanied Fadalah b. Ubayd, the Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and said, “Counsel me, may God have mercy on you.” He said, “Preserve from me three traits by which God will benefit you: if you are able to know but not be known, then do so; if you are able to listen but not speak, then do so; and if you are able to sit but not have people sit with you, then do so.”"],[15593,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever desires the treasure of hadith, let him adhere to 'There is no might and no power except with God.'\""],[15594,"On the day of Khaybar I bought a necklace of gold and beads for twelve dinars. I separated them and found in its gold more than twelve dinars. I mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, \"Gold is not to be sold for gold until it is separated.\""],[15595,"On the day of Khaybar a necklace containing beads attached to gold was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, which a man had purchased for seven or nine. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said, \"No, until what is between them is distinguished.\" He said, \"I only wanted the stones.\" He said, \"No, until what is between them is distinguished.\" He said, so he returned it until it was distinguished."],[15596,"Remove the gold and put it on one side of the scale and put the gold on the other side, and do not take except like for like, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not take except like for like.\""],[15597,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Place between yourselves and the Fire a barrier, even with half a date.\""],[15598,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Islam is a spacious house, so whoever enters it is accommodated by it. The Hijrah is a spacious house, so whoever enters it is accommodated by it. Whoever is called to Islam and becomes Muslim, and is called to Hijrah and emigrates, has left no pursuit of good and no escape from evil.\""],[15599,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ, and he called for water and drank. I said, 'Were you not fasting?' He said, 'Yes, but I vomited.'"],[15600,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'Three matters in which play is not permissible: divorce, marriage, and manumission.'"],[15601,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'There is no imprisonment (i.e., no detention as a legal punishment).'"],[15602,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever grows a grey hair in Islam, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection.' A man said, 'Some men pluck out grey hairs.' He said, 'Whoever wishes may pluck out his grey hair,' or he said, 'his light.'"],[15603,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever grows a grey hair in Islam in the path of God, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection.' A man said at that, 'Some men pluck out grey hairs.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Whoever wishes, let him pluck out his light.'"],[15604,"Abu 'Ali al-Janbi narrated to him that he heard Fadalah b. 'Ubayd narrate from the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said: 'Whoever dies upon one of these ranks will be resurrected upon it on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[15605,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'Whoever dies upon one of these ranks will be resurrected upon it on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[15606,"Abu 'Ali al-Janbi was informed that he heard Fadalah b. 'Ubayd say that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Blessed is he who is guided to Islam, whose livelihood is sufficient, and who is content with it.'"],[15607,"From Abu 'Ali al-Janbi, from Fadalah b. 'Ubayd al-Ansari, that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'He has succeeded who is guided to Islam, whose livelihood is sufficient, and who is content with it.'"],[15608,"Abu 'Ali 'Amr b. Malik al-Janbi narrated to him from Fadalah b. 'Ubayd, from the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he said: 'Three people, do not ask about them: a man who parted from the community and disobeyed his imam and died disobedient; a female slave or a male slave who fled from his master and died; and a woman whose husband was absent from her while he had provided for her the expenses of this world, and she displayed her beauty after him—do not ask about them.'"],[15609,"Abu 'Ali al-Janbi narrated to him from Fadalah b. 'Ubayd that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Three people, do not ask about them: a man who contends with God in His pride, for His cloak is pride and His waist-wrapper is might; a man who doubts the command of God; and one who despairs of the mercy of God.'"],[15610,"From Abu 'Ali al-Janbi, from Fadalah b. 'Ubayd, who said: The Prophet ﷺ heard a man supplicating in his prayer without praising his Lord and without invoking blessings upon His Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'This one has been hasty. When one of you prays, let him begin by praising his Lord and extolling Him, then invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, then supplicate for whatever he wishes.'"],[15611,"From Abu 'Ali al-Janbi, from Fadalah b. 'Ubayd, who said: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, a man entered and prayed, then said, “O Allah, forgive me and have mercy on me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “You have been hasty, O worshipper. When you pray and then sit, praise Allah as He deserves, then invoke blessings upon me, then call upon Him.” Then another man prayed; he praised Allah and invoked blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Ask and you will be given it.”"],[15612,"From Abu 'Ali al-Janbi, from Fadalah b. 'Ubayd, who said: The Prophet ﷺ heard a man supplicating in his prayer while he had not glorified his Lord nor invoked blessings upon his Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said, “This one has been hasty. When one of you prays, let him begin by glorifying his Lord and extolling Him, then let him invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, then let him ask for whatever he wishes.”"],[15613,"From Abu 'Ali al-Janbi, from Fadalah b. 'Ubayd, who said: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, a man entered and prayed, then said, “O Allah, forgive me and have mercy on me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “You have been hasty, O worshipper. When you pray and then sit, praise Allah as He deserves, then invoke blessings upon me, then call upon Him.” Then another man prayed; he praised Allah and invoked blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Ask and you will be given it.”"],[15614,"Abu 'Ali 'Amr b. Malik al-Janbi narrated to him that he heard Fadalah b. 'Ubayd saying: A man entered into prayer and did not praise, did not glorify, and did not invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You have been hasty, O worshipper.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught them, and he heard a man praying who praised Allah alone and invoked blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O worshipper, supplicate and you will be answered; ask and you will be given it.”"],[15615,"From 'Amr b. Malik al-Janbi, from Fadalah b. 'Ubayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Shall I not tell you who the believer is? It is the one whom people trust with their wealth and their lives. The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. The mujahid is the one who strives against his own soul in obedience to Allah. The emigrant is the one who abandons sins and transgressions.”"],[15616,"He heard 'Amr b. Malik al-Janbi saying: I heard Fadalah b. 'Ubayd saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: “The mujahid is the one who strives against his own soul for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Exalted.”"],[15617,"When the Prophet ﷺ prayed, some men would fall down from their standing position because of the exhaustion they suffered; they were the people of the Suffah, so much so that the Bedouins would say, “These are madmen.” When he finished the prayer, he turned to them and said, “If you knew what you have with Allah, you would love to increase in poverty and need.” Fadalah said, “I was with the Prophet ﷺ that day.”"],[15618,"Abu 'Ali 'Amr b. Malik al-Janbi narrated to him from Fadalah b. 'Ubayd, who said: I heard him saying: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led the people in prayer, some men would fall down from their standing position during the prayer because of the privation they suffered; they were among the people of the Suffah. The Arabs would say, “These are madmen.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, he turned to them and said, “If you knew what you have with Allah, you would love to increase in poverty and need.” Fadalah b. 'Ubayd said, “I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that day.”"],[15619,"Abu 'Ali al-Janbi narrated to him that he heard Fadalah b. 'Ubayd saying: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led the people in prayer, some men would fall down from their standing position due to privation; they were the people of the Suffah, so much so that the Bedouins would say, “These are madmen.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, he turned to them and said to them, “If you knew what you have with Allah, you would love to increase in poverty and need.” Fadalah b. 'Ubayd said, “I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that day.”"],[15620,"\"Abu Ali Al-Janbi reported to him that he heard Fadalah ibn Ubayd saying, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'I am the leader and the one who carries the burden for those who believe, embrace Islam, and migrate for the sake of a house in the suburbs of Paradise, a house in the middle of Paradise, and a house in the highest level of Paradise. Whoever does that will never be devoid of good nor escape from evil. So, let him die whenever he wishes to die.'\""],[15621,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No deceased person dies except that his deeds are sealed, except for one who dies as a murabit in the path of Allah; indeed, his deeds continue to grow for him, and he is safe from the trial of the grave.”"],[15622,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Everyone who dies will have fully complete his action, except one who is on the frontier (in Allah's path), for his deeds will be made to go on increasing till the Day of Resurrection, and he will be safe from the trial in the grave. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2500)"],[15623,"From 'Amr b. Malik al-Janbi, from Fadalah b. 'Ubayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The rider greets the one standing, and the few greet the many.”"],[15624,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: “The horseman greets the one walking and the one standing, and the few greet the many.”"],[15625,"From Abu 'Ali al-Janbi, from Fadalah b. 'Ubayd, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon on the Day of Sacrifice and said: \"Indeed, your blood and your honor are sacred, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours.\""],[15626,"A necklace containing gold and beads from the spoils of war was brought to the Prophet ﷺ to be sold. The Prophet ﷺ took out the gold that was in the necklace and sold it separately, then said: \"Gold for gold, weight for weight.\""],[15627,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Allah, whoever believes in You and bears witness that I am Your Messenger, endear to him meeting You, make Your decree easy for him, and give him little of this world. And whoever does not believe in You and does not bear witness that I am Your Messenger, do not endear to him meeting You, do not make Your decree easy for him, and give him much of this world.\""],[15628,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to command us to level the graves.\""],[15629,"He said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Level your graves.\""],[15630,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"He commands leveling them.\""],[15631,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Level the graves flat with the surface of the ground when you bury.\""],[15632,"I heard Fadalah b. 'Ubayd say: On the day of Khaybar, a necklace containing beads and gold from the spoils of war was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to be sold. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that the gold in the necklace be removed separately. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: \"Gold for gold, weight for weight.\""],[15633,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would wake up in a state of major ritual impurity and then continue fasting.\""],[15634,"Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Ibn 'A'ishah narrated to us, they said: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Yazid b. Abi Habib, from Abu Marzuq, from Fadalah b. 'Ubayd: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ vomited and broke his fast.\""],[15635,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them on a day he used to fast, so he called for a vessel containing water and drank. We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this is a day you used to fast?' He said, 'Yes, but I vomited.'"],[15636,"That they were supplications with which the Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate."],[15637,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me, and among what he taught me, he said: 'Guard the five prayers.' I said, 'These are times in which I have occupations, so command me with a comprehensive matter that, if I do it, will suffice me.' He said, 'Guard the two afternoon prayers.' I said, 'What are the two afternoon prayers?' He said, 'A prayer before sunrise and a prayer before sunset.'"],[15638,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ghusl on Friday, the day of 'Arafah, and the Day of Sacrifice."],[15639,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'What is lawful for us from dead meat?' He said, 'What is your food?' He said, 'We drink in the evening and drink in the morning.' He said, 'That is hunger,' and he permitted them dead meat in that situation. Abu Nu'aym said: 'Uqbah explained it to me, saying, 'A cup in the evening and a cup in the morning.'"],[15640,"'Abd al-Malik b. 'Ata' al-'Amiri al-Bakka'i brought out to us a letter from the Prophet ﷺ for them and said to us, 'Write it down,' but he did not dictate it to us. He claimed that the son of the daughter of al-Fujay' narrated to him: 'This is a letter from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to al-Fujay' and whoever follows him, that he has submitted, and whoever establishes prayer, gives zakah, obeys Allah and His Messenger, gives a fifth of the spoils, supports the Prophet of Allah, testifies to his Islam, and separates from the polytheists, he is secure with the security of Allah and Muhammad ﷺ.'"],[15641,"From Furāt b. Ḥayyān—and the Messenger of God ﷺ had ordered that he be killed, and he was a spy for Abū Sufyān and an ally—he passed by a circle of the Anṣār and said, \"I am a Muslim.\" A man among them said, \"O Messenger of God, he says, 'I am a Muslim.'\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Among you are men who reveal their faith to me; among them is al-Furāt b. Ḥayyān.\""],[15642,"That he asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the alliance of the pre-Islamic era. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Perhaps you are asking about the ally of Lakhm and Tamīm?\" He said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"Islam only increases it in strength.\""],[15643,"He said to him, \"I would not go ahead of you while you are older than me and earlier in migration, and the mosque is your mosque.\" Furāt said, \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say something about you, so I will never go ahead of you.\" He said, \"Did you witness him on the day I came to him at al-Ṭāʾif and he sent me as a spy?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So Ḥanẓala went forward and led them in prayer. Then Furāt said, \"O Banū ʿAjlān, I put this man forward only because the Messenger of God ﷺ sent him as a spy to al-Ṭāʾif, and he came back and reported the news to him. He said, 'You have spoken the truth. Return to your dwelling, for you have been present tonight.' When he turned away, he said to us, 'Take this man and his like as your imams.'\""],[15644,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, shall I fight with those of my people who come forward against those who turn away?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Then when I turned away, he called me and said, \"Call them to Islam; if they refuse, then fight them.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, tell me about Sabaʾ: is it a man or a woman?\" He said, \"It is a man of the Arabs who had ten sons; six of them went south, and four went north. As for those who went south: al-Azd, Kinda, Madhḥij, al-Ashʿariyyūn, Ḥimyar, and Anmār, from whom are Bajīla. As for those who went north: ʿĀmila, Ghassān, Lakhm, and Judhām.\""],[15645,"That he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, we have neighbors from Sabaʾ—people of might, dominion, and arrogance. Give me permission to call them to Islam; if they refuse, then give me permission to fight them with my people and those who obey me.\" So he gave him permission. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ had a change of mind and said, \"You mentioned the matter of Sabaʾ as you did. Call them to Islam; if they respond, accept from them and refrain from them; and if they refuse, do not confront them until my command comes to you.\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, do you think Sabaʾ is a land or a woman?\" He said, \"It is neither a land nor a woman; rather, it is a man who fathered ten tribes. Six of them went south and four went north. The Yemenis are Madhḥij, al-Azd, Kinda, Ḥimyar, al-Ashʿariyyūn, and Anmār.\" A man said, \"O Messenger of God, what is Anmār?\" He said, \"The father of Bajīla and Khathʿam. And four of them went north: Lakhm, Judhām, Ghassān, and ʿĀmila.\""],[15646,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, shall I not fight those of my people who turn back with those who come forward?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Then it occurred to me, and I said, \"O Messenger of God, no—rather the people of Sabaʾ: they are mightier and stronger.\" So the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me and gave me permission to fight Sabaʾ. When I left him, God revealed concerning Sabaʾ what He revealed. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"What has the Ghaṭafānī done?\" He sent to my dwelling and found that I had already departed, so he brought me back. When I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, I found him sitting among his companions. He said, \"Call the people. Whoever responds to you, accept from them; and whoever refuses, do not be hasty until you have spoken to me.\" A man among the people said, \"O Messenger of God, what is Sabaʾ? Is it a land or a woman?\" He said, \"It is not a land or a woman; rather, it is a man who fathered ten of the Arabs. Six of them went south and four went north. As for those who went north: Lakhm, Judhām, ʿĀmila, and Ghassān. As for those who went south: al-Azd, Kinda, Ḥimyar, al-Ashʿariyyūn, Anmār, and Madhḥij.\" A man said, \"O Messenger of God, what is Anmār?\" He said, \"They are those of whom are Bajīla and Khathʿam.\""],[15647,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, \"Do you dislike your two days and the two days of Hamdān?\" He said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God—the destruction of family and clan.\" He said, \"Verily, it is better for those of you who remain.\""],[15648,"Farwa b. ʿĀmir al-Judhāmī had sent the Messenger of God ﷺ his submission to Islam and gifted him a white mule. Farwa was a servant of Caesar, the king of the Byzantines, appointed over the Arabs under his authority. His dwelling was ʿUmān and its surroundings. When the Byzantines learned of his affair, they imprisoned him. He said in his prison: [poem]."],[15649,"From ʿUrwa, in naming those who witnessed the ʿAqaba pledge from the Anṣār, then from Banū Bayāḍa: Farwa b. ʿAmr; and he witnessed Badr."],[15650,"From Jābir: \"The Prophet ﷺ used to send a man from the Anṣār of Banū Bayāḍa called Farwa b. ʿAmr, and he would estimate the fruit of the people of Madinah.\""],[15651,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ used to send Farwa b. ʿAmr to estimate the palm trees. When he entered a garden, he would calculate what was in it from the branches, then strike some of them against others according to what he saw in them, and he would not err.\""],[15652,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I have become Muslim while I have two sisters as wives.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Divorce whichever of them you wish.”"],[15653,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while I had two sisters whom I had married in the Jāhiliyyah. He said, “When you return, divorce one of them.”"],[15654,"I said, “O Messenger of God, I have become Muslim while I have two sisters as wives.” He said, “Divorce whichever of them you wish.”"],[15655,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, we are owners of grapevines and vineyards, and the prohibition of wine has come down. What should we do?” He said, “Make them into raisins.” They said, “What should we do with the raisins?” He said, “Soak them in the morning and drink in the evening, and soak them in the evening and drink in the morning.” They said, “O Messenger of God, should we not leave it until it ferments?” He said, “Do not put it in large jars or gourds; put it in water skins, for if it is delayed beyond its pressing, it becomes vinegar.” I said, “O Prophet of God, we are as you know, our region is as you know, and we live among those you know. Who is our guardian?” He said, “God and His Messenger.”"],[15656,"“We brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ the head of al-ʿAbsī, the liar.”"],[15657,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying, “Our land is cold and we have vineyards. What should we do with them?” He said, “Make them into raisins.” Then he mentioned something similar."],[15658,"I came as a delegate to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “We make food and drink and feed it to our cousins.” He said, “Does it intoxicate?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “It is forbidden.” When I was taking leave of him, I mentioned it to him and said, “O Prophet of God, they will not be able to abstain from it.” He said, “Whoever cannot abstain from it, strike his neck.”"],[15659,"I came as a delegate to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “We make food and drink and feed it to our cousins.” He said, “Does it intoxicate?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “It is forbidden.” When I was taking leave of him, I mentioned it to him and said, “O Prophet of God, they will not be able to abstain from it.” He said, “Whoever cannot abstain from it, strike his neck.”"],[15660,"I said, “O Messenger of God, we are as you know, our region is as you know, and we have settled among those you know. Who is our guardian?” He said, “God and His Messenger.” He said, “I said, ‘Sufficient for me.’”"],[15661,"From Ibn al-Daylamī, who was the nephew of the Negus and had served the Prophet ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever recites ‘Say: He is God, the One’ one hundred times in prayer or otherwise, God will record for him a clearance from the Fire.”"],[15662,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There will be a sound in Ramadan.” They said, “O Messenger of God, at its beginning, or in its middle, or at its end?” He said, “No, rather in the middle of Ramadan, when the night of the middle is the night of Friday, there will be a sound from heaven by which seventy thousand will be thunderstruck, seventy thousand will be struck dumb, seventy thousand will be blinded, and seventy thousand will be made deaf.” They said, “O Messenger of God, who among your community will be safe?” He said, “Whoever stays in his house, seeks refuge through prostration, and raises his voice in glorifying God with takbīr, then another sound will follow it. The first sound is the sound of Gabriel, and the second is the sound of Satan. The sound is in Ramadan, the turmoil is in Shawwāl, the tribes are separated in Dhū al-Qaʿdah, and raids are made on pilgrims in Dhū al-Ḥijjah and in Muḥarram. And what is Muḥarram? Its beginning is a trial for my community, and its end is a joy for my community. A riding camel in that time with its saddle will be enough for a believer to escape from a village that yields a hundred thousand.”"],[15663,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ in the mosque when his gaze fixed upon a man walking in the mosque. He said, “O so-and-so.” He replied, “At your service, O Messenger of God.” He did not dispute the speech except to say, “O Messenger of God.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Do you testify that I am the Messenger of God?” He said, “No.” He said, “Do you read the Torah?” He said, “Yes, and the Gospel.” He said, “And the Qur’an?” He said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, if I wished I could read it.” Then he adjured him, “Do you find me in the Torah and the Gospel?” He said, “I find you, your like, your appearance, and your emergence. We had hoped that it would be from among us, but when you came forth, we were confused as to whether you are he. Then we looked and saw that you are not he.” He said, “And why is that?” He said, “Because with him from his community are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment, whereas with you there are only a few.” He said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I am he, and they are indeed my community, and they are more than seventy thousand, and seventy thousand.”"],[15664,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when his gaze fell upon a man. He called the man, and a Jewish man wearing a shirt, trousers, and sandals approached. The man began saying, \"O Messenger of Allah,\" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ responded, \"Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" The man refused to respond, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not say anything except, \"O Messenger of Allah\" to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him, \"Do you read the Torah?\" He replied, \"Yes.\" He then asked, \"And the Gospel?\" He replied, \"Yes.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked, \"And the Furqan?\" He replied, \"Yes,\" while adding, \"And I swear by the Lord of Muhammad, if I wished, I could recite it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then asked, \"I ask you by the One who revealed the Torah and the Gospel, have you found me mentioned in them?\" He replied, \"Yes, we find a description like yours coming out from your homeland. We used to hope that you would be among us. Then when you came out, we realized that you were the one. But when we looked again, we realized that you were not the one. So he asked, \"Where am I from?\" He replied, \"We find among his nation seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without being held to account, and indeed you are only a few.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ approached and said the Takbeer twice and then said, \"By the One whom my soul is in His Hand, I am indeed the one, and my nation is more than seventy thousand and seventy thousand.\""],[15665,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when revelation came down upon him. When revelation came down upon him, his gaze would melt while his eyes were open, and he would devote his hearing and sight and heart to what came from Allah. When it finished, he said to a scribe: Write: {Not equal are those believers who sit [at home] and those who strive in the cause of Allah} — the verse. Then the blind man stood up and said: What is our sin? Revelation came down upon him, so we said to the blind man: Revelation is descending upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He remained standing, saying: I repent to Allah. When it finished, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Write: {other than those who have a disability}."],[15666,"We came to the Prophet ﷺ among those Bedouins who came to him, and we sat waiting for him. He came out with anger on his face, and sat for a long time without speaking. Then he said: \"I came out to you when the Night of Decree and the Messiah of Misguidance had become clear to me, and I came out to explain them to you and give you glad tidings about them. But at the entrance of the mosque I met two men arguing, with Satan between them, so I came between them and forgot it, and it was snatched away from me. I shall give you a hint of it.\""],[15667,"He informed him that he saw the Prophet ﷺ and that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"As for the Night of Decree, seek it in the last ten nights, on the odd nights.\""],[15668,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I saw the Night of Decree, then I was made to forget it, so seek it in the last ten nights.\""],[15669,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were sitting waiting for him, when he came out to us with anger on his face. He sat for a long time without speaking, then it was relieved from him, and he said: \"I came out to you when the Night of Decree and the Messiah of Misguidance had become clear to me, and I came out to you to explain them to you. But I met two men at the mosque arguing, with Satan between them, so I came between them, and it was snatched away from me. So seek it in the last ten nights. As for the Messiah of Misguidance, he is bald on the forehead, one-eyed, broad-chested, with blood in him, as if he were Ibn al-‘Uzzā or Ibn al-‘Uzzā ibn so-and-so.\""],[15670,"Qays b. ʿĀṣim came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I buried alive eight daughters of mine in the Jāhiliyyah. He said: \"Free a slave for each one of them.\" I said: I am a camel owner. He said: \"Then offer a camel for each one of them, if you wish.\""],[15671,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about oaths of alliance. He said: \"Whatever oath of alliance existed in the Jāhiliyyah, hold fast to it, but there is no oath of alliance in Islam.\""],[15672,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered him \"to wash with water and lote leaves.\""],[15673,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and sought a private audience, then embraced Islam. \"The Prophet ordered him to wash with water and lote leaves.\" So he washed. The prayer was called, and he entered between Abū Bakr and ʿUmar and stood between them. When the prayer was over, the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Qays b. ʿĀṣim asked me about three matters that no one except Abū Bakr asked me about.\""],[15674,"To the Prophet ﷺ: I buried alive in the Jāhiliyyah twelve daughters, or thirteen daughters. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Free a life for each one of them.\""],[15675,"“My sons, fear Allah and make your eldest your leader, for when a people make their eldest their leader they succeed their father, but when they make their youngest their leader he is disparaged among your peers. You must acquire wealth, for it is a means of honor for the generous and by it one is made independent of the vile. Beware of begging from people, for it is the last of a man’s earnings. When I die, do not wail over me, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not wailed over. When I die, bury me in a land where Bakr b. Wa’il will not know of my burial, for I used to raid them in the Jahiliyyah.”"],[15676,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he saw me I heard him say, “This is the chief of the Arabs.” When we dismounted, I went to him and began to speak with him. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what wealth is there upon which I will bear no blame, from a guest who seeks my hospitality and from dependents who have become numerous?” He said, “Excellent wealth is forty, and the most is sixty. Woe to the owners of two hundred, except the one who gives from its milk and its strength, lends its back for riding, and slaughters its fat ones and feeds the contented and the beggar.” I said, “O Prophet of Allah, how noble and beautiful are these qualities! O Messenger of Allah, no valley in which I am can accommodate the abundance of my camels.” He said, “How do you manage?” I said, “The camels go out in the morning and the people go out, and whoever wishes takes hold of a camel’s head and goes off with it.” He said, “What do you do about lending the backs for riding?” I said, “I do not lend out the young nor the old toothless one that has turned away.” He said, “Is your wealth dearer to you or the wealth of your clients?” I said, “My own wealth is dearer to me than the wealth of my clients.” He said, “You shall have from your wealth what you ate and consumed, or wore and wore out, or gave away and sent forth; otherwise it is gathered against you.” I said, “By Allah, if I remain alive I will certainly exhaust its number.” Al-Hasan said, “By Allah, he did so. When death came to Qays, he said, ‘O my sons, take from me, for I find no one more sincere to you than myself. When I die, make your elders your leaders and do not make your young ones your leaders, lest people deem you foolish and then hold you in contempt. You must set right your wealth, for it is a means of honor for the generous and by it one is made independent of the vile. Beware of begging, for it is the last of a man’s earnings; no one begs except that he abandons his earning. When I die, do not wail over me, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding wailing. Shroud me in the clothes in which I used to pray and fast. When you bury me, do not bury me in a place where anyone can see me, for there were scratches between me and Bakr b. Wa’il in the Jahiliyyah, and I fear that they will exhume me and then do something by which your religion and your worldly life would be lost.’” Al-Hasan, may Allah have mercy on him, said, “He advised them in life and advised them in death.”"],[15677,"“O my sons, when I die, make your eldest your leader so that you may succeed your fathers, and do not make your youngest your leader, for that would disparage you among your allies. Do not appoint a wailing woman over me, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding wailing. You must set right your wealth, for it is a means of honor for the generous and by it one is made independent of the vile. Do not give away the necks of the camels except to those entitled to them, and do not withhold them from what is due to them. Beware of every root of evil; whatever pleases you one day, what displeases you is more. Beware of the sons of your enemies, for they are enemies to you on the path of their fathers. When I die, bury me in a place where this clan of Bakr b. Wa’il cannot see me, for there were scratches between me and them in the Jahiliyyah, and I fear that they will exhume me and thereby corrupt their worldly life and corrupt your hereafter.’ Then he called for his quiver and ordered his eldest son, whose name was ‘Ali, saying, ‘Take out an arrow from my quiver.’ He took it out, and he said, ‘Break it,’ so he broke it. Then he said, ‘Take out two arrows,’ and he took them out, and he said, ‘Break them,’ so he broke them. Then he said, ‘Take out three arrows,’ and he took them out, and he said, ‘Break them,’ so he broke them. Then he said, ‘Take out thirty arrows,’ and he took them out, and he said, ‘Bind them with a bowstring,’ so he bound them. Then he said, ‘Break them,’ but he could not break them. He said, ‘O my sons, thus are you in unity, and thus are you in division.’ Then he began to recite poetry.”"],[15678,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was born in the Year of the Elephant, and between the Fijar and the Elephant were twenty years. He said: They named it the Fijar because they acted wickedly and made lawful things they had forbidden. Between the Fijar and the building of the Kaaba were fifteen years, and between the building of the Kaaba and the sending of the Prophet ﷺ were five years. So our Prophet ﷺ was sent when he was forty years old."],[15679,"“I and the Messenger of Allah were born in the Year of the Elephant, so we are of the same age.”"],[15680,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, in how many days should I recite the Quran? He said, “In fifteen.” He said, “I find myself stronger than that.” He said, “In a week.” He said, “I find myself stronger than that.” He continued reciting it like that for a time until he grew old and used to bandage his eyes. Then he reverted and used to recite it in fifteen days. He said, “Would that I had accepted the first concession of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[15681,"Abu Malik al-Janbi 'Amr b. Hashim narrated to us: Muslim al-Mula'i narrated to us, from Mujahid, who said: I used to lead my master Qays b. al-Sa'ib, and he would say: Has the sun declined? When I said yes, he prayed Zuhr. And he would say: This is what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do. The Prophet ﷺ used to pray 'Asr while the sun was white and lively. The Prophet ﷺ used to pray Maghrib while a fasting person would wonder whether to break his fast. And the Prophet ﷺ used to pray Fajr when light spread over the sky."],[15682,"The year of drought forced Nabigha of Banu Ja'da to come to 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr while he was sitting in Madinah, and he recited poetry to him in the mosque."],[15683,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorced Hafsah with one divorce. Her two maternal uncles, Qudamah and 'Uthman, the sons of Maz'un, came to her. She said: By Allah, he did not divorce me out of satiety. The Prophet ﷺ came and entered, and she covered herself with her garment. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Jibril ﷺ came to me and said: \"Take Hafsah back, for she fasts much and prays much, and she will be your wife in Paradise.\""],[15684,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was in Madinah, until the stars became visible to them. The Prophet ﷺ stood and prayed two rakʿahs, prolonging the standing. When he finished his prayer, he turned to the people and said: “When you see any of these signs, it is only a warning from God ﷻ. When you see them, pray like the most recent prayer you have prayed.”"],[15685,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “After me there will be rulers over you who delay the prayers. The prayers are for you and against them. So pray with them as long as they pray facing the qiblah with you.”"],[15686,"that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Perform the Fajr prayer when it is light, for it is greater in reward.\""],[15687,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When Allah loves a servant, He protects him from the world just as one of you guards his sick one from water.\""],[15688,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When Allah ﷻ decreed His creation, He lay on His back, placed one of His legs over the other, and said: 'It is not appropriate for anyone of My creation to do this.'\" Abū Saʿīd said, \"No doubt, by Allah, I will never do it.\""],[15689,"Abu Muslim, a shaykh who used to be in the mosque of Hammam, narrated to us from Qatadah, from Muʿawiyah b. Qurrah, from his father, who said: “In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we used to be driven away from praying between the pillars.”"],[15690,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about vessels. He said: “Vessels do not make anything forbidden. So soak [dates or raisins] in whatever you wish, but avoid every intoxicant.”"],[15691,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I slaughter a sheep and I feel compassion for it.' He said, 'And the sheep—if you show compassion to it, Allah will show compassion to you.'"],[15692,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I take a sheep to slaughter it and I feel compassion for it.' He said, 'And the sheep—if you show compassion to it, Allah will show compassion to you.'"],[15693,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The superiority of Aishah over women is like the superiority of tharid over all other foods.”"],[15694,"When the Prophet of God ﷺ sat, a group of his companions would sit with him. Among them was a man who had a small son who would come to him from behind his back and sit in front of him, until the boy died. The man then refrained from attending the circle, remembering God and grieving over him. The Prophet ﷺ missed him and said, “Why do I not see so-and-so?” They said, “O Messenger of God, his young son whom you saw has died, and that has kept him from attending the circle.” The Prophet ﷺ met him and asked about him, and was told that he had died. He consoled him, then said, “O so-and-so, which would you prefer: to enjoy him for your entire life, or that tomorrow you will not come to any gate of the gates of Paradise except that you find him already there ahead of you, opening it for you?” He said, “O Prophet of God, that he precedes me to the gates of Paradise and opens them for me is dearer to me.” He said, “That is yours.” A man from the Ansar stood up and said, “O Messenger of God, may God make me your ransom, is this for so-and-so specifically, or for every Muslim whose child has died as a forerunner?” He said, “Rather, for every Muslim whose child has died as a forerunner, that will be his.”"],[15695,"I went to embrace Islam when the Prophet ﷺ was sent, and I wanted to bring with me two or three men into Islam. I came to the watering place where people gathered, and there I saw the shepherd of the village who tended their sheep. He said, “I will not tend your sheep for you.” They said, “Why?” He said, “A wolf comes every night and takes a sheep, while this idol of ours stands there, causing no harm, bringing no benefit, changing nothing, and disapproving of nothing.” They returned, and I hoped they would embrace Islam. When morning came, the shepherd came running, saying, “Good news! Good news! The wolf came and is now bound before the idol.” I went with them, and they kissed it and prostrated to it, saying, “This is what you should do.” Then I went to the Prophet ﷺ and told him this story. He said, “Satan toyed with them.”"],[15696,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The earth will be filled with oppression and injustice as it was filled with equity and justice, until God sends a man from me whose name is my name and whose father’s name is my father’s name. He will fill it with equity and justice as it was filled with oppression and injustice. He will remain among you seven or eight years; if more, then nine. The sky will not withhold any of its rain, nor the earth any of its vegetation.”"],[15697,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: “Whoever is near death and places his will in accordance with the Book of God, that will be an expiation for what he neglected of his zakat during his life.”"],[15698,"I heard 'Abd al-Malik b. Marwan say to Qabath b. Ashyam al-Laythi, \"O Qabath, are you older or the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" He replied, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ is greater than I, and I am older than him. The Messenger of God ﷺ was born in the Year of the Elephant, and he was sent as a prophet at the head of forty years from the Elephant.\""],[15699,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ delivering a sermon on the evening of 'Arafah wearing a Yemeni striped garment."],[15700,"I entered a trellis in Madinah where Qarazah b. Ka'b and Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari were, and he mentioned a hadith of theirs in which they said, \"And we have been given a concession to weep at times of calamity, without wailing.\""],[15701,"A questioner asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying, \"If an aggressor attacks me,\" and he ordered him to fight him. He said, \"What about us?\" He ﷺ said, \"If he kills you, you will be in Paradise; and if you kill him, he will be in the Fire.\""],[15702,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out with Abu Bakr, hiding from Quraysh, and they passed by a shepherd. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Is there a ewe that has been mounted by a ram?” He said, “No, but here is a ewe that hardship has left behind.” He said, “Bring it to me.” So he brought it to him, and he wiped its udder and prayed for blessing, then milked it and gave Abu Bakr to drink. Then he milked again and gave the shepherd to drink, then he milked and drank. The shepherd said, “By Allah, I have never seen the like of you. Who are you?” He said, “If I tell you, will you keep it secret from me?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “I am Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Are you the one whom Quraysh claim is a Sabian?” He said, “They say that.” He said, “I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah, and none but a messenger is able to do what you did.” Then he said, “Shall I follow you?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Not today, but when you hear that we have prevailed, then come to us.” So he came to the Prophet ﷺ after he had become victorious in Madinah."],[15703,"From ‘Urwah, in naming those who attended the ‘Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Mazin b. al-Najjar: Qays b. Abi Sa‘sa‘ah, and he attended Badr. Abu Sa‘sa‘ah’s name was ‘Amr b. Zayd b. ‘Awf b. Mabdhul."],[15704,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, in naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from the Khazraj, then from Banu Mazin b. al-Najjar: Qays b. Abi Sa‘sa‘ah, and Abu Sa‘sa‘ah’s name was ‘Amr b. Zayd b. ‘Awf b. Mabdhul b. ‘Amr b. Ghanm b. Mazin b. al-Najjar."],[15705,"“There is no god but Allah. Upon this spot will be shed of the blood of Muslims something that will not be shed upon any other spot on earth.” Qays became angry and said, “What makes you know that, O Abu Ishaq? Is this not from the unseen which Allah has kept to Himself?” Ka‘b said, “There is nothing on earth except that it is written in the Torah which Allah sent down to Moses—what will happen upon it and what will come forth from it until the Day of Resurrection.” Muhammad b. Yazid said, “Who is Qays b. Kharashah?” He said, “A man from Qays. Do you not know him? He is a man from your land.” He said, “By Allah, I do not know him.” He said, “Qays b. Kharashah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ‘I pledge allegiance to you upon what has come to you from Allah and upon speaking the truth.’ The Prophet ﷺ said, ‘O Qays, if time extends for you and after me you are ruled by governors with whom you cannot speak the truth.’ Qays said, ‘By Allah, I will not pledge allegiance to you upon anything except that I fulfill it for you.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Then nothing will harm you.’” He said, “Qays used to criticize Ziyad and his son ‘Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad. So ‘Ubayd Allah sent for him and said, ‘Are you the one who fabricates lies against Allah and His Messenger?’ He said, ‘No, but if you wish I will tell you who fabricates lies against Allah and His Messenger: the one who abandons acting upon the Book of Allah ﷻ and the Sunnah of His Messenger ﷺ.’”"],[15706,"The position of Qays b. Sa‘d with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was like that of the chief of police with a commander."],[15707,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Makkah, Qays b. Sa‘d was in his vanguard before him, in the position of the chief of police. The Prophet ﷺ was spoken to about Qays, to remove him from the place where he had stationed him, for fear that he might go too far in something. So he removed him from that."],[15708,"Qays b. Saʿd al-Anṣārī, who was the bearer of the Messenger of God's ﷺ standard, intended to perform the pilgrimage. He combed one side of his head, and then saw that his sacrificial animal had been garlanded, so he entered the state of iḥrām and left the other side uncombed."],[15709,"I was with Qays b. Saʿd, who had served the Prophet ﷺ for ten years. He performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. I will never forget the trace of his finger on the socks, because they were new."],[15710,"Abū Bakr: By God, I did not sleep last night—or as he said—because of him. So come with us to Qays b. Saʿd and let us speak to him about his brother. They went to him and spoke to him. Qays said: As for anything Saʿd has already carried out, I will never reverse it. But I call you both to witness that my share belongs to him."],[15711,"Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah divided his wealth among his sons and then passed away while his wife was pregnant, and he did not know about her pregnancy. She gave birth to a boy. Umar and Abu Bakr sent for Qais ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah regarding this matter. Qais said, \"As for what Sa'd divided and executed, I will not reconsider it, but my share is for him.\" I asked, \"Did he divide according to the Book of Allah?\" He said, \"We found that they would not divide except according to the Book of Allah.\""],[15712,"He informed him of this report, the report of Qays b. Saʿd, that he divided his wealth among his sons and then departed to Syria and died."],[15713,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to do it before the zakāt was revealed. Then he neither commanded us nor forbade us, and we still do it."],[15714,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to fast on ʿĀshūrāʾ before the month of Ramaḍān was revealed. When the month of Ramaḍān was revealed, he neither commanded us nor forbade us, and we still fast it. He also commanded us to give the zakāt al-fiṭr, and when the zakāt was revealed, he neither commanded us nor forbade us, and we still give it."],[15715,"Before Ramaḍān was revealed, and when Ramaḍān was revealed, we were neither commanded nor forbidden from it, and we used to fast it. We were also commanded to give half a ṣāʿ for every person—free or slave, young or old, male or female. When the zakāt was revealed, we were neither commanded nor forbidden from it, and we used to give it."],[15716,"The Prophet ﷺ came to us, and we placed water for him. Then he bathed, and we brought him a wars-dyed wrap, and he covered himself with it. It is as if I can still see the trace of the wars on his folds."],[15717,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to Saʿd's house and stood at its door. He greeted with salām, and Saʿd responded and lowered his voice. Then he greeted, and Saʿd responded and lowered his voice. Then he greeted, and Saʿd responded and lowered his voice. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ turned back, and Saʿd followed him, hurrying after him. He said: O Messenger of God, may my father and mother be your ransom. By God, nothing prevented me from responding to your greeting except that I wanted you to give us more of your greetings. Then he entered and placed water to cool down and bathed. He was brought a wrap dyed with wars, and he put it on. I saw the stain of wars on his folds. Then he came and sat down and said: O God, bless the Anṣār and the descendants of the Anṣār and the descendants of the descendants of the Anṣār. When he wanted to leave, a donkey was brought to him, and he placed on it a velvet cloth that was neither silk nor wool. Saʿd sent his son with him to return the donkey. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Carry him in front of me.\" Saʿd said: O Messenger of God, should I carry him in front of you? He said: \"Yes, he is more entitled to the front of his donkey.\" Saʿd said: O Messenger of God, the donkey is yours. He said: \"Carry him behind me.\""],[15718,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, Ḥusayn b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḍumayrah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Qays b. Saʿd b. ʿUbādah b. Daylam, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The owner of the mount is more entitled to its front.\""],[15719,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: The owner of the mount is more entitled to its front. Ḥabīb said: I am not ignorant of what the Messenger of God ﷺ said, but I fear for you."],[15720,"My father sent me to the Prophet ﷺ to serve him. He came to me after I had prayed two rakʿahs—or he said the two rakʿahs—while I was lying down, and he nudged me with his foot and said: \"Shall I not show you a gate from the gates of Paradise?\" I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: \"There is no power and no strength except with God.\""],[15721,"My father sent me to the Prophet ﷺ to serve him. He came upon me after I had prayed two rakʿahs, tapped me with his foot, and said, “Shall I not point you to a gate among the gates of Paradise?” I said, “Indeed, O Messenger of God.” He said, “There is no might and no power except with God.”"],[15722,"I came to al-Ḥīrah and saw them prostrating to a governor of theirs. So I said, “O Messenger of God, you are more deserving that we prostrate to you.” He said, “Do not do so. If I were to command that, I would command women to prostrate to their husbands because of the right God has placed upon them toward them.”"],[15723,"There was nothing in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ except that I saw it. Indeed, singing and clapping was performed for the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Eid, and taqlīs means jesting and playing."],[15724,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “My Lord has forbidden me wine, the kūbah drum, and singing slave-girls.” Then he said, “Beware of al-ghubayrāʾ, for it is wine.”"],[15725,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is forbidden.”"],[15726,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “The greatest usury is for a man to overstep in insulting his brother, and the greatest of major sins is for a man to insult his parents.” They said, “How could he insult them, O Messenger of God?” He said, “He insults a man, who then insults them.”"],[15727,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “If faith were suspended from the Pleiades, men from Persia would attain it.”"],[15728,"The Messenger of God ﷺ visited us in our home and said, “Peace be upon you and the mercy of God.” Saʿd returned the greeting softly. Then he said, “Peace be upon you and the mercy of God,” and Saʿd returned the greeting softly. Then he said, “Peace be upon you and the mercy of God,” and Saʿd returned the greeting softly. The Messenger of God ﷺ then turned back. Saʿd followed him and said, “O Messenger of God, I could hear your greeting and would return it softly so that you would give us more greetings.” His guest, the Messenger of God ﷺ, then departed. Saʿd ordered the spot to be washed, and it was washed, and he performed a full bath. Then a woman handed him—or he handed her—a wrap dyed with wars and saffron, and he wrapped himself in it. The Messenger of God ﷺ raised his hands, saying, “O God, place Your blessings and mercy upon the family of Saʿd b. ʿUbādah.” Then he ate some food. When he wanted to depart, Saʿd brought a donkey and placed a velvet cloth on it, and the Messenger of God ﷺ mounted. Saʿd said, “O Qays, accompany the Messenger of God ﷺ.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “O Qays, ride.” I declined. Then he said, “Either mount or depart.” So I departed."],[15729,"The Prophet ﷺ came to us at the market and said, “O company of merchants, indeed this market is accompanied by swearing, so mix it with charity.”"],[15730,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us at the market and said, “O company of merchants, indeed this market is attended by idle talk and swearing, so mix it with charity.”"],[15731,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us at the market while we were called brokers. He named us with a better name than we named ourselves, saying, “O company of merchants, indeed swearing and idle talk mix with your selling, so mix it with charity.”"],[15732,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us in the market while we were selling slaves in the city and we called ourselves brokers. He called us by a better name than what we called ourselves and said: \"O merchants, this trade is accompanied by buying and swearing, so purify it with charity.\""],[15733,"We used to trade in Madinah and call ourselves brokers. The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us and named us with a better name than we had named ourselves, saying, “O company of merchants, indeed this selling is attended by idle talk and swearing, so mix it with something of charity.”"],[15734,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were selling in the market and we were calling ourselves brokers (al-samāsirah). He said, “O company of merchants, indeed this market of yours is mixed with idle talk, so mix it with charity, or with some charity.” The wording is that of the hadith of ʿAlī b. al-Jaʿd."],[15735,"On the authority of Qays b. Abī Gharazah: “They used to be called brokers (al-samāsirah).”"],[15736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were called brokers (al-samāsirah), and he said, “O company of merchants, indeed this selling is attended by idle talk and swearing, so mix it with charity.”"],[15737,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the merchants while they were called by a name that he changed. He said, “O company of merchants, indeed your selling is attended by idle talk and oaths, so mix it with some charity.” The wording is that of the hadith of Ḥajjāj."],[15738,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were trading in the market, and he said, “O company of merchants.” The people rejoiced and craned their necks toward him. We used to be called brokers (al-samāsirah), and he was the first to call us merchants. He said, “Indeed the devil and sin attend the sale, so mix your selling with charity.”"],[15739,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while we were trading in al-ʿAqīq, and we used to be called brokers (al-samāsirah). He called us by a name that was better than what we called ourselves, and he said, “O company of merchants, indeed this selling is attended by swearing and lying, so mix it with some charity.”"],[15740,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were called brokers (al-samāsirah), and he said to us, “O company of merchants, indeed this selling of yours is attended by swearing and the devil, so mix it with charity.”"],[15741,"We used to trade in the market in Madinah and call ourselves brokers (al-samāsirah). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and called us by a better name than what we had called ourselves, and he said, “O company of merchants, indeed this selling is attended by idle talk and swearing, so mix it with some charity”—meaning mix it, combine it."],[15742,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O company of merchants, selling is attended by swearing and lying, so mix it with charity.”"],[15743,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man selling food and said, “O owner of this food, is the bottom of this like its top?” He said, “Yes.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever deceives the Muslims is not one of them.”"],[15744,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Choose four of them.”"],[15745,"I embraced Islam while I had eight wives, and they embraced Islam with me and emigrated with me. He said, “Choose four of them.” I began to say to the one I wanted to keep, “Come forward,” and to the one I did not want to keep, “Turn away.”"],[15746,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon from a crop-eared she-camel, while an Abyssinian was holding its reins."],[15747,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon from a crop-eared she-camel, its nose-rein held by an Abyssinian slave."],[15748,"He said: I passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was performing ablution, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has given us much good through you. He washed his palms, then rinsed his mouth three times, and snuffed water three times, washed his face three times, and his forearms three times, and wiped his head without specifying a number, and the tops of his feet without specifying a number. Then he said: \"O Abu Kahil, put the purification in its proper places, and keep the leftover water of your purification for your family. Do not leave your family thirsty, and do not burden your servant.\""],[15749,"Harsh words occurred between two men of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until they came to blows. I met one of them and said: What is the matter between you and so-and-so? I heard him speak well of you and make much supplication for you. Then I met the other and said something similar. I continued going back and forth between them until they reconciled. Then I said: What have I done? I have destroyed myself and reconciled them. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of the matter. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, I heard nothing from this one or that one. He said: \"O Abu Kahil, reconcile between people even with such-and-such\" — a word I did not understand. I said: What did he mean by it? He said: He meant lying."],[15750,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"O Abu Kahil, shall I inform you of a decree that Allah has decreed upon Himself?\" I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"May Allah keep your heart alive and not let it die until your body dies. Know...\""],[15751,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"O Abu Kahil, shall I inform you of a decree that Allah has decreed upon Himself?\" I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"May Allah keep your heart alive and not let it die until your body dies. Know...\""],[15752,"I heard Qays b. al-Sa'ib say: \"A person may make up for the month of Ramadan by feeding a poor person each day. So feed a poor person on my behalf for each day, one sa'. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was my business partner in the pre-Islamic period, and he was the best partner; he did not argue or dispute.\""],[15753,"About fasting, so he fed on his behalf."],[15754,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever fasts a day voluntarily, a tree is planted for him in Paradise; its fruit is smaller than a pomegranate and larger than an apple; its sweetness is like the sweetness of honey, and its taste is like the taste of honey. Allah will feed the fasting person from it on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[15755,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts a day voluntarily, a tree is planted for him in Paradise, its fruit smaller than a pomegranate and larger than an apple, its sweetness like the sweetness of honeycomb, and its taste like the taste of honey; God will feed the fasting person from it on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[15756,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts a day voluntarily, a tree is planted for him in Paradise, its fruit smaller than a pomegranate and larger than an apple, its sweetness like the sweetness of honeycomb, and its taste like the taste of honey; God will feed the fasting person from it on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[15757,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw a man praying two rakʿahs after the morning prayer, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The morning prayer twice?” The man said: “I had not prayed the two rakʿahs before it, so I prayed them now.” The Prophet ﷺ remained silent."],[15758,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was praying two rakʿahs after the morning prayer, so he said: “What is this prayer?” I said: “I had not prayed the two rakʿahs of dawn, and these two are those.” The Messenger of God ﷺ remained silent."],[15759,"He entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was praying, and he had not prayed the two rakʿahs, so he prayed with the Prophet ﷺ. When he finished his prayer, he stood and prayed the two rakʿahs of dawn. The Prophet ﷺ saw him and said: “O Qays, what are these two?” He informed him of what he had done, and the Prophet ﷺ did not disapprove of that."],[15760,"Qabīṣah b. Mukhāriq al-Hilālī came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and greeted him. He returned the greeting, welcomed him, then said to him: “What has brought you, O Qabīṣah?” He said: “O Messenger of God, my age has advanced, my skin has become thin, my strength has weakened, I have become a burden on my family, and I am unable to do things I used to do. Teach me words through which God may benefit me, and be brief.” He ﷺ said: “O Qabīṣah, say three times when you pray the morning prayer: ‘Glory be to God, and with His praise; glory be to God, the Magnificent, and with His praise; and there is no might nor power except with God.’ For if you say that, you will be safe, by God’s permission, from blindness, leprosy, and vitiligo. And say: ‘O God, guide me from Yourself, pour upon me from Your bounty, spread over me from Your mercy, and send down upon me from Your blessings.’” The Messenger of God ﷺ began to say them while Qabīṣah counted them on his fingers."],[15761,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Verily, ʿiyāfah, ṭarq, and ṭīrah are from al-jibt.”"],[15762,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “ʿIyāfah, ṭarq, and ṭīrah are from al-jibt.”"],[15763,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “ʿIyāfah, ṭarq, and ṭīrah are from shirk.”"],[15764,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “ʿIyāfah, ṭarq, and ṭīrah are from al-jibt.” ʿAwf said: “ʿIyāfah is the chasing away of birds, and ṭarq is drawing lines in the ground.”"],[15765,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “ʿIyāfah, ṭīrah, and ṭarq are from al-jibt.”"],[15766,"Kinānah: I said to him, “You are the chief of your people, and they came to you asking, but you did not give them anything.” He said, “As for this, I will not give anything. If he were bitten by a strap until it dried him out, it would be better for him than asking people in such a case. I will tell you about that. I undertook a guarantee of payment for my people, so I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, ‘O Messenger of God, I have undertaken a guarantee of payment for my people, and I have come to you so that you may help me with it.’ He said, ‘Rather we will carry it on your behalf, O Qabīṣah, and pay it to them from zakāt.’ Then he said, ‘O Qabīṣah, begging is forbidden except in one of three cases: a man who is struck by a calamity that destroys his wealth, so he asks until he obtains a means of livelihood, then he refrains; a man who is struck by need until three men of sound judgment from his people testify that begging has become lawful for him, so he asks until he obtains a means of livelihood, then he refrains; and a man who undertakes a guarantee of payment, so he asks until he reaches the amount, then he refrains. Anything other than that is illicit gain, which he consumes as illicit gain.’”"],[15767,"I incurred a liability, so I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ to ask him about it. He said: “Stay, O Qabīṣah, until the zakāh comes, then we will give you from it.” Then he said: “O Qabīṣah, begging is not lawful except for one of three: a man who incurs a liability, so begging becomes lawful for him until he obtains it, then he refrains; and a man afflicted by poverty until three men of sound judgment among his people say, ‘So-and-so has been afflicted by poverty,’ so begging becomes lawful for him until he obtains a means of livelihood — or he said: a sufficiency of livelihood. Other than these, begging is unlawful gain, O Qabīṣah; its eater consumes unlawful gain.”"],[15768,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ to ask him about a liability. He said: “Stay until the zakāh comes to us, and either we will give you or we will assume it on your behalf.” Then he said about it: “Begging is not lawful except for three: a man who incurs a liability between people and asks for it until he pays it off, then refrains; and a man afflicted by need until three men of sound judgment among his people testify that he has been afflicted by what makes it lawful — or he said: begging becomes lawful for him — so it is lawful until he obtains a means of livelihood or a sufficiency of livelihood, then he refrains. Other than that, begging is unlawful gain, O Qabīṣah; its eater consumes unlawful gain.” The wording is from the hadith of Ibn ʿUlayyah."],[15769,"On behalf of my people, so I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, I have incurred a liability on behalf of my people, so help me with it.” He said: “Rather, we will assume it on your behalf, O Qabīṣah. It is yours from the zakāh when it comes.” Then he said: “O Qabīṣah, begging is not lawful except for one of three: a man who incurs a liability on behalf of his people, seeking reconciliation, so he asks, and when he reaches the amount, he refrains; and a man afflicted by poverty, so three men of sound judgment among his people come forward and he asks until he obtains a means or a sufficiency, then he refrains. Other than that, O Qabīṣah, begging is unlawful gain,” twice."],[15770,"And from Qabīṣah b. Mukhāriq al-Hilālī, they both said: When this verse was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ: “And warn your closest kindred,” the Prophet of God ﷺ went to a rock on a mountain and climbed onto its highest stone, then said: “O Banū ʿAbd Manāf, I am a warner. My likeness and yours is only that of a man who saw the enemy and went to warn his family, fearing that they would be taken before he reached them, so he began shouting: ‘O my companions, O my companions, you have been attacked, you have been attacked.’”"],[15771,"I heard Qabīṣah b. Burmah say: I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when I heard him say: “The people of good in this world are the people of good in the Hereafter, and the people of evil in this world are the people of evil in the Hereafter.”"],[15772,"From ʿUrwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū Sawād b. Kaʿb — whose name is Kaʿb Ẓufur —: Qatādah b. al-Nuʿmān b. Zayd."],[15773,"From Ibn Shihāb, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū Ẓufur: Qatādah b. al-Nuʿmān."],[15774,"From Muḥammad b. Isḥāq, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Aws, then from Banū Ẓufur: Qatādah b. al-Nuʿmān b. Zayd b. ʿĀmir b. Sawād b. Kaʿb b. Ẓufur b. al-Khazraj b. ʿAmr b. al-Aws."],[15775,"And it is said: Khazamah."],[15776,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had forbidden eating the meat of sacrificial animals after three days. I went on a journey and returned to my family, and there was the woman with a basket containing dried meat that she had brought me. I said to her: “Where did you get this dried meat?” She said: “From the sacrifices.” We said: “Did the Messenger of God ﷺ not forbid us to eat them after three days?” She said: “He has permitted eating them.” I was not satisfied with her words until I went to my brother Qatādah b. al-Nuʿmān and asked him about that. He sent to me: “Eat your food, for the Messenger of God ﷺ has permitted that.” So I ate it."],[15777,"that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever fasts the Day of ʿArafah, a year ahead of him and a year behind him are forgiven.\""],[15778,"that when he came to his family from a journey, he found with them a large bowl of tharīd made from the meat of sacrificial animals, and he refused to eat it. He went to Qatādah b. al-Nuʿmān and informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the people during the time of Hajj: \"I had commanded you not to eat the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days so that people might be satiated. Now I make it lawful for you, so eat as you wish.\""],[15779,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever fasts the Day of ʿArafah, a year ahead of him and a year behind him are forgiven.\""],[15780,"It was a night of intense darkness and rain. I thought, if only I could take advantage of this night by attending ʿIshāʾ with the Prophet ﷺ. So I did. When the Prophet ﷺ finished, he saw me, and he had a palm branch on which he leaned while walking. He said, \"What brings you here at this hour, O Qatādah?\" I said, \"I took the opportunity to attend the prayer with you, O Messenger of Allah.\" He gave me the palm branch and said, \"Indeed, Satan has taken your place with your family. Go with this palm branch, take hold of it until you reach your house, then take it from behind the house and strike him with the palm branch.\" I left the mosque, and the palm branch lit up like a candle with light. I used it for light and came to my family, and I found them asleep. I looked in the corner, and there was a hedgehog in it. I kept striking it with the palm branch until it went out."],[15781,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Gently, O Qatādah, do not revile Quraysh. Soon you will see men among them whose deeds will make your deeds seem insignificant in comparison, and whose actions will make your actions seem insignificant, were it not that Quraysh might transgress, I would inform them of what they have with Allah.\""],[15782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah sent Gabriel to me in the best form that he used to come to me. He said, 'Peace be upon you, O Muhammad, and he said, 'Indeed, I have revealed to the world that you pass by and they become distressed, constrained, and oppressed, and you remain steadfast with my allies until they love to meet me, and you make it easy and spacious and fragrant for my enemies until they hate to meet me. Indeed, I have made it a prison for my allies and a paradise for my enemies.'\""],[15783,"A bow was given to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he handed it to me on the day of Uhud. I shot with it in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until it broke at its string notch. I remained at my post in front of the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, facing the arrows with my face. Whenever an arrow headed toward the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I tilted my head to shield the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ without shooting any arrow myself. The last of them was an arrow from which my eyeball protruded onto my cheek. The ranks dispersed, and I took my eyeball in my hand and hastened with it in my hand to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw it in my hand, his eyes shed tears, and he said: \"O Allah, Qatādah has shielded the face of Your Prophet with his face, so make it the best of his two eyes and the sharpest in sight.\" So it became the best of his two eyes and the sharpest in sight."],[15784,"\"On the day of Uhud, I stood facing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, shielding the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with my face. Abū Dujānah Simāk b. Kharashah shielded the back of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his back until his back was filled with arrows. That was on the day of Uhud.\""],[15785,"On the day of Uhud, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Who will take this sword with its right?\" ʿAlī stood up and said, \"I will, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Sit down.\" So he sat. Then he said a second time: \"Who will take this sword with its right?\" Abū Dujānah stood up the second time, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ handed him his sword Dhū al-Faqār. Abū Dujānah stood up, tied a red band around his eyes, raised his eyebrows over his eyes out of pride, then walked before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with the sword."],[15787,"I went out one night, while it was dark, and I said to myself, \"If only I could go to the Prophet ﷺ so that I could pray with him and have a private conversation with him.\" So, I did just that. When I entered the mosque, the sky lit up and the Prophet ﷺ saw me and said, \"O Qatadah, what has brought you here?\" I replied, \"I wanted to be comforted by you instead of my parents.\" He said, \"Take this staff and use it as a walking stick, for it will light up ten steps in front of you and ten steps behind you.\" Then he said, \"When you enter your home, strike it on the ground like the sturdiest stone on a person's chest, as that will repel the devil.\" So, I left and it illuminated my way, then I struck it on the ground as the sturdiest stone until the devil left my house."],[15788,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and embraced Islam. He said to me: \"O Qatādah, bathe with water and lotus leaves, and shave off the hair of disbelief from yourself.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command whoever embraced Islam to be circumcised, and he was eighty years old."],[15789,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The servant will continue to be in an expansion of his religion as long as he does not drink wine. When he drinks it, God tears away His covering from him, and Satan becomes his guardian, his hearing, his sight, and his leg, driving him to every evil and turning him away from every good.”"],[15790,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ appointed me over my people, I took his hand and bade him farewell. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “May God make piety your provision, forgive your sin, and direct you toward good wherever you may be.”"],[15791,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command us to fast the days of the white nights: the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth, and he said, “That is the fast of the age.” And their wording is the same."],[15792,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he used to command us to fast the white nights: the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth, and he would say, “The fast of the age, or of the like of the fast of the age.” This is how Shuʿbah reported it from Anas, from ʿAbd al-Malik b. al-Minhal, from his father, and he erred in it; the correct version is the hadith of Hammām."],[15793,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite in the dawn prayer, “And tall palm trees” (Qāf 50:10)."],[15794,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ recite in the first rakʿah of the dawn prayer, “And tall palm trees with arranged fruit clusters” (Qāf 50:10)."],[15795,"That he prayed the dawn prayer with the Prophet ﷺ, and he recited, “And tall palm trees” (Qāf 50:10)."],[15796,"I prayed the dawn prayer with the Prophet ﷺ, and he recited in the first rakʿah, “Qāf. By the glorious Quran” (Qāf 50:1)."],[15797,"I prayed the dawn prayer with the Prophet ﷺ, and he recited, “And tall palm trees” (Qāf 50:10)."],[15798,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ recite in the dawn prayer, “Qāf. By the glorious Quran” (Qāf 50:1). When he reached, “And tall palm trees with arranged fruit clusters” (Qāf 50:10), I said to myself, “What drives them?”"],[15799,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ recite in the dawn prayer, “And tall palm trees with arranged fruit clusters” (Qāf 50:10)."],[15800,"I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ and heard him recite, “And tall palm trees with arranged fruit clusters” (Qāf 50:10)."],[15801,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite in the morning prayer: “And tall date-palms with ranged clusters.” (Qaf 50:10)"],[15802,"I prayed the dawn prayer behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he recited Qaf. By the Glorious Quran until he reached: “And tall date-palms with ranged clusters.” (Qaf 50:10). I kept repeating it, not knowing what he said."],[15803,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite Qaf in the first rakʿah of the dawn prayer."],[15804,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to say, \"O Allah, divert from me the evils of manners, actions, desires, and diseases.\""],[15805,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, stretch out your hand so that I may pledge allegiance to you for myself and for my daughter al-Huwaysilah, even if I have lied against God and deceived you.” He said: “Khalid b. al-Walid fell upon us with his cavalry, and we said: ‘We are Muslims,’ so he left us. We then raided al-Ubullah with him and divided its spoils, filling our hands.”"],[15806,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ break the fast when the sun set."],[15807,"Concerning praying between the pillars in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[15808,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ in a group from Muzaynah, and we pledged allegiance to him. I had put my hand through the opening of his shirt and touched the seal. ʿUrwah said: “I never saw Muʿawiyah or his son in winter or summer except with their lower garments loosened, never fastening them.” The wording is that of the hadith of ʿAli b. ʿAbd al-ʿAziz."],[15809,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, touched the seal between his shoulder blades, and kissed his hands. Then he came and said: “From which tribe are you?” I said: “From Muzaynah.”"],[15810,"O Messenger of Allah, if a sheep lies down for me to slaughter it and I feel mercy for it? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By the sheep, if you show it mercy, God will show you mercy.”"],[15811,"To the Prophet ﷺ: “I slaughter a sheep and feel mercy for it.” He said: “By the sheep, if you show it mercy, God will show you mercy.”"],[15812,"The Prophet sent his grandfather Muawiya to a man who married the wife of his father, and he had him killed and confiscated his wealth."],[15813,"From his father: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'Show me the seal.' So I put my hand into the collar of his shirt until I placed my hand on it."],[15814,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and put my hand into his collar opening. He did not stop making supplication for me while I was touching the seal. I saw on his shoulders something like a wen—the seal of prophethood."],[15815,"We lived through a period of our time with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we had no food except the two black things: dates and water."],[15816,"'O my son, if you are in a gathering whose good you hope for, and a need causes you to hurry away, and you say, \"Peace be upon you,\" then you will be their partner in whatever they attain in that gathering.'"],[15817,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Fasting the white days is the fasting of the whole age and its breaking of the fast.'"],[15818,"A man used to visit the Prophet ﷺ and he had a son with him. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'Do you love him?' He said, 'May Allah love you as I love him.' Then his son died. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Where is so-and-so?' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, his son has died.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'Would it not please you that you will not come to any gate among the gates of Paradise except that he will come until he opens it for you?' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, is that for him specifically or for all of us?' He said, 'No, rather for all of you.' And the wording is that of the hadith of 'Amr b. Marzuq."],[15819,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'A group of people from my ummah will continue to be victorious; those who abandon them will not harm them until the Hour begins.'"],[15820,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'When the people of Sham become corrupt, there is no good in you.'"],[15821,"That the Prophet ﷺ wiped his head and sought forgiveness for him."],[15822,"That he came to the Prophet ﷺ after he had milked and tied the udder."],[15823,"\"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, 'By Him in whose hand is my soul, they both (referring to the father and mother) have greater weight on the Day of Judgment than anyone else.'\""],[15824,"My father said: “When you pass by a gathering, greet its members. If they are engaged in good, you are their partner in it; and if they are engaged in something else, you will have a reward.” Thus I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say."],[15825,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever says ‘Allahu Akbar’ once at sunset on the seashore, raising his voice, God will grant him for every drop in the sea ten good deeds, erase from him ten evil deeds, and raise him ten degrees, the distance between each two degrees being a hundred years’ journey on a swift horse.”"],[15826,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when modesty was mentioned in his presence. They said, “O Messenger of God, is modesty part of the religion?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Rather, it is the entire religion.”"],[15827,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when modesty was mentioned in his presence. They said, “O Messenger of God, is modesty part of the religion?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Rather, it is the entire religion.”"],[15828,"I set out with my father to the Messenger of God ﷺ and found him with his buttons undone. He turned me around behind him and placed his hand on the seal [of prophethood]."],[15829,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever eats from these two plants should not come near us in our mosque. If you must eat them, then kill their odor by cooking.”"],[15830,"That he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “We used to have lords and goddesses whom we worshiped besides God. We called upon them, but they did not answer; we asked them, but they did not give. We have come to you, and God has guided us through you, so now we worship God.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Prosperous is he who has been granted sound intellect.”"],[15831,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"We used to have lords and mistresses whom we worshipped besides God. We called upon them, but they did not answer; we asked them, but they did not give. Then we came to you, and God guided us through you, so we now worship God.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"He has prospered who is granted sound intellect.\""],[15832,"An elder sat with us in Ayyub's shop, wearing a woolen cloak. He overheard people talking, so he said, \"Tell me, my master, about the Messenger of Allah.\" I said, \"Name him for me.\" He said, \"Qurrah ibn Da'mus al-Numayri.\" He said, \"I came to the city, so I went to the Messenger of Allah with people. I wanted to get close to him, but I couldn't. So I called out to him, 'O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for the young boy al-Numayri.' He said, 'May Allah forgive you.'\""],[15833,"A sheikh sat with us in the shop of Ayoub, may he be blessed with a woolen cloak. He heard some people talking and said to me, \"My lord told me about the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ .\" I said, \"Name him.\" He said, \"Qurrah bin Damoosah Al-Numairi.\" He said, \"I came to Al-Madinah and visited the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , and there were people with him. I tried to get closer to him, but I couldn't. So, I called out to him, 'O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for the boy Al-Numairi.' He said, 'May Allah forgive you.'\""],[15834,"A man from his people and others from the Arabs came to him and said, \"Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Muttalib has come out calling to a religion other than ours.\" Qabath stood up and went to the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he entered upon him, he ﷺ said to him, \"Sit down, O Qabath.\" Qabath was taken aback. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"You are the one who said, 'If the women of Quraysh came out with their sleeves, they would repel Muhammad and his companions.'\" Qabath said, \"By the One who sent you with the truth, my tongue did not move with it, nor did my lips murmur it, nor did anyone hear it from me. It was nothing but something that crossed my mind. I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.\" He ﷺ said, \"And what you have brought is truth.\""],[15835,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The prayer of two men, one of whom leads the other, is purer with God than the prayer of four praying separately; the prayer of four, one of whom leads them, is purer with God than the prayer of eight praying separately; and the prayer of eight, one of whom leads them, is purer with God than the prayer of a hundred praying separately.\""],[15836,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, \"The prayer of two men, where one of them leads the other, is more virtuous in the sight of Allah than the prayer of four men performed individually. And the prayer of four men, where one of them leads the others, is more virtuous in the sight of Allah than the prayer of eight men performed individually. And the prayer of eight men, where one of them leads the others, is more virtuous in the sight of Allah than the prayer of one hundred men performed individually.\" Ishaq ibn Rahawayh said, \"Qabath (the narrator) has fully comprehended the words of the Prophet ﷺ .\""],[15837,"From 'Urwah b. al-Zubayr, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God ﷺ from Quraysh, then from Banu Jumah: Qudamah b. Maz'un."],[15838,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pelting Jamrat al-'Aqabah on a reddish camel, with no striking, no driving, and no saying 'to you, to you.'"],[15839,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pelting Jamrat al-'Aqabah on a reddish camel of his, with no striking, no driving, and no saying 'to you, to you.'"],[15840,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pelting the Jamrah from the bottom of the valley."],[15841,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ circumambulating the House on a camel and touching the corner with his staff. This is the wording of 'Abbad b. Musa."],[15842,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Adopt the ways of Ma'add, be rough and hardy, and walk barefoot.\""],[15843,"It was said to Qutham b. al-Abbas: How did 'Ali inherit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the exclusion of al-Abbas? He said: \"Because he was the first of us to join him and the closest of us in attachment to him.\""],[15844,"It was said to Qutham b. al-Abbas: How did 'Ali inherit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to your exclusion? He said: \"He was the first of us to join him and the closest of us in attachment to him.\""],[15845,"From 'Urwah, concerning the naming of those who attended al-'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Salimah: Ka'b b. Malik b. Abi al-Qayn b. Ka'b b. Sawwad."],[15846,"From Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those who attended al-'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Salimah: Ka'b b. Malik."],[15847,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about a man, “He is from the people of the Fire.” People kept waiting to see what would happen to him until the day of Hunayn, when he fought and displayed great valor. They informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of that, and he said, “He is from the people of the Fire.” Then the man was wounded, and he took an arrow from his quiver and slit his own throat. They said, “O Messenger of Allah, Allah has confirmed your words.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Arise, Bilal, and announce that none enters Paradise except a believer, and that Allah ﷻ may support this religion even through a wicked man.”"],[15848,"From his father, who raised it to the Prophet ﷺ as I think, regarding His saying, “It is the same for us whether we grieve or are patient; we have no escape.” He said: The people of the Fire say, “Come, let us be patient.” So they are patient for five hundred years. When they see that it does not benefit them, they say, “Come, let us grieve.” They then weep for five hundred years. When they see that it does not benefit them, they say, “It is the same for us whether we grieve or are patient; we have no escape.”"],[15849,"We went out from Madinah intending [to meet] the Messenger of God ﷺ, and with us went out the pilgrim of our people from among the polytheists. Then he mentioned something similar."],[15850,"He had a debt owed to him by 'Abd Allah b. Abi Hadrad. He demanded it from him until their voices rose. The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by them and said, 'O Ka'b,' and gestured with his hand as if he meant half. So he took half of what was owed to him and left half."],[15851,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The example of the believer is like a stalk of grain that the wind turns over: at one time it knocks it down, and at another it straightens it. The example of the disbeliever is like a firmly rooted cedar tree standing on its trunk, which nothing bends until it is uprooted all at once.'"],[15852,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ eat with three fingers, then I saw him lick his three fingers when he wanted to wipe them."],[15853,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Two hungry wolves sent among a flock of sheep are not more destructive to it than a man's greed for wealth and honour is to his religion.\""],[15854,"A black slave-girl of theirs slaughtered a sheep for them with a flint. The Prophet ﷺ was asked about that, and he commanded us to eat it."],[15855,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him and Aws b. al-Hadathan during the days of Tashriq, and he called out: \"Truly, none will enter Paradise except a believer, and the days of Mina are days of eating and drinking.\""],[15856,"Ka'b b. Malik: The Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he was reciting poetry."],[15857,"A slave-girl came tending sheep for me, and a wolf ate a sheep. I struck the slave-girl's face, then I regretted it and came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. I said: \"O Messenger of God, if I knew she was a believer I would set her free.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to the slave-girl: \"Who am I?\" She said: \"The Messenger of God.\" He said: \"And who is God?\" She said: \"The One who is in the heaven.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Set her free, for she is a believer.\""],[15858,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"People must stop raising their eyes to the sky [during supplication in prayer], or their eyesight will be snatched away.\""],[15859,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever seeks knowledge for one of three things—to contend with fools by it, to boast with it before scholars, or to attract people’s attention to himself—\" then he said concerning it harsh words."],[15860,"When the day of Uhud came and we reached the mountain pass, I was the first to recognize him. I said, 'This is the Messenger of God ﷺ.' He gestured to me with his hand to be silent. Then he put his armor on me and wore my armor. I was struck until I received twenty or he said 'some ten odd wounds,' everyone who struck me thought I was the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[15861,"Twelve men from the Aqabah pledge, and the Messenger of God ﷺ had commanded them to bring him seventy men the following year. We stayed for a year, one of us going to his companion with provisions, riding gear, and food until seventy men from us came to him."],[15862,"Ka'b: I was never in a military expedition in which I had more ease in mounts and provisions than in that expedition. When the Messenger of God ﷺ set out, I said, 'I will prepare tomorrow and then catch up with him.' I began my preparations, but evening came and I had not finished. Then I said, 'I will work hard on my preparations tomorrow, and the people are still near—I will catch up with them.' Evening came and I had not finished. When the third day came, I began my preparations, evening came and I had not finished. I said, 'How far! The people have traveled for three days.' So I stayed behind. When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned, people began making excuses to him. I came and stood before him and said, 'I was never in an expedition in which I had more ease in mounts and provisions than in this one.' The Messenger of God ﷺ turned away from me and commanded the people not to speak to us, and commanded our women to stay away from us. One day I climbed over a wall and found Jabir b. Abdullah there. I said, 'O Jabir, I adjure you by God: do you know that I ever betrayed God and His Messenger even for a single day?' He remained silent and would not speak to me. Then one day, while I was in that state, I heard a man on the hill path calling, 'Ka'b! Ka'b!' He approached me and said, 'Give good news to Ka'b.'"],[15863,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was detaining a debtor of mine. He gestured to me with his hand and said, 'O Ka'b, take half and leave half.'"],[15864,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever visits a sick person plunges into mercy, and when he sits with him, he intercedes for him therein.'"],[15865,"He wanted to marry a Jewish or Christian woman, so he asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he forbade him, saying, 'She will not make you chaste.'"],[15866,"Ka'b b. Ujrah shaved his head, and the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded him to ransom himself, so he ransomed himself with a cow."],[15867,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Ka'b b. Ujrah while he was in ihram: 'Have the creatures of your head harmed you?' He said, 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said, 'Shave and ransom yourself, either by fasting three days, or by feeding six poor people, each poor person a sa' of dates, or by sacrificing a sheep.'"],[15868,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , met me and wiped my head and said, \"This is sufficient for your harm.\" Then the lice scattered and he said, \"Go and shave your head and give charity to six poor people.\""],[15869,"Every hair on my head had lice from its root to its tip. When the Prophet ﷺ saw me, he commanded me to shave. Then this verse was revealed, and he said, \"Feed six poor persons with three sa's of dates.\""],[15870,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw crawling creatures on his face and said, \"I see, O Ka'b, that the vermin of your head have harmed you?\" He said, \"Yes indeed, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Shave your head, and feed six poor persons, or fast three days, or sacrifice a ewe.\""],[15871,"A man passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ noticed his vigor and activity. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, if only this were in the cause of Allah!\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If he went out striving to provide for his young children, then he is in the cause of Allah. If he went out striving to provide for two elderly parents, then he is in the cause of Allah. If he went out striving for himself to keep himself chaste, then he is in the cause of Allah. And if he went out for show and pride, then he is in the cause of Satan.\""],[15872,"\"Shall I not give you a gift? I said yes, so he said give it to me. We said, O Messenger of Allah, how do we send blessings upon you, the people of the household, as Allah has taught us how to send peace? He said, Say: O Allah, send peace upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent peace upon Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.\""],[15873,"\"Can I give you a gift?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"How do we greet you, O Messenger of Allah? And how do we pray upon you?\" He said, \"Say: 'O Allah, send peace and blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent peace and blessings upon Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious. And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.'\" Al-Zubair bin 'Adiy narrated from 'Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla."],[15874,"When the verse {Indeed, Allah and His angels confer blessings upon the Prophet} was revealed... (the rest of the hadith)."],[15875,"We said to the Prophet ﷺ , \"We have already known how to greet you, but how should we send blessings upon you?\" He replied, \"Say: Allahumma salli 'ala Muhammadin wa 'ala ali Muhammadin, kama sallaita 'ala Ibrahim wa 'ala ali Ibrahim, innaka hamidun majid. Wa barik 'ala Muhammadin wa 'ala ali Muhammadin, kama barakta 'ala Ibrahim wa 'ala ali Ibrahim, innaka hamidun majid.\""],[15876,"We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we know how to greet you with peace, so how do we pray upon you?\" He said, \"Say, 'O Allah, send your blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as you have sent blessings upon Ibrahim. Indeed, You are worthy of praise and glory. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You have blessed Ibrahim. Indeed, You are worthy of praise and glory.\""],[15877,"A blind man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “I hear the call, but perhaps I cannot find a guide and it is difficult for me. Should I set up a mosque in my house?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Does the call reach you?” He said, “Yes.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “When you hear the call, then go out.”"],[15878,"I attended one of the two Eids with Ka'b. When the people left, most of them went to the mosque, and I saw him heading toward the house. I said, \"O my father, will you not head to the mosque? For I see the people heading to it.\" He said, \"Much of what you see is rudeness and lack of knowledge. These two rak'ahs are the supererogatory prayer of this day until the prayer calls you.\""],[15879,"I went out with my father, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, on the day of Eid to the prayer place. He sat before the imam came, and the imam did not come until when the imam had finished, they departed going toward the mosque as if they were a neck (a group). I said to him, \"Do you not see the people?\" He said, \"This is an innovation and abandonment of the Sunnah.\""],[15880,"To Umar: \"I slaughtered a cow.\""],[15881,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “No man performs ablution in his house and then goes out intending prayer except that he is in prayer until he finishes his prayer, so he should not interlace his fingers in prayer.”"],[15882,"“He slaughtered a cow.”"],[15883,"You heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: I heard him say: “The daughter of a brother and the daughter of a sister are not made lawful through breastfeeding.”"],[15884,"\"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we know how to greet you, but how do we send blessings upon you?' The Prophet ﷺ replied, 'You say, O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O Allah, shower blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You showered blessings upon Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.'\""],[15885,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I not guide you to the best character of the people of this world and the Hereafter? Whoever maintains ties with the one who cuts him off, forgives the one who wrongs him, and gives to the one who deprives him.” Luwayn said: It is said—and Allah knows best—ʿAbd Allah b. Abi al-Husayn is given the kunya Abu al-Husayn. Abu al-Ahwas narrated from Abu Ishaq from ʿAbd Allah b. Abi al-Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, and he did not mention Kaʿb b. ʿUjrah."],[15886,"I attended two gatherings with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. As for one of them, a funeral was brought and it was said: This is so-and-so, and what a bad man he was; and he was spoken of with evil. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do you testify to that?” They said: Yes. He said: “It is confirmed.” As for the other, the funeral of a man was brought and they said: This is so-and-so, and they spoke well of him. He said: “Do you testify to that?” They said: Yes. He said: “It is confirmed.”"],[15887,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us while we were nine, among whom were six from the non-Arabs. He said: “There will be rulers. Whoever affirms their lies, assists them in their wrongdoing, and carries out their plots is not of me nor am I of him, and he will not come to the Pond.”"],[15888,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to shave his head because of lice. He said: “Fast three days, or feed six poor people, or slaughter a sacrifice.”"],[15889,"\"The Prophet ﷺ commanded me, when lice harmed me, to shave my head, then to fast three days or feed six poor people, and he knew that I had nothing to sacrifice.\""],[15890,"\"Narrate to us a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in which there is no disagreement.\" So he narrated from Ka'b b. 'Ujrah that he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever visits a sick person wades in mercy, and when he sits with him, he is immersed in it.\" He said: He said to his companions: \"We are immersed, if Allah wills.\""],[15891,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, may Allah protect you from rulers who will come after me. Whoever enters upon them and believes them in their lying and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will never come to the Pond.\""],[15892,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when he mentioned a tribulation and brought it near. A veiled man passed by, and he said: \"This one, on that day, will be upon the truth.\" I stood up and took hold of his upper arms, and I turned his face toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, this one?\" He said: \"Yes.\" And it was 'Uthman b. 'Affan."],[15893,"I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was telling us about the trials. A man with a face covering passed by, so he said: “This one and his companions will be upon guidance on that day.” So I got up and caught up with him, and I uncovered the veil from his head, and behold it was Uthman b. Affan. I said: O Messenger of God, this one? He said: “Yes.”"],[15894,"“Abu al-Yasar Kab b. Amr died in the year fifty-five in Madinah.”"],[15895,"What did he do? Was he killed? I said: God is mightier for him and more supportive than that. He said: What do you want with me? I said: Capture, but the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade killing you. He said: I am not the first to be crucified. So I captured him, then I brought him to the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[15896,"A woman came to me to buy dates from me. I said: In the house there are dates better than this. She entered the house with me, and I leaned toward her, pinched her, and kissed her. Then I became remorseful. I went to Abu Bakr and mentioned that to him, and he said: Cover yourself and do not tell anyone. But I could not bear it, so I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: “Did you betray a warrior in his family with something like this?” until I wished I had not embraced Islam except at that very hour, until I thought I was among the people of the Fire. The Messenger of God ﷺ lowered his head for a long time, then God revealed to him: {Establish prayer at the two ends of the day} to the end of the verse. Abu al-Yasar said: So I came to him and he recited it to me. His companions said: O Messenger of God, is this for him specifically or for the people generally? He said: “Rather for the people generally.”"],[15897,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever grants respite to a debtor in difficulty or waives [the debt] for him, God will shade him in His shade on the day there is no shade except His shade.”"],[15898,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever would like to seek shade from the scorching heat of Hell, let him give respite to a debtor or waive [the debt] for one in difficulty.”"],[15899,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Whoever provides financial relief or grants respite to a debtor, Allah will provide shade for him on the Day when there will be no shade except His shade.\""],[15900,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution, and he wiped the inside of his beard and the back of his neck."],[15901,"And from his brother: They were both horsemen on the day of Khaybar, and they were given six shares: four for their two horses and two for themselves. They sold the two shares for two young camels."],[15902,"He informed him that Safwan b. Umayyah sent him during the conquest to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with milk, a young gazelle, and truffle-like plants, while the Prophet ﷺ was at the upper part of the valley. I entered without seeking permission and without greeting. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Go out and say: Peace be upon you, may I enter?' That was after Safwan had embraced Islam. Abu 'Asim said: Al-daghabis is a plant that grows in the desert."],[15903,"A bedouin man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Tell me of a deed that will bring me near to Paradise and keep me far from the Fire.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Are these two your greatest concerns?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Speak the truth and give from your surplus.' He said, 'By Allah, I cannot speak the truth at every moment, and I cannot give from the surplus of my wealth.' He said, 'Feed people and spread peace.' He said, 'This is also difficult.' He said, 'Do you have camels?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then look to a camel from your camels and a water skin, then go to a household who do not drink water except every other day, and give them water. Perhaps you will not lose your camel or tear your water skin until Paradise becomes due for you.' The bedouin went off saying 'Allahu Akbar,' and neither his water skin was torn nor his camel lost until he was killed as a martyr."],[15904,"“O Messenger of God,” and he inclined toward him, then said, “Where is the year of the army of ‘Ithran?” The Prophet ﷺ recognized that army; I was in that army. Tariq b. al-Muraqqa’ said, “Who will give me a spear for its reward?” I said, “And what is its reward?” He said, “The first daughter born to me, I will marry her to him.” So I gave him my spear. Then it slipped from him somewhat. Later I learned that a daughter had been born to him and had reached maturity. I said, “Give me my wife in marriage.” He refused except with a dowry. The Prophet ﷺ said, “How old is she?” He said, “She has seen gray hair.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “It is better for you that you neither sin nor cause him to sin. Leave her.”"],[15905,"My acquaintance with your Prophet ﷺ was five nights before his death. I heard him say: \"There was no prophet but had an intimate friend among his community, and my intimate friend is Abu Bakr b. Abi Quhafah. Indeed, Allah ﷻ has taken your companion as an intimate friend.\""],[15906,"My acquaintance with your Prophet ﷺ was five nights before his death. I heard him say: \"There was no prophet but had an intimate friend among his community, and my intimate friend is Abu Bakr b. Abi Quhafah. Indeed, Allah ﷻ has taken your companion as an intimate friend.\""],[15907,"My acquaintance with your Prophet ﷺ was five nights before his death. I heard him say: \"There was no prophet but had an intimate friend among his community, and my intimate friend is Abu Bakr b. Abi Quhafah. Indeed, Allah ﷻ has taken your companion as an intimate friend.\""],[15908,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding an expedition he undertook: \"He did not miss any expedition until the expedition of Tabuk, except Badr. The Prophet ﷺ did not reproach anyone who stayed behind from Badr; he only went out seeking the caravan. Quraysh came out to protect their caravan, so they met without prior arrangement, as Allah the Exalted said. By my life, the noblest of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ battlefields among the people is Badr, but I would not love to have witnessed it in place of my pledge on the night of al-'Aqabah, when we gathered upon Islam.\""],[15909,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding an expedition he undertook: \"He did not miss any expedition until the expedition of Tabuk, except Badr. The Prophet ﷺ did not reproach anyone who stayed behind from Badr; he only went out seeking the caravan. Quraysh came out to protect their caravan, so they met without prior arrangement, as Allah the Exalted said. By my life, the noblest of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ battlefields among the people is Badr, but I would not love to have witnessed it in place of my pledge on the night of al-'Aqabah, when we gathered upon Islam.\""],[15910,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding an expedition he undertook: \"He did not miss any expedition until the expedition of Tabuk, except Badr. The Prophet ﷺ did not reproach anyone who stayed behind from Badr; he only went out seeking the caravan. Quraysh came out to protect their caravan, so they met without prior arrangement, as Allah the Exalted said. By my life, the noblest of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ battlefields among the people is Badr, but I would not love to have witnessed it in place of my pledge on the night of al-'Aqabah, when we gathered upon Islam.\""],[15911,"He was the guide of his father Ka'b when he lost his sight. He said: I heard my father Ka'b narrating his account of when he stayed behind from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the expedition of Tabuk, and the account of his two companions. He said: I never stayed behind from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in any other expedition, except that I had stayed behind from him in the expedition of Badr, and neither Allah nor His Messenger reproached anyone who stayed behind from it. That is because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ only went out seeking the caravan of Quraysh, until Allah brought him and his enemy together without a prior appointment."],[15912,"He was the guide of his father Ka'b when he lost his sight. He said: I heard my father Ka'b narrate his account of when he stayed behind from the Messenger of God ﷺ in the expedition of Tabuk, and the account of his two companions. He said: I never stayed behind from the Messenger of God ﷺ in any expedition other than it, except that I had stayed behind from him in the expedition of Badr, and neither God nor His Messenger rebuked anyone who stayed behind from it. That is because the Messenger of God ﷺ had set out only intending the caravan of Quraysh, until God brought him and his enemy together without an appointment."],[15913,"He was the guide of his father Ka'b when he lost his sight. He said: I heard my father Ka'b narrate his account of when he stayed behind from the Messenger of God ﷺ in the expedition of Tabuk, and the account of his two companions. He said: I never stayed behind from the Messenger of God ﷺ in any expedition other than it, except that I had stayed behind from him in the expedition of Badr, and neither God nor His Messenger rebuked anyone who stayed behind from it. That is because the Messenger of God ﷺ had set out only intending the caravan of Quraysh, until God brought him and his enemy together without an appointment."],[15914,"Ka'b said: I was present with the Messenger of God ﷺ at al-'Aqabah, and I did not stay behind from any expedition he undertook except the expedition of Badr, and the Messenger of God ﷺ did not rebuke anyone who stayed behind from Badr. The Messenger of God ﷺ had set out only intending the caravan of Quraysh. Then he mentioned the hadith."],[15915,"From 'Abd Allah b. Ka'b b. Malik: When God accepted his repentance, he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, God saved me only through truthfulness, and part of my repentance is that I will never speak a lie and that I divest myself of my wealth to God ﷻ and His Messenger. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Keep some of your wealth, for it is better for you.\" He said: I will keep my share of Khaybar."],[15917,"That he said to the Messenger of God ﷺ when his repentance was accepted: O Messenger of God, I divest myself of my wealth as charity to God and His Messenger. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Keep some of your wealth, for it is better for you.\""],[15918,"Ka'b said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the night of al-'Aqabah, when we pledged allegiance to him upon Islam, and I did not witness Badr. I would not love to have in its place a battle like Badr, even though it was more talked about among the people than it. It was an expedition for which God did not rebuke anyone who stayed behind from it. The Messenger of God ﷺ had set out only intending the caravan, until God brought him and his enemy together without an appointment. When the Messenger of God ﷺ intended to raid in a direction, we would mislead others about it, until it was the expedition of Tabuk, which the Messenger of God ﷺ undertook—in the hadith of Zayd—then he mentioned the hadith."],[15919,"From Ka'b b. Malik: When God accepted his repentance, he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, God saved me only through truthfulness, and part of my repentance is that I will never speak a lie and that I divest myself of my wealth as charity to God and His Messenger. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Keep some of your wealth, for it is better for you.\" Ka'b said: Then I will keep my share of Khaybar."],[15920,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: He said: O Messenger of God, part of my repentance is that I divest myself of my wealth as charity to God and to His Messenger. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Keep some of your wealth, for it is better for you.\""],[15921,"To the Prophet ﷺ—and he was one of the three who stayed behind and then God accepted their repentance—Ka'b said to the Prophet ﷺ: Part of my repentance is that I will speak nothing but truth and that I divest myself of all my wealth as charity to God and His Messenger. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Keep some of your wealth.\""],[15922,"That he heard one night Ka'b, who was one of the three whose repentance was accepted, say: When I was given the good news of repentance, I set out intending to go to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the people began to meet me in group after group, congratulating me on God's acceptance of my repentance, until when I entered the mosque, Talha b. 'Ubayd Allah rose toward me and shook my hand."],[15923,"I said: O Messenger of God, part of my repentance is that I divest myself of my wealth and that I abandon the abode of my people in which I committed the sin. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"A third of that will suffice you.\""],[15924,"That when he was given the good news of his repentance, he prostrated and gave the one who brought him the good news his two garments."],[15925,"The Prophet ﷺ would not arrive from a journey except during the day, at forenoon. When he arrived, he would begin with the mosque, pray two rak'ahs in it, then sit in it."],[15926,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he arrived from a journey, would begin with the mosque, offer two rak'ahs of voluntary prayer in it, then give salutation and sit in his prayer place. Then the Muslims would come and greet him."],[15927,"That his father Ka'b used to say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he arrived from a journey, would come to the mosque, pray two rak'ahs in it, then sit for the people regarding their legal rulings and their questions.\""],[15928,"That his father, Ka'b b. Malik al-Ansari, used to say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he arrived from a journey, would begin with the mosque, pray two rak'ahs in it, then sit for the people regarding their legal rulings and their questions, for as long as it seemed appropriate to him to sit.\""],[15929,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rarely set out on a journey except on Thursday."],[15930,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When Egypt is conquered, treat the Copts well, for they have protection and kinship,\" meaning that the mother of Ishmael was one of them."],[15931,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you conquer Egypt, treat the Copts well, for they have protection and kinship.\""],[15932,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"When you conquer Egypt, treat the Copts well, for they have protection and kinship.\""],[15933,"We used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we would go to Banu Salimah while we could still see the places where our arrows fell in Banu Salimah, the farthest part of Madinah."],[15934,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Maghrib, and men from Banu Salimah prayed with him while they could see the places where arrows fell."],[15935,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Maghrib, then the people would return to their families while they could still see the places where arrows fell when shot."],[15936,"He informed him that men from Banu Salimah used to attend Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then they would leave to their families while they could still see the places where arrows fell. Ma'mar and Ibn Jurayj did not say in this hadith 'from Ibn Ka'b, from his father.'"],[15937,"A man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ reported to him that they used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and then depart to their families; and they would return to the Banu Salamah while they could still see the places where arrows struck when they were shot. This is how Yunus narrated it from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn Ka'b: A man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ reported to me."],[15938,"Umm Mubashshir said to Ka'b when he was present: Convey my greetings of peace to my son, meaning Mubashshir. Ka'b said: May Allah forgive you, O Umm Mubashshir! Have you not heard what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said? He said: 'The soul of the believer is a bird that hangs in the trees of Paradise until Allah returns it to its body on the Day of Resurrection.' She said: I seek Allah's forgiveness."],[15939,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'The souls of the believers are in birds hanging in Paradise until Allah returns them to their bodies on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[15940,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed the soul of the believer is a bird that hangs in the trees of Paradise until Allah returns it to his body on the day He resurrects him.'"],[15941,"She said: O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, if you meet my son, convey to him from me greetings of peace. He said: May Allah forgive you, O Umm Bishr; we are too busy for that. She said: O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, have you not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The souls of the believers are in the crops of birds that hang in the trees of Paradise'? He said: Yes. She said: Then it is so."],[15942,"When death approached him, Umm Mubashshir came to him and said: Convey my greetings of peace to my son. He said to her: Have you not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The spirit of the believer is a bird that hangs in the trees of Paradise until it is resurrected on the Day of Resurrection'? She said: Yes, but I forgot."],[15943,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The soul of the believer, when he dies, is a bird that hangs in the trees of Paradise until Allah returns it to his body on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[15944,"Umm Mubashshir said: Convey to my son Mubashshir from me greetings of peace. Ka'b said: It is not like this that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said it; rather the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The souls of the martyrs are in green birds that hang wherever they wish.' She said: Then I seek Allah's forgiveness. He said: 'This is how I heard it.'"],[15945,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he was detaining a man for two uqiyyahs (of silver), so the Prophet ﷺ said to the man: 'Will you reduce it by half?' The man said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'Then give him what remains of his due.'"],[15946,"He reported to him that he requested Ibn Abi Hadrad to repay a debt he owed him at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque, until their voices rose and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard them while he was in his house. He came out to them, and the curtains of his chamber were raised, and he saw Ka'b. He said: 'O Ka'b b. Malik.' He said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'Drop half of this debt of his.' He said: I have dropped it, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'Get up and pay it.'"],[15947,"He reported to him that he requested Ibn Abi Hadrad to repay a debt he owed him in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque. Their voices rose until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard them while he was in his house, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them until he raised the curtain of his chamber and called out: 'O Ka'b b. Malik.' He said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He gestured with his hand to drop half of his debt, and Ka'b said: I have done it, O Messenger of Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Get up and pay it.'"],[15948,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited temporary marriage (mut'ah) with women."],[15949,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade mutʿah marriage and the meat of domestic donkeys."],[15950,"I bear witness concerning the Messenger of God ﷺ that on the day of Khaybar he forbade the meat of domestic donkeys."],[15951,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ was pleased, you would see his face as if it were a piece of the moon."],[15952,"I heard Kaʿb b. Mālik say: \"When the Messenger of God ﷺ was pleased with something, his face would light up as if it were a piece of the moon, until that could be recognized from him.\""],[15953,"When the Prophet ﷺ was pleased, his face would light up as if it were a piece of the moon."],[15954,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ was pleased with something, his face would light up as if it were a halo of the moon."],[15955,"A Jewish woman sent a roasted sheep to the Messenger of God ﷺ at Khaybar. He said to her, \"What is this?\" She said, \"A gift,\" and she was cautious not to say it was charity. He ate and his companions ate. Then he said to them, \"Stop.\" Then he said to the woman, \"Did you poison this sheep?\" She said, \"Who told you?\" He said, \"This bone,\" meaning its leg bone, and it was in his hand. She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Why?\" She said, \"I thought that if you were a liar, the people would be relieved of you, and if you were a prophet, it would not harm you.\" The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped on the withers, and he ordered his companions to have themselves cupped. Some of them died. Al-Zuhrī said, \"The woman accepted Islam, and they mentioned that he had her killed.\""],[15956,"Mulāʿib al-Asinnah came to the Prophet ﷺ with a gift. The Prophet ﷺ offered him Islam, but he refused to accept Islam. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I do not accept the gift of a polytheist.\""],[15957,"Mulāʿib al-Asinnah came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a gift. He offered him Islam, but he refused to accept Islam. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I do not accept the gift of a polytheist.\""],[15958,"Mulāʿib al-Asinnah came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a gift. He offered him Islam, but he refused to accept Islam. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I do not accept the gift of a polytheist.\""],[15959,"ʿĀmir b. Mālik b. Jaʿfar, who was called Mulāʿib al-Asinnah, came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was a polytheist. The Messenger of God ﷺ offered him Islam, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I do not accept the gift of a polytheist.\""],[15960,"ʿĀmir b. Mālik b. Jaʿfar, who was called Mulāʿib al-Asinnah, came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was a polytheist. The Messenger of God ﷺ offered him Islam, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I do not accept the gift of a polytheist.\""],[15961,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Every matter of importance that does not begin with praise [of Allah] is cut short or severed.\""],[15962,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"People will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection, and I and my Ummah will be upon a hill. My Lord, Mighty and Majestic, will clothe me with a red robe, then I will be permitted to speak, and I will say whatever Allah wills me to say. That is the Praiseworthy Station.\""],[15963,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have settled in the neighborhood of Banu So-and-so, and the one who harms me most is the one whose house is closest to mine.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abu Bakr, Umar, and Ali to go to the mosque, stand at its door, and call out: \"Verily, forty houses constitute a neighbor. And he whose neighbor fears his harmful acts will not enter Paradise.\""],[15964,"\"He had sheep that grazed at Mount Sal'. One of them fell and died, so I went down to it and slaughtered it. Ka'b asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he saw no harm in it.\""],[15965,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the group he sent to Ibn Abi al-Huqayq to kill him from killing women and children.\""],[15966,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade those who killed Ibn Abi al-Huqayq, when they set out against him, from killing women and children.\""],[15967,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined upon us not to kill any child or woman.\""],[15968,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined upon us not to kill any child or woman.\""],[15969,"\"The Prophet ﷺ forbade the killing of women and children.\""],[15970,"He said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"Allah has revealed about poetry what He has revealed.\" He said: \"The believer strives with his sword and his tongue. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, it is as if you are shooting them with arrows.\""],[15971,"He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about poetry?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The believer strives with his sword and his tongue. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, it is as if you are piercing them with arrows.\""],[15972,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, it is as if you are piercing them with arrows through what he says to them of poetry.\""],[15973,"Ka'b b. al-Ashraf, the Jew, was a poet. He used to satirize the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions and incite the disbelievers of Quraysh against them in his poetry. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah, its people were a mixture: among them were Muslims united by the call of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; among them were polytheists who worshipped idols; among them were Jews; and among them were people of the forts and strongholds, allies of the two tribes, Aws and Khazraj. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived, he wanted to reform them and make peace with them. A man might be a Muslim while his father was a polytheist, and a man might be a Muslim while his brother was a polytheist. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived, the polytheists and Jews of Madinah used to harm the Prophet ﷺ and his companions severely. Allah commanded His Prophet ﷺ and the Muslims to bear that patiently and to pardon them. Concerning them Allah, exalted be He, revealed: 'You will surely hear from those who were given the Book before you and from those who associate others with Allah much abuse' up to His saying 'of matters requiring resolve.' And concerning them Allah, exalted be He, revealed: 'Many of the People of the Book wish they could turn you back to disbelief after your faith' up to His saying 'until Allah brings His command.' When Ka'b b. al-Ashraf refused to desist from harming the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Muslims, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Sa'd b. Mu'adh, Muhammad b. Maslamah al-Ansari, then al-Harithi, Abu 'Isa b. Habr al-Ansari, and al-Harith, the nephew of Sa'd b. Mu'adh—in a group of five men. They came to him in the evening at his gathering place in al-'Awali. When Ka'b b. al-Ashraf saw them, he sensed something wrong and was alarmed by them. He said to them, 'What has brought you?' They said, 'A need we have brought to you.' He said, 'Let some of you come near me and tell me about it.' Some of them came near him and said, 'We have come to you to sell you some of our coats of mail so that we might use their price.' He said, 'By Allah, if you do that, you have been in hardship since this man came among you.' He promised them that they should come to him at night when people had dispersed. So they came to him, and one of them called out to him. He got up to go out to them. His wife said, 'They have not come to you at this hour with anything you will like.' He said, 'Yes, they have told me their story.' So he went out to them. Muhammad b. Maslamah embraced him and said to his companions, 'Do not let him get away from you, even if you kill me and him together.' One of them stabbed him with a sword in his side. When they killed him, the Jews and those polytheists with them were alarmed. They came to the Prophet ﷺ in the morning and said, 'Our companion was attacked last night—he was one of our chiefs—and he was killed treacherously.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ reminded them of what he used to say in his poetry and how he used to harm them with it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ invited them to write a document between him and them and the Muslims at large containing the general affairs of the people, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote it."],[15974,"Ka'b b. al-Ashraf, the Jew, was a poet. He used to satirize the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions and incite against them. He said, 'Who will take care of Ka'b for me?' When he refused to desist from harming the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Muslims, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Sa'd b. Mu'adh, Muhammad b. Maslamah, and Abu 'Isa b. al-Harith, the nephew of Sa'd b. Mu'adh, with five men. They came to Ka'b, and he mentioned a similar account."],[15975,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Allah, bless my Ummah in its early morning.'"],[15976,"From the Prophet ﷺ concerning the slaughter of the fetus. He said: 'Its slaughter is the slaughter of its mother.'"],[15977,"Indeed the last sermon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ preached to us, he said: 'O company of the Muhajirun, you have begun to increase, while the Ansar have reached their limit. They are my close supporters to whom I have resorted, so honor their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers.'"],[15978,"From his father, who was one of the three whose repentance was accepted, that the Prophet ﷺ stood to give a sermon. He praised Allah, extolled Him, sought forgiveness for the martyrs who were killed on the day of Uhud, and said: 'O company of the Muhajirun, you are increasing, while the Ansar do not increase. Indeed the Ansar are my inner circle to whom I resort, so honor their noble ones and overlook their wrongdoers.'"],[15979,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from pursuing the confederates, he took off his armor for his Ummah, performed ghusl, and used aromatic incense stones."],[15980,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from pursuing the confederates, he took off his armor for his Ummah, performed ghusl, and used aromatic incense stones."],[15981,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari when he heard him reciting: 'Your brother has been given one of the flutes of the family of Dawud.' And Yunus did not say in this hadith 'from his father.'"],[15982,"He was called Mula'ib al-Asinnah (the player with spears). He came to the Prophet ﷺ at Tabuk. The Prophet ﷺ offered him Islam, but he refused. He gave a gift to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'We do not accept the gift of a polytheist.' Then he said: 'Send whomever you wish to the people of Najd, for I will be their protector.' So the Prophet ﷺ sent a group, among them al-Mundhir b. 'Amr—the one about whom it was said, 'He stretched his neck to die.' 'Amir b. al-Tufayl heard about them, and he mentioned the hadith."],[15983,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Who is your chief, O Banu Salimah?' They said: 'Al-Jadd b. Qays, though we consider him stingy.' He said: 'And what disease is worse than stinginess?' They said: 'Then who is our chief, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Bishr b. al-Bara' b. Ma'rur.'"],[15984,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who is your chief, O Banu Salimah?' They said: 'Our chief is al-Jadd b. Qays.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Why do you make him your chief?' They said: 'Because he has more wealth than us, though we consider him stingy.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'And what disease is worse than stinginess? That is not your chief.' They said: 'Then who is our chief, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Your chief is Bishr b. al-Bara' b. Ma'rur.'"],[15985,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked, “Which people are best?” He said, “A believer between two noble lineages.”"],[15986,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The believer is unsuspecting and noble, while the evildoer is treacherous and base.”"],[15987,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Who saw the place where Hamzah was killed?” A man said, “May Allah honor you, I saw the place where he was killed.” So he went and stood over Hamzah and saw that his belly had been split open and he had been mutilated. He said, “O Messenger of Allah, he has been mutilated.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked to look at him, and he stood among the slain and said, “I am a witness over these. Wrap them in their blood, for there is no one wounded in the way of Allah but that his wound will come on the Day of Resurrection bleeding, its color the color of blood and its fragrance the fragrance of musk. Put forward the one who had memorized the most Qur’an and place him first in the grave niche.”"],[15988,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur, who had a throat infection, and ordered that he be cauterized with fire until it was treated."],[15989,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about an animal slaughtered by a woman using a stone, and he saw no harm in it."],[15990,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out in intense heat and ordered an expedition to Tabuk. At that time I believed in Allah and His Messenger, but my soul yearned for shade and fresh dates, and I was a strong young man. My soul said to me, “You have two camels; you will find an excuse to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” And my soul said to me, “Stay behind from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” So I was in that state, and the Prophet ﷺ departed in the morning. I went to the market intending to equip myself, but it was as if my hands were held back. The Prophet ﷺ traveled until when he was about two farsakhs from Madinah, he stopped. Then there was a rider catching up with him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Be Abu Khaythamah.” And it was Abu Khaythamah. He said: In Madinah there were eighty-seven hypocrites, along with me, Hilal b. Umayyah, and Murarah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked Abu Khaythamah, “What has Ka‘b b. Malik done?” He said, “I left him walking in the alleys of Madinah.” Mu‘adh said, “By Allah, as far as I know he loves Allah and His Messenger.” He said: A group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed in our quarter, and some of them said, “By Allah, they have fuller bellies than us, more fearful at the meeting, and weaker hearts.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called ‘Ammar b. Yasir and said, “Go to those people and ask them, ‘What did you mock?’ If you ask them, they will say, ‘We were only engaging in idle talk and playing.’” So he said to them, “You have burned. May Allah burn you.” Then it was revealed: “And if you ask them, they will surely say, ‘We were only engaging in idle talk and playing.’ Say, ‘Is it Allah and His verses and His Messenger that you were mocking?’” He said: A man who was not one of them but had heard them came and clung to the Prophet’s foot, saying, “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I did not incline toward them, but I heard what they said.” The Prophet ﷺ moved on, and the man kept clinging to him and offering excuses and walking with him until blood flowed from his heels. The Prophet ﷺ returned from his expedition, and Hilal b. Umayyah and Murarah b. Rabi‘ah came to him, and he seated us in a corner. It was said to Ka‘b b. Malik, “By Allah, he is not pleased with your two companions, so consider what excuse you will make.” I said, “I will seek help for what I did through lying, but I find nothing better than truthfulness.” So I went to him and said, “Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.” He said, “And upon you. What kept you back, O Ka‘b?” I said, “By Allah, I did not stay behind out of weakness or need, but it was a trial.” He said, “Sit with your two companions.” Then he said to his Companions, “Do not sit with these men, do not speak to them, and do not trade with them.” He sent word to their wives, “Do not let them approach you.” The wife of Hilal b. Umayyah sent word to the Prophet ﷺ that Hilal was an old man, and asked permission to give him something without speaking to him. He granted her permission. The wife of Ka‘b sent word that the wife of Hilal b. Umayyah had asked permission to hand him something, and she asked permission regarding me. I said, “With what will you seek permission? Will you say that I am an old man? By Allah, I am a young man. Will you say that I am ill? By Allah, I am healthy.” So he sent word to her not to do that. Umm Salamah was an excellent intercessor when it was her night. She said, “O Messenger of Allah, will you speak to Hilal b. Umayyah concerning us?” Then one night he said, “Do you know that Allah has accepted the repentance of the three?” She said, “Shall I send to their families and give them the good news?” He said, “Then the people will not leave us to sleep this night, but wait until morning.” The Prophet ﷺ arose, prayed the morning prayer, then turned to his Companions and said, “Do you know that Allah has accepted the repentance of the three?” Two men raced to Ka‘b b. Malik: one rode a horse and took the valley bottom, and one went on foot until he climbed the mountain. He said, “O Ka‘b b. Malik, do you know that Allah has accepted your repentance?” I fell down in prostration, and when he drew near I threw my cloak to him. Then I went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Is it from you or from Allah?” He said, “From Allah ﷻ.”"],[15991,"We set out for the pilgrimage in which we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-‘Aqabah, along with the polytheists of our people. With us was al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur, our elder and our leader. When we reached the outskirts of al-Bayda’, he said, “O people, do you know that I have formed an opinion, and I do not know whether you will agree with me?” We said, “What is it, O Abu al-Bashar?” He said, “I think I should pray toward this structure and not turn my back to it.” We said, “No, by Allah, do not do that. We have heard that our Prophet ﷺ prays only toward Syria.” He said, “By Allah, I will pray toward it.” Whenever prayer time came, he faced the Ka‘bah, and we faced Syria, until we arrived in Makkah. Al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur said to me, “O son of my brother, come with me to the Messenger of Allah so that we may ask him about what we did during this journey, for I have felt uneasy about your opposing me.” We went out to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we met a man in al-Abtah. We said to him, “Can you direct us to Muhammad b. ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Abd al-Muttalib?” He said, “Do you know him if you see him?” We said, “No, by Allah, we do not know him, and we have never seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said, “Do you know al-‘Abbas b. ‘Abd al-Muttalib?” We said, “Yes, we know him. He used to come to us for trade.” He said, “When you enter the mosque, look for al-‘Abbas, for he is the man who is with him.” We entered the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and al-‘Abbas were sitting in a corner of the mosque. We greeted and sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do you know these two men?” When he turned, he said, “Yes, this is al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur, the leader of his people, and this is Ka‘b b. Malik.” By Allah, I will never forget the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “The poet?” He said, “Yes.” Al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, I formed an opinion during this journey of mine, and I wanted to ask you about it so that you may inform me about what I did.” He said, “And what is that?” He said, “I decided not to turn my back to this structure, so I prayed toward it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You were upon a qiblah; if only you had remained patient upon it.” So he returned to the qiblah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. His family said, “He died upon that,” but we know better: he returned to the qiblah of the Messenger of Allah and prayed with us toward Syria."],[15992,"We set out for the pilgrimage in which we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-‘Aqabah, along with the polytheists of our people. With us was al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur, our elder and our leader. When we reached the outskirts of al-Bayda’, he said, “O people, do you know that I have formed an opinion, and I do not know whether you will agree with me?” We said, “What is it, O Abu al-Bashar?” He said, “I think I should pray toward this structure and not turn my back to it.” We said, “No, by Allah, do not do that. We have heard that our Prophet ﷺ prays only toward Syria.” He said, “By Allah, I will pray toward it.” Whenever prayer time came, he faced the Ka‘bah, and we faced Syria, until we arrived in Makkah. Al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur said to me, “O son of my brother, come with me to the Messenger of Allah so that we may ask him about what we did during this journey, for I have felt uneasy about your opposing me.” We went out to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we met a man in al-Abtah. We said to him, “Can you direct us to Muhammad b. ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Abd al-Muttalib?” He said, “Do you know him if you see him?” We said, “No, by Allah, we do not know him, and we have never seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said, “Do you know al-‘Abbas b. ‘Abd al-Muttalib?” We said, “Yes, we know him. He used to come to us for trade.” He said, “When you enter the mosque, look for al-‘Abbas, for he is the man who is with him.” We entered the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and al-‘Abbas were sitting in a corner of the mosque. We greeted and sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do you know these two men?” When he turned, he said, “Yes, this is al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur, the leader of his people, and this is Ka‘b b. Malik.” By Allah, I will never forget the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “The poet?” He said, “Yes.” Al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, I formed an opinion during this journey of mine, and I wanted to ask you about it so that you may inform me about what I did.” He said, “And what is that?” He said, “I decided not to turn my back to this structure, so I prayed toward it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You were upon a qiblah; if only you had remained patient upon it.” So he returned to the qiblah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. His family said, “He died upon that,” but we know better: he returned to the qiblah of the Messenger of Allah and prayed with us toward Syria."],[15993,"We set out for the pilgrimage in which we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-‘Aqabah, along with the polytheists of our people. With us was al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur, our elder and our leader. When we reached the outskirts of al-Bayda’, he said, “O people, do you know that I have formed an opinion, and I do not know whether you will agree with me?” We said, “What is it, O Abu al-Bashar?” He said, “I think I should pray toward this structure and not turn my back to it.” We said, “No, by Allah, do not do that. We have heard that our Prophet ﷺ prays only toward Syria.” He said, “By Allah, I will pray toward it.” Whenever prayer time came, he faced the Ka‘bah, and we faced Syria, until we arrived in Makkah. Al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur said to me, “O son of my brother, come with me to the Messenger of Allah so that we may ask him about what we did during this journey, for I have felt uneasy about your opposing me.” We went out to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we met a man in al-Abtah. We said to him, “Can you direct us to Muhammad b. ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Abd al-Muttalib?” He said, “Do you know him if you see him?” We said, “No, by Allah, we do not know him, and we have never seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said, “Do you know al-‘Abbas b. ‘Abd al-Muttalib?” We said, “Yes, we know him. He used to come to us for trade.” He said, “When you enter the mosque, look for al-‘Abbas, for he is the man who is with him.” We entered the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and al-‘Abbas were sitting in a corner of the mosque. We greeted and sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do you know these two men?” When he turned, he said, “Yes, this is al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur, the leader of his people, and this is Ka‘b b. Malik.” By Allah, I will never forget the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “The poet?” He said, “Yes.” Al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, I formed an opinion during this journey of mine, and I wanted to ask you about it so that you may inform me about what I did.” He said, “And what is that?” He said, “I decided not to turn my back to this structure, so I prayed toward it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You were upon a qiblah; if only you had remained patient upon it.” So he returned to the qiblah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. His family said, “He died upon that,” but we know better: he returned to the qiblah of the Messenger of Allah and prayed with us toward Syria."],[15994,"We set out for the pilgrimage in which we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-‘Aqabah, along with the polytheists of our people. With us was al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur, our elder and our leader. When we reached the outskirts of al-Bayda’, he said, “O people, do you know that I have formed an opinion, and I do not know whether you will agree with me?” We said, “What is it, O Abu al-Bashar?” He said, “I think I should pray toward this structure and not turn my back to it.” We said, “No, by Allah, do not do that. We have heard that our Prophet ﷺ prays only toward Syria.” He said, “By Allah, I will pray toward it.” Whenever prayer time came, he faced the Ka‘bah, and we faced Syria, until we arrived in Makkah. Al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur said to me, “O son of my brother, come with me to the Messenger of Allah so that we may ask him about what we did during this journey, for I have felt uneasy about your opposing me.” We went out to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we met a man in al-Abtah. We said to him, “Can you direct us to Muhammad b. ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Abd al-Muttalib?” He said, “Do you know him if you see him?” We said, “No, by Allah, we do not know him, and we have never seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said, “Do you know al-‘Abbas b. ‘Abd al-Muttalib?” We said, “Yes, we know him. He used to come to us for trade.” He said, “When you enter the mosque, look for al-‘Abbas, for he is the man who is with him.” We entered the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and al-‘Abbas were sitting in a corner of the mosque. We greeted and sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do you know these two men?” When he turned, he said, “Yes, this is al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur, the leader of his people, and this is Ka‘b b. Malik.” By Allah, I will never forget the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “The poet?” He said, “Yes.” Al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, I formed an opinion during this journey of mine, and I wanted to ask you about it so that you may inform me about what I did.” He said, “And what is that?” He said, “I decided not to turn my back to this structure, so I prayed toward it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You were upon a qiblah; if only you had remained patient upon it.” So he returned to the qiblah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. His family said, “He died upon that,” but we know better: he returned to the qiblah of the Messenger of Allah and prayed with us toward Syria."],[15995,"I was my father's guide when he lost his sight. Whenever I took him out on Friday and he heard the call to prayer for the Friday prayer, he would ask forgiveness for Abu Umamah As'ad b. Zurarah. I remained for a while hearing that from him, so I said: It is nothing but incapacity unless I ask him about this. So I took him out as I used to take him out, and when he heard the call to prayer for the Friday prayer, he asked forgiveness for him. I said, 'O my father, what do you think about your asking forgiveness for As'ad b. Zurarah every time you hear the call to prayer for the Friday prayer?' He said, 'O my son, As'ad was the first to gather us for Friday prayer in Madinah before the arrival of the Messenger of God ﷺ, in a depression of the Harrah of Banu Bayadah in Naqi' al-Khadamat.' I said, 'How many were you that day?' He said, 'Forty men.'"],[15996,"He had a debt owed to him by 'Abd Allah b. Abi Hadrad. He met him and held him, and they talked and their voices rose. The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by them and said, 'O Ka'b,' and gestured with his hand as if he meant half. So he took half of what was owed to him and left half."],[15997,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'When one of you feels pain, let him place his hand where he feels the pain, then say seven times: I seek refuge in the might of God and His power over all things from the evil of what I feel.'"],[15998,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a group of the Ansar while they were building a mosque. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Make your mosque spacious, and you will fill it.'"],[15999,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to a group of the Ansar who were pebbling a mosque, and he said, 'Make it spacious, and you will fill it.'"],[16000,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ lick his three fingers after eating."],[16001,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The example of the believer is like a stalk of grain that the winds bend: at one time it straightens it, and at another it knocks it down. The example of the disbeliever is like a firmly rooted cedar tree standing on its trunk until it is uprooted all at once.'"],[16002,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The example of the believer is like a stalk of grain that the winds bend: at one time they knock it down, and at another they straighten it, until his appointed time comes. The example of the disbeliever is like a firmly rooted cedar tree standing on its trunk, which the winds do not bend until it is uprooted all at once.'"],[16003,"When his excuse was revealed, he came to the Prophet ﷺ, took his hand, and kissed it."],[16004,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ eat food, then lick his fingers."],[16005,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to mark the boundaries of the protected grazing land."],[16006,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to eat with three fingers, and when he finished he would lick them."],[16007,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ eat food, then lick the three fingers he ate with."],[16008,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"People must stop hearing the call on Friday and then not attending it, or God will seal their hearts and they will certainly be among the heedless.\""],[16009,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said, \"I had a vision of the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr), and I was aware of it but then I forgot it. So seek it in the last ten nights, in the odd nights.\""],[16010,"Ka'b b. Ujrah died in the year fifty-two at the age of seventy-seven."],[16011,"Ka'b b. Ujrah died in the year fifty-two while he was seventy-five years old."],[16012,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Ka'b b. Ujrah: 'Perhaps the vermin of your head have harmed you?' He said, 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said, 'Shave your head and sacrifice a cow, marking it or garlanding it.'"],[16013,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"I place you under Allah's protection, O Ka'b b. Ujrah, from rulers who will come after me. Whoever frequents their doors, confirms them in their lies, and assists them in their oppression is not of me, and I am not of him. And whoever frequents their doors or does not frequent them, but does not confirm them in their lies and does not assist them in their oppression is of me, and I am of him, and he will come to the Cistern.\""],[16014,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"I place you under Allah's protection, O Ka'b b. Ujrah, from rulers who will come after me. Whoever frequents their doors, confirms them in their lies, and assists them in their oppression is not of me, and I am not of him. And whoever frequents their doors or does not frequent them, but does not confirm them in their lies and does not assist them in their oppression is of me, and I am of him, and he will come to the Cistern.\""],[16015,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"I place you under Allah's protection, O Ka'b b. Ujrah, from rulers who will come after me. Whoever frequents their doors, confirms them in their lies, and assists them in their oppression is not of me, and I am not of him. And whoever frequents their doors or does not frequent them, but does not confirm them in their lies and does not assist them in their oppression is of me, and I am of him, and he will come to the Cistern.\""],[16016,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever grants respite to one in difficulty or makes it easy for him, Allah will shade him in His shade on the Day when there is no shade except His shade.\""],[16017,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him while his lice were falling onto his face, and he said: \"Do your lice bother you?\" He replied: \"Yes.\" So he ordered him to shave while they were at al-Hudaybiyyah, and it was not clear that they would shave there, as they were hoping to enter Makkah. Then Allah, exalted is He, revealed the ransom, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to feed a faraq among six poor persons, or sacrifice a sheep, or fast three days."],[16018,"Ka'b b. Ujrah, the brother of Banu Salim, suffered an ailment in his head while he was at al-Hudaybiyyah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, under siege. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to fast three days, or feed six poor persons, or slaughter a sheep, and this verse was revealed concerning him."],[16019,"His head became infested with lice, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him while he was kindling a fire under a pot of his. He said to him: \"It seems that the vermin of your head are bothering you?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Shave, and offer a sacrificial animal.\" He said: \"I cannot find a sacrificial animal.\" He said: \"Then feed six poor persons.\" He said: \"I cannot find [the means].\" He said: \"Then fast three days.\" So I shaved and fasted."],[16020,"This verse was revealed concerning us when we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Hudaybiyyah, while we were in ihram and the polytheists had confronted us. I had thick hair, and lice began falling onto my face. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by and said: \"Do the vermin of your head bother you?\" I said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Then shave.\" Then this verse was revealed: {then a ransom of fasting, or charity, or sacrifice}. He said: \"The fasting is three days, the charity is six poor persons, and the sacrifice is a sheep.\""],[16021,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us; and 'Abd Allah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us, Mus'ab b. 'Abd Allah al-Zubayri narrated to me; and Yahya b. Ayyub al-'Allaf narrated to us, Yahya b. Bukayr narrated to us, all of them from Malik b. Anas, from Humayd b. Qays, from Mujahid, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from Ka'b b. Ujrah that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Perhaps your vermin are bothering you?\" I said to him: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Shave your head, and fast three days, or feed six poor persons, or sacrifice a sheep.\""],[16022,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us; and Yahya b. Ayyub al-'Allaf narrated to us, Yahya b. Bukayr narrated to us; and 'Abd Allah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us, Mus'ab b. 'Abd Allah al-Zubayri narrated to us, all of them from Malik, from 'Abd al-Karim b. Malik al-Jazari, from Mujahid, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from Ka'b b. Ujrah that he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and lice in his head bothered him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to shave his head and said: \"Fast three days, or feed six poor persons, two mudds each, or sacrifice a sheep; whichever of these you do will suffice you.\""],[16023,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me during an 'umrah, when he saw lice in my head: \"O Ka'b, do your vermin bother you?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then shave, and slaughter a sheep, or fast three days, or feed six poor persons.\""],[16024,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me at al-Hudaybiyyah while I was cooking a pot and lice were falling onto my face. He said: \"Do the vermin of your head bother you?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then shave, then fast three days, or slaughter a sheep, or feed a faraq among six poor persons.\""],[16025,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by Ka'b b. Ujrah when the vermin of his head had troubled him. He commanded him to shave. Then revelation came to him, so the Prophet ﷺ said, \"If you wish, fast three days; if you wish, give a faraq to be divided among six needy people; or if you wish, slaughter a sheep.\""],[16026,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him while his lice were falling onto his face. He said, \"Do your vermin trouble you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to shave at al-Hudaybiyyah. It was not clear to them that they would shave there, and they were hoping to enter Makkah. Then Allah, exalted is He, sent down the expiation. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to feed a faraq to six needy people, or to offer a sheep, or to fast three days."],[16027,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was at al-Hudaybiyyah cooking a pot, and lice were falling thickly onto my face. He said, \"Do the vermin of your head trouble you?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then shave, then fast three days, or slaughter a sheep, or feed a faraq to six needy people.\""],[16028,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me while my lice were falling onto my face. He said, \"Do these vermin of yours trouble you?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, and he commanded me to shave my head. They were at al-Hudaybiyyah, and it was not clear to them that they would shave there, and they were hoping to enter Makkah. Then Allah, exalted is He, sent down the expiation. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to feed a faraq to six needy people, or to fast three days, or to slaughter a sheep."],[16029,"This verse was revealed concerning me. I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Come closer.\" I came closer two or three times. He said, \"Do your vermin trouble you?\" I said, \"Yes.\" Then he commanded me to fast, or to give charity, or to offer a sacrifice, whatever was easy."],[16030,"This verse was revealed concerning me. I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Come closer.\" I came closer two or three times. He said, \"Do your vermin trouble you?\" Ibn ʿAwn said: I think he said, \"Yes.\" Then he commanded me to fast, or to give charity, or to offer a sacrifice, whatever was easy. Ibn ʿAwn said: I forgot what he said about the fasting and the charity, so I discussed it with Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī, and he said, \"I heard this hadith from him.\" I said, \"How is it?\" He said, \"Fasting three days, or charity to six needy people, or a sacrifice, whatever was easy.\" Ayyūb used to say that he said, \"Do the vermin of your head trouble you?\""],[16031,"The Prophet ﷺ came to me at the time of al-Hudaybiyyah while I was lighting a fire under a cooking pot of mine, and lice were scattering over me. He said, \"Do the vermin of your head trouble you?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Shave, and feed six needy people three sāʿs, or fast three days, or offer a sacrifice.\""],[16032,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he was lighting a fire under a cooking pot. He said, \"Have the vermin of your head troubled you?\" So the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to shave and to fast three days, or to feed a faraq to six needy people, or to offer a sacrifice. Sufyān said: Then this verse was revealed: {And whoever among you is ill or has an ailment of the head...}"],[16033,"Ali came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the time of Hudaybiyah and found me sitting under a cooking pot while lice were crawling on my face. He asked, \"Does the itchiness bother you?\" I replied, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Shave your head, observe fasting for three days, feed six poor people, or sacrifice a sheep as expiation for your negligence.\" This narration is from the hadith of Ibn Ulayyah."],[16034,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to shave his head and offer a sacrifice, or fast three days, or feed a faraq to six needy people."],[16035,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by him while he was at al-Hudaybiyyah, before entering Makkah, in a state of iḥrām, lighting a fire under a cooking pot of his, and lice were falling thickly onto his face. He said, \"Do these vermin of yours trouble you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then shave your head, and feed a faraq to six needy people—the faraq is three sāʿs—or fast three days, or offer a sacrificial animal.\" Ibn Abī Najīḥ said: Or slaughter a sheep."],[16036,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he was lighting a fire under a cooking pot of his, and lice were falling thickly onto his face. He said, \"Do your vermin trouble you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then shave your head, and offer a sacrifice, or fast three days, or feed three sāʿs to six needy people.\""],[16037,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by me at the time of al-Hudaybiyyah while I was lighting a fire under a cooking pot of mine, and the vermin of my head were falling. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Do the vermin of your head trouble you?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Shave, and fast three days, or feed six needy people, or slaughter an animal.\""],[16038,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped by him at al-Hudaybiyah while his head was teeming with lice, and said, \"Are the vermin of your head harming you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Shave your head.\" Then he commanded me to fast three days, or feed six poor persons, or sacrifice whatever is easy."],[16039,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, how do we send blessings upon you?” He said: ʿSay: O Allah, send Your salah (grace, honour and mercy) upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent Your salah upon the family of Ibrahim, You are indeed Praiseworthy, Most Glorious. And send Your blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You sent Your blessings upon the family of Ibrahim, You are indeed Praiseworthy, Most Glorious.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 1396)"],[16040,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we have learned how to greet you, so how should we pray for you?\" He said, \"Say: 'O Allah, send peace and blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You sent peace and blessings upon Ibrahim. Surely, You are praiseworthy, glorious. And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim. Surely, You are praiseworthy, glorious.\""],[16041,"The Prophet ﷺ saw him while he was in ihram and had flowing hair, and at the base of every hair and at its top there was a louse or a nit. He said, \"This is indeed a harm. Can you find a sacrifice?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then go and shave it. If you wish, fast three days, or feed six poor persons, with a sa' of dates between every two poor persons.\""],[16042,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"If you wish, offer a sacrificial animal; if you wish, fast three days; and if you wish, feed three sa's of dates to six poor persons.\""],[16043,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me in the year of al-Hudaybiyah while I had flowing hair, and from the base of every hair to its tip there were lice and nits. He said, \"This is indeed a harm.\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Shave it and slaughter, or fast three days, or give three sa's of dates in charity to six poor persons.\""],[16044,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him—while the vermin of his head were harming him—\"Slaughter a ewe as a sacrifice, or fast three days, or give three sa's in charity to six poor persons.\""],[16045,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me at the time of al-Hudaybiyah while I had abundant hair, and said, \"It seems the vermin of your head are harming you?\" I said, \"Yes indeed.\" He said, \"Shave it, and slaughter a ewe, or fast three days, or give three sa's in charity among six poor persons.\""],[16046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him—while the vermin of his head were harming him—\"Slaughter a sacrificial animal, or fast three days, or give three sa's in charity to six poor persons.\""],[16047,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by him at the time of al-Hudaybiyah and said, \"Have the vermin of your head harmed you?\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Shave it, then slaughter a ewe, or fast three days, or feed three sa's of dates to six poor persons.\""],[16048,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us—all of them from Malik, from 'Ata' b. 'Abd Allah al-Khurasani: A man in the market of Kufa narrated to me from Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me while I was blowing under a cooking pot for my companions, and my head and beard were full of lice. He took hold of my forehead and said, \"Shave this, and fast three days, or feed six poor persons.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ knew that I did not have anything with which to offer a sacrifice."],[16049,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He passed by him during the 'Umrah of al-Hudaybiyah when the vermin of his head had become numerous, and said to him, \"O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, this is indeed a harm.\" He said, \"Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. Is there any concession for me?\" He said, \"Offer a sacrificial animal, or fast three days, or feed six poor persons.\""],[16050,"I was afflicted with vermin on my head while I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of Hudaybiyah, until I feared for my eyesight. Then Allah, exalted is He, revealed: {And whosoever among you is ill or has an ailment of the head, then a ransom of fasting, charity, or sacrifice.} So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called me and said: \"Shave your head, fast three days, or feed six poor people a faraq of raisins, or sacrifice a sheep.\" So I shaved my head and then offered a sacrifice."],[16051,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"There are phrases that follow up the prayers, the one who says them will not be disappointed: thirty-three times 'Glory be to Allah,' thirty-three times 'Praise be to Allah,' and thirty-three times 'Allah is Greatest' after every prescribed prayer.\""],[16052,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There are expiations for those whose statements do not fail, who glorify Allah thirty-three times and praise Him thirty-three times after every prayer, and who glorify Him thirty-four times.\""],[16053,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There are phrases that follow up the prayers, the one who says them or does them will not be disappointed: thirty-three glorifications, thirty-three praises, and thirty-four declarations of Allah's greatness after every prayer.\""],[16054,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There are phrases that follow up the prayers, the one who says them or does them will not be disappointed: thirty-three times glorification, thirty-three times praise, and thirty-four times declaration of Allah's greatness after every prayer.\""],[16055,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There are phrases that follow up the prayers, the one who says them or does them will not be disappointed: you glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise Allah thirty-three times, and declare Allah's greatness thirty-four times after every prayer.\""],[16056,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There are phrases that follow up the prayers, the one who says them or does them will not be disappointed: glorify after every prayer thirty-three times, praise thirty-three times, and declare greatness thirty-four times.\""],[16057,"\"O Messenger of Allah, we already know how to greet you, so how do we pray upon you?\" He replied, \"Say: Allahumma salli 'ala Muhammadin wa 'ala ali Muhammadin kama sallayta 'ala Ibrahim, innaka Hamidun Majidun. Allahumma barik 'ala Muhammadin wa 'ala ali Muhammadin kama barakta 'ala Ibrahim, innaka Hamidun Majidun.\""],[16058,"We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we know this greeting of peace, but how should we send blessings upon you?\" He said, \"Say, 'O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim. Verily, You are praiseworthy and glorious. O Allah, shower blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You showered blessings upon Ibrahim. Verily, You are praiseworthy and glorious."],[16059,"Kaʿb bin 'Ujra met me and said, \"Shall I give you a present? Once the Prophet ﷺ came to us and we said, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ ! We know how to greet you; but how to send 'Salat' upon you? He said, 'Say: Allahumma Salli ala Muhammadin wa 'ala ʿAli Muhammadin, kama sal-laita 'ala all Ibrahima innaka Hamidun Majid. Allahumma barik 'ala Muhammadin wa 'ala all Muhammadin, kama barakta 'ala all Ibrahima, innaka Hamidun Majid.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6357)"],[16060,"When this verse was revealed: \"Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon the Prophet. O you who have believed, ask [Allah to confer] blessing upon him and ask [Allah to grant him] peace\" (Quran 33:56), we said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we already know how to greet you, but how should we send blessings upon you?\" The Prophet replied, \"You should say: 'O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious. Send blessings upon us with them and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious. Grant us peace, O Prophet, and the mercy and blessings of Allah.'\""],[16061,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Yes, I said yes.\" A man asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, we have learned or you have taught us (to say) 'Peace be upon you.' So how should we send peace upon you?\" He said, \"Say: O Allah, send your peace upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as you have sent peace upon the family of Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as you have blessed the family of Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.\""],[16062,"The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we are familiar with this greeting, but how about the prayer?\" He said, \"Say, 'O Allah, send peace and blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You sent peace and blessings upon the family of Ibrahim. Surely, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed the family of Ibrahim. Surely, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.\""],[16063,"\"When 'Indeed, Allah and His angels pray upon the Prophet' was revealed, I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, peace be upon you, we already know how to say salaam to you, but how should we pray upon you, O Messenger of Allah?' He replied, 'Say: O Allah, pray upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You prayed upon Ibrahim and upon the family of Ibrahim. Indeed, You are praiseworthy and glorious.'\""],[16064,"His father said: \"We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, how should we send salah upon you?' He said: 'Say: Alahumma salli 'ala Muhammad wa 'ala ali Muhammad, kama sallaita 'ala Ibrahima wa barik 'ala Muhammad kama barakta 'ala ali Ibrahim fil-'alamin, innaka hamidun majid (O Allah, send salah upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent salah upon the family of Ibrahim, and send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon the family of Ibrahim among the nations. You are indeed Worthy of praise, Full of glory.)'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1290)"],[16065,"We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we know how to greet you, so how should we send prayers upon you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Say: 'O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim. Surely, You are praiseworthy and glorious. And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim. Surely, You are praiseworthy and glorious.\""],[16066,"We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we have known this greeting of peace upon you, so how should we send blessings upon you?\" He said, \"Say: 'O Allah, send peace upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You have sent peace upon Ibrahim and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You have blessed Ibrahim. You are indeed Praiseworthy, Glorious.'\""],[16067,"He said to the Prophet, \"This is the peace upon you, we know it, so how do we pray upon you?\" He said, \"Say, 'O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Surely, You are praiseworthy, glorious. And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Surely, You are praiseworthy, glorious.' \" And he didn't mention in the hadith Abdul Rahman ibn Abi Layla."],[16068,"One day we sat in front of the dwellings of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque, among us a group of the Ansar, a group of the Muhajirun, and a group of Banu Hashim. We disputed about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: which of us was closer to him and more beloved to him? We, the Ansar, said: 'We believed in him, followed him, fought alongside him, and his battalion was at the forefront of the enemy, so we are closer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and more beloved to him.' Our brothers, the Muhajirun, said: 'We are the ones who emigrated to Allah and His Messenger, leaving behind our tribes, families, and properties. We witnessed what you witnessed and were present at what you were present at, so we are closer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and more beloved to him.' Our brothers from Banu Hashim said: 'We are the clan of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We witnessed what you witnessed and were present at what you were present at, so we are closer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and more beloved to him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us, turned to us, and said: 'You are certainly saying something.' We told him what we had said. He said to the Ansar: 'You have spoken the truth. Who can dispute this with you?' We informed him of what our brothers, the Muhajirun, had said. He said: 'They have spoken the truth and been dutiful. Who can dispute this with them?' We informed him of what Banu Hashim had said. He said: 'They have spoken the truth and been dutiful. Who can dispute this with them?' Then he said: 'Shall I not judge between you?' We said: 'Yes, by our fathers and mothers, you, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'As for you, O Ansar, I am your brother.' They said: 'Allah is Greatest! We have won him, by the Lord of the Ka'bah.' 'As for you, O Muhajirun, I am one of you.' They said: 'Allah is Greatest! We have won him, by the Lord of the Ka'bah.' 'As for you, Banu Hashim, you are from me and to me.' We all arose pleased and delighted with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[16069,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were sitting on a leather cushion. He said: \"There will be rulers after me. Whoever enters upon them, believes them in their lies, and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will never come to the Hawd. And whoever does not believe them in their lies, and does not help them in their wrongdoing, he is of me, and I am of him, and he will come to the Hawd.\""],[16070,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were nine: five Arabs and four non-Arabs. He said: \"Listen, have you not heard that there will be rulers after me? Whoever enters upon them, believes them in their lies, and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to the Hawd. And whoever does not enter upon them and does not help them in their wrongdoing is of me, and I am of him, and he will come to the Hawd.\""],[16071,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah protect you from rulers who will come after me.\" I said, \"What is that?\" He said: \"Whoever enters upon them, believes them in their lies, and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will never come to the Hawd. And whoever does not enter upon them, does not believe them in their lies, and does not help them in their wrongdoing, he is of me, and I am of him, and he will come to my Hawd.\""],[16072,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “May God protect you from rulers who will come after me.” I said, “And what is that?” He said: “Whoever enters upon them, confirms their lies, and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will never reach the watering place. But whoever does not enter upon them, does not confirm their lies, and does not help them in their wrongdoing—that one is of me and I am of him, and he will reach my watering place.”"],[16073,"I was carried to the Messenger of God ﷺ while lice were scattering over my face. He said: “I did not think the ailment had reached with you what I see. Do you have a sheep?” I said, “No.” He said: “Then fast three days, or feed such and such number of needy people, each needy person half a sāʿ of wheat.”"],[16074,"Concerning me this verse was revealed: {And whoever among you is ill or has an ailment of his head, then a ransom of fasting or charity or sacrifice}. I said, “How was your situation?” He said: “We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ while we were in a state of iḥrām, and lice fell into my head, my beard, and my moustache until they reached my eyebrows. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: ‘I did not think it had reached with you to this extent. Call the barber.’ So he called the barber and he shaved his head. Then he said: ‘Do you have a sacrificial animal?’ I said, ‘No.’ He said: ‘Then fast three days, or feed six needy people, with a ṣāʿ between every two needy people.’ Thus it was revealed concerning me specifically and for the people generally.”"],[16075,"He went out with the Prophet ﷺ in a state of iḥrām, and his head and beard became infested with lice. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he sent for him and called the barber, and he shaved his head. Then he said: “Do you have a sacrificial animal?” He said, “I am not able to obtain one.” So he ordered him to fast three days or feed six needy people, a ṣāʿ for each needy person. Then God ﷻ revealed concerning him specifically: {And whoever among you is ill or has an ailment of his head, then a ransom of fasting or charity or sacrifice}. Then it became general for the Muslims.”"],[16076,"I entered iḥrām from al-Ḥudaybiyah while I had abundant hair, and I became infested with lice and small vermin took hold of me. The Prophet ﷺ saw me and said: “Shave! Shave!” So I shaved. He said: “Do you have a sacrificial animal with you?” I said, “I do not find one.” He said: “Even whatever is easy.” I said, “I do not find one.” He said: “Then fast three days, or feed six needy people, half a ṣāʿ of wheat.” He said: “Concerning me this verse was revealed: {And whoever among you is ill or has an ailment of his head}.” And the wording is from the ḥadīth of Ibn Fuḍayl."],[16077,"A blind man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I hear the call, but perhaps I cannot find a guide.” He said: “When you hear the call, then answer the caller to God.”"],[16078,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There will be rulers over you.”"],[16079,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Shall I not tell you about the men among you who will be from the people of Paradise?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “The Prophet is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, the truthful one is in Paradise, the newborn is in Paradise, and the man who visits his brother on the far side of the town is in Paradise. Shall I not tell you about the women among you who will be from the people of Paradise?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “The loving, prolific one who, if she wrongs or is wronged, says, ‘This forelock of mine is in your hand; I will not taste sleep until you are pleased.’”"],[16080,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us while I was the seventh of seven, among us five from Quraysh, and he said: “Will you not listen?” He said it three times. “There will be rulers after me. Whoever enters upon them, confirms their lies, and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and I am free of him. But whoever does not enter upon them, does not confirm their lies, and does not help them in their wrongdoing, then he is of me and I am of him, and he will meet me and be with me.”"],[16081,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us while we were seven on a cushion and said: “O Kaʿb b. ʿUjrah, I seek refuge for you with God from the rule of fools.” I said, “O Messenger of God, what is the rule of fools?” He said: “Rulers who will come after me. Whoever enters upon them, confirms their lies, and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will never reach the watering place. But whoever does not come to them, does not confirm their lies, and does not help them in their wrongdoing, then he is of me and I am of him, and he will reach the watering place.”"],[16082,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us while we were seven on a cushion and said: “O Kaʿb b. ʿUjrah, I seek refuge for you with God from the rule of fools.” I said, “O Messenger of God, what is the rule of fools?” He said: “Rulers who will come after me. Whoever enters upon them, confirms their lies, and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will never reach the watering place. But whoever does not come to them, does not confirm their lies, and does not help them in their wrongdoing, then he is of me and I am of him, and he will reach the watering place.”"],[16083,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , came out to us, while we were seven people sitting on cushions. He said, \"O Ka'b ibn 'Ujrah, I seek refuge for you in Allah from the leadership of the foolish.\" I asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the leadership of the foolish?\" He said, \"They are rulers who will come after me, and whoever enters their presence and believes in their lies and supports them in their injustice, he is not from me and I am not from him, and he will not come to the Hawd (a reservoir in Paradise where the Prophet will give his companions water to drink). But whoever does not go to them and does not believe in their lies and does not support them in their injustice, then he is from me and I am from him, and he will come to the Hawd.\""],[16084,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “There will be rulers over you. Whoever visits their doors and helps them in their wrongdoing and believes them in their lies—he is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will never reach the Pond. Whoever does not visit their doors, does not believe them in their lies, and does not help them in their wrongdoing—he is of me, and I am of him, and he will reach the Pond.”"],[16085,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were seven people—four of our freedmen and three of our Arabs—leaning our backs against his mosque. He said, “What has seated you here?” We said, “We sat waiting for the prayer.” He paused briefly, then turned his face toward us and said, “Do you know what your Lord says?” We said, “No.” He said, “Your Lord says: Whoever prays the prayer at its time, guards it, and does not neglect it out of disregard for its right—he has a covenant from Me that I will admit him to Paradise. Whoever does not pray it at its time and does not guard it out of disregard for its right—he has no covenant from Me. If I will, I will punish him, and if I will, I will forgive him.”"],[16086,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said, “What has seated you here?” We said, “We are waiting for the prayer.” He said, “Do you know what your Lord says?” We said, “No.” He said, “He says: Whoever prays the prayers at their times and does not neglect them out of disregard for their right—he has a covenant from Me that I will admit him to Paradise. If he does not pray them at their times and neglects them out of disregard for their right—he has no covenant with Me. If I will, I will punish him, and if I will, I will pardon him.”"],[16087,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to the mosque while we were a group of seven—four Arabs and three freedmen. He sat down and said, “Do you know what your Lord said?” We said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Whoever prays the prayer at its time and does not abandon it out of disregard for it will meet me on the Day of Resurrection, and he has a covenant with Me by which I will admit him to Paradise. Whoever does not pray it at its time and abandons it out of disregard for it will meet me on the Day of Resurrection, and he has no covenant with Me. If I will, I will punish him, and if I will, I will forgive him.”"],[16088,"The Prophet ﷺ came out to us while we were seven—three Arabs and four freedmen. The Prophet ﷺ came out to us from one of his chambers until he sat with us and said, “What has seated you here?” We said, “We are waiting for the prayer.” He tapped the ground with his fingers, then bowed his head for a while, then raised his head toward us and said, “Do you know what your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, says?” We said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “He says: Whoever prays the prayers at their times and establishes their limits has a covenant from Me that I will admit him to Paradise. Whoever does not pray the prayers at their times and does not establish their limits has no covenant with Me. If I will, I will enter him into the Fire, and if I will, I will enter him into Paradise.”"],[16089,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one day to the pulpit and said as he ascended one step, 'Ameen,' then he ascended the next step and said, 'Ameen,' then he ascended the third step and said, 'Ameen.' When he descended from the pulpit and finished, we said, 'O Messenger of Allah, today we heard from you something we had never heard before.' He said, 'Did you hear it?' We replied, 'Yes.' He then said, 'Verily, Jibril ﷺ came to me while I was ascending a step and said, \"May Allah distance the one who does not have his parents reach old age and enter Paradise from both of them.\" I said, 'Ameen.' Jibril ﷺ then said, \"May Allah distance the one in whose presence you are mentioned and he does not send blessings upon you.\" I said, 'Ameen.' Jibril ﷺ then said, \"May Allah distance the one who reaches the month of Ramadan and does not have his sins forgiven.\" I said, 'Ameen.'\""],[16090,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a raiding party and said, “If Allah grants them safety, I will thank Him,” or he said, “It is upon me, if Allah grants them safety, that I thank Him.” They gained spoils and returned safely. He said, “O Allah, to You belongs praise in gratitude, and to You belongs favor in bounty.” The people waited for him to do something, but they did not see him do anything. They said, “O Messenger of Allah, you said what you said.” He said, “Did I not say: O Allah, to You belongs praise in gratitude, and to You belongs favor in bounty?”"],[16091,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ka'b b. Ujrah: “After me there will be rulers whom he described with tyranny. Whoever enters upon them and believes them in their lies and helps them in their wickedness—he is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will never reach the Pond. Whoever does not believe them in their lies and does not help them in their wickedness—he is of me, and I am of him, and he will reach the Pond. O Ka'b b. Ujrah, flesh grown from unlawful earnings deserves not to enter Paradise; the Fire is more worthy of it, and the Fire is more deserving of it.”"],[16092,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Ka'b b. Ujrah, people go forth in the morning: one who buys his own soul and sets it free, and one who sells his own soul and destroys it.”"],[16093,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Ka'ab bin Ujrah, people are of two categories, those who redeem themselves and those who destroy themselves.\""],[16094,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Ka'b b. Ujrah, people go forth in the morning: one who buys his own soul and sets it free, and one who sells his own soul and destroys it.”"],[16095,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever performs ablution and perfects the ablution, then heads to the mosque of Quba' intending nothing else and nothing prompts him to go early except prayer in the mosque of Quba', and prays four rak'ahs in it, reciting in each rak'ah Umm al-Qur'an—he will have the reward of one performing 'umrah to the House of Allah.”"],[16096,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Maghrib in the mosque of Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal. When he finished, some people stood up to pray voluntary prayers. The Prophet ﷺ said, “You should perform this prayer in the houses.”"],[16097,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man does not purify himself in his house and then go out except that he is in prayer until he performs his prayer. So let none of you interlace his fingers while he is in prayer.”"],[16098,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a veiled man passed by us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There will be division and disagreement among the people, and this man and his companions will be upon the truth.\" Ka'b said: I caught up with him and looked at him until I recognized him. We used to ask Ka'b who the man was, but he refused to tell us until Ka'b went out with Ali to Kufa and remained there until he died. Then we came to know that the man was Ali ؓ."],[16099,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day to his companions, \"What do you say about a man who is killed in the path of Allah?\" They said, \"Paradise.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Paradise, if Allah wills.\" He said, \"What do you say about a man who dies in the path of Allah?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"Paradise, if Allah wills.\" He said, \"What do you say about a man who dies and two just men stand and say, 'We know nothing but good'?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"Paradise, if Allah wills.\" He said, \"What do you say about a man who dies and two just men stand and say, 'We know no good'?\" They said, \"The Fire.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A sinner, but Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.\""],[16100,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not revile Ali, for he was possessed (devoted) in the essence of Allah, the Exalted.\""],[16101,"That the imam would come and not pray until the imam and the people had departed, going as if they were a neck (a group) toward the mosque. I said, \"Do you not see?\" He said, \"This is an innovation and abandonment of the Sunnah.\""],[16102,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when he said, \"O so-and-so, have you married?\" He said, \"No.\" Then he said to me, \"Have you married?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"A virgin or a previously married woman?\" I said, \"No, rather a previously married woman.\" He said, \"Why not a virgin whom you could bite and she could bite you?\""],[16103,"What did Ka'b ransom with when he shaved his head? He said, \"He slaughtered a cow.\""],[16104,"I bear witness that I saw four or five of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing saffron-dyed garments, among them Ka'b b. 'Ujrah."],[16105,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"When one of you performs ablution and then comes to the mosque, he should not interlace his fingers, for he is in prayer.\""],[16106,"That one of us would interlace his fingers in prayer. I said, \"I am not in prayer.\" He said, \"Did you not perform ablution while intending Jumu'ah?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then you are in prayer.\""],[16107,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “When you perform ablution and then go out heading to the mosque, do not interlace your fingers, for you are in prayer.”"],[16108,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Kaʿb, when you leave your house intending prayer, do not interlace your fingers.”"],[16109,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ who said, \"When you perform ablution, and you perfect the ablution, then you deliberately go to the mosque, do not interlock your fingers together.\""],[16110,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Hour will not come until a man manages the affairs of fifty women.”"],[16111,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded Kaʿb b. ʿUjrah to shave his head because of lice. Then he said: “Fast three days, or feed six poor people with two mudds each, or slaughter a sacrifice.”"],[16112,"The vermin of my head troubled me, so I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about that. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {And whoever among you is ill or has an ailment of the head, then a ransom of fasting, charity, or sacrifice}. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called me and said: “Do you have a faraq to distribute among six poor people?”—and the faraq is three sāʿs—“or the sacrifice of a sheep, or you fast three days?” I said: O Messenger of Allah, choose for me. He said: “Feed six poor people.”"],[16113,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever relieves a believer of a distress, Allah will relieve him of a distress on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever conceals the fault of a believer, Allah will conceal his fault. Whoever removes a hardship from a believer, Allah will remove a hardship from him.\""],[16114,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to shave my head and offer a sheep as ransom.\""],[16115,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us and said: \"Who is here? Do you hear? There will be rulers after me who act without obedience to Allah. Whoever shares in their deeds and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him. Whoever does not share in their deeds and does not help them in their wrongdoing is of me, and I am of him.\""],[16116,"I slaughtered a sheep."],[16117,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: \"There will be rulers over you after me who speak with wisdom from the pulpits, but when they descend, it is snatched from them, and their hearts are more foul than carrion. Whoever believes them in their lying and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to the Pond. Whoever does not believe them in their lying and does not help them in their wrongdoing is of me, and I am of him, and he will come to the Pond.\""],[16118,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes sin just as water extinguishes fire.\""],[16119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you have rulers, whoever enters upon them and believes them in their lying and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to the Pond. Whoever enters upon them and does not believe them in their lying and does not help them in their wrongdoing is of me, and I am of him. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, no flesh or blood that grew from unlawful earnings will enter Paradise; every flesh and blood that grew from unlawful earnings, the Fire is more deserving of them. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, people go out in the morning and return in the evening: one goes out to ransom his soul and sets it free, and another goes out and destroys it. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, prayer is a proof, and fasting is a shield.\""],[16120,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you have rulers, whoever enters upon them and believes them in their lying and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to the Pond. Whoever enters upon them and does not believe them in their lying and does not help them in their wrongdoing is of me, and I am of him. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, no flesh or blood that grew from unlawful earnings will enter Paradise; every flesh and blood that grew from unlawful earnings, the Fire is more deserving of them. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, people go out in the morning and return in the evening: one goes out to ransom his soul and sets it free, and another goes out and destroys it. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, prayer is a proof, and fasting is a shield.\""],[16121,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you have rulers, whoever enters upon them and believes them in their lying and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to the Pond. Whoever enters upon them and does not believe them in their lying and does not help them in their wrongdoing is of me, and I am of him. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, no flesh or blood that grew from unlawful earnings will enter Paradise; every flesh and blood that grew from unlawful earnings, the Fire is more deserving of them. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, people go out in the morning and return in the evening: one goes out to ransom his soul and sets it free, and another goes out and destroys it. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, prayer is a proof, and fasting is a shield.\""],[16122,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said, \"I saw the Night of Decree, but then I forgot it. Seek it in the last ten odd nights.\""],[16123,"“That he suffered an ailment in his head, and the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to shave [his head] and to ransom with a cow.”"],[16124,"[He asked] the Prophet ﷺ: With what should I perform the rite? He commanded him to offer a sacrificial animal, to garland it, then to drive it until he stops it at Arafah with the people, then to move on with it with the people, and thus he should do with the sacrificial animal."],[16125,"From Urwah: “Regarding the naming of those who attended al-Aqabah from the Ansar: Abu al-Yasar Kab b. Amr b. Abbad, and he attended Badr.”"],[16126,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq: “Regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Khazraj: Abu al-Yasar Kab b. Amr b. Abbad b. Amr b. Ghanm b. Sawwad b. Ghanm b. Kab b. Salamah b. Ali.”"],[16127,"“And it is said that he was the last to die of the people of Badr.”"],[16128,"Abu al-Yasar had a debt owed to him by a man. He came to him to demand payment at his family’s home. He [the debtor] said to his slave girl: Say he is not here. But he heard his voice, so he said: Come out, I heard your voice. He came out to him, and he said: What made you do what you did? He said: Hardship. He said: By God? He said: By God. He said: Go, for you owe nothing. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever grants respite to a debtor in difficulty or waives [the debt] for him will be in the shade of God on the Day of Resurrection, or under God’s protection.”"],[16129,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever grants respite to a debtor in difficulty or waives [the debt] for him, God will shade him in the shade of His Throne.”"],[16130,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever loves that God shade him in His shade, let him give respite to one in difficulty or waive [the debt] for him.”"],[16131,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever loves that God shade him in His shade, let him give respite to one in difficulty or waive [the debt] for him.”"],[16132,"Abu al-Yasar al-Ansari said: I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ when Abu ʿAmir al-Ashʿari came to him and said: He sent me on such-and-such [an expedition], then I came to Muʾtah. When the ranks were drawn up, Jaʿfar mounted his horse, put on his coat of mail, took the banner, and advanced on foot until he reached the people. Then he called out, “Who will convey this [banner] to its owner?” A man from the people said, “I will.” So he sent it with him, then he advanced and struck with his sword until he was killed. The eyes of the Messenger of God ﷺ overflowed with tears. He prayed Zuhr with us, then entered and did not speak to us. Then the ʿAsr prayer was called, and he came out and prayed, then entered and did not speak to us. He did the same at Maghrib and ʿIsha, entering and not speaking to us. Normally when he prayed he would turn his face toward us, but he came out to us at Fajr at the time he used to come out, while I and Abu ʿAmir al-Ashʿari were sitting. He sat between us and said, “Shall I tell you about a dream I saw? I entered Paradise and saw Jaʿfar with two wings stained with blood, and Zayd facing him, and Ibn Rawahah with them, as if he were turning away from them. I will tell you about that: when Jaʿfar advanced and saw death, he did not turn his face away; Zayd was the same; but Ibn Rawahah turned his face away.”"],[16133,"I set out with my father seeking knowledge among this neighborhood of the Ansar before they perished. The first one we met was Abu al-Yasar al-Sulami, the Companion of the Prophet ﷺ. He had a slave boy with him. He was wearing a striped cloak, and his slave boy was wearing a striped cloak, and [there was also] a Maʿafiri garment and a copy of the Quran with a strap. My father said to him, “I think I see a trace of anger on your face.” He said, “Yes, I was owed money by so-and-so, son of so-and-so, the highwayman. I went to his family and said, ‘Is he there?’ They said, ‘No.’ Then a young son of his came out to me, and I said to him, ‘Where is your father?’ He said, ‘He heard your voice and went into my mother’s curtained bed.’ I said, ‘Come out to me, for I know where you are.’ So he came out to me. I said, ‘What made you hide from me?’ He said, ‘By God, I will tell you and not lie to you. I feared, by God, that if I spoke to you I would lie to you, or if I promised you I would break my promise. I was a Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I was, by God, in difficulty.’ He said, ‘By God?’ I said, ‘By God.’ He said, ‘By God?’ I said, ‘By God.’ He said, ‘By God?’ I said, ‘By God.’ Then I forgot about the document, so I erased the debt and said, ‘If you find a means to pay, then pay; otherwise, you are absolved.’ I bear witness—these two eyes of mine saw, and he placed his two fingers on his eyes, and these two ears of mine heard, and he placed his two fingers in his ears, and this heart of mine comprehended, and he pointed to the place of his heart—that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, ‘Whoever gives respite to one in difficulty or waives [the debt] for him, God will shade him in His shade on a day when there is no shade but His shade.’”"],[16134,"I set out with my father seeking knowledge among this neighborhood of the Ansar before they perished. The first one we met was Abu al-Yasar al-Sulami, the Companion of the Prophet ﷺ. He had a slave boy with him. He was wearing a striped cloak, and his slave boy was wearing a striped cloak, and [there was also] a Maʿafiri garment and a copy of the Quran with a strap. My father said to him, “I think I see a trace of anger on your face.” He said, “Yes, I was owed money by so-and-so, son of so-and-so, the highwayman. I went to his family and said, ‘Is he there?’ They said, ‘No.’ Then a young son of his came out to me, and I said to him, ‘Where is your father?’ He said, ‘He heard your voice and went into my mother’s curtained bed.’ I said, ‘Come out to me, for I know where you are.’ So he came out to me. I said, ‘What made you hide from me?’ He said, ‘By God, I will tell you and not lie to you. I feared, by God, that if I spoke to you I would lie to you, or if I promised you I would break my promise. I was a Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I was, by God, in difficulty.’ He said, ‘By God?’ I said, ‘By God.’ He said, ‘By God?’ I said, ‘By God.’ He said, ‘By God?’ I said, ‘By God.’ Then I forgot about the document, so I erased the debt and said, ‘If you find a means to pay, then pay; otherwise, you are absolved.’ I bear witness—these two eyes of mine saw, and he placed his two fingers on his eyes, and these two ears of mine heard, and he placed his two fingers in his ears, and this heart of mine comprehended, and he pointed to the place of his heart—that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, ‘Whoever gives respite to one in difficulty or waives [the debt] for him, God will shade him in His shade on a day when there is no shade but His shade.’”"],[16135,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say, “O God, I seek refuge in You from being crushed [by a falling building], and I seek refuge in You from falling [from a height], and I seek refuge in You from drowning and burning, and I seek refuge in You from the devil seizing me at the time of death, and I seek refuge in You from dying from a snakebite.”"],[16136,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The transgressing faction will kill ʿAmmar.”"],[16137,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The transgressing faction will kill ʿAmmar.”"],[16138,"The Prophet ﷺ declared sacred what is between the two lava tracts of Madinah."],[16139,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness.”"],[16140,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness.”"],[16141,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is not an act of righteousness to fast while traveling.\""],[16142,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; and Abū Shuʿayb al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh b. Jaʿfar al-Raqqī narrated to us; and Abū Yazīd al-Qarāṭīsī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Shaybah al-Ḥizāmī narrated to us; and Muʿādh b. al-Muthannā narrated to us, saying: Musaddad narrated to us. They said: Sufyān b. ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Ṣafwān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ṣafwān, from Umm al-Dardāʾ, from Kaʿb b. ʿĀṣim, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16143,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16144,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16145,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16146,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16147,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16148,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16149,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16150,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16151,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16152,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16153,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness.”"],[16154,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivering a sermon during the Farewell Pilgrimage on the middle of the days of Tashriq, saying: “Is this day sacred?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Indeed your sanctity among yourselves is like the sanctity of this day of yours. Shall I tell you who the Muslim is? The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. Shall I tell you who the believer is? The one whom the Muslims trust with their lives and their wealth. And shall I tell you who the emigrant is? The emigrant is the one who abandons the evil deeds that Allah has forbidden him. And the believer is inviolable to the believer, like the sanctity of this day: his flesh is forbidden to him to eat it in his absence and to backbite him; his honor is forbidden to him to violate it; his face is forbidden to him to slap it; and harming him is forbidden to him to harm him; and it is forbidden to him to push him with a shove that knocks him down.”"],[16155,"Karāmah bt. al-Ḥusayn b. al-Ḥārith b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Kaʿb al-Māzinī narrated to me – and ʿAbd Allāh b. Kaʿb was in charge of the Prophet’s baggage on the day of Badr – she said: I heard my father narrate from Abū ʿAyyāsh al-Zuraqī, from Jābir b. ʿAbd Allāh: Kaʿb b. ʿĀṣim al-Ashʿarī narrated to me, saying: “I saw the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon on the middle of the days of sacrifice by the Jamrah.”"],[16156,"“And the name of Abū Sulmā was Rabīʿah b. Riyāḥ b. Qurẓ b. al-Ḥārith b. Māzin b. Thaʿlabah b. Thawr b. Hadmah b. Lāṭī b. ʿUthmān b. Muzaynah.”"],[16157,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah on his return from al-Ṭāʾif, Bujayr b. Zuhayr b. Abī Sulmā wrote to his brother Kaʿb b. Zuhayr b. Abī Sulmā, informing him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had killed a man in Makkah who had been satirizing and harming him, and that the remaining poets of Quraysh, Ibn al-Zibaʿrā and Hubayrah b. Abī Wahb, had fled in every direction. He said: “If you have any need for yourself, then flee to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for he does not kill anyone who comes to him repentant. And if you do not do so, then save yourself by your own means.” Kaʿb had composed some verses in which he had attacked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the letter reached Kaʿb, the earth became constricted for him, and he feared for himself, and those of his enemies who were in his presence spread rumors about him. They said, “He will be killed.” When he found no way out, he composed his poem in which he praised the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned his fear and the rumors of the slanderers about him from the next day. Then he departed until he reached Madinah. He stayed with a man from Juhaynah with whom he was acquainted, as he mentioned to me. Then the man went with him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after he had prayed the morning prayer. He prayed with the people, then he pointed out the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Prophet, to him and said, “This is the Messenger of Allah, so stand up to him and ask for his protection.” He mentioned to me that he stood up to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he placed his hand in his hand, and the Messenger of Allah did not know him. He said, “O Messenger of Allah, Kaʿb b. Zuhayr has come to seek your protection, repentant and Muslim. Will you accept from him if I bring him to you?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Yes.” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am Kaʿb b. Zuhayr.” Ibn Isḥāq said: ʿĀṣim b. ʿUmar b. Qatādah narrated to me, saying: A man from the Anṣār jumped at him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, let me deal with this enemy of Allah and strike his neck.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Leave him alone, for he has come repentant and remorseful.” He became angry with this clan of the Anṣār because of what their companion had done to him, and that is because he had not..."],[16158,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah on his return from al-Ṭāʾif, Bujayr b. Zuhayr b. Abī Sulmā wrote to his brother Kaʿb b. Zuhayr b. Abī Sulmā, informing him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had killed a man in Makkah who had been satirizing and harming him, and that the remaining poets of Quraysh, Ibn al-Zibaʿrā and Hubayrah b. Abī Wahb, had fled in every direction. He said: “If you have any need for yourself, then flee to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for he does not kill anyone who comes to him repentant. And if you do not do so, then save yourself by your own means.” Kaʿb had composed some verses in which he had attacked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the letter reached Kaʿb, the earth became constricted for him, and he feared for himself, and those of his enemies who were in his presence spread rumors about him. They said, “He will be killed.” When he found no way out, he composed his poem in which he praised the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned his fear and the rumors of the slanderers about him from the next day. Then he departed until he reached Madinah. He stayed with a man from Juhaynah with whom he was acquainted, as he mentioned to me. Then the man went with him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after he had prayed the morning prayer. He prayed with the people, then he pointed out the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Prophet, to him and said, “This is the Messenger of Allah, so stand up to him and ask for his protection.” He mentioned to me that he stood up to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he placed his hand in his hand, and the Messenger of Allah did not know him. He said, “O Messenger of Allah, Kaʿb b. Zuhayr has come to seek your protection, repentant and Muslim. Will you accept from him if I bring him to you?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Yes.” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am Kaʿb b. Zuhayr.” Ibn Isḥāq said: ʿĀṣim b. ʿUmar b. Qatādah narrated to me, saying: A man from the Anṣār jumped at him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, let me deal with this enemy of Allah and strike his neck.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Leave him alone, for he has come repentant and remorseful.” He became angry with this clan of the Anṣār because of what their companion had done to him, and that is because he had not..."],[16159,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed every nation has a trial, and the trial of my nation is wealth.”"],[16160,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Retaliation is of three types: a prince, one commanded, or an arrogant one.”"],[16161,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “If the son of Adam were given two valleys of wealth, he would wish for a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents.”"],[16162,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe his head once, like this, until he reached the back of the head.”"],[16163,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe his head from its front to its back, and he brought his hands out from beneath his ears.”"],[16164,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and rinsed his mouth three times and sniffed water into his nose three times, taking fresh water for each one, and washed his face three times. When he wiped his head, he said, “Like this,” and he gestured with his hand from the front of his head until he reached the bottom of his neck from the back of it."],[16165,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was performing ablution, and the water was flowing from his face over his beard and chest; he was separating between rinsing the mouth and sniffing water into the nose."],[16166,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing ablution, and he wiped over his head."],[16167,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out for the conquest of Makkah, he appointed Abu Ruham Kulthum b. al-Husayn al-Ghifari as his deputy over Madinah."],[16168,"He heard Abu Ruham al-Ghifari, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who pledged allegiance under the tree, say: I went on the expedition to Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When we traveled one night, I rode close to him, and drowsiness overcame me. I would start awake and find my mount near his mount, and its closeness alarmed me for fear of striking his foot in the stirrup, so I would draw my mount back. This continued until part of the night had passed, when sleep overpowered my eyes and my mount jostled against his foot in the stirrup and struck his foot. I did not wake except at his saying, 'Hass' (a word of pain). I said, 'Seek forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Move on.' The Prophet ﷺ then began asking me about those who had stayed behind from Banu Ghifar, and I informed him. He asked me, 'What happened to the long, reddish, hairless ones?' I told him that they had stayed behind. Then he said, 'What happened to the dark-complexioned, short, curly-haired, hairless ones who have livestock with branded young she-camels?' The narrator said: I tried to remember among Banu Ghifar, but I could not recall them until I remembered that they were a group from Aslam. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, those are a group from Aslam who stayed behind.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What prevents any one of those, when he stays behind, from carrying an active man on one of his camels in the path of Allah? Indeed, the dearest of my people to me that they should not stay behind from me are the Emigrants from Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam, and Ghifar.'"],[16169,"He heard Abu Ruham, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who pledged allegiance under the tree, say: I went on an expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I spent a night traveling close to him. Then he mentioned the hadith."],[16170,"He heard Abu Ruham, who was one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who pledged allegiance under the tree, say: I went on the expedition to Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he returned, he traveled at night through al-Akhdar, and I rode close to him. Drowsiness was cast upon us, and I kept waking and finding my mount near his mount, and its closeness alarmed me until I feared striking his foot in the stirrup, so I held my mount back. This continued until part of the night had passed, when sleep overcame my eyes and my mount jostled against the mount of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the stirrup and struck his foot. I did not wake except at his saying, 'Hass.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me.' He said, 'Move on.' The Prophet ﷺ then began asking me about those who had stayed behind from Banu Ghifar, and I informed him. He asked me, 'What happened to the group of reddish, tall, hairless ones?' I told him that they had stayed behind. Then he said, 'What happened to the dark-complexioned, short, curly-haired ones who have livestock with branded young she-camels?' The narrator said: I tried to remember among Banu Ghifar, but I could not recall them until I remembered that they were a group from Aslam who had stayed behind. They had been allies among us. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'What prevents any one of those, when he stays behind, from carrying an active man on one of his camels in the path of Allah? Indeed, the dearest of my people to me that they should not stay behind from me are the Emigrants from Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam, and Ghifar.' Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated it from al-Zuhri, and between the nephew of Abu Ruham and Ibn Ukaymah there is a connection."],[16171,"He heard Abu Ruham Kulthum b. Husayn, one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who pledged allegiance under the tree, say: I went on the expedition to Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One night I traveled with him while we were at al-Akhdar, close to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Drowsiness was cast upon us, and I kept waking and finding my mount near the mount of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and its closeness alarmed me for fear of striking his foot in the stirrup. I kept steering my mount away from him until part of the way had passed, and we were in part of the night, when sleep overcame my eyes and my mount jostled against the mount of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his foot in the stirrup. I did not wake except at his saying, 'Hass.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me.' He said, 'Move on.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then began asking me about those who had stayed behind from Banu Ghifar, and I informed him. He asked me, 'What happened to the group of reddish, tall, hairless ones?' I told him that they had stayed behind. He said, 'What happened to the dark-complexioned, curly-haired, short ones?' I said, 'By Allah, I do not recognize these as being from us.' He said, 'Yes, those who have livestock with branded young she-camels?' I then remembered them among Banu Ghifar, but I could not recall them until I remembered that they were a group from Aslam who had been allies among us. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, those are a group from Aslam who had been allies among us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What prevents any one of those, when he stays behind, from carrying an active man on one of his camels in the path of Allah? Indeed, the dearest of my people to me that they should not stay behind from me are the Emigrants from Quraysh, the Ansar, Ghifar, and Aslam.'"],[16172,"I and my brother were present at Khaybar, and we had horses. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted us six shares: four shares for the two horses and two shares for us. We sold our two shares for two young camels."],[16173,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would gather us—me, ‘Abd Allah, ‘Ubayd Allah, and Qutham—then he would spread his arms like this, extend his span, and say, “Whoever reaches me first will have such-and-such.”"],[16174,"From Kariz b. Samah, who had been a delegate to the Prophet ﷺ, he said: It was said, “O Messenger of God, pray against the Banu ‘Amir.” He said, “I was not sent as an invoker of curses.”"],[16175,"“The Prophet ﷺ tied a red banner for the Banu Sulaym.”"],[16176,"She heard her father asking the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “I vowed to sacrifice at Buwanah.” He asked, “Is there an idol or a tyrant worshipped there?” He said, “No.” He said, “Fulfill your vow.”"],[16177,"Kardam b. Sufyan al-Thaqafi came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I vowed to slaughter a herd of camels at Buwanah.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “Upon an idol?” He said, “No.” He said, “Upon one of the gatherings of the Jahiliyyah?” He said, “No.” He said, “Fulfill your vow wherever it may be, O Kardam. There is no vow and no oath in disobedience to God.”"],[16178,"He was called Abu Tha‘labah. On a hot day I had sandals and he had none. He said, “Give me your sandal.” I said, “No, unless you marry me to your daughter.” He said, “Give it to me, and I will marry her to you.” When we departed, he sent my sandals back to me and said, “You have no wife with me.” I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Leave her; there is no good for you in her.”"],[16179,"He was called Abu Tha‘labah. On a hot day I had sandals and he had none. He said, “Give me your sandal.” I said, “No, unless you marry me to your daughter.” He said, “Give it to me, and I will marry her to you.” When we departed, he sent my sandals back to me and said, “You have no wife with me.” I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Leave her; there is no good for you in her.”"],[16180,"I set out with my father from Madinah for some need, heading to Makkah. That was when the Prophet ﷺ was first mentioned in Makkah. He brought us to a sheep owner. In the middle of the night a wolf came and took a lamb from his flock. The shepherd jumped up and said, “O dweller of the valley, your neighbor!” We heard a voice but saw no speaker: “O wolf, release it.” The lamb came running, without a bite, until it entered the flock. And it was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in Madinah: {And there were men among mankind who sought refuge in men among the jinn} (the verse)."],[16181,"It is also said: Hillan b. Ghaniyy b. Yu‘sir b. Sa‘d b. Qays Ghaylan b. Mudar."],[16182,"From ‘Urwah, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God ﷺ: Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi, ally of Hamzah b. ‘Abd al-Muttalib. Abu Marthad died in the year twelve, at the age of sixty-six."],[16183,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Do not sit on graves and do not pray toward them.”"],[16184,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Do not sit at graves, and do not pray toward them.”"],[16185,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “ʿIsa son of Maryam ﷺ will descend at the white minaret in Damascus.”"],[16186,"While I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man from the Bedouins of Najd came to him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, is there an end to Islam?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Yes, any household of the Arabs or non-Arabs for whom Allah intends good, He will bring Islam upon them.” The Bedouin said: “Then what, O Messenger of Allah?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then trials will occur like the shadows.” The Bedouin said: “Not at all, O Messenger of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul! You will return in them as striking serpents, some of you striking the necks of others.”"],[16187,"From ʿUrwah regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of the conquest from the Muslims of Quraysh, then from Banu Muharib b. Fihr: Kurz b. Jabir."],[16188,"He went out with his father to a funeral which the Prophet ﷺ attended, while I was a boy old enough to understand. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"God loves that when a worker performs a deed, he does it well.\""],[16189,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"O people, seek Paradise with all your effort and flee from the Fire with all your effort, for Paradise's seeker does not sleep, and the Fire's fleer does not sleep. Indeed, the Hereafter today is surrounded by hardships, and this world is surrounded by desires.\""],[16190,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and stayed with him, then I left him. I came to him after a year and said: “O Messenger of Allah, do you not recognize me?” He said: “No.” I said: “I am the one who was with you last year.” He said: “What has changed you after me?” He said: “I have not eaten food during the day since I parted from you.” He said: “Who commanded you to torment yourself? Fast one day of the month of Surur.” I said: “Give me more,” and he increased for me until he said: “Fast three days of the month.”"],[16191,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ come out from the mountain pass of al-Matabikh until he came to the well of prayer, wearing a waist-wrapper wrapped around him, and he prayed two rakʿahs of Zuhr or ʿAsr, crossing its two ends."],[16192,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying near the upper well in a single garment."],[16193,"He told him that he used to trade in wine during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came from Syria with wine in leather skins, intending to trade with it. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have brought a good drink.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Kaysan, it has been forbidden.” Kaysan said: “Shall I go and sell it, O Prophet of Allah?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It has been forbidden, and its price is forbidden.” So Kaysan went to the skins, took them by their legs, and poured them all out."],[16194,"He told him that his father carried wine to Madinah before the Prophet ﷺ forbade it. He came to him and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: “What have you carried, O Abu Rafiʿ?” He said: “Wine, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Do you not know that it has been forbidden after you?” He said: “Should I sell it to the Jews?” He said: “Its seller is like its drinker.” So Abu Rafiʿ split his skins open at al-Bathaʾ."],[16195,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ from Yemen, and I pledged allegiance to him and accepted Islam at his hand."],[16196,"A Bedouin said: “O Messenger of Allah, is there an end to Islam?” He said: “Yes, any household of the Arabs or non-Arabs for whom Allah intends good, He will bring Islam upon them.” He said: “Then what, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Then trials will occur like the night.” The Bedouin said: “Not at all, O Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Not at all, by the One in whose hand is my soul! You will surely return in them as striking serpents, some of you striking the necks of others.”"],[16197,"While I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man from the Bedouins came to him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, is there an end to Islam?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Yes, any household of the Arabs or non-Arabs for whom Allah intends good, He will bring Islam upon them.” The Bedouin said: “Then what, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Then trials will occur like the shadows.” The Bedouin said: “Not at all, O Messenger of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul! You will surely return in them as striking serpents, some of you striking the necks of others.”"],[16198,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The eldest among brothers is in the position of the father.\""],[16199,"Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was the husband of the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ and the son of her maternal aunt. His mother was Hala bt. Khuwaylid b. Asad b. ‘Abd al-‘Uzza b. Qusayy, the sister of Khadija bt. Khuwaylid on her father's side, and her mother was Fatima bt. Za'ida. He is al-Asamm b. Jundub b. Harim b. Rawaha b. Hujr b. ‘Abd b. Ma‘is b. ‘Amir b. Lu'ayy. It is said that the name of Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was Mihsham, and he was called Jirw al-Batha'. Al-Zubayr said: Muhammad b. al-Hasan and Yahya b. Muhammad narrated to me, saying: \"The name of Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was Laqit.\" Al-Zubayr said: Muhammad b. al-Dahhak narrated to me from his father, saying: \"The name of Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was al-Qasim, and that is the established name. Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ died in Dhu al-Hijja in the year twelve.\""],[16200,"Zaynab, the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, became Muslim while her husband Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was a polytheist. Then he became Muslim after some time, and no marriage was renewed. ‘Abd al-Razzaq said: \"Ma‘mar mentioned from Jabir from al-Sha‘bi.\""],[16201,"He informed him that Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ b. ‘Abd al-‘Uzza b. ‘Abd Shams b. ‘Abd Manaf had married the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ. He was brought to the Prophet ﷺ among the ransom captives, and Zaynab came to him. ‘Amr said: \"I think they were both confirmed upon their marriage from the time of ignorance.\""],[16202,"Zaynab, the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ, became Muslim while her husband Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was a polytheist. Then he became Muslim after that, and the Prophet ﷺ confirmed them upon their marriage."],[16203,"The Messenger of God ﷺ returned Zaynab to Abu al-‘As under the first marriage and did not renew anything. There was disagreement about this, and others said with a new marriage."],[16204,"Zaynab, the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ, became Muslim a year before her husband Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘. Then he became Muslim, and the Prophet ﷺ returned her to him with a new marriage."],[16205,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my father is old and cannot perform Hajj, Umrah, or carry a burden.\" He ﷺ said, \"Perform Hajj and Umrah on behalf of your father and carry the burden for him.\" \"And the wording is from the hadith of Ali ibn Abdul Aziz.\""],[16206,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, my father is an old man who cannot perform Hajj or ‘Umrah or travel.\" He said, \"Perform Hajj on behalf of your father and ‘Umrah.\""],[16207,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The likeness of the believer is like the bee: it eats only what is good and produces only what is good.\""],[16208,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The likeness of the believer is like the bee: it eats only what is good and produces only what is good.\""],[16209,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A dream is one of forty parts, or one of forty-six parts, of prophethood. It is upon the leg of a bird; when it is interpreted, it comes to pass.” Shuʿba said in his narration, and I think he said: “Do not interpret it except with affection or sound judgment.”"],[16210,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The dream of a believer is one part of forty parts of prophethood. It is upon the leg of a bird as long as he does not relate it. When he relates it, it comes to pass.”"],[16211,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “A dream is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood. A dream is suspended upon the leg of a bird until its owner relates it. When he relates it, it comes to pass. So let him relate it only to a knowledgeable person, a sincere adviser, or a beloved friend.”"],[16212,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “A dream is upon the leg of a bird as long as it is not interpreted. When it is interpreted, it comes to pass.”"],[16213,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “A dream is upon the leg of a bird as long as it is not interpreted. When it is interpreted, it comes to pass.”"],[16214,"We said: “O Messenger of God, will all of us see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? And what is the sign of that in His creation?” He said: “Does not each of you see the moon clearly with it?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “God is greater.”"],[16215,"I said: “O Prophet of God, will all of us see our Lord?” He said: “Yes.” I said: “What is the sign of that in His creation?” He said: “Does not each of you look at the moon on the night of the full moon? It is only a creature among the creatures of God, and God is greater and more majestic.”"],[16216,"He said, \"Indeed, we used to slaughter sacrificial animals in the month of Rajab, and we would eat from them and feed others. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'There is no harm in that.' And Waki' said, 'I will never abandon it.'\""],[16217,"I said: “O Messenger of God, where was our Lord before He created the heaven and the earth?” He said: “He was in a cloud, beneath which was air and above which was air. Then He created His Throne upon the water.”"],[16218,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God, exalted is He, laughs at the despair of His servants and the nearness of His relief.” Abu Razin said: “I said: ‘O Messenger of God, does the Lord laugh?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ He said: ‘We will never be deprived of good from a Lord who laughs.’”"],[16219,"I said: “O Messenger of God, how does God revive the dead?” He said: “Have you not passed by a valley of your people and found it barren, then passed by it and found it green, then passed by it and found it barren, then passed by it and found it green? Thus does God revive the dead.”"],[16220,"I said: “O Messenger of God, where is my mother?” He said: “Your mother is in the Fire.” He said: “Then where are those of your family who have passed away?” He said: “Are you not content that your mother be with my mother?”"],[16221,"The Prophet ﷺ disliked questions and found fault with them. But when Abu Razin asked him, he answered him and was pleased by that."],[16222,"I arrived at Kufa with a companion of mine to bring back sandals from there. We went early to the market, while it had not yet arisen. I said to my companion, 'If only we entered the mosque' - and the mosque in those days was where the date-sellers were. So we entered, and there was a man from Qays called Ibn al-Muntafiq. I heard him saying: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was described to me and made clear to me, so I sought him in Makkah and was told he was in Mina. I sought him in Mina and was told he was at Arafat. I caught up with him while he was among a group of his companions riding. It was said to me, \"Move aside from the path of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Leave the man alone; what does he need?\" I drew near until I took hold of the nose-rein of his camel or its halter, and I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I ask you about what will save me from the Fire and what will bring me to Paradise.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head to the sky, then lowered it, then turned his face toward me and said, \"If you have been brief in the question, you have asked about something tremendous and lengthy. So remember from me: worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him; establish the prescribed prayer; pay the obligatory zakat; fast Ramadan; and whatever you would love people to do to you, do it to them; and whatever you would hate people to do to you, leave people alone from it. Let the camel go,\" or \"the mount.\" Hammam said: \"As for Hajj, he had already performed Hajj when he asked him.\""],[16223,"from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They said, \"At Arafah.\" So I went to him, and I started to draw near to him until the neck of my mount passed the neck of his mount. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, teach me what will save me from the punishment of Allah and admit me to His Paradise.\" He said, \"Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him; establish the prescribed prayer; pay the obligatory zakat; perform Hajj and Umrah,\" and I think he said, \"and fast Ramadan; and look at what you would love people to bring to you and do it to them, and what you would hate them to bring to you, leave them alone from it.\" \"Ibn Awn was confused in the chain of this hadith and did not control it from Muhammad b. Juhadah, but Hammam controlled it.\""],[16224,"from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They said, \"At Arafah.\" So I went to him, and I started to draw near to him until the neck of my mount passed the neck of his mount. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, teach me what will save me from the punishment of Allah and admit me to His Paradise.\" He said, \"Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him; establish the prescribed prayer; pay the obligatory zakat; perform Hajj and Umrah,\" and I think he said, \"and fast Ramadan; and look at what you would love people to bring to you and do it to them, and what you would hate them to bring to you, leave them alone from it.\" \"Ibn Awn was confused in the chain of this hadith and did not control it from Muhammad b. Juhadah, but Hammam controlled it.\""],[16225,"\"Laaqit ibn 'Amir went to the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , accompanied by his friend named Nuhayk ibn 'Asim ibn Malik ibn Muntafiq. Laaqit said, 'I left and my friend and I reached Madinah in the middle of the month of Rajab when we came to the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , after he finished the Fajr prayer. He stood up to address the people and said, 'O people, I have concealed my voice from you for four days to make you hear it today. So, is there anyone whose people have sent him?' They said, 'Inform us what the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said.' He replied, 'Perhaps he is preoccupied with his own speech or the speech of his companion, or perhaps the deviators are distracting him. Indeed, I am responsible to convey. Have I conveyed?' He repeated this three times. Then he said, 'Listen and live, listen and live, sit down.' The people sat down, and my friend and I stood until he finished. When he was at ease, I asked, 'O Messenger of Allah, what knowledge of the unseen do you possess?' He laughed and shook his head, knowing that I sought some confidential information from him. He said, 'By the oath of Allah, your Lord, has kept five things of the unseen that only He knows.' He pointed with his hand and I asked, 'O Messenger of Allah, what are they?' He replied, 'The knowledge of when a person will die, which none of you know; and the knowledge of when the sperm will fertilize the ovum, which none of you know; and the knowledge of what will happen tomorrow, which none of you know, whether you will be eating tomorrow or not; and the knowledge of the unseen matters that will happen on the Day of Judgment, where the righteous will be honored and the wicked will be humiliated, and your Lord will continue to laugh, knowing that your return is close.' Laaqit said, 'I said, we will not be deprived of a Lord who laughs, which is good news. And the knowledge of the Hour.'\""],[16226,"The orphan Ibn Amir went to visit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , accompanied by his companion, known as Nihik bin Asim bin Malik bin Muntafiq. Laqit said, \"I went out with my companion until we reached the city of Medina in the month of Rajab. We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he finished the morning prayer and stood up to address the people. He said, 'O people, know that I have withheld my voice from you for four days in order to make you hear today. Is there anyone who has been sent by his people?' They said, 'We do not know what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ says.' He then said, 'Perhaps he was preoccupied with talking to himself or with the conversation of his companion, or perhaps he was distracted by misguidance. Know that I am responsible, have I conveyed the message? Listen and you shall live, listen and you shall live, listen and sit down.' The people sat down and I and my companion remained standing until he finished his speech and regained his composure. I then said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what knowledge do you have of the unseen?' He laughed and shook his head. He knew that I was seeking knowledge of the gender of my unborn child, and he said, 'Your Lord has knowledge of five things from the unseen which no one other than Him knows.' He gestured with his hand and I asked, 'What are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'He knows the time of death of every one of you, but you do not know it. He knows when a fetus is in the womb, but you do not know it. He knows what will happen tomorrow, but you do not know it. He knows what you will eat tomorrow, but you do not know it. And He knows what will happen on the Day of Judgment, but you do not know it. And He watches over you, worried and fearful, while your Lord continues to laugh, knowing that your return is near.' Laqit said, 'I said, we will never be deprived of a Lord who laughs, which is a good thing. And He knows what will happen on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[16227,"\"Layth ibn 'Amir went to visit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and with him was his companion named Nahik ibn 'Asim ibn Malik ibn Muntfiq. Layth said, 'I went out, and my companion and I reached Madinah during the last part of the month of Rajab. We went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after he finished the dawn prayer. He stood among the people and delivered a sermon, saying, \"O people, behold, I have been hiding my voice from you for four days in order to be able to address you today. Is there anyone who has been sent by his people?\" They said, \"Inform us of what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ says.\" He then said, \"Perhaps he is preoccupied with his own matters or with the matters of his companion, or he is being misled. Behold, I am responsible. Have I conveyed the message?\" He said, \"Listen so that you may live! Listen so that you may live! Sit down.\" The people sat down, and my companion and I remained standing until he finished. When his heart and sight settled, I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what knowledge do you have of the unseen?\" By Allah, he smiled and shook his head, and he knew that I wanted to ask him about a certain matter. He said, \"Your Lord has foreknowledge of five matters of the unseen that no one knows except Him.\" He then gestured with his hand and I asked, \"What are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Knowledge of the appointed time of one's death, which you do not know, and knowledge of when the sperm enters the womb, which you do not know, and knowledge of what will happen tomorrow, which you do not know, and knowledge of the unseen, which you do not know, and knowledge of the Day of Judgment, which is under His control. Your Lord laughs in His knowledge that He knows that your return is near.\" Layth said, \"I said, 'We will never be deprived of a Lord who laughs well.' And knowledge of the Day of Judgment.\""],[16228,"\"Laqeet bin Amir went as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , accompanied by his friend called Nihik bin Asim bin Malik bin Montafiq. Laqeet left and I followed with my friend until we reached the city of Madinah during the month of Rajab. We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he finished the Fajr prayer and stood among the people as a speaker. He said, 'O people, know that I have hidden my voice from you for four days so that I can be heard today. Is there anyone sent by his people?' They said, 'Inform us what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ says.' He said, 'Perhaps he is preoccupied with his own thoughts or the thoughts of his friend, or perhaps he is led astray by the misguidance. Behold, I am responsible, have I conveyed the message?' So listen and live, listen and live, sit down.' The people sat down and I and my friend remained standing until he finished addressing the people, with a serene heart and clear sight. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what knowledge of the unseen do you possess?' He laughed, swore by Allah, shook his head, and knew that I sought his approval. He said, 'Your Lord has knowledge of five things from the unseen that no one else knows except Him.' He pointed with his hand and said, 'What they are, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Knowledge of the appointed time of death of every individual, which you do not know, knowledge of when the sperm is in the womb, which you do not know, knowledge of what will happen tomorrow, which you are not aware of what you will eat tomorrow, and knowledge of the unseen of the future, which causes you to be afraid and worried, but your Lord still laughs and He has known that your return is indeed near.' Laqeet said, 'I said, we will never be deprived of a Lord who laughs, it is good indeed, and knowledge of the Hour.'\""],[16229,"\"Lāqiṭ ibn ʿAamir went and arrived to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, accompanied by his companion named Nahīk ibn ʿAasim ibn Mālik ibn Muntafiq. Lāqiṭ said, 'I left and my companion and I arrived to Madinah during the month of Rajab. We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after he finished the morning prayer, and he stood up to address the people. He said, 'O people, indeed I have hidden my voice for you for the past four days so that I may speak to you today. Does anyone know what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said?' They replied, 'Tell us what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.' He continued, 'Indeed, perhaps he was preoccupied with his own thoughts, or the words of his companion, or the whisperings of the misled. Verily, I am accountable, have I conveyed?' So listen and live, so listen and live, so sit down.' The people sat down, and my companion and I stood until he finished his address. When he became relaxed and calm, I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what knowledge of the unseen do you possess?' The Messenger of Allah laughed and shook his head, and he knew that I sought knowledge of the unborn child. He said, 'Your Lord has knowledge of five things of the unseen that no one knows except Him.' And he gestured with his hand. I said, 'What are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He replied, 'The knowledge of when a person will pass away, which none of you know, the knowledge of when sperm will be in the womb and when it will not be, which none of you know, the knowledge of what will happen tomorrow and whether tomorrow you will eat, which none of you know, and the knowledge of the unseen day which will be upon you, anxious and fearful, and your Lord will still be laughing, knowing that your return is near.' Lāqiṭ said, 'I said, \"We will not be deprived of a Lord who laughs, that is good.\" And the knowledge of the hour.'\""],[16230,"Layth ibn 'Amir went to meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he had a companion with him named Nuhayk ibn 'Asim ibn Malik ibn Muntafiq. Layth said, \"I went out and my companion and I traveled until we reached Madinah in the month of Rajab. We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as he finished the Fajr prayer and stood up to deliver a sermon. He said, 'O people, behold, I have saved my voice for you for the past four days so that I may address you today. Are there any individuals whose people have sent them?' They replied, 'Inform us what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is saying.' He said, 'Perhaps he is distracte\u000f by his own thoughts or the talk of his companion, or perhaps he is distracte\u000f by the wandering thoughts. Behold, I am being asked if I have conveyed the message. Behold, listen carefully and you shall live. Behold, listen carefully and you shall live. Behold, sit down.' The people sat down and my companion and I remained standing until he finished his speech. When his heart and eyes were at rest, I asked, 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you know of the unseen?' He laughed by the oath of Allah, shook his head, and knew that I was seeking scientific knowledge from him. He said, 'Your Lord has knowledge of five things from the unseen that only He knows. 'He then pointed with his hand and I asked, 'What are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Knowledge of when a person's life will end, a knowledge that you don't possess, and knowledge of when a person's semen is in the uterus, a knowledge that you don't possess, and knowledge of what will happen tomorrow, a knowledge that you don't possess, and knowledge of the Day of Judgment, which will come to you suddenly and you will not know it, and knowledge of what will happen in the unseen future, a knowledge that you don't possess.\" Layth said, \"I said, 'We will not be deprived of a Lord who laughs, and knowledge of the Hour.'\""],[16231,"Laeet bin Aamir left and went to the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , accompanied by his companion named Nahiik bin Aasim bin Maalik bin Mintafiq. Laeet said, \"I went out and my companion and I reached Al-Madinah during the month of Rajab. We came to the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , when he finished his morning prayer. He stood among the people and delivered a sermon, saying, 'O people, I have hidden my voice from you for four days to listen to you today. Is there anyone whose people have sent him?' They said, 'Inform us about what the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said.' He said, 'Perhaps he is preoccupied with his own talk or the talk of his companion, or he is being deceived. Indeed, I am accountable, have I conveyed [the message]?' So listen so you may live, so listen so you may live, so sit down.' The people sat down, and my companion and I stood until he finished. When his mind and sight returned to us, I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what knowledge of the unseen do you have?' He laughed and shook his head, and he knew that I was seeking information from him. He said, 'Your Lord has knowledge of five things from the unseen that no one knows except Him.' He gestured with his hand, so I said, 'What are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'The knowledge of when a person's life will end, which you do not know, the knowledge of semen when it is in the womb, which is known while you do not know, the knowledge of what will happen tomorrow, which has been known while you are not aware, and the knowledge of the unseen Day of Judgment, in which you are humble and fearful. And your Lord continues to smile, knowing that your return is near.' Laeet said, I said, 'We will not be deprived of a Lord who smiles, and [He has] good. And the knowledge of the Hour.'\""],[16232,"Al-Laqit ibn 'Amir went out and encountered the Messenger of Allah ﷺ along with his companion, whose name was Nihik ibn 'Asim ibn Malik ibn Muntafiq. Laqit said, \"I went out with my companion until we reached al-Madinah during the month of Rajab, after the Messenger of Allah had finished the Fajr prayer. He stood up amongst the people as a preacher and said, 'O people, be aware that I have been hiding my voice from you for the past four days, so that I may convey to you today. Is there anyone who will convey his people's message to them?' The people said, 'We know not what the Messenger of Allah will say.' Then he continued, 'It may be that he is preoccupied with his own affairs or the affairs of his companion, or the misguidance may distract him. Verily, I am accountable. Did I convey?' Listen attentively so that you may live on. Yes, listen attentively so that you may live on. Sit down.' The people sat down, and my companion and I stood until he was done with us. When he was relaxed and his vision clear, I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what knowledge do you have of the unseen?' He laughed and shook his head. He knew that I desired his discourse on this matter, so he said, 'Your Lord has knowledge of five unseen things, which no one knows except Him.' Then he gestured with his hand, and I said, 'What are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Knowledge of when one of you will have a wet dream, which you do not know. Knowledge of when the semen combines in the womb, which you do not know. Knowledge of what will happen tomorrow, which you do not know, whether you will eat breakfast or not. Knowledge of when the Hour will occur, which is unknown to you. And knowledge of what is in the unseen, which will cause you to be humble and fearful, while your Lord still laughs, knowing that your return is near.' Laqit said, 'I said, we shall never be deprived of a Lord who laughs is for our own good. And knowledge of the Hour.'\""],[16233,"Laqit ibn Amir went out and arrived at the Messenger of Allah, with him was his friend named Nuhik ibn Asim ibn Malik ibn Muntafiq. Laqit said, \"I went out and my friend and I traveled until we reached Madinah in the month of Rajab, when we came to the Messenger of Allah after he finished the morning prayer and stood in front of the people as a speaker. He said, 'O people, I have hidden my voice from you for four days so that I could make you hear it today. Is there anyone among you whose people have sent him?' They said, 'Tell us what the Messenger of Allah said.' He said, 'Perhaps he is preoccupied with his own speech or the speech of his companion, or the evil ones are distracting him. Indeed, I am responsible, have I conveyed the message? Indeed, I am responsible, have I conveyed the message? Indeed, I am responsible, have I conveyed the message? Now sit down.' The people sat down, and both my friend and I stood until the Messenger of Allah was done talking. When he had finished, I asked, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you have any knowledge of the unseen?' He smiled and shook his head and knew that I was seeking information about a fetus. He said, 'Your Lord has knowledge of five things from the unseen that nobody knows except Him.' And he pointed with his hand. I said, 'What are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Knowledge of when a person will die, and you do not know it. Knowledge of when the sperm will be in the womb, and you do not know it. Knowledge of what will happen tomorrow, and you do not know it, and knowledge of the unseen on the Day of Judgment when you will be gathered, and your Lord will be watching you closely and will laugh. He knows that your return is near.' Laqit said, 'I said, we will never be deprived of a Lord who laughs favorably. And knowledge of the Day of Judgment"],[16234,"Laeqit ibn Amir left and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his companion named Nahiq ibn Asim ibn Malik ibn Montafiq. Laeqit said: \"I went out and my companion and I traveled until we reached Madinah on the 27th of Rajab. We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he finished the morning prayer and stood up to give a sermon. He said, 'O people, know that I have been hiding my voice from you for the past four days so that I can speak to you today. Is there anyone whose people have sent him?' They said, 'We do not know what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is saying.' He replied, 'Perhaps he is preoccupied with his own talk or with the talk of his companion, or perhaps he is distracted by misguidance. Know that I have a question for you, have you conveyed [my message]?' 'Yes,' they replied. 'Then listen and live, listen and live, sit down.' So the people sat down, and my companion and I stood until he had finished speaking. Then, when his heart and sight were settled, I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what knowledge do you have of the unseen?' He laughed and shook his head and knew that I was seeking a favor from him. He said, 'Your Lord is inclined to five things of the unseen that no one knows except Him.' And he pointed with his hand. So I asked, 'What are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'The knowledge of the exact time of one's death, which you do not know, and the knowledge of the time when a drop of semen is inside the womb, which is known but you do not know, and the knowledge of what will happen tomorrow, which is known, but you do not know if you will be alive or not, and the knowledge of the unseen of that Day [of Judgment], which is mighty and concerning which you will feel awe. And your Lord laughs knowing that your return is soon.' Laeqit said, 'I said, \"We will not be without a Lord who laughs, which is good.\" And the knowledge of the Hour.'"],[16235,"Laqit ibn 'Amir went to visit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his companion named Nihik ibn 'Asim ibn Malik ibn Muntafiq. Laqit said, \"I went out with my companion until we reached Madinah, during the month of Rajab, and we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after he finished praying Fajr. He stood among the people as a preacher and said, 'O people, indeed I have saved my voice for you for four days so that I can address you today. Is there anyone among you who has been sent by his people?' They said, 'Inform us about what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ says.' He said, 'Perhaps he is being occupied by his own speech or the speech of his companion, or he may be distracted by misguidance. Indeed, I have a question: have I conveyed the message?' He repeated this three times and said, 'Listen carefully, live a good life, and sit down.' The people sat down, and my companion and I remained standing until he finished speaking. Then, when he had some rest, I asked him, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you have knowledge of the unseen?' He smiled and shook his head, and he knew that I was trying to make him reveal something. He said, 'Your Lord has some knowledge of the unseen, of which only He has knowledge, and He motioned with his hand. I asked, 'What is it, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Knowledge of when one will die, which you do not know, and knowledge of when the sperm will be in the womb, which has been known, and knowledge of what will happen tomorrow, which has been known, for you do not know whether you will be alive or not. And knowledge of the unseen, which brings fear to those who possess it, while your Lord continues to laugh, to show that He knows your return is near.' Laqit said, 'I said, We will not be deprived of a Lord who laughs is a good thing, and knowledge of the Hour.'\""],[16236,"from the Prophet ﷺ about game that disappears from its owner. He said, \"Perhaps the vermin of the earth killed it.\""],[16237,"I set out with a companion of mine until we reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but we did not find him. Aisha fed us dates and prepared for us some porridge. Then the Prophet ﷺ came walking briskly, swaying. He said, \"Have you fed them anything?\" We said, \"Yes.\" While we were in that state, the shepherd drove the sheep to the enclosure, and in his hand was a newborn lamb. He said, \"Has it given birth?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then slaughter a sheep.\" Then he turned his face toward us and said, \"Do not think\" - and he did not say \"Do not think\" - \"that we slaughtered the sheep because of you two. We have a hundred sheep, and we do not want them to increase beyond that. When a lamb is born to the shepherd, we order him to slaughter a sheep.\""],[16238,"I set out with a companion of mine until we reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but we did not find him. Aisha fed us dates and prepared for us some porridge. Then the Prophet ﷺ came walking briskly, swaying. He said, \"Have you fed them anything?\" We said, \"Yes.\" While we were in that state, the shepherd drove the sheep to the enclosure, and in his hand was a newborn lamb. He said, \"Has it given birth?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then slaughter a sheep.\" Then he turned his face toward us and said, \"Do not think\" - and he did not say \"Do not think\" - \"that we slaughtered the sheep because of you two. We have a hundred sheep, and we do not want them to increase beyond that. When a lamb is born to the shepherd, we order him to slaughter a sheep.\""],[16239,"I set out with a companion of mine until we reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but we did not find him. Aisha fed us dates and prepared for us some porridge. Then the Prophet ﷺ came walking briskly, swaying. He said, \"Have you fed them anything?\" We said, \"Yes.\" While we were in that state, the shepherd drove the sheep to the enclosure, and in his hand was a newborn lamb. He said, \"Has it given birth?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then slaughter a sheep.\" Then he turned his face toward us and said, \"Do not think\" - and he did not say \"Do not think\" - \"that we slaughtered the sheep because of you two. We have a hundred sheep, and we do not want them to increase beyond that. When a lamb is born to the shepherd, we order him to slaughter a sheep.\""],[16240,"that he came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned something, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Perform ablution thoroughly and pass between the fingers.\""],[16241,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said, \"Perform ablution thoroughly and pass between the fingers, and when you inhale water into the nose, do it deeply, unless you are fasting.\" \"Their wording is identical.\""],[16242,"that he came to Aisha, he and a companion of his, seeking the Prophet ﷺ, but they did not find him. Aisha fed them both porridge. It was not long before the Prophet ﷺ came walking briskly, swaying. He said, \"Did you feed them both?\" We said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, prayer?\" He said, \"Perform ablution thoroughly and pass between the fingers, and inhale water into the nose deeply, unless you are fasting.\""],[16243,"that he came to Aisha, he and a companion of his, seeking the Prophet ﷺ, but they did not find him. Aisha fed them both porridge. It was not long before the Prophet ﷺ came walking briskly, swaying. He said, \"Did you feed them both?\" We said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, prayer?\" He said, \"Perform ablution thoroughly and pass between the fingers, and inhale water into the nose deeply, unless you are fasting.\""],[16244,"that he came to Aisha, he and a companion of his, seeking the Prophet ﷺ, but they did not find him. Aisha fed them both porridge. It was not long before the Prophet ﷺ came walking briskly, swaying. He said, \"Did you feed them both?\" We said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, prayer?\" He said, \"Perform ablution thoroughly and pass between the fingers, and inhale water into the nose deeply, unless you are fasting.\""],[16245,"He said: \"We have a neighbor who drinks wine and commits vile acts, so raise his matter to the authority.\" He said: \"I killed ninety-nine alongside the Messenger of God ﷺ; I would not love that I had killed the like of them and that I had uncovered the veil of a Muslim.\""],[16246,"Laqit b. Sabira al-Sakuni: \"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with my two legs crooked, not touching the ground. He supplicated for me, and I walked on the ground.\""],[16247,"I saw Lubayy b. Labba al-Asadi, and he was a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ or had met the Prophet ﷺ. A horse of his won, and he draped it with an Adeni striped cloak, and I saw on him a garment of silk or a fine cloak."],[16248,"\"I have not filled my belly with food since I became Muslim with the Prophet ﷺ; I eat what suffices me and drink what suffices me.\" Al-'Ala' said: \"He means my strength.\""],[16249,"He informed him that he was sitting in the market when a woman passed carrying a child. The people rose, and I rose with them, and we went until we reached the Prophet ﷺ while he was saying: \"Who is the father of this child with you?\" She remained silent. A young man beside her said: \"I am his father, O Messenger of God.\" He turned to her and said: \"Who is the father of this child with you?\" She remained silent. The young man said: \"O Messenger of God, she is young in age, recently wed, and she will not speak to you. I am his father, O Messenger of God.\" The Prophet ﷺ looked at some of his companions as if asking them about him. They said: \"We know nothing but good,\" or something like that. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Have you been married?\" He said: \"Yes.\" The Prophet ﷺ ordered that he be stoned. We went out with him and dug for him until we made it possible, then we threw stones at him until he became still. Then we returned to our gatherings. While we were thus, an old man came asking about the stoned man. We stood up to him, seized him by the collar, and took him to the Prophet ﷺ. We said: \"O Messenger of God, this man came asking about the wicked one.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Stop! He is more fragrant to God than the scent of musk.\" We left with the old man, and behold, he was his father. We reached him and helped him with his washing, shrouding, and burial. He said: \"I do not know whether he said the prayer over him or not.\""],[16250,"We were boys working in the market. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered a man and he was stoned. A man came asking us about him, so we brought him to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, this man came asking us about this wicked one who was stoned today.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not say wicked. By God, he is more fragrant to God than musk.\""],[16251,"We were boys running to the market. A man who confessed to adultery was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he was stoned. A man came asking us about the place of that stoned man. We came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, this man is asking us about that wicked one.\" He said: \"Do not say wicked. By God, he is more fragrant to God than musk.\""],[16252,"My father said to me: 'O my son, when I die, bury me in a niche grave. When you place me in my niche, say: \"In the name of God and upon the creed of the Messenger of God.\" Then scatter the soil over me gently. Then recite at my head the opening of al-Baqarah and its conclusion, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say that.'"],[16253,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ recited this verse: {So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you as a witness against these?}, the Messenger of God ﷺ wept and said: \"O Lord, this I witnessed over those among whom I was present, so how about those whom I did not see?\""],[16254,"It was presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Khaybar a cooked sheep. He and Bashir bin Al-Bara' bin Ma'rur ate from it, then both of them became seriously ill. Eventually, Bashir died. When he died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to the Jewish woman who had presented it and said, \"What did you feed us, may Allah curse you?\" She replied, \"I poisoned you.\" He asked, \"What made you do that?\" She said, \"I heard you mention that if you were a prophet, it would not harm you, but if you were not, I wanted to relieve people from you.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered her to be crucified."],[16255,"Urwa reported: \"Regarding the naming of the one who witnessed the Battle of Badr from the Ansar, then from the tribe of Banu Zuhrā ibn ‘Abd al-Ashhal: Muhammad ibn Muslimah ibn Khalid ibn ‘Adi ibn Majda‘ah ibn Harithah ibn al-Harith.\""],[16256,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from the Aws, from Banu Harithah: Muhammad b. Maslama.\""],[16257,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq: \"In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Harithah: Muhammad b. Maslama b. Khalid b. 'Adi b. Majda'a b. Harithah b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj b. 'Amr b. Malik b. al-Aws, and he was an ally of Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal.\""],[16258,"Muhammad ibn Muslimah passed away in Medina in the year forty-three, at the age of seventy-seven years."],[16259,"\"Muhammad b. Maslama died in Safar in the year forty-three.\""],[16260,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When Allah casts the proposal of a woman into the heart of a man, there is no harm in him looking at her.\" This is what Yahya ibn Al-Ala'a reported from Al-Hajjaj, from Muhammad ibn Uthman."],[16261,"I sought to marry a woman, so I began to hide myself to look at her. It was said to him, “Do you do this while you are a companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘When God casts into the heart of one of you the desire to propose to a woman, there is no harm in his looking at her.’” Hafs b. Ghiyath narrated it thus, and Yazid b. Harun concurred with him."],[16262,"I saw Muhammad b. Maslamah directing his gaze at the daughter of al-Dahhak. I said, “Glory be to God! You look at her while you are one of the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said, “Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘When God casts into a person’s heart the desire to propose to a woman, there is no harm in his looking at her.’” Yahya b. Sa‘id narrated it from Muhammad b. Sulayman b. Abi Hathma, from his paternal uncle Sahl b. Abi Hathma, just as Hafs b. Ghiyath and Yazid b. Harun narrated it from al-Hajjaj."],[16263,"I was sitting with Muhammad b. Maslamah when the daughter of al-Dahhak passed behind him, and he began to track her with his gaze. I said, “Glory be to God! You do this while you are a companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said, “Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘When God casts the desire to propose to a woman into a man’s heart, there is no harm in his looking at her.’”"],[16264,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “When God casts into a person’s heart the desire to propose to a woman, there is no harm in his looking at her.” Abd al-Wahid b. Ziyad narrated it thus from al-Hajjaj, from Muhammad b. Sulayman b. Abi Hathma, from his father."],[16265,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “When God casts into a person’s heart the desire to propose to a woman, there is no harm in his looking at her.” Abu Mu‘awiya narrated it thus from al-Hajjaj, from Sahl b. Muhammad b. Abi Hathma, from his paternal uncle Sulayman b. Abi Hathma."],[16266,"I saw Muhammad b. Maslamah al-Ansari look at the daughter of al-Dahhak, who was on a wall playing, and he kept looking at her. It was said to him, “Do you look at her while you are a companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said, “Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘When God casts into a person’s heart the desire to propose to a woman, there is no harm in his looking at her.’” Hammad b. Salama narrated it thus and contradicted others in it. The narrators differed concerning al-Hajjaj b. Artah in this hadith. The correct version in my view, and God knows best, is what Hafs b. Ghiyath and Yazid b. Harun narrated from al-Hajjaj, from Muhammad b. Sulayman b. Abi Hathma, from his paternal uncle Sahl b. Abi Hathma, from Muhammad b. Maslamah."],[16267,"Al-Mughira said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled in it a ghurra (a slave, male or female).” Umar said, “If you are truthful, bring someone who knows that.” Muhammad b. Maslamah testified that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ rule in it a ghurra."],[16268,"Umar consulted the people about the fetus that a woman miscarries. Al-Mughira said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled in it a ghurra, a male or female slave.” Umar said, “If you are truthful, bring someone to testify with you.” Muhammad b. Maslamah testified that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ rule that."],[16269,"Al-Mughira said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled in it a ghurra, a male or female slave.” Umar said, “Who will testify with you if you are truthful?” Muhammad b. Maslamah testified that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ rule that."],[16270,"Al-Mughira b. Shu‘ba said, “I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ rule in it a ghurra, a male or female slave.” He said, “Then bring me someone to testify with you.” So Muhammad b. Maslamah came to him."],[16271,"A grandmother came to Abu Bakr seeking her inheritance from her son or daughter. Abu Bakr said, “I find nothing for you in the Book of God, and I have not heard the Messenger of God ﷺ rule anything for you. I will ask the people this evening.” When he had prayed Zuhr, he turned to the people and said, “A grandmother has come to me asking for her inheritance from her son or daughter. I find nothing for her in the Book, and I have not heard the Messenger of God ﷺ rule anything for her. Has any of you heard anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning her?” Al-Mughira b. Shu‘ba stood and said, “I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ rule for her one-sixth.” So Abu Bakr gave her one-sixth. Then he said, “Did anyone hear that with you?” Muhammad b. Maslamah stood and said, “I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ rule for her one-sixth.” So Abu Bakr gave her one-sixth. Then during the caliphate of Umar, the other grandmother—the one who differed from her—came to him. Umar said, “The ruling was only for the other one, not you. But if you both are present, then the sixth is between you, and whichever of you is alone, it is hers.”"],[16272,"A grandmother came to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq asking about her inheritance in the Book of God. Abu Bakr said to her, “You have nothing in the Book of God, and I do not know of anything for you in the Sunnah of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Go back until I ask the people.” He asked the people, and al-Mughira b. Shu‘ba said, “I was present when the Messenger of God ﷺ gave her one-sixth.” Abu Bakr said, “Is there anyone else with you?” Muhammad b. Maslamah al-Ansari stood and said the like of what al-Mughira said, so Abu Bakr carried it out for her. Then the other grandmother came to Umar b. al-Khattab asking about her inheritance. He said, “You have nothing in the Book of God. The ruling that was made was only for the other one, not you. I will not add anything to the prescribed shares, but it is that sixth. If you both are present, it is between you, and whichever of you is alone, it is hers.”"],[16273,"She said: 'I have a right in what he left, so what is my right?' Abu Bakr said: 'I do not know of anything for you in the Book of God. I will ask; so return.' When he had prayed the noon prayer, he said: 'Who heard anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ regarding grandmothers?' al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah said: 'I heard him.' He said: 'How did you hear him?' He said: 'He gave the grandmother a sixth.' He said: 'Does anyone other than you know that?' Then Muhammad b. Maslamah stood and said: 'He spoke the truth; it is as he said.' So the woman came and he gave her a sixth. When Abu Bakr ؓ passed away, and it was Umar ؓ, a woman came to him about the like of that and said what the woman who had spoken to Abu Bakr had said. He replied to her with the like of his answer. Then he asked, and they said: 'al-Mughirah said such-and-such, and Muhammad b. Maslamah testified with him.' So he gave her a sixth. Then Umar said on his own initiative: 'If you two are both present, it is for you both; but whichever of you is alone with it, it is for her.'"],[16274,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, what should I do when the worshippers differ?' He said: 'Go out with your sword to the harrah and strike it with it. Then enter your house until a decree of death comes to you or an erring hand.'"],[16275,"When the Prophet ﷺ passed judgment on the Banu Qurayzah, the Aws felt distressed by that. So the Messenger of God ﷺ sent to every house of the Aws two captives, and he sent to the Banu Harithah two captives."],[16276,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say when he stood up to pray, \"Allahu Akbar, I have directed my face towards the One who created the heavens and the earth, purely submitting to Him, and I am not of those who associate partners with Allah. Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for Allah, the Lord of the worlds, who has no partner. And with that I have been commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the King, there is no deity but You. Glory be to You, and praise be to You.\" Then he recited, and when he bowed he said, \"O Allah, to You I have bowed, and in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. You are my Lord, I have bowed for You, and my hearing, my sight, my flesh and my blood have bowed for Allah, the Lord of the worlds.\" Then he raised his head and said, \"Allah hears the one who praises Him. Our Lord, to You is the praise, filling the heavens and the earth and whatever You will of anything after that.\" And when he prostrated he said, \"O Allah, to You I have prostrated, and in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. You are my Lord, I have prostrated for You, and my face has prostrated to the One who created it, shaped it, and opened its hearing and sight. Blessed is Allah, the best of creators.\""],[16277,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say in his prostration: 'O God, to You I prostrated, in You I believed, and to You I submitted, and You are my Lord. My face prostrated to the One who created it and shaped it and split open its hearing and its sight. Blessed is God, the best of creators.' And when he bowed he said: 'O God, to You I bowed, in You I believed, to You I submitted, and upon You I relied. You are my Lord. My hearing, my sight, my blood, my marrow, my bone, and my sinew have humbled themselves to God, Lord of the worlds.' Then he raised his head from bowing and said: 'God hears the one who praises Him. Our Lord, and to You be praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever You will of anything after.'"],[16278,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'O Muhammad b. Maslamah, there will be tribulation, division, and difference. When that occurs, break your sword, break your arrows, cut your bowstring, and sit in your house.' And indeed the tribulation occurred, and I did what the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me. Then I turned and saw a sword hanging from the tent pole, so I drew it, and it turned out to be a sword of wood. He said: 'I did what the Prophet ﷺ commanded me, and I took this to frighten people with it.'"],[16279,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: 'There will be division, tribulation, and difference. Strike your sword against the side of Uhud and sit in your house until an erring hand comes to you or God grants you relief.'"],[16280,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Your Lord has fragrant breezes in the days of your lifetime, so expose yourselves to Him, that perhaps a breeze of them may touch you and you will never be wretched after it.'[1]"],[16281,"Muhammad b. Maslamah said: 'I arrived from a journey, and the Messenger of God ﷺ took hold of my hand and did not let go of my hand until I let go of his.'"],[16282,"The Prophet ﷺ ate meat at the end of the matter, then prayed and did not perform ablution."],[16283,"I passed by and saw the Messenger of God ﷺ on al-Safa with his cheek against the cheek of a man. I went on, and it was not long before the Messenger of God ﷺ called me and said: 'O Muhammad b. Maslamah, what prevented you from greeting?' Muhammad b. Maslamah said: 'O Messenger of God, I saw you doing something with this man that you had not done with anyone else among the people, and I disliked to cut you off from your conversation. Who was it, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'It was Gabriel ﷺ . He said: \"What is wrong with Muhammad b. Maslamah that he did not greet? If he had greeted, we would have returned the greeting to him.\"' He said: 'What did he say to you, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'He kept advising me about the neighbor until I expected that he would command me to make him an heir.'"],[16284,"Your cousin—meaning the Messenger of God ﷺ—handed me a sword and said: 'Fight with it as long as the enemy is fought with it. But when you see people killing one another, take it to a rock and strike it against it, then keep to your house until a decree of death or an erring hand comes to you.' He said: 'Let him go.'"],[16285,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'After me there will be tribulations. If you encounter any of them, bring your sword to the side of the harrah and strike it with it, then join al-Rabadhah and be the owner of a camel until an erring hand or a decree of death kills you.'"],[16286,"He came to his sheep and caught two hares; he slaughtered them with a sharp white stone, then brought them to the Prophet ﷺ holding them. He said, “O Messenger of God, I slaughtered them with a sharp white stone.” He said, “Eat both of them.”"],[16287,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with two hares hanging from his hand and said, “O Messenger of God, I came to some sheep of mine and found these two hares, but I had no iron blade with which to slaughter them, so I slaughtered them with a sharp white stone. May I eat them?” He said, “Yes.”"],[16288,"He caught two hares and slaughtered them with a sharp white stone, then asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he commanded him to eat them."],[16289,"I slaughtered two hares with a sharp white stone and brought them to the Prophet ﷺ, and he commanded me to eat them."],[16290,"I slaughtered two hares with a sharp white stone, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him and said, “Should I eat them?” He said, “Yes.”"],[16291,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ and said, “Is there anyone among you who has eaten today?” We said, “Some of us have eaten and some have not.” He said, “Whoever has not eaten should complete his fast, and whoever has eaten something should complete the rest of his day.” Then he sent word to the people of al-ʿArūḍ, ordering them to do likewise."],[16292,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ: “Whoever among you has eaten should abstain for the rest of his day, and whoever has not eaten should fast.” And he sent word to the people of al-ʿArūḍ and ordered them to fast it."],[16293,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered his caller on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ: “Whoever is fasting should continue his fast, and whoever has eaten or drunk should complete his fast.”"],[16294,"I was tending sheep for my family in the mountain pass of Uḥud when I caught two young rabbits. I took a stone and slaughtered them with its edge. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and he said, “Eat it.”"],[16295,"I heard Muḥammad b. Ḥāṭib say, “I was born in Abyssinia.”"],[16296,"When my mother brought me from the land of Abyssinia after Ḥāṭib died, she came to the Prophet ﷺ, and one of my hands had suffered a burn from fire. She said, “O Messenger of God, this is Muḥammad b. Ḥāṭib, and he has been afflicted with this burn from fire.” Muḥammad b. Ḥāṭib said, “I would not tell a lie about the Messenger of God ﷺ; I do not know whether he blew or wiped over my head and prayed for blessing for me and my descendants.”"],[16297,"Some food from a cooking pot fell on my hand, so my mother took me to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said some words over it: “Remove the affliction, O Lord of mankind,” and I think he also said, “Heal, for You are the Healer.”"],[16298,"The cooking pot fell on my hand and it got burned. I was taken to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he would blow on it and say, \"Remove the affliction, Lord of the people.\" I think he also said, \"And heal, You are the Healer.\""],[16299,"I came near a cooking pot of ours while I was a young boy, and my hand got burned. My mother caught up with me and brought me to a man at al-Batha'. She said, \"O Muhammad, Muhammad's hand got burned.\" The Prophet ﷺ began to blow on it."],[16300,"I came near a cooking pot belonging to my mother and tipped it over onto myself while I was a boy, and my mother took me to the Prophet ﷺ. He performed ruqya on me and said, \"Remove the affliction, Lord of the people, and heal; You are the Healer, there is no healer but You.\" He said, I did not retain the words, so I asked my mother about them and she told me during the time of Uthman."],[16301,"I reached for a cooking pot that we had, and my hand got burned. My mother took me to a man in the cemetery and said to him, \"O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"At your service, at your service.\" Then she brought me close to him, and he began to blow and speak words that I did not understand. Later I asked my mother what he was saying, and she said, \"He was saying: 'Remove the affliction, Lord of the people, and heal; You are the Healer, there is no healer but You.'\""],[16302,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I have seen a land with palm trees, so go out.\" He said: So Hatib and Ja'far went out across the sea to the Negus, and I was born on the ship."],[16303,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The separation between the lawful and the unlawful is the voice and the striking of the duff.\""],[16304,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"If one of you is deprived of a wife and children, let him take up jihad.\""],[16305,"'Umar looked at the son of Abdul Hamid, whose name was Muhammad, and a man was speaking to him, saying, \"May Allah do such and such to you, O Muhammad,\" and began to insult him. So 'Umar called him and said, \"O son of Zayd, I do not see Muhammad ﷺ being insulted because of you. By Allah, you will never be called Muhammad as long as I am alive.\" So he named him Abdul Rahman. Then he sent to the Banu Talha, who were seven men, and their leader and elder was Muhammad bin Talha, to change their names. Muhammad said, \"I remind you by Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, for by Allah, Muhammad ﷺ named me Muhammad.\" So he said, \"Stand up, there is no way to change something named by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[16306,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: Three things; if you see them, then it is near, it is near: the destruction of the inhabited and the building up of ruins, that raiding becomes a support, and that a man becomes obstinate with his trust like a camel rubbing against a tree."],[16307,"From his father, who was among those who accompanied the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of God ﷺ came to them in the mosque of Banu Zufar and sat on the rock that is in the mosque of Banu Zufar today, with him Abdullah b. Mas'ud, Mu'adh b. Jabal, and some of his companions. The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded a reciter, and he recited until he came to this verse: {How will it be when We bring from every nation a witness, and We bring you as a witness against these?} The Messenger of God ﷺ wept until his jaws trembled, then said, \"O Lord, I bore witness over those among whom I lived, so what about those I did not see?\""],[16308,"The Messenger of God ﷺ arrived in Madinah when I was two weeks old, and I was brought to him. He wiped my head and said, \"Name him with my name, but do not give him my kunya.\" I performed the Farewell Pilgrimage with him when I was ten years old. He said: Muhammad lived long until his head grew gray, but the place where the Prophet's hand had touched did not turn gray."],[16309,"He was present with the Messenger of God ﷺ at the Farewell Pilgrimage when he was ten years old and had a forelock."],[16310,"Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Jahsh b. Ri'ab b. Ya'mar b. Sabira b. Murra b. Kathir b. Ghanm b. Dudan b. Asad b. Khuzayma b. Mudrika b. Ilyas b. Mudar b. Nizar, an ally of Banu Umayya. His paternal grandmother was Umayma bt. Abd al-Muttalib, the paternal aunt of the Messenger of God ﷺ. His father was killed as a martyr on the Day of Uhud, and his paternal aunt was Zaynab bt. Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ."],[16311,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ when he passed by Ma'mar while he was sitting at his house in the market with his thighs uncovered. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Ma'mar, cover your thighs, for the thighs are 'awrah.\""],[16312,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by Ma'mar while I was with him, and his thighs were uncovered. He said, \"O Ma'mar, cover your thighs, for the thigh is 'awrah.\""],[16313,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and a man from Banu 'Adi passed by us with his thigh uncovered. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Cover your thigh, O Ma'mar, for it is part of the 'awrah.\""],[16314,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ in the market, and he passed by Ma'mar at his door with his thigh uncovered. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Cover your thigh, O Ma'mar, for it is part of the 'awrah.\""],[16315,"That he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"If a man were killed in the path of God, then brought back to life, then killed in the path of God, then brought back to life, he would not enter Paradise until his debt is settled, and there is neither gold nor silver there; it is only good deeds and bad deeds.\""],[16316,"That a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, if I am killed in the path of God?\" He said, \"Paradise.\" When he turned away, he said, \"Except for debt. Gabriel ﷺ confided to me just now.\""],[16317,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Jahsh, who was a companion, say that a man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, what do you think if I fight in the path of God until I am killed?\" He said, \"Paradise.\" When the man turned away, he said, \"Bring him back to me.\" When he came, he said, \"Gabriel ﷺ said, 'Unless he has a debt.'\""],[16318,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: Gabriel ﷺ said to me, \"If a servant is killed in the path of God while he has a debt, he will not enter Paradise until his debt is settled.\""],[16319,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the courtyard of the mosque. He raised his head to the sky and said, \"Glory be to God! What strictness has been sent down?\" We remained for the rest of our day and night. When morning came, I went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, what strictness has been sent down?\" He said, \"If a man were killed in the path of God, then brought back to life, then killed, then brought back to life, he would not enter Paradise while he has a debt.\""],[16320,"\"Zaynab bt. Jahsh used to wash the head of the Messenger of God ﷺ in a brass basin.\" 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar said, \"I saw that basin.\""],[16321,"From Muhammad b. Abi 'Amira, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"If a servant were dragged on his face from the day he was born until the day he dies of old age in obedience to God, he would consider that insignificant on the Day of Resurrection and would wish to increase it just as he wishes to increase reward and recompense.\""],[16322,"From 'Urwa, \"In naming those who attended al-'Aqaba from the Ansar, then from the Aws, from Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal: Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayyihan, and he was a naqib and he attended Badr, and he was the first to pledge allegiance to Islam at al-'Aqaba.\""],[16323,"From Ibn Shihāb: \"Regarding the naming of those who were present at al-ʿAqabah from the Anṣār: Abū al-Haytham b. al-Tayhān, and he was a naqīb (leader).\""],[16324,"\"Abū al-Haytham b. al-Tayhān died in the year twenty, and his name was Mālik.\""],[16325,"\"The first to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of al-ʿAqabah was Abū al-Haytham b. al-Tayhān. He said, 'O Messenger of God, between us and the people there are ropes—and ropes means alliances and covenants—so perhaps we will cut them, then you will return to your people, and we will have cut the ropes and fought the people for your sake.' The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed at his words and said, 'Blood for blood, destruction for destruction.' When Abū al-Haytham was satisfied with what the Messenger of God ﷺ said in reply, he turned to his people and said, 'O people, this is the Messenger of God ﷺ. I bear witness that he is truthful, and today he is in God's sanctuary and safety, among his people and clan. Know that if you bring him out, the Arabs will cast you off with a single bow. If you are pleased to fight in the way of God and to lose wealth and children, then call him to your land, for he is truly the Messenger of God ﷺ. But if you fear desertion, then from now on.' ʿAbdullāh said, 'We have accepted from God and His Messenger what He has given us, and we have given you of ourselves what you asked of us, O Messenger of God. So let us, O Abū al-Haytham, be alone with the Messenger of God ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him.' Abū al-Haytham said, 'I am the first to pledge allegiance.' Then they all pledged allegiance. Satan shouted from the top of the mountain and said, 'O Quraysh, this is the Khazraj and the Aws allying themselves with Muḥammad to fight you.' They were alarmed and frightened by that, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Do not let this sound frighten you, for it is only the enemy of God, Iblīs; no one you fear hears him.' The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up and shouted at Satan, saying, 'O son of Azabb, this is your doing, and I will soon be free to deal with you.'\""],[16326,"\"I missed the ʿIshāʾ prayer one night, and I kept tossing and turning without sleep. I said, 'If only I went out to the mosque and prayed what was decreed for me.' So I did, then I leaned against a corner of it. ʿUmar entered and, when he saw me, he did not recognize me and said, 'Who is this?' I said, 'Abū Bakr.' He said, 'What brought you out at this hour?' I said, 'Hunger.' He said, 'And I, nothing brought me out except what brought you out.' Before long, the Messenger of God ﷺ entered. When he saw our dark shapes, he did not recognize us and said, 'Who are these two?' ʿUmar rushed ahead of me and said, 'This is Abū Bakr and this is ʿUmar.' He said, 'What brought you two out at this hour?' We told him the news. He said, 'And I, nothing brought me out except what brought you two out. Come with us to the house of al-Wāqimī.' We came to the door and asked permission. The woman came out, and he said, 'Where is so-and-so?' She said, 'He went to fetch fresh water for us from the orchard of Banū Ḥārithah.' She opened the door, and we entered. Before long he came carrying a water-skin on his back, and he hung it on a palm branch. Then he came to us and said, 'Welcome! What better visitors have visited the people than the visitors who visited me tonight?' Then he brought a cluster of unripe dates, and we began picking them in the moonlight and eating. Then he took the knife and went among the sheep. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, 'Beware of the milking ewe'—or he said, 'the one with milk.' He slaughtered a sheep for us, skinned it, cut it into the pot, and ordered the woman, who kneaded and baked. Then he brought us bread and meat, and we ate. Then he went to the water-skin, which the wind had cooled, and gave us water to drink. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Praise be to God. We went out only because hunger drove us out, and we did not return until we had this. This is among the blessings about which you will be questioned on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[16327,"\"I missed the ʿIshāʾ prayer one night, and I kept tossing and turning without sleep. I said, 'If only I went out to the mosque and prayed what was decreed for me.' So I did, then I leaned against a corner of it. ʿUmar entered and, when he saw me, he did not recognize me and said, 'Who is this?' I said, 'Abū Bakr.' He said, 'What brought you out at this hour?' I said, 'Hunger.' He said, 'And I, nothing brought me out except what brought you out.' Before long, the Messenger of God ﷺ entered. When he saw our dark shapes, he did not recognize us and said, 'Who are these two?' ʿUmar rushed ahead of me and said, 'This is Abū Bakr and this is ʿUmar.' He said, 'What brought you two out at this hour?' We told him the news. He said, 'And I, nothing brought me out except what brought you two out. Come with us to the house of al-Wāqimī.' We came to the door and asked permission. The woman came out, and he said, 'Where is so-and-so?' She said, 'He went to fetch fresh water for us from the orchard of Banū Ḥārithah.' She opened the door, and we entered. Before long he came carrying a water-skin on his back, and he hung it on a palm branch. Then he came to us and said, 'Welcome! What better visitors have visited the people than the visitors who visited me tonight?' Then he brought a cluster of unripe dates, and we began picking them in the moonlight and eating. Then he took the knife and went among the sheep. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, 'Beware of the milking ewe'—or he said, 'the one with milk.' He slaughtered a sheep for us, skinned it, cut it into the pot, and ordered the woman, who kneaded and baked. Then he brought us bread and meat, and we ate. Then he went to the water-skin, which the wind had cooled, and gave us water to drink. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Praise be to God. We went out only because hunger drove us out, and we did not return until we had this. This is among the blessings about which you will be questioned on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[16328,"He heard Umar bin Al-Khattab say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out at noon and found Abu Bakr in the mosque, so he asked him, \"What brought you out at this hour?\" Abu Bakr replied, \"What brought you out, O Messenger of Allah?\" Then Umar bin Al-Khattab came and asked, \"What brought you out?\" Abu Bakr replied, \"What brought both of you out?\" Umar sat down and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ started talking to them. Then he said, \"There is strength in both of you that can go to this palm tree and bring back food, drink, and dates.\" They both said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Come with us to the house of Abu Al-Haytham bin Tayhan Al-Ansari.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went ahead of us, greeted and sought permission three times, and Umm Al-Haytham listened to his greetings from behind the door, hoping that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would increase his greetings for her. When he wanted to leave, Umm Al-Haytham hurried after them and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I heard your greetings, but I wanted you to increase your greetings for us.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her kindly, then he said, \"Where is Abu Al-Haytham?\" She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he is nearby. He went to fetch water for us. Come in, for the time is near, if Allah wills.\" So she spread a sheet for them under the tree, and Abu Al-Haytham came rejoicing to meet them. His eyes were comforted by seeing them. He climbed a palm tree and cut off some bunches for them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Count (the bunches), O Abu Al-Haytham.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you are eating from its fruit and its dates. Then he brought them water and they all drank. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This is part of the blessings that you asked about.\" Abu Al-Haytham got up to slaughter a sheep for them, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Beware of debt.\" Umm Al-Haytham started kneading dough and baking for them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his head, as did Abu Bakr and Umar, near the dish, so they were awakened and found food laid out before them. They ate until they were satisfied, and then Abu Al-Haytham brought the remaining bunches, and they ate from its dates and its fruit. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ greeted them and prayed for them with goodness."],[16329,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ went out at an hour when he did not usually go out. Then Abū Bakr went out, and he said to him, \"What brought you out, O Abū Bakr?\" He said, \"Hunger brought me out.\" He said, \"And I, what brought me out is what brought you out.\" Then ʿUmar went out, and he said to him, \"What brought you out, O ʿUmar?\" He said, \"By the One who sent you with the truth, hunger brought me out.\" Then some of his companions came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said to them, \"Come with us to the house of Abū al-Haytham b. al-Tayhān.\" They went, and when they reached Abū al-Haytham's house, his wife said, \"Abū al-Haytham has gone to fetch fresh water for us, so go around to the garden.\" She opened the garden gate for them, and they sat down. Abū al-Haytham came, and his wife said to him, \"Do you know who is with you?\" He said, \"No.\" She said, \"With you are the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions.\" He entered, tied his horse to a palm tree, then came to them and greeted them warmly and welcomed them. Then he went to his date-palm grove, brought a cluster, picked fresh dates for them, and brought it and poured it before them. Then Abū al-Haytham reached for a small flock of his in a corner of the garden to slaughter a sheep for them. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"As for one with milk, no.\" He took a sheep, slaughtered it, skinned it, cut it into pieces, and cooked it with water and salt. Then he went to his wife and asked her, \"Do you have anything?\" She said, \"Yes, we have some barley that we were saving.\" They ground it together, then she kneaded it and baked it. Abū al-Haytham broke the bread and poured that cooked meat over it. Then he brought it to the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions, and they ate. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O Abū al-Haytham, do you not have a servant?\" He said, \"No, by the One who sent you with the truth, we have no servant.\" He said, \"When you hear that captives have come to us, come to us and we will provide you with a servant.\" Captives came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Abū al-Haytham came to him while two boys—or he said two youths—were before him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O Abū al-Haytham, choose one of them\"—or he said, \"choose between them.\" Abū al-Haytham said, \"O Messenger of God, choose for me.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ rolled up his sleeves and said, \"The one whose advice is sought is entrusted. O Abū al-Haytham, take this one.\" When Abū al-Haytham turned away with him, he said, \"O Abū al-Haytham, treat him well, for I saw him praying.\" He said, \"Yes, we will feed him from what we eat and clothe him from what we wear, and we will not burden him with work he cannot bear.\" Abū al-Haytham went to his family, and they rejoiced greatly and said, \"Praise be to God who provided us with a servant to serve us and help us with our property.\" Abū al-Haytham said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ enjoined me concerning him.\" His wife said, \"Yes, we will feed him from what we eat and clothe him from what we wear, and we will not burden him with work he cannot bear.\" He said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ enjoined me concerning him.\" His wife said, \"Glory be to God! A servant whom God and His Messenger have given us—do you want to deprive us of him?\" Abū al-Haytham said to the boy, \"You are free for the sake of God. If you like to stay with us, we will feed you from what we eat and clothe you from what we wear, and we will not burden you with work except what you can bear. And if you wish, go wherever you wish.\""],[16330,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out at an hour when he did not usually go out and when no one would meet him. Abū Bakr came to him, and he said, \"What brought you out, O Abū Bakr?\" He said, \"I went out to the Messenger of God ﷺ to look at his face and greet him.\" Before long, ʿUmar came, and he said, \"What brought you out, O ʿUmar?\" He said, \"Hunger.\" He said, \"And I have felt some of what you feel. Come with us to Abū al-Haytham b. al-Tayhān al-Anṣārī.\" He was a man with many horses and sheep, but he had no servant. They went to him and did not find him, but found his wife. He said, \"Where is your companion?\" She said, \"He went out early to fetch fresh water from the canal of Banū So-and-so.\" Before long, he came with a water-skin and set it down. Then he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, embracing him and ransoming him with his father and mother. He took them to the shade of his garden and spread a mat for them. Then he went to a palm tree and brought a cluster. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Why did you not pick out its fresh dates?\" He said, \"I wanted you to enjoy its fresh and unripe dates.\" They ate and drank from that water. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished, he said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, this is among the blessings about which you will be questioned on the Day of Resurrection: this cool shade, the fresh dates, and the water.\" He said, \"Go and prepare food for them.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Do not slaughter a milking animal.\" He slaughtered a young she-goat or a kid for them, then came to them and they ate."],[16331,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out at an hour when he did not usually go out and when no one would meet him. Abū Bakr came to him, and he said, \"What brought you out, O Abū Bakr?\" He said, \"I went out to the Messenger of God ﷺ to look at his face and greet him.\" Before long, ʿUmar came, and he said, \"What brought you out, O ʿUmar?\" He said, \"Hunger.\" He said, \"And I have felt some of what you feel. Come with us to Abū al-Haytham b. al-Tayhān al-Anṣārī.\" He was a man with many horses and sheep, but he had no servant. They went to him and did not find him, but found his wife. He said, \"Where is your companion?\" She said, \"He went out early to fetch fresh water from the canal of Banū So-and-so.\" Before long, he came with a water-skin and set it down. Then he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, embracing him and ransoming him with his father and mother. He took them to the shade of his garden and spread a mat for them. Then he went to a palm tree and brought a cluster. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Why did you not pick out its fresh dates?\" He said, \"I wanted you to enjoy its fresh and unripe dates.\" They ate and drank from that water. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished, he said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, this is among the blessings about which you will be questioned on the Day of Resurrection: this cool shade, the fresh dates, and the water.\" He said, \"Go and prepare food for them.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Do not slaughter a milking animal.\" He slaughtered a young she-goat or a kid for them, then came to them and they ate."],[16332,"One day the Messenger of God ﷺ went out and came upon Abū Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ. He said, \"What brought you two out of your houses?\" They said, \"Hunger.\" He said, \"And I, by the One in whose hand is my soul, nothing brought me out except what brought you two out. Get up.\" They got up with him, and he went to a man from the Anṣār. The Anṣārī was not there, but his wife was. He said to her, \"Where is so-and-so?\" She said, \"He went to fetch fresh water for us.\" While they were thus, the Anṣārī came carrying a water-skin. When he saw the Prophet ﷺ and his two companions, he said, \"God is greatest! No one is more honored than our guests.\" He hung up the water-skin, cut a cluster of dates for them—unripe, fresh, and dry—and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"Why did you not pick out the best?\" He said, \"Choose, O Messenger of God, with your own eyes.\" He took the knife, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"Beware of the milking ewe.\" He slaughtered for them, and they ate. When they finished, the Prophet ﷺ said to them, \"You will surely be asked about this blessing on the Day of Resurrection. Hunger drove you out of your houses, and you did not return until you had obtained this blessing.\""],[16333,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abū Bakr, and ʿUmar came to us, and we fed them fresh dates and gave them water to drink. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"This is among the blessings about which you will be questioned on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[16334,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The one whose advice is sought is entrusted.\""],[16335,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever says 'al-salāmu ʿalaykum,' ten good deeds are written for him. Whoever says 'al-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatu Allāh,' twenty good deeds are written for him. Whoever says 'al-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatu Allāh wa barakātuhu,' fifty good deeds are written for him.\""],[16336,"On the authority of Muhammad b. Ishaq: \"In naming those who attended Badr: Abu Usayd Malik b. Rabi'a b. al-Budn b. 'Amir b. 'Awf b. Haritha b. 'Amr b. al-Khazraj b. Sa'ida b. Ka'b b. al-Khazraj b. Haritha b. Tha'laba b. 'Amr b. 'Amir.\""],[16337,"Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi lost his sight before the killing of 'Uthman, and he said: \"Praise be to Allah who granted me my sight during the life of the Prophet ﷺ; then when Allah willed the trial for His servants, He withheld my sight from it.\""],[16338,"\"Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi, whose name was Malik b. Rabi'a, died in the year thirty, at the age of ninety.\""],[16339,"Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi said to me after he had lost his sight: \"O my nephew, if you and I were now at Badr, and Allah restored my sight, I would show you the mountain pass from which the angels came out upon us, without any doubt or dispute.\""],[16340,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best dwellings of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, then Banu Sa'ida, and in all the dwellings of the Ansar there is good.\" Sa'd b. 'Ubada said: \"I see that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has only favored others over us.\" He said: \"You have been favored over many.\""],[16341,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as he was leaving the mosque, when men and women had mingled on the road, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Step back, for it is not for you to occupy the center of the road. Keep to the edges of the road.\" And the woman would cling to the wall until her garment would catch on something from the wall due to her clinging."],[16342,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Badr when we lined up for battle: \"If they draw near you, shoot them with arrows.\""],[16343,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When they draw near you, shoot them with arrows.\""],[16344,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by us with some companions, and we went out with him. We set off until we reached a walled garden called al-Shawt, and then we reached two walled gardens and sat between them. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Sit here.\" The Jawniyya woman had been brought and secluded in the house of Umayma bt. al-Harith b. Sharahil, and with her was a nurse of hers. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, he said: \"Give yourself to me.\" She said: \"Does a queen give herself to a commoner?\" He reached out his hand to place it upon her, and she said: \"I seek refuge in Allah from you.\" He said: \"You have sought refuge with One who grants refuge.\" Then he came out to us and said: \"O Abu Usayd, clothe her with two Raziqi garments and send her back to her family.\""],[16345,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib: \"O Abu al-Fadl, do not leave your house, you and your sons, tomorrow until I come to you.\" So they waited for him until he came after the sun had risen high. He entered upon them and said: \"Peace be upon you.\" They said: \"And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\" He said: \"How are you this morning?\" They said: \"Well; we praise Allah.\" Then he said: \"Come close, come close, come close; move toward one another.\" Until when they had made room for him, he enveloped them with his cloak and said: \"O Lord, this is my uncle and the like of my father, and these are my household, so shield them from the Fire as I shield them with this cloak of mine.\" He said: \"Then the threshold of the door and the walls of the house said 'Amen,' saying: 'Amen, Amen, Amen.'\""],[16346,"It is called the Well of Goods, into which the Prophet ﷺ spat and blessed. Abu Umayr cut the fruit of his wall and put it in his room. The Ghul would come to his water trough and steal his dates, spoiling them. Abu Umayr complained to the Prophet ﷺ, who said, \"That is the Ghul, O Abu Umayr. Listen to her and when you hear her entering, say 'In the name of Allah, the Messenger of Allah has prevented me.' Then the Ghul said, 'O Abu Umayr, let me go and I will not burden you. I will go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and bring you a proof from Allah that I will not go to your house or steal your dates.' I will guide you to a verse from the Book of Allah that you can recite over your house, so that you do not go to your family or uncover your utensils.' She gave him the proof that pleased him, and said, 'The verse that I guide you to is Ayat al-Kursi.' Then she went and disappeared. Abu Umayr came to the Prophet ﷺ and narrated the story to him, where she had gone. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'She told the truth, but she is a liar.'"],[16347,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom, I have seen a place for a market; will you not look at it?\" He said: \"Yes.\" So he stood with him until he came to the place of the market. When he saw it, it pleased him, and he struck it with his foot, then said: \"This is an excellent market of yours; let it not be diminished, and let no tax be imposed upon it.\""],[16348,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Salih al-Tammar narrated to us, from Yazid b. Zayd, from Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi, who said: \"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the grave of Hamza b. 'Abd al-Muttalib. They began to pull the striped cloak over his face, and his feet would become uncovered; and they pulled it over his feet, and his face would become uncovered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Place it over his face, and put some of this shrub over his feet.'\" He said: \"Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head and saw his companions weeping. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A time will come upon people when they go out to the countryside and find there food, clothing, and mounts—or he said: mounts—and they write to their families: Come to us, for you are in a land of passage and drought. But Madinah is better for them, if only they knew. No one patiently endures its hardship and severity except that I will be an intercessor and a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[16349,"Regarding the Messenger of Allah ﷺ giving the Ansar a choice, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The best of the tribes of the Ansar are the dwellings of Banu al-Najjar, then Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal, then Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, then Banu Saʿidah, and in all of the Ansar there is good.\" Abu Usayd said: If I were to say anything other than the truth, I would have started with my own grandfather. And Abu Usayd was a Saʿidi."],[16350,"Abu Usayd, the Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him, saying: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"The best dwellings of the Ansar are the dwellings of Banu al-Najjar, then Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal, then the dwelling of al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, then the dwelling of Banu Saʿidah, and in all the dwellings of the Ansar there is good.\" Abu Usayd said: If I were a liar, I would have started with my own people, Banu Saʿidah. That reached Saʿd b. ʿUbadah, and he felt distressed about it. He said: We were created and we became the least important of the four. Saddle my donkey for me so I can go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. His nephew Sahl said to him: Will you go to reject the saying of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Allah and His Messenger know best. So he ordered his donkey to be unsaddled."],[16351,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal, then Banu Saʿidah, then Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj.\""],[16352,"The people came to the Prophet ﷺ for the digging of the trench, pledging allegiance to him upon emigration. When he finished, he said: \"O company of Ansar, do not pledge allegiance upon emigration. The people only emigrate to you. Whoever meets Allah while loving the Ansar, he meets Allah while Allah loves him. And whoever meets Allah while hating the Ansar, he meets Allah while Allah hates him.\""],[16353,"While I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, a man from the Ansar came and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there any way I can be dutiful to my parents after their death? He said: Yes, four qualities: praying for them, seeking forgiveness for them, fulfilling their promises after their death, honoring their friends, and maintaining the ties of kinship that you have only through them. He said: This is what remains upon me."],[16354,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is no prayer after the ʿAsr prayer.\""],[16355,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mixing dates and raisins together."],[16356,"I heard Abu Usayd al-Saʿidi, while Ibn ʿAbbas was giving a legal opinion allowing a dinar for two dinars, and Abu Usayd said to him harshly. Ibn ʿAbbas said: I did not think anyone who knows my relation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say such a thing to me, O Abu Usayd. Abu Usayd said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"A dinar for a dinar, a dirham for a dirham, a saʿ of wheat for a saʿ of wheat, a saʿ of barley for a saʿ of barley, a saʿ of salt for a saʿ of salt, no excess between any of that.\" Ibn ʿAbbas said: This is something I said by my own opinion, and I had not heard anything about it."],[16357,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Eat olive oil and anoint yourselves with olive oil, for it comes from a blessed tree.\""],[16358,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Eat olive oil and anoint yourselves with it, for it comes from a blessed tree.\""],[16359,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me about the night he was taken on the night journey."],[16361,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I did not pass by any angel among the angels except that they ordered me to be cupped.\""],[16362,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and we stopped at a place. They slept through the prayer until the sun rose. The Prophet ﷺ got up, ordered Bilal to give the call to prayer, and they performed ablution and prayed two rak'ahs. Then Bilal gave the iqamah, and the Prophet ﷺ led us in prayer. Then he narrated to us what will happen until the Day of Resurrection, which those who memorized it memorized and those who forgot it forgot."],[16363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept at dawn and did not wake up until the sun had risen. He woke up, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Bilal to give the call to prayer. Then he prayed two rak'ahs, then he gave the order and prayed Fajr."],[16364,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us and then narrated to us what will happen until the Hour is established."],[16365,"About the Prophet ﷺ in one of his sermons, he said, \"O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.\" A man said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, what about those who trim their hair?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"And those who trim their hair too.\""],[16366,"He witnessed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the Day of the Tree and the Day of the Hady, when it was detained before reaching its place of sacrifice. A man from the polytheists said, 'O Muhammad, what compels you to bring these people upon us while we are unwilling?' He said, 'These are better than you and your forefathers. They believe in Allah and the Last Day. By the One in whose hand is my soul, he has indeed ؓ.'"],[16367,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I passed by a man and he did not host me or offer me hospitality. Then he passes by me—should I host him?' He said, 'Rather, host him.'"],[16368,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw 'Ali wearing worn-out clothes and said, 'Do you have any wealth?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'From what kind of wealth?' I said, 'From everything; Allah has given me.' He said, 'Then let Allah's blessing and honor upon you be seen.'"],[16369,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looking shabby in appearance. He said, 'Do you have any wealth?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'From what kind of wealth?' I said, 'From everything; Allah has given me camels, horses, slaves, and sheep.' He said, 'When Allah ﷻ gives you wealth, let it be seen upon you.'"],[16370,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looking shabby in appearance. He said, 'Do you have any wealth?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'From what kind of wealth?' I said, 'From everything; Allah has given me camels, horses, slaves, and sheep.' He said, 'When Allah ﷻ gives you wealth, let it be seen upon you.'"],[16371,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looking shabby in appearance. He said, 'Do you have any wealth?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'From what kind of wealth?' I said, 'From everything; Allah has given me camels, horses, slaves, and sheep.' He said, 'When Allah ﷻ gives you wealth, let it be seen upon you.'"],[16372,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he saw me in a bad state. He asked me, \"Do you have any wealth?\" I said, \"Yes, I have been given wealth by Allah from camels, cows, horses, and slaves.\" He said, \"When Allah gives you something good, let the blessings and kindness of Allah be upon you.\""],[16373,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he saw me in a poor appearance. He said to me, 'Do you have any wealth?' I said, 'Yes, from all kinds of wealth. Allah has given me camels, cattle, horses, and slaves.' He said, 'If Allah gives you good, let Allah's blessing and His honor upon you be seen.'"],[16374,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he saw me in a poor appearance. He said to me, 'Do you have any wealth?' I said, 'Yes, from all kinds of wealth. Allah has given me camels, cattle, horses, and slaves.' He said, 'If Allah gives you good, let Allah's blessing and His honor upon you be seen.'"],[16375,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing a shabby garment. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'Do you have wealth?' He said, 'Yes, Allah has given me from every kind of wealth.' He said, 'From what kind of wealth?' He said, 'Allah has given me horses and slaves.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'When Allah gives you wealth, let the trace of His blessing and honor be seen upon you.'"],[16376,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing a lowly garment. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Do you have wealth?\" He said, \"Yes, Allah has granted me every kind of wealth.\" He said, \"From which kind of wealth?\" He said, \"Allah has granted me horses and slaves.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"When Allah grants you wealth, let the mark of His favor and His honor be seen on you.\""],[16377,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing a lowly garment. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Do you have wealth?\" He said, \"Yes, Allah has granted me every kind of wealth.\" He said, \"From which kind of wealth?\" He said, \"Allah has granted me horses and slaves.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"When Allah grants you wealth, let the mark of His favor and His honor be seen on you.\""],[16378,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing two cloaks or two wraps. He said, \"Do you have any wealth?\" I said, \"Yes, of every kind of wealth.\" He said, \"Then let the favor of Allah be seen on you.\" The next morning I went to him wearing a red fine garment."],[16379,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing shabby clothes and was in a poor appearance. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Do you have any wealth?\" He said, \"Yes, of all kinds of wealth.\" He said, \"Then let what Allah has provided you be seen on you.\""],[16380,"My father entered upon the Prophet ﷺ in patched garments. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Do you have any wealth?\" He said, \"Of every kind of wealth. Allah has granted me camels, cattle, and sheep.\" He said, \"Then let what Allah has granted you be seen on you.\""],[16381,"My father entered upon the Prophet ﷺ in patched garments. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Do you have any wealth?\" He said, \"Of every kind of wealth. Allah has granted me camels, cattle, and sheep.\" He said, \"Then let what Allah has granted you be seen on you.\""],[16382,"That ‘Awf b. Mālik, meaning his father, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing worn-out clothes. He said, \"O ‘Awf b. Mālik, do your camels not give birth when their ears are sound, and then you go to some of them and slit their ears and say, 'This is a baḥīrah,' and you go to some of them and split their ears and then say, 'This is a ṣurum'? Do not do so. Allah's forearm is stronger than your forearm, and Allah's razor is sharper. Everything Allah has given you is lawful, so do not make anything of your wealth unlawful.\" Then he said to him, \"O ‘Awf b. Mālik, which of your slaves is more beloved to you: the one who obeys you and follows your command, or the one who does not obey you and does not follow your command?\" He said, \"Rather my slave who obeys me and follows my command.\" He said, \"Thus are you before your Lord, Exalted is He.\""],[16383,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and began asking the Prophet ﷺ. When the Prophet ﷺ saw his poor appearance, he said, \"Do you have any wealth?\" He said, \"Yes, every kind of wealth. Allah has granted me camels, sheep, and horses.\" He said, \"When Allah grants you wealth, let it be seen on you.\""],[16384,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was in poor appearance. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do you have any wealth?\" I said, \"Yes, of every kind of wealth. Allah has granted me.\" He said, \"When you have wealth, let it be seen on you.\""],[16385,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with a Bedouin manner about me and wearing Bedouin clothing. He said to me, \"Do you have wealth?\" He said: I said, \"Of every kind of wealth. Allah has granted me.\" He said, \"When Allah grants you wealth, let the mark of Allah's favor be seen.\""],[16386,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with a Bedouin manner about me and wearing Bedouin clothing. He said to me, \"Do you have wealth?\" He said: I said, \"Of every kind of wealth. Allah has granted me.\" He said, \"When Allah grants you wealth, let the mark of Allah's favor be seen.\""],[16387,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with a Bedouin manner about me and wearing Bedouin clothing. He said to me, \"Do you have wealth?\" He said: I said, \"Of every kind of wealth. Allah has granted me.\" He said, \"When Allah grants you wealth, let the mark of Allah's favor be seen.\""],[16388,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ, who saw him in poor condition. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Do you not have wealth?” He said: He replied, “Yes.” He said, “Then let the blessing of God be visible upon you.”"],[16389,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ wearing worn-out clothes. He said, “Do you have wealth?” I said, “Yes, of every kind of wealth God has given me,” and he enumerated horses, camels, slaves, and sheep. He said, “When God gives you good, let it be visible upon you.”"],[16390,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ wearing worn-out clothes. He said, “Do you have wealth?” I said, “Yes, of every kind of wealth God has given me,” and he enumerated horses, camels, slaves, and sheep. He said, “When God gives you good, let it be visible upon you.”"],[16391,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ in a shabby condition. He said to me, “Do you have any wealth?” I said, “Yes, camels, sheep, and slaves.” He said, “Then why is it not visible upon you?”"],[16392,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ in a shabby, poor condition. He said, “Do you have wealth?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “What is your wealth?” He said, “Camels, horses, and slaves.” He said, “When God gives you wealth—or he said good—let it be visible upon you. For when God honors a servant, He loves to see His honor upon him.”"],[16393,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ in a shabby, poor condition. He said, “Do you have wealth?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “What is your wealth?” He said, “Camels, horses, and slaves.” He said, “When God gives you wealth—or he said good—let it be visible upon you. For when God honors a servant, He loves to see His honor upon him.”"],[16394,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ in a shabby, poor condition. He said, “Do you have wealth?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “What is your wealth?” He said, “Camels, horses, and slaves.” He said, “When God gives you wealth—or he said good—let it be visible upon you. For when God honors a servant, He loves to see His honor upon him.”"],[16395,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he looked me up and down and said, “Are you an owner of camels or an owner of sheep?” He said, “Of every kind God has given me, abundantly and pleasantly.” He said, “Then you breed them with their eyes and ears intact, and you slit the ear of this one and call it ṣarmāʾ.” Then Sufyān said something I did not understand, “and you say ‘the baḥīrah of God,’ while God’s foreleg is stronger and God’s razor is sharper. And if He willed, He could bring it to you already slit.”"],[16396,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he looked me up and down and said, “Are you an owner of camels or an owner of sheep?” He said, “Of every kind God has given me, abundantly and pleasantly.” He said, “Then you breed them with their eyes and ears intact, and you slit the ear of this one and call it ṣarmāʾ.” Then Sufyān said something I did not understand, “and you say ‘the baḥīrah of God,’ while God’s foreleg is stronger and God’s razor is sharper. And if He willed, He could bring it to you already slit.”"],[16397,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ saw him disheveled and dusty in the appearance of a Bedouin. He said to him, “What wealth do you have?” He said, “Of every kind of wealth God has given me.” He said, “When God bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves that it be seen upon him.”"],[16398,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he said the takbīr to enter prayer, raised his hands until they were level with his ears, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing—the wording is the same."],[16399,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he entered prayer, raised his hands to the top of his ears, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing."],[16400,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he said the takbir, raised his hands until they were level with his ears, and when he raised his head from bowing he did likewise."],[16401,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raise his hands when he said the takbir until they were level with his ears, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing."],[16402,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he said the takbir, raised his hands until they were near his ears, and when he bowed he did the same, and when he raised his head from bowing he did the same."],[16403,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ raise his hands until they were level with the tops of his ears. Yazīd b. Zurayʿ added: \"and when he bowed likewise, and when he raised his head from bowing likewise.\""],[16404,"He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raise his hands when he said the takbir, when he intended to bow, and when he raised his head from bowing, around his ears."],[16405,"He said to them: \"Put forward a man from among you to lead you in prayer, and I shall tell you why I do not lead you in prayer. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever visits a people should not lead them in prayer; let a man from among them lead them.'\""],[16406,"He said to his companions: \"Shall I show you how the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was?\" That was at a time other than prayer time. He stood, then bowed, saying the takbir, then raised his head and stood for a short while, then prostrated, then raised his head and waited, then prostrated, then raised his head and waited for a short while, then prostrated. The wording is that of ʿĀrim."],[16407,"\"I am going to lead you in prayer, but I do not intend the prayer; I only want to show you how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray.\" Ayyūb said: I asked Abū Qilābah, \"How was his prayer?\" He said, \"Like the prayer of our shaykh, ʿAmr b. Salamah. The shaykh would complete the takbirs, and when he raised his head from the first rakʿah he would lean on the ground and then stand.\""],[16408,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as young men and stayed with him for about twenty nights or days. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: \"When you return to your families,\" or he said, \"to your lands, teach them.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was merciful. \"Command them to pray such-and-such a prayer at such-and-such a time, and such-and-such a prayer at such-and-such a time. When the prayer is due, let one of you call the adhan, and let the eldest of you lead the prayer.\" The wording is that of the hadith of ʿĀrim."],[16409,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The eldest of a people should lead them in prayer.\" Malik b. al-Ḥuwayrith, when he raised his head from the second prostration, would sit and then rise."],[16410,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among a group of young men of similar age and stayed with him for twenty nights. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was merciful, gentle, and forbearing. He thought that we missed our families and longed for them, so he asked us about those we had left behind, and we told him. He said: \"Return to your families, stay with them, teach them, and command them.\" And he said: \"When the prayer is due, let one of you call the adhan, and let the eldest of you lead the prayer.\""],[16411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you are with your companion, call the adhan and the iqamah, and let the elder of you two lead the prayer.\""],[16412,"Two men came to the Prophet ﷺ intending to travel. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"When you two set out, then give the call to prayer (adhan), then say the iqamah, and let the older of you lead the prayer.\""],[16413,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him and to a companion of his, \"When the prayer time arrives, then give the call to prayer (adhan), then say the iqamah, and let the older of you lead the prayer.\""],[16414,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him and to a companion of his, \"When the prayer time arrives, then give the call to prayer (adhan), then say the iqamah, and let the older of you lead the prayer.\" I said to Abu Qilabah, \"Then where does the recitation come in?\" He said, \"They were close in age.\""],[16415,"About the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: He would pray at other than prayer times, and when he raised his head from the second prostration in the first rak'ah, he would sit upright, then stand, supporting himself on the ground.\""],[16416,"The Prophet ﷺ made us recite it. On that day, He will not punish nor bind."],[16417,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When Allah wants to create a soul and the man has intercourse with the woman, his fluid flies into every vein and nerve of hers. Then on the seventh day, Allah ﷻ makes green for him every vein between him and Adam.\" Then he recited: {In whatever form He willed, He assembled you}."],[16418,"\"Shall I not tell you how your Prophet ﷺ used to pray?\" We said, \"Yes.\" So he stepped forward and prayed two rak'ahs, making them brief. Abu Qilabah and I differed about his knees: I said he kept them close to the ground, and Abu Qilabah said he kept them apart."],[16419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever I am his mawla (patron), Ali is his mawla.\""],[16420,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali: \"Are you not pleased that you are to me as Harun was to Musa?\""],[16421,"Malik b. al-Huwayrith said: \"The first of the men to embrace Islam was Ali, and among the women, Khadijah.\""],[16422,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the steps of the pulpit and said, \"Ameen.\" Then he ascended another step and said, \"Ameen.\" Then he ascended another step and said, \"Ameen.\" He said, \"Jibril ﷺ came to me and said, 'O Muhammad, whoever reaches the age of his parents or one of them and does not enter Paradise, may Allah distance him.' Say Ameen, so I said Ameen. And whoever reaches the month of Ramadan and is not forgiven, may Allah distance him.' Say Ameen, so I said Ameen. And whoever hears your name and does not send blessings upon you, may Allah distance him.' Say Ameen, so I said Ameen."],[16423,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise, and their father is better than them.\""],[16424,"\"I went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I never prayed behind an imam of a people whose prayer was lighter than that of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[16425,"I went on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and we never prayed behind an imam whose prescribed prayer was lighter than his."],[16426,"That his father Malik and his paternal uncles Qays and Ubayd, the sons of al-Khashkhash, came to the Prophet ﷺ and complained to him about a man from their cousins raiding the people. So the Messenger of God ﷺ wrote for them: \"This is a letter from Muhammad, the Messenger of God ﷺ, to Malik, Ubayd, and Qays, the sons of al-Khashkhash. You are granted security as Muslims for your blood and your property. You will not be taken to account for the crime of others, and none will commit a crime against you except your own hands.\""],[16427,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"God does not accept from a suqqūr any sarf or ʿadl.\" It was said, \"What is a suqqūr, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"One who brings a man to his wife [for illicit intercourse].\""],[16428,"That he was present with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the conquest [of Makkah], at Khaybar, and at al-Ta'if. He was a poet, and he said, \"O Messenger of God, give me a ruling about poetry.\" He said, \"For the space between your chest and your shoulder to be filled with pus is better than for it to be filled with poetry.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, wipe over my head.\" He placed his hand on my head, and after that I never uttered a line of poetry. Malik lived to old age until his head and beard turned white, but the place where the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ had been did not turn white."],[16429,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ate food one day and then said, \"Cover for me so that I may bathe.\" I said, \"Were you in a state of major ritual impurity, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I informed Umar b. al-Khattab of that, and he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said to him, \"This one claims that you ate while you were in a state of major ritual impurity?\" He said, \"Yes, when I have performed ablution I eat and drink, but I do not pray or recite until I bathe.\""],[16430,"From the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"This companion of yours is indeed a memorizer and a destroyer. The last thing the Messenger of God ﷺ enjoined upon us was that he said: 'Whoever memorizes something from me, let him relate it. And whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.'\""],[16431,"Malik said: \"This companion of yours is heedless and a destroyer. The Messenger of God ﷺ enjoined us during the Farewell Pilgrimage, saying: 'Hold fast to the Quran, for you will return to a people who desire hadith from me. Whoever understands something, let him relate it. And whoever fabricates a lie against me, let him take a seat or something from Hell.'\" \"I do not know which of the two he said.\""],[16432,"From Hassan, the freed slave of Malik b. Abdullah al-Khath'ami, and Malik was one of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: \"I saw Malik b. Abdullah performing ablution, and on his shin there was a vein inscribed 'For God.' I began to look at it, and he said, 'What are you looking at? Indeed, no writer wrote it.'\""],[16433,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Abu Qatadah, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever sees me in a dream will see me while awake, and Satan cannot imitate me.\""],[16434,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Whoever's feet become dusty in the path of God, God has forbidden him to the Fire.\""],[16435,"It was said to him: \"Will you not ride, since God has carried you?\" He said: \"Indeed the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever's feet become dusty in the path of God, God has forbidden him to the Fire.'\""],[16436,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a man praying when the prayer had already been commenced. He spoke to him something I do not know what it was. When we finished, we surrounded him saying, \"What did the Messenger of God ﷺ say to you?\" He said: \"He said: 'It is likely that he will pray the morning prayer as four [rakʿahs].'\""],[16437,"He said to his brother Malik b. Haidah, \"Go with us to the Prophet ﷺ, for he knows you but does not know me. He has detained some people of Banu Bahdam, my neighbors.\" So they came to him, and Malik b. Haidah said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have embraced Islam and my neighbors have embraced Islam, so release them.\" He did not answer him. Then he repeated it, and he did not answer him. Then he repeated it, and he did not answer him. Then he stood up, enraged, and said, \"If you do that, they claim that you call to the matter but act contrary to it.\" I began to rebuke him and forbid him. He said, \"What is he saying?\" They said, \"He says such and such.\" He said, \"If he does that, that is upon me, not upon them for it. Leave him his neighbors.\""],[16438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no Muslim over whom three rows pray but that it becomes obligatory [for him to be forgiven].\" He said: When Malik met the people of a funeral procession, he would divide them into three rows."],[16439,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever frees a Muslim slave, it will be his ransom from the Fire: a bone from the bones of the one he freed for a bone from his own bones.\""],[16440,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever reaches one of his parents and then is not forgiven, may Allah distance him. And whoever takes in an orphan between two parents into his food and drink until Allah makes him self-sufficient, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.\""],[16441,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever takes in an orphan between two Muslims into his food and drink until he becomes independent of him, Paradise becomes absolutely obligatory for him. Any man who reaches his parents or one of them and then enters the Fire, may Allah distance him. Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim slave, it will be his ransom from the Fire.\""],[16442,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever takes in an orphan between two Muslim parents until he becomes self-sufficient, Allah has made Paradise absolutely obligatory for him.\""],[16443,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever takes in an orphan between two Muslims into his food and drink until he becomes independent of him, Paradise becomes absolutely obligatory for him. And whoever frees a Muslim man, it will be his ransom from the Fire, each limb of his ransoming a limb of his.\""],[16444,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"If you meet a collector of tithes, kill him\" — meaning by that the one who takes zakat without right."],[16445,"Ibn Sallam said: Malik b. Awf al-Nasri was a leader, a bold champion. The first mention of him and his notable valor was on the day of al-Fijar with his people. His deeds were many that day. He was in command of Hawazin when they met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he drove with the people their wealth and their children. Durayd b. al-Simmah opposed him, but he insisted and refused. They followed his command and did not approve of his opinion. He was their leader that day. When he saw the defeat of his companions, he headed for the Prophet ﷺ, being bold in attack, intending to strike him, as he claimed. Murthad b. Abi Murthad al-Ghanawi confronted him and killed him. He took his horse, Mahaj. He did not advance. Then he wanted him again and shouted at him, but he did not advance. He said:"],[16446,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the delegation of Hawazin at Hunayn when he asked them about Malik b. Awf al-Nasri: \"What has Malik done?\" They said, \"He is in al-Ta'if.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Inform Malik that if he comes to me as a Muslim, I will return to him his family and his wealth and give him a hundred camels.\" So this reached Malik, and he left al-Ta'if. Malik had feared for himself from Thaqif, lest they learn that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said to him what he said and detain him. So he ordered a mount of his to be prepared, and he ordered a horse of his to be brought to him from al-Ta'if. He left at night, mounted his horse, and caught up with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, reaching him at al-Ji'ranah or Makkah. He returned to him his family and his wealth and gave him a hundred camels."],[16447,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a well, and in it was a black man, dead. He said: He looked into the well, and there he was thrown into the well. The Prophet ﷺ asked, \"Why is he thrown into the well?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he was harsh in religion; he would pray sometimes and sometimes not pray.\" He said, \"Woe to you, take him out.\" So the Prophet ﷺ ordered that he be washed and shrouded. He said, \"Carry him.\" And he said, \"The angels almost preceded us.\" He said: And he prayed over him."],[16448,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever is prompted at death to say the testimony that there is no god but Allah will enter Paradise.\""],[16449,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Leave people alone so that some may obtain from others, but if your brother seeks your sincere advice, then advise him sincerely.”"],[16450,"From ʿUrwa: “Regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of God ﷺ among the Muslims, then among the Ansar, then among the Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal: Maḥmūd b. Maslama.”"],[16451,"From Ibn Shihāb: “Regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of God ﷺ among the Ansar, then among the Banū Ḥāritha: Maḥmūd b. Maslama.”"],[16452,"From Ibn Shihāb: “Regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of God ﷺ among the Ansar, then among the Banū Ḥāritha: Maḥmūd b. Maslama.”"],[16453,"“Mu‘āwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān died with four nights having passed of Rajab in the year 60.” Ibn Kathīr said: “His age was in his seventy-some years, up to eighty.”"],[16454,"“Muʿāwiya died in the year sixty, and his age was between seventy-something and eighty.”"],[16455,"He heard Muʿāwiya say: “The Messenger of God ﷺ died at sixty-three, and Abū Bakr and ʿUmar did too, and I am sixty-three.”"],[16456,"“Muʿāwiya was tall, fair-skinned, and bald on the front of his head.”"],[16457,"“Muʿāwiya came to us, and he was the fairest of people and the most handsome of them.”"],[16458,"“I saw Muʿāwiya at al-Abṭaḥ with a white head and beard as if it were snow.”"],[16459,"Muʿāwiya set out from Syria intending Makkah and stopped at a place between Makkah and Madinah called al-Abwāʾ. He looked into an ancient well and was struck by facial paralysis. He hastened his journey until he arrived in Makkah. The chamberlain came to him and said, “O Commander of the Faithful, the people are at the door; I do not miss any face.” He said, “Then spread out for me, then.” Then he called for a turban, wrapped it around his head, and split it over his face. Then he went out, praised God and extolled Him, and then said: “To proceed: If I am granted health, then indeed the righteous before me were granted health, and I would not wish to conceal that I hope to be among them. If one of my limbs has become ill, I cannot count my healthy ones. If some of your elite have found fault with me, I have been at war against your common people. I have no desire to wish from God more than what He has given me. May God have mercy on a man who prays for my well-being.” The voices rose with supplication and he was moved to tears. Marwān said to him, “What makes you weep, O Commander of the Faithful?” He said, “I recalled what I had turned away from: my age has advanced, my bones have become thin, tears have increased in my eyes, I have been struck in my best part and what appears of me. Were it not for my desire for Yazīd, I would have perceived my right course.”"],[16460,"I was taking a midday nap in a church in Jericho, which at that time was a mosque where people prayed. Then ʿAwf b. Mālik awoke from his sleep, and there was a lion with him in the room walking toward him. He rose in alarm to his weapon, and the lion said to him, “Wait! I have only been sent to you with a message for you to convey.” I said, “Who sent you?” He said, “God sent me to you so that you may inform Muʿāwiya the traveler that he is among the people of Paradise.” I said, “Who is Muʿāwiya?” He said, “The son of Abū Sufyān.”"],[16461,"I raided with Muʿāwiya b. Abī Sufyān in the land of the Romans, and a fox fell into his saddle. He called out, “O servants of God, O Muslims!” The first to answer was Muʿāwiya, and he dismounted and the people dismounted. They said, “We will suffice the commander.” He said, “Indeed, it has reached me that the first to bring aid is Gabriel, so I desired to be the second.”"],[16462,"Ali ﷺ : \"My slain and Muawiyah's slain are in Paradise.\""],[16463,"I heard Mujalid ibn Sa'id saying, \"May Allah have mercy on Mu'awiya, how strong was his love for the Arabs.\""],[16464,"Abu Sufyan: Leave your brother."],[16465,"I heard al-A'mash say: If you saw Muawiyah, you would say, 'This is the Mahdi.'"],[16466,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ with the arrowhead of a Bedouin near al-Marwah saying, \"When he prohibited mut'ah.\""],[16467,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ during his Umrah at al-Marwah with an arrowhead.\""],[16468,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ near al-Marwah with an arrowhead during his Hajj.\""],[16469,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ near al-Marwah with an arrowhead.\""],[16470,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ at al-Marwah with the arrowhead of a Bedouin.\""],[16471,"He informed him, \"That he saw the Messenger of God ﷺ shorten his hair with an arrowhead.\" We said to Ibn Abbas, \"This has only reached us from Muawiyah.\" Ibn Abbas said, \"Muawiyah was not accused regarding the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[16472,"Muawiyah said to me, \"Have you considered one who performs tamattu' and drives the sacrificial animal—does he touch anything of his hair?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"I bear witness that I took from the hair of the Messenger of God ﷺ at al-Marwah when he finished his circumambulation with an arrowhead from his quiver.\""],[16473,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"That he prohibited wearing gold.\""],[16474,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"That he prohibited wearing jewelry and gold.\""],[16475,"From Abu Sa'id al-Khudri ؓ, who said: Mu'awiya came out to a circle in the mosque and said, \"What made you sit?\" They said, \"We sat to remember Allah.\" He said, \"By Allah, nothing made you sit except that?\" They said, \"By Allah, nothing made us sit except that.\" He said, \"Indeed, I did not make you swear out of suspicion of you. No one of my standing with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has fewer hadiths from him than I. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to a circle of his Companions and said, 'What made you sit?' They said, 'We sat to remember Allah and praise Him for guiding us to Islam and blessing us with you.' He said, 'By Allah, nothing made you sit except that?' They said, 'By Allah, nothing made us sit except that.' He said, 'Indeed, I did not make you swear out of suspicion of you. Jibril ﷺ came to me and informed me that Allah ﷻ boasts of you to the angels.'\""],[16476,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Do not pry into people, lest you corrupt them.\""],[16477,"\"The Prophet ﷺ passed away at the age of sixty-three, Abu Bakr passed away at the age of sixty-three, and 'Umar passed away at the age of sixty-three.\""],[16478,"\"The Prophet ﷺ passed away at the age of sixty-three.\""],[16479,"I heard Muawiyah say, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away at the age of sixty-three, Abu Bakr passed away at the age of sixty-three, and Umar passed away at the age of sixty-three.\""],[16480,"The Prophet ﷺ passed away at the age of sixty-three, Abu Bakr passed away at the age of sixty-three, and 'Umar passed away at the age of sixty-three."],[16481,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ placed truth upon the tongue and heart of 'Umar.\""],[16482,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us on the day of 'Ashura and said, \"This is a day whose fasting is not prescribed for you, and I am fasting. Whoever wishes to fast may fast, and whoever wishes to break it may break it.\""],[16483,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Excellent is the tribe of al-Azd and the Ash'aris.\" Mu'awiya said, \"It was not like that; he said, 'They are from me and to me.'\""],[16484,"[He said] to Mu'awiya during the exchange between them regarding the pledge to Yazid: \"And you, O Mu'awiya, informed me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'If there are two caliphs on earth, kill one of them.'\""],[16485,"When you come to my tent, stand among the people and inform them of what I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, the traders are wicked.\" A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, has Allah not permitted trade?\" He said, \"Indeed, they speak and lie, and they swear and sin.\""],[16486,"About something that Muawiyah saw in the prayer, he said: \"I prayed with him (Muhammad) the Friday prayer in the enclosure. When he finished, I stood in my place and prayed. When he entered (the enclosure), he sent for me and said, 'Do not repeat what you did when you pray the Friday prayer. Do not connect it with another prayer until you speak or leave. For the Prophet ﷺ commanded that.' Additionally, he added in his narration, 'Do not connect it with another prayer until you speak or leave.'\""],[16487,"Mu'awiya said, \"Do not do that, for I know the Messenger of Allah ﷺ better.\""],[16488,"About the two prostrations that are prayed after Jumu'ah in the mosque and the two prostrations after 'Asr.\" Mu'awiya said, \"And I know the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ better.\""],[16489,"That he heard Muʿāwiyah delivering a sermon in Madinah on the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while in his hand was a lock of hair. He said, “Where are your scholars, O people of Madinah? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding this.” And he said, “Those before you were destroyed only when their women adopted this.”"],[16490,"That he heard Muʿāwiyah delivering a sermon, saying, “O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘This is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ, and Allah has not prescribed its fasting. I am fasting, so whoever wishes to fast, let him fast, and whoever wishes to break his fast, let him break it.’”"],[16491,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “Juhaynah is from me and I am from them. They are angry for my anger and pleased for my pleasure. I become angry for their anger and pleased for their pleasure. Whoever angers them has angered me, and whoever angers me has angered Allah.” Muʿāwiyah said to him, “He only said this hadith about the Quraysh.” ʿImrān said, “I heard it from the Prophet ﷺ, while you were dead at that time.”"],[16492,"We were sitting around Muʿāwiyah’s bed, and he came out to us and said, “What were you talking about?” They said, “We were talking about something from the talk of the Anṣār.” Muʿāwiyah said, “Shall I give you more, a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” They said, “Yes, O Commander of the Believers.” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘Whoever loves the Anṣār, Allah loves him; and whoever hates the Anṣār, Allah hates him.’”"],[16493,"I heard Muʿāwiyah: when the muʾadhdhin said the takbīr twice, he said the takbīr twice; and when he bore witness twice, he bore witness twice. Then he turned to me and said, “This is how I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say at the adhān.”"],[16494,"He heard the muʾadhdhin say the takbīr, and he said the takbīr; and he bore witness as he bore witness. Then he said, “This is how Muʿāwiyah narrated to us that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say as the muʾadhdhin said. When he said, ‘I bear witness that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah,’ he said, ‘And I bear witness,’ then he was silent.”"],[16495,"I entered with Muʿāwiyah upon ʿĀʾishah, the Mother of the Believers. She said, “O Muʿāwiyah, you killed Ḥujr and his companions, and you did what you did. Were you not afraid that I would hide a man for you who would kill you in retaliation for Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr?” He said, “No, for I am in a secure house. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘Faith restrains assassination; a believer does not assassinate.’ O Mother of the Believers, how am I regarding your needs, your messengers, and your affairs?” She said, “Good.” He said, “Then leave me and Ḥujr until we meet before Allah.”"],[16496,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever is pleased that men stand up for him when they see him coming, let him take a seat in the Fire.”"],[16497,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade false hair, and false hair is when a woman attaches hair."],[16498,"“That the Prophet ﷺ forbade false hair.”"],[16499,"“O people, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has forbidden you false hair.” He then brought a black rag and threw it before them, then said, “It is this: a woman puts it on her head and then covers herself with a veil over it.”"],[16500,"Muʿāwiyah came to Madinah and stood on the pulpit with a lock of hair in his hand. He said, “I did not think that anyone would do this, because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called it false hair.”"],[16501,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whomever God wills good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.\""],[16502,"I was sitting with Mu'awiyah, and when the muezzin gave the call to prayer and said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but God,\" Mu'awiyah said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but God.\" Then the muezzin said, \"I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God,\" and Mu'awiyah said, \"I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.\" Then the muezzin said, \"Come to prayer,\" and Mu'awiyah said, \"There is no might and no power except with God.\" Then he said, \"Come to success,\" and Mu'awiyah said, \"There is no might and no power except with God.\" Then he said, \"God is greatest, God is greatest,\" and Mu'awiyah said, \"God is greatest, God is greatest.\" Then he said, \"There is no god but God,\" and Mu'awiyah said, \"There is no god but God.\" Then Mu'awiyah said, \"This is how I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[16503,"That Muhammad is the Messenger of God. He said, \"I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.\" He said, \"Come to prayer.\" He said, \"There is no might and no power except with God.\" He said, \"Come to success.\" He said, \"There is no might and no power except with God.\" He said, \"God is greatest, God is greatest.\" Mu'awiyah said, \"God is greatest, God is greatest.\" He said, \"There is no god but God.\" He said, \"There is no god but God.\" Then he said, \"This is how I heard your Prophet ﷺ say.\""],[16504,"He heard Mu'awiyah on the pulpit of the Prophet ﷺ with a lock of hair in his hand, saying, \"I found this among my family, and they claimed that women add it to their hair. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'God has cursed the one who attaches hair extensions and the one who has them attached.'\""],[16505,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A life grant is permissible for its recipients.\""],[16506,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"A life grant is permissible.\""],[16507,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A life grant is like an inheritance.\""],[16508,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"The people with the longest necks are the Muadhin (callers to prayer).\""],[16509,"We entered upon Mu'awiyah, and the caller called to prayer. He said, \"God is greatest, God is greatest,\" and Mu'awiyah said just as he said. He said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but God,\" and he said the same again. He said, \"I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God,\" and he said the same. Then he said, \"This is how I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say.\""],[16510,"I witnessed 'Uthman delivering a sermon on the pulpit standing, and I witnessed Mu'awiyah delivering a sermon sitting. He said, \"Indeed, I have not been ignorant of the Sunnah, but I have grown old, my bones have become frail, and your needs have increased. I wanted to attend to some of your needs while sitting, then stand and take my share of the Sunnah.\""],[16511,"Listen carefully, O son of my brother, to a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Talhah is among those who have fulfilled their vow.\""],[16512,"He saw Mu'awiyah delivering a sermon on the pulpit with a lock of hair in his hand, and he heard him say, \"Where are your scholars, O people of Madinah? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbidding the like of this, and he said: 'The Children of Israel were punished only when their women adopted these.'\""],[16513,"He heard Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan, with a lock of hair in his hand, saying, \"I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ forbidding the like of this, and saying: 'The Children of Israel were punished only when their women adopted these.'\""],[16514,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik, and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us: Mālik informed us; ḥ, and Abū Yazīd al-Qarāṭīsī narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh b. ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Ḥumayd b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, that he heard Muʿāwiyah b. Abī Sufyān in the year of his ḥajj while he was on the pulpit, and he took a lock of hair that was in the hand of a guard, saying: \"O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the like of this and saying: 'The Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women adopted this.'\" The wording is that of the ḥadīth of al-Qaʿnabī."],[16515,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the like of this and saying: \"The Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women adopted it.\""],[16516,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the like of this lock of hair, saying: \"The Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women adopted it.\""],[16517,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ forbidding the like of this and saying: \"The Children of Israel were punished only when their women adopted the like of this.\""],[16518,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the like of this and saying: \"The Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women adopted this.\""],[16519,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Ḥumayd b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: Muʿāwiyah came to Madinah and said: \"Where are your scholars?\" He brought out a bundle of hair from his sleeve and said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding this, and he said: 'The Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women adopted the like of this.'\""],[16520,"That he heard Muʿāwiyah delivering a sermon, saying: \"O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'This is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ, and its fasting has not been made obligatory upon us. Whoever among you wishes to fast, let him fast, for I am fasting.'\" So the people fasted."],[16521,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik, and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us: Mālik informed us; ḥ, and Abū Yazīd al-Qarāṭīsī narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh b. ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Mālik informed us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Ḥumayd b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, that he heard Muʿāwiyah on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ in the year of his ḥajj while he was on the pulpit, saying: \"O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'This day is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ. Its fasting has not been prescribed for you, but I am fasting. Whoever wishes, let him fast, and whoever wishes, let him break his fast.'\""],[16522,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; they said: Sufyān narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Ḥumayd b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: Muʿāwiyah came to Madinah and said: \"Where are your scholars? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on this day,\" and he said: \"I am fasting, so whoever wishes, let him fast, and whoever wishes, let him break his fast\"—meaning the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ."],[16523,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"This day is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ. Its fasting has not been prescribed for you, but I am fasting. Whoever wishes, let him fast it\"—meaning the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ."],[16524,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"This is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ. Its fasting has not been prescribed for you, but I am fasting. Whoever wishes to fast it, let him fast it, and whoever wishes to break his fast, let him break his fast.\""],[16525,"He informed him that he heard Muʿāwiyah while he was delivering a sermon to the people on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ, saying: \"O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'This is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ. Its fasting has not been prescribed for you, but I am fasting.'\" And he was saying that: \"Whoever among you wishes to fast it, let him fast, and whoever wishes to break his fast, let him break his fast.\""],[16526,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “This is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ, and its fasting has not been made obligatory upon you, but I am fasting. So whoever wishes may fast, and whoever wishes may break the fast.”"],[16527,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “I am only a distributor, and God is the One who gives.”"],[16528,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “I am only a distributor, and God is the One who gives.”"],[16529,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “I am only a distributor, and God is the One who gives.”"],[16530,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “When God desires good for someone, He gives him understanding in religion.”"],[16531,"“And what is that?” They said: “You prayed two rakʿahs while ʿUthmān prayed four.” He said: “I prayed two rakʿahs with the Messenger of God ﷺ.” They kept at him until he went out and prayed four."],[16532,"“Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say, when he was building the mosque, to ʿAmmār: ‘You are indeed eager for jihād, and you are among the people of Paradise, and the transgressing party will kill you’?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Then why did you kill him?” He said: “By God, you keep slipping in your urine. Did we kill him? It was only the one who brought him who killed him.”"],[16533,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to ʿAmmār: “The transgressing party will kill you.”"],[16534,"I was with Muʿāwiyah after the ʿaṣr prayer, and he saw people praying two rakʿahs after it. He said: “What is this prayer? We prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and we did not see anyone praying it.”"],[16535,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray in a single garment."],[16536,"Muʿāwiyah used to say: “By God, I have never feared speaking before anyone as I feared before ʿĀʾishah, and I never heard her speech except that it reminded me of the speech of the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[16537,"Muʿāwiyah began saying to some of those present: “Do you know that the Messenger of God ﷺ said such and such?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “Did he not also say concerning tamattuʿ with ḥajj and ʿumrah, and then forbid it?” Those who confirmed the first report said: “No, by God, he did not say this, and we do not know that he said it.”"],[16538,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to the people: “If the imam prays sitting, then pray sitting.” Al-Qasim said: “The people marveled at Mu'awiyah's truthfulness.”"],[16539,"“This is a sunnah I prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ and with Abu Bakr and 'Umar ؓ.” They said: “Your paternal cousin completed it as four [rak'ahs].” He said: “I only remember this.”"],[16540,"“You are praying a prayer that the Messenger of God ﷺ did not pray, and he used to forbid it,” meaning the two rak'ahs after 'Asr."],[16541,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever drinks wine, flog him.” He said it three times. “Then if they drink a fourth time, kill them.”"],[16542,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If he drinks wine, flog him.” He said at the fourth time: “Kill him.”"],[16543,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever dies without a pledge of allegiance on his neck dies a death of Jahiliyyah.”"],[16544,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ heard the muezzin say “Allahu Akbar,” he said the like of his words. When he said “Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah,” he said the like of his words. When he said “Ashhadu anna Muhammadan Rasul Allah” twice, he said the like of his words."],[16545,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say while Bilal was calling the adhan: When he said “Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar,” the Prophet of God said “Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar.” Then he said “Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah,” and the Prophet of God said “Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah.” Then he said “Ashhadu anna Muhammadan Rasul Allah,” and the Messenger of God ﷺ said the like of it, then he fell silent."],[16546,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever forgets something in his prayer, let him prostrate twice while sitting.”"],[16547,"“This is how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.”"],[16548,"“This is how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.”"],[16549,"He says the like of what he says until he reaches his saying “Hayya 'ala al-salah, hayya 'ala al-falah,” and he says “La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah.” Then he says the like of what he says. Then he said: “This is how I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say.”"],[16550,"This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it."],[16551,"He saw Muʿāwiyah lead the people in prayer, and he stood up after two rakʿahs. The people glorified Allah (to alert him), but he gestured to them to stand up. When he finished his prayer, he performed two prostrations before the salutation, and the people prostrated with him. Then he said: O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: �Whoever is assailed by doubt in his prayer should perform two prostrations while sitting.�"],[16552,"The Prophet ﷺ said: �Whoever forgets something in his prayer should perform two prostrations.�"],[16553,"He said that there would be a king from Qaḥṭān. Muʿāwiyah became angry and stood up, praised Allah as He deserves, then said: To proceed: It has reached me that some men among you speak of things that are not in the Book of Allah and are not reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. That is due to your ignorance. Beware of vain desires that mislead their people. I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: �This matter (authority) rests with Quraysh. No one opposes them except that Allah throws him on his face, as long as they uphold the religion.�"],[16554,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: �This matter rests with Quraysh. No one opposes them except that Allah throws him on his face, as long as they uphold the religion.�"],[16555,"He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: �This matter will remain with Quraysh. No one opposes them except that he is thrown on his face, as long as they uphold the religion.�"],[16556,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us: Mālik informed us, from Yazīd b. Ziyād, from Muḥammad b. Kaʿb al-Quraẓī, who said: Muʿāwiyah b. Abī Sufyān said while on the pulpit: �O people, there is none to withhold what Allah gives, and none to give what Allah withholds, and no one possessed of fortune benefits from his fortune before Him. Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion.� Then he said: �I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on these wooden planks.�"],[16557,"\"O people, there is no one who can prevent what Allah has given, nor is there anyone who can give what Allah has prevented. And the wealth and status of a person cannot benefit them from Allah. Whoever Allah wants good for, He will give them understanding of the religion. I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .\""],[16558,"I heard Muʿāwiyah b. Abī Sufyān delivering a sermon in Madinah, saying: You will certainly know, O people, that there is none to withhold what Allah gives, and none to give what Allah withholds, and no one possessed of fortune benefits from his fortune before Him. Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion. I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on these wooden planks."],[16559,"�Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion. This wealth is green and sweet. Whoever takes it by right will be blessed in it.� Then he said: �I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the pulpit. The listener who obeys has no argument against him, and the listener who disobeys has no argument for him.�"],[16560,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: �Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion and inspires him with right guidance.�"],[16561,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: �O Allah, there is none to withhold what You give, and none to give what You withhold. Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion.�"],[16562,"Some people during the time of Muʿāwiyah used to attend the dawn prayer and then sit with the storyteller of the congregation. When he finished, they would move to a corner of the mosque and remember Allah and recite the Book of Allah until the day grew bright. Muʿāwiyah was informed of them and came hurrying—or walking quickly—until he stood before them and said: I have come to give you glad tidings from Allah for what He has provided you. A group of people during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—I think he said—used to do something like what you do. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, as if I am imitating his walk, until he stood before them and said: �Rejoice! By Him in Whose hand is my soul, Allah ﷻ boasts of you to the angels.�"],[16563,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever loves the Ansar, it is out of love for me that he loves them, and whoever hates the Ansar, it is out of hatred for me that he hates them.”"],[16564,"Mu'awiya delivered a sermon and said something that the people disapproved of, so they rebutted him. That pleased him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “There will be rulers who speak and are not rebutted; they will tumble into the Fire, one following another.”"],[16565,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out until he climbed the pulpit, mentioned the martyrs of Uhud, prayed over them, and prolonged the prayer. Then he said, “A servant among God's servants was given the choice by God between this world and what is with Him, and he chose what is with God.” None understood it except Abu Bakr, who said, “We would ransom you with our fathers and mothers.” He said, “Gently, O Abu Bakr. The best of people in my eyes in companionship and in generosity with his wealth is the son of Abu Quhafa.”"],[16566,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.”"],[16567,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.”"],[16568,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.”"],[16569,"Come to prayer, come to success. He said, “There is no might nor power except with God. This is how I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say it.”"],[16570,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “I am not of idle play, and idle play is not of me.”"],[16571,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whoever adds to his hair something that is not part of it, he is adding falsehood to it.”"],[16572,"I heard Mu'awiya b. Abi Sufyan in Madinah, with a lock of women's hair in his hand, saying: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the like of this and said, “The Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women adopted this.”"],[16573,"I heard Mu'awiya, while he was delivering a sermon on the pulpit, say: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.”"],[16574,"What is the matter with your women that they put on their heads the like of this? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Any woman who puts on her head hair from someone else's hair, it is falsehood.”"],[16575,"He heard Mu'awiyah on the minbar, and with him was a bundle of women's hair, so he said: 'What is the matter with Muslim women that they do this? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Any woman who adds hair to her head that is not from it, it is falsehood.”'"],[16576,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"There will not cease to be a group in this nation fighting upon the command of God; the enmity of those who oppose them will not harm them, nor the abandonment of those who abandon them, until the command of God, the Exalted, comes to them while they are upon that.\""],[16577,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever hears the muezzin and says the like of what he says, he will have the like of his reward.\""],[16578,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade al-shighar (a type of marriage in which a man gives his daughter or sister in marriage to another on the condition that the other gives his daughter or sister in marriage to him, with no dower between them)."],[16579,"…that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. Mu'awiyah said: 'I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.' Then Mu'awiyah said: 'Thus I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ.'"],[16580,"I heard Mu'awiyah while he was on the minbar in Madinah saying: 'O people of Madinah, where are your jurists? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbid the like of this forelock'—and he placed it on his head, and I did not see it on a bride nor on anyone else more beautiful than it was on Mu'awiyah."],[16581,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, on the day of 'Ashura' we used to fast it in the pre-Islamic era, then God prescribed for us the fasting of Ramadan, and removed from us the fasting of 'Ashura', so whoever wishes may fast it and whoever wishes may break his fast.'"],[16582,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not hasten to something that you think that if you hasten to it you will attain it, even though God has not decreed it for you; and do not delay from something that you think that if you delay from it, it will pass you by, even though God has decreed it upon you.\""],[16583,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not be importunate in asking; for by God, none of you asks me for something and the asking brings it out from me, and I give it to him while I am averse to it, and then he is blessed in what I gave him.\""],[16584,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed, a man asks me for something and I withhold it so that you may intercede and thus be rewarded.\""],[16585,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whomever God wills good for, He gives him understanding in religion.\""],[16586,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whomever God wills good for, He gives him understanding in religion.\""],[16587,"From Muawiya."],[16588,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me not to come to my family at the first sight of the new moon, not to perform ablution with copper water, and to use the tooth-stick whenever I rose from my siesta."],[16589,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he said concerning Laylat al-Qadr, “Twenty-seven.”"],[16590,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Seek Laylat al-Qadr on the night of the twenty-seventh.”"],[16591,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ — and he would mention these words, often narrating them on Fridays: “Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in religion. This wealth is green and sweet; whoever takes it with its due right will be blessed in it. Beware of mutual praise, for it is slaughter.”"],[16592,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The world is sweet and green; whoever takes it with its due right will be blessed in it.”"],[16593,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said in his sermon — I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Beware of mutual praise, for it is slaughter.”"],[16594,"“You certainly pray this prayer — we accompanied the Messenger of God and saw him, and we did not see him pray this prayer after the prayer” — meaning after Asr."],[16595,"Muawiya entered a house in which were Abdullah b. Amir and Ibn al-Zubayr. Ibn al-Zubayr remained seated while Abdullah b. Amir stood, and he was the more dignified of the two men. Muawiya said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever is pleased to have men stand for him, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[16596,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever is pleased to have men stand for him, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[16597,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever is pleased to have people stand for him, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[16598,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever is pleased to have men stand for him, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[16599,"“Leveling graves is from the Sunnah. The Jews and Christians have raised (theirs), so do not imitate them.”"],[16600,"To a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ: “Do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking from vessels of gold and silver?” They said, “O Allah, yes.”"],[16601,"To a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ: “Do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking from vessels of gold and silver?” They said, “O Allah, yes.”"],[16602,"Muʿāwiyah asked a group of the Prophet's companions, 'Do you know that the Prophet ﷺ forbade drinking from vessels made of gold and silver?' They replied, 'By Allah, yes.'"],[16603,"I was among a gathering of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the presence of Mu‘āwiyah. Mu‘āwiyah said, “I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing silk?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness.” He said, “I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking from vessels of gold and silver?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness.”"],[16604,"I heard Mu‘āwiyah, while a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ was with him, say, “I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing silk?” They said, “O Allah, yes.”"],[16605,"One day, while the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were with him: “Do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing gold except in small pieces?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “Do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade riding on leopard skins?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “Do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade combining Hajj and ‘Umrah?” They said, “O Allah, no.”"],[16606,"I was in the presence of Mu‘āwiyah, and with him were some people from the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār. Mu‘āwiyah said, “I adjure you by Allah, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing gold except in small pieces?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking from silver vessels?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade combining Hajj and ‘Umrah?” They said, “O Allah, yes.”"],[16607,"Mu‘āwiyah performed Hajj and summoned a group of the Anṣār. He said, “I adjure you by Allah, did you not learn that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gold?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness.” He said, “I adjure you by Allah, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid silk saddle cloths?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “I adjure you by Allah, did you not hear that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leopard saddle cloths?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness.”"],[16608,"He witnessed Mu‘āwiyah while some people from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ were with him. He said, “I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing gold except in small pieces?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness.” He said, “I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade riding on leopard skins?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness.”"],[16609,"Mu‘āwiyah performed Hajj and summoned a group of the Anṣār inside the Ka‘bah. He said, “I adjure you by Allah, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid gold?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness. Did you not hear that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leopard saddle cloths?” They said, “Yes.” He said, “And I bear witness. Did you not hear that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade silk?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness.”"],[16610,"When Mu‘āwiyah pledged allegiance to Yazīd, he performed Hajj and passed by Madinah. He addressed the people and said, “We have pledged allegiance to Yazīd, so pledge allegiance.” Al-Ḥusayn b. ‘Alī ؓ stood up and said, “I, by Allah, am more entitled to it than him. My father is better than his father, my grandfather is better than his grandfather, my mother is better than his mother, and I am better than him.” Mu‘āwiyah said, “As for your saying that your grandfather is better than his grandfather, you have spoken the truth: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is better than Abū Sufyān b. Ḥarb. As for your saying that your mother is better than his mother, you have spoken the truth: Fāṭimah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is better than the daughter of Majdal. As for your saying that your father is better than his father, his father contended with your father, and Allah ruled in favor of his father over your father. As for your saying that you are better than him, he is more capable than you and more intelligent. What would please me with the like of you is a thousand.”"],[16611,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The enemy will not prevail over a people if they—” or he said, “I saw them with a man from Banū Bakr b. Wā’il.”"],[16612,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The matter will only increase in severity, the people will only increase in avarice, and the Hour will not come except upon the worst of people.”"],[16613,"I heard Muawiyah, while he was in blessed Makkah on the day of Ashura, say: The Messenger of God ﷺ fasted it and said: “Whoever among you has not fasted, let him fast it.”"],[16614,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade wearing gold except in small pieces, and riding on leopard skins.”"],[16615,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade riding on leopard skins and wearing gold except in small pieces.”"],[16616,"Muawiyah b. Abi Sufyan said: “The people of Makkah expelled the Messenger of God ﷺ, so the caliphate shall not be among them, and the people of Madinah killed Uthman ؓ, so the caliphate shall never return to them.”"],[16617,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “My community will remain triumphant over the people until the command of God comes.”"],[16618,"I entered upon Muawiyah while he was writhing in pain, and his sore was between his shoulders. He said: It does not please me that I should not find what you see. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “No harm afflicts a believer in his body except that it is an expiation for his sins.”"],[16619,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “No Muslim is afflicted with harm in his body except that it is an expiation for his sins.” And this is the severest harm."],[16620,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he returns, flog him; then if he returns, kill him.”"],[16621,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever drinks wine, lash him; if he returns, lash him; if he returns, lash him three times; if he returns a fourth time, strike his neck.”"],[16622,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever drinks wine, lash him; if he returns, lash him; if he returns, lash him; if he returns a fourth time, strike his neck.”"],[16623,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever drinks wine, lash him; if he returns, lash him; if he returns, lash him; if he returns, lash him; if he does it a fourth time, kill him.”"],[16624,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Quraysh are the governors of the people in good and evil until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[16625,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed those who shred sermons into pieces like the shredding of poetry.”"],[16626,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever supplicates with these five phrases, he will not ask Allah for anything except that He gives it to him: ‘There is no god but Allah, and Allah is greater. There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. There is no god but Allah, and there is no power and no strength except with Allah.’”"],[16627,"Muawiyah: “I have not ceased to aspire to the caliphate since the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: ‘If you rule, then do good.’”"],[16628,"“I prayed with Muawiyah, the Commander of the Believers. He stood in the second rakʿah, so the people said subhan Allah to him. He gestured to them with his hand to stand. When he finished his prayer, he prostrated two prostrations for that, then left.” And he said: “Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.”"],[16629,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever loves that the children of Adam stand up for him, the Fire is due for him.”"],[16630,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of you is the best of you to his family.”"],[16631,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out upon a group of companions gathered together and said: “What has gathered you?” They said: “We remember Allah and what He has blessed us with and what He saved us from of ignorance and its ignorance.” He said: “By Allah, is it for that that you gathered?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you are truthful, Allah Almighty will boast of you to the angels.”"],[16632,"Your location until I come to you, so he came out to us while he stumbled. When he prayed Asr, he said, \"Shall I inform you about something that the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Indeed, they used to pray the first prayer with him, then they would sit down and he would come out to them and say, 'What kept you after I left?' They would say, 'Nothing.' He would then say, 'If you were to see towards your Lord, a door from the sky was opened and I see your angels competing with each other in presenting you in front of Allah while you are waiting for the prayer.'\""],[16633,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There is no sin except that Allah may forgive it, except one who was a polytheist or killed a believer deliberately.”"],[16634,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every sin may be forgiven, except that a man dies while he is a disbeliever or he kills a believer deliberately.”"],[16635,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Every sin, Allah may forgive it, except the man who dies as a disbeliever, or a man who killed a believer deliberately.”"],[16636,"I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a statement by which Allah benefited me. I heard him say: “Turn away from the people. Do you not see that if you follow suspicion in the people, you will corrupt them, or you would almost corrupt them?”"],[16637,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.”"],[16638,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The listener who obeys has no case against him, and the listener who disobeys has no case for him.”"],[16639,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “O people, do not rush ahead of me into bowing and prostrating. Whatever I get ahead of you with when I bow, you will catch up with it when I rise. I have become heavy”—meaning, I have grown older. The wording is from the hadith of Sulayman b. Bilal."],[16640,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he said: “Do not rush ahead of me with bowing and prostrating, for whatever I get ahead of you with when I prostrate, you will catch up with it when I rise, and whatever I get ahead of you with when I bow, you will catch up with it when I rise. I have become heavy.”"],[16641,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.”"],[16642,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade asking difficult, unnecessary questions."],[16643,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “What remains of this world is only affliction and tribulation. The likeness of any one of you is like a vessel: if its top is good, its bottom is good.”"],[16644,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: A man transgressed against himself. He came to a man and said, “The other man killed ninety-nine people, all of them wrongfully. Is there any repentance for me?” He said, “No.” So he killed him. Then he came to another and said, “The other man killed a hundred people, all of them wrongfully. Is there any repentance for him?” He said, “If I told you that God does not accept the repentance of one who repents, I would have lied to you. Here is a place where there are people who worship. Go to them and worship God with them.” So he set out toward them and died on that path. The angels of mercy and the angels of punishment disputed over him, so God sent an angel to them and said, “Measure between the two places. Whichever he is closer to, he belongs to them.” They found him closer to the monastery of the penitents by a finger’s length, so he was forgiven. The wording is from the hadith of al-Walid."],[16645,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “God is not overcome, nor deceived, nor informed of what He does not know. Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.”"],[16646,"I heard Muawiyah on the pulpit in Damascus saying: “O people, beware of the hadiths of the Messenger of God ﷺ except a hadith that was mentioned in the time of Umar, for Umar ؓ was a man who made people fear God.” Then I heard him say: “Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.’”"],[16647,"I heard Muawiyah on the pulpit in Damascus saying: “O people, beware of the hadiths of the Messenger of God ﷺ except a hadith that was mentioned in the time of Umar, for Umar ؓ was a man who made people fear God.” Then I heard him say: “Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.’”"],[16648,"I heard Muawiyah on the pulpit in Damascus saying: “O people, beware of the hadiths of the Messenger of God ﷺ except a hadith that was mentioned in the time of Umar, for Umar ؓ was a man who made people fear God.” Then I heard him say: “Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.’”"],[16649,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"My nation will continue to stand up for the truth, fighting against those who fight them and oppose them until the Day of Judgment.\""],[16650,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever Allah wills good for, He grants him understanding of the religion.\""],[16651,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I am only a treasurer, and it is Allah who gives. So whoever I give a gift to while I am content with it, he is blessed in it. And whoever I give a gift to because of greed of the soul and intense asking, he is like one who eats but is never satisfied.\""],[16652,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the pulpit: \"I am only a treasurer, and it is Allah who gives. So whoever I give a gift to while I am content with it, he is blessed in it. And whoever I give a gift to because of greed of the soul and intense asking, he is like one who eats but is never satisfied.\""],[16653,"He was speaking with Muawiyah when the muezzin called the adhan. He ordered him to listen quietly, then he said takbir as he said takbir. Then when the muezzin said 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah,' he said 'And we bear witness that there is no god but Allah.' When the muezzin said 'I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah,' he said 'And we bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' Ibn Hubayra said: I asked him, 'Is this something you saw or heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He replied, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say takbir when he heard the muezzin. When he said 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah,' he said 'And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.' And when he said 'I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah,' he said 'And I bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah.'\""],[16654,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The eye is the string that ties the anus. When the eye sleeps, the string is untied, so whoever sleeps must perform ablution.\""],[16655,"Muawiyah gave a sermon to the people and mentioned in his sermon that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade seven things, and I convey that to you and forbid you from them: wailing, poetry, images, displaying adornment, skins of beasts of prey, gold, and silk."],[16656,"O people, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nine things, and I forbid you from them: wailing, poetry, displaying adornment, images, skins of beasts of prey, singing, gold, heat, and silk."],[16657,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nine things, and I forbid you from them. Indeed among them are wailing, singing, images, poetry, gold, heat, saddles, and silk."],[16658,"What are these hadiths that have reached me from you that you narrate? I have resolved to banish you from Syria. He replied: By Allah, were it not for females, I would not love to remain there even for an hour. Muawiyah said: What is the hadith you narrate about tila (a beverage)? He replied: Indeed, it is not lawful for me to say about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he did not say. I heard him say: \"Whoever falsely attributes to me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[16659,"What are these hadiths that have reached me from you that you narrate? I have resolved to banish you from Syria. He replied: By Allah, were it not for females, I would not love to remain there even for an hour. Muawiyah said: What is the hadith you narrate about tila (a beverage)? He replied: Indeed, it is not lawful for me to say about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he did not say. I heard him say: \"Whoever falsely attributes to me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[16660,"He heard Muawiyah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to stand on the pulpit one day before Ramadan and say: \"Fasting is on such and such a day, and we are going to fast in advance. Whoever wishes to fast in advance may do so, and whoever wishes to leave it may do so.\""],[16661,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"You will conquer lands where wormwood grows.\""],[16662,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Leave the Turks alone as long as they leave you alone.”"],[16663,"Write to the ruler of Armenia a reply to his letter—may your mother be bereaved of you—and do not stir them up with anything, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Leave the Turks alone as long as they leave you alone.”"],[16664,"Muawiyah, if I had approached you before this period, I would have cut off a part of you, then I would have stood up and prayed Dhuhr in Makkah. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said: \"The people of the Book divided into seventy-two sects, and this nation will divide into seventy-three sects, all of them are in the Fire except one, which is the group (Al-Jama'ah).\" And he said: \"There will come out from my nation people who deal with desires as the dog deals with its master. Not a vein or a joint will be left except that they enter it.\" By Allah, O Arabs, if you do not uphold what Muhammad, ﷺ , brought, then others among the people are more deserving of upholding it."],[16665,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the people of the Book divided into seventy-two sects in their book, and this Ummah (nation) will divide into seventy-three sects, all of which are in the Fire except one, and that is the group. And indeed, there will emerge from my Ummah (nation) people who will interpret these desires just as the dog licks its owner's hand, and there will not remain a vein or joint except that they will enter it.\""],[16666,"Mu’awiya showed them the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he reached the wiping of his head, he placed his palms on the front of his head, then brought them back until he reached the back of the neck, then returned them until he reached the place from which he began."],[16667,"He showed them the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he reached the wiping of his head, he placed his palms on the front of his head, then passed them until he reached the back of the neck, then returned them until he reached the place from which he began. Al-Walid said: And ‘Abdullah b. al-‘Ala’ b. Zabr reported to me from Abu al-Azhar from Mu’awiya likewise, and Hariz b. ‘Uthman reported to me from ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Maysara from al-Miqdam b. Ma’dikarib from the Messenger of God ﷺ the like of it."],[16668,"He attended Mu’awiya performing ablution, and he wiped his ears, their outer and inner parts, and said: “This is the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[16669,"About Mu’awiya’s ablution, showing them the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ: he performed ablution three times, except for washing his feet, which was without a fixed number."],[16670,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “If you pursue the private faults of people, you will corrupt them, or you will almost corrupt them.” Abu al-Darda’ would say: A word Mu’awiya heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ by which God benefited him."],[16671,"He used to teach the people the tashahhud while on the pulpit, from the Prophet ﷺ: “Greetings, prayers, and good words are due to God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[16672,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade difficult and obscure questions. Ishaq said: Rawh b. ‘Ubada narrated to us from al-Awza’i who said: “Al-ghulutat are the hard and severe questions.”"],[16673,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There will continue to be a group from my nation, steadfast, unharmed by those who abandon them, until the command of God comes, while they are victorious over the people.”"],[16674,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Adhere to truthfulness, for it leads to righteousness, and both are in Paradise. Beware of lying, for it leads to wickedness, and both are in the Fire.”"],[16675,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Emigration is of two kinds: one is to abandon evil deeds, and the other is to emigrate to God and His Messenger. Emigration does not cease as long as repentance is accepted, and repentance continues to be accepted until the sun rises from the west. When it rises, it will rise upon every heart with what is in it, and people will have enough of deeds.”"],[16676,"I accompanied the Prophet ﷺ and listened to him, and I heard most of his prayer was that he would say: “Glory be to You, Lord of the worlds.”"],[16677,"“Fulfill my need, O Commander of the Believers, for by Allah my burden is great: I have become father of ten, brother of ten, and uncle of ten.” When Marwān turned away while Ibn ʿAbbās was sitting with Muʿāwiyah on his couch, Muʿāwiyah said: “I adjure you by Allah, O Ibn ʿAbbās, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘When the sons of al-Ḥakam reach thirty men, they will take the signs of Allah among them as spoils, His servants as slaves, and His Book as corruption. When they reach four hundred and ninety-nine, their destruction will be quicker than the ripening of fruit’?” Ibn ʿAbbās said: “O Allah, yes.” Then Marwān mentioned a need of his, and Marwān b. ʿAbd al-Malik referred it back to Muʿāwiyah, and he spoke to him about it. When he turned away, Muʿāwiyah said: “I adjure you by Allah, O Ibn ʿAbbās, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned this one and said: ‘Abū al-Jabābirah al-Arbaʿah (father of the four tyrants)’?” Ibn ʿAbbās said: “O Allah, yes.”"],[16678,"I heard Muʿāwiyah on the pulpit, and he narrated little from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, exalted is He, brought forth the progeny of Adam from his loins until they filled the earth, and they were like this.” Jaʿfar clasped his hands, one over the other."],[16679,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"There will always be a group of my Ummah who will remain steadfast in the command of Allah. Those who betray them or oppose them will not be able to harm them until the command of Allah comes and they will be prominent among the people.\""],[16680,"He mentioned to them the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: that he wiped his head until water dripped from his head or nearly dripped, and that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached the wiping of his head, he placed his palms on the front of his head, then passed them until he reached the back of the neck with them, then returned them until he reached the place from which he began."],[16681,"I heard Abū al-Azhar say: Muʿāwiyah stood at Dayr Misḥal, which is at the gate of Homs, and said: “Indeed, the fast is on such-and-such a day, and we will begin tomorrow.” Then Mālik b. Hubayrah stood up to him and said: “O Muʿāwiyah, is this an opinion you have formed or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Fast the month and its beginning.’”"],[16682,"He used to send a guard from his guards to me, like the guards of Kūbah and Qarū, saying: “Indeed, this is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ. The Prophet ﷺ used to fast it, and we are fasting. So whoever wishes to fast it, let him fast.”"],[16683,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A nation is not deemed holy in which justice is not carried out and the weak does not take his right from the strong without stammering.”"],[16684,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Goodness is a habit and evil is obstinacy.” Ibn Bint Shuraḥbīl added in his hadith from the Prophet ﷺ: “And whoever Allah wills good for, He grants him understanding in religion.”"],[16685,"We were sitting in the mosque when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: “You talk about how I am the last of you to die, but I am the first of you to die, and you will follow me in groups,” meaning one after another. Then he recited this verse and said: {Say: He is able to send upon you punishment from above you or from beneath your feet} until he reached {For every report there is a fixed time, and you will come to know}. Then he said: “A band of my community will not cease fighting for the truth, victorious, not caring who abandons them or opposes them, until the command of Allah comes upon that.” Then he recited this verse: {O Jesus, I will take you and raise you to Me and purify you from those who disbelieve, and I will make those who follow you above those who disbelieve until the Day of Resurrection.}"],[16686,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever Allah wills good for, He grants him understanding in religion.”"],[16687,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever Allah wills good for, He grants him understanding in religion.”"],[16688,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever Allah wills good for, He grants him understanding in religion.”"],[16689,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Hijrah will not cease until repentance ceases” – three times – “and repentance will not cease until the sun rises from its west.”"],[16690,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A community is not sanctified if its weak cannot take their right from its strong without being oppressed.” Then he said: If he says yes, carry him to me by post. So he asked him and he said yes, so he carried him by post from Egypt to Syria. Muawiya asked him and he informed him, so Muawiya said: “I too have heard it, but I wished to confirm it.”"],[16691,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, every intoxicant is forbidden to every believer.”"],[16692,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever dies without an imam dies a death of Jahiliyyah.”"],[16693,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever Allah wishes good for, He gives him understanding in religion.”"],[16694,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever Allah wishes good for, He gives him understanding in religion.”"],[16695,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade obscure and ambiguous questions."],[16696,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: “I am only a conveyer, and Allah guides; and I am a distributor, and Allah gives. Whoever receives something from me with good conduct and desire, that is the one who is blessed in it. And whoever receives something with bad conduct and bad desire, that is the one who eats but is never satisfied.”"],[16697,"Abu Hazzan Atiyya b. Abi Jamilah narrated to them, tracing it back to Muawiya b. Abi Sufyan, and Muawiya tracing it back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; he said: “I am only a conveyer, and Allah guides; and I am only a distributor, and Allah gives. Whoever receives something from us with good conduct and good desire, that is the one who is blessed in it. And whoever receives something from us with bad conduct and bad desire, that is the one who eats but is never satisfied.”"],[16698,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I am only a deliverer (of the message), while Allah guides and divides, and Allah gives. So whoever receives from me something with good guidance and good desire, then that is the one who is blessed in it. And whoever receives from me something with bad desire and bad guidance, then that is the one who eats but does not feel satisfied.\""],[16699,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There will not cease to be a group from my ummah standing upon the command of Allah, not harmed by those who oppose them or forsake them, until the command of Allah comes while they are victorious over the people.”"],[16700,"I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"If Allah wants to do good to a person, He makes him comprehend the religion. I am just a distributor, but the grant is from Allah. (And remember) that this nation (true Muslims) will keep on following Allah's teachings strictly and they will not be harmed by any one going on a different path till Allah's order (Day of Judgment) is established.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 71)"],[16701,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Who-ever loves to meet Allah, Allah (too) loves to meet him and who-ever hates to meet Allah, Allah (too) hates to meet him\".ʿAisha, or some of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ said, \"But we dislike death.\" He said: It is not like this, but it is meant that when the time of the death of a believer approaches, he receives the good news of Allah's pleasure with him and His blessings upon him, and so at that time nothing is dearer to him than what is in front of him. He therefore loves the meeting with Allah, and Allah (too) loves the meeting with him. But when the time of the death of a disbeliever approaches, he receives the evil news of Allah's torment and His Requital, whereupon nothing is more hateful to him than what is before him. Therefore, he hates the meeting with Allah, and Allah too, hates the meeting with him.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6507)"],[16702,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding riding on the skins of beasts of prey and the building of tall structures."],[16703,"It was sent down on the day of Arafah on a Friday. Then he recited this verse: “So whoever hopes for the meeting with his Lord, let him do righteous work and not associate anyone in the worship of his Lord.” And he said: It is the last verse that was sent down."],[16704,"‘Whoever lies upon me intentionally, then let him take his seat in the Fire’. (Using translation from Muslim 3)"],[16705,"I heard Mu'awiyah on the pulpit saying: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, he would say: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no one's wealth or fortune avails against You.'"],[16706,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'O Allah, whoever I cursed in the pre-Islamic era and then entered Islam, make that a means of nearness to You for him.'"],[16707,"In his sermon he said: 'The wealth is our wealth and the fay' is our fay'. Whomever we wish we give, and whomever we wish we withhold.' No one responded to him. On the second Friday he said the same and no one responded. On the third Friday he made the same statement, so a man from those present in the mosque stood up to him and said: 'No, rather the wealth is our wealth and the fay' is our fay'. Whoever comes between us and it, we will take him to Allah with our swords.' Mu'awiyah descended, sent for the man, and admitted him. The people said: 'The man is doomed.' Then the people entered and found the man with him on the couch. Mu'awiyah said to the people: 'This man has revived me, may Allah revive him. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There will be leaders after me who will speak and no one will refute them; they will plunge into the Fire as monkeys plunge.\" I spoke on the first Friday and no one replied to me, so I feared that I might be one of them. Then I spoke on the second Friday and no one replied to me, so I said to myself: I am one of the people. Then I spoke on the third Friday, and this man stood up and replied to me, so he revived me, may Allah revive him.'"],[16708,"He said: 'It is not from the Sunnah to fast while traveling.'"],[16709,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say many times: When the muezzin calls the adhan and pronounces the shahadah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pronounce the shahadah as he does. When the muezzin says 'Hayya 'ala al-salah', he would say: 'There is no power and no strength except with Allah.' When the muezzin says 'Hayya 'ala al-falah', he would also say: 'There is no power and no strength except with Allah.'"],[16710,"I heard Mu'awiyah say: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat milk, then stand and pray without performing wudu.'"],[16711,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'O people, knowledge comes only by learning, and fiqh comes only by understanding. Whoever Allah wills good for, He grants him understanding in the religion. It is only the scholars among His servants who truly fear Allah.'"],[16712,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Ten houses in the Hijaz are more enduring than twenty houses in Syria.'"],[16713,"Mu'awiyah came out to us after we had prayed Zuhr while we were supplicating to Allah. He said: 'Stay where you are until I come to you.' He came out to us wearing a cloak and after he prayed 'Asr he said: 'Shall I not tell you something that the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did? They prayed the first prayer with him, then sat until they prayed 'Asr with him. He came out to them and said: \"Have you been sitting here all this time?\" They said: \"No.\" He said: \"If you could see your Lord, blessed and exalted, He opened a gate of the gates of heaven and boasted to His angels about your gathering while you were waiting for the prayer.\"'"],[16714,"Mu'awiyah entered upon 'Ammar, and when he left his presence he said: 'O Allah, do not make his death at our hands, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The transgressing faction will kill 'Ammar.\"'"],[16715,"The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ said: 'O Messenger of Allah, among us are men who practice tiyarah (bird omens).' He said: 'That is something you find within yourselves; it will not harm you.' They said: 'Among us are men who go to soothsayers.' He said: 'Do not go to any soothsayer.'"],[16716,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about tiyarah, and he said: 'That is something you find within yourselves; it will not harm you.'"],[16717,"Mu'awiya b. al-Hakam al-Sulami, who was one of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, said: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: What do you think about things we used to do in the pre-Islamic era? We used to practice tiyara (drawing evil omens from birds). The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"That is something one of you finds in his heart, so do not let it deter you.\" I said: O Messenger of God, we also used to go to soothsayers. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not go to soothsayers.\""],[16718,"From Mu'awiya b. al-Hakam, similar to the hadith of Malik: \"In the prayer of the Prophet ﷺ there were eleven rak'ahs, and he would lie down on his right side.\""],[16719,"I set out to a small flock of sheep that a slave girl of mine was tending in the direction of Uhud and al-Jawwaniyya, and I found that a wolf had taken one of its sheep. I am a man from the children of Adam, and I get angry as they get angry, so I struck her a blow. Then I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him, and he made that seem grave to me. I said: O Messenger of God, should I not free her? He said: \"Yes, bring her to me.\" So I brought her to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: \"Where is God?\" She said: 'God ﷻ is in heaven.' He said: \"Who am I?\" She said: 'You are the Messenger of God ﷺ.' He said: \"Free her, for she is a believer.\""],[16720,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ: I had a slave girl who was tending some small sheep in the direction of Uhud when I looked at her one time and found that a wolf had gone off with one of them. I am one of the children of Adam and I get angry as they get angry, but I slapped her a slap. The Messenger of God ﷺ made that seem grave to me, so I said: Should I not free her? He said: \"Bring her to me.\" So I brought her, and he said: \"Where is God?\" She said: 'In heaven.' He said: \"Who am I?\" She said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ.' He said: \"Free her, for she is a believer.\""],[16721,"I said: O Messenger of God, among us are men who practice tiyara. He said: \"That is something you find in your hearts, so it will not harm you.\" He said: I said: And among us are men who go to soothsayers. He said: \"Do not go to them.\" He said: And among us are men who draw lines (in the sand). He said: \"A prophet drew lines, so whoever's line coincides with his knowledge, he knows.\""],[16722,"I said: O Messenger of God, we are people who have only recently left the pre-Islamic era, and God has brought Islam, and there are men among us who practice tiyara. He said: \"That is something they find in their chests, so let it not deter them.\" He said: O Messenger of God, and men among us go to soothsayers. He said: \"No, do not go to them.\" He said: And men among us draw lines. He said: \"A prophet of the prophets used to draw lines, so whoever's line coincides with his, that is it.\""],[16723,"I said: O Messenger of God, among us are men who practice tiyara. He said: \"That is something you find in your chests, so it will not harm you.\" I said: And among us are men who go to soothsayers. He said: \"Do not go to them.\" I said: And among us are men who draw lines. He said: \"A prophet drew lines, so whoever's line coincides with his knowledge, he knows.\""],[16724,"I said: O Messenger of God, we are a people who have only recently left the pre-Islamic era, and God has brought Islam, and among us are men who go to soothsayers. He said: \"Do not go to them.\" I said: And among us are men who practice tiyara. He said: \"That is something they find in their chests, so it will not harm them.\" I said: And among us are men who draw lines. He said: \"A prophet among the prophets used to draw lines, so whoever's line coincides with his, that is it.\""],[16725,"He said: I said: O Messenger of God, we are a people who have only recently left the pre-Islamic era, and God ﷻ has brought Islam, and there are men among us who draw lines. He said: \"A prophet among the prophets used to draw lines, so whoever's line coincides with his, that is it.\" He said: And among us are men who practice tiyara. He said: \"That is something they find in their chests, but it will not harm them.\" I said: And among us are men who go to soothsayers. He said: \"Do not go to them.\""],[16726,"While I was with the Prophet ﷺ , a man from the people sneezed, so I said, \"May Allah have mercy on you.\" The people stared at me with their eyes. I said, \"May their mothers be excused, why are you looking at me?\" He (the Prophet) said, \"The people struck their hands on their thighs.\" When I saw that they silenced me, I remained silent. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, I did not see a better teacher before or after him. Verily, he did not strike me, nor did he humiliate me, nor did he curse me. But he said, 'Indeed, our prayer is not for the purpose of talking to people, rather it is for glorifying Allah, praising Him, and reciting the Quran.'\""],[16727,"I prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and a man from the people sneezed, so I said: May God have mercy on you. The people stared at me, so I said: Woe is my mother! What is the matter with you that you look at me? They began striking their hands on their thighs, so I knew they were signaling me to be quiet, but I remained silent. When the Messenger of God ﷺ had finished praying—may my father and mother be his ransom—he did not strike me, nor scold me, nor revile me. Then he said: \"Indeed, this prayer is not permissible for any of people's speech in it. It is only glorification, magnification, and recitation of the Qur'an,\" or as the Messenger of God ﷺ said."],[16728,"I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and a man among the people sneezed. So I said, \"May Allah have mercy on you\" or \"May Allah have mercy on all of you.\" Then the people stared at me, so I said, \"May my mother and father be sacrificed for me\" (a common Arabic expression of confusion or surprise), then they began hitting their thighs with their hands. I realized that the people were trying to silence me with their eyes. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, I have never seen a teacher who was more gentle in teaching than him, neither before nor after him. He did not scold, reproach, or insult me. He said, \"In this prayer, there is no place for people's speech. It is only for glorifying Allah, declaring His greatness, and reciting the Quran.\" \"And Ayyub did not mention 'Ata' ibn Yasar in his narration.\""],[16729,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Woe to the one who speaks and makes his people laugh by lying. Woe to him, woe to him.\""],[16730,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Woe to the one who speaks and lies to make the people laugh. Woe to him, woe to him.\""],[16731,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, the one who talks to people and lies to make them laugh — woe to him, woe to him.\""],[16732,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Woe to the one who talks to people falsely to make them laugh. Woe to him, woe to him.\""],[16733,"I heard the Prophet of Allah ﷺ say about the one who talks to people and makes them laugh: \"Woe to him, woe to him.\""],[16734,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom should I treat with the utmost devotion? He said: \"Your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your father, then the nearest relative, then the next nearest.\""],[16735,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom should I treat with the utmost devotion? He said: \"Your mother\" — he said it three times. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then whom should I treat with the utmost devotion? He said: \"Your father.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, then whom? He said: \"Then the nearest relative, then the next nearest.\""],[16736,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom should I treat with the utmost devotion? He said: \"Your mother, then your mother, then your mother, then your father, then the nearest relative, then the next nearest.\""],[16737,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom should I treat with the utmost devotion? He said: \"Your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your father, then the nearest relative, then the next nearest.\""],[16738,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom should I treat with the utmost devotion? He said: \"Your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your father.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then the nearest relative, then the next nearest.\""],[16739,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom should I treat with the utmost devotion? He said: \"Your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Your father, then the nearest relative, then the next nearest.\""],[16740,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, we ask one another for our wealth among ourselves. He said: \"Yes, a man may ask in times of strife between him and his people, but when it reaches the point of pressing need or near destitution, he should refrain.\""],[16741,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a people who ask one another for our wealth among ourselves. He said: \"One of you may ask in cases of need and strife, to set things right between his people, but when it reaches the point of pressing need or near destitution, he should abstain.\""],[16742,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: By Allah, I did not come to you until I had sworn by these fingers of mine that I would not follow you or follow your religion. I have come to a man who understands nothing except what Allah ﷻ and His Messenger ﷺ teach me. I ask you by Allah: With what did your Lord send you to us? He said: \"Sit down.\" Then he said: \"With Islam.\" I said: What is the sign of Islam? He said: \"That you bear witness that there is no deity but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that you establish prayer, give zakah, and abandon shirk. Every Muslim is inviolable to another Muslim; they are two brothers, two supporters. Allah does not accept from a polytheist who associates partners with Him after his Islam any deed. My Lord is calling me and asking me whether I have conveyed to His servants, so let the one who is present among you convey to the one who is absent. You will be called with your mouths bridled with the fidam. The first thing that one of you will be asked about is his thigh and his palm.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, is this our religion? He said: \"Yes. You will be gathered on your faces, on your feet, and as riders.\""],[16743,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection you will be called with your mouths muzzled with the fadam.” Then he said: “Indeed, the first part of any of you to be made visible will be his thigh and his palm.”"],[16744,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will be gathered on foot and riding, and you will be dragged on your faces.”"],[16745,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, choose for me. He gestured with his hand towards Syria and said: “O people, indeed you will be gathered on foot and riding, and you will be dragged on your faces, with your mouths muzzled with the fadam, and the first part of any of you to begin will be his thigh.”"],[16746,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever is asked by his master for surplus wealth and does not give it to him, it will be turned into a bald-headed snake on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[16747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one asks a master for surplus that he has and withholds it, except that his surplus which he has will come on the Day of Resurrection as a bald-headed snake.”"],[16748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A man does not approach his leader asking for favors from him, and the leader withholds them, except that Allah will make him on the Day of Resurrection a coward, deafening his favor that he withholds.\""],[16749,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “For every forty grazing camels, a two-year-old she-camel is due. Whoever gives it seeking reward will have its reward, and whoever withholds it, we will take it and half of his camels as an ordinance from the ordinances of your Lord. It is not lawful for Muhammad or for the family of Muhammad.”"],[16750,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “For every grazing herd of camels, for every forty, a two-year-old she-camel is due. Camels are not to be separated from their condition. Whoever gives it as a trader will have its reward, and whoever withholds it, I will take it and half of his wealth as an ordinance from the ordinances of our Lord. The family of Muhammad has no share in it.”"],[16751,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “For every grazing herd of camels, for every forty, a two-year-old she-camel is due. Whoever gives it seeking reward will have its reward, and whoever withholds it, we will take it and half of his camels as an ordinance from the ordinances of our Lord. It is not lawful for the family of Muhammad to have any of it.”"],[16752,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, what parts of our private areas may we expose and what may we leave? He said: “Guard your private area except from your wife and those whom your right hand possesses.” He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if we are among one another? He said: “If you can ensure that no one sees your private area, then do so.” They said: What if one of us is alone by himself? He said: “Allah is more deserving that one be shy before Him.” And he placed his hand over his private area."],[16753,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, our private areas, what may we expose of them and what may we leave? He said: “Guard your private area except from your wife or those whom your right hand possesses.” I said: What if we are among one another? He said: “If you can ensure that no one sees your private area, then do so.” I said: What do you think if one of us is sitting alone? He said: “Allah is more deserving that one be shy before Him.”"],[16754,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, our private areas, what may we expose of them and what may we leave? He said: “Cover your private area except from your wife or those whom your right hand possesses.” Al-Hajabi added in his narration: I said: What about people being among one another? He said: “If you can ensure that no one sees it, then let no one see it.” I said: What if one of us is alone? He said: “Allah is more deserving that one be shy before Him.”"],[16755,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, what may we expose of our private areas and what may we leave? He said: “Guard your private area except from your wife and those whom your right hand possesses.” I said: What if we are among one another? He said: “Guard your private area as much as you can.” He said: What if we are in seclusion? He said: “Allah is more deserving that one be shy before Him.”"],[16756,"I said: O Messenger of God, our private parts—what may we expose of them and what must we guard? He said: “Guard your private part except from your wife or what your right hand possesses.” I said: When people are with one another? He said: “If you can ensure that no one sees it, then let no one see it.” I said: O Prophet of God, what about one of us when he is alone? He said: “God is more deserving that one be modest before Him.”"],[16757,"The Prophet ﷺ detained some people from my tribe on suspicion. A man from my tribe came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon and said: O Muhammad, why are my neighbors being held? The Prophet ﷺ remained silent. He said: Some people say that you forbid something and then make it lawful for yourself. The Prophet ﷺ said: “What are you saying?” I began to intervene between them with words, fearing that he would hear it and invoke against my tribe an invocation after which they would never prosper. The Prophet ﷺ kept on until he understood it, then said: “They have said it,” or he said: “He has said it regarding them. By God, if I had done so, it would be against me and not against them. Release his neighbors for him.”"],[16758,"The Prophet ﷺ detained a man on suspicion, then someone interceded for him and he released him."],[16759,"I said: O Prophet of God, our wives—what may we do with them and what must we avoid? He said: “Your field, so come to your field as you wish, except that you do not strike the face, do not revile, and do not abandon except within the house. Feed when you eat, clothe when you clothe yourself. How could it be otherwise, since some of you have been intimate with some?”"],[16760,"I said: O Messenger of God, our wives—what may we do with them and what must we avoid? He said: “Your field, so come to your field as you wish, except that you do not strike the face, do not revile, and do not abandon except within the house. Feed when you eat, clothe when you clothe yourself. How could it be otherwise, since some of you have been intimate with some?”"],[16761,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Three eyes will not see the Fire: an eye that stood guard in the path of God, an eye that wept out of fear of God, and an eye that lowered its gaze from what God has forbidden.”"],[16762,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A black woman who is childbearing is better than a beautiful one who does not give birth. I will vie with you in numbers among the nations, even by the miscarried fetus that remains bloated at the gate of Paradise. It will be said to him: Enter Paradise. He will say: O Lord, and my parents? It will be said to him: Enter Paradise, you and your parents.”"],[16763,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: God said: “I am as My servant thinks of Me.”"],[16764,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “God, exalted is He, created one hundred mercies. One mercy is among His creation, by which they show mercy to one another, and He reserved for His friends ninety-nine.”"],[16765,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Anger spoils a matter just as vinegar spoils honey.”"],[16766,"When charity was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, he would not eat from it, and when a gift was brought to him, he would eat from it."],[16767,"Food would be brought to the Prophet ﷺ. If it was charity, he would not eat from it, and if it was a gift, he would eat from it."],[16768,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do you refrain from mentioning the wicked? Mention him with what is in him so that people may know him.”"],[16769,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There is no backbiting for the immoral person.”"],[16770,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows, of which you are eighty rows, and the rest of humanity make up the remainder, and you will complete seventy nations, you being the best and most honorable of them in the sight of God ﷻ.”"],[16771,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever changes his religion, kill him. God does not accept the repentance of a servant who disbelieves after his Islam.”"],[16772,"I said, “O Messenger of God, what is the right of my neighbor upon me?” He said, “If he falls ill, visit him; if he dies, attend his funeral; if he asks you for a loan, lend to him; if he is in need, cover him; if good befalls him, congratulate him; if a calamity befalls him, console him; do not raise your building above his building so as to block the wind from him, and do not annoy him with the smell of your cooking pot unless you ladle out some for him.”"],[16773,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Stick to Greater Syria.”"],[16774,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “It is from God ﷻ, not from His Messenger: may God curse the one who cuts down lote trees.”"],[16775,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There is no might and no power except with God; it is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise.”"],[16776,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Secret charity extinguishes the wrath of the Lord.”"],[16777,"I said, “O Messenger of God, I have two neighbors; to which of them should I give a gift?” He said, “To the one whose door is nearer to you.”"],[16778,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! I have two neighbors; which of them should I give a gift to?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"(Give) to the one whose door is nearer to you.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2595)"],[16779,"The Prophet ﷺ recited, {On that Day God will pay them in full their true recompense}, and he said it like that."],[16780,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wiping his hand on his thigh and saying, {On that Day God will pay them in full their true recompense, and they will know that God is the Clear Truth}."],[16781,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “You complete seventy nations; you are the best of them and the most honored of them in the sight of Allah, may He be glorified and exalted.”"],[16782,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: There was a servant among the servants of Allah to whom Allah gave wealth and children. A portion of his life passed, and a portion remained. He said to his sons: “What kind of father have I been to you?” They said: “The best of fathers.” He said: “By Allah, I will not leave with anyone any wealth that came from me to him, except that I will take it back—or you will do to me what I say to you.” So he took a covenant from them. He said: “If not, then when I die, burn me with fire, then crush me, then look for a windy day and scatter me, that perhaps I may elude Allah.” He said: So he was summoned and gathered, and it was said to him: “What made you do what you did?” He said: “I feared Your punishment.” He said: “Go forth, for you have been forgiven.”"],[16783,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You complete seventy nations; you are the last of them and the most honored of them in the sight of Allah, may He be glorified and exalted.”"],[16784,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “You will come on the Day of Resurrection with muzzles on your mouths. The first part of a person to speak will be his thigh and his hand.”"],[16785,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In Paradise there is a sea of water, a sea of wine, a sea of milk, and a sea of honey; then rivers are split open from them afterwards.”"],[16786,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, with what did our Lord send you to us? He said: “That you worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prayer, and give the zakat. Every Muslim is inviolable to another Muslim. This is your religion; wherever you are, it will suffice you.”"],[16787,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the right of one of our wives over him? He said: “That you feed her when you eat, clothe her when you clothe yourself, do not strike the face, and do not shun her except within the house.”"],[16788,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah does not accept the repentance of a servant who associates partners with Him after his Islam.”"],[16789,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah does not accept the repentance of a servant who associates partners with Him after his Islam.”"],[16790,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not come to you until I had sworn by the number of these fingers of mine that I would not come to you. By the One who sent you with the truth, what is it with which Allah sent you? He said: “With Islam.” I said: What is Islam? He said: “That you submit your heart to Allah, direct your face to Allah, pray the obligatory prayer, and pay the obligatory zakat. Two brothers, supporters: Allah does not accept the repentance of a servant who associates partners with Him after his Islam.”"],[16791,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not come to you until I had sworn by the number of these fingers of mine that I would not come to you. By the One who sent you with the truth, what is it with which Allah sent you? He said: “With Islam.” I said: What is Islam? He said: “That you submit your heart to Allah, direct your face to Allah, pray the obligatory prayer, and pay the obligatory zakat. Two brothers, supporters: Allah does not accept the repentance of a servant who associates partners with Him after his Islam.”"],[16792,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not come to you until I had sworn by the number of these fingers of mine that I would not come to you. By the One who sent you with the truth, what is it with which Allah sent you? He said: “With Islam.” I said: What is Islam? He said: “That you submit your heart to Allah, direct your face to Allah, pray the obligatory prayer, and pay the obligatory zakat. Two brothers, supporters: Allah does not accept the repentance of a servant who associates partners with Him after his Islam.”"],[16793,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'I have sworn by the number of these'—and he pointed to his fingers—'that I will not follow you nor follow what you have brought. I adjure you by Allah: what is the religion with which Allah sent you?' He said, 'He sent me with Islam.' I said, 'What is Islam?' He said, 'That you say: I have submitted myself to Allah and turned my face to You, and that you establish the prayer and give the zakah. Two brothers, supportive helpers; Allah does not accept repentance from anyone who associates partners after his Islam.'"],[16794,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'I have sworn by the number of these'—and he pointed to his fingers—'that I will not follow you nor follow what you have brought. I adjure you by Allah: what is the religion with which Allah sent you?' He said, 'He sent me with Islam.' I said, 'What is Islam?' He said, 'That you say: I have submitted myself to Allah and turned my face to You, and that you establish the prayer and give the zakah. Two brothers, supportive helpers; Allah does not accept repentance from anyone who associates partners after his Islam.'"],[16795,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'I have sworn by the number of these'—and he pointed to his fingers—'that I will not follow you nor follow what you have brought. I adjure you by Allah: what is the religion with which Allah sent you?' He said, 'He sent me with Islam.' I said, 'What is Islam?' He said, 'That you say: I have submitted myself to Allah and turned my face to You, and that you establish the prayer and give the zakah. Two brothers, supportive helpers; Allah does not accept repentance from anyone who associates partners after his Islam.'"],[16796,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the right of the wife of one of us upon him?' He said, 'That you feed her when you eat, clothe her when you clothe yourself, do not strike the face, do not revile her, and do not abandon her except in the house.'"],[16797,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, 'What is the right of the woman upon the husband?' He said, 'That he feeds her when he eats, clothes her when he clothes himself, does not strike the face, does not revile, and does not abandon except in your house.'"],[16798,"Gabriel ﷺ descended upon the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Muhammad, Mu'awiyah b. Mu'awiyah al-Muzani has died. Would you like to pray over him?' He said, 'Yes.' Then he struck with his wings, and no tree or hill remained but that it lowered itself, and his bier was raised for him until he saw it, and he prayed over him. Behind him were two rows of angels, in each row seventy thousand. The Prophet ﷺ said to Gabriel, 'O Gabriel, what made him reach this station with Allah?' He said, 'His love for \"Say: He is Allah, the One,\" and his recitation of it coming and going, standing and sitting, and in every state.'"],[16799,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was marching to Tabuk when Gabriel ﷺ came to him and said, 'O Muhammad, would you like to attend the funeral of Mu'awiyah b. Mu'awiyah al-Muzani?' He said, 'Yes.' Gabriel made a gesture with his hand like this, and the mountains and hills parted for him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came walking, and with him was Gabriel ﷺ , and with Gabriel were seventy thousand angels, and he prayed over Mu'awiyah b. Mu'awiyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Gabriel ﷺ , 'By what did Mu'awiyah attain this?' He said, 'By his frequent recitation of \"Say: He is Allah, the One.\" He used to recite it standing, sitting, lying down, and walking. This is what brought him to what he attained.'"],[16800,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is better for one of you to postpone his family and wealth than to miss the time of Asr prayer.\""],[16801,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'People wake up in a barren state, then Allah brings them provision from Himself, and they wake up associating partners, saying, \"We were given rain by such-and-such a star.\"'"],[16802,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'If there is healing in anything, it is a drink of honey, a cupping incision, or a branding with fire, but I do not like to be branded.'"],[16803,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, 'A morning or an evening in the path of Allah is better than the world and what it contains.'"],[16804,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'A morning in the path of Allah or an evening is better than the world and what it contains.'"],[16805,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'A morning in the path of Allah or an evening is better than the world and what it contains.'"],[16806,"I prayed Maghrib with the Prophet ﷺ, and he forgot and said the salam after two rak'ahs, then left. A man said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, you forgot and said the salam after two rak'ahs.\" He ordered Bilal to make the iqamah for prayer, then he completed that rak'ah. The people asked about the man who said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you forgot.\" It was said, \"Do you know him?\" I said, \"No, unless I see him.\" He passed by me, and I said, \"He is this one.\" They said, \"This is Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah.\""],[16807,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and recited to him the saying of Suwayd b. 'Amir al-Mustaliqi."],[16808,"I was present with the Prophet ﷺ at Hunayn. He said, \"What is your name?\" I said, \"Ghurab.\" He said, \"You are Muslim.\""],[16809,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When you pray the morning prayer, say before speaking to anyone: 'O Allah, protect me from the Fire' seven times. For if you die that day, protection from the Fire will be written for you. And when you pray Maghrib, say before speaking to anyone the like of that; for if you die that night, protection from the Fire will be written for you.\""],[16810,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on a military expedition. When we descended upon the people, I advanced ahead of my companions on my horse. The women and children came out to meet us, crying out. I said to them, \"Do you want to secure yourselves?\" They said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"Say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\" They said it. Then my companions came and blamed me, saying, \"We were about to get the spoils, and you prevented us.\" Then we returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"Do you know what he did? Allah has written for him such-and-such reward for every person.\" Then he brought me near him and said, \"When you pray the morning prayer, say before speaking to anyone: 'O Allah, protect me from the Fire' seven times. For if you die that day, Allah will write for you protection from the Fire. And when you pray Maghrib, say before speaking to anyone: 'O Allah, protect me from the Fire' seven times. For if you die that night, Allah will write for you protection from the Fire.\""],[16811,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote for him a document of instruction to those after him whom Allah would put in authority, and sealed it."],[16812,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepting the pledge of women in the year of the conquest on al-Safa. A woman whose hand seemed like a man's hand came forward, and he refused to accept her pledge until she went and changed her hand with yellow dye. And a man came to him with a ring of iron on his hand, and he said, \"Allah has not purified a hand that has a ring of iron on it.\""],[16813,"He used to enter Madinah and take care of his business in the market, then return to his family. When he put down his cloak, he remembered that he had not prayed in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"By Allah, I have not prayed in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for he told us: 'Whoever of you goes down to this town should not return to his family until he prays two rak'ahs in this mosque, then returns to his family.'\""],[16814,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed him over the captives of Qurayzah. He would look at the private part of a boy; if he saw that pubic hair had grown, his neck was struck; if it had not grown, he put him among the spoils of the Muslims."],[16815,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinate, then perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks."],[16816,"A green jar containing camphor was given as a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he divided it among the Muhajirun and the Ansar. He said, \"O Umm Sulaym, prepare nabidh for us in it.\""],[16817,"I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in what he instructed al-'Ala' when he dispatched him to al-Bahrayn. He said, \"It is not permissible for anyone to be ignorant of the obligatory duties and the sunnahs, and what is beyond that is permissible for him.\" And he wrote to al-'Ala': \"Treat the Magians according to the sunnah of the People of the Book.\""],[16818,"I heard Ibn Mukhallad say: “I was born when the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Madinah, and he died when I was ten years old.”"],[16819,"\"The Prophet ﷺ came when I was four years old, and he passed away when I was fourteen. The hadith of Abdur Rahman ibn Mahdi is with me, and Allah knows best.\""],[16820,"In the year sixty-two, Maslamah b. Makhlad died."],[16821,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Strip women of clothing, and they will keep to the curtained litters.”"],[16822,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The emigrants will precede the people to Paradise by forty autumns, enjoying themselves therein while the people are held back for the reckoning. Then the second group will be [preceded by] a hundred autumns.”"],[16823,"The Prophet ﷺ said concerning Mu'awiyah: “O Allah, give him authority in the lands and protect him from the evil of the punishment.”"],[16824,"The Prophet ﷺ said concerning Mu'awiyah: “O Allah, teach him the Book and arithmetic, and give him authority in the lands.”"],[16825,"“I have not come to you as a visitor, but I have come to you with a need. Do you remember the day when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Whoever learns of a fault of his brother and conceals it, Allah will conceal his fault on the Day of Resurrection’?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “It is for this that I have come.”"],[16826,"Mu'awiyah said: “No Qurayshi woman gave birth to a Qurayshi man better for her in her religion than Muhammad ﷺ, and no Qurayshi woman gave birth to a Qurayshi man better for her in her worldly life than me.” Ma'n b. Yazid al-Sulami said: “No Qurayshi woman gave birth to a Qurayshi man better for her in her religion than Muhammad ﷺ, and no Qurayshi woman gave birth to a Qurayshi man worse for her in her worldly life than you.” He said: “And why?” He said: “Because you have accustomed them to a practice, and it is as if I see them seeking it from someone other than you, and you will bring them cast down in the roads.” He said: “Woe to you! By Allah, I have been concealing it from myself since such and such a time.”"],[16827,"A Bedouin came and took hold of the halter of the Prophet's ﷺ she-camel and said: “O Prophet of Allah, guide me to a deed that will bring me near to Paradise and distance me from the Fire.” He said: “You have been brief in your question, but you have asked broadly. Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, perform the five prayers, fast Ramadan, and whatever you would dislike people to do to you, dislike it for them.”"],[16828,"I gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I, my father, and my grandfather. He proposed marriage on my behalf and gave me in marriage. I brought a dispute to him and he ruled in my favor. My father came with two dinars intending to give them in charity. He placed them with a man, and I took them and brought them to him. He said: “By Allah, I did not intend you.” I brought the dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “You have what you intended, O Yazid, and you, O Ma'n, have what you took.”"],[16829,"“I brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ruled in my favor. He proposed marriage on my behalf and gave me in marriage, and I and my grandfather gave allegiance to him.”"],[16830,"“I gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I and my grandfather. I brought a dispute to him and he ruled in my favor, and he proposed marriage on my behalf and gave me in marriage.” Then Ma'n said: “Booty is not lawful until it is distributed, and none of it is accepted until it is distributed to the people.”"],[16831,"We were in the land of the Romans, and a man from the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ from Banu Sulaym, called Ma'n b. Yazid al-Sulami, was appointed as our commander. He said: I acquired a red jar containing dinars, so I brought it to him. He took a fifth of it and said: 'Were it not that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"There is no extra share (nafal) except from the fifth,\" I would have given it to you.' He said: Then he offered me from his own share, but I said: 'I have no need of it.'"],[16832,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Gather in your mosques, and when a group gathers, let them inform me.' We were the first of the people to gather, so we came to him and informed him. He came walking with us until he sat with us. A speaker among us spoke and said: 'Praise be to God, besides whose praise there is no stopping point, and beyond whom there is no passage,' or something like this. The Messenger of God ﷺ became angry and stood up. We blamed one another and said: 'God favored us that he came to us first of the people, and he did such and such.' We came to him and found him in the mosque of Banu so-and-so. We spoke to him, and he came back with us until he sat in his previous place, or near it. Then he said: 'Indeed, praise be to God. Whatever He wills, He places before Him, and whatever He wills, He places behind Him. Indeed, some eloquence is magic.' Then he turned to us, spoke to us, commanded us, and taught us."],[16833,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The son of Maryam will kill the Dajjal at the gate of Ludd.'"],[16834,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The son of Maryam will kill the Dajjal at the gate of Ludd, or beside Ludd.'"],[16835,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, and he mentioned the Dajjal, then said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, the son of Maryam will certainly kill him at the gate of Ludd.'"],[16836,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: 'The son of Maryam will kill the Masih at the gate of Ludd.'"],[16837,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The son of Maryam will kill the Dajjal at the gate of Ludd.'"],[16838,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The son of Maryam will kill the Masih at the gate of Ludd.'"],[16839,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: 'The son of Maryam will kill the Masih at the gate of Ludd.'"],[16840,"From his uncle Mujammi' b. Jariyah, who said: We returned with the Messenger of God ﷺ from Madinah until, when the Messenger of God ﷺ reached Kura' al-Ghamim, the people began to spread the news toward the Messenger of God ﷺ. Some of the people said to others: 'What is with the people?' He said: 'It was revealed to the Messenger of God ﷺ.' So we were stirred until we found the Messenger of God ﷺ standing at Kura' al-Ghamim. When the people gathered, he recited to them: 'Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory.' Some of the people said: 'O Messenger of God, is it a victory?' He said: 'Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, it is the victory.' Then it was divided among the people of al-Hudaybiyyah into eighteen shares. The army was one thousand five hundred, including three hundred horsemen, and the horseman received two shares. The wording is that of the hadith of Ibn al-Tabba'."],[16841,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out for the funeral of a man from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf until he reached the cemetery. He said: 'Peace be upon the inhabitants of the graves' three times: 'Whoever of you is among the believers and Muslims, you are our predecessors and we are your followers. May God grant us and you well-being.'"],[16842,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, 'Isa b. Yunus narrated to us, from Yahya b. Sa'id, from al-Qasim b. Muhammad, from Mujammi' and 'Abd al-Rahman b. Yazid: 'A man of theirs called Khidham married his daughter called Khansa', but she disliked it. She came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he annulled it. We used to say that she was a previously married woman (thayyib).'"],[16843,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Your brother, the Negus, has died, so pray over him.” Ibn Abi Shaybah added in his narration: “And we lined up behind him in two rows.”"],[16844,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded that a neighbor should not prevent his neighbor from fixing a wooden peg in his wall."],[16845,"He informed him that two brothers from the Banu al-Mughirah, one of them swore an oath of manumission against his companion that he would not let him place a wooden beam in his wall. They then met Mujammi‘ b. Yazid and some men from the Ansar, who said, “We bear witness that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘A neighbor shall not prevent his neighbor from placing a wooden beam in his wall.’” So he said, “O my brother, I have come to know that it has been decreed in your favor against me, so why did you set up pillars instead of against my wall?” And he set up pillars. ‘Amr said, “And I saw those pillars.”"],[16846,"Makhramah b. Nawfal, whose kunyah was Abu al-Miswar, died in the year 54, at the age of seventy. It has also been said that he was one hundred and fifteen years old. He accepted Islam on the day of the conquest and was among those whose hearts were reconciled."],[16847,"“When the Messenger of God ﷺ proclaimed Islam openly, all the people of Makkah embraced it, and that was before the prayer was made obligatory, so much so that when he would recite a verse of prostration, they would prostrate, though none of them could even prostrate due to the crowding.” Until the leaders of Quraysh arrived — al-Walid b. al-Mughirah, Abu Jahl b. Hisham, and others — for they had been in al-Ta’if at their estates. They said, “Will you abandon the religion of your forefathers?” And so they disbelieved."],[16848,"“Al-Miswar b. Makhramah died on the day the news of Yazid b. Mu‘awiyah’s death came to Ibn al-Zubayr, in the year 64. Ibn al-Zubayr prayed over him at al-Hajun. He was struck by a stone from a catapult while he was praying in the Hijr, and he lingered for five days, then died in the month of Rabi‘ al-Awwal in the year 64. He was born two years after the Hijrah, and was brought to Madinah in the latter part of Dhu al-Hijjah in the year 8, and he witnessed the year of the conquest when he was six years old. The Prophet ﷺ died when he was eight years old.” Meaning al-Miswar b. Makhramah."],[16849,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not walk about naked.”"],[16850,"Subay‘ah al-Aslamiyyah’s husband died while she was pregnant, and she did not remain except for a few nights until she gave birth. When she had completed her postnatal bleeding, she received a marriage proposal. She asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for permission to marry after she had given birth, and he permitted her, so she married."],[16851,"Subay‘ah bt. al-Harith’s husband died, and she gave birth after eight or seven [days]. The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded her to get married."],[16852,"Subay‘ah al-Aslamiyyah’s husband died while she was pregnant, and she did not remain except for a few nights until she gave birth. When she had recovered from her postnatal bleeding, she received a marriage proposal. She asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for permission to marry after she had given birth, and he permitted her, and she married."],[16853,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us; my father narrated to me, from Hisham b. ‘Urwah, from his father, from al-Miswar b. Makhramah: Subay‘ah bt. al-Harith al-Aslamiyyah’s husband died while she was pregnant, and she did not remain except for a short while until she gave birth. When she had recovered from her postnatal bleeding, she received a marriage proposal. She asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for permission to marry, and he permitted her, and she married."],[16854,"Subay‘ah gave birth a few days after her husband’s death. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked permission to marry, and he permitted her."],[16855,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Subay'ah to marry when she became pure from her post-natal bleeding. Thus said Ibn Ashkib, 'Asim b. 'Umar."],[16856,"Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah's husband died while she was pregnant. Only a few nights passed before she gave birth. She sought permission from the Prophet ﷺ when she became pure from her post-natal bleeding, and he permitted her, so she married."],[16857,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to his companions and said: \"Allah ﷻ sent me as a mercy to all people, so convey on my behalf, may Allah have mercy on you, and do not differ as the disciples differed concerning 'Isa ﷺ . He called them to the like of what I call you to. As for those whose place was near, they answered and submitted. As for those whose place was far, they disliked it, so 'Isa ibn Maryam complained of that to Allah ﷻ. Then they woke up and each man among them spoke the language of the people to whom he was sent. 'Isa ibn Maryam ﷺ said to them: 'This is a matter which Allah has firmly resolved for you, so go and do it.' The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'We, O Messenger of Allah, will convey on your behalf, so send us wherever you wish.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent 'Abd Allah b. Hudhafah to Kisra, sent Salit b. 'Amr to Hawdhah b. 'Ali, the ruler of al-Yamamah, sent al-'Ala' b. al-Hadrami to al-Mundhir b. Sawa, the ruler of Hajar, sent 'Amr b. al-'As to Jayfar and 'Abbad, the two sons of al-Julanda, kings of Oman, sent Dihyah al-Kalbi to Caesar, sent Shuja' b. Wahb al-Asadi to al-Mundhir b. al-Harith b. Abi Shimr al-Ghassani, and sent 'Amr b. Umayyah al-Damri to the Negus. They all returned before the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, except al-'Ala' b. al-Hadrami, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while he was in al-Bahrayn."],[16858,"From al-Miswar b. Makhramah and Marwan b. al-Hakam, each of them confirming the other, they said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out at the time of al-Hudaybiyyah with some ten and a few hundred of his companions, until when they were at Dhu al-Hulayfah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ garlanded the sacrificial animal and marked it, then entered ihram for 'umrah. He sent ahead of him a spy from Khuza'ah to inform him about Quraysh. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled until when he was at Ghadir al-Ashtat, near 'Usfan, his Khuza'i spy came to him and said: 'I left Ka'b b. Lu'ayy and 'Amir b. Lu'ayy, and they have gathered the Ahabish against you and gathered forces against you, and they will fight you and bar you from the Sacred House.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Advise me. Do you think I should raid the dependents of these who have helped them, and capture them? If they stay put, they stay bereaved and robbed, and if they come, it will be a neck cut off by Allah. Or do you think we should head for the House, and whoever bars us from it, we fight?' Abu Bakr said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best, O Prophet of Allah. We have only come as pilgrims, and we have not come to fight anyone, but whoever comes between us and the House, we will fight him.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Then set out in the afternoon.' So they set out, until when they were on part of the road, the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Khalid b. al-Walid is at al-Ghamim with a cavalry of Quraysh as an advance guard, so take the right.' By Allah, Khalid was not aware of them until he saw the dust of the army, so he set off galloping as a warner to Quraysh. The Prophet ﷺ traveled until when he was at the mountain pass from which they would descend upon them, his mount knelt down. The people said: 'Hal! Hal!' They said: 'Al-Qaswa' has become stubborn.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Al-Qaswa' has not become stubborn, and that is not her nature, but she was held back by the One who held back the elephant.' Then he said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, they will not ask me for any plan by which they honor the sacred things of Allah but that I will grant it to them.' Then he prodded her and she leaped up with him, and he turned away from them until he stopped at the farthest part of al-Hudaybiyyah at a small water hole. The people were only drawing water from it sparingly. It was not long before the people exhausted it. They complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of thirst. He drew an arrow from his quiver, then commanded them to place it in the water. By Allah, it kept gushing for them with enough to drink until they left it. While they were thus, Budayl b. Warqa' al-Khuza'i came to them with a group of his people from Khuza'ah, and they were the trusted advisers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among the people of Tihamah. He said: 'I left Ka'b b. Lu'ayy and 'Amir b. Lu'ayy, and they have camped at the water holes of al-Hudaybiyyah, and with them are the camels with young, and they will fight you and bar you from the House.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'We have not come to fight anyone, but we have come as pilgrims. War has worn down Quraysh and harmed them. If they wish, I will make a truce with them for a period, and they should leave the way open between me and the people. If I prevail, then if they wish to enter into what the people have entered, they may do so, and if not, they will have rested. But if they refuse, then by the One in whose hand is my soul, I will fight them for this cause of mine until my neck is severed, or Allah will surely carry out His command.' Budayl said: 'I will convey to them what you say.' He went until he came to Quraysh and said: 'We have come to you from this man, and we heard him say something. If you wish, we will present it to you.' Their foolish ones said: 'We have no need for you to tell us anything about him.' Those of sound judgment among them said: 'Give us what you heard him say.' He said: 'I heard him say such and such,' and he told them what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. 'Urwah b. Mas'ud al-Thaqafi stood up and said: 'O people, am I not the father?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Am I not the child?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Do you suspect me?' They said: 'No.' He said: 'Do you not know that I called upon the people of 'Ukaz, and when they failed me, I came to you with my family and children and those who obeyed me?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'This man has offered you a plan of right guidance, so accept it and let me go to him.' They said: 'Go to him.' He went to him and began to speak with the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said something similar to what he had said to Budayl. 'Urwah said at that: 'O Muhammad, do you think that if you exterminate your people, have you heard of anyone among the Arabs who destroyed his own family before you? And if it is the other way, by Allah, I see faces and I see a rabble of people likely to flee and abandon you.' Abu Bakr said: 'Suck the clitoris of al-Lat! Would we flee and abandon him?' He said: 'Who is this?' He said: 'Abu Bakr.' He said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, were it not for a favor you owe me that I have not repaid, I would answer you.' He kept speaking with the Prophet ﷺ, and whenever he spoke to him, he took hold of his beard. Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah was standing at the head of the Prophet ﷺ with a helmet, and with him was a sword. Whenever 'Urwah reached his hand to the beard of the Prophet ﷺ, he struck his hand with the scabbard of the sword and said: 'Take your hand away from the beard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' 'Urwah raised his head and said: 'Who is this?' He said: 'This is al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah.' He said: 'O treacherous one, am I not striving to rectify your treachery?' Al-Mughirah had accompanied a people in the Jahiliyyah, killed them, and taken their wealth, then came and embraced Islam. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'As for Islam, I accept it, but as for the wealth, I have nothing to do with it.' Then 'Urwah began to gaze at the companions of the Prophet ﷺ with his eyes. He said: 'By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not spit but that it fell into the hand of one of them and he rubbed it on his face and skin, and when he commanded them, they hastened to his command, and when he performed ablution, they almost fought over his ablution water, and when he spoke, they lowered their voices in his presence, and they did not stare at him out of reverence for him.' 'Urwah returned to his companions and said: 'O people, by Allah, I have gone as an envoy to kings, and I have gone as an envoy to Caesar, Kisra, and the Negus. By Allah, I have never seen a king whose companions honor him as the companions of Muhammad honor Muhammad. By Allah, he did not spit but that it fell into the palm of one of them and he rubbed it on his face and skin, and when he commanded them, they hastened to his command, and when he performed ablution, they almost fought over his ablution water, and when they spoke, they lowered their voices in his presence, and they did not stare at him out of reverence for him. He has offered you a plan of right guidance, so accept it.' A man from Banu Kinanah said: 'Let me go to him.' They said: 'Go to him.' When he appeared before the Prophet ﷺ and his companions, the Prophet ﷺ said: 'This is so-and-so, and he is from a people who honor sacrificial camels, so send them out to him.' They were sent out to him, and the people met him reciting the talbiyah. When he saw that, he said: 'Glory be to Allah, it is not right for these people to be barred from the House.' When he returned to his companions, he said: 'I saw the sacrificial camels garlanded and marked, and I do not think they should be barred from the House.' A man among them called Mikraz b. Hafs said: 'Let me go to him.' They said: 'Go to him.' When he appeared before them, the Prophet ﷺ said: 'This is Mikraz b. Hafs, and he is a wicked man.' He began to speak with the Prophet ﷺ. While he was speaking with him, Suhayl b. 'Amr came and said: 'Come, let us write a treaty between us and you.' He called for the scribe. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Write: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.' Suhayl said: 'As for \"the Most Gracious,\" by Allah, I do not know what it is, but write: In Your name, O Allah, as you used to write.' The Muslims said: 'By Allah, we will not write it except with: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Write: In Your name, O Allah.' Then he said: 'This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, has agreed upon.' Suhayl said: 'By Allah, if we knew that you were the Messenger of Allah, we would not have barred you from the House nor fought you. But write: Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'By Allah, I am the Messenger of Allah, even if you deny me. Write: Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'On condition that you leave the way open between us and the House so that we may circumambulate it.' Suhayl said: 'By Allah, the Arabs will never say that we were taken by force, but you may have it next year.' So he wrote. Suhayl said: 'And on condition that no man from us comes to you, even if he follows your religion, but that you return him to us.' The Muslims said: 'Glory be to Allah, how can he be returned to the polytheists when he has come as a Muslim?' While they were thus, Abu Jandal b. Suhayl b. 'Amr came dragging his chains, having escaped from the lower part of Makkah, until he threw himself among the Muslims. Suhayl said: 'This, O Muhammad, is the first one with whom I make you agree that you return him to me.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'We have not yet concluded the treaty.' He said: 'By Allah, then I will never make peace with you for anything.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Then grant him to me.' He said: 'I will not grant him to you.' He said: 'Yes, then do it.' He said: 'I will not do it.' Mikraz said: 'Yes, we grant him to you.' Abu Jandal said: 'O assembly of Muslims, shall I be returned to the polytheists when I have come as a Muslim? Do you not see what I have suffered?' He had been severely tortured for the sake of Allah. 'Umar b. al-Khattab said: 'By Allah, I never doubted since I embraced Islam except on that day. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Are you not truly the Prophet of Allah?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Are we not on the truth and our enemy on falsehood?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Then why do we accept humiliation in our religion?' He said: 'I am the Messenger of Allah, and I do not disobey Him, and He will help me.' I said: 'Did you not tell us that we would come to the House and circumambulate it?' He said: 'Yes, but did I tell you that you would come to it this year?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'You will come to it and circumambulate it.' Then I went to Abu Bakr and said: 'O Abu Bakr, is this not truly the Prophet of Allah?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Are we not on the truth and our enemy on falsehood?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Then why do we accept humiliation in our religion?' He said: 'O man, he is the Messenger of Allah, and he does not disobey his Lord, and He will help him. So hold fast to his stirrup until you die. By Allah, he is upon the truth.' I said: 'Did he not tell us that we would come to the House and circumambulate it?' He said: 'Yes, but did he tell you that you would come to it this year?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'You will come to it and circumambulate it.' When he finished the treaty, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: 'Arise and slaughter, then shave.' By Allah, not one of them stood up until he said it three times. When none of them stood up, he got up and entered upon Umm Salamah and mentioned to her what he had encountered from the people. Umm Salamah said: 'O Prophet of Allah, do you want that? Go out, then do not speak a word to any of them until you slaughter your sacrificial camel and call your barber to shave you.' He got up and went out, and did not speak to anyone among them until he did that: he slaughtered his sacrificial camel and called his barber, who shaved him. When they saw that, they arose and slaughtered, and some of them began to shave others, until some of them almost killed others out of grief. Then believing women came, and Allah ﷻ revealed: {O you who believe, when believing women come to you as emigrants} until He reached {the ties of the disbelieving women}. That day 'Umar divorced two wives he had in polytheism. One of them was married by Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan and the other by Safwan b. Umayyah. Then the Prophet ﷺ returned to Madinah. Abu Basir, a man from Quraysh, came, and he was a Muslim. They sent two men after him and said: 'The pact you made with us.' So he handed him over to the two men. They went out until when they reached Dhu al-Hulayfah with him, they dismounted to eat from some dates of theirs. Abu Basir said to one of the two men: 'By Allah, I think this sword of yours, O so-and-so, is good.' The other drew it and said: 'Yes, by Allah, it is good. I have tried it and tried it again.' Abu Basir said: 'Show me, let me look at it.' He handed it to him, and he struck him with it until he died. The other fled until he came to Madinah and entered the mosque running. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him, he said: 'This man has seen something terrifying.' When he reached the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'By Allah, my companion has been killed, and I will be killed.' Abu Basir came and said: 'O Prophet of Allah, by Allah, Allah has fulfilled your protection. You returned me to them, then Allah saved me from them.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Woe to his mother, a kindler of war, if only he had someone.' When he heard that, he knew that he would return him to them, so he went out until he reached the coast. Abu Jandal b. Suhayl escaped from them and joined Abu Basir. No man from Quraysh who had embraced Islam left but that he joined Abu Basir, until a band of them gathered. By Allah, they did not hear of any caravan of Quraysh headed to Syria but that they intercepted it, killed them, and took their wealth. Quraysh sent to the Prophet ﷺ, adjuring him by Allah and kinship, to send to them, and whoever came to him would be safe. The Prophet ﷺ sent for them, and Allah ﷻ revealed: {And it is He who restrained their hands from you and your hands from them in the interior of Makkah} until He reached {the arrogance of the Jahiliyyah}. Quraysh's arrogance was that they did not acknowledge that he was the Prophet of Allah, did not acknowledge 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,' and came between him and the House."],[16859,"He heard al-Miswar b. Makhramah and Marwan b. al-Hakam relating from the news of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the expedition of al-Hudaybiyyah. Among what 'Urwah reported to me from them was that they said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote the treaty with Suhayl b. 'Amr on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah for the agreed period, among what Suhayl b. 'Amr stipulated upon him was that he said: 'No one from us shall come to you, even if he follows your religion, but that you return him to us and leave the way between us and him.' Suhayl refused to make peace with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except on that condition, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote the treaty with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned Abu Jandal b. Suhayl that day to his father Suhayl b. 'Amr. No man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ but that he returned him during that period, even if he was a Muslim. Then believing women came as emigrants. Umm Kulthum bt. 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt left to join the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while she was pregnant. Her family came asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to return her to them, until Allah ﷻ revealed concerning the believing women what He revealed."],[16860,"The affair of al-Hudaybiyyah from its beginning to its end.\""],[16861,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he divided Khaybar, divided it into eighty shares. The men were one thousand eight hundred, and the horses were two hundred. For the horses, four hundred shares, each share for eighteen hundred shares, and for every hundred shares a commander. 'Umar b. al-Khattab was a commander, 'Ali a commander, Talhah a commander, al-Zubayr a commander, and 'Asim b. 'Adi a commander. The share of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with 'Asim b. 'Adi."],[16862,"He informed him that 'Ali b. Abi Talib proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl while he was married to Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When Fatimah heard of that, she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said to him: 'Your people are saying that you do not become angry for your daughters, and here is 'Ali marrying the daughter of Abu Jahl.' Al-Miswar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the pulpit, and I heard him declare the shahadah, then he said: 'To proceed: I married Abu al-'As b. al-Rabi', and he told me and was truthful to me. Fatimah, the daughter of Muhammad, is a part of me, and I dislike that you should tempt her. By Allah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the daughter of the enemy of Allah will never be joined with one man.' So 'Ali abandoned the proposal."],[16863,"He said to him: 'Do you have any need you would command me with?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'Will you give me the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? I fear that the people may overpower you for it. By Allah, if you give it to me, no one will ever reach it until my soul reaches here. 'Ali b. Abi Talib proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl in addition to Fatimah. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressing the people about that on this pulpit of his, and I was then a youth. He said: 'Fatimah is from me, and I fear that she will be tempted in her religion.' Then he mentioned the in-law relationship of Banu 'Abd Shams and praised Abu al-'As in his marriage alliance with him. He said: 'He was truthful to me and promised me and fulfilled it. I do not forbid what is lawful nor make lawful what is forbidden, but by Allah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the daughter of the enemy of Allah will never be joined.'"],[16864,"Ali b. Abi Talib proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl and set a date for the marriage. Fatimah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Your people are saying that you do not become angry for your daughters, and 'Ali has proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood, praised Allah, and extolled Him, then said: 'Fatimah is but a part of me, and I dislike that she be tempted.' He mentioned Abu al-'As b. al-Rabi' and praised him well, and said: 'He will never join the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the daughter of the enemy of Allah.'"],[16865,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'None of you should pray while he finds any impurity,' meaning feces or urine."],[16866,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A child does not inherit until it cries out at birth.' Its crying out is that it screams, cries, or sneezes."],[16867,"Regarding a sale or a gift she had given: 'By Allah, 'A'ishah must stop, or I will place her under a restriction.' 'A'ishah said: 'Did he say this?' They said: 'Yes.' So 'A'ishah said: 'It is for Allah a vow upon me that I shall never speak a word to Ibn al-Zubayr ever.' Then 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr sought intercession with her when her avoidance of him grew long, and 'A'ishah said: 'By Allah, I will not accept anyone's intercession for him, nor will I break my vow that I made ever.' When that grew long for Ibn al-Zubayr, he spoke to al-Miswar b. Makhramah and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad b. 'Abd Yaghuth, who were from Zuhrah, and said: 'I adjure you both by Allah to enter me upon 'A'ishah, for it is not lawful for her to vow to sever ties with me.' So al-Miswar and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad brought Ibn al-Zubayr, wrapping him in their cloaks, until they sought permission to enter upon 'A'ishah. They said: 'Peace be upon the Prophet and the mercy of Allah. May we enter?' 'A'ishah said: 'Enter.' They said: 'All of us, O Mother of the Believers?' She said: 'Enter, all of you,' while 'A'ishah did not know that Ibn al-Zubayr was with them. When they entered, Ibn al-Zubayr rushed to the curtain, embraced 'A'ishah, and began adjuring her and weeping. Al-Miswar and 'Abd al-Rahman began adjuring 'A'ishah to speak to him and accept from him, and they said to her: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ indeed forbade what you already know of abandonment, for it is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three nights.' When they repeated the reminder and the admonition to 'A'ishah, she began to remind them and weep and say: 'I have made a vow, and the vow is serious.' They continued with her until she spoke to Ibn al-Zubayr, and she freed forty slaves for that vow of hers. Then she used to remember that vow of hers after she had freed forty slaves and weep until her tears soaked her veil."],[16868,"It is narrated from 'Awf b. al-Harith b. Tufayl, the son of 'A'ishah's maternal uncle, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that 'A'ishah told him that 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr said about a sale or a gift that 'A'ishah had given: 'By Allah, 'A'ishah must stop, or I will place her under a restriction.' She said: 'Did he say this?' They said: 'Yes.' 'A'ishah said: 'Then it is for Allah a vow that I shall never speak a word to Ibn al-Zubayr ever.' Then Ibn al-Zubayr sought intercession with her when her avoidance of him grew long, and she said: 'By Allah, I will not accept anyone's intercession for him ever, nor will I break my vow that I made ever.' When that grew long for Ibn al-Zubayr, he spoke to al-Miswar b. Makhramah and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad b. 'Abd Yaghuth, who were from Banu Zuhrah, and said: 'I adjure you both by Allah to enter me upon 'A'ishah, for it is not lawful for her to vow to sever ties with me.' So al-Miswar b. Makhramah and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad brought him, wrapping him in their cloaks, until they sought permission to enter upon 'A'ishah. They said: 'Peace be upon the Prophet and the mercy of Allah. May we enter?' 'A'ishah said: 'Enter.' They said: 'All of us, O Mother of the Believers?' She said: 'Yes, enter, all of you,' while 'A'ishah did not know that Ibn al-Zubayr was with them. When they entered, Ibn al-Zubayr entered the curtain, embraced 'A'ishah, and began adjuring her and weeping. Al-Miswar and 'Abd al-Rahman began adjuring 'A'ishah to speak to him and accept from him, and they said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade what you already know of abandonment, for it is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three nights.' When they repeated the reminder and the admonition to 'A'ishah, she began to remind them and weep and say: 'I have made a vow, and the vow is serious.' They continued with her until she spoke to Ibn al-Zubayr, then she freed forty slaves for her vow. Then she used to remember that vow of hers after she had freed forty slaves and weep until her tears soaked her veil."],[16869,"'Awf b. al-Harith b. al-Tufayl, the son of 'A'ishah's ؓ maternal uncle, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to me that 'A'ishah was told that 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr said about a sale or gifts that 'A'ishah had given: 'By Allah, 'A'ishah must stop, or I will place her under a restriction.' She said: 'Did he say this?' They said: 'Yes.' She said: 'It is for Allah a vow upon me that I shall never speak a word to Ibn al-Zubayr ever.' Then Ibn al-Zubayr sought intercession with her through people when she prolonged his abandonment, and she said: 'By Allah, I will not accept anyone's intercession for him, nor will I break my vow ever.' When that grew long for Ibn al-Zubayr, he spoke to al-Miswar b. Makhramah and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad b. 'Abd Yaghuth, who were from Banu Zuhrah, and said: 'I adjure you both by Allah to enter me upon 'A'ishah, for it is not lawful for her to vow to sever ties with me.' So al-Miswar b. Makhramah and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad b. 'Abd Yaghuth brought him, wrapping him in their cloaks, until they sought permission to enter upon 'A'ishah. They said: 'Peace be upon the Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. May we enter?' 'A'ishah said: 'Enter.' They said: 'All of us, O Mother of the Believers?' She said: 'Yes, enter, all of you,' while 'A'ishah did not realize that Ibn al-Zubayr was with them. When they entered, Ibn al-Zubayr entered the curtain, embraced 'A'ishah, and began adjuring her and weeping. Al-Miswar b. Makhramah and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad began adjuring 'A'ishah by Allah to speak to him and accept from him, and they said to her: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade abandonment as you know, and he said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three nights.\"' When they repeated the reminder and the admonition to 'A'ishah, she began to remind them and weep and say: 'I have made a vow, and the matter of a vow is serious.' They continued with her until she spoke to Ibn al-Zubayr, then she freed forty slaves for her vow. Then she used to remember that vow of hers after she had freed forty slaves and weep until her tears soaked her veil."],[16870,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us at 'Arafat. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: 'Now then, indeed the people of shirk and idols used to depart from this place when the sun was on the tops of the mountains like turbans of men on their faces, and we depart after it sets. And they used to depart from al-Mash'ar al-Haram when the sun was spread out.'"],[16871,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Beware of wrongdoing, for wrongdoing will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[16872,"Tell him to meet me at a time he mentioned. So he met him, and al-Miswar praised Allah and said: 'There is no tie, lineage, or in-law relation dearer to me than your lineage and your in-law relation, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fatimah is a branch of me. What pleases her pleases me, and what distresses her distresses me. On the Day of Resurrection, all lineages will be cut off except my lineage and my tie.\" And under you is her daughter; if I married her to you, that would distress her.' So he went away excusing him."],[16873,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'Whoever takes something from the land will be made to carry around his neck on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths.'"],[16874,"A Jew passed by me while I was behind the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ was performing ablution. His garment fell on his back, and there was the seal of prophethood on his back. The Jew said: 'Lift his garment from his back.' So I went to lift the Prophet's ﷺ garment from his back, and the Prophet ﷺ blew a handful of water in my face."],[16875,"And he said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Every tie and lineage will be severed on the Day of Resurrection except my tie and my lineage.\"'"],[16876,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in prayer, and he left out something he did not recite. A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, it was such and such.' He said: 'Why did you not remind me of it?' He said: 'I thought it had been abrogated.'"],[16877,"From 'Urwah, on the naming of those who attended al-'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Salimah: Mu'adh b. Jabal b. 'Amr b. 'A'idh b. 'Adi b. Ka'b b. Udayy b. Sa'd b. 'Adi b. Asad b. Saridah b. Tazid b. Jusham, and he attended Badr."],[16878,"From Ibn Shihab, on the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar: Mu'adh b. Jabal."],[16879,"Because he was the maternal brother of Suhayl b. Muhammad b. al-Jadd b. Qays b. Sakhr b. Khansa' b. Sinan b. 'Ubayd b. 'Adi b. Ghanm b. Ka'b b. Salama\""],[16880,"Mu'adh b. Jabal died when he was twenty-eight years old, and the one who raises his age says thirty-two years."],[16881,"Mu'adh b. Jabal died when he was twenty-eight years old, and the one who raises his age says thirty-two years."],[16882,"I heard Malik b. Anas say: Mu'adh b. Jabal died when he was twenty-eight years old, and one who speaks says thirty-two."],[16883,"I heard Malik b. Anas say: Mu'adh b. Jabal died when he was twenty-eight years old, and one who speaks says thirty-two."],[16884,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Mu'adh b. Jabal is ahead of the scholars by a bowshot.\""],[16885,"\"Mu'adh b. Jabal passed away when he was thirty-three or thirty-four years old.\""],[16886,"\"Mu'adh b. Jabal died in the plague of 'Amwas in the year seventeen or eighteen.\""],[16887,"\"So he asked the Messenger of God ﷺ to intercede with his creditors, and he did.\" But they did not reduce anything for him. Had anyone been let off for another's intercession, Mu'adh would have been let off for the Messenger of God's ﷺ intercession. \"Then the Prophet ﷺ summoned him, and he did not cease until he sold his property and divided it among his creditors.\" Mu'adh stood up with no property. \"Then when the Prophet ﷺ performed the Hajj, he sent him to Yemen to set him right.\" He said: Mu'adh was the first to do business with this wealth, and he arrived before Abu Bakr from Yemen when the Messenger of God ﷺ had already passed away."],[16888,"That the affair of this community in its latter time will return to being brothers openly and enemies in secret. And we seek refuge with God from our letter descending other than the place it descended from our hearts, for we wrote it only as sincere counsel to you. Peace be upon you. Then 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ wrote back to them: From 'Umar b. al-Khattab to Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah and Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ. Peace be upon you both. Now then, your letter reached me in which you mention that you had admonished me and that my own affairs are important to me. I have become the one entrusted with the affair of this community, its red and its black; the noble and the lowly, the enemy and the friend sit before me, and for everyone there is a share of justice. You wrote: Look how you are in that situation, O 'Umar. Indeed, there is no power and no strength for them in that except through God. You wrote warning me of what the nations before us were warned of, and it is ancient. Indeed, the alternation of night and day, with the death terms of people, brings near every distant thing and brings every new thing and brings every promised thing until people come to their abodes of Paradise or the Fire. You wrote warning me that the affair of this community will return in its latter time to being brothers openly and enemies in secret. But you are not those people, and this is not the time of that; that is a time when desire and fear appear, when some people's desire for one another will be for the good of their worldly affairs. You wrote seeking refuge with God from your letter descending other than the place it descended from your hearts, and that you wrote it as sincere counsel to me. You have spoken truly, so do not stop writing to me, for I cannot do without you. Peace be upon you both."],[16889,"He said: The Commander of the Faithful says to you: Put this toward some of your needs. So he said: May God maintain him and have mercy on him. Then he said: Come, O slave girl, take these seven to so-and-so and these five to so-and-so, until he had distributed it all. The boy returned and told him, and he found that he had prepared the like of it to Mu'adh b. Jabal. He said: \"Take this to Mu'adh b. Jabal and leave it in the house until you see what he does.\" So he took it to him, and he said: The Commander of the Faithful says to you: Put this toward some of your needs. He said: May God have mercy on him and maintain him. Come, O slave girl, go to the house of so-and-so with such-and-such, and go to the house of so-and-so with such-and-such. Then Mu'adh's wife looked in and said: By God, we are poor, so give us. And nothing remained in the cloth except two dinars, so he tossed them to her. The boy returned to 'Umar and told him, and he was pleased and said: \"They are brothers, one from another.\""],[16890,"Do you know what the qanit is? They said no. He said: \"The one obedient to God.\""],[16891,"Mu'adh, when he would perform the night prayer, would say: \"O Allah, eyes have slept and stars have set, and You are the Ever-Living, the Sustainer. O Allah, my pursuit of Paradise is slow and my fleeing from the Fire is weak. O Allah, appoint for me guidance with You that You will return to me on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, You do not break the promise.\""],[16892,"I enjoin upon you two matters: if you preserve them, you will be preserved. You are not free from need of your share of this world, and you are more in need of your share of the Hereafter. So prefer your share of the Hereafter over your share of this world until it becomes firmly established for you, so that it departs with you wherever you depart."],[16893,"\"You have not ceased to annoy me since today.\" She said: \"It was certainly distressing to me to annoy you.\" He said: \"An angel of stern rebuke has not ceased that whenever you said 'Woe to such-and-such,' he said: 'Are you indeed like that?' and I say: 'No.'\""],[16894,"\"I saw Mu'adh b. Jabal killing lice and fleas in the mosque.\""],[16895,"From one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, from Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Two men do not love each other for the sake of Allah except that Allah sets down for them a seat upon which they are made to sit until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, finishes the reckoning.\" Mu'adh b. Jabal said: \"Abu Ubaydah has spoken the truth.\""],[16896,"A hadith I heard from the occupant of this grave—meaning the Prophet ﷺ: \"Indeed, the least amount of ostentation is shirk (polytheism), and the most beloved of servants to Allah are the pious, the hidden ones, who when they are absent are not missed, and when they are present are not recognized. Those are the leaders of guidance and the lamps of knowledge.\""],[16897,"'Abd Allah said to him: \"What is the matter with you, O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, that you are talking to yourself?\" He said: \"What is with me? The enemy of Allah wants to divert me from what I heard from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said to me: 'You will now struggle for the rest of your life in your house, not going out to the gathering. For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever strives in the path of Allah has a guarantee upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Whoever visits a sick person has a guarantee upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Whoever goes to the mosque in the morning or evening has a guarantee upon Allah. Whoever sits in his house and does not backbite anyone with evil has a guarantee upon Allah.' So the enemy of Allah wants to make me leave my house for the gathering.\""],[16898,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Five things: whoever does one of them has a guarantee upon Allah—whoever visits a sick person, or goes out with a funeral procession, or goes out as a warrior, or enters upon his leader intending to honor and respect him, or sits in his house so that people are safe from him and he is safe from people.\""],[16899,"Mu'adh b. Jabal informed him, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with a changed complexion and said: \"I am Muhammad. I have been given the openings of speech and its closings, so obey me as long as I am among you. And when I am taken away, then upon you is the Book of Allah: make lawful its lawful and forbid its forbidden. Death has come to you; it has come to you with rest and relief. It is a decree from Allah that has preceded. Trials have come to you like patches of dark night. Whenever messengers pass, messengers come. Prophethood has been abrogated and has become kingship. May Allah have mercy on one who takes it by its right and departs from it as he entered it. Hold back, O Mu'adh, and count.\" He said: When I reached five, he said: \"Yazid, may Allah not bless Yazid.\" Then his eyes shed tears and he said: \"Husayn has been announced dead to me, and I was brought his soil and informed of his killer. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no one is killed among a people who do not defend him except that Allah causes division between their chests and hearts, sets their worst ones over them, and clothes them in factions.\" Then he said: \"Alas for the offspring of the family of Muhammad from a successor appointed, living in luxury, who will kill my successor and the successor of the successor. Hold back, O Mu'adh.\" When I reached ten, he said: \"Al-Walid is the name of a Pharaoh, a destroyer of the laws of Islam. Before him is a man from his household. Allah will surely draw his sword, and there will be no sheath for it. The people will differ and will be like this\"—and he interlaced his fingers—then he said: \"After one hundred and twenty: swift death and rapid killing. In that is their destruction. Then a man from the descendants of al-Abbas will rule over them.\""],[16900,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when they mentioned a man who was with him, and they said: \"How incapable he is!\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You have backbitten your brother.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we said what is in him.\" He said: \"If you said what is not in him, then you would have slandered him.\""],[16901,"Mu'adh b. Jabal wanted to travel, so he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, advise me.\" He said: \"Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, give me more.\" He said: \"And when you do wrong, then do good.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, give me more.\" He said: \"Be upright and make your character good.\""],[16902,"That you should rely upon me. I have narrated to you a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"Whoever dies with 'there is no god but Allah' in his heart, certain of it, enters Paradise.\""],[16903,"While he was ill, he said: Uncover for me the curtain of the dome; I shall relate to you a hadith that, were it not for the state I am in, I would not relate to you. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever dies affirming 'There is no god but God' with certainty from his soul enters Paradise.\""],[16904,"When Mu'adh b. Jabal was near death, he said: Raise from me the curtains of the dome, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever dies worshipping God, associating nothing with Him, enters Paradise.\""],[16905,"Mu'adh said: Uncover for me the curtain of the dome, for were it not for what has come upon me from God I would not inform you of what I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: \"Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger enters Paradise.\""],[16906,"Someone who witnessed Mu'adh b. Jabal when death came to him informed us, saying: Raise from me the curtain of the dome so that I may relate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. Nothing prevented me from relating it to you except that you might rely upon it. I heard him say: \"Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God sincerely from his heart enters Paradise and the Fire will not touch him.\""],[16907,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever gives a man security and then kills him, the Fire is guaranteed for him, even if the slain man was a disbeliever.\""],[16908,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with two men of the Ash'aris, one on my right and the other on my left, while the Messenger of God ﷺ was cleaning his teeth. Both of them asked for appointment to office. He said: \"O Abu Musa—or, O 'Abd Allah—\" I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, they did not reveal to me what was in their minds, and I was not aware that they were seeking office. It was as if I could see his tooth-stick beneath his lip. He said to me: \"We do not appoint over our work anyone who desires it. But go, O Abu Musa—or, O 'Abd Allah b. Qays—\" So he sent him to Yemen, then followed him with Mu'adh b. Jabal. When he arrived, he placed a cushion for him and said: \"Dismount.\" There was a man bound in chains. He said: \"What is this?\" He said: This man was a Jew, then he embraced Islam, then he returned to his religion—the religion of evil. He said: \"I will not sit until he is killed, by the decree of God and His Messenger,\" three times. So he ordered it and he was killed."],[16909,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him and Mu'adh b. Jabal to Yemen and ordered them to teach the people the Qur'an. Mu'adh came to Abu Musa to visit him, and there was a man bound with iron at his place. He said: O my brother, were we sent to torment people, or were we sent to teach them and command them with what benefits them? He said to him: He embraced Islam and then disbelieved. He said: By the One who sent Muhammad with the truth, I will not leave until I burn him with fire. Abu Musa said: We still have a remnant of him among us. Mu'adh said: By God, I will never leave. So firewood was brought, the fire was kindled in it, and he threw him in."],[16910,"A man embraced Islam and then became a Jew. Mu'adh came to him while he was with Abu Musa and said to him: What is this? He said: He embraced Islam and then became a Jew. He said: \"I will not sit until you kill him, by the decree of God and His Messenger.\""],[16911,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said while we were sitting on a carpet: \"There will be a trial.\" They said: How should we act? He said: He returned his hand to the carpet, grasped it, and said: \"They will do like this.\" He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned to them: \"There will be a trial,\" but many of the people did not hear him. Mu'adh b. Jabal said: Do you not hear what the Messenger of God ﷺ is saying? They said: What did he say? He said: He says: \"There will be a trial.\" They said: What then should we do, O Messenger of God, and how should we act? He said: \"Return to your former affair.\""],[16912,"We came to the Messenger of Allah while he was praying. When he finished his prayer, I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I saw you doing something that I have not seen you do in a prayer.\" He said, \"It was a voluntary prayer of desire and caution. I asked Allah three times in it, so He gave me two and prevented me from one. I asked Him not to subject my Ummah to an enemy other than themselves, who would overpower them, so He gave it to me. And I asked Him not to send upon them a calamity that would destroy them, so He gave it to me. And I asked Him not to make their misfortune between themselves, so He turned it away from me.\""],[16913,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"No servant dies bearing witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God, tracing that back to a certain heart, except that he enters Paradise.\" It was said to him: Did you hear this from Mu'adh? He said: I heard this from Mu'adh relating it from the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[16914,"I entered the congregational mosque in Basra and sat with an old man with white head and beard. He said: Mu'adh b. Jabal narrated to me from the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said: \"No soul dies bearing witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God, tracing that back to a believing heart, except that God forgives him.\" I said: Did you hear this from Mu'adh b. Jabal? It was as if the people rebuked him. He said: Do not rebuke him or reproach him; leave him. I heard that from Mu'adh b. Jabal tracing it from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: I said to the people: Who is this? They said: 'Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah."],[16915,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out while Mu'adh b. Jabal was at the door. When he saw him, he said: \"O Mu'adh.\" He said: At your service, O Messenger of God. He said: \"Whoever dies associating nothing with God enters Paradise.\" Mu'adh said: O Messenger of God, shall I not inform the people? He said: \"Leave them; let them vie with one another in deeds, for I fear they will rely upon it.\""],[16916,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever dies not associating anything with God will enter Paradise.” Muadh said: “O Messenger of God, shall I not give the people this glad tidings?” He said: “I fear they will rely on it.”"],[16917,"I heard him say that Muadh was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ when he told him: “Give the people the glad tidings that whoever dies not associating anything with God will enter Paradise.”"],[16918,"On the authority of Attab, the freedman of Hurmuz, a man from the people of Wasit, on the authority of Anas b. Malik, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ with this hand of mine to hear and obey as much as I could, and I heard him narrate that Muadh b. Jabal was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ when the Messenger of God ﷺ told him: “Give the people the glad tidings that whoever dies not associating anything with God will enter Paradise.” Muadh said: “O Messenger of God, shall I not give the people this glad tidings?” He said: “Indeed I fear they will rely on it.”"],[16919,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God sincerely from his heart will enter Paradise.”"],[16920,"Abdullah b. Maslamah al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us; Salamah b. Wardan narrated to us, on the authority of Anas b. Malik, that he heard him say: Muadh b. Jabal came to me and I said: “Where have you come from, O Muadh?” He said: “I have come from the Prophet of God ﷺ.” I said: “What did he say to you?” He said: “Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God sincerely will enter Paradise.” I said: “Should I go and ask the Prophet ﷺ?” He said: “Go.” So I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Prophet of God, Muadh b. Jabal told me that you said: ‘Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God sincerely will enter Paradise.’” He said: “Muadh spoke the truth, Muadh spoke the truth, Muadh spoke the truth.”"],[16921,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, with nothing between me and him but the rear frame of the saddle, when he said to me: “O Muadh.” I said: “At your service, O Messenger of God, and at your command.” He said: “Do you know what God’s right upon His servants is?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Indeed God’s right upon His servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.” Then he rode on for a while and said: “O Muadh b. Jabal.” I said: “At your service and at your command.” He said: “Do you know what the servants’ right upon God is if they do that?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Indeed the servants’ right upon God is that He not punish them.”"],[16922,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O Muadh.” I said: “At your service.” He said: “Give the people the glad tidings that whoever says, ‘There is no god but God,’ will enter Paradise.”"],[16923,"I was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ when he said: “O Muadh b. Jabal, do you know what God’s right upon His servants is?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “That they associate nothing with Him.” Then he said: “Do you know what their right upon Him is if they do that?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “That He not punish them.”"],[16924,"You heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ seated me behind him and said: “Do you know what God’s right upon His servants is?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “His right upon them is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.” Then he said: “Do you know, if they do that, what their right upon Him is? Their right upon Him is that He not punish them.”"],[16925,"Relate to us some of the rare hadiths of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: I was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ on a donkey when he said: “O Muadh.” I said: “At your service, O Messenger of God.” He said: “Do you know what God’s right upon His servants is?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Indeed, the right upon them is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.” Then he said: “Do you know what the servants’ right upon God is if they do that?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Indeed, their right upon God, if they do that, is that He not punish them.”"],[16926,"Muadh b. Jabal seized the devil during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. I came to him and said: “I have heard that you seized the devil during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” He said: “Yes. The Messenger of God ﷺ handed over to me the dates of the zakat, and I put them in a room of mine. I would find a shortfall in them every day, so I complained about that to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He told me: ‘It is the work of the devil, so lie in wait for him.’ I lay in wait for him one night. When a portion of the night had passed, he came in the form of an elephant. When he reached the door, he slipped in through the crack of the door in a form other than his own. He approached the dates and began gobbling them. I tightened my clothes around me, then I grabbed him around the middle, and I said: ‘I bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. O enemy of God, you have gotten at the dates of the zakat and taken them, while they are more entitled to them than you. I will certainly bring you before the Messenger of God ﷺ so that he will expose you.’ He made a pact with me that he would not return. In the morning I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said to me: ‘What happened to your captive?’ I said: ‘He made a pact with me that he would not return.’ He said: ‘He will return, so lie in wait for him.’ So I lay in wait for him the second night. He did the same as before, and I did the same as before, and he made a pact with me that he would not return, so I let him go. Then I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ to inform him, and there was his caller calling out: ‘Where is Muadh?’ He said to me: ‘O Muadh, what happened to your captive?’ I told him, and he said: ‘He will return, so lie in wait for him.’ So I lay in wait for him the third night. He did the same as before, and I did the same to him, and I said: ‘O enemy of God, you made a pact with me twice, and this is the third time. I will certainly bring you before the Messenger of God so that he will expose you.’ He said: ‘I am a devil with dependents, and I only came to you from Nasibin. If I could find something other than this, I would not have come to you. We used to be in this city of yours until your companion was sent. When two verses were sent down upon him that drove us out of it, we settled in Nasibin. They are not recited in any house except that the devil does not enter it for three days. If you let me go, I will teach them to you.’ I said: ‘Yes.’ He said: ‘The Throne Verse and the end of Surat al-Baqarah, from His saying, “The Messenger has believed in what was sent down to him,” to the end of it.’ So I let him go. Then I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ to inform him, and there was his caller calling out: ‘Where is Muadh b. Jabal?’ When I entered upon him, he said to me: ‘What happened to your captive?’ I said: ‘He made a pact with me that he would not return,’ and I told him what he had said. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: ‘The wicked one spoke the truth, though he is a liar.’ He said: So after that I would recite those two verses over it and would not find any shortfall in it."],[16927,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband because of his right over her. No woman will find the sweetness of faith until she fulfills her husband’s right, even if he asks her for herself while she is on a camel saddle.”"],[16928,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, this matter began as mercy and prophethood, then it will become mercy and caliphate, then it will become rule that is biting, then it will become oppressive rule, then it will become corruption on the earth. They will approve of silk, adultery, and alcohol, and they will be provided for in these matters until they meet Allah.\""],[16929,"We heard the Messenger of Allahﷺ saying, \"Verily, this matter [Islam] began as mercy and prophecy, then it will be caliphate and mercy, then it will become a biting monarchy and forcefulness, and then corruption on the earth, where they indulge in adultery, silk, and alcohol and are victorious in that. They will continue to be provided for until they meet Allah, the Blessed and Exalted.\""],[16930,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to Yemen, he said to him: “Any man who apostatizes from Islam, call him; if he repents, accept it from him, and if he does not repent, strike his neck. And any woman who apostatizes from Islam, call her; if she repents, accept it from her, and if she refuses, seek her repentance.”"],[16931,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, may He be exalted, has given you as charity a third of your wealth at your death, as an increase for you in your lives, so that He may make it purification for your deeds.”"],[16932,"He used to perform ablution for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a cup patched with brass and give him drink in it."],[16933,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The head of this matter is Islam; whoever submits is safe. Its pillar is prayer, and the peak of its hump is jihad; none attains it except the best of them.”"],[16934,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man who was saying: “O Allah, I ask You for patience.” He said: “You have asked Allah for affliction, so ask Him for well-being.” He passed by a man who was saying: “O Possessor of majesty and honor.” He said: “Your supplication has been answered.” He passed by a man who was saying: “O Allah, I ask You for the completion of Your blessing.” He said: “Do you know what the completion of blessing is?” He replied: “A supplication I made, hoping for good.” He said: “Part of the completion of blessing is seeking refuge from the Fire and entering Paradise.”"],[16935,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man who was saying: “O Allah, I ask You for patience.” He said: “You have asked Allah for affliction, so ask Allah for well-being.” He passed by a man who was saying: “O Possessor of majesty and honor.” He said: “Your supplication has been answered, so ask.” He passed by a man who was saying: “O Allah, I ask You for the completion of Your blessing.” He said: “Son of Adam, do you know what the completion of blessing is?” He replied: “A supplication I made, hoping for good through it.” He said: “The completion of blessing is entering Paradise and deliverance from the Fire.”"],[16936,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Zuhr and ‘Asr and Maghrib and ‘Isha’ during the expedition of Tabuk."],[16937,"He informed him that they went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Tabuk. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to combine Zuhr and ‘Asr and Maghrib and ‘Isha’ together. He said: One day he delayed the prayer, then came out and prayed Zuhr and ‘Asr together, then entered, then came out and prayed Maghrib and ‘Isha’ together. Then he said: “Tomorrow, if Allah wills, you will come to the spring of Tabuk. You will reach it at mid-morning, so whoever reaches it must not touch any of its water until I come.” He said: We arrived, and two men had already reached it before us. The spring was like a sandal strap, trickling with a little water. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked them: “Did you touch any of its water?” They said: Yes. He rebuked them and said to them whatever Allah willed him to say. Then they scooped a little water from the spring with their hands until it collected in something, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ washed his face and hands in it, then poured it back into the spring. The spring then flowed with abundant water and the people drew water. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Soon, O Mu‘adh, if you live long enough, you will see this place filled with jinn.” This is what al-Dabarī said, and he erred; it is only “filled with gardens.”"],[16938,"I heard Mu‘adh b. Jabal say: “We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk. He would not set out until the heat had abated, then he would combine Zuhr and ‘Asr. Then when evening came, he would stop and combine Maghrib and ‘Isha’.”"],[16939,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Zuhr and ‘Asr and Maghrib and ‘Isha’ during the expedition of Tabuk until we returned."],[16940,"We went out with the Prophet ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk, and he used to pray Zuhr and ‘Asr together and Maghrib and ‘Isha’ together."],[16941,"The Prophet ﷺ went on the expedition of Tabuk in intense heat, and he combined Zuhr and ‘Asr and Maghrib and ‘Isha’."],[16942,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Zuhr and 'Asr, and Maghrib and 'Isha' during the expedition of Tabuk.\""],[16943,"\"The Prophet ﷺ combined Zuhr and 'Asr, and Maghrib and 'Isha' during the expedition of Tabuk.\""],[16944,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey and he seated me behind him. I touched nothing softer than the skin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor did I find a scent more fragrant than the scent of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"O Mu'adh, have you heard any sound since last night?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"A messenger from my Lord came to me and gave me glad tidings that whoever of my Ummah dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I not go out to the people and give them glad tidings?\" He said, \"Leave them; let them race for the straight path.\""],[16945,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took my hand one day and said, \"O Mu'adh, by Allah, I love you.\" Mu'adh said to him, \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, and I, by Allah, love you.\" He said, \"I enjoin you, O Mu'adh, never to omit saying after every prayer: 'O Allah, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well.'\" Mu'adh enjoined this upon al-Sunabihi, al-Sunabihi enjoined it upon Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman enjoined it upon 'Uqbah b. Muslim."],[16946,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The feet of a servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about four matters: about his life and how he spent it, about his youth and how he wore it out, about his wealth and from where he acquired it and on what he spent it, and about his knowledge and what he did with it.\""],[16947,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Three things, whoever does them has committed a crime: whoever raises a banner unjustly, or disobeys his parents, or walks with an oppressor—he has committed a crime. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: {Surely We will exact retribution from the criminals}.\""],[16948,"\"Relate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that you have not forgotten and that has not become confused for you.\" He said, \"Seat me.\" So some of the people took his hand and some sat behind him. Then he said, \"I will narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I have not forgotten and that has not become confused for me. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no prophet who did not warn his people about the Dajjal, and I warn you about the matter of the Dajjal: he is one-eyed, and my Lord is not one-eyed. Between his eyes is written 'kafir,' which the literate and the illiterate will read. With him are a Paradise and a Fire, but his Fire is a Paradise and his Paradise is a Fire.'\""],[16949,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is not permissible for a woman to allow anyone into her husband's house without his permission, and she should not leave the house when he dislikes it. She should not abandon her husband's bed, even if he is more unjust than she is. She should not forsake him, even if he is oppressing her, until she goes to him and apologizes. If he accepts her apology, then Allah accepts her apology."],[16950,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led the people in the Battle of Tabuk. When he woke up, he prayed the morning prayer with the people. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me about an action that will admit me into Paradise and I will not ask you about anything else.\" He said, \"You have asked about something great, but it is easy for the one for whom Allah intends good.\" Then he said, \"Believe in Allah and the Last Day, establish prayer, worship Allah alone without associating any partners with Him, and remain upon that until you die.\""],[16951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled with the people at night during the expedition of Tabuk. When morning came, he prayed the Morning Prayer with the people. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise, and I will not ask you about anything else.\" He said, \"Excellent, excellent! You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom Allah wills good.\" Then he said, \"You believe in Allah and the Last Day, you establish prayer, and you worship Allah alone with no partner until you die upon that.\""],[16952,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled with the people at night during the expedition of Tabuk. When morning came, he prayed the Morning Prayer with the people. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise, and I will not ask you about anything else.\" He said, \"Excellent, excellent! You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom Allah wills good.\" Then he said, \"You believe in Allah and the Last Day, you establish prayer, and you worship Allah alone with no partner until you die upon that.\""],[16953,"O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stuck out his tongue, then placed his finger on it. Mu'adh was appalled and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will we be held accountable for all that we say and will it be recorded against us?\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck Mu'adh's shoulder several times and said, \"May your mother be bereaved of you, O son of the mother of Mu'adh! Do people topple onto their faces in the Fire of Hell except because of the harvests of their tongues?\""],[16954,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Nothing weighs an servant's scale like a riding animal on which he spends in the cause of Allah or carries others on it in the cause of Allah.\""],[16955,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The people of Paradise will enter Paradise hairless, beardless, with kohl-lined eyes, at the age of thirty-three.\""],[16956,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever says when he finishes the morning prayer, before speaking: “There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise; in His hand is all good, and He has power over all things,” ten times, will be given for them seven [rewards]. Ten good deeds will be written for him, ten evil deeds will be erased from him, ten degrees will be raised for him, and they will be for him equal to freeing ten slaves. They will be a protection for him from Satan and a shield from what is disliked, and no sin will overtake him that day except associating partners with Allah. And whoever says them when he finishes the sunset prayer will be given the like of that for a third of it."],[16957,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who loves beauty, and I love to be praised,” as if he feared for himself. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “What prevents you from loving to live praiseworthy and die missed? I was only sent to perfect the beauties of character.”"],[16958,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever seeks knowledge in order to vie with the scholars, or to argue with the foolish in gatherings, will not smell the fragrance of Paradise.”"],[16959,"A man said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Tell me of a deed that will admit me into Paradise if I do it.” He said: “Excellent, excellent! You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom Allah makes it easy: you establish the obligatory prayer, you pay the prescribed zakah, and you do not associate anything with Allah.”"],[16960,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The Milky Way in the sky is the sweat of the serpent beneath the Throne.”"],[16961,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to send Muadh to Yemen, he consulted some of his companions, among them Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, and Usayd b. Hudayr. He consulted them, and Abu Bakr said: “Were it not that you consulted us, we would not have spoken.” He said: “In matters about which nothing has been revealed to me, I am like one of you.” Then the people spoke, each one speaking according to his own opinion. He said: “What do you think, O Muadh?” He said: “I think what Abu Bakr said.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, exalted is He, hates, above His heaven, that Abu Bakr ؓ should err.”"],[16962,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform ablution once, twice, and three times—three times; he used to do all of that."],[16963,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform tayammum with clean earth, and I never saw him wipe his hands and face except once."],[16964,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe his face with the edge of his garment during ablution."],[16965,"The Prophet ﷺ recited it: “Can your Lord [cause a table spread to descend]?”"],[16966,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Khaybar, and we captured sheep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed a portion of them among us, and that sufficed us, and he placed the rest in the spoils of war."],[16967,"The Prophet ﷺ used to urge his companions to engage in single combat."],[16968,"Indeed, the Messenger of God ﷺ divided among us the livestock of Khaybar, and some remnants of it remained, so he sold them and put their price into the shares."],[16969,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was skinning a sheep, and he said to me, “O Mu'adh, bring it here or show me,” then he pushed it twice between the flesh and the skin, then said, “O Mu'adh, like this,” then he went on to the prayer."],[16970,"Whichever part of the day you wish: if you wish, in the morning, and if you wish, in the evening. I said, 'But the people dislike it in the evening.' He said, 'And why?' I said, 'They say that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The change in the breath of the fasting person is more fragrant with God than the scent of musk.\"' He said, 'Glory be to God! The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded them to use the tooth-stick when he commanded them, while he knew that there must be some change in the mouth of the fasting person even if he uses the tooth-stick. He was not one to command them to deliberately make their mouths foul. There is no good in that at all; rather, there is evil in it, except for one who is afflicted with an affliction he cannot avoid.' I said, 'And dust in the path of God is likewise? Only the one forced to it and who finds no way around it is rewarded?' He said, 'Yes. As for one who throws himself into affliction deliberately, he has no reward from that.'"],[16971,"The Messenger of God ﷺ only commanded ablution from that which fire has changed by washing the hands and mouth for cleanliness, and it is not obligatory."],[16972,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A pregnant woman, if she kills intentionally, is not to be killed until she gives birth to the child in her womb and until she is provided for; and if she commits adultery, she is not to be stoned until she gives birth to the child in her womb and until she is provided for.\""],[16973,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: he said, \"Whoever recites the Qur'an and acts according to what is in it and dies in the community, God will raise him on the Day of Resurrection with the noble scribes and the judges. Whoever recites the Qur'an while it slips away from him and he does not abandon it, he will have his reward twice. Whoever is eager for it, cannot do it, and does not abandon it, God will raise him on the Day of Resurrection with the nobles of his people, and they will be given superiority over all creatures as eagles are given superiority over other birds, and as a spring in a meadow is preferred over what surrounds it. Then a caller will call out, 'Where are those whom tending livestock did not distract from reciting My Book?' They will stand, and each of them will be clothed with the crown of honor and given victory in his right hand and eternity in his left. If his parents were Muslims, they will be clothed with a garment better than the world and what is in it, and they will say, 'How is this for us?' It will be said, 'Because of what your child used to recite of the Qur'an.'\""],[16974,"While we were riding with the Prophet ﷺ, his mount went ahead, then my mount caught up with his until I thought his mount recognized the tread of my mount, until my knee bumped his knee. I said, 'O Messenger of God, I have wanted to ask you many times, but I am prevented by this verse: {O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if they are shown to you, will distress you}.' He said, 'What is it, O Mu'adh?' I said, 'The deed that admits to Paradise and keeps me away from the Fire.' He said, 'You have asked about a great thing, and yet it is easy: the testimony that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God, establishing prayer, giving zakat, pilgrimage to the House, and fasting Ramadan.' Then he said, 'Shall I inform you of the head of this matter, its pillar, and its peak? Jihad.' Then he said, 'Fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes sins.' Then he said, 'Shall I tell you what gives people mastery over all that?' He took hold of his tongue and placed it between two of his fingers. I said, 'O Messenger of God, will everything we say be recorded against us?' He said, 'May your mother be bereaved of you! Do people ever fall on their faces in the Fire except because of what their tongues reap? You remain safe as long as you are silent, but when you speak, it is written either for you or against you.'"],[16975,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A person will be with the one he loves.\""],[16976,"When the Prophet ﷺ was in his prayer, he would raise his hands opposite his ears, and when he said the takbir he would lower them, then he would pause. Sometimes I saw him place his right hand over his left. When he finished the Opening of the Book, he would pause; when he finished the surah, he would pause; then he would raise his hands opposite his ears, say the takbir, and bow. We would not bow until we saw him bowing. Then he would stand upright from his bowing until every limb returned to its place. Then he would raise his hands opposite his ears, say the takbir, and fall into prostration. He would make his forehead and nose touch the ground. Then he would rise as if he were an arrow, not leaning on his hands. When he sat in the last part of his prayer, he would lean on his left thigh, his right hand on his right thigh, and point with his finger when he supplicated. When he said the salam, he would quickly stand up.\""],[16977,"The Messenger of God ﷺ rode a donkey of his called Ya'fur, whose halter was made of palm fiber. He said, 'Ride, O Mu'adh.' I said, 'Go on, O Messenger of God.' He said, 'Ride.' So he mounted me behind him, and the donkey threw us down. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up laughing. Then he mounted a second time and said, 'Ride,' and I rode. The donkey carried us as far as God willed. He said: he reached back with his hand and struck my back with a whip or a stick that he had, and said, 'O Mu'adh b. Umm Mu'adh, do you know what right God has over people?' I said, 'God and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'God's right over His servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.' Then he rode on as far as God willed, then he reached back with his hand and struck my back, and said, 'O Mu'adh b. Umm Mu'adh, do you know what right the servants have over God if they do that?' I said, 'God and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'The right of the servants over God is that He will admit them to Paradise if they do that.'"],[16978,"While I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ, he set out on the expedition to Tabuk and traveled by night one night, and we traveled by night with him. Then he prayed the morning prayer and we prayed with him, then he went on in the morning and we went with him. The Messenger of God ﷺ rode on, and the groups and camels dispersed, eating as they went, and he was wearing a Najrani cloak. My eye caught the ring of the Messenger of God's she-camel while he was asleep, and I thought it would fall off. While I was like that, my she-camel let out a cry that broke it, and its hoof twisted, and the she-camel of the Messenger of God ﷺ was startled by its striking, and the Prophet ﷺ woke up. He turned and saw me, and said, 'O Mu'adh.' I said, 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said, 'Come closer.' I came closer, and he said that three times, and I came closer until the two mounts were side by side. Mu'adh said to himself, 'There is a word in my mind that has taken hold of me and made me ill; I have not asked you about it, and I have not heard anyone ask you about it.' He said, 'Ask me, O Mu'adh.' I said, 'Tell me, O Messenger of God, about a deed that will admit me to Paradise.' He said, 'Excellent, excellent! You have asked about a great matter, yet it is easy: you testify that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, establish prayer, give zakat, and worship God alone.'"],[16979,"While I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ, he set out on the expedition to Tabuk and traveled by night one night, and we traveled by night with him. Then he prayed the morning prayer and we prayed with him, then he went on in the morning and we went with him. The Messenger of God ﷺ rode on, and the groups and camels dispersed, eating as they went, and he was wearing a Najrani cloak. My eye caught the ring of the Messenger of God's she-camel while he was asleep, and I thought it would fall off. While I was like that, my she-camel let out a cry that broke it, and its hoof twisted, and the she-camel of the Messenger of God ﷺ was startled by its striking, and the Prophet ﷺ woke up. He turned and saw me, and said, 'O Mu'adh.' I said, 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said, 'Come closer.' I came closer, and he said that three times, and I came closer until the two mounts were side by side. Mu'adh said to himself, 'There is a word in my mind that has taken hold of me and made me ill; I have not asked you about it, and I have not heard anyone ask you about it.' He said, 'Ask me, O Mu'adh.' I said, 'Tell me, O Messenger of God, about a deed that will admit me to Paradise.' He said, 'Excellent, excellent! You have asked about a great matter, yet it is easy: you testify that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, establish prayer, give zakat, and worship God alone.'"],[16980,"That he should give the people their stipends and raid with them. While he was giving the people — and that was at the end of time — a man from the people of the countryside came and said, 'O Mu'adh, order my stipend for me, for I am a man from the people of the countryside from such-and-such a place, so perhaps I may reach my family before nightfall.' He said, 'No, by Allah, I will not give you until I give these,' meaning the people of Madinah. 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"All the prophets will enter Paradise forty years before Sulayman b. Dawud, and the poor of the Muslims will enter Paradise forty years before their rich, and the righteous slaves will enter Paradise forty years before the others, and the people of cities will enter Paradise forty years before the people of the countryside because of the virtue of the cities, the congregations, the Friday prayers, and the circles of remembrance. And when a trial occurs, they are singled out for it rather than them.\"'"],[16981,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Glad tidings to the one who increases in remembrance of Allah during jihad in the path of Allah, for for every word there are seventy thousand good deeds, each good deed tenfold, along with what he has with Allah of increase.\" It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about spending?' He said, \"Spending is according to the measure of that.\" 'Abd al-Rahman said: I said to Mu'adh, 'Spending is only seven hundredfold.' Mu'adh said, \"Your understanding is little. That is only when they spend while residing with their families, not on a raid. When they raid and spend, Allah stores for them from the treasury of His mercy what the knowledge of servants and their description cannot comprehend. Those are the party of Allah, and the party of Allah are the victorious.\""],[16982,"I said to Mu'adh, 'I love you and I love your speech.' He said, 'Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Those who love one another for the sake of Allah's majesty will be in the shade of Allah's Throne on the Day of Resurrection, when there is no shade except His shade.\"'"],[16983,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Those who love one another for Allah will be in His shade on a day when there is no shade except His shade.\""],[16984,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Those who love each other for the sake of Allah's glory will be in the shade of the throne on a day when there is no shade except His shade.\""],[16985,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Those who love one another for Allah are in the shade of the Throne.\""],[16986,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"Those who love each other for the sake of Allah will be in the shade of Allah on a day when there is no shade except His shade.\""],[16987,"\"And by Allah, do you love me?\" I said. \"By Allah, indeed I love you for the sake of Allah,\" he said. He replied, \"Rejoice, for I have heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'Those who love one another for the sake of Allah will be shaded by His throne on the day when there will be no shade except His shade.'\""],[16988,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik, from Abu Hazim b. Dinar, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani that he said: I entered the mosque of Damascus and saw a young man with bright front teeth, long of silence, and the people were with him; when they differed about something they referred it to him and issued from his opinion. I asked about him and was told, 'Mu'adh b. Jabal.' The next day I went early and found that he had preceded me in going early, and I found him praying. I waited for him until he finished his prayer, then I came to him from in front and greeted him and said, 'By Allah, I love you for Allah.' He said, 'By Allah?' I said, 'By Allah.' He said, 'By Allah?' I said, 'By Allah.' He said, 'By Allah?' I said, 'By Allah.' He said: Then he took hold of the knot of my cloak and pulled me to him and said, 'Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Allah said, \"My love has become incumbent for those who love one another for My sake, and those who sit together for My sake, and those who give to one another for My sake, and those who visit one another for My sake.\"'"],[16989,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Those who love one another for Allah are in the shade of Allah's Throne on a day when there is no shade except His shade.\""],[16990,"I entered the mosque of Hims and there were men narrating hadiths from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, among them a young man with dark, wide eyes and bright front teeth. When he spoke, the people all listened to his speech, and when they disputed about something they accepted his word. He was Mu'adh b. Jabal. We sat with him and I said, 'I love you.' He took hold of my clothing and pulled me to him until my knee touched his knee, then said, 'Shall I give you glad tidings from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who narrates it from Allah ﷻ? He said: \"My love has become incumbent for those who love one another, sit together, visit one another, and give to one another for My sake.\"'"],[16991,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who narrates from Allah ﷻ, he said: \"My love has become incumbent for those who love one another, sit together, and give to one another for My sake.\""],[16992,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Those who love one another for Allah are in the shade of Allah's Throne on a day when there is no shade except His shade. People will be terrified and they will not be terrified, and people will fear and they will not fear.\" He said: Then I got up from him and went to 'Ubadah b. al-Samit. 'Ubadah said, 'And better than it: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"My love has become due for those who love one another for My sake, and My love has become due for those who sit together for My sake, and My love has become due for those who visit one another for My sake.\"'"],[16993,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah brighten a servant who hears my words and does not add to them, for many a carrier of understanding conveys it to one more receptive than him.\""],[16994,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah brighten a servant who hears my words and does not add to them, for many a carrier of understanding conveys it to one more receptive than him.\""],[16995,"O Messenger of God, teach me a deed which, if I do it, I will enter Paradise? He said: \"Do not associate anything with God, even if you are burned; obey your parents, even if they expel you from your property; do not drink wine, for it is the key to every evil; do not ever abandon the prayer deliberately, for whoever abandons the prayer deliberately, God's protection is removed from him; do not dispute authority with its people, even if you think you have a right; spend on your family according to your means, and do not lift the stick from them; make them fear God; do not steal from the spoils; do not flee from battle.\""],[16996,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The first thing my Lord forbade me after the worship of idols was drinking wine and quarreling with men.\""],[16997,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: On the Day of Resurrection, the one deprived of intellect, the one who perished in the interval between prophets, and the one who perished as a child will be brought. The one deprived of intellect will say: \"O Lord, if You had given me intellect, no one to whom You gave intellect would have been more fortunate with his intellect than me.\" The one who perished as a child will say: \"O Lord, if You had given me a lifespan, no one to whom You gave a lifespan would have been more fortunate with his lifespan than me.\" The one who perished in the interval will say: \"O Lord, if a messenger from You had come to me, no human to whom a covenant from You came would have been more fortunate with Your covenant than me.\" Then the Lord, Exalted is He, will say: \"I command you with a command; will you obey Me?\" They will say: \"Yes, by Your might, O Lord.\" He will say: \"Go and enter Hellfire.\" If they were to enter it, it would not have harmed them at all. Then tongues of fire will emerge upon them, and they will think that it has destroyed everything God created. Then He will command them a second time, and they will return as before. Then the Lord, may He be glorified, will say: \"I created you with My knowledge, and to My knowledge you will return.\" Then the Fire will take them."],[16998,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Shall I inform you about the kings of the people of Paradise?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Every weak and oppressed person with two worn garments, to whom no attention is paid; if he were to swear by God, God would fulfill his oath.\""],[16999,"The Messenger of God ﷺ one day mentioned the trials, magnifying them and emphasizing their severity. Ali b. Abi Talib said: \"O Messenger of God, what is the way out of them?\" He said: \"The Book of God. In it is the account of those before you, the news of those after you, and the judgment of what is between you. Whoever abandons it out of arrogance, God will crush him. Whoever seeks guidance in other than it, God will lead him astray. It is the firm rope of God, the wise reminder, and the straight path. It is the one about which, when the jinn heard it, they said: {Indeed, we have heard a wondrous Quran.} It is the one with which tongues do not differ, and much repetition does not wear it out.\""],[17000,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O God, whoever believes in me, testifies to my truthfulness, and bears witness that what I have brought is the truth, then make his wealth and children few and hasten his taking to You. And whoever does not believe in me, does not testify to my truthfulness, and does not know that what I have brought is the truth from You, then make his wealth and children abundant and prolong his life.\""],[17001,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever feeds a believer until he satisfies him from hunger, God will admit him through a gate of Paradise that no one will enter except one like him.\""],[17002,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Verily, Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient person. Whoever meets God having broken his pledge of allegiance will meet Him while maimed. Whoever deliberately departs from the community by a handspan has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck. Whoever dies without there being an imam of the community over him to whom obedience is due dies a death of ignorance.\""],[17003,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The banner of the treacherous one on the Day of Resurrection will be raised near his buttocks.\""],[17004,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I was shown that I was placed in a scale and my community in the other, and I balanced it. Then Abu Bakr was placed in a scale and my community in the other, and he balanced it. Then Umar was placed in a scale and my community in the other, and he balanced it. Then Uthman was placed in a scale, and he balanced it. Then the scale was raised.\""],[17005,"Twelve, and she left their father in their house; the youngest of them was one whose beard had fully grown. She stood up and greeted Mu'adh while two men from her sons held her upper arms. She said: \"Who sent you, O man?\" Mu'adh said to her: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me.\" The woman said: \"The Messenger of God sent you, and you are the messenger of the Messenger of God? Will you not tell me, O messenger of the Messenger of God, what is the right of a husband over his wife?\" Mu'adh said: \"She should fear God as much as she can, and she should listen and obey.\" She said: \"I adjure you to tell me what is the right of a husband over his wife.\" Mu'adh said to her: \"Are you not satisfied to listen and obey and fear God?\" She said: \"Yes, but I left the father of these as an old man in the house.\" Mu'adh said: \"By the One in Whose hand is Mu'adh's soul, if you were to return to him and find that leprosy had torn his flesh and pierced his nostrils, and you found his nostrils flowing with pus and blood, then you placed them in your mouth in order to fulfill his right, you would never fulfill it.\""],[17006,"I came to the mosque of Damascus and there was a group of companions of Muhammad ﷺ , and among them was a young man with intense black eyes and a radiant face. Whenever they disagreed about something, they would refer it to the young man. So, I asked my companion, \"Who is this?\" He said, \"This is Mu'adh ibn Jabal.\" He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'Those who love each other for the sake of Allah will be upon pulpits of light, under the shade of the Throne of the Most Merciful on a day when there is no shade except His shade.'\""],[17007,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Those who love each other for the sake of Allah will be in the shade of the Throne on a day when there is no shade except His shade. They will be on pulpits of light and will be envied by the Prophets and the truthful (Siddeeqeen).\""],[17008,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The things I fear most for my community are three: a man who recites the Book of God until you see splendor upon him, and he has been granted the cloak of Islam by God, then he draws his sword and strikes his neighbor with it, accusing him of polytheism.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of God, is the one who accuses more deserving of it or the one accused?\" He said: \"The one who accuses. And a man to whom God grants authority, so he says: 'Whoever obeys me has obeyed God, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed God.' He lies. It is not for a caliph to be a shield apart from the Creator. And a man whom stories make light-headed; every time he finishes one tale, he tells a longer one. If he reaches the Dajjal, he will follow him.\""],[17009,"We raided with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and we captured some sheep. The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed a portion of them among us and placed the remainder in the spoils."],[17010,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Yemen and said: “Perhaps you will pass by my mosque and my grave. I have sent you to a people whose hearts are tender; they fight for the truth. Fight with those of them who obey you against those who disobey you. Then they will return to Islam, until a woman hastens to her husband, a child to his parent, and a brother to his brother. So alight between the two tribes, al-Sakūn and al-Sakāsik.”"],[17011,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Take the stipend as long as it is a stipend. But when it becomes bribery in religion, do not take it. You will not abandon it; poverty and need will prevent you. Indeed, the millstone of Islam is turning, so turn with the Book wherever it turns. Indeed, the Book and the ruling authority will separate, so do not part with the Book. Indeed, there will be rulers over you who decide for themselves what they do not decide for you. If you disobey them, they will kill you, and if you obey them, they will lead you astray.” They said, “O Messenger of God, what should we do?” He said, “As the companions of Jesus son of Mary did: they were sawn with saws and carried on wood. Death in obedience to God is better than life in disobedience to God.”"],[17012,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “The great battle, the conquest of Constantinople, and the emergence of the Dajjāl will occur within seven months.”"],[17013,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The great battle, the conquest of Constantinople, and the emergence of the Dajjāl will occur within seven months.”"],[17014,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “R aiding is of two kinds. As for one who raids seeking the countenance of God, obeying the imam, spending generously, sharing with his companion, and avoiding corruption in the land, then his sleeping and his waking are entirely good. As for one who raids out of pride, show, and reputation, disobeying the imam, and spreading corruption in the land, he will not return even with his basic needs.”"],[17015,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the Night of Decree. He said, \"It is in the last ten nights, on the seventh, or the fifth, or the third.\""],[17016,"He said, “By God?” twice or three times. I said, “By God.” Then he said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘My love or my mercy is assured for those who love one another for My sake, sit together for My sake, visit one another for My sake, and give generously to one another for My sake.’”"],[17017,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Seek refuge in God from greed that leads to avarice, from greed for what is not to be desired, and from greed for what cannot be desired.”"],[17018,"The Prophet ﷺ underwent cupping while fasting."],[17019,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: “Which deed is most beloved to God Almighty?” He said: “That you die with your tongue moist from the remembrance of God.”"],[17020,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise will not regret anything except an hour that passed them in which they did not remember God.”"],[17021,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Seek help in fulfilling needs through concealment, for every possessor of a blessing is envied.”"],[17022,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ who said: “Do you know what God will say to the believers on the Day of Resurrection, and the first thing they will say?” They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “He will say to the believers on the Day of Resurrection: Did you love to meet Me?” They will say: Yes, O Lord, we hoped for Your pardon and Your forgiveness. He said: “Then I have made My pardon and My forgiveness binding for you.”"],[17023,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever eats or drinks or kills game and forgets to mention God’s name, let him eat from it as long as he did not deliberately omit the naming.”"],[17024,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about hoarding, what it is. He said: “When he hears of reduced prices it grieves him, and when he hears of high prices he rejoices at it. What an evil servant is the hoarder: if God lowers prices he is sad, and if God raises them he rejoices.”"],[17025,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If my community knew what benefit it has in fenugreek, they would buy it even for its weight in gold.”"],[17026,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever walks to a person of innovation to honor him has helped in the demolition of Islam.”"],[17027,"Abu Abdullah, a man from al-Anbar, narrated to us, from Thawr b. Yazid, from Khalid b. Ma‘dan, from Mu‘adh b. Jabal, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about borrowing dough and bread. He said: “Glory be to God! This is only among noble character traits: take the small and give the large, or take the large and give the small. The best of you is the one who is best in repayment.”"],[17028,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “O people, adopt fear of God as a trade: provision will come to you without capital or commerce.” Then he recited {And whoever fears God, He will make for him a way out and provide for him from where he does not expect}."],[17029,"The Messenger of God ﷺ attended the marriage contract of a man among his companions and said to him: “Upon goodness and harmony, a blessed bird, and abundance in provision. May God bless you all. Play the tambourine over his head.” A tambourine was brought and struck, and trays bearing fruit and sugar were brought and scattered over him. The people withheld their hands, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “What is the matter with you that you do not snatch?” They said: O Messenger of God, did you not forbid snatching? He said: “I only forbade you from snatching from military expeditions; as for wedding feasts, no.” He said: Then he pulled it away from them and they pulled it away from him."],[17030,"The Prophet ﷺ was in our house displaying horses. ‘Uyaynah b. Hisn entered upon him and said to the Prophet ﷺ: You know more about horses than I, and I know more about men than you. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Which men are best?” He replied: Men who carry their swords on their shoulders, display their lances on the withers of their horses, and wear striped cloaks from the people of Najd. The Prophet ﷺ said: “You have lied. The best of men are the men of Yemen; faith is Yemeni. The largest tribe in Paradise is Madhhij, and the people consumed by Himyar are better than their consumers; Hadramawt is better than Kindah. May God curse the four kings: Jamd, Mishrah, Mikhwas, and Abda‘a, and their sister al-‘Amarradah.”"],[17031,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to perform ablution with water as long as it has not become stagnant, turning green or yellow.”"],[17032,"And concerning prayer in a single garment, and what is lawful for a man from his menstruating wife? Mu‘adh said: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about that, and he said: “When the two circumcised parts meet, the major ablution becomes obligatory. As for prayer in a single garment, wrap it around yourself. As for what is lawful from a menstruating woman, what is above the waist-wrapper is lawful, but abstaining from that is better.”"],[17033,"You asked me about what I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “The major ablution is obligatory after major ritual impurity.”"],[17034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever ties the jizyah around his neck has disowned what Muhammad ﷺ brought.”"],[17035,"I answered the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: Leave me, for I will not return. So he let him go. When he went to the Prophet ﷺ the next morning, he said: “O Mu‘ādh, what did your captive do?” He said: I released him. On the second night, he sensed him and seized him. He again pleaded with him and swore that he would not return, so he let him go. On the third night, he sensed him, seized him, and again he pleaded and swore that he would not return, but he refused to release him. He said: Let me go and I will teach you a verse that, if you recite it, we will not approach that place. He taught him the Verse of the Throne, so he let him go. He went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the morning and told him what had happened, and he said: “He spoke the truth, though he is a liar.”"],[17036,"I heard Abū Shaybah say: Mu‘ādh was walking with a man, and he lifted a stone from the road and said: What is this? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever lifts a stone from the road, a good deed is written for him, and whoever has a good deed will enter Paradise.”"],[17037,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found him standing in prayer. He remained standing until morning, then he prostrated a prostration in which I thought his soul had been taken. He looked at me and said: “O Mu‘ādh, did you see?” I said: O Messenger of Allah, yes, I saw you prostrate a prostration in which I thought your soul had been taken. He said: “Do you know why?\" I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: I prayed as much as my Lord decreed, and my Lord came to me and said: O Muhammad, what shall I do with your ummah? I said: My Lord, You know best. He repeated it three or four times, and the last time He said: What shall I do with your ummah? I said: You know best, O Lord. He said: I will not grieve you over your ummah. So I prostrated to my Lord and your Lord, thankful, for He loves the thankful.”"],[17038,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit its doer into Paradise. He said: “Excellent, excellent! You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one whom Allah makes it easy. Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the obligatory prayers, pay the obligatory zakāh, fast Ramadān, and perform Hajj to the House. I will tell you the head of this matter, its pillar, and its peak. The head is the testimony that there is no god but Allah, its pillar is prayer, and its peak is jihād. I will tell you the gates of goodness: fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin just as water extinguishes fire, and a servant’s prayer in the middle of the night.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: “Their sides forsake their beds” [Q 32:16]. “I will tell you what is more controlling than all of that.” He shook his mount, and I drew near to the people, then I drew near to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is more controlling than all of that? He gestured with his hand to his tongue. I said: The tongue? As if I was careless about it. He said: “May your mother bereave you, O Mu‘ādh b. Jabal! Will people be thrown into the Fire of Hell on their faces except by the harvest of their tongues?”"],[17039,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Caution will not avail against destiny, but supplication benefits against what has descended and what has not descended. So hold fast to supplication, O servants of Allah.”"],[17040,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a nobleman of a people comes to you, honor him.”"],[17041,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Whoever fights in the way of Allah for the interval between two milkings of a she-camel, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.” The interval between two milkings is the time it takes to milk her for the one who milks her."],[17042,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever fights in the way of Allah, a Muslim man, for the interval between two milkings of a she-camel, Paradise becomes obligatory for him. Whoever asks Allah for martyrdom sincerely from himself, then dies or is killed, has the reward of a martyr. If he is wounded or suffers an injury in the way of Allah, on the Day of Resurrection it will come with the color of saffron and the fragrance of musk. Whoever is wounded in the way of Allah bears the seal of the martyrs.”"],[17043,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever asks Allah for martyrdom sincerely from himself, then dies or is killed, has the reward of a martyr. Whoever is wounded or suffers an injury in the way of Allah, on the Day of Resurrection it will come with the color of saffron and the fragrance of musk. Whoever is wounded in the way of Allah bears the seal of the martyrs.”"],[17044,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever fights in the way of Allah for the interval between two milkings of a she-camel, Paradise becomes obligatory for him. Whoever asks for martyrdom sincerely from himself, then dies or is killed, has the reward of a martyr. Whoever is wounded or suffers an injury in the way of Allah, on the Day of Resurrection it will come at its fullest, its color like saffron and its fragrance like musk.”"],[17045,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever fights in the way of Allah for the interval between two milkings of a she-camel, Paradise becomes obligatory for him. Whoever asks Allah for martyrdom sincerely from his heart in the way of Allah, Paradise becomes obligatory for him. Whoever is wounded with a wound in the way of Allah or suffers an injury, on the Day of Resurrection it will come at its fullest, its color like saffron and its fragrance like musk. Whoever departs with wounds in the way of Allah is sealed with the seal of the martyrs.”"],[17046,"The last words with which I parted from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were that I said: Which deeds are most beloved to Allah? He said: \"That you die while your tongue is moist with the remembrance of Allah.\""],[17047,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No soul dies while having with Allah the weight of an ant of good except that it is sealed over with clay.\""],[17048,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"It is not lawful for a woman to give permission in her husband's house while he is unwilling, nor to go out while he is unwilling, nor to obey anyone in that matter, nor to be harsh with him, nor to forsake his bed, nor to strike him—even if he is more unjust than her—until she pleases him. If he is pleased and accepts from her, then with her it is good; Allah accepted her excuse and made her face fair, and there is no sin upon her. But if he refuses to be pleased with her, then she has indeed conveyed her excuse.\""],[17049,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Which deeds are most beloved to Allah? He said: \"That you die while your tongue is moist with the remembrance of Allah.\""],[17050,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The building of Bayt al-Maqdis is the ruin of Yathrib; the ruin of Yathrib is the coming of the great battle; the coming of the great battle is the conquest of Constantinople; and the conquest of Constantinople is the emergence of the Dajjal.\""],[17051,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Allah, may He be exalted, looks upon His creation on the night of the middle of Sha'ban and forgives all His creation except for a polytheist or one who harbors enmity.\""],[17052,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the dawn prayer with us until the sun almost rose. When he had prayed the dawn prayer with us, he said: \"Last night I prayed what was decreed for me, then I laid my side in the mosque. My Lord came to me in the most beautiful form and said: O Muhammad, do you know what the highest assembly disputes about? I said: No, my Lord. He said it three times. I said: No, my Lord. Then He placed His hand between my shoulders, and I felt its coolness between my breasts, and everything was revealed to me and I knew it. I said: About ranks and expiations. He said: What are the ranks? I said: Feeding food, spreading peace, and praying while people are asleep. He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: What are the expiations? I said: Performing ablution thoroughly in extreme cold, waiting for prayer after prayer, and walking to the Friday prayers. He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: Ask, O Muhammad. I said: O Allah, I ask You for the doing of good deeds, the abandonment of evil deeds, love of the poor, and that You forgive me and have mercy on me. And when You intend a trial among Your servants, take me to You without being tried. O Allah, I ask You for Your love and the love of those who love You and the love of deeds that bring me near to Your love.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Learn these words and study them, for they are true.\""],[17053,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am a guarantor of a house in the outskirts of Paradise, a house in the middle of Paradise, and a house in the highest part of Paradise for one who abandons disputation even if he is right, abandons lying even in jest, and has good character.\""],[17054,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me by the hand and said: \"Indeed I love you, O Mu'adh.\" He said: I said: \"And I, by Allah, love you, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"I enjoin upon you words that you should say after every prayer: My Lord, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well.\""],[17055,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, returning that to a certainty in the heart, will enter Paradise.\""],[17056,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed facing Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen months after coming to Madinah. Then Allah revealed a verse commanding him to turn to the Ka'bah. He said: {We have certainly seen the turning of your face toward the heaven} (the verse)."],[17057,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever's last words are 'There is no god but Allah' will enter Paradise.\""],[17058,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not keep looking at those afflicted with leprosy.”"],[17059,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Say: He is God, the One (Qul Huwa Allāhu Aḥad) is equivalent to one-third of the Qur’an.”"],[17060,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “No woman harms her husband in this world but that his wife from the ḥūr al-ʿīn will say: ‘Do not harm him, may God destroy you! He is only a guest with you, soon to part from you to us.’”"],[17061,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “You will alight at a place called al-Jābiyah or al-Jūbiyyah, where a disease like the gland of a camel will afflict you. Through it God will cause your souls and your offspring to be martyred, and He will purify your deeds by it.”"],[17062,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Among the most hateful of creation to God ﷻ is one who believed and then disbelieved.”"],[17063,"There will be trials in which wealth becomes abundant and the Qur’an is spread open, so that a man, a woman, the young, the old, the believer, and the hypocrite all read it. Yet he reads it and is not followed; so he says: ‘By God, I will definitely read it openly,’ but he is still not followed. Then he heads to a mosque and innovates speech that is not from the Book of God nor from the Sunnah of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Beware of it, for it is an innovation of misguidance. Beware of it, for it is an innovation of misguidance. Beware of it, for it is an innovation of misguidance.”"],[17064,"“What makes you weep?” I said: “By God, I am not weeping over any worldly thing I might obtain from you, nor over any kinship between me and you, but I weep over what I used to hear from you; it is now departing.” He said: “Do not weep. Knowledge and faith—their affair is that whoever seeks them finds them. Seek knowledge where Ibrāhīm sought it, for he asked God and was not forgetful. And after me, seek it from four men; if you do not find it with them, then search among the people. Seek knowledge from ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd, Abū al-Dardāʾ, Salmān, and ʿAbdullāh b. Salām. And beware of the deviation of the wise man, for Satan casts misguided wisdom upon the tongue of a wise man. Take knowledge when it comes to you.” He said: “I said to Muʿādh b. Jabal: ‘How can I know the deviation of the wise man and the judgment of the hypocrite?’ He said: ‘Indeed, truth is light.’ And beware of making hasty judgments in matters. Some men among the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ said one day: ‘Our sons are better than us; they were born upon Islam and did not associate partners, whereas we had associated partners.’ That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: ‘We are better than our sons, and our sons are better than their sons, and our sons’ sons are better than their sons’ sons.’”"],[17065,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Indeed, he is the tenth of ten.”"],[17066,"He said concerning the plague: “A mercy from your Lord, the call of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you.”"],[17067,"The plague struck Syria, so Muʿādh stood and addressed them in Ḥimṣ, saying: “Indeed, this plague is a mercy from your Lord, the call of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you.”"],[17068,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God has never sent a prophet but that among his nation were Qadariyyah and Murjiʾah, who confuse his nation’s affair for him. Indeed, God ﷻ has cursed the Qadariyyah and the Murjiʾah on the tongue of seventy prophets.”"],[17069,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Muʿādh b. Jabal: “Whoever abandons the prayer deliberately has indeed been absolved of God’s protection.”"],[17070,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “O Mu‘adh b. Jabal, whoever abandons the prayer has indeed absolved himself of the protection.”"],[17071,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no Muslim who sleeps upon the remembrance of Allah in a state of purity, then awakens during the night and asks Allah for good of this world and the Hereafter except that He grants it to him.” Musa b. Isma‘il added: Hammad said: Abu Zabyah passed by us and narrated to us from Mu‘adh from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[17072,"That the Prophet ﷺ saw a man wearing a cloak of silk, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “A collar of fire.”"],[17073,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “There is no servant who stands in this world in a position of reputation-seeking and showing-off except that Allah will make him heard of on the heads of the creation on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[17074,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Abdullah b. Salam is the tenth of ten who are in Paradise.”"],[17075,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with the Isha prayer, and he delayed it for us until someone said: \"He has prayed and did not come out, and few people said that he will come out.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said, \"Take this prayer as a means of darkness, for you have been given preference with it over the rest of the nations, and no one before you has prayed it.\""],[17076,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the ‘Isha prayer one night, and he delayed it until one might think that he had already prayed and was not going to come out. Then he came out afterward, and a person said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I thought that you had prayed and were not going to come out. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Delay this prayer (i.e., pray it later into the night), for you have been favored with it over all other nations, and no one before you prayed it.”"],[17077,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out with him, advising him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned toward Madinah and said: “Indeed these people of my household think that they are the closest of people to me, but it is not so. My allies among you are the God-fearing, whoever they may be and wherever they may be. O Allah, I do not permit for them the corruption of what You have set right. By Allah, my nation will be overturned from its religion just as a vessel is overturned in the wide watercourse.”"],[17078,"That when he sent him to Yemen, he went out with him advising him, while Mu‘adh was riding and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was walking beneath his mount. When he finished, he said: “O Mu‘adh, it may be that you will not meet me after this year of mine, and perhaps you will pass by my mosque and my grave.” Mu‘adh b. Jabal wept out of grief at the separation from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Do not weep, O Mu‘adh, for weeping is from Satan.”"],[17079,"“Indeed this matter is the mercy of your Lord, the call of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you. O Allah, grant the family of Mu‘adh their share of this matter.”"],[17080,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Six are among the signs of the Hour: my death, the conquest of Jerusalem, that a man will be given a thousand dinars and be dissatisfied with them, a tribulation whose heat will enter the house of every Muslim, a death that will seize people like the sheep-pox, and that we will raid the Romans and they will march with twelve banners, under each banner twelve thousand.”"],[17081,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ on a red camel. He said: “Mu‘adh.” I said: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Do you know what is the right of Allah upon the servants?” I said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “His right upon them is that they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him.” Then he said: “Do you know what is the right of the servants upon Allah if they do that?” I said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Their right upon Him is that He admits them to Paradise.”"],[17082,"I was traveling with the Prophet ﷺ while he was on a donkey called Ya‘fur."],[17083,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Avoid the three things that provoke curses: defecating in water sources, in the middle of the road, and in the shade."],[17084,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he used to avoid urine and commanded his companions to do so. Mu'adh said: The majority of the punishment of the grave is from urine. Ibn Abi Maryam said concerning the hadith of 'Abdullah b. Hurayth."],[17085,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to collect zakat from the people of Yemen and commanded me to take from cattle: from every thirty, a tabi' (one-year-old male calf); from every forty, a musinnah (two-year-old female); from sixty, two tabi's; from seventy, a musinnah and a tabi'; from eighty, two musinnahs; from ninety, three tabi's; from one hundred, a musinnah and two tabi's; from one hundred and twenty, three musinnahs or four tabi's. And he commanded me not to take anything below that until it reaches a musinnah or a jadha'ah (a one-year-old sheep or goat). He said: 'The awqas (young animals below the zakat threshold) have no obligatory due.' Awqas means the young ones."],[17086,"The Messenger of Allah took my hand and said, \"Verily, I love you, O Mu'adh. Do not forget to say in every prayer: 'O Allah, help me to remember You, to be grateful to You, and to worship You excellently'. Ibn Lahiah As-Sunabihi is not mentioned.\""],[17087,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: If you wish, I will tell you the first thing Allah ﷻ will say to the believers on the Day of Resurrection. He will say: 'Did you love to meet Me?' They will say: 'Yes, our Lord.' He will say: 'Why?' They will say: 'We hoped for Your mercy and Your pardon.' He will say: 'My mercy has become binding for you.'"],[17088,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to Yemen. He led them in the dawn prayer and recited Surah al-Nisa'. When he reached {And Allah took Ibrahim as an intimate friend} (Quran 4:125), a woman said: 'The eye of Ibrahim's mother has been delighted.'"],[17089,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said: 'O Mu'adh, do you know what Allah's right upon people is?' I said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'His right upon them is that they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. Do you know, O Mu'adh, what people's right upon Allah is if they do that? That He will not punish them.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, shall I give the people glad tidings?' He said: 'Leave them; let them act.'"],[17090,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ when he said: 'O Mu'adh, do you know what Allah's right upon the servants is and what the servants' right upon Allah is? Allah's right upon the servants is that they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. The servants' right upon Allah is that He will not punish anyone who dies without associating anything with Him.'"],[17091,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a donkey called 'Ufayr when he said to me: 'O Mu'adh, do you know what Allah's right upon the servants is? That they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. And the servants' right upon Allah is that He will not punish anyone who does not associate anything with Him.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, shall I give the people glad tidings?' He said: 'Do not give them glad tidings, lest they rely on that alone.'"],[17092,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will we be held accountable for everything we say?' He said: 'May your mother be bereaved of you, O Mu'adh b. Jabal! Will people be thrown into Hellfire on their faces for anything other than the harvests of their tongues?'"],[17093,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen. When I had set out, he sent after me and I returned. He said: 'Do you know why I sent for you? Do not take anything without knowledge, for it is misappropriation. Whoever misappropriates will bring what he misappropriated on the Day of Resurrection. This is why I called you back; now go on with your task.'"],[17094,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to Yemen and commanded him to take from every thirty cattle a tabi' (one-year-old male) or tabi'ah (one-year-old female), from every forty a musinnah (two-year-old female), and from every adult person one dinar or its equivalent in Ma'afiri garments."],[17095,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen and commanded me to take from cattle: from every forty a musinnah, and from every thirty a tabi' or tabi'ah, and from every adult person one dinar or its equivalent in Ma'afiri garments."],[17096,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen and commanded me to take from every drachma or equivalent a certain amount, and he commanded me to take from every thirty cows a sale, and from every forty sheep a sheep known for its age, and he commanded me to take from watered land a tenth or its equivalent, and from dry land half of its tenth."],[17097,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded him, when he sent him to Yemen, to take from every thirty cattle a tabi' (one-year-old male or female) and from every forty a musinnah (two-year-old cow), and from every person who has reached puberty a dinar or its equivalent in Ma'afir garments."],[17098,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen and commanded me to take from cattle: from every thirty a tabi' or tabi'ah—that is, a jadha' (one-year-old)—and from every forty a musinnah, and from every person who has reached puberty a dinar or its equivalent in Ma'afir garments."],[17099,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and in the morning I drew near to him while we were traveling. I said, “O Prophet of Allah, will you not tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise and keep me far from the Fire?” He said, “You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom Allah makes it easy: worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, fast the month of Ramadan, and perform pilgrimage to the House.”"],[17100,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and in the morning I drew near to him while we were traveling. I said, “O Prophet of Allah, will you not tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise and keep me far from the Fire?” He said, “You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom Allah makes it easy: worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, fast the month of Ramadan, and perform pilgrimage to the House.”"],[17101,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and in the morning I drew near to him while we were traveling. I said, “O Prophet of Allah, will you not tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise and keep me far from the Fire?” He said, “You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom Allah makes it easy: worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, fast the month of Ramadan, and perform pilgrimage to the House.”"],[17102,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “When one of you comes to prayer while the imam is in a certain state, let him do as the imam does.”"],[17103,"Prayer was transformed through three stages, and fasting was transformed through three stages. As for the stages of prayer: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah and prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis (Jerusalem) for seventeen months. Then Allah revealed: {We have certainly seen the turning of your face toward the heaven, and We will surely turn you to a qiblah with which you will be pleased} (2:144). So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned toward the Ka'bah. This was one stage. They used to gather for prayer and call one another to it until they struck the bell or nearly did so. Then a man called 'Abdullah b. Zayd came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, if I were to tell you that while I was between sleep and wakefulness, I saw a figure wearing two green garments standing and facing the qiblah, saying, ‘Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar’ until he finished the adhan, repeating each phrase twice. Then at the end of his adhan he said, ‘Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, la ilaha illa Allah.’ Then he paused for a while, then stood and said the same as he had said, except that he added, ‘Qad qamat al-salah.’” He said, “Teach it to Bilal.” So Bilal was the first to call the adhan with it. Then 'Umar b. al-Khattab came and said, “O Messenger of Allah, something like what came to 'Abdullah b. Zayd came around me, except that he preceded me to you.” These are two stages. People used to come to prayer after the Prophet ﷺ had already prayed part of it, and they would signal to them with their fingers how many rak'ahs he had prayed: one, two. Then Mu'adh came after the Prophet ﷺ had already prayed part of the prayer, and he entered the prayer. He said, “I will not find him in any state except that I am in it, then I will make up what I missed.” He came after part of the prayer had been missed and entered the prayer. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, Mu'adh stood up to make up what he had missed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Mu'adh has set a precedent for you, so do likewise.” These are the three stages. As for the stages of fasting: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah and began fasting three days every month. He fasted 'Ashura and fasted for seventeen months from Rabi' to Rabi' to the month of Ramadan. Then Allah ﷻ made the month of Ramadan obligatory upon him and revealed to him: {Fasting is prescribed for you} up to His saying: {a ransom of feeding a poor person} (2:183-184). So whoever wished fasted, and whoever wished fed a poor person instead, and that sufficed him. Then Allah established fasting for the resident healthy person and granted a concession for the sick and the traveler, and fixed the feeding for the elderly person who cannot fast. And He revealed to him: {The month of Ramadan in which was revealed the Qur'an, a guidance for the people and clear proofs of guidance and criterion. So whoever of you witnesses the month, let him fast it} (2:185). They used to eat, drink, and approach their wives as long as they had not slept. When they slept, they refrained from that. Then a man called Sirmah spent his day fasting while working. He came to his family and slept before breaking his fast. In the morning he was still fasting. The Prophet ﷺ saw him late in the day and he was extremely exhausted. He said, “Why do I see you exhausted?” He said, “I worked yesterday, then I came and slept before breaking my fast.” Then 'Umar came after having approached his wife after sleeping, and he mentioned that to him. Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {It has been made permissible for you the night preceding fasting to go to your wives} (2:187) to the end of the verse."],[17104,"We used to come to prayer, and when a man came after having missed part of the prayer, the one next to him would signal to him how much he had missed, and he would make it up. So we were among those bowing, prostrating, standing, and sitting. One day I came after having missed part of the prayer, and I was signaled what I had missed. I said, “I will not find him in any state except that I am in it.” So I was in the same state as I found them. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, I stood up and prayed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ faced the people and said, “Who said such and such?” They said, “Mu'adh b. Jabal.” He said, “Mu'adh has set a precedent for you, so follow him. When one of you comes after having missed part of the prayer, let him pray with the imam what remains, and when the imam finishes, let him make up what he missed.”"],[17105,"People at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when one of them missed part of the prayer, would ask and they would signal to him how much he had missed, so he would pray what he had missed and then enter with them in their prayer. Mu'adh came while the people were sitting in their prayer, so he sat with them. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the salam, he stood and made up what he had missed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do as Mu'adh b. Jabal did.”"],[17106,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to me, “O Mu'adh, do you know what Allah's right upon His servants is?” I said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “His right upon them is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.” Then he said, “Do you know what their right upon Him is if they do that?” I said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Their right upon Him is that He will not punish them.”"],[17107,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was on a donkey, and he said, “O Mu'adh, do you know what Allah's right upon the servants is and what the servants' right upon Allah is?” I said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Allah's right upon the servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him, and the servants' right upon Allah is that if they do that, He will not punish them.”"],[17108,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, “O Mu'adh, do you know what Allah's right upon the servants is?” I said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Indeed, Allah's right upon the servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.” Then he said, “Do you know what the servants' right is if they do that?” I said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “That He will not punish them.”"],[17109,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who meets a woman he does not know, and he does not do anything with her except talk?\" So Allah revealed the verse, \"Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night. Indeed, good deeds do away with misdeeds. That is a reminder for those who remember.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to the man, \"Perform ablution and then pray.\" Mu'adh said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is this command specific to him or is it for all believers in general?\" The Prophet ﷺ said three times, \"No, it is for all believers in general.\""],[17110,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, a man has been afflicted by a woman whom it is not permissible for him to have relations with. He has not left anything that can afflict him from his wife except that it has afflicted him, except that he has not had intercourse with her.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Perform ablution well, then stand and pray.\" Then Allah revealed this verse {Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night. Indeed, good deeds do away with misdeeds. That is a reminder for those who remember.} Mu'adh then asked, \"Is this for him specifically, O Messenger of Allah, or for all Muslims in general?\" He said, \"For all Muslims in general.\""],[17111,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed a prayer and lengthened its standing, its bowing, and its prostrations. When he finished the prayer, we said, 'O Messenger of God, you performed a prayer and lengthened its standing, its bowing, and its prostrations?' He said, 'It was a prayer of hope and fear. I asked my Lord for three things, and He gave me two and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to set over my community an enemy from other than them who would uproot them, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to destroy them with a drought year, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to make their violence among themselves, but He withheld that from me.'"],[17112,"One day the Messenger of God ﷺ performed a prayer and lengthened its standing, its bowing, and its prostrations. When he finished, I said, 'O Messenger of God, you performed a prayer and lengthened its standing, its bowing, and its prostrations.' He said, 'It was a prayer of hope and fear. I asked my Lord in it for three things, and He gave me two and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to set over my community an enemy from other than them who would uproot them, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to set over them a drought year that would destroy them with hunger, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to make their violence among themselves, but He withheld that from me and kept it away from me.'"],[17113,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Among the things I fear most for my community are three: the slip of a scholar, the disputation of a hypocrite using the Quran, and a worldly life that is opened up for you.'"],[17114,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, 'The virtue of the congregational prayer over the prayer of a man alone is twenty-five.'"],[17115,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, 'Two men among the Children of Israel traced their lineages in the time of Moses ﷺ , one of them a Muslim and the other a polytheist. The polytheist traced his lineage and said, \"I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so,\" until he counted nine forefathers. Then he said to his companion, \"Trace your lineage, may you have no mother.\" He said, \"I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so, and I disavow whoever is beyond that.\" Then Moses called out among the people and gathered them, then said, \"Judgment has been given between you two. As for you, who traced your lineage to nine forefathers, you will be the tenth of them in the Fire. As for the one who traced his lineage to his two parents, you are a man of the people of Islam.\"'"],[17116,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Two men among the Children of Israel traced their lineages, one of them a Muslim and the other a disbeliever. The disbeliever said, \"Trace your lineage.\" The disbeliever traced his lineage to nine forefathers, and the Muslim said, \"I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so, and I disavow whoever is above them.\" Then the caller of Moses ﷺ went out: \"O you two who traced your lineages, I have judged between you. As for you, O disbeliever, you traced your lineage to nine forefathers, so you are the tenth of them in the Fire. As for you, O Muslim, you limited yourself to two Muslim parents, so you are from the people of Islam and are disavowed of whoever is besides them.\"'"],[17117,"Two men exchanged insults in the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and there were two men with him. One of them became angry until he began to writhe because of anger. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'I know a word that, if he said it, would remove what is in him of anger.' I drew near to him and said, 'O Prophet of God, what is it, O Prophet?' I wanted to know [the word for] anger. I drew near to him and said, 'O Prophet of God, what is it, O Prophet of God?' I wanted to know whether it was specific to him or general for the believers. He said, 'O God, I seek refuge in You from Satan the accursed.' I drew near to the man and said it to him, but he did not say it, and he only increased in anger."],[17118,"Two men exchanged insults in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and one of them became severely angry. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'I know a word that, if he said it, God would remove from him what he feels.' It was said to the Prophet ﷺ, 'What is it?' He said, 'O God, I seek refuge in You from Satan the accursed.'"],[17119,"Two men exchanged insults in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and one of them became angry. He said, 'I know a word that, if he said it, his anger would go away: I seek refuge in God from Satan the accursed.'"],[17120,"Two men exchanged insults in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and one of them became severely angry, until I imagined that his nose was writhing. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'I know a word that, if this angry man said it, God would remove it from him: I seek refuge in God from Satan the accursed.'"],[17121,"The Prophet ﷺ was delayed from the dawn prayer with us until the sun was almost upon us. Then he came out and prayed with us, and he made his prayer brief. Then he turned away and faced us and said, 'Stay in your places. Let me inform you what delayed me from you today in this prayer. In this night of mine I prayed as much as God willed, then sleep overcame my eyes and I slept. I saw my Lord, exalted is He, in the best and most beautiful form. He said, \"O Muhammad.\" I said, \"At Your service, O Lord.\" He said, \"What does the highest assembly dispute about?\" I said, \"I do not know, O Lord.\" Then He said, \"O Muhammad.\" I said, \"At Your service, O Lord.\" He said, \"What does the highest assembly dispute about?\" I said, \"I do not know.\" He placed His palm between my shoulders, and I felt the coolness of His fingertips between my breasts, and I came to know everything and perceived it. Then He said, \"O Muhammad.\" I said, \"At Your service, O Lord.\" He said, \"What does the highest assembly dispute about?\" I said, \"About expiations.\" He said, \"What are they?\" I said, \"Walking on foot to the Friday prayers, completing ablution in the cold, and degrees.\" He said, \"What are those?\" I said, \"Feeding food, gentle speech, and praying at night while people sleep.\" He said, \"Ask.\" I said, \"O God, I ask You for good deeds, abandonment of evil acts, love of the poor, and that You forgive me and have mercy on me. When You intend a trial among Your creation, save me to You without being tried. I ask You for Your love, the love of those who love You, and the love of an action that brings me near to Your love.\"'"],[17122,"I went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the expedition of Tabuk. I saw a private moment and seized it, so I urged my camel toward him until I drew alongside him. I said, 'O Messenger of God, teach me a deed that will admit me to the Garden.' He said, 'You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for whomever God makes it easy. You worship God and do not associate anything with Him, you establish the obligatory prayer, you pay the obligatory zakat, and you fast Ramadan.' Then he moved on and I moved on."],[17123,"I went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk. I saw a secluded spot and seized the opportunity, so I urged my camel toward him until I came alongside him. I said, \"O Messenger of God, teach me a deed that will admit me to Paradise.\" He said, \"You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom God makes it easy: that you worship God and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, give the obligatory zakat, and fast Ramadan.\" Then he rode on and I rode on."],[17124,"I went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk. I saw a secluded spot and seized the opportunity, so I urged my camel toward him until I came alongside him. I said, \"O Messenger of God, teach me a deed that will admit me to Paradise.\" He said, \"You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom God makes it easy: that you worship God and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, give the obligatory zakat, and fast Ramadan.\" Then he rode on and I rode on."],[17125,"I went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk. I saw a secluded spot and seized the opportunity, so I urged my camel toward him until I came alongside him. I said, \"O Messenger of God, teach me a deed that will admit me to Paradise.\" He said, \"You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom God makes it easy: that you worship God and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, give the obligatory zakat, and fast Ramadan.\" Then he rode on and I rode on."],[17126,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise and keep me far from the Fire.\" He said, \"You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom God makes it easy: that you worship God and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, give the obligatory zakat, and fast Ramadan. And if you wish, I will tell you of the gates of goodness.\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"Fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and a man's standing in the depths of the night seeking the face of God.\" He said: Then he recited this verse: {Their sides forsake their beds}."],[17127,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise and keep me far from the Fire.\" He said, \"You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom God makes it easy: that you worship God and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, give the obligatory zakat, and fast Ramadan. And if you wish, I will tell you of the gates of goodness.\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"Fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and a man's standing in the depths of the night seeking the face of God.\" He said: Then he recited this verse: {Their sides forsake their beds}."],[17128,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Yemen. I said, \"O Messenger of God, advise me.\" He said, \"You must have good character, for the best of people in character are the best of them in religion.\""],[17129,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, advise me.\" He said, \"Fear God wherever you are, and follow up a bad deed with a good deed that will erase it, and treat people with good character.\""],[17130,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, advise me.\" He said, \"Fear God wherever you are.\" I said, \"Tell me more.\" He said, \"Follow up a bad deed with a good deed that will erase it, and treat people with good character.\""],[17131,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, advise me.\" He said, \"Fear God wherever you are.\" I said, \"Tell me more.\" He said, \"Follow up a bad deed with a good deed that will erase it.\" I said, \"Tell me more.\" He said, \"Treat people with good character.\""],[17132,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"There are no two Muslims who lose three children but that God will admit their parents to Paradise through the abundance of His mercy.\" They said, \"And two, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"And two.\" They said, \"And one, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"And one.\" Then he narrated that \"the miscarried fetus will drag its mother by its umbilical cord to Paradise.\""],[17133,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"There are no two Muslim spouses who lose three children but that God will admit their parents to Paradise through the abundance of His mercy.\" I said, \"What do you think if they are two?\" He said, \"And two.\" I said, \"What do you think if it is one?\" He said, \"And one.\" Then he said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, the miscarried fetus will drag its mother by its umbilical cord to Paradise when she seeks reward for it.\""],[17134,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The one with three is assured.\" Mu'adh b. Jabal said, \"And two, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"And the one with two.\""],[17135,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There are no two Muslim parents who lose three children in Islam before they reach maturity except that Allah will admit them to Paradise by the virtue of His mercy toward them.” Mu'adh said: I said, “O Messenger of Allah, and two?” He said, “And two.” I said, “And one?” He said, “And one, to the point that a miscarried fetus will drag its mother by its umbilical cord if she seeks reward for it.”"],[17136,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise.” He said, “Excellent, excellent! You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom Allah makes it easy: worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, and pay the obligatory zakah. Shall I not guide you to the gates of goodness? Shall I not guide you to the head of the matter, its pillar, and the peak of its hump? As for the head of the matter, it is Islam; whoever submits is safe. As for its pillar, it is prayer. As for the peak of its hump, it is jihad in the way of Allah. Shall I not guide you to the gates of goodness? Fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and a servant’s standing in the depths of the night.” Then he recited this verse: {Their sides forsake their beds} (Q 32:16). “Shall I not inform you of what is more controlling than all that?” Then a rider or riders approached, and I thought they would distract the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from me, so I said, “O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Shall I not guide you to what is more controlling than all of that?” He pointed with his hand to his tongue. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, will we be held accountable for what we say?” He said, “May your mother be bereaved of you, O Mu'adh! Do people get thrown into the Fire on their faces except by the harvests of their tongues?”"],[17137,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking him, and it was said to me, “He has gone out.” I went on, and no one I passed but said, “He passed by a while ago.” I found him standing in prayer. When he finished his prayer, I said, “You have prayed a long prayer.” He said, “I prayed with hope and fear. I asked Allah for three things, and He granted me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to destroy my ummah by drowning, and He granted it to me. I asked Him not to give dominance over them to an enemy from outside them, and He granted it to me. I asked Him not to make their harm among themselves, and He refused it to me.”"],[17138,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed a prayer one day and prolonged it. When he finished, I said, “O Messenger of Allah, you prolonged the prayer today.” He said, “I prayed a prayer of hope and fear. I asked Allah three things for my ummah, and He granted me two and refused one. I asked that no enemy from other than them be given power over them, and He granted it to me. I asked that He not destroy them by drowning, and He granted it to me. I asked that He not make their harm among themselves, and He refused it to me.”"],[17139,"Umar was indeed among the people of Paradise. Whatever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw in wakefulness or sleep is true. He said, “While I was in Paradise, I saw therein a dwelling and said, ‘For whom is this?’ It was said, ‘For Umar b. al-Khattab.’”"],[17140,"“By Allah, Umar is in Paradise,” and I would not love to have red camels in exchange for what I said, but you dispersed before I could tell you why I said that. Then he told them: “The dream that the Prophet ﷺ saw concerning Umar.” He said, “And the dream of the Prophet ﷺ is true.”"],[17141,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, to whom should I give from the surplus of what Allah has bestowed upon me?” He said, “Begin with your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, then the nearest and the nearest. And do not forget the neighbors and the one in need.”"],[17142,"“The Quran was sent down from seven gates upon seven letters, all of them healing and sufficient.”"],[17143,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to take from date palms, wheat, barley, and raisins (or he said, from grapes)."],[17144,"“The Prophet ﷺ imposed the tithe on what the sky watered, on what was watered by springs, and on what springs irrigated among grains. As for melons, cucumbers, vegetables, greens, pomegranates, and sugarcane, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has pardoned them.”"],[17145,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever grows a single gray hair in Islam, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever shoots an arrow in the way of Allah, a degree will be raised for him by it.”"],[17146,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever is placed in charge of any affair of the Muslims and hides himself from the weak among the Muslims, Allah will hide Himself from him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[17147,"I was sitting beside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said to me, \"O Mu'adh, do you know what Allah's right upon His servants is?\" I replied, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"To worship Him alone and not associate anything with Him.\" Then he said, \"O Mu'adh, what is the right of the servants upon Allah if they do that?\" I replied, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"That He will not punish them.\""],[17148,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a donkey. He said to me, \"O Mu'adh b. Jabal, what is the right of Allah upon His servants?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"That they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him.\" Then he said to me, \"O Mu'adh, what is the right of the servants upon Allah if they do that?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"That He will not punish them.\""],[17149,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Mu'adh, do you know what the right of Allah upon His servants is?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"That they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. Do you know what the right of the servants upon Allah is if they do that? That He will not punish them.\""],[17150,"'Umar b. al-Khattab went out to the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found Mu'adh b. Jabal weeping at the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"What makes you weep, O Mu'adh?\" He said, \"Something I heard from the occupant of this grave makes me weep.\" He said, \"And what is it?\" He said, \"I heard him say: 'A small amount of showing off is polytheism. Whoever shows enmity to the friends of Allah has declared war on Allah. Allah loves the hidden, pious ones who, when they are absent, are not missed, and when they are present, they are not invited or recognized. Their hearts are lamps of guidance, emerging from every dusty, dark place.'\""],[17151,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ missed him on Friday. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished praying, he came to Mu‘adh and said to him, “O Mu‘adh, why did I not see you?” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, a Jew has against me an uqiyyah of gold, so I set out to come to you, but he detained me from you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “O Mu‘adh, shall I not teach you a supplication with which you may supplicate? Even if you had a debt like Mount Ṣabir, Allah would discharge it for you—and Ṣabir is a mountain in Yemen. So supplicate with it, O Mu‘adh. Say: allāhumma mālika al-mulk, tuʾtī al-mulka man tashāʾu wa-tanziʿu al-mulka mimman tashāʾ, wa-tuʿizzu man tashāʾu wa-tudhillu man tashāʾ, bi-yadika al-khayr, innaka ʿalā kulli shayʾin qadīr. tūliju al-layla fī al-nahār wa-tūliju al-nahāra fī al-layl, wa-tukhriju al-ḥayya mina al-mayyit wa-tukhriju al-mayyita mina al-ḥayy, wa-tarzuqu man tashāʾu bi-ghayri ḥisāb. raḥmāna al-dunyā wa-l-ākhirah wa-raḥīmahuma, tuʿṭī man tashāʾu minhumā wa-tamnaʿu man tashāʾu, irḥamnī raḥmatan tughniynī bihā ʿan raḥmati man siwāk (O Allah, Owner of sovereignty: You give sovereignty to whom You will and You take sovereignty from whom You will; You honor whom You will and You abase whom You will. In Your hand is all good; indeed You are over all things competent. You cause the night to enter into the day and You cause the day to enter into the night; You bring forth the living from the dead and You bring forth the dead from the living; and You provide for whom You will without account [Al Imran 3:26-27]. O Most Merciful of this world and the Hereafter, and their Most Compassionate: You give to whom You will of them and You withhold from whom You will. Have mercy on me with a mercy by which You will make me independent of the mercy of anyone besides You.”)"],[17152,"'Amr b. Bakr b. Bakkar al-Qa'nabi narrated to me: Mujashi' b. 'Amr b. Hassan al-Asadi narrated to us: al-Layth b. Sa'd narrated to us from 'Asim b. 'Umar b. Qatada, from Mahmud b. Labid, from Mu'adh b. Jabal that a son of his died, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to him consoling him for his son. He wrote to him: \"In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to Mu'adh b. Jabal. Peace be upon you. I praise Allah, besides whom there is no god, to you. To proceed: May Allah make your reward great, inspire you with patience, and grant us and you gratitude. For our souls, our wealth, and our families are among Allah's pleasant gifts and His deposited trusts. He lets us enjoy them until a term and takes them back at a known time. We ask Him for gratitude for what He gives and patience when He tests. Your son was among Allah's pleasant gifts and His deposited trusts. Allah let you enjoy him in happiness and joy, and took him from you with a great reward: prayer, mercy, and guidance, if you seek recompense. So be patient, and do not let your anguish nullify your reward, lest you regret. Know that anguish does not bring back the dead nor repel grief. What is to come is as if it has already happened. Peace.\""],[17153,"He used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ, then come to his people and pray with them."],[17154,"While we were traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Where are the foremost?\" They said, \"Some people have gone ahead and some have stayed behind.\" He said, \"Where are the foremost who are engrossed in the remembrance of Allah? Whoever loves to graze in the meadows of Paradise, let him remember Allah often.\" The wording is that of the hadith of 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar b. Aban."],[17155,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever performs these five prayers and fasts the month of Ramadan — I do not know whether he mentioned the zakah of his wealth or not — it is a right upon Allah to forgive him, whether he emigrates or stays where his mother gave birth to him.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I go out and announce it to the people?\" He said, \"No, leave the people to act, for Paradise has one hundred levels; between each two levels is like what is between heaven and earth, and the highest of them is al-Firdaws.\""],[17156,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishes prayer, gives zakah, and fasts Ramadan, it is a right upon Allah to forgive him.\" Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Hisham b. Sa'd."],[17157,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, advise me.\" He said, \"You must fear Allah as much as you can. Remember Allah at every stone and tree. Whatever evil you have done, offer repentance to Allah for it: the secret by secret, and the open by open.\""],[17158,"A man had a claim against me, and I feared him. So I stayed home and remained for two days without going out. Then I went out and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “O Muʿādh, what kept you back?” I said: A man had a right over me; I feared him until I became ashamed, and I disliked that he should meet me. He said: “Shall I not instruct you in some words you can say—if you have debts like mountains, Allah will pay them off for you?” I said: Yes. He said: \"Say: (O Allah, Owner of Sovereignty, You give sovereignty to whom You will and You take sovereignty away from whom You will,’ up to His saying, ‘without reckoning,’ to the end, [Al Imran 3:26-27] Merciful of this world and the Hereafter and Compassionate to them both; You grant of them to whom You will and You withhold of them from whom You will. O Allah, enrich me so that I have no need of poverty, pay off my debt for me, and cause me to die in Your service and in striving in Your path.)\""],[17159,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If a woman knew the right of her husband, she would not sit down as long as his lunch and dinner are present until he finishes.\""],[17160,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Two phrases, one of which has no barrier before the Throne, and the other fills what is between heaven and earth: 'There is no god but Allah' and 'Allah is the Greatest.'\" Ibn 'Umar said to Ibn Abi 'Amra, \"Did you hear him say that?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar wept until his beard was dyed with his tears.\" Then he said, \"They are two phrases that we hold onto and love.\""],[17161,"From Mu'adh."],[17162,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to some Arab villages and ordered me to take the land’s share.” Al-Ashjaʿī said, “meaning the third and the fourth.”"],[17163,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to some Arab villages and ordered me to take the land’s share.” Al-Ashjaʿī said, “meaning the third and the fourth.”"],[17164,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ appointed me over the alms of the Muslims, and I placed it in an upper room.” Then he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[17165,"Muʿādh was in Yemen, and they brought up to him the case of a Jew who died and left a Muslim brother. Muʿādh said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘Islam increases and does not decrease,’ so he made him inherit.”"],[17166,"A man among us died a Jew or a Christian and left a Muslim son. That was brought to Muʿādh’s attention, and he made the son inherit. He said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘Islam increases and does not decrease.’”"],[17167,"And he said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘Islam increases and does not decrease.’” The shaykh said, “ʿAmr b. Kurdī is ʿAmr b. Abī Ḥakīm, from whom Shuʿbah narrated.”"],[17168,"“on my right side since I became Muslim.”"],[17169,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I shall place my intercession for those who die without associating anything with God.”"],[17170,"From Muʿādh b. Jabal: When the Prophet ﷺ traveled, the Emigrants used to be nearest to him. One night we missed him from his place, and we feared something had happened to the Messenger of God ﷺ, so we went looking for him. We found a sound like the rumbling of a mill, and we met him returning. I said, “We missed you, O Messenger of God, and feared something had happened to you.” He said, “No, but a messenger came to me from my Lord and gave me the choice between admitting half of my community to Paradise or intercession, and I chose intercession.” We said, “We ask you by the right of Islam and the right of our companionship that you make us among them.” He said, “Then you are among them.” Then two men came and said the same, and he said to them, “Yes.” Then another came, until the people were numerous, and he said, “I shall place in my intercession whoever of my community dies without associating anything with God.”"],[17171,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Satan is the wolf of man, like the wolf of sheep, seizing the stray and isolated one. Beware of the ravines; keep to the main body, the congregation, and the mosques.”"],[17172,"The Prophet of God ﷺ used to say, “Satan is the wolf of man, like the wolf of sheep, seizing the stray, the outlying, and the remote sheep.”"],[17173,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There is no supplication dearer to God for a servant to call upon Him with than saying: O God, I ask You for well-being”—he said, or he said, “pardon—in this world and the Hereafter.”"],[17174,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: There is no supplication more beloved to God for a servant to call upon Him with than to say: O God, I ask You for well-being. He said, or he said: safety in this world and the Hereafter."],[17175,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ did not say anything to me about the shortfalls of cattle.”"],[17176,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no divorce over what one does not possess, and no manumission over what one does not possess.”"],[17177,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no divorce for what one does not own, and no freeing for one who does not own.”"],[17178,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No human being has performed a deed more saving for him from God’s punishment than the remembrance of God.” They said: Not even jihad in the path of God? He said: “Not even, unless you strike with your sword until it breaks,” three times."],[17179,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not hasten the affliction before it descends, and draw near and be steadfast; for if you hasten it before it descends, the flood will surely sweep you away here and here.”"],[17180,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If I adopt a pulpit, my forefather Abraham adopted it; and if I adopt the staff, my forefather Abraham ﷺ adopted it.”"],[17181,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If slavery were to remain upon anyone of the Arabs, it would today be only captivity or ransom.”"],[17182,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is nothing due on shortfalls.”"],[17183,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever equips a warrior or looks after his family with good, he is with us.”"],[17184,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, men who are neither prophets nor martyrs will have pulpits of light placed for them on the Day of Resurrection, their faces being light, and they will be safe on the Day of Resurrection from the greatest terror.” A man said: O Prophet of God, who are those? He said: “They are those who separate from their tribes, loving one another for God.”"],[17185,"So narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ that we may benefit from. He said: Yes, and what hour of lying is this? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever dies while certain of three things—that God is true, that the Hour is coming, and that God will resurrect those in the graves—. And Ibn Sīrīn said: I forgot whether he said “enters Paradise” or “is saved from the Fire.”"],[17186,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever dies without associating anything with Allah, Paradise becomes guaranteed for him.\""],[17187,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, between the edge of the Fire and its bottom there is a rock whose weight equals seven pregnant camels with their fat, their flesh, and their offspring. It falls into it from the edge of the Fire until it reaches its bottom over seventy autumns.\""],[17188,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent him to Yemen, he said to him: \"How will you judge if a case comes to you?\" He said: \"I will judge by the Book of Allah.\" He said: \"And if it is not in the Book of Allah?\" He said: \"Then by the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"And if it is not in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"I will exert my own judgment and spare no effort.\" He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck his chest and said: \"Praise be to Allah Who has guided the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to that which pleases the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[17189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me as a zakat collector to the people of Yemen and ordered me to take from cattle: from every thirty a tabi' — the tabi' being a one-year-old — or a tabi'ah, and from every forty a musinnah. He said: They proposed that I take what is between forty and fifty, between sixty and seventy, and between eighty and ninety; but I refused them and said to them: 'Until I ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that.' So I came and informed the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered me to take from every thirty a tabi', from forty a musinnah, from sixty two tabi'ahs, from seventy a musinnah and a tabi', from eighty two musinnahs, from ninety three tabi's, from one hundred a musinnah and two tabi's, from one hundred and ten two musinnahs and a tabi', and from one hundred and twenty three musinnahs or four tabi's. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me not to take anything from what falls between those numbers until it reaches a musinnah or a jadha'. He also asserted that the awqas (gaps between the specified numbers) have no obligatory zakat."],[17190,"The people said: 'O Mu'adh, supplicate to Allah to lift this punishment from us.' He said: 'It is not a punishment, but it is the call of your Prophet and the death of the righteous before you, and a martyrdom by which Allah singles out whomever He wills among you.'"],[17191,"When death came to him, he wept. They said: 'What makes you weep?' He said: 'By Allah, I do not weep out of fear of death, nor over a worldly life I leave behind me. But I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"They are only two handfuls: a handful in the Fire and a handful in Paradise, and I do not know in which of the two handfuls I will be.\"'"],[17192,"I witnessed al-Hasan at the time of his death while he was making his will. He said to the scribe: 'Write: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is what al-Hasan testified. He testified that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, truthfully from his heart. Whoever testifies to this at his death truthfully will enter Paradise.' I heard that from Mu'adh b. Jabal; he enjoined it at his death, narrating it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[17193,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, by the One Who sent you with the truth, something arises in my chest such that being a burnt coal is dearer to me than speaking of it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Praise be to Allah. Satan has despaired of being worshipped in this land of mine, but he is content with the trivial acts among your deeds.'"],[17194,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Six are among the signs of the Hour: my death, the conquest of Jerusalem, a death that takes people like the quza' that afflicts sheep, a man being given a thousand dinars and being displeased with them, a tribulation whose fear enters the heart of every Muslim, and the Byzantines invading us and marching with eighty banners.'"],[17195,"From Makhul, who raised it to Mu'adh b. Jabal, and Mu'adh raised it to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: 'Keep your children, your disputes, your legal penalties, your buying and your selling away from your mosques. Perfume them on the day of your gathering, and place your purification facilities at their doors.'"],[17196,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Obey every ruler, pray behind every imam, and do not revile any of my Companions.'"],[17197,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Shall I not guide you to a treasure among the treasures of Paradise?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah (There is no might nor power except with Allah).'"],[17198,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was on a camel with a packsaddle fastened on it. He said, “O Mu’adh.” I replied, “At your service, happily.” He said, “Do you know what is God’s right upon His servants?” I said, “God and His Messenger know best.” He said, “God’s right upon them is that they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him.” Then he said, “Do you know what is the servants’ right upon God if they do that?” I said, “God and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Their right upon Him, if they do that, is that He forgives them and admits them to Paradise.”"],[17199,"I said, “O Messenger of God, I have come from a people who prostrate to one another. Should we not do that for you?” He said, “If I were to command a human being to prostrate to a human being, I would command women to prostrate to their husbands.”"],[17200,"Mu’adh b. Jabal said: I said, “O Messenger of God, give me counsel.” He said, “Worship God as though you see Him, count yourself among the dead, remember God ﷻ by every rock and every tree, and if you commit a bad deed, then perform beside it a good deed: the secret for the secret and the open for the open.” Then he said, “Shall I not tell you what gives a person most control over that?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He took hold of the tip of his tongue. I said, “O Messenger of God, it is as if he is taking it lightly.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “And does anything cast people upon their faces into the Fire except this?” And he took hold of the tip of his tongue."],[17201,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent him to Yemen. When he came to them, he said, “O people, I am the messenger of the Messenger of God ﷺ to you. He informs you that the return is to God: to a Garden or a Fire, eternal abiding and no death, and residence and no departure.”"],[17202,"From Ibn Ishaq in naming those who attended Badr: Mu’adh b. ’Afra’, and he is Mu’adh b. al-Harith b. Rifa’a b. Sawda’ b. Malik b. Ghanm b. Malik b. al-Najjar. ’Afra’ is his mother, and she is the mother of ’Awf and Mu’awwidh. All of them attended Badr. ’Afra’ is the daughter of ’Ubayd b. Tha’laba b. Ghanm b. Malik b. al-Najjar."],[17203,"He was circumambulating the House, and he circumambulated after ’Asr and did not pray. A man from Quraysh said to him, “What prevents you from praying?” He said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbid prayer after two prayers: after Subh until the sun rises, and after ’Asr until the sun sets.”"],[17204,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There is no prayer after two prayers: after the morning prayer until the sun rises, and after ’Asr until the sun sets.”"],[17205,"From his grandfather Mu’adh, a man of Banu Taym, that he was circumambulating after ’Asr with Mu’adh b. ’Afra’ and did not pray. I said, “What prevented you from praying?” He said, “The Prophet ﷺ forbade prayer in two hours: after Subh until the sun rises, and after ’Asr until the sun sets.”"],[17206,"It is said: Yazid b. Hushaym b. al-Khazraj attended Badr, killed Abu Jahl, and ’Ikrima b. Abi Jahl cut off his hand. Then he lived until the time of ’Uthman ؓ."],[17207,"While I was standing in the ranks on the day of Badr, I looked to my right and left and found myself between two young boys of the Ansar, of recent teeth. I wished I were between stronger men than them. One of them nudged me and said, “Uncle, do you know Abu Jahl?” I said, “Yes, and what do you need with him, nephew?” He said, “I have been told that he insults the Messenger of God ﷺ. By Him in whose hand is my soul, if I see him, my blackness will not part from his blackness until the more hasty of us dies.” I marveled at that. Then the other nudged me and said the same to me. It was not long before I saw Abu Jahl moving among the people. I said to them, “This is your companion you ask about.” They rushed at him with their swords and struck him until they killed him. Then they went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him. He said, “Which of you killed him?” Each of them said, “I killed him.” He said, “Did you wipe your swords?” They said, “No.” He looked at the two swords and said, “Both of you killed him.” He ruled his spoils for Mu’adh b. ’Amr b. al-Jamuh. They were Mu’adh b. ’Afra’ and Mu’adh b. ’Amr b. al-Jamuh."],[17208,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say in his sermon at al-Banawa or al-Nabawa near al-Ta’if: “You will soon know the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire, or the best of you from the worst of you.” Nafi’ said, “I do not know except that he said, ‘the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire.’” A man said, “By what, O Messenger of God?” He said, “By good praise and bad praise. You are witnesses of one another.”"],[17209,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “When you give names, make them express servitude.”"],[17210,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade sitting with the legs drawn up and wrapped in a cloth on Friday while the imam is delivering the khutbah."],[17211,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade sitting with the legs drawn up and wrapped in a cloth on Friday."],[17212,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever gives up fine clothing while able to afford it, out of humility for Allah (Mighty and Majestic), Allah will call him before the heads of all creatures on the Day of Resurrection and let him choose from the garments of faith to wear whichever he wishes.\""],[17213,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever gives up fine clothing out of humility while able to afford it, Allah will call him before the heads of all creatures on the Day of Resurrection and let him choose from the garments of Paradise to wear whichever he wishes.\""],[17214,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever eats food and says: 'Praise be to Allah who fed me this and provided it for me without any strength or power on my part,' Allah forgives his previous sins. And whoever puts on a garment and says: 'Praise be to Allah who clothed me with this and provided it for me without any strength or power on my part,' Allah forgives his previous sins.\""],[17215,"A man came to a gathering in which the Prophet ﷺ was present and said: \"Al-salām ʿalaykum.\" He replied to his greeting and said: \"Ten good deeds.\" Then another came and said: \"Al-salām ʿalaykum wa raḥmatullāh.\" He said: \"Twenty.\" Then another came and said: \"Al-salām ʿalaykum wa raḥmatullāh wa barakātuh.\" He said: \"Forty.\" And he said: \"This is how the merit increases.\""],[17216,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah (Exalted is He) said: 'My servant does not remember Me within himself except that I remember him in an assembly of My angels, and he does not remember Me in an assembly except that I remember him in the highest company.'\""],[17217,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The utmost coarseness, disbelief, and hypocrisy belongs to one who hears Allah's caller calling to prayer and inviting to success but does not respond to him.\""],[17218,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Enough misery and failure for a believer is to hear the mu'adhdhin calling the iqamah for prayer and not respond to him.\""],[17219,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever recites 'Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad' ten times, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.\" ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb said: \"Then we should increase it, O Messenger of Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah is more abundant and better.\""],[17220,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever recites a thousand verses in the path of Allah will be recorded on the Day of Resurrection with the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous—and how excellent are those as companions.\""],[17221,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever recites a thousand verses in the path of Allah, Allah will record him with the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous.\""],[17222,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever stands guard behind the Muslims in the path of God as a volunteer, not compelled by any authority, will not see the Fire with his own eyes except as the fulfillment of the oath, for God, exalted is He, says: {And there is none of you but will pass over it}.\""],[17223,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Remembrance surpasses spending in the path of God by a hundredfold.\""],[17224,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"Remembrance in the path of God is multiplied above spending by seven hundredfold.\""],[17225,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, that a man asked him: \"Which of the mujahidin has the greatest reward?\" He said: \"The one of them who remembers God the most.\" He said: \"And which of the fasting people has the greatest reward with God?\" He said: \"The one of them who remembers God the most.\" Then he mentioned prayer, zakat, Hajj, and charity, and in all of that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one of them who remembers God the most.\" Then Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said to Umar ؓ: \"O Abu Hafs, those who remember God have gone away with every good.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed.\""],[17226,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"It is a duty upon one who leaves a gathering to greet them, and a duty upon one who comes to a gathering to greet.\" A man stood up while the Messenger of God ﷺ was speaking and did not greet, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"How quickly he forgot!\""],[17227,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever builds a building without wrongdoing or aggression, or plants a tree without wrongdoing or aggression, will have a continuous reward as long as anyone of God's creation ﷻ benefits from it.\""],[17228,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever builds a building without wrongdoing or aggression will have its reward as long as anyone of the Most Merciful's creation ﷻ benefits from it.\""],[17229,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he said: \"Whoever gives for God's sake, withholds for God's sake, loves for God's sake, and hates for God's sake has completed his faith.\""],[17230,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"The best of virtues is that you maintain ties with one who cuts you off, give to one who deprives you, and forgive one who insults you.\""],[17231,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he said: \"Whoever suppresses anger while able to carry it out will be called by God before the heads of all creatures and given the choice of any of the wide-eyed maidens he wishes. And whoever refrains from wearing fine clothes while able to do so out of humility for God ﷻ will be called by God before the heads of all creatures and given the choice of any of the robes of faith he wishes.\""],[17232,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever suppresses anger while able to carry it out, God will let him choose any of the wide-eyed maidens on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever gives up a garment of beauty while able to wear it, God will clothe him with the cloak of faith. Whoever arranges the marriage of a servant of God, God will place the crown of sovereignty on his head.\""],[17233,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever steps over the Muslims on Friday has taken a bridge to Hell.\""],[17234,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he used to say: \"The one who laughs in the prayer, the one who turns around, and the one who cracks his fingers are all of one rank.\""],[17235,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one who turns around in the prayer, the one who laughs, and the one who cracks his fingers are all of one rank.\""],[17236,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"That I should see off a warrior in the path of God and help him with an early morning departure or an evening departure is more beloved to me than the world and all that it contains.\""],[17237,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he commanded his companions to go on a military expedition. Then he saw a man who had stayed behind. The man said: \"Until I pray the noon prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then greet him and bid him farewell, and he may supplicate for me with a supplication that will be a precedence on the Day of Resurrection.\" So when the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed, the man came forward greeting him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Do you know by how much your companions have preceded you?\" He said: \"Yes, they have preceded me by their early morning departure yesterday and today.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, they have preceded you by a distance greater than what is between the two easts and the two wests in excellence.\""],[17238,"That he asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the best of faith. He said: \"The best of faith is that you love for the sake of God, hate for the sake of God, and set your tongue to work in the remembrance of God.\" He said: \"And what else, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"And that you love for people what you love for yourself, hate for them what you hate for yourself, and that you say what is good or remain silent.\""],[17239,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"Shall I inform you why God named Abraham His intimate friend who fulfilled? Because he used to say every morning and every evening: 'Glory be to God when you enter the evening and when you rise in the morning,' until he completed the verse.\""],[17240,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he used to say: \"The verse of glory: To God belongs praise, who has not taken a son, and has no partner in dominion, and has no protector out of weakness; and magnify Him with all magnificence.\""],[17241,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The verse of glory is: 'And say: Praise be to God, who has not taken a son, and has no partner in dominion, and has no protector out of weakness; and magnify Him with all magnificence.'\""],[17242,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Mount these animals sound and dismount from them sound.\""],[17243,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a group of people who were standing on their mounts and riding beasts. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Mount them sound, dismount from them sound, and do not make them chairs for your conversations and gatherings. For perhaps a mounted beast is better than its rider and more remembering of God than him.\""],[17244,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever protects a believer from a hypocrite who backbites him, God will send an angel to protect his flesh on the Day of Resurrection from the fire of Hell. And whoever slanders a Muslim with something intending to disgrace him by it, God will detain him on the bridge of Hell until he comes out of what he said.\""],[17245,"I went on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ, the expedition of such and such. The people cramped the campsites and cut off the road. So the Messenger of God ﷺ sent a caller who announced among the people: 'Whoever cramps a campsite or cuts off a road, there is no military expedition for him.'"],[17246,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he sent a caller to announce: “Whoever constricts a dwelling place or cuts off a road, there is no jihad for him.”"],[17247,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When you hear the muezzin repeating the call to prayer, say what he says.”"],[17248,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There are servants whom Allah will neither speak to, purify, nor look at on the Day of Judgment.\" They asked, \"Who are those, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Those who disrespect their parents, those who are desirous to be away from them, those who disown their children, and those who are ungrateful to the people who have shown them kindness and disassociate themselves from them.\""],[17249,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God has servants whom He will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them, and for them is a painful punishment.” It was said, “Who are they, O Messenger of God?” He said, “One who disavows his parents and turns away from them, one who disavows his child, and a man upon whom a people bestowed favor but he denied their favor and disavowed them.”"],[17250,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God has servants whom He will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them, and for them is a painful punishment.” It was said, “Who are they, O Messenger of God?” He said, “One who disavows his parents and turns away from them, one who disavows his child, and a man upon whom a people bestowed favor but he denied their favor and disavowed them.”"],[17251,"The Prophet ﷺ sent a military expedition, and a woman came to him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my husband goes out on this expedition, and I offer his prayers and fast according to his fasting, and I worship through his worship. So guide me to an action by which I can attain the same reward as him.\" He said, \"Can you stand in prayer continuously without sleeping, and fast without breaking your fast, and remember Allah without forgetting?\" She replied, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there anyone who can do that?\" He said, \"Even if you were to be confined and tied, you would not be able to attain even a tenth of that.\""],[17252,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “My husband has gone out as a warrior in the path of God, and I used to follow his prayer when he prayed and his actions. So tell me of a deed that will make me reach his deed until he returns.” The Prophet ﷺ said to her, “Can you stand without sitting, remember without slackening, and fast without breaking the fast until he returns?” She said, “I cannot do that, O Messenger of God.” He said, “By Him in whose hand is my soul, if you did that, you would not reach a tenth of his deed until he returns.”"],[17253,"On the authority of the Prophet, ﷺ , he said, \"Whoever sits in his place of prayer from the dawn prayer until he prays the forenoon prayer, he will only say what is good. His sins will be forgiven, even if they are more than the foam of the sea.\" And the wording belongs to the Hadith of Rishdeen."],[17254,"It is reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \"Whoever recites the beginning of Surat al-Kahf and its end, it will be a light for him from his feet to his head; and whoever recites all of it, it will be a light for him from his feet to his head, from the earth to the sky.\""],[17255,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.”"],[17256,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever says ‘Glory be to God, the Magnificent’ a tree is planted for him in Paradise. And whoever recites the Qur’an, masters it, and acts upon what is in it, God will clothe his parents on the Day of Resurrection with a crown whose light is more beautiful than this moon.”"],[17257,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever teaches knowledge, for him is a reward as long as anyone acts upon it, without diminishing the reward of the one who acts.”"],[17258,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever is dutiful to his parents, blessedness be to him; God will increase his lifespan.”"],[17259,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ give the grandmother a sixth."],[17260,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “There is no servant who is entrusted with a flock and is deceitful toward it except that he enters the Fire.”"],[17261,"I heard it said of these non-Arabs: “We were commanded that if one of us dropped a morsel, he should pick it up, remove whatever harm was on it, and eat it, and not leave it for Satan.”"],[17262,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"If a morsel of any of you falls, let him remove any harm from it and eat it, and not leave it for the Shaytan.\""],[17263,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When a morsel of any of you falls, let him remove whatever harm is on it and eat it.”"],[17264,"Regarding the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was accepting the people’s pledge of allegiance: “He did not pledge them upon death; he pledged them upon not fleeing, and he used to shake hands with women from beneath the garment.”"],[17265,"He has a place of refuge. I shall surely narrate to you a hadith that I have not narrated to you: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There is no servant whom Allah has placed in charge of a flock and who dies while being dishonest to it, except that Allah has forbidden Paradise to him.”"],[17266,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Any man whom Allah has placed in charge of a flock and who dies while being dishonest to it, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him.”"],[17267,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah will not place a servant in charge of a flock who dies while being dishonest to it, except that Allah has forbidden Paradise to him.”"],[17268,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The punishment of this community is the sword, and their appointed time is the Hour, and the Hour is more calamitous and bitter.”"],[17269,"“The Prophet ﷺ gave the grandmother one-sixth.”"],[17270,"Who knows the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the grandfather? Maʿqil b. Yasar said: “He ruled for him one-sixth.”"],[17271,"Who knows what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled regarding the grandfather? Maʿqil b. Yasar said to him: “I do.” He said: “How much is for him?” He said: “One-sixth.” He said: “Who is with him?” He said: “I do not know.” He said: “May you not know.”"],[17272,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the grandfather one-sixth.”"],[17273,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in the case of a grandfather among us for one-sixth.”"],[17274,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, I take a goat to slaughter it and then I take pity on it.” He said: “If you take pity on it, Allah will take pity on you.”"],[17275,"From Al-Hasan regarding the saying of Allah, the Exalted: {So do not prevent them from remarrying their husbands when they have agreed between themselves on reasonable terms}, he said: Ma'qil b. Yasar narrated to me that it was revealed concerning him. He said: I married a sister of mine to a man, and he divorced her, then left her until when her waiting period ended, he proposed to her. I said, 'I married you to her, prepared her trousseau for you, and honored you, yet you divorced her. Then you come to propose to her? No, by Allah, she will never return to you, ever.' He was a man of no harm, and she wanted to go back to him, so Allah revealed this verse. So I said, 'Now I will do it, O Messenger of Allah.' So I married her to him."],[17276,"From my right, and I gave her in marriage."],[17277,"So he narrated to him and asked him and was courteous to him. While they were thus, Ma'qil said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no governor who is put in charge of any affair of the Muslims and does not sincerely advise those behind him but Allah will cast him into Hell on his face on the day when Allah gathers the first and the last.'"],[17278,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Al-Madinah is my place of emigration and my resting place in the earth. It is a duty upon my ummah to honor my neighbors as long as they avoid major sins. Whoever among them does not do that, Allah will give him to drink from the pus of the people of Hell.' We said: 'O Abu Yasar, what is the pus of the people of Hell?' He said: 'The extract of the people of the Fire.'"],[17279,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Muslims protect each other, their blood is equal, and a believer is not killed for an unbeliever, nor is a person with a covenant killed within their covenant.\""],[17280,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever Allah places in charge of a flock and he dies while he is deceiving it, Allah will certainly forbid Paradise to him.'"],[17281,"'I will tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever is put in charge of a flock and does not surround them with sincere advice will not find the scent of Paradise, and indeed its scent can be detected from a distance of a hundred years' journey.' So Ibn Ziyad said: 'Would that you had told me this before now.' He said: 'Now, were it not for the state I am in, I would not have told you this.'"],[17282,"'Ma'qil, I will tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. If I knew that I had any life left, I would not have told it to you. I heard him say: 'There is no servant whom Allah places in charge of a flock who dies on the day he dies while he is deceiving his flock but Allah will forbid Paradise to him.'' And the wording is that of 'Ali b. al-Ja'd."],[17283,"That she wished to return to him, but Ma'qil prevented her, so Allah, the Exalted, revealed concerning that: {And when you divorce women and they have fulfilled their term, do not prevent them from remarrying their husbands when they have agreed between themselves on reasonable terms}."],[17284,"Ma'qil said: 'I do not think I will survive what I am in, but I will tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'And what is it?' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no one who is placed in charge of a flock and dies on the day he dies while he is deceiving it but he will not find the scent of Paradise,' or he said: 'he will be from the people of the Fire.' He said: 'Would that you had told me this hadith before this day?' He said: 'Were it not for what I am in, I would not have told you.'"],[17285,"That he married his sister to a man in the time of the Prophet ﷺ. She remained with him as long as she did, then he divorced her with a single divorce and did not take her back until the waiting period ended. Then he desired her and she desired him. He proposed to her along with the other suitors. So [Ma'qil] said to him: 'O you wretch! I honored you with her and married you to her, then you divorced her. By Allah, she will never return to you, ever, for the rest of your life.' But Allah knew his need for her and her need for him, so Allah, the Exalted, revealed: {And when you divorce women and they have fulfilled their term, do not prevent them from remarrying their husbands when they have agreed between themselves on reasonable terms} to the end of the verse. When Ma'qil heard it, he said: 'I hear and obey my Lord.' Then he called him and said: 'I will marry you to her and honor you.'"],[17286,"'Indeed, I will tell you a hadith that, were it not for the state I am in, I would not have reported. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever Allah places in charge of a flock and does not surround those behind it with sincere advice is among the people of the Fire.' He said: 'Should this not have been before now?'"],[17287,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever enters into one of the prices of the believers in order to raise it against them, it is a duty upon Allah to punish him in the great fire of Hell.'"],[17288,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whoever enters into any of the prices of the Muslims in order to raise it against them, it is a right upon God to cast him into a great part of the Fire.”"],[17289,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast.”"],[17290,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came upon a man who was having himself cupped while he was fasting, and he said, “The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast.”"],[17291,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade the woman who attaches hair extensions and the one for whom it is done."],[17292,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed the woman who attaches hair extensions and the one who requests it."],[17293,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “That one of you be stabbed in the head with an iron needle is better for him than touching a woman who is not lawful for him.”"],[17294,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “That a man be stabbed in the head with an iron needle is better for him than touching a woman who is not lawful for him.”"],[17295,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Worship during turmoil is like emigration to me.”"],[17296,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Deeds during turmoil are like emigration to me.”"],[17297,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Worship during turmoil is like emigration to me.”"],[17298,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Worship during turmoil is like emigration to me.”"],[17299,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Worship during tribulation is like emigration to me.”"],[17300,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Worship during tribulation is like emigration to me.”"],[17301,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Worship during turmoil or tribulation is like emigration to me.”"],[17302,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Two groups of my community do not receive my intercession: a tyrannical, oppressive ruler, and one extreme in religion who bears witness against them and then disavows them.”"],[17303,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Two men of my community do not receive my intercession: a tyrannical, oppressive ruler, and another extreme in religion, deviating from it.”"],[17304,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “For everything there is a key, and the key of the heavens is saying ‘There is no god but God.’”"],[17305,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Any people among whom the call to prayer is sounded in the morning are in God’s protection until evening, and any people among whom the call to prayer is sounded in the evening are in God’s protection until morning.”"],[17306,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Cupping on Tuesday, on the seventeenth of the month, is a remedy for a year’s ailment.”"],[17307,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Your Lord, the Exalted, says, \"O Son of Adam, devote yourself to My worship, and I will fill your heart with contentment and your hands with provision. O Son of Adam, do not distance yourself from Me, for then I will fill your heart with poverty and your hands with occupation.\""],[17308,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “God does not listen to anything as He listens to the muezzins’ call to prayer and a beautiful voice reciting the Qur’an.”"],[17309,"While on the road, I saw the like of it and picked it up and moved it aside. He took my hand and said, “O son of my brother, what made you do what you did?” I said, “O uncle, I saw you do something and I did the same.” He said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘Whoever removes an annoyance from the path of the Muslims, a good deed is recorded for him, and whoever has a good deed accepted from him enters Paradise.’” This is the wording of the hadith of al-‘Abbas al-‘Anbari."],[17310,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ conquered Khaybar, the people captured donkeys and plundered them until the cooking pots boiled over. The Messenger of God ﷺ came, and it was said that the people’s donkeys had been slaughtered. The Prophet ﷺ forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys, and a man began to overturn his cooking vessel with the head of his bow or the post of his house."],[17311,"We were in Madinah, and it had abundant fruit, and the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade fadikh (a drink made from dates)."],[17312,"Wine was forbidden while we were drinking fadikh, and I began pouring it out, saying, “This is the last time for wine.”"],[17313,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no man who takes charge of a people and then does not protect them as he protects himself and his family except that God will admit him into the fire of Hell.”"],[17314,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when al-Mughira b. Shuʿba entered, wearing leather socks. He was the first person I saw wearing leather socks in Islam. The people began touching them and saying, “What is this?” They said, “These are leather socks.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “You will soon have many leather socks.” They said, “O Messenger of God, what do you command us regarding ablution for prayer?” He said, “Wipe over them, or perform ablution while wearing them.”"],[17315,"A man mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ that he had found a woman of beauty and noble lineage, except that she was barren. He forbade him from marrying her, then he returned and he again forbade him, and said: “Marry the loving and fertile, for I will boast of your numbers.”"],[17316,"ʿUthman b. ʿAffan used to suffer greatly from prostatic fluid, so he sent a man to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: “That is prostatic fluid. Every male emits it. Wash it with water, perform ablution, and pray.”"],[17317,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said, \"Recite it for your deceased,\" meaning Surah Yasin."],[17318,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Al-Baqarah is the pinnacle of the Qur'an, and its two last verses came down with every verse. Eighty angels descended with them. Surah Al-Baqarah and Surah Ya-Sin are connected to one another; they will be together in Paradise. The heart of the Qur'an is Surah Ya-Sin. Whoever recites it seeking Allah, the home, and the hereafter, Allah will forgive him. Recite it during the prayer for your deceased.\""],[17319,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Act according to the Book of God and do not reject anything of it. Whatever is unclear to you, ask the people of knowledge about it and they will inform you. Believe in the Torah and the Gospel, for in them is clarification and intercession, and what is lawful is confirmed.”"],[17320,"Indeed, God used to benefit us through knowledge by sitting with you. You used to narrate to us from the Prophet ﷺ. Maʿqil said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever is given charge of any affair of the Muslims and does not surround them with sincere counsel as he surrounds his own household, let him take his seat in the Fire.” He said: I have never heard this from you before today. He said: “I would not have narrated it to you except while I am in this state of mine.” He said: Then Ziyad went out dragging his garment."],[17321,"When her father became gravely ill, Ziyad heard of it and came until he sought permission at the door. I sat by my father, and Ziyad entered. He recognized death in my father’s face and said: “O Maʿqil, will you not provide us with something from you? God used to benefit us through things we heard from you.” He said to him: “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘There is no governor over a community, whether large or small, who does not act justly among them except that God will cast him on his face into the Fire.’” He lowered his head for a while, then bowed it, then raised his head and said: “O Maʿqil, is this something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, or is it from hearsay?” He said: “Rather, I heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[17322,"He said: Narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no governor appointed over any community of my nation, whether small or large, who does not act justly among them except that God will cast him on his face into the Fire.”"],[17323,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no governor placed in charge of a community, whether small or large, who then does not act justly among them except that God will cast him into the Fire.”"],[17324,"My father fell ill with the illness in which he died. Ziyad came to visit him and said: “Allow him to enter alone.” So they allowed him. When he entered upon him, he said: “Your hadith used to benefit us, so narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ.” He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no governor who rules over any community of my nation, whether small or large, who does not act justly among them except that God will cast him on his face into the Fire.” That distressed him, and he said: “Is this something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, or did you hear it from his Companions?” He said: “Rather, it is something I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[17325,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ and came upon a place where there was garlic. Some people ate from it, then came to the prayer area. The Messenger of God ﷺ noticed its smell and said: “Whoever eats of this plant should not approach our prayer area.” The wording is from the hadith of Abu al-Walid."],[17326,"We were in Madinah, and it had abundant fruit. “The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us fadikh.”"],[17327,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God, might and majesty be to Him, has disliked for you gossip and speculation, excessive questioning, and squandering wealth.\""],[17328,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever buys a slave intending to manumit him should not stipulate manumission for his owners, for that is his contract from slavery.\""],[17329,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"There is no ruler who is entrusted with a flock and does not protect it and advise them sincerely, except that he will not enter Paradise with them.\""],[17330,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Act upon the Quran, deem lawful what it deems lawful, deem unlawful what it deems unlawful, follow its example, and do not disbelieve in any part of it. Whatever is unclear to you, refer it to God or to the ruler after me, so that they may inform you. And believe in the Torah, the Gospel, the Psalms, and what the prophets received from their Lord. Let the Quran and its clear explanations heal you, for it is an intercessor whose intercession is accepted, a witness whose testimony is believed, and for every verse of it there is light until the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, I have been given Surat al-Baqarah as part of the Remembrance, and I have been given Ta-Ha and al-Tur from the tablets of Moses, and I have been given the Opening of the Book and the closing verses of al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne, and I have been given the Mufassal as an additional portion.\""],[17331,"\"We went on Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found Aisha taking off her clothes. He asked her, 'What is wrong with you?' She responded, 'I have been informed that you have made your Ihram lawful and made the people accompanying you lawful.' He said, 'Indeed, whoever does not have a sacrificial animal, but as for us, we have not made our Ihram lawful yet, as we still have bodily impurities until we reach Arafat.'\""],[17332,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God has disliked for you three things: disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding while demanding.\""],[17333,"There was an oath between two neighbors of mine, and the oath fell upon one of them. Then I heard Maqil b. Yasar say: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever swears an oath by which he seizes the property of his brother will meet God while He is angry with him.'\""],[17334,"\"We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Hudaybiyyah while I was lifting a branch of the tree from his face. We pledged allegiance to him that we would not flee, and we did not pledge allegiance to him upon death.\" We said to him, \"How many were you?\" He said, \"One thousand four hundred.\""],[17335,"\"I was lifting the branches of the tree from the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" The people pledged allegiance that they would not flee, and they were then one thousand four hundred."],[17336,"\"I saw myself on the day of the tree while the Prophet ﷺ\" was accepting the people's allegiance, and I was lifting a branch of its branches from his head. We did not pledge allegiance to him upon death, but rather we pledged allegiance to him that we would not flee."],[17337,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"There is no shepherd who betrays his flock except that he will be in the Fire.\""],[17338,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever separates is not one of us.\" Asad said: \"He separates between a child and his mother, and between siblings.\""],[17339,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ: \"A case involving a grandfather was brought to him, and he gave him a third or a sixth.\""],[17340,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever says in the morning three times: 'I seek refuge in the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing from the accursed devil,' and recites three times the end of Surat al-Hashr, Allah appoints over him seventy thousand angels who send blessings upon him until evening. If he dies on that day, he dies as a martyr. If he says it in the evening, the like of that is for him.\""],[17341,"I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day, and he said to me, \"Would you like Fatimah?\" meaning his daughter. I said, \"Yes.\" He stood, leaning on me, and said, \"Indeed, another will bear the burden, while the reward will be yours.\" It was as if there was nothing upon me until we entered upon Fatimah. He said to her, \"How do you find yourself?\" She said, \"By Allah, my grief has intensified, my need has intensified, and my illness has prolonged.\" He said, \"Are you not pleased that I have married you to the one who was earliest in Islam of my Ummah, the most knowledgeable of them, and the most forbearing of them?\""],[17342,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to judge among my people. I said, \"I am not good at it.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Allah is with the judge as long as he does not deliberately act unjustly.\""],[17343,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to judge among my people. I said, \"I am not good at judging.\" He said, \"Judge among them, for Allah ﷻ is with the judge as long as he does not deliberately act unjustly.\""],[17344,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Al-Baqarah is the summit of the Quran and it is accompanied by eighty angels with every verse of it. Allah revealed 'There is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence' from beneath the Throne, so Surah Al-Baqarah and Surah Yasin were attached to it. The heart of the Quran is Surah Al-Baqarah, and whoever recites it seeking Allah and the Last Home, Allah will forgive him. Recite it over your dead.\""],[17345,"\"She is entitled to a dower like that of her peers, without reduction or excess, and upon her is the waiting period, and she has the inheritance.\" Abu Sinan al-Ashja'i stood up among a group from Ashja' and testified, \"Indeed the Prophet ﷺ ruled that in the case of Barwa' bint Washiq al-Ashja'iyyah.\""],[17346,"About a man who married a woman and did not assign her a dower and did not consummate the marriage until he died, he made them repeat [the question], then said, \"Indeed I will give my opinion concerning her. If it is correct, it is from Allah, and if it is wrong, it is from myself. I hold that she is entitled to a dower like that of a woman from among her peers, without reduction or excess, and upon her is the waiting period, and she has the inheritance.\" Ma'qil b. Sinan al-Ashja'i stood up and said, \"I testify that you have ruled concerning her with the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the case of Barwa' bint Washiq,\" a woman from Banu Rawas, a clan from Banu 'Amir b. Sa'sa'ah, and this is what Sufyan adopts."],[17347,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in the case of Barwa' bint Washiq the like of what you have ruled.\" Ibn Mas'ud was pleased."],[17348,"'Abdullah was brought a case of a man who left behind his wife and had not consummated the marriage with her. They referred it back to him concerning her for a month, and he did not rule anything. He said, \"I will give my opinion concerning her. If it is wrong, it is from myself, and if it is correct, it is from Allah: the like of her peers' dower, upon her the waiting period, and she has the inheritance.\" Abu Sinan al-Ashja'i stood up and said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in the case of Barwa' bint Washiq with that.\" 'Abdullah was pleased with that."],[17349,"From 'Abdullah concerning a man who married a woman and then died leaving her, and he had not consummated the marriage and had not assigned her a dower. He said, \"She is entitled to the full dower, upon her is the waiting period, and she has the inheritance.\" Ma'qil b. Sinan said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rule with that in the case of Barwa' bint Washiq.\""],[17350,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was being cupped on the eighteenth of Ramadan, and he said, \"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.\""],[17351,"He informed me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Ghifar, Aslam, Juhaynah, and Muzaynah are allies of Allah ﷻ and His Messenger.\""],[17352,"He informed him that Ma'qil ibn abi Maqil al-Asadi, a companion of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to him: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade facing the two qiblas (Kaaba in Makkah and Masjid al-Aqsa in Jerusalem) while in a state of impurity (due to feces and urine).\""],[17353,"He narrated to him that the Prophet ﷺ forbade facing either of the two qiblahs with excrement or urine."],[17354,"That his mother Zaynab came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Ma'qil had promised me that he would not perform Hajj unless I was with him. He performed Hajj on his riding camel, but I was not able. I asked him for the harvest of his date palms, and he said: It is the sustenance of my family. I asked him for a young camel he had, and he said: It is in the way of Allah, I will not give it to you. He said: 'Abu Ma'qil, what does Umm Ma'qil say?' He said: She is truthful. He said: 'Give her your young camel, for Hajj is the way of Allah.' So he gave her his young camel. She said: I am a woman who has become ill and old, and I fear I will not live to perform Hajj until I die. Is there anything that suffices for Hajj? He said: 'Yes, an Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj.' So she performed Umrah in Ramadan."],[17355,"From Urwah regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr: al-Miqdad b. Amr."],[17356,"\"Al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad b. Amr.\""],[17357,"\"Because he adopted and allied with him. He was dark-skinned, large-bellied, dyed his beard yellow, had an aquiline nose and a long nose. He died in Madinah at the age of seventy, and Uthman b. Affan ؓ prayed over him.\""],[17358,"\"I saw al-Miqdad, and he was huge.\""],[17359,"I saw al-Miqdad, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, sitting on a chest from the chests of the money-changers in Hims, having become too large for it due to his bone size, intending to go on a military expedition. I said: Allah has excused you. He said: The surah of the sending forth refused us: {Go forth, light and heavy}."],[17360,"\"Al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad was from Kindah.\""],[17361,"\"I was the companion of al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad in the Jahiliyyah. He was a man from Bahra'. He shed blood among them, so he fled to Kindah and allied with them. Then he shed blood among them, so he fled to Makkah and allied with al-Aswad b. Abd Yaghuth.\""],[17362,"It is only four thousand. He disputed with him before Umar. Uthman said: I lent him seven thousand. Al-Miqdad said: Will you swear that it is seven thousand? He said: You have been fair. But he refused to swear. He said: Take what he gives you. He said: By Allah, besides whom there is no deity, it is only seven thousand? He said: What prevents you from swearing that this is night and this is day?"],[17363,"\"Al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad died at al-Jurf, and men carried him to Madinah on their necks in the year thirty-three. Uthman b. Affan prayed over him. He was called Abu Ma'bad, and his age was about seventy.\""],[17364,"That I should ask the Prophet ﷺ about pre-ejaculate fluid, and his daughter was my wife. So I instructed al-Miqdad, and he asked him. He said: \"In it is ablution.\""],[17365,"Ali b. Abi Talib said to al-Miqdad: Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for me about a man who plays with his wife and talks to her and then emits pre-ejaculate fluid. Were it not that I feel shy before him and that his daughter is my wife, I would have asked him. So al-Miqdad asked him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He should wash his penis, then perform ablution, then sprinkle water on his private part.\""],[17366,"I said to al-Miqdad: Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for were it not that his daughter is under me, I would ask him about one of us who draws near his wife and emits madhy but does not control that and does not touch her. So al-Miqdad asked the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you emits madhy and does not touch her, let him wash his penis and his testicles.\""],[17367,"Ali said to me: Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a man who plays with his wife and madhy comes out of him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who plays with his wife and madhy comes out of him? He said: \"He washes his private part and performs wudu as he would for prayer.\""],[17368,"A man came and praised Uthman, so al-Miqdad stood up and threw dirt in his face. Uthman said to him: What is with you? He said: As for me, I will not leave anything I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Throw dirt in the faces of the praisers.\""],[17369,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Throw dirt in the faces of the praisers.\""],[17370,"When we emigrated to Madinah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided us into groups of ten, so I was among the ten who were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We had a sheep whose milk we drank among ourselves. One night he was late, and we had set aside his share. I got up while hungry and drank it. Then the Prophet ﷺ came while I had not slept. He came to the vessel in which we used to put the milk and looked but found nothing in it. I jumped up and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I slaughter it for you? He said: \"No.\""],[17371,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ and he divided us: ten in a house, ten in a house. I was with the Prophet ﷺ, and we had a sheep that sustained us."],[17372,"When we arrived in Madinah, the Prophet ﷺ grouped us in tens, ten in each house. I was among the ten among whom the Prophet was. He said: We had only a sheep whose milk we shared. When the Prophet ﷺ was late, we would drink and leave the Prophet's ﷺ share. One night he was late, and we slept. Al-Miqdad said: The Prophet ﷺ has taken long; I do not think he will come tonight. Perhaps someone invited him. He said: So I drank it. When the night passed, he came and entered. When he entered, he gave the greeting without raising his voice, then went to the bowl. When he saw nothing, he was silent, then said: \"O Allah, feed the one who fed us tonight.\" So I jumped up, took the knife, and brought it to him. He wiped its udder, and something came out, then he drank, then slept."],[17373,"A delegation from the people of Iraq was sent to Uthman, and they began praising him. Al-Miqdad began throwing dirt in their faces and said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to throw dirt in the faces of the praisers.\""],[17374,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, except that I heard Talha narrating about the Day of Uhud.\""],[17375,"I arrived in Madinah with two companions of mine. We sought hospitality from people, but no one hosted us. So we came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, severe hunger has befallen us, and we sought hospitality from people, but no one hosted us. He took us to his home, where he had four she-goats. He said: \"O Miqdad, milk them.\" The Prophet ﷺ apportioned a share for each of us, and I used to do that. I set aside the share of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but he was late. I lay down on my bed, and my soul said to me: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to a household of the Ansar and ate and drank with them. If only you drank this drink. My soul kept at me until I drank it. When it settled in my belly, regret over what had passed and what had just happened seized me. My soul said to me: Now he will come thirsty and find nothing. So I lay down and covered myself with the garment. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and gave a greeting that the awake could hear but that would not wake the sleeping one. Then he came to the vessel, uncovered it, and saw nothing. He said: \"O Allah, feed the one who fed me and give drink to the one who gave me drink.\" I seized the opportunity of his supplication and got up, took the blade, and approached the goats. I looked for the fattest among them to slaughter. I approached one and felt her, and found her full of milk. I looked at another and found her full of milk. I looked at the next and found her full of milk. I looked at all of them and found them all full of milk. I took the vessel and milked into it, then said: Drink. He said: \"The news first, O Miqdad.\" I said: Drink, then the news. He said: \"Some of your misdeed, O Miqdad.\" So he drank, then said: \"Drink.\" I said: Drink, O Messenger of Allah. He drank until he was satisfied. Then I took from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and drank. Then I told him the news. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"This is a blessing that descended from heaven. Why did you not tell me so I could give your two companions to drink?\" I said: If you and I get it, I do not care who misses it."],[17376,"And he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you see the praisers, throw dirt in their faces.\""],[17377,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us, when we see the praisers, to throw dirt in their faces.\""],[17378,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Throw dust in the faces of the flatterers.”"],[17379,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Throw dust in the faces of the flatterers.”"],[17380,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces.”"],[17381,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to throw dust in the faces of the flatterers."],[17382,"And he said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to throw dust in the faces of the flatterers.”"],[17383,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you hear the flatterers, throw dust in their faces.”"],[17384,"And he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces.”"],[17385,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I and a man from the polytheists exchange two blows and he cuts off my hand, then when I move to strike him he says: “There is no god but Allah.” Should I kill him or spare him? He said: “Rather spare him.” I said: Even if he cut off my hand? He said: “Even if he did.” I repeated it twice or three times, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “If you kill him after he says: ‘There is no god but Allah,’ then you are like him before he said it, and he is like you if you kill him.”"],[17386,"He reported to him from al-Miqdad b. ʿAmr, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was a man from Kindah and an ally of Banu Zuhrah. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the polytheists and we exchange two blows, and he cuts off one of my hands, then I strike him and later am able to kill him, but when I intend to bring my weapon down upon him he says: “There is no god but Allah.” Should I kill him or leave him? He said: “Rather leave him.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he cut off one of my hands? He said: “Even if he did.” I repeated it, and he said: “If you kill him after he says: ‘There is no god but Allah,’ then you are in his position before he said it, and he is in your position before you kill him.”"],[17387,"He reported to him that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the disbelievers and he fights me, and he strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it off, then he takes refuge from me behind a tree and says: “I have submitted to Allah.” Should I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he has said it? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not kill him.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, he cut off my hand, then he said that after cutting it off. Should I kill him? He said: “Do not kill him. For if you kill him, then he is in your position before you kill him, and you are in his position before he said the word that he said.”"],[17388,"Al-Miqdad said to the Prophet ﷺ: O Prophet of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the disbelievers and he fights me, and he strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it off, then he takes refuge from me behind a tree and says: “I have submitted to Allah.” Should I kill him after he has said it, O Prophet of Allah? He said: “Do not kill him.” He said: He cut off my hand, then he said that after cutting it off? The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not kill him. For if you kill him, he will be in your position before you kill him, and you will be in his position before he said his word that he said.”"],[17389,"He reported to him that al-Miqdad b. ʿAmr al-Kindi, who was an ally of Banu Zuhrah and was among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, related to him that he said: O Messenger of Allah, if I meet a man from the disbelievers and we fight, and he strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it off, then he takes refuge from me behind a tree and says: “I have submitted to Allah.” Should I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he has said it? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not kill him.” He said: O Messenger of Allah, he cut off one of my hands, then he said that after cutting it off. Should I kill him? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not kill him. For if you kill him, then he is in your position before you kill him, and you are in his position before he said his word that he said.”"],[17390,"He informed him that he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"What do you think of a man from the disbelievers who fought me, and we exchanged two blows. He struck one of my hands with a sword and cut it off, then he sought refuge from me behind a tree and said, 'I have embraced Islam.' Should I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he has said that?\" He said: \"Do not kill him, for if you were to kill him, he would be in your position before you killed him, and you would be in his position before he uttered his word that he said.\""],[17391,"He informed him that he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the disbelievers and fight him, and he cuts off my hand, then he seeks refuge from me behind a tree and says, 'I have submitted to Allah.' Should I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he has said that?\" He said: \"Do not kill him, for if you were to kill him, you would be in his position before he uttered his word that he said.\""],[17392,"He informed him from al-Miqdad b. ʿAmr, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—he was a man from Kindah and an ally of Banu Zuhrah—that he said: \"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the disbelievers, and he and I exchange two blows. He strikes me and severs one of my hands, then I strike him. Then I am able to kill him, but when I intend to strike him with my weapon, he says, \"There is no god but Allah.\" Should I kill him or leave him?'\" He said: \"No, rather leave him.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, even if he cut off one of my hands?\" He said, \"Even if he did.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, even if he cut off one of my hands?\" He said, \"Even if he did.\" I repeated it, and he said: \"If you kill him after he says, 'There is no god but Allah,' then you are in his position before he said it, and he is in your position before you kill him.\""],[17393,"\"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the disbelievers and he fights me, and he strikes one of my hands and cuts it off, then he seeks refuge from me behind a tree and says, 'I have submitted to Allah.' Should I kill him, O Messenger of Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not kill him.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he cut off one of my hands, then he said that after cutting it off.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you kill him, then you are in his position before he uttered his word that he said, and he is in your position before you kill him.\""],[17394,"He informed him that he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the polytheists and he fights me, and he strikes one of my hands and cuts it off, then he seeks refuge from me behind a tree and says, 'I have submitted to Allah.' Should I kill him after he has said that?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not kill him after he has said that.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he cut off one of my hands, then he said that after cutting it off.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you kill him, then he is in your position before you kill him, and you are in his position before he uttered his word that he said.\""],[17395,"He informed him that al-Miqdad b. ʿAmr was an ally of Banu Zuhrah and was among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He informed him that he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the disbelievers and we fight, and he strikes one of my hands with a sword and cuts it off, then he seeks refuge from me behind a tree and says, 'I have submitted to Allah.' Should I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he has said that?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not kill him, for if you were to kill him, he would be in your position before you killed him, and you would be in his position before he uttered his word that he said.\""],[17396,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us from Malik; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, ʿAbd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us, all of them from Malik b. Anas, from Abu al-Nadr, from Sulayman b. Yasar, from al-Miqdad, that ʿAli ordered him to ask the Prophet ﷺ about a man who approaches his wife and emits madhy—what is incumbent upon him? For his daughter is with me, and I feel shy to ask him. Al-Miqdad said: \"So I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said: 'When one of you experiences that, let him wash his private part and perform wuduʾ as he does for prayer.'\""],[17397,"A man from Ghafiq owed a man from Mahrah one hundred dinars during the time of ʿUthman. They acquired good spoils of war. The Mahri said, \"I will hasten to you seventy dinars on condition that you cancel the hundred from me.\" The hundred was disputed. The Ghafiqi agreed to that. Then al-Miqdad passed by them, and he took hold of the rein of his mount to make him a witness. When he related the account to him, he said: \"Both of you have been warned of war from Allah and His Messenger.\""],[17398,"How amazing are people whom I passed by just now, wishing for tribulation, claiming that Allah would test them in it as He tested His Messenger ﷺ and his companions. By Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The fortunate one is he who is kept away from tribulations,\" repeating it three times, \"and if he is tested, he remains patient.\""],[17399,"How amazing are people whom I passed by just now, wishing for tribulation, claiming that Allah would test them in it as He tested His Messenger ﷺ and his companions. By Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The fortunate one is he who is kept away from tribulations,\" repeating it three times, \"and if he is tested, he remains patient.\""],[17400,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The heart of the son of Adam changes more quickly than a pot when it reaches a full boil.\""],[17401,"\"Blessed are these two eyes that saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. By Allah, I wish we had seen what you saw and witnessed what you witnessed.\" He turned to him and said: \"What makes a man wish for a gathering that Allah has kept him from, when he does not know how he would have been had he witnessed it? By Allah, there were people present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whom Allah will cast on their faces into Hell—they did not answer him nor believe him. Will Allah not deprive one of you? Do you not recognize the favors of your Lord, believing in what your Prophet ﷺ brought? You have been spared affliction through others. By Allah, the Prophet ﷺ was sent in the harshest condition in which any prophet was sent—in a period of cessation and ignorance, when they saw no religion superior to idol worship. He came with a criterion that distinguished between truth and falsehood and separated a father from his child, until a man would see his father, son, or brother as a disbeliever, and Allah had opened the lock of his heart to faith, and he would know that whoever enters the Fire has perished. His eye would not be pleased while he knows that his close friend is in the Fire. And indeed it is that which Allah, exalted is He, said: {Our Lord, grant us from our spouses and offspring comfort to our eyes}.\""],[17402,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There will not remain on the face of the earth a house of mud or of hair but that Allah will bring Islam upon them either through the might of a mighty one or the humiliation of a humiliated one. Either He honors them and guides them to Islam, or He humiliates them and they pay the jizyah.”"],[17403,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “On the Day of Resurrection, the sun will be brought near to the creation until it is from them at a distance of a mīl.” Sulaym said: By Allah, I do not know what he meant by “mīl”—a distance on land, or the mīl (kohl stick) used to apply kohl to the eye? He ﷺ said: “Then people will be in sweat according to their deeds. Among them will be one whose sweat reaches his ankles, among them one whose reaches his knees, among them one whose reaches his waist, and among them one who will be bridled by sweat completely.” And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured toward his mouth."],[17404,"I will not speak good or evil about anyone until I see what his deeds are sealed with, after something I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He was asked: And what did you hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed the heart of the son of Adam changes more violently than a pot when it reaches a full boil.”"],[17405,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “People will be gathered—from a miscarried fetus to a decrepit old man—as thirty-three-year-olds, in the form of Adam, the beauty of Joseph, and the character of Job, with kohl-lined eyes, having luxuriant hair.”"],[17406,"That the Prophet ﷺ asked them about fornication, so they said: It is forbidden; Allah and His Messenger have forbidden it. He then said: “For a man to fornicate with ten women would be better for him than to fornicate with his neighbor's wife.” He said: And he asked them about theft, so they said: It is forbidden; Allah and His Messenger have forbidden it. He then said: “For a man to steal from ten houses would be easier for him than to steal from his neighbor's house.”"],[17407,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever loves Allah and His Messenger sincerely, not falsely, and meets the believers and loves them, and regards the affairs of the pre-Islamic era as having the status of a fire into which he is thrown, then he has tasted the taste of faith.” Or he said: “Then he has attained the summit of faith.” The doubt is from Safwan."],[17408,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “When the leader seeks to stir up discord among the people, he corrupts them.”"],[17409,"“These two eyes have prospered indeed, having seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Then al-Miqdad's anger welled up and he said: “O people, do not wish for something that Allah has kept hidden, for how many have seen him and yet not benefited from seeing him.”"],[17410,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me on an expedition, and when I returned, he asked me: “How do you find yourself?” I said: I did not cease until I thought I had servants of my own. And by Allah, I will never again be appointed over two men after this."],[17411,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray toward a column, a wooden post, or a tree except that he would place it between his right eyebrow and his left eyebrow, and he would not face it directly."],[17412,"From Duba'ah bt. al-Zubayr—and she was the wife of al-Miqdad—she said: People used to go to relieve themselves only after a gap of two or three days, and they would defecate like camels. Then one day al-Miqdad went out to relieve himself until he reached al-Khabkhabah, which is in Baqi' al-Gharqad. He entered a ruin for his need. While he was sitting, a rat brought out from a hole a dinar, and it kept bringing out dinar after dinar until it reached seventeen dinars. I brought them and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of the story. He said: “Did your hand follow the hole?” I said: No, by the One who sent you with the truth. He said: “There is no zakah due on them. May Allah bless you in them.” Duba'ah said: Its last of them did not run out until I saw cords of silver in the house of al-Miqdad."],[17413,"Al-Miqdad went to relieve himself and entered a ruin. There was a rat bringing out from a hole a dinar, dinar by dinar, until it brought out seventeen dinars. Then it brought out the end of a green cloth. Al-Miqdad said: I stood up and pulled the end of the cloth, and I found in it a dinar, making eighteen dinars. Al-Miqdad took them and sought permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ. When he entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, he told him the story and said: Take its charity, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Did you reach your hand into the hole?” Al-Miqdad said: No, by the One who sent you with the truth. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to al-Miqdad: “May Allah bless you in them.”"],[17414,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"Something I heard from you that I doubted.\" He said, \"If any of you doubts a matter, let him ask me about it.\" He said, \"Your statement about your wives: 'I hope for them after me the truthful ones (al-ṣiddīqīn).'\" He said, \"Who do you count as al-ṣiddīqīn?\" We said, \"Our children who die young.\" He said, \"Rather, al-ṣiddīqīn are those who give charity.\" He said it three times."],[17415,"It is called subḥa. \"The Prophet ﷺ allotted for his horse a share and for him a share.\""],[17416,"To al-Miqdām b. Maʿdī Karib, \"O Abū Karīma.\""],[17417,"\"Al-Miqdām b. Maʿdī Karib was given the kunya Abū Yaḥyā. Al-Miqdām b. Maʿdī Karib died in the year eighty-seven, and he was ninety-one years old.\""],[17418,"\"I saw five of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ trim their moustaches, let their beards grow, and dye them yellow; among them was al-Miqdām b. Maʿdī Karib.\""],[17419,"I came to al-Miqdām b. Maʿdī Karib while he was in a village some miles from Ḥimṣ on the day of Eid. We said, § \"Come out and lead us in the Eid prayer.\" He said, \"No, pray individually.\""],[17420,"\"I saw Abū Umāma al-Bāhilī and al-Miqdām b. Maʿdī Karib, and upon them were two burnūses.\""],[17421,"I heard al-Miqdām b. Maʿdī Karib, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while most people were saying, \"The decree is in one hundred years,\" meaning after one hundred years the Resurrection will occur. Al-Miqdām said, \"You have said too much. Allah will not be unable to delay this community half a day,\" meaning five hundred years."],[17422,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The night of the guest is an obligatory right upon every Muslim. If the guest remains in his courtyard in the morning, then it is a debt upon him: if he wishes, he may collect it, and if he wishes, he may forgo it.\""],[17423,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"The night of the guest is an obligatory right upon every Muslim. If the guest remains in his courtyard in the morning, then it is a right upon him, or a debt: if he wishes, he may collect it, and if he wishes, he may forgo it.\""],[17424,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Hosting guests is a duty upon every Muslim. Whoever begins his morning in his home, then he has a debt upon him, if he wishes, he may fulfill it, and if he wishes, he may leave it.\""],[17425,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The night of the guest is an obligatory right. If he remains in his courtyard in the morning, then it is a debt upon him: if he wishes, he may collect it, and if he wishes, he may forgo it.\""],[17426,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever leaves behind a dependent (kallan), then it is to Allah and His Messenger—or he said, then it is to us—and whoever leaves behind wealth, then it is for his heirs. And I am the heir of the one who has no heir: I inherit his wealth and release his captive. The maternal uncle is the patron of the one who has no patron: he inherits his wealth and releases his captive.\""],[17427,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am closer to every believer than his own self. Whoever leaves behind a debt or dependents, they are my responsibility, and whoever leaves behind wealth, it is for his heirs. I am the guardian of the one who has no guardian: I inherit his wealth and ransom his prisoner. The maternal uncle is the guardian of the one who has no guardian: he inherits his wealth and ransoms his prisoner.\""],[17428,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever leaves behind a debt or a bequest, it is upon me. And whoever leaves behind wealth, it is for his inheritors. And I am the guardian of the one who has no guardian, so I will repay his debt and inherit his wealth. And the paternal uncle is the guardian of the one who has no guardian, so he will repay his debt and inherit his wealth.\""],[17429,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever leaves behind a debt or dependents, they are my responsibility, and whoever leaves behind wealth, it is for his heirs. I am the guardian of the one who has no guardian: I ransom his prisoner and inherit his wealth.\""],[17430,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The martyr has nine qualities with Allah\" – or he said \"ten qualities\" – \"he is forgiven with the first drop of his blood; he is shown his seat in Paradise; he is adorned with the adornment of faith; he is protected from the punishment of the grave; he is married to the wide-eyed houris; he is safe from the greatest terror; a crown of dignity is placed on his head, a ruby better than the world and all it contains; he is married to ninety-two wives from the wide-eyed houris; and he intercedes for seventy of his relatives.\""],[17431,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade riding on the skins of wild beasts."],[17432,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"No one has eaten food better than that which he eats from the work of his own hand, and Dawud used to eat only from the work of his own hand.\""],[17433,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gesturing with his hand and saying: \"None of you has eaten food in this world better for him than that which he eats from the work of his own two hands.\""],[17434,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"No one of the children of Adam has eaten food that is better for him than that which he eats from the work of his own two hands.\" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"And Dawud ﷺ used to eat from the work of his own two hands.\""],[17435,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whatever you feed your wife is charity for you, whatever you feed your child is charity for you, whatever you feed your servant is charity for you, and whatever you feed yourself is charity for you.\""],[17436,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Hasan is from me, and Husayn is from Ali.\""],[17437,"Al-Miqdam b. Ma'di Karb and Amr b. al-Aswad – a man from Asad from the people of Qinnasrin, one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ – came as a delegation to Mu'awiya, may Allah have mercy on him. Mu'awiya said to al-Miqdam: \"Did you know that al-Hasan b. Ali has died?\" Al-Miqdam said the istirja' (recited 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return'). Mu'awiya said to him: \"Do you consider it a calamity?\" He said: \"Why should I not consider it a calamity, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed him in his lap and said: 'This one is from me, and Husayn is from Ali'?\" Then he said to the Asadi: \"What do you say?\" He said: \"A burning coal that Allah has extinguished.\" Al-Miqdam said: \"As for me, I will not leave today until I anger you and make you hear what you dislike.\""],[17438,"Al-Miqdam b. Ma'di Karb and Amr b. al-Aswad – a man from Asad from the people of Qinnasrin, one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ – came as a delegation to Mu'awiya, may Allah have mercy on him. Mu'awiya said to al-Miqdam: \"Did you know that al-Hasan b. Ali has died?\" Al-Miqdam said the istirja' (recited 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return'). Mu'awiya said to him: \"Do you consider it a calamity?\" He said: \"Why should I not consider it a calamity, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed him in his lap and said: 'This one is from me, and Husayn is from Ali'?\" Then he said to the Asadi: \"What do you say?\" He said: \"A burning coal that Allah has extinguished.\" Al-Miqdam said: \"As for me, I will not leave today until I anger you and make you hear what you dislike.\""],[17439,"Al-Miqdam b. Ma'di Karb and Amr b. al-Aswad – a man from Asad from the people of Qinnasrin, one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ – came as a delegation to Mu'awiya, may Allah have mercy on him. Mu'awiya said to al-Miqdam: \"Did you know that al-Hasan b. Ali has died?\" Al-Miqdam said the istirja' (recited 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return'). Mu'awiya said to him: \"Do you consider it a calamity?\" He said: \"Why should I not consider it a calamity, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed him in his lap and said: 'This one is from me, and Husayn is from Ali'?\" Then he said to the Asadi: \"What do you say?\" He said: \"A burning coal that Allah has extinguished.\" Al-Miqdam said: \"As for me, I will not leave today until I anger you and make you hear what you dislike.\""],[17440,"\"The delegation of al-Miqdam ibn Ma'di Karib and Amr ibn al-Aswad, a man from the tribe of Qinsarin, from the companions of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , went to Muawiyah (may Allah have mercy upon him). Muawiyah said to al-Miqdam, 'Did you not know that al-Hasan ibn Ali has passed away?' Al-Miqdam then paused and Muawiyah said to him, 'Do you see it as a calamity?' Al-Miqdam responded, 'Why wouldn't I see it as a calamity? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed him in his chamber and said, \"This is from me and Hasan is from Ali.\" Muawiyah then asked al-Aswad, 'What do you say?' And he replied, 'It is like a burning coal that Allah has extinguished.' Al-Miqdam said, 'As for me, I will not rest today until I make you angry today and tell you what you dislike.'\""],[17441,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your fathers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your mothers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning the nearest kin, then the next nearest.\""],[17442,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed Allah, Exalted is He, enjoins you concerning your mothers—three times; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your fathers—twice; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning the nearest kin, then the next nearest.\""],[17443,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your mothers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your mothers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your fathers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning the nearest kin, then the next nearest.\""],[17444,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your mothers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your mothers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your fathers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning the nearest kin, then the next nearest.\""],[17445,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he said: \"You should take the pre-dawn meal, for it is the blessed nourishment.\""],[17446,"He was on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they camped beside enclosures belonging to the Jews at Khaybar. The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took [fruit] from them, so the Jews went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and complained to him about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Khalid b. al-Walid, and he called out: \"The prayer is to be held in congregation, and none will enter Paradise except a Muslim.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \"What becomes lawful for you from the property of those under covenant without right to it?\" They said: \"Whatever we find in the Book of Allah as lawful we deem lawful, and whatever we find as unlawful we deem unlawful.\" \"Indeed, I forbid the property of those under covenant, every fanged beast of prey, and whatever has been subjected for service among riding animals except what Allah has named.\""],[17447,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he said: \"Measure out your food, and you will be blessed in it.\""],[17448,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A human being fills no vessel worse than the belly. Sufficient for the son of Adam are morsels that keep his back upright. If it must be, then one third for food, one third for drink, and one third for himself.\""],[17449,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The son of Adam has not contained a vessel worse than the belly. Sufficient for the Muslim are morsels that keep his back upright. If it must be, then one third for his food, one third for his drink, and one third for himself.\""],[17450,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Seek refuge in Allah from greed that leads to an unsound disposition, and from greed that leads to something not to be coveted.\""],[17451,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among the people and praised Allah and spoke highly of Him. He then said, \"Indeed, Allah advises you regarding women. Indeed, Allah advises you regarding women. Verily, they are your mothers, and your daughters, and your aunts. Surely, a man from the People of the Book marries a woman, and he does not refer to her family lineage. So, one of them would not be pleased with her companion.\""],[17452,"He heard al-Miqdam b. Ma'di Karib say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade certain things on the day of Khaybar, among them domestic donkeys and others.\""],[17453,"He heard al-Miqdam b. Ma'di Karib say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade certain things on the day of Khaybar, among them domestic donkeys and others.\""],[17454,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade things, until he mentioned domestic donkeys."],[17455,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a leader seeks out suspicions about people, he corrupts them.”"],[17456,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “There is no man placed over a people except that he will come on the Day of Resurrection leading them with a banner before him that he carries, and they follow him. He will be asked about them, and they will be asked about him.”"],[17457,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, this matter is among your people, so advise them concerning us.” He said to them: “I remind you of Allah: do not oppress my community after me.” Then he said to the people: “There will be rulers after me, so render obedience to them. Indeed, the ruler is like a shield; protection is sought with it. If they act rightly and command you to good, then that is for you and for them. But if they do evil in what they command you, then that is upon them, and you are free of it. Indeed, when a ruler pursues suspicion about people, he corrupts them.”"],[17458,"I heard al-Miqdam b. Ma'di Karib say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought water for ablution.” He performed ablution, washing his palms three times, then washing his face three times, then washing his forearms three times, then rinsing his mouth and sniffing water into his nose three times each, then wiping his head and his ears, their outer and inner parts, and washing his feet three times each."],[17459,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ” perform ablution, and when he reached wiping his head, he placed his palms on the front of his head, then passed them until he reached the back of the neck, then returned them to the place where he began."],[17460,"“These two eyes have prospered that saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Al-Miqdam became angry and said: “O people, do not wish for a matter that Allah has hidden from you.”"],[17461,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Obey your rulers whatever the case. If they command you to something of what I brought you, then they are rewarded for it and you are rewarded for obeying them. If they command you to something of what I did not bring you, then it is upon them and you are free of it. That is because when you meet Allah, you will say: ‘Our Lord, no injustice.’ He will say: ‘No injustice.’ Then you will say: ‘Our Lord, You sent messengers to us and we obeyed them by Your permission; You appointed successors over us and we obeyed them by Your permission; and You placed rulers over us and we obeyed them for You.’ He will say: ‘You have spoken truth. It is upon them and you are free of it.’”"],[17462,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “A time will come upon people when whoever does not have yellow or white will not enjoy life.”"],[17463,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When it is the end of time, people will inevitably need dirhams and dinars; a man will use them to maintain his religion and his worldly life.”"],[17464,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When one of you loves his brother, let him inform him of that.\""],[17465,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “No one fills a vessel worse than the belly. If his self overcomes him, then let him leave a third for himself.”"],[17466,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one dies as a miscarried fetus or decrepit old person — rather people are between that — except that he will be resurrected as a thirty-year-old. Whoever is from the people of Paradise will have the appearance of Adam, the form of Joseph, and the heart of Job. Whoever is from the people of the Fire will be made huge and magnified like mountains.”"],[17467,"We said to Al-Miqdam ibn Ma'di Karb Al-Kindi, \"O Abu Kareemah, people claim that you never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .\" He said, \"Indeed, by Allah, I did see him and he even took hold of my earlobe like this. And I used to walk with my uncle, then he said to my uncle, 'Do you think he remembers?' We said, 'O Abu Kareemah, tell us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .' He said, 'I heard him say, 'All that is between the umbilical cord and the toothless old man will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection with the creation of Adam, the heart of Ayyub, and the beauty of Yusuf, darkened with kohl.' We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, then what about the disbeliever?' He said, 'He will be enlarged for the Fire until his skin becomes forty cubits thick and the molar tooth will be like Uhud.''"],[17468,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The night of the guest is an obligatory right. If he wakes up deprived at his dwelling place, his aid becomes obligatory upon the Muslims until they take for him his right from his crops and his livestock because of the hospitality he was denied.”"],[17469,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The sun will draw near to the people on the Day of Resurrection until it is about two miles away from them, and its heat will intensify and scorch them. They will be in sweat according to their deeds: among them is one whom sweat reaches his ankles, among them is one whom it reaches his knees, among them is one whom it reaches his waist, and among them is one whom the sweat bridles completely.” He said: And I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gesturing with his hands toward his mouth. Ibrahim b. 'Irq said: This is how 'Umar b. Khath'am narrated it from Sulaym, from al-Miqdam."],[17470,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Any man who is a guest of a people and they do not offer him hospitality, he has the right to demand from them the equivalent of his hospitality.”"],[17471,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Whoever stays with a people, it is their duty to offer him hospitality. If they do not offer him hospitality, then he has the right to punish them with the equivalent of his hospitality.”"],[17472,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was given the Book and what equals it. Soon a satiated man reclining on his couch will say: 'Between us and you is this Book; whatever we find in it of lawful we declare lawful, and whatever we find in it of unlawful we declare unlawful.' Indeed, it is not so. The fanged beasts of prey are not lawful, nor domestic donkeys, nor the lost property of a person under covenant unless he has no need of it. And any man who is a guest of a people and they do not offer him hospitality, it is his right to seize from them the equivalent of his hospitality.”"],[17473,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was given the Book and the like of it. Soon a satiated man reclining on his couch will say: 'Adhere to the Qur'an; whatever you find in it of lawful, declare it lawful, and whatever you find in it of unlawful, declare it unlawful.' Indeed, the domestic donkey is not lawful for you, nor any fanged beast of prey, nor the lost property of a person under covenant unless its owner has no need of it. And whoever stays with a people, it is their duty to offer him hospitality.”"],[17474,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will conquer lands in which there are houses called bathhouses. It is forbidden for the males of my ummah to enter them.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, they remove sickness and cleanse dirt.” He said: “Then they are lawful for the males of my ummah in waist-wrappers, and forbidden for the females of my ummah.”"],[17475,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib entered upon him while angry. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is it between us and Quraysh? When they meet each other, they meet with cheerful faces, but when they meet us, they meet us with something other than that.” The Prophet ﷺ became angry until his face turned red, then said: “Faith will not enter the heart of a man until he loves you for the sake of Allah and His Messenger. A man's paternal uncle is of the same stock as his father.”"],[17476,"Al-'Abbas entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, Quraysh meet each other with radiant faces and meet us contrary to that.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry until sweat flowed between his eyes, then said: “A servant will not taste the sweetness of faith until he loves you for the sake of Allah and His Messenger.”"],[17477,"Al-'Abbas came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ angry, and he said: “What brought you?” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is it between us and Quraysh?” He said: “What is it between you and them that brought you here?” He said: “They meet one another with radiant faces, but when they meet us, they meet us with something other than that.” He became angry until a vein between his eyes throbbed. When his anger subsided, he said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, faith will not enter the heart of a man until he loves you for the sake of Allah and His Messenger.” Then he said: “What is the matter with men who harm me concerning al-'Abbas? Verily, a man's paternal uncle is of the same stock as his father.”"],[17478,"Some people from the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, we hear harsh words from some people; one of them says: 'The likeness of Muhammad is only that of a palm tree that grew in a dung heap.'” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and said: “O people, who am I?” They said: “You are the Messenger of Allah.” He said: “I am Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib. We never heard him trace his lineage before that. Allah created His creation and placed me among the best of His creation. Then He divided them into two groups and placed me in the better group. Then He made them into tribes and placed me among the best of them as a tribe. Then He made them into households and placed me in the best household. So I am the best of you in household and the best of you in person.”"],[17479,"Some people from the Ansar said to the Prophet ﷺ: “We hear from some people of Quraysh, until one of them says: 'The likeness of Muhammad is only that of a palm tree that was planted in a dung heap.'” The Prophet ﷺ said: “O people, who am I?” They said: “You are the Messenger of Allah.” He said: “I am Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib.” They said: “We never heard him trace his lineage before that at all.” Then he said: “Allah created His creation, then divided them into two groups and placed me in the better group. Then He made them into tribes and placed me among the best of them as a tribe. So I am the best of you in household and the best of you in person.”"],[17480,"The Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib gathered and said: Will you not ask the Messenger of God ﷺ to assign to you what he assigned to the Banu So-and-so — to assign to you the collection of the poor-due? They met 'Ali and spoke to him, and he said: God ﷻ and His Messenger have refused that for you — that He should assign to you the filth of people's hands, or he said: the washings of people's hands. 'Abd al-Muttalib said to his father: Send me. So al-'Abbas sent his son al-Fadl. We came to the Prophet ﷺ and entered, and he gave each one of us special attention. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"What are you two doing here?\" I said: O Messenger of God, your people and the sons of your paternal uncle have sent us so that you assign to them what you have assigned to the people of the poor-due. He said: God and His Messenger have refused for you that you should eat the filth, or he said: the washings of people's hands."],[17481,"The Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib gathered and said: Will you not ask the Messenger of God ﷺ to assign to you what he assigned to the Banu So-and-so — to assign to you the collection of the poor-due? They met 'Ali and spoke to him, and he said: God ﷻ and His Messenger have refused that for you — that He should assign to you the filth of people's hands, or he said: the washings of people's hands. 'Abd al-Muttalib said to his father: Send me. So al-'Abbas sent his son al-Fadl. We came to the Prophet ﷺ and entered, and he gave each one of us special attention. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"What are you two doing here?\" I said: O Messenger of God, your people and the sons of your paternal uncle have sent us so that you assign to them what you have assigned to the people of the poor-due. He said: God and His Messenger have refused for you that you should eat the filth, or he said: the washings of people's hands."],[17482,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in the Masjid al-Haram while the people were circumambulating the Kaaba between him and the Qiblah without any barrier between him and them."],[17483,"He saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying toward the House with no one between him and the circumambulation area."],[17484,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed at the edge of the circumambulation area with no barrier between him and the circumambulation area. This is the wording of 'Abd Allah b. Salih. Ibn 'Abd al-Hakam said in his hadith: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ when he finished his sa'y, he prayed at the edge of the circumambulation area with no barrier between him and those circumambulating."],[17485,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying near the Corner while men were passing in front of him."],[17486,"The Prophet ﷺ came out of the Ka'bah and stood near the Corner and prayed two rak'ahs while people were passing in front of him circumambulating the House, men and women."],[17487,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray near the Corner by the water-dispensing place while men and women were passing in front of him."],[17488,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying near the Black Corner while men and women were passing in front of him with no barrier between him and them."],[17489,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw a man praying while seated and said: \"The prayer of one seated is half the prayer of one standing.\" So the people forced themselves to stand."],[17490,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a vessel of nabidh, and he poured water over it until it became mild, then he drank from it."],[17491,"The Messenger of God ﷺ circumambulated the House on a hot, thirsty day and asked for water. A man said: O Messenger of God, we have a drink made from this raisin — shall I give you some to drink? He said: \"Yes.\" The man sent to his house and brought a large cup. The Prophet ﷺ brought it near his mouth and found it had a strong smell, so he disliked it and returned it."],[17492,"From his father Muti', whose name was al-'As, and the Messenger of God ﷺ named him Muti'. He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say when he killed that group of people: \"Makkah will not be invaded after this year, and no one of Quraysh will be killed patiently after this year.\""],[17493,"The Prophet ﷺ said on the Day of the Conquest: 'No Qurayshī is to be executed in retaliation after this day.'"],[17494,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of the conquest of Makkah: 'No Qurayshī is to be executed in retaliation after this day until the Day of Resurrection.' And no one from the rebellious Quraysh embraced Islam except Muṭīʿ; his name had been al-ʿĀṣ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Muṭīʿ."],[17495,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of the conquest of Makkah: 'No Qurayshī is to be executed in retaliation after this day until the Day of Resurrection.' And no one from the rebellious Quraysh embraced Islam except Muṭīʿ; his name had been al-ʿĀṣ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Muṭīʿ."],[17496,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ after I had prayed with my family, and the prayer was called, so I sat down. When he finished praying, he said: 'Are you not a Muslim?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What prevented you from praying with the people?' He (the narrator) said: 'I had prayed with my family.' He said: 'Then pray with the people even if you have already prayed with your family.' This is how Sufyān narrated it from Zayd b. Aslam from Bishr b. Miḥjan, and he erred in it; it is actually Busr b. Miḥjan. Thus narrated Mālik and the companions of Zayd b. Aslam."],[17497,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik; and Abū Yazīd al-Qarāṭīsī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us: Mālik informed us; and ʿAlī b. al-Mubārak al-Ṣanʿānī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl b. Abī Uways narrated to us: Mālik narrated to me, from Zayd b. Aslam, from a man of Banū al-Dīl called Busr b. Miḥjan, from his father, that he was in a gathering with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was called to prayer, so he stood up and led them in prayer, then returned, while Miḥjan was still in his place. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'What prevented you from praying with the people? Are you not a Muslim man?' He said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but I prayed with my family.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'When you come, pray with the people even if you have already prayed.'"],[17498,"I prayed ẓuhr or ʿaṣr in my house, then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and sat with him. The prayer was called, and the Prophet ﷺ prayed, but I did not pray. When he finished, he said: 'Are you not a Muslim?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What is the matter with you that you did not pray?' I said: 'I had already prayed in my house.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'When the prayer is called, pray even if you have already prayed.'"],[17499,"I went to the Prophet ﷺ and spoke to him about a matter. Then the prayer was established and I was sitting. The Prophet ﷺ prayed, then he left and found me sitting. He said to me, \"Are you a Muslim?\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"So what prevented you from praying with us?\" I said, \"Indeed, I have already prayed in my saddlebag.\" He said, \"Even if you have already prayed in your saddlebag.\""],[17500,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Sulaymān b. Bilāl narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from Busr b. Miḥjan, from his father, who said: I prayed ẓuhr or ʿaṣr in my house, then I went out to the mosque and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sitting with people around him. I sat with them. Then the prayer was called, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and prayed with the people, then came out and found me sitting in the place where he had seen me. He said: 'Are you not a Muslim man?' I said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I am indeed a Muslim.' He said: 'What prevented you from entering and praying with the people?' I said: 'I had already prayed with my family.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When you have prayed with your family and then come to the mosque and find the people praying, pray with them.'"],[17501,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque and found a man who had finished his prayer and was reciting the tashahhud, saying: 'O Allah, I ask You by Allah, the One, the Eternal Refuge, who neither begot nor was begotten, nor is there to Him any equivalent, to forgive me my sins; indeed You are the Forgiving, the Merciful.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'He has been forgiven, he has been forgiven, he has been forgiven.'"],[17502,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me until we climbed Uḥud and looked over Madinah. He said: 'Woe to its mother, a town whose people will abandon it when it is most flourishing! The Dajjāl will come to it and will find at every one of its entrances an angel with a drawn sword.' Then he descended until he came to the mosque, and there was a man standing and praying and reciting. He said: 'Do you see him? That is ʿAbd Allāh b. Qays. He is indeed an awwāh (one who sighs much in prayer), a forbearing man.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, shall I give him the good news?' He said: 'Beware, do not let him hear you, for you will destroy him.' Then he descended further, and when we reached the mosque, we found Burayda al-Aslamī at one of the gates of the mosque. In the mosque there was a man who prolonged his prayer, and Burayda was a man who liked to joke. He said: 'O Miḥjan, will you not pray as Sukba prays?' He did not answer him, and returned. When he came to his house, he said: 'The best of our religion is its easiest; the best of your religion is its easiest; the best of your religion is its easiest; the best of your religion is its easiest' — three times."],[17503,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on an errand. Then he came upon me while I was leaving on the road from Madinah, and he took me by the hand, and we went until we climbed Uḥud. He turned toward Madinah and said: 'Woe to its mother, a town whose people will abandon it when it is most flourishing.' I said: 'O Prophet of Allah, who will eat its fruit?' He said: 'The birds and beasts of prey in health, and the Dajjāl will not enter it. Every time he wants to enter it, an angel with a drawn sword will meet him at every one of its entrances.' Then he turned and came until he was at the door of the mosque, and there was a man praying. He said: 'Does he say it truthfully?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this is so-and-so; this is the man who prays the most among the people of Madinah.' He said: 'Do not let him hear you, for you will destroy him.'"],[17504,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Ḥājiz, to the right of Madinah, on an errand. When I returned, I went with him until he climbed Uḥud and looked over Madinah. He said: 'Woe to your mother, a town whose people will abandon you when you are at your best.' Then he descended, and I descended with him, until we came to the door of the mosque. He saw a man praying, and he put his hand on my shoulder and illuminated him with his light. He said: 'Does he say it truthfully?' He said it three times. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this is so-and-so, and he is the most devoted worshipper among the people of Madinah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Beware, do not let him hear you, for you will destroy him.' He said it three times."],[17505,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Ḥājiz, to the right of Madinah, on an errand. When I returned, I went with him until he climbed Uḥud and looked over Madinah. He said: 'Woe to your mother, a town whose people will abandon you when you are at your best.' Then he descended, and I descended with him, until we came to the door of the mosque. He saw a man praying, and he put his hand on my shoulder and illuminated him with his light. He said: 'Does he say it truthfully?' He said it three times. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this is so-and-so, and he is the most devoted worshipper among the people of Madinah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Beware, do not let him hear you, for you will destroy him.' He said it three times."],[17506,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The righteous will depart one after another, until only worthless people remain, like the dregs of dates and barley. Allah will pay no heed to them.”"],[17507,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The righteous will depart one after another, and the righteous will be taken, the first and then the first, until only worthless people remain, like the dregs of dates and barley. Allah will pay no heed to them.”"],[17508,"A man struck his brother, so he fled, and we found him with Abu Bakr. We took him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he let us exact retaliation from him."],[17509,"That is, he meant al-Munqa` b. Tamim."],[17510,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with the sadaqah of our camels, and he ordered that it be accepted. I said, “In it are two she-camels as a gift for you.” So the gift was set aside from the sadaqah. A few days later, people began saying that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was going to send Khalid b. al-Walid to the slaves of Egypt — or he said “to Egypt” (Abu Ghassan was unsure) — and would allocate the sadaqah to them. I said, “By Allah, we have no property with us or with our families other than that, and their sadaqah is here.” So I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was on a she-camel of his, and with him was a black man whose head was level with the head of the Prophet ﷺ. I had never seen anyone taller than him. As I drew near, he seemed to lean toward me, but the Prophet ﷺ held him back. I said, “The people have been saying such-and-such.” The Prophet ﷺ raised his hand until I saw the whiteness of his armpits and said: “O Allah, I do not permit them to tell lies about me.” Al-Munqa` said: “I never narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except a statement that a Book has spoken or a Sunnah that has been established. Lies are told about him during his lifetime, so how will it be after his death?”"],[17511,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world compared to the Hereafter is only like when one of you puts his finger in the sea; let him see what he brings back.”"],[17512,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world compared to the Hereafter is only like what one of you brings back when he puts his finger in the sea; let him see what he brings back.” Then he took hold of two joints of my forefinger."],[17513,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world compared to the Hereafter is only like what one of you brings back when he puts his finger in this sea; let him see what he brings back.”"],[17514,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, and indicated with his finger: “By Allah, the world compared to the Hereafter is only like what one of you brings back when he puts his finger in the sea and then takes it out; let him see what he brings back.”"],[17515,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world compared to the Hereafter is only like when one of you walks to the sea and dips his finger in it.”"],[17516,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The righteous will depart, the first and then the first, until only something like the dregs of dates remain. Allah will pay no heed to them.”"],[17517,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The righteous will depart one after another.”"],[17518,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ suffering from gout and complained to him, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The midday heats have belied you.\""],[17519,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Return the needle and the thread; whoever embezzles a needle or thread will be burdened to bring it, and he will not be able to bring it.\""],[17520,"From al-Mustawrid, a man of Banū Fihr who had companionship [with the Prophet], that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, the world compared to the Hereafter is only like a man dipping his finger into the sea and then withdrawing it.\""],[17521,"I was in the riding party with the Messenger of God ﷺ when his eye fell upon a discarded lamb that they had cast aside. He said, \"Do you consider this worthless to its owners?\" They said, \"It is because of its worthlessness that they cast it aside.\" He said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, the world is more worthless to God than this is to its owners.\""],[17522,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I and the Hour have been sent like these two,\" [and he indicated with] the index and middle fingers."],[17523,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Ibn Lahīʿa narrated to us, from al-Ḥārith b. Yazīd, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Jubayr, who said: We were in a gathering in which al-Mustawrid and ʿAmr b. Ghaylān b. Salama were present. Al-Mustawrid said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Whoever undertakes a task for us and has no wife, let him take a wife; whoever has no servant, let him take a servant; whoever has no dwelling, let him take a dwelling; and whoever has no mount, let him take a mount.\" Abū Bakr said, \"You have said much, O Messenger of God.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever takes anything beyond that is an embezzler.\""],[17524,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Whoever undertakes a task for us, if he has no wife, let him marry; or if he has no servant, let him take a servant; or if he has no dwelling, let him take a dwelling; or if he has no mount, let him take a mount. Whoever takes anything beyond that is an embezzler or a thief.\""],[17525,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Whoever is our agent, let him acquire a wife; if he has no servant, let him acquire a servant; and whoever has no dwelling, let him acquire a dwelling.\""],[17526,"\"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ\" when he performed ablution, he would rub between the toes of his feet with his little finger."],[17527,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Every nation has a term, and the term of the nation of Muḥammad is one hundred years.\" He said, \"When it passes the hundred, what God promised it will come to it.\""],[17528,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Every nation has a term, and the term of my nation is one hundred years. When one hundred years pass over my nation, what God promised it will come to it.\" Ibn Lahīʿa said, \"That is, an abundance of tribulations.\""],[17529,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The likeness of the world in relation to the Hereafter is only as when a man dips his finger into the sea and then withdraws it—with how much does it return?\""],[17530,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I was sent in the very time of the Hour, and I preceded it just as this one precedes,\" and he gestured with his two fingers, the index and the middle finger."],[17531,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The world has taken nothing from the Hereafter except as a needle dipped into the sea takes from its water.\""],[17532,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever consumes a meal at the expense of his brother, Allah will feed him a meal like it from the Fire of Jahannam.\""],[17533,"He narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever consumes a meal at the expense of a Muslim man in this world, Allah will feed him the like of it in Jahannam; and whoever is clothed with a garment at the expense of a Muslim man, Allah will clothe him with the like of it from Jahannam; and whoever takes a stand on behalf of a Muslim for show, Allah will make him stand in a position of notoriety and show.\""],[17534,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The Hour will not come until the Romans are the most numerous of people.\" This reached 'Amr b. al-'As, who said: \"What are these reports that are mentioned from you?\" Al-Mustawrid said to him: \"I said what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" 'Amr said: \"If you say that, they are the most forbearing of people at the time of calamity, the most patient of people at the time of affliction, and the best of people to their weak and their poor.\""],[17535,"I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"The righteous will depart one after another, and there will remain the dregs of society, like the dregs of dates and barley, and Allah will pay no attention to them.\""],[17536,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us at Arafah and said, \"Every household among the Muslims should offer a sacrifice and have a meal called 'Ateerah.' Do you know what 'Ateerah' means? It means what you call Rajabiyyah.\""],[17537,"We were standing with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"O people, indeed, every household has a sacrifice and an 'Atirah in every year. Do you know what is 'Atirah? It is what people call Al-Rajabiyah.\""],[17538,"I arrived to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Arafah and he was saying, \"Do you know it?\" I do not know what they (the people) responded to him. So the Prophet ﷺ said, \"It is upon the people of every household to sacrifice a sheep in every Rajab and a sheep in every Eid al-Adha.\""],[17539,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whomever you seize of the men of the Jews, kill him.\" Muhayyisa jumped upon Ibn Sunayna, a man from the Jewish merchants whom he used to associate with and do business with, and killed him. Huwayyisa at that time had not yet embraced Islam and was older than Muhayyisa. When he killed him, Huwayyisa began to beat him and say: \"O enemy of Allah, you killed him? By Allah, perhaps there is fat in your belly from his wealth.\" I said: \"By Allah, if he had ordered me to kill you, I would have struck your neck.\" He said: \"By Allah, it was the first thing of Huwayyisa's Islam.\" He said: \"By Allah, if Muhammad ordered you to kill me, you would kill me?\" Muhayyisa said: \"Yes, by Allah.\" Huwayyisa said: \"By Allah, a religion that has reached this point is truly astonishing.\" So Huwayyisa embraced Islam."],[17540,"He was called Nafi' Abu Tayba. He went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ask him about his earnings (from cupping). He said: \"Do not touch it.\" He returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Feed it to your watering camel; put it in its stomach.\""],[17541,"He was called Abu Tayba, and he earned a great deal. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the earnings of the cupper, he sought a concession from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but he refused him. He continued to speak with him and mention his need to him until he said to him: \"Throw its earnings into the belly of your watering camel.\""],[17542,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission regarding the earnings of the cupper, and he forbade him from it. He did not cease to go back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mention his need to him until he gave him permission to feed it to his watering camel and his slaves."],[17543,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A community in which the right of the weak is not taken without him being made to suffer is not sanctified.\""],[17544,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, a man comes to me wanting my wealth.\" He said: \"Remind him of Allah.\" He said: \"What if he does not take heed?\" He said: \"Then seek help against him from the Muslims around you.\" He said: \"What if there is no one around me?\" He said: \"Then seek help against him from the authority.\" He said: \"What if the authority sells me out?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fight in defense of your wealth until you are among the martyrs of the Hereafter or you prevent that.\""],[17545,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, if a man comes to me wanting my property, how do you command me?\" He said, \"Remind him of God.\" I said, \"What do you think if I do that and he does not refrain?\" He said, \"Seek help from the Muslims.\" I said, \"What do you think if I do that and I find no one among the Muslims?\" He said, \"Seek help from the ruler.\" I said, \"What do you think if the ruler forsakes me and insists only on seizing my property?\" He said, \"Then fight him until you defend your property or you become one of the martyrs of the Hereafter.\""],[17546,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"What do you think about a man who meets me in a desolate land wanting my property?\" He said, \"Remind him of God.\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, what if he does not take heed?\" He said, \"Then seek help against him from other Muslims besides yourself.\" He said, \"What if there is no one around me?\" He said, \"Then seek help against him from the ruler.\" He said, \"What do you think if the ruler refuses to help me?\" He said, \"Then fight in defense of your property until you become one of the martyrs of the Hereafter or you defend your property.\""],[17547,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"What do you think if a man comes to me wanting to take my property?\" He said, \"Remind him of God.\" He said, \"What do you think if I remind him of God and he does not take heed?\" He said, \"Seek help against him from the ruler.\" He said, \"What do you think if the ruler forsakes me?\" He said, \"Seek help from the Muslims who are present with you.\" He said, \"What do you think if no one is present with me?\" He said, \"Then fight in defense of your property, or you will be killed and become one of the martyrs of the Hereafter.\""],[17548,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"A tribulation will convulse the earth like the horns of cattle.\" Then a veiled man passed by, and he said, \"This one and his companions will be upon guidance on that day.\" And it turned out to be ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān."],[17549,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the road to Madinah when he said, \"What will you do in a tribulation that will spread through the regions of the earth like the horns of cattle?\" We said, \"O Messenger of God, what should we do?\" A man was in front of him, so he said, \"Follow this man and his companions.\" I went quickly to that man, who was hastening, and I took hold of him and turned him toward the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"This one, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"He was ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān.\""],[17550,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the road to Madinah, he said, \"What will you do about a tribulation that will arise in the regions of the earth like the horns of cattle?\" They said, \"What should we do, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"You must adhere to this man and his companions,\" or \"Follow this man and his companions.\" I hurried until I turned the man around and said, \"O Prophet of God, this one?\" He said, \"This one.\" And it turned out he was ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān."],[17551,"He said: \"By God, were it not for something I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, I would not have stood in this place.\" When Muʿāwiyah heard mention of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he seated the people and said: \"While we were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ, ʿUthmān passed by, having combed his hair and wearing a waist-wrapper. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'A tribulation will surely emerge from under my foot—or from under this foot of mine—and this man and whoever follows him will be upon guidance on that day.' I stood up and took hold of ʿUthmān's shoulder and turned him toward the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I said, 'This one?' He said, 'Yes, this one and whoever follows him will be upon guidance on that day.'\" Then ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥawālah al-Anṣārī stood up from near the pulpit and said, \"You are indeed the companion of this affair?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"By God, I was present at that gathering, and if I had known that I had anyone in the army who would confirm it, I would have been the first to speak of it.\""],[17552,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"A group of my community will continue to be upon the truth, victorious over those who oppose them, and they will be like a vessel among eaters until the command of God comes and they are in that state.\" We said, \"O Messenger of God, where are they?\" He said, \"On the outskirts of Jerusalem.\" He said: And he also told me that \"al-Ramlah is the elevated place, because it faces west and east.\""],[17553,"The Prophet ﷺ supplicated against the Muḍar tribe. I said, \"O Messenger of God, God has granted you and answered you, and your people have been destroyed. So supplicate for them that He sends them rain.\" He said, \"O God, give us abundant, wholesome, swift, plentiful, widespread, immediate, not delayed, beneficial and not harmful rain.\" He said, \"It was not even a Friday or so before we were rained upon.\""],[17554,"The Prophet ﷺ supplicated against the Muḍar tribe. I said, \"O Messenger of God, God has granted you and answered you, and your people have been destroyed. So supplicate for them that He sends them rain.\" He said, \"O God, give us abundant, wholesome, swift, plentiful, widespread, immediate, not delayed, beneficial and not harmful rain.\" He said, \"It was not even a Friday or so before we were rained upon.\""],[17555,"\"Tell us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, may your father be for God's sake, and be careful.\" He said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ supplicated against the Muḍar tribe, so I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of God, God has granted you and answered you and aided you, and your people have been destroyed. So supplicate to God for them that He sends them rain.' He said, 'O God, give us abundant, wholesome, fertile, swift, plentiful, widespread, immediate, not delayed, beneficial and not harmful rain.'\" He said, \"It was not even a Friday before we were rained upon.\""],[17556,"\"Tell us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, may your father be for God's sake, and be careful.\" He said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ supplicated against the Muḍar tribe, so I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of God, God has granted you and answered you and aided you, and your people have been destroyed. So supplicate to God for them that He sends them rain.' He said, 'O God, give us abundant, wholesome, fertile, swift, plentiful, widespread, immediate, not delayed, beneficial and not harmful rain.'\" He said, \"It was not even a Friday before we were rained upon.\""],[17557,"I said: O Messenger of God, which part of the night is most heard? He said: \"The last part of the night. Then prayer is accepted until dawn breaks. Then no prayer until the sun is at the height of a spear or two spears. Then prayer is accepted until the shadow stands as a spear. Then no prayer until the sun declines. Then prayer is accepted until the sun is the length of a spear or two spears. Then no prayer until the sun sets.\""],[17558,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I and the caretaker of an orphan, for him or for another, will be in Paradise like these two,\" and Sufyan gestured with his two fingers."],[17559,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The caretaker of an orphan, for him or for another, if he is God-fearing, will be with me in Paradise like these two,\" meaning the forefinger and the middle finger."],[17560,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was praying over a funeral when a woman came with a censer wanting the funeral, so he shouted at her until she entered the thickets of Madinah."],[17561,"We went out with a group of merchants selling cloth, and with them was a weigher who weighed for a fee. We arrived at Makkah, and the Prophet ﷺ bought trousers from them, and he said to the weigher: \"Weigh and give more.\""],[17562,"I saw my father clip his nails and then bury them. He said: My little daughter, \"This is how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.\""],[17563,"I heard my father narrate, and he had lived through the Jahiliyyah and Islam. He said: I set up traps for myself at al-Abwa'. A gazelle fell into one of the traps, and the rope flipped over. We went out following its tracks, and I found a man who had taken it. We disputed and took the matter to the Prophet ﷺ. We found him camped at al-Abwa' under a tree, shading himself with a leather mat. He judged it between us as two halves. I said: O Messenger of God, these are my traps on its leg. He said: \"That is it.\" I said: O Messenger of God, we are at a water source, and camels come to us thirsty, so we give them water. Is there any reward for us in that? He said: \"Yes, in every living being with a warm liver there is reward.\" I said: O Messenger of God, tall camels meet us with their udders tied, and we are hungry. He said: \"Say: O owner of the camels, O owner of the camels, three times. If he comes, then fine; otherwise, untie their udder straps, milk, drink, and retie their udder straps, and leave for the milk its channels.\""],[17564,"I heard my father narrate, and he had lived through the Jahiliyyah and Islam. He said: I set up traps for myself at al-Abwa'. A gazelle fell into one of the traps, and the rope flipped over. We went out following its tracks, and I found a man who had taken it. We disputed and took the matter to the Prophet ﷺ. We found him camped at al-Abwa' under a tree, shading himself with a leather mat. He judged it between us as two halves. I said: O Messenger of God, these are my traps on its leg. He said: \"That is it.\" I said: O Messenger of God, we are at a water source, and camels come to us thirsty, so we give them water. Is there any reward for us in that? He said: \"Yes, in every living being with a warm liver there is reward.\" I said: O Messenger of God, tall camels meet us with their udders tied, and we are hungry. He said: \"Say: O owner of the camels, O owner of the camels, three times. If he comes, then fine; otherwise, untie their udder straps, milk, drink, and retie their udder straps, and leave for the milk its channels.\""],[17565,"I heard my father narrate, and he had lived through the Jahiliyyah and Islam. He said: I set up traps for myself at al-Abwa'. A gazelle fell into one of the traps, and the rope flipped over. We went out following its tracks, and I found a man who had taken it. We disputed and took the matter to the Prophet ﷺ. We found him camped at al-Abwa' under a tree, shading himself with a leather mat. He judged it between us as two halves. I said: O Messenger of God, these are my traps on its leg. He said: \"That is it.\" I said: O Messenger of God, we are at a water source, and camels come to us thirsty, so we give them water. Is there any reward for us in that? He said: \"Yes, in every living being with a warm liver there is reward.\" I said: O Messenger of God, tall camels meet us with their udders tied, and we are hungry. He said: \"Say: O owner of the camels, O owner of the camels, three times. If he comes, then fine; otherwise, untie their udder straps, milk, drink, and retie their udder straps, and leave for the milk its channels.\""],[17566,"We were on a military expedition, and with us was a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Mujashi' from Banu Sulaym. Sheep became scarce, so he ordered a caller, who announced that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A jadha'ah fulfills what a thaniyyah fulfills.\""],[17567,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of the conquest and said: O Messenger of God, this is my brother Mujalid b. Mas'ud, so accept his pledge of allegiance for emigration. He said: \"There is no emigration after the conquest of Makkah, but I will accept his pledge for Islam.\""],[17568,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with my brother Ma'bad to pledge allegiance for emigration. He said: \"The people of emigration have gone with what is in it.\" I said: Then upon what will you accept his pledge? He said: \"I will accept his pledge upon Islam, or faith, and jihad.\" Later I met Ma'bad, and I asked him, and he was the older of the two, and he said: He spoke the truth."],[17569,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him upon emigration, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Rather, we pledge allegiance upon Islam, for there is no emigration after the conquest, and you will be among the followers in excellence.”"],[17570,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of the conquest and said: “O Messenger of Allah, this is my brother Mujalid b. Mas'ud, so accept his pledge upon emigration.” He said: “There is no emigration after the conquest of Makkah, but I accept his pledge upon Islam.”"],[17571,"He said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night he departed from al-Ji'ranah until he entered the evening as a performer of 'umrah, then entered Makkah at night and completed his 'umrah, then left that same night and arrived at al-Ji'ranah as if he had spent the night there. Then when the sun had passed its zenith, he departed from al-Ji'ranah into the valley of Sarif until the road met the Madinah road at Sarif.” Muharrish said: “That is why his 'umrah was hidden from many people.”"],[17572,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'umrah from al-Ji'ranah, then returned as if he had spent the night there.” That is why his 'umrah was hidden from many people."],[17573,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'umrah from al-Ji'ranah, and I looked at his back as if it were an ingot of silver, and he arrived in the morning as if he had spent the night there.”"],[17574,"From 'Urwah: “Among those named as having witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is Marthad b. Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi.”"],[17575,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Marthad b. Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi, the ally of Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, to a tribe of Hudhayl, and among the Muslims killed there was, from Banu Hashim, Marthad b. Abi Marthad.”"],[17576,"After Uhud, a group from 'Adal and al-Qarah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, there is Islam among us, so send with us a group of your companions to teach us the religion, recite the Qur'an to us, and teach us the laws of Islam.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent six of his companions, including Marthad b. Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi, the ally of Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib. He mentioned the story, saying: “As for Marthad b. Abi Marthad, Khalid b. al-Bukayr, and 'Asim b. Thabit, they said: 'By Allah, we will never accept a covenant or pact from a polytheist.' They fought them until they killed them.”"],[17577,"From Ibn Shihab, naming those killed on the day of al-Raji': Marthad b. Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi."],[17578,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If you want your prayer to be accepted, let the best among you lead you, for they are your delegation between you and your Lord.”"],[17579,"From Marthad, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Allah drew two lines in His book, then lifted the pen and wrote in one of them the creation, and wrote in the other what the creation will do.”"],[17580,"That the Prophet ﷺ was urinating, or he said: I passed by him while he had urinated, so I greeted him and he did not return my greeting until he finished his ablution, then he returned my greeting."],[17581,"That he greeted the Prophet ﷺ while he was urinating, and he did not return the greeting until he had performed ablution."],[17582,"I passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and greeted him while he was performing ablution. He did not return my greeting until he finished, then he returned my greeting and apologized to me, saying: 'Nothing prevented me from returning your greeting except that I disliked mentioning Allah while not in a state of purity.'"],[17583,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with three people on a riding beast, and he said: 'The third is cursed.'"],[17584,"I heard Muhajir, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, say: 'I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for years, and he never said to me about anything I did, \"Why did you do it?\" nor about anything I left, \"Why did you leave it?\"' Ibn Bukayr said: 'This Bukayr mentioned in the hadith is my grandfather.'"],[17585,"From Mas'ud, the servant of his grandfather Farwah Abu Tamim, he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr passed by me. Abu Bakr said to me: \"O Mas'ud, go to Abu Tamim, your master, and tell him to send with us a guide who will take us by the most hidden route, and a camel and provisions.\" So I went to my master and told him, and he sent me along with a camel and a skin of milk. I came to them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to pray with Abu Bakr on his right. I stood behind them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pushed Abu Bakr in the chest, and we stood behind him.'"],[17586,"That the Prophet ﷺ named him Muta' and said to him: 'O Muta', you are obeyed among your people.' And he said to him: 'Go to your companions,' and he mounted him on a piebald horse and gave him the banner, saying: 'Whoever enters under this banner of mine is safe from punishment.'"],[17587,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Khazraj, then from Banu al-Najjar: Abu Muhammad al-Ansari, whose name is Mas'ud b. Aws b. Asram b. Zayd b. Tha'labah b. Ghanm b. Malik b. al-Najjar."],[17588,"That a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ bought a Berber slave girl for two hundred dinars, then he sent her to Abu Muhammad al-Badri, one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who had been at Badr, and he gave him the Berber slave girl as a gift. When she came to him, he said: 'This is one of the Magians whom the Prophet ﷺ forbade, along with those who associate partners with Allah.' I narrated this hadith to a man, and he told me that Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to him that an uncle of his died in the Maghrib and he had been at Badr."],[17589,"From 'Urwah, in naming those who were martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar, then from Banu Zurayq: Mas'ud b. Sa'd b. Khalid."],[17590,"From Ibn Shihab, in naming those who were martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar, then from Banu Zurayq: Mas'ud b. Sa'd b. Qays."],[17591,"Narrated by the Prophet, ﷺ , he said, \"The servant will continue to ask and request while he is wealthy until he shaves his face [i.e., until death], and he will not have any standing before Allah.\""],[17592,"To the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning the Makhzumi woman who stole a velvet cloth: 'We will ransom her for forty uqiyyahs.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'That she be purified is better for her,' and he ordered that her hand be cut off."],[17593,"We heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and that distressed us greatly, for she was from Quraysh. We came to the Prophet ﷺ and spoke to him, saying: 'O Messenger of Allah, we will ransom her for forty uqiyyahs.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'That she be purified is better for her.' When we heard the softness of the Messenger of Allah's words, we went to Usamah b. Zayd and spoke to him, saying: 'Intercede for us with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning this woman, and we will ransom her for forty uqiyyahs.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw that, he stood among us as a preacher and said: 'O people, why do you insist so much regarding one of the limits set by Allah that has fallen upon a maidservant among the maidservants of Allah? By the One in whose hand is my soul, if Fatimah daughter of Muhammad had committed what this woman has fallen into, I would cut off her hand.' The people despaired, and he cut off her hand."],[17594,"When the woman stole that velvet cloak from the house of the Messenger of God ﷺ and he ordered that her hand be cut off, that weighed heavily on us. She was a woman of Quraysh, so we came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and spoke to him, saying, \"We will ransom her for forty uqiyyahs.\" He said, \"Let her be purified; that is better for her.\" When we heard the gentleness in the Messenger of God's ﷺ words, we went to Usama b. Zayd and said to him, \"Will you not speak to the Messenger of God ﷺ about the matter of this woman, for we will ransom her for forty uqiyyahs?\" When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw that, he stood up to give a sermon and said, \"O people, why do you keep pressing me regarding one of the prescribed punishments of God that has fallen upon a servant woman among God's maidservants? By Him in whose hand my soul is, if Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, had done what this woman did, I would carry out the punishment on her.\""],[17595,"\"I sent a sheep to the Messenger of God ﷺ and then went off on some errand. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent half of it back to them.\" I returned to Umm Khunas, his wife, and found meat with her. I said, \"O Umm Khunas, what is this meat?\" She said, \"This is the meat that your beloved ﷺ sent back to us from the sheep you sent to him.\" He said, \"Why do you not feed your dependents from it since the morning?\" She said, \"This is their leftover, and I have fed all of them. They used to slaughter two or three sheep, and it was not enough for them.\""],[17596,"Masruq b. Wa'il came to the Messenger of God ﷺ in Madinah at al-'Aqiq, embraced Islam, and his Islam was good. He said, \"O Messenger of God, I would like you to send to my people a man to call them to Islam and to write a letter for us to my people, that perhaps God may guide them by it.\" So he said to Mu'awiya, \"Write for him: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. To the Afnad of Hadramawt: regarding performing prayer, giving zakat, charity according to one's means, the animal kept at home for milk, and the fifth on hidden treasures; on well-irrigated land one-tenth. No combining, no separating, no shighar marriage, no tying a pregnant camel's legs to prevent her young from nursing, no keeping animals away from water to gather them for zakat, no driving them to the collector, no two camels tied together in one hobble. Whoever withholds zakat has committed usury. Every intoxicant is forbidden.\" And he sent Ziyad b. Labid al-Ansari to them. As for combining, it is not gathering flocks together; as for separating, it is not separating them to reduce the number; as for shighar, it is a man marrying off his daughter on condition that the other marries him to his daughter without a dowry; as for shinaq, it is tying a camel in its resting place; and as for ijba', it is selling fruit before it is safe from blight."],[17597,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"There is no ill omen, but good fortune may be in three things: a woman, a horse, and a house.\""],[17598,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, I am away from water for a month and I have my family with me; may I have intercourse with them?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, I am away for months.\" He said, \"Even if you are away for thirty years.\""],[17599,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"You must be truthful, for it leads to Paradise.\""],[17600,"He was called Bahir, from Sama'il, a village in Oman. One day we sacrificed an atira—that is, a slaughtered animal—before him, and I heard a voice from the idol saying, \"O Mazin, listen and be glad! Good has appeared and evil is concealed. A prophet has been sent from Mudar with the great religion of God. So abandon carved stones and you will be safe from Saqar.\" I was startled by that and said, \"This is indeed strange.\" Then after some days I sacrificed another atira and heard a voice from the idol saying, \"Come to me, come! Hear what you do not know. This is a sent prophet who has come with truth sent down. Believe in him so that you may turn away from the heat of a fire that blazes, whose fuel is rocks.\" I said, \"This is indeed strange, and it is good intended for me.\" While we were in that state, a man arrived from the Hijaz. We said, \"What news is behind you?\" He said, \"A man has appeared called Ahmad, who says to those who come to him, 'Answer the caller of God.'\" I said, \"This is the news of what I have heard.\" So I went to the idol and smashed it to pieces, mounted my riding camel, and came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He explained Islam to me and I embraced it, and I said..."],[17601,"That his grandfather, Mazin b. Khaythama, and Hubayl b. Ka'b, one of the Banu Mazin, were sent by Mu'adh b. Jabal on the day he encamped between al-Sakun and al-Sakasik and fought until the people submitted as delegations to the Messenger of God ﷺ. \"And he established brotherhood between al-Sakun and al-Sakasik.\""],[17602,"Rifa'a b. Zayd came as a delegate to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he wrote a document for him in which was: \"In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is a document from Muhammad, the Messenger of God, to Rifa'a b. Zayd. I have sent him to his people generally and to those who join them, calling them to God and to His Messenger. Whoever believes is in the party of God and in the party of His Messenger ﷺ, and whoever turns away has protection for two months.\" When he came to his people, they answered him. Then he traveled until he stopped at the Harra of al-Rajla'. He had not stayed long when Dihya al-Kalbi came from Qurayza, where the Messenger of God ﷺ had sent him, until when he was in one of their valleys called Shinan, with merchandise of his, al-Hunayd b. 'Uways and his father al-'Uways al-Duba'i—a branch of Judham—raided him and seized everything he had. Then a group of Rifa'a's people went to him, and among those who came was al-Nu'man b. Abi Ji'al. They met them and fought, and Qurra b. Ashqar al-Dala'i threw a stone at al-Nu'man b. Abi Ji'al, hitting his heel and bloodying it, and said, \"I am the son of Uthala!\" Then al-Nu'man b. Abi Ji'al shot him with an arrow, hitting his knee, and said, \"I am the son of Iqala!\" Hassan b. Milla al-Dabbi had accompanied Dihya al-Kalbi before that and taught him the Opening of the Book. They recovered what was in their hands and returned it to Dihya. Then Dihya came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him their news, and asked him for the blood of al-Hunayd and his father 'Uways. That is what stirred up Zayd and Judham. So the Messenger of God ﷺ sent Zayd b. Haritha and sent an army with him. Ghatafan, Judham, Wa'il, and those of Salman and Sa'd b. Hudhayl had already set out when Rifa'a came to them with the letter of the Prophet ﷺ. He stopped at the Harra of al-Rajla', and Rifa'a was at Kura' al-Ghamim, with him a horseman from Banu al-Dubayb, while the rest of Banu al-Dubayb were at Wadi Madariq on the side of the Harra."],[17603,"On the authority of his grandfather, raising it to the Prophet ﷺ: He commanded applying prepared antimony at bedtime and said, \"Let the fasting person avoid it.\""],[17604,"The Prophet ﷺ was at Qudayd when a man came to him. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Have you eaten anything today for the day of Ashura?\" He said, \"No, except that I drank some water.\" He said, \"Then do not eat anything until the sun sets, and command those behind you to fast this day.\""],[17605,"Matar b. al-'Ala' narrated to me: my aunt Amina bt. Abi al-Sha'tha' and Qutba, her freedwoman, narrated to me that they saw Madluk, Abu Sufyan, and heard him say: I came to the Prophet ﷺ with my freedmen and embraced Islam. Amina said, \"I saw that the part of the Prophet's ﷺ head that he wiped was black, while the rest of his hair had turned white.\""],[17606,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ in the pre-Islamic period saying to the people: “Say: There is no god but God, and you will prosper.” Some of them spat in his face, some threw dust at him, and some insulted him, until midday came. Then a young girl came with a bowl of water and washed his face and hands, and he said: “O my little daughter, do not fear poverty or humiliation for your father.” I asked: Who is this? They said: Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ, and she was a radiant young girl."],[17607,"I performed Hajj with my father. When we were at Mina, there was a gathering. I said to my father: What is this gathering? He said: Around this Sabian (i.e., the Prophet). And there was the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: “O people, say: There is no god but God, and you will prosper.”"],[17608,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When Allah decrees for a man to die in a certain land, He grants him a need therein.\""],[17609,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When God ﷻ decrees a servant’s death in a land, He creates for him a need there.”"],[17610,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He was asked, which deeds are best? He said: “Faith in God alone, then jihad, then an accepted Hajj, which surpasses all other deeds as the distance between the rising of the sun and its setting.”"],[17611,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: Which deeds are best? He said: “Faith in God and jihad in His path.” Then [the man’s thigh] trembled, and he said: Then what? He said: “Then a deed that is better than all other deeds, except like an accepted Hajj.”"],[17612,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: Which deeds are best? He said: “Faith in God and jihad in His path.” Then the questioner’s thigh trembled, and he said: Then what? He said: “Then a deed that is better than all other deeds, except like an accepted Hajj.”"],[17613,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was speaking to his companions, he said to them: “A group of riders will appear to you from this direction; they are the best people of the East.” Umar b. al-Khattab stood up and went in that direction, where he met thirteen riders. He welcomed them, drew near, and asked: Who are the people? They said: A group from Abd al-Qays. He said: What has brought you to this land? Trade? They said: No. He said: Are you selling these swords of yours? They said: No. He said: Perhaps you have come seeking this man? They said: Yes. He walked with them, talking, until he saw the Prophet ﷺ and said: This is your companion whom you seek. The people threw themselves from their saddles; some ran, some jogged, and some walked until they reached the Prophet ﷺ and took his hand and kissed it, then sat with him. Al-Ashajj, who was the youngest of the group, stayed behind; he made the camels kneel, hobbled them, gathered the people’s belongings, then came walking slowly until he reached the Prophet ﷺ, took his hand and kissed it. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “You have two qualities that God and His Messenger love.” He said: What are they, O Prophet of God? He said: “Forbearance and deliberateness.” He said: O Prophet of God, is it a disposition I was created with, or a character I have acquired? He said: “Rather, it is a disposition you were created with.” He said: Praise be to God who created me with what God and His Messenger love. Then the people turned to some dates they had and began eating. The Prophet ﷺ spoke to them about the dates, naming this one such-and-such and that one such-and-such. They said: Yes, O Prophet of God, we are not more knowledgeable of their names than you. He said: “Yes.” Then they said to a man among them: Feed us from the remainder of the portion left in your bag. He brought them barni dates. The Prophet ﷺ said: “This is barni. It is among the best of your dates; it is a medicine with no disease in it.”"],[17614,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah on the day of the conquest, and on his sword there was gold and silver."],[17615,"I heard my grandfather Mazidah al-Abdi say: “The Prophet ﷺ tied the banners of the Ansar and made them yellow.”"],[17616,"He was with the Prophet ﷺ that year, and they forgot it."],[17617,"I went out for Hajj and passed by people praying at a mosque, saying: This is the tree of the pledge of Ridwan, when the Messenger of God ﷺ accepted the pledge. I went to Said b. al-Musayyib and informed him. He said: My father told me that he was among those who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ under the tree. He said: When we went out the following year, we forgot it and could not locate it. Said said: “If the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ did not know it, and you know it, then you are more knowledgeable.”"],[17618,"“I saw the tree, then I came to it later but did not recognize it.”"],[17619,"that his father came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “What is your name?” I said, “Hazn.” He said, “You are Sahl.” He said, “I will not give up its name.” Saʿīd said, “That harshness remains among us to this hour.”"],[17620,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his grandfather, “What is your name?” He said, “Hazn.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Rather, you are Sahl.” He said, “I will not change a name my father gave me.” So that harshness has remained among us ever since."],[17621,"When death approached Abū Ṭālib, and Abū Jahl b. Hishām and ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Umayya were with him, the Prophet ﷺ came to him and said, “O uncle, say ‘There is no god but Allah,’ a word with which I will plead for you before Allah.” They said, “O Abū Ṭālib, will you turn away from the religion of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib?” Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {Indeed, you do not guide whom you love, but Allah guides whom He wills, and He knows best those who are guided}."],[17622,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[17623,"that the Prophet ﷺ said, “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[17624,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “If you must do it, then once,” meaning wiping the pebbles."],[17625,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about a man who smooths the pebbles and dust where he prostrates: “If you must do it, then once.”"],[17626,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do not wipe while you are praying, but if you must do it, then once,” meaning smoothing the pebbles."],[17627,"that he asked the Prophet ﷺ about wiping during prayer, and he said, “Once, or leave it.”"],[17628,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to him regarding wiping during prayer, “If you must do it, then once.”"],[17629,"from the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “The Throne shook at the death of Saʿd b. Muʿādh.”"],[17630,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ observed iʿtikāf in a dome of palm leaves whose door was a mat, while the people were in the mosque.”"],[17631,"The ring of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was made of iron coated with silver. Sometimes it would be on my hand, and Mu'ayqib was in charge of the ring of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[17632,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Fire is forbidden for the one who is gentle, soft, easygoing, and close to the people.\""],[17633,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, when were you a prophet? He said: \"While Adam was between the spirit and the body.\""],[17634,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, when were you a prophet? He said: \"While Adam was between the spirit and the body.\""],[17635,"I heard a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Maymun b. Sunbad say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The uprightness of my community is through its wicked ones.\""],[17636,"Beware of our youth. Maymun or Mihran, the freed slave of the Prophet ﷺ, informed me that he passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"O Maymun – or Mihran – we are a household forbidden from receiving charity, and our freed slaves are from ourselves, so do not consume charity.\""],[17637,"I entered upon Umm Kulthum bt. Ali with something from the charity, and she said: A freed slave of ours called Kaysan or Hurmuz informed me that he passed by the Prophet ﷺ. He said: He called me, so I came, and he said: \"O so-and-so, we are a household forbidden from taking charity, and the freed slave of a people is from themselves, so do not consume charity.\""],[17638,"From al-Munaydhir, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who was in Ifriqiya, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever says in the morning: 'I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet,' I am the guarantor to take him by the hand until I admit him to Paradise.\""],[17639,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to al-Mundhir b. Sawa: \"Whoever prays our prayer, faces our qibla, and eats our slaughtered meat, that is the Muslim who has the protection of Allah and the protection of the Messenger ﷺ.\""],[17640,"That the Muslims said on the day of the Battle of Ma'una when the enemy surrounded them: \"O Allah, we cannot find anyone to convey our message to Your Messenger other than You. O Allah, convey our greetings and inform him of our situation.\""],[17641,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed after Uhud for the rest of Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa'dah, Dhu al-Hijjah – and the polytheists oversaw that pilgrimage – and al-Muharram. Then he sent the people of Bi'r Ma'unah on an expedition at the beginning of four months after Uhud."],[17642,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed after Uhud for the rest of Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa'dah, Dhu al-Hijjah – and the polytheists oversaw that pilgrimage – and al-Muharram. Then he sent the people of Bi'r Ma'unah on an expedition at the beginning of four months after Uhud."],[17643,"From al-Miswar b. Makhramah and Marwan b. al-Hakam, they said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions set out from al-Hudaybiyyah, numbering some one hundred and ten companions, until they reached Dhu al-Hulayfah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ garlanded the sacrificial animal and marked it, then entered ihram for Umrah."],[17644,"On the authority of his family, during the era of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, my father has died and had obligated himself to walk to Makkah and to slaughter a camel, but he left no wealth. Should I fulfill it on his behalf by walking for him and slaughtering a camel from my own wealth?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Yes, fulfill it on his behalf, and slaughter, and walk. Do you not see that if your father owed a debt to a man and you paid it on his behalf from your wealth, would the man not go back satisfied? And God is more deserving that He be satisfied.”"],[17645,"He polished the sword of the Messenger of God ﷺ Dhu al-Faqar, and it had a silver pommel, rings on its scabbard, and a silver ring in its middle."],[17646,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever circumambulates the House seven times without engaging in idle talk therein, it is like the reward of freeing a slave.”"],[17647,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he went out one night, having delayed the Isha prayer until a short while—or an hour—of the night had passed, while the people were waiting in the mosque. He said, “What are you waiting for?” They said, “We are waiting for the prayer.” He said, “Indeed, you will continue to be in prayer as long as you wait for it.” Then he said, “Indeed, it is a prayer that no one among the nations before you ever prayed.” Then he raised his head toward the sky and said, “The stars are a safeguard for the sky; if the stars are obliterated, there will come to the sky what they are promised. I am a safeguard for my Companions; when I am taken, there will come to my Companions what they are promised. My Companions are a safeguard for my community; when my Companions are taken, there will come to my community what it is promised. O Bilal, give the call to commence.”"],[17648,"There was a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and none of them had a mount except he would alternate riding it, apart from me. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ would dismount and then say to me, “Ride.” I would say, “I have strength,” until he did that two or three times, then he would say, “You are nothing but a water channel.” He said: “It became one of the names dearest to me.”"],[17649,"There was a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and none of them had a mount except he would alternate riding it, apart from me. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ would dismount and then say to me, “Ride.” I would say, “I have strength,” until he did that two or three times, then he would say, “You are nothing but a water channel.” He said: “It became one of the names dearest to me.”"],[17650,"And the first of the emigrants to come to us was Mus'ab b. 'Umayr, one of the Banu 'Abd al-Dar b. Qusayy. I said to him, “What has the Messenger of God ﷺ done?” He said, “He is in his place, and his companions are following in my footsteps.”"],[17651,"When the pilgrimage season came, a group of the Ansar from Banu Malik b. al-Najjar performed Hajj, among them Mu'adh b. 'Afra' and As'ad b. Zurara, and from Banu Zurayq Rafi' b. Malik and Dhakwan b. 'Abd Qays, and from Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayhan, and from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf 'Uwaym b. Sa'ida. The Messenger of God ﷺ came to them and told them the news of what God had chosen for him of prophethood and honor, and he recited the Quran to them. When they heard his words, they listened and their souls were at peace with his call. They recognized what they used to hear from the People of the Book of their mention of him by his description and what he called them to, so they believed him and had faith in him, and they were among the means of good.” Then they said to him, “You have known what is between the Aws and the Khazraj of bloodshed. We love what God has guided to and commanded you with, and we are for God and for you striving. We advise you to do as you see fit. Stay, in the name of God, until we return to our people and tell them of your affair and call them to God and His Messenger. Perhaps God will make peace between us and unite our affair, for today we are distant from one another and hateful to one another. If you come to us today while we have not reconciled, we will have no unified support for you. But we will appoint for you the next year's pilgrimage season.” The Messenger of God ﷺ was pleased with what they said. So they returned to their people and called them secretly, and told them about the Messenger of God ﷺ and what God had sent him with, and what he called to with the Quran, until there remained hardly a house among the houses of the Ansar but some people had embraced Islam in it without fail. Then they sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ: “Send us a man from your side to call the people with the Book of God, for that is more like to be followed.” The Messenger of God ﷺ sent Mus'ab b. 'Umayr, the brother of Banu 'Abd al-Dar, to them. He stayed among Banu Ghanm with As'ad b. Zurara, calling people secretly. Islam spread and its people increased, while they kept their calling hidden. Then As'ad b. Zurara and Mus'ab b. 'Umayr set out until they came to the well of Murri—or near it—and sat there. They sent for a group of the people of the land, and they came to them in secret. While Mus'ab b. 'Umayr was talking to them and reciting the Quran to them, Sa'd b. Mu'adh was informed about them. He came to them in his protective gear, carrying a spear, until he stood over them and said, “Why do you come to us in our homes with this solitary, unique, abandoned stranger, making fools of our weak ones with falsehood and calling them to it? I do not want to see you after this in anything of our protection.” So they went back. Then they returned a second time to the well of Murri—or near it. Sa'd b. Mu'adh was informed of them a second time, and he threatened them with a lesser threat than the first. When As'ad saw some softness in him, he said, “O son of my maternal aunt, listen to his words. If you hear something objectionable, reject it from him; and if you hear something good, respond to it.” He said, “What does he say?” Mus'ab b. 'Umayr recited to them: “Ha Mim. By the clear Book, indeed We have made it an Arabic Quran that you may understand.” Sa'd b. Mu'adh said, “I hear nothing but what I recognize.” He went back, and God had guided him, but he did not show Islam to them until he returned to his people. He called Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal to Islam and made his Islam public, saying, “Whoever doubts it, whether young or old, male or female, let him bring us something more guided than it and we will take it. By God, a matter has come in which necks will be struck.” Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal accepted Islam upon Sa'd's conversion and his call, except for those not mentioned. It was the first house among the houses of the Ansar to accept Islam entirely. Then Banu al-Najjar expelled Mus'ab b. 'Umayr and were harsh on As'ad b. Zurara. Mus'ab b. 'Umayr moved to Sa'd b. Mu'adh and remained with him, calling people and God guiding through his hands, until there remained hardly a house among the houses of the Ansar but some people had embraced Islam in it without fail. Their nobles accepted Islam, and 'Amr b. al-Jamuh accepted Islam, and their idols were broken. The Muslims became the most honored of its people, and their affair became sound. Mus'ab b. 'Umayr returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ and was called “the reciter.”"],[17652,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by Mus'ab b. 'Umayr when he returned from Uhud, and he stood over him and his companions and said, “I bear witness that you are alive with God. So return them and pray over them. For by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, no one greets them but they return the greeting until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[17653,"A boy from among us set out and came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I am going to ask you a question.” He said, “What is it?” He said, “I ask you to make me one of those for whom you will intercede on the Day of Resurrection.” He said, “Who ordered you to ask this, or who taught you this, or who guided you to this?” He said, “No one ordered me to do this except my own self.” He said, “Then you are among those for whom I will intercede on the Day of Resurrection.” The boy went away joyful to tell his family. When he turned away, he said, “Bring the boy back to me.” They brought him back, dejected, fearing that something had occurred. He said, “Help me on behalf of yourself by increasing in prostration.”"],[17654,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Indeed God, exalted is He, is gentle and loves gentleness, and is pleased with it, and assists with it what He does not assist with harshness. So when you ride these dumb beasts, alight them at their resting places. If the land becomes barren, travel swiftly upon them, for the land is folded by night what it is not folded by day. Beware of camping in the middle of the road, for it is the path of the beasts and the refuge of snakes.”"],[17655,"“Three slaves belonging to Banu Ghifar” witnessed Badr with the Prophet ﷺ, and 'Umar used to give them one thousand for each man."],[17656,"The Messenger of God ﷺ turned to Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith on the day of Hunayn and said, \"Who are you?\" He said, \"The son of your mother.\" He said good to him."],[17657,"Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah b. Abi 'Amir b. Mas'ud b. Mu'attib b. Malik b. Ka'b b. 'Amr b. Ma'd b. 'Awf b. Qays b. Munabbih; his kunyah is Abu 'Abd Allah. His mother was a woman from Banu Nasr b. Mu'awiyah. He governed Basra for about two years, then he governed Kufa and died there in the year fifty. The first of his expeditions with the Messenger of God ﷺ was al-Hudaybiyyah."],[17658,"Al-Mughirah died in the year fifty."],[17659,"'Umar b. al-Khattab, when he first sent to Kufa, sent Abu 'Ubayd al-Thaqafi, Abu al-Mukhtar, and he was killed. Then he sent Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas, and he remained five years, then he removed him. Then he sent 'Ammar b. Yasir, and he remained a year, then he removed him, and he sent al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah, and he remained a year. Then 'Umar was killed. When 'Uthman was appointed, he sent Sa'd to Kufa, and he remained a year, then he removed him and sent al-Walid b. 'Uqbah, and he remained five years, then he removed him and sent Sa'id b. al-'As, and he remained five years, then he removed him and sent Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, and he remained a year. Then 'Uthman ؓ was killed and there was the fitnah. Then the first whom Mu'awiyah appointed over Kufa was al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah, for nine years; then he died. Then he sent Ziyad b. Abihi, and he remained four years, then he died. Then he sent al-Dahhak b. Qays, and he remained three years, then he removed him. Then he sent al-Nu'man b. Bashir, and he remained four months. Then Mu'awiyah died and there was the fitnah. Then there was the affair of Muslim b. 'Aqil and his companions."],[17660,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went to relieve himself, and I went with him with a water vessel, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was wearing a Syrian jubba. When the Messenger of God ﷺ had finished relieving himself, he performed wudu and wiped over the khuffs."],[17661,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said regarding the skin of a dead animal: \"Its tanning is its purification.\""],[17662,"'Umar consulted the people about the miscarriage of a woman. Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah said, \"I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ decree a ghurrah, a male or female slave.\" He said, \"Will you bring me someone who testifies with you?\" Muhammad b. Maslamah testified for him."],[17663,"He tied his garments on and took with him a shield, then set off until they came to him. He said to the people, \"Throw me a burnus,\" and he sat on it. The 'ilj said, \"You Arabs, I know what brought you to come to us. You are a people who do not find in your lands enough food to fill you, so take, we will give you of food what you need. We are a people of Magians, and we hate to kill you; you are encroaching on our land.\" Al-Mughirah said, \"By God, that is not what brought us. But we were a people who worshipped stones and idols. Whenever we saw a stone better than another, we threw it away and took the other, and we did not know a Lord until God sent to us a Messenger from among ourselves. He called us to Islam, and we followed him. He commanded us to fight our enemy, those who abandoned Islam. We did not come for food, but we came to kill your fighters and take your offspring captive. As for what you mentioned of food, by my life, we did not find enough food to fill us, and sometimes we did not find enough water to quench our thirst. So we came to this land of yours and found in it abundant food. No, by God, we will not leave it until it is ours or yours.\" The 'ilj said in Persian, \"He spoke truth, and your eye will be gouged out tomorrow at al-Qadisiyyah.\" His eye was gouged out the next day; an arrow hit him."],[17664,"From Abu Firas, a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, from al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah, who said: I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ wanting to marry. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Go to so-and-so and look at what they have, for that is more conducive to love. If you are pleased with her, I will marry you to her.\" So he went to them and greeted them and said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me. Did he command you to show me?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So she unveiled herself from her curtain and said, \"Look.\" He said, \"I married her, and I have never married anyone dearer to me than her. I have married sixty women.\""],[17665,"Four descended into the grave of the Messenger of God ﷺ, one of them 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf. Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah used to be called the one with the most recent contact with the Messenger of God ﷺ. So I will be the last of the people to have contact with him."],[17666,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ one night on a journey. He said, \"Do you have water with you?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He dismounted from his mount and walked until he was hidden from me in the darkness of the night. Then he came, and I poured water on him from the vessel. He washed his hands and face, and he was wearing a woolen jubba. He could not get his forearms out of its tightness until he brought them out from the bottom of the jubba and washed his forearms and wiped his head. Then I reached to remove his khuff, and he said, \"Leave them, for I put them on while they were pure,\" and he wiped over them."],[17667,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey. He performed wudu and wiped over his khuffs."],[17668,"He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he dismounted and said, \"Is there any water for purification?\" So I brought him water, and he washed his hands and face. Then he went to wash his forearms, but the jubba was tight on him—it was a jubba of the Roman-style cloaks—so he drew his arms out from under the jubba, pulling them out, and washed his forearms. Then I reached for his leather socks, and he said, \"Leave the leather socks, for I put my feet into them while they were pure.\" Then he wiped over the leather socks."],[17669,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you wipe over your leather socks?\" He said, \"Yes, for I put them on while they were pure.\""],[17670,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Do you have any water with you?\" I said, \"Yes.\" So he dismounted from his riding camel, then walked until he was hidden from me. When he returned, I met him with the water vessel, and he performed ablution: he washed his palms and his face. He was wearing a Syrian jubba with tight sleeves, so he took his hand out from under the jubba and washed his forearms, then wiped his head. Then I reached for his leather socks to remove them, and he said, \"Leave them, for I put them on while they were pure.\" Then he wiped over his leather socks."],[17671,"I was traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night when he said, \"Who is this?\" I said, \"I am al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah.\" He said, \"Hold on.\" So I held his she-camel for him, and he went off until I could no longer see him. Then he came back, and I helped him perform ablution. He rolled up his sleeves, but the sleeve of the jubba was tight, so he took his hands out from under it and performed ablution: he washed his hands, his face, and his forearms, and wiped over his leather socks. I said, \"Will you not remove your leather socks?\" He said, \"I put them on while they were pure.\""],[17672,"The Prophet ﷺ tapped my back with a stick he had with him, and he turned aside, and I turned aside with him until we reached—I do not know where in the land. He made his camel kneel and dismounted, then went off until he was hidden from me. Then he came back and said, \"Do you have any water with you?\" I had a small water skin with me, so I poured water for him. He washed his palms and his face, then went to wash his forearms while wearing a Syrian jubba with tight sleeves, so he took his hands out from under the garment and washed his hands, his face, and his forearms, and wiped—Ibn 'Awn said: he mentioned something about his forelock and his turban, but I am not sure whether I got it right—and he wiped over his leather socks. Then he said, \"Do you need anything?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have no need.\" So we set off and came to the people, and Ibn 'Awf had already led them in the dawn prayer. He had prayed one rak'ah with them, and I went to alert him, but he prevented me. So we prayed what we caught up with and made up what we had missed."],[17673,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he went to relieve himself while wearing a Roman jubba. Then he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, and he said, \"I put them on while I was in a state of purity—or while I had performed ablution.\""],[17674,"I helped the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution, and he wiped over his leather socks. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, did you forget?\" He said, \"Rather, you forgot. This is what my Lord, Mighty and Exalted, commanded me.\""],[17675,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he went to relieve himself. Then he gestured to me, and I brought him water. He was wearing a Syrian jubba that had no sleeves, so he threw it over his shoulders and said, \"Pour water over me.\" So I poured water over him, and he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. And this was a sunnah: for the traveler, three days and their nights; for the resident, one day and one night."],[17676,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: that he went out to relieve himself, and al-Mughirah followed him with a water vessel containing water. He poured water over him until he finished his need, then he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[17677,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over the socks.\""],[17678,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[17679,"That he poured water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from his vessel, and he washed his face. Then he went to wash his forearms, but his sleeves were too tight for his forearms, so he took them out from under the jubba—and it was made of wool—then he washed them and wiped over his leather socks."],[17680,"That the Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[17681,"He informed him that he went on the campaign of Tabuk with the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ went aside to relieve himself, and I carried a water vessel with him before the dawn prayer. When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned to me, I began to pour water from the vessel onto his hands. He washed his hands three times, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, then washed his face. Then he tried to pull his jubba off his forearms, but the sleeves of his jubba were too tight, so he inserted his hands into the jubba up to the elbows, then he performed ablution over his leather socks. Then he came forward, and I came with him until we found that the people had put 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf forward to lead them in prayer. The Prophet ﷺ caught one of the two rak'ahs and prayed the last rak'ah with the people. When 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf said the salam, the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up to complete his prayer. That alarmed the Muslims, and they said subhan Allah excessively. When the Prophet ﷺ finished his prayer, he turned to them and said, 'You have done well' or 'You have been correct,' expressing his approval that they had prayed the prayer at its time. Ibn Shihab said: Isma'il b. Muhammad b. Sa'd narrated to me from Hamza b. al-Mughira b. Shu'ba the like of the hadith of 'Abbad b. Ziyad, and he added: Al-Mughira said: I rushed to inform 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, but the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Leave him.' And he mentioned something similar."],[17682,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks."],[17683,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wipe over the tops of the leather socks."],[17684,"That 'Umar ؓ consulted them regarding a woman's miscarriage, meaning the stillborn fetus. Al-Mughira b. Shu'ba said: I said to him, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled regarding it that a slave or slave girl is due.' 'Umar said: If you are truthful, bring someone who knows that. I brought Muhammad b. Maslama, and he came and said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled regarding it that a slave or slave girl is due.'"],[17685,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever sells wine, let him also butcher pigs.'"],[17686,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wipe over the turban and the leather socks."],[17687,"That the Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his forelock."],[17688,"That the Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks, wiped the front of his head, placed his hands on the turban, and wiped over the turban. He did not mention al-Hasan."],[17689,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey. He said: 'Stay back, O Mughira, and proceed, O people.' Then he went and relieved himself, and I brought him a water vessel. When he finished, I poured water from it for him. He washed his face, then he tried to take his hands out of a Byzantine jubba he was wearing, but the sleeves of the jubba were too tight, so he took his hands out from under the jubba and washed them, then he wiped over his leather socks, then he prayed."],[17690,"He has not relied on God who seeks ruqya or cauterizes."],[17691,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'He has not relied on God who cauterizes or seeks ruqya.'"],[17692,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'He has not relied on God who seeks ruqya or cauterizes.'"],[17693,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled regarding the fetus: a ghurra, a male slave or a female slave."],[17694,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbid mutilation."],[17695,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Hunayn stand over a slain man from Thaqif and say, 'May God distance you, for you used to hate Quraysh.'"],[17696,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished his prayer, he would say, 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from his fortune against You.'"],[17697,"[He asked him] to write to him something he had heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: Al-Mughirah wrote to him that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say when he finished the prayer, 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from his fortune against You.' And he used to forbid idle talk, excessive asking, wasting wealth, withholding [what is due] and demanding [what is not], disobedience to mothers, and burying daughters alive."],[17698,"[He asked him] to write to him something he had heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ when he finished the prayer. He said, 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from his fortune against You.'"],[17699,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished the prayer, he would say, 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from his fortune against You.'"],[17700,"[He asked him] to write to him something he had heard from the Prophet ﷺ. He wrote to him: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'God dislikes for you three things: idle talk, excessive asking, and wasting wealth.'"],[17701,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'God, Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden you disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding [what is due] and demanding [what is not]. And He dislikes for you idle talk, excessive asking, and wasting wealth.'"],[17702,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said, 'God, Exalted be He, dislikes idle talk, excessive asking, and wasting wealth, and He forbade burying daughters alive, disobedience to mothers, and withholding [what is due] and demanding [what is not].'"],[17703,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'God dislikes for you three things: idle talk, excessive asking, and wasting wealth. And He has forbidden disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding [what is due] and demanding [what is not].'"],[17704,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a group of the Ansar who were shooting at a pigeon. He said, 'Do not take a living creature as a target.'"],[17705,"That the Prophet ﷺ, when he finished from a prayer, said: “There is no god but Allah.” Then he mentioned the hadith."],[17706,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to say after the prayer: “There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful.”"],[17707,"That he should write to him something from the hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So he wrote to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking refuge from three things: from disobedience to mothers, from burying daughters alive, and from “withhold and give.” And I heard him forbid three things: from “it was said and he said,” from wasting wealth, and from excessive asking. And I heard him say: “O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You his fortune.”"],[17708,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he said the taslim, said: “There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You his fortune.”"],[17709,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say after the prayer: “There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You his fortune.”"],[17710,"That he should write to him something he had heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So he wrote to him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “forbade from ‘it was said and he said,’ excessive asking, wasting wealth, disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and ‘withhold and give.’”"],[17711,"Muʿāwiyah wrote to al-Mughīrah: Write to me something you heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying after the prayer. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say after his prayer: “There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You his fortune.”"],[17712,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to say after the prayer, when he said the taslim: “There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You his fortune.”"],[17713,"That he should write to him something he had heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So he wrote to him in his own handwriting: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say when he finished from the prayer: “There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You his fortune.”"],[17714,"That he should write to him something he had heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So he wrote to him in his own handwriting: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say when he finished from the prayer: “There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You his fortune.”"],[17715,"Saʿd b. ʿUbādah said: If I saw a man with my wife, I would strike him with the sword. That reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he said: “Do you marvel at Saʿd’s jealousy? By Allah, I am more jealous than Saʿd, and Allah is more jealous than me. And because of that He forbade immoralities, what is apparent of them and what is concealed. And no person is more beloved to Him than one who offers excuses, than Allah, mighty and majestic is He; because of that He sent His messengers as bearers of good tidings and warners. And no person is more beloved to Him than praise, than Allah, mighty and majestic is He; and because of that He promised Paradise.” The wording is that of the hadith of Abu al-Walīd."],[17716,"We traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he struck my mount’s neck with his hand, then said: “Do you have water with you?” I said: Yes, this is a small waterskin of water with me. He said: “Leave it.” Then he dismounted and relieved himself, then came to me and said: “Do you want to relieve yourself?” I said: No. He said: “Then he washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth three times, and sniffed water three times, then washed his face three times. Then he wanted to take out his forearms, but he had on a woolen jubbah that was tight, and he could not take his forearms out of it, so he took his hands out from under the jubbah, then washed his forearms three times each, then wiped his head and wiped over the leather socks. Then we traveled and caught up with the people while ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf was leading them in prayer, and I wanted to alert him to the Prophet’s ﷺ presence, but he prevented me. So we prayed one rakʿah with him, then we made up the second.” The wording is that of the hadith of Hishām b. ʿAmmār."],[17717,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say when he concluded the prayer: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[17718,"From al-Mughira b. Shuʿba: He wrote to Muʿawiya that the Messenger of God ﷺ, when he concluded the prayer, would say: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[17719,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say after the prayer: \"There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner or associate. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is the Ever-Living who never dies. In His hand is all good, and He is over all things capable. O Allah, there is no one who can prevent what You have given, and no one can give what You have prevented. And there is no might or power except with You.\""],[17720,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ would say when he finished the prayer: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[17721,"About the last thing the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say, so he wrote to him that he would say after giving the salutation: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You,” after he had given the salutation to his right and to his left. He would give the salutation to his right until the whiteness of his right cheek was seen, and to his left until the whiteness of his left cheek was seen."],[17722,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Beware of he-said-she-said, withholding and demanding, disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and squandering wealth.”"],[17723,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ would say at the end of every prayer: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[17724,"From the Prophet ﷺ with this same hadith."],[17725,"He asked him to write to him something he had heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he wrote to him: When he prayed and finished, he would say: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner.” Ibn ʿAwn said: I think he said: “His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[17726,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ would say at the end of his prayer: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[17727,"Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say anything at the end of the prayer? Al-Mughira b. Shuʿba said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say at the end of the prayer: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[17728,"Muʿawiya wrote to al-Mughira b. Shuʿba: Did the Messenger of God ﷺ say anything after the prayer? He said: He would say: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[17729,"The Messenger of Allah wiped over the top and the bottom of the leather socks. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 550)"],[17730,"A woman was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ who had struck her co-wife with a tent pole and killed her and what was in her womb. The Messenger of God ﷺ made her blood money the responsibility of the woman’s male relatives, and for the fetus there was a ghurra: a male or female slave. A man from the people stood up and said: “O Messenger of God, how can we pay blood money for one who did not eat, drink, cry out, or raise its voice?” He said: “This one speaks with the speech of a soothsayer. For it there is a ghurra: a male or female slave.”"],[17731,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade three things: undutifulness to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding and demanding (miserliness), and he prohibited he-said-she-said, excessive questioning, and squandering wealth."],[17732,"He heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ and then wrote to him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God, exalted be He, dislikes for you three things: undutifulness to mothers, burying daughters alive, withholding and demanding, he-said-she-said, excessive questioning, and squandering wealth."],[17733,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and he said, “O Mughīrah, take the water vessel.” So I took it, then I went out with him. The Messenger of God ﷺ went away until he was hidden from me, relieved himself, then came back wearing a Syrian jubbah with tight sleeves. He tried to take his hand out of its sleeve, but it was too tight, so he took his hand out from below it. I poured water for him, and he performed ablution as for prayer, wiped over his leather socks, and then prayed."],[17734,"He performed ablution for the Prophet ﷺ, and he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks and over the turban."],[17735,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to relieve himself, and I followed him with a vessel of water. When he finished, I began pouring water for him. He washed his face, and he was wearing a Roman or Syrian jubbah whose sleeve was tight, so he took his hand out from below it, washed his forearms, and wiped over the turban and the leather socks."],[17736,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If the imam forgets and has stood up completely, he must perform the two prostrations of forgetfulness; but if he has not stood up completely, there is no forgetfulness upon him.”"],[17737,"No one asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Dajjal more than I did. He said, “What will you do? He will not harm you.” I said, “Should I not kill Ibn Ṣayyād?” He said, “What would you do by killing him? If he is the Dajjal, you will never be able to kill him, and if he is not the Dajjal, what will you do with him?”"],[17738,"We used to pray the noon prayer with the Prophet of God ﷺ in the midday heat. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to us: “Cool the prayer, for the intense heat is from the scorching breath of Hell.”"],[17739,"No one asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Dajjal more than I did. The Prophet of God said, “Why do you ask about him? He will not harm you.”"],[17740,"No one asked the Prophet ﷺ about him—meaning the Dajjal—more than I did. He said, “He will not harm you.” I said, “They say that with him there is a river and such.” He said, “He is too insignificant to God for that.”"],[17741,"No one asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Dajjal more than I did. He said, “Why do you ask about him? You will not live to see him. Indeed, he will not emerge until inheritance is no longer divided and no one is alarmed for booty.”"],[17742,"No one asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the Dajjal more than I did. He said to me, “What harm can he do to you?” I said, “They say that with him there is a mountain of bread and a river of water.” He said, “He is too insignificant to God for that.”"],[17743,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, it has reached me that with the Dajjal are rivers of water and mountains of bread. He said: \"He is more insignificant to Allah than that.\" I was among the people who asked about him the most, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"It is not that which will harm you.\""],[17744,"The Prophet ﷺ was not asked about the Dajjal more than I asked him. He said: \"O my son, and what will afflict you from him?\" I said: The people say that with him are food and drink. He said: \"He is more insignificant to Allah than that.\""],[17745,"No one asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Dajjal more than I asked him. He said: \"And what are you asking me about him?\" He said: I said: The people say that with him are a garden and a fire, and food and drink. He said: \"He is more insignificant to Allah than that.\""],[17746,"No one asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Dajjal more than I asked him. He said: \"What troubles you about him that you ask about him? He will not harm you.\" I said: They claim that with him are rivers and food. He said: \"He is more insignificant to Allah than that.\""],[17747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will not cease to be a group of people from my Ummah prevailing over the people until Allah's command comes to them while they are prevailing.\""],[17748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will not cease to be a group of people from my Ummah prevailing until Allah's command comes to them while they are prevailing.\""],[17749,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will always be a group from my Ummah (nation) who will remain steadfast on the truth, visible and apparent, until the Hour (Day of Judgment) is established.\""],[17750,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will not cease to be people from my Ummah prevailing until Allah's command comes to them while they are prevailing.\""],[17751,"I was with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ when a horse was presented to him. A man said: \"Carry me on this.\" He said: \"To carry a boy who has ridden horses despite his being unskilled is dearer to me than to carry you on it.\" The man became angry and said: \"I, by Allah, am a better horseman than you and your father.\" I became angry when he said that to the Caliph of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I stood up to him, seized his head, and dragged him on his nose, and it was as if his nose was the spout of a waterskin. The Ansar wanted to exact retaliation from me. That reached Abu Bakr, and he said: \"It has reached me that some people claim that I will let them exact retaliation from al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah. To expel them from their homes is closer to me than to let them exact retaliation from Allah's restrainers who restrain His servants.\""],[17752,"He was at the head of the Prophet ﷺ with a sword, and he was veiled. 'Urwah began to touch the beard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was speaking. Al-Mughirah said to him: \"You must stop your hand or it will not return to you,\" while al-Mughirah was wearing a sword. 'Urwah said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who is this?\" He said: \"This is your nephew, al-Mughirah.\" He said: \"O treacherous one, I have not washed my head from your treachery.\""],[17753,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Al-'Anaqah does not create a foster relationship.\" We said: \"What is al-'Anaqah?\" He said: \"A woman who gives birth and the milk slows in her breast, so she breastfeeds her neighbor once or twice.\""],[17754,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ came to the tribe of Bani Fulan, and he ordered his legs to be noosed and he felt faint, standing.\""],[17755,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to a people's trash dump, and I brought him water. He performed ablution while wearing a Roman jubbah with short sleeves. He took his hand out from under that jubbah, washed his face, wiped his head, and wiped over his leather socks, then stood and prayed."],[17756,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinated in the trash dump of Banu so-and-so and said: \"O Mughirah, do you have water with you?\" He said: \"Yes, a waterskin of water.\" He was wearing a Syrian jubbah with tight sleeves. He performed ablution and wiped over his feet while wearing leather socks."],[17757,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to a people's waste area and urinated standing."],[17758,"Al-Mughira said: We were astray, then Allah sent a prophet among us and guided us to His religion and provided us with a grain that is in these lands of yours. When we ate from it and fed our families, they said, \"We cannot bear to remain until you bring us to these lands.\" He said, \"Then we will kill you.\" He said, \"If you kill us, we will enter Paradise, and if we kill you, you will enter the Fire.\""],[17759,"While I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dismounted and relieved himself. Then he came, and I poured water for him from a water skin that I had with me. He performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[17760,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he went aside to relieve himself. When he finished, I brought him a water skin containing water and poured it for him. He performed ablution, and he had on a jubba with narrow sleeves, so he brought his hand out from under the jubba and washed his forearms and wiped over his leather socks."],[17761,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah hears the one who praises Him,\" he would say, \"O Allah, there is no one to withhold what You give, and no one to give what You withhold, and no one's wealth avails him against You.\""],[17762,"Al-Mughira stood and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.'\""],[17763,"Al-Mughira stood and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.'\""],[17764,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Lying about me is not like lying about anyone else.\""],[17765,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Lying about me is not like lying about anyone else.\""],[17766,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Lying about me is not like lying about anyone else.\""],[17767,"He was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[17768,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[17769,"A co-wife struck her fellow co-wife with a tent pole and killed her. Judgment was given for her blood money [to be paid] by the killer's male relatives, and for what was in her womb, a ghurra. The Bedouin said, 'Will you make me pay for one who neither ate nor drank nor cried out nor wailed? Should such a one be requited?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Is it rhymed prose like the rhymed prose of the Bedouins?' Abu Hudhayfah added in his hadith: And judgment was given for what was in her womb as a ghurra."],[17770,"A man of Hudhayl had two wives. One of them threw at the other a stone or a tent pole and caused her to miscarry. That was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ judged in it a ghurra. Her guardians said, 'How should we pay blood money for one who neither cried out nor wailed nor drank nor ate? Should such a one be requited?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Is it rhymed prose like the rhymed prose of the Bedouins?' And he judged its blood money upon the woman's guardians."],[17771,"While I was traveling one night, I came to a riding camel of a rider among the caravan. Al-Mughira b. Shu'ba said: I said, 'Who are you?' He said, 'I am the Messenger of God.' So I held back until he caught up with me, and I kept pace with him. Then he dismounted and went aside to relieve himself. He said, 'Do you have water?' I said, 'Would it harm you?' He said, 'Then I brought him water, and he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. We did not part until we had prayed the dawn prayer.'"],[17772,"'I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ relieve himself, then perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks.'"],[17773,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Najran. They said to me, among what they said, 'According to what you recite, {O sister of Harun}, there was between Musa and 'Isa what you know.' He said: So I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said, 'Would you not have informed them that they used to be named with their names and with the names of the righteous who came before them?'"],[17774,"That he stood in the first two rak'ahs, and they glorified [to alert him], but he did not sit. When he finished his prayer, he prostrated twice after the salam. Then he said, 'Thus did the Messenger of God ﷺ do.'"],[17775,"'The Prophet ﷺ recited the tashahhud when he raised his head from the two prostrations of forgetfulness.'"],[17776,"Yes, he is a man who comes after people have settled in their homes and taken their rest. It is said to him, \"Enter Paradise,\" and he says, \"O Lord, how can I enter it when people have settled in their homes and taken their rest?\" He said, \"Are you not pleased that you have what a king has among the kings of the world?\" He said, \"I am pleased, my Lord.\" He said, \"You have that and the like of that and the like of that and Sufyan (a narrator) interlocked his fingers five times and he said, 'I am pleased, my Lord.'\" He said, \"You have that and what your soul desires and your eyes find delight in.\" He said, \"I am pleased, my Lord.\" Moses said, \"O Lord, inform me about the highest rank of the people of Paradise.\" He said, \"Those are the ones you wished for and I will inform you about them. I planted their honor with my own hands and sealed it with my own seal and no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and it has not occurred to human heart.\" And the confirmation of that is the statement of Allah, \"No person knows what is kept hidden for them of joy as a reward for what they used to do\" (Quran 32:17)."],[17777,"I heard al-Mughira while he was delivering a sermon on the pulpit, saying: We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a campaign. 'He went off for a need, and I followed him with a water vessel. He brought out his hands from a jubbah he was wearing that had narrow sleeves, and he brought them out from beneath it. He washed his face and hands, wiped his head, and wiped over his leather socks.'"],[17778,"It was said to al-Mughira b. Shu'ba, 'From where did the Prophet ﷺ have leather socks?' He said, 'Dihya al-Kalbi gave them to him as a gift.'"],[17779,"That he saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks. I said, 'O Abu 'Amr, and from where did the Prophet ﷺ have leather socks?' He said, 'Dihya al-Kalbi gave them to him as a gift.'"],[17780,"'I was among those who dug the grave of the Prophet ﷺ.' He said: We dug a lahd for him. When the Prophet ﷺ was placed in the grave, I threw down the axe, then I said, 'The axe, the axe.' So I descended and placed my hands on the lahd. Al-Mughira used to say, 'I am the closest of people in time to the Messenger of God ﷺ.'"],[17781,"A man said in the presence of al-Mughira b. Shu'ba, 'May God bless Muhammad, the Seal of the Prophets; there is no prophet after him.' Al-Mughira said, 'It is enough for you to say, Seal of the Prophets, for we used to be told that 'Isa b. Maryam is to come forth. If he is to come forth, then he was before him and after him.'"],[17782,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks."],[17783,"The Prophet ﷺ urinated, performed ablution, and wiped over his socks and sandals."],[17784,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on one of his military expeditions and dismounted to relieve himself. I brought him water for ablution while he was wearing a tight jubbah. He brought his hand out from under it, and I poured water over it. He performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[17785,"I would sit rather than stand upright, but this is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us."],[17786,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ preferred to pray on a tanned fur or a straw mat."],[17787,"He walked with the Prophet ﷺ and came to one of those valleys. He entered it, relieved himself, then came out and performed ablution, removing his leather socks. When he put them back on, he later noticed an odor, so he repeated the ablution and wiped over the leather socks. I said, \"Did you forget, O Prophet of Allah?\" He said, \"No, rather you forgot. This is what my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me.\""],[17788,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, did you forget?\" He said, \"Rather you forgot. This is what my Lord commanded me.\""],[17789,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, did you forget?\" He said, \"Rather you forgot. This is what my Lord commanded me.\""],[17790,"One day I ate, then came to the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was praying. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, he said, \"Whoever has eaten anything from this plant should not approach our mosque.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, give me your hand.\" He gave it to me, and I placed it on my chest. He saw that it was bandaged, and said, \"Except for a valid excuse.\""],[17791,"The Prophet ﷺ noticed the smell of garlic and said, \"Who is this?\" Al-Mughira b. Shu'ba said, \"I adjure you, or I swear to you, O Messenger of Allah, to put your hand in.\" When he did, there was a bandage on his chest. He said, \"I see that you have an excuse.\""],[17792,"The last military expedition we went on with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he commanded us to wipe over our leather socks: \"For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident one day and one night, as long as he does not take them off.\""],[17793,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, then prayed and placed me on his right side."],[17794,"I went out with the Prophet ﷺ on one of his journeys, and we traveled until, when it was the time of pre-dawn, he went off to a secluded spot and hid from me. Then he came and called for water for ablution, wearing a Syrian jubbah with tight sleeves. He took his hand out from beneath the jubbah, washed his face and hands, and wiped over his leather socks."],[17795,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate some food, and then the prayer was commenced. He stood up, having already performed ablution before that. I brought him water to perform ablution, but he scolded me. That distressed me, by Allah, so I complained to Umar. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah has been hurt by your scolding him, and he fears that you may hold something against him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I hold nothing against him but good. However, he brought me water to perform ablution, but I had only eaten food. If I had done so, the people after me would have done it.\""],[17796,"I heard Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah saying, \"If the Prophet ﷺ intended to pray until the soles of his feet or shins became swollen, it would be said to him, and he would say, 'Should I not be a grateful servant?'\""],[17797,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray until his feet would crack. It was said to him, \"Hasn't Allah forgiven you for your past and future sins?\" He said, \"Should I not be a grateful servant?\""],[17798,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray until his feet swelled. He was asked about it and was told that Allah had forgiven his past and future sins. He replied, \"Should I not be a grateful servant?\""],[17799,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"My solace and comfort has been placed in prayer.\""],[17800,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not revile the dead, for you would hurt the living.\""],[17801,"I heard al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah say: The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone. So when you see them, supplicate to Allah and pray until it clears.\""],[17802,"The sun eclipsed on the day Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone. So when you see them, you must supplicate until it clears.\""],[17803,"When Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet ﷺ, died, the sun eclipsed. The people said, \"It eclipsed because of Ibrahim's death.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said, \"O people, the sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone, but they are two signs among the signs of Allah. So when that happens, pray until it clears.\""],[17804,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no one but has a companion from the jinn assigned with him.\" They said, \"Even you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Even me, but Allah helped me against him, so he became a Muslim, and he only commands me to good.\""],[17805,"That the Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his socks."],[17806,"And he said, \"Thus did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.\""],[17807,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever narrates a hadith from me while thinking it is a lie is one of the two liars,\" or he said, \"the liars.\""],[17808,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Whoever narrates a hadith from me while thinking it is a lie is one of the liars.\""],[17809,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Whoever narrates a hadith from me while thinking it is a lie is one of the liars.\""],[17810,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ holding the waist-wrap of Sufyan b. Sahl, who is Ibn Abi Sahl, and saying, \"Do not let your lower garment hang low, for Allah does not love those who let their lower garments hang low.\""],[17811,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taking hold of the cloak of Sufyan b. Sahl while saying, “O Sufyan, do not let your garment hang below the ankles, for Allah does not love those who let their garments hang low.” This is how Yazid b. Harun narrated it from Sharik, from ‘Abd al-Malik b. ‘Umayr, from Husayn b. ‘Uqbah, and he said: Sufyan b. Sahl."],[17812,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The slogan of my Ummah on the Sirat will be: ‘Sallim, sallim (Grant safety, grant safety).’”"],[17813,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The slogan of my Ummah on the Sirat will be: ‘Rabbi sallim (My Lord, grant safety).’”"],[17814,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A people will come out of the Fire and enter Paradise, and in Paradise they will be called the Jahannamiyyun. They will call upon Allah to remove that name from them, and Allah will erase it from them, when they have come out of the Fire.” Then he mentioned the hadith."],[17815,"The Prophet ﷺ performed wudu and wiped over his leather socks."],[17816,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ at his stopping place, and I followed him. He said, “Where did you leave the people?” I said, “I left them at such-and-such a place.” He made his mount kneel and dismounted, then went away and concealed himself from me. He stayed away for about as long as a man takes to relieve himself, then came back and said, “Do you have water with you?” I said, “Yes.” So I poured water over his hands, and he washed his face and his hands, and wiped his head. He was wearing a Syrian jubbah whose sleeves were tight, so he inserted his hand from beneath the jubbah and raised it up over his hands, then washed his hands and his face, and wiped his head and his leather socks. Then he said, “Do you need anything?” I said, “No.” He said, “Then we rode on until we caught up with the people.”"],[17817,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over his forelock and his turban, and wiped over his leather socks,” and I was witnessing that."],[17818,"Two matters I will not ask anyone about after having witnessed them with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: wiping over the leather socks, and the prayer of an imam behind one of his subjects. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and we stopped at a place. The Prophet ﷺ went aside to relieve himself. When he had finished, I brought him water. He performed wudu while wearing a jubbah with tight sleeves, so he took his hand out from beneath the jubbah, and he wiped over his forelock, over his turban, and over his leather socks. Then we came to the people while they were praying, and the people had put ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf forward as imam. We caught one rak‘ah with them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made up the other rak‘ah."],[17819,"I came with the Prophet ﷺ to ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf, and he stepped back, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured to him, and we prayed what we caught up with, and made up what we had missed."],[17820,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey. When it was the pre-dawn time, I urged on my mount and came along with him. He went off until he disappeared from me, then came back and said, “Do you need anything?” I said, “I have no need.” He said, “Do you have water with you?” I said, “Yes.” So he performed wudu and wiped over his leather socks. Then he went on until he reached the people while they were praying, with ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf leading them. He moved at the arrival of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured with his hand to ‘Abd al-Rahman, meaning, “Stay in place.” So we prayed what we caught up with, and made up what we had missed."],[17821,"And (that) I should send blessings upon a man from my subjects, and I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over his socks and praying behind Abdur Rahman ibn Awf."],[17822,"“I poured water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he washed his hands, rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, washed his face and his forearms, and wiped over his forelock, over the turban, and over the leather socks.”"],[17823,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “wiped over his forelock, over his turban, and over his leather socks.”"],[17824,"He poured water from a small waterskin for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: He performed ablution and washed his face, wearing a narrow-sleeved Syrian jubbah. He brought out his hands and washed them, and wiped over his turban and his leather socks. We came to 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf while he was praying, having already led them in one rak'ah. We prayed with him the rak'ah we caught up with and made up the rak'ah we had missed."],[17825,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks and the turban."],[17826,"I asked al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah: Did any of the Companions lead the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in prayer besides Abu Bakr? He said: Yes. I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on such-and-such a journey. When it was the last part of the night, he struck the neck of my riding camel and turned aside, and I turned aside with him. He relieved himself, then said, 'O Mughirah, your need?' I said, 'I have no need.' He said, 'Is there any water?' He called for a waterskin or small waterskin, washed his hands, and washed his face. Then he went to uncover his forearms, but the sleeve of a Syrian jubbah he was wearing was too tight. He brought his hands out from under the jubbah and washed his hands, wiped his forelock, and wiped over the leather socks. He said: Then we reached the people when the prayer had been called and 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf was leading them and had already prayed one rak'ah with them. I went to inform him, but he stopped me. We prayed the part we caught up with and made up what we had missed."],[17827,"The Prophet ﷺ poured water, washed his hands, then washed his face. When he wanted to wash his forearms, he was wearing a narrow-sleeved Syrian jubbah. He brought his hands out from under the jubbah, washed his forearms, then wiped his forelock, wiped his head and over his turban and his leather socks."],[17828,"He raised it to the Prophet ﷺ who said: 'The rider walks behind the funeral procession, and the walker walks behind it, on its right, and on its left. The miscarried fetus is prayed over, and forgiveness and mercy are invoked for its parents.'"],[17829,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: 'The miscarried fetus is prayed over, and well-being and mercy are invoked for its parents.' Sufyan did not raise it (to the Prophet)."],[17830,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The rider is behind the funeral procession, and the walker may be where he wishes in relation to it, and the child is prayed over.'"],[17831,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: 'The rider is behind the funeral procession, and the walker may be where he wishes, and the child is prayed over.'"],[17832,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: 'The rider is behind the funeral procession, and the walker may be where he wishes, and the child is prayed over.'"],[17833,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection, and their owners are helped through them.'"],[17834,"I prayed beside the Prophet ﷺ and he smelled from me the odor of garlic. He said, 'What is this odor?' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my chest was ailing, so I ate it.' The Prophet ﷺ did not find fault with it."],[17835,"My father- it is as if I can see him, long-haired and one-eyed- came to him. When he returned to us, we asked him: What did he say to him? He said: When I praised Allah and extolled Him, I said: 'We were the farthest of people in abode, the most severe of people in hunger, the greatest of people in misery, and the farthest of people from every good, until Allah sent to us a Messenger who promised us victory in this world and Paradise in the Hereafter. We have not ceased to recognize from our Lord, since the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, success and victory, until we came to you.'"],[17836,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ withdrew, and I withdrew with him. I approached him, and he said, “Do you have water with you?” I said, “Yes.” He washed his palms and his face, then began to wash his forearms while wearing a jubba. It was tight, so he brought his hand out from underneath the jubba and washed both arms, then wiped over his leather socks. Then he came to pray while ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf was leading the people in prayer. When they saw the Prophet ﷺ, they cleared their throats. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān started to step back, but he gestured to him, “Continue.”"],[17837,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ lagged behind, and I lagged behind with him. He relieved himself, and I brought him the water vessel. He performed ablution and washed his face. He intended to wash his forearms, but he was wearing a Syrian jubba with tight sleeves, so he brought his hands out from beneath the jubba and washed his face and forearms, and wiped over his turban and leather socks. Then we came to the people while ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf was leading them in the dawn prayer. When he saw the Prophet ﷺ, he wanted to step back, but he gestured to him to continue his prayer. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I prayed one rakʿah behind ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf. When he finished his prayer, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and prayed another rakʿah for himself, and did not add anything to it."],[17838,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned to him a woman I intended to marry. He said, “Go and look at her, for that is more likely to create affection between you.” So I came to a woman of the Anṣār and proposed to her through her parents, informing them of the Prophet’s ﷺ statement. They seemed to dislike that. The woman heard that while she was in her chamber, and she said, “If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded you to look, then look; otherwise I implore you not to.” It was as if she considered it a grave matter. He said, “So I looked at her, and then I married her.”"],[17839,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned to him a woman I intended to marry. He said, “Go and look at her, for that is more likely to create affection between you.” So I came to a woman of the Anṣār and proposed to her through her parents, informing them of the Prophet’s ﷺ statement. They seemed to dislike that. The woman heard that while she was in her chamber, and she said, “If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded you to look, then look; otherwise I implore you not to.” It was as if she considered it a grave matter. He said, “So I looked at her, and then I married her.”"],[17840,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned to him a woman I intended to marry. He said, “Go and look at her, for that is more likely to create affection between you.” So I came to a woman of the Anṣār and proposed to her through her parents, informing them of the Prophet’s ﷺ statement. They seemed to dislike that. The woman heard that while she was in her chamber, and she said, “If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded you to look, then look; otherwise I implore you not to.” It was as if she considered it a grave matter. He said, “So I looked at her, and then I married her.”"],[17841,"I proposed to a girl from the Anṣār and mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “Have you seen her?” I said, “No.” He said, “Then look at her, for that is more likely to create affection between you.”"],[17842,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ to make me the imam of my people. He said, “Lead the prayer as the weakest of the people would pray, and do not appoint a muʾadhdhin who takes payment for his call to prayer.”"],[17843,"I was a guest of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He ordered a side of meat to be roasted for me, and he trimmed my mustache with a blade over a toothstick, clipping it. Then Bilāl came to call him to prayer, so he threw down the blade and said to him, “May your hands be dusty.” My mustache had grown full, so he trimmed it for me."],[17844,"I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night and he ordered a stick to be brought, which was then sharpened. He took the stick and started scraping his own teeth with it, and then Bilal came to call him for prayer. He threw away the stick and asked, \"Why are his hands dirty?\" I said, \"It's because he had just fulfilled a promise and cleaned his teeth with a miswak (a teeth cleaning twig).\""],[17845,"I had Suhoor (pre-dawn meal) with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ consisting of grilled meat. He was using a toothstick (miswak) and said, \"Your mustache has fulfilled its duty, O Mu'ghirah!\" Then, he trimmed it with a blade (sharp edge)."],[17846,"I sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah cut for me from the side of a sheep with a knife. Bilal called the Adhan for Fajr prayer, so he threw the knife and said, \"Why do his hands not have soil on them?\" My mustache was long, and I had fulfilled my vow, so he said, \"Shall I trim it for you?\" So he trimmed it on a siwak stick."],[17847,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad narrated to us, from Muḥammad b. ʿAmr, from Abū Salamah, from al-Mughīrah b. Shuʿbah: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he went out on one of his journeys—and when he went to relieve himself, he would go far—told me to follow him with water for ablution. He came wearing a Syrian jubba, brought his hand out from beneath it, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks."],[17848,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he went to relieve himself, would go far. He went to answer the call of nature during one of his journeys and said, “Bring me water for ablution.” I brought him water, and he brought his hands out from beneath the jubba, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks."],[17849,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to relieve himself, he would go far. He said, “Follow me with water.” So I followed him with a water skin. He was wearing a Syrian jubba with tight sleeves, so he brought his hands out from beneath the jubba, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks."],[17850,"“I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to relieve himself, he would go far.”"],[17851,"Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"I have thought about a certain woman; will you permit me to see her?\" He said: \"Yes.\" And indeed I used to contrive for her among the trunks of the palm trees so that she would pass by me."],[17852,"Abu Bakr said: \"I do not find anything for you in the Book of Allah, and I have not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ give a ruling for you in anything. I will ask the people this evening.\" When he prayed Zuhr, he turned to the people and said: \"A grandmother has come to me asking about her inheritance from her grandson or her granddaughter's son, and I have not found anything for her in the Book, nor have I heard the Prophet ﷺ rule anything for her. Has any of you heard anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning her?\" Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah stood up and said: \"I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her a sixth.\" He said: \"Did anyone hear that with you?\" Muhammad b. Maslamah stood up and said: \"I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her a sixth.\" So Abu Bakr gave her a sixth. When it was the caliphate of Umar, the other grandmother came to him. Umar ؓ said: \"The ruling was only for someone other than you, but if you both come together, then the sixth is between you, and whichever of you is alone with it, it is hers.\""],[17853,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik. H. And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: Abdullah b. Abd al-Hakam narrated to us. H. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: Abdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us. H. And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us: Amr b. Marzuq narrated to us. They said: Malik reported to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Uthman b. Ishaq b. Kharashah, from Qabisah b. Dhu'ayb, who said: A grandmother came to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ asking him about her inheritance in the Book of Allah. Abu Bakr said to her: \"You have nothing in the Book of Allah, and I do not know of anything for you in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so go back until I ask the people.\" He asked the people, and al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah said: \"I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he gave her a sixth.\" Abu Bakr said: \"Is there anyone else with you?\" Muhammad b. Maslamah al-Ansari stood up and said the like of what al-Mughirah said, so Abu Bakr carried it out for her. Then the other grandmother came to Umar b. al-Khattab asking him about her inheritance. He said: \"You have nothing in the Book of Allah, and the ruling that was given was only for someone other than you, and I am not going to add anything to the fixed shares, but it is that sixth, so if you both come together, it is between you, and whichever of you is alone with it, it is hers.\" The wording is that of the hadith of Ibn Abd al-Hakam."],[17854,"Al-Mughirah said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in it with a ghurrah (a slave).\" Umar said: \"If you are truthful, bring someone who knows that.\" Muhammad b. Maslamah testified that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rule in it with a ghurrah."],[17855,"Al-Mughirah said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in it with a ghurrah of a male or female slave.\" Umar said: \"Who will confirm you?\" Muhammad b. Maslamah testified for him."],[17856,"Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in it with a ghurrah.\" Muhammad b. Maslamah al-Ansari testified for him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled with it."],[17857,"When the Prophet ﷺ wanted something, he would distance himself."],[17858,"\"That he was with two men of his people who were disbelievers, and he killed them and took their spoils, then he came to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ disapproved of what he had done, and he offered him their spoils, but he did not accept it.\""],[17859,"\"That he accompanied a group of polytheists and found them heedless, so he killed them and took their property, then he brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He disapproved of what he had done and refused to accept it.\""],[17860,"Al-Mughirah said: \"I said to Umar: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in it with the ghurrah.' Umar said: 'If you are truthful, bring me someone who knows this with you.' Muhammad b. Maslamah said: 'I bear witness that the Prophet ﷺ ruled in the miscarriage of a woman with the ghurrah.' So Umar ؓ ruled accordingly.\""],[17861,"\"That he accompanied a group of polytheists and found them heedless, so he killed them and took their property, then he brought it to the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ refused to accept it.\""],[17862,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us and informed us of what would happen in his community until the Day of Resurrection. He who grasped it grasped it, and he who forgot it forgot it.\""],[17863,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on a journey and encamped, then he went to relieve himself. I followed him with a water vessel, and when he came back I met him and poured water for him. He performed ablution, and he had on leather socks, so he wiped over them, then he prayed the morning prayer.\""],[17864,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[17865,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey, and al-Mughira was on that journey. He said: One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to relieve himself, so I followed his tracks with a water vessel and cleared the way for him. He performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[17866,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[17867,"The Prophet ﷺ said: On the night of the cave, Allah commanded a tree and it grew in front of the Prophet ﷺ, and Allah commanded the spider and it wove in front of the Prophet ﷺ, and He commanded two wild pigeons and they stood at the mouth of the cave. The young men of Quraysh approached, one man from every clan, with their staffs, clubs, and swords, until when they were about forty cubits from the Prophet ﷺ, some of them hurried to look into the cave. He saw two pigeons at the mouth of the cave, so he returned to his companions. They said to him, \"What is wrong with you? Why did you not look into the cave?\" He said, \"I saw two pigeons at the mouth of the cave, so I knew that no one was inside.\" The Prophet ﷺ heard what he said and knew that Allah had protected him by means of them. So he supplicated for them, invoked blessings upon them, prescribed their recompense, and they were settled in the Haram."],[17868,"I sought permission to see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ between Makkah and Madinah. He said, \"Meet me tonight, even if you are exhausted,\" and I did not prefer anything over him until morning."],[17869,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[17870,"Regarding what he witnessed from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Tabuk, he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on the expedition of Tabuk, and he wiped over his leather socks.\""],[17871,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, they both said: Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya b. Sa'id, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyab, from Ma'mar b. 'Abd Allah b. Nadla, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever hoards is a sinner.\""],[17872,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one hoards except a sinner.\" Muhammad said: Sa'id used to hoard, and Ma'mar used to hoard."],[17873,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"No one hoards except a sinner.\""],[17874,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one hoards except a sinner.\" I said to Sa'id, \"You hoard.\" He said, \"Ma'mar used to hoard.\""],[17875,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"No one hoards except a sinner.\""],[17876,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, \"No one hoards except a sinner.\""],[17877,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No one hoards except a sinner.\""],[17878,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me to announce among the people in Mina: \"The days of tashriq are days of eating and drinking.\""],[17879,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Food for food, like for like.\""],[17880,"\"Sell it, then buy barley with it.\" The boy went and took a sa' and some of a sa' extra. When he came, Ma'mar informed him of that, and Ma'mar said, \"Why did you do that? Go and return it. Do not take except like for like, for I used to hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Food, like for like.' And our food that day was barley.\" It was said, \"It is not like it.\" He said, \"I fear that it may resemble riba.\""],[17881,"I heard Ma'mar say: I used to saddle the mount for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Ma'mar, tonight I found looseness in my saddle straps.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I fastened them as I always fasten them, but someone who grudges me that wants to replace me.\" He said, \"Indeed, I will not do that.\" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his Hajj, he ordered me, and I took the razor and sharpened it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Ma'mar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has given you access to the lobe of his ear while the razor is in your hand.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I regard that as a favor and grace to me.\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then increase that.\""],[17882,"That the Prophet ﷺ, when he stood in prayer, would grasp his left hand with his right hand. He said: And I saw 'Alqamah do it."],[17883,"That the Prophet ﷺ would give salutation to his right and to his left."],[17884,"That he prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, and when he said, \"Not of those who incurred anger, nor of those who went astray,\" he said Amin, lowering his voice with it."],[17885,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted him land in Hadramawt."],[17886,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came with a leather strap around his neck. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this man and my brother were in a pit digging it, and the pickaxe fell and struck his companion's head and killed him.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Pardon him.\" He refused. Then he stood and mentioned similar words, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Pardon him.\" He refused. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Take him away, for if you kill him, you will be like him.\" He went out with him until he passed by, then called out, \"Do you not hear what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ says?\" He returned, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If you kill him, you will be like him.\" He said, \"Yes, I pardon him.\" Then he went out dragging his strap until he disappeared from us."],[17887,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man was brought with a leather strap being led. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the guardian of the slain man, \"Will you pardon him?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Will you take the blood money?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Will you kill him?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Take him away.\" He turned away from him, then he said, \"Come, will you pardon?\" similar to his first statement. The guardian of the slain man gave a similar answer three times. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the fourth, \"Indeed, if you pardon, he will bear your sin and the sin of your companion.\" So he left him. He said: I saw him dragging his strap."],[17888,"“I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ when he stood for prayer raise his hands, and when he raised his head from bowing he did that.”"],[17889,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever wrongfully usurps a man's land will meet God while He is angry with him.”"],[17890,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ bowed, he would spread his fingers, and when he prostrated, he would press his fingers together."],[17891,"I was a boy who could not understand my father’s prayer. Alqama b. Wa’il narrated to me from my father Wa’il b. Hujr, who said: “I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he said the takbir, he raised his hands, then wrapped himself and took his right hand with his left and placed his hands inside his garment. When he wanted to raise his head from bowing, he raised his hands, then prostrated and placed his forehead between his palms. When he raised his head from prostration, he raised his hands, until he finished his prayer.”"],[17892,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating on the ground, placing his forehead and his nose in his prostration.”"],[17893,"“The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution, rinsed his nose with water, and interlaced his fingers with his fingers.”"],[17894,"The Prophet ﷺ called for a bucket of water, drank from it, then spat into it."],[17895,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and it would not please me to have, in exchange for my face [i.e., my seeing him], the face of any man from the Bedouin Arabs. I saw him praying: he would say the takbīr when rising and when prostrating, and he would give salām to his right and to his left when he finished, until I could see the whiteness of his cheek from here and here."],[17896,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, when he began the prayer, raise his hands until the tips of his thumbs were level with the lobes of his ears."],[17897,"“I prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he gave salutation to his right: ‘Peace be upon you and the mercy of God and His blessings,’ and to his left: ‘Peace be upon you and the mercy of God.’” Mūsā b. Qays narrated it thus from Salama, who reported from ʿAlqama b. Wāʾil, and he added in the salutation “and His blessings.”"],[17898,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and said, \"You claim that I am among the last of you to die, but I am the first of you to die, and you will follow me in bands, destroying one another.\""],[17899,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Whoever goes to a soothsayer and asks him about something, repentance is withheld from him for forty nights; and if he believes what he said, he has disbelieved.\""],[17900,"I tried to be seen by the Prophet ﷺ at the mosque of al-Khayf. His companions said to me, “Move away, O Wathilah,” meaning, get out of the Prophet’s ﷺ sight. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Leave him, for he has only come to ask.” So I drew near and said, “May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God. Give us a ruling about a matter we can take from you after you are gone.” He said, “Let your own self help you.” I said, “How can I do that?” He said, “Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt, even if the muftis give you a fatwa.” I said, “How can I know that?” He said, “Place your hand over your heart, for the heart is at rest with what is lawful and is not at rest with what is unlawful. The scrupulousness of a Muslim is that he leaves the small matter for fear of falling into the major one.” I said, “May my father and mother be your ransom, what is bias?” He said, “It is when a man helps his people in wrongdoing.” I said, “Who is the greedy?” He said, “The one who seeks a livelihood from an unlawful source.” I said, “Who is the scrupulous?” He said, “The one who halts at what is doubtful.” I said, “Who is the believer?” He said, “The one from whom people feel safe regarding their wealth and their lives.” I said, “Who is the Muslim?” He said, “The one from whose tongue and hand people are safe.” I said, “Which struggle is most excellent?” He said, “A word of justice before a tyrannical ruler.”"],[17901,"I set out as an emigrant to the Messenger of God ﷺ. When the people came, some standing and some sitting, the Messenger of God ﷺ did not see anyone sitting without approaching him and asking, “Do you need anything?” He began with the first row, then the second, then the third, until he came near me and said, “Do you need anything?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said, “What is your need?” I said, “Islam.” He said, “It is better for you.” He said, “Will you emigrate?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “A desert emigration or a permanent emigration?” I said, “Which of them is better?” He said, “The permanent emigration is that you stay with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the desert emigration is that you return to your desert, and you must hear and obey in your hardship and ease, in what you dislike and what you like, and when others are preferred over you.” He said, “So I stretched out my hand to him and pledged allegiance to him.” He said, “He made an exception for me when I did not make one for myself, saying, ‘In what you are able.’” He said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ called for the expedition to Tabuk. I went out to my family and found my father sitting in the sun with his back to it. I greeted him with the greeting of Islam. He said, ‘Have you become a Sabian?’ I said, ‘I have submitted.’ He said, ‘Perhaps God will make it good for you and us.’ I accepted that from him. While I was with him, my sister came to me and greeted me. I said, ‘O sister, provide me with the provision a woman gives her brother going on a campaign.’ She brought me dough in a bucket, and the bucket was in a provision bag. I set out, and the Messenger of God ﷺ had already departed. I began calling out, ‘Is there anyone who will carry a man in exchange for his share?’ An old man from the Ansar called out to me and said, ‘His share is ours on condition that we carry him alternating behind us and that his food is with us.’ I said, ‘Yes, go with the blessing of God.’ I went out with the best companion. He gave me a mount beyond what I had stipulated and favored me with food besides what he ate with it, until God granted us spoils. I obtained some young camels and drove them until I came to him while he was in his tent. I called him and he came out and sat on a saddlebag from his camel’s saddlebags. Then he said, ‘Drive them away from you.’ I drove them away. Then he said, ‘Drive them toward you.’ I drove them toward him. He said, ‘I do not see your young camels except as noble.’ I said, ‘They are only your share of the spoils that I stipulated for you.’ He said, ‘Take your young camels, O son of my brother, for we did not intend anything other than your share.’"],[17902,"I said, “O Prophet of God, tell me.” He said, “If you wish, I will tell you what you came to ask about; and if you wish, ask.” I said, “Rather tell me, O Messenger of God, for that is more pleasing to my soul.” He said, “You came to ask about certainty and doubt.” I said, “That is it, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Certainty is what settles in the chest and the heart is at rest with it, even if the muftis give you a fatwa. Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt, for good is tranquility and doubt is unease. When you doubt, leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt.” I said, “O Prophet of God, may my father and mother be your ransom, what is bias?” He said, “That you help your people in wrongdoing. The scrupulous is the one who halts at doubtful matters, and the greedy for this world is the one who seeks it from an unlawful source, and sin is what causes unease in the chest.”"],[17903,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"It is not permissible for a woman to dispose of any of her wealth except with her husband's permission, once he has taken charge of her marriage.\""],[17904,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"You will continue to be in good as long as there remains among you someone who saw someone who saw me and accompanied me.\""],[17905,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God ﷻ said: \"I am as My servant thinks of Me, so let My servant think as he wishes.\""],[17906,"I saw Wathilah b. al-Asqa' enter the mosque of Damascus and pray in it. He spat under his left foot and then rubbed it. When he finished, I said to him: \"Do you spit in the mosque when you are one of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" He said: \"This is how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.\""],[17907,"We entered upon Yazid b. al-Aswad to visit him, and Wathilah b. al-Asqa' entered upon him. When he saw him, he extended his hand and wiped his face and chest with it, for he had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ with that hand. Wathilah said: \"What do you think of your Lord?\" He said: \"Good.\" Wathilah said: \"Then rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say that God says: 'I am as My servant thinks of Me; if good, then good, and if evil, then evil.'\""],[17908,"He narrated to him, saying: I was in the Suffah, and they were twenty men. We were struck by hunger, and I was the youngest of the group, so they sent me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to complain to him of their hunger. He looked around in his house and said, \"Is there anything?\" They said, \"Yes, here is a piece of bread and some milk.\" He said, \"Bring it to me.\" He crumbled the bread into fine crumbs, then poured the milk over it, then carried it in his hand until he made it like tharid. Then he said, \"O Wathilah, call ten of your companions for me and leave ten behind.\" I did so. Then he said, \"Sit down. In the name of Allah.\" They sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of the top of the tharid and said, \"Eat from around it. In the name of Allah. Indeed, blessing comes to it from above it, and because it is replenished.\" He said: I saw them eating, picking between their fingers until they became full with satiety. When they had finished, he said to them, \"Depart to your place and send your companions to me.\" I stood up, amazed at what I had seen. Then he turned to the ten and commanded them similarly, and they ate until they became full with satiety, and there was still some left in it."],[17909,"A group from Banu Sulaym came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we take captives and we practice coitus interruptus with them.\" He said, \"And you indeed do that?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"There is no soul that Allah wills to come forth from the loins of a man except that it comes forth, whether he wishes or refuses. So there is no harm upon you if you do not do it.\""],[17910,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, the most wicked of falsehoods is for a man to claim descent from other than his father, or to lie against the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or to lie about what his own eyes have seen.\""],[17911,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No man goes to a fortune-teller and asks him anything except that repentance is withheld from him for forty nights. If he believes what the fortune-teller says, then he has disbelieved in Allah.\""],[17912,"I met Wathilah b. al-Asqa' and said, \"You gave allegiance with this hand of yours to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"Give me your hand so that I may kiss it.\" He gave it to me, and I kissed it."],[17913,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever has three children born to him and does not name one of them Muhammad has been ignorant.\""],[17914,"A man entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was in it alone, so he moved aside for him. The man said, “O Messenger of Allah, the place is spacious.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, a Muslim has a right.”"],[17915,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He is not one of us who does not show mercy to our young and honor our elders.\""],[17916,"I went out intending to see 'Ali. It was said to me, \"He is with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So I went to him and found them in an enclosure of reeds. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn were gathered together under a garment. He said, \"O Allah, indeed You have made Your blessings, Your mercy, Your forgiveness, and Your good pleasure upon me and upon them.\""],[17917,"I heard my father say: 'Indeed he succeeds who purifies himself and mentions the name of his Lord and prays'—the throwing of wheat on the day of Fitr before the prayer in the prayer place."],[17918,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the noon prayer in Makkah as two rak'ahs, the prayer of a traveler."],[17919,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr at al-Batha' two rak'ahs, then he traveled and prayed Asr two rak'ahs until he arrived in Madinah, where he completed it."],[17920,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at al-Abtah, and the Prophet ﷺ was in a dome of tanned leather. He performed ablution from a stone basin, and Bilal came out with the leftover water. Then he prayed Zuhr and Asr while men, women, and donkeys passed in front of him from beyond the spear."],[17921,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever sees me, then he has indeed seen me, for Satan is not able to resemble me.”"],[17922,"“We performed Hajj with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and we continued to pray two rak‘ahs until we returned.”"],[17923,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man praying who had let his garment hang down, and he cut it off from him."],[17924,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the price of blood."],[17925,"The Messenger of God ﷺ established brotherhood between Salman and Abu al-Darda. Salman came to visit Abu al-Darda and found Umm al-Darda in worn-out clothing. He said, \"What is the matter with you, O Umm al-Darda?\" She said, \"Your brother Abu al-Darda stands in prayer at night and fasts during the day, and he has no need for anything of this world.\" Abu al-Darda came and welcomed Salman and brought him some food. Salman said to him, \"Eat.\" He said, \"I am fasting.\" Salman said, \"I swear you must break your fast.\" He refused to eat until he ate with him, so he ate with him. Then he spent the night at his place. When it was night, Abu al-Darda wanted to get up, but Salman prevented him. Then he said, \"O Abu al-Darda, your body has a right over you, your Lord has a right over you, and your family has a right over you. Give every rightful one his due.\" When it was near dawn, he said, \"Now get up if you wish.\" So they both got up, performed ablution, and prayed. Then they went out to the prayer. Abu al-Darda approached to inform the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Your body has a right over you, just as Salman said.\""],[17926,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbid the earnings of a cupper and the dower of a prostitute."],[17927,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ with two men from Banu 'Amir. He said, \"What people are you from?\" We said, \"From Banu 'Amir.\" He said, \"You two are from me.\""],[17928,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the price of blood, the price of a dog, and the dower of a prostitute. He cursed the woman who tattoos and the one who asks to be tattooed, and the one who consumes riba and the one who pays it."],[17929,"From the Prophet, ﷺ who said, \"Whoever sees me in a dream, it is as if he has seen me in wakefulness, for surely Satan cannot take my form.\""],[17930,"\"I drew near to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at al-Abṭaḥ when the sun had declined from its meridian. Bilāl went out and called the adhān for the prayer.\""],[17931,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ in a red leather tent. He said: \"I saw Bilāl bring out his ablution water, and I saw the people rushing to that water. Whoever got some of it wiped himself with it, and whoever did not get any of it took from the moisture on his companion's hand. Then I saw Bilāl bring out a short spear and plant it in the ground. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out wearing a red ḥulla with his garments raised, and he prayed two rakʿahs with the people facing the spear. I saw people and animals passing in front of the spear.\""],[17932,"I was with my uncle in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon. He said, \"The affairs of my Ummah will continue to be righteous as long as twelve caliphs pass.\" He lowered his voice with this statement, so I asked my uncle who was in front of me, \"What did he say, uncle?\" He replied, \"O my son, all of them will be from the Quraysh.\""],[17933,"\"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at al-Abṭaḥ in a leather tent. Bilāl went out and called the adhān for the Ẓuhr prayer. Then he entered and helped him perform ablution, then brought out the leftover water in a small vessel. We crowded around it—some getting it with their hands and others being sprinkled with whatever water was destined for them. Then he entered and brought out a short spear and planted it between him and the qibla, while a woman and a donkey passed by. Then he called the iqāma, and the Prophet ﷺ came out wearing a red ḥulla, as if I were looking at the gleam of his shins. He led us in Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr, two rakʿahs each.\""],[17934,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying at al-Abṭaḥ, having planted a short spear in front of him, while a donkey and a woman passed in front of him.\""],[17935,"O Salama, \"Nothing remains of what I used to know except this prayer; and there is no soul that I would like to protect me from death, not even the soul of a fly.\""],[17936,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I was sent and the Hour are like this from this; it almost overtook me.\""],[17937,"Abu Juḥayfah saw me carrying a garment to the bleacher, and on it was written ‘a devil.’ He forbade me, and this is the correct [version]."],[17938,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said, “An ʿumrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj.”"],[17939,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “If a man gets up from his seat and then returns to it, he has more right to it.”"],[17940,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivering a sermon during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he said, 'Let those present convey to those who are absent.'"],[17941,"That he heard Wābisa b. Maʿbad, the Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, say: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about righteousness and sin, and he said, 'O Wābisa, you have come to ask me about righteousness and sin.' I said, 'Indeed, by the One who sent you with the truth, it is for this that I came to ask you.' He said, 'Righteousness is that which your heart feels at ease with, and sin is that which wavers in your heart, even if people give you rulings about it.'"],[17942,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, intending not to leave anything of righteousness and sin without asking him about it. I went to him while he was among a group of Muslims around him, and I began to step over them to draw near to him. Some of them rebuked me, saying, 'Step back, O Wābisa, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' I said, 'I want to draw near to him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Leave Wābisa; come near me, O Wābisa.' So he brought me close until I stood before him. Then he said, 'Will you ask me, or shall I inform you?' I said, 'No, rather you inform me.' He said, 'You have come to ask about righteousness and sin.' I said, 'Yes.' He gathered his fingertips and began tapping them on my chest, and said, 'Righteousness is that which the soul feels at ease with and the heart feels at ease with, and sin is that which wavers in the soul and hesitates in the chest, even if people give you rulings about it, whatever rulings they give you.'"],[17943,"When the Prophet ﷺ conquered Makkah, the people of Makkah began bringing their children to him, and he would wipe their heads and supplicate for blessing for them. I was brought to him while I was perfumed with khalūq, and he did not wipe my head, and nothing prevented him from that except that my mother had perfumed me with khalūq. So he did not wipe my head because of the khalūq. Abu al-Qāsim said: This is how Zayd b. Abī al-Zarqāʾ narrated it, from Jaʿfar, from Thābit b. al-Ḥajjāj, from ʿAbdallāh al-Hamdānī, from Abū Mūsā, from al-Walīd b. ʿUqba; but the correct chain is from ʿAbdallāh al-Hamdānī, who is Abū Mūsā, from al-Walīd b. ʿUqba."],[17944,"I had leprosy, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for me, and I was cured of it."],[17945,"Al-Walīd was imprisoned in Makkah, and when he wanted to emigrate, he sold a property of his called al-Manā for a she-camel in al-Ṭāʾif, and he said..."],[17946,"I said, 'O Muhammad, how does the one who comes to you come to you?' meaning Jibrīl ﷺ . The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'He comes to me from the sky; his two wings are pearls, and the soles of his feet are green.'"],[17947,"Musaylima, Ibn Shighāf, and Ibn al-Nawwāḥa sent me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We arrived before him, and the two of them preceded me in speaking, for they were older than me. They pronounced the testimony of faith, then said, 'We bear witness that you are a prophet, and that Musaylima is after you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What do you say, O boy?' I said, 'I bear witness to what you bore witness to, and I reject what you rejected.' He said, 'Then I bear witness, as many as the grains of dust of the world, that Musaylima is a liar.' Then he said, 'Seize them both.' So they were seized, and he ordered that they be taken to the house of Kaysān. Then a man from his Companions interceded for them, and he released them."],[17948,"From Wāqid, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said, 'Whoever obeys Allah, Exalted is He, has remembered Him, even if his prayer, fasting, and recitation of the Qur'an are little. And whoever disobeys Allah has not remembered Him, even if his prayer, fasting, and recitation of the Qur'an are abundant.'"],[17949,"From the Prophet ﷺ that a man who had killed someone was brought to him. The killer was handed over to the guardian of the slain man so that he could execute him. When they went off with him, and there was a rope around his neck, the Prophet ﷺ said to those sitting with him: “The killer and the slain are in the Fire.” A man went to the guardian and told him what the Messenger of God ﷺ had said, so he let him go. I saw him when he let him go, and he went off dragging his rope. Ismāʿīl said: I mentioned that to Ḥabīb b. Abī Thābit, and he said, on the authority of Ibn Ashwaʿ: The Messenger of God ﷺ had ordered that man to pardon, but it was as if he did not do so. When he was told what the Messenger of God ﷺ had said, he let him go."],[17950,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding “raising his hands for the prayer.” Ḥuṣayn said: Ibrāhīm said: I do not know; perhaps Wāʾil did not see the Prophet ﷺ except on that day, so how did he memorize it while ʿAbd Allāh and his companions did not memorize it? Is he more knowledgeable about the Messenger of God ﷺ, or ʿAbd Allāh? He only used to raise his hands at the opening."],[17951,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ used to raise his hands before the bowing and after it.” I mentioned that to Ibrāhīm, and he became angry and said: He saw him, but Ibn Masʿūd and his companions did not see him."],[17952,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ when he said “nor of those who go astray” say “Āmīn.”"],[17953,"“The Prophet ﷺ granted him a piece of land in Ḥaḍramawt.”"],[17954,"The Messenger of God ﷺ granted me a piece of land and sent Muʿāwiyah with me, saying, “Mark it for him and give it to him.” Muʿāwiyah said to me: Let me ride behind you. I said: You are not one of the riders behind kings. He said: Give me your sandal to wear. I said: Wear the shade of the she-camel. When Muʿāwiyah became caliph, I came to him and he seated me with him on the couch. Then he reminded me of the hadith. Simāk said: He said: I wish I had carried him in front of me."],[17955,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not call the grapevine karm, but say ḥabalah or ḥabal.”"],[17956,"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ when Suwayd b. Ṭāriq asked him about wine, and he forbade him. He said: We treat illness with it and put it in medicine. The Prophet ﷺ said: “It is not a medicine, but a disease.”"],[17957,"Yazīd b. Salamah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, we have many vineyards. Should we not press them and sell it and seek healing with it? He said: “No, it is a disease.”"],[17958,"A man from Ḥaḍramawt and a man from Kindah came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Ḥaḍramī said: O Messenger of God, this man has seized from me land that belonged to my father. The Kindī said: It is my land, in my possession; I cultivate it. He has no right in it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do you have evidence?” He said: No. He said: “Then his oath is yours.” He said: O Messenger of God, he is a wicked man who does not care what he swears to; he does not refrain from anything. The Prophet ﷺ said: “You have from him nothing but that.” He went off to swear. When he turned away, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, if he swears falsely about his property to consume it wrongfully, he will surely meet God while He is turning away from him.”"],[17959,"A man forced himself upon a woman in the darkness of dawn while she was heading to the mosque, overpowering her. She sought help from a man who passed by her, and her attacker fled. Then a group of people with numbers passed by her, and she sought their help. They caught up with the one she had sought help from, while the other had outrun them. They brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. She told him that he had forced himself upon her, and the people told him that they had caught him running away. He said: I was only helping her against her attacker, and these people caught me and seized me. She said: He is lying; he is the one who forced himself upon me. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Take him and stone him.” A man from the people stood up and said: Do not stone him. I am the one who did the deed with her. So he confessed. Thus three gathered before the Messenger of God ﷺ: the one who forced himself upon her, the one who helped her, and the woman. He said: “As for you, you have been forgiven,” and he said good words to the one who helped her. ʿUmar said: Stone the one who confessed to adultery. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, he has repented to God with a repentance that if the people of Yathrib were to repent with it, it would be accepted from them.”"],[17960,"A woman went out in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ intending to pray, and a man met her and had his way with her. She screamed, and he fled. Then a man passed by her, and she said, “That man did such-and-such to me.” So they went and seized the man whom she thought had fallen upon her. They said, “Is this the one?” She said, “Yes, it is he.” They brought him to the Prophet ﷺ, and when he ordered that he be stoned, the one who had actually fallen upon her stood up and said, “I am her companion.” He said, “Come near to me, for God has forgiven you,” and he spoke kindly to the other man. They said to him about the man who had fallen upon her, “Will you stone him?” He said, “He has repented with such a repentance that if the people of Madinah were to repent with it, it would be accepted from them.”"],[17961,"“O Messenger of God, what do you think if rulers are set over us who demand their right from us but deny us our right? What do you command us?” He turned away from him. Then he asked him again, and he turned away. Then he asked him a second or third time, and he said, “Listen and obey. Upon them is what they have been charged with, and upon you is what you have been charged with.”"],[17962,"Yazid b. Salama came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon and said, “O Messenger of God, what do you think if there are people over us who take from us what is rightfully due but deny us the right of God?” The Prophet ﷺ remained silent and did not answer him. Then he repeated it a second time, and he did not answer him. Then he repeated it a third time, and the Prophet ﷺ said, “Upon him is what he bears, and upon you is what you bear. If you obey him, you will be guided, so listen to him and obey.”"],[17963,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “This man killed my brother, O Messenger of God.” He said, “How did you kill him?” He said, “I struck his head with an axe, and I did not intend to kill him.” He said, “Do you have wealth with which to pay his blood money?” He said, “No.” The Prophet ﷺ said to the man, “Take him.” So he went out with him to kill him, but the Prophet ﷺ said, “If he kills him, he will be like him.” The man brought him back when he heard his words and said, “Here he is, so order concerning him whatever you wish.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Let him go.”"],[17964,"While I was with the Prophet ﷺ, a man entered leading another man by a rope until he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, this man killed my brother.” He said, “Did you kill him?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “How did you kill him?” He said, “We were gathering firewood from a tree, and he insulted me, so I struck him with an axe on the side of his head and killed him.” He said, “Do you have wealth with which to pay for yourself?” He said, “No, by God, I have no wealth except my axe and my cloak.” He said, “Do you think your people will pay on your behalf?” He said, “I am less important to my people than that.” So the man threw his rope to him and said, “Take charge of your companion.” When he turned away, the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “If he kills him, he is like him.” A man came to him and said, “Woe to you! The Messenger of God ﷺ says, ‘If he kills him, he is like him.’” He said, “O Messenger of God, I did not take him except by your command.” He said, “Do you not want him to bear his sin and the sin of your companion?” He said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Then it is so.” He threw his rope and said, “Go wherever you wish.”"],[17965,"Al-Ash'ath b. Qays al-Kindi and a man from Hadramawt brought a dispute before the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning some land that was in the possession of al-Ash'ath b. Qays al-Kindi and which the Hadrami claimed. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to the Hadrami, “Bring your proof.” He said, “I have no proof.” He said, “Then if you have no proof, al-Ash'ath will swear an oath.” He said, “My right is lost, O Messenger of God, if you make it subject to the oath of al-Ash'ath.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever swears an oath in which he is lying in order to seize thereby the property of a Muslim man will meet God on the Day of Resurrection while He is angry with him.”"],[17966,"I prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said the takbir when he began the prayer and raised his hands, and when he intended to bow he raised his hands, and after he raised his head from bowing."],[17967,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “This is Wa'il b. Hujr. He has come to you not out of desire or fear, but out of love for God and His Messenger.” He spread his cloak for him, seated him beside him, drew him close, and took him up onto the pulpit. He addressed the people and said to his companions, “Be gentle with him, for he has recently left kingship.” I said, “My family has overcome me regarding what belongs to me.” He said, “I will give it to you and give you double it.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, “O Wa'il b. Hujr, when you pray, place your hands level with your ears, and a woman places her hands level with her breasts.”"],[17968,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Blessed is the one who sees me, and the one who sees the one who sees me,” three times."],[17969,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “nor of those who go astray,” he said, “Amin,” so that we could hear him."],[17970,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ and prayed behind him. He began to recite, and when he said, “{not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray},” he said “Āmīn” aloud."],[17971,"He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, and when he recited the Opening of the Book and said, “{not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray},” he said “Āmīn” and raised his voice with it."],[17972,"I prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ. He began with the Opening of the Book, and when he finished it, he said “Āmīn” until those behind him heard it."],[17973,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ recite “{not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray},” and he said “Āmīn,” prolonging his voice with it."],[17974,"I prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he recited the Opening of the Book. When he finished it, he said “Āmīn,” prolonging his voice with it."],[17975,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ and prayed behind him. He began to recite, and when he said, “{not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray},” he said “Āmīn” aloud until I heard it."],[17976,"I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, and when he said, “{not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray},” he said “Āmīn,” extending his voice with it."],[17977,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ enter prayer, and when he finished the Opening of the Book, he said “Āmīn” three times."],[17978,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, and when he recited “{not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray},” he said “Āmīn” so as to coincide with the believing angels."],[17979,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ when he said, “{not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray},” say “Āmīn,” and those behind him said “Āmīn.”"],[17980,"I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he recited {not those who have evoked [Your] anger or those who are astray}, he said \"Ameen\" until I heard him while I was behind him."],[17981,"“I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, when he was about to bow, raise his hands until they reached his ears.”"],[17982,"“He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, and he said takbīr and raised his hands.”"],[17983,"I prayed behind the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he began the prayer, he said the takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his ears."],[17984,"I prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ and saw him raising his hands up to his ears."],[17985,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ raising his hands when he made the opening takbir until they reached just below his ears."],[17986,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ raise his hands and say the takbir."],[17987,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, when he began the prayer, raising his hands to just below his ears."],[17988,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ place his right hand over his left hand in prayer."],[17989,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ enter the prayer, say the takbir, then place his right forearm over his left forearm."],[17990,"I prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ and saw him placing the right hand over the other."],[17991,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ place his right hand over his left hand in prayer, near the wrist."],[17992,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ lean with one hand upon the other in prayer."],[17993,"He prayed behind the Messenger of God ﷺ and heard a man say: 'Praise be to God, abundant, pure, blessed praise.' When the Prophet ﷺ finished his prayer, he said: 'Who is the owner of these words?' He said: 'I, O Messenger of God. By God, I intended nothing but good by them.' He said: 'The gates of heaven were opened for them, and nothing stopped them short of the Throne.'"],[17994,"The Prophet ﷺ was praying when a man came and entered the row, saying: 'God is great, greatly great, and glory be to God morning and evening.' When the Prophet ﷺ said the salam, he said: 'Who is the owner of these words?' The man said: 'I, O Messenger of God. I intended nothing but good by them.' He said: 'I saw the gates of heaven opened, and they did not stop short of the Throne.'"],[17995,"The Prophet ﷺ was in prayer when someone entered the mosque and also began to pray. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Allah is the Greatest, very Great, and Glory be to Allah with abundant praise.\" Then, the Prophet ﷺ was raised up to the heavens, and then he returned to his prayer. When he finished his prayer, he asked, \"Who was the person who spoke the words?\" The person replied, \"It was me, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the doors of heavens were opened for them, and nothing prevented it except the Throne.\""],[17996,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, and he heard a man saying: “Allah is greater, greatly; and glory be to Allah, with His praise, abundantly.” When he finished, he said: “Who is the one who said those words?” The man said: “I intended only good.” He said: “The gates of heaven were opened for them, and nothing stopped them short of the Throne.”"],[17997,"I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he heard a man saying: “Allah is greater, greatly; praise be to Allah, abundantly, pure and blessed therein.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I saw them as twelve angels rushed to them, and the gates of heaven were opened for them.”"],[17998,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he entered the prayer, raised his hands and said the takbir, then wrapped himself in his garment, then placed his right hand over his left. When he wanted to bow, he did like this with his garment and brought out his hands, then raised them and said the takbir and bowed. When he wanted to prostrate, his knees fell to the ground before his palms. When he prostrated, he placed his forehead between his palms and kept his upper arms away from his sides. Hammam said: “And to the best of my knowledge, in the hadith of Muhammad b. Juhadah: when he rose, he rose upon his knees and supported himself on his thighs.”"],[17999,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he said the takbir in the prayer, raised his hands until they were level with his ears."],[18000,"“A woman was coerced during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he averted the punishment from her and imposed it upon the one who had intercourse with her, and it was not mentioned that he assigned her a dowry.”"],[18001,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ placing his nose on the ground along with his forehead when he prostrated.”"],[18002,"“He came to the Prophet ﷺ and saw him placing his nose along with his forehead in prostration.”"],[18003,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ pray, and I saw the trace of his nose along with his forehead in the thick soil.”"],[18004,"“I used to shake hands with the Prophet ﷺ, or my skin touched his skin, and then I would sniff my hand for three days afterward, and it was more fragrant than musk.”"],[18005,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command burying hair and nails."],[18006,"When my father came to the Prophet ﷺ, he saw him placing his right hand over his left, and he raised his hands with every takbīr."],[18007,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to prostrate between his palms."],[18008,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ raise his hands when he began the prayer, place the right over the left, and keep his palms together."],[18009,"When the Prophet ﷺ prayed, he raised his hands with the takbīr."],[18010,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ place his right hand over his left; and when he sat, he spread his left leg, placed his forearms on his thighs, and pointed with his index finger."],[18011,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ begin the prayer, say the takbīr, and raise his hands; then he grasped his left with his right. When he wanted to bow, he said the takbīr and raised his hands, then placed his palms on his knees and spread his fingers. When he raised his head, he said the takbīr and raised [his hands]. When he prostrated, he placed his forehead between his palms and set his toes upright. When he rose, he folded his left leg and set the toes of his right foot upright. When he sat, he placed his left palm on his left thigh, placed his right elbow on his right thigh, bent his little finger and the one next to it, made a circle with his middle finger and thumb, and pointed with his index finger, supplicating with it."],[18012,"I prayed behind the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: I will surely memorize the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he began the prayer, he said the takbīr and raised his hands until they were level with his ears; then he grasped his left with his right. When he said the takbīr for bowing, he raised his hands again just as he had raised them for the opening takbīr of the prayer. When he bowed, he placed his palms on his knees. When he raised his head from bowing, he raised his hands again. When he sat for the tashahhud, he spread his left leg on the ground, then sat on it; he placed his left palm on his left thigh, placed his right elbow on his right thigh, then bent his fingers and made a circle with his thumb and middle finger, then began supplicating with the other [finger]."],[18013,"I watched the Prophet ﷺ: he raised his hands in prayer when he said the takbīr; then when he said the takbīr [for bowing] he raised his hands; then when he said, “God hears the one who praises Him,” he raised his hands. Then he sat and spread his left leg, placed his left hand on his left knee, placed his right forearm on his right thigh, then pointed with his index finger, placed his thumb on his middle finger and made a circle with it, and closed his fingers. Then he prostrated, and his hands were level with his ears."],[18014,"I said, 'I will certainly look at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to see how he prays.' So I observed him: he said the takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his ears, then he placed his right hand over the back of his left hand, between the wrist and the forearm. Then when he wanted to bow, he raised his hands similarly and placed his hands on his knees. Then he raised his head, raising his hands similarly. Then he prostrated, placing his palms in line with his ears. Then he sat, spreading his left leg, and placed his left hand [on his left thigh]; he placed the edge of his right elbow on his right thigh, then he closed two of his fingers and made a circle [with his thumb and middle finger], then he raised his finger, and I saw him moving it, supplicating with it. Then I came later, in a time of cold, and I saw the people wearing heavy garments and moving their hands from beneath the clothes.' And the wording is from the hadith of Mu'awiya b. 'Amr."],[18015,"He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ. When he said the takbir, he raised his hands. When he prostrated, he kept his upper arms away from his armpits. When he sat, he spread his left leg, placed his left hand on his left thigh, placed his right hand on his right thigh, and pointed with his index finger.' And the wording is from the hadith of Muslim."],[18016,"He informed him: I said, 'I will certainly look at the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, how he prays.' So he stood and raised his hands until they were level with his ears, then he took his left hand with his right. Then when he wanted to bow, he raised his hands until they were level with his ears, then placed his palms on his knees. Then he raised [his head], raising his hands like that. Then he prostrated, placing his hands in line with his ears. Then he prostrated, placing his hands in line with his ears. Then he sat, spread his left leg, placed his left palm on his left knee, then placed the edge of his right elbow on his right thigh, closed two fingers, and made a circle. Then I saw him say, 'Like this,' and Zuhayr raised his index finger."],[18017,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he started the prayer: he raised his hands until they were level with his ears; when he wanted to bow and after he raised [his head] from bowing; and when he sat, he laid down his left leg and stood upright his right [leg], placed his left hand on his left thigh and his right hand on his right thigh, closed two fingers, made a circle, and pointed like this with the index finger."],[18018,"I said, 'I will certainly look at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, how he prays.' He faced the qibla and raised his hands until they were level with his ears, then he took his left hand with his right. When he wanted to bow, he raised them similarly, then placed his hands on his knees. When he raised his head from bowing, he raised them similarly. Then when he prostrated, he placed his head at that position between his hands."],[18019,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he said the takbir, he raised his hands; when he wanted to bow, he raised his hands; when he wanted to prostrate, he raised his hands; and when he sat for tashahhud, he pointed with his index finger."],[18020,"I said, 'I will certainly look at the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, how he prays.' So he stood, faced the qibla, said the takbir, and raised his hands until he brought them level with his ears. Then he grasped his left hand with his right. Then he bowed, raising his hands and bringing them level with his ears, then placed his palms on his knees. Then he raised his head and raised his hands, bringing them level with his ears. Then he prostrated, placing his head between his palms. Then he prayed another rak'a like it. Then he sat, spread his left leg, then supplicated, placing his left palm on his left knee and his right palm on his right knee, and supplicated with his index finger."],[18021,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ strike with his right hand on his left during prayer.\""],[18022,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ. When he prostrated, he spread his left [leg] and stood upright his right [leg]."],[18023,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ when he prostrated: he placed his forehead between his palms."],[18024,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrate, standing his two feet upright and aligning them."],[18025,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ when he stood [from prostration], he leaned on one of his hands."],[18026,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ when he started the prayer: he raised his hands level with his ears."],[18027,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, when he prostrated, place his knees before his hands, and raise his hands before his knees."],[18028,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ and his Companions in winter, and I saw them in hooded cloaks and wrappers, with their hands inside them, raising them to their throats — or he said, to their chests."],[18029,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and I had long hair. He said, “Dhubāb.” So I went and cut some of my hair, then came back to him. He said to me, “Why did you cut your hair?” I said, “I heard you say Dhubāb, and I thought you were criticizing me.” He said, “I did not criticize you; this is better.”"],[18030,"The Prophet ﷺ sent a man to collect zakah. He came with a mangy, emaciated young camel in poor condition and said, “This is from the zakah of So-and-so son of So-and-so the Such-and-such.” The Prophet ﷺ ascended the pulpit, praised and extolled Allah, then said, “I sent my envoy to collect zakah, and he came to the man — the Prophet’s supplication ﷺ — and he brought a humped she-camel, leading it until he reached the son of So-and-so the Such-and-such, and he brought this mangy young camel. May Allah not bless his camels.” News of it reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he led it to him. Then he ascended the pulpit, praised and extolled Allah, then said, “So-and-so son of So-and-so the Such-and-such heard of the Prophet’s supplication ﷺ and came with this humped she-camel. May Allah bless him and his camels.”"],[18031,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Remorse is repentance.”"],[18032,"The Prophet ﷺ said “Āmīn” aloud."],[18033,"I said, “I will certainly watch the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He would say takbir when going down and when rising, raise his hands, and give salutation to his right and to his left."],[18034,"He prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would say takbir when going down and when rising, raise his hands at the takbir, and give salutation to his right and to his left. Shuʿbah said: Abān b. Taghlib said to me about this hadith: “until the whiteness of his face appeared.” I mentioned that to ʿAmr b. Murrah, and he said, “Or something like that.”"],[18035,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ give salutation to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek was visible."],[18036,"I prayed behind ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Yaḥṣubī, and he gave salutation to his right: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,” and to his left the same. He said: I said to him, “From where did you take this?” He said, “I prayed behind Wāʾil b. Ḥujr, and he said, ‘I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did the same until I saw the whiteness of his cheeks.’”"],[18037,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Not (the path) of those who earn Your anger nor of those who go astray.\" He said, \"Lord, forgive me. Amen.\""],[18038,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a killer was brought, dragging his rein. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the guardian of the slain man, “Will you pardon him?” He said, “No.” He said, “Will you take blood money?” He said, “No.” He said, “Will you kill him?” He said, “Yes.” He repeated it to him three times, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “If you pardon him, he will bear his own sin.” He said, “So he pardoned him.” He said, “I saw him dragging his rein after he had been pardoned.”"],[18039,"He prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, and when he said, “nor of those who go astray,” he said “Āmīn,” lowering his voice, placed his right hand over his left hand, and gave salutation to his right and to his left."],[18040,"He prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ; when he said “{nor of those who go astray},” he said “Āmīn” and lowered his voice with it. Then he placed his right hand over his left hand, putting them on his belly. When he said “God hears the one who praises Him,” he said “O God, our Lord, to You is the praise.” And he gave salutation to his right and to his left with two salutations."],[18041,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he said “{nor of those who go astray},” said “Āmīn,” raising his voice with it."],[18042,"I prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ and I heard him when he said “{nor of those who go astray},” he said “Āmīn” and lowered his voice with it. He placed his right hand over his left and gave salutation to his right and to his left."],[18043,"I heard Wāʾil b. Ḥujr al-Ḥaḍramī say: “I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ give salutation until I saw the whiteness of his cheek from this side and from that side.”"],[18044,"“I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he said Āmīn aloud and gave salutation to his right and to his left until I saw the whiteness of his cheek.”"],[18045,"“I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was ill, so much so that he complained; he prayed seated on his side, leaning to his right.”"],[18047,"I was present with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a vessel containing water was brought to him. He poured water over his right hand three times, then dipped his right hand into the vessel and poured from it over his left hand three times. Then he dipped his right hand into the water, scooped a handful, and with it rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, and blew it out three times. Then he inserted both palms into the vessel, carried water with them, and washed his face three times, combed his beard with his fingers, and wiped the inner parts of his ears. Then he inserted his little finger into the inside of his ear to make the water reach. Then he wiped his neck and the inner part of his beard with the leftover water from his face. He washed his right forearm three times, including beyond the elbow, and washed the left similarly with the right, exceeding the elbow. Then he wiped his head three times and wiped the outer parts of his ears, and wiped his neck and the inner part of his beard with the leftover water from his head. Then he washed his right foot three times, passed his fingers between its toes, made the water go beyond the ankle, and raised the water up the shin. Then he did the same with the left. Then he took a handful of water with his right hand and placed it on his head so that it trickled down the sides of his head, and he said: “This is the complete ablution.” Then he entered his prayer niche, and the people formed rows behind him. He looked to his right and his left, then raised his hands for the takbīr until they reached the level of his earlobes. Then he placed his right hand over his left on his chest. Then he recited the Fātiḥa aloud until he finished it, then he said Āmīn aloud upon finishing the recitation of the Fātiḥa, so that those behind him heard it. Then he recited another sūra along with the Fātiḥa. Then he raised his hands for the takbīr until they reached the level of his earlobes, then he bent into rukūʿ, placed his palms on his knees, spread his fingers, and took his time in rukūʿ until his bowing was balanced and became perfectly still, as if they were a flowing river; if a full cup were placed on it, it would not spill. Then he raised his head with humility and raised his hands until they reached the level of his earlobes and said: “God hears the one who praises Him.” Then he stood upright and paused until every bone returned to its place. Then he went down with the takbīr into prostration, pressing his forehead and nose on the ground until the mark of his nose was visible in the sand, and he spread his forearms and placed his head between them. Then he raised his head with the takbīr and sat briefly, resting on his left thigh and standing his right foot upright, fixing the toes of both. Then he went down into prostration similarly. Then he raised his head with the takbīr. Then he did likewise throughout the entire prayer until four rakʿas were completed. Then he sat for the tashahhud, placed his right palm on his right knee, lowered his thigh, and made a circle with his finger, supplicating with it beneath his garment. That was in winter, and his companions behind him had their hands in their clothes, doing this. He performed supererogatory prayer, then gave salutation to his right until the whiteness of his right cheek was seen, then gave salutation to his left until the whiteness of his left cheek was seen."],[18048,"“A bucket of water was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he drank, then he spat into the bucket, then he poured into the well — or he drank from the bucket, then he spat into the well — and there arose from it a scent like musk.”"],[18049,"He “saw the Prophet ﷺ when a bucket was brought to him, and he performed ablution from it, rinsing his mouth, then he spat into it — musk, or better than musk — and he blew his nose outside it.”"],[18050,"“Do not fast during travel in Ramadan; whoever fasts must make it up.” Abu al-Fayḍ said: I met Abu Qirṣāfa Wāthila b. al-Asqaʿ and asked him, and he said: “If you fasted and fasted and fasted, you would not make it up.”"],[18051,"“With good, O son of my brother.”"],[18052,"I met Wathila on the day of Eid and said, “May Allah accept from us and from you.” He replied, “Yes, may Allah accept from us and from you.”"],[18053,"“Do not pray behind him. As for me, if I had prayed behind him, I would have repeated my prayer.”"],[18054,"“Wathila b. al-Asqa‘ died in the year eighty-five, at the age of ninety-eight.”"],[18055,"“Wathila b. al-Asqa‘ died in the year eighty-three, and he was one hundred and five years old.”"],[18056,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do not show gloating over your brother, lest Allah heal him and afflict you.”"],[18057,"“Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with no error, no addition, and no forgetting.” He said, “Did any of you recite anything from the Qur’an tonight?” We said, “Yes, but we are not very good at memorizing it; we add a wāw or an alif, or we omit.” He said, “This Qur’an is written among you, and you do not fail to memorize it, yet you claim you add and omit. So how about hadiths we heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, which perhaps we heard from him only once? It is enough for you, when we narrate a hadith to you, that it be according to its meaning.”"],[18058,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever sells a defect without naming it remains in Allah’s wrath, and the angels keep cursing him.”"],[18059,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “People will be enlisted as armies: an army in Yemen, an army in Syria, an army in the East, and an army in the West.” A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am a young man, and perhaps I shall live to see that. Which of them do you command me to join?” He said, “Adhere to Syria, for it is Allah’s chosen land; He drives His chosen servants to it. Adhere to Syria, for Allah has guaranteed Syria and its people to me. Whoever refuses, let him join his Yemen.”"],[18060,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Every building is a liability upon its owner except what is like this,” and he gestured with his hand, “and every knowledge is a liability upon its holder on the Day of Resurrection, except for one who acts upon it.”"],[18061,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come out to us—and we were merchants—and he would say, “O company of merchants, beware of lying.”"],[18062,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Form rows, and let the best of you lead you in prayer, for Allah selects from the angels and from people.”"],[18063,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A man should not wipe his forehead until he finishes his prayer, but there is no harm in wiping sweat from his temples, for the angels continue to pray for him as long as the trace of prostration is between his eyes.”"],[18064,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever slanders a dhimmi, he will be flogged on the Day of Resurrection with whips of fire.\" I said to Makhul: \"What is the harshest thing that can be said?\" He said: \"It is said to him: 'O son of a disbeliever.'\""],[18065,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Keep your children, your insane, your buying and selling, your disputes, your raised voices, the implementation of your legal punishments, and the unsheathing of your swords away from the mosques. Perfume them on Fridays, and place purification facilities at their doors.\""],[18066,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying to Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman and Mu'adh b. Jabal while they were consulting him about where to settle. He gestured toward Sham. Then they asked him again, and he gestured toward Sham. Then they asked him again, and he gestured toward Sham. He said: \"You must go to Sham, for it is the choicest of Allah's lands, inhabited by His chosen ones from among His creation. Whoever refuses, let him join his Yemen and drink from its waterholes, for Allah has guaranteed me Sham and its people.\""],[18067,"Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: I heard Mu'adh and Hudhayfah consulting the Prophet ﷺ about where to settle. He gestured toward Sham. Then they consulted him again, and he gestured toward Sham. Then they consulted him again, and he gestured toward Sham. On the third time he said: \"You must go to Sham, for it is the choicest of Allah's lands, inhabited by His chosen ones from among His servants. Whoever refuses, let him join his Yemen and drink from its waterholes, for Allah has indeed guaranteed me Sham and its people.\""],[18068,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"The Night of Decree is bright, neither hot nor cold, with no clouds, no rain, no wind, and no shooting stars in it. One of the signs of its day is that the sun rises without rays.\""],[18069,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"On the Day of Resurrection, Allah will raise a servant who has no sin. Allah will say: 'Which of the two matters would you prefer, that I recompense you according to your deeds or according to My blessings upon you?' He will say: 'My Lord, You know that I never disobeyed You.' He will say: 'Seize My servant by one of My blessings.' No good deed will remain for him except that this blessing will consume it. He will then say: 'My Lord, by Your blessing and Your mercy.' He will say: 'By My blessing and My mercy.' Then a servant who considers himself virtuous, seeing no sin for himself, will be brought. He will be asked: 'Did you befriend My friends?' He will say: 'I was at peace with people.' He will say: 'Did you show enmity to My enemies?' He will say: 'My Lord, there was nothing between me and anyone.' Allah, exalted is He, will say: 'My mercy will not reach one who does not befriend My friends and show enmity to My enemies.'\""],[18070,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fasting is a shield and a fortress among the fortresses of the believer. Every deed is for its doer except fasting. Allah, exalted is He, says: 'Fasting is for Me, and I reward for it.'\""],[18071,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The worst gatherings are the marketplaces and the roads, and the best gatherings are the mosques. If you do not sit in the mosque, then stay in your home.\""],[18072,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said: \"The worst gatherings are the markets and roads, and the best gatherings are the mosques. So if you don't sit in the mosque, then stay in your house.\""],[18073,"A questioner asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"What is the reason that on the day of Friday the call to prayer is made for the Salah (prayer) in the middle of the day, while you have forbidden it on other days?\" He replied, \"Verily, Allah heats up Hellfire every day in the middle of the day and cools it down on the day of Friday.\""],[18074,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not withhold from the servants of Allah the surplus of water, pasture, or fire, for Allah has made them common for the needy travelers and a support for the weak.\""],[18075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"On Friday, Allah sends angels to the doors of the mosques to record the people: the first, the second, the third, the fourth, the fifth, and the sixth. When they reach the seventh, it is as if they have offered a sparrow.\""],[18076,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to gain understanding in the religion.\""],[18077,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us not to form circles on Friday before the imam comes out, and to face the qiblah, and not to do so on the two Eids after the prayer.\""],[18078,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ conquered Khaybar, a banquet was prepared for him. He ate reclining, and he anointed himself. Then the sun struck him, so he put on the shade."],[18079,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “None of you should say, ‘I poured out the water,’ but let him say, ‘I urinate.’”"],[18080,"When the deceased was placed in his grave, the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “In the name of God, and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” And he placed a clod behind his neck, a clod between his shoulders, one between his knees, and another behind him."],[18081,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “You should eat gourd, for it increases the brain. And you should eat lentils, for they were declared holy on the tongue of seventy prophets.”"],[18082,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Lesbianism among women is fornication between them.”"],[18083,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ who was bald, cross-eyed, short-necked, bow-legged, sunken-eyed, left-handed, knock-kneed, and wide-legged. He said: “O Messenger of God, tell me what God has obligated upon me.” When he told him, he said: “I pledge to God that I will not add to His obligation.” He said: “Why?” He said: “Because He created me bald, cross-eyed, sunken-eyed, left-handed, knock-kneed, and wide-legged.” Then he turned away. Gabriel ﷺ came to him and said: “O Muhammad, where is the one who remonstrated with his Lord? He remonstrated with a Generous Lord, and He satisfied him.” He said: “Tell him: Would you not be pleased to be resurrected in the form of Gabriel on the Day of Resurrection?” So the Prophet ﷺ sent for the man and said: “You remonstrated with a Generous Lord, and He satisfied you. Would you not be pleased that God resurrects you on the Day of Resurrection in the form of Gabriel?” He said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “Then I pledge to God that my body will not have strength for anything that pleases God except that I will bear it.”"],[18084,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ began the prayer, he would say: “Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise. Blessed is Your name, exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god other than You.”"],[18085,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever does not pass water between his fingers, God will pass fire between them on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[18086,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever sells a defect without disclosing it remains in God’s displeasure,” or he said: “the angels continue to curse him.”"],[18087,"“Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ without any delusion, addition, or forgetfulness.” He said: “Did any of you recite anything from the Qur’an tonight?” We said: “Yes, but we are not very good at preserving it. We add the wāw and the alif and we omit.” He said: “This Qur’an is written among you, and you do not spare effort in preserving it, yet you claim that you add and omit. How then with hadiths we heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, which perhaps we heard from him only once? It is sufficient for you if we narrate to you the hadith according to its meaning.”"],[18088,"About the incident when they insulted me in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ : Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn came on a certain day. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw his garment over them and said, \"O Allah, these are the people of my household. O Allah, remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, and am I included?\" He said, \"By Allah, indeed you are included. This is the most trustworthy act in myself.\""],[18089,"Fatimah: “Go to the Messenger of God ﷺ and invite him to come.” The Messenger of God ﷺ came, and the two of them entered, and I entered with them. The Messenger of God ﷺ called Hasan and Husayn and seated each of them on his thigh, and he drew Fatimah close to his lap. Then he wrapped his garment over them while I was leaning. Then he said: {God only desires to remove impurity from you, O People of the House, and to purify you thoroughly.} Then he said: “These are my family, these are my family, most deserving.” Wathila said: I said, “O Messenger of God, and I, am I from your family?” He said: “And you are from my family.” Wathila said: “And that is among the most hopeful things I hope for.”"],[18090,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God chose the Banu Kinanah from the descendants of Ishmael, and He chose Quraysh from Kinanah, and He chose the Banu Hashim from Quraysh, and He chose me from the Banu Hashim.”"],[18091,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, I have committed a hadd offense, so enforce the punishment on me.\" He turned away from him twice. Then the prayer was established, and when he had said the salam, the man said, \"O Messenger of God, I have committed a hadd offense, so enforce the punishment on me.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"Did you perform ablution when you came?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"And you prayed with us?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then go, for God has pardoned you.\""],[18092,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"One of the greatest falsehoods is to claim that one has seen something when they haven't, to falsely attribute something to someone other than their father, or to say that they heard something when they didn't.\""],[18093,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever seeks knowledge and attains it, God writes for him a double portion of reward; and whoever seeks knowledge and does not attain it, God writes for him a single portion of reward.\""],[18094,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"You claim that I am the last of you to die and the first of you to depart. Then you will come after me in bands, killing one another.\""],[18095,"I heard Wathilah b. al-Asqaʿ say: The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and said, \"You claim that I am among the last of you to die and that I am among the first of you to die. Then you will follow me in bands, striking one another's necks.\""],[18096,"I was among the people of the Ṣuffah, and I saw that not one of us had a complete garment, and sweat had affected our skins with a film of dust and dirt. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us to give glad tidings to the poor of the Muhājirūn. A man with a fine appearance approached, and the Prophet ﷺ would not utter a word except that the man felt compelled to bring words that overpowered the Prophet's ﷺ speech. When he left, he said, \"God does not love this man and his voice—they twist their tongues with people as a cow twists its tongue with pasture. Likewise, God will twist their tongues and their faces in the Fire.\""],[18097,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said, \"Among the worst of fabrications is that someone attributes to me what I did not say, or claims his eyes saw in a dream what they did not see, or claims descent from someone other than his father.\""],[18098,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Among the worst of fabrications is that someone attributes to me what I did not say, or claims descent from someone other than his father, or claims his eyes saw in a dream what they did not see.\""],[18099,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The gravest fabrication in the sight of God is that someone says about me what I did not say, or claims affiliation with someone other than his patrons, or claims his eyes saw in a dream what they did not see.\""],[18100,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The worst fabrication is that someone falsely attributes to me what I did not say, or claims his eyes saw what they did not see, or claims descent from someone other than his father.\""],[18101,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Among the gravest fabrications is that a man claims descent from someone other than his father, or claims his eyes saw in a dream what they did not see, or says about God and His Messenger what they did not say.\""],[18102,"that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, the greatest of fabrications is that one should say about me what I did not say, or that a man should claim paternity of another than his father, or that he should show his eyes in a dream what they did not see.”"],[18103,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the greatest of fabrications is that one should say about a man what I did not say, or claim descent from other than his father, or show his eyes in a dream what they did not see.”"],[18104,"I entered with Abu Salamah al-Himsi upon him, and he narrated to me from Abdul Wahid al-Nasri, from Wathilah b. al-Asqa', from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: “A woman acquires three inheritances: her freed slave, her foundling, and the child who has no defect.”"],[18105,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A Muslim’s blood, honor, and wealth are inviolable to another Muslim. A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim; he does not wrong him nor forsake him. Piety is here”—and he pointed with his hand to his heart—“and it is sufficient evil for a man to belittle his Muslim brother.”"],[18106,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Whoever establishes a good practice will have its reward as long as it is acted upon during his life and after his death, until it is abandoned. And whoever establishes an evil practice will bear its sin until it is abandoned. And whoever dies on guard in the path of Allah, the reward of the guard will continue for him until he is resurrected on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[18107,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “The scriptures of Ibrahim were sent down on the first night of Ramadan, the Torah was sent down on the sixth of Ramadan, the Gospel was sent down on the thirteenth of Ramadan, the Psalms were sent down on the eighteenth of Ramadan, and the Qur’an was sent down on the fourteenth of Ramadan.”"],[18108,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was given the seven long surahs in place of the Torah, I was given the Mathani in place of the Psalms, and I was favored with the Mufassal.”"],[18109,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was given the seven long surahs in place of the Torah, I was given the Mathani in place of the Gospel, I was given the Mi’in in place of the Psalms, and you were favored with the Mufassal.”"],[18110,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There will certainly enter Paradise through the intercession of a man from my nation more than the Banu Tamim.”"],[18111,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I have been commanded to use the siwak so persistently that I feared it would be made obligatory upon me.”"],[18112,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I have been commanded to use the siwak so persistently that I indeed feared it would be made obligatory upon me.”"],[18113,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came to him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a punishment from the punishments of Allah, so carry out Allah’s punishment on me.” He turned away from him. Then he came to him a second time, and he turned away from him. Then he came to him a third time, and he turned away from him. Then the prayer was established, and when the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer, the man said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a punishment from the punishments of Allah, so carry out Allah’s punishment on me.” He said: “Did you not perform ablution and do it well, and purify yourself and do it well, and pray with us just now?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Go, for it is your expiation.”"],[18114,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a Bedouin entered and said, “O God, have mercy on me and Muhammad, and do not have mercy on anyone else along with us.” They said to him, “Woe to you! You have restricted something vast.” Then the Bedouin moved aside and urinated standing up, and they rushed toward him. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Leave him until he finishes his urine.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ called for a bucket of water and poured it over his urine."],[18115,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “O God, have mercy on us and forgive us,” and he forbade us to pray toward graves or sit on them."],[18116,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The Hour will not come until there are ten signs: a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula, the Dajjal, the descent of Jesus son of Mary, Gog and Magog, the Beast, the rising of the sun from its west, and a fire that emerges from Ta’izz of Aden, driving people to the gathering place, gathering even the small ants and the ants.”"],[18117,"From Abu al-Darda’, Wathilah b. al-Asqa’, Abu Umamah, and Anas b. Malik, they said: We were in a gathering with some Jews, discussing predestination, when the Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us angry. He frowned, rebuked, and scowled, then said, “Stop! Fear God, O community of Muhammad. Two deep valleys, dark and bottomless, the blaze of the Fire will not overwhelm you.” Then he ordered the Jews to get up. Then he stood and spread out his right hand and spread out his left fingers, then said, “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is a book from God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, with the names of the people of Paradise and the names of their fathers, mothers, and clans. Your Lord has finished. Your Lord has finished. Your Lord has finished. I have warned and I have conveyed. O God, I have indeed conveyed.”"],[18118,"When I embraced Islam, I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said to me, “Go and wash with water and lote leaves, and remove the hair of disbelief from yourself.”"],[18119,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say to a wife who was under him, “You must have tranquility and dignity.”"],[18120,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The child belongs to the bed, and the fornicator gets the stone. A woman is not allowed to dispose of any of her wealth except with her husband’s permission.”"],[18121,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The best of your youth are those who imitate your elders, and the worst of your elders are those who imitate your youth.”"],[18122,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The imam is a guarantor, and the muezzin is entrusted. O God, forgive the muezzins and guide the imams.”"],[18123,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"There is no Muslim who is put in charge of any affair of the Muslims except that God sends to him two angels who keep him upright as long as he adheres to the truth. But when he intends deliberate injustice, He leaves him to his own self.\""],[18124,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed effeminate men and masculine women, and he said: \"Expel them from your houses.\" So the Prophet ﷺ expelled the Ethiopians, and Umar expelled so-and-so."],[18125,"I heard Wathilah b. al-Asqa' say: I was one of the People of the Suffah. My companions complained of hunger and said: \"O Wathilah, go to the Messenger of God ﷺ and ask him for food for us.\" So I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, my companions are complaining of hunger.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O A'ishah, do you have anything?\" She said: \"O Messenger of God, I have nothing but crumbs of bread.\" He said: \"Bring it.\" She came with a leather sack, and the Messenger of God called for a large dish. He emptied the bread into the dish, then began to fix the tharid with his own hands while it swelled until the dish was full. Then he said: \"O Wathilah, go and bring ten of your companions, and you will be their tenth.\" So I went and brought ten of my companions, and I was their tenth. He said: \"Sit down and take; in the name of God; take from its sides and do not take from its top, for the blessing descends from its top.\" They ate until they were full, then they stood up, and in the dish was the same amount as had been in it. Then he began to fix it with his hand while it swelled until it was full. Then he said: \"O Wathilah, go and bring ten of your companions.\" So I brought ten, and he said: \"Sit down.\" They sat and ate until they were full, then they stood up. Then he said: \"Go and bring ten of your companions.\" So I went and brought ten, and they did the same. Then he said: \"Is there anyone left?\" I said: \"Yes, ten.\" He said: \"Go and bring them.\" So I went and brought them, and he said: \"Sit down.\" They sat and ate until they were full, then they stood up, and there remained in the dish the same amount as before. Then he said: \"O Wathilah, take this to A'ishah.\""],[18126,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God ﷻ said: \"I am as My servant thinks of Me; whether he thinks good or thinks evil.\""],[18127,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: God ﷻ said: \"I am as My servant thinks of Me, so let him think of Me as he wishes.\""],[18128,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever builds a mosque for God in which prayers are performed, God will build for him a house in Paradise better than it.\""],[18129,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say in his funeral prayer over a Muslim man: \"O God, so-and-so is in Your protection and under the rope of Your shelter, so protect him from the trial of the grave and the punishment of the Fire, for You are worthy of faithfulness and truth. O God, forgive him and have mercy on him, for You are the Forgiving, the Merciful.\""],[18130,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"It is not lawful for anyone to sell something without making clear what is in it.\""],[18131,"We came to Wathilah bin Al-Asqa'ah, companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and we asked him to narrate to us a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that doesn't have any additions or subtractions. He became angry and said, \"One of you may recite from his Mushaf that is hanging in his house and he may increase or decrease from it.\" So we said, \"We only intended for you to narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ without any intermediary.\" He said, \"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding a companion of ours who had become mandatory (to free). So he said, 'Free him, for Allah will free every part of him from the Fire for every part of him that exists.'\" This is how Ibn Ayyub Al-Alafi narrated to us from Mahdi bin Ja'far from Dhamrah from Al-Awza'i from Ibrahim bin Abi 'Abalah from the original source of his book."],[18132,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk. Some people from Banu Sulaym came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, a companion of ours has made hellfire obligatory for himself (i.e., committed a deadly sin).\" He said, \"Let a slave be freed on his behalf. By every limb of it, Allah will ransom a limb of him from the Fire.\""],[18133,"A group from Banu Sulaym came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"A companion of ours has made hellfire obligatory for himself.\" He said, \"Let a slave be freed on his behalf. By every limb of it, Allah will ransom a limb of him from the Fire.\""],[18134,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about a man who has made hellfire obligatory for himself?\" meaning the Fire. He said, \"He should free a slave. Every limb of it will ransom a limb of him from the Fire.\""],[18135,"A child of al-Rayyan died, and Wathila attended it. When they left the cemetery, Wathila sat at the gate of Damascus. Al-Rayyan passed by him, and Wathila said to him: O Abu Sa'id, may Allah mend your misfortune and forgive your deceased one. He said: Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever buries three of his children, Allah will forbid the Fire to him.'"],[18136,"My father, when he prayed the morning prayer, would sit facing the qiblah and not speak until the sun rose. Perhaps I would speak to him about some need, and he would not answer me. I said: What is this? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever prays the morning prayer, then recites \"Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad\" one hundred times before speaking, then every time he recites \"Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad,\" a year's sins are forgiven for him.'"],[18137,"He used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays and say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast them and say: 'Deeds are presented to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, on these two days.'"],[18138,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Gold and silk are lawful for the females of my community and forbidden for the males of my community.'"],[18139,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves his people—is he a zealot? He said: 'No.' I said: Who is the zealot? He said: 'The one who helps his people in wrongdoing.'"],[18140,"She heard her father say: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is tribalism? He said: 'That you help your people in wrongdoing.'"],[18141,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Among the greatest of major sins is for a man to attribute to me what I did not say.'"],[18142,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'Among the greatest of major sins is for a man to deny his child.'"],[18143,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform the Asr prayer with two units of prayer on the flat ground."],[18144,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed at al-Abtah with a short spear or something like a short spear in front of him, and the road and passersby were behind it."],[18145,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed toward the short spear, and the road was behind it."],[18146,"When Ja'far came to the Messenger of God ﷺ from the land of Abyssinia, the Messenger of God ﷺ kissed him between his eyes, then said: \"I do not know whether I am happier at Ja'far's arrival or at the conquest of Khaybar.\""],[18147,"Bilal used to call the adhan for the Messenger of God ﷺ in two tones, two tones."],[18148,"Bilal called the adhan for the Messenger of God ﷺ at Mina in pairs, pairs, and he called the iqamah in pairs, pairs."],[18149,"We came to the Messenger of God ﷺ when the prayer was due, and Bilal stood up and called the adhan, placing his fingers in his ears and turning around. The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought water for ablution, and he performed ablution along with his companions, and some water remained, so we began to rush for the leftover water. Then he brought out a spear and planted it, and he commenced the prayer, then prayed Zuhr two rak'ahs and Asr two rak'ahs. Then he said, \"When I arrive in Madinah, come to me.\" The Prophet ﷺ had allotted something for us to give us, and Abu Bakr ؓ handed it over to us."],[18150,"I saw Bilal calling the adhan and turning around, and I was following his mouth this way and that way, with his two fingers in his ears. He said: And the Messenger of God ﷺ was in a red dome of his. He said: So Bilal came out in front of him with the spear and planted it in al-Abtah, and the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed Zuhr and Asr facing it, while dogs, donkeys, and women passed in front of him. He was wearing a red suit of his, and it is as if I am looking at the shine of his calves."],[18151,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ at al-Abtah, and Bilal came out and called the adhan, and it is as if I am looking at him, and I was following his mouth this way and that way, meaning right and left. He brought out the leftover water of his ablution, and it was between one who obtained some and one who sprinkled it. Then he planted a spear, and he came out wearing a red suit, and it is as if I am looking at the shine of his calves. Then he prayed Zuhr and Asr, two rak'ahs each, until he returned."],[18152,"Bilal brought out the leftover water of the Prophet's ﷺ ablution, and the people took from it, some obtaining and some sprinkling, until a boy would insert his hand under the people's armpits and it would drip."],[18153,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina two rak'ahs, and he continued praying two rak'ahs until he returned to Madinah."],[18154,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"I do not eat while reclining.\""],[18155,"Bilal came out and planted a spear, and the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed facing it while donkeys and dogs passed in front of him, and he brought out the leftover water of the Messenger of God's ﷺ ablution. Al-Humaydi added in his narration: and women."],[18156,"I handed over to the Prophet ﷺ at al-Abtah in a dome. Bilal came out and called the prayer, then Bilal went in and brought out the spear. The Prophet ﷺ came out, fixed the spear in the ground, and led the prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us while a donkey and a woman passed in front of him."],[18157,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Abu Bakr and Umar are the masters of the middle-aged men of Paradise, from the earlier and later generations, except for the prophets and messengers.”"],[18158,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed at al-Batha with a spear in front of him, and a dog, a donkey, and a woman passed beyond it."],[18159,"Bilal called the adhan for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Batha, putting his fingers in his ears and turning around."],[18160,"When Bilal called the adhan, he would put his fingers in his ears and turn around during his adhan."],[18161,"“I saw Bilal call the adhan, and I followed his mouth here and here.” Sufyan turned right and left. Yahya said: Sufyan said: Hajjaj used to mention it from Awn that he said: “and he turned around in his adhan,” but when we met Awn, he did not mention turning around in it."],[18162,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ place his nose on the ground just as he placed his forehead."],[18163,"The Prophet ﷺ averted the legal punishment from a woman who had been coerced."],[18164,"We came to the Prophet ﷺ at al-Abtah in a red dome of his. He said, “Who are you?” We said, “Banu Amir.” He said, “Welcome! You are from me.”"],[18165,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ along with a man from Banu Amir. He said, “Who are you?” We said, “From Banu Amir.” He said, “Welcome to you! You are from me.”"],[18166,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at al-Abtah in a red dome with a group from Banu Amir. He said to us, “Which tribe are you from?” We said, “From Banu Amir.” He said, “Then I am from you.” Then Bilal came out, placed water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to purify himself, then called the adhan, putting his fingers in his ears and turning around during his adhan. He fixed a spear for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he prayed facing it. He prayed Zuhr as two rak‘ahs and Asr as two rak‘ahs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, “Come to me in Madinah,” and promised us some barley. We came to Madinah and found that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had died, so we came to Abu Bakr and asked him to fulfill what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had promised us."],[18167,"On the day of departing Mina, we camped at al-Abtah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Bilal, and he called the prayer. Then he brought out the water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ’s ablution, and the people rushed to it, some getting some and some sprinkling. Then he brought out a spear and fixed it between him and the road."],[18168,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey where they slept until the sun rose. He said, \"Indeed, you were dead and Allah has revived your souls. So whoever slept and missed the prayer, let him pray it when he wakes up, and whoever forgot a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers.\""],[18169,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “When one of you rises from his sleep, let him say: Praise be to God who restored to us our souls after when we were dead.”"],[18170,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The world will be opened to you until you decorate your houses as the Kaaba is decorated.” We said, “And we upon our religion?” He said, “Yes, but you today are better than on that day.” We said, “On that day?” He said, “Rather, you today are better.”"],[18171,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ pray on the Day of Sacrifice. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “It does not suffice for anyone.” He said, “But we have a jadha‘ah.” He said, “It suffices for you and does not suffice for anyone after you.”"],[18172,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the price of blood, the dowry of a prostitute, and the price of a dog.”"],[18173,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the price of blood, the wage of a cupper, and the earnings of a prostitute.”"],[18174,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey when he heard someone saying: “God is greatest, God is greatest.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “A call of truth.” Then he said, “I bear witness that there is no god but God.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “The word of sincerity.” Then he said, “I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Its speaker has come out of the Fire.” Then the Prophet ﷺ said, “You will find this man is an owner of goats or an owner of dogs that he hunts with.”"],[18175,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent a collector of alms, and he used to take from the rich and give to the poor. Ibn Abi Za’idah said in his hadith: “I was an orphan boy, and he gave me a young she-camel from it.”"],[18176,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ sent among us a collector of alms, and he took the alms from our rich and put it among our poor. I was an orphan boy with no property, and he gave me a young she-camel from it.”"],[18177,"I performed Hajj with the Messenger of God ﷺ while I was a boy. While we were encamped at Mina, someone said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ has departed.” I hastened to my mount, spurred it on, and rode toward him until we reached al-Baṭḥā’. There was a small group of people and a tent pitched. Bilal came out to us with ablution water and a short spear, then he gave the call to prayer. The Messenger of God ﷺ came out, performed ablution, and left some leftover water. The people began taking from it and wiping their faces and heads. He turned, and I did the same as they did. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed with the short spear in front of him while the people were coming and going.”"],[18178,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said, “Whoever sees me in a dream, it is as if he has seen me while awake, for Satan is not able to take my form.”"],[18179,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Al-Bathaa, and Bilal called for the prayer. The Prophet ﷺ came out of his dome made of udm (a type of fabric) and sat in its courtyard. Then he was brought some water for purification, and he performed ablution. After that, the people rushed to receive the blessings of his remaining water from his drinking and ablution. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a female goat, and it was tethered in front of him, and he prayed with the people. Indeed, infants, women, sheep, and camels passed in front of him.\""],[18180,"I saw Bilal come out at midday with a short spear and plant it in the ground. Then he stood to give the call to prayer, placed his fingers in his ears, and turned his head this way and that, right and left, until he finished his adhan. Then he entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and brought out a small amount of water. Some took it and some were sprinkled with it. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came out wearing a red cloak, and it is as if I can still see the whiteness of his shins beneath it. He prayed toward the spear while women on camel litters passed in front of him. The wording is that of the hadith of Abu Bilal."],[18181,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the one who consumes riba and the one who pays it."],[18182,"A short spear was planted for the Prophet ﷺ in the open ground, and he prayed toward it."],[18183,"He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at al-Batha, and a short spear was planted in front of him. He prayed Zuhr as two rak'ahs and 'Asr as two rak'ahs, and the donkey and the woman passed from behind the spear. The wording is that of the hadith of Sulayman b. Harb."],[18184,"The Prophet ﷺ went out at midday to al-Batha, performed ablution, and prayed Zuhr as two rak'ahs and 'Asr as two rak'ahs, with a short spear in front of him. Shu'bah said: 'Awn added from Abu Juhaifah: \"A donkey and a woman passed from behind it.\" Then the people stood up and began taking his hand and wiping their faces with it. I took his hand and placed it on my face, and it was cooler than snow and more fragrant than musk."],[18185,"A woman came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a black slave girl. The woman said, \"O Messenger of God, I owe a believing slave. Will this one suffice for me?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, \"Where is God?\" She said, \"In the heaven.\" He said, \"Who am I?\" She said, \"You are His Messenger.\" He said, \"Do you testify that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Do you believe in what has come from God?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Free her, for she is a believer.\""],[18186,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"He cursed the one who consumes ribā, the female tattooer, and the image-maker.\""],[18187,"\"We had a slave boy who was a cupper, so the Prophet ﷺ forbade us from eating anything from his earnings.\""],[18188,"\"We halted with the Prophet of Allah ﷺ at al-Abṭaḥ. Bilāl called the adhān for the Ẓuhr prayer, then came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and entered upon him in a tent, bringing with him a small vessel of water made of tanned leather. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ performed ablution, and some water remained in it. Then he came out, and I saw us rushing for it. Then Bilāl took a short spear and planted it in the ground. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ came out and led us in two rakʿahs, and I saw a woman and a dog passing in front of us while we were praying.\""],[18189,"Bilāl went out at noon and called the adhān. Then he entered and came out with a small vessel containing the leftover water from the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, holding it in his hand. Had he placed it on the ground, people would have broken it. They began taking some of it—one getting some of it and another sprinkling water from it onto himself—then he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth."],[18190,"\"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Abṭaḥ. I said, 'I will certainly observe how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prays today.' Bilāl went out, then entered and came out with the leftover water from the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. People rushed to it, some taking from it and others being sprinkled. Then he went in and brought out a short spear and planted it in the ground. Then the Prophet ﷺ came out wearing a red ḥulla, as if I were looking at the whiteness of his shins from behind it. Bilāl called the iqāma, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stepped forward while we lined up behind him. He led us in prayer while a donkey, a woman, and a dog were in front of him.\""],[18191,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out as a traveler and continued praying two rakʿahs until he returned.\""],[18192,"\"I prayed Ẓuhr with the Prophet ﷺ at Minā as two rakʿahs.\" Al-Ḥaḍramī said: \"This is a mistake; it is actually Wakīʿ from Sufyān and Ibn Abī Laylā.\""],[18193,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ in a red leather tent. Bilāl brought out the leftover water of his ablution, and people rushed to it—some took some of it and some did not. Then Bilāl brought out a short spear and planted it in the ground. The Prophet ﷺ came out and prayed facing it, while people and animals passed in front of him.\""],[18194,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at al-Abtah two rak'ahs, the 'Asr prayer."],[18195,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Abtah pray the 'Asr prayer as two rak'ahs."],[18196,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray 'Asr at al-Abtah as two rak'ahs, and he placed in front of him a spear between him and the passers-by on the road."],[18197,"From Abu Juḥayfah ؓ : The Prophet ﷺ commanded at Mina, so he fixed a spear and prayed facing it."],[18198,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with this white from him — and he pointed to his 'anfaqah (hair between lower lip and chin). 'Amr b. Khalid added in his narration: It was said to him, 'What were you like that day?' He said, 'I was shaving arrows and fletching them.'"],[18199,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with white hair in his 'anfaqah, below his lower lip."],[18200,"They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you have become grey-haired.\" He replied, \"Hud and its sisters have made me grey-haired.\""],[18201,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting one day with people in front of him saying something he disliked — their talk and clamor. It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, will you not forbid them?' He said, 'If I forbade them al-Hajun, one of them would almost go there though he had no need.'"],[18202,"I heard Abu Juḥayfah say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out in the midday heat. He was brought water for ablution and performed ablution. The people began taking some of the leftover water from his ablution and wiping themselves with it. Then he prayed Zuhr as two rak'ahs and 'Asr as two rak'ahs, with a spear in front of him.' This is the wording of the hadith of 'Asim b. 'Ali, and the others are similar."],[18203,"The Prophet ﷺ stopped at al-Abtah, and I went out among those looking at him. I saw that he had been brought water for ablution, so he performed ablution, then fixed a spear and prayed two rak'ahs with his companions when the sun had passed its zenith."],[18204,"They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, set prices for us.' He said, 'Indeed Allah is the One who sets prices, withholds, and gives generously. I hope to meet Allah while none of you has a claim against me for injustice in honor or wealth.'"],[18205,"Yazid Abu Khalid al-Baysari narrated to us: Abu Malik informed us: Salamah b. Kuhayl informed me from Abu Juḥayfah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Sit with the scholars, ask the elders, and mix with the wise.'"],[18206,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Sit with the elders, ask the scholars, and mix with the wise.'"],[18207,"I belched in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"What did you eat, O Abu Juhaifa?\" I said, \"Bread and meat.\" He said, \"The people who will hunger longest on the Day of Resurrection are those who were most satiated in this world.\""],[18208,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a white complexion and his hair was straight.\""],[18209,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he wrote for us an order for twelve young she-camels. When he passed away, the people withheld it from us until they assembled."],[18210,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, white-haired and graying, and al-Hasan b. Ali resembled him. He ordered for us twelve young she-camels, so we went to collect them, but his death came to us, and they gave us nothing. When Abu Bakr stood up, he said, 'Whoever has a promise owed by the Messenger of God ﷺ, let him come forward.' I informed him, and he ordered them for us."],[18211,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, and al-Hasan b. Ali resembled him."],[18212,"I said to Abu Juhaifa, 'Did you see the Prophet ﷺ?' He said, 'Yes, and al-Hasan resembled him.'"],[18213,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, and al-Hasan resembled him."],[18214,"I walked with Abu Juhaifa to the Friday prayer, and I said, 'Did you see the Messenger of God ﷺ?' He said, 'Yes, and al-Hasan b. Ali was made to resemble him.'"],[18215,"From Wahb Abu Juhaifa: I said, 'Did you see the Prophet ﷺ?' He said, 'Yes, and al-Hasan b. Ali resembled him.'"],[18216,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"There is no male slave or female slave who neglects to walk in the service of his Muslim brother except that he walks the like of it in the displeasure of God ﷻ; and he does not neglect to spend an expenditure in the way of God except that he spends multiplied multiples in the displeasure of God; and he does not abandon the Hajj for some worldly purpose except that he sees those left behind before he fulfills that need.\""],[18217,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ when a garment was brought from the fuller—or being taken to the fuller—with 'Satan' written on it. He ordered it to be erased, and he said, \"I seek refuge in God from Satan.\" Ubayd b. Ya'ish raised it [as a Prophetic hadith], while others left it as the statement of a Companion."],[18218,"Members of a household follow one another into the Fire until none of them remains, neither free man, slave, nor slave woman; and members of a household follow one another into Paradise until none of them remains, neither free man, slave, nor slave woman."],[18219,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I do not eat reclining.”"],[18220,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “I do not eat reclining.”"],[18221,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I do not eat reclining.”"],[18222,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I do not eat reclining.”"],[18223,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I do not eat reclining.”"],[18224,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I do not eat reclining.”"],[18225,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “As for me, I do not eat reclining.”"],[18226,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I do not eat reclining.”"],[18227,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I do not eat reclining.”"],[18228,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I do not eat reclining.”"],[18229,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to a man who was with him, “I do not eat reclining.”"],[18230,"I ate a tharīdah of wheat bread with fat meat, then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and began to belch. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Restrain your belching, for the people who are most satiated in this world will be the most hungry on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[18231,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray until his ankles would swell. It was said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, Allah has forgiven you for what you have done in the past and what you will do in the future.\" He replied, \"Shall I not be a grateful servant?\""],[18232,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man who had let his lower garment hang down in prayer, so he gathered it up for him."],[18233,"“Sit with the elders, mix with the wise, and ask the scholars.”"],[18234,"We mentioned noble ancestors in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. One of them said, “My grandfather was renowned for horses,” another said, “My grandfather was renowned for camels,” and another said, “My grandfather was renowned for sheep.” Then the prayer time came, and the Prophet ﷺ led them in prayer. When he raised his head from bowing, he said, “God hears the one who praises Him. Our Lord, to You belongs all praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever else You will after that. There is none to withhold what You give, none to give what You withhold, and none to avert what You decree. No possessor of good fortune can benefit from his fortune before You.”"],[18235,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ complaining about his neighbor. He said, “Put your goods out on the road.” So he put them out, and people began to pass by him and curse him. He then came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, what I have met from the people!” He said, “And what did you meet from them?” He said, “They curse me.” He said, “God cursed you before the people did.” He said, “I will not do it again.” Then the one who had complained about him came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to him, “Take up your goods, for you have been sufficed.”"],[18236,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “An ʿumrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj.”"],[18237,"I accompanied ʿAli from Madinah to Makkah and saw some things from him that I disliked. I said, “If I return to the Messenger of God, I will surely complain about you to him.” When I arrived, I met the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “I saw such-and-such from ʿAli.” He said, “Do not say this, for he is the most entitled of people to you after me.”"],[18238,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Your brother the Najashi has died, so stand up and pray for him.” A man said, “O Messenger of God, how can we pray for him when he died in his disbelief?” He said, “Do you not hear the words of God, Mighty and Majestic: ‘And indeed among the People of the Book are those who believe in God and in what has been sent down to you and in what was sent down to them’ to the end of the verse?”"],[18239,"When God granted the Prophet ﷺ Ṣafiyyah as a captive, he said to his companions, “What do you say about this slave woman?” They said, “They say that you are the most entitled of people to her and the most deserving.” He said, “I have freed her and married her, and I have made her emancipation her dowry.” A man said, “O Messenger of God, what about the wedding feast?” He said, “The wedding feast is a right, the second is a courtesy, and the third is ostentation and sin.”"],[18240,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken on the Night Journey, he heard a rustling sound in Paradise and said, \"O Jibril, what is this rustling?\" He said, \"This is Bilal.\" Abu Bakr said, \"If only Bilal's mother had given birth to me, and Abu Bilal, and I were like Bilal.\""],[18241,"The Prophet ﷺ went out at night to relieve himself and left the door of the house open. When he returned, he found Iblis standing in the middle of the house. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Begone, O wicked one, from my house!\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When you go out of your houses at night, close their doors.\""],[18242,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Knowledge is about to be snatched away from people until you will not be able to attain any of it.\" Ziyad b. Labid said, \"How will knowledge be snatched away from us when we have recited the Qur'an and taught it to our children?\" He said, \"May your mother be bereaved of you, O Ibn Labid! This Torah and Gospel are in the hands of the Jews and Christians, yet they do not raise their heads with them.\""],[18243,"He was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man passed by while another man was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I love him for the sake of Allah.\" He said, \"Have you told him that?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Get up and tell him.\""],[18244,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Perhaps after me you will conquer great cities and set up gatherings in their markets. When that happens, return the greeting, lower your gaze, guide the blind, and help the oppressed.\""],[18245,"The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we eat but do not feel full.\" He said, \"Perhaps you eat separately.\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Gather together over your food and mention the name of Allah over it, and it will be blessed for you.\""],[18246,"When I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after the killing of Hamzah, he spat in my face three times, then said, \"Do not let me see your face.\""],[18247,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to me, \"Wahshi?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Did you kill Hamzah?\" I said, \"Yes, and praise be to Allah who honored him at my hands and did not disgrace me at his hands.\" Quraysh said to him, \"Will you love him when he is the killer of Hamzah?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, ask forgiveness for me.\" He spat on the ground three times and pushed my chest three times, then said, \"O Wahshi, go out and fight in the way of Allah as you fought to obstruct the way of Allah.\""],[18248,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man praying alone in the row, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18249,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man praying alone behind the rows, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18250,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed while a man was praying alone behind the rows, so he ordered him to repeat his prayer."],[18251,"A man prayed alone behind the row, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18252,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying alone behind the people, so he ordered him and he repeated the prayer."],[18253,"A man prayed alone behind the rows, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to repeat it."],[18254,"A man prayed alone behind the rows, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18255,"A man prayed behind the rows, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him and he repeated the prayer."],[18256,"He saw a man praying in a row behind the people, not praying with the rows, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18257,"A man prayed behind the rows, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer, and he repeated it."],[18258,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man praying alone in a row, so he ordered him and he repeated the prayer."],[18259,"A man prayed alone behind the rows, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18260,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who prays alone behind the row. He said: 'He should repeat it.'"],[18261,"A man prayed alone behind the rows, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him and he repeated it."],[18262,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying alone behind the row, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18263,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying alone behind the row, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18264,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying alone behind the row, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18265,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Do not use animals as pulpits.” And I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The worst of these beasts of prey is the fox.”"],[18266,"I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ in a row by myself, and when he finished he said: “Repeat the prayer.”"],[18267,"I prayed behind the row, so he ordered me and I repeated my prayer."],[18268,"A man prayed alone behind the row, so the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered him to repeat it."],[18269,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying alone behind the row, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18270,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left and there was a man praying alone behind the people. He said, \"O you who are praying alone, why don't you join them and enter with them, or bring someone to stand beside you if the place becomes tight for you? Repeat your prayer, for indeed, there is no prayer for you.\""],[18271,"A man prayed alone behind the row, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18272,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while I was praying behind the row by myself, so he ordered me to repeat the prayer."],[18273,"A man prayed alone behind the row, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18274,"I prayed in a row by myself behind the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he ordered me to repeat the prayer."],[18275,"I heard Wabisa b. Ma'bad say: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about everything, even about the dirt that is under the fingernails, and he said: “Leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt.”"],[18276,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ when he bowed in his prayer: if water had been poured on his back, it would have settled there."],[18277,"The Prophet ﷺ sent al-Walīd b. ʿUqba b. Abī Muʿayṭ to Banū al-Muṣṭaliq as a collector of zakāt."],[18278,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Some people from the people of Paradise will go to some people from the people of the Fire and say, \"Why did you enter the Fire? By Allah, we did not enter Paradise except because of what we learned from you.\" They will say, \"We used to say and not act.\"'"],[18279,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Makkah, the people of Makkah began bringing their children to him, and he would wipe their heads and supplicate for them. I was brought to him while I had been perfumed with khalūq, and he did not wipe my head, nor touch me, and nothing prevented him from that except that my mother had perfumed me with khalūq. So he did not touch me because of the khalūq."],[18284,"The Prophet ﷺ would turn away once to his right and once to his left."],[18285,"“I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ and I saw him turn away from both of his sides.” This is Muslim's wording, and Sulayman b. Harb said: “He would turn away to his right and to his left.”"],[18286,"“I was with the Prophet ﷺ one day, and he used to lead us in prayer, and he would turn away to his right and to his left, from both of his sides.”"],[18287,"The Prophet ﷺ would turn away when he had prayed, to his right and to his left, meaning the taslīm."],[18288,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would lead us in prayer and then turn away to his right and to his left."],[18289,"“The Prophet ﷺ would lead us and he would turn away on both of his sides.”"],[18290,"“The Prophet ﷺ would hold his left with his right in prayer.”"],[18291,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ stand to pray. He said: “I saw him when he placed one hand over the other, the right over the left.”"],[18292,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would place one of his hands over the other in prayer.”"],[18293,"“The Prophet ﷺ would lead us, and he would take his left with his right.”"],[18294,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, food that I do not leave except out of scrupulousness.” He said: “Let nothing creep into your chest that resembles Christianity.”"],[18295,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the food of the Christians. He said: “Let no food resemble Christianity in your chest.” He said: “And I saw him placing one of his hands over the other.”"],[18296,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came to him and said, \"There is food from which I refrain out of scruple; may I eat it?\" He said, \"Let not anything creep into your chest that resembles Christianity.\""],[18297,"I heard the Prophet of God ﷺ when a man asked him, saying, \"Among foods there is a food from which I refrain out of scruple.\" He said, \"Let not anything creep into your chest that resembles Christianity.\""],[18298,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, I leave food because of some purpose in my soul concerning it.\" He said, \"Let not anything creep into your soul or your chest that resembles Christianity.\""],[18299,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"We leave some food out of scruple from it.\" He said, \"Let not any food creep into your chest that resembles Christianity.\""],[18300,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the food of the Christians. He said, \"Let not any food creep into your chest that resembles Christianity.\""],[18301,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ that he was asked if there is any time during the day that prevents us from performing prayers. He answered, \"No, except during the rising and setting of the sun. For it rises between the two horns of Satan and sets between the two horns of Satan.\""],[18302,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"God will torture those who torture people in this world.\""],[18303,"Some people in Basra in the time of Ziyad used to take dirhams for dinars on credit. A man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Hisham b. 'Amir al-Ansari stood and said: 'Indeed, the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade selling gold for silver on credit, and he informed us that that is riba.'"],[18304,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever is afflicted by bloodshed or injury, he is between one of three options. If he desires a fourth, then restrain him: between exacting retaliation, pardoning, or taking the blood money. If he takes one and then transgresses after that, for him is the Fire, abiding eternally therein forever."],[18305,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The most insolent of people against God is a man who kills someone other than his killer, or seeks revenge for a blood of the pre-Islamic era among the people of Islam, and one who makes his eyes see in sleep what they did not see.\""],[18306,"Abu Shuraih b. 'Amr al-Khuza'i—who was among the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ—informed him that on the day of the conquest, Banu Ka'b encountered a man from Hudhayl whom they were seeking for a blood feud from the pre-Islamic era. He was in the sacred precinct, heading toward the Messenger of God ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him upon Islam, but they killed him. When the news of his killing reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, he became angrier than he had ever been. Banu Ka'b went to Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ seeking their intercession with the Prophet ﷺ. When evening came, he stood before the people, praised God as He deserves, then said: To proceed: God made Makkah sacred, and people did not make it sacred. God made it permissible for me only for an hour of the day yesterday, then it became sacred as God made it sacred. The most hostile of people against God are three: a man who kills within it, a man who kills someone other than his killer for a pre-Islamic blood feud, and by God, I will certainly pay the blood money for this man whom you killed. Abu Shuraih said: So the Messenger of God ﷺ paid his blood money."],[18307,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Drink in moderation, and do not get intoxicated.\""],[18308,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon on a red she-camel.”"],[18309,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever lets his garment drag out of pride, he will be dragged into the Fire,” meaning his lower garment."],[18310,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to my people of Aslam and said: “Command your people to fast this day, the day of Ashura. Whoever among them you find has already eaten in the first part of his day, let him fast the rest of it.”"],[18311,"Ali prayed on the Day of Siffin over Ammar b. Yasir and Hashim b. Utbah. Ammar was the nearer of the two to Ali, and Hashim was the nearer of the two to the qiblah."],[18312,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, do we initiate deeds, or has the decree already been decided?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God took the progeny of Adam from his back, then made them testify concerning themselves, then He spread them out in a scale-pan and said, 'These are in the Garden and these are in the Fire.' The people of the Garden are facilitated for the deeds of the people of the Garden, and the people of the Fire are facilitated for the deeds of the people of the Fire.\""],[18313,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, do we initiate deeds, or has the decree already been decided?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God took the progeny of Adam from his back, then made them testify concerning themselves: 'Am I not your Lord?' They said, 'Yes.' Then He spread them out in a scale-pan and said, 'These are in the Garden and these are in the Fire.' As for the people of the Garden, they are facilitated for the deeds of the people of the Garden, and as for the people of the Fire, they are facilitated for the deeds of the people of the Fire.\""],[18314,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"The one who tortures people in this world, God will torture him in the Hereafter.\" So Umayr released them and left them."],[18315,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"God will torture on the Day of Resurrection those who torture people in this world.\""],[18316,"One of the two said to the agent, \"What is this, O so-and-so? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'God will torture those who torture people in this world.'\""],[18317,"that he came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"What is your name?\" He replied: \"Shihāb.\" He said: \"Rather, you are Hishām.\""],[18318,"\"Indeed we do it.\""],[18319,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Dig graves, make them wide, make them good, and bury two or three in a single grave, and put forward the one who knows the most Qur'an.\" My father was the third of three, and he was the one who knew the most Qur'an, so he was put forward."],[18320,"The wounds were severe on the day of Uhud, so they complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ about the wounds. He said: \"Dig graves, make them wide, make them good, and bury two or three in the grave, and put forward the one who knows the most Qur'an.\" So they put my father forward in front of two men."],[18321,"They complained to the Prophet ﷺ about the wounds and the digging for every person on the day of Uhud. He said: \"Dig graves, make them deep, make them good, and bury two or three in a grave.\" They said: \"Who should we put forward?\" He said: \"The one who knows the most Qur'an.\""],[18322,"that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Dig graves, make them good, make them wide, and bury two or three in a grave, and put forward the one who knows the most Qur'an.\" So my father was put forward in front of two men. 'Abd al-Wārith added to the chain of this hadith: Abū al-Dahmā'."],[18323,"Hishām b. 'Āmir: The Ansār came to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Uhud and said: \"O Messenger of God, there is wounding and hardship. What do you command us?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Dig graves, make them wide, and put two or three men in the grave.\" They said: \"Which of them should we put forward?\" He said: \"Put forward the one who knows the most Qur'an.\" So they put my father forward between two men, or two others."],[18324,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Between the creation of Adam and the rising of the Hour, there is no trial greater than the Dajjāl.\""],[18325,"\"You bypass me to a group of companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ who were not more attached to the Messenger of God ﷺ, nor better memorizers than me. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Between the creation of Adam and the rising of the Hour, there is no trial greater than the Dajjāl.'\""],[18326,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Between the creation of Adam and the rising of the Hour, there is no matter greater than the Dajjāl.\""],[18327,"Hishām b. 'Āmir saw men stepping over him to 'Imrān b. Husayn and to others among the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he said: \"You step over to men who were not more present with the Messenger of God ﷺ than I, nor more called upon for his hadith than I. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Between the creation of Adam and the rising of the Hour, there is no trial greater than the trial of the Dajjāl.'\""],[18328,"from the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon another Muslim for more than three nights. For both of them deviate from the truth as long as they remain in a state of severance. The first of them to return will have his precedence in returning as expiation. If he greets him and he does not accept and does not return his greeting, the angels return it to him, and Satan returns to the other. And if they die in a state of severance, they will not enter Paradise.\""],[18329,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"It is not permissible for a Muslim to forsake his fellow Muslim for more than three days. They must meet each other, and if one of them turns away, he is at fault. And the first one must greet the other with peace, which will count as his expiation. And if they both die while estranged from each other, they will never enter Paradise together. But if one of them greets the other and his greeting is not accepted, the angel will return the greeting, whereas the devil will return to the other.\""],[18330,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, the head of the Dajjal has curls from behind, and he will say, \"I am your Lord.\" Whoever says, \"You are my Lord,\" will be put to trial, and whoever says, \"You have lied; my Lord is God, upon Him I rely, and to Him I turn in repentance,\" then he will not be harmed — or he said, \"then there is no trial upon him.\"'"],[18331,"Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us; they said: Sulayman b. Harb narrated to us; they said: Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, who said: Hisham b. 'Amir came to Basra and found them exchanging gold in their stipends. He stood and said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade selling gold for silver on credit, and he informed us that that is riba.' The wording is that of Sulayman b. Harb."],[18332,"I heard Abu Qilabah: In the time of Ibn Ziyad, people used to take dinars for dirhams on credit. A man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Hisham b. 'Amir stood and said: 'Indeed, the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade selling gold for silver on credit, and he informed us that that is riba.'"],[18333,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever accuses a believer of disbelief, it is like killing him.'"],[18334,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The two sons of al-'As are believers: Hisham and 'Amr.'"],[18335,"Hisham: When it came to me, I climbed with it thus, I tried to make it out and I say, but I could not understand it. It occurred to me that it was revealed about us and about what we used to say. So I sat on my camel, then I caught up with Madinah. The Messenger of God ﷺ stayed waiting for permission to be granted to him to emigrate, and for his Companions among the Emigrants, who had arrived in groups. Abu Bakr stayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ waiting for permission to be given to him to set out, and Abu Bakr had asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for permission to emigrate, so he said: 'Do not be hasty; perhaps God will make for you a companion.' Abu Bakr hoped that the Messenger of God ﷺ meant himself. Abu Bakr had prepared for that two mounts, which he fed in his house."],[18336,"That he came as a delegate to the Messenger of God ﷺ among a group of his people, and the Messenger of God ﷺ heard him being called Abu al-Hakam. He said: 'Why do these people call you Abu al-Hakam?' He said: 'O Messenger of God, I used to judge between my people in the matter that occurred between them, and these and those would be pleased, so I was called Abu al-Hakam, but I have no child, so I am Abu al-Hakam.' He said: 'Do you have children?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What is the name of the oldest of them?' He said: 'Shurayh.' He said: 'Then you are Abu Shurayh.'"],[18337,"I came as a delegate to the Prophet ﷺ and he saw them calling me Abu al-Hakam. He said: 'Indeed, God is the Judge, so why are you called Abu al-Hakam?' I said: 'When there is something between my people, they take their dispute to me, and I judge between them, and they are pleased with my judgment.' He said: 'Do you have any children?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What is the name of the oldest of them?' I said: 'Shurayh.' He said: 'Then you are Abu Shurayh.'"],[18338,"That he came as a delegate to the Messenger of God ﷺ among his people, and he heard them calling Hani' Abu al-Hakam. The Messenger of God ﷺ called him and said: 'Indeed, God is the Judge, so why are you called Abu al-Hakam? Do you have a child?' He said: 'No, but my people, when they differ about something, they come to me and I judge between them, and both parties are pleased.' He said: 'How good this is.'"],[18339,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, tell me something that will make Paradise obligatory for me.' He said: 'Feeding food and spreading the greeting of peace make Paradise obligatory.'"],[18340,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, command me to an action.' He said: 'Feed food and spread the greeting of peace.'"],[18341,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed that will admit me to Paradise. He said: \"Among the things that necessitate forgiveness are spreading salam and good speech.\""],[18342,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me something that makes Paradise obligatory. He said: \"You must have good speech and providing food.\""],[18343,"Abu Shuraih al-Ka'bi, whose name was Khuwaylid, died in the year sixty-eight in Madinah, and there is disagreement about his death."],[18344,"Abu Shuraih al-Khuza'i, Ka'b b. 'Amr, died in the year fifty-eight."],[18345,"It is also said: 'Amr b. Khuwaylid.\""],[18346,"Abu Shuraih al-Ka'bi: \"Whoever sees me quarreling with a son-in-law of mine, [after] he has given me his daughter in marriage and I have given him my daughter in marriage, then I am insane that day, so cauterize my head. And whoever sees any [stray] kid or milk belonging to Abu Shuraih being sold in the market, then it is my plunder. And whoever sees me disputing with a neighbor of mine over a single brick, then I am insane, so cauterize my head.\" He said: Then a neighbor of his called 'Ajrafah tested him and took ten cubits from his house. They said to him: \"O Abu Shuraih, he has taken ten cubits from your house.\" He said: \"He knows best.\" He said: Then his neighbor later returned it to him and went back to his right."],[18347,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik. And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us: Malik informed us, from Sa'id b. Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Shuraih al-Ka'bi, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. His reward is a day and a night, and hospitality is three days. Whatever is after that is charity. It is not lawful for him to stay with him until he turns him out.\" Their wording is the same."],[18348,"My two ears heard it and my two eyes saw it when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke and said: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest, his reward.\" They said: \"And what is his reward, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"A day and a night. Hospitality is three [days], and whatever is beyond that is charity for him. He should not stay with him until he turns him out.\" And he said: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent.\""],[18349,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let them speak goodness or remain silent. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let them not harm their neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let them honor their guest. His reward is his day and his night.\" It was asked, \"And what is his reward?\" He ﷺ replied, \"His day and his night.\""],[18350,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. His reward is a day and a night, and it is not lawful for him to stay with his companion until he turns him out. Hospitality is three [days], and whatever he spends on him after that is charity.\""],[18351,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Hospitality is three days. Whatever is beyond that is charity.\""],[18352,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent.\""],[18353,"He informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent.\""],[18354,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent.\""],[18355,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent.\""],[18356,"Shall I tell you a statement that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the day after the conquest? My two ears heard it, my heart comprehended it, and my two eyes saw him when he said it. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: 'Allah made Makkah sacred, not the people. It is not lawful for any person who believes in Allah and the Last Day to shed blood in it or to cut down its trees. If anyone uses the fighting of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as an excuse, say to him: Allah permitted His Messenger but did not permit you. It was only permitted to me for a short time during the day, and today its sanctity has returned as it was yesterday. Let those present convey to those absent.' It was said to Abu Shuraih, 'What did 'Amr say to you?' He said, 'He said: I know this better than you, O Abu Shuraih. The sanctuary does not protect a disobedient person, nor one fleeing after shedding blood, nor one fleeing after committing a crime.'"],[18357,"He heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then he went out to the gathering of his people and sat with them. I got up and sat with him, and he narrated to his people just as 'Amr b. Sa'id narrated. Abu Shuraih said: I said, 'O this one, we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he conquered Makkah. On the day after the conquest, the Khaza'ah attacked a man from Hudhayl and killed him while he was a polytheist. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up as a preacher and said: O people, Allah made Makkah sacred on the day He created the heavens and the earth. It is sacred by Allah's sanctity until the Day of Resurrection. It is not lawful for any person who believes in Allah and the Last Day to shed blood in it or to cut down its trees. It was not made lawful for anyone before me, nor will it be made lawful for anyone after me. It was only made lawful for me for this hour out of anger against its people. Then its sanctity returned as it was yesterday. Let those of you who are present convey to those who are absent. Whoever tells you that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fought in it, say: Allah made it lawful for His Messenger but did not make it lawful for you. O people of Khaza'ah, restrain your hands from killing. It has become too much that killing should occur. You have killed a killed one, and I will pay his blood money. Whoever kills after this standing of mine, his family has the better of two options: if they wish, they may take the killer, and if they wish, they may take the blood money.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ paid the blood money for the man killed from Hudhayl. And the wording is that of al-Nufayli's hadith."],[18358,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Allah made Makkah sacred, not the people. It is not lawful for anyone who believes in Allah and the Last Day to shed blood in it or to cut down its trees. If someone seeks a concession saying it was made lawful for the Prophet ﷺ, then indeed Allah made it lawful for me for a short time during the day, and did not make it lawful for anyone other than me. Then it is sacred as it was yesterday. O Khaza'ah, you killed this killed one from Hudhayl, and I, by Allah, am his payer of blood money. Whoever kills someone in it after this, his family has two choices: if they wish, they may kill, and if they wish, they may take the blood money.'"],[18359,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'By Allah, he does not believe; by Allah, he does not believe; by Allah, he does not believe.' They said, 'Who is that, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'The neighbor whose neighbor is not safe from his harmful acts.' They said, 'What are his harmful acts?' He said, 'His evil.' And the wording is that of 'Asim b. 'Ali's hadith."],[18360,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Beware of sitting on the roads.' So we said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the road's right?' He said, 'Lowering the gaze, returning the greeting, enjoining good, and forbidding evil.'"],[18361,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The imam is a shield. If he completes the prayer, it is for you; and if he falls short, the shortcoming is upon him and the completion is for you.'"],[18362,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: 'Rejoice! Do you not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'This Quran is a rope, one end of it is in Allah's hand and the other end is in your hands. Hold fast to it, for you will never go astray nor perish after it ever.'"],[18363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What does a neighbor expect from his neighbor if he does not let him place a beam on his wall?'"],[18364,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever takes a handspan of land unjustly will be made to wear it around his neck on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths.'"],[18365,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever is afflicted with a killing or injury, he may choose one of three: to take retaliation, to forgive, or to take blood money. If he takes blood money, then restrain him. If he transgresses after that, he will have the fire of Hell.'"],[18366,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever is afflicted by bloodshed or injury—and injury means wounding—then he has the choice among one of three options. If he desires a fourth, then restrain him: to kill, to pardon, or to take blood money. Whoever does any of that and then transgresses again, for him is the fire of Hell, abiding eternally therein forever."],[18367,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever is afflicted by bloodshed or injury, his companion has the choice among one of three options: either to exact retaliation, or to pardon, or to take the blood money. If he desires a fourth, then restrain him. And if he chooses any of those and then transgresses to the fourth, he shall be in the Fire, abiding eternally therein."],[18368,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him be good to his neighbor. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent.\""],[18369,"On the authority of 'Urwah, regarding the naming of those who attended the 'Aqabah pledge from the Ansar, then from Banu Harithah: Abu Burdah b. Niyar b. 'Amr b. 'Ubayd—he was their ally from Baliyy—and he was a Badri."],[18370,"On the authority of Ibn Shihab, regarding \"the naming of those who attended the 'Aqabah pledge from the Ansar, then from Banu Harithah: Abu Burdah b. Niyar b. 'Amr.\""],[18371,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"In the first rite of this day, the Day of Sacrifice, there is prayer, then sacrifice after the prayer.\" I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I slaughtered before praying, and I have a jadha'ah from 'Ataq that is dearer to me than the meat of two sheep. Should I slaughter it? He said: \"Yes, but it will not suffice for anyone after you.\""],[18372,"I took the hand of the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Sacrifice and went with him to the house. I said to the servant girl: Feed us from the meat of your sacrificial animal. He said: \"It is not a sacrificial animal; it is only a sheep for meat. The sacrificial animal is only after the prayer.\" I said: O Messenger of God, we have a fosterling of ours, a jadha'ah. Should I sacrifice it? He said: \"Yes, but it will not suffice for anyone after you.\""],[18373,"He slaughtered a sheep early, then mentioned it to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I slaughtered our young sheep early. He asked: \"Before the prayer?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"That is a sheep for meat.\" He said: I have a jadha'ah that is dearer to me than a musinnah; will it suffice for me? He said: \"Yes, but it will never suffice for anyone after you.\""],[18374,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ led the prayer. Then I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: I went out with my sacrificial animal to the prayer place and slaughtered it before the prayer. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Sacrifice another instead.\" I looked for one among the goats but did not find any, so the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to sacrifice a jadha' from the sheep."],[18375,"I met my maternal uncle, and with him was a banner. I said, \"Where are you going?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to a man who married his father's wife after him—to strike his neck and kill him.\""],[18376,"My maternal uncle, Abu Burdah, passed by me with a flag. I said, \"Where to?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to a man who married his father's wife—I will bring his head.\""],[18377,"The Prophet ﷺ came to the tribes to supplicate for them, and he left a tribe without coming to them. They found that objectionable, so they searched a companion of theirs and found a necklace in the pack-saddle of a man among them; he had stolen it. So they returned it, and he came to them and prayed over them."],[18378,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"The world will not pass away until it belongs to a base son of a base man.\""],[18379,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No servant of my community sends blessings upon me with a sincere heart but Allah will bless him ten times for it, record ten good deeds for him, raise him ten degrees by it, and erase ten bad deeds from him.\""],[18380,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"It is not lawful for anyone to strike anyone more than ten lashes except in a prescribed punishment from the prescribed punishments of Allah.\""],[18381,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, \"No one is to be lashed more than ten lashes except in a prescribed punishment from the prescribed punishments of Allah.\""],[18382,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"No lashing above ten lashes except in a prescribed punishment from the prescribed punishments of Allah.\""],[18383,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No one is lashed ten lashes except in a prescribed punishment from the prescribed punishments of Allah.\""],[18384,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"A man from the soothsayers will come forth who will study the Quran with a study no one after him will achieve.\""],[18385,"It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, which earning is best?\" He said, \"A man's work with his own hand.\""],[18386,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best earning of a man is his child, and every righteous sale.\""],[18387,"I was walking with the Prophet ﷺ on one of the roads of Madinah, and he passed by some food. He inserted his hand [into it] and pulled out on his hand some bad food. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever cheats is not one of us.\""],[18388,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Yemen, and he invited him to Islam, so he accepted Islam. He wiped over his head and prayed for blessing for him, and he lodged him with Yazid b. Abi Sufyan. Then when Abu Bakr equipped the army for Syria, he went out with them and did not return."],[18389,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pass by a man who had food in a container. He looked at it and said: \"You have cheated him. Whoever cheats us is not one of us.\""],[18390,"I heard Abu al-Hamra' say: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ come to the door of Ali and Fatimah for six months, saying: \"Allah only desires to take away impurity from you, O People of the House, and to purify you thoroughly.\""],[18391,"From Abu al-Hamra', the servant of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When I was taken on the Night Journey to heaven, I entered Paradise and saw on the leg of the Throne written: There is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I supported him with Ali and aided him.\""],[18392,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by the house of Habbar b. al-Aswad and heard the sound of singing. He said: \"What is this?\" It was said: A wedding. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began saying, repeating: \"This is marriage, not fornication.\""],[18393,"Habbar married off his daughter, and at her wedding he beat the bellows and the sieve. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard that and said: \"What is this?\" They said: Habbar married off his daughter, and at her wedding he beat the bellows and the sieve. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Proclaim the marriage, proclaim the marriage. This is marriage, not fornication.\""],[18394,"He said to Ma'iz b. Malik: Go to the Prophet ﷺ and tell him your story. So he came to him and told him, but the Prophet ﷺ turned away from him several times. He kept repeating that to the Prophet ﷺ, so the Prophet ﷺ sent to his people and said: \"Does he have insanity?\" They said: No. He said: \"Is he a virgin or a previously married man?\" They said: Rather, a previously married man. He said: So he ordered that he be stoned. He said: \"Woe to you, O Hazzal! If you had covered him with your cloak, it would have been better for you.\""],[18395,"There was a slave girl who tended sheep for her family. A man from among us called Ma'iz b. Malik came to her and had intercourse with her. She came and told my grandfather Hazzal. So my grandfather Hazzal began encouraging him to confess before the Prophet ﷺ, saying: Woe to you! If you do not do so, Allah will send down upon His Messenger [a revelation] informing him of your affair. He did not stop until Ma'iz b. Malik came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, it was fornication. He turned away from him three or four times. Then the Prophet ﷺ ordered that he be stoned. He said: A man faced him with the jawbone of a camel and struck his shin with it, knocking him down, and they stoned him until they killed him while he was calling for help from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"Indeed, if he had come to me, he would not have returned to that.\" Then he said to the one who encouraged him: \"Woe to you, O Hazzal! If you had covered him with your garment, it would have been better for you,\" and he struck his hand on the knee of Hazzal."],[18396,"He informed me, saying: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina on a she-camel, and behind him rode al-Fadl b. Abbas.\""],[18397,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ while I was riding behind my father, and he was on his she-camel al-Adba' on the Day of Sacrifice, with the people around him. I said to my father: What is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying? He said: He is saying: \"Throw the pebbles like the small stones used for throwing.\""],[18398,"I was riding behind my father, and I saw the Prophet ﷺ on a camel saying: \"Labbayk, for Hajj and Umrah together.\""],[18399,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The beggar has a right even if he comes on a horse.”"],[18400,"A man from my people gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some dates as a gift. He said: “What kind of dates are these?” The man said: “Juzami.” He said: “O Allah, bless the Juzami.”"],[18401,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying on his mount, facing towards the east.”"],[18402,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon on his she-camel, saying: “Beware of treachery, for it is an evil inner characteristic. Beware of injustice, for it will be darkness on the Day of Resurrection. Beware of miserliness, for it destroyed those before you; it led them to shed their blood and sever their ties of kinship.”"],[18403,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in his sandals.”"],[18404,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in his sandals.”"],[18405,"The gathering brought us together in Tripoli, among us Hubayb al-Ghifari and Amr b. al-As, both companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Amr said: “The most virtuous is Ramadan.” Al-Ghifari said: “We do not differentiate between the make-up of Ramadan; Allah only said: ‘a number of other days.’”"],[18406,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever lets his garment drag out of pride, he will be dragged into the Fire.”"],[18407,"“Abu Tha'laba al-Khushani died in the year seventy-five.”"],[18408,"I said, O Messenger of God, give me a ruling concerning the luqatah (found property). He said, \"What is found on a well-traveled road or an inhabited one, announce it for a year; if you do not find its owner, it is yours. And what you find in an uninhabited village or a road that is not well-traveled, on it is the khums (one-fifth).\" I said, O Messenger of God, give me a ruling concerning my bow. He said, \"Eat whatever your bow returns to you.\" I said, \"What if it disappears from me?\" He said, \"Even if it disappears from you, after you have not seen in it the trace of an arrow or a blade.\""],[18409,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade every predator possessing fangs."],[18410,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, 'Abdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, that the Messenger of God ﷺ \"forbade every predator possessing fangs.\""],[18411,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade every predator possessing fangs."],[18412,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris, from Abu Tha'labah, who said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the snatched kill (al-khatfah), the plundered property (al-nuhbah), the animal that is tied up and shot (al-mujaththamah), and every predator possessing fangs.\""],[18413,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbidding every predator possessing fangs."],[18414,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ \"forbade every predator possessing fangs.\""],[18415,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ declaring forbidden the flesh of domestic donkeys and every predator possessing fangs."],[18416,"Every predator possessing fangs was declared forbidden."],[18417,"He told him, he said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the killing of any toothed animal from the wild beasts.\""],[18418,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ \"forbade eating every predator possessing fangs.\""],[18419,"The Messenger of God ﷺ declared forbidden the flesh of domestic donkeys."],[18420,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade every predator possessing fangs and the flesh of domestic donkeys."],[18421,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of domestic donkeys, and that pregnant women be had intercourse with, and every beast of prey with fangs."],[18422,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding every beast of prey with fangs."],[18423,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he forbade the meat of domestic donkeys and every beast of prey with fangs."],[18424,"He heard Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade eating every beast of prey with fangs.'"],[18425,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the meat of domestic donkeys and the meat of every beast of prey with fangs."],[18426,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the meat of every beast of prey with fangs."],[18427,"He informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding every beast of prey with fangs."],[18428,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the vessels of the idolaters. He said: 'Eat in them, drink, and cook, if you find no alternative.' He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade every beast of prey with fangs."],[18429,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we are in the land of the enemy and we need their vessels.' He said: 'Avoid them as much as you can. If you find nothing else, wash them and eat and drink in them.'"],[18430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade in the year of Khaybar the meat of domestic donkeys, and that a pregnant woman from the captives be had intercourse with until she gives birth, and every beast of prey with fangs."],[18431,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who raised his gaze and lowered it, then said: 'A small calamity.' Abu Tha'labah said: 'A small calamity of good or a small calamity of evil?' He said: 'A small calamity of good.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land with game. What is lawful for us from it and what is forbidden to us?' He said: 'The domestic donkey and every beast of prey with fangs are forbidden. Whatever your bow and your trained dog bring back to you is lawful for you.' Then he asked him about something concerning the People of the Book and their vessels. He said: 'If you find an alternative to them, do not approach them. If you need them, wash them, then eat and drink in them.'"],[18432,"He heard Abu Tha'labah say: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we are in the land of the People of the Book and we eat with them in their vessels, and our land is a land of game where we hunt with the bow, the trained dog, and the dog that is not trained. Tell me what is lawful for me and what is forbidden to me.' He said: 'As for what you mentioned, that you are in the land of the People of the Book and eat in their vessels: if you find vessels other than theirs, do not eat in them; if you find nothing else, wash them and eat in them. As for what you mentioned about the matter of game: whatever you hunt with your bow and mention the name of Allah over it, eat it. As for what your dog that is not trained catches, if you reach it while it is still alive and slaughter it, eat it; if you do not reach it before it dies, do not eat it. As for what your trained dog catches, eat what it holds back for you, and mention the name of Allah over it.'"],[18433,"On the authority of Abu Tha'laba, he raised it: Mu'awiya once [raised it] and another time did not raise it: \"Indeed, Allah will not let this Ummah be unable [to hold out] for half a day. And when you see the Levant as a man's dining table and his household, then at that point Constantinople will be conquered.\""],[18434,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The jinn are of three types: a type that has wings and flies through the air, a type that are snakes, and a type that settles and travels.\""],[18435,"He raided Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they were struck by hunger. They found domestic donkeys there, so the people slaughtered some of them. The Prophet ﷺ was informed, so he ordered 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, who called out among the people: \"The meat of domestic donkeys is not lawful for anyone who bears witness that I am the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So they overturned their pots with what was in them. They found onions and garlic in their gardens and ate from them while they were hungry, and they suffered. When the people went to the mosque, the smell of the mosque was onions and garlic. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever eats from this foul plant should not come near us.\""],[18436,"The Prophet ﷺ said about the one who finds his game after three [days]: \"He may eat it unless it has become putrid.\""],[18437,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"My Lord will never be unable to delay my Ummah for half a day.\""],[18438,"He raided Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while the people were hungry. He found domestic donkeys there, so the people slaughtered some of them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed, so he ordered 'Abd al-Rahman, who announced among the people: \"The meat of domestic donkeys is for the one who does not bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah.\" So they overturned their pots with what was in them. They found onions and garlic in their gardens. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever eats from this plant should not come near us.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Plunder is not lawful, nor is any predator with fangs lawful, nor is the mujaththamah lawful.\""],[18439,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a gold ring on his hand, so he began tapping it with a stick he had. When the Prophet ﷺ became inattentive, he threw it away. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I think we have only caused you pain and made you incur a loss.\""],[18440,"A man sat by the Prophet ﷺ wearing a gold ring. The Prophet ﷺ tapped his hand with a stick he had in his hand, then the Prophet ﷺ became inattentive to him, and the man threw away his ring. The Prophet ﷺ looked at him and said: \"Where is your ring?\" He said: \"I threw it away.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I think we have caused you pain and made you incur a loss.\""],[18441,"He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we are in the land of the People of the Book, and we cook in their pots and drink from their vessels.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you do not find other than them, wash them with water.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of game, so what should we do?\" He said: \"If you send your trained dog and mention the name of Allah, then eat. And if it is not trained and you slaughter it, then eat. And if you shoot your arrow and mention the name of Allah, then eat.\""],[18442,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: \"We need the vessels of the polytheists on our journeys, and we cook in them and drink from them.\" He said: \"Wash them with water, then cook in them and drink.\""],[18443,"I heard Abu Tha'laba al-Khushani say: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me what is lawful for me and what is forbidden to me.\" He looked up at me and then down, and said: \"A little prophet-like one.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, a little prophet-like one of good or a little prophet-like one of evil?\" He said: \"Rather a little prophet-like one of good. Do not eat the meat of domestic donkeys, nor any predator with fangs.\""],[18444,"He informed him that he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: \"We live as neighbors to the People of the Book, and they cook pork in their pots and drink wine from their vessels.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you find other than them, then eat in them and drink. And if you do not find other than them, wash them with water, then eat in them and drink.\""],[18445,"I heard Abu Tha'laba al-Khushani say: I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, inform me of what is lawful for me and what is forbidden to me.' He raised his gaze toward me and then lowered it, and said, 'Righteousness is what the soul feels at ease with and the heart feels assured about, and sin is what the soul does not feel at ease with and the heart does not feel assured about.'"],[18446,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped at a place and encamped, the people would scatter from him into the ravines and valleys. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and said, 'That is only from Satan.' After that, when they stopped at a place, they would draw close together, so much so that you would say, 'If a cloth were spread over them, it would cover them all,' or something like that."],[18447,"I came to Abu Tha'laba al-Khushani and said, 'O Abu Tha'laba, what do you do about this verse?' He said, 'Which verse?' I said, 'His saying: {O you who believe, upon you is [responsibility for] yourselves. Those who have gone astray will not harm you when you have been guided.}' He said, 'By Allah, you have asked one who knows about it. I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it, and he said, \"Rather, enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong, until you see miserliness obeyed, passion followed, the world preferred, and each person impressed with his own opinion. Then keep to your own self and leave alone the affairs of the common people. For behind you are days of patience, in which the one who is patient is like one grasping a live coal. The one who works good in that time will have the reward of fifty men.\"' Someone other than 'Utbah b. Abi Hakim added to me: It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, the reward of fifty men among us or among them?' He said, 'No, rather the reward of fifty men among you.'"],[18448,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, the most beloved of you to me and the closest of you to me in the Hereafter in seating are those of you with the best character, and the most hateful of you to me and the farthest of you from me in the Hereafter are those of you with the worst character, the prattlers, the boasters, and the self-important pretenders to understanding.'"],[18449,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, Allah has made obligations obligatory, so do not neglect them; and He has prohibited things, so do not violate them; and He has set limits, so do not transgress them; and He has remained silent about things out of mercy, not out of forgetfulness, so do not search into them.'"],[18450,"that the Prophet ﷺ said, “Allah [audits] his servants during the night of the middle of [month of ] Shaʿbān then forgives the Believers and [purposefully] overlooks the disbelievers and leaves the people of hate in their hatefulness until they let go of it.\""],[18451,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed your religion is prophethood and mercy, then caliphate and mercy, then rule and compulsion, then tyrannical rule, and then a biting monarchy in which even the free and silk are considered permissible.'\""],[18452,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I shoot with my bow, and some of what I hunt I am able to slaughter properly and some I am not. What of it is lawful for me and what is forbidden to me? And I am in the land of the People of the Book, and they eat pork and drink wine in their vessels, so may I eat and drink in them?' He said, 'He raised his gaze toward me and lowered it, then said, \"A little turn of fortune.\"' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, a little turn of fortune for good or a little turn of fortune for evil?' He said, 'Rather a little turn of fortune for good.' Then he said, 'Whatever your bow returns to you and you have mentioned the name of Allah over it, then eat it. And if you find an alternative to the vessels of the disbelievers, then do not eat in them; but if you find no alternative, then wash them thoroughly with water and then eat in them.'"],[18453,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, Allah looks upon His servants on the night of the middle of Sha'ban, and He forgives the believers, grants respite to the disbelievers, and leaves the people of malice with their malice until they call upon Him.'"],[18454,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast Sha'ban and Ramadan, joining them both together."],[18455,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a journey, he would begin with the mosque and pray two rak'ahs in it, then he would visit Fatimah, then he would go to his wives. He returned from a journey and prayed two rak'ahs in the mosque, then he came to Fatimah. She met him at the door of the house and began kissing his mouth and his eyes and weeping. He said, 'What makes you weep?' She said, 'I see you disheveled and exhausted, and your clothes have become worn out.' He said to her, 'Do not weep, for Allah has sent your father with a matter by which there will not remain on the face of the earth any house of mud, or stone, or fur, or hair except that Allah will bring into it honor or humiliation, until it reaches wherever the night reaches.'"],[18456,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a journey, he would begin with the mosque and pray two rak'ahs in it, then he would begin with the house of Fatimah, then he would go to the houses of his wives. He entered upon her, and she placed her hand on his cheek and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, your clothes have become worn out.' He said, 'O Fatimah, Allah has sent your father with a matter by which there will not remain a house of mud or fur except that Allah will bring into it honor through your father, until it reaches wherever the night reaches.'"],[18457,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him, and he said, 'A little turn of fortune.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, a little turn of fortune for good or a little turn of fortune for evil?' He said, 'No, rather a little turn of fortune for good.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I went out with an uncle of mine on a journey, and he suffered from sore feet. He said, \"Lend me your sandals.\" I said, \"I will not lend them to you unless you marry me to your daughter.\" He said, \"I have married her to you.\" Then when we came to our family, he sent my sandals back to me and said, \"You have no wife with us.\"' The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, 'There is no good for you in her.'"],[18458,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him, and he said, 'A little turn of fortune.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, a little turn of fortune for good or a little turn of fortune for evil?' He said, 'No, rather a little turn of fortune for good.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I went out with an uncle of mine on a journey, and he suffered from sore feet. He said, \"Lend me your sandals.\" I said, \"I will not lend them to you unless you marry me to your daughter.\" He said, \"I have married her to you.\" Then when we came to our family, he sent my sandals back to me and said, \"You have no wife with us.\"' The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, 'There is no good for you in her.'"],[18459,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him, and he said, “Nuwaybah.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, is it a small turn for good or a small turn for evil?” He said, “No, rather a small turn for good.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I set out with an uncle of mine on a journey, and he suffered from being barefoot, so he said, ‘Lend me your sandals.’ I said, ‘I will not lend them to you unless you marry me to your daughter.’ He said, ‘I have married her to you.’ Then when we came to our home, he sent my sandals back to me and said, ‘You have no wife with us.’ So the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, ‘There is no good for you in her.’”"],[18460,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him, and he said, “Nuwaybah.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, is it a small turn for good or a small turn for evil?” He said, “No, rather a small turn for good.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I set out with an uncle of mine on a journey, and he suffered from being barefoot, so he said, ‘Lend me your sandals.’ I said, ‘I will not lend them to you unless you marry me to your daughter.’ He said, ‘I have married her to you.’ Then when we came to our home, he sent my sandals back to me and said, ‘You have no wife with us.’ So the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, ‘There is no good for you in her.’”"],[18461,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him, and he said, “Nuwaybah.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, is it a small turn for good or a small turn for evil?” He said, “No, rather a small turn for good.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I set out with an uncle of mine on a journey, and he suffered from being barefoot, so he said, ‘Lend me your sandals.’ I said, ‘I will not lend them to you unless you marry me to your daughter.’ He said, ‘I have married her to you.’ Then when we came to our home, he sent my sandals back to me and said, ‘You have no wife with us.’ So the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, ‘There is no good for you in her.’”"],[18462,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him, and he said, “Nuwaybah.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, is it a small turn for good or a small turn for evil?” He said, “No, rather a small turn for good.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I set out with an uncle of mine on a journey, and he suffered from being barefoot, so he said, ‘Lend me your sandals.’ I said, ‘I will not lend them to you unless you marry me to your daughter.’ He said, ‘I have married her to you.’ Then when we came to our home, he sent my sandals back to me and said, ‘You have no wife with us.’ So the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, ‘There is no good for you in her.’”"],[18463,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him, and he said, “Nuwaybah.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, is it a small turn for good or a small turn for evil?” He said, “No, rather a small turn for good.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I set out with an uncle of mine on a journey, and he suffered from being barefoot, so he said, ‘Lend me your sandals.’ I said, ‘I will not lend them to you unless you marry me to your daughter.’ He said, ‘I have married her to you.’ Then when we came to our home, he sent my sandals back to me and said, ‘You have no wife with us.’ So the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, ‘There is no good for you in her.’”"],[18464,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him, and he said, “Nuwaybah.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, is it a small turn for good or a small turn for evil?” He said, “No, rather a small turn for good.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I set out with an uncle of mine on a journey, and he suffered from being barefoot, so he said, ‘Lend me your sandals.’ I said, ‘I will not lend them to you unless you marry me to your daughter.’ He said, ‘I have married her to you.’ Then when we came to our home, he sent my sandals back to me and said, ‘You have no wife with us.’ So the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, ‘There is no good for you in her.’”"],[18465,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Regarding buried treasure, one-fifth is due.”"],[18466,"Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land whose people are People of the Book; they eat the flesh of swine and drink wine. How do you command us regarding their vessels and cooking pots?” He said, “If you find other vessels, use them; otherwise, wash them with water, then eat and drink in them.”"],[18467,"Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land whose people are People of the Book; they eat the flesh of swine and drink wine. How do you command us regarding their vessels and cooking pots?” He said, “If you find other vessels, use them; otherwise, wash them with water, then eat and drink in them.”"],[18468,"Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land whose people are People of the Book; they eat the flesh of swine and drink wine. How do you command us regarding their vessels and cooking pots?” He said, “If you find other vessels, use them; otherwise, wash them with water, then eat and drink in them.”"],[18469,"I came to the Messenger of Allah and said, “O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land whose people are People of the Book; they eat the flesh of swine and drink wine. How do you command us regarding their cooking pots and vessels?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “If you find other vessels, use them; otherwise, wash them with water, cook in them, and drink.”"],[18470,"I came to the Messenger of Allah and said, “O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land whose people are People of the Book; they eat the flesh of swine and drink wine. How do you command us regarding their cooking pots and vessels?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “If you find other vessels, use them; otherwise, wash them with water, cook in them, and drink.”"],[18471,"I came to the Messenger of Allah and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land whose people are People of the Book, who eat the flesh of swine and drink wine. How do you command us regarding their pots and vessels? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: If you find other than them, then (use those); otherwise, rinse them with water and cook in them and drink."],[18472,"Two children of mine died, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, two children of mine have died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever has two children die, Allah will admit him to Paradise by the abundance of His mercy toward them.\" Then Abu Hurayrah met me and said: Are you the one to whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke about the two children? I said: Yes. He said: That he spoke to me about it is dearer to me than whatever Palestine would be closed off from."],[18473,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: Is there zakah on donkeys? He said: \"No, except the unique, isolated verse: {Whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it}.\""],[18474,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, we come to the land of the People of the Book. I asked him about their vessels. He said: \"Wash them, then cook in them.\""],[18475,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, write for me a land grant. He said: \"How can I write when it is in the land of war?\" He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, they will surely possess what is under their feet. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased with that, so he looked at his companions and wrote for him. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of game; what is lawful for us of what is forbidden to us? He said: \"When you send your trained dog or your taught dog, and you mention Allah's name, and it seizes and kills, then eat. When you send your dog that is not trained, whatever you catch while it is still alive and slaughter, then eat; whatever you do not catch alive, do not eat. And whatever your arrow returns to you with, eat.\""],[18476,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, write for me a land grant. He said: \"How can I write when it is in the land of war?\" He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, they will surely possess what is under their feet. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased with that, so he looked at his companions and wrote for him. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of game; what is lawful for us of what is forbidden to us? He said: \"When you send your trained dog or your taught dog, and you mention Allah's name, and it seizes and kills, then eat. When you send your dog that is not trained, whatever you catch while it is still alive and slaughter, then eat; whatever you do not catch alive, do not eat. And whatever your arrow returns to you with, eat.\""],[18477,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, write for me a land grant. He said: \"How can I write when it is in the land of war?\" He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, they will surely possess what is under their feet. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased with that, so he looked at his companions and wrote for him. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of game; what is lawful for us of what is forbidden to us? He said: \"When you send your trained dog or your taught dog, and you mention Allah's name, and it seizes and kills, then eat. When you send your dog that is not trained, whatever you catch while it is still alive and slaughter, then eat; whatever you do not catch alive, do not eat. And whatever your arrow returns to you with, eat.\""],[18478,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Our land is a land of game. I shoot my arrow and mention Allah's name, I send my trained dog and mention Allah's name, and I send my dog that is not trained and mention Allah's name. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whatever your arrow holds back for you and you mentioned Allah's name, eat. Whatever your trained dog holds back for you and you mentioned Allah's name, eat. Whatever your dog that is not trained holds back for you and you catch it alive and slaughter it, eat. If you do not catch it alive, do not eat.\""],[18479,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Our land is a land of game. I shoot my arrow and mention Allah's name, I send my trained dog and mention Allah's name, and I send my dog that is not trained and mention Allah's name. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whatever your arrow holds back for you and you mentioned Allah's name, eat. Whatever your trained dog holds back for you and you mentioned Allah's name, eat. Whatever your dog that is not trained holds back for you and you catch it alive and slaughter it, eat. If you do not catch it alive, do not eat.\""],[18480,"\"Yazid b. Abi Sufyan died in Syria in the year eighteen, and he had appointed Mu'awiyah as his successor, and 'Umar confirmed him.\""],[18481,"When Abu Bakr sent Yazid b. Abi Sufyan to Syria, he went out walking with him. Yazid said to him: Either ride or I will dismount. He said: I will not ride and you will not dismount. I am seeking reward for my steps."],[18482,"From Ya'la b. 'Ata' al-Ta'ifi, from Jabir b. Yazid b. al-Aswad, from his father, who said: We prayed Fajr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He turned around and saw two men behind the people. He summoned them, and they were brought trembling. He said: What prevented you two from praying with the people? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we prayed at our mounts. He said: Do not do that. When one of you prays at his mount and then catches the prayer with the imam, let him pray it with him, for it will be a supererogatory prayer."],[18483,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the morning prayer in the mosque of al-Khayf. After he finished, he saw two men at the back of the mosque. He sent for them, and they were brought trembling in their shoulders. He said, \"What is the matter with you that you did not pray with us?\" They said, \"We already prayed in our camps.\" He said, \"When one of you comes to the congregation and has already prayed in his home, let him pray with them, for it will be a supererogatory prayer for him.\""],[18484,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed a prayer. When he finished his prayer, he noticed two men at the back of the people. He ordered that they be brought, and they were brought trembling in their shoulders. He said, \"What prevented you from praying with us?\" They said, \"O Prophet of Allah, we prayed in the camps, then we came.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"When you two have prayed in your camps and then catch the prayer, pray it, for it will be a supererogatory prayer for you.\""],[18485,"We prayed the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina. There were two men at the back of the mosque who did not pray. He called for them, and they were brought trembling in their shoulders. He said, \"What prevented you from praying with us?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we had already prayed in our camps.\" He said, \"Do not do that. When you two have prayed in your camps and then come to the imam while he has not prayed, pray with him, for it will be a supererogatory prayer for you.\""],[18486,"He was with the Prophet ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage. He prayed the dawn prayer in the mosque of al-Khayf. When he finished his prayer, there were two men at the back of the mosque. They were brought trembling in their shoulders. He said, \"What is the matter with you that you did not pray with us?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we prayed in our camps, then we came while you were praying, so we sat down.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When one of you has prayed in his camp and then comes while the imam is praying, let him pray with him, for it will be a supererogatory prayer for him.\""],[18487,"I prayed the morning prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina in the mosque of al-Khayf. When he said the salutation, he faced the people and noticed two men among the last of the people who had not prayed with the people. He said, \"Bring me these two men.\" They were brought trembling in their shoulders. He said, \"What prevented you from praying with the people?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we had already prayed in the camps.\" He said, \"Do not do that. When one of you has prayed in his camp and then catches the prayer with the people, let him pray it with them, for it will be a supererogatory prayer for him.\""],[18488,"I attended the prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque of al-Khayf. When he finished the prayer, he noticed two men sitting to the side. They were brought trembling in their shoulders. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What prevented you from the prayer?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we prayed in our camps.\" He said, \"When you have prayed in your camps and then catch the prayer with the people, pray it with them. The one you prayed in your camps is the obligatory prayer.\""],[18489,"I performed the farewell Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and I prayed the morning prayer with him in Mina. When he finished his prayer, he saw two men behind the people who had not prayed with them. He said, \"Bring those two men to me.\" They were brought to him trembling. He asked them, \"Did you not pray with us?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we had already prayed in our camps, and we thought that we would not be able to catch the prayer.\" He said, \"Do not do that when you have already prayed in your camps, and then if you catch the prayer, pray it, and it will be a voluntary prayer for you.\" One of them said, \"Ask Allah to forgive me, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"O Allah, forgive him.\""],[18490,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, give me your hand.\" He gave it to me, and it was cooler than snow and more fragrant than musk."],[18491,"I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The people crowded around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and at that time I was among the strongest and most vigorous of men. I pressed through the people until I took the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and placed it on my chest. I never found anything cooler or more fragrant than the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[18492,"I recited to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one hundred verses of the poetry of Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt. Whenever I passed a verse, he said, \"Continue.\" And I heard him say in that gathering, \"The neighbor has more right to his property that is close to him.\""],[18493,"My father Yazid went out with some dinars to give as charity. He gave them to me and said, \"Give them to a man from the mosque.\" I gave them to someone else. Then I went to my father and told him. He said, \"That is not what I intended.\" I took the matter to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to me, \"O Ma'n, you have what you took,\" and to my father, \"O Yazid, you have what you intended.\""],[18494,"When the Muslims were routed on the day of Hunayn and the disbelievers pursued them, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a handful of earth and threw it in their faces, saying, \"Turn back! May the faces be ugly!\" None of us met his brother except that he complained of grit and was wiping his eyes."],[18495,"From Yazid b. 'Amir, who witnessed Hunayn with the polytheists then embraced Islam. He said: We asked him about the terror that Allah cast into their hearts on the day of Hunayn, how it was. He took a pebble and threw it at a basin, and it made a ringing sound. He said, \"We would feel in our chests something like that.\""],[18496,"Saʿīd b. al-Sāʾib al-Ṭāʾifī narrated to us, from Nūḥ b. Ṣaʿṣaʿah, from Yazīd b. ʿĀmir, who said: I came while the Prophet ﷺ was in prayer—either in Ẓuhr or in ʿAṣr—and I had already prayed them at home. When I found the Prophet ﷺ in prayer, I sat down and did not join them in prayer. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ turned to us and saw me sitting, and said, “Have you not become Muslim, O Yazīd?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of God, I have become Muslim.” He said, “What prevents you from entering prayer with the people?” I said, “I had prayed at home, and I thought that you had already prayed.” He said, “When you come to prayer and find the people praying, then pray with them, even if you have already prayed; it will be a supererogatory prayer for you, and this one will be the prescribed one.”"],[18497,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “O Yazīd, love for people what you love for yourself.”"],[18498,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not compete with one another except in two things: a man to whom Allah has given the Qur'an, so he recites it during the night and during the day, or a man to whom Allah has given wealth, so he spends it and gives in charity.\" A man said: \"If Allah had given me what He has given so-and-so, I would do like him.\" And a man to whom Allah has given wealth, so he spends it and gives in charity, another man said: \"Like that.\""],[18499,"From his paternal uncle Yazīd b. Thābit: They went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ one day with a funeral procession, until when they reached al-Baqīʿ, he said, “What is this?” They said, “This is so-and-so, a freedwoman of Banū so-and-so.” He recognized her and said, “Why did you not inform me about her?” They said, “We buried her at midday while you were taking a nap, so we did not want to disturb you.” Then he stood and the people lined up behind him, and he said four takbīrs over her. Then he said, “No one among you should die while I am still among you unless you inform me, for my prayer for him is a mercy.”"],[18500,"From his paternal uncle Yazīd b. Thābit, who was older than Zayd, who said: We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ. When we reached al-Baqīʿ, he noticed a new grave and asked about it. They said, “So-and-so.” He recognized her and said, “Should you not have informed me?” They said, “You were taking a nap and fasting, so we disliked to trouble you.” He said, “Do not do that. Let me not know of anyone among you who dies while I am still among you unless you inform me, for my prayer over him is a mercy for him.” Then he came to the grave, and we lined up behind him, and he said four takbīrs over it."],[18501,"He was with the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions when a funeral procession appeared. When he saw it, he stood up, and his companions stood up, and they remained standing until it had gone far. By God, I do not know whether it was from being disturbed by it or from the narrowness of the place. I do not think it was anything but the funeral of a Jew or a Jewess, and we did not ask him about his standing."],[18502,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “None of you should take his brother’s belongings, neither in jest nor in earnest. If one of you takes his brother’s staff, let him return it.”"],[18503,"When the Prophet ﷺ supplicated and raised his hands, he wiped his face with his hands."],[18504,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave us a grant in addition to our share of the khums, and I received an old camel."],[18505,"From Yazīd b. Salamah al-Juʿfī, who said: Yazīd said to the Messenger of God ﷺ, “I have heard from you many hadiths, and I fear that the first of them will make me forget the last, so tell me a word that will be comprehensive.” He said, “Fear God regarding what you know.”"],[18506,"From Yazīd b. Salamah al-Juʿfī, who said: “O Messenger of God, what do you think if we have rulers who take from us the right that is due to them and withhold from us the right that is due to us?” Al-Ashʿath said to him, “Sit down.” He repeated it a second time, then a third, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Upon them is what they are burdened with, and upon you is what you are burdened with.”"],[18507,"A man from his family died while he was not on the religion of Islam. He said: My sister inherited from him instead of me, because she was on his religion. Then my father became Muslim and witnessed Ḥunayn with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then he died, and I secured his inheritance. He had left behind a slave boy and palm trees. Then my sister became Muslim and disputed with me over the inheritance before ʿUthmān. ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Arqam told him that ʿUmar ruled that whoever becomes Muslim before an inheritance is divided is entitled to his share. ʿUthmān ruled accordingly, and she took the former inheritance and shared with me in this one. The wording is from the hadith of Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī."],[18508,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Your slaves, your slaves! Feed them from what you eat and clothe them from what you wear. If they commit a sin that you do not wish to forgive, then sell the servants of God and do not punish them.”"],[18509,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When a man makes a bond of brotherhood with another man, let him ask him about his name, his father's name, and from what tribe he is, for that is more conducive to affection."],[18510,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: No one kills a sparrow except that it will cry out on the Day of Resurrection, saying: 'O Lord, this one killed me in vain; he neither benefited from killing me, nor did he leave me to live in Your earth.'"],[18511,"O Messenger of Allah, what is Saba'? Was he a prophet or a woman? He said: Rather, he was a man of the Arabs. He said: What did he beget? He said: He begot ten sons. Six dwelt in Yemen and four in Syria. Those in Yemen were Kindah, Madhhij, al-Azd, al-Ash'ariyyun, Anmar, and Himyar. And in Syria: Lakhm, Judham, 'Amilah, and Ghassan."],[18512,"I came as a delegate to the Prophet ﷺ, and he asked me about al-Yamamah: in which tribe is the numerical majority of its people? I wanted to say in Banu 'Abd Allah b. al-Du'al, but then I disliked lying to the Prophet of Allah, so I said: The majority among them is in Banu 'Ubayd. He said: You have spoken the truth. A land that has grown despite hardship, and its people will never perish. They said: O Messenger of Allah, why is that? He said: Because they work with their own hands and share their food with their slaves."],[18513,"From Yazid b. Shajarah, and Yazid b. Shajarah was one whose word and deed were trusted. He said: He gave us a sermon and said: O people, remember the blessing of Allah upon you. How excellent is the blessing of Allah upon you! You see among green, yellow, and red, and in the saddles there is what there is. He used to say: When the people form rows for prayer and are arrayed for battle, the gates of heaven are opened, as are the gates of Paradise and the gates of Hell, and the wide-eyed houris are adorned and look out. When a man advances, they say: 'O Allah, grant him victory.' When he retreats, they veil themselves from him and say: 'O Allah, forgive him.' So strike hard at the faces of the enemy, may my father and mother be your ransom, and do not disgrace the houris. For the first drop of his blood that is shed atones for every sin he has committed, and two wives from the wide-eyed houris descend to him, wiping the dust from his face and saying: 'Your time has come.' And he replies: 'Your time has come.' Then he is clothed in one hundred garments, not of the weaving of the children of Adam but of the vegetation of Paradise, which, if placed between two fingers, would be spacious enough. He also used to say: I have been informed that swords are the keys to Paradise. This wording is from 'Abd al-Samad b. Hassan."],[18514,"\"That the world has become filled with green, red, and yellow, and in the houses there is nothing. So if you meet the enemy, go forward, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'No man takes a step in the way of Allah except that the houris of Paradise look at him. And if he is delayed, they become shy and conceal themselves from him. And if he is martyred, the first drop of blood from him will be an expiation for his sins, and two houris of Paradise will descend upon him, shaking off the dust from his face, and they will say, 'Welcome to you.' And he will say, 'Welcome to both of you.'\""],[18515,"From 'Urwah, in the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Quraysh, from the Banu Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza: Yazid b. Zam'ah. Ibn Lahi'ah said it thus, and in my view this is an error."],[18516,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, in the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Quraysh, then from the Banu Asad: Yazid b. Zam'ah b. al-Aswad b. al-Muttalib. A horse of his called al-Janah bolted with him and killed him."],[18517,"From Ibn Shihab, in the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Quraysh, then from the Banu Asad: Yazid b. Zam'ah."],[18518,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man from Banu Tamim has taken all my wealth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: I have no wealth to give you. Then he said: Would you like to be appointed as 'arif over your people? Or shall I appoint you as 'arif over your people? I said: No. He said: Indeed, the 'arif will be thrust into the Fire with a shove."],[18519,"When the Prophet ﷺ prayed over a deceased person, he would say the takbir four times, then say: O Allah, Your servant and the son of Your maidservant is in need of Your mercy, and You are free from need of punishing him. If he was a doer of good, then increase his good; and if he was a doer of evil, then overlook [his sins]. Then he would supplicate as Allah willed him to supplicate."],[18520,"I went on the expedition of hardship with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Ya'la used to say: That expedition is the most reliable of my deeds in my sight. I had a hired hand, and he fought a man. One of them bit the other, and the one who was bitten pulled his hand from the biter's mouth, tearing out one of his front teeth. They came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he declared the tooth to be of no consequence. I think he said: The Prophet ﷺ said: 'He leaves his hand in your mouth for you to gnaw it, as if it were in the mouth of a male camel biting it.'"],[18521,"I participated in the Battle of Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , alongside Abu Bakr As-Siddiq. This battle was one of my greatest achievements, and I hired a helper to fight alongside me. During the battle, my helper got into a fight with another man and he bit his hand, causing him to lose his two fingers. The injured man then complained to the Prophet ﷺ about what happened. The Prophet ﷺ dismissed the complaint and said, \"Would you want your hand to make him suffer by biting it like a stallion bites?\""],[18522,"I went on the expedition of Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a refractory young camel, and I had a hired hand with me. My hired hand fought a man, and the man bit him. He pulled his hand from the man's mouth, and his front tooth fell out. He was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to him: 'Would he leave his hand in your mouth for you to gnaw it as a stallion gnaws?' So he declared the tooth to be of no consequence."],[18523,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ after biting another man's hand. The one bitten pulled his hand away, and the biter's front tooth fell out. The Prophet ﷺ made it void and said: \"You wanted to bite it as a stallion bites.\""],[18524,"From his father and his paternal uncle Salamah b. Umayyah: The two of them went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk, and a companion of ours was with us. A man fought with him and bit him, so our companion pulled his hand out of his mouth, and a part of his mouth fell out. He went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked for compensation. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Will one of you go to his brother and bite him like a stallion bites, then come asking for compensation?\" And the Messenger of God ﷺ made it void."],[18525,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ at al-Ji'ranah wearing a jubbah and showing traces of khaluq. Hammam said: Or he said traces of yellow dye. The man said: \"How do you order me to proceed in my 'umrah?\" Revelation came down upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he was covered with a cloth. Ya'la used to say: \"I wished that I could see the Messenger of God ﷺ while revelation came to him.\" 'Umar said to me: \"Would you like to see the Messenger of God ﷺ while revelation is coming down upon him?\" So he lifted the edge of the cloth, and I looked at him, and he was snoring. Hammam said: \"I think he also said: like the snoring of a young virgin.\" When it was over, he said: \"Where is the one asking about the 'umrah? Remove the jubbah, and wash off from yourself\"—either he said \"the traces of khaluq\" or \"the traces of yellow dye,\" Hammam was unsure—\"and do in your 'umrah what you do in your hajj.\""],[18526,"I said to 'Umar b. al-Khattab: \"I wish I could see the Messenger of God ﷺ when revelation came down upon him.\" He said: \"We were on a journey with the Messenger of God ﷺ. He stopped at a place, and a bedouin came to him wearing a jubbah dyed with saffron. He said: 'O Messenger of God, I have entered ihram for 'umrah, and the people are mocking me. What should I do?' The Messenger of God ﷺ remained silent. Then God sent down revelation. 'Umar gestured to me with his hand, so I put my head into the tent. There was the Messenger of God ﷺ with his eyes and forehead red. When it was over, he said: 'Where is the one asking about the 'umrah?' The man said: 'It is I, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Remove your jubbah, and whatever you would do in your hajj, do it in your 'umrah.'\""],[18527,"A bedouin came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while we were with him and said: \"O Messenger of God, I have entered ihram while wearing khaluq, a woolen jubbah, and a turban.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Remove your turban and your shirt, wash off this yellow dye from yourself, and whatever you would do in your hajj, do it in your 'umrah.\""],[18528,"I wished to see the Prophet ﷺ when revelation came down upon him. When we were at al-Ji'ranah, revelation came down upon him, so he covered himself with a cloth. 'Umar called me and uncovered the cloth from his face, and I saw him snoring with his face red. Before that, a bedouin had come to him wearing patched garments, smeared with khaluq, and said: \"O Messenger of God, I have entered ihram for 'umrah while wearing this. How do you order me to proceed?\" He did not answer him until revelation came down upon him. When it was over, he said: \"Where is the questioner?\" The man said: \"Here I am.\" He said: \"What do you think? If you were in ihram for hajj and this was on you, what would you do?\" He said: \"I would remove these patched garments and wash off this khaluq.\" He said: \"Then go and remove these patched garments, wash off this khaluq, and do in your 'umrah what you would do in your hajj.\""],[18529,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ at al-Ji'ranah wearing a jubbah, with his beard and head dyed yellow. He said: \"O Messenger of God, I have entered ihram while I am as you see.\" He said: \"Wash off the yellow dye, remove the jubbah, and whatever you would do in your hajj, do it in your 'umrah.\""],[18530,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by al-Ji'ranah when he returned from Hunayn and distributed their spoils. A bedouin came to him wearing a shirt or a jubbah and having dyed himself with yellow dye. He said: \"O Messenger of God, I have entered ihram for 'umrah. What do you think?\" He did not answer him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ—the bedouin repeated: \"I have entered ihram for 'umrah. What do you think?\" He did not answer him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ withdrew for revelation, and 'Umar stood up to cover him with his cloth. Ya'la b. Munyah said: \"I love to see the Messenger of God ﷺ while revelation comes to him.\" 'Umar called him, so he put his head under the cloth and found him snoring like a sleeping person. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up, called the bedouin, and ordered him to remove his jubbah and his shirt. He said to him: \"Wash, and wear the lower garment and the cloak, and do in your 'umrah what you do in your hajj.\""],[18531,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The most beloved of you to me and the nearest of you to me in the Hereafter in sitting will be the best of you in character. And the most hated of you to me and the farthest of you from me in the Hereafter in sitting will be the worst of you in character: the talkative, the eloquent boasters, and those who speak with affectation in religious matters.\""],[18532,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God has made obligations, so do not neglect them; He has forbidden things, so do not violate them; He has set limits, so do not transgress them; and He has remained silent about things out of mercy, not out of forgetfulness, so do not search into them.\""],[18533,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"God looks upon His servants on the night of mid-Sha'ban and forgives the believers, gives respite to the disbelievers, and leaves the people of malice with their malice until they call upon Him.\""],[18534,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ and saw three amazing things from him. He said: We stopped at a land with many trees, and he said to me: \"Go to those two trees and tell them that the Messenger of God ﷺ commands them to come together.\" I went to them and said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ commands you to come together.\" They came together, and the Messenger of God ﷺ relieved himself. Then he said: \"Go and tell them to separate.\" I told them, and they separated. A woman came with a child and said: \"O Messenger of God, this child suffers epileptic fits seven times a month.\" He said: \"Bring him closer to me.\" He spat into his mouth and said: \"Get out, enemy of God! I am the Messenger of God.\" Then he said to her: \"When you return, inform me of what he does.\" When he returned, she met him with two rams and some ghee and aqit. He said to me: \"Take from her one of the two rams and what she has with it.\" She said: \"O Messenger of God, I have not seen that from him.\" Then a camel came to him, and he saw its eyes flowing with tears. He said: \"To whom does this belong?\" They said: \"To the family of so-and-so.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for them and said: \"What is wrong with this camel that it complains about you?\" They said: \"It was a water-carrying camel for us, and it grew old, so we wanted to slaughter it.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Leave it among the camels.\" So they left it."],[18535,"Abdullah b. Ya'la b. Murrah al-Thaqafi narrated to me, from his father, who said: One day I applied depilatory paste and then perfumed myself with khaluq. I came to the Prophet ﷺ, extended my hand to him, and said, “O Messenger of God, pray for me.” He said, “What is this on your hand?” I said, “I applied depilatory paste and then perfumed myself with khaluq.” He said, “Do you have a wife?” I said, “No.” He said, “Do you have a concubine?” I said, “No.” He said, “Go and wash it, then wash it three times.”"],[18536,"A prescribed prayer was due while we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ led us, and he did not advance ahead of us. I said to Abu Sahl, “What prompted him to do that?” He said, “The place was narrow.”"],[18537,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a smear of khaluq on him and said, “Wash this off yourself.”"],[18538,"The Prophet ﷺ saw me wearing khaluq and said, “O Ya'la, do you have a wife?” I said, “No.” He said, “Go and wash it, then wash it off yourself, then wash it off yourself, then do not do it again.” He said: I went and washed it, then washed it, then washed it, then never did it again until this moment."],[18539,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ with a yellow stain of saffron on him. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Wash this off yourself, then wash it, then do not do it again.” He said: So he washed it and did not do it again."],[18540,"I passed by the Prophet ﷺ wearing khaluq. He said, “O Ya'la, do you have a wife?” I said, “No.” He said, “Go and wash it, then wash it, then wash it, then do not do it again.” He said: So I washed it, then washed it, then washed it, then never did it again."],[18541,"I passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ wearing saffron khaluq. He said, “O Ya'la, do you have a wife?” I said, “No.” He said, “Go and wash it, then wash it, then wash it, then do not do it again.” He said: So I went and washed it, then washed it, then washed it, then never did it again."],[18542,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was in prayer. I went to a sister of mine and smeared my face with some khaluq. When the Prophet ﷺ passed by, he wiped the faces of others and left me. It was said, “The Prophet ﷺ left you only because of the khaluq on your face.” So I went to a well among the wells of Madinah and plunged into it. When the next prayer came, I came to him, and he wiped my face, then said, “The boy has returned with the good of his religion.”"],[18543,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever wrongfully takes anything from the earth will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying its dust to the gathering place.”"],[18544,"I heard Ya'la al-Thaqafi say: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whoever takes land without right will be burdened with carrying its dust to the gathering place.”"],[18545,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “Any man who wrongfully takes a handspan of land, God will oblige him to bring it until he reaches the end of the seventh earth, then he will be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection until judgment is passed among the people.”"],[18546,"From Ya'la b. Murrah al-Thaqafi, he said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “Whoever steals a handspan of land or a crop will come carrying it on the Day of Resurrection to the lowest of the earths.”"],[18547,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man, “Give me this camel as a gift, or sell it to me.” He said, “It is yours, O Messenger of God.” So he branded it with the zakah brand, then sent it off."],[18548,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whoever usurps a handspan of land or more will be made to carry it on the Day of Resurrection until he reaches the water, then he will carry it to the gathering place.”"],[18549,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Answer your brother, for you are for him on one of two things: either it is good, so you are most entitled to witness it, or it is otherwise, so you forbid him from it and command him to do good.”"],[18550,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Do not mutilate the servants of God.”"],[18551,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do not mutilate the servants of God.”"],[18552,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Do not depict my servants.'\""],[18553,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever finds a small lost item, a garment or the like, let him announce it for three days. Whoever finds more than that, six days. If its owner comes, then it is his, otherwise let him give it as charity. Then if its owner comes, let him inform him.”"],[18554,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ and were invited to a meal. There was Husayn playing in the road. The Prophet ﷺ hurried ahead of the people, then spread out his arms. Husayn began to dart here and there while he made him laugh, until he caught him. He placed one hand on his chin and the other between his head and his ears, then embraced him and kissed him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Husayn is from me and I am from him. May God love whoever loves him. Hasan and Husayn are two grandsons among the descendants of the prophets.”"],[18555,"Ya‘la b. Murrah reported to him that they went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ to a meal to which they had been invited. There was Husayn playing with some boys in the street. The Messenger of God ﷺ went ahead of the people and opened his arms. The boy began to dart here and there while the Messenger of God ﷺ made him laugh, until he caught him. He placed one hand under his chin and the other on the top of his head, then drew him close and kissed him, and said, “Husayn is from me and I am from Husayn. May God love whoever loves Husayn. Husayn is a tribe among the tribes of Israel.”"],[18556,"He saw Hasan and Husayn coming walking toward the Messenger of God ﷺ. When one of them came, he placed his hand on his neck. Then the other came, and he placed his other hand on his neck. He kissed this one, then kissed that one, then said, “O God, I love them, so love them. O people, indeed children are a cause of miserliness and cowardice.”"],[18557,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the last footstep that the Lord of the Worlds will tread upon is with His face.\""],[18558,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and he went away to relieve himself. Two dark-complexioned women came and joined each other. The tree of Talhah or Sumrah came, and it circled around them and returned to its place. Then a camel came dragging its tether along the ground until it became wet with the tears around it. He said to his companions, \"Do you know what this camel is saying?\" They said, \"What is it saying?\" He said, \"Its people wanted to slaughter it, so it called out for help. So it was sent back to me,\" He said, \"Will one of you undertake to do good to it?\" They said, \"Of course, by Allah, we will always honor it.\" Then he passed by two graves in which two people were being punished. He said, \"They are being punished, but the sins for which they are being punished are not significant.\" Then he took two fresh moist date-palm stalks and placed them on their graves. He said, \"Perhaps their torment will be lightened as long as these date-palm stalks remain moist.\""],[18559,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “When God wills to take a servant’s soul in a land, He creates for him a need there.”"],[18560,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “When God wills to take a servant’s soul in a land, He creates for him a need there.”"],[18561,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “When God wills to take a servant’s soul in a land, He creates for him a need there.”"],[18562,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Should I perform ablution after eating camel meat?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Should I pray in their resting places?” He said, “No.” He said, “Should I perform ablution after eating sheep meat?” He said, “No.” He said, “Should I pray in their folds?” He said, “Yes.”"],[18563,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a she-camel and said, “Who will milk her?” A man said, “I will.” He said, “What is your name?” He said, “Murra (bitter).” He said, “Sit down.” Then another stood up, and he said, “What is your name?” He said, “Murra.” He said, “Sit down.” Then another stood up, and he said, “What is your name?” He said, “Jamra (ember).” He said, “Sit down.” Then Ya‘īsh stood up, and he said, “What is your name?” He said, “Ya‘īsh (he lives).” He said, “Milk her.”"],[18564,"‘Abdullāh b. Dāwūd b. Dilhāth b. Ismā‘īl b. ‘Abdullāh b. Musri‘ b. Yāsir b. Suwayd al-Juhanī, the Companion of the Prophet, narrated to us. He said: My father Dāwūd narrated to me, from his father Dilhāth, from his father Ismā‘īl, from his father ‘Abdullāh, from his father Musri‘, from his father Yāsir b. Suwayd, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched him in a cavalry unit or a military expedition while his wife was pregnant. A child was born to him, and his mother carried him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, this child has been born while his father is with the cavalry, so name him.” The Prophet ﷺ took him, passed his hand over him, and said, “O Allah, increase their men, shorten their days, do not make them needy, and do not let their young ones experience want.” Then he said, “Name him Musri‘ (swift), for he has hastened into Islam.”"],[18565,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he had some people from Rabī‘a with him disputing over blood money. He was saying, “The upper hand is better than the lower hand: your mother and your father, your sister and your brother, then the next closest and the next closest.” Then he said, “Who is this with you, O Abū Rimtha?” I said, “My son.” He said, “Indeed, he will not be held liable for you, nor will you be held liable for him.” Then I looked and saw on the cartilage of his shoulder something like a camel’s dropping or a pigeon’s egg. I said, “Shall I treat this for you? I am from a household that practices medicine.” He said, “The one who placed it will treat it.”"],[18566,"I set out with my father toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When I saw him, my father said to me, “Do you know who this is?” I said, “No.” He said, “This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I shuddered when he said that to me, for I had thought that the Messenger of Allah was something unlike people. But he was a human with abundant hair, having traces of henna, and wearing two green cloaks. My father greeted him, then they sat talking for a while. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to my father, “Is this your son?” He said, “Yes, by the Lord of the Ka‘ba.” He said, “Truly?” He said, “Truly, I bear witness to it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled, laughing at the confirmation of my resemblance to my father and at my father’s oath concerning me. Then he said, “Indeed, he will not be held liable for you, nor will you be held liable for him.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited, “And no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another.” My father saw something like a wen between his shoulders and said, “I am like the most skilled of men in medicine; shall I not treat it?” He said, “Gently; its physician is the One who created it.”"],[18567,"I entered with my father upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. My father saw what was on his back and said, “Let me treat what is on your back, for I am a physician.” He said, “You are a kind companion, but Allah is the Physician.” He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to my father, “Who is this with you?” He said, “My son; I bear witness to you concerning him.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Indeed, you will not be held liable for him, nor will he be held liable for you.” And he mentioned that he saw traces of henna on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[18568,"I came with my father to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “Is this your son?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Do you love him? Indeed, he will not be held liable for you, nor will you be held liable for him.”"],[18569,"I set out with my father to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I saw on his shoulder something like an apple. My father said to him, “I am a physician; shall I not lance it?” He said, “Its physician is the One who created it.”"],[18570,"He entered upon the Prophet ﷺ with a son of his. He said, “Is this your son?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Indeed, he will not be held liable for you, nor will you be held liable for him.”"],[18571,"I set out with my father toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When I saw him, my father said, “Do you know who this is?” I said, “No.” He said, “This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I shuddered when I saw that, for I had thought that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was something unlike people. But he was a human with abundant hair, having traces of henna, and wearing two green cloaks. My father greeted him, then they sat and talked for a while. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to my father, “Is this your son?” He said, “Yes, by the Lord of the Ka‘ba.” He said, “Truly?” He said, “I bear witness to that.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled, laughing at the confirmation of my resemblance to my father and at my father’s oath concerning me. Then he said, “Indeed, he will not be held liable for you, nor will you be held liable for him.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited, “And no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another.” Then my father looked at something like a wen between his shoulders and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am like the most skilled of men in medicine; shall I treat it?” He said, “No, its physician is the One who created it.”"],[18572,"I entered the mosque with my father, and there was the Prophet ﷺ sitting in the shade of the Ka‘ba. He said to me, “Do you see the man in the shade of the Ka‘ba? That is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I was seized with a severe trembling. He was wearing two green garments, or two green cloaks, and had traces of henna. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Is this your son?” He said, “Yes, by the Lord of the Ka‘ba.” He said, “He will not be held liable for you, nor will you be held liable for him.”"],[18573,"I set out with my father to the Prophet ﷺ, and there he was with abundant hair, having traces of henna, wearing two green garments."],[18574,"I and my father were going towards the Messenger of God ﷺ. When we were partway, he met me, and my father said, “Do you know who this is?” I said, “No.” He said, “This is the Messenger of God ﷺ.” I had thought that the Messenger of God ﷺ did not resemble people. [He said:] And behold, it was a man with long hair, on which there was a trace of henna, wearing two green cloaks. It was as if I were looking at the gleam of his shins. He said to my father, “Who is this with you?” He said, “My son, by God, truly.” The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed at my father’s swearing about me, then said, “You have spoken truth. Indeed, he will not commit a crime against you, nor will you commit a crime against him.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ recited this verse: “No bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another.”"],[18575,"I went to the Prophet peace be upon him, and with me was my son. I said to my son, when I saw him, \"This is the Prophet of Allah.\" Then he (my son) had a seizure. So I said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"O Prophet of Allah, I am a physician and my father was a physician from a family of physicians. Show me your back, if there is a lump on it, I will treat it, and if it is something else, I will inform you. For there is no one more knowledgeable than me regarding injuries and wounds.\" He said, \"There is no physician except Allah, and upon him are two green bandages, and he has hair that has turned gray, and his beard is red.\" Then he said, \"Is this your son?\" I said, \"Yes, I swear by the Lord of the Kāba.\" He said, \"Is it from yourself?\" I said, \"I testify to it.\" He said, \"Indeed, it does not harm you nor does it harm him.\""],[18576,"I reached the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was giving a sermon, saying: “The upper hand is the one that gives. Your mother and your father, then your sister and your brother, then the nearest to you, then the nearest.” Then some people from Banu Yarbuʿ came and said, “O Messenger of God, this is Banu Yarbuʿ that killed so-and-so.” He said, “Indeed, no soul will bear the crime of another.”"],[18577,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he had hair that reached his shoulders, dyed with henna and katam."],[18578,"I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ praying, then he gave the greeting of peace to his right and to his left until we saw the whiteness of his cheeks."],[18579,"An imam of ours, known as Abu Rimthah, led us in the afternoon prayer in our prayer place. With us was a man who had been present at the first takbir of the prayer. When Abu Rimthah finished, the man stood up to make up [what he had missed]. Abu Rimthah looked and said, “I prayed this prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Abu Bakr and Umar were standing in the front row to his right. There was a man who had been present at the first takbir of the prayer. The Prophet ﷺ prayed, then gave the greeting of peace to the right and left until we saw the whiteness of his cheeks. Then he turned around and faced the people. The man who had caught with him the first takbir of the prayer stood up to make up [what he had missed]. Umar jumped towards him, grabbed him by the shoulders, and shook him, then said, ‘Sit down, for the People of the Book were only destroyed because there was no separation between their prayers.’ The Prophet ﷺ raised his eyes to him and said, ‘God has guided you to the right course, O Ibn al-Khattab.’”"],[18580,"The Messenger of God ﷺ named me Yusuf, seated me in his lap, and wiped my head."],[18581,"The Messenger of God ﷺ named me Yusuf."],[18582,"The Messenger of God ﷺ named me Yusuf, seated me in his lap, and prayed for blessing for me."],[18583,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ take a piece of barley bread, place a date on it, and say, “This is a condiment for this,” then he ate it."],[18584,"The Messenger of God ﷺ named me."],[18585,"The Messenger of God ﷺ named me Yusuf."],[18586,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man and woman from the Ansar: “Perform ʿumrah in the month of Ramadan, for an ʿumrah in it is like a Hajj.”"],[18587,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What is it upon any one of you to take two garments for Friday besides the two garments of his household's work?\""],[18588,"Yasir b. 'Amr was a chieftain in the time of al-Hajjaj."],[18589,"The Prophet ﷺ died when I was ten years old."],[18590,"As'ad b. Zurarah, who was the grandfather of Muhammad, was afflicted with a pain in his throat called quinsy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I will indeed reach or strive to the utmost in the case of Abu Umamah with an excuse.\" So he cauterized him with his own hand, and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What a bad death for the Jews; they will say, 'Could he not have warded off death from his companion?' I have no power for him or for myself against Allah in anything.\""],[18591,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Battle of Hunayn. We traveled on an intensely hot day, and we alighted under the shade of trees. When the sun declined, I put on my armor, mounted my horse, and went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in his tent. I said: \"Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Has the time for departure come?\" He said: \"Yes.\" Then he said: \"O Bilal!\" Bilal sprang up from under a samurah tree as if his shadow were the shadow of a bird. He said: \"At your service and at your command; I am your ransom.\" He said: \"O Bilal, saddle my horse for me.\" He brought out a saddle whose two sides were of palm fiber, with no ornament and no pride. He saddled it, and he mounted, and we mounted. We faced them that evening and that night. The two cavalries exchanged glances. The Muslims turned their backs in flight, as Allah had said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger.\" Then he spurred his horse forward, took a handful of dust, and the one who was closer to him than I was to him informed me that he threw it in their faces and said: \"Ugly be the faces!\" So Allah routed them. Ya'la b. 'Ata' said: Their sons narrated to me from their fathers that they said: \"Not one of us remained but that his eyes and mouth were filled with dust, and we heard a clattering from the sky and the earth like the passing of iron over a basin.\" The wording is that of 'Affan."],[18592,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, two riders appeared. When he saw them, he said: \"Two Kindis, two Madhhijis.\" When they came to him, they were indeed two men from Madhhij. One of them drew near to give him the oath of allegiance. When he took his hand, he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what about one who saw you, believed in you, confirmed you, and followed you? What will he have?\" He said: \"Tuba (glad tidings) for him.\" He said: \"Then he wiped over his hand and departed.\""],[18593,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: \"I am riding tomorrow to the Jews, so do not initiate the greeting of salam with them. If they greet you, then say, 'And upon you.'\""],[18594,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"We are going tomorrow to some Jews, so do not initiate the greeting of salam with them. If they greet you, then say, 'And upon you.'\""],[18595,"Sariq bought from a man who had recited Surah al-Baqarah some cloth that he had brought, and they haggled. Then the man disappeared, but he later caught up with him and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Sell, O Sariq.\" He said: \"I went with him and the Prophet's companions bargained with me for him for three days. Then it occurred to me, so I set him free.\""],[18596,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and 'A'ishah in a single garment, half of it over the Prophet ﷺ and half of it over 'A'ishah.\""],[18597,"Sa'd asked the Prophet ﷺ about the bequest, and he said to him: \"A fourth.\""],[18598,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning the matter of gambling. 'Abd al-Rahman said: I heard my father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever plays gambling and then gets up to pray is like one who performs ablution with pus and the blood of a pig.\" Then it is said: \"Will Allah accept his prayer?\""],[18599,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with my son, and he said: 'What children do you have?' I said: So-and-so, so-and-so, and 'Abd al-'Uzza. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The best of your names are 'Abd Allah, 'Abd al-Rahman, and al-Harith.'"],[18600,"Abu Amr b. Hafs said: \"By Allah, you have not been just. You dismissed an agent whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed, you sheathed a sword which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had unsheathed, you lowered a banner which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had raised, and you envied the son of your uncle.\" Umar said: \"You are a close relative and young in age.\""],[18601,"Muawiya said to him: \"Did you not go out with the people?\" He said: \"Yes, but I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I wanted to place it with you, fearing that you might not meet me. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'O people, whoever among you is given authority over something and then closes his door against a needy Muslim, Allah will close His gate against him entering Paradise. And whoever's main concern is this world, Allah will forbid him from my company, for I have been sent with the ruin of this world, not with its construction.'\""],[18602,"A slave girl from Khaybar passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while she was pregnant. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"To whom does she belong?\" They said: \"To so-and-so.\" He said: \"Does he have intercourse with her?\" It was said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then what will he do with her child? Will he claim it as his when it is not his child, or will he enslave it while it grows up in his hearing and sight? I have considered cursing him with a curse that would enter with him into his grave.\""],[18603,"Abū Saʿd: “Preserve the testament of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” Then ʿAbd al-Malik b. Marwān said: “And what is that?” He said: “Preserve [the rights of] their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers.” Abū Saʿd was the husband of Asmāʾ bt. Yazīd b. al-Sakan b. ʿAmr b. Ḥarām."],[18604,"I brought a debtor to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “Stay close to him.” Then he passed by him at the end of the day and said: “O brother of the Banū al-ʿAnbar, what do you intend to do with your captive?” The Messenger of God ﷺ was narrating to the people on the pulpit, and he descended to my grandfather, wiped his face, and bestowed upon him a fine garment."],[18605,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Were it not for devoted worshippers bowing, suckling infants, and grazing livestock, the punishment would have been poured upon you, then crushed to bits.”"],[18606,"I said: “O Messenger of God, whom should I treat with utmost kindness?” He said: “Your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, and your freed slave who is next to you—that is a binding right and a joined kinship.”"],[18607,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a garment of Maʿāfir clothing was brought. Abū Sufyān said: “May God curse this garment and the one who made it.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not curse them, for they are from me and I am from them.”"],[18608,"I heard Abū Zamʿah al-Balawī, one of the companions of the tree—he pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ beneath it. One day he came to the mosque of al-Fusṭāṭ and stood in the open courtyard. He had heard some strictness from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr, so he said: “Do not be harsh with the people, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘A man of the Children of Israel killed ninety-seven people, then went to a monk and said: “I have killed ninety-seven people; do you find any repentance for me?” He said: “No,” so he killed the monk. Then he went to another monk and said: “I have killed ninety-eight people; do you find any repentance for me?” He said: “No,” so he killed him. Then he went to a third and said: “I have killed ninety-nine people, including two monks; do you find any repentance for me?” He said: “You have done great evil. If I were to say that God is not forgiving and merciful, I would lie. So repent to God.” He said: “As for me, I will not part from you after what you have said.” So he stayed with him on the condition that he not disobey him, and he served him. One day a man died and his reputation was ugly. When he was buried, he sat by his grave and wept bitterly. Then another died, and his reputation was good. When he was buried, he sat by his grave and laughed heartily. His companions found this objectionable, so they gathered before their leader and said: “How can you take in this killer of souls? He has done what you saw.” It troubled him and them. So he came to their leader once while accompanied by a companion of his, and he spoke with him, asking: “What do you command me?” He said: “Go and kindle a oven.” He did, then came back with the news that he had done so. He said: “Go and throw yourself into it.” The monk became distracted from him, and the other went and threw himself into the oven. Then the monk came to his senses and said: “I think the man has thrown himself into the oven because of my words.” He went to him and found him alive in the oven, sweating. He took him by the hand and pulled him out of the oven, then said: “It is not fitting for you to serve me; rather, I will serve you. Tell me about your weeping over the first deceased and your laughing over the other.” He said: “As for the first, when he was buried I saw the evil he was experiencing, and I remembered my own sins and wept. As for the other, I saw the good he was receiving and laughed.” After that he became one of the great men of the Children of Israel.’”"],[18609,"I went to the Prophet ﷺ , then I entered between him and his garment and held onto it. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing that it is not permissible to prevent?\" He said, \"Water.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing that it is not permissible to prevent?\" He said, \"Salt.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing that it is not permissible to prevent?\" He said, \"If you do good, it will be good for you.\""],[18610,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever says ‘There is no god but Allah’ will enter Paradise.”"],[18611,"He witnessed with the Prophet ﷺ while he was besieging the people of al-Ta’if, and he would lead us in the afternoon prayer at a time when, if a person shot his arrows, he could see where the arrows fell."],[18612,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among the people during the Farewell Pilgrimage and said: “There is no prophet after me, and no community after you. So worship your Lord, establish your five prayers, fast your month, and obey those in authority over you, and you will enter the Paradise of your Lord.”"],[18613,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about fasting. He said: “Fast one day of the month.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, I am capable of more.” He said: “Fast two days of the month.” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, give me more.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Give me more, give me more—fast three days of every month.”"],[18614,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: “What kept you?” He said: “I recited this verse: {O you who believe, take care of your own selves; those who have gone astray will not harm you if you are guided}.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Those among the disbelievers who go astray will not harm you if you are guided.”"],[18615,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the perfection of piety?” He said: “That you do in private the deed you do in public.”"],[18616,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God, Blessed and Exalted, said: \"Whoever is not content with My decree and does not bear patiently My trial, let him seek a lord other than Me.\""],[18617,"I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ when he turned to us and said: \"Who would love to wake up and never fall ill?\" We started answering him and said: \"We would, O Messenger of God.\" He said: then we recognized it in his face, and he said: \"Would you love to be like braying donkeys?\" They said: \"No, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"Would you not love to be people of trial and people of expiation? For by the One in whose hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, God tests the believer with trial, and He does not test him with it except for His honor toward him. God has granted him a station that he did not reach by any of his deeds, so He tests him with trials that will make him attain that degree.\""],[18618,"She said to him—and he had a male camel and a female camel—\"Give me your male camel so I can perform Hajj on it.\" He said: \"It is dedicated for the sake of God.\" She said: \"It is for the sake of God that I perform Hajj on it.\" She said: \"Then give me the female camel and perform Hajj on your male camel.\" He said: \"I do not prefer anyone over myself.\" She said: \"Then give me some of your provision.\" He said: \"I have no surplus beyond what I will take with me and leave for you all. If I had any with me, I would give it to you.\" She said: \"If you do what you do, then convey my greetings to the Messenger of God ﷺ when you meet him and tell him what I said to you.\" When he met the Messenger of God ﷺ, he conveyed her greetings and told him what she had said. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Umm Taliq spoke the truth. If you had given her your male camel, it would have been in the way of God; if you had given her your female camel, it would have been in the way of God; and if you had given her some of your provision, God would have replaced it for you.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of God, what equals a Hajj?\" He said: \"An 'Umrah in Ramadan.\""],[18619,"On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of God ﷺ did not look in any direction without seeing Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith fighting. So the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed Abu Sufyan is the best of my family, or among the best of my family.\""],[18620,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave a sermon and said: \"Indeed a man was given the choice by his Lord to live in this world as long as he wished, eating from it, or to meet his Lord; and he chose meeting his Lord.\" Abu Bakr wept. The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do you not marvel at this old man? The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned a righteous man whom his Lord gave the choice between this world and meeting his Lord, and he chose meeting his Lord.\" Abu Bakr was the most knowledgeable of them about what the Messenger of God ﷺ meant. Abu Bakr said: \"We would ransom you, O Messenger of God, with our wealth and our children.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"No one among people has been more generous to us in his companionship and his wealth than Ibn Abi Quhafah. If I were to take a close friend, I would take Ibn Abi Quhafah, but [our relationship is] the love and brotherhood of faith. Your companion is the beloved of God.\""],[18621,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade his companions on the day of al-Hijr from using their well, so the one with dough threw away his dough and the one with hays threw away his hays."],[18622,"That he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and Abu Sirmah al-Ansari both saying: \"We captured some female captives during the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq—that is the expedition in which the Messenger of God ﷺ obtained Juwayriyah bt. al-Harith. Among us were those who wanted to take them as wives, and among us were those who wanted to enjoy them and then sell them. We discussed withdrawal (coitus interruptus) and mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: 'It does not matter if you do not practice withdrawal, for God has decreed whatever He is creating until the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[18623,"That the Prophet ﷺ \"forbade eating the dab (lizard).\""],[18624,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said: \"If one of you owns something that is worth the price of a slave, let him manumit it, for every limb of it will ransom a limb of him from the Fire.\""],[18625,"\"He cooked a pot for the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Hand me a foreleg'—and he used to like the foreleg—so I handed him the foreleg. Then he said: 'Hand me the foreleg,' so I handed him the foreleg. He said: 'Hand me the foreleg,' and I said: 'O Prophet of God, how many forelegs does a sheep have?' He said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you had remained silent, you would have given me forelegs as long as I asked for it.'\""],[18626,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Among the worst of thieves is he who steals the tongue of the ruler. Among the gravest of sins is he who seizes the property of a Muslim without right. Among good deeds is visiting the sick, and part of perfecting that visit is that you place your hand upon him and ask him how he is. Among the most excellent of intercessions is that you intercede between two people in a marriage until you bring them together. Among the clothing of the prophets is the shirt before the trousers. And among the things by which supplication is answered is sneezing.”"],[18627,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no group of people who gather together to study the Book of Allah except that they are guests of Allah, and the angels surround them, and tranquility descends upon them, and Allah mentions them to those who are near to Him. And there is no servant who leaves his home in search of knowledge, fearing that he may die or be harmed, except that he is like a traveler on the path of Allah. And whoever goes slower than him in his actions, his lineage will not make him go faster.\""],[18628,"From a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Abu Suwayd, that the Prophet ﷺ “prayed for those who had partaken of the pre-dawn meal.”"],[18629,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, so-and-so has died, so pray over him.” Umar said: “He was a transgressor, so do not pray over him.” The man said: “O Messenger of God, do you not recall the night in which you were accompanied on guard duty? For he was among them.” The Messenger of God ﷺ stood and prayed over him, then followed until he came to his grave, and sat until he was done with him. Then he threw three handfuls of earth over him and said: “The people praise you with evil, but I praise you with good.” Umar said: “And what is that, O Messenger of God?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Leave us be, O Ibn al-Khattab. Whoever strives in the path of God, Paradise is assured for him.”"],[18630,"the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , was commanded to pray for the people of Al-Baqi and he prayed for them three times in his night prayer. When he prayed for them the third time, he said, \"O Abu Muawiyah, saddle my mount for me.\" So I saddled the mount for him, and he rode and went to the people of Al-Baqi. Then he alighted and stood among them. He said, \"May you be refined by what you have faced from among the tribulations that come one after another, like pieces of a dark night. Some of them are worse than the others. May you be refined by what you have faced from them.\" Then the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , came and said, \"O Abu Muawiyah, I have been given, or I have been given the choice of the keys of what Allah will open for my nation after me, whether it is Paradise or meeting with my Lord.\" I said, \"By my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, I chose the meeting with my Lord.\" He said, \"I have chosen the meeting with my Lord.\" The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , did not stay except for seven or eight nights before he passed away."],[18631,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A settled person should not sell for a bedouin. Leave the people alone so that some may benefit from others; and if a man asks his brother for sincere advice, then let him advise him.' This is how Mansur b. Abi al-Aswad reported it from Hakim b. Abi Yazid, and he added to the people's narration in this hadith: 'A settled person should not sell for a bedouin.'"],[18632,"Abu Sulayman, the freed slave of Umm Salama, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed me that Abu al-Ramda al-Balawi informed him that a man among them drank wine, and they brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was flogged. Then he drank a second time, and they brought him, and he flogged him. I do not know whether he said on the third or the fourth time: he was ordered to be placed on a calf, and I struck his neck."],[18633,"Subay'ah gave birth after her husband's death by twenty-three nights. She desired [marriage]. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and he was informed, and he said: \"If she does, then her term has been fulfilled.\""],[18634,"I came to the Messenger of Allah and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am the man who came to you first.\" He said, \"Why do I not see you looking thin?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have not eaten any food during the day since I pledged allegiance to you.\" He said, \"Who told you to torture yourself?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am strong.\" He said, \"Fast the month of patience and two days after it.\" I said, \"I am strong.\" He said, \"Fast the month of patience and three days after it, and fast the sacred months.\""],[18635,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ undergo cupping.\""],[18636,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ from a journey and greeted him. When I went to leave, he said: \"Wait for lunch, O Abu Umayyah.\" I said: \"I am fasting, O Prophet of Allah.\" He said: \"I inform you about the traveler: Allah has waived fasting and half of the prayer for him.\""],[18637,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Among the signs of the Hour are three, one of which is that knowledge will be sought from the young.\""],[18638,"We were with Anbasah b. Sa'id. One day I rode to al-Hajjaj, and a man called Abu Ghadiyah al-Juhani came to him. Abd al-A'la b. Abd Allah said, 'Get up to him and bring him down, and say: Now you will return.' So we went out to him and said, 'Now you will return.' He dismounted. Abd al-A'la entered and asked for water. He was brought water in a glass cup, but he refused to drink from glass. Then he was brought it in a cup of naddar wood, and he drank. He said: 'I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ while I was returning wealth to my family.' Rashid b. Abyad, who was with me at Abd al-A'la's, said, 'With this right hand of yours?' Abd al-A'la rebuked him and said, 'Divide it for him.' He said: 'And I witnessed his sermon on the day of al-Aqabah, while he was saying: \"Indeed your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. Indeed, do not return after me to disbelief, striking one another's necks.\" Then, when the day came that Uthman was besieged, I heard a man saying, \"Indeed, will you not kill this one?\" I looked at him, and behold, it was Ammar. Had it not been for those behind him from his companions, I would have pinned his belly to the ground. I said, \"O God, if You will, let me meet him.\" Then when the day of Siffin came, I saw a man of evil leading a battalion on foot. I looked at the armor, and it had slipped from his knee, and I thrust him, and behold, it was Ammar.'"],[18639,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'No journey should be undertaken except to the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the Aqsa Mosque.'"],[18640,"He informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever is wealthy enough to marry and then does not marry is not of me.'"],[18641,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Abu Bakr and Umar appeared, so he said: “Praise be to Allah who has strengthened me through them.”"],[18642,"There was a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Abu Al-Khattab who asked the Prophet ﷺ about Witr prayer. The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"I prefer to perform Witr prayer during the second half of the night. Surely, Allah descends from the highest heaven to the lowest heaven and says, 'Is there anyone who asks so I may grant? Is there anyone who seeks forgiveness so I may forgive? Is there anyone who supplicates so I may respond?' Until the dawn comes up.\""],[18643,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you see women placing on their heads something like the humps of cattle, then let them know that no prayer will be accepted from them.”"],[18644,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ knocked on my door while I had been intimate with my wife. I disliked going out to him until I performed ghusl, so I was slow in coming to him. I caught up with him and informed him. He said to me: “Did you ejaculate?” I said: “No.” He said: “Indeed, only wudu was required of you.”"],[18645,"The Prophet ﷺ once prayed and entered his house, and amongst the people was a man with long hands who the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to call \"Dhu al-Yadayn\" (the one with two hands). Dhu al-Yadayn said, \"O Messenger of Allah, did the prayer become shorter or did you forget?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"It did not become shorter nor did I forget.\" He said, \"But you forgot the prayer.\" The Prophet ﷺ then advanced and prayed two Rak'ahs with them, then he made the salutation and pronounced the Takbeer and prostrated like his first prostration, or even longer. Then he pronounced the Takbeer and raised his head, then he pronounced the Takbeer and prostrated like his first prostration, or even longer. Then he pronounced the Takbeer and raised his head, and Muhammad did not preserve the salutation afterwards, or not?\""],[18646,"I was in Madinah and a woman passed by me, so I grabbed her side while I could hear the Messenger—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—accepting the people’s pledges. I went to him and he would not accept my pledge, saying: “The one who pinched yesterday.” I said: “By Allah, I will not do it again, O Messenger of Allah,” so he accepted my pledge."],[18647,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hold fast to obedience to your leaders and do not oppose them, for obedience to them is obedience to Allah, and disobedience to them is disobedience to Allah. Allah sent me to call to His way with wisdom and good exhortation. Whoever succeeds me in that is from me, and I am from him.”"],[18648,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There will be after me successors (khulafaʾ), and after the successors commanders (umaraʾ), and after the commanders kings (muluk), and after the kings tyrants (jababirah). Then a man from my household will emerge and fill the earth with justice as it was filled with injustice. Then al-Qahtani will be given authority. By the One who sent me with the truth, he will not be less than him.”"],[18649,"“I saw on the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uhud two coats of mail.”"],[18650,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever gives water to a thirsty person and quenches his thirst, a gate of Paradise is opened for him and it is said to him, ‘Enter through it.’ And whoever feeds a hungry person and satisfies him, and gives water to a thirsty person and quenches his thirst, all the gates of Paradise are opened for him and it is said to him, ‘Enter through whichever you wish.’”"],[18651,"Mismaʿ saw me praying behind the middle pillar of the House and said: My father narrated to me from my grandfather that “he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray two rakʿahs behind it.”"],[18652,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"A group of people will travel without having any company from these blessings, meaning a camel or anything. No one among you should be accompanied by a stray person, and no one should turn away a seeker if you seek profit and safety. No one should be accompanied by someone from the people if you truly believe in Allah and the Last Day. There will be no sorcerer or sorceress, no fortune-teller or fortune-telling woman, no astrologer or astrologer woman, and no poet or poetess. If Allah wants to punish any of His servants, He sends him to the lower heaven. Therefore, abstain from disobeying Allah in the evening.\""],[18653,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The grave says to the dead person when he is placed in it: ‘Woe to you, son of Adam! What deceived you about me? Did you not know that I am the house of trial, the house of darkness, the house of solitude, and the house of worms? What deceived you about me when you used to pass by me strutting (faddadan)?’ If he was righteous, an advocate of the grave answers on his behalf, saying: ‘What do you think if he was one of those who enjoined good and forbade evil?’ The grave then says: ‘Then I will return to him as greenery, and his body will return as light, and his soul will ascend to the Lord of the Worlds.’” A man said: “O Abu al-Hajjaj, what is al-faddad?” He said: “The one who strides forward with one foot and drags the other, like your walk, O son of my brother, at times; and at that time he was dressing and adorning himself.”"],[18654,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Cursed is the one who begs by the Face of Allah, and cursed is the one who is asked by the Face of Allah and then refuses the one asking him.”"],[18655,"From Abu Nuhaylah, a man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, that he was struck by an arrow, and it was said to him, “Pull it out.” He said: “O Allah, decrease the pain but do not decrease the reward.” It was said to him, “Make supplication.” He said: “O Allah, make me among those brought near, and make my mother among the fair maidens with wide, lovely eyes (al-hur al-ʿin).”"],[18656,"Abu ʿAtiyyah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down and mentioned that a man had died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Did any of you see him engaged in any good deed?” A man said: “Yes, I stood guard with him one night in the cause of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and those with him stood up, and when he was placed in the grave, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ scooped up earth with his hand and threw it, then said: “Your companions think that you are among the people of the Fire, but I testify that you are among the people of Paradise.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿUmar b. al-Khattab: “Do not ask about people’s deeds, but ask about their innate nature (fitrah).”"],[18657,"And he is one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ bought a horse from a bedouin. He went ahead to pay him the price of his horse, and the Prophet ﷺ walked quickly while the bedouin walked slowly. Some men began to intercept the bedouin and bargain with him over the horse, not knowing that the Prophet ﷺ had already bought it, until one of them offered the bedouin more than the price for which the Prophet ﷺ had bought the horse. The bedouin called out to the Prophet ﷺ, saying: “If you are buying this horse, then buy it; otherwise I will sell it.” When the Prophet ﷺ heard the bedouin’s call, he said: “Did I not already buy it?” The bedouin said: “No, by Allah, we have not made a transaction.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, I did buy it.” People began to crowd around the Prophet ﷺ and the bedouin while they were arguing. The bedouin kept saying: “Bring a witness who testifies that I sold it to you.” Every Muslim who came said to the bedouin: “Woe to you! The Prophet ﷺ would never say anything but the truth.” Then Khuzaymah came and listened to the exchange between the Prophet ﷺ and the bedouin. The bedouin kept saying: “Bring a witness that I sold it to you.” Khuzaymah said: “I testify that you have sold it.” The Prophet ﷺ turned to Khuzaymah and said: “On what basis do you testify?” He said: “By affirming your truthfulness, O Messenger of Allah.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the testimony of Khuzaymah equal to the testimony of two men."],[18658,"My brother and I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the mosque of al-Khayf praying, and we had already prayed the obligatory prayer in the house, so we did not pray with them. He said: “What prevented you two from praying with us?” We said: “We had already prayed the obligatory prayer in the house.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a man prays the obligatory prayer in his house and then finds a congregation, let him pray with them, and his prayer in his house will be a supererogatory prayer.”"],[18659,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a man from his people while he was in Madinah after his migration there. We found him striking the necks of captives at a small water source, and he continued until the blood flowed over the water. Safwan said: 'the blood flowed,' meaning it covered the water."],[18660,"From Abu Wahb al-Jushami, who was a Companion: He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Name yourselves with the names of the prophets. The most beloved of names to God are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman, and the truest of them are Harith and Hammam, and the ugliest of them are Harb and Murrah. Tether horses, wipe their forelocks and hindquarters – or he said their flanks – and put garlands on them, but do not put bowstrings as garlands. Upon you are every dark bay with a blaze and white stockings, or a chestnut with a blaze and white stockings, or a black with a blaze and white stockings.'"],[18661,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The oath by which a man seizes the property of his brother – may it sever the womb.'"],[18662,"I saw Abu Amr al-Ansari, who was a Badri, an Aqabi, and an Uhudi, fasting and writhing from thirst. He was saying to a servant of his: 'Woe to you, shield me.' The servant shielded him until he drew his bow with a weak draw and shot three arrows. Then he said: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of God, whether it falls short or reaches its target, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection.' It was said that he was killed at sunset."],[18663,"The Prophet ﷺ went out on the day of Fitr to the prayer ground, with Ubayy b. Ka'b on his right and Umar – or he said Ibn Umar – on his left. When he finished, he passed by the door of Abu Kathir or Abu Kabir, while the butchers were in their courtyard and the people had recently left the pre-Islamic era. He said to them: 'How do you sell?' They said: 'Such and such.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Sell however you wish, but do not mix dead meat with slaughtered meat before the people. O people, beware: do not hoard, do not bid each other up, do not go out to meet caravans, no urban dweller may sell for a bedouin, no man may sell over the sale of his brother, and no man may propose over the proposal of his brother until he gives permission. A woman should not ask for the divorce of another woman in order to overturn her vessel; let her marry, for her provision is upon God ﷻ.'"],[18664,"The Prophet saw me and saw a red man. He said, \"You are the father of the rose.\""],[18665,"Abu Tayba passed by us in the month of Ramadan. We said: 'Where have you come from?' He said: 'I cupped the Prophet ﷺ.'"],[18666,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, two children of mine have died in Islam.' He said: 'Whoever has two children die in Islam, God will admit him to Paradise by the abundance of His mercy toward them.' Later, he met Abu Hurayra and said to him: 'Are you the one to whom the Messenger of God ﷺ said that about the two children?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'That he said it to me is dearer to me than Hims and Palestine being conquered for me.'"],[18667,"I used to serve the Prophet ﷺ. When he wanted to perform ghusl, he would say: 'Turn away from me.' So I would turn my back to him. Then Hasan or Husayn was brought, and he urinated on his chest. I came to wash it, and he said: 'The urine of a girl is washed, but the urine of a boy is sprinkled with water.'"],[18668,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever supports two daughters, or two sisters, or two maternal aunts, or two paternal aunts, or two grandmothers, he is with me in Paradise like these two' – and the Messenger of God ﷺ joined his index finger and the one next to it. 'If they are three, he is given relief. If they are four or five, then O servants of God, help him, lend to him, lend to him, strike him, strike him.'"],[18669,"We entered upon Abu Ma'bad al-Juhani to visit him. We said: 'Will you not hang something (as an amulet)?' He said: 'Death is closer than that. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever hangs something (as an amulet), he is entrusted to it.'"],[18670,"The Prophet ﷺ said, Enjoining, all that is good is a Sadaqa.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6021)"],[18671,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr, it is like the ransom of a slave from the Children of Isma'il.\""],[18672,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I and the Hour were sent like this,\" and he joined the middle finger and the index finger, \"so I preceded it as this preceded this.\""],[18673,"The Prophet ﷺ saw him standing in the sun and said: \"What is the matter with him?\" They said: \"He vowed to stand in the sun and fast and not speak.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Sit, seek shade, speak, and fast.\""],[18674,"I heard Abu Asib, the servant of the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , say that the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"Jibril came to me with fever and plague, so I held the fever in Medina and sent the plague to the Sham as a testimony for my Ummah and a punishment for the disbelievers.\""],[18675,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When you see the believing man given asceticism in this world and paucity of speech, draw near to him, for he has received wisdom.\""],[18676,"On the authority of 'Urwah, regarding \"the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Khaybar from the Ansar, then from the Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, with the Messenger of God ﷺ: Abu al-Diyah or Abu Sabah.\""],[18677,"Nubayh b. Wahb narrated to me from Abu 'Aziz b. 'Umayr, the brother of Mus'ab b. 'Umayr, who said: I was among the captives on the day of Badr, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Treat the captives kindly.\" I was among a group of the Ansar, and when they brought their lunch and dinner, they would eat dates and feed me bread, following the instruction of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to them."],[18678,"Abu Qays died, and he was one of the righteous of the Ansar. His son Qays proposed to his wife, and she said: \"I consider you as a son, and you are one of the righteous of your people, but I will go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and seek his advice.\" So she went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"Abu Qays has died.\" He said to her something good. She said: \"His son Qays has proposed to me, and he is one of the righteous of his people, but I used to regard him as a son.\" He said to her: \"Return to your house.\" Then this verse was revealed: {And do not marry those [women] whom your fathers married}."],[18679,"\"We caught two fledglings of a dubsi bird in the markets when Abu al-Hasan, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, entered, and he took a mitikhah and struck him with it.\""],[18680,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Five are among the practices of the messengers: modesty, forbearance, cupping, the siwak, and perfuming oneself."],[18681,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us: Malik informed us, from 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr b. Muhammad b. 'Amr b. Hazm, from 'Abbad b. Tamim, that Abu Bashir al-Ansari informed him that he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a messenger. 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr said: I think he said: while the people were in their midday resting place: 'No collar of wool or any collar is to remain on the neck of a camel except that it is cut off.' Malik said: I think that is because of the evil eye."],[18682,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was leading them in prayer one day, and a woman passed by al-Batha. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured to her to move back, so she returned until he had finished praying, then she passed by."],[18683,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding fever, he said: 'Cool it with water, for it is from the heat of Hell.'"],[18684,"His father came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'What children do you have?' He said: 'Abd al-'Uzza, Sabrah, and al-Harith.' He said: 'Do not name 'Abd al-'Uzza; name him 'Abd Allah, for the best names are 'Abd Allah, 'Ubayd Allah, al-Harith, and Hammam.' And he supplicated for his son, and they have remained in honor until today."],[18685,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no prayer without ablution, and no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah upon it. And he does not believe in Allah who does not believe in me, and he does not believe in me who does not recognize the right of the Ansar.'"],[18686,"We used to sit with Abu Zuhayr al-Numayri, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and he would relate hadith and do so well. When one of us made a supplication, he would say: 'Seal it with amin, for amin in supplication is like the seal on a page.' Abu Zuhayr said: I will inform you about that. We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night walking, and we came upon a man in a tent who was persistent in asking. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped to listen to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'He has made it incumbent if he seals it.' A man among the people said to him: 'With what should he seal it, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'With amin. If he seals it with amin, he has made it incumbent.' The man who had asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went back and said: 'Seal it, O so-and-so, with amin, and rejoice.'"],[18687,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do not kill locusts, for they are the mighty army of Allah.'"],[18688,"When the Prophet ﷺ went to his bed, he would say: 'O Allah, forgive me my sin, drive away the devil, release my pledge, make my scale heavy, and place me in the highest company.'"],[18689,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to his bed at night, he would say: 'In the name of Allah I have laid down my side. O Allah, forgive me my sin, drive away my devil, release my pledge, and make my scale heavy.'"],[18690,"'By Allah, you have dismissed a governor whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed, sheathed a sword which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew, and lowered a banner which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ tied.'"],[18691,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If someone whose religion and character you approve of comes to you, marry him. If you do not, there will be temptation on earth and widespread corruption.\" He said it three times."],[18692,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has a palm tree and I am building my wall with it. Order him to give it to me so that I can build my wall with it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Give it to him in exchange for a palm tree in Paradise.\" He refused. Abu al-Dahdah went to the man and said: \"Sell me your palm tree for my wall.\" He did. Abu al-Dahdah then came and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have bought the palm tree for my wall, so give it to him, and I have given it to you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said repeatedly: \"How many heavy-laden clusters are there for Abu al-Dahdah!\" Abu al-Dahdah went to his wife and said: \"O Umm al-Dahdah, leave the wall, for I have sold it for a palm tree in Paradise.\" She said: \"A profitable sale,\" or words to that effect."],[18693,"When the verse {Who is it that would loan Allah a goodly loan} was revealed, Abu al-Dahdah said: \"O Messenger of Allah, does Allah want a loan from us?\" He said: \"Yes, O Abu al-Dahdah.\" He said: \"Show me your hand.\" He extended his hand to him, and he said: \"I have loaned my Lord my wall, and in my wall are six hundred palm trees.\" Then he went to the wall and called out: \"O Umm al-Dahdah,\" while she was in the wall. She said: \"At your service.\" He said: \"Leave, for I have loaned it to my Lord.\""],[18694,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ wearing two coats of mail on the day of Uhud."],[18695,"I was praying when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called me, but I did not answer him. When I finished the prayer, he said: \"What prevented you from answering me when I called you? Indeed Allah says: {O you who have believed, respond to Allah and to the Messenger when he calls you to that which gives you life}.\" Then he said: \"Do not leave the mosque until I teach you a surah in the Quran.\" I walked with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he was about to leave the mosque, and I reminded him. He said: \"The Opening of the Book, the Seven Oft-Repeated Verses, and the Great Quran which I have been given.\""],[18696,"We used to go to the market in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and pass by the mosque, and we would pray in it. One day we passed by while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting on the pulpit. I said: \"Something must have happened.\" So I sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse: {We have certainly seen the turning of your face toward the heaven} until he finished the verse. I said to my companion: \"Come, let us pray two rak'ahs before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ descends, so that we may be the first to pray.\" We hid ourselves and prayed them. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended and led the people in the noon prayer that day."],[18697,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"My Lord has promised me to admit seventy thousand of my community into Paradise without reckoning, and each thousand will intercede for seventy thousand. Then my Lord will scoop three scoops with His hands.\" Qays said: \"I said to Abu Sa'd: 'Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes, with my own ears, and my heart understood it.'\" Abu Sa'd said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'That, if Allah wills, will encompass the emigrants of my community, and Allah will complete it from our Bedouins.'\""],[18698,"Abu Saad Al-Khair Al-Ansari informed them in Qurqisia that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Seventy thousand people from my Ummah will enter Paradise without being held to account. With each thousand, there will be another seventy thousand. They are the ones who migrated (to Medina) and those who follow them from the Bedouins will also be included in this.\""],[18699,"I went out with Abu Sa'd al-Khayr to buy sacrificial animals. He pointed to a ram that had flesh, neither too tall nor too short, and said: \"Buy this one, for it resembles the ram of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[18700,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Remorse is repentance, and the one who repents from sin is like one who has no sin.\""],[18701,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Perform ablution from what the fire has touched and what was boiled in cauldrons.”"],[18702,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “When God gathers the first and the last on the Day of Resurrection, for a day about which there is no doubt,” a caller will call: “Whoever associated anyone in a deed he did for God, let him seek his reward from other than God, for God is the most self-sufficient of partners from association.”"],[18703,"He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever forsakes his brother for a year has shed his blood.”"],[18704,"He informed him that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever forsakes his brother for a year, it is like shedding his blood.”"],[18705,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The forsaking of a believer by his brother for a year is like shedding his blood.”"],[18706,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ seeking his aid against a debtor of his. He said to him: “Stay close to him.” Then he met him after that and said: “O brother of the Banū al-ʿAnbar, what happened to your captive?”"],[18707,"A man from Ashja‘ asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “I have a wife who is breastfeeding, and I dislike that she become pregnant. Should I practice coitus interruptus with her?” He said: “Whatever is decreed in the womb will come to be.”"],[18708,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, make the passing of my community by piercing and plague.”"],[18709,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, make the killing of my community in Your cause by piercing and plague.”"],[18710,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, make the killing of my community in Your cause by piercing and plague.”"],[18711,"“I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he besieged al-Ta’if, and he would lead us in the afternoon prayer at a time when, if a man shot an arrow, he could see where his arrows fell.”"],[18712,"From his grandfather, who was a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When a servant has a station with Allah that he cannot attain by his deeds, Allah afflicts him in his body, his wealth, or his children, then gives him patience over that until he reaches the station that was preordained for him from Allah, may He be glorified.”"],[18713,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever stands in a station of showing off and seeking reputation, God will expose him on the Day of Resurrection and make his reputation known.\""],[18714,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever stands in a station of showing off, God will expose him; and whoever stands in a station of seeking reputation, God will make his reputation known.\""],[18715,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever shows off for other than God, has disassociated himself from God.\""],[18716,"From his father Abu Hind al-Dari that they came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, six persons: Tamim b. Aws b. Kharijah b. Sawdan b. Jadhima b. Dira' b. 'Adi b. al-Dar, his brother Nu'aym b. Aws, Yazid b. Qays, Abu Hind b. 'Abd Allah, his brother al-Tayyib b. 'Abd Allah—the Messenger of God ﷺ named him 'Abd al-Rahman—and Fakih b. al-Nu'man. They embraced Islam and asked him to give them land from the land of Syria. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Ask wherever you wish.\" They got up from him consulting one another about which place they would ask him for. Tamim said: \"I think we should ask him for Jerusalem and its district.\" Abu Hind said: \"Do you see the king of the Persians today? Is he not in Jerusalem?\" Tamim said: \"Yes.\""],[18717,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O Banu Bayadah, marry Abu Hind and marry (your daughters) to him.\""],[18718,"I said: \"O Messenger of God, command me a deed that I can adhere to and perform.\" He said: \"You must strive in the way of God, for there is nothing like it.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, tell me a deed that I can adhere to and perform.\" He said: \"You must emigrate, for there is nothing like it.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, tell me a deed that I can adhere to and perform.\" He said: \"You must prostrate, for you will not prostrate to God a single prostration except that God raises you a degree and removes from you a sin.\""],[18719,"I said: \"O Messenger of God, tell us a deed that we can adhere to and perform.\" He said: \"You must emigrate, for there is nothing like it.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of God, tell us a deed that we can adhere to and perform.\" He said: \"You must strive (in the way of God), for there is nothing like it.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of God, tell us a deed that we can adhere to and perform.\" He said: \"You must fast, for there is nothing like it.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, tell us a deed that we can adhere to and perform.\" He said: \"You must prostrate, for you will not prostrate to God a single prostration except that God raises you a degree and removes from you a sin.\""],[18720,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Increase in prostration, for every servant who prostrates to God a single prostration, God raises him a degree.\""],[18721,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: \"O Abu Fatimah, if you want to meet me, then increase in prostration.\""],[18722,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not revile him\" — meaning Ma'iz b. Malik."],[18723,"From 'Urwah, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Tha'labah b. 'Amr b. 'Awf: Abu Habbah."],[18724,"From Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Tha'labah b. 'Amr b. 'Awf: Abu Habbah b. 'Amr b. Thabit."],[18725,"There is no harm in what a man throws at the jamarat of pebbles, meaning as to their number.\" 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr b. 'Uthman said: I mentioned that to 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr, and he said: Abu Habbah spoke the truth, and Abu Habbah was a Badri."],[18726,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I was taken up until I reached a level place where I could hear the scratching of pens.\""],[18727,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Then I was taken up until I reached a level place where I could hear the scratching of pens.\""],[18728,"The Prophet ﷺ met Ubayy b. Ka'b and said: \"Jibril has commanded me to recite to you {Lam yakun alladhina kafaru} (Qur'an 98).\" Ubayy said: \"O Messenger of God, was I mentioned there?\" He said: \"Yes.\" So he wept."],[18729,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not combine my name and my teknonym.\""],[18730,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who said, \"O Allah, I ask You for my wealth and the wealth of my master.\""],[18731,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"Whoever harms, God will harm him; and whoever causes hardship, God will cause hardship upon him.\""],[18732,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya b. Sa'id, from Muhammad b. Yahya b. Habban, from Lu'lu'a, from Abu Sirmah, from the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said: \"Whoever harms, God will harm him, and whoever causes hardship, God will cause hardship upon him.\""],[18733,"From Abu Maryam, the Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said: \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever is put in charge of any affair of the Muslims and then hides himself from their need, their poverty, and their destitution, God will hide Himself from his need, his poverty, and his destitution on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[18734,"\"I went on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ. He handed me the banner, and I threw stones in front of him, and that pleased him, and he supplicated for me.\""],[18735,"\"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said to him: 'A baby girl was born to me tonight.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'And tonight Surat Maryam was revealed to me. Name her Maryam.' So she was named Maryam.\""],[18736,"A bedouin came forward until he reached the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was sitting with a crowd of people around him. He said: 'Will you not give me something that I can learn and carry with me, that will benefit me and not harm you?' The people said: 'Be quiet, sit down.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Leave him, for the man has only asked in order to learn.' So they made way for him until he sat down. He said: 'What was the first matter of your prophethood?' He said: 'God took from me the covenant just as He took the covenant from the prophets.' Then he recited: {And when We took their covenant from the prophets, and from you, and from Noah, Abraham, Moses, and Jesus son of Mary; and We took from them a solemn covenant.} 'And the Messiah son of Mary gave glad tidings of me, and the mother of the Messenger of God ﷺ saw in her sleep that a lamp emerged from between her legs, and the palaces of Syria were illuminated by it.' The bedouin said: 'Hey!' and brought his head closer to him, and there was something in his ear, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'And behind that.'"],[18737,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ mounted us on weak camels from the camels of zakat for the pilgrimage. We said: 'O Messenger of God, we do not think these can carry us.' He said: 'There is no camel but that there is a devil on its peak. When you mount them, remember God's blessing upon you as He commanded you, then use them for your needs, for it is God who carries.'\""],[18738,"\"I heard 'Ali b. al-Madini say: 'Abu Sakinah—no companionship is known for him.'\""],[18739,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Honor bread, for God has honored it. Whoever honors bread, God will honor him.\""],[18740,"That he passed by the Prophet ﷺ while he had with him some dates. The Prophet ﷺ reached out to take a handful from him to scatter among his Companions, but he clutched the edge of his cloak to his chest and his belly. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “May God increase you in stinginess.”"],[18741,"From Abu Kabshah, the companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: While the Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting, a woman passed by him, so he got up and went to his family, then came out to us dripping. We said: “O Messenger of God, it seems something happened.” He said: “Yes, so-and-so passed by me, and desire for women entered my soul, so I went to one of my wives. Do likewise, for among the most virtuous of your deeds is coming to what is lawful.”"],[18742,"That he heard Abu Kabshah, the companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, narrate from the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said: “Horses have goodness tied to their forelocks, their people are aided through them, and the one who spends on them is like one extending his hand in charity.”"],[18743,"The Messenger of God ﷺ “liked looking at citron, and he liked looking at red pigeons.”"],[18744,"When the expedition to Tabuk took place, some people hurried to al-Hijr to enter it. An announcement was made among the people that prayer was to be held in congregation. He said: I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was holding his camel and saying: “Why would you enter upon a people with whom God is angry?” A man called to him in astonishment at them: “O Messenger of God?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Shall I not tell you of something more astonishing than that? The Messenger of God is from among yourselves, in your midst, telling you of what was before you and what will be after you. Be upright and aim aright, for God pays no heed to your punishment in the least.”"],[18745,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever lends his horse to a Muslim, and the horse then produces offspring, he has the reward of seventy horses ridden in the path of God. If it does not produce offspring, he has the reward of one horse ridden in the path of God.”"],[18746,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The best of you is the one who is best to his family.”"],[18747,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, and I shall tell you a hadith three times, swearing by them: The wealth of a servant is not diminished by charity, nor is a servant wronged with an injustice and bears it patiently except that God increases him in honor thereby, nor does a servant open the door of begging except that a door of poverty is opened for him.”"],[18748,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Mecca, Zubayr ibn al-Awam was on the left of the entrance and Mikdad was on the right. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Mecca and the people calmed down, they brought their horses. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, wiped the dust off their faces with his garment, and said, \"I have made two arrows for the horse and one arrow for the rider, so whoever shortens it, Allah will take away from him.\""],[18749,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his military expeditions, then we stopped at a place and we came to him. He raised his hands and said, \"Faith is here (pointing to Yemen) and wisdom is until (pointing to Lahm) and leprosy.\""],[18750,"From the Prophet of God ﷺ that he used to undergo cupping on the crown of his head and between his shoulders, and he would say: “Whoever spills this blood, it will not harm him to treat one thing with anything.”"],[18751,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My community is four types: a man given wealth and he spends it in obedience to Allah. Another man sees him and says, ‘If I had wealth like his, I would do with it as he did.’ They are equal in reward.”"],[18752,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me the example of this community as four people: a man whom Allah gave knowledge and wealth, and he acts on his knowledge with his wealth; a man whom Allah gave knowledge but not wealth, and he says, ‘If Allah had given me like what He gave this man, I would do with it as he does.’ They are equal in reward. And a man whom Allah gave wealth but not knowledge, so He lets him squander it in falsehood, not fearing a Lord in it nor maintaining ties of kinship with it. And a man whom Allah gave neither knowledge nor wealth, and he says, ‘If Allah had given me like what He gave this man, I would do with it as he does.’ They are equal in sin.”"],[18753,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My community is four types: a man whom Allah gave wealth and he placed it in the path He ordained. A Muslim man sees him and says, ‘Would that I had wealth like so-and-so’s, so I could do with it as he does.’ They are equal in reward. And a man whom Allah gave wealth and he spends it on his play, desires, and pleasures. A man sees him and says, ‘Would that I had wealth like so-and-so’s, so I could do with it as he did.’ They are equal in sin.”"],[18754,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The example of this community is like four people: a man whom Allah gave wealth and knowledge, and he acts on his knowledge, spending it in its right; and a man whom Allah gave knowledge but not wealth, and he says, ‘If I had wealth like this man’s, I would do with it as he does.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘They are equal in reward.’ And a man whom Allah gave wealth but not knowledge, and he blunders through his wealth, spending it in other than its right; and a man whom Allah gave neither knowledge nor wealth, and he says, ‘If I had wealth like so-and-so’s, I would do with it as he does.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘They are equal in sin.’”"],[18755,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “I shall tell you a hadith, so memorize it. The people of this world are only four: a servant whom Allah provided wealth and knowledge, and he fears his Lord in it, maintains ties of kinship with it, and works for Allah in it with its right—this one is in the best of stations. And a servant whom Allah provided knowledge but not wealth, and he is sincere in intention, saying, ‘If I had wealth, I would do as so-and-so does.’ Their reward is equal. And a servant whom Allah provided wealth but not knowledge, and he blunders through his wealth without knowledge, not fearing his Lord in it, nor maintaining ties of kinship with it, nor working for Allah in it with any right—this one is in the worst of stations. And a servant whom Allah provided neither wealth nor knowledge, and he says, ‘If I had wealth, I would do as so-and-so does.’ That is his intention, and their sin is equal.”"],[18756,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The example of my community is four people: a man whom Allah provided wealth and he works in it with obedience to Allah. A man sees him and says, ‘If I had wealth like his, I would do with it as he did.’ They are equal in reward. And a man whom Allah provided wealth and he blunders in it and corrupts it. A man sees him and says, ‘If I had wealth like his, I would do with it as he did.’ They are equal in sin.”"],[18757,"Narrated by Abu Muwayhibah, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ : The Prophet ﷺ passed by me one night and said, \"O Abu Muwayhibah, go forth, for I have been commanded to seek forgiveness for the people of this Baqi [graveyard].\" So I went forth, or he said: \"So we went forth,\" and when we reached Al-Baqi, he sought forgiveness for the people of the graves. Then he said, \"May you be blessed with what you have experienced until now. If you only knew what has been saved for you by Allah, you would have seen that trials would descend upon you like the darkest part of the night. The last of them would go on while the first of them is even worse than the last.\" Then he said, \"O Abu Muwayhibah, did you know that Allah has bestowed upon me the treasures of the earth and eternal life in it, followed by Paradise and the meeting with my Lord?\" I said, \"May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, so take the keys to the treasures of the earth and eternal life in it.\" He said, \"No, O Abu Muwayhibah, I have chosen the meeting with my Lord.\" Then he sought forgiveness for the people of the graves and then left. When morning came, he began to complain of the ailment that he passed away from. (Sahih Muslim)"],[18758,"Abu Salma, the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated to me: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Excellent, excellent! Five things, how heavy they are on the Scale: “There is no god but Allah,” “Allah is greatest,” “Glory be to Allah and with His praise,” and a righteous child who dies for a Muslim man and he seeks reward for it.’”"],[18759,"He informed him that while he was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, a Jewish man came to him as a funeral passed by and said, “O Muhammad, does this funeral speak?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah knows best.” The Jew said, “It speaks.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whatever the People of the Book tell you, do not believe them and do not deny them, but say, ‘We believe in Allah, His Books, and His Messengers.’ If it is false, they will not be believed; if it is true, they will not be denied.”"],[18760,"He informed him that while he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a Jewish man came to him and said, “O Muhammad, does this funeral speak?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah knows best.” The Jew said, “I bear witness that it speaks.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whatever the People of the Book tell you, do not deny them and do not believe them, but say, ‘We believe in Allah, His Messengers, and His Books.’ If it is true, you will not deny it; if it is false, you will not believe it.”"],[18761,"While he was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, a Jewish man came to him and said, “O Muhammad, does this funeral speak?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Allah knows best.” The Jew said, “I bear witness that it speaks.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whatever the People of the Book tell you, do not believe them and do not deny them, but say, ‘We believe in Allah, His Books, and His Messengers.’ If it is true, you will not deny it; if it is false, you will not believe it.”"],[18762,"He informed him that while he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , a man from the Jews came and said, \"O Muhammad, does this funeral speak?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah knows best.\" The Jew said, \"I bear witness that it speaks.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What people of the scripture tell you, neither believe nor disbelieve them. Rather, say, 'We have believed in Allah and in what was revealed to us and what was revealed to Abraham, Ishmael, Isaac, Jacob, and the Descendants, and in what was given to Moses and Jesus and to the prophets from their Lord. We make no distinction between any of them, and we are Muslims in submission to Him.' If it is true, then you have not disbelieved them, and if it is false, then you have not believed them.\""],[18763,"He informed him that while he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a Jewish man came to him and said, “Does this funeral speak?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah knows best.” The Jew said, “I bear witness that it speaks.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whatever the People of the Book tell you, do not believe them and do not deny them, but say, ‘We believe in Allah, His Books, and His Messengers.’ If it is true, you will not deny them; if it is false, you will not believe them.”"],[18764,"He informed him that while he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a Jewish man came to him and said, “O Muhammad, does this funeral speak?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah knows best.” The Jew said, “I bear witness that it speaks.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whatever the People of the Book tell you, do not believe them and do not deny them, but say, ‘We believe in Allah, His Books, and His Messengers.’ If it is true, you will not deny them; if it is false, you will not believe them.”"],[18765,"Narrated by Abu Sayyara al-Mutui, who was a freed slave of Banu Bajalah, he said, \"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have some bees.' He said, 'Give a tenth (of the honey as charity).' I said, 'And protect its mountain for and he protected its mountain for me.'\" (Note: This translation may vary depending on the interpretation of certain words)"],[18766,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have some honeybees.\" He said, \"Give it a tenth.\" I said, \"Can I burn their hives?\" So, he permitted me to burn their hives."],[18767,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking his help for the dowry of a woman. He said, 'How much did you give her as dowry?' I said, 'Two hundred dirhams.' He said, 'If you were to scoop from Bathan, you would not add more.'"],[18768,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; he had married a woman with a dowry of two hundred dirhams. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said, 'If you were to scoop from Bathan, you would not add more.'"],[18769,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, 'How much did you give as dowry, O Abu Hadrad?' I said, 'Five awaq.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'If you were to scoop from Bathan, you would not add more.'"],[18770,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Adopt the ways of Ma'add, be rough, and walk barefoot.'"],[18771,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Who will drive these camels of ours, or who will deliver these camels of ours?' A man stood up and said, 'What is your name?' He said, 'So-and-so.' He said, 'Sit down.' Then another stood up and said, 'I will.' He said, 'What is your name?' He said, 'Najiya.' He said, 'You are for it, so drive them.'"],[18772,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Leave the people alone so that some may benefit from others; and if they ask you for sincere advice, then advise them sincerely.'"],[18773,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Leave the people alone so that some may receive provision from others; and if one of you asks his brother for sincere advice, then let him advise him.'"],[18774,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Leave the people alone so that some may receive provision from others; and if a man asks another for sincere advice, then let him advise him.'"],[18775,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Leave the people alone so that some may receive provision from others; and if one of you consults his brother, then let him advise him.'"],[18776,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage. He addressed the people and said to them, 'Do such-and-such and do such-and-such, and avoid such-and-such and avoid such-and-such.' Then he said to them, 'Have I conveyed?' They said, 'Yes.' Then he raised his hands and said, 'O Allah, bear witness.' He said it three times. And I heard him say among what he said, 'Take the stipend as long as it is a stipend; but when Quraysh fight over the kingship among themselves, and the stipend becomes a bribe for your religion, then do not take it.'"],[18777,"Subay'ah bt. al-Harith gave birth after her husband's death by twenty-some nights. When she recovered from her postpartum bleeding, she desired [marriage], and that was disapproved for her. Her case was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"If she does, then her term has ended.\""],[18778,"Subay'ah gave birth after her husband's death by twenty-three or twenty-five nights. When she recovered from her postpartum bleeding, she desired [marriage]. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"If she does, then her term has become lawful.\""],[18779,"Subay'ah bt. al-Harith gave birth after her husband's death by twenty-three or twenty-five nights. When she recovered from her postpartum bleeding, she sought marriage, and that was disapproved for her or criticized. She mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"If she does that, then her term has become lawful.\""],[18780,"Subay'ah gave birth after her husband's death by twenty-three or twenty-five days. When she recovered, she desired husbands, and that was disapproved for her. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"What prevented her? Her term has ended.\""],[18781,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked upon Khaybar, he said to his companions while I was among them: \"Stop.\" Then he said: \"O Allah, Lord of the heavens and what they shade, Lord of the earths and what they carry, Lord of the devils and what they mislead, and Lord of the winds and what they scatter, I ask You for the good of this town and the good of its people, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of its people and the evil of what is in it. Advance in the name of Allah.\" And he used to say it for every town he entered."],[18782,"I heard Abu Aminah al-Fazari say: \"I saw the Prophet ﷺ undergo cupping.\""],[18783,"A thief was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who confessed a confession, but no goods were found with him. He said: \"I do not think you stole.\" He said: \"Yes, I did.\" He said: \"I do not think you stole.\" He said: \"Yes, I did.\" He said: \"Take him and cut off his hand.\" So they cut off his hand. Then they brought him, and he said: \"Ask Allah for forgiveness and repent to Him.\" He said: \"I ask Allah for forgiveness and repent to Him.\" He said: \"O Allah, turn to him in mercy; O Allah, turn to him in mercy.\""],[18784,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ from a journey. When he wanted to eat, I turned away. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Will you not have lunch?\" I said: \"I am fasting.\" He said: \"Shall I inform you about the traveler? Allah has waived fasting and half of the prayer for him.\""],[18785,"The Prophet ﷺ was eating lunch while traveling, and I was sitting near him. He said, 'Come to lunch.' I said, 'I am fasting.' He said, 'God has relieved the traveler of half the prayer and of fasting.'"],[18786,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'There will be rulers over you who control your provisions, who will speak to you and lie to you, and who will act and do evil. They will not be satisfied with you until you approve of their evil and believe their lies. So give them their due as long as they are satisfied with it. But if they go beyond that, then whoever is killed for that is a martyr.'"],[18787,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw me performing ablution and said, 'The sole of the foot, O Abu al-Haytham.'"],[18788,"Abd al-A'la said, 'Bring him in.' So he entered, wearing tattered clothes, a tall man, lean among men, as if he were not from this community. When he sat down, he said: 'I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ.' I said, 'With your right hand?' He said, 'Yes. He addressed us on the day of al-Aqabah, saying: \"O people, indeed your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. Indeed, have I conveyed?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"O God, bear witness.\" He said, \"Do not return after me to disbelief, striking one another's necks.\"' He said: 'We used to consider Ammar b. Yasir among the best of us.' He said: 'When the day of Siffin came, he came walking at the head of the battalion on foot, until when he was between the two ranks, he thrust a man in the knee with a spear. He stumbled, and the helmet fell away from him, and I struck him, and behold, it was the head of Ammar.' He said: 'A mawla of ours was saying, \"Which hand killed him?\"' He said: 'I have never seen a man more clearly astray in my view than him: he heard from the Prophet ﷺ what he heard, then he killed Ammar.'"],[18789,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'After me there will be severe trials. The best people in them will be those Muslims among the Bedouins who do not seek any share of people's blood or wealth.'"],[18790,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever leaves three consecutive Friday prayers out of negligence, God will seal his heart.'"],[18791,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever leaves the Friday prayer three times out of negligence, God will seal his heart.'"],[18792,"Abu al-Ja'd al-Damri, who was a Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever leaves the Friday prayer three times out of negligence, God will seal his heart.'"],[18793,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever leaves the Friday prayer three times out of negligence, God will seal his heart.'"],[18794,"From Abu Sallam, the servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “There is no servant, or person, or Muslim who says when he reaches the evening and when he reaches the morning: ‘I am pleased with Allah as my Lord, with Islam as my religion, and with Muhammad as my Prophet,’ but it becomes a right upon Allah to please him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[18795,"I had camels that I used for carrying loads. I came to Madinah and witnessed with the Prophet ﷺ Khaybar—or he said Hunayn—and we used to carry water for him on our camels. I had a trade in Madinah, so the Prophet ﷺ supplicated for blessing and supplicated for my parents."],[18796,"I was among the delegation who came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we were forty men. He forbade us from using gourds, green jars, hollowed stumps, and pitch-coated vessels. He said: Then he ordered some arak sticks for us and said: “Use these as tooth-sticks.” We said: “O Messenger of Allah, we have fresh herbage and we make do with it.” He raised his hands and said: “O Allah, forgive ‘Abd al-Qays since they submitted willingly, not reluctantly.”"],[18797,"“I was among the delegation who came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from ‘Abd al-Qays. He provisioned us with arak sticks so we could clean our teeth with them.” We said: “O Messenger of Allah, we have palm branches, but we accept your honor and your gift.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, forgive ‘Abd al-Qays since they submitted willingly, not under compulsion, while my people sat and did not submit except in humiliation, having suffered losses.”"],[18798,"“I used to pray the afternoon prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then go to Dhu al-Hulayfah on foot and reach it before the sun had set.”"],[18799,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who is disobedient to parents will not enter Paradise, nor the one who reminds others of his favors, nor the one addicted to wine.”"],[18800,"I saw a slave girl walking in one of the streets of Madinah, walking unsteadily. I reached my hand to her waist. The next day I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while the people were pledging allegiance to him. I stretched out my hand and said: “Give me your pledge, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Are you the one who pinched yesterday? Indeed, you are the one who pinched yesterday.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, accept my pledge, for by Allah I will never do it again.” He said: “Then how excellent!”"],[18801,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There will be rulers over you who will take control of your necks and speak to you, and they will lie to you; they will act and do wrong. They will not be pleased with you until you deem their ugly deeds good and believe their lies. So give them their due as long as they are content with it.”"],[18802,"From Abu Layla al-Ashʿari, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: “Hold fast to obedience to your leaders and do not oppose them, for obedience to them is obedience to Allah, and disobedience to them is disobedience to Allah. Allah sent me only to call to His way with wisdom and good exhortation. Whoever succeeds me in that is my ally. Whoever is given any authority over your affairs and acts otherwise, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. You will soon be ruled by commanders who, if asked for mercy, will not show mercy, and if asked for their rights, will not give them, and if commanded to do good, will reject it. You will keep away from them, and your assemblies will disperse until they cannot impose anything upon you except that you bear it willingly or unwillingly. The least that is your due is that you do not accept any gift from them and do not attend their gatherings.”"],[18803,"I heard my father say: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'O Messenger of God, is it part of tribalism that a man loves his people?' He said: 'No, but tribalism is that a man helps his people in wrongdoing.'"],[18804,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, two children of mine have died in Islam.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever has two children die in Islam, God will admit him to Paradise by the abundance of His mercy toward them.'"],[18805,"\"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and believed in him and affirmed him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ gave me a drink of sawiq. The Messenger of God ﷺ drank the first of it and I drank the last of it, and I have not ceased to find its moisture on my heart when I thirst and its coolness when I am exposed to the sun.\""],[18806,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The woman with prolonged menstrual bleeding leaves off prayer during the days of her menstrual periods, then she performs ghusl and prays, then performs wudu for every prayer.\""],[18807,"\"Sneezing, postpartum bleeding, drowsiness, nosebleed, menstruation, vomiting, and yawning in prayer are from Satan.\""],[18808,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say one day when the month of Ramadan had begun: \"If the servants knew what is in the month of Ramadan, the servants would wish that the month of Ramadan were a whole year.\" A man from Khuza'ah said: \"O Messenger of God, tell us.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Paradise is adorned for the month of Ramadan from the beginning of the year to the beginning of the year, until when it is the first night, a wind blows from beneath the Throne and rustles the leaves of the trees of Paradise. The wide-eyed houris look at that and say: 'O Lord, make for us from Your servants in this month spouses by whom our eyes will be delighted and their eyes will be delighted by us.' There is no servant who fasts the month of Ramadan except that God marries him to a wife each day from the wide-eyed houris confined in pavilions. Upon each woman among them are seventy garments, no garment of the same color as another, and she is given seventy kinds of perfume, no kind resembling another. Each woman among them is on a couch of ruby studded with pearls, on seventy beds whose linings are of rich brocade, and above the seventy beds are seventy canopied couches. For each woman among them are seventy servant boys to serve her and seventy servant boys to receive her, and with each servant boy is a platter of gold containing a kind of food, the last of which he finds the same pleasure as the first. Her husband is given the like of that on a couch of red ruby, upon him are two bracelets of gold studded with red ruby. This is for every day he fasted from the month of Ramadan, besides the good deeds he has done.\""],[18809,"Abu Jubayrah b. al-Dahhak: Among us this verse was revealed, meaning the Banu Salamah. The Messenger of God ﷺ came to Madinah, and there was no man among us but had two or three names. When a man was called by a name, they would say: \"O Messenger of God, he dislikes this.\" So it was revealed: {And do not call each other by offensive nicknames} - the verse."],[18810,"Among us, the company of the Ansar, this verse was revealed: {And do not call each other by offensive nicknames}. The Messenger of God ﷺ arrived and a man had two or three names. The Messenger of God ﷺ would sometimes call them by some of those names, and it would be said: \"O Messenger of God, he becomes angry from this.\" So it was revealed: {And do not call each other by offensive nicknames}."],[18811,"The Ansar used to give charity and give what God willed, then a year of drought befell them and they withheld, so God revealed: {And do not throw yourselves into destruction}."],[18812,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Trustworthiness is among the Azd, and modesty is among Quraysh.\""],[18813,"From his grandfather Abu Hasan, who was a participant in Badr and a Companion of the 'Aqabah pledge, who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man got up and forgot his sandals. Another man took them and placed them under himself. The man came back and said: \"My sandals.\" The people said: \"We have not seen them.\" A man said: \"Here they are.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What about frightening a believer?\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I did it only in jest.\" He said: \"What about frightening a believer?\" two or three times."],[18814,"That he came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Remove from yourself the hair of disbelief and get circumcised.\""],[18815,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Seek good from those with handsome faces.\""],[18816,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"When one of you leaves his house, let him say: In the name of Allah; there is no power and no strength except with Allah; whatever Allah wills; I have put my trust in Allah; Allah is sufficient for me, and He is the best Disposer of affairs.\""],[18817,"\"Fatimah's kunyah is Umm Abiha (the mother of her father).\""],[18818,"\"More than one person told me that Fatimah was the youngest of them and the most beloved of them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,\" and al-Zubayr b. Bakkar claimed that Ruqayyah was younger than Fatimah."],[18819,"\"The Prophet ﷺ had a son al-Qasim, and he was the eldest of his children, then Zaynab, then 'Abd Allah, who was called al-Tayyib and also called al-Tahir. He was born after prophethood and died young, then Umm Kulthum, then Fatimah, then Ruqayyah, in this order, the first then the first. Al-Qasim died in Makkah, then 'Abd Allah died.\""],[18820,"\"Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was given the kunyah Umm Abiha. It is said she was the youngest child of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Khadijah, and it is also said she was the twin of 'Abd Allah, son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[18821,"Fatimah died six months after the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Ali b. Abi Talib buried her at night."],[18822,"Fatimah lived six months after the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[18823,"Ali buried Fatimah at night."],[18824,"Ali buried Fatimah at night."],[18825,"Fatimah remained six months after the Prophet ﷺ, then she died."],[18826,"Aisha said: Fatimah lived six months after the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[18827,"Fatima stayed after the Prophet ﷺ for three months, and she was not seen smiling after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that her tooth corner moved."],[18828,"When death came to Fatimah, she instructed Ali to prepare a washing place for her, so she washed and purified herself, and she called for her shroud garments. She was brought coarse, rough garments, and she put them on and touched some of the perfume. She instructed Ali not to uncover her when she died and to wrap her as she was in her garments. I said to him: Did she teach anyone to do that? He said: Yes, Kathir b. Abbas, and he wrote on the edges of his shroud: Kathir b. Abbas bears witness that there is no god but God."],[18829,"I heard Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah say: Fatimah bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ died when she was twenty-seven years old."],[18830,"Fatimah died when she was twenty-eight years old. Her birth was when Quraysh were building the Kaaba. Quraysh built the Kaaba seven years and six months before the Prophet's ﷺ mission. The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Makkah for ten years after his mission, then he emigrated and stayed ten years. Then Fatimah lived after him six months and died in the year eleven of the Hijrah."],[18831,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, it will be said: O people of the gathering, lower your gazes until Fatimah bt. Muhammad passes. She will pass wearing two green or red garments."],[18832,"I used to see the Messenger of God ﷺ kissing Fatimah, so I said: O Messenger of God, I see you doing something I did not see you do before. He said to me: O Humayra, when I was taken on the night journey to heaven, I was admitted into Paradise and stood by a tree of the trees of Paradise. I had not seen in Paradise a tree more beautiful than it, nor whiter leaves, nor better fruit. I took a fruit from its fruit and ate it, and it became a drop in my loins. When I descended to earth, I had intercourse with Khadijah, and she conceived Fatimah. So when I long for the scent of Paradise, I smell the fragrance of Fatimah. O Humayra, Fatimah is not like the women of human beings, nor does she suffer illness as they suffer."],[18833,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Fatimah: God becomes angry for your anger and is pleased for your pleasure."],[18834,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pass by the house of Fatimah for six months whenever he went out for the dawn prayer and say: The prayer! {Indeed Allah only intends to remove from you the impurity, O people of the household, and to purify you with a thorough purification}."],[18835,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are Maryam bt. ‘Imran, Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, Asiyah bt. Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh, and Fatimah bt. Muhammad ﷺ.”"],[18836,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of the women of the worlds are Maryam bt. ‘Imran, Asiyah bt. Muzahim, Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, and Fatimah bt. Muhammad ﷺ .”"],[18837,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This is an angel from the angels who sought permission from his Lord to greet me and visit me. He did not descend down to the earth before this moment, and he gave me glad tidings that Hasan and Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise and their mother is the leader of the women of Paradise.\""],[18838,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “An angel from the sky who had never visited me asked Allah’s permission to visit me, and he gave me glad tidings, or informed me, that Fatimah is the foremost lady of the women of my ummah.”"],[18839,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Which of your household is most beloved to you? He said: “The most beloved of my family to me is Fatimah.”"],[18840,"I entered with my maternal aunt upon ‘A’ishah and said: O Mother of the Believers, which of the people was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? She said: “Fatimah.”"],[18841,"My maternal aunt said: O Mother of the Believers, who was the most beloved of the people to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? She said: “His daughter Fatimah.”"],[18842,"He informed him that he heard the Prophet ﷺ on the pulpit saying: “My daughter is only a part of me; what distresses her distresses me, and what harms her harms me.”"],[18843,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit, praised and extolled Allah, then said: “My daughter – meaning Fatimah – is only a part of me; what distresses her distresses me, and what harms her harms me.”"],[18844,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fatimah is a part of me; whoever angers her angers me.”"],[18845,"‘Ali proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl, and that reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he said: “Fatimah is a part of me; what harms her harms me, and what angers her angers me.”"],[18846,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fatimah is a branch from me; what angers her angers me, and what gladdens her gladdens me.”"],[18847,"Ali b. Abi Talib proposed to me. That reached Fatimah, so she came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Asma' is getting married to Ali.\" He said, \"It was not for her to offend Allah and His Messenger.\""],[18848,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Fatimah one day while Ali was standing, she was lying down, and her sons were beside her. Al-Hasan asked for water, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to a milch camel and milked it for them. He brought it, and al-Husayn woke up and began trying to drink before him until he cried. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Your brother asked for water before you.\" Fatimah said, \"It is as if al-Hasan is more preferred by you.\" He said, \"He is not more preferred by me than him; they are both in the same position with me. Indeed I, you, these two, and this sleeping one will be in one place on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[18849,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon us while I was sleeping. Al-Hasan asked for water, so he went to a waterskin of ours and poured some from it. Then he brought the vessel, and al-Husayn got up to ask him for water. He said, \"Your brother asked for water before you; he will drink, then you will drink.\" Fatimah said, \"It is as if he is the more beloved of the two to you.\" He said, \"He is not the more beloved of the two to me; they are both in one position with me. Indeed I, you, these two, and this sleeping one will be in one place.\""],[18850,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fatimah guarded her chastity, so Allah has forbidden her and her descendants to the Fire.\""],[18852,"Ali b. Abi Talib entered upon Fatimah and saw that she had applied kohl and worn dyed clothing, meaning during their Hajj with the Prophet ﷺ. He said to her, \"Who ordered you to do this?\" She said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Ali said, \"I went off incensed against Fatimah, seeking a ruling from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'She has spoken truly, she has spoken truly.'\""],[18853,"From his mother Fatimah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us on the evening of Arafah and said, \"Allah has boasted of you and forgiven you generally, and Ali specifically. I am the Messenger of Allah to you, not favoring my kin. This is Jibril informing me that the truly fortunate one is the one who loves Ali during his life and after his death, and the truly wretched one is the one who hates Ali during his life and after his death.\""],[18854,"And he told me—meaning the Messenger of God ﷺ—that I am the first of his family to join him."],[18855,"The Messenger of God ﷺ called Fatimah after the conquest and whispered to her, and she wept. Then he spoke to her and she laughed. Umm Salamah said: “I did not ask her until when the Messenger of God ﷺ died. I asked Fatimah about her weeping and her laughter, and Fatimah said: ‘He told me that he will die, then he told me that I am the mistress of the women of the people of Paradise after Maryam daughter of ‘Imran. That is why I laughed.’”"],[18856,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to her one day and said, \"Where are my sons?\" referring to Hasan and Husayn. She replied, \"We woke up and there is nothing in our house that they can taste.\" Ali said, \"I will take them, for I fear that they will cry for you and you have nothing with you.\" So he went to a certain Jew, and the Prophet ﷺ followed him and found them playing with some dates in front of them. He said, \"O Ali, won't you turn my sons over before the heat becomes intense for them?\" Ali replied, \"We woke up and there is nothing in our house. If you sit, O Prophet of Allah, until I gather some dates for Fatimah.\" So the Prophet ﷺ sat until some dates were gathered for Fatimah, and he put them in a piece of cloth. Then he turned to carry one of them, while I carried the other, until we turned them over."],[18857,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew four lines on the ground and said, \"Do you know what this is?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best women of the people of Paradise are Maryam bt. Imran, Asiyah bt. Muzahim, Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, and Fatimah bt. Muhammad ﷺ.\""],[18858,"I will tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I have kept seeking martyrdom for that hadith but have not been granted it. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the expedition of Tabuk saying, while we were traveling with him, \"Allah commanded me to marry Fatimah to Ali, so I did.\" Jibril ﷺ said, \"Allah built a garden of hollow pearl, between each hollow and the next a pearl of ruby studded with gold, and made its roofs green chrysolite, and placed in it arches of pearl crowned with ruby. Then He placed over it chambers, a brick of silver, a brick of gold, a brick of pearl, a brick of ruby, and a brick of chrysolite. Then He placed in it springs flowing in its corners, and it was bordered with rivers, and He placed over the rivers domes of pearl linked with chains of gold, and it was bordered with various trees, and He built in every branch a dome, and placed in every dome a couch of white pearl whose covering is fine silk and brocade, and its ground was spread with saffron and perfumed with musk and ambergris, and He placed in every dome a houri. The dome has one hundred doors, at each door two guardians and two trees, in every dome a spread, and around the domes was written the Verse of the Throne.\" I said, \"O Jibril, for whom has Allah built this garden?\" He said, \"He built it for Fatimah, your daughter, and Ali b. Abi Talib, besides her other gardens, as a gift He bestowed and to delight your eyes, O Messenger of Allah.\""],[18859,"Abu Bakr came to the Prophet ﷺ and sat before him. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you know my sincerity and my precedence in Islam, and I, and I...\" He said, \"And what is that?\" He said, \"Marry Fatimah to me.\" He was silent about it, or he turned away from him. Abu Bakr returned to Umar and said, \"I am ruined and have ruined you.\" He said, \"And what is that?\" He said, \"I proposed Fatimah to the Prophet ﷺ and he turned away from me.\" He said, \"Stay where you are until I go to the Prophet ﷺ and seek the like of what you sought.\" Umar came to the Prophet ﷺ and sat before him. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you know my sincerity and my precedence in Islam, and I, and I...\" He said, \"And what is that?\" He said, \"Marry Fatimah to me.\" He turned away from him. Umar returned to Abu Bakr and said, \"He is awaiting Allah's command concerning her. Come with us to Ali so that we may order him to seek the like of what we sought.\" Ali said, \"They came to me while I was on a path. They said, 'Your cousin's daughter is being proposed to.' They alerted me to a matter, so I got up dragging my cloak, one end on my shoulder and the other on the ground, until I came to the Prophet ﷺ and sat before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you know my precedence in Islam and my sincerity, and I, and I...' He said, 'And what is that, O Ali?' I said, 'Marry Fatimah to me.' He said, 'What do you have?' I said, 'My horse and my body armor.' He said, 'As for your horse, you cannot do without it. As for your armor, sell it.' So I sold it for four hundred and eighty, and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ and placed it in his lap. He took a handful from it and said, 'O Bilal, buy us perfume with it and order them to prepare her.' He made for her a bed carved with straps and a leather cushion stuffed with palm fiber, and filled the house with a heap, meaning sand. He said, 'When she comes to you, do not do anything until I come to you.' She came with Umm Ayman and sat on one side of the house while I was on the other side. The Prophet ﷺ came and said, 'Here is my brother.' Umm Ayman said, 'Your brother whom you have married to your daughter.' The Prophet ﷺ entered and said to Fatimah, 'Bring me water.' She went to a bowl in the house, put water in it, and brought it to him. He rinsed his mouth into it. Then he said to her, 'Stand up,' and he sprinkled between her breasts and on her head. Then he said, 'O Allah, I seek refuge for her and her descendants with You from the accursed Satan.' Then he said to her, 'Turn around,' so she turned around, and he sprinkled between her shoulders. Then he said, 'O Allah, I seek refuge for her and her descendants with You from the accursed Satan.' Then he said, 'Bring me water.' I did what he wanted: I filled the bowl with water and brought it to him. He took some with his mouth, then spat it into it, then poured it on my head and before me. Then he said, 'O Allah, I seek refuge for him and his descendants with You from the accursed Satan.' Then he said, 'Enter upon your family with the name of Allah and blessing.'"],[18860,"A man came to Fatimah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O daughter of the Messenger of Allah, did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ leave anything with you that you might give me as a gift?\" She said, \"O servant girl, bring that palm-stalk.\" She looked for it and did not find it. She said, \"Woe to you, look for it, for it is equal to me to al-Hasan and al-Husayn.\" She looked for it, and it turned out she had used it as a broom in her sweeping. In it was written: Muhammad ﷺ said, \"He is not a believer whose neighbor is not safe from his harm. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent. Allah loves the modest, the forbearing, the weak, the chaste, and He hates the obscene, the vulgar, the begging importunate. Modesty is part of faith and faith is in Paradise. Obscenity is part of vulgarity and vulgarity is in the Fire.\""],[18861,"O Abdullah, he disliked that. That remained among the oaths of al-Nu'man upon him until al-Husayn obeyed him concerning riding. He said, \"Since you have sworn, you have burdened me with what I dislike. Ride on the front of your mount and I will ride behind you, for I heard Fatimah bt. Muhammad ﷺ say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A man is more entitled to the front of his mount and the front of his bed, and to pray in his own home, except an imam who gathers the people to him.'\" Al-Nu'man said, \"The daughter of Muhammad the Messenger of Allah has spoken truly. I heard my father Bashir say as Fatimah said, and the Messenger of Allah said, 'except one who gives permission.' So Husayn rode on the saddle and the Ansari rode behind him.\""],[18862,"When 'When the victory of Allah and the conquest comes' was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Fatimah and said, \"My soul has been announced to me as departing,\" so she wept. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, \"Do not weep, for you are the first of my family to join me.\" So I laughed. Some of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ saw her and said to her, \"I saw you weep and laugh.\" She said, \"He said to me, 'My soul has been announced to me,' so I wept. Then he said, 'Do not weep, for you are the first of my family to join me,' so I laughed.\""],[18863,"Fatima wept over the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O my father, from his Lord how near he is! O my father, to Gabriel I announce his death! O my father, the Garden of Firdaws is his abode.”"],[18864,"“That you should pour dust over the Messenger of God ﷺ. O my father, from his Lord how near he is! O my father, the Garden of Firdaws is his abode. O my father, to Gabriel we announce his death. O my father, he answered a Lord who called him.”"],[18865,"A’ishah said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ fell ill in my house. Fatimah came walking to him—and by the One in Whose hand is A’ishah’s soul, her walk was just like the walk of the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ whispered something to her and she wept; then he whispered to her and she laughed. I said: ‘I have never seen laughter closer to weeping than this day.’ I said: ‘O Fatimah, tell me what he said to you.’ She said: ‘I would not do that, and the Messenger of God ﷺ has seen your place.’ When the Messenger of God ﷺ died, she asked her and she said: ‘The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Gabriel used to review the Qur’an with me once every year, but this year he reviewed it with me twice, and I think I am only being called by it, so I will answer. Fear God.”’ She said: ‘So I grieved.’ Then he whispered to me and said: ‘Are you not pleased that your husband is the first of the Muslims in Islam and the most knowledgeable of them in knowledge? For you are the mistress of the women of my community, just as Maryam was mistress over the women of her people.’”"],[18866,"A’ishah used to say: “In the illness in which the Messenger of God ﷺ was taken, he said to Fatimah: ‘O my little daughter, lean over me.’ So she leaned over him and he whispered to her for a while. Then she uncovered and she was weeping while A’ishah was present. Then after a while the Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘Lean over me, O my little daughter.’ So she leaned over him and he whispered to her for a while. Then she uncovered from him and laughed. A’ishah said: ‘I said: O my little daughter, tell me what your father whispered to you.’ Fatimah said: ‘He whispered to me in a state of secret, and you thought that I would disclose his secret while he is alive. That distressed A’ishah that there should be a secret kept from her. When God took him, A’ishah said to Fatimah: ‘O my little daughter, will you not tell me that report?’ She said: ‘As for now, yes. He whispered to me the first time and told me that Gabriel ﷺ used to review the Qur’an with him once every year, and that he reviewed the Qur’an with him twice this year. He told me that he told him that no prophet lived except half the lifespan of the one before him, and that he told me that ‘Isa son of Maryam lived one hundred and twenty years, and I think I will only depart at the head of sixty. That made me weep. And he said: “O my little daughter, among the women of the Muslims there is no woman with a greater affliction than you, so do not be less than a woman in patience.” And he whispered to me the second time and told me that I am the first of his family to join him, and he said: “You are the mistress of the women of the people of Paradise except what there is of the virgin Maryam daughter of ‘Imran.” So I laughed at that.’”"],[18867,"Her walk was like the walk of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: “Welcome to my daughter,” and seated her on his right or on his left. Then he whispered a conversation to her and she wept. I said to her: “The Messenger of God ﷺ singled you out with his conversation and then you weep?” Then he whispered a conversation to her and she laughed. I said: “I have never seen joy closer to grief than this day.” I asked her about what he said, and she said: “I would not divulge the secret of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” Until when he was taken, I asked her and she said: “He whispered to me and said: ‘Gabriel used to review the Qur’an with me once every year, and this year he reviewed it with me twice, so I do not think it is except that my term has come, and you are the first of my household to join me, and what an excellent predecessor I am for you.’ So I wept at that. Then he said: ‘Are you not pleased that you will be the mistress of the women of the community, or the women of the Muslims?’ So I laughed at that.”"],[18868,"The wives of the Messenger of God ﷺ gathered, and not one of them was absent. Fatimah came walking, and her walk did not differ from the walk of her father ﷺ. He said: “Welcome, O my daughter,” and seated her on his right or on his left. Then he whispered something to her and she wept; then he whispered to her and she laughed. We said to her: “The Messenger of God ﷺ singled you out among us with a secret, and you weep?” When the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up, I said to her: “Tell me what he whispered to you.” She said: “I would not divulge the secret of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” When the Messenger of God ﷺ died, I said to her: “I ask you by the right I have over you, tell me.” She said: “As for now, yes. He whispered to me and said: ‘Gabriel used to review the Qur’an with me once every year, and this year he reviewed it with me twice, and I do not think that is except at the approach of my term. So fear God and be patient, for what an excellent predecessor I am for you.’ So I wept. Then he whispered to me and said: ‘Are you not pleased that you will be the mistress of the women of the believers’—or he said ‘the women of this community’—so I laughed.”"],[18869,"I said to Fatimah daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ: “I saw you lean over the Prophet ﷺ during his illness and weep, then lean over him a second time and laugh.” She said: “I leaned over him and he told me that he was dying, so I wept. Then I leaned over him and he told me that I am the first of his household to join him and that I am the mistress of the women of the people of Paradise except what there is of Maryam daughter of ‘Imran, so I laughed.”"],[18870,"While I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ in a room and he was playing with me and I was playing with him, Fatimah entered. The Messenger of God ﷺ took her by the hand and seated her behind him, and whispered to her something I do not know what it was. I looked at Fatimah weeping. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ turned to me and spoke to me and played with me. Then he turned to her and played with her and whispered to her something. I looked at Fatimah, and there she was laughing. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up and went out. I said to Fatimah: “What did the Messenger of God ﷺ whisper to you?” She said: “Not every time the Messenger of God ﷺ confides in me do I tell you.” I said: “I remind you of God and the womb.” She said: “He told me that he will be taken and that his term has come, so I wept at parting from the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then he turned to me and whispered to me that I am the first of his household to join him, so I laughed at meeting the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[18871,"Fatimah daughter of the Prophet ﷺ entered, and he whispered something to her and she wept. Then he called her for something and she laughed. When he died, I said: “Tell me what made you weep and then made you laugh.” She said: “His own death was announced to him, so I wept. Then he whispered to me and said: ‘You are the first of my family to join me,’ so I laughed.” A’ishah said: “She lived only six months after him.”"],[18872,"The Messenger of God ﷺ called Fatimah during his illness and whispered to her, and she wept. Then he whispered to her and she laughed. I asked her about that: “What did you see—that he whispered to you and you wept, then whispered to you and you laughed?” She said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ told me of his death, so I wept. Then he told me that I am the first of his family to follow him, so I laughed.”"],[18873,"On the authority of Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that she brought al-Hasan and al-Husayn to the Messenger of God ﷺ during the illness in which he died, and said, “O Messenger of God, these are your two sons, so give them something as inheritance.” He said, “As for al-Hasan, he has my awe and my nobility, and as for Husayn, he has my courage and my generosity.”"],[18874,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Every children of a female have a paternal clan to which they belong, except the children of Fatimah, for I am their guardian and their paternal clan.”"],[18875,"Whenever the Messenger of God ﷺ entered the mosque, he said, “O God, forgive me my sins and open for me the gates of Your mercy,” and whenever he left, he said the like, except that he said, “The gates of Your bounty.”"],[18876,"Whenever the Messenger of God ﷺ entered the mosque, he sent blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O God, forgive me my sins and open for me the gates of Your mercy,” and whenever he left, he sent blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O God, forgive me my sins and open for me the gates of Your bounty.”"],[18877,"“Zaynab was the eldest of the daughters of the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[18878,"To the Messenger of God ﷺ was born al-Qasim, who was the eldest of his children, then Zaynab. He said: Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ was married to Abu al-As b. al-Rabi b. Abd al-Uzza b. Abd Shams, and she bore him Ali and Umamah. Ali was being nursed among the Banu Ghadirah, and the Messenger of God ﷺ took him away from them while his father was still a polytheist. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever shares with me in anything, I have more right to it; and any disbeliever who shares with a Muslim in anything, he has more right to it than him.” Al-Zubayr said: Umar b. Abi Bakr al-Mu’ammal narrated to me: Ali b. Abi al-As b. al-Rabi, the son of Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ, died when he had nearly reached puberty, and the Messenger of God ﷺ had seated him behind him on his riding camel on the Day of the Conquest."],[18879,"On the authority of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ asked permission of Abu al-As b. al-Rabi to go to the Prophet ﷺ when the Messenger of God ﷺ had emigrated, and he gave her permission. So she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then Abu al-As b. al-Rabi caught up with her in Madinah, and he sent word to her: “Obtain a guarantee of safety from your father.” So she put her head out from the door of her room while the Messenger of God ﷺ was leading the people in the dawn prayer, and she said, “O people, I am Zaynab, and I have granted protection to Abu al-As.” When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished the prayer, he said, “I did not know of this until I heard it just now. The lowest of the Muslims may grant protection.”"],[18880,"“Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ granted protection to Abu al-As, and the Prophet ﷺ upheld her protection. And Umm Hani bt. Abi Talib granted protection to her brother Aqil, and the Prophet ﷺ upheld her protection.”"],[18881,"Zaynab emigrated to the Messenger of God ﷺ while her husband was a disbeliever. Then the Muslims captured Abu al-As b. al-Rabi, and Zaynab said, “I have granted protection to Abu al-As.” The Prophet ﷺ upheld her protection and said, “The lowest of the Muslims may grant protection.”"],[18882,"Among the captives on the day of Badr was Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Abd Shams, the son-in-law of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the husband of his daughter Zaynab. Abu al-As was one of the notable men of Mecca in wealth and trustworthiness. He belonged to Halah bint Khuwaylid, and Khadijah was his maternal aunt. Khadijah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to marry Zaynab to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not oppose her; that was before revelation came down upon him. She regarded him as being in the place of her own child. When Allah honored His Prophet with prophethood, Khadijah and his daughters believed in him, affirmed him, bore witness that what he had brought was the truth, and followed his religion, while Abu al-As remained firm upon his polytheism. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had married Utbah ibn Abi Lahab to one of his two daughters, Ruqayyah or Umm Kulthum. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ openly confronted Quraysh with the command of Allah and they openly opposed him, they said: You have relieved Muhammad of his concern, so return his daughters to him and occupy him with them. They went to Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi and said: Separate from your wife, and we will marry you to any woman you wish. He said: No, by Allah, then I will not separate from my wife, and I would not love to have, in place of my wife, any woman of Quraysh. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to praise him favorably regarding his relation by marriage, as it has reached me. They then went to the wicked Utbah ibn Abi Lahab and said: Divorce your wife, the daughter of Muhammad, and we will marry you to any woman of Quraysh you wish. He said: If you marry me to the daughter of Aban ibn Said ibn al-As, or the daughter of Said ibn al-As, I will separate from her. So they married him to the daughter of Said ibn al-As, and he separated from her, though the enemy of Allah had not consummated the marriage with her. Allah removed her from his hand as an honor for her and a humiliation for him, and Uthman ibn Affan married her after him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while in Mecca, was not able to declare lawful or unlawful, being overcome in his affair. Islam had already separated Zaynab, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when she became Muslim, from Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi, except that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not able to separate them. So she remained with him upon her Islam while he remained upon his polytheism, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ migrated to Medina, while she was still living with him in Mecca. When Quraysh marched to Badr, Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi marched among them, and he was taken among the captives on the day of Badr, and he was in Medina with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Ibn Ishaq said: Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from his father Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: When the people of Mecca sent for the ransom of their captives, Zaynab, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, sent ransom for Abu al-As, and with it she sent a necklace of hers which Khadijah had given to her when she was brought in to Abu al-As at the time he consummated the marriage with her. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw it, he felt intense tenderness for her, and said: \"If you think it proper to release her captive for her and return her property to her, then do so.\" They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So they released him and returned to her what belonged to her. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had taken from him and made him promise that he would clear the way for Zaynab to come to him, as this was among the conditions he imposed upon him for his release. That was not made public by him nor by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that it would be known. But when Abu al-As left for Mecca and his way was clear, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Zayd ibn Harithah and a man of the Ansar immediately, and said: \"Be at the valley of Yajij until Zaynab passes by you, then accompany her until you bring her to me.\" So they went out to their place, and that was a month after Badr, or thereabouts. When Abu al-As arrived in Mecca, he ordered her to join her father, and she went out openly. Ibn Ishaq said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm said: I was told from Zaynab that she said: While I was preparing in Mecca to join my father, Hind bint Utbah met me and said: O daughter of my uncle, if you need any goods that would help you on your journey, or money by which you may reach your father, then I have what you need, so do not hold back from me, for what enters between men does not enter between women. She said: By Allah, I do not think she said that except intending to do it, but I feared her, so I denied that I intended such a thing. Then I prepared myself. When I finished my preparations, my brother-in-law Kinanah ibn al-Rabi, my husband’s brother, brought me a camel, so I mounted it. He took his bow and his quiver, then went out with her by day, leading her while she was in her howdah. The men of Quraysh spoke of that, so they went out in pursuit of her until they caught up with her at Dhu Tuwa. The first to reach her was Habbar ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Qusayy, and Nafi ibn Abd al-Qays al-Zuhri at Qaynah of Banu Abi Ubaydah ibn Utbah ibn Nafi, the one in Ifriqiyyah. Habbar frightened her with the spear while she was in her howdah, and the woman was pregnant, as they claim; when she was terrified, she miscarried what was in her womb. Her brother-in-law dismounted and scattered his quiver, then said: By Allah, no man will come near me but that I will put an arrow into him. So the people drew back from him. Abu Sufyan came among the chiefs of Quraysh and said: O man, hold back your arrows from us so that we may speak to you. So he held back, and Abu Sufyan approached and addressed him, saying: You have not acted correctly. You went out with a woman openly before the people, while you know our calamity and disaster, and what has come upon us from Muhammad. If his daughter goes out to him openly from among us, the people will think that this is due to humiliation that befell us because of our calamity that occurred, and that it is weakness and feebleness on our part. By my life, we have no need to detain her from her father, but return the woman until the talk dies down and the people say that we have turned her back; then take her out secretly and send her to her father. He said: So he did so, and she stayed for several nights until, when the people had quieted down, he took her out at night until he handed her over to Zayd ibn Harithah and his companion, and they brought her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu al-As remained in Mecca, while Zaynab was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; Islam had separated the two of them. Then, shortly before the conquest, Abu al-As went out as a merchant to Syria. He was a trustworthy man, carrying property of his own and property belonging to men of Quraysh who had entrusted merchandise to him. When he finished his trade, he returned with the caravan, and a detachment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met him. They captured what was with him, while he escaped them in flight. When the detachment arrived with what they had captured of his property, Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi came under cover of night until he entered upon Zaynab, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and sought her protection, so she granted him protection; he had come seeking his property. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out for the morning prayer, as Yazid ibn Ruman narrated to me, he pronounced the takbir and the people pronounced the takbir. Zaynab came out from the women’s section and said: O people, I have granted protection to Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave salams from the prayer, he turned to the people and said: \"O people, did you hear?\" They said: Yes. He said: \"Indeed, by the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I knew nothing of anything that had happened until I heard it; and indeed the least of the Muslims may grant protection on behalf of them.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed until he entered upon his daughter and said: \"O my little daughter, honor his lodging, but do not let him have access to you, for you are not lawful for him.\" Ibn Ishaq said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to the detachment who had seized the property of Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi: \"This man is one of us, as you know, and you have seized property belonging to him. If you do good and return to him what is his, then we would love that; but if you refuse, then it is the fay of Allah which He has granted you, and you have the greater right to it.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, rather, we will return it. So they returned his property to him, until a man would bring a rope, another man would bring an old waterskin and a small waterskin, and one of them would even bring a pack peg, until, when they had returned all of his property to him and he was missing nothing from it, he carried it to Mecca. He returned to every owner of property among Quraysh his property, from those who had entrusted merchandise to him. Then he said: O assembly of Quraysh, is there any property of yours still with me that he has not taken? They said: No, and may Allah reward you with good, for we have found you to be chaste and noble. He said: Then I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger. By Allah, nothing prevented me from accepting Islam with him except fear that you would think I only wanted to consume your wealth. But now that Allah has delivered it to you and I am free of it, I have accepted Islam. Then he set out until he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[18883,"On the authority of A’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that when the Messenger of God ﷺ came to Madinah, his daughter Zaynab left Makkah with Kinanah or the son of Kinanah. They went out after her, and Habbar b. al-Aswad caught up with her and kept thrusting her camel with his spear until he threw her down, and she miscarried what was in her womb and bled. She was carried away, and the Banu Hashim and the Banu Umayyah disputed over her. The Banu Umayyah said, “We have more right to her,” because she was married to their son Abu al-As. She was with Hind bt. Utbah b. Rabiah, and Hind kept saying to her, “This is because of your father.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Zayd b. Harithah, “Will you not go and bring Zaynab?” He said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Take my ring and give it to her.” So Zayd set out, and he kept acting gently until he met a shepherd. He said, “For whom are you herding?” He said, “For Abu al-As.” He said, “Whose sheep are these?” He said, “For Zaynab bt. Muhammad.” He walked with him for a while, then said, “Would you like me to give you something that you will give to her and not mention it to anyone?” He said, “Yes.” So he gave him the ring, and the shepherd went off and brought his sheep in and gave her the ring. She recognized it and said, “Who gave you this?” He said, “A man.” She said, “Where did you leave him?” He said, “At such-and-such a place.” She remained silent until nightfall, then she went out to him. When she came to him, he said to her, “Mount in front of me on my camel.” She said, “No, but you mount in front of me.” So he mounted and she mounted behind him until she arrived. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say, “She is the best of my daughters; she suffered because of me.” This reached Ali b. Husayn, so he went to Urwah and said, “What is this hadith that has reached me from you, that you narrate it diminishing the right of Fatimah?” Urwah said, “By God, I would not like to have everything between the east and the west if I were to diminish a right that belongs to Fatimah. But after this, I will never narrate it again.”"],[18884,"\"These people gathered around a pagan idol. Then suddenly, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appeared and called the people to believe in the oneness of Allah. The day broke and people started to disperse from around him. Then a woman appeared, carrying a cup and a handkerchief. The Prophet ﷺ took it from her, drank from it, performed ablution, and then raised his head towards her and said, 'O my daughter, cover your neck and do not fear any harm for your father.' I asked, 'Who is she?' They said, 'She is Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'\""],[18885,"“A man brought Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ, and two men of Quraysh caught up with him and fought him until they overpowered him and took her away from him, and she fell on a rock and miscarried and bled. Then they took her to Abu Sufyan, and the women of Banu Hashim came to him, and he handed her over to them. Then she came after that as an emigrant, and she remained ill until she died from that illness. They used to consider her a martyr.”"],[18886,"Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ died, and we went out with him. We saw the Messenger of God ﷺ deeply troubled and intensely sad. We said, “We will not speak to him” until we reached the grave, and he had not yet finished its niche. The Messenger of God ﷺ sat down and we sat around him, and he spoke to himself for a little while and kept looking at the sky. Then the grave was finished, and the Messenger of God ﷺ went down into it. I saw him become even sadder. Then he finished and came out, and I saw that he was relieved and smiled. We said, “O Messenger of God, we saw you troubled and sad, and we could not speak to you, and then we saw you relieved. What was that?” He said, “I was remembering the narrowness of the grave and its distress and the weakness of Zaynab, and that was hard for me, so I called upon God to lighten it for her, and He did. She was squeezed with a squeeze that was heard by all between the two horizons except jinn and humans.”"],[18887,"When Zaynab bint Rasul Allah ﷺ died, grief appeared in the Prophet ﷺ, then it was relieved. We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we saw you grieving then it was relieved.' He said, 'I saw Zaynab and her weakness, and that was made easy for her and for me. She was squeezed with a squeeze that reached the two horizons.'"],[18888,"Ruqayyah was with Utbah b. Abi Lahab. When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down {Perish the hands of Abu Lahab}, the Prophet ﷺ asked Utbah to divorce Ruqayyah, and Ruqayyah asked him for that. So he divorced her, and Uthman b. Affan ؓ married Ruqayyah, and she died with him."],[18889,"Ruqayyah bint Rasul Allah ﷺ was with Utbah b. Abi Lahab, but he parted from her. Uthman b. Affan married Ruqayyah in Makkah, and she emigrated with him to the land of Abyssinia. She bore him Abdullah, by whom he was given his kunya. She came with him to Madinah, and he stayed behind from Badr because of her, with the permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted him a share along with the shares of the people of Badr. He said, 'And my reward, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'And your reward.'"],[18890,"Ruqayyah died on the day Zayd b. Harithah, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, came with the good news of Badr."],[18891,"Utaybah b. Abi Lahab married Umm Kulthum bint Rasul Allah ﷺ but did not consummate the marriage until the Prophet ﷺ was sent. Ruqayyah was with his brother Utbah b. Abi Lahab. When Allah ﷻ sent down {Perish the hands of Abu Lahab}, Abu Lahab said to his two sons Utaybah and Utbah, 'My head is forbidden from your heads if you do not divorce the two daughters of Muhammad.' Their mother, bint Harb b. Umayyah, who is the carrier of firewood, said, 'Divorce them, my sons, for they have become dear to him.' So they divorced them. When Utaybah divorced Umm Kulthum, he came to the Prophet ﷺ after parting from Umm Kulthum and said, 'I disbelieve in your religion and I have parted from your daughter. You do not love me and I do not love you.' Then he attacked him and tore the shirt of the Prophet ﷺ while he was leaving for Syria as a merchant. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, I ask Allah to set His dog upon you.' He went out in a trading party of Quraysh until they stopped at a place in Syria called al-Zarqa at night. A lion surrounded them that night, and Utaybah began to say, 'Woe to my mother! By Allah, it will eat me just as Muhammad prayed against me. Ibn Abi Kabshah made me weep while he is in Makkah and I am in Syria.' The lion came at him from among the people, seized his head, and crushed him with a bite, killing him. Zuhayr b. al-Ala said: Hisham b. Urwah narrated to us from his father that when the lion surrounded them that night, they went away and slept, and Utaybah was placed in their midst. The lion came stepping over until it seized Utaybah's head and crushed him. Uthman b. Affan, may Allah have mercy on him, succeeded after Ruqayyah to Umm Kulthum, ؓ ."],[18892,"Umm Kulthum bint Rasul Allah ﷺ was with Utaybah b. Abi Lahab, the one whom the lion ate, but he parted from her. When Ruqayyah died with Uthman, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Kulthum to him, and she died with him without bearing him any child. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'If I had ten, I would marry them all to you.'"],[18893,"Uthman married Umm Kulthum bint Rasul Allah ﷺ, and she died with him without bearing him any child."],[18894,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood by the grave of his second daughter who had been with Uthman and said, 'Is there any father of a widow? Is there any brother of a widow? Uthman married her. If they had been ten, I would have married them all to Uthman. I did not marry him except by revelation from heaven.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met Uthman at the door of the mosque and said, 'O Uthman, this is Jibril informing me that Allah ﷻ has married Umm Kulthum to you with a dowry like Ruqayyah's and with companionship like hers.'"],[18895,"He informed him that he saw on Umm Kulthum bint Rasul Allah ﷺ a striped silk garment."],[18896,"He saw on Zaynab bint Rasul Allah ﷺ a striped silk garment. Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani said: This is how Ma'mar narrated it, as Zaynab, and he erred. The correct is Umm Kulthum."],[18897,"He informed him that he heard Abu Qatadah say: The Prophet ﷺ used to pray while Umamah bint Zaynab bint al-Nabi ﷺ, who is the daughter of Abu al-As b. al-Rabi b. Abd al-Uzza, was on his neck. When he bowed, he put her down, and when he stood from prostration, he took her and put her back on his neck."],[18898,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us, all from Malik b. Anas, from Amir b. Abdullah b. al-Zubayr, from Amr b. Sulaym, from Abu Qatadah: The Prophet ﷺ prayed while carrying Umamah bint Abi al-As b. al-Rabi. When he bowed, he put her down, and when he stood, he carried her."],[18899,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ leading the people in prayer while Umamah bint Abi al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was on his shoulder. When he bowed he put her down, and when he rose from prostration he returned her."],[18900,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying while carrying Umamah bint Abi al-‘As on his neck. When he bowed he put her down, and when he rose he raised her."],[18901,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to prayer carrying Umamah bint Abi al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ on his shoulder—her mother was Zaynab bint the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he bowed he put her down from his shoulder, and when he finished his prostration he carried her on his shoulder. He continued doing that with her until he finished his prayer."],[18902,"The Prophet ﷺ used to come out carrying Zaynab's daughter on his shoulder while leading the people in prayer. When he stood he carried her, and when he bowed he put her down."],[18903,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying while Umamah bint Abi al-‘As was on his shoulder. When he bowed he put her down, and when he stood he carried her."],[18904,"He heard Abu Qatadah saying, \"While we were sitting in the mosque, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us carrying Umamah, the daughter of Abu Al-As, on his shoulder. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed while she was on his shoulder, and when he prostrated, he put her down until he finished his prayer.\""],[18905,"He heard Abu Qatadah say: \"While we were sitting in the mosque waiting for the prayer, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us carrying his daughter's daughter Umamah bint Abi al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ on his shoulder—her mother was Zaynab. He was carrying her on his shoulder, saying the takbir while she was on his shoulder. When he bowed he placed her on the ground, and when he stood he returned her to his shoulder until he finished his prayer, doing that.\""],[18906,"I heard Abu Qatadah al-Ansari say: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying with the people while Umamah bint Abi al-‘As was on his shoulder. When he prostrated he put her down.\""],[18907,"\"While we were sitting in the mosque waiting for the prayer, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with Umamah bint Abi al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ on his shoulder—her mother was Zaynab bint the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he bowed he placed her on the ground, and when he stood he returned her to his shoulder until he finished his prayer, doing that with her.\""],[18908,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying with his daughter's daughter Umaymah—or Umamah bint Abi al-‘As. He would carry her when he stood and put her down when he sat, until he finished his prayer."],[18909,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying while carrying Umamah bint Zaynab bint the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, daughter of Abi al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘. When he bowed he put her down, and when he stood he carried her, until he finished his prayer."],[18910,"The prayer in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed while carrying Umamah was the Fajr prayer."],[18911,"A necklace of onyx studded with gold was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and his wives were gathered in a room, all of them, while Umamah bint Abi al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was a young girl playing with dust in a corner of the room. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"How do you see this?\" We looked at it and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we have never seen anything more beautiful or more wonderful than this.\" He said, \"Hand it back to me.\" When he took it he said, \"By Allah, I will place it on the neck of the most beloved of the household to me.\" ‘A’ishah said: The earth darkened between me and him, fearing that he would place it on the neck of someone other than me among them, and I saw that they were all struck by the same thing that struck me, and we all fell silent. Then he came with it and placed it on the neck of Umamah bint Abi al-‘As, and we were relieved."],[18912,"And Abu al-'As b. al-Rabi' bequeathed his daughter Umamah to al-Zubayr b. al-'Awwam along with his estate, so al-Zubayr married her to 'Ali b. Abi Talib after the death of Fatimah bint Rasul Allah ﷺ. Fatimah ؓ had enjoined that upon him. 'Ali b. Abi Talib was killed while Umamah bint Abi al-'As was with him, and she did not bear him any child. Umm al-Haytham al-Nakha'iyyah said concerning that:"],[18913,"\"Abu al-Hayyaj b. Abi Sufyan b. al-Harith b. 'Abd al-Muttalib succeeded to [the marriage of] Umamah bint Abi al-'As b. al-Rabi'—and her mother was Zaynab bint Rasul Allah ﷺ.\""],[18914,"Umamah bint Abi al-'As—her mother was Zaynab bint Rasul Allah ﷺ—was married to 'Ali b. Abi Talib. When he died leaving her, he had said to her: \"Do not marry; and if you desire marriage, then do not deviate from the advice of al-Mughirah b. Nawfal.\" Then Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan proposed to her. She came to al-Mughirah seeking his counsel, and he said to her: \"I am better for you than he, so entrust your affair to me.\" She did so. He invited some men and married her. Umamah bint Abi al-'As died while married to al-Mughirah b. Nawfal, and she did not bear him any child. Thus Zaynab has no descendants."],[18915,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Khadijah during her final illness and said to her: “What I see of you grieves me, O Khadijah, but Allah may bring much good out of what grieves (you). Do you know that Allah has married me along with you in Paradise to Maryam bint ʿImran, Kulthum the sister of Musa, and Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh?” She said, “Has Allah done that, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Yes.” She said, “May it be with harmony and children.”"],[18916,"“When Khadijah died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was so deeply grieved by it that people feared for him, until he married Aishah.”"],[18917,"“Khadijah was the first to embrace Islam with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, along with ʿAli b. Abi Talib.”"],[18918,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned Khadijah bint Khuwaylid. Her father desired to marry her to him. She prepared food and drink and invited her father and a group from Quraysh. They ate and drank until they became intoxicated. Then Khadijah said to her father: \"Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah has proposed to me; arise and marry me to him.\" So he married her to him. She perfumed him and dressed him in a fine garment, for such was their practice with fathers when they gave their daughters in marriage. When the intoxication left him, he looked and saw himself perfumed and wearing a fine garment. He said: \"What is the matter with me?\" She said: \"You married me to Muhammad.\" He said: \"I married you to the orphan of Abu Talib? No, by my life!\" Khadijah said: \"Are you not ashamed? You want to make a fool of yourself, informing Quraysh and the people that you were drunk.\" She kept at him until he consented."],[18919,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married fifteen women. Of them, six were from Quraysh, one from the allies of Quraysh, seven from the rest of the Arabs, and one from the Children of Israel. In the Jahiliyyah, he married only one of them, and only she bore him children. The first woman he married in the Jahiliyyah was Khadijah bint Khuwaylid b. Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Qusayy. Before him, she had been married to 'Atiq b. 'A'idh b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar b. Makhzum. Then after 'Atiq, Abu Halah Hind b. Zurarah b. Nabbash b. Habib b. Surad b. Salamah b. Jarwah b. Usayd b. 'Amr b. Tamim succeeded to her marriage. She bore him Hind b. Hind.\" Zuhayr said: Yunus b. 'Ubayd said: Hind passed through al-Basrah while traveling, and he died there; on that day neither market nor pasture was held. The Prophet ﷺ married her after those two. She bore him in the Jahiliyyah 'Abd Manaf, and she bore him in Islam two boys and four girls."],[18920,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , married Khadijah bint Khuwaylid in Makkah. Before that, she was married to Atiq Ibn Abi A'idh Al-Makhzumi. Then he married Aisha in Makkah. He did not marry a virgin other than her. Then he married Hafsa bint Umar, who was previously married to Khunays Ibn Hudhafah As-Sahmi. Then he married Sawda bint Zam'a, who was previously married to As-Sakan Ibn Amr, the brother of Bani 'Amir Ibn Lu'ayy. Then he married Umm Habiba, the daughter of Abu Sufyan, who was previously married to Ubaydullah Ibn Jahsh Al-Asadi, Asad Ibn Khuzaymah. Then he married Zaynab bint Jahsh, who was previously married to Zayd Ibn Harithah. Then he married Maymuna bint Al-Harith and he took Juwayriya bint Al-Harith, from the Banu Mustaliq tribe as a captive in his raid when he demolished the Mannat Al-Muraysi. And he took Safiyya bint Huyayy bin Akhtab from the Banu Nadir tribe. She was among those whom Allah gave him as spoils of war. He divided her among his companions and offered her to Rayhana bint Zayd from the Banu Quraiza tribe, then he emancipated her and she reunited with her family while still maintaining her seclusion. The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , divorced Al-Aliyah bint Zabyan and separated from the sister of Banu Amr bin Kilab and the sister of Banu Al-Jawna Al-Kindiyyah because of the beauty that was in them. Zainab bint Khuzaymah Al-Hilaliyyah passed away while the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , was alive. It has reached us that Al-`Aliyah bint Zabyan got married before Allah prohibited his wives. She married her cousin from her own people and bore children with him."],[18921,"\"The first woman whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married was Khadijah. Then he married Sawdah bint Zam'ah. Then he contracted marriage with 'A'ishah in Makkah and consummated it with her in Madinah. In Madinah he married Zaynab bint Khuzaymah al-Hilaliyyah. Then he married Umm Salamah. Then he married Juwayriyyah bint al-Harith; she was among those whom Allah granted him as spoils. Then he married Maymunah bint al-Harith—she was the one who gave herself to the Prophet ﷺ. Then he married Safiyyah bint Huyayy; she was among those whom Allah granted him as spoils on the day of Khaybar. Then he married Zaynab bint Jahsh, who had been the wife of Zayd b. Harithah. Zaynab bint Khuzaymah died while married to the Prophet ﷺ, and Khadijah also died in Makkah. He married a woman from Banu Kilab of Banu Rabi'ah called al-'Aliyah bint Zabyan, and he divorced her when she was brought in to him.\""],[18922,"That the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were: Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, 'A'ishah bint Abi Bakr, Umm Salamah bint Abi Umayyah, Hafsah bint 'Umar, Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, Juwayriyyah bint al-Harith, Maymunah bint al-Harith, Zaynab bint Jahsh, Sawdah bint Zam'ah, and Safiyyah bint Huyayy—until there were gathered with him nine besides Khadijah, including al-Kindiyyah from Banu al-Jawn and al-'Aliyah bint Zabyan from Banu 'Amir of Banu Kilab, and Zaynab bint Khuzaymah, a woman from Banu Hilal. Al-Zuhri said: 'Urwah b. al-Zubayr informed me: When al-Kindiyyah was brought in to the Prophet ﷺ, she said: \"I seek refuge in Allah from you.\" He said: \"You have sought refuge in a Mighty One. Join your family.\""],[18923,"Ibn Abi Mulaykah and 'Amr b. Dinar said: Nine women were gathered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, including Safiyyah, besides Khadijah; all of them died while he was still alive. 'Uthman b. Abi Sulayman added two women besides the nine, both from Banu 'Amir b. Sa'sa'ah, both of whom he married. One of them was called Umm al-Masakin, and she was the best of his wives to the poor. He married a woman from Banu al-Jawn, but when she came to him she sought refuge from him, so he divorced her. He married a woman from Kindah but did not consummate the marriage with her. After the Prophet ﷺ she married, and 'Umar separated them and beat her husband. She said: \"Fear Allah, O 'Umar! If I am one of the Mothers of the Believers, then impose the veil upon me and give me what you have given them.\" He said: \"That is not the case.\" She said: \"Then let me marry.\" He said: \"No, by the blessing, and I will not entice anyone to that.\""],[18924,"The mother of all the sons and daughters of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—other than Ibrahim—was Khadijah bint Khuwaylid. In the Jahiliyyah she was called al-Tahirah, daughter of Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Qusayy. Her mother was Fatimah bint Za'idah bint Jundub—he is al-Asamm b. Sakhr b. 'Abd Ma'is b. 'Amir b. Lu'ayy. Her mother was Halah bint 'Abd Manaf b. al-Harith b. Munqidh b. 'Amr b. Ma'is b. 'Amr b. Lu'ayy. Her mother was al-'Ariqah, whose name was Qilabah bint Sa'd b. Sahm b. 'Amr b. Husays b. Ka'b b. Lu'ayy. Hibban b. 'Abd Manaf, the full brother of Halah, was the one who shot Sa'd b. Mu'adh, may Allah have mercy on him, on the day of the Trench, saying: \"Take it, for I am the son of al-'Ariqah!\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah make your face sweat in the Fire.\" The arrow struck Sa'd's median vein—may Allah have mercy on Sa'd—and he died as a martyr. Before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Khadijah bint Khuwaylid had been married to 'Atiq b. 'A'idh b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr b. Makhzum, and she bore him Hind b. 'Atiq. Then Abu Halah Malik b. Nabbash b. Zurarah b. Wafdan b. Habib b. Salamah b. 'Adi of Banu Usayd b. 'Amr b. Tamim, an ally of Banu 'Abd al-Dar b. Qusayy, succeeded to her marriage. She bore him Hind b. Abi Halah. So Hind b. 'Atiq, and Hind and Halah, the sons of Abu Halah Malik b. Nabbash b. Zurarah, were half-brothers of the children of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Khadijah bint Khuwaylid through their mother."],[18925,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Khadijah in Makkah. She was the first woman he married. Before him, she had been married to Abu Halah al-Tamimi. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her when he was twenty-one years old, and she died seven years after his mission began.\" Al-Zubayr said: 'Umar b. Abi Bakr al-Mu'ammili narrated to me that 'Amr b. Asad married Khadijah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her when he was twenty-five years old, while Quraysh was building the Ka'bah. Al-Zubayr said: Muhammad b. Hasan narrated to me from Khalid b. Isma'il from Ibn Jurayj who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married when he was thirty-seven years old. Al-Zubayr said: Muhammad b. Hasan narrated to me from 'Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Yahya b. 'Urwah from his father who said: 'Amr b. Asad said: \"Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah is proposing to Khadijah bint Khuwaylid. This stallion—his nose is not to be struck [i.e., he is no one to be refused].\" Al-Zubayr said: Muhammad b. Hasan narrated to me from Muhammad b. Fulayh from Yazid b. 'Iyad from Ibn Shihab who said: Khadijah bint Khuwaylid was married to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before the Qur'an was revealed to him. Then the Qur'an was revealed to him while she was his wife. She was the first to believe the Prophet ﷺ and have faith in him. She died in Makkah three years before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left for Madinah."],[18926,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not marry any other woman while Khadijah was alive until she died.\""],[18927,"I heard al-Zuhri say: \"The Prophet ﷺ did not marry any other woman while Khadijah was alive until she died.\""],[18928,"“Khadijah died three years or so before the Prophet ﷺ left for Madinah, and he married Aishah close to Khadijah’s death. He did not marry another wife while Khadijah was alive.”"],[18929,"“Khadijah died in Makkah three years before the Hijrah. She was the first of the women and men to believe in the Prophet ﷺ. He married no other woman in the pre-Islamic period, and none of his children came from any woman but her.”"],[18930,"“Khadijah died three years before the Prophet ﷺ left (Makkah).”"],[18931,"“Khadijah died three years before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ emigrated.”"],[18932,"\"Khadijah passed away before the obligation of prayers was ordained.\""],[18933,"“I came to Makkah to buy perfume and fragrance for my family, and I stayed with al-ʿAbbas b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib, who was a merchant. While I was with him at sunrise, I saw a young man come and look up at the sky, then turn his gaze toward the Kaʿbah. Soon a boy came and stood to his right, and then a woman came and stood behind them. The young man said ‘Allahu akbar’ and the other two said ‘Allahu akbar’; he bowed and they bowed; he prostrated and they prostrated. I said, ‘O ʿAbbas, this is something momentous.’ Al-ʿAbbas said, ‘Momentous indeed. Do you know who the young man is?’ I said, ‘No.’ He said, ‘This is Muhammad b. ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib, my brother’s son. Do you know who the woman is?’ I said, ‘No.’ He said, ‘This is Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid b. Asad b. ʿAbd al-ʿUzza, the leading woman of Quraysh, the wife of my brother’s son. And this is ʿAli b. Abi Talib, my brother’s son. My brother’s son claims that his Lord, the Lord of the heavens and the earth, has commanded him to this religion. By Allah, I know of no one on the face of the earth on this religion except these three.’”"],[18934,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew four lines on the ground. Then he said, “Do you know what these are?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “The best women of Paradise are: Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, Fatimah bt. Muhammad, Maryam bt. ʿImran, and Asiyah bt. Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh.”"],[18935,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The foremost women of Paradise are Maryam bt. ʿImran, then Fatimah bt. Muhammad, then Khadijah, then Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh.”"],[18936,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Suffice you among the women of all the worlds: Maryam bt. ʿImran, Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, Fatimah bt. Muhammad, and Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh.”"],[18937,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The best of its women is Maryam bt. ʿImran, and the best of its women is Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid.”"],[18938,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The best of its women are Maryam bt. ʿImrān and Khadījah bt. Khuwaylid.”"],[18939,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about Khadījah bt. Khuwaylid. He said: “I saw her on a river among the rivers of Paradise, in a house of hollow pearl; there is no idle talk in it and no toil.”"],[18940,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting with Khadījah, Jibrīl ﷺ came to him and said: “O Muhammad, convey to Khadījah greetings of peace from me, and give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is no harm and no toil.”"],[18941,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave Khadījah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is no clamor and no toil."],[18942,"From Abū Hurayrah and Abū Saʿīd: They said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave Khadījah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is no clamor and no toil.”"],[18943,"Jibrīl came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “Here is Khadījah coming to you with a vessel containing condiment, food, and drink. When she comes to you, convey to her greetings of peace from her Lord, and give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is no clamor and no toil.”"],[18944,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave Khadījah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is no clamor and no toil."],[18945,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Jibrīl said to me: ‘Give Khadījah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is no clamor and no toil.’”"],[18946,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was commanded to give Khadījah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is no clamor and no toil.”"],[18947,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to mention Khadījah often, so I said: “How often you mention Khadījah! Allah has replaced Khadījah for you with an old woman with reddish gums who died long ago.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry with an anger like I never saw him become angry, and he said: “Allah granted me from her what He did not grant me from any of you.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, forgive me, may Allah forgive you. By Allah, you will never hear me mention Khadījah after this day with anything you dislike.”"],[18948,"I was never jealous of any wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as I was jealous of Khadījah, and she had died three years before he married me, because of what I used to hear of his mentioning her. His Lord commanded him to give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, and indeed, when he slaughtered a sheep, he would keep sending portions of it to Khadījah’s friends."],[18949,"I was never jealous of anyone as I was jealous of Khadījah because of what I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention of her. She said: “Allah commanded him to give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl.”"],[18950,"I did not feel jealous of any of the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as I felt jealous of Khadijah because of how often he ﷺ mentioned her."],[18951,"Halah bt. Khuwaylid, the sister of Khadijah, asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ. He likened her asking permission to Khadijah's asking permission and was gladdened by that. He said, 'O Allah, Halah!' I became jealous, and I have not been jealous of anyone as I was jealous of Khadijah. Minjab added in his narration: 'because of how often he mentioned her. He married me three years after her.'"],[18952,"I did not feel jealous of any woman as I felt jealous of Khadijah, and that is only because of how often the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned her."],[18953,"When the Prophet ﷺ was brought something, he would say, 'Take it to so-and-so, for she was a friend of Khadijah.'"],[18954,"From the Prophet ﷺ, Aishah said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned Khadijah, he never tired of praising her and asking forgiveness for her. One day he mentioned her and jealousy overcame me until I said, 'Allah has compensated you with someone better than an old woman.' She said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ become angry with such anger that I sank into myself. I said to myself, 'O Allah, if You remove the anger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from me, I will never mention her with anything bad as long as I live.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw what I had experienced, he said, 'What did you say? By Allah, she believed in me when the people disbelieved in me, she affirmed my truthfulness when the people called me a liar, and she was granted children from me when you were deprived of them from me.' He then went back and forth to me for a month."],[18955,"When the Prophet ﷺ mentioned Khadijah, he would praise her. I said, 'Why do you mention her when Allah has replaced her for you with someone better?' He said, 'Allah has not replaced her for me with anyone better than her. She believed in me when the people called me a liar, she shared her wealth with me when the people deprived me, and Allah granted me children from her when He did not grant me from any other.'"],[18956,"A woman entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Food was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he began eating from it and placing it before her. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do not keep your hands busy.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'This woman used to visit us in the days of Khadijah. Indeed, honor or preservation of the covenant is part of faith.' When he mentioned Khadijah, what takes hold of women from jealousy took hold of me, so I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah has replaced for you an old woman with a young one.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry and then said, 'What is my fault if Allah granted her children from me and did not grant you?' I said, 'By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never mention her after this except with good.'"],[18957,"Gabriel was with the Prophet ﷺ when Khadijah came. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'O Gabriel, this is Khadijah.' Gabriel ﷺ said, 'Convey to her greetings from Allah and from me.'"],[18958,"Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at Hira. He said, 'This is Khadijah. She has come with a dish of dates mixed with butter (hays) in her small basket. Say to her that Allah conveys greetings to her.' When she came, he said to her, 'Gabriel informed me of you and of the hays in your basket before you arrived, and said that Allah conveys greetings to her.' She said, 'He is Peace, and from Him is peace, and upon Gabriel be peace.'"],[18959,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Khadijah, 'I hear a voice and see a light, and I fear that I may be possessed.' Khadijah said, 'Allah would not do that to you, O son of Abdullah.' She then went to Waraqah b. Nawfal and mentioned that to him. He said, 'If he is truthful, then this is a namus (angel of revelation) like the namus of Moses. If he is sent while I am alive, I will strengthen him, help him, and assist him.'"],[18960,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, where are my children from you?' He said, 'In Paradise.' I said, 'Without any deeds?' He said, 'Allah knows best what they would have done.' I said, 'Then where are my children before you?' He said, 'In the Fire.' I said, 'Without any deeds?' He said, 'Allah knew what they would have done.'"],[18961,"Mus'ab b. Abdullah narrated to me."],[18962,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married A'ishah when she was six years old, and she was brought to him when she was nine, and her dolls were with her, and he died when she was eighteen."],[18963,"A'ishah died in the year fifty-seven."],[18964,"Do not bury me with them; bury me with my companions in al-Baqi'. I will never be pure again."],[18965,"The Prophet ﷺ adopted me, Um Abdullah, and I have never had any children."],[18966,"To the Prophet ﷺ: All your wives have a kunyah except me. The Prophet ﷺ said to her, 'Take the kunyah Umm 'Abd Allah.' So she was called Umm 'Abd Allah until she died, though she never gave birth."],[18967,"She said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not give me a kunyah? All your wives have one. He said, 'Yes, take the kunyah by your son 'Abd Allah.' So she was given the kunyah Umm 'Abd Allah."],[18968,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, all your wives have a kunyah except me. He said, 'You are Umm 'Abd Allah.'"],[18969,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave A'ishah a kunyah though she had no child."],[18970,"The Prophet ﷺ married A'ishah bt. Abi Bakr al-Siddiq. He did not marry any other virgin. She was then six years old. They claimed that Gabriel said, 'This is your wife,' before he married her. He married her in Makkah before the Hijrah and after Khadijah's death. Then he consummated the marriage with her in Madinah when she was nine, and he died when she was eighteen."],[18971,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I was brought a girl in a piece of silk after Khadijah's death, and it was you.' I said: If this is from Allah, He will bring it to pass. Then I was brought a girl again in a piece of silk, and I uncovered her, and it was you. I said: If this is from Allah, He will bring it to pass. A'ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me after Khadijah's death before his departure from Makkah, when I was seven or six years old. When we came to Madinah, women came to me while I was playing on a swing, and I had bangs. They prepared me and adorned me, then they brought me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was nine."],[18972,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I was brought you in a piece of silk in a dream on three nights, and it was said: This is your wife. I uncovered the cloth, and it was you. I said: If this is from Allah, He will bring it to pass.'"],[18973,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I saw you in a dream twice. A man was carrying you in a piece of silk and saying: This is your wife; uncover her. So I uncovered her, and it was you. I said: If this is from Allah, He will bring it to pass.'"],[18974,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was seven, and I was presented to him when I was nine, and he died when I was eighteen."],[18975,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was seven years old, and he consummated the marriage with me when I was nine."],[18976,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was seven, and I was taken to him when I was nine years old. He came in to me while I was playing with dolls, and I had girlfriends who played with me. Sometimes they felt shy of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would send them to me."],[18977,"The Prophet ﷺ married her when she was six years old and consummated the marriage with her when she was nine years old, and she remained with him for nine years."],[18978,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was six years old and consummated the marriage with me when I was nine years old."],[18979,"The Prophet ﷺ married her when she was six, and she was taken to him when she was nine, and she stayed with him for nine years."],[18980,"The Prophet ﷺ married her three years before his departure from Makkah, or close to that, and he married her when she was six years old. Then he consummated the marriage with her after his arrival in Madinah, and she was nine years old on the day of consummation."],[18981,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her when she was seven and consummated the marriage with her when she was nine, and he died leaving her when she was eighteen."],[18982,"I married the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was six years old, and he consummated the marriage with me when I was nine years old."],[18983,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me at nine years of age, and I accompanied him for nine years."],[18984,"The Prophet ﷺ married her when she was seven years old and consummated the marriage with her when she was nine."],[18985,"I was taken to the Prophet ﷺ when I was nine years old, and I stayed with him for nine years."],[18986,"The Prophet ﷺ married Aisha when she was nine years old, and she remained with him for nine years."],[18987,"Khawlah bt. Hakim b. Umayyah b. al-Awqas, the wife of Uthman b. Maz'un, and that was in Makkah: \"O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry?\" He said, \"Whom?\" She said, \"If you wish, a virgin, and if you wish, a previously married woman.\" He said, \"Who is the virgin?\" She said, \"The daughter of the most beloved of Allah's creation to you, Aishah bt. Abi Bakr.\" He said, \"And who is the previously married woman?\" She said, \"Sawdah bt. Zam'ah; she has believed in you and followed you in what you are upon.\" He said, \"Go and mention them both to me.\" So she came and entered the house of Abu Bakr and found Umm Ruman, the mother of Aishah, and said, \"O Umm Ruman, what good and blessing has Allah brought upon you! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has sent me to seek Aishah's hand for him.\" She said, \"I wish you would wait for Abu Bakr, for he is coming.\" So Abu Bakr came and she said, \"O Abu Bakr, what good and blessing has Allah brought upon you! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has sent me to seek Aishah's hand for him.\" He said, \"Is she suitable for him when she is only the daughter of his brother?\" So he sent me back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I mentioned that to him. He said, \"Go back to him and say to him: You are my brother in Islam and I am your brother, and your daughter is suitable for me.\" So she went to Abu Bakr, and he said to Khawlah, \"Call the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for me.\" He came, and he gave her in marriage to him. On that day I was a girl of six years.\""],[18988,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was a girl of six years, and consummated the marriage with me when I was a girl of nine years."],[18989,"The Prophet ﷺ married her when she was nine years old, and he died when she was eighteen years old."],[18990,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ emigrated, he left us and left his daughters behind. When he settled in Madinah, he sent Zayd b. Harithah and with him Abu Rafi', his freedman, and gave them two camels and five hundred dirhams which he took from Abu Bakr, with which they were to buy what they needed of riding animals. Abu Bakr sent with them Abdullah b. Urayqit al-Du'ali with two or three camels, and he wrote to Abdullah b. Abi Bakr to transport his family: the mother of Abu Bakr, Umm Ruman, myself, my brother, and Asma', the wife of al-Zubayr. They set out together until they reached Qudayd. Zayd b. Harithah bought three camels with those five hundred dirhams, then they all entered Makkah and found Talhah b. Ubayd Allah intending to emigrate. We all set out together, and Zayd and Abu Rafi' departed with Fatimah, Umm Kulthum, and Sawdah bt. Zam'ah. Zayd carried Umm Ayman and her children Ayman and Usamah. They accompanied us until when we were at al-Bayda' of Namir, my camel bolted while I was in a litter with my mother in it. My mother began saying, \"Oh my daughter! Oh my bride!\" until our camel was caught, and it had descended from the mountain pass, the pass of Harsha, and Allah granted safety. Then we arrived in Madinah, and I alighted with the family of Abu Bakr. The Prophet ﷺ came down to me, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at that time was building the mosque and some houses around the mosque, and he lodged his family in them. We stayed in them for some days. Then Abu Bakr said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what prevents you from consummating marriage with your wife?\" He said, \"The bridal gift.\" So Abu Bakr gave him twelve uqiyah and a nashsh, and he sent it to us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consummated the marriage with me in this house of mine in which I am now, which is the one in which he died and was buried. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ brought Sawdah bt. Zam'ah with him into one of those houses, and he used to stay with her. The Prophet ﷺ had married me while I was playing with the girls, and I was not told that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had married me until my mother took me and confined me in the house. Then it occurred to me that I had been married, but I did not ask her until she herself told me."],[18991,"The Prophet ﷺ proposed to Aishah to Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr had already given her in marriage to Jubayr b. Mut'im. So he dissolved that, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her when she was a girl of six years. He left her for three years, then consummated the marriage with her when she was a girl of nine years."],[18992,"I adorned Aishah for the Prophet ﷺ until I brought her in to him. When she entered upon him, we were brought a vessel of milk, and the Prophet ﷺ drank from it, then handed it to Aishah. She turned away, so I said, \"Take it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" She took it and drank, then handed it to me and I drank. I began rotating the vessel so that I might find the spot from which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had drunk. Then I handed it to a woman with me, and she said, \"I do not desire it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not combine lying and hunger.\""],[18993,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me while I was wearing a hawf, and no sooner had he married me than shyness was cast upon me. Sufyan said: A hawf is a garment of leather straps that the Bedouins clothe their daughters with."],[18994,"They fattened me with everything, but I did not gain weight, so they fattened me with cucumber and fresh dates, and I gained weight."],[18995,"When the Prophet ﷺ married me, my family fattened me with everything, but I did not gain weight, so they fed me cucumber and fresh dates, and I gained weight upon that in the best manner."],[18996,"My mother approached me with everything with which women are approached, but I did not respond to that. So they fed me cucumber and dates when they wanted to present me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I responded in the best manner."],[18997,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me, and I was brought in to him in Shawwal. So which of the Prophet's ﷺ wives was more favored with him than I?\" He said: And she used to like her women to enter upon their husbands in Shawwal."],[18998,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was a girl of six years, and consummated the marriage with me when I was a girl of nine years, and he consummated the marriage with me in Shawwal. So which of your women was more favored with him than I? And she used to like her women to enter upon their husbands in Shawwal."],[18999,"She said about one who dislikes marriage in Shawwal: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me in Shawwal, and I was entered upon him in Shawwal.'"],[19000,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Aisha bint Abu Bakr in Shawwal and consummated the marriage with her in Medina during Shawwal, after sixteen months of his migration to Medina. Aisha passed away on the night of Tuesday, in the seventeenth night of Ramadan, after the Witr prayer, in the fifty-eighth year. She was buried on the same night."],[19001,"On the authority of Nafi and others from the people of knowledge, they said: \"We performed prayer upon Aisha and Umm Salamah, the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, in the middle of Al-Baqi' cemetery, and Abu Hurayrah was the Imam (leading the prayer) on the day that we prayed upon Aisha. Abdullah ibn Umar attended, and Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr and Abdurrahman ibn Abi Bakr entered the grave of Aisha. She passed away in the year sixty-eight during the month of Ramadan, seventeen nights had passed after the Witr prayer, and she was buried on the same night.\""],[19002,"The Prophet ﷺ 'unveiled Aisha in her family's home before he consummated the marriage with her.'"],[19003,"I was given qualities no other woman was given: he married me when I was six years old, and the angel brought him my image in his palm, so he looked at it. He consummated the marriage with me when I was nine years old. I saw Jibril, and no woman besides me saw him. I was the most beloved of his wives to him, and my father was the most beloved of his companions to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell ill with his final illness, and no one attended him but me and the angels."],[19004,"I was given seven things that none of the Prophet's ﷺ wives were given: I was among the people most beloved to him in person, and my father was among the people most beloved to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me as a virgin, and he did not marry any virgin other than me. Jibril used to descend upon him with revelation while I was with him under a blanket, and that was not done for anyone besides me. I had two days and two nights, while his wives had one day and one night. And my innocence was sent down from heaven, and groups of people almost perished because of me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken in death between my chest and neck."],[19005,"I was given six things that no woman after Maryam was given: Jibril descended with my image in his palm when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was commanded to marry me. He married me as a virgin, and he did not marry any virgin other than me. My innocence was sent down from heaven. And he mentioned the hadith similarly."],[19006,"'There are seven qualities in me that were not in any other woman except what Allah gave Maryam bt. Imran, and by Allah I do not say this to boast over any of my companions.' Abdullah b. Safwan said to her, 'And what are they, O Mother of the Believers?' She said, 'The angel descended with my image. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was seven, and I was given to him when I was nine. He married me as a virgin, and no one among the people shared me with him. Revelation used to come to him while I and he were under one blanket. I was the most beloved of people to him, and the daughter of the most beloved of people to him. Verses of the Quran were sent down concerning me, and the ummah almost perished because of me. I saw Jibril, and no one among his wives besides me saw him. He was taken in death in my house, and no one attended him but me and the angel.'"],[19007,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; Isa b. Yunus narrated to us from Umar b. Sa'id from Ibn Abi Mulaykah that Abu Amr Dhakwan, the freed slave of Aisha, informed him that Aisha said: 'Among the blessings Allah bestowed upon me is that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken in death in my house, on my day, and between my chest and neck, and that Allah joined my saliva with his at the moment of death.' She said, 'My brother Abd al-Rahman entered upon me while I was supporting the Messenger of Allah ﷺ against my chest, and in his hand was a siwak. He began looking at it, so I said, \"Shall I take it for you?\" He gestured with his head, yes. So I softened it for him, then I handed it to him, and he passed it over his teeth. In front of him was a small leather water container—or she said a wooden bowl—with water in it. He began dipping his hand in it, then wiping his face and saying, \"There is no god but Allah. Death has its agonies.\" Then he raised his hand and said, \"In the highest company,\" until he was taken, and his hand fell ﷺ.'"],[19008,"'Among Allah's blessings upon me and His good favor toward me is that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died in my house and on my day, and was taken between my chest and neck, and my saliva was joined with his on the day he was taken.' He said: I said to her, 'This being in your house and on your day and between your chest and neck, how was your saliva joined with his?' She said, 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abu Bakr entered upon me on the morning of Monday with a fresh siwak in his hand. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ staring at it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was fond of the siwak.' So I said, 'Split it and hand it to me.' He split it in two and handed it to me. I chewed it to soften it, then I put it in the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ mouth, and he used it as a siwak. Thus my saliva was joined with his.'"],[19009,"She said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt pain that day when he returned from the mosque, so he lay down in my lap. A man from the family of Abu Bakr entered upon me with a green siwak in his hand.' She said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at his hand with a look, and I knew he wanted it. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, would you like me to give you this siwak?\" He said, \"Yes.\"' She said, 'So I took it and chewed it for him until I softened it, then I gave it to him. He used it as a siwak more vigorously than I had ever seen him use a siwak before. Then he put it down. I found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ growing heavy in my lap, so I went to look at his face, and behold his gaze was fixed, and he was saying, \"Rather, the highest companion from Paradise.\" I said, \"You were given the choice and you chose, by the One who sent you with the truth.\"' She said, 'Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken in death.'"],[19010,"She said: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken, his back was leaning against me. Abd al-Rahman b. Abu Bakr entered with a siwak in his hand, and the Prophet ﷺ called for it. I took the siwak, softened it, then handed it to him. He began using it as a siwak, then his hand grew heavy and he grew heavy upon me, while saying, \"O Allah, in the highest company.\"' She said, 'Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken, while he was between my chest and neck.'"],[19011,"I heard Aisha say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died on my day, in my house, and between my chest and neck, and Allah joined my saliva with his.' She said, 'Abd al-Rahman entered upon me with a siwak. The Prophet's ﷺ hand had grown weak, so I took it, chewed it, then I brushed his teeth with it.'"],[19012,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died between my arms and chest. After seeing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ die while he had a cup of water in which he would put his hand and wipe his face with the water, I will never dislike the severity of death for anyone. Then he said, \"O Allah, assist me in the agony of death.\""],[19013,"I heard Aisha say: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing with the rider of a white horse, holding the horse's forelock. When he came to me, I said, 'Who is the rider of the horse?' He said, 'So you saw him?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'And whom does he resemble?' I said, 'Dihyah b. Khalifah al-Kalbi.' He said, 'That was Jibril, and he conveys greetings to you.' I said, 'And upon him whom he sent, and upon you and upon him be peace.'"],[19014,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ with a man on a hackney, wearing a turban that he had fastened behind him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was placing his hand on the hackney's mane. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, who is this?' He said, 'Did you see him?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Who is he?' I said, 'Dihya al-Kalbi.' He said, 'That is Jibril ﷺ .'"],[19015,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'O Aisha, this is Jibril, he conveys greetings of peace to you.' So I said, 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.'"],[19016,"The Prophet ﷺ said to her, 'This is Jibril, and he is conveying greetings of peace to you.' So I said, 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; you see what we do not see.'"],[19017,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'This is Jibril, he conveys greetings of peace to you.' So I said, 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.'"],[19018,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'This is Jibril, he conveys greetings of peace to you.' So I said, 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.'"],[19019,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I saw you speaking with Dihya al-Kalbi while your hand was on the horse's mane.' He said, 'Did you see him?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'That is Jibril, and he conveys greetings of peace to you.' So I said, 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; from such a companion and such a guest, how excellent a companion and how excellent a guest.'"],[19020,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'O Aisha, Jibril conveys greetings of peace to you.' I said, 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.'"],[19021,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Aisha, 'This is Jibril, he conveys greetings of peace to you.' So Aisha said to him, 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.'"],[19022,"The Prophet ﷺ said to her, 'Jibril conveys to you greetings of peace from your Lord.' She said, 'I say: to my Lord be peace, and from Him be peace, and upon Jibril be peace.'"],[19023,"Jibril asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ. He said, 'Who is this with you?' He said, 'Aisha.' He said, 'Convey to her greetings of peace from me.' He said, 'Excellent, excellent, O Aisha, this is Jibril, he conveys greetings of peace to you.'"],[19024,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in the house, a man entered upon us on a horse. The Prophet ﷺ stood, then returned. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, who is this?' He said, 'This is Jibril, and he has commanded me to convey greetings of peace to you.' So I said, 'Return the greeting to him: to him from me be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.'"],[19025,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished from the Confederates, he entered the place of washing to bathe. Then Jibril came and said, 'O Muhammad, you have put down your weapons, but we have not put down our weapons yet; go to Banu Qurayza.' Aisha said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I saw him through the dust, with dust bound around his head.'"],[19026,"\"It was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ while I was with him, and I closed the door between me and him. When it was lifted from him, he said, 'O Aisha, Gabriel ﷺ is greeting you.'\""],[19027,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: 'Indeed it eases death for me that I have been shown you as my wife in Paradise.'"],[19028,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, who are your wives in Paradise?' He said: 'Indeed you are among them,' or he said: 'Behold, you are among them.' It occurred to me that that was because he had not married a virgin other than me."],[19029,"She is the wife of the Messenger of God ﷺ in this world and the Hereafter."],[19030,"She is the wife of our Prophet ﷺ in this world and the Hereafter, but God tested us to know whether we obey her or him."],[19031,"A man disparaged Aisha in the presence of Ali, so Ammar said to him: 'Be quiet, despised and reviled! Would you harm the beloved of the Messenger of God ﷺ?'"],[19032,"A man was with Ali and spoke ill of Aisha, so Ammar said to him: 'Who is this one whom you disparage, the wife of our Prophet ﷺ in Paradise? Be quiet, despised!'"],[19033,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Umm Salama: 'O Umm Salama, do not harm me concerning Aisha, for by God, revelation has never descended upon me while I was under the blanket of any woman among you except her.'"],[19034,"Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: The wives of the Prophet ﷺ sent Fatima to the Prophet ﷺ. She sought permission while he was lying with me under my cloak, and he granted her permission while I remained silent. She said: 'O Messenger of God, your wives have sent me to ask you for justice regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafa.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: 'O my little daughter, do you not love me?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then love her.'"],[19035,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Many men have reached perfection, but among women none have reached perfection except Maryam daughter of Imran and Asiya wife of Pharaoh.' And the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The excellence of Aisha over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food.'"],[19036,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The excellence of Aisha over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food.'"],[19037,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The excellence of Aisha over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food.'"],[19038,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed the excellence of Aisha over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food.'"],[19039,"I heard Anas b. Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, “The excellence of ‘A’ishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food.”"],[19040,"Al-Qa‘nabī narrated to us: Sulaymān b. Bilāl narrated to us. Ḥ And ‘Alī b. al-Mubārak al-Ṣan‘ānī narrated to us: Ismā‘īl b. Abī Uways narrated to us: Sulaymān b. Bilāl narrated to me, from ‘Abd Allāh b. ‘Abd al-Raḥmān b. Ma‘mar Abī Ṭuwālah, from Anas b. Mālik, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “The excellence of ‘A’ishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over food,” or “The excellence of tharid over food is like the excellence of ‘A’ishah over women.”"],[19041,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The excellence of ‘A’ishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over food.”"],[19042,"“O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is most beloved to you?” He said, “‘A’ishah.” He said, “From the men?” He said, “Abū Bakr.”"],[19043,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him on the expedition of Dhāt al-Salāsil. So I came to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is most beloved to you?” He said, “‘A’ishah.” I said, “From the men?” He said, “Her father.” I said, “Then who?” He said, “‘Umar.” I said, “Then who?” And he counted several men."],[19044,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is most beloved to you?” He said, “And why?” I said, “So that I may love whom you love.” He said, “‘A’ishah.”"],[19045,"She said concerning ‘A’ishah: “The Prophet ﷺ could not restrain his love for her.”"],[19046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day, “By Allah, O ‘A’ishah, it is not hidden from me when you are pleased and when you are angry.” I said, “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, how do you know that?” He said, “When you are pleased and you swear, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Muhammad,’ but when you are angry and you swear, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Abraham.’” I said, “You have spoken the truth, O Messenger of Allah.”"],[19047,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day, “By Allah, O ‘A’ishah, it is not hidden from me when you are pleased and when you are angry.” I said, “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, how do you know that?” He said, “When you are pleased and you swear, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Muhammad,’ but when you are angry and you swear, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Abraham.’” I said, “You have spoken the truth, O Messenger of Allah.”"],[19048,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day, “By Allah, O ‘A’ishah, it is not hidden from me when you are pleased and when you are angry.” I said, “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, how do you know that?” He said, “When you are pleased and you swear, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Muhammad,’ but when you are angry and you swear, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Abraham.’” I said, “You have spoken the truth, O Messenger of Allah.”"],[19049,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed I know when you are pleased with me and when you are angry.” I said, “And how do you know that, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “When you are pleased with me and you swear, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Muhammad,’ and when you are angry and you swear, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Abraham.’” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I only avoid your name.”"],[19050,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “Indeed I know when you are pleased with me and when you are angry with me.” I said, “From where do you know that?” He said, “When you are pleased with me, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Muhammad,’ and when you are angry with me, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Abraham.’” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I only avoid your name.”"],[19051,"I raced the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I beat him."],[19052,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and he stopped at a place. He said to his companions, “Go ahead.” Then he said, “Come, so I can race you.” So I raced him and I beat him. Later, I went out with him on another journey after I had put on weight. We stopped at a place, and he said to his companions, “Go ahead.” Then he said, “Come, so I can race you.” So I raced him, and he beat me. He struck me between my shoulders and said, “This is for that.”"],[19053,"I raced the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I beat him. Then when I had gained weight, he raced me and beat me. He said, “O Aisha, this is for that.”"],[19054,"Aisha said to Abu Bakr, “I saw three moons fall into my room.” Abu Bakr said, “Three of the best people on earth will be buried in your house.” Yahya said: I heard people saying that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died in her house, Abu Bakr said, “One of your moons, and he is the best of them.”"],[19055,"Abu Bakr said, “If your dream is true, three of the best people on earth will be buried in your house.” When the Prophet ﷺ died, Abu Bakr said to her, “The best of your moons, O Aisha.” And Abu Bakr and Umar were buried in her house."],[19056,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Did any of you see a dream?” Aisha said, “O Messenger of Allah, I saw three moons fall into my room.” He said to her, “If your dream is true, there will be buried in your house—I think he said—the best of the people of Paradise.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, and he is the best of her moons. Then Abu Bakr passed away, then Umar passed away, and they were buried in her house."],[19057,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys until we were at al-Bayda’ or Dhat al-Jaysh, and my necklace broke. The Prophet ﷺ stayed to search for it, and the people stayed with him, but they had no water with them. The people came to Abu Bakr and said, “Do you see what Aisha has done? She has detained the Prophet ﷺ and the people, and they have no water with them.” So he admonished me and said to me whatever Allah willed him to say, and he began poking me in my side with his hand. Nothing prevented me from moving except that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was resting on my thigh. He slept until morning without wudu’, and Allah sent down the verse of tayammum. Usayd b. Hudayr said, “This is not the first of your blessings, O family of Abu Bakr.” Then we made the camel I had been riding stand up, and we found the necklace beneath it."],[19058,"Aisha’s necklace fell, so the Prophet ﷺ sent some men to search for it. Morning overtook them while they had no water, so they prayed without purification and complained about that to the Prophet ﷺ. Then tayammum was revealed. Ma‘mar said: Ayyub informed me that Abu Bakr passed by Aisha and said, “You have detained the people and caused them hardship.” Ma‘mar said: Hisham reported from his father, and Ayyub also said it. When tayammum was revealed, Abu Bakr was pleased with that and said, “I did not know you were so blessed. No disliked matter befalls you except that Allah makes in it good for the Muslims.”"],[19059,"She borrowed a necklace from Asma’, and it fell from her neck. She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he sent men to search for it, and they searched and found it. The time for prayer came, so they prayed without purification, then they returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. Then Allah sent down the concession. Usayd b. Hudayr said, “May Allah reward you with good. By Allah, no disliked matter befalls you except that Allah makes for you and for the believers good from it.”"],[19060,"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ were two groups: one group included Aisha, Hafsa, Safiyya, and Sawda, and another group included Umm Salama and the rest of the Prophet’s ﷺ wives."],[19061,"Whenever Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to go on a journey, he used to draw lots amongst his wives, and Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to take with him the one on whom lot fell. He drew lots amongst us during one of the Ghazwat which he fought. The lot fell on me and so I proceeded with Messenger of Allah ﷺ after Allah's order of veiling (the women) had been revealed. I was carried (on the back of a camel) in my howdah and carried down while still in it (when we came to a halt). So we went on till Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished from that Ghazwa of his and returned. When we approached the city of Medina he announced at night that it was time for departure. So when they announced the news of departure, I got up and went away from the army camps, and after finishing from the call of nature, I came back to my riding animal. I touched my chest to find that my necklace which was made of Zifar beads (i.e. Yemenite beads partly black and partly white) was missing. So I returned to look for my necklace and my search for it detained me. (In the meanwhile) the people who used to carry me on my camel, came and took my howdah and put it on the back of my camel on which I used to ride, as they considered that I was in it. In those days women were light in weight for they did not get fat, and flesh did not cover their bodies in abundance as they used to eat only a little food. Those people therefore, disregarded the lightness of the howdah while lifting and carrying it; and at that time I was still a young girl. They made the camel rise and all of them left (along with it). I found my necklace after the army had gone. Then I came to their camping place to find no call maker of them, nor one who would respond to the call. So I intended to go to the place where I used to stay, thinking that they would miss me and come back to me (in my search). While I was sitting in my resting place, I was overwhelmed by sleep and slept. Safwan bin Al-Muattal As-Sulami Adh-Dhakwani was behind the army. When he reached my place in the morning, he saw the figure of a sleeping person and he recognized me on seeing me as he had seen me before the order of compulsory veiling (was prescribed). So I woke up when he recited Istirja' (i.e. \"Inna li l-lahi wa inna llaihi raji'un\") as soon as he recognized me. I veiled my face with my head cover at once, and by Allah, we did not speak a single word, and I did not hear him saying any word besides his Istirja'. He dismounted from his camel and made it kneel down, putting his leg on its front legs and then I got up and rode on it. Then he set out leading the camel that was carrying me till we overtook the army in the extreme heat of midday while they were at a halt (taking a rest). (Because of the event) some people brought destruction upon themselves and the one who spread the Ifk (i.e. slander) more, was ʿAbdullah bin Ubai Ibn Salul.\" (Urwa said, \"The people propagated the slander and talked about it in his (i.e. ʿAbdullah's) presence and he confirmed it and listened to it and asked about it to let it prevail.\" ʿUrwa also added, \"None was mentioned as members of the slanderous group besides (ʿAbdullah) except Hassan bin Thabit and Mistah bin Uthatha and Hamna bint Jahsh along with others about whom I have no knowledge, but they were a group as Allah said. It is said that the one who carried most of the slander was ʿAbdullah bin Ubai bin Salul.\" ʿUrwa added, \"ʿAisha disliked to have Hassan abused in her presence and she used to say, 'It was he who said: My father and his (i.e. my father's) father and my honor are all for the protection of Muhammad's honor from you.\"). ʿAisha added, \"After we returned to Medina, I became ill for a month. The people were propagating the forged statements of the slanderers while I was unaware of anything of all that, but I felt that in my present ailment, I was not receiving the same kindness from Messenger of Allah ﷺ as I used to receive when I got sick. (But now) Messenger of Allah ﷺ would only come, greet me and say,' How is that (lady)?' and leave. That roused my doubts, but I did not discover the evil (i.e. slander) till I went out after my convalescence, I went out with Um Mistah to Al-Manasi' where we used to answer the call of nature and we used not to go out (to answer the call of nature) except at night, and that was before we had latrines near our houses. And this habit of our concerning evacuating the bowels, was similar to the habits of the old 'Arabs living in the deserts, for it would be troublesome for us to take latrines near our houses. So I and Um Mistah who was the daughter of Abu Ruhm bin Al-Muttalib bin ʿAbd Manaf, whose mother was the daughter of Sakhr bin 'Amir and the aunt of Abu Bakr As-Siddiq and whose son was Mistah bin Uthatha bin ʿAbbas bin Al-Muttalib, went out. I and Um Mistah returned to my house after we finished answering the call of nature. Um Mistah stumbled by getting her foot entangled in her covering sheet and on that she said, 'Let Mistah be ruined!' I said, 'What a hard word you have said. Do you abuse a man who took part in the battle of Badr?' On that she said, 'O you Hantah! Didn't you hear what he (i.e. Mistah) said? 'I said, 'What did he say?' Then she told me the slander of the people of Ifk. So my ailment was aggravated, and when I reached my home, Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me, and after greeting me, said, 'How is that (lady)?' I said, 'Will you allow me to go to my parents?' as I wanted to be sure about the news through them. Allah's Apostle allowed me (and I went to my parents) and asked my mother, 'O mother! What are the people talking about?' She said, 'O my daughter! Don't worry, for scarcely is there a charming woman who is loved by her husband and whose husband has other wives besides herself that they (i.e. women) would find faults with her.' I said, 'Subhan-Allah! (I testify the uniqueness of Allah). Are the people really talking in this way?' I kept on weeping that night till dawn I could neither stop weeping nor sleep then in the morning again, I kept on weeping. When the Divine Inspiration was delayed. Messenger of Allah ﷺ called ʿAli bin Abi Talib and Usama bin Zaid to ask and consult them about divorcing me. Usama bin Zaid said what he knew of my innocence, and the respect he preserved in himself for me. Usama said, '(O Messenger of Allah ﷺ!) She is your wife and we do not know anything except good about her.' ʿAli bin Abi Talib said, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Allah does not put you in difficulty and there are plenty of women other than she, yet, ask the maid-servant who will tell you the truth.' On that Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Barira (i.e. the maid-servant) and said, 'O Barira! Did you ever see anything which aroused your suspicion?' Barira said to him, 'By Him Who has sent you with the Truth. I have never seen anything in her (i.e. Aisha) which I would conceal, except that she is a young girl who sleeps leaving the dough of her family exposed so that the domestic goats come and eat it.' So, on that day, Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up on the pulpit and complained about ʿAbdullah bin Ubai (bin Salul) before his companions, saying, 'O you Muslims! Who will relieve me from that man who has hurt me with his evil statement about my family? By Allah, I know nothing except good about my family and they have blamed a man about whom I know nothing except good and he used never to enter my home except with me.' Saʿd bin Muʿadh the brother of Banu ʿAbd Al-Ashhal got up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! I will relieve you from him; if he is from the tribe of Al-Aus, then I will chop his head off, and if he is from our brothers, i.e. Al-Khazraj, then order us, and we will fulfill your order.' On that, a man from Al-Khazraj got up. Um Hassan, his cousin, was from his branch tribe, and he was Saʿd bin Ubada, chief of Al-Khazraj. Before this incident, he was a pious man, but his love for his tribe goaded him into saying to Saʿd (bin Muʿadh). 'By Allah, you have told a lie; you shall not and cannot kill him. If he belonged to your people, you would not wish him to be killed.' On that, Usaid bin Hudair who was the cousin of Saʿd (bin Muʿadh) got up and said to Saʿd bin 'Ubada, 'By Allah! You are a liar! We will surely kill him, and you are a hypocrite arguing on the behalf of hypocrites.' On this, the two tribes of Al-Aus and Al Khazraj got so much excited that they were about to fight while Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing on the pulpit. Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept on quietening them till they became silent and so did he. All that day I kept on weeping with my tears never ceasing, and I could never sleep. In the morning my parents were with me and I wept for two nights and a day with my tears never ceasing and I could never sleep till I thought that my liver would burst from weeping. So, while my parents were sitting with me and I was weeping, an Ansari woman asked me to grant her admittance. I allowed her to come in, and when she came in, she sat down and started weeping with me. While we were in this state, Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, greeted us and sat down. He had never sat with me since that day of the slander. A month had elapsed and no Divine Inspiration came to him about my case. Allah's Apostle then recited Tashah-hud and then said, 'Amma Badu, O ʿAisha! I have been informed so-andso about you; if you are innocent, then soon Allah will reveal your innocence, and if you have committed a sin, then repent to Allah and ask Him for forgiveness for when a slave confesses his sins and asks Allah for forgiveness, Allah accepts his repentance.' (continued...) (continuing... 1): -5.462:... ... When Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his speech, my tears ceased flowing completely that I no longer felt a single drop of tear flowing. I said to my father, 'Reply to Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf concerning what he has said.' My father said, 'By Allah, I do not know what to say to Messenger of Allah ﷺ .' Then I said to my mother, 'Reply to Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf concerning what he has said.' She said, 'By Allah, I do not know what to say to Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' In spite of the fact that I was a young girl and had a little knowledge of Qur'an, I said, 'By Allah, no doubt I know that you heard this (slanderous) speech so that it has been planted in your hearts (i.e. minds) and you have taken it as a truth. Now if I tell you that I am innocent, you will not believe me, and if confess to you about it, and Allah knows that I am innocent, you will surely believe me. By Allah, I find no similitude for me and you except that of Joseph's father when he said, '(For me) patience in the most fitting against that which you assert; it is Allah (Alone) Whose Help can be sought.' Then I turned to the other side and lay on my bed; and Allah knew then that I was innocent and hoped that Allah would reveal my innocence. But, by Allah, I never thought that Allah would reveal about my case, Divine Inspiration, that would be recited (forever) as I considered myself too unworthy to be talked of by Allah with something of my concern, but I hoped that Messenger of Allah ﷺ might have a dream in which Allah would prove my innocence. But, by Allah, before Messenger of Allah ﷺ left his seat and before any of the household left, the Divine inspiration came to Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So there overtook him the same hard condition which used to overtake him, (when he used to be inspired Divinely). The sweat was dropping from his body like pearls though it was a wintry day and that was because of the weighty statement which was being revealed to him. When that state of Messenger of Allah ﷺ was over, he got up smiling, and the first word he said was, 'O ʿAisha! Allah has declared your innocence!' Then my Mother said to me, 'Get up and go to him (i.e. Messenger of Allah ﷺ). I replied, 'By Allah, I will not go to him, and I praise none but Allah. So Allah revealed the ten Verses:- - \"Verily! They who spread the slander Are a gang, among you.............\" (24.11-20) Allah revealed those Qur'anic Verses to declare my innocence. Abu Bakr As-Siddiq who used to disburse money for Mistah bin Uthatha because of his relationship to him and his poverty, said, 'By Allah, I will never give to Mistah bin Uthatha anything after what he has said about Aisha.' Then Allah revealed:-- \"And let not those among you who are good and wealthy swear not to give (any sort of help) to their kinsmen, those in need, and those who have left their homes for Allah's cause, let them pardon and forgive. Do you not love that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is oft-Forgiving Most Merciful.\" (24.22) Abu Bakr As-Siddiq said, 'Yes, by Allah, I would like that Allah forgive me.' and went on giving Mistah the money he used to give him before. He also added, 'By Allah, I will never deprive him of it at all.' Aisha further said:.\" Messenger of Allah ﷺ also asked Zainab bint Jahsh (i.e. his wife) about my case. He said to Zainab, 'What do you know and what did you see?\" She replied, \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! I refrain from claiming falsely that I have heard or seen anything. By Allah, I know nothing except good (about ʿAisha).' From amongst the wives of the Prophet ﷺ Zainab was my peer (in beauty and in the love she received from the Prophet) but Allah saved her from that evil because of her piety. Her sister Hamna, started struggling on her behalf and she was destroyed along with those who were destroyed. The man who was blamed said, 'Subhan-Allah! By Him in Whose Hand my soul is, I have never uncovered the cover (i.e. veil) of any female.' Later on the man was martyred in Allah's Cause.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 4141)"],[19062,"When the people of the slander said what they said about her and Allah declared her innocent. He said: Each of them narrated to me a portion of the hadith that Aisha ؓ narrated, and some of their hadith confirms the others, though some were more retentive than others. They claimed that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to go out on an expedition, he would draw lots among his wives, and whichever of them came out in the lot, he would take her with him. Aisha said: He drew lots among us for an expedition he undertook, and my lot came out, so I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after Allah had revealed the hijab. I would descend and be carried in my howdah. We traveled until, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished that expedition and we approached Madinah returning, he announced departure one night. I got up when he announced departure to relieve myself. When I had finished my business, I came back to my baggage and found that a necklace of mine made of onyx beads had broken. So I went back searching for my necklace. The group that was loading the camels came and carried my howdah and placed it on my camel that I used to ride, thinking I was inside. At that time women were light; they had not become heavy with flesh, and they ate only small amounts of food. So the people did not notice the lightness of the howdah. I was a young girl. They sent the camel off and departed. I found my necklace after the army had moved on, and I came to their campsite, but there was no one there to call or answer. So I went to the place where I had been and thought that they would miss me and come back to me. While I was sitting at my place, sleep overcame me and I fell asleep. Safwan b. al-Mu‘attal al-Sulami, then al-Dhakwani, was behind the army. He set out early at night and reached my place in the morning. He saw the dark shape of a sleeping person and came to me. He recognized me when he saw me, as he used to see me before the hijab. I woke up when he uttered the words of recovery upon recognizing me, and I covered my face with my jilbab. He did not speak a word to me, and I did not hear a word from him except his utterance of recovery, until he made his mount kneel and stepped on its foreleg, and I mounted it. He led me on the mount until we reached the army after they had halted. Then those who were destroyed were destroyed. The one who assumed the greater part of the slander was Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul. We arrived in Madinah, and I fell ill for a month after arriving while the people were spreading the words of the slanderers. I was unaware of any of that, but it troubled me in my illness that I did not recognize from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the kindness I used to see from him when I was sick. He would only enter upon me, say, “How is this one?” and then leave. That troubled me, and I was unaware of the evil until I went out after I recovered. Umm Mistah went out with me toward al-Manasi‘, which was our place for relieving ourselves. We would not go out except from night to night, and that was before privies were made near our houses. Our practice was the practice of the early Arabs in going out to the open desert for relieving ourselves. We were bothered by having privies near our houses. So I set out with Umm Mistah, who was the daughter of Abu Ruhm b. al-Muttalib b. Abd Manaf, and her mother was the daughter of Sakhr b. Amir, the grandmother of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, and her son was Mistah b. Uthatha b. al-Muttalib. I and Umm Mistah headed back to my house after we had finished our business. Umm Mistah tripped over her long outer garment and said, “May Mistah perish.” I said to her, “How bad what you said! Do you revile a man who witnessed Badr?” She said, “O you, have you not heard what he said?” I said, “What did he say?” Then she told me the words of the slanderers. I became more ill in addition to my illness. When we returned to my house, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us, greeted, and said, “How is this one?” I said to him, “Will you permit me to go to my parents?” At that time I wanted to confirm the news from them. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted me, so I went to my parents and said to my mother, “O mother, what are the people talking about?” She said, “O daughter, take it lightly. By Allah, rarely is there a beautiful woman loved by a man who has co-wives except that they say much against her.” I said, “Glory be to Allah! The people have been talking about this?” I spent that night until morning with tears not ceasing and no sleep soothing my eyes. She said: Then I woke up crying. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Ali b. Abi Talib and Usama b. Zayd when the revelation was delayed, and he consulted them about separating from his wife. As for Usama, he advised the Messenger of Allah ﷺ based on what he knew of his wife’s innocence and the affection he felt for them. Usama said, “O Messenger of Allah, she is your wife, and we know nothing but good of her.” As for Ali, he said, “O Messenger of Allah, Allah has not restricted you; there are many women besides her. Ask the servant girl, and she will tell you the truth.” She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Barira and said to her, “O Barira, have you seen anything that makes you suspicious?” Barira said, “By the One who sent you with the truth, I have not seen anything about her that I would hold against her, except that she is a young girl who sleeps off from the dough of her family, and a domestic animal comes and eats it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood that day and sought excuse against Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul. He said while on the pulpit, “O assembly of Muslims, who will excuse me from a man whose harm has reached me concerning my household? By Allah, I know nothing but good about my household, and they have mentioned a man about whom I know nothing but good, and he used to enter upon my family only with me.” She said: Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh al-Ansari stood and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I will excuse you from him. If he is from the Aws, I will strike his neck; and if he is from our brothers the Khazraj, command us and we will do your command.” Sa‘d b. Ubada stood up, who was the chief of the Khazraj that day. Before that he had been a righteous man, but zeal carried him away, and he said to Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh, “You lie! By the life of Allah, you will not kill him, nor can you.” Usayd b. Hudayr stood up, who was the cousin of Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh, and said to Sa‘d b. Ubada, “You lie! By the life of Allah, he will kill him, for you are a hypocrite arguing on behalf of the hypocrites.” The two tribes, Aws and Khazraj, rose up until they were about to fight, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was calming them until they became silent, and he became silent. She said: I spent that day with tears not ceasing and no sleep soothing my eyes. My parents came to me in the morning, and I had wept through my night, with no sleep and tears not ceasing, and they thought that weeping would split my liver. While they were sitting with me and I was weeping, a woman from the Ansar asked permission to enter, and I permitted her. She sat weeping with me. While we were like that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and sat down. He had not sat with me since the accusation was made. He had stayed a month without receiving revelation concerning my matter. He testified and then said, “To proceed, O Aisha, it has reached me about you such and such. If you are innocent, Allah will soon prove your innocence; but if you have committed a sin, seek Allah’s forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant confesses his sin and then repents, Allah turns to him.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his speech, my tears stopped until I could not feel a drop. I said to my father, “Respond to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about what he said.” He said, “By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I said to my mother, “Respond to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about what he said.” She said, “By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah.” I said, while I was a young girl who did not read much of the Quran, “By Allah, I know that you have heard this talk until it settled in your hearts and you believed it. So if I tell you that I am innocent, and Allah knows I am innocent, you will not believe me. And if I confess to you something, and Allah knows I am innocent of it, you will believe me. By Allah, I find no example for me and you except the father of Yusuf when he said: ‘So patience is most fitting, and Allah is the One sought for help.’” Then I turned and lay on my bed. By Allah, at that time I knew that I was innocent and that Allah would prove my innocence, but by Allah, I did not think that Allah would send down revelation concerning me that would be recited, for my matter was too insignificant in my view for Allah to speak about me with a recited command. But I hoped that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would see a dream in his sleep by which Allah would prove my innocence. She said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not leave his place, and no one from the household went out, until Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down revelation upon him. He was seized by what used to seize him of the intense condition, until sweat like pearls poured from him even on a cold day, due to the weight of the Quran being revealed to him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was relieved, he was laughing. The first word he spoke was, “As for Allah, He has declared you innocent.” My mother said, “Get up to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I said, “By Allah, I will not get up to him, and I will not praise anyone but Allah.” Allah, Mighty is His mention, sent down: “Indeed, those who came with the slander…” the whole ten verses. When Allah sent down this about my innocence, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who was supporting Mistah b. Uthatha because of his kinship and poverty, said, “By Allah, I will never spend anything on Mistah after what he said about Aisha.” Then Allah sent down: “And let not those of virtue among you and wealth swear not to give to the near of kin, the needy, and the emigrants in the way of Allah. Let them pardon and overlook. Do you not love that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.” Abu Bakr said, “Yes, by Allah, I love that Allah should forgive me.” So he restored to Mistah the support he used to give him and said, “By Allah, I will never take it away from him.” Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked Zaynab bt. Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, about my matter. He said, “O Zaynab, what do you know or what have you seen?” She said, “O Messenger of Allah, I protect my hearing and my sight. By Allah, I know nothing but good.” Aisha said: She was the one who rivaled me among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and Allah protected her by her piety. Her sister Hamna began to fight on her behalf, and she perished among those who perished among the people of the slander. Al-Zuhri said: This is what has reached us of the account of these people from the hadith of Aisha."],[19063,"All of them narrated to me a portion of her hadith, and some were more retentive than others and more accurate in narrating. I have memorized from each man among them the hadith he narrated to me, and some of their hadith confirms others. They claimed that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to go out on a journey, he drew lots among his wives, and whichever of them came out in the lot, he took her with him. She said: He drew lots among us for an expedition he undertook, and my lot came out, so I went out with him after the hijab had been revealed. I was carried in a howdah and descended in it. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished that expedition and returned, and we approached Madinah, he announced departure one night. I got up when they announced departure and walked until I had passed beyond the army. When I had finished my business, I came back to the baggage and felt my chest, and found that a necklace of mine made of onyx beads had broken. So I went back searching for my necklace, and its search detained me. The people who were loading my camel came and carried my howdah and placed it on my camel that I rode, thinking I was inside. At that time women were light; they had not become heavy and flesh had not covered them, and they ate only small amounts of food. So they carried it, and I was a young girl. They sent the camel off and departed. I found my necklace after the army had moved on, and I came to their campsite, but there was no one in it. I headed to my place where I had been, and I thought that they would miss me and return to me. While I was sitting at my place, sleep overcame my eyes. Safwan b. al-Mu‘attal al-Sulami, then al-Dhakwani, was behind the army. He reached my place in the morning and saw the dark shape of a sleeping person. He came to me, and he used to see me before the hijab. I woke up at his utterance of recovery when he made his mount kneel and stepped on its foreleg, and I mounted it. He led me on the mount until we reached the army after they had halted, resting at noon. Then those who were destroyed were destroyed. The one who assumed the greater part of the slander was Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul. I arrived in Madinah and fell ill there for a month, while the people were spreading the words of the slanderers, and I was unaware of any of that. But it troubled me in my illness that I did not recognize from the Messenger of Allah the kindness I used to see from him when I was sick. He would only enter, greet, and say, “How is this one?” Then he would leave. That troubled me, and I remained unaware until I recovered. I went out with Umm Mistah toward al-Manasi‘, our place for relieving ourselves. We would not go out except from night to night, and that was before privies were made near our houses. Our practice was the practice of the early Arabs in the open desert. I and Umm Mistah, daughter of Abu Ruhm, were walking when she tripped over her long outer garment and said, “May Mistah perish.” I said to her, “How bad what you said! Do you revile a man who witnessed Badr?” She said, “O you, have you not heard what they said?” I said, “What did they say?” She told me the words of the slanderers, and I became more ill in addition to my illness. When I returned to my house, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and said, “How is this one?” I said, “Permit me to go to my parents.” At that time I wanted to confirm the news from them. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted me, so I went to my parents and said to my mother, “What are the people talking about?” She said, “O daughter, take the matter lightly. By Allah, rarely is there a beautiful woman loved by a man who has co-wives except that they say much against her.” I said, “Glory be to Allah! The people have been talking about this?” She said: I spent that night until morning with tears not ceasing and no sleep soothing my eyes. Then I woke up. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Ali b. Abi Talib and Usama b. Zayd when the revelation was delayed, to consult them about separating from his wife. As for Usama, he advised the Messenger of Allah ﷺ based on what he knew of his wife’s innocence and the affection he felt for them. Usama said, “She is your wife, O Messenger of Allah, and we know nothing but good.” As for Ali, he said, “O Messenger of Allah, Allah has not restricted you; there are many women besides her. Ask the servant girl, and she will tell you the truth.” She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Barira and said to her, “Have you seen anything from her that makes you suspicious?” Barira said, “No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I have not seen anything about her that I would hold against her, except that she is a young girl who sleeps off from the dough until a domestic animal comes and eats it.” She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood that day and sought excuse against Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Who will excuse me from a man whose harm has reached me concerning my family? By Allah,” he said it three times, “I know nothing but good about my family, and they have mentioned a man about whom I know nothing but good, and he used to enter upon my family only with me.” She said: Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh stood and said, “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I will excuse you from him. If he is from the Aws, we will strike his neck; and if he is from our brothers the Khazraj, command us and we will do your command.” Sa‘d b. Ubada stood, who was the chief of the Khazraj and had been a righteous man before, but zeal carried him away. He said, “You lie! By the life of Allah, you will not kill him, nor can you do that.” Usayd b. Hudayr said, “You lie! By the life of Allah, he will kill him, for you are a hypocrite arguing on behalf of the hypocrites.” The two tribes Aws and Khazraj rose up until they were about to fight, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing on the pulpit. He came down to calm them until they became silent, and he became silent. I wept all day with tears not ceasing and no sleep soothing my eyes. My parents came to me in the morning, and I had wept through my day and night until I thought that weeping would split my eye. While they were sitting with me and I was weeping, a woman from the Ansar asked permission to enter, and I permitted her. She sat weeping with me. While we were like that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and sat down. He had not sat with me since the accusation was made. He had stayed a month without receiving revelation concerning my matter. He testified and then said, “To proceed, O Aisha, it has reached me about you such and such. If you are innocent, Allah will soon prove your innocence; but if you have committed a sin, seek Allah’s forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant confesses a sin and then repents, Allah turns to him.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his speech, my tears stopped until I could not feel a drop. I said to my father, “Respond to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about what he said.” He said, “By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I said to my mother, and she said the same. I said, while I was a young girl who did not read much of the Quran, “By Allah, I know that you have heard what has been said, and it has settled in your hearts and you have believed it. So if I tell you that I am innocent, and Allah knows I am innocent, you will not believe me. And if I confess to you something, and Allah knows I am innocent of it, you will believe me. By Allah, I find no example for me and you except the father of Yusuf when he said: ‘Patience is most fitting…’” She said: Then I turned on my bed, hoping that Allah would prove my innocence. But by Allah, I did not think that revelation would be sent down concerning my matter that would be recited, for I was too insignificant in my view for the Quran to speak about my matter. But I hoped that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would see a dream that would prove my innocence. She said: By Allah, he did not leave his seat, and no one left the house, until revelation came down upon him. He was seized by what used to seize him of the intense condition, until sweat like pearls poured from him on a cold day. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was relieved, and he was laughing. The first word he spoke was, “O Aisha, praise Allah, for Allah has declared you innocent.” My mother said to me, “Get up to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I said, “By Allah, I will not get up to him, and I will not praise anyone but Allah.” Allah sent down: “Indeed, those who came with the slander…” the whole verses. When Allah sent down this about my innocence, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who was supporting Mistah b. Uthatha because of his kinship, said, “By Allah, I will never spend anything on Mistah after what he said about Aisha.” Then Allah sent down this verse: “And let not those of virtue among you…” to the end of the verse. Abu Bakr said, “Yes, I love that Allah should forgive me.” So he restored to Mistah the support he used to give him. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked Zaynab bt. Jahsh about my matter. He said, “O Zaynab, what do you know and what have you seen?” She said, “I protect my hearing and my sight. By Allah, I know nothing but good about her.” Aisha said: She was the one who rivaled me, and Allah protected her by her piety."],[19065,"When the people of the slander said about her what they said, and God declared her innocent. Each of them narrated to me a portion of the hadith that was narrated to me from Aisha, and some of their hadith confirms others, even though some of them were more retentive of her hadith than others. They mentioned that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ wanted to set out on a journey, he would cast lots among his wives, and whichever of them the lot fell upon, he would take her with him. Aisha said: He cast lots among us during a military expedition he undertook, and my lot came out, so I went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ after the veil had been revealed. I was carried in my howdah and brought down while in it. We traveled until, when the Messenger of God ﷺ had finished that expedition of his and returned, and we drew near to Madinah, he announced one night that we would depart. I got up when he announced the departure and walked until I passed beyond the army. When I had finished my business and came back to my mount, I found that a necklace of mine made of A'far beads had broken, so I went back to look for my necklace, and my search for it detained me. The group that used to make me ready came and lifted my howdah onto my camel, the one I used to ride, thinking that I was in it. At that time we were light, as meat had not made us heavy; one of us would eat only a morsel of food, so the people did not notice the lightness of the howdah when they lifted it. I was a young girl, so they set the camel moving and went on. I found my necklace after the army had moved on, and came to their camp, but there was no one there to call out or answer. I went to the place where I had been staying, thinking that they would miss me and come back to me. While I was sitting in my place, sleep overcame me and I fell asleep. Safwan b. al-Mu'attal al-Sulami had been behind the army, and he traveled on and arrived at my place in the morning. He saw the form of a sleeping person and recognized me when he saw me, for he had seen me before the veil. I woke up when he uttered \"inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji'un\" upon recognizing me, and I covered my face with my outer garment. By God, he did not speak a word to me, and I did not hear a word from him until he made his camel kneel, pressed down on its foreleg, and I mounted it. He set off leading the camel with me until he caught up with the army after they had halted in the extreme heat of midday. Then those who perished from the people of the slander perished, and the one who took upon himself the greatest share of the sin was Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul. We arrived in Madinah, and I fell ill for a month after we arrived, while the people were indulging in the talk of the slanderers, and I was unaware of any of that. What disturbed me during my illness was that I did not perceive from the Messenger of God ﷺ the kindness that I used to see from him when I was sick; he would only enter upon me and say, \"How is that one of you?\" then leave. That disturbed me, but I was unaware of the evil until I went out after I had recovered, along with Umm Mistah, to the place for relieving ourselves, which was our open-air toilet. We would only go out at night to night, and that was before we had small closets near our houses. Our practice was the practice of the early Arabs in going out to the desert for defecation, and we were annoyed by having closets near our houses. So I went out with Umm Mistah toward my house after we had finished our business. Umm Mistah stumbled in her long garment and said, \"May Mistah perish!\" I said, \"What a bad thing you have said! Do you revile a man who was present at Badr?\" She said, \"O you, have you not heard what he said?\" I said, \"What did he say?\" She informed me of the talk of the slanderers, and I became more ill on top of my illness. When I returned to my house, the Messenger of God ﷺ came in and said, \"How is that one of you?\" I said, \"Will you permit me to go to my parents?\" At that time I wanted to make sure of the news from them. He permitted me, and I went to my mother and father and said, \"O mother, what are the people talking about?\" She said, \"O daughter, take it lightly, for by God, rarely is a beautiful woman loved by a man who has other wives but that they speak much against her.\" I said, \"Glory be to God! Have the people really been talking about that?\" She said, \"Yes.\" I wept that night until morning, my tears not ceasing and I could not sleep. Then I spent the next day weeping. The Messenger of God ﷺ called Ali b. Abi Talib and Usama b. Zayd when the revelation was delayed, to seek their counsel about separating from his wife. As for Usama, he advised the Messenger of God ﷺ according to what he knew of his wife's innocence and the affection he had in his heart for them, and said, \"O Messenger of God, she is your wife, and we know nothing but good about her.\" As for Ali b. Abi Talib, he said, \"O Messenger of God, God has not made things narrow for you; there are many women besides her. If you ask the slave girl, she will tell you the truth.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ called Barīra and said to her, \"O Barīra, have you seen anything that causes you doubt?\" Barīra said, \"No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I have never seen any fault in her that I could find, except that she is a young girl who sleeps and lets her family's dough be eaten by the domestic animals.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ stood that day and asked to be excused from Abdullah b. Ubayy. He said while on the pulpit: \"O assembly of Muslims, who will excuse me from a man whose harm to my family has reached me? By God, I know nothing but good about my family. They have mentioned a man of whom I know nothing but good, and he never used to enter upon my family except with me.\" Sa'd b. Mu'adh stood up and said, \"O Messenger of God, I will excuse you from him. If he is from the Aws, I will strike his neck, and if he is from our brothers of the Khazraj, you command us and we will do your command.\" Sa'd b. Ubada, who was the leader of the Khazraj, stood up, and he had been before that a righteous man, but zeal took hold of him, and he said to Sa'd b. Mu'adh, \"You have lied! By the life of God, you shall not kill him, and you are not able to kill him.\" Usayd b. Hudayr, who was the cousin of Sa'd b. Mu'adh, stood up and said to Sa'd b. Ubada, \"You have lied! By the life of God, we will kill him, for you are a hypocrite arguing on behalf of the hypocrites.\" The two tribes, the Aws and the Khazraj, became agitated until they were about to fight, while the Messenger of God ﷺ was standing on the pulpit. He kept calming them down until they fell silent, and he fell silent. She said: I remained that day with my tears not ceasing and I could not sleep, while my parents were with me. I had spent two nights and a day without sleeping or my tears ceasing, thinking that weeping would split my liver. While they were sitting with me and I was weeping, a woman of the Ansar asked permission to enter upon me. I granted her permission, and she began to weep with me. While we were thus, the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon us and sat down. She said: He had not sat with me since the talk had begun, and he had waited a month without receiving revelation concerning my affair. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ pronounced the testimony of faith when he sat down, then said: \"Now then, O Aisha, it has reached me about you such and such. If you are innocent, God will soon declare your innocence. If you have committed a sin, ask God for forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant acknowledges a sin and then repents to God, God accepts his repentance.\" When he finished his speech, my tears dried up so that I did not feel a single drop. I said to my father, \"Answer the Messenger of God about what he said.\" He said, \"By God, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of God.\" I said to my mother, \"Answer the Messenger of God.\" She said, \"By God, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of God.\" I said, while I was a young girl who did not read much of the Quran, \"You, by God, have heard this talk until it has settled in your hearts and you have believed it. If I say to you that I am innocent, and God knows that I am innocent, you will not believe me. But if I confess to something, and God knows that I am innocent, you will surely believe me. By God, I find for myself and for you no example except the father of Joseph, who said: 'So patience is most fitting. And God is the one sought for help against what you describe' (Quran 12:18).\" Then I turned away and lay down on my bed. She said: At that time I knew that I was innocent and that God would declare my innocence, but by God, I did not think that God would send down concerning my affair a revelation that would be recited, for my affair was too insignificant in my own eyes for God to speak about me in a matter that would be recited. But I hoped that God would show His Messenger a dream in which He would declare my innocence. By God, the Messenger of God ﷺ had not left his seat, and no one of the household had gone out, when God sent down revelation upon him. He was seized by the intense state that used to seize him, until sweat dripped from him like pearls on a cold day, because of the weight of the Quran that was being revealed to him. When the state left the Messenger of God, he recovered and was smiling. The first words he spoke were: \"O Aisha, God has declared your innocence.\" My mother said to me, \"Get up and go to him.\" I said, \"By God, I will not get up and go to him, and I will praise no one but God.\" Then God sent down: \"Indeed, those who came with the slander are a group among you...\" the ten verses in full. When God sent down this concerning my innocence, Abu Bakr, who used to spend on Mistah because of his kinship and poverty, said, \"By God, I will never spend anything on him again because of what he said about Aisha.\" Then God sent down: \"And let not those of virtue among you and wealth swear not to give...\" the verse. Abu Bakr said, \"Yes, by God, I love that God should forgive me.\" So he returned to spending on Mistah as he used to, and said, \"By God, I will never withhold it from him.\" Aisha said: The Messenger of God ﷺ had asked Zaynab bt. Jahsh about my affair, saying, \"O Zaynab, what do you know or what have you seen?\" Zaynab said, \"I protect my hearing and my sight. By God, I know nothing but good.\" She was the one who used to rival me among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, but God protected her through her piety. Her sister Hamna began to fight on her behalf and perished among those who perished from the people of the slander. Ibn Shihab said: This is what has reached us of the hadith of these people."],[19069,"Where the people of the slander said about her what they said, and God declared her innocent of all of it. A group narrated to me parts of her account, and some of them were more retentive of her account than others and more precise in its presentation. I have retained from each one of them the hadith that he narrated to me from Aisha. Aisha said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ intended a journey, he would cast lots among his wives, and whichever of them the lot fell upon, he took her with him. He cast lots among us for a military expedition he undertook, and my lot came out, so I went out with him after the veil had been prescribed. I was carried in my howdah and set down in it. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished that expedition of his and returned, and we drew near Madinah, he announced one night the departure. I got up when they announced departure and walked until I passed beyond the army. When I had finished my business, I came back to the camp and felt for my chest, and found that a necklace of mine made of Yemeni onyx beads had broken. I went back searching for my necklace, and the search for it detained me. Then the people who were saddling my camel came and lifted my howdah and loaded it onto my camel that I used to ride, thinking that I was in it. Women in those days were light, not heavy, and flesh had not weighed them down; they ate only a morsel of food. So the people did not find the howdah heavy when they lifted it, and they loaded it. I was a girl of tender age. They set the camel going and departed. I found my necklace after the army had gone on. I came to their campsite and there was no one in it. I went to the place where I had been staying, thinking that they would miss me and come back to me. While I was sitting in my place, sleep overcame me and I slept. Safwan b. al-Mu'attal al-Sulami, then al-Dhakwani, had halted in the rear of the army and then set off in the night. He reached my place in the morning and saw the dark shape of a sleeping person. He came to me, and he had seen me before the veil. I woke up at his saying 'Indeed we belong to God and to Him we shall return.' By God, he did not speak a word to me, nor did I hear from him any word other than his utterance of 'Indeed we belong to God and to Him we shall return,' until he made his mount kneel and stepped on its foreleg, and I mounted it. He set off leading the mount with me until we reached the army after they had halted to rest in the midday heat. Then those who perished perished. The one who took upon himself the greater part of the slander was Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul. We arrived in Madinah, and I fell ill there for a month. The people were spreading the talk of the slanderers while I was unaware of any of that. What troubled me during my illness was that I did not recognize from the Messenger of God the gentleness I used to see from him when I was sick. He would only enter, greet, and then say, 'How is that one of yours?' That troubled me, and I was unaware of anything until I recovered. I went out with Umm Mistah toward the open area for relieving ourselves. We did not go out except from night to night, and that was before privies were built near our houses. Our practice was the practice of the early Arabs in going out to relieve themselves. I and Umm Mistah bt. Abi Ruhm were returning after we had finished our business, walking, when Umm Mistah stumbled over her long garment and said, 'May Mistah perish!' I said to her, 'How bad is what you said! Do you revile a man who was present at Badr?' She said, 'O you there, have you not heard what he said?' I said, 'And what did he say?' She informed me of what the slanderers said, and I became more ill on top of my illness. When I returned to my house, the Messenger of God entered and said, 'How is that one of yours?' I said, 'Permit me to go to my parents.' She said: At that time I wanted to ascertain the news from them. The Messenger of God permitted me, so I went to my parents and said to my mother, 'What are the people talking about?' She said, 'My little daughter, take the matter lightly. By God, there is rarely a woman who is beautiful and loved by a husband who has co-wives but that they speak much against her.' I said, 'Glory be to God! Have the people really been talking about this?' She said: I spent that night until morning, with my tears not ceasing and no sleep touching my eyes. In the morning, the Messenger of God ﷺ called Ali b. Abi Talib and Usama b. Zayd, when the revelation was slow in coming, to consult them about separating from his wife. She said: As for Usama, he advised him according to what he knew of the innocence of his wife and what he knew in himself of affection for them. Usama said, 'O Messenger of God, she is your wife, and we know nothing but good.' As for Ali, he said, 'O Messenger of God, God has not made things narrow for you; women other than her are many. Ask the servant girl, and she will tell you the truth.' The Messenger of God called Barira and said to her, 'Have you seen anything from Aisha that troubles you?' Barira said, 'No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I have not seen anything from her that I could fault her for, except that she is a young girl who sleeps over the dough until the domestic animal comes and eats it.' She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up that same day and sought to be excused from Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul. The Messenger of God said, 'Who will excuse me from a man whose harm to my family has reached me?' He said it three times. 'By God, I know nothing but good about my family, and they have mentioned a man about whom I know nothing but good, and he never enters upon my family except with me.' Sa'd b. Mu'adh stood up and said, 'I, by God, O Messenger of God, will excuse you from him. If he is from the Aws, we will strike his neck, and if he is from our brothers of the Khazraj, you will command us and we will do to him as you command.' Sa'd b. Ubada stood up, and he was the chief of the Khazraj. He had been a righteous man before that, but zeal overcame him. He said, 'You have lied, by God's life, you will not kill him, and you cannot kill him.' Usayd b. Hudayr b. Simak stood up and said to Sa'd b. Ubada, 'You have lied, by God's life, he will surely kill him, for you are a hypocrite arguing on behalf of hypocrites.' The two tribes, Aws and Khazraj, rose up in excitement while the Messenger of God was standing on the pulpit, calming them until they fell silent, and he fell silent. I wept that day and night, my tears not ceasing and no sleep touching my eyes, until I thought that weeping would split my liver. While I was weeping, a woman of the Ansar asked permission to enter, and I permitted her. She sat weeping with me. While we were like that, the Messenger of God entered and sat down, and he had not sat with me since what was said about me had been said. A month had passed and nothing had been revealed to him concerning my affair. The Messenger of God recited the testimony of faith, then said, 'To proceed, O Aisha, I have received such and such about you. If you are innocent, God will declare you innocent, and if you have committed a sin, then ask God for forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant acknowledges a sin and then repents, God turns to him in forgiveness.' When the Messenger of God finished his speech, my tears stopped until I felt not a drop of them. I said to my father, 'Answer the Messenger of God regarding what he said.' He said, 'By God, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of God.' I said the same to my mother, and she said the same. I said, while I was a young girl who did not recite much of the Quran, 'By God, I know that you have heard what has been talked about, and it has settled in your hearts, and you have believed it. If I say that I am innocent, and God knows that I am innocent, you will not believe me in that. And if I confess to you a matter, and God knows that I am innocent of it, you will surely believe me. By God, I find no likeness for me and for you except what Abu Yusuf said: {So patience is most fitting.} And I was a young girl who did not recite much of the Quran.' Then I turned on my bed, hoping that God would declare me innocent of what I was innocent of. But by God, I did not think that revelation would be sent down concerning my affair, recitation that would be recited. For I considered myself too insignificant for Quran to be revealed about me. But I hoped that God would show His Messenger a dream in which He would declare me innocent. She said: By God, the Messenger of God had not left his seat, nor had anyone of the household gone out, when revelation came down upon him. He was seized by the intense distress that used to seize him at the time of revelation, until drops like pearls on a cold day were dripping from him. Then it was lifted from him while he was smiling. The first thing he said was, 'O Aisha, praise God, for God has declared you innocent.' My mother said to me, 'Get up and go to the Messenger of God ﷺ.' I said, 'No, by God, I will not get up to him, and I will not praise anyone but God, may He be glorified and exalted.' And God sent down {Indeed, those who came with the slander} and the rest of the verses. When God sent down this concerning my innocence, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who had been spending on Mistah b. Uthatha because of his kinship with him, said, 'By God, I will never spend anything on Mistah after what he said about Aisha.' Then God sent down this verse: {And let not those of virtue among you and wealth swear not to give...} to the end of the verse. Abu Bakr said, 'Yes, I would love for God to forgive me,' and he returned to giving Mistah what he used to spend on him. She said: The Messenger of God had asked Zaynab bt. Jahsh about my affair, saying, 'O Zaynab, what do you know and what have you seen?' She said, 'I protect my hearing and my sight. By God, I know nothing but good about her.' Aisha said: She was the one among the Prophet's wives ﷺ who used to rival me. God protected her through piety. Her sister Hamna used to fight on her behalf, and she perished among those who perished."],[19070,"(the wife of the Prophet) \"Whenever Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to go on a journey, he would draw lots amongst his wives and would take with him the one upon whom the lot fell. During a Ghazwa of his, he drew lots amongst us and the lot fell upon me, and I proceeded with him after Allah had decreed the use of the veil by women. I was carried in a Howdah (on the camel) and dismounted while still in it. When Messenger of Allah ﷺ was through with his Ghazwa and returned home, and we approached the city of Medina, Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered us to proceed at night. When the order of setting off was given, I walked till I was past the army to answer the call of nature. After finishing I returned (to the camp) to depart (with the others) and suddenly realized that my necklace over my chest was missing. So, I returned to look for it and was delayed because of that. The people who used to carry me on the camel, came to my Howdah and put it on the back of the camel, thinking that I was in it, as, at that time, women were light in weight, and thin and lean, and did not use to eat much. So, those people did not feel the difference in the heaviness of the Howdah while lifting it, and they put it over the camel. At that time I was a young lady. They set the camel moving and proceeded on. I found my necklace after the army had gone, and came to their camp to find nobody. So, I went to the place where I used to stay, thinking that they would discover my absence and come back in my search. While in that state, I felt sleepy and slept. Safwan bin Mu'attal As-Sulami Adh-Dhakwani was behind the army and reached my abode in the morning. When he saw a sleeping person, he came to me, and he used to see me before veiling. So, I got up when I heard him saying, \"Inna lil-lah-wa inn a ilaihi rajiun (We are for Allah, and we will return to Him).\" He made his camel knell down. He got down from his camel, and put his leg on the front legs of the camel and then I rode and sat over it. Safwan set out walking, leading the camel by the rope till we reached the army who had halted to take rest at midday. Then whoever was meant for destruction, fell into destruction, (some people accused me falsely) and the leader of the false accusers was ʿAbdullah bin Ubai bin Salul. After that we returned to Medina, and I became ill for one month while the people were spreading the forged statements of the false accusers. I was feeling during my ailment as if I were not receiving the usual kindness from the Prophet ﷺ which I used to receive from him when I got sick. But he would come, greet and say, 'How is that (girl)?' I did not know anything of what was going on till I recovered from my ailment and went out with Um Mistah to the Manasi where we used to answer the call of nature, and we used not to go to answer the call of nature except from night to night and that was before we had lavatories near to our houses. And this habit of ours was similar to the habit of the old 'Arabs in the open country (or away from houses). So. I and Um Mistah bint Ruhm went out walking. Um Mistah stumbled because of her long dress and on that she said, 'Let Mistah be ruined.' I said, 'You are saying a bad word. Why are you abusing a man who took part in (the battle of) Badr?' She said, 'O Hanata (you there) didn't you hear what they said?' Then she told me the rumors of the false accusers. My sickness was aggravated, and when I returned home, Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me, and after greeting he said, 'How is that (girl)?' I requested him to allow me to go to my parents. I wanted then to be sure of the news through them I Messenger of Allah ﷺ allowed me, and I went to my parents and asked my mother, 'What are the people talking about?' She said, 'O my daughter! Don't worry much about this matter. By Allah, never is there a charming woman loved by her husband who has other wives, but the women would forge false news about her.' I said, 'Glorified be Allah! Are the people really taking of this matter?' That night I kept on weeping and could not sleep till morning. In the morning Messenger of Allah ﷺ called ʿAli bin Abu Talib and Usama bin Zaid when he saw the Divine Inspiration delayed, to consul them about divorcing his wife (i.e. ʿAisha). Usama bin Zaid said what he knew of the good reputation of his wives and added, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Keep you wife, for, by Allah, we know nothing about her but good.' ʿAli bin Abu Talib said, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Allah has no imposed restrictions on you, and there are many women other than she, yet you may ask the woman-servant who will tell you the truth.' On that Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Barirah and said, 'O Barirah. Did you ever see anything which roused your suspicions about her?' Barirah said, 'No, by Allah Who has sent you with the Truth, I have never seen in her anything faulty except that she is a girl of immature age, who sometimes sleeps and leaves the dough for the goats to eat.' On that day Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and requested that somebody support him in punishing ʿAbdullah bin Ubai bin Salul. Allah's Apostle said, 'Who will support me to punish that person (ʿAbdullah bin Ubai bin Salul) who has hurt me by slandering the reputation of my family? By Allah, I know nothing about my family but good, and they have accused a person about whom I know nothing except good, and he never entered my house except in my company.' Saʿd bin Muʿadh got up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! by Allah, I will relieve you from him. If that man is from the tribe of the Aus, then we will chop his head off, and if he is from our brothers, the Khazraj, then order us, and we will fulfill your order.' On that Saʿd bin 'Ubada, the chief of the Khazraj and before this incident, he had been a pious man, got up, motivated by his zeal for his tribe and said, 'By Allah, you have told a lie; you cannot kill him, and you will never be able to kill him.' On that Usaid bin Al-Hadir got up and said (to Saʿd bin 'Ubada), 'By Allah! you are a liar. By Allah, we will kill him; and you are a hypocrite, defending the hypocrites.' On this the two tribes of Aus and Khazraj got excited and were about to fight each other, while Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing on the pulpit. He got down and quieted them till they became silent and he kept quiet. On that day I kept on weeping so much so that neither did my tears stop, nor could I sleep. In the morning my parents were with me and I had wept for two nights and a day, till I thought my liver would burst from weeping. While they were sitting with me and I was weeping, an Ansari woman asked my permission to enter, and I allowed her to come in. She sat down and started weeping with me. While we were in this state, Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and sat down and he had never sat with me since the day they forged the accusation. No revelation regarding my case came to him for a month. He recited Tashah-hud (i.e. None has the right to be worshipped but Allah and Muhammad is His Apostle) and then said, 'O ʿAisha! I have been informed such-and-such about you; if you are innocent, then Allah will soon reveal your innocence, and if you have committed a sin, then repent to Allah and ask Him to forgive you, for when a person confesses his sin and asks Allah for forgiveness, Allah accepts his repentance.' When Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his speech my tears ceased completely and there remained not even a single drop of it. I requested my father to reply to Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf. My father said, By Allah, I do not know what to say to Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' I said to my mother, 'Talk to Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf.' She said, 'By Allah, I do not know what to say to Allah's Apostle. I was a young girl and did not have much knowledge of the Qur'an. I said. 'I know, by Allah, that you have listened to what people are saying and that has been planted in your minds and you have taken it as a truth. Now, if I told you that I am innocent and Allah knows that I am innocent, you would not believe me and if I confessed to you falsely that I am guilty, and Allah knows that I am innocent you would believe me. By Allah, I don't compare my situation with you except to the situation of Joseph's father (i.e. Jacob) who said, 'So (for me) patience is most fitting against that which you assert and it is Allah (Alone) whose help can be sought.' Then I turned to the other side of my bed hoping that Allah would prove my innocence. By Allah I never thought that Allah would reveal Divine Inspiration in my case, as I considered myself too inferior to be talked of in the Holy Qur'an. I had hoped that Messenger of Allah ﷺ might have a dream in which Allah would prove my innocence. By Allah, Allah's Apostle had not got up and nobody had left the house before the Divine Inspiration came to Allah's Apostle. So, there overtook him the same state which used to overtake him, (when he used to have, on being inspired divinely). He was sweating so much so that the drops of the sweat were dropping like pearls though it was a (cold) wintry day. When that state of Messenger of Allah ﷺ was over, he was smiling and the first word he said, ʿAisha! Thank Allah, for Allah has declared your innocence.' My mother told me to go to Messenger of Allah ﷺ . I replied, 'By Allah I will not go to him and will not thank but Allah.' So Allah revealed: \"Verily! They who spread the slander are a gang among you . . .\" (24.11) When Allah gave the declaration of my Innocence, Abu Bakr, who used to provide for Mistah bin Uthatha for he was his relative, said, 'By Allah, I will never provide Mistah with anything because of what he said about Aisha.' But Allah later revealed: -- \"And let not those who are good and wealthy among you swear not to help their kinsmen, those in need and those who left their homes in Allah's Cause. Let them forgive and overlook. Do you not wish that Allah should forgive you? Verily! Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful.\" (24.22) After that Abu Bakr said, 'Yes ! By Allah! I like that Allah should forgive me,' and resumed helping Mistah whom he used to help before. Messenger of Allah ﷺ also asked Zainab bint Jahsh (i.e. the Prophet's wife about me saying, 'What do you know and what did you see?' She replied, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! I refrain to claim hearing or seeing what I have not heard or seen. By Allah, I know nothing except goodness about Aisha.\" Aisha further added \"Zainab was competing with me (in her beauty and the Prophet's love), yet Allah protected her (from being malicious), for she had piety.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2661)"],[19071,"I was with al-Walid b. 'Abd al-Malik one night as he was reciting Surat al-Nur while reclining. When he reached {Indeed, those who came with the slander are a group among you} until he reached {And the one who took upon himself the greater part of it will have a great punishment}, he sat up and said, 'O Abu Bakr, who took upon himself the greater part of it? Was it not 'Ali b. Abi Talib?' I said to myself, 'What should I say? If I say no, I fear I will encounter evil from him, and if I say yes, I will have brought a grave matter against a man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, something he did not say.' Then I said to myself, 'Allah has accustomed me to truthfulness for good.' 'No, O Commander of the Faithful.' He struck the bed with his staff two or three times, then said, 'Then who?' He repeated that several times. I said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul.' 'Urwa b. al-Zubayr, Sa'id b. al-Musayyab, 'Alqama b. Waqqas, and 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Utba narrated to me, and some of the people had better wording than others, but each of them memorized his hadith, that 'A'isha said: 'Ali made a suggestion concerning my affair, may Allah forgive him. Then she said: When the Messenger of Allah intended a journey, he would cast lots among his wives. He went on the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq and drew lots among his wives, and my lot came out, so I went out with the Messenger of Allah after the hijab had been revealed. I was carried in my howdah and taken down from it. We traveled until when the Messenger of Allah finished that expedition and returned, and we drew near to Madinah, he announced departure one night. I got up when he announced departure and walked until I passed beyond the army. When I had finished my business and came back to my mount, I noticed that a necklace of mine made of onyx of Zafar had broken, so I went back searching for my necklace, and that search detained me. The group that was loading the mounts came and lifted my howdah onto my camel that I used to ride, thinking that I was in it. Women at that time were light, not weighed down by flesh, for one of us would eat only a morsel of food, so the people did not find the lightness of the howdah strange when they lifted it. I was a young girl of recent age. They sent the camel off and departed. I found my necklace after the army had gone on. I came to their camp, and there was no one to call or answer. I made for my place where I had been, thinking that they would miss me and come back to me. While I was sitting in my place, sleep overcame me and I slept. Safwan b. al-Mu'attal al-Sulami, then al-Dhakwani, was behind the army. He traveled through the night and reached my place in the morning. He saw the black shape of a sleeping person and recognized me when he saw me, for he used to see me before the hijab. I woke up at his istirja' when he recognized me, and I covered my face with my jilbab. By Allah, he did not speak a word to me, nor did I hear from him anything except his istirja' when he made his mount kneel and stepped on its foreleg, so I mounted it, and he set off leading the mount with me until he brought me to the army after they had stopped in the intense midday heat. Then those who perished among the people of the slander perished. The one who took upon himself the greater part of the sin was 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul. We arrived in Madinah, and I fell ill for a month after our arrival. The people were spreading the words of the slanderers while I was unaware of any of that, and what made me suspicious in my illness was that I did not recognize from the Messenger of Allah the gentleness that I used to see from him when I was ill. He would only enter upon me and say, \"How is this one of you?\" then leave. That made me suspicious, but I did not know of the evil until I went out after I had recovered, I and Umm Mistah, toward my house when we had finished our business. Umm Mistah stumbled and said, 'May Mistah perish.' I said, 'What a bad thing you have said. Do you revile a man who witnessed Badr?' She said, 'O you, have you not heard what he said?' I said, 'And what did he say?' She told me about the slander of the people of the lie, and I became more ill on top of my illness. When I returned to my house, the Messenger of Allah entered upon me and said, \"How is this one of you?\" I said, 'Will you permit me to go to my parents?' He said, \"Yes.\" At that time I wanted to ascertain the news from them, so he permitted me, and I went to my mother and father. I said, 'O mother, what are the people talking about?' She said, 'O my daughter, take it lightly. By Allah, seldom is a beautiful woman loved by a man who has co-wives but that they speak much against her.' I said, 'Glory be to Allah! Have the people really spoken of this?' She said, 'Yes.' I cried that night until morning, my tears did not stop, and I did not taste sleep. Then I continued crying in the morning. The Messenger of Allah called 'Ali b. Abi Talib and Usama b. Zayd when the revelation was delayed, to consult them about separating from his wife. As for Usama, he indicated to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he knew of the innocence of his wife and what he knew in his heart of affection for them, and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, she is your family, and we know nothing but good.' As for 'Ali b. Abi Talib, he said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah has not put you in difficulty, and there are many women besides her. If you ask the servant girl, she will tell you the truth.' So the Messenger of Allah called Barira and said, \"O Barira, have you seen anything suspicious?\" Barira said, 'No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I have never seen anything against her that I could fault, except that she is a young girl who falls asleep over her family's dough, and the domestic animal comes and eats it.' On that day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the pulpit and sought someone to excuse him from 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul, saying, \"O people of Islam, who will excuse me from a man whose harm has reached me in my family? By Allah, I know nothing about my family but good, and they have mentioned a man about whom I know nothing but good, and he used not to enter upon my family except with me.\" Sa'd b. Mu'adh stood up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I will excuse you from him. If he is from the Aws, I will strike his neck, and if he is from our brothers of the Khazraj, you command us and we will do as you command.' Sa'd b. 'Ubada stood up, and he was the chief of the Khazraj that day, and before that he had been a righteous man, but zeal took hold of him, and he said to Sa'd b. Mu'adh, 'You lie, by the life of Allah, you will not kill him, and you are not able to kill him.' Usayd b. Hudayr, who was the cousin of Sa'd b. Mu'adh, stood up and said to Sa'd b. 'Ubada, 'You lie, by the life of Allah, he will certainly kill him, for you are a hypocrite arguing on behalf of the hypocrites.' She said: The two tribes, Aws and Khazraj, were stirred up until they were about to fight, while the Messenger of Allah was standing on the pulpit. He kept calming them until they fell silent, and he fell silent. She said: I wept that day, my tears did not stop, and I did not taste sleep, and my parents were with me. I had wept for two nights and a day, thinking that weeping would split my liver. While they were sitting with me and I was weeping, a woman of the Ansar asked permission to enter, and I gave her permission, and she sat weeping with me. While we were in that state, the Messenger of Allah entered upon us and sat down. She said: He had not sat with me since what was said to me had been said, and a month had passed without revelation concerning my affair. She said: When he sat, the Messenger of Allah pronounced the tashahhud, then said, \"To proceed, O 'A'isha, it has reached me about you such and such. If you are innocent, Allah will declare your innocence, but if you have committed a sin, then ask Allah for forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant admits his sin and then repents to Allah, Allah turns to him in forgiveness.\" She said: When the Messenger of Allah finished his words, my tears dried up until I felt not a drop of them. I said to my father, 'Answer the Messenger of Allah about what he said.' He said, 'By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah.' I said to my mother, 'Answer the Messenger of Allah.' She said, 'By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah.' I said, though I was a young girl who did not recite much of the Qur'an, 'By Allah, you have heard this talk until it has settled in your hearts and you have believed it. If I tell you that I am innocent, and Allah knows that I am innocent, you will not believe me about that. But if I admit a sin, while Allah knows that I am innocent, you will certainly believe me. By Allah, I find no example for myself and for you except the father of Yusuf, when he said, {So patience is most fitting, and Allah is the one sought for help against what you describe}.' Then I turned and lay down on my bed, knowing then that I was innocent and that Allah would declare my innocence. But by Allah, I did not think that Allah would send down revelation concerning my affair that would be recited, for my affair in my own estimation was too insignificant for Allah to speak about me in a matter to be recited. Rather, I hoped that Allah would show His Messenger a vision in sleep by which He would declare my innocence. She said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah did not leave his seat, nor did anyone of the household leave, until Allah sent down revelation upon him, and he was seized by what used to seize him of the intense experience, until drops of sweat like pearls flowed from him on a cold day because of the weight of the Qur'an that was being revealed to him. When the Messenger of Allah was relieved, he was relieved while smiling. The first word he spoke was, \"O 'A'isha, as for Allah, He has declared your innocence.\" My mother said to me, 'Get up and go to him.' I said, 'No, by Allah, I will not get up and go to him, and I praise none but Allah.' And Allah sent down {Indeed, those who came with the slander are a group among you}, the ten verses in full. When Allah sent down this concerning my innocence, Abu Bakr, who used to spend on Mistah because of their kinship and his poverty, said, 'By Allah, I will never spend anything on Mistah again, because of what he said about 'A'isha.' So Allah sent down {And let not those of virtue and wealth among you swear not to give...} the verse. Abu Bakr said, 'By Allah, I love that Allah should forgive me,' and he resumed the spending on Mistah that he used to give, and said, 'By Allah, I will never withdraw it from him.' 'A'isha said: The Messenger of Allah asked Zaynab bt. Jahsh about my affair, saying, \"O Zaynab, what do you know or have you seen?\" Zaynab said, 'I protect my hearing and my sight. By Allah, I know nothing but good.' She was the one who rivaled me among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, but Allah protected her through piety. Her sister Hamna began to fight on her behalf and perished among those who perished from the people of the slander. Al-Zuhri said: This is what has reached us from the hadith of these people."],[19073,"The people indeed spoke about this matter and it spread, and the Messenger of Allah stood up as a preacher concerning it, and I was not aware of it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, along with a group of his companions, upon a Nubian slave girl of mine, and the Messenger of Allah said, “What do you know about Aisha?” She said, “I know of no fault in her except that she sleeps and the sheep enters and eats her dough and her mat.” He said, “I am not asking you about this.” She said, “Then what about?” When she understood, she said, “Glory be to Allah! I know of Aisha only as the goldsmith knows the pure red gold.” Then the Prophet ﷺ went out, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, “Advise me, O assembly of Muslims, concerning a people who have maligned my family, while I have never known any evil in them, and they have maligned them by one who, by Allah, I have never known any evil in, and I have never been absent except that he was with me, and he never entered my house except that I was present.” Sa'd b. Mu'adh said, “I think their necks should be struck.” A man from the Khazraj said, “You have lied, by Allah. By Allah, if they had been from your own clan, you would not have ordered their killing.” Hassan was from the Khazraj, until there was a dispute between the Aws and the Khazraj in the mosque. Among those who spread it were Hassan b. Thabit, Mistah b. Uthathah, and Hamnah bt. Jahsh, along with others. It was spoken about in the presence of Abdullah b. Ubayy, and he would listen to it, encourage it, and spread it. Aisha said: One night I went out with the mother of Mistah for my need, and while we were walking, she stumbled and said, “May Mistah perish.” I said, “Glory be to Allah! Do you curse your son Mistah, who is among the first emigrants and who witnessed Badr?” Then she walked for a while and stumbled again and said the same thing, and I said the same to her. She said, “By Allah, I do not curse him except because of you.” I said, “What is my affair?” She informed me of the matter. Then I went to relieve myself and returned, and I fell ill with fever. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and said, “What is the matter with you, O Aisha?” I said, “I have a fever; give me permission to go to my parents.” So he permitted me, and I went. My mother was downstairs and my father was on the roof of the house praying. My mother said, “What is the matter with you, O Aisha?” I said, “The mother of Mistah told me such-and-such.” She said, “Have you only now heard of it?” So I wept, and she wept. My father heard the weeping and said, “What is the matter with my daughter?” My mother said, “She has heard of that matter just now.” He said, “O my daughter, return to your house until we come to you tomorrow.” So he came the next day, while there was a woman from the Ansar with the Prophet ﷺ. Her presence did not prevent the Prophet ﷺ from speaking. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, “To proceed: O Aisha, if you have done wrong and erred, then seek forgiveness from Allah and repent.” I said to my father, “Speak.” He said, “With what shall I speak?” I said to my mother, “Speak.” She said, “With what shall I speak?” So I praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, “To proceed: By Allah, if I say to you that I did it — while Allah knows that I did not do it — you would say, ‘She has confessed to what she did not do.’ And if I say that I did not do it — while Allah knows that I did not do it — you would say, ‘She has lied.’ And I find no example for myself and for you except what the righteous servant said: {So patience is most fitting. And Allah is the one sought for help against what you describe}.”"],[19074,"When the matter concerning me that was mentioned came up, and I knew nothing of it, the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up to address the people. He pronounced the testimony of faith, praised God, and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: \"To proceed: advise me concerning people who have slandered my family. By God, I have never known any evil in my family, and they have slandered them by means of one of whom, by God, I have never known any evil. He has never entered my house except when I was present, and I have never been absent on a journey but that he was absent with me.\" Saʿd b. Muʿādh stood up and said: \"We think, O Messenger of God, that we should strike their necks.\" A man from the Khazraj stood up—and the mother of Ḥassān b. Thābit belonged to the clan of that man—and said: \"You have lied. By God, if they had been from the Aws, you would not have liked to strike their necks.\" This went on until there was almost evil between the Aws and the Khazraj in the mosque, and I knew nothing of it. When evening came that day, I went out for some need of mine, and Umm Misṭaḥ was with me. She stumbled and said: \"May Misṭaḥ perish!\" I rebuked her and said: \"Do you revile your own son?\" She said: \"By God, I do not revile him except because of you.\" I said: \"In what matter concerning me?\" She related the story. I said: \"Has this really happened?\" She said: \"Yes, by God.\" I returned to my house as if the need for which I had gone out I had not gone out for at all, and I found no trace of it, little or much. I fell ill and said to the Messenger of God: \"Send me to my father's house.\" He sent the servant boy with me. I entered the house and found Umm Rūmān downstairs, and Abū Bakr was above in the house reciting. My mother said: \"What has brought you, my little daughter?\" I told her and mentioned the story to her. It had not affected her as it had affected me. She said: \"My little daughter, take the matter lightly. By God, rarely is there a beautiful woman loved by a man who has co-wives but that they envy her and speak about her.\" I said: \"Does my father know about it?\" She said: \"Yes.\" I said: \"And the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" She said: \"Yes.\" She said: I was moved to tears and wept. Abū Bakr heard my voice while he was above in the house reciting, so he came down and said to my mother: \"What is the matter with her?\" She said: \"The matter that was mentioned about her has reached her.\" His eyes overflowed, and he said: \"I adjure you, my little daughter, return to your house.\" She said: So I returned. She said: The Messenger of God came to my house and asked my maidservant about me. She said: \"By God, I know no fault in her except that she would sleep until the sheep came in and ate her leaven or her dough.\" She said: One of his companions rebuked her and said: \"Tell the truth to the Messenger of God.\" She said: \"Glory be to God, I know nothing about her except what the goldsmith knows about red gold.\" The matter reached that man about whom it had been said concerning her, and he said: \"Glory be to God, I have never uncovered any female.\" ʿĀʾishah said: He was killed as a martyr in the path of God. She said: My parents came to me in the morning and stayed with me until the Messenger of God entered upon me after he had prayed the afternoon prayer. My parents were on my right and left. The Prophet ﷺ pronounced the testimony of faith, praised God, and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: \"To proceed: O ʿĀʾishah, if you have committed a sin or wronged, then repent to God, for God accepts repentance from His servants.\" She said: A woman of the Anṣār had come and was sitting at the door. I said: \"Are you not ashamed before this woman to mention something?\" He admonished me, so I turned to my father and said: \"Answer him.\" He said: \"What shall I say?\" I turned to my mother and said: \"Answer him.\" She said: \"What shall I say?\" When they did not answer him, I pronounced the testimony of faith, praised God, and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: \"To proceed: By God, if I say to you that I did not do it—and God bears witness that I am truthful—that will not benefit me with you. You have spoken about it and your hearts have absorbed it. And if I say that I did it—and God bears witness that I did not—you will say she has confessed against herself. By God, I find no likeness for me and for you except—\" She said: I sought the name of Yaʿqūb but could not recall it, so I said: \"—except the father of Yūsuf when he said: {So patience is most fitting, and God is the one sought for help} [Q 12:18].\" She said: Then revelation came down upon the Messenger of God at that very moment, and it was lifted from him. I could discern joy in his face while he was wiping his forehead and saying: \"Rejoice, O ʿĀʾishah, for God has declared your innocence.\" She said: I was as angry as I had ever been. My parents said to me: \"Rise and go to him.\" I said: \"By God, I will not rise to him, nor praise him, nor praise you two. But I praise God who sent down my innocence. You heard it, so did you not deny it? But I praise God who sent down my innocence.\" As for Zaynab bt. Jaḥsh, God protected her through her religion, and she said nothing but good. As for her sister Ḥamnah, she perished among those who perished. Those who spoke about it were Misṭaḥ b. Uthāthah, Ḥassān b. Thābit, Ḥamnah, and the hypocrite ʿAbd Allāh b. Ubayy b. Salūl—he was the one who instigated it and gathered them, and he took upon himself the greater part of it. Abū Bakr swore that he would never again benefit Misṭaḥ with any benefit. Then God revealed: {Let not those of virtue and affluence among you swear not to give to the near of kin and the needy} [Q 24:22]—meaning Abū Bakr—{to give to the near of kin and the needy}—meaning Misṭaḥ—{Do you not love that God should forgive you? And God is Forgiving, Merciful} [Q 24:22]. Abū Bakr said: \"Yes, by God, O Lord, we love that You forgive us.\" So he returned to benefiting him as he used to."],[19076,"Umm Mistah entered upon me, and we went out to Hayr 'Ad. Umm Mistah stepped on a bone or a thorn and said, “May Mistah perish.” I said, “What a bad thing you have said about a man from the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ .” She said, “I bear witness that you are among the heedless believing women. Do you know what has flown upon you?” I said, “No, by God.” She said, “How long has it been since the Messenger of God was with you?” I said, “The Messenger of God does with his wives whatever he wishes; he begins with whichever of them he wishes and comes to whichever he wishes.” She said, “Verily he has closed over you such-and-such.” I fell down in a faint. It reached Umm Ruman, my mother, and when the matter reached her, she came to me, carried me, and took me to her house. It reached the Messenger of God that Aisha had heard of the matter, so he came to her, entered upon her, sat beside her, and said, “O Aisha, God has made repentance ample.” This only increased my distress beyond what I already had. While we were like that, Abu Bakr came, entered upon me, and said, “O Messenger of God, what are you waiting for regarding this one who betrayed you and disgraced me?” She said, “This increased my distress upon distress.” She said, “Then he sent for Ali and said, ‘O Ali, what do you think regarding Aisha?’ He said, ‘God and His Messenger know best.’ He said, ‘You must tell me what you think regarding Aisha.’ He said, ‘God has given women ample alternatives, but send for Burayrah, her servant, and ask her; perhaps she has become aware of something of her affair.’ So he sent for Burayrah, and she came. He said to her, ‘Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of God?’ She said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Then I will ask you about something, so do not hide it from me.’ She said, ‘Yes, O Messenger of God. There is nothing you ask me about except that I will inform you of it, and I will not hide from you anything, God willing.’ He said, ‘You have been with Aisha, so have you seen anything of her that you dislike?’ She said, ‘No, by the One who sent you with prophethood. I have not seen anything from her since I have been with her except one trait.’ He said, ‘And what is it?’ She said, ‘I kneaded dough for myself and said to Aisha, “Guard this dough until I fetch a firebrand and bake.” She got up to pray and became heedless of the dough, then a sheep came and ate it.’ Then he sent for Usamah and said, ‘O Usamah, what do you think regarding Aisha?’ He said, ‘God and His Messenger know best.’ He said, ‘You must tell me what you think about her.’ He said, ‘Then I think you should keep her until God brings about something for you regarding her.’ She said, ‘It was only a short while before revelation descended, and joy kept being seen on the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and her vindication came from heaven, meaning from God. The Messenger of God said, “Rejoice, O Aisha, then rejoice, O Aisha, for God has informed me of your vindication.” I said, “Without praise from you or your companion.” She said, “At that point I spoke. And when he came to her, he used to say, ‘How is that one of yours?’”"],[19077,"I said: O Mother of the Believers, or O my mother, will you not tell me how it was—meaning the affair of the slander? She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ married me while I was playing in the rain in Makkah, and I had nothing that men desire, and I was six years old. When it reached me that he had married me, God cast modesty upon me. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ emigrated and I was with him, and I was brought to him, and he had come to me when I was nine years old. The Messenger of God set out on a journey and took me out with him. I was light in a howdah of mine that had curtains. When they departed, I sat in it, and they lifted it while I was inside, and they tied it on the back of the camel. They halted at a campsite. I went out for my need and returned, and they had hastened to depart. I sat in the howdah, and they had seen me when I moved the curtains. When I sat in it, I struck my hand on my chest and found that I had forgotten a necklace that was with me. So I went out quickly seeking it, and returned, and the people had departed. I saw nothing but dust from afar. They had placed the howdah on the camel's back, thinking I was in it because of my lightness. Then there was a man holding the head of his camel. I said: Who is the man? He said: Safwan b. al-Mu'attal al-Sulami. Are you the Mother of the Believers? I said: Yes. He said: Indeed we belong to God and to Him we return. I said: Turn your face away from me and put your foot on the foreleg of your camel. He said: I will do so, with the blessing of an eye and honor. She said: Then I caught up with the people when they halted, and he went and set me down by the howdah. The people looked at me and I was unaware. She said: I noticed the coldness of my parents and the coldness of the Messenger of God, and I did not know what had been said, until my servant or my foster-daughter entered and said such-and-such. She said: A man of the Muhajirun said to me: How heedless you are! A shivering fever seized me, and my mother took every garment in the house and threw it over me. The Messenger of God consulted some of his companions and said: \"What do you think?\" Some of them said: There are many women, and you can find a replacement. Some said: You are the Messenger of God, and revelation descends upon you, and our affair follows your affair. Some said: By God, God will make it clear, so do not hasten. She said: My father's face became as if yellow orpiment had been poured on it. She said: The Messenger of God entered upon me and saw what I was in. He said: \"What is wrong with her?\" My mother said: Because of what is with her, because of what you all said. And it was said. He did not speak and did not say anything. She said: That increased me in what I was already feeling. She said: He came to me and said: \"Fear God, O Aisha. If you have done any of this, repent to God, for God accepts repentance from His servants and forgives evil deeds.\" She said: I sought the name of Ya'qub but could not recall it, so I said: Only I say as the father of Yusuf said: \"So patience is beautiful, and God is the one sought for help against what you describe.\" \"I only complain of my anguish and my sorrow to God, and I know from God what you do not know.\" She said: While the Messenger of God was with his companions and his face was as if orpiment had been melted on it, until revelation descended upon him. When revelation came to him, he did not blink, and his companions knew that revelation was coming to him. They began to look at his face, and it was beaming and brightening. When the revelation was completed, he said: \"Rejoice, O Abu Bakr, God has sent down the excuse of your daughter and her innocence.\" He went to her and gave her the good news. She said: And he recited to him what had been revealed concerning me. She said: Abu Bakr came hurrying, almost falling. She said: I said: By the praise of God, not by the praise of your companion from whom you came. The Messenger of God came and sat at my head, and took my hand. I pulled my hand away from him. Abu Bakr struck me and said: Will you pull your hand away from the Messenger of God, or do such a thing to the Messenger of God? The Messenger of God laughed. She said: This was my affair."],[19078,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me while I wore a huf (amulet). No sooner did he marry me than Allah cast upon me modesty and the huf.” He said: “The huf is something the Bedouins make for children from suras (chapters of the Qur’an) that the Bedouins put on their sons.”"],[19079,"When my exoneration came down from heaven, the Prophet ﷺ came and informed me of that. I said, 'Praise be to Allah, not to you.'"],[19080,"I was accused of that of which I was accused while I was unaware. While the Prophet ﷺ was sitting with me, he then sat up straight, wiped his face, and said: 'O Aisha, rejoice.' I said: 'By the praise of Allah, not by your praise.' Then he recited to me these verses: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware, believing women} and the verses."],[19081,"When I learned of what they were saying, I resolved to go to a well and throw myself into it."],[19082,"When what happened regarding my necklace took place, the people of the slander said what they said. Then I went out with the Prophet ﷺ on another expedition, and my necklace also fell, such that searching for it detained the people until dawn broke. I met from Abu Bakr whatever Allah willed. He said to me, 'O my little daughter, on a journey you are a burden and a trial, and the people have no water.' Then Allah sent down the concession of tayammum. Abu Bakr said, 'Indeed, by Allah, O my little daughter, you are, as I have known, blessed.'"],[19083,"«The Messenger of God ﷺ summoned Ali and Usama and consulted them.» As for Usama, he spoke well and said, \"Your family, and we know nothing but good; this is falsehood and lying.\" As for Ali, he said, \"Women are many, and you are able to seek out and ask the young woman, for she will tell the truth.\" And he mentioned the Hadith of the Ifk."],[19084,"While I was sitting with Aisha, a woman from the Ansar came and said, \"Allah has done such and such to so-and-so and so-and-so.\" Aisha asked, \"What is that?\" The woman replied, \"So-and-so and so-and-so.\" Aisha said, \"Has the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard about it?\" The woman answered, \"Yes.\" Aisha asked, \"And Abu Bakr?\" The woman replied, \"Yes.\" Aisha then fainted and when she regained consciousness, she had a high fever. Her clothes were thrown on her and the Prophet ﷺ came and she was lying down. He asked, \"What is wrong with her?\" They said, \"She has been overcome by a fever caused by distress.\" He said, \"Perhaps her condition is because of a conversation she had with someone.\" So he sat down and Aisha said, \"By Allah, if I was to take an oath with you that you would not believe me, and if I were to confess to you, you would not accept my confession. My likeness and your likeness is like the likeness of Jacob and his sons. (Allah knows) I called upon my father and he did not answer me. I called upon my mother and she did not answer me. I called upon my aunt and she responded to my call.' [Allah says] 'And Allah is the One whose help is to be sought over that which you describe. (12:18)' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and the excuse was revealed to him. He came back and said, 'It is due to the praise of Allah, not due to the praise of me or anyone else.'\""],[19085,"When the Prophet ﷺ traveled, he traveled with one of his wives and drew lots among them. He traveled with Aisha bt. Abi Bakr. She had a howdah, and the howdah had men who carried it and set it down. The Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions made a stop, and Aisha went out for a need and went far off, and no one noticed her. The Prophet ﷺ and the people woke up and had already departed. The men who carried the howdah came and carried it, thinking only that she was inside it, and they set off. Aisha came back and found that they had departed, so she sat in her place. A man from the Ansar called Safwan b. al-Mu'attal woke up; he did not approach women. He came near her, and he had a camel with him. When he saw her, he mounted her, and he had seen her before the veil. He led the camel with her until they reached the people, with the Prophet ﷺ and Aisha with him. They spoke much about it, and that reached the Prophet ﷺ, and it weighed heavily on him until he withdrew from her and consulted Zayd b. Thabit and others about her. He said, \"O Messenger of God, leave her; perhaps God will bring about something for you concerning her.\" Ali b. Abi Talib said, \"Women are many.\" The Prophet ﷺ then charged her, and Aisha went out one night walking among women, and Umm Mistah stumbled and said, \"May Mistah perish.\" Aisha said, \"How bad is what you have said! Do you say this about a man among the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" She said, \"You do not know what they are saying,\" and she told her the news. Aisha fell down unconscious. Then the Quran came down with her excuse in Surat al-Nur: {Indeed, those who brought the falsehood are a group among you} until it reached {and the one who took upon himself the greater part of it will have a great punishment}. And it came down: {And let not those of virtue among you swear} until His saying {and God is Forgiving, Merciful}. Abu Bakr used to give to Mistah and be kind to him and maintain ties with him, and he was one of those who spoke much against Aisha. Abu Bakr swore that he would not give him anything. Then this verse came down: {Do you not love that God should forgive you?} The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to go to her and give her good news. Abu Bakr came and told her of her excuse and what God had sent down. She said, \"No, by your praise, nor by the praise of your companion.\""],[19086,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Aisha, \"O Aisha, God has sent down your excuse.\" She said, \"By God's praise, not by your praise.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ left Aisha's presence, then he sent for Abdullah b. Ubayy and had him flogged with two hadd punishments, and he sent for Mistah and Hamnah and had them flogged."],[19088,"«When the Prophet ﷺ intended a journey, he cast lots among his wives.»"],[19089,"The man about whom it was said what was said said, \"By God, I have never uncovered a female since I have been born, and he was killed as a martyr in the path of God.\" Urwah did not name him."],[19090,"«...to strike Hassan b. Thabit with the sword, one blow.»"],[19092,"From Ibn Abbas regarding: {Indeed, those who brought the falsehood are a group among you}: «He means they brought the lie against Aisha; four of you.»"],[19093,"From Mujahid regarding His saying {Indeed, those who brought the falsehood are a group among you}: He said, \"The companions of Aisha.\""],[19094,"From Sa'id b. Jubayr regarding {Indeed, those who brought the falsehood} meaning «the lie» {a group among you} meaning «Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul the hypocrite, Hassan b. Thabit, Mistah b. Uthathah, and Hamnah bt. Jahsh.»"],[19095,"From Qatadah regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {Indeed, those who brought the falsehood} meaning the lie. He said, \"This concerns Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, and what was spread about her and said to her.\""],[19096,"From Ibn Abbas regarding {Do not consider it evil for you; rather it is good for you}: «He means good for the Messenger of God ﷺ and an exoneration for the mistress of the women of the believers, and good for Abu Bakr and the mother of Aisha and Safwan b. al-Mu'attal. Do not consider what was said to you of the lie evil for you; rather it is good for you because you will be rewarded for that.»"],[19097,"«Whoever waded into the matter of Aisha, according to the extent to which he waded into her matter.»"],[19098,"Will you leave this one while he enters upon you, and he is one of those who undertook the greater part of it among them? She said, \"And I did not see him except that a great punishment had befallen him.\""],[19099,"Allah: {And the one who undertook the greater part of it among them—for him is a great punishment}? She said, \"And what punishment is more severe than blindness?\" Then she said, \"Indeed he defends or attacks on behalf of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[19100,"A'ishah said, \"Or do you not see that he is in great punishment? And Hassan's sight was afflicted.\""],[19101,"Allah: {And the one who undertook the greater part of it among them—for him is a great punishment}? A'ishah said, \"Is he not in great punishment? There, his sight has already gone.\""],[19102,"Allah: {And the one who undertook the greater part of it among them—for him is a painful punishment} in the recitation of 'Abd Allah. Then she said, \"Is he not in punishment? His sight has been taken away.\" Then he recited to her a verse he had composed about her: \"A chaste and dignified woman, not suspected of any fault, and she rises hungry from the flesh of unwary women.\""],[19103,"\"And the one who took charge of his arrogance was Abdullah bin Ubayy.\""],[19104,"From Ibn 'Abbas: {And the one who undertook the greater part of it} \"He means its spreading and broadcasting.\" {Among them} \"He means 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul.\" {For him is a great punishment} \"He means in this world the flogging—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ flogged him eighty lashes—and in the Hereafter his destination is to the Fire.\""],[19105,"{The one who undertook the greater part of it}: 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul, Mistah b. Uthathah, Hassan b. Thabit, and Hamnah bt. Jahsh; and most of that was from 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy."],[19106,"From Mujahid concerning His saying {And the one who undertook the greater part of it among them—for him is a great punishment}: he said, \"'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul.\""],[19107,"\"She was not innocent of him nor was he innocent of her.\" {For him is a great punishment}: \"And in this verse there is a lesson for all Muslims: when there is a sin among them by someone who assisted it by deed or word or alluded to it or was pleased by it or approved it, then he shares in that sin according to the measure of what came from him. And when a sin occurs among the Muslims, then one who witnessed it and disliked it is like one who was absent, and one who was absent and approved it is like one who witnessed it.\""],[19108,"From Qatadah concerning His saying {And the one who undertook the greater part of it among them—for him is a great punishment}: he said, \"The one who undertook the greater part of it was Hassan b. Thabit and Mistah b. Uthathah.\""],[19109,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ consulted about her, and they said good, and they said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this is a lie and falsehood,\" and the believing women—he means Zaynab bt. Jahsh and Barirah, the freedwoman of A'ishah, and all the wives of the Prophet ﷺ—said, \"This is a great lie.\""],[19110,"\"Because among them was Zaynab bt. Jahsh.\" {Of themselves good} \"Should not some of them have thought good of others, since they did not see this?\" {And they said, \"This is a slander\"} \"Should they not have said, 'This accusation is a clear lie'?\""],[19111,"From Qatadah regarding His saying: {Why, when you heard it, did you not say, \"It is not for us to speak of this. Exalted are You, O Allah; this is a great slander?\"} He said: \"You should say, 'You have lied,' and say, 'This is a clear lie.' By my life, not to repeat evil about your Muslim brother when you hear it is better for you and safer than spreading it, broadcasting it, and believing it.\""],[19112,"In his saying \"{If only when you heard it, the believing men and believing women had thought well of one another}\", some of them said to others, \"Why don't you listen to his saying?\""],[19113,"From Ibn Abbas: \"{Why did they not bring four witnesses to it?} If they had, they and those who testified would be liars. {And when they do not produce the witnesses, then it is they, in the sight of Allah, who are the liars.} He means: the lie itself.\""],[19114,"From Sa'id b. Jubayr regarding His saying: {Why did they not bring} meaning \"for the slander\" {four witnesses to it? And when they do not produce the witnesses, then it is they, in the sight of Allah, who are the liars} meaning \"those who slandered Aisha.\""],[19115,"From Abu Sakhr: \"{Why did they not bring four witnesses to it? And when they do not produce the witnesses, then it is they, in the sight of Allah, who are the liars.} Everyone who slanders a Muslim and then does not bring four witnesses is a slanderer upon whom the punishment for slander is due.\""],[19116,"From Ibn Abbas: \"{And if it had not been for the favor of Allah upon you and His mercy in this world and the Hereafter} meaning: had it not been for what Allah graciously bestowed upon you and concealed you with, {a great punishment would have touched you for what you plunged into} meaning: from the lie. {A great punishment} meaning: one without end.\""],[19117,"From Sa'id b. Jubayr: \"{And if it had not been for the favor of Allah upon you and His mercy in this world and the Hereafter} In it there is an inversion; He says: {If it had not been for the favor of Allah upon you and His mercy in this world and the Hereafter, a great punishment would have touched you} meaning 'would have befallen you' {for what you plunged into} meaning 'for what you said concerning the slander.' {A great punishment} 'the punishment would have befallen you in this world and the Hereafter.'\""],[19118,"From Qatadah regarding His saying: {And if it had not been for the favor of Allah upon you and His mercy, a great punishment would have touched you for what you plunged into.} He said: \"This is concerning the affair of Aisha ؓ and what was said; the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ almost perished because of it.\""],[19119,"From Ibn Abbas: \"{When you received it with your tongues and said with your mouths that of which you had no knowledge} He says: 'Allah knows the opposite of it.' {And you thought it was insignificant while it was, in the sight of Allah, tremendous.} He says: 'You slandered the mistress of the women, the mother of the believers, the wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and attributed to her what was not in her and never entered her heart. I created her pure and protected her from every indecency.'\""],[19120,"And I heard from so-and-so. {And you said with your mouths} meaning 'with your tongues,' meaning 'from slandering her.' {That of which you had no knowledge} meaning 'without knowing that what you said of slander was true.' {And you thought it was insignificant} He says: 'You thought that slander was a minor sin.' {While it was, in the sight of Allah, tremendous} meaning 'in the burden.'"],[19121,"From Mujahid in his statement, \"When you received it with your tongues,\" he said, \"Some of you narrate it from others.\""],[19122,"From Mujahid regarding His saying: {When you received it} \"You narrated it one from another.\""],[19123,"I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah say: Aisha used to recite this verse: {When you received it with your tongues} and she would say: \"It is only the lie of a liar.\" And Ibn Abi Mulaykah said: \"She knows best about it; it was only revealed concerning her.\""],[19124,"I heard Aisha recite it: {When you received it with your tongues}"],[19125,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Usamah regarding the affair of 'A'ishah when she was accused of the slander, \"What do you say?\" He said, \"Glory be to Allah! It is not lawful for us to speak of this. Glory be to You! This is a great slander.\""],[19126,"\"That we speak of this. Glory be to You! This is a great slander.\" He means by the slander, the great fabrication, like His saying regarding Maryam: {And their saying about Maryam is a great slander}."],[19127,"{\"That we speak of this\"} meaning \"with the accusation, and our eyes did not see it.\" {Glory be to You} meaning \"should you not say, 'Glory be to You'?\" {This is a great slander} meaning should you not say the like of what Sa'd b. Mu'adh al-Ansari said? That is because when Sa'd heard the saying of those who spoke about the affair of 'A'ishah, he said, \"Glory be to You! This is a great slander.\" And the slander is that which one fabricates, saying what did not happen."],[19128,"\"That you should ever return to the like of it, if you are believers.\" He means Mistah b. Uthathah, Hamnah bt. Jahsh, and Hassan b. Thabit. {If you are believers} he says, \"if you are truthful in Allah and His Messenger.\""],[19129,"\"That you should ever return to the like of it\" meaning \"the accusation.\""],[19130,"Regarding His saying {Allah admonishes you that you should ever return to the like of it}, he said, \"He forbids you.\""],[19131,"In His saying \"Allah advises you to never return to the like of it\""],[19132,"From Ibn 'Abbas: {And Allah makes clear to you the verses} \"He means the verses that He sent down regarding 'A'ishah and the declaration of her innocence.\" {And Allah is Knowing, Wise} \"Knowing of what is in your hearts of regret for what you indulged in; Wise in that He decreed eighty lashes for the slander.\""],[19133,"From Sa'id b. Jubayr: {And Allah makes clear to you the verses} meaning \"what He mentioned of admonitions.\""],[19134,"\"That immorality should spread among those who believe\" \"He means the chaste men and chaste women among the believers.\" {For them is a painful punishment} \"He means painful.\" {In this world and the Hereafter} \"He means in this world the flogging, and in the Hereafter the punishment in the Fire.\" {And Allah knows, and you do not know} \"He means He knows what you have entered into and the severity of the punishment in it, and you do not know the severity of Allah's wrath upon the one who did this.\""],[19135,"From Mujahid regarding His saying {Indeed, those who love that immorality should spread among those who believe}: it appears in a hadith concerning the affair of 'A'ishah."],[19136,"About Qatadah in his saying \"Indeed, those who love for immorality to be spread among the believers, for them is a painful punishment\" meaning \"adultery\"."],[19137,"\"That it should become widespread and apparent, i.e., adultery.\" {Among those who believe} meaning \"Safwan and 'A'ishah.\" {For them is a painful punishment} meaning \"painful.\" {In this world and the Hereafter} So the punishment of 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy in this world was the prescribed punishment, and in the Hereafter the punishment of the Fire. {And Allah knows, and you do not know}."],[19138,"From Qatadah regarding His saying {Indeed, those who love that immorality should spread among those who believe}: \"That adultery should appear. For them is the punishment of the Fire.\""],[19139,"{And Allah is Kind} – meaning, from mercy, Merciful to you since you regretted and returned to the truth."],[19140,"{And Allah is Kind} – meaning, Kind to you when He pardoned and did not punish you for what you said of slander."],[19141,"That I may accept your repentance.” {And Allah is Hearing, Knowing} – “of your words, knowing of what is in your hearts of remorse and repentance.”"],[19142,"From Sa'id b. Jubayr: {O you who believe, do not follow the footsteps of Satan} – meaning, “Satan's beautification until he slandered 'A'ishah.” {And whoever follows the footsteps of Satan} – meaning, “Satan's beautification.” {For he commands immorality} – meaning, “acts of disobedience,” {and wrongdoing} – “what is not recognized, meaning like what was said about 'A'ishah.” {And had it not been for the favor of Allah upon you and His mercy} – meaning, “His blessing,” {none of you would have been pure} – meaning, “none of you would ever have been righteous.” {But Allah purifies whom He wills} – meaning, “He makes righteous whom He wills.”"],[19143,"From Mujahid regarding His saying: {And let not those of virtue among you and wealth swear not to give to the near of kin, the needy, and the emigrants in the way of Allah. And let them pardon and overlook. Do you not love that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.} He said: Abu Bakr swore that he would not benefit an orphan in his care who spread that – meaning regarding 'A'ishah. When this verse was revealed, he said: I love that Allah should forgive me, and I will be better to him than I was."],[19144,"From Mujahid regarding His saying: {And let not those of virtue among you and wealth swear...} He said: Abu Bakr swore not to benefit an orphan who was in his care. 'Abd al-Malik said: He is Mistah b. Uthathah b. 'Abbad b. al-Muttalib. He spread that. When this verse was revealed, {Do you not love that Allah should forgive you?}, Abu Bakr said: Yes, I love that Allah should forgive me, and I will be better to the orphans than I was."],[19145,"{That they give to the near of kin, the needy, and the emigrants in the way of Allah. And let them pardon and overlook.} “I have placed in you, O Abu Bakr, virtue, and given you wealth, knowledge of Allah, and recognition of kinship. So be compassionate, O Abu Bakr, toward Mistah, for he has kinship, emigration, poverty, and witnessed events I approved of, among them Badr.” {Do you not love that Allah should forgive you?} – meaning, “so forgive Mistah.” {And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful} – meaning, “for I am forgiving to those who err, merciful to My allies.”"],[19146,"In his saying (And let not those of virtue and abundance among you swear not to give [aid] to their relatives and the needy), it is said that there were people from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ who accused Aisha with something foul and spread it, talked about it, and some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ swore not to give charity to anyone who talks about such things and does not give to them. So Allah said, \"Let not those of virtue and abundance among you swear not to give [aid] to their relatives and the needy.\" He ordered them to join their kinship and give from their wealth as they used to do before that, so Allah commanded to forgive them and to pardon them."],[19147,"From Qatadah regarding His saying: {And let not those of virtue among you and wealth swear...} up to {...the needy}. He says: Those of virtue and wealth among you should not swear not to give to the near of kin... up to {Forgiving, Merciful}. This verse was revealed about a man of Quraysh called Mistah, who had kinship with Abu Bakr and was an orphan in his care. He was among those who spread about 'A'ishah what they spread. When Allah revealed her innocence and excuse, Abu Bakr swore that he would not give him anything. He said: Do you not love that Allah should forgive you? He said: Yes. He said: So pardon and overlook. Abu Bakr said: No, I will not withhold from him any good I used to give him before today."],[19148,"\"Do not compete\" meaning do not swear oaths \"the people of virtue among you\" meaning in wealth \"and abundance in provision\" meaning Abu Bakr \"and let them pardon and overlook\" meaning and let them forgive someone who is well-regarded \"to give to their near relatives\" meaning the near relative Mas'adah ibn Uthatha, for he was a relative of Abu Bakr's maternal cousin because Mas'adah was poor \"and to the emigrants in the cause of Allah\" because he was one of the emigrants \"Do you not love\" meaning Abu Bakr \"that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving and Merciful\" meaning Forgiving of sins, Merciful towards the believers. So the Prophet ﷺ said to Abu Bakr, \"Do you not love that Allah should forgive you?\" Abu Bakr replied, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Then pardon and overlook.\" Abu Bakr said, \"I have pardoned and overlooked. I will not prevent him from good after today.\""],[19149,"Regarding His saying: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware, believing women are cursed in this world and the Hereafter} – every one who slanders a chaste woman Allah curses. He said: “No, this verse was revealed specifically regarding the affair of 'A'ishah.”"],[19150,"“Adultery.” I said: Allah says {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware, believing women...} He said: “This was revealed specifically regarding 'A'ishah.”"],[19151,"The Prophet ﷺ flogged Hassan b. Thabit, 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy, Mistah, and Hamnah bt. Jahsh, each of them eighty lashes for slandering 'A'ishah. Then they repented after that, except 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy among the hypocrites; he died upon his hypocrisy."],[19152,"From Salamah b. Nubayt, from al-Dahhak b. Muzahim, he said: This verse was revealed specifically regarding the wives of the Prophet ﷺ: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware, believing women} – the verse."],[19153,"From Qatadah regarding His saying: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware and believing women are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and for them is a great punishment.} He said: It was revealed concerning the affair of 'A'ishah ؓ."],[19154,"From Ibn 'Abbas: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste women} \"meaning the pure ones\" {unaware, believing women} \"meaning those who affirm the oneness of Allah and His messengers\" {are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and for them is a great punishment} \"meaning He expelled them from faith.\""],[19155,"From Ibn 'Abbas regarding His saying: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware and believing women are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and for them is a great punishment.} He means \"the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. The people of hypocrisy accused them, so He made the curse and wrath obligatory for them, and they incurred wrath from Allah. All of that concerns the wives of the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[19156,"From al-Kalbi regarding His saying: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware and believing women are cursed} \"This verse specifically refers to the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. As for whoever accuses a Muslim woman, he is an evildoer, as Allah said, or he may repent.\""],[19157,"He recited Surat al-Nur and explained it. When he reached this verse: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware and believing women are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and for them is a great punishment.} he said: \"This is about 'A'ishah and the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. He did not grant repentance to those who did that, but He granted repentance to those who accuse a believing woman other than the wives of the Prophet ﷺ.\" Then he recited: {And those who accuse chaste women and then do not produce four witnesses - lash them with eighty lashes and do not accept from them testimony ever. And those are the defiantly disobedient.} \"For these He made repentance.\" {Except for those who repent after that and correct themselves, for indeed Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.} \"He made repentance for those who accuse a believing woman, but He did not make repentance for those who accuse a wife of the Prophet ﷺ.\" Then he recited this verse: {They are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and for them is a great punishment.} \"Some of the people wanted to stand up to Ibn 'Abbas to kiss his head for the excellence of his explanation.\""],[19158,"From Qatadah regarding His saying: {On that Day Allah will pay them in full their true due} \"the people of truth will be given their truth, and the people of falsehood their falsehood, and they will know that Allah is the clear truth.\""],[19159,"'Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul doubted the religion, and he was the chief of the hypocrites. He wanted the doubt to be removed from him and to be certain when certainty would not benefit him.\""],[19160,"{and they will know that Allah is the clear truth} meaning \"the clear justice.\""],[19161,"{And good women are for good men} meaning by good women 'A'ishah. Allah made her good for His Messenger ﷺ. Jibril ﷺ brought her to him in a piece of silk before she was formed in her mother's womb, and said to him: \"This is 'A'ishah bt. Abi Bakr, your wife in this world and your wife in the Hereafter, in place of Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid.\" That was at the death of Khadijah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delighted with her for himself and his eye was comforted by her. Then he said: {And good men are for good women} \"meaning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Allah made him good for Himself and made him the master of the children of Adam.\" {Good women} meaning 'A'ishah ؓ."],[19162,"\"The good (deeds) mean the beautiful (words) for the good people among men and women who believe in the believers (men) and the believers (women) are better, and the good men and women for the good (deeds) because the good (words) are suitable for them.\""],[19163,"In his saying, \"The evil women are for the evil men, and the evil men are for the evil women, and the good women are for the good men, and the good men are for the good women.\" He said, \"This was revealed concerning Aisha when the hypocrite accused her falsely and slandered her. Allah exonerated her from that. Abdullah ibn Ubayy was the evil one, so he was the one more deserving of having evil women, and they were more deserving of having him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was good, so he was more deserving of having good women, and Aisha was a good woman, and she was more deserving of having a good husband.\""],[19164,"The woman with Abdullah bin Ubayy was a hypocrite, and then the Quran was revealed with the verse {The impure women} meaning \"the woman of Abdullah\" {are for the impure men} meaning \"Abdullah bin Ubayy\" {and impure men are for impure women} meaning \"Abdullah bin Ubayy is for his wife\" {and pure women are for pure men} meaning \"Aisha and the wives of the Prophet ﷺ \" {and pure men are for pure women} meaning \"the Prophet ﷺ \" {They are free from what they say} until the end of the verse."],[19165,"From Salamah b. Nubayt, from al-Dahhak b. Muzahim, regarding His saying: {Evil words are for evil men} he said: \"evil words from speech are for evil people.\" And regarding His saying: {And good words are for good men} he said: \"good words from speech are for good people.\""],[19166,"In his saying, \"The good and the evil,\" he said, \"It is the bad speech and the good speech. The good speech is for the believers and the bad speech is for the disbelievers.\""],[19167,"Regarding His saying: {Evil words are for evil men} he said: \"evil words from speech are for evil people, and evil people are for evil words from speech. And good words from speech are for good people, and good people are for good words from speech.\""],[19168,"From Mujahid regarding His saying: {Evil words are for evil men, and good words are for good men} he said: \"evil speech and good speech - for the good believer and for the evil disbeliever.\""],[19169,"Regarding His saying {Evil women are for evil men, and good women are for good men}, he said: “The evil words are for the evil people, and the good words are for the good people.”"],[19170,"In his statement \"evil women are for evil men, and good women are for good men\", he said \"evil women are from the speech of evil people, and good women are from the speech of good people\"."],[19171,"In his saying \"The evil women for the evil men,\" he said, \"The evil speech is for the evil people.\" And in his saying, \"The good women for the good men,\" he said, \"The good speech is for the good people.\""],[19172,"In his saying, \"Evil women are for evil men, and evil men are for evil women, and good women are for good men, and good men are for good women,\" it is said that evil women belong to evil men from among the people, and evil men belong to evil women from among the people, and good women belong to good men from among the people. Don't you see that you hear the word \"evil\" from a righteous man and you say, \"May Allah forgive so-and-so, this is not from his character nor from what he says.\""],[19173,"From Ibn Abbas regarding His saying {Evil women are for evil men, and evil men are for evil women}, he said: “Evil words are for evil men, and evil men are for evil words. {And good women are for good men} he said: “And good words are for good men. It was revealed concerning those who said about the Prophet's wife ﷺ what they said of slander.” And it is also said: “Evil women are for evil men: evil deeds belong to the wicked, and good deeds belong to the good.”"],[19174,"When the people indulged in talk about Aisha's affair, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Aisha. She said: I came while I was trembling without fever. He said: “O Aisha, what are the people saying?” I said: No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I will not offer any excuse to you until my innocence comes down from heaven. Then Allah revealed fifteen verses of Surah al-Nur concerning her. Then al-Hakam recited until he reached {Evil women are for evil men, and evil men are for evil women, and good women are for good men, and good men are for good women}. He said: “Evil women are for evil men, and evil men are for evil women, and good women are for good men, and good men are for good women.”"],[19175,"From Qatadah regarding His saying {Evil women are for evil men, and evil men are for evil women}: “of speech and action.” {And good women are for good men, and good men are for good women}: “of speech and action.”"],[19176,"From Ibn Abbas: {Those are declared innocent of what they say}: “He means Allah's declaration of innocence from the lie of Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul.” {For them is forgiveness}: “He means protection in this world and forgiveness in the Hereafter.” {And noble provision}: “He means the provision of Paradise and a great reward.”"],[19177,"{For them is forgiveness} means “for their sins,” {and noble provision} means “good provision in Paradise. When Aisha's innocence was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ embraced her, and she is among his wives in Paradise.”"],[19178,"From Mujahid regarding His saying {Those are declared innocent of what they say}: He said: “Everyone is declared innocent of speech that is not rightfully his.”"],[19179,"From Mujahid regarding His saying {Those are declared innocent of what they say}: “Whoever is good is declared innocent of every evil word he utters; Allah will forgive it. And whoever is evil is declared innocent of every righteous word he utters; Allah will reject it and not accept it from him.”"],[19180,"From Mujahid regarding His saying {Those are declared innocent of what they say}: “That is because whatever good word a disbeliever says belongs to the believer, and whatever evil word a believer says belongs to the disbeliever. Each sees speech that is not rightfully his.”"],[19181,"In his saying, \"{They are absolved of what they say},\" he said, \"Here Aisha is cleared, \"{They have forgiveness and noble provision}.\""],[19182,"From Qatadah regarding His saying {Those are declared innocent of what they say, for them is forgiveness and noble provision}: “Forgiveness for their sins, and it is Paradise.”"],[19183,"“The expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq was in Sha'ban of the year six. In that expedition, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took Aisha with him after drawing lots among his wives, and her lot came out. In that expedition, the people of falsehood said what they said about her, and Allah ﷻ sent down her innocence.”"],[19184,"“It was in the year six of the Hijrah, the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq. In this expedition, the people of falsehood said about Aisha what they said, and the Quran was revealed concerning her: {Indeed, those who came with falsehood...} the verses.”"],[19185,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ flogged them eighty lashes each."],[19186,"When my exoneration was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the pulpit and mentioned that and recited the Quran. When he descended, he ordered two men and a woman, and they were flogged with their prescribed punishment."],[19187,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah will flog those who slandered Aisha eighty lashes each before all creatures. My Lord will seek forgiveness for the Muhajirun among them, and I will consult you, O Aisha.\" Aisha heard the speech and wept while she was in the house. Then she said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth as a prophet, your joy is more beloved to me than my own joy.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled, laughing, and said: \"The daughter of her father.\""],[19188,"To me, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I have been to you like Abu Zar'in father to Umm Zar'in.\" Then he started narrating the Hadith of Umm Zar'in and her companions. One of them said, \"My husband is Ayayaa Tabaaqaa, every sickness has a cure except for his stubbornness or foolishness or when he combines them all.\" Another said, \"My husband is the meat of a skinny camel in a rough and steep mountain, he is neither fat nor easy to move.\" Another said, \"My husband is Al-Asannaaq, if I remain silent, he divorces me, and if I speak, he suspends me.\" Another said, \"My husband is someone who becomes restless when he drinks, and when he sleeps, he snores. He doesn't insert his hand in the pot, but still knows what's boiling.\" Another said, \"My husband's news is incomplete, I fear that I won't complete it.\" Urwah said to her, \"These are five women complaining.\" Another said, \"My husband is a free man, like the night of Tihama. He is not hot, nor cold, nor afraid.\" Another said, \"When he enters, he roars, and when he leaves, he becomes a lion. He doesn't ask about his properties.\" Another said, \"My husband's scent is the scent of thyme and musk. I smell it more than others smell it.\" Another said, \"My husband is tall and his hairs are long, he has a great pile of ashes. Our house is close to the marketplace.\" Another said, \"My husband is Abu Malik, and who is Abu Malik? He is a man with many camels, but few blessed ones. When they hear the sound of female singers, they know it's them.\" Another said, \"My husband is Abu Zar' and who is Abu Zar'? He is a man from noble lineage, with ears and body full of fat. I managed to deceive him, so I deceived him to get pregnant. I am the daughter of Abu Zar', and who is the daughter of Abu Zar'? Her clothes are filled, and her cloak is small. She is the best among women, but her neighbors hate her. Her father and mother obey her. She is the servant of Abu Zar', and who is the servant of Abu Zar'? She never spreads our secrets, nor spoils our reputation, nor misbehaves in our house. Abu Zar' came to me when I was in labor, and he pat me until he took me to Sahil, Taee and Dayis. I am with him, I drink, and I relax. In the morning, when I wake up, I say that I am not ugly. Abu Zar' left me, and the female camels were in labor. He saw a woman with two sons playing under her, with pomegranates on both sides. Abu Zar' married her, and divorced me. After that, I married a young man, who rode a fast horse and carried a piercing spear. He pleased me and provided me with a rich gift. He came to me on every occasion as a husband should. He said to me, 'I am your husband, and you are my wife. If I gathered everything from him, I would put it in a smaller vessel than the vessels of Abu Zar', and it wouldn't fill it.' Aisha said, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'So I have been to you like Abu Zar'in father to Umm Zar'in.'\""],[19189,"Eleven women sat (at a place) and promised and contracted that they would not conceal anything of the news of their husbands. The first one said, \"My husband is like the meat of a slim weak camel which is kept on the top of a mountain which is neither easy to climb, nor is the meat fat, so that one might put up with the trouble of fetching it.\" The second one said, \"I shall not relate my husband's news, for I fear that I may not be able to finish his story, for if I describe him, I will mention all his defects and bad traits.\" The third one said, \"My husband, the \"too-tall\"! if I describe him (and he hears of that) he will divorce me, and if I keep quiet, he will keep me hanging (neither divorcing me nor treating me as a wife).\" The fourth one said, \"My husband is (moderate in temper) like the night of Tihama: neither hot nor cold; I am neither afraid of him, nor am I discontented with him.\" The fifth one said, \"My husband, when entering (the house) is a leopard (sleeps a lot), and when going out, is a lion (boasts a lot). He does not ask about whatever is in the house.\" The sixth one said, \"If my husband eats, he eats too much (leaving the dishes empty), and if he drinks he leaves nothing; if he sleeps he sleeps he rolls himself (alone in our blankets); and he does not insert his palm to inquire about my feelings.\" The seventh one said, \"My husband is a wrong-doer or weak and foolish. All the defects are present in him. He may injure your head or your body or may do both.\" The eighth one said, \"My husband is soft to touch like a rabbit and smells like a Zarnab (a kind of good smelling grass).\" The ninth one said, \"My husband is a tall generous man wearing a long strap for carrying his sword. His ashes are abundant (i.e. generous to his guests) and his house is near to the people (who would easily consult him).\" The tenth one said, \"My husband is Malik (possessor), and what is Malik? Malik is greater than whatever I say about him. (He is beyond and above all praises which can come to my mind). Most of his camels are kept at home (ready to be slaughtered for the guests) and only a few are taken to the pastures. When the camels hear the sound of the lute (or the tambourine) they realize that they are going to be slaughtered for the guests.\" The eleventh one said, \"My husband is Abu Zarʿ and what is Abu Zarʿ (i.e., what should I say about him)? He has given me many ornaments and my ears are heavily loaded with them and my arms have become fat (i.e., I have become fat). And he has pleased me, and I have become so happy that I feel proud of myself. He found me with my family who were mere owners of sheep and living in poverty, and brought me to a respected family having horses and camels and threshing and purifying grain. Whatever I say, he does not rebuke or insult me. When I sleep, I sleep till late in the morning, and when I drink water (or milk), I drink my fill. The mother of Abu Zar and what may one say in praise of the mother of Abu Zar? Her saddle bags were always full of provision and her house was spacious. As for the son of Abu Zar, what may one say of the son of Abu Zar? His bed is as narrow as an unsheathed sword and an arm of a kid (of four months) satisfies his hunger. As for the daughter of Abu Zar, she is obedient to her father and to her mother. She has a fat well-built body and that arouses the jealousy of her husband's other wife. As for the (maid) slave girl of Abu Zar, what may one say of the (maid) slavegirl of Abu Zar? She does not uncover our secrets but keeps them, and does not waste our provisions and does not leave the rubbish scattered everywhere in our house.\" The eleventh lady added, \"One day it so happened that Abu Zar went out at the time when the milk was being milked from the animals, and he saw a woman who had two sons like two leopards playing with her two breasts. (On seeing her) he divorced me and married her. Thereafter I married a noble man who used to ride a fast tireless horse and keep a spear in his hand. He gave me many things, and also a pair of every kind of livestock and said, Eat (of this), O Um Zar, and give provision to your relatives.\" She added, \"Yet, all those things which my second husband gave me could not fill the smallest utensil of Abu Zar's.\" ʿAisha then said: Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"I am to you as Abu Zar was to his wife Um Zar.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 5189)"],[19190,"For me, Messenger of Allah ﷺ , you were like a father who plants and a mother who waters. So I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, who is Abu Zar and who is Umm Zar?\" He said, \"Ten women gathered together and swore that they would not lie about their husbands. One of them said, 'I will not tell his secret, for I fear I will not be able to carry it.' Another said, 'He is like a wild bull on a mountain, neither fat nor thin, so he cannot be easily reached or moved.' Another said, 'When he eats, he devours and when he drinks, he drinks passionately, and his hands do not go into the dish without bringing out the bones.' Another said, 'He is like a night of full moon, neither hot nor cold, and there is no fear in him.' Another said, 'When he enters, he becomes like a leopard, and when he comes out, he becomes like a lion, and he does not ask about what he has entrusted.' Another said, 'His scent is like that of basil, and his touch is like that of a rabbit.' Another said, 'He is tall and slim, with mighty shoulders and ashes around him, and he is close to the house and can be easily called for.' Another said, 'He is a wealthy man, with many camels that travel long distances, though there are few blessings in their paths.' When they hear the sound of the flute, they are certain that he is the one.' Another said, 'He is Abu Zar.' I asked, 'Who is Abu Zar?' She replied, 'He is a man of blessings and agriculture who has made me forget my adornments, my ears and the flesh of my arms. He has possessed my own self, and whenever I am with him, I feel calm. I awake in the morning and drink. I quench my thirst and do not feel repulsed. I say, 'I will never be disgusted.' He took me from my family and placed me in the family of Suhayl, where I reside with loud noises, echoes, cracks, and dust. He is the son of Abu Zar.' I asked, 'Who is the son of Abu Zar?' She replied, 'His resting place is like a mountain peak, and the length of a sugar cane is enough for him.' She is the daughter of Abu Zar.' I asked, 'Who is the daughter of Abu Zar?' She replied, 'Her clothes are perfect, and her cloak is tied around her waist. She is a source of joy for her father and mother, and a decoration for her family. She is not metaphorical, but rather a servant of Abu Zar.' I asked, 'Who is the servant of Abu Zar?' She replied, 'He does not spread our secrets widely, nor does he spoil our manners. Abu Zar left me, and the camels began to give birth. He then saw a woman with two sons, like young leopards, playing under her. He married her and divorced me, and so I married a young man secretly. He left me poor, and took his share, then he brought me a lot of gifts and said, 'This is for your family, O Umm Zar.' I said, 'If all of this were placed in a vessel from Abu Zar's belongings, it would not be enough to fill it.' Aisha said, 'So I said, O Messenger of Allah, you are better for me than Abu Zar to Umm Zar.'"],[19191,"The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said to Aisha, \"O Aisha, I have been to you like Abu Zar's sowing (father of Zar) to Um Zar's sowing (mother of Zar) except that Abu Zar divorced and I do not divorce.\""],[19192,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I was to you like the father of a seed to the mother of a seed.\""],[19193,"\"I took pride in the wealth of my father during the days of ignorance, as it amounted to a hundred thousand ounces. The Prophet ﷺ said to me, 'Be silent, O Aisha, for in my eyes, I am to you as Abu Zar would be to Umm Zar.' Then, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ started talking about how eleven women had gathered during the pre-Islamic days and made a covenant to inform each other about their husbands without lying. It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'The night is a night of famine, without heat or cold, without fear.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'The wind is the wind of Zarnab, and it carries the scent of rabbits, and I am the majority, and the people are in majority.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'By Allah, I do not know. It is a column with lofty pillars, a tall palm trunk, and a great heavy fire, close to the house where people gather.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'I married Malik, and Malik who? He has many grazing camels, a few blessings. When they hear the sound of strainers, they are certain that it is they.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'I mention my husband, and when I mention him, I mention Ojara and Buja, and I fear that I will not mention him.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'By Allah, I do not know. When he enters, he is like a cheetah, and when he leaves, he is like a lion. He does not ask about what he entrusted.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'The flesh of a camel is lean on a mountain, neither in the fat nor in the easy ascent. It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'By Allah, I do not know. When he eats, he gulps, when he drinks, he gasps, when he slaughters, he says \"help me\", and when he sleeps, he snores, and his palm does not enter the palm of his hand, so he knows how to emit semen.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'I married Al-Asnanq. If he speaks, I am divorced, if he is silent, I am praised.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'The consequences of every disease has a cure, and it is either a tanner, a speck, or he gathers them all for you.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'I married Abu Zar, and who is Abu Zar? He is someone from adornments in my ears and full of fat in my shoulder, and he himself boasted, so I met him in a booty of war. He placed me between those who were staying and those who were returning, between the runners and the walker, and the taker of shares. I sleep with him, and I wake up in the morning and drink, and I have my morning food, and he has given me abundance from every creature as a gift.' Aisha said, 'So I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, indeed, you are better than Abu Zar.'\""],[19194,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and said, \"O Aisha, I was to you like Abu Zar'a to Umm Zar'a.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There was a village from the villages of Yemen in which there were twelve women. They went to a gathering and some of them said to others, 'Come, let us mention our husbands and speak truthfully about them.' It was said to the first one, 'Speak.' She mentioned the hadith (narration) and the second woman, who was 'Umrah bint 'Amir, spoke. It was said to the third one, 'Speak.' She was Hubbah bint Ka'ab. It was said to the fourth one, 'Speak.' She was Hudhud bint Abi Haramah. It was said to the fifth one, 'Speak.' She was Kabshah. It was said to the sixth one, 'Speak.' She was Hind. It was said to the seventh one, 'Speak.' She was Hubbah bint Alqamah. It was said to the eighth one, 'Speak.' She was Asma bint 'Abd. It was said to the ninth one, 'Speak.' She was not named. It was said to the tenth one, 'Speak.' She was Kubayshah bint Al-Arqam. It was said to Umm Zar'a, 'Speak.' She was Bint Al-Uka'il bin Sa'adah. She said, 'Abu Zar'a and who is Abu Zar'a?' Then she mentioned the hadith."],[19195,"I used to play with toys, and my friends would come to me. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, they would flee from him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would catch them and bring them back to me."],[19196,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come to me while I was playing with dolls."],[19197,"Abd Allah b. Maslama al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Hisham b. Urwa narrated to me from his father, from Aisha, that she used to play with dolls—meaning toys—in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. My friends would come and hide from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send them to me so they could play with me."],[19198,"I used to play with these dolls, and my slave girls would come to me and play with me. When they saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ they would hide, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send them to me."],[19199,"I used to play with dolls during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[19200,"I used to play with dolls during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[19201,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me while I was on a swing."],[19202,"By Allah, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing at the door of my room while the Abyssinians were playing with spears in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was screening me with his cloak so that I could look at their play from between his ears and his shoulder. Then he stood for my sake until I was the one who departed. So appreciate the capacity of a young girl eager for amusement."],[19203,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing at the door of my room while the Abyssinians were playing with their spears in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ screened me with his cloak so that I could look at their play. He kept standing for my sake until I was the one who departed. So appreciate, O son of my sister, the capacity of a young girl eager for amusement."],[19204,"The Prophet ﷺ placed my chin on his shoulder so that I could look at the Abyssinians' spear play, until I was the one who turned away from them."],[19205,"Abu Bakr ؓ entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while two slave-girls were with Aisha, singing during the days of Mina, and the Prophet ﷺ was lying with his garment covering his face. Abu Bakr said: \"Is this done in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" The Prophet ﷺ uncovered his face and said: \"Leave them, O Abu Bakr, for these are the days of Eid.\""],[19206,"Abu Bakr ؓ entered upon me on a day of Eid while two slave-girls were with me, singing and mentioning the day of Bu'ath, the day on which the champions of Aws and Khazraj were killed. Abu Bakr said: \"Servants of God! Is the pipe of Satan in the presence of the Messenger of God?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O Abu Bakr, every people has a festival, and today is our festival.\""],[19207,"Abu Bakr entered upon her while the Messenger of God ﷺ was with her on the day of Fitr or Adha, and two slave-girls were with her singing. Abu Bakr said: \"The pipe of Satan?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Leave us, O Abu Bakr, for every people has a festival, and our festival is this day.\""],[19208,"She had two slave-girls singing on a day of Eid, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was with her and did not forbid them. Abu Bakr entered and scolded them. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Leave her, O Abu Bakr, for every people has a festival, and this is our festival.\""],[19209,"The exonerated truthful one, daughter of the truthful, beloved of the Beloved of God, narrated to me."],[19210,"The truthful one, daughter of the truthful, the innocent, the exonerated, narrated to me such-and-such."],[19211,"It was said to him: \"Was Aisha skilled in the laws of inheritance?\" He said: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I saw the elders of the companions of Muhammad ﷺ asking her about the laws of inheritance.\""],[19212,"I never saw anyone more eloquent than Aisha ؓ."],[19213,"A man said: \"All the Mothers of the Believers are dearer to me than Aisha.\" I said: \"As for you, you have contradicted the Messenger of God ﷺ; she was the dearest of them to him.\""],[19214,"I never saw a woman more knowledgeable in medicine, expenditure, or poetry than Aisha."],[19215,"I said to Aisha: \"O Mother of the Believers, I am not surprised at your insight into poetry, for I say you are the wife of the Messenger of God ﷺ and the daughter of the most learned of people. But I am surprised at your insight into medicine.\" She said: \"O son of my sister, when the Messenger of God ﷺ advanced in age and fell ill, delegations came, and remedies were described to him, so from that.\""],[19216,"We arrived as emigrants and took a rugged mountain pass, and a strong, unruly camel I was riding bolted with me. By God, I will never forget my mother’s words: “O little bride!” I climbed onto its head, and I heard someone saying: “By God, I think its reins have been thrown.” So I threw them, and it began to turn around as though a person were standing beneath it holding it."],[19217,"I entered with Abu Bakr when he first came to Madinah, and there was Aisha lying down, overcome by fever. Abu Bakr came to her and said, “How are you, my little daughter?” and kissed her cheek."],[19218,"Mu‘awiyah — by God, I have never seen any orator more eloquent or more astute than Aisha ؓ."],[19219,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “If the knowledge of all the women of this community were gathered — including the wives of the Prophet ﷺ — Aisha’s knowledge would be greater than theirs.”"],[19220,"Some people were disparaging Abu Bakr, so she sent for a group of them, let down her curtains, and reproached and rebuked them, saying: “My father — and what a father! My father, no hands can reach him. Far, far from it! By God, he is a towering mountain and an extending shade. By God, he succeeded when you called him a liar, and he took the lead when you lagged behind.”"],[19221,"“Umar fathered ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Umar and his full sister Hafsah bt. ‘Umar, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and ‘Abd al-Rahman the elder; their mother was Zaynab bt. Maz‘un b. Habib b. Wahb b. Hudhafah b. Jumah. She was among the emigrant women; before the Prophet ﷺ she had been married to Khunays b. Hudhafah al-Sahmi. Her father and her paternal uncle Zayd attended Badr, and her maternal uncles ‘Uthman, Qudamah, and ‘Abd Allah b. her maternal aunt, and al-Sa’ib b. ‘Uthman attended Badr.”"],[19222,"Hafsah became widowed from Khunays b. Hudhafah al-Sahmi, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ and had attended Badr, and he died in Madinah. I met Abu Bakr and offered her to him, but he remained silent, and what troubled me troubled me. Then when the Messenger of God ﷺ married her, I said to him, “What made you do what you did?” He said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ had mentioned her, and for that reason I kept silent.” The wording is that of the hadith of Musa b. ‘Uqbah and Ibn Abi ‘Atiq."],[19223,"A slave girl of Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, cast a spell on her, and she confessed it against herself. Hafsah ordered ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Zayd, and he killed her. ‘Uthman disapproved of that, so ‘Abd Allah went to him and said, “She cast a spell on her and confessed it.” ‘Uthman had disapproved of what she did without the ruler’s authority."],[19224,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ divorced Hafsah, then took her back.”"],[19225,"Umar entered upon Hafsah while she was crying, so he said, \"What makes you cry? Perhaps the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has divorced you. Indeed, if the Prophet ﷺ has divorced you, he will return you to me because of me. By Allah, if he has divorced you, I will never speak to you again.\""],[19226,"The Messenger of God ﷺ intended to divorce Hafsah, but Gabriel came and said, “Do not divorce her, for she fasts much and prays much, and she will be your wife in Paradise.”"],[19227,"The Prophet ﷺ divorced Hafsah, and that reached ‘Umar b. al-Khattab, so he placed dust on his head and said, “God will not care about you, O Ibn al-Khattab, after this.” Then Gabriel descended upon the Prophet ﷺ and said, “God commands you to take Hafsah back out of mercy for ‘Umar.”"],[19228,"“Hafsah died in the year Ifriqiya was conquered, and she died while Marwan was governor of Madinah.”"],[19229,"Yazid b. Abi Habib said: \"Mu'awiyah b. Hudayj raided Ifriqiyah three times: the first in the year thirty-four, the second in the year forty, and the third in the year fifty.\""],[19230,"Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: “I did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ pray in his voluntary prayer while sitting until one or two years before God took him. Then I saw him pray in his voluntary prayer while sitting, reciting the surah slowly until it became longer than a longer one.”"],[19231,"The Prophet ﷺ would fast on Monday, Thursday, and the Monday of the coming week."],[19232,"Four things the Prophet ﷺ never abandoned: fasting on Ashura, the ten days, three days of every month, and the two rak'ahs before dawn."],[19233,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me one day and placed his garment between his thighs. Abu Bakr came seeking permission, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him permission while he was in that state. Then Umar came seeking permission, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him permission while he was in that state. Then some people came, and he granted them permission. Then Ali came, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him permission while he was in that state. Then Uthman came seeking permission, and he covered himself with his garment and then granted him permission. They spoke for a while and then left. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr, Umar, Ali, and some of your companions entered upon you while you were in your state without changing. But when Uthman entered, you covered yourself with your garment.' He said, 'Should I not feel shy before one before whom the angels feel shy?'"],[19234,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'People from my Ummah will attack this House, until when they are in the desert, the first of them will be swallowed up, and the middle of them will not return—or he will be saved.'"],[19235,"From Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that Utarid b. Hajib brought a garment that Chosroes had given him. Umar b. al-Khattab said, 'Will you not buy it, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Only one who has no share will buy it.'"],[19236,"Marwan used to send to Hafsah asking her for the mushaf from which the Quran was copied, but Hafsah refused to give it to him. When we buried Hafsah, Marwan sent to Ibn Umar: 'Send me that mushaf,' so he sent it to him."],[19237,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, what is the matter with the people? They have exited ihram, but you have not exited ihram from your umrah.' He said: 'I have matted my hair and garlanded my sacrificial animal, so I will not exit ihram until I slaughter.'"],[19238,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded his wives to exit ihram in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage. Hafsah said: 'What prevents you from exiting ihram?' He said: 'I have matted my hair and garlanded my sacrificial animal, so I will not exit ihram until I slaughter my sacrificial animal.'"],[19239,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded his wives to exit ihram in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage. Hafsah said: 'What prevented you from exiting ihram?' He said: 'I have matted my hair and garlanded my sacrificial animal, so I will not exit ihram until I slaughter my sacrificial animal.'"],[19240,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded his wives in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage to exit ihram. Hafsah said: 'What prevents you, O Messenger of God, from exiting ihram?' He said: 'I have matted my hair and garlanded my sacrificial animal, so I will not exit ihram until I exit ihram from my Hajj.'"],[19241,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded his wives to exit ihram with an umrah, we said: 'What prevents you, O Messenger of God, from exiting ihram with us?' He said: 'I have already offered my sacrificial animal and matted my hair, so I will not exit ihram until I slaughter.'"],[19242,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded his wives to exit ihram in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage. Hafsah said: 'What prevents you, O Messenger of God, from exiting ihram?' He said: 'I have garlanded my sacrificial animal and matted my hair, so I will not exit ihram until I slaughter the sacrificial animal.'"],[19243,"He used to pray two rak'ahs before Subh — meaning the Prophet ﷺ."],[19244,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray two light rak'ahs after dawn broke and the muezzin called for prayer."],[19245,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik (h) and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: Abdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us: Malik informed us (h) and Ali b. al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us: Ismail b. Abi Uways narrated to us: Malik narrated to me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Hafsah: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ, when the muezzin fell silent after the adhan, would pray two light rak'ahs before the iqamah for the prayer.'"],[19246,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'When the call to the Subh prayer was given, he would pray two light rak'ahs before standing for the prayer.'"],[19247,"When the muezzin gave the call for the dawn prayer, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would stand and pray the two rak'ahs of dawn, then go out to the mosque while food was forbidden. And he would not have the call given until daybreak appeared."],[19248,"When dawn broke, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pray two light rak'ahs."],[19249,"Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed me that he, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, used to pray two rak'ahs before the morning prayer, making them light."],[19250,"The Prophet ﷺ would perform two light prostrations when dawn broke."],[19251,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray two light rak'ahs after dawn broke."],[19252,"When dawn broke, the Prophet ﷺ would pray two light rak'ahs."],[19253,"When dawn broke, the Prophet ﷺ would pray two light rak'ahs."],[19254,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray two light prostrations when dawn became clear, before the prayer."],[19255,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the two rak'ahs of dawn in my house, and he used to make them light."],[19256,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray two rak'ahs when dawn broke."],[19257,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray two rak'ahs when dawn broke."],[19258,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray the two rak'ahs of dawn when dawn broke."],[19259,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Five creatures, there is no blame on the one who kills them while in ihram: the crow, the mouse, the vicious dog, and the kite."],[19260,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Going out on Friday is obligatory for every one who has reached puberty, and the bathing is like his bathing from janabah.”"],[19261,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Going out on Friday is obligatory for every one who has reached puberty, and the bathing is like his bathing from janabah.”"],[19262,"It is not permissible for a woman believing in Allah and the Hereafter to observe mourning on the dead for more than three (days), except in case of her husband. (Using translation from Muslim 1491)"],[19263,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The coming out of Ibn Sayyad is only due to an anger that will seize him.”"],[19264,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Whoever does not resolve to fast before dawn, there is no fast for him.”"],[19265,"She said: “I did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ pray sitting down until a year or two before his death. Then he would pray his voluntary prayer sitting, and he would recite the surah slowly until his recitation became longer than a longer one.”"],[19266,"Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, reported to him, saying: “I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pray sitting at all until a year before his death. Then he would pray his voluntary prayer sitting, and he would recite the surah slowly until it became longer than a longer one.”"],[19267,"“I did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ sitting in his voluntary prayer until a year or two before his death. Then I saw him pray sitting in his voluntary prayer, and he would recite the surah slowly until his recitation of it became longer than a longer one.”"],[19268,"Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: “I did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ sitting in his voluntary prayer until a year or two before he passed away. Then I saw him pray sitting in his voluntary prayer, reciting the surah slowly until his recitation became longer than a longer one.”"],[19269,"Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: “I did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ pray sitting in his voluntary prayer until a year or two before he passed away. Then I saw him pray sitting in his voluntary prayer, reciting the surah slowly until his recitation of it became longer than his recitation standing.”"],[19270,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “A company will surely come to this House to raid it, until when they are in a desert of the land, the middle of them will be swallowed up, and the first of them will call out to the last of them, and none of them will remain except the fugitive who tells about them.” A man said to my grandfather: I bear witness that you have not lied about Hafsah, and Hafsah did not lie about the Messenger of God ﷺ. Sufyan said: And Umayr b. Qays used to narrate it from Umayyah."],[19271,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would use his right hand for his food, drink, and clothing, and his left hand for anything else."],[19272,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lay down, he placed his right hand under his right cheek. His right hand was for his food, drink, purification, and water, and his left hand for anything else."],[19273,"From Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: The Prophet ﷺ would kiss while fasting."],[19274,"The Prophet ﷺ would kiss while fasting."],[19275,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would touch the face of some of his wives while fasting."],[19276,"The Prophet ﷺ would kiss some of his wives while fasting."],[19277,"From Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ would fast three days of the month: Monday, Thursday, and the Monday of the following week."],[19278,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I hope that no one who witnessed Badr and al-Ḥudaybiyyah will enter the Fire, if God wills.” I said, “O Messenger of God, has not God said, {And there is none of you but will come to it; this is, upon your Lord, an inevitability decreed}?” He said, “Have you not heard Him say, {Then We shall save those who were God-fearing, and leave the wrongdoers in it on their knees}?”"],[19279,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and His Messenger to mourn over a deceased person for more than three days, except over her husband.”"],[19280,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day—or who believes in God and His Messenger—to mourn over a deceased person for more than three days, except over her husband.”"],[19281,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and His Messenger to mourn for more than three days, except over a husband.”"],[19282,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “I hope that no one who witnessed Badr and al-Ḥudaybiyyah will enter the Fire, if God wills.” I said, “O Messenger of God, {And there is none of you but will come to it; this is, upon your Lord, an inevitability decreed}.” He said, “Have you not heard Him say, {Then We shall save those who were God-fearing, and leave the wrongdoers in it on their knees}?”"],[19283,"He informed him that he said to Ḥafṣah, “Does one of you become angry at the Prophet ﷺ for a day until nightfall?” She said, “Yes.”"],[19284,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray the two rakʿahs of Fajr when the dawn became bright."],[19285,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Five creatures there is no sin upon the one who kills them in the state of iḥrām: the crow, the mouse, the scorpion, the rabid dog, and the kite.”"],[19286,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever does not resolve to fast before dawn has no fast.”"],[19287,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Let none of you cease from seeking to have a child; for when a man dies and has no child, his name is cut off.”"],[19288,"Ḥafṣah said, “Avoid this man, for we used to speak of the Dajjāl emerging from an outburst of anger he would have.” And Maʿmar from al-Zuhrī reported the like of it."],[19289,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray two light prostrations (two brief rakʿahs) when the dawn rose."],[19290,"Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said, “O Messenger of God, what is the matter with you that you have not exited [ihram]?” — the hadith."],[19291,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Ibn Sayyad emerges only out of anger that overtakes him.”"],[19292,"I said, “O Messenger of God, what is the matter with the people that they have exited [ihram] while you have not exited from your ʿumrah?” He said, “I have matted my hair and garlanded my sacrificial animal, so I will not exit until I slaughter it at Mina.”"],[19293,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray the two rakʿahs of Fajr when dawn broke."],[19294,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to make the two rakʿahs just before Fajr light."],[19295,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray two light-raka'at when he saw the dawn."],[19296,"When the call for the Morning Prayer was given, the Prophet ﷺ would prostrate two prostrations before the Morning Prayer, making them light."],[19297,"When the muezzin finished the call for the Morning Prayer, the Prophet ﷺ would pray two light rakʿahs before the prayer was established."],[19298,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray two rakʿahs after Fajr."],[19299,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the two rakʿahs of Fajr when dawn broke."],[19300,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to exit [ihram] during his Hajj that he performed."],[19301,"The Prophet ﷺ matted his hair when he performed Hajj and shaved when he exited [ihram]."],[19302,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded his wives to exit [ihram] in the year of the Farewell Hajj."],[19303,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when dawn broke, would not pray except two light rakʿahs."],[19304,"From the Prophet ﷺ something, except that he narrated once from a woman among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ that a dabb (spiny-tailed lizard) was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and some of his companions began eating it, among them Saʿd. Then a woman among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ called out to him that it was a dabb. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Eat it, there is no harm in it, but it is not from the food of my people.\""],[19305,"She heard Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrate that the Prophet ﷺ said, \"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn over a deceased person for more than three days, except over a husband.\""],[19306,"From one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, she said, I said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"Why have the people exited ihram while you have not?\" He said, \"I have matted my hair and garlanded my sacrificial animal, so I will not exit ihram until the sacrificial animal is released.\""],[19307,"From one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ: \"Whoever goes to a diviner (ʿarrāf), God will not accept his prayer for forty days.\" [Mawqūf]"],[19308,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The one who drinks from a silver vessel will have the fire of Hell gurgling in his belly.\""],[19309,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to kiss while fasting."],[19310,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ wanted to sleep, he would place his right hand under his right cheek and then say, \"O God, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants.\""],[19311,"ʿUmar said, \"Shall I buy it for you, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"Only the one who has no share of the Hereafter wears it.\""],[19312,"Four things the Prophet ﷺ never abandoned: fasting ʿĀshūrāʾ, the ten days (of Dhū al-Ḥijjah), and three days of every month."],[19313,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Fast three days of every month, or from the month Monday, Thursday, and the following Thursday.\""],[19314,"The translation of the passage into English is: \"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast three days every month, on Mondays and Thursdays.\""],[19315,"She was called al-Shifāʾ, and she used to perform ruqyah for the ant (i.e., a skin condition called namlah). The Prophet ﷺ said to her, \"Teach it to Hafsah.\""],[19316,"The Prophet ﷺ was placing his garment between his thighs when Abu Bakr sought permission from him, and he granted him permission while in that state. Then Umar sought permission, and he granted him permission while in that state. Then Ali sought permission among some of the Prophet's companions, and he granted him permission while in that state. Then Uthman sought permission, and he clothed himself with his garment, and they conversed. Then they left, and I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr sought permission and you granted him permission while you were in that state. Then Umar sought permission, and you granted him permission while you were in that state. Then Ali sought permission among some of your companions, and you granted him permission while you were in that state. Then Uthman sought permission and you clothed yourself with your garment.\" He said, \"Should I not be shy about something from which the angels are shy?\" Ibn Juraij said, \"And my father informed me with a similar narration.\""],[19317,"On the authority of ʿUrwah b. al-Zubayr, regarding the naming of those who emigrated to the land of Abyssinia with Jaʿfar b. Abī Ṭālib from the Banū Asad b. Khuzaymah: ʿUbayd Allāh b. Jaḥsh b. Riʾāb died in the land of Abyssinia as a Christian, and with him was Umm Ḥabībah bt. Abī Sufyān, whose name is Ramlah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her afterward; ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān gave her in marriage to him in the land of Abyssinia. Umm Ḥabībah's mother was Ṣafiyyah bt. Abī al-ʿĀṣ, the sister of ʿAffān b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ, the paternal aunt of ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān."],[19318,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Ḥabībah while she was in the land of Abyssinia; the Negus gave her in marriage to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not send anything to her. The dowers of the Prophet's ﷺ wives were four hundred dirhams."],[19319,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Ḥabībah bt. Abī Sufyān b. Ḥarb b. Umayyah b. ʿAbd Shams b. ʿAbd Manāf b. Quṣayy b. Kilāb b. Murrah b. Kaʿb b. Luʾayy b. Ghālib b. Fihr b. Mālik. Umm Ḥabībah's name is Ramlah. ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān ؓ gave Umm Ḥabībah ؓ in marriage to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ because Umm Ḥabībah's mother was Ṣafiyyah bt. Abī al-ʿĀṣ, and Ṣafiyyah was the paternal aunt of ʿUthmān, the full sister of ʿAffān. Shuraḥbīl b. Ḥasanah brought Umm Ḥabībah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[19320,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me, so I said: \"Would you be interested in my sister, the daughter of Abu Sufyan?\" He said: \"What would I do?\" I said: \"Marry her.\" He said: \"Your sister?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Would you like that?\" I said: \"Yes, I am not leaving you alone, and the one I love—or she said: the one most entitled—to share good with me is my sister.\" He said: \"She is not lawful for me.\" She said: \"By God, I have been told that you are seeking Durrah bint Abi Salamah.\" He said: \"The daughter of Abu Salamah?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"By God, even if she were not my stepdaughter in my care, she would not be lawful to me. She is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding. Thuwaybah nursed me and her. So do not offer me your daughters or your sisters.\""],[19321,"She heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The angels do not accompany a traveling group in which there is a bell.\""],[19322,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, God builds for him a house in Paradise.\""],[19323,"\"We used to do it during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , we would walk from Jam' to Mina.\" Al-Humaidi added in his narration: Sufyan and Salim ibn Shawwal said: \"There was a man from the people of Makkah whom we never heard anyone narrating from except 'Amr ibn Dinar. This is the narration.\""],[19324,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray on the khumrah."],[19325,"Some people from the people of Yemen came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he taught them prayer, the customary practices, and the obligatory duties. They said, 'O Messenger of God, we have a drink we make from wheat and barley.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Al-ghubayrāʾ?' They said, 'Yes.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Do not make it.'"],[19326,"[It was said] to the Prophet ﷺ: 'I have the best and most beautiful women of the Arabs: Umm Ḥabībah bt. Abī Sufyān. Shall I marry you to her?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'And Muʿāwiyah you take as a scribe?' He said, 'Yes.'"],[19327,"I heard Muʿāwiyah b. Abī Sufyān say: I asked Umm Ḥabībah whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray in the garment in which he had intercourse with her. She said, 'Yes, if there was no impurity on it.'"],[19328,"I heard Muʿāwiyah b. Abī Sufyān say: I asked Umm Ḥabībah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray in the garment in which he had intercourse. She said, 'Yes, if he saw no impurity on it.'"],[19329,"I entered upon Umm Ḥabībah bt. Abī Sufyān and she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray in a single garment, wrapped in it."],[19330,"I heard Muʿāwiyah b. Abī Sufyān say: I asked Umm Ḥabībah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray in the garment in which he had intercourse with you. She said, 'Yes, if he saw no impurity on it.'"],[19331,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I was shown what my community will face after me of shedding each other's blood, and I asked Him to grant me intercession for them on the Day of Resurrection, and He did.'"],[19332,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I was shown what my community will face after me and the shedding of their blood, and I asked Allah to grant me intercession for them, and He did.'"],[19333,"Umm Ḥabībah said: O Messenger of Allah, a woman among us may have two husbands, then she dies and enters Paradise, she and her two husbands. To which of them will she belong, to the first or the last? He said: 'She will choose the one who had the best character with her in this world; he will be her husband in Paradise. O Umm Ḥabībah, good character takes away the good of this world and the Hereafter.'"],[19334,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'Marry the daughter of Abū Sufyān,' meaning her sister. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Would you like that?' She said, 'Yes, I am not the only one for you, and the dearest of those who share good with me is my sister.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'That is not lawful.' Umm Ḥabībah said, 'O Messenger of Allah, it has been said that you are marrying Durrah bt. Abī Salamah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The daughter of Umm Salamah?' Umm Ḥabībah said, 'Yes.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Even if she were not my stepdaughter under my care, she would not be lawful, for she is the daughter of my brother through suckling. Thuwaybah suckled me and Abū Salamah. So do not offer me your daughters or your sisters.'"],[19335,"Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed her that she said: \"O Messenger of God, marry my sister, the daughter of Abu Sufyan.\" She claimed that the Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: \"Would you like that?\" She said: \"Yes, O Messenger of God, I am not leaving you alone, and the one I would love to share good with me is my sister.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"That is not lawful for me.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, we have been talking that you want to marry Durrah bint Abi Salamah.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The daughter of Abu Salamah?\" She said: \"Yes.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"By God, even if she were not my stepdaughter in my care, she would not be lawful for me, because she is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding. Thuwaybah nursed me and Abu Salamah. So do not offer me your daughters or your sisters.\""],[19336,"Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: \"O Messenger of God, marry my sister, the daughter of Abu Sufyan.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: \"Would you like that?\" She said: \"I am not leaving you alone, and the best one to share good with me is my sister.\" He said: \"That is not lawful for me.\" She said: \"By God, we have been told that you want to marry Durrah bint Abi Salamah.\" He said: \"The daughter of Umm Salamah?\" She said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"By God, even if she were not my stepdaughter, she would not be lawful for me, for she is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding. Thuwaybah nursed me and her. So do not offer me your daughters or your sisters.\""],[19337,"She said: \"O Messenger of God, would you be interested in Hamnah bint Abi Sufyan?\" He said: \"What would I do?\" She said: \"Marry her.\" He said: \"Would she be lawful to me?\" She said: \"By God, I have been told that you are seeking Zaynab bint Abi Salamah in marriage.\" He said: \"My stepdaughter in my care? By God, even if she were not my stepdaughter in my care, she is the daughter of my brother. Thuwaybah nursed me and her. So do not offer me your daughters, your sisters, or your mothers.\""],[19338,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , entered upon me, so I said, \"Do you have any interest in my sister, the daughter of Abu Sufyan?\" The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"What would you do?\" I said, \"I want to marry her.\" He asked, \"Your sister?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Do you really want that?\" I said, \"Yes, I am not compelled, and I love whoever you choose for me, even if it is my sister.\" He said, \"She is not permissible for me.\" I said, \"By Allah, I have been informed that you are proposing to marry the daughter of Abu Salama.\" He asked, \"The daughter of Abu Salama?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"By Allah, if she was not my stepdaughter, she would not have been lawful for me. She is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding, and Thawiba breastfed both me and her. Therefore, do not present your daughters and sisters to me.\""],[19339,"To the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"We have been talking that you are to marry Durrah bint Abi Salamah.\" He said: \"On top of Umm Salamah? Even if I had not married Umm Salamah, she would not be lawful to me, for her father is my brother through breastfeeding.\""],[19340,"Zaynab bint Abi Salamah informed him that she entered upon Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, when her father Abu Sufyan died. Umm Habibah called for perfume containing yellow dye, khalūq or other than it, and applied some of it to a slave girl, then touched her own cheeks with it, then said: \"By God, I have no need of perfume, except that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three nights, except for a husband, four months and ten days.'\""],[19341,"When the news of her father's death came, she called for perfume and wiped it on her forearms, and said: \"By God, I have no need of perfume, were it not that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three nights, except for a husband, four months and ten days.'\""],[19342,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three nights, except for a husband, four months and ten days.\""],[19343,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three nights, except for a husband.\""],[19344,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three, except for a husband.\""],[19345,"O Messenger of God, my daughter's husband has died, and I fear for her eyesight. Should I apply kohl to her eyes?\" He said: \"One of you would throw a dung pellet at the end of a year, but it is only four months and ten days.\""],[19346,"A woman asked Umm Salamah and Umm Habibah: \"May a woman apply kohl during her waiting period from her husband's death?\" She said: \"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about that, and he said: 'One of you during the pre-Islamic era, when her husband died, would stay for a year, then throw a dung pellet. But it is only four months and ten days, until the term ends.'\""],[19347,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he heard the mu'adhdhin, would say what he said until he fell silent."],[19348,"From his paternal aunt Umm Habibah bt. Abi Sufyan, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he was with me and heard the caller, would say what he said until he fell silent."],[19349,"Umm Habibah bt. Abi Sufyan narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\" Umm Habibah said: \"I have not abandoned them since I heard them from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" 'Amr said: \"I have not abandoned them since I heard them from 'Anbasah.\" And the wording is that of 'Amr b. 'Awn."],[19350,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\""],[19351,"From Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who is his sister, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Twelve rak'ahs—whoever prays them, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise: four rak'ahs before Zuhr, two rak'ahs after Zuhr, two rak'ahs before 'Asr, two rak'ahs after Maghrib, and two rak'ahs before Subh.\""],[19352,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah will build for him thereby a house in Paradise: four rak'ahs before Zuhr, two rak'ahs after Zuhr, two rak'ahs before 'Asr, two rak'ahs after Maghrib, and two rak'ahs before Subh.\""],[19353,"I will relate to you a hadith that Umm Habibah bt. Abi Sufyan narrated to me. She narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs along with the daytime prayer, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\""],[19354,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day and night, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise: four before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after 'Isha', and two before the dawn prayer.\""],[19355,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day and night, apart from the obligatory ones, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\""],[19356,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise; and whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\""],[19357,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise: four rak'ahs before Zuhr, two rak'ahs after Zuhr, two rak'ahs before 'Asr, two rak'ahs after Maghrib, and two rak'ahs after 'Isha'.\""],[19358,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever prays twelve voluntary units of prayer in their night and day, other than the obligatory prayers, Allah will build a house for them in Paradise.\""],[19359,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs other than the obligatory ones, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\""],[19360,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever consistently performs four rak'ahs before the noon prayer and four after it will be forbidden to Hell.\""],[19361,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said: \"Whoever consistently performs four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.\""],[19362,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever consistently performs four rak'ahs before the noon prayer and four after it will be forbidden to Hell.\""],[19363,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.\""],[19364,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.\""],[19365,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr, Allah will forbid his body to the Fire.\""],[19366,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever touches his private part, let him perform wudu'.\""],[19367,"Indeed my sister Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to me that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a night or day, apart from the obligatory prayers, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\" So I have not abandoned them since I heard them."],[19368,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day and night, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\""],[19369,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever touches his penis, let him perform wudu'.\""],[19370,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Whoever touches his penis, let him perform wudu'.\""],[19371,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever bows four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four rak'ahs after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.\""],[19372,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.”"],[19373,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, a house will be built for him in Paradise.”"],[19374,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.”"],[19375,"The Prophet said: “Whoever prays four before Zuhr and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.”"],[19376,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.”"],[19377,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in his night and day, Allah will build a house for him in Paradise.”"],[19378,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah will build a house for him in Paradise.”"],[19379,"He entered upon Umm Habibah, and she gave him sawiq to drink. Then he got up to pray, and she said to him, “Perform wudu, O son of my brother, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Perform wudu from what the fire has touched.’”"],[19380,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Perform wudu from what the fire has touched.”"],[19381,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Perform wudu from what the fire has touched.”"],[19382,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Wudu is required from what the fire has touched.”"],[19383,"He informed him that he entered upon his maternal aunt Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. She prepared sawiq for him, and he drank it. She said, “O my son, perform wudu, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Wudu is required from what the fire has touched.’”"],[19384,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Perform ablution from what the fire has touched.\""],[19385,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded ablution from food that the fire has touched."],[19386,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Perform ablution from what the fire has touched.\""],[19387,"He entered upon Umm Habibah and she gave him a cup of sawiq to drink, so he called for water and rinsed his mouth. She said to him, \"O son of my sister, will you not perform ablution? For the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Perform ablution from what the fire has changed or touched.'\""],[19388,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Indeed, the angels do not accompany a companion in which there is a bell.\""],[19389,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Truly, the caravan that has a bell in it is not accompanied by the angels.\""],[19390,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Truly, the caravan that has a bell in it is not accompanied by the angels.\""],[19391,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The angels do not accompany a traveling group in which there is a bell.\""],[19392,"Abu Hurairah reported the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ as saying “The angels do not accompany the fellow travelers who have a dog or bell (with them).” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2555)"],[19393,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Truly, the caravan that has a bell in it is not accompanied by the angels.\""],[19394,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The angels do not accompany a traveling group in which there is a bell.\""],[19395,"Sufyān said to him: 'Repeat to me the hadith of Umm Ṣāliḥ.' He said: 'Umm Ṣāliḥ narrated to me.' And ʿAbbās b. Muḥammad al-Mujāshiʿī narrated to us: Muḥammad b. Abī Yaʿqūb al-Kirmānī narrated to us: Muḥammad b. Yazīd b. Khunays al-Makkī narrated to us, from Saʿīd b. Ḥassān, who said: Umm Ṣāliḥ narrated to me, from Ṣafiyya bt. Shayba, from Umm Ḥabība, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'All the speech of the son of Adam is against him, not for him, except commanding good, forbidding evil, or remembrance of God.' A man among the people said: 'How severe this hadith is!' Sufyān al-Thawrī said: 'And what is its severity? Has not your Prophet ﷺ come to you from your Lord ﷻ, and He said: \"On the day the Spirit and the angels stand in rows, they will not speak except one whom the Most Merciful permits, and he speaks what is right. That is the True Day\" [78:38]? And He said: \"There is no good in much of their private conversation, except for one who commands charity, or good, or reconciliation between people\" [4:114], to the end of the verse.'"],[19396,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was in her house and heard the caller to prayer. He said as he says. When he said, 'Come to prayer,' the Messenger of God ﷺ rose to pray."],[19397,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Whoever prays twelve rakʿahs in a day, apart from the obligatory prayer, God will build for him a house in Paradise.'"],[19398,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The angels do not accompany a group in which there is a bell.'"],[19399,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Perform ablution from what fire has touched.'"],[19400,"'We used to do it at the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ in the dark before dawn from Muzdalifa to Minā.'"],[19401,"'I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ in a garment, on me and on him; in it was what was.'"],[19402,"The Prophet ﷺ used to kiss while fasting."],[19403,"The Prophet ﷺ used to kiss while fasting."],[19404,"'And the Prophet ﷺ married her, and the Negus paid a dowry on his behalf of four hundred dinars.'"],[19405,"Some people from the people of Yemen came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he taught them the customary practices, prayer, and the obligatory duties. They said, 'We have a drink we make from wheat and barley.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Al-ghubayrāʾ?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then do not consume it.' They said, 'But they will not abandon it.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Whoever does not abandon it, strike his neck.'"],[19406,"Zubayr ibn Bakkar said: \"Um Salama, before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , was with Abu Salama, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Asad, and she gave birth to Salama, Umar, and Zainab, then she passed away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then became responsible for her.\""],[19407,"He heard the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , say: \"No Muslim is afflicted with a calamity and says 'Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return. O Allah, I seek recompense for my calamity from You. O Allah, replace it for me with something better than it,' except that Allah will replace it for him with something better.\" So when Abu Salamah passed away, Umm Salamah said: \"Indeed, we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return. O Allah, I seek recompense for my calamity in Abu Salamah from You. O Allah, replace him for me with someone better.\" So I kept saying to myself that someone better than Abu Salamah would come, until the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , proposed to me. So I said: \"I am afflicted and I am possessive, and I am old.\" The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said: \"As for being old, I am older than you. As for being possessive, I supplicate to Allah to remove it from you. And as for children, they are in the hands of Allah and His Messenger.\" So Umar bin Abu Salamah married me to him."],[19408,"that the Prophet ﷺ married Umm Salamah for household goods worth ten dirhams"],[19409,"Umm Salamah: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to me, I said to him: 'I have three shortcomings: I am advanced in age, I am a woman who has children, and I am a very jealous woman.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'As for age, I am older than you. As for the children, they belong to Allah and His Messenger. As for jealousy, I will pray to Allah and He will remove it from you.' So the Prophet ﷺ married her. When he entered upon her, he said: 'You and your family have honor with me. I have not spent seven nights with any of my wives, and if I spend seven with you, I will spend seven with my other wives.'"],[19410,"The first of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ who passed away was Zainab bint Jahsh, she passed away during the caliphate of Umar. The last of them to pass away was Umm Salamah, she passed away during the time of Yazid bin Muawiyah, at the age of sixty-two."],[19411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me after the afternoon prayer and prayed two rak'ahs. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what are these two rak'ahs?' He said, 'I used to pray them after noon, but something came to me and kept me busy until I prayed the afternoon prayer, so I prayed them now.'"],[19412,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed them in her house"],[19413,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her when he married her: 'If you wish, I will spend seven nights with you, then I will spend seven nights with the rest of my wives.'"],[19414,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Jibril kept enjoining me to use the siwak until I feared for my molars.'"],[19415,"O Messenger of Allah, is there jihad upon women? He said, 'Their jihad is here,' and he gestured with his hand toward Makkah."],[19416,"A man gave a woman a sheep as charity, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered her to accept it."],[19417,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me one day and prayed two rak'ahs after 'Asr. I had not seen him pray them, so I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what are these two rak'ahs?\" He said, \"The delegation of Banu Tamim arrived, and I used to pray two rak'ahs after Zuhr, but I had not prayed them, so these are those two.\""],[19418,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to prefer to travel on Thursday."],[19419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you sees in his dream what he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge from what he saw.\""],[19420,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: Abdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us: Malik informed us, from Abd Rabbihi b. Sa'id, from Abu Salama, from Umm Salama, who said: Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah gave birth half a month after her husband's death, then two men proposed to her, one of them young and the other middle-aged. She inclined to the young man, but the middle-aged man said: \"She is not lawful.\" Her family was absent, and he hoped that when her family came, they would prefer him over her. She came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"You have become lawful, so marry whomever you wish.\""],[19421,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ghusl from a single vessel with one of his wives."],[19422,"Subay'ah gave birth half a month after her husband's death."],[19423,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever has an animal that he wants to slaughter, then when the crescent of Dhul Hijjah appears, he should not touch any of his hair or nails until it is slaughtered.\""],[19424,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Let her go, O Umm Salamah, for every nation has a celebration, and this is our celebration day.\""],[19425,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik, from Nafi', from Sulayman b. Yasar, from Umm Salamah that a woman used to experience irregular bleeding during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Umm Salamah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on her behalf. He said, \"She should consider the number of nights and days in which she used to menstruate in the month before she was afflicted with what she has, and she should abandon the prayer for that amount of the month. When that period has passed, she should bathe, fasten a cloth, and then pray.\""],[19426,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed 'Asr, he would leave and then pray two rak'ahs in his house."],[19427,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more prompt in praying Zuhr than you, and you are later in praying 'Asr than him."],[19428,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ under a covering and I menstruated. He said: \"Go back and tie your lower garment tightly around you, then return.\""],[19429,"Some people sent me to Umm Salamah to ask her on which days the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasted most. She said: \"Saturday and Sunday,\" and he would say: \"They are two festival days for the polytheists, so I love to differ from them.\""],[19430,"Asma' wept over Ja'far or Hamzah for three days, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered her to stop weeping and to apply kohl."],[19431,"One day, while the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was resting in her house and a man from his companions was with him, they were conversing when a man came and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how much charity is due on such-and-such dates?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Such-and-such.\" The man said: \"So-and-so has transgressed against me and taken from me such-and-such dates, increasing by one sa'.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"How will it be when someone is appointed over you who transgresses against you more severely than this transgression?\" The people plunged into discussion and the talk overwhelmed them until one of them said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what if a man is absent from you with his camels, livestock, and crops, and he pays the zakah of his wealth, but someone transgresses against him regarding the right? What should he do while he is absent from you?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever pays the zakah of his wealth with a good heart, seeking thereby the face of Allah and the hereafter, and does not withhold anything of his wealth, and establishes the prayer, then pays the zakah, and someone transgresses against him regarding the right, he takes up arms and fights, and is killed, he is a martyr.\""],[19432,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The one who drinks from a silver vessel only causes the fire of Hell to gurgle in his belly.\""],[19433,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, meaning to his wives: \"The one who is kind to you after me is indeed the truthful and dutiful one. O Allah, give Ibn 'Awf to drink from Salsabil.\""],[19434,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting one day in my house and said: \"Let no one enter upon me.\" I waited, and Husayn entered. I heard the sobbing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ weeping. I looked, and there was Husayn in his lap or beside him, and he was wiping his head and weeping. I said: \"By Allah, I did not know when he entered.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Jibril was in the house and said: 'Do you love him?' I said: 'In this world, yes.' He said: 'Your community will kill this one in a land called Karbala.' Jibril took some of its soil and showed it to the Prophet ﷺ. When Husayn was surrounded and killed, he said: 'What is the name of this land?' They said: 'Karbala.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke the truth: a land of grief and affliction.'\""],[19435,"A single vessel of about half a faraq used to be set for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would begin with it; he and I would wash together."],[19436,"I had a gold gazelle, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to give it as charity, and I did so."],[19437,"She said: There was a woman who had prolonged bleeding during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and Umm Salamah asked the Prophet ﷺ about her situation. The Prophet ﷺ said: Let her note the number of days and nights she used to menstruate before the bleeding that she has now, and their portion of the month, and leave off prayer for that amount. When that passes, she should perform ghusl, then bind a cloth over her private part and pray."],[19438,"I heard Umm Salama say, \"Abu Bakr went out during the time of the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , as a merchant to Busra. Abu Bakr was not prevented from suspecting the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , with his share of the profits from trade. This was due to their admiration for the gains of trade and their love for it. The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , did not prevent Abu Bakr from sharing in his trade because of his love for his company and his trust in Abu Bakr. He was pleased with his company, as the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , admired trade and had a liking for it.\""],[19439,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would fondle her while she was menstruating, with a waist-wrapper on her."],[19440,"On the evening of the day of sacrifice, the Messenger of God ﷺ saw Wahb b. Zam'ah and a man from the family of Abu Umayyah wearing shirts. The Prophet ﷺ said to Wahb, “Have you performed the ifadah, O Abu 'Abd Allah?” He said, “No.” He said, “Take off your shirt.” Wahb said, “Why is that, O Messenger of God?” He said, “This is a day in which I permit you, when you have thrown the Jamrat al-'Aqabah, to become free of everything forbidden to you in the state of ihram except women. But if evening comes and one of you has not performed the ifadah, he remains in a state of ihram until he performs it.”"],[19441,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her while she was wrapping her head veil. He said, “One fold, not two folds.”"],[19442,"She heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Any woman who takes off her clothes outside her own house, God tears away His veil from her.”"],[19443,"Yahya b. Sulaym b. Zayd, the client of the Messenger of God ﷺ, narrated to us from al-Sa'b b. 'Abd Allah b. Abi Umayyah: Umm Salamah told me that she heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “There will certainly come upon people a time in which the truthful one lies, the liar is believed, the trustworthy one betrays, the treacherous one is entrusted, a man gives testimony without being asked to testify, swears an oath without being asked to swear, and the happiest person in the world will be Luka' b. Luka', who does not believe in God and His Messenger.”"],[19444,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon Abu Salamah when his gaze had already become fixed. He closed his eyes and said, “When the soul is taken, the sight follows it.” Some of his family clamored, so he said, “Do not pray against yourselves except for good, for the angels say 'Amen' to what you say.” Then he said, “O God, forgive Abu Salamah, raise his degree among the rightly guided, and be his successor among his descendants who remain. Forgive us and him, O Lord of the worlds. O God, make his grave spacious for him and fill it with light.”"],[19445,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, “In heaven there are two angels: one commands severity and the other commands gentleness, and each is right. They are Jibril and Mika'il. There were two prophets: one commanded gentleness and the other commanded severity, and each was right—he mentioned Ibrahim and Nuh. I have two companions: one commands gentleness and the other commands severity, and each is right—he mentioned Abu Bakr and 'Umar.”"],[19446,"She said on the day 'A'ishah died: \"Today the most beloved person in the world to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has died.\" Then she said: \"I seek Allah's forgiveness; except for her father.\""],[19447,"Umm Salamah, when Abu Salamah died, I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what should I say?\" He said: \"Say: 'O Allah, forgive him and grant me a beneficial successor from him.'\" I said it, and Allah granted me the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as a successor."],[19448,"The Prophet ﷺ never left my house in the morning without raising his eyes to the sky and saying: \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from leading astray or being led astray, from slipping or being made to slip, from wronging or being wronged, and from acting ignorantly or being treated ignorantly.\""],[19449,"She was delousing the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Zaynab, the wife of 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, came and began talking to me while I talked to her, and I raised my eyes to her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Attend to your delousing, for you are not talking to her with your eyes.\" Zaynab said: \"Then I began to complain of the narrowness of the dwelling.\" He said: \"This is just as the wife of 'Uthman b. Maz'un did; her place did not suffice her until she moved onto his head.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Thus it is for any emigrant woman who stakes out a plot in Madinah; she has her plot.\" So she inherited her share from 'Abdullah's house and secured her house in Madinah."],[19450,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray thirteen raka'ah in the night, but when he became old or weak, he would pray seven raka'ah."],[19451,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “When sins become widespread in my Ummah, Allah will envelop them all in punishment.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, will there not be righteous people among the people on that day?” He said, “Yes.” I said, “Then what will happen to them?” He said, “What befalls the people will befall them, and then they will attain forgiveness from Allah and His good pleasure.” This is the wording of the hadith of Abu al-Rabi'."],[19452,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he would depilate, would begin with his pubic area, and that is what he would attend to."],[19453,"Umm Salamah: A daughter of mine fell ill, so I steeped something for her in a jug of hers. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered while it was boiling and said, “What is this?” I said, “My daughter fell ill, so I steeped this for her.” He said, “Indeed, Allah did not place your cure in what has been forbidden to you.”"],[19454,"This verse: “Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O People of the House, and to purify you thoroughly” is about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn."],[19455,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me with a distressed face. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, why do I see you distressed?” He said, “The dinars that they brought to us—I forgot them in the corner of my bed. I forgot to distribute them before evening.”"],[19456,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he became angry, his face would turn red."],[19457,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “Sit at the door so that no one enters upon me.” So I stood at the door when al-Husayn came, and he was a young boy. I went to grab him, but the boy got ahead of me and entered upon his grandfather. I said, “O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom. You commanded me that no one should enter upon you, and your son came. I went to grab him, but he got ahead of me.” When that prolonged, I looked from the door and found you turning something in your palm while your tears were flowing and the boy was on your belly. He said, “Yes, Jibril came to me and informed me that my Ummah will kill him, and he brought me the soil upon which he will be killed. It is that which I am turning in my palm.”"],[19458,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Indeed, among my Companions are those who will not see me after I die.”"],[19459,"“We never sifted flour for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ever.”"],[19460,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Why didn’t you make use of its hide?”"],[19461,"I heard Umm Salamah say: 'Ali was upon the truth; whoever followed him followed the truth and whoever abandoned him abandoned the truth—a covenant taken before this day of his.'"],[19462,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the desert when a caller cried out to him, 'O Messenger of Allah!' He turned but saw no one. Then he turned again and saw a gazelle tied up. It said, 'Come near me, O Messenger of Allah.' He came near it and said, 'What do you need?' It said, 'I have two fawns in that mountain. Untie me so I can go nurse them, then I will return to you.' He said, 'Will you do that?' It said, 'May Allah punish me with the punishment of a she-camel that withholds her milk if I do not.' So he released it, and it went and nursed its two fawns, then came back and he tied it again. The Bedouin woke up and said, 'Do you need anything, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Yes, release this one.' So he released it, and it ran off saying, 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah.'"],[19463,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not gulp down his drink; he would drink two or three times."],[19464,"The Prophet ﷺ recited this verse: \"Indeed, he has done a non-righteous deed.\""],[19465,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah, 'Bring me your husband and your two sons.' She brought them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw over them a Fadakite cloak, then placed his hand upon them and said, 'O Allah, these are the family of Muhammad, so place Your blessings and benedictions upon the family of Muhammad, for You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.' Umm Salamah said, 'I lifted the cloak to enter with them, but he pulled it from my hands and said, 'You are upon good.'"],[19466,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah, 'Bring me your husband and your two sons.' She brought them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw over them a cloak, then said, 'These are the family of Muhammad, so place Your blessings and benedictions upon the family of Muhammad as You placed them upon the family of Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.'"],[19467,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited every intoxicant and every narcotic."],[19468,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding His saying, “that they not disobey you in what is right,” he said: “Wailing.”"],[19469,"The Prophet ﷺ took a garment and wrapped it over ʿAlī, Fāṭimah, al-Ḥasan, and al-Ḥusayn, then recited this verse: “Allah intends only to remove from you the impurity, O people of the household, and to purify you thoroughly.”"],[19470,"“O Messenger of Allah, my hands have become calloused from the mill, kneading bread and dough.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “If Allah provides you something it will come to you. I shall direct you to something better than that. When you lie down in your bed, glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise Allah thirty-three times, and magnify Allah thirty-four times. That is better for you than a servant. And when you pray the morning prayer, say ten times after the morning prayer and ten times after the sunset prayer: ‘There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise. He gives life and causes death. In His hand is all good, and He is capable of all things.’ Each one of them is recorded as ten good deeds, erases ten evil deeds, and each one is like freeing a slave from the children of Ishmael. No sin committed that day is lawful to remain except that it erases it, unless it be associating partners with Allah. ‘There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner’—it guards you from every devil and from every thing between your saying it in the morning and your saying it in the evening.”"],[19471,"Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was speaking with a man, and he said, “O Umm Salamah, who is this?” I said, “Diḥyah al-Kalbī.” I did not know that it was Jibrīl ﷺ until I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ telling his companions what had taken place between them. I said to Abū ʿUthmān, “Who narrated this to you?” He said, “Usāmah b. Zayd.”"],[19472,"I performed Hajj with my master and entered upon Umm Salamah. She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Pronounce talbiyah, O nation of Muhammad, for a Hajj and an ʿUmrah.”"],[19473,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded giving charity. Zaynab, the wife of Abdullah b. Mas'ud, said, “Will it suffice me for charity that I give to my husband, who is poor, and to the orphans of my brother, on whom I spend in any case?” He said, “Yes.” She was a skilled craftswoman."],[19474,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that a daughter of hers had lost her husband and complained of her eyes, and she wanted to apply kohl to her. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"One of you used to throw a dung pellet at the head of the year, but it is only four months and ten [days].\""],[19475,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a sheep's shoulder, and he ate from it, then prayed without touching water."],[19476,"On the authority of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, from the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A woman whose husband has died should not dye her hair, nor apply kohl, nor wear perfume, nor wear a dyed garment, nor wear jewelry.\""],[19477,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The one who drinks from a silver vessel only makes the fire of Hell gurgle in his belly.\""],[19478,"On the authority of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: There was shouting in the room of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he came out wearing a cloak thrown over his shoulders and said: 'What are these people doing?' They said: 'They are disputing, O Messenger of God.' The Prophet of God ﷺ judged between them, then said: 'I judge between you, and it may be that one of you is more eloquent in presenting his case than his brother, so I judge in his favor based on what I discern. If I award someone something that is not his due, I am only giving him a portion of the Fire.'"],[19479,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever enters the state of iḥrām from Jerusalem, his past sins will be forgiven.\""],[19480,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"O Umm Salamah, do not harm me concerning A'ishah, for revelation has not descended upon me while I was with any of my wives except A'ishah; indeed revelation descended upon me while she was with me under my blanket.\""],[19481,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever says every day: 'O Allah, forgive me and the believing men and women,' a reward equal to every believer will be added to his account.\""],[19482,"She asked Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, about nabidh. She said: I will inform you what the Messenger of God ﷺ used to forbid his family from: He used to forbid us from mixing raisins with dates."],[19483,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: It is not appropriate for anyone to be in a state of major ritual impurity in this mosque except me and Ali."],[19484,"I entered upon Umm Salamah while she was weeping. I said: What makes you weep? She said: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ—meaning in a dream—with dust on his head and beard. I said: What is wrong with you, O Messenger of God? He said: I have just witnessed the killing of al-Husayn."],[19485,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: None loves Ali except a believer, and none hates him except a hypocrite."],[19486,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: The one consulted is entrusted."],[19487,"She heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: When evil appears on the earth, God sends His punishment upon the people of the earth. I said: O Messenger of God, what if there are righteous people among them? He said: Yes, even if there are righteous people among them, what befalls the people will befall them too; then they will return to God's mercy and forgiveness."],[19488,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ali: Are you not content to be to me as Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me?"],[19489,"Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr came to the Prophet ﷺ while she was ill, and he said to her, “Will you not come out with us on this journey of ours?” She said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am ill and I fear my illness will hold me back.” He said, “Enter ihram for Hajj and say: O Allah, my place of exiting ihram is wherever You hold me back.”"],[19490,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Witr with seven or five Rak’ah, and he would not say Salam or speak in between them.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1192)"],[19491,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Angels do not accompany a group that has a bell in it.”"],[19492,"The Prophet ﷺ used to wake up in a state of janabah and then fast."],[19493,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Whoever loves Ali has loved me, and whoever loves me has loved Allah. Whoever hates Ali has hated me, and whoever hates me has hated Allah.”"],[19494,"«I brought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a roasted side (of meat), and he ate from it, then stood for prayer and did not perform wudu.»"],[19495,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Whoever is tested with judging between Muslims, let him treat them equally in the seating, in gesture and gaze, and let him not raise his voice against one of the two litigants more than the other.»"],[19496,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to «perform wudu from what fire has touched.»"],[19497,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ when I began menstruating, so I left the bed. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Wrap a waist-wrapper around yourself and come back.”"],[19498,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds,” letter by letter."],[19499,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever spends on two daughters, two sisters, or two female relatives, seeking reward for his spending on them until God suffices them and enriches them from His bounty, they will be a screen for him from the Fire.”"],[19500,"“My abundant wealth may destroy me, for I am the wealthiest of Quraysh.” She said: “My son, give charity, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Among my Companions are those who will never see me after I die.’” So 'Abd al-Rahman went out and met 'Umar and told him what Umm Salamah had said. 'Umar came and entered upon her and said: “Am I one of them?” She said: “No, and I will never say that to anyone after you.”"],[19501,"May your face be rubbed in dust, for the Prophet ﷺ said to a freed slave of ours called Rabah, whom he saw prostrating: “May your face be rubbed in dust, O Rabah.”"],[19502,"And the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever possesses one of three qualities, Allah will marry him to the wide-eyed maidens of Paradise: whoever has a hidden, desirable trust and fulfills it out of fear of Allah, or a man who pardons his killer, or a man who recites ‘Say: He is Allah, the One’ after every prayer.”"],[19503,"I heard Umm Salamah say: “Ali is upon the truth; whoever follows him follows the truth, and whoever abandons him abandons the truth—a covenant pledged before his death.”"],[19504,"I came to Umm Salamah to inform her about al-Husayn, and she said to me in what she narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in my house one day when Fatimah came to him with some porridge. He said: “Go and bring your husband—or your cousin—and your two sons.” She went and brought Ali, Hasan, and Husayn, and they ate from that food while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a bed of ours, with a Khaybar cloak beneath him. He took the cloak and wrapped them in it, then raised his hands toward the sky and said: “O Allah, these are my family and my household, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly.” Umm Salamah said: “O Messenger of Allah, am I not of your household?” He said: “You are upon good.”"],[19505,"Sometimes the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dyed his cloak and waist-wrapper with saffron or wars, then went out wearing them."],[19506,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform nine or ten units of non-obligatory prayers, without separating them with a greeting or speech."],[19507,"“I and the Messenger of God ﷺ used to bathe from one vessel, about half a faraq, taking turns in washing together, he starting before me.”"],[19508,"Ibn 'Abbas and some people sent me to Umm Salamah to ask her which days the Messenger of God ﷺ fasted most. She said, “Saturday and Sunday were the days he fasted most of all, and he would say, ‘They are the two festival days of the polytheists, so I like to differ from them.’”"],[19509,"“I and the Messenger of God ﷺ used to bathe from one vessel, both of us in a state of janabah, until my hand and his hand differed.”"],[19510,"The Prophet ﷺ used to make the intention to fast at night, then he would get up in the morning and say, “Do you have anything?” We would say, “We have nothing. Are you not fasting?”"],[19511,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not harm me regarding Aisha, for revelation has not descended under the blanket of any one of you except Aisha ؓ.”"],[19512,"that the Prophet ﷺ commanded her to pray the morning prayer in Makkah."],[19513,"that you should marry until you complete the waiting period, the longer of the two terms. She remained for twenty nights, then she gave birth. So she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he said, \"Marry.\" And Fatimah bint Qays used to narrate from the Messenger of God ﷺ when she was given an irrevocable divorce that he commanded her to move to Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is blind, and she could set down her garments in his presence before her waiting period ended. And Muhammad b. Usamah b. Zayd used to narrate that whenever she mentioned anything of that, Usamah threw at her whatever was in his hand."],[19514,"that the Prophet ﷺ ate from the shoulder of a sheep, then the call to prayer was made, and he prayed without touching water—the afternoon prayer."],[19515,"that a woman asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: \"O Messenger of God, I have a daughter whom I married off, and she was afflicted with measles so that her hair fell out, and we want to present her to her husband.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"May God curse the one who attaches hair extensions and the one who asks for them.\""],[19516,"O Messenger of God, is there an obligation for a woman to perform ghusl if she has a wet dream? He said, \"Yes, if she sees fluid, let her perform ghusl.\""],[19517,"It was my night on which the Messenger of God ﷺ would come to me, on the evening of the Day of Sacrifice. He came to me, and Wahb b. Zam'ah entered upon me, and with him another man from the family of Abu Umayyah, both wearing shirts. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Have you performed the ifadah circumambulation yet, O Abu Abdullah?\" He said, \"No, by God, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"Remove your shirt from yourself.\" So he removed it from his head, and his companion removed his shirt from his head. Then he said, \"Why, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"This is a day on which permission has been given to you: when you have thrown the pebbles, you may exit ihram from everything that was forbidden to you except women. But if you have intercourse before you circumambulate this House, you become in a state of ihram as you were before throwing the pebbles.\""],[19518,"that the Prophet ﷺ performed i'tikaf the first year during the first ten days, then he performed i'tikaf during the middle ten days, then he performed i'tikaf during the last ten days. And he said, \"I saw the Night of Decree in them, but I was made to forget it.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ continued to perform i'tikaf during them until the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away."],[19519,"She said: I used to perform ghusl together with the Messenger of Allah from a single vessel."],[19520,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with me, and he woke up with his eyes red. He shook his head and said: “Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near.” I said: What is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “A gap has been opened in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj like this,” and he formed a circle with ten fingers. The narrator said: I do not know whether [it was] like a ring or like a fingertip. I said: Do you fear for us destruction, O Messenger of Allah, even though righteous people are among us? He said: “Yes, when wickedness becomes widespread.” Umm Ruman said: 'A'ishah said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about this hadith, and he narrated it to me just as Umm Salamah said."],[19521,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said what he said about the hem, Umm Salamah said: What about us? He said: “Let it hang down a handspan.” She said: Then the feet will be exposed. He said: “Let it hang down a cubit.”"],[19522,"She said: One of us, when she performed ghusl, would take care that no one saw her yellow [traces]."],[19523,"She said: My eye has become accustomed to kohl that contains perfume, and her husband had died. Is it permissible for me to apply kohl? She said: “By Allah, I do not command you to do anything that Allah and His Messenger have forbidden.”"],[19524,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “It is not lawful for a woman to mourn more than three days, except a woman mourning her husband for four months and ten days.”"],[19525,"He used to say: I have a hadith which, if I wanted to consume the world by means of it, I would consume it, but Allah will not ask me about a hadith I raise to the ruler. My father said: I said: What is it? He said: When Zayd went out, I came to my maternal aunt the next day and said to her: O mother, Zayd has gone out. She said: The poor man, he will be killed as his fathers were killed. I said to her: Men of understanding have gone out with him. She said: I was with Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, when they discussed the caliphate. Umm Salamah said: I was with the Prophet ﷺ when they discussed the caliphate after him. They said: The descendants of Fatimah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “They will never attain it, ever; rather it will be among the descendants of my paternal uncle, my father’s full brother, until they hand it over to the Dajjal.”"],[19526,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: “Fast three days of every month, from its beginning: Monday, Thursday, and the following Thursday.”"],[19527,"Umm Salamah: This verse was revealed in my house: {Indeed, Allah intends only to remove from you the impurity, O people of the household, and to purify you with thorough purification.} I was sitting at the door, so I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, am I not one of the people of the household?' He said, 'You are upon good.'"],[19528,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr, 'Enter ihram for Hajj and say: My place of exiting ihram is wherever You restrain me.'"],[19529,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'If the first thing my Lord enjoined upon me and forbade me, after idol worship and drinking wine, was quarreling with men.'"],[19530,"that the Prophet ﷺ said, 'I have seen what my Ummah will face after me, so I have delayed my intercession until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[19531,"Um Salamah was in the Battle of Khaybar and she said, \"I heard the sound of the sword hitting the teeth of Marhab.\""],[19532,"that the Prophet ﷺ forbade a man to pray with his hair tied up"],[19533,"By the One who took his soul—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—he did not pass away until most of his prayer was performed sitting, except for the obligatory prayers. The deed most pleasing to him was that which its doer persisted in, even if it was little."],[19534,"The deeds most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were those done persistently, even if few."],[19535,"He did not die until most of his prayer was performed sitting, and the deed most beloved to him was that which its doer persevered in, even if little—meaning the Prophet ﷺ."],[19536,"By the One who took his soul, he did not die until most of his prayer was performed while he was sitting, and the deed most beloved to him was the righteous deed that a servant persists in, even if it was little."],[19537,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A woman should not ask for her sister's divorce in order to empty her own plate, for her provision is upon Allah ﷻ.'"],[19538,"From the Prophet ﷺ: that he came to her, wrapped his cloak, placed it on the threshold of the door, leaned on it, and said: 'Would you like, O Umm Salamah?' She said: 'I am a woman of intense jealousy, and I fear that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ may see from me what he dislikes.' He then left, then returned and said: 'Would you like, O Umm Salamah? If there is an increase in your dowry, we will increase it.' She repeated her words, so Umm Abd said: 'O Umm Salamah, do you know what the women of Quraysh are saying? They say that Umm Salamah rejected Muhammad only because she wanted a young man from Quraysh, younger in age and with more wealth.' She said: So she went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he married her."],[19539,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The pillars of my pulpit are fixed stations in Paradise.'"],[19540,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The pillars of my pulpit are fixed stations in Paradise.'"],[19541,"I used to perform ghusl, I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from a single vessel."],[19542,"The Prophet ﷺ used to deliver the khutbah leaning on a trunk in the mosque. When the pulpit was made, the trunk yearned, so the Prophet ﷺ embraced it, and it became still."],[19543,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise.'"],[19544,"The Prophet ﷺ did not fast any month in full except that he used to fast Sha'ban and connect it with Ramadan."],[19545,"From A'isha and Umm Salama, they said: The Prophet ﷺ did not fast any month other than Ramadan except Sha'ban, for he used to connect it to Ramadan so that it became two consecutive months. And he would fast a month until we said he would not break his fast, and he would break his fast until we said he would not fast."],[19546,"The Prophet ﷺ used to fast Sha'ban and Ramadan."],[19547,"That she wanted to marry another man. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, so he took her away from the man her father had married her to, and the Prophet ﷺ married her to the one she wanted."],[19548,"Umm Salama asked the Prophet ﷺ about a woman who experiences a wet dream. He said, \"Does she find desire?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then she should perform ghusl.\""],[19549,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ under his blanket when I got my menses, so I slipped away from him. He said, \"What is the matter with you? Have you started your menses?\" meaning menstruation. I said, \"Yes.\" She said: So I tied my menstrual garments tightly around me, then returned and lay down with the Prophet ﷺ."],[19550,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray after 'Asr at all except once. Some people came to him after Zuhr and kept him busy until he forgot, and he did not pray anything after Zuhr until he prayed 'Asr. When he had prayed 'Asr, he entered my house and prayed two rak'ahs."],[19551,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"There is no small amount of harm to a neighbor.\""],[19552,"Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah gave birth twenty nights after her husband's death, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered her to marry."],[19553,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"There is no harm in the skin of a dead animal if it is tanned.\""],[19554,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and one of his wives performed ghusl from a single vessel."],[19555,"The Prophet ﷺ used to prefer to travel on Thursday."],[19556,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never fasted a complete month except Sha'ban; he used to connect it with Ramadan."],[19557,"Subay'ah gave birth after her husband's death, then two men proposed to her. They said she had not become lawful. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"You have become lawful, so marry whomever you wish.\""],[19558,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is no servant who is afflicted with a calamity and says: 'Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return. O Allah, with You I seek reward for my calamity, so reward me in it and give me something better in its place,' except that Allah will reward him in his calamity and give him something better than it.\""],[19559,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss her while he was fasting."],[19560,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Verily, one of the first things my Lord forbade me and enjoined me to avoid, after the worship of idols and the drinking of wine, was quarrelling with men."],[19561,"A woman entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the house of Umm Salamah and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees?\" Umm Salamah said: \"Woe to you! You have exposed women.\" The woman said: \"Indeed, Allah is not ashamed of the truth.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever of you sees that, let her perform ghusl.\""],[19562,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, Allah mentions men in everything and does not mention us.” Then Allah revealed: {Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women...} to the end of the verse."],[19563,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ under a blanket, and I felt what women feel of menstruation. He said, “That is what has been decreed for the daughters of Adam.” So I slipped away, set my affairs right, then returned. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Come and enter with me under the blanket.” She said: So I entered with him."],[19564,"The husband of Subay‘ah bint al-Harith died, and she gave birth a few days after his death. The Prophet ﷺ commanded her to marry."],[19565,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “I have istihadah (non-menstrual bleeding).” He said, “That is not menstruation; it is only a vein. The woman should refrain for the days of her menstrual periods, then perform ghusl, then fasten a cloth and pray.”"],[19566,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Expel the Jews from the Arabian Peninsula.”"],[19567,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave instructions at the time of his death, saying, “Fear Allah regarding the Copts of Egypt, for you will prevail over them and they will be a support and helpers for you in the way of Allah.”"],[19568,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated that Bakr ibn Sahl narrated from Abdullah ibn Yusuf, who said that Malik reported from Amr ibn Muslim al-Jundai, who reported from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who reported from Umm Salamah, who said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When the ten days of Dhul-Hijjah begin, whoever intends to offer a sacrifice should not cut his hair or trim his nails.\""],[19569,"The Mahdi was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ , and he said, \"He is from the offspring of Fatimah.\""],[19570,"From ‘A’ishah and Umm Salamah: they said, “Safiyyah bint Huyayy menstruated before the sacrifice, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her while she was weeping and said, ‘Will she hold us back? Had you performed the ifadah circumambulation on the Day of Sacrifice?’ She said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Then depart.’”"],[19571,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us while a certain man was complaining. He said, “What is this?” We said, “We suspect the evil eye for him.” He said, “Why do you not seek ruqyah for him from the evil eye?”"],[19572,"Umm Salamah: I mentioned the false messiah, the Dajjal, one night and sleep did not come to me. When morning came, I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He said, “Do not do that, for if he emerges while I am among you, Allah will suffice you through me; and if he emerges after I die, He will suffice you through the righteous.” Then he stood and mentioned the Dajjal, saying, “There is no prophet but he warned his nation about him, and I warn you about him. He is one-eyed, and indeed Allah is not one-eyed. Indeed, the false messiah, the Dajjal—it is as if his eye is a floating grape.”"],[19573,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me ahead among the weak members of his family on the night of Muzdalifah.” She said: So I threw the pebbles at night, then proceeded to Makkah and prayed fajr there, then returned to Mina."],[19574,"She said to the Prophet ﷺ, “I have not performed the circumambulation of departure.” The Prophet ﷺ said to her, “When the people pray fajr, perform circumambulation on your camel behind the rows, then depart.”"],[19575,"Abu Hurayrah, Ibn ‘Abbas, and Abu Salamah gathered and discussed a woman who gives birth after her husband’s death. Ibn ‘Abbas said, “The longer of the two terms.” Abu Salamah said, “When she gives birth, she becomes lawful.” Abu Hurayrah said, “I am with my brother’s son.” So they sent Kurayb to Umm Salamah, and she mentioned the hadith of Subay‘ah that the Prophet ﷺ “commanded her to marry.”"],[19576,"Subay'ah bint al-Harith delivered her child a few days after her husband's death, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed her to remarry."],[19577,"Fatimah experienced istihadah (irregular bleeding). She used to wash in a large tub and would come out with yellowish or dusky discharge. Umm Salamah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on her behalf. He said, \"She should wait for the days of her menstruation and leave the prayer during them, and she should bathe for the rest and pray.\" Ayyub said: I said to Sulayman b. Yasar, \"May her husband approach her?\" He said, \"We only say what we heard.\""],[19578,"Fatimah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"I see blood.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed her to bathe and perform ablution for each prayer."],[19579,"A woman asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying, \"I have istihadah and do not become pure. Should I abandon prayer?\" He said, \"No, but leave [prayer for] the number of days and nights in which you used to menstruate, then bathe, fasten a cloth, and pray.\""],[19580,"She mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ the hems of women's garments. He said, \"Let them lower it by a handspan.\" I said, \"Then their ankles would be uncovered.\" He said, \"Then a cubit, and they should not add to that.\""],[19581,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"After me there will be a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, and a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula.\" She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will the earth sink while there are righteous people among them?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, \"When the majority of its inhabitants are wicked.\""],[19582,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would wake up in a state of janabah without having had a wet dream, then he would bathe and continue his fast."],[19583,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never prayed either of the two [rak'ahs] at my place except once. One day he entered after 'Asr and prayed two rak'ahs. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is this prayer? You never used to pray it. And a prayer after 'Asr was revealed?\" He said, \"No, but they are two rak'ahs I used to pray after Zuhr, but I was distracted from them, so I made them up.\""],[19584,"Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that when she arrived in Madinah, she told them that she was the daughter of Umayyah b. al-Mughirah, but they disbelieved her, saying, \"How untruthful strangers are!\" Eventually, some of them prepared to go for Hajj and said, \"Will you write to your family?\" She wrote with them. When they returned to Madinah, they confirmed her truthfulness and she gained even more respect from them. She said: When Zaynab was weaned, the Prophet ﷺ came to me and proposed to me. I said, \"Someone like me should not be married. As for me, I am past childbearing, and I am jealous and have dependents.\" He said, \"I am older than you. As for jealousy, Allah will remove it. As for the dependents, they are for Allah and His Messenger.\" So he married her. He would come to her and say, \"Where is Zunab?\" until one day 'Ammar b. Yasir came and snatched her away, saying, \"This one prevents the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" She was nursing her. Then the Prophet ﷺ came and said, \"Where is Zunab?\" Quraybah bint Abi Umayyah said, and she happened to be with her, \"'Ammar b. Yasir took her.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I will come to you tonight.\" She said: I got up and placed my leather mats, and I set aside some grains of barley that were in a jar, and I took out some fat and made a dish for him. She said: The Prophet ﷺ spent the night, and in the morning when he woke he said, \"Your family has high regard for you. If you wish, I will spend seven nights with you, and if I spend seven with you, I will spend seven with my [other] wives.\""],[19585,"That the Prophet ﷺ, when he married her, said, \"If I spend seven nights with you, I will spend seven nights with my [other] wives.\""],[19586,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to her when he entered upon her, \"You and your family have high regard for me. If I spend seven nights with you, I will spend seven with my [other] wives.\""],[19587,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from 'Abd Rabbihi b. Sa'id, from Abu Bakr b. 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'A'ishah and Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wake up in a state of janabah without having had a wet dream, then he would fast."],[19588,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from 'Abd Rabbihi b. Sa'id, from Abu Bakr b. 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'A'ishah and Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wake up in a state of janabah from intercourse, not from a wet dream, then he would fast."],[19589,"Zaynab bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted protection to Abu al-'As b. al-Rabi', so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The lowest of them may grant protection on behalf of the Muslims.'"],[19590,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed with Umm Salamah for three days when he consummated the marriage with her, then he said: 'It is not that you are of little importance to your family. If I stay seven days with you, I will stay seven days with my other wives.'"],[19591,"When the Prophet ﷺ married Umm Salamah, he stayed with her for three days, and he said: 'There is no belittlement of you before your family. If you wish, I will stay seven days with you, and if I stay seven with you, I will stay seven with my other wives.'"],[19592,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to experience the dawn while in a state of major impurity (janabah) without performing a ritual bath (ghusl), and he would then fast."],[19593,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wake up in a state of janabah from women, without a wet dream, then he would continue fasting."],[19594,"Umm Salamah: When Abu Salamah died in Madinah, I said: 'She has become a stranger in a strange land; I will weep for him with a weeping that will be talked about.' She said: 'While I was thus, a woman from the highlands came to console me, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met her and said: 'Do you want to let Satan enter a house from which Allah has expelled him twice?' She said: 'So I left off weeping and did not weep for him.'"],[19595,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I have forbidden you from visiting graves, but now go and visit them, for there are lessons to be learned from them.\""],[19596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pause in his recitation: {In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, Master of the Day of Judgment}."],[19597,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner, such and such good deeds will be written for him.'"],[19598,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, my uncle Hisham b. al-Mughirah used to feed people, maintain family ties, and do such and such. If he had met you, he would have become Muslim.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'He used to give for the sake of this world alone and its remembrance, and he never once said: Forgive me on the Day of Judgment.'"],[19599,"Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: \"We were with the Prophet ﷺ while we were in ihram, and a rider would pass by us, and one of us would let her garment hang over her face from above her head\" — and sometimes she said: \"from above the khimar.\""],[19600,"Umm Salamah said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we are not given a share of inheritance nor do we fight and become martyrs.\" Then Allah revealed: {And do not wish for that by which Allah has made some of you exceed others} until the end of the verse. Then it was revealed: {Indeed, I do not allow to be lost the work of any worker among you, whether male or female}."],[19601,"She wore a necklace containing small hairs of gold, and the Prophet ﷺ saw it and disliked it, so he turned away from her. She then removed it, and he said: \"What assures you that on the Day of Resurrection He will not make you wear in its place hairs of fire?\""],[19602,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Whoever prays four rak'ahs before 'Asr, Allah will forbid his body to the Fire.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have seen you praying and leaving off.\" He said: \"I am not like any one of them.\""],[19603,"Fatimah came to her father with a dish while he was lying down. He said, \"Go and call my son and your cousin.\" She covered them with a garment, then he said, \"O Allah, these are the people of my household and my protection. Remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly.\" Umm Salamah asked, \"Can I be with them, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"You are the wife of the Prophet ﷺ . You may choose to be with me or to do what is best.\""],[19604,"She used to wear gold ornaments, and she asked the Prophet ﷺ: \"Is this a treasure?\" He said: \"If you pay its zakah, then it is not a treasure.\""],[19605,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only prohibited gold. We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what about musk that comes into contact with gold?\" He said: \"No, unless it is with silver; then smear it with saffron.\""],[19606,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer with five or seven units, without speaking or making a final salaam in between them."],[19607,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"No one wears a garment to show off with it, so that people look at him, but Allah will not look at him until he takes it off, whenever he takes it off.\""],[19608,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Whoever learns knowledge to boast with it before the scholars, or to argue with it against the foolish, is in the Fire.\""],[19609,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever is tested with judging among the Muslims must not judge while he is angry.\""],[19610,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss while fasting."],[19611,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever is faced with a dispute among Muslims should seek to reconcile them in that very moment, through gestures, seating, and position.\""],[19612,"Whoever is tested with judging between the Muslims should not raise his voice against one of the two disputants more than he raises it against the other."],[19613,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do not cut bread with a knife as the Persians cut it. When one of you wants to eat meat, he should not cut it with a knife; rather, he should take it with his hand and bite it with his mouth, for it is more wholesome and more nourishing.\""],[19614,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not smell food as beasts of prey smell it.\""],[19615,"Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, reported that she brought a roasted side of meat to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He ate from it, then stood up for prayer and did not perform ablution."],[19616,"In my house this verse was revealed: {Allah only intends to remove from you the impurity, O people of the household, and to purify you with a thorough purification}. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn and said: \"O Allah, these are my family.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, am I not from the household?\" He said: \"If Allah wills.\""],[19617,"Marwan sent me to Umm Salamah, and I asked her. She said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me after performing ablution, and I handed him a bone or a shoulder. He ate, then stood up for prayer and did not perform ablution.\""],[19618,"Umm Salamah was asked about what fire has altered. She said: \"The Prophet ﷺ ate a shoulder, then prayed and did not perform ablution.\""],[19619,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me after the afternoon prayer and prayed two rak'ahs. I said: What are these two rak'ahs, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I used to pray them before the afternoon prayer, but some people came and occupied me, so I prayed them now."],[19620,"A slave-boy of hers divorced his free wife with two divorce declarations, so Umm Salamah sought a ruling from the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: She is forbidden to him until she marries another husband."],[19621,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to rise in the morning in a state of major ritual impurity from sexual intercourse, not from a wet dream, then complete his fast."],[19622,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade qunūt in the morning prayer."],[19623,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ under a blanket, and I slipped out from under his blanket. He said: What is the matter with you? Have you started menstruating? I said: Yes. He said: Tie your waist-wrapper firmly and return to where you were."],[19624,"He asked Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, about the prayer of the Prophet ﷺ. She said: He used to pray the later evening prayer, then glorify Allah, then pray after it whatever Allah willed of the night. Then he would depart and sleep for as long as he had prayed. Then he would wake from that sleep and pray for as long as he had slept. That last prayer of his would continue until morning."],[19625,"She described the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was a clear recitation, letter by letter."],[19626,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Al-Qasim b. al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ali, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Hajj is the jihad of every weak person."],[19627,"I heard Umm Salamah say: I said to the Prophet ﷺ: Why are we not mentioned in the Quran as men are mentioned? One day nothing startled me except a recitation on the minbar while I was combing my hair. I wrapped up my hair, then went out to my chamber and put my ear near the palm branches, and there he was saying on the minbar: O you who believe, Allah says in His Book: {Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women} to the end of the verse."],[19628,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have not heard Allah mention women in the context of emigration. So Allah revealed: {Indeed, I do not allow the work of any worker among you to be lost, male or female}."],[19629,"On the authority of Salama, a man from the children of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, who said: Al-Zubayr brought a dispute against a man to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ruled in favor of al-Zubayr. The man said: He only ruled in his favor because he is his paternal aunt's son. Then the verse was revealed: {But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge} the verse."],[19630,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss when he was fasting. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1685)"],[19631,"The Prophet ﷺ used to kiss me while I was fasting and he was fasting."],[19632,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed two rak'ahs in her house after the afternoon prayer, which he did not pray before or after."],[19633,"The messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A man will be pledged allegiance between the Rukn and the Maqam, with a number of the people of Badr. Then troops from the people of Iraq and the replaced ones from the people of Sham will come to him, and a group from the people of Sham will fight against them until they reach an open land, where they will be swallowed up. A man from the Quraysh, whose relatives are like dogs, will then come and fight against them, and he will defeat them.\" It was said that the one who fails is the one who fails in gaining the spoils of a dog."],[19634,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who braids my hair tightly; should I undo it for major ritual impurity? He said: \"No, it is sufficient for you to take handfuls of water with your palms and pour it over your skin, and you will be purified.\""],[19635,"Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, does a woman have a wet dream? He said: \"When the yellowish fluid descends, she should perform ghusl.\""],[19636,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When dinner is served and the prayer begins, start with dinner.\""],[19637,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I will be your forerunner at the Hawd. Let none of you come and be driven away as a stray camel is driven away. I will say: For what is this? It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you. I will say: Away with them!\""],[19638,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You bring disputes to me, and I am only a human being. I judge between you according to what I hear from you. If I award someone something from his brother's right, I am only cutting off for him a piece of the Fire.\""],[19639,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he performed ablution, used to run his fingers through his beard."],[19640,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, why are we not mentioned in the Qur'an as men are mentioned? Then nothing startled me except a call from the minbar while I was combing my hair. I wrapped up my hair and turned my ear toward the palm branches, and I heard him reciting: {Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women} the verse."],[19641,"The most I know is that the Prophet ﷺ was brought a bag of money containing eight hundred dirhams."],[19642,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Cupping on the head is a remedy for insanity, leprosy, night blindness, leukoderma and headache.”"],[19643,"The Prophet ﷺ would wake up in a state of major ritual impurity and then fast that day."],[19644,"The Prophet ﷺ used to wake up in a state of sexual impurity, then he would perform the ritual purification and observe fasting."],[19645,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I saw for Abu Jahl freed slaves in Paradise.” When Ikrimah embraced Islam, he said: “It is this one.”"],[19646,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Perform ablution from whatever fire has touched.”"],[19647,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “When the mukatab has enough to pay off his contract, then veil yourself from him.”"],[19648,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “When the mukatab has the means to pay, then veil yourself from him.”"],[19649,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Maymunah was with him, when Ibn Umm Maktum approached. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Veil yourselves from him.” We said: “O Messenger of God, is he not blind, unable to see us or recognize us?” He said: “Are you two not able to see him?”"],[19650,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “Say at the Maghrib call to prayer: O God, at the approach of Your night and the departure of Your day, at the voices of Your callers and the presence of Your prayers, forgive me.” And when she woke during the night, she would say: “Lord, forgive, have mercy, and guide to the straightest path.”"],[19651,"From the Prophet ﷺ, a hadith like the one that follows it."],[19652,"The Prophet ﷺ swore not to enter upon some of his wives for a month. When twenty-nine days had passed, he went to them in the morning or in the evening. It was said to him: “O Prophet of God, you swore not to enter for a month.” He said: “The month is twenty-nine days.”"],[19653,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say after the prayer: “O God, I ask You for wholesome provision, accepted deeds, and beneficial knowledge.”"],[19654,"The general bequest of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at his death was: “The prayer and what your right hands possess.”"],[19655,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There is no servant who is afflicted by a calamity and says, ‘Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we return. O Allah, reward me in my calamity and compensate me with something better than it,’ except that Allah rewards him in his calamity and compensates him with something better than it.” When Abu Salamah died, I said, “Who is better than Abu Salamah, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” Then I resolved and said it, and I married the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[19656,"From Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The angels do not accompany a caravan in which there is a bell.”"],[19657,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman b. Abi al-Mawali narrated to us, from Abdullah b. al-Hasan, from Umm Salamah, that she swore about a slave of hers whom she had freed, saying: “May Allah not free me from the Fire if I ever free him.” Then she remained as long as Allah willed, then she said: “Glory be to Allah! I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him expiate his oath and then do what is better.’ So I freed the slave, then I expiated her oath.”"],[19658,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever does not have one of three things does not count for anything: piety that restrains him from prohibitions, forbearance that restrains him from the foolish, or character by which he lives among people.”"],[19659,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gathered Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn, then he brought them under his garment, then he said: “O Allah, these are my family.” Umm Salamah said: I said, “O Messenger of Allah, include me with them.” He said: “You are from my family.”"],[19660,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lay down to sleep, then he woke up while he was disturbed in spirit. Then he lay down and slept, then he woke up with red soil in his hand, turning it over. I said, “What is this soil, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Jibril told me that this one will be killed in the land of Iraq – meaning Husayn. I said to Jibril, ‘Show me the soil of the land in which he will be killed,’ so this is its soil.”"],[19661,"Abu Bakr went out on a trade journey to Busra one year before the death of the Prophet ﷺ, and with him were Nu'ayman and Suwaybit b. Harmalah, both of whom had been present at Badr. Nu'ayman was in charge of the provisions. Suwaybit, who was a humorous man, said to him, “Feed me.” He said, “Until your companion comes.” Then he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[19662,"My menses came upon me while I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I slipped away. He said to me: “O Umm Salamah, perhaps you have menstruated?” I said, “Yes.” He said: “Then return and lie down.” She said: So I returned and lay down, and between me and him there was only a waist wrapper that did not go beyond the knees."],[19663,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to enter upon his wives in the morning and greet them. Among them was a woman who had honey, and every time he entered upon her she would offer him some of it, so he would stay with her like that. Aishah and Hafsah were upset by that, so when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon them they said, “We detect the smell of maghafir from you.” So he abandoned that honey."],[19664,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you drink milk, rinse your mouth from it, for it has fat.”"],[19665,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “When you drink milk, rinse your mouth from it, for it has fat.”"],[19666,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to his wives in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage, “This is the pilgrimage, then keep to the insides of the houses.”"],[19667,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ wanted to eat while he was in a state of major ritual impurity, he performed wudu' as he did for prayer."],[19668,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, “Is there jihad incumbent upon women?” He said, “Their jihad is here,” and he gestured with his hand toward Makkah."],[19669,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The best prayer of women is in the innermost parts of their houses.”"],[19670,"That a sheep of theirs died and they did not manage to slaughter it before it died. The Messenger of God ﷺ learned of that and said, “Why did you not make use of its skin?”"],[19671,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ that he used to supplicate with these words: “O God, You are the First, nothing is before You; and You are the Last, nothing is after You. I seek refuge in You from every creature whose forelock is in Your hand, and I seek refuge in You from sin and laziness, from the punishment of the Fire, from the punishment of the grave, from the trial of wealth and the trial of poverty, and I seek refuge in You from wrongdoing and debt. O God, purify my heart from sins as You purified the white garment from dirt. O God, distance me from my sins as You distanced the East from the West. This is what Muhammad asked of his Lord. O God, I ask You for the best asking, the best supplication, the best success, the best deeds, the best reward, the best life, the best death. Keep me firm, make my scales heavy, confirm my faith, raise my rank, accept my prayer, forgive my sin, and I ask You for the highest degrees of Paradise. Amin. O God, I ask You for the beginnings of good, its endings, its comprehensive aspects, its first and last, its outward and inward, and the highest degrees of Paradise. Amin. O God, save me from the Fire, grant me forgiveness night and day, and the righteous abode in Paradise. Amin. O God, I ask You for complete deliverance from the Fire and to enter Paradise safely. O God, I ask You to bless me in my self, my hearing, my sight, my soul, my character, my creation, my family, my life and my death. O God, accept my good deeds, and I ask You for the highest degrees of Paradise. Amin.”"],[19672,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Among my companions are those who will never see me after I die.\" Then 'Umar came and entered upon her and said: \"I adjure you by Allah, am I one of them?\" She said: \"No, and I will never vouch for anyone after you.\" So 'Umar ؓ wept."],[19673,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you are present with a dying person, say good, for the angels say 'Amin' to what you say.\""],[19674,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you is afflicted with a calamity, let him say: 'O Allah, recompense me in my calamity, and give me something better in its place.'\" So when Abu Salamah died, I said: \"Who will Allah give me after Abu Salamah?\" She said: \"So Allah gave me better than him: Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[19675,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Among my companions are those who will never see me after I depart from them.\""],[19676,"We entered upon Umm Salamah, and she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A seeker of refuge will seek refuge at the House, and an army will be sent against him until, when they are in a desert plain, they will be swallowed up.\" I said: \"O Prophet of Allah, what about one who is unwilling?\" He said: \"He will be swallowed up with them, but on the Day of Resurrection he will be raised according to what was in his heart.\""],[19677,"Umm Salamah said: \"O Abu 'Abdillah, is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ insulted among you?\" I said: \"Who insults the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" She said: \"Is not 'Ali insulted, and those who love him? And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to love him.\""],[19678,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I detest a woman who leaves her house dragging her garment, complaining about her husband.\""],[19679,"Some of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ entered upon Umm Salamah and said: \"O Mother of the Believers, tell us about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" She said: \"His public and private conduct were the same.\" Then she regretted it and said: \"I have disclosed a secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So when he entered, she informed him, and he said: \"You have done well.\""],[19680,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a slave boy of hers praying, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “May your face be covered in dust, O Rabah.”"],[19681,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Allah did not metamorphose anything that would have descendants or offspring.”"],[19682,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ embraced 'Ali with one hand and Fatimah with the other, drew over them a black cloak that was on him, and kissed 'Ali and Fatimah, then said: 'O Allah, to You, not to the Fire—I and my household.' Umm Salamah said: I said, 'And I, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'And you.'"],[19683,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ embraced 'Ali with one hand and Fatimah with the other, drew over them a black cloak that was on him, and kissed 'Ali and Fatimah, then said: 'O Allah, to You, not to the Fire—I and my household.' Umm Salamah said: I said, 'And I, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'And you.'"],[19684,"We entered upon Umm Salamah and she brought out to us a pouch containing hair of the Prophet ﷺ dyed with henna. She said, 'This is from the hair of the Prophet ﷺ.'"],[19685,"The Prophet ﷺ used to begin with drink when he was fasting, and he would not gulp it down; he would drink two or three times."],[19686,"\"The verse was revealed in her house: 'Indeed, Allah desires to repel all impurity from you, O people of the household, and purify you with a thorough purification.' The Prophet, ﷺ , took a cloak and covered Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn with it. Then he said, 'O Allah, these are the people of my household, so remove all impurity from them and purify them thoroughly.' I asked, while standing at the doorstep, 'O Messenger of Allah, even if I am with them?' He replied, 'Indeed, you are in goodness and will go towards goodness.'\""],[19687,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: 'O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.'"],[19688,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me, and Fatimah came to him with a dish. He put it in front of him and said to me, \"Pray for your husband and your sons.\" So I prayed for them and they ate, and underneath them was a Khaibari blanket. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gathered the blanket around them and said, \"These are the people of my household, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly.\""],[19689,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite this verse: 'Indeed, he did a deed other than righteous.'"],[19690,"The Prophet ﷺ recited this variant reading: 'Indeed, he did a deed other than righteous.'"],[19691,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he recited, “He did a deed other than righteous.”"],[19692,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say often: “O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.” She said: I said, “O Messenger of Allah, do hearts indeed turn?” He said: “Yes. Allah has not created any human among the children of Adam except that his heart is between two of Allah's fingers. If He wills, He keeps it upright; if He wills, He causes it to deviate. So we ask Allah, our Lord, not to deviate our hearts after He has guided us, and we ask Him to grant us mercy from Himself; indeed He is the Bestower.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, teach me a supplication to make for myself.” He said: “Say: O Allah, forgive me my sin, remove the rage of my heart, and protect me from misleading trials.”"],[19693,"She said: “They killed him, may Allah kill them. They dishonored him, may Allah curse them. For I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Fāṭimah ؓ came to him.” Then she mentioned the hadith."],[19694,"ʿAbdullāh b. ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ sent him to Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, to ask her whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss while fasting. If she said no, then tell her that ʿĀʾishah narrates that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss while fasting. Abū Qays said: I came to her and she said, “Free or slave?” I said, “Slave.” She said, “Come near.” I drew near and said, “ʿAbdullāh b. ʿAmr sent me to you to ask whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss while fasting.” She said, “No.” I said, “ʿĀʾishah narrates that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss while fasting.” She said, “Perhaps he was unable to control himself out of love for her.”"],[19695,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever of you performs Hajj, let him pronounce talbiyah for both of them together—a Hajj and an ʿUmrah.”"],[19696,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “They distracted us from the middle prayer, the ʿAṣr prayer. May Allah fill their bellies and their graves with fire.”"],[19697,"Umm Sulaym entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, is a woman required to perform ghusl if she experiences a wet dream?” He said, “Yes, if she sees the fluid.”"],[19698,"Umm Salamah said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “Is there any reward for me in [caring for] the children of Abu Salamah, since I spend on them, and I am not [merely] a partner with them?” He said, “Yes, you have the reward of what you spend on them.”"],[19699,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I had a eunuch with me, and he heard him saying to Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah, \"O Abdullah, if Allah grants you victory over Ta'if tomorrow, then you should marry the daughter of Ghaylan, for she accepts four (sexual intercourses) and menstruates for eight days.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"These people should not enter upon you.\""],[19700,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I am only a human being, and you bring disputes to me. Perhaps one of you is more eloquent in his argument than another, and I judge in his favor according to what I hear. So if I award someone something from the right of his brother, he should not take it, for I am only cutting off for him a piece of the Fire.”"],[19701,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded her to join him on the Day of Sacrifice in Makkah."],[19702,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a slave girl with a mark on her face and said, “Seek ruqyah for her, for she has been affected by the evil eye.”"],[19703,"Umm Sulaym entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, is a woman required to perform ghusl if she experiences a wet dream?” He said, “Yes, if she sees the fluid.”"],[19704,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I am only a human being, and you bring disputes to me. Perhaps one of you is more eloquent in his argument than another, and I judge in his favor according to what I hear. So if I award someone something from the right of his brother, he should not take it, for I am only cutting off for him a piece of the Fire.”"],[19705,"I complained to the Prophet ﷺ that I was ill. He said, “Perform tawaf behind the people while riding.” She said, “So I performed tawaf while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying with the people beside the House, reciting ‘By the Mount and a written book.’”"],[19706,"I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I fell ill before performing tawaf around the House. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Ride and perform tawaf while riding behind the people.” At that time he was praying toward the side of the House."],[19707,"She said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed while he was fasting.”"],[19708,"She and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ghusl from one vessel for janabah."],[19709,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to kiss while fasting."],[19710,"The Messenger of God ﷺ and she used to perform ghusl from a single vessel."],[19711,"The Messenger of God ﷺ and she used to perform ghusl from a single vessel."],[19712,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us, they said: Mālik b. Anas narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Bakr, from Ḥumayd b. Nāfiʿ, that Zaynab bt. Abī Salamah informed him, saying: I heard Umm Salamah say: A woman came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, my daughter's husband has died, and she has sore eyes; may I apply kohl to her? He said: \"No\" twice or three times, each time saying \"No.\" Then he said: \"It is only four months and ten [days]. One of you used to throw a dung pellet at the head of the year [to end her mourning].\""],[19713,"A woman whose husband died complained of her eye, so they came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked his permission for kohl, and mentioned that they feared for her eye. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"One of you used to stay in her house for a year. When a year had passed, she would throw a dung pellet. Is it not [now only] four months and ten [days]?\""],[19714,"The daughter of Nuʿaym b. ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAdawī came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My daughter's husband has died; she was married to al-Mughīrah al-Makhzūmī. She is observing ʿiddah and complaining of her eyes; may she apply kohl? He said: \"No.\" Then she was silent for a while, then said: She complains of her eyes more than we think; may she apply kohl? He said: \"No.\" Then he said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim woman to mourn more than three days except for a husband, [for whom it is] four months and ten [days].\""],[19715,"\"My bed was opposite the prayer place of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[19716,"\"My bed was opposite the prayer place of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[19717,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray on a khumrah."],[19718,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray on a straw mat."],[19719,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"He ate a shoulder, then prayed and did not perform wudu.\""],[19720,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to supplicate and say: 'O God, You are the First, so there is nothing before You, and You are the Last, so there is nothing after You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of every creature whose forelock is in Your hand, and I seek refuge in You from sin, laziness, the punishment of the Fire, the punishment of the grave, the trial of wealth, the trial of poverty, and I seek refuge in You from wrongdoing and debt. O God, purify my heart from wrongdoing as the white garment is purified from filth, and distance between me and my errors as You have distanced between the East and the West.'"],[19721,"From her mother, Umm Kulthum bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ consummated marriage with me, he said: 'O Umm Salamah, I have sent the Negus a gift of musk and a fine garment, and I think he has died, and I think my gift will be returned to me.' She said: It was as the Messenger of God ﷺ said, so he gave his wives an uqiyah each, and he gave me the rest of the musk and the garment."],[19722,"She said: When Abu Salamah died, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was with him, I got up intending to weep over him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: 'What are you about to do?' I said: 'O Messenger of God, I will weep for Abu Salamah.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Do not do that, for the family of the deceased has, at the death of their deceased, what they supplicate for him.'"],[19723,"She said: 'O Messenger of God, shall I weep over Abu Salamah?' He said: 'Do not do that, for the family of the deceased has, at the death of their deceased, what they supplicate for him.'"],[19724,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'What are you about to do?' I said: 'O Messenger of God, Abu Salamah—I will weep over him.' He said: 'Do not do that, for the family of the deceased has, at the death of their deceased, what they supplicate for him.'"],[19725,"That her grandmother, Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, handed her a brass basin and said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ used to bathe in it.' Talhah said: It held about a sa' or less."],[19726,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he said the salam, would remain briefly."],[19727,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he said the salam, would remain in his place for a short while."],[19728,"The Prophet ﷺ one night looked at the sky and said: 'Glory be to God! What trials have been sent down tonight, or what treasures have been opened? Wake the women of the chambers, for many a woman clothed in this world will be naked on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[19729,"Some women used to attend the dawn prayer with the Prophet ﷺ, and they would leave wrapped in their cloaks, not being recognized from the darkness."],[19730,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said one night: 'Glory be to God! What trials have been sent down? What treasures have been opened? Wake the women of the chambers, for many a woman clothed in this world will be naked on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[19731,"The Messenger of God ﷺ woke up one night saying: \"There is no god but God. What treasures have been opened tonight? There is no god but God. What trials have been sent down tonight? Who will wake up the women in the chambers? For many a woman is clothed in this world yet naked in the Hereafter.\""],[19732,"\"That they should approach women from behind in their private parts and they disliked that, so they went to Umm Salamah and mentioned that to her. She asked the Prophet ﷺ, who then said: 'Your women are like fields for you, so approach your fields however you like.'\""],[19733,"This verse was revealed: 'God only desires to remove impurity from you, O People of the House' while I was in my house. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ called al-Hasan and al-Husayn and seated one of them on his right thigh and the other on his left thigh, and Fāṭimah threw a cloak over them. When it was revealed: 'God only desires to remove impurity from you, O People of the House,' I said: 'Am I with you, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'You are with us.'"],[19734,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about women's trailing garments, and he said: 'A handspan.' I said: 'Then their feet will show.' He said: 'Then a forearm's length.'"],[19735,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever drinks from a vessel of gold or silver only makes the fire of Hell gurgle in his belly.\""],[19736,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn for any deceased person more than three days, except for her husband.\""],[19737,"On the authority of Umm Salamah and ʿĀʾishah that they both heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn for any deceased person more than three days, except for her husband.\""],[19738,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik, from Muḥammad b. ʿUmārah b. Ḥazm, from Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. al-Ḥārith al-Taymī, from a female slave of Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf, that she asked Umm Salamah: 'I am a woman who lets her garment trail and walks in a dirty place.' Umm Salamah said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"What comes after it purifies it.\"'"],[19739,"We had a sheep that we used to milk, and the Messenger of God ﷺ missed it and said: 'What happened to your sheep?' They said: 'It died.' He said: 'What did you do with its hide?' They said: 'O Messenger of God, we threw it away.' He said: 'Why did you not make use of it? For its tanning is its purification; it becomes lawful just as vinegar becomes lawful from wine.'"],[19740,"The Prophet ﷺ was in the chamber of Umm Salamah when her son 'Umar, or 'Abdullah, passed in front of him. He gestured with his hand like this, so he went back. Then Zaynab passed, and he gestured with his hand like this, but she continued on. He said: \"They [women] prevail.\""],[19741,"The Prophet ﷺ said regarding 'Ammar, \"He will be killed by a rebellious group.\""],[19742,"The prophet said about Ammar, \"He will be killed by the rebellious group.\""],[19743,"I have not forgotten on the Day of the Trench a trace on his chest as he was handing them the milk and saying: \"O Allah, the true good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirun.\" When he saw him—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—he said: \"O Ibn Sumayyah, the transgressing party will kill you.\""],[19744,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The transgressing party will kill 'Ammar.\""],[19745,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The transgressing party will kill 'Ammar.\""],[19746,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The transgressing party will kill 'Ammar.\""],[19747,"It was narrated from Umm Salamah that the Prophet ﷺ used to pray two short Rak’ah after Witr, sitting down. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1195)"],[19748,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray two rak'ahs after his Witr while sitting."],[19749,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up from his sleep saying 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we shall return.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the matter with you?' He said: 'A group of my Ummah will be swallowed up by the earth. They will be sent to a man who will come to Makkah, but he will be prevented, and they will be swallowed up at a single place of destruction while their origins differ. Among them will be one who is reluctant and will come against his will.'"],[19750,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: 'Indeed We have granted you al-Kawthar.'"],[19751,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform wudu with one mudd and take a bath with one sa'."],[19752,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked the blood surah three times, then he would have intercourse after the three."],[19753,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say often: 'O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, how often you supplicate with this supplication!' He said: 'O Umm Salamah, indeed the heart of the son of Adam is between two fingers of the fingers of the Lord of the worlds; if He wills, He makes it upright, and if He wills, He causes it to deviate.'"],[19754,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The urine of a boy is to be sprinkled, and the urine of a girl is to be washed.\""],[19755,"\"I used to rub the semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[19756,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I used to bathe from a single vessel.\" I would say to him, \"Leave some for me, leave some for me.\""],[19757,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"In every unit of prayer there is a tashahhud and a greeting upon the messengers and upon the righteous servants of Allah who followed them.\""],[19758,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me about Allah's saying: {Hūr ʿīn}.\" He said: \"Hūr: white ones; ʿīn: wide-eyed. Their whiteness is like the inner side of a vulture's wing.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me about His saying: {as though they were hidden pearls}.\" He said: \"Their purity is like the purity of pearls inside shells, untouched by hands.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me about His saying: {in them are good and beautiful ones}.\" He said: \"Good in character, beautiful in faces.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me about His saying: {as though they were hidden eggs}.\" He said: \"Their delicacy is like the delicacy of the membrane you have seen inside the egg, next to the shell, which is the outer layer.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me about His saying: {loving, equal in age}.\" He said: \"They are those who were taken in this world as old, sun-darkened, white-haired women. After old age, Allah created them anew and made them virgins, loving, affectionate, beloved, equal in age, born at the same time.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, are the women of this world better or the hūr al-ʿīn?\" He said: \"The women of this world are better than the hūr al-ʿīn, like the outer garment is better than the lining.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, and why is that?\" He said: \"Because of their prayers, their fasting, and their worship of Allah. Allah clothes their faces with light and their bodies with silk. They are white in color, green in garments, yellow in jewelry. Their censers are pearls and their combs are gold. They say: 'We are the immortal ones, never dying. We are the blissful ones, never distressed. We are the residents, never departing. We are the content ones, never discontented. Glad tidings to the one for whom we are and who is for us.'\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, a woman among us marries two, three, or four husbands, then dies and enters Paradise, and they enter with her. Who will be her husband?\" He said: \"O Umm Salamah, she will be given a choice, and she will choose the one who had the best character. She will say: 'O Lord, this one had the best character with me in this world, so marry me to him.' O Umm Salamah, good character takes away the good of this world and the Hereafter.\""],[19759,"The Prophet ﷺ instructed Fāṭimah to extend her garment by a handspan."],[19760,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do good deeds and do not rely solely on my intercession, for my intercession is for the sinners among my Ummah.\""],[19761,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The transgressing faction will kill ʿAmmār.\""],[19762,"A group of rebels would kill you. (Using translation from Muslim 2916a)"],[19763,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Whoever says in the morning: 'Praise be to Allah, before whose greatness all things humble themselves,' ten good deeds are recorded for him.\""],[19764,"When the Prophet ﷺ went out to prayer, he would say: \"O Allah, make me the closest of those who draw near to You, the most directed of those who turn to You, and the most persistent of those who ask You.\""],[19765,"\"Women used to sit after childbirth for forty nights in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we would pray with wars (a yellow dye) on our faces due to skin discoloration.\""],[19766,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mixing dates with raisins and cooking the mango."],[19767,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to the mosque and called out at the top of his voice: Verily, this mosque is not permissible for anyone in a state of major ritual impurity or a menstruating woman, except for the Prophet, his wives, Fatimah daughter of Muhammad, and Ali. Behold, I have made it clear to you lest you go astray."],[19768,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Any woman who dies while her husband is pleased with her will enter Paradise."],[19769,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: A believer does not hate Ali, and a hypocrite does not love him."],[19770,"By the One by whom Umm Salamah swears, the closest of people to the Messenger of God ﷺ was Ali. We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the house of Aishah, and I was the last to leave the house. Then we sat down closer to the door, and Ali leaned over him. He was the last of the people to have a private conversation with him, whispering to him and confiding in him."],[19771,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no swearing of oaths in Islam, and whatever oaths were made in the pre-Islamic era, Islam has only increased them in severity.\""],[19772,"The Prophet ﷺ called a servant girl of his, and she was slow to come to him. He said: Were it not for the fear of retaliation on the Day of Resurrection, I would have hurt you with this siwak."],[19773,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The one who will be compassionate toward you after me is the truthful and dutiful one. O Allah, give Ibn Awf to drink from Salsabil of Paradise.”"],[19774,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say during his illness in which he passed away, \"Prayer and what your right hands possess.\" He continued to say it until his tongue could no longer utter it."],[19775,"Safinah, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that Umm Salamah informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Angels do not accompany a group that has a bell in it.”"],[19776,"The Prophet ﷺ heard the clamor of a dispute at the door of Umm Salamah, so he went out to them and said, “You bring disputes to me, but I am only a human being. Perhaps one of you is more eloquent in presenting his argument than another, so I rule in his favor according to what I hear and what I think is truthful. Whoever I rule in favor of with something from his brother's right, it is a piece of the Fire; let him take it or leave it.”"],[19777,"“O Messenger of Allah, do you have any interest in my sister, the daughter of Abu Sufyan?” He said, “No, she is not lawful for me.” She said, “I have heard that you are proposing to Durrah bint Abi Salamah.” He said, “The daughter of Umm Salamah? By Allah, even if she were not my stepdaughter in my care, she would not be lawful for me. She is the daughter of my brother through suckling; Thuwaybah suckled me and her. So do not offer me your sisters or daughters.”"],[19778,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You bring disputes, but I am only a human being. Perhaps one of you is more eloquent in presenting his argument than another. I only judge between you based on what I hear from you. Whoever I judge in favor of with something from his brother's right, let him not take it, for I am only cutting off for him a piece of the Fire of Hell, which he will bring on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[19779,"Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said, “If she sees the fluid, let her perform ghusl.” I said to her, “You have shamed the women! Does a woman have wet dreams?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “May your right hand be dusty! How else would her child resemble her?”"],[19780,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her and heard an effeminate man saying to Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah, “If Allah opens al-Ta’if tomorrow, I will guide you to a woman who comes forward with four and turns back with eight.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Expel them from your homes.”"],[19781,"She said, “O Messenger of Allah, the children of Abu Salamah are in my care and they have nothing except what I spend on them. Do I have a reward if I spend on them?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Spend on them, and you will have the reward for what you spend on them.”"],[19782,"«While I was lying down with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the velvet cloth, I began to menstruate.» She said: She and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were in the velvet cloth."],[19783,"She used to take a bath along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from a single vessel for major ritual impurity."],[19784,"«That she and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ghusl from a single vessel from janabah.»"],[19785,"Then I met her servant Nafi, and he sent him to her, and he asked her, then he returned to him and informed him that she narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to «enter the morning in a state of janabah from sexual intercourse, not from a wet dream, then he would enter the morning fasting.»"],[19786,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about women? He said: «They should let down a span.» I said: Then they will be uncovered. He said: «Then a forearm's length, not more than that.»"],[19787,"A woman asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I suffer from istihadah and I do not become pure; should I abandon the prayer? He said: «No, but leave the number of days and nights that you used to menstruate, and their measure from the month, then perform ghusl, and tie a cloth, and pray.»"],[19788,"That a woman used to have profuse bleeding during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Umm Salamah sought a ruling for her from the Prophet ﷺ about that. He said: «Let her look at the number of nights and days that she used to menstruate, and their measure, and leave the prayer; then when that is completed, let her perform ghusl and tie a cloth and pray.»"],[19789,"That a woman used to have profuse bleeding during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Umm Salamah sought a ruling for her from the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: «Let her look at the number of days and nights that she used to menstruate before what occurred to her, and their measure from the month; so she should leave the prayer for that. Then when that is completed and prayer time comes, let her perform ghusl and pray.»"],[19790,"The Prophet ﷺ used to «enter the morning in a state of janabah without a wet dream, then perform ghusl and continue his fast.»"],[19791,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever is planning to perform the Hajj and has an animal for sacrifice, should refrain from cutting his hair and nails.\""],[19792,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Indeed, the one who eats or drinks in vessels of silver and gold is only gulping down the fire of Jahannam into his belly.»"],[19793,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever drinks from a silver vessel is only gulping into his belly the fire of Hell, unless he repents.”"],[19794,"Mu'awiyah sent for Umm Salamah, so she went with the messenger. He asked Umm Salamah, and she said: “The Prophet ﷺ forbade them—meaning the two rak'ahs after 'Asr. The Prophet ﷺ was in my house performing wudu' for Zuhr, and he had sent out a zakat collector. The Muhajirun were with him, and their situation was preoccupying him, when someone knocked at the door. He went out and prayed Zuhr, then came back and distributed what had been brought. He remained occupied like that until he prayed 'Asr, then entered his home and prayed two rak'ahs, after which he said, 'The matter of the zakat collector kept me busy from praying them after Zuhr, so I prayed them after 'Asr.'”"],[19795,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A man will be pledged allegiance between the pillar and the Maqam with the number of the people of Badr. Then, the hordes of the people of Iraq and the replacements from Syria will come to him, and an army from Sham will attack them. They will continue fighting until they reach an open area where they will be swallowed up by the earth. Then, a man from Quraysh, his paternal uncles will be dogs, will come to them and they will be defeated by Allah.\" It was said that the one who fails in the share of the booty of a dog is called 'al-kha'ib.'"],[19796,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There will be disputes upon the death of a caliph, and a man from the Banu Hashim tribe will come out from Madinah to Mecca. People will come to him and pledge allegiance to him between the corner and the Maqam (in Mecca), although he will not be willing. He will prepare an army from Sham (Greater Syria) until they reach the open desert, where they will be swallowed by the earth. Then, the battalions of the people of Iraq and the replacements from Sham will come to him, and a man from Sham will gather his relatives. He will prepare an army against them, but Allah will defeat them, and the circle (of power) will be around them. This will be the Day of Kalb (the tribe). Those who fail from the spoils of war of Kalb will be disappointed, and he will unearth treasures and distribute wealth. Islam will be thrown down by him to the ground and live like that for seven or six years.\" Ubaidullah said: \"So, I reported it to Laith, and he said: Mujaheed narrated it to me.\""],[19797,"“O Messenger of God, Hisham b. al-Mughirah used to feed people, host guests, maintain ties of kinship, and free captives. If he had lived until your time he would have embraced Islam. Is there any reward for him in that?” He said: “He was your paternal uncle; he used to give for the sake of this world, its renown, and its adornment, and he never once said, ‘Forgive me on the Day of Judgment.’”"],[19798,"“One of us would menstruate while she had only a single garment, yet today one of us can spare her servant to wash her clothes and purify them.”"],[19799,"Umm Salamah was asked whether a woman should cover her face while in ihram. She said: “Riders used to pass by us while we were with the Prophet ﷺ, and one of us would let her cloth hang down over her face.”"],[19800,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ and I used to bathe from a single vessel, each of us taking water separately.”"],[19801,"The Prophet ﷺ was with her one day in her house when a servant came and said: “Ali and Fatimah are at the door.” He said: “Move aside for me, away from my household.” So I moved to a corner of the house. Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn—two small boys—came in. He took Hasan and Husayn and placed them in his lap, took Ali with one hand and drew him close, and covered them with a black velvet cloth. Then he said: “O God, to You, not to the Fire—I and my household.” She said: I called out to him, saying, “And me, O Messenger of God?” He said: “And you.”"],[19802,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When you attend a sick person or a deceased person, say good, for the angels say ‘Amin’ to what you say.” She said: When Abu Salamah died, I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, Abu Salamah has died.” He said: “Say: O God, forgive me and him, and grant me a good successor after him.” I did so, and God gave me as a successor one better than him: Muhammad ﷺ."],[19803,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite: {“Yes, My verses came to you, but you denied them and were arrogant.”}"],[19804,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever lacks even one of three qualities should not count on any of his deeds: God-consciousness that restrains him from disobeying Allah, or forbearance with which he restrains a fool, or good character with which he lives among people.”"],[19805,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was weeping over Abu Salamah. He said: “Shall I guide you to something better than what you are saying? Say the words of recall and say: ‘O Allah, grant me a good outcome, mend my affliction, and replace him for me with one better than him.’” So I returned and said what he had told me, then I began to say: “And where will I find one like Abu Salamah?” She said: “And Allah replaced him for me with one better than Abu Salamah—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[19806,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “No person revives land, and from it a thirsty liver drinks or a healthy creature benefits, except that Allah writes for him a reward for it.”"],[19807,"He informed him that Umm Salamah, the Prophet’s wife, informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit his wives every morning and greet them. One of them had honey, and whenever he visited her she would bring him some of it, so he would stay with her for that reason. Aisha and Hafsah were troubled by that, and when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited them, they said: “We smell the scent of maghafir from you.” So he gave up that honey."],[19808,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"May Allah curse the one who takes a bribe and the one who gives it in a judgment.\""],[19809,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and said: “Why do I see you looking disheveled?” I said: “I drank a medicine to purge myself.” He said: “And what is it?” I said: “Shubrum.” He said: “What do you have to do with shubrum? It is hot like fire. Use senna and sanut, for in them is a cure for everything except death.”"],[19810,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “If one of you has a mukatab and he has what he can pay, let her veil herself from him.”"],[19811,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “There is no servant who is afflicted by a calamity…” the hadith, and it is in the Book of Death."],[19812,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “There is no servant who is afflicted by a calamity…” the hadith."],[19813,"The Prophet of God ﷺ went to her house and prayed two rak'ahs in it after 'Asr. 'A'ishah sent to Umm Salamah, “What is this prayer that the Prophet ﷺ prayed in your house?” She said, “The Prophet ﷺ used to pray two rak'ahs after Zuhr. The delegation of Banu al-Mustaliq came to him concerning what their governor al-Walid b. 'Uqbah had done to them. They kept making excuses to the Prophet ﷺ until the mu'adhdhin came to call him to 'Asr prayer. He prayed the obligatory prayer, then prayed those two rak'ahs with me in my house, which he did not pray before or after.”"],[19814,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had sent to them [an agent] to collect the zakah on their wealth. When they heard of him, a mounted group of them set out and said, “We will travel with the messenger of the Messenger of God ﷺ and carry him.” When he heard of that, he thought they were coming to him to kill him, so he returned and said, “Banu al-Mustaliq have withheld their zakah, O Messenger of God.” The people came until they arrived in Madinah, then they stood in rows behind the Messenger of God ﷺ in prayer. When he finished the prayer, they departed and said, “We seek refuge in God from the anger of God and the anger of His Messenger. We heard, O Messenger of God, of your messenger whom you sent to collect the zakah on our wealth, and we were pleased with that and our eyes were comforted by it. We wanted to meet him and travel with the messenger of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then we heard that he had returned, so we feared that what turned him back was anger from God and His Messenger.” They kept making excuses to the Prophet ﷺ until this verse was revealed."],[19815,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Angels do not accompany a group that has a bell.”"],[19816,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Any woman who takes off her clothes in other than her husband's house, God will tear apart His veil from her.”"],[19817,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding a menstruating woman: she washes what has affected her garment and does not wash the entire garment."],[19818,"I wore a necklace containing hairs of gold. The Prophet ﷺ saw me and disliked it, so he turned away from me. I removed it, and he said, “What assures you that God will not make you wear hairs of fire in its place on the Day of Resurrection?”"],[19819,"The Prophet ﷺ entered while I was wearing hairs of gold. He turned away from me, so I said, “O Messenger of God, will you not look at my adornment?” He said, “It is from that I turn away.” I cut them off, and he turned his face toward me."],[19820,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The womb is a branch that holds onto the waist of the Most Merciful, pleading for its right. He says: ‘Are you not pleased that I maintain ties with whoever maintains you and cut off whoever cuts you off? Whoever maintains ties with you has maintained ties with Me, and whoever cuts you off has cut Me off.’”"],[19821,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to get up in the morning in a state of major ritual impurity from intercourse, not from a wet dream, and he would not break his fast nor make it up."],[19822,"Al-Harith b. Hisham came to the Prophet ﷺ in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I used to maintain ties of kinship, be kind to the neighbor, shelter the orphan, feed the guest, and feed the poor—and all of this Hisham b. al-Mughirah used to do. What do you think about him, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Every grave whose occupant does not testify that there is no god but Allah is a brand from the Fire. I found my uncle Abu Talib in a deep place of the Fire, and Allah brought him out because of his position with me and his kindness to me, and placed him in a shallow part of the Fire.”"],[19823,"The Prophet ﷺ used to get up in the morning in a state of major ritual impurity without having had a wet dream, then he would get up fasting."],[19824,"Umm Salamah said: “When the Prophet ﷺ proposed to me, I said to him: ‘I have three traits: I am old in age, I am a woman with many children, and I am a woman of intense jealousy.’ The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘As for the children, they belong to Allah and His Messenger; as for jealousy, I will pray to Allah to remove it from you; and as for age, I am older than you.’ So the Prophet ﷺ married her while she was nursing her daughter Zaynab bt. Abi Salamah. The Prophet ﷺ would enter and leave without approaching her, and he would play with her daughter when he entered. Then Ammar b. Yasir entered and said: ‘Where is this daughter of yours who has preoccupied the family of the Prophet ﷺ?’ He took her and sought a wet-nurse for her named Sa'yan. The Prophet ﷺ entered and said: ‘Where is Zunab?’ A woman said: ‘Ammar entered and took her and sought a wet-nurse for her named Sa'yan.’ Then the Prophet ﷺ consummated the marriage with his wife.”"],[19825,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not harm me regarding Aisha, for revelation has not descended upon me under the blanket of any one of you except Aisha.”"],[19826,"She was asked about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she said: “He would pray Isha, then glorify Allah as much as Allah willed, then sleep, then wake up for a period similar to his sleep, then sleep and get up; that was his prayer until the morning.”"],[19827,"The Prophet ﷺ was occupied and missed performing the two units (rak'ahs) before Asr prayer, so he performed them after Asr prayer."],[19828,"The Prophet ﷺ used to be intimate with her while he was fasting."],[19829,"When the Prophet ﷺ wanted to sleep while in a state of major ritual impurity, he would perform ablution as for prayer; and when he wanted to eat, he would wash his hands and then eat."],[19830,"She said to the Prophet ﷺ: “I have not performed the farewell circumambulation of the House.” He said: “When you have prayed, circumambulate from behind the people on your camel.”"],[19831,"Umm Salamah: O Messenger of God, a woman whose husband has died—do you permit kohl? He said, \"One of you used to, when her husband died, take a piece of dung and throw it behind her back, then say: 'I will not apply kohl until this dung is transformed.' But it is only four months and ten days.\""],[19832,"Al-Harith ibn Abi Rabia and Abdullah ibn Safwan entered upon Umm Salama and I was with them. They asked her about the army that would be swallowed up, and this was during the time of Ibn Zubayr. She said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A person will seek refuge by entering the House, then Allah will send a wind, and when they are in an open plain of land, they will be swallowed up.'\" She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will they be swallowed up with those who are reluctant?\" He said, \"They will be swallowed up along with them, but they will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection according to their intentions.\""],[19833,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"An army will raid this House until, when they are at a desert tract of the land, they will be swallowed up.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, what about the one who is compelled?\" He said, \"He will be resurrected according to his intention.\""],[19834,"that you should marry until you complete the waiting period, the longer of the two terms. So she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he said, \"Marry whomever you wish.\""],[19835,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever drinks from vessels made of gold and silver, is actually swallowing fire from the Hellfire.\""],[19836,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say on this pulpit: \"I will precede you to the Kawthar. While I am upon it, you will pass by me in groups, and you will be turned away. I will call out: 'Come, come!' A caller will call out and say: 'They have introduced innovations after you.' So I will say: 'Away with them!'\""],[19837,"that while she was combing her hair, nothing startled her except the Messenger of God ﷺ calling from the pulpit, saying: \"O people, while I was at the Pond, you were brought to me group by group. A group of you went this way and that way. I said, 'What is wrong with them? Come to me.' A crier cried out and said, 'They have changed after you.' So I said, 'Away with them, away with them!'\""],[19838,"She said: O Messenger of Allah, is a woman required to perform ghusl if she sees in her dream that her husband has intercourse with her? He said: “Yes, if she sees the fluid.” Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of Allah, does that happen to a woman? He said: “Yes, may your forehead be covered with dust. From where does the resemblance to maternal uncles come? May you be bereft of your mother! Whichever of the two fluids reaches the womb first will prevail in determining resemblance.”"],[19839,"She said: I know of the largest amount of wealth that came to the Prophet ﷺ until Allah took him. There came to him in the darkness of the night a bag containing eight hundred dirhams and a letter. He sent it to me, and it was my night. Then he returned after the last 'isha prayer and prayed in the room at a prayer place of his, and I had prepared a bed for him and for myself. So I waited. He prolonged the prayer, then went out, then came back, and he kept doing that until the call for the dawn prayer was given. He prayed and then returned and said: “Where is that bag that distracted me last night?” He called for it and distributed it. Then he said: “Woe to you!” I said: O Messenger of Allah, you did something you had not done before. He said: “I was praying, and it was brought to me, so I would leave the prayer to look at it, then return and pray.”"],[19840,"From the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[19841,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw some camels, on one of which was a bell. When he heard its sound, he said: “What is this?” A man said: The julyul. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “And what is the julyul?” He said: The bell. He said: “Yes, go and cut it off and throw it away.” So he did, then the man returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, what does it matter? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The angels do not accompany a group that has a bell with it.”"],[19842,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would wake up in a state of janabah and fast that day."],[19843,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever enters ihram for an 'umrah from Bayt al-Maqdis, it will be forgiven for him.”"],[19844,"When the Prophet ﷺ mentioned what he mentioned about the izār, Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of Allah, what about women? He said: “They should let it down by a handspan.” She said: Then their feet will show. He said: “Then a cubit, and let them not add to that.”"],[19845,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not apply perfume while you are in ihram, and do not touch henna, for it is perfume.”"],[19846,"From a freedwoman of hers whom she sent to Umm Salamah; she said: I heard Umm Salamah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me while I was in my waiting period following the death of Abu Salamah: “Do not comb your hair with perfume or with henna, for it is a dye.” I said: With what should I comb my hair, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “With lote-tree leaves; wrap your head with it.”"],[19847,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me when Abu Salamah had died, and I had put some aloe on my eye. He said: “What is this, O Umm Salamah?” I said: It is only aloe, O Messenger of Allah; there is no perfume in it. He said: “It brightens the face, so apply it at night and remove it during the day.”"],[19848,"I entered upon Umm Salamah while she was praying in a shift and a headcover. I asked her about decorative embroidery on a garment. She said: “We used to wear a garment like this — referring to a garment she had with silk embroidery on it — in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[19849,"“Nothing was dearer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than a shirt.”"],[19850,"“Maymunah bint al-Harith b. Hazn b. Bujayr b. al-Haram b. Ruwaybah b. Abd Allah b. Hilal b. Amir b. Sa'sa'ah — she is the one who gave herself to the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[19851,"“Maymunah entrusted her affair to Umm al-Fadl, and Umm al-Fadl entrusted it to al-Abbas, so he married her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[19852,"“Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, died in the year of al-Harrah, in the year sixty-three.”"],[19853,"“I saw the Mother of the Believers Maymunah shaving her head after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I said to Yazid b. al-Asamm: He said: “I think she was letting herself go.”"],[19854,"She said: I screened the Prophet ﷺ while he performed ghusl from janabah. He began by washing his hands, then poured water with his right hand over his left and washed his private part and whatever had been affected by it. Then he struck his hand on the wall or the ground, then performed wudu as for prayer except for his feet, then poured water over himself, then moved his feet aside and washed them."],[19855,"She said: I brought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ his water for ghusl from janabah. He washed his hand twice or three times, then inserted his hands into the vessel and poured water from them over his private part and washed it with his left hand. Then he struck his left hand on the ground and rubbed it vigorously. Then he performed wudu as for prayer, then poured three handfuls of water over his head, filling his palms, then washed the rest of his body. Then he moved away from that spot and washed his feet. Then I brought him the towel, but he returned it."],[19856,"She said: I placed water for the Prophet ﷺ to perform ghusl from janabah. He tilted the vessel over his right hand and washed it twice or three times, then poured water over his private part and washed it with his left hand. Then he struck his hand on the ground and washed it, then rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, washed his face and hands. Then he poured water over his head and body, then moved aside and washed his feet. Then I handed him the towel, but he did not take it and began shaking the water off his body."],[19857,"The Prophet ﷺ took the bath of Janaba. (sexual relation or wet dream). He first cleaned his private parts with his hand, and then rubbed it (that hand) on the wall (earth) and washed it. Then he performed ablution like that for the prayer, and after the bath he washed his feet. (Using translation from Bukhārī 260)"],[19858,"She said: I placed, or water was placed, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for his ghusl. He poured water with his right hand over his left until he cleaned it, then poured water with his right hand over his private part and washed it with his left and whatever had been affected by it until he cleaned it. Then he wiped his hand on the wall, on the dust, then washed it until he cleaned it. Then he rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, and performed wudu as for prayer. Then he poured water over his head and his body, then moved from his place and washed his feet."],[19859,"Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other except the mosque of the Kaʿbah.”"],[19860,"She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A prayer in it – meaning his mosque – is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the mosque of the Kaʿbah.”"],[19861,"She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I both became junub, so I performed ghusl from a large basin, and some water remained from my washing. The Prophet ﷺ came and performed ghusl from it. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, it is leftover from my washing.” He said, “Water does not become junub.”"],[19862,"She said: “I used to perform ghusl, I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from a single vessel.”"],[19863,"Maymuna said: “I used to perform ghusl, I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from a single vessel.”"],[19864,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to “perform ghusl with water leftover from Maymuna’s ghusl.”"],[19865,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Why did you not tan its hide?”"],[19866,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Why did you not tan it and make use of it?” They said, “It is carrion.” He said, “Tanning the hide is its purification.”"],[19867,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep belonging to a freed slave woman of ours, which had been given to her as charity. He said, “What is wrong with the people of this [sheep] that they did not take its hide, tan it, and benefit from it?” They said, “O Messenger of God, it is dead.” He said, “Only its eating is forbidden.” It was said to Sufyan that Maʿmar does not say “and tan it” in it, and says that al-Zuhri rejected tanning. Sufyan said, “But I memorized it, and we only wanted from him this phrase that others transmitted: ‘Only its eating is forbidden.’” Sufyan sometimes did not mention Maymuna in it, but when he was asked about it, he said Maymuna in it."],[19868,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us: Sufyan b. ʿUyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUtba, from Ibn ʿAbbas, from Maymuna, that the Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said, “Why did they not remove its hide, tan it, and benefit from it?” They said, “It is dead.” He said, “Only its eating is forbidden.”"],[19869,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a dead sheep belonging to a freed slave woman of Maymuna and said, “Why did you not make use of its hide?” They said, “How, when it is dead, O Messenger of God?” He said, “Only its meat is forbidden.”"],[19870,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said, “Why did you not benefit from its skin?” They said, “O Messenger of God, it is dead.” He said, “Only its eating is forbidden.”"],[19871,"A sheep died and the Prophet ﷺ was asked about it. He said, “Only its meat is forbidden to you, and its hide is permitted for you.”"],[19872,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said, “Were the people of this [sheep] unable to benefit from its hide?”"],[19873,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a mouse that fell into clarified butter. He said, “Take it and what is around it and throw it away, and eat your clarified butter.”"],[19874,"A mouse fell into clarified butter and died. The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked, and he said, “Throw it away and what is around it, and eat it.” Al-Humaydi said: It was said to Sufyan that Maʿmar narrates it from al-Zuhri, from Saʿid, from Abu Hurayra. Sufyan said, “I never heard al-Zuhri narrate it except from ʿUbayd Allah, from Ibn ʿAbbas, from Maymuna, from the Prophet ﷺ. I heard it from him many times.”"],[19875,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a mouse that fell into clarified butter, and he said, “Throw it away and what is around it, and eat it.”"],[19876,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a mouse falling into clarified butter. He said, “If it is solid, throw it away and what is around it; if it is liquid, do not approach it.”"],[19877,"Maymuna said: The Messenger of God ﷺ woke up one morning in low spirits and spent the evening likewise. I said, “O Messenger of God, why do I see you in low spirits?” He said, “Gabriel promised me he would come to me, and he has never broken his promise to me.” They looked, and there was a puppy under a wooden couch of theirs. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered that puppy to be taken out, and ordered that place to be washed with water. Then Gabriel came, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “You promised me you would come to me, and you have never broken your promise to me.” He said, “Did you not know that we do not enter a house containing a dog or an image?”"],[19878,"Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ woke up one day gloomy. Maymuna said: I said, “O Messenger of God, I have found your appearance strange today.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Gabriel had promised me he would meet me tonight, but he did not meet me. By God, he has not broken his promise to me.” She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ remained so all that day. Then a puppy came to his mind under a mat of ours. He ordered it to be taken out, then he took some water in his hand and sprinkled it on its place. When evening came, Gabriel met him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “You had promised me you would meet me last night.” He said, “Yes, but we do not enter a house containing a dog or an image.” That morning the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered the killing of dogs, even ordering the killing of the big dog of the large orchard, while leaving the dog of the small orchard."],[19879,"A year of famine struck the people, and the Bedouins would come to Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ would order a man to take another man by the hand and host him and give him supper. One night a Bedouin came, and the Messenger of God ﷺ had some food and a little milk. The Bedouin ate it and left nothing for the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then he brought him one or two more nights, and he kept eating it all. So I said, \"O Messenger of God, O God, do not bless this Bedouin; he eats the food of the Messenger of God ﷺ and leaves him nothing.\" Then he brought him one night, and he ate only a little of the food and drank only a little of the milk. I said to the Messenger of God ﷺ, \"That's it.\" Then he brought him one night after he had embraced Islam, and he said, \"The disbeliever eats with seven intestines, while the believer eats with one intestine.\""],[19880,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married her while she was ritually permitted (not in ihram)."],[19881,"From one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, Maymunah — and he was her brother through breastfeeding — from the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There is no Muslim over whom a community prays [the funeral prayer] except that they are granted intercession for him.” Abu al-Malih used to say: “The community is forty or more.”"],[19882,"The Prophet ﷺ ate a shoulder at her place, then prayed without performing wudu’."],[19883,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never left my house without raising his gaze to the sky and saying: 'O Allah, I seek refuge with You from going astray or being led astray, from slipping or being made to slip, from acting ignorantly or being treated ignorantly, and from wronging or being wronged.'"],[19884,"She asked: 'Where is the man from?' I said: 'From the people of Iraq.' She asked: 'From which people of Iraq?' I said: 'From the people of Kufa.' She asked: 'From which people of Kufa?' I said: 'From Banu Amir.' She then said: 'Welcome, near you are on nearness, and spacious you are on spaciousness. So what has brought you?' I said: 'There occurred between Ali, Talhah, and al-Zubayr what occurred, so I came and pledged allegiance to Ali.' She said: 'Then join him, for by Allah, he has not gone astray nor been led astray.' She repeated that three times."],[19885,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The believer eats in one intestine, while the disbeliever eats in seven intestines.'"],[19886,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said one day: 'What will you be when religion is corrupted, blood is shed, adornment becomes widespread, buildings are raised high, two brothers differ, and the Ancient House (the Kaaba) is burned?'"],[19887,"One day the Messenger of God ﷺ came out looking dejected. I said, \"Why do I see you dejected?\" He said, \"Gabriel promised me, and he has not broken his promise.\" He remained like that all day and night. I had a dog under a bed of ours, so he ordered it removed. Then he took some water in his hand and sprinkled it in its place. Then Gabriel came and said, \"We do not enter a house where there is an image or a dog.\" She said: He would be spoken to about the small dog of the orchard, but he never permitted it."],[19888,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"Whoever takes on a debt intending to repay it, God will settle it for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[19889,"Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, took on a debt of eight hundred dirhams. It was said to her, \"Will you take a debt when you have nothing to repay it with?\" She said, \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Whoever takes on a debt while being determined to repay it, God will help him repay it.'\""],[19890,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stayed overnight at her house on her night. Then he got up to perform ablution for prayer. She heard him saying during his ablution, \"Labbayk, labbayk, labbayk,\" three times, and \"I have been helped, I have been helped,\" three times. She said: When he came out, I said, \"O Messenger of God, may my father be sacrificed for you, I heard you say during your ablution, 'Labbayk, labbayk,' three times, and 'I have been helped, I have been helped,' three times, as if you were speaking to someone. Was anyone with you?\" He said, \"This is the rajiz poet of Banu Ka'b, seeking my help, claiming that Quraysh aided Banu Bakr against them.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ went out and ordered Aisha to prepare his equipment without informing anyone. She said: Her father entered upon her and said, \"My dear daughter, what is this equipment?\" She said, \"By God, I do not know.\" He said, \"This is not the season for raiding Banu al-Asfar. Where does the Messenger of God ﷺ intend to go?\" She said, \"I have no knowledge.\" She said: We stayed for three days. Then he prayed the dawn prayer with the people, and I heard the rajiz poet reciting his verses to him."],[19891,"From Maymuna bint al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ prostrated, he would keep his arms away from his sides so that his back was visible, and he would open his armpits."],[19892,"When the Prophet ﷺ prostrated, if a small animal had wanted to pass beneath him, it could have passed, because of the gap he left."],[19893,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ prostrated, he kept his arms away from his sides, so much so that if a small animal wanted to pass under his hands, it would pass."],[19894,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ prostrated, he kept his arms away from his sides until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen, leaning on his right side and relaxing his left."],[19895,"A dabb lizard was gifted to Maymuna. Two men from her people came to her, so she ordered it to be prepared and served it to them. Then the Prophet of God ﷺ came while they were eating. He welcomed them, then he took some food to eat. When he brought a morsel to his mouth, he said, \"What is this?\" They said, \"A dabb lizard that was gifted to us.\" She said: He put down the morsel, and the two men wanted to throw away what was in their mouths, but the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Do not do that. You are people of Najd and you eat it, but we are people of Tihamah and we find it repulsive.\""],[19896,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ married me at Sarif while we were both ritually permitted (not in ihram).\""],[19897,"Maymunah said to me: “O son of my brother, come, let me recite a ruqyah over you with the ruqyah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” She said: “In the name of Allah I recite over you, and Allah heals you from every disease in you. Remove the affliction, O Lord of the people; heal, for there is no healer but You.”"],[19898,"From al-Hilaliyyah, she who was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that she had a black slave girl and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I want to free this one.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Will you not ransom with her your brother's daughter or your sister's daughter from tending sheep?”"],[19899,"From Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, from the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Do not make nabidh in the muzaffat or in the naqir.”"],[19900,"From Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, from the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Do not make nabidh in the muzaffat or in the naqir.”"],[19901,"Narrated Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , she said, \"My sister, Umm Hufaidh, gifted me with a dish of meat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his dinner and Khalid bin Al-Walid was with him, who is her nephew. She presented the dish of meat to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ leaned towards it, thinking it was chickens. So, I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you know what this is?' He replied, 'No.' Then, he took his hand off it. So, I said, 'This is lizard meat.' He said, 'That is the food of the people of the desert.' Khalid asked, 'Is it Haram (forbidden)?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'No.' Then, Khalid ate from it, with the Prophet ﷺ looking on.\""],[19902,"From the Prophet ﷺ, likewise."],[19903,"I freed a slave girl of mine, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and I told him of her manumission. He said: “May Allah reward you. But if you had given her to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater in reward for you.”"],[19904,"She freed a slave girl of hers without asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When it was her day on which he would come to her, she said: “Are you aware, O Messenger of Allah, that I have freed my slave girl so-and-so?” He said: “Have you done so?” She said: “Yes.” He said: “Indeed, if you had given her to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater in reward for you.”"],[19905,"I said: “I perform witr with three [rak‘ahs], then go out to the prayer fearing that I might miss it.” He said: “It is not valid except with five or seven.” I informed Mujahid and Yahya b. al-Jazzar of his statement, and they said to me: “Did you not ask him from whom?” [He said:] “So I asked him, and he said: ‘From the trustworthy one, from Maymunah and ‘A’ishah, from the Prophet ﷺ.’”"],[19906,"Maymunah bint al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to me, saying: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while I was opposite him, and I was menstruating; and sometimes his garment would touch me when he prostrated.”"],[19907,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while I was opposite him, and I was menstruating; and sometimes his garment would touch me when he prostrated."],[19908,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to have intimate contact with his wives while they were menstruating, instructing them to wear a waist-wrapper."],[19909,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray on the khumrah (small mat)."],[19910,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray on the khumrah."],[19911,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray on the khumrah that had been spread for him in the mosque."],[19912,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray on the khumrah."],[19913,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to have intimate contact with any of his wives while she was menstruating, he would order her to wear a waist-wrapper and then have contact with her."],[19914,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray wearing a woolen cloak, part of it on him and part on one of his wives while she was menstruating. Humaydi said in his version: 'part on me and part on him while I was menstruating.'"],[19915,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while I was sleeping beside him; when he prostrated, his garment would touch me while I was menstruating."],[19916,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood between the row of men and the row of women and said to the women: \"When you hear the adhan of this Abyssinian, say what he says.\""],[19917,"From the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be intimate with a woman from among his wives when she was menstruating, with a cloth upon her reaching to the knees or to the middle of the thighs.\" Ibn Jurayj mentioned it from Ibn Shihab, from Habib, the mawla of 'Urwah, from Nudbah."],[19918,"Regarding the bed of his wife, while the daughter of Mishrah was with him that day, she said: \"What is the matter with you?\" She said: \"This is how he treats me when I menstruate.\" She said: \"So I went to Maymunah and informed her.\" He said: \"And she said: 'She sent me to him saying: What is it that you do? Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be intimate with one of us while she was menstruating, and she had nothing on except her waist-wrapper, reaching to the middle of her thigh.'\""],[19919,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be intimate with a woman from among his wives while she was menstruating, if she had a waist-wrapper reaching to the middle of the thighs or the knees, with which she wrapped herself.\""],[19920,"From Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be intimate with a woman from among his wives while she was menstruating, if she had a waist-wrapper reaching to the middle of the thighs or the knees.\""],[19921,"That the mole of Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , looked and saw that his bed was separated from the bed of his wife, the daughter of Mishrah. So she returned to Maymuna and informed her of her return message. Then she said, \"I saw his bed separate from mine, so I think there has been a separation between them.\" Maymuna said to them, \"Go back to the wife of Ibn Abbas and ask her about it.\" So I returned and asked her, and she said, \"There is no separation between us, but when I have my period, he separates his bed from mine.\" Maymuna sent a message to Abdullah expressing her anger towards him, and she said, \"O Abdullah, do you prefer to go against the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ? By Allah, if a woman from her husbands wears a garment that does not reach the halfway point of her thighs, he can have intimate relations with her.\""],[19922,"Nudbah, the freed slave woman of Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that Maymunah sent her to 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas, who was the son of her sister. She said: \"I went to him and found him having separated his bed from the bed of his wife, the daughter of Mishrah. She said: 'Where is he? Is he angry with his wife?' It was said: 'No, but when she menstruates, he distances himself from her.' She said: 'So I returned to Maymunah and informed her how I found him.' She said: 'Call him for me.' So I called him for her, and she said: 'Do you turn away from what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do? By Allah, he used to be intimate with a woman from among his wives when she had a waist-wrapper reaching to the middle of the thighs or the knees.'\""],[19923,"While she was sitting with Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, Ibn 'Abbas entered upon her. She said: \"Why do I see you disheveled?\" He said: \"Umm 'Ammar, my hairdresser, is menstruating.\" She said: \"O my dear son, what does menstruation have to do with the hand? Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to enter upon one of us while she was reclining and menstruating, knowing that, and he would recline upon her and recite the Quran while reclining upon her. And he would enter upon her while she was standing and menstruating, and he would recline in her lap and recite the Quran. And she would stand while menstruating and spread the mat for him in his prayer place, and he would pray on it. O my dear son, what does menstruation have to do with the hand?\""],[19924,"\"O my dear son, why do I see your head disheveled?\" He said: \"My hairdresser, Umm 'Ammar, is menstruating.\" She said: \"O my dear son, what does menstruation have to do with the hand? Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to place his head in the lap of one of us while she was menstruating, and he would pray upon her.\""],[19925,"Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to her that some men from Quraysh passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dragging a sheep of theirs like a donkey. The Prophet ﷺ said to them: \"Why don't you take its skin?\" They said: \"It is carrion.\" He said: \"Water and qaraz (acacia pods) purify it.\""],[19926,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about a mouse that fell into clarified butter. He said: \"Throw it away and what is around it, and eat the rest.\""],[19927,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a mouse that falls into clarified butter. He said: \"If it is solid, throw it away and what is around it; but if it is liquid, do not go near it.\""],[19928,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood between the row of men and the row of women and said: \"O assembly of women, when you hear the adhan of this Abyssinian and his iqamah, say what he says, for you will have for every letter a thousand thousand degrees.\" 'Umar said: \"This is for the women, so what is for the men?\" He said: \"Double, O 'Umar.\""],[19929,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood between the row of men and women and said, \"O company of women, when you hear the call to prayer of this Abyssinian and his iqamah, then say as he says, for verily for you for every letter is a thousand thousand degrees.\" Umar said, \"This is for women, so what is for men?\" He said, \"Twice that, O Umar.\""],[19930,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep belonging to a female client of Maymunah, which had been given to her from charity. He said, \"Why did they not take its hide and tan it and benefit from it?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, it is dead.\" He said, \"Only its eating is forbidden.\""],[19931,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Why did you not tan its hide and make use of it?\""],[19932,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the killing of dogs."],[19933,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one day looking sluggish. I said, \"Why do I see you sluggish?\" He said, \"Gabriel promised me and did not break [his promise], so he remained thus for that day and its night. In the house there was a dog under a couch of ours, so he took it out and took water with his hand and wiped its place with it. Then Gabriel came and said, 'We do not enter a house in which there is a picture or a dog.' He was consulted about the small dog of the garden, but he did not give permission for it.\""],[19934,"\"I used to perform ghusl together with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from a single vessel.\""],[19935,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Water is not made impure by anything.\""],[19936,"\"I placed water for the Prophet ﷺ to perform ghusl, and he performed ghusl from janabah. He tilted the vessel with his left hand over his right and washed his palms, then poured water over his private part and washed it, then rubbed his hand on the ground, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water and washed his face and forearms, then poured water over his head, then poured water over the rest of his body, then moved aside and washed his feet.\" She said, \"Then I brought him a cloth, but he cast it aside and began shaking off the water with his hand like this.\""],[19937,"I performed ghusl from janabah, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and performed ghusl with the water left over from my ghusl. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I had performed ghusl from it.\" He said, \"Water does not carry janabah.\""],[19938,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Water is not made impure by anything.\""],[19939,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ was brought a towel, but he did not touch it, and he began shaking off the water with his hand like this,\" meaning shaking it off."],[19940,"Abu Al-Malih Al-Hudhali went out in a funeral. When the deceased was placed on the bed, he approached the people and said, \"Straighten your rows and improve your intercession.\" Then Abu Al-Malih said, \"Abdullah bin Salit informed me, and he was the brother of Maymunah, the mother of the believers, from Maymunah, from the Prophet ﷺ , who said, 'Whoever prays upon him, a nation will intercede for their brother.' And the nation is forty to one hundred, the group is ten to forty, and the individual is three to ten.\""],[19941,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The sisters are believers,\" meaning Maymunah bint al-Harith, Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith, Salma the wife of Hamzah, and Asma' bint Umays."],[19942,"On the authority of Maymunah: They disputed about the Prophet ﷺ's fasting on the Day of Arafah. Maymunah said: 'I shall send him some dates for you. If he is not fasting, he will not leave them.' So she sent him a bowl of milk, and he drank it while the people were watching."],[19943,"I prayed with Abu al-Malih over a funeral. He said: 'Straighten your rows and let your intercession be good, and if I were to choose a man, I would choose him.' Abdullah b. Abi al-Salil narrated to us, from one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, Maymunah—and he was her foster brother—that the Prophet ﷺ said: 'There is no Muslim man over whom a community prays but they are granted intercession for him.' Abu al-Malih said: 'The community is from forty to one hundred.'"],[19944,"On the authority of Maymunah, and Yazid was an orphan in her care. He mentioned that a siwak was always kept in a vessel. If work or prayer occupied her, otherwise she would take the siwak and use it."],[19945,"The Prophet ﷺ married me at Sarif while we were both in the state of ihram (or: not in ihram)."],[19946,"The Prophet ﷺ married her while he was not in ihram, and she was my maternal aunt."],[19947,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while he was not in ihram."],[19948,"When the Prophet ﷺ sat, he would settle on his left thigh."],[19949,"A dabb (spiny-tailed lizard) was gifted to us, so I cooked it. Two men from my people, the Quraysh, entered, and I offered it to them as a treat. Then the Prophet ﷺ entered while they were eating. He placed his hand, then lifted it and said: 'What is this?' I said: 'A dabb that was gifted to us; I cooked it.' He pushed it away. They went to throw away what was in their hands, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: 'Eat, for you are people of Najd and you eat it, while we are people of Tihamah and we find it repulsive.'"],[19950,"Maymunah narrated to me: 'When one of us was menstruating and stood up intending to return, he would instruct her to wrap herself with a waist-wrapper, and then he would engage in intimacy with her.'"],[19951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while I was beside him, and sometimes his garment would touch me when he prostrated."],[19952,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed in a khamisah (a black rectangular cloak), part of which was over her while she was menstruating."],[19953,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray on a khumrah (a small mat)."],[19954,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray in his mosque on a small mat of his. He would touch me with his hands while I was sleeping beside him, and I was menstruating."],[19955,"On the authority of Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet (PBUH), who said: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying, \"My Ummah will always remain upon good as long as they do not introduce (or tolerate) the child of Zina (illegitimate child) among them. But if they introduce it (or tolerate it), then I fear that Allah will afflict them with a punishment.\""],[19956,"From Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: I manumitted a slave girl of mine. The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me, and I informed him of her manumission. He said, “May Allah reward you. Indeed, had you given her to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater for your reward.”"],[19957,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The world is sweet and green.\""],[19958,"The people doubted whether the Prophet ﷺ was fasting on the Day of ʿArafah. Maymunah sent him some milk while he was standing at the standing place, and he drank from it while the people were looking."],[19959,"I heard Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, say: “The Prophet ﷺ used to lie with me while I was menstruating, and between me and him was a garment.”"],[19960,"Some of her family said to her, “Do not do it,” and they disapproved of it. She said, “Yes, indeed I heard my Prophet and close friend ﷺ say: ‘There is no Muslim who incurs a debt intending to repay it except that Allah will repay it on his behalf in this world.’”"],[19961,"Nudbah, the freed slave woman of Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, sent her to Ibn ʿAbbas, who was the son of her sister. She said: I came and found that his bed had been moved away from the bed of his wife, the daughter of Mishrah. I said, “Where is he? Is he angry with his wife?” They said, “No, but when she menstruates, he keeps apart from her.” I returned to Maymunah and told her how I had found him. She said, “Call him for me.” So I called him, and she said to him, “Do you turn away from what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do? By Allah, he used to touch a woman from among his wives when she had garments on, reaching the middle of the thighs or the knees.”"],[19962,"From the Hilaliyyah woman who was with the Prophet ﷺ, that she had a black servant girl. She said, “O Messenger of Allah, I want to manumit this one.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Will you not help your brother’s sons with her in tending the sheep?”"],[19963,"I asked him if I can offer three units of prayer after Isha and then go out for prayer, fearing that I might miss it. He replied, \"It is not correct except with five or seven (units of prayer).\" So, I asked him from whom did he hear this? He said, \"From a trustworthy person, from Maymunah, from Aisha, from the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[19964,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine.”"],[19965,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to us one day: “How will you be when religion becomes confused, the common people become prominent, reports differ, and the Ancient House is burned?”"],[19966,"The Prophet ﷺ said to her when she freed her servant, \"If you had ransomed your family with her from the livestock of the sheep, it would have been better.\""],[19967,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray two rakʿahs before ʿAsr."],[19968,"The Prophet ﷺ ate a shoulder at her place, then prayed and did not perform ablution."],[19969,"I heard Maymunah say: I manumitted my slave girl during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “Had you given her to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater for your reward.”"],[19970,"Her family said to her, \"You take loans while you do not have what to repay?\" She said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever incurs a debt while telling himself he will repay it, Allah will help him with it.'\""],[19971,"Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, took a loan of three hundred dirhams. It was said to her, \"O Mother of the Believers, you take loans while you do not have [the means]?\" She said, \"Yes. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever incurs a debt and intends to repay it, Allah will help him with it.'\""],[19972,"He heard Maymuna say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a shoulder cut, then prayed without performing wudu'.\""],[19973,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited Ha Mim 'Ayn Sin Qaf and said, \"O Maymuna, do you recite Ha Mim 'Ayn Sin Qaf? I have forgotten what is between its beginning and its end.\" I recited it, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it."],[19974,"\"Maymuna was shrouded in a dyed yellow garment.\""],[19975,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and said, \"Is there any food?\" I said, \"No, except a bone that was given to a female client of ours from the charity.\" He said, \"Bring it, for it has reached its proper place.\""],[19976,"\"Sawda bt. Zam'a b. Qays b. 'Abd Shams b. 'Abd Wudd b. Nasr b. Malik b. Hasl b. 'Amir b. Lu'ayy b. Ghalib b. Fihr, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her after Khadija bt. Khuwaylid in Makkah.\""],[19977,"Then \"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Sawda bt. Zam'a. She had previously been married to al-Sakran b. 'Amr, the brother of Banu 'Amir b. Lu'ayy.\""],[19978,"Khawla bt. Hakim b. al-Awqas, the wife of 'Uthman b. Maz'un, and that was in Makkah, said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry?\" He said, \"Who?\" She said, \"If you wish, a virgin, and if you wish, a previously married woman.\" He said, \"Who is the previously married woman?\" She said, \"Sawda bt. Zam'a. She has believed in you and followed you in what you are upon.\" He said, \"Go and mention her to me.\" She said, \"I left and entered upon Sawda and said, 'O Sawda, what good and blessing has Allah brought to you?' She said, 'What is that?' Khawla said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to propose to you on his behalf.' She said, 'I would love that. Enter upon my father and mention that to him.' I said, 'He is an old man and has been left behind from the Hajj.' So I entered upon him and greeted him with the greeting of the people of the Jahiliyyah. Then she said, 'Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib sent me to propose to Sawda on his behalf.' He said, 'A noble equal. What does your companion say?' She said, 'She desires that.' He said, 'Call her to me.' So I called her. He said, 'O Sawda, this woman claims that Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib is proposing to you, and he is a noble equal. Would you like me to marry you to him?' She said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then call him for me.' So I called him and he came, and he married her to him. Then her brother 'Abd Allah b. Zam'a came from the Hajj and began to pour dust on his head. After he had become Muslim, he said, 'I was foolish on the day I poured dust on my head because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Sawda bt. Zam'a.'\""],[19979,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not favor some of us over others in the division [of nights]. Rarely did a day pass except that he visited us and drew near each woman among us without intercourse, until he reached the one whose day it was and spent the night with her. Sawda bt. Zam'a said to him, and she had become old, and he intended to separate from her: \"My day with you and my share are for 'A'isha.\" He accepted that from her. About her it was revealed: {And if a woman fears from her husband ill-treatment or aversion, there is no sin upon them both if they make terms of peace between them} (Qur'an 4:128)."],[19980,"And she said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I do not desire what women desire.\""],[19981,"\"Sawda gifted her day to 'A'isha, so he used to allocate to 'A'isha her own day and Sawda's day.\""],[19982,"When Sawdah bint Zam'ah became old, she gave her day to 'A'ishah, so the Prophet ﷺ would allot to 'A'ishah the day of Sawdah."],[19983,"that the Prophet ﷺ should divorce her. She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, keep me and do not divorce me, and give my day to 'A'ishah.' Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {There is no blame} upon them if they make peace between themselves, and peace is better. Whatever they agree upon is permissible."],[19984,"The Prophet ﷺ wanted to separate from Sawdah, so he called Abu Bakr and 'Umar to witness her divorce. She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have no desire for this world except to be gathered on the Day of Resurrection among your wives, so that I may have the same reward as them.'"],[19985,"From al-Haytham or Abu al-Haytham — Abu Bakr was unsure — that the Prophet ﷺ divorced Sawdah once. She sat in his path, and when he passed by she asked him to take her back and to give her allotted share of him to whichever of his wives he wished, hoping to be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection as his wife. So he took her back and accepted that."],[19986,"Sawdah was a large woman whose body frightened people."],[19987,"Sawdah and Zaynab said: 'The camel will never move us again after what we heard from the Prophet ﷺ,' meaning his saying, 'This is the last, then the riding of mats.' He said: So his wives performed Hajj except those two."],[19988,"From Sawdah bint Zam'ah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, when 'Uthman b. Maz'un walks, he prays for us until he comes to us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, 'If you knew what death knows, O daughter of Zam'ah, you would know that it is more severe than you imagine.'"],[19989,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'People will be resurrected barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised. Sweat will bridle them and reach the lobes of their ears.' I asked, 'Will we see one another?' He said, 'People will be preoccupied. {Every man that Day will have concern enough to make him heedless of others}.'"],[19990,"The captives of Badr were brought while Sawdah bint Zam'ah was with the family of 'Afra' at their camel resting place, at 'Awf and Mu'awwidh, the two sons of 'Afra'. That was before the veil was imposed on them. She said: It was said, 'The captives of Badr have been brought.' So I went to my dwelling and there I saw Suhayl b. 'Amr, his hands bound together to his neck in a corner of the room. When I saw him, I could not control myself and said, 'Abu Yazid, you surrendered what was in your hands. Why did you not die nobly?' She said: By Allah, nothing alerted me except the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from inside the house: 'Against Allah and His Messenger?' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I could not control myself when I saw Abu Yazid, so I said what I said.'"],[19991,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Why did you not take its skin, tan it, and benefit from it?\""],[19992,"\"O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who is unable to perform Hajj; should I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do you think that if your father had a debt and you paid it off, would that be sufficient for him?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then perform Hajj on his behalf.\""],[19993,"that she gave her day to 'A'ishah."],[19994,"We had a sheep that died, so we threw it away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said, 'Why did you not make use of its hide?' We sent for it, skinned it, tanned the hide, and made it into a water skin. We drank from it until it became an old worn-out skin."],[19995,"So we tanned its hide and used to make nabidh in it until it became an old worn-out skin."],[19996,"Sawda, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: \"We had a sheep that died, so we tanned its skin, and we continued to soak [dates] in it until it became worn out like an old waterskin.\""],[19997,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said: \"Why did you not make use of its hide?\""],[19998,"We had a sheep that died, so we threw it away. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said: \"What happened to your sheep?\" We said: \"It died, so we threw it away.\" He said: \"Why did you not benefit from its hide?\" I said: \"It is carrion.\" Then he recited this verse: {Say, \"I do not find within that which was revealed to me [anything] forbidden to one who would eat it unless it be a dead animal...\"} (Qur'an 6:145) [and said]: \"He has only forbidden you from eating it.\" So they sent for its hide, tanned it, and used it until it became an old waterskin among them."],[19999,"\"Among the women who emigrated from the Banu Asad were Zaynab bint Jahsh and some other women,\" and he mentioned them."],[20000,"Then \"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Zaynab bint Jahsh, and before that she was married to Zayd b. Harithah.\""],[20001,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Zaynab bint Jahsh b. Ri'ab b. Asad b. Khuzaymah; her mother was Umaymah bint 'Abd al-Muttalib b. Hashim, the paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"She was the first of the Prophet's ﷺ wives to die.\""],[20002,"\"Zaynab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, died in the year twenty.\""],[20003,"\"Zaynab bint Jahsh died during the caliphate of 'Umar ؓ.\""],[20004,"I heard Anas b. Malik say: \"Zaynab bint Jahsh used to boast over the other wives of the Prophet ﷺ, saying: 'Your families married you off, but Allah married me from above the heavens.'\""],[20005,"The Prophet ﷺ entered his house with 'Umar b. al-Khattab, and there was Zaynab bint Jahsh praying; while in her prayer she was supplicating. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"She is indeed devoted and humble [awwahah].\""],[20006,"A number of men from Quraysh proposed to me, so I sent my sister Hamnah to the Messenger of God ﷺ to consult him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, \"Where is she in comparison to one who will teach her the Book of her Lord and the Sunnah of her Prophet?\" She said, \"And who is he, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"Zayd b. Harithah.\" Hamnah became extremely angry and said, \"O Messenger of God, will you marry the daughter of your paternal aunt to your freedman?\" She said: She came to me and informed me, and I became angrier than she had been, and I said something even stronger than what she had said. Then God revealed: {It is not for a believing man or a believing woman, when God and His Messenger have decreed a matter, to have any choice in their affair}. She said: So I sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"I seek God's forgiveness and I obey God and His Messenger. Do what you see fit.\" So he married me to Zayd. I used to disparage him, and he complained about me to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ admonished me, but I returned to my behavior and rebuked him with my tongue. He complained about me to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Keep your wife and fear God.\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, I will divorce her.\" She said: So he divorced me. When my waiting period ended, I was not aware of anything until the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me in my house while my hair was uncovered. I said, \"This is a command from heaven.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, without a proposal or witnesses?\" He said, \"God is the matchmaker, and Gabriel is the witness.\""],[20007,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Zaid, \"Mention it to her.\" Zaid said, \"So I departed and said, 'O Zainab, rejoice! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sends his regards to you.' She said, 'I don't do anything until I consult my Lord.' So she went to her mosque and the Qur'an was revealed, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to her without seeking permission.\""],[20008,"If the Messenger of God ﷺ had concealed anything of the revelation, he would have concealed this verse: {And you concealed within yourself what God was to disclose, and you feared the people, while God has more right that you fear Him. So when Zayd had accomplished his desire from her, We married her to you}."],[20009,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ concealed something of the Book of God, he concealed this verse: {And when you said to the one whom God had blessed and you had blessed}, up to His saying {accomplished his desire from her, We married her to you}."],[20010,"Concerning His saying {And when you said to the one whom God had blessed and you had blessed}, he said, \"God blessed him with Islam, and the Prophet ﷺ blessed him with manumission.\"{Keep your wife}, Qatadah said: Zayd came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Zaynab's tongue has become harsh toward me, and I want to divorce her.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Fear God and keep your wife.\" The Prophet ﷺ wanted him to divorce her, but he feared what people would say if he commanded him to divorce her, so God revealed: {And you concealed within yourself what God was to disclose, and you feared the people, while God has more right that you fear Him. So when Zayd had accomplished his desire from her}.He said: When Zayd divorced her, {We married her to you}."],[20011,"Regarding His statement: “and if the one who Allāh had favored says…” (Aḥzāb 33:37) and he was Zayd b. Ḥārithah: Allah had favored him with Islam, and “and you had blessed” the Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed him [from slavery].[Regarding] “and hold on to your wife and fear Allah and you hide within yourself what Allah has made known and you fear people...” (Aḥzāb 33:37), he said, he used to hide within himself [that] he liked that he would divorce her.. He said that al-Ḥasan said, \"No Āyah was revealed upon him more severe that His statement, '...and you hide within yourself', and if the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were to hide anything from the Waḥī, he would have hidden it.\"[Regarding] “then when Zayd had fulfilled his desire with her,” [means] when Zayd had divorced her, “we married you to her.” He said, Zayb b. Jaḥsh used to boast to the wives of the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"As for you all, your fathers married you off. And as for me, then the Owner of the Throne married me off.\"[Regarding] \"... fear Allah,\", he said, meaning O Prophet of Allah her [lack of] character has been hard on me and I am divorcing this woman. And the Prophet ﷺ, when he said this, said, \"Hold on to your wife and fear Allah.\""],[20012,"From Qatadah concerning His saying {And when you said to the one whom God had blessed}, \"with Islam,\" {and you had blessed}, \"that you manumitted him.\" {Keep your wife}, \"he is Zayd b. Harithah.\""],[20013,"It was revealed concerning Zaynab bt. Jahsh: {And you concealed within yourself what God was to disclose}."],[20014,"From Ibn Jurayj concerning His saying {And you concealed within yourself what God was to disclose}, \"In the heart of the Messenger of God ﷺ was his love for Zayd's divorcing her and his marrying her, but God insisted that He disclose what the Prophet ﷺ had concealed in his heart.\""],[20015,"“I never saw the Messenger of Allah give a wedding feast for any of his wives like the feast he gave for Zainab, for which he slaughtered a sheep.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1908)"],[20016,"Concerning His saying {The established way of God among those who passed away before}, he said, \"David and the woman whom he married, whose husband was named al-Yasa'. That is a precedent for Muhammad and Zaynab.\""],[20017,"Concerning His saying {And the command of God is a decree decreed}, \"Thus it is part of His established way regarding David and the woman, and the Prophet ﷺ and Zaynab.\""],[20018,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ came to the house of Zayd b. Harithah and asked permission. Zaynab gave him permission while she had no head covering, so she threw the sleeve of her chemise over her head. He asked her about Zayd, and she said, \"He went out a short while ago, O Messenger of God.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up, murmuring to himself. Zaynab said: I followed him and heard him saying, \"Blessed is the Turner of hearts.\" He kept saying it until he disappeared."],[20019,"Zainab said, \"I am the one whom Allah married from the heavens.\" Aisha said, \"I am the one whom Sufwan bin al-Muattal blamed when he carried me.\" Then Zainab said to her, \"What did you say when you rode?\". She said, \"I said 'Allah is sufficient for me, and He is the best disposer of affairs.'\" Zainab said, \"You said the word of the believers.\""],[20020,"About Qatadah's saying, \"And it is not for a believing man or believing woman, when Allah and His Messenger have decided a matter, that they should [thereafter] have any choice about their affair. And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger has certainly strayed into clear error.\" He said, \"This verse was revealed regarding Zainab bint Jahsh, who was the cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to her, and she accepted, thinking that he was proposing to her for himself. However, when she found out that he was proposing to her on behalf of Zaid bin Harithah, she refused and disputed. So Allah revealed this verse, 'And it is not for a believing man or believing woman...'.\""],[20021,"\"I used to comb the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[20022,"The Prophet ﷺ proposed to Zaynab, who was the daughter of his paternal aunt, while he intended her for Zayd. She thought he intended her for himself, but when she learned he intended her for Zayd, she refused. Then God revealed: {It is not for a believing man or a believing woman, when God and His Messenger have decreed a matter, to have any choice in their affair}. So she accepted and submitted."],[20023,"The Prophet ﷺ held a wedding feast for one of his wives, meaning Zaynab. Umm Sulaym prepared some hays (a dish of dates, clarified butter, and dried curd), then placed it in a stone pot while they were at that time in severe hardship. She said, \"Take this to the Messenger of God ﷺ, convey my greetings to him, and tell him that this is a small gift from us.\" So I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, Umm Sulaym sent this to you, and she sends you her greetings and says to you, 'O Messenger of God, this is a small gift from us to you.'\" He looked at it and said, \"Put it down.\" I placed it in a corner of the house. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, \"Go and invite so-and-so, so-and-so, and so-and-so,\" naming many men, \"and any Muslims you meet.\" So I invited those he named and any Muslims I met, and I came back while the house, the bench area, and the chamber were full. We asked Anas, \"How many were they?\" He said, \"About three hundred.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ called me to bring the pot, so I brought it. He placed his hand on it, pronounced the name of God, and supplicated. Then he said, \"Let them form circles of ten, and let each person eat from what is in front of him.\" They formed circles of ten, pronounced the name of God, ate, and left. Whenever one group finished, they departed and others came to take their place, until all of them had eaten. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, \"Take it away.\" I do not know whether it was more when I placed it or when I lifted it. Some groups of people remained in the house of the Messenger of God ﷺ conversing, and they prolonged their talk, which weighed heavily on the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ was the most modest of people, and they were unaware that they were burdening him, for it was difficult for him to tell them. So the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up and left them. When they saw that the Messenger of God ﷺ had returned, they thought they had overstayed, so they rushed to the door and departed. Anas said: Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came and let down the curtain and entered. He remained for a short while, and revelation came down upon him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came out reciting: {O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless you are given permission}, to the end of the verses. Anas said: I am the most recent of people in connection with these verses; the Messenger of God ﷺ recited them to me."],[20024,"He informed me of the most amazing thing I saw from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . He said, \"When the Prophet of Allah ﷺ married Zaynab bint Jahsh, my mother said to me, 'O Anas, indeed the Prophet of Allah ﷺ has become a groom and I do not see that he has had breakfast. So come with this empty bag of dates and a container of milk, enough for a long time.' So she prepared a meal for him, and she said, 'O Anas, take this to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his wife.' When I brought the bag of dates with the container of milk to the Prophet ﷺ , which had the meal, he said, 'Place it in the corner of the house and go call Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, and some of his companions. Then call the people of the mosque and whoever you see on the way.' I was surprised by the little amount of food and the large number of people he commanded me to invite, so I disliked disobeying him until the house and the room were filled. He asked, 'O Anas, do you see anyone else?' I said, 'No, O Prophet of Allah.' He said, 'Bring that container.' So I brought the container, and he dipped three fingers into it, and the container began to increase and rise until they all ate from it and left, and there remained in the container almost the same amount as I brought. He said, 'Place it in front of Zaynab.' So I left and plugged the door with a mat.\" Thabit said, \"We asked, 'O Abu Hamzah, how many were the ones who ate from that container?' He said, 'I estimate it to be seventy-one or seventy-two.'\""],[20025,"I heard Anas b. Malik say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a wedding feast for Zaynab bint Jahsh with bread and meat.\""],[20026,"I am the most knowledgeable of people about this verse. When Zaynab was given to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, she was with him in the house. He prepared food, then the people came. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would go out while the people remained in their places, then return while the people were still sitting. Then Allah revealed: {O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless you are given permission for a meal, without waiting for its preparation. But when you are invited, enter, and when you have eaten, disperse, and do not linger for conversation. Indeed, that was troubling the Prophet, and he is shy of you, but Allah is not shy of the truth. And when you ask them for something, ask them from behind a screen.} So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set up the screen, and the people got up."],[20027,"I heard Anas b. Malik say: \"The verse of the screen was revealed concerning Zaynab bint Jahsh.\""],[20028,"Anas said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became a bridegroom with Zaynab bint Jahsh. He had married her in Madinah. He invited the people to a meal after the sun had risen high. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat, and some men sat with him after the people had left, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and walked, and I walked with him until he reached the door of Aishah's room. Then he thought that they had left, so he returned, and I returned with him, and there they were, still standing. So he drew a curtain between me and him, and the verse of the screen was revealed.\""],[20029,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a woman and was impressed by her. He went in to Zaynab bint Jahsh and satisfied his need with her, then came out and said: \"When a woman approaches, she takes the form of a devil, and when she leaves, she leaves in the form of a devil. So whoever finds that, let him go to his wife, for that will subdue what is in himself.\""],[20030,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his wives: \"The first of you to follow me will be the one with the longest hand among you.\" Aishah said: \"After the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, whenever we gathered, we would stretch our hands against the wall to see who was the longest. We continued doing that until Zaynab bint Jahsh b. Ri'ab died. She was a short woman, and she was not the tallest of us. Then we realized that by 'length of hand' the Prophet ﷺ meant charity. She was a skilled woman who worked with her hands and gave charity from it in the way of Allah.\""],[20031,"He prayed with Umar over Zaynab, and she was the first of the Prophet's ﷺ wives to die. He liked that he himself would lower her into her grave, so he sent to the wives of the Prophet ﷺ asking who should lower her into her grave. They said: 'Whoever used to see her in her lifetime should lower her into her grave.'"],[20032,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came in to us saying: \"Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. Today a gap like this has been opened in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj,\" and he made a circle with his thumb and the finger next to it. She said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will we be destroyed while there are righteous people among us?\" He said: \"Yes, when wickedness becomes widespread.\" Abd al-Razzaq did not mention Umm Habibah in the chain from Ma'mar."],[20033,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came in to her alarmed, saying: \"Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. Today a gap like this has been opened in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj,\" and he made a circle with his thumb and the finger next to it. Zaynab said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will we be destroyed while there are righteous people among us?\" He said: \"Yes, when wickedness becomes widespread.\""],[20034,"Al-Zuhri narrated to us, and we do not need anyone else in it: Urwah b. al-Zubayr informed me, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Habibah bint Umm Habibah, from her mother Umm Habibah, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke from sleep with his face red, saying: \"There is no god but Allah. Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. Today a gap like this has been opened in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj,\" and Sufyan held up ten fingers. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will we be destroyed while there are righteous people among us?\" He said: \"Yes, when wickedness becomes widespread.\" Sufyan said: I remember in this hadith four women from al-Zuhri, and they had seen the Prophet ﷺ: two of his wives, Umm Habibah and Zaynab, and two of his stepdaughters, Zaynab bint Umm Salamah and Habibah bint Umm Habibah, whose father was Ubayd Allah b. Jahsh, who died in the land of Abyssinia."],[20035,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke from his sleep alarmed, saying: \"Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. Today a gap like this has been opened in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj,\" and he made a circle with his two fingers, the thumb and the one next to it. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will we be destroyed while there are righteous people among us?\" He said: \"Yes, when wickedness becomes widespread.\""],[20036,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us, all of them from Malik b. Anas, from 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr, from Humayd b. Nafi', from Zaynab bt. Umm Salamah, who said: I entered upon Zaynab bt. Jahsh when her brother died. She called for perfume and applied some of it, then said, \"I have no need for perfume, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three days, except for a husband, four months and ten days.'\""],[20037,"That the Prophet ﷺ was sleeping with her while Husayn was crawling in the house. She became heedless of him, and he crawled until he reached the Prophet ﷺ, climbed onto his belly, and then placed his penis on his navel. She said: The Prophet ﷺ woke up, and I got up to him and removed him from his belly. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Leave my son.\" When he finished urinating, he took a jug of water and poured it over him, then said, \"Water is poured over a boy, and a girl is washed.\" She said: He performed wudu, then stood to pray while holding him. When he bowed and prostrated, he put him down, and when he stood, he carried him. When he sat, he began supplicating and raising his hands and speaking. When he finished the prayer, I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I saw you do something today that I have not seen you do before.\" He said, \"Jibril came to me and informed me that my son will be killed.\" I said, \"Then show me.\" So he brought me red soil."],[20038,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke from his sleep with his face red, and he was saying, \"There is no god but Allah. Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. Today a breach has been opened in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj like this,\" and he held up his hand, meaning ten. Zaynab said: I said, \"Will we perish while there are righteous people among us?\" He said, \"Yes, when wickedness becomes widespread.\""],[20039,"I entered upon Zaynab bt. Jahsh and her face was red. I said, \"What is the matter with you?\" She said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was sleeping and struck me with a majassa he had with him.\" I said, \"What is the majassa?\" She said, \"The white palm branch.\" He said, \"By Allah, this is the time when great tribulations have descended.\" She said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will we perish while there are righteous people among us?\" He said, \"Yes, then those who fear Allah will be saved.\""],[20040,"\"We had a pot of yellow dye in which I would dip the head of the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[20041,"I asked the wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she said: She is a woman with prolonged menstrual bleeding. He said, \"She should sit for the days of her menstrual periods, then perform ghusl, delay Zuhr and hasten Asr, perform ghusl and pray, delay Maghrib and hasten Isha and pray them together, and perform ghusl for Fajr.\""],[20042,"That the Prophet ﷺ gave women inheritance in their allotted plots of land."],[20043,"The Prophet ﷺ took a midday nap in my house when Husayn approached, and he was a boy, until he sat on the belly of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then placed his penis in his navel. She said: I got up to him, and he said, \"Bring me water.\" I brought him water, and he poured it over him, then said, \"A girl is washed, and water is poured over a boy.\""],[20044,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Zaynab bt. Khuzaymah, and she is Umm al-Masakin (Mother of the Poor). She was named that because of her frequent feeding of the poor. She was from Banu Hilal b. 'Amir b. Sa'sa'ah, and she died while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was alive. She did not remain with him except a short while."],[20045,"One day I was with Zaynab, the wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we were making something for her with red ochre. While we were doing that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us. When he saw the red ochre, he turned back. When Zaynab saw that, she knew that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked what she had done. She took water and washed her clothes and covered up every trace of red. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned, looked in, and saw nothing, so he entered."],[20046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Zainab bint Khuzayma al-Hilaliyya, the mother of the poor. She was previously married to Huthayn or Tufayl ibn al-Harith. She died in Madinah, being his first wife to pass away."],[20047,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took Juwayriyyah bt. al-Harith b. Abi Dirar from Banu al-Mustaliq of Khuza'ah captive in his expedition in which he demolished Manat, the expedition of al-Muraysi'."],[20048,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took Juwayriyyah bt. al-Harith b. Abi Dirar b. 'A'idh b. Malik b. al-Mustaliq of Khuza'ah captive, and the name of al-Mustaliq is Khuzaymah, on the day he fought Banu al-Mustaliq."],[20049,"Juwayriyyah bt. al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, died in the year fifty-six."],[20050,"Juwayriyah was a slave of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he freed her, made her emancipation her dower, and freed every captive from Banū al-Muṣṭaliq."],[20051,"Juwayriyah said to the Prophet ﷺ: Your wives boast over me and say, “The Messenger of God ﷺ did not marry you.” He said, “Did I not make your dower great? Did I not free forty of your people?”"],[20052,"I wrote to Nāfiʿ asking him whether the call to Islam preceded fighting. He wrote back to me that that was at the beginning of Islam, and that the Messenger of God ﷺ raided Banū al-Muṣṭaliq while they were heedless and their cattle were being watered. He killed their fighting men, took their women and children captive, and Juwayriyah bt. al-Ḥārith fell to him. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad, who was in that army on that day, narrated this hadith to me."],[20053,"The Messenger of God ﷺ chose Juwayriyah for himself."],[20054,"The Messenger of God ﷺ learned that Banū al-Muṣṭaliq were gathering forces against him, led by al-Ḥārith b. Abī Ḍirār, the father of Juwayriyah bt. al-Ḥārith, wife of the Prophet ﷺ. When the Messenger of God ﷺ heard of them, he set out against them until he met them at a watering place of theirs called al-Muraysīʿ, on the side of Qudayd toward the coast. The people pressed upon one another and fought. God defeated Banū al-Muṣṭaliq; al-Ḥārith b. Abī Ḍirār, Juwayriyah's father, was killed along with others of them who were killed, and God granted His Messenger their children and women as spoils. The Messenger of God ﷺ took many captives from them and divided them among the Muslims. Among the women taken that day was Juwayriyah bt. al-Ḥārith b. Abī Ḍirār, the leading woman of her people."],[20055,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by her early in the morning while she was praying in the mosque. Then he passed by her again close to midday and asked, \"Are you still doing the same thing?\" She replied, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Shall I teach you some words that are equivalent to freeing slaves? They are: Subhan Allah (Glory be to Allah) the number of His creations three times, Subhan Allah satisfaction with Himself three times, Subhan Allah the weight of His Throne three times, and Subhan Allah the ink of His words.\" Her name was Burrah, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named her Juwayriyah."],[20056,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by her after he had prayed the dawn prayer, or after the dawn prayer, while she was remembering God until the forenoon had risen and she was still doing so. He said, “Since I left you I have said three phrases that are greater and weightier, or more balanced, than what you have said: ‘Glory be to God as many times as the number of His creatures; glory be to God as much as pleases His Self; glory be to God as much as the weight of His Throne; glory be to God as much as the ink of His words.’”"],[20057,"Juwayriyah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon her and said, “Is there any food?” She said, “No, by God, O Messenger of God. I have no food except a bone of a sheep given to my freedwoman from charity.” He said, “Bring it close, for it has reached its proper place.”"],[20058,"From Juwayriyah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her and said, “Is there any food?” She said, “No, by God, except a bone of a sheep given to my freedwoman from charity.” He said, “Bring it close, for it has reached its proper place.”"],[20059,"We had a freedwoman who was given something as charity. I prepared it, and he—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—said, “Bring it close, for it has reached its proper place.”"],[20060,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon her and said, “Do you have any food?” She said, “No, by God, except a bone of a sheep given to my freedwoman from charity.” He said, “Bring it close, for it has reached its proper place.”"],[20061,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me and said, “Is there any food?” I said, “No, except a bone given to our freedwoman from charity.” He said, “Bring it close, for it has reached its proper place.”"],[20062,"He informed him that Juwayriyah bt. al-Ḥārith, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, told him that her freedwoman had been given some meat as charity, so she prepared it. When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned, he said, “Do you have any supper?” I said, “O Messenger of God, such-and-such a woman was given a portion of meat as charity, and I prepared it.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Bring it close, for it has reached its proper place,” and he ate some of it."],[20063,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever wears silk in this world, Allah will clothe him on the Day of Resurrection with a garment of fire, or a garment of His fire.\""],[20064,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever wears silk in this world, Allah will clothe him with a garment of fire.\""],[20065,"The Prophet ﷺ used to dislike that food be eaten until the heat of its steam had gone."],[20066,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took Safiyyah bt. Huyayy b. Akhtab captive from the Banu al-Nadir on the day of Khaybar, while she was a bride married to Kinanah b. Abi al-Huqayq."],[20067,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took Safiyyah bt. Huyayy captive from the Banu al-Nadir, and she was among what Allah granted him as spoil."],[20068,"A’ishah said “Safiyyah was called after the word safi (a special portion of the Prophet).” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2994)"],[20069,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ encamped at Khaybar while Safiyyah was a bride in her bridal finery. She saw in a dream as if the sun descended until it fell on her chest. She related that to her husband, and he said, \"By Allah, you desire nothing but this king who has come down upon us.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered it and struck off her husband's neck in execution. Some of the young men of the Prophet ﷺ then showed interest in marrying her, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw dates for them on a leather mat and said, \"Eat the wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah for Safiyyah.\""],[20070,"The Prophet ﷺ said to her, \"What is this greenness in your eyes?\" She said, \"I told my husband, 'I saw in what a sleeper sees a moon that fell into my lap,' and he slapped me and said, 'Do you want the king of Yathrib?'\" She said, \"And nothing was more hateful to me than the Messenger of Allah; he killed my father and my husband. But he kept apologizing to me and said, 'O Safiyyah, your father stirred up the Arabs and did such and such,' until that left my heart.\""],[20071,"The Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[20072,"The Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[20073,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[20074,"The Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[20075,"The Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[20076,"He informed him that the Prophet ﷺ ascertained that Safiyyah was free from pregnancy by a menstrual period."],[20077,"The Prophet ﷺ held a wedding feast for Safiyyah with saweeq and dates."],[20078,"It reached Safiyyah that Hafsah had said, “(You are) the daughter of a Jew,” so she wept. The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her while she was crying and said, “What is the matter with you?” She said, “Hafsah said to me that I am the daughter of a Jew.” The Prophet ﷺ said to her, “You are the daughter of a prophet, and your uncle is a prophet, and you are under (married to) a prophet—so in what does she boast over you?” Then he said, “Fear Allah, O Hafsah.”"],[20079,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was upset with Safiyyah over something. Safiyyah said to me, 'Would you like to make the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pleased with me? Then my day will be yours.' So I put on a veil of mine dyed with saffron and sprinkled it with water, then came and sat beside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said to me, 'Move away from me, for it is not your day.' I said, 'That is the bounty of Allah; He gives it to whom He wills,' and I told him the matter, and he became pleased with her."],[20080,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey when Safiyyah's camel became ill. Zaynab had an extra mount, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, 'Safiyyah's camel has become ill; would you give her a camel?' She said, 'Should I give to that Jewess?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry and boycotted her for the remainder of Dhu al-Hijjah, all of Muharram, Safar, and some days of Rabi', until she had packed up her belongings and her bed, thinking that he had no need of her. Then one day as she was sitting at midday, she saw his shadow approaching, and she put her bed and belongings back."],[20081,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in i'tikaf in the mosque. I came to him at night and talked with him, then I stood up to leave, and he stood up with me to escort me back. Her residence was in the house of Usamah b. Zayd. Two men of the Ansar passed by, and when they saw the Prophet ﷺ they hastened. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Slow down! It is Safiyyah bint Huyay.' They said, 'Glory be to Allah, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Satan runs through the son of Adam like blood, and I feared that he might cast something into your hearts'—or he said, 'evil.'"],[20082,"Safiyyah bint Huyay, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to me: I came to the Prophet ﷺ to talk with him while he was in i'tikaf in the mosque. He stood up with me one night to escort me to my house. Two men of the Ansar met him, and when they saw him they felt shy and turned back. He said, 'Come here; it is only Safiyyah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ.' They said, 'Allah forbid! Glory be to Allah.' He said, 'I am not telling you that you should think evil, but I know that Satan runs through a person like blood.'"],[20083,"Ali, the messenger of Allah, entered while I was crying, so he said, \"What is making you cry, O daughter of Huwayy?\" I said, \"It has reached me that Aisha and Hafsah are preferred over me and they say, 'We are better than her, we are the daughters of the cousin of the Messenger of Allah, and his wives.'\" He said, \"Did you not say, 'How can they be better than me when my father is Harun, my uncle is Musa, and my husband is Muhammad?\""],[20084,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'An army will surely attack this House, and when they are in a desert plain, the earth will swallow the middle of them. Then the first of them will call out to the last of them, and all of them will be swallowed up. None of them will escape except the fugitive who reports about them.'"],[20085,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'People will not cease attacking this House until an army comes to attack it. When they are in a desert plain, the first of them and the last of them will be swallowed up, and the middle of them will not escape.' It was said, 'What if there are among them those who are unwilling?' He said, 'Allah will resurrect them according to their intentions.'"],[20086,"Safiyyah bint Huyay, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that she came to visit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in i'tikaf in the mosque during the last ten days of Ramadan. She spoke with him for a while, then she stood up to leave, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up with her to escort her. When she reached near the door of the mosque, by the door of Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, two men of the Ansar passed by. They greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and then went on. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, 'Slow down! She is Safiyyah bint Huyay.' They said, 'Glory be to Allah, O Messenger of Allah,' and what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said weighed heavily on them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Satan reaches through a person to the extent of the blood, and I feared that he might cast something into your hearts.'"],[20087,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed me and made my emancipation my dower."],[20088,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came in to me while I had four thousand date pits in front of me, with which I was glorifying Allah. He said, 'O daughter of Huyay, what is this?' I said, 'I am glorifying Allah with them.' He said, 'I have glorified Allah since I stood at your head with more than this.' I said, 'Teach me, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Say: Glory be to Allah as many times as the number of things He has created.'"],[20089,"We went out for Hajj and passed by Madinah. We entered upon Safiyyah bint Huyay and asked her about beverages. She said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nabidh made in earthen jars.' Thus ends the hadith of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, ؓ ."],[20090,"Asma' bint Abi Bakr al-Siddiq died in the year seventy-three, a few nights after her son 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr. She was a sister of 'A'ishah through her father. The mother of Asma' bint Abi Bakr was Qutaylah bint 'Abd al-'Uzza b. 'Abd As'ad, of the Banu Malik b. Hasal. On the day she died, Asma' was one hundred years old. She was born twenty-seven years before the calendar, and seventeen years before the sending of the Prophet ﷺ. Asma' was born to Abu Bakr when he was twenty-one years old."],[20091,"that he should descend.\""],[20092,"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ used to wear saffron-dyed gowns while in ihram."],[20093,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was praying toward the corner, after he was commanded to proclaim openly what he was commanded, and he was reciting: \"{So which of the favors of your Lord will you deny?}\" while the polytheists were listening."],[20094,"\"We slaughtered a horse and ate it, we and the family of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[20095,"We performed Hajj with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Abu Bakr was with us. When we were at al-'Arj, we dismounted, with 'A'isha beside him and I beside my father. Abu Bakr sat waiting for his servant. Our mount and the mount of the Messenger of God ﷺ were one. The servant appeared without his camel. Abu Bakr said to him: \"Where is your camel?\" He said: \"I lost it last night.\" She said: \"One camel, and you lose it?\" He began to beat him while the Messenger of God ﷺ smiled and said: \"Look at this offender and what he is doing.\""],[20096,"The Prophet ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said: \"O people, the sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of God. They do not eclipse for the death of anyone or for his life. So when you see that, hasten to prayer, charity, and remembrance of God. I have seen among you fifty thousand or seventy thousand—Fulayh was uncertain—entering Paradise without reckoning, like the image of the moon on the night of the full moon.\" A man stood and said: \"Supplicate God to make me one of them.\" He said: \"O God, make him one of them. O people, you will not ask me about anything that has been revealed except that I will inform you of it.\" A man stood and said: \"Who is my father?\" He said: \"Your father is so-and-so,\" referring to the father to whom he was attributed."],[20097,"I heard Asma' bt. Abi Bakr say: \"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me while I was weighing something and counting.\" He said: \"O Asma', do not count, lest God count against you.\" Asma' said: \"After that day, I never counted or numbered anything that God created.\""],[20098,"Asma bint Abi Bakr said: \"O Messenger of God, I have no wealth except what al-Zubayr brings into his house. May I give small amounts from it?\" He said: \"Give small amounts as much as you are able, and do not withhold, lest God withhold from you.\""],[20099,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , saying, \"I do not possess anything except something which Zubair gives me.\" He said, \"Be humble and do not exaggerate, for it will be shown to you.\""],[20100,"I said: \"O Messenger of God, I have no wealth from which to give small amounts except what al-Zubayr brings into my house.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O Asma, give small amounts, and do not withhold, lest it be withheld from you.\""],[20101,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “A woman entered the Fire on account of her cat.”"],[20102,"She said on the night of Jamʿ: O my son, has the moon set? She was praying, and had alighted near Muzdalifah. I said: No. She prayed a little, then said: O my son, has the moon set? He said: The moon had set. I said: Yes. She said: Then depart. So we departed and went on with her until she threw the pebble at the Jamrah, then she returned and prayed the morning prayer at her lodging. I said to her: O you, you have gone very early in the dark. She said: “O my son, the Prophet of God ﷺ gave permission for the women’s litters.”"],[20103,"He said to her: O mother, the Commander of the Faithful has commended you to me. Do you have any need? She said: I have no need of you, and I am not your mother; rather, I am the mother of the crucified one. Wait, let me tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “In Thaqif there will emerge a liar and a destroyer.” As for the liar, we have already seen him – she meant al-Mukhtar – and as for the destroyer, it is you. Al-Hajjaj said: a destroyer of the hypocrites."],[20104,"Peace be upon you, O Abu Khubayb – he said it three times. I had forbidden you from this – he said it three times. You used to fast constantly and stand in prayer constantly, and maintain ties of kinship. This reached al-Hajjaj: the standing of Abd Allah b. Umar, so he had him brought down and threw him into the graves of the Jews. Then he sent to Asma bint Abi Bakr that she should come to him, and her sight had gone. She refused. So he sent to her: Either you come, or I will send someone to drag you by your forelocks. She said: By God, I will not come to you until you send someone to drag me by my forelocks. His messenger came back to him and told him. He said: O boy, hand me my sandals. He handed him his shoes, and he got up walking with a swagger until he came to her. He said: How do you see what God has done to the enemy of God? She said: I see that you ruined his worldly life for him, and he ruined your hereafter for you. As for what you used to taunt her about, the one with the two belts – indeed, I had two belts: one with which I covered the food of the Messenger of God ﷺ from ants, and one that women cannot do without. And I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Among Thaqif there is a destroyer and a liar.” As for the liar, we have come to know him; and as for the destroyer, you are the one. He said: Then he left."],[20105,"When al-Hajjaj entered upon her, it was said to her: This is the commander al-Hajjaj. She said: Indeed, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Among Thaqif there is a liar and a destroyer.” As for the liar, we have already seen him; and as for the destroyer, it is you."],[20106,"We entered upon Asma bint Abi Bakr and asked her about mut‘a. She said: “We practiced it during the lifetime of the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[20107,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: When a person enters his grave, his righteous deeds surround him – prayer and fasting. The angel comes to him from the direction of prayer and turns him back, and from the direction of fasting and turns him back. Then he calls to him: Sit up. So he sits up. He says to him: What do you say about this man? He said: Which man? He said: Muhammad. He said: By God, I do not know; I heard people saying something and I said it. The angel says: Upon that you lived, and upon that you died, and upon that you will be resurrected. He said: And a beast is prepared for him in his grave, black and dark, with a whip whose lash is a live coal. It strikes him as long as God wills; no one hears his voice except that he would pity him."],[20108,"When Ibn al-Zubayr was killed, she had something that the Prophet ﷺ had given her in a miscarriage. She lost it, so she ordered that it be searched for. When she found it, she fell down in prostration."],[20109,"She heard a woman ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, \"I have a co-wife, and I pretend from my husband what I do not actually receive, to anger her by that. Is there any sin on me in that?\" He said, \"The one who pretends to have been given what he was not given is like the one who wears two garments of falsehood.\""],[20110,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The believing sisters are Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ; Umm al-Fadl, the wife of al-Abbas; Asma' bt. Umays, the wife of Ja'far; and the wife of Hamzah—she is their sister through their mother.\""],[20111,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her while she had some spurge that she was crushing. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What are you doing with this?\" She said, \"O Prophet of Allah, I will give it to so-and-so to drink.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"It is a disease.\" Then he entered upon her while she had some senna with her. He said, \"What are you doing with this?\" She said, \"So-and-so will drink it.\" He said, \"If anything could ward off death, senna would ward it off.\""],[20113,"\"She gave birth at Dhul-Hulayfah, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered her to perform ghusl and enter ihram.\""],[20114,"I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"You are not like that.\""],[20115,"She gave birth to Muhammad b. Abi Bakr at Dhu al-Hulayfah. Abu Bakr asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he instructed him to tell her to perform ghusl and enter ihram."],[20116,"Al-Qa'nabi reported that 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad, who narrated from Mujahid, who narrated from Asma bint 'Umais, that she came to the Prophet ﷺ with the two sons of Ja'far. She said, \"The people have killed the sons of your brother.\" He said, \"Cover them for them.\""],[20117,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at her sons, the sons of Ja'far, and said, \"Why are their bodies so thin?\" She said, \"The evil eye afflicts them quickly; should I perform ruqyah for them?\" He said, \"With what?\" She presented words that had no harm, and he said, \"Perform ruqyah for them.\""],[20118,"When revelation came down upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would almost fall unconscious. One day it came down upon him while he was in 'Ali's lap, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Did you pray 'Asr, O 'Ali?\" He said, \"No, O Messenger of Allah.\" He called upon Allah, and He returned the sun for him until he prayed 'Asr. She said, \"I saw the sun rise after it had set, when it was returned, until he prayed 'Asr.\""],[20119,"'Ali proposed to me, and that reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he said, \"She should not harm Allah and His Messenger.\""],[20120,"'Umar said to Asma' bt. 'Umays, \"We preceded you in the Hijrah.\" She replied, \"Yes, by Allah, you did precede us, and we were among the barefoot and naked, while you were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—he taught your ignorant and instructed your learned, and commanded you to noble character.\""],[20121,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, some people claim that we are not among the female emigrants.\" He said, \"Whoever says that has lied. You have two emigrations: you emigrated to the Negus and you emigrated to me.\""],[20122,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Among the misfortune of a person in this world are three: a bad house, a bad wife, and a bad mount.\" She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is a bad house?\" He said, \"Its courtyard being narrow and its neighbors being wicked.\" It was said, \"What is a bad mount?\" He said, \"Its refusing to be ridden and its poor condition.\" It was said, \"What is a bad wife?\" He said, \"Her womb being barren and her character being bad.\""],[20123,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked her, \"What do you use as a laxative?\" She said, \"I used to use shubrum.\" He said, \"Hot, hot.\" She said, \"Then I used senna as a laxative.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If there were in anything a cure for death, it would be senna.\""],[20124,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Half of what is dug for my ummah of graves is from the evil eye.\""],[20125,"Asma bint 'Umays was a friend of Aisha, whom she prepared and presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as a wife along with me. We found nothing to drink except a small quantity of milk. The Prophet ﷺ drank from it and then handed it to the girl. She felt shy, so I said, \"Do not reject the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .\" The girl drank from it and then he said, \"Give it to your companions.\" We replied, \"We do not desire it.\" He said, \"Do not gather falsehood and hunger.\" I said, \"If any of us says that she desires something, is it considered falsehood?\" He said, \"Verily, falsehood is written as falsehood, even if it is a joke.\""],[20126,"\"What an evil servant is the one who fancies himself and becomes vain forgetting the Most Great, the Most High. What an evil servant is the one who forces and behaves hostility, forgetting the Compeller, the Most High. What an evil servant is the one who is heedless and diverted, forgetting about the graves and the trials. What an evil servant is the one who is violent and tyrannical, forgetting his beginnings or his end. What an evil servant is the one who seeks the world through the religion. What an evil servant is the one who seeks the religion through his desires. What an evil servant is the one who puts all hope in his own zeal. What an evil servant is the worshipper who is misled by his desire. What an evil servant is the one whose aspirations humiliate him.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2448)"],[20127,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her for some of his needs, then he left. So, she complained to him about her need. He said, \"How would it be for you if you were tested with a slave who has been granted control over the rivers of the earth and its fruits, and whoever follows him, he feeds him and clothes him, and whoever disobeys him, he withholds from him.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the slave girl is confined to the oven for an hour to bake bread, and I am almost tempted during my prayer, so what about us in that case?\" He said, \"Allah will protect the believers on that day with what He protects the angels from glorification. Indeed, there will be between his eyes a mark that each believer, whether literate or illiterate, will read.\""],[20128,"I went with my brother to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was wearing two bracelets of gold. He said: \"Would it please you for Allah to adorn you with two bracelets of fire?\" So I removed them and threw them away, and I do not know which of the people took them."],[20129,"The Prophet ﷺ recited this verse: \"Say: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins. Indeed, He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.\""],[20130,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the Dajjal and said: \"Before his emergence there will be three years when the sky withholds a third of its rain and the earth a third of its vegetation.\" Then he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[20131,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he saw a woman wearing two bracelets of gold. He said: \"Would it please you for Allah to adorn you with two bracelets of fire?\" She took them off her hand and threw them away, and I do not know who took them."],[20132,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “He has not fasted—the one who fasts perpetually.”"],[20133,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used not to shake hands with women."],[20134,"O Messenger of God, what is this good deed that we have been forbidden to disobey you in? He said: “That you do not wail.” I said: “O Messenger of God, the Banu so-and-so helped me mourn my paternal cousin so-and-so, and I must repay them.” He refused me, but I repeated it to him several times, and he permitted me to repay them. After repaying them, I never wailed again, nor did I wail otherwise, up to this very hour. No woman remained but she has wailed, except me."],[20135,"She pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day he took the pledge from the women. She leaned forward and stretched out her hand to pledge allegiance, but he withdrew his hand and said: “I do not shake hands with women; I only take their pledge verbally.” She said: I was wearing a garment and jewelry. He said: “O Asma!” I said: “At your service, O Messenger of God, and may you be granted happiness.” He said: “Would it please you to be branded with this jewelry?” I said: “And what is that, O Messenger of God?” He said: “Whoever wears gold, or adorns any of his children with something like a small earring or a locust leg, will be branded with it on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20136,"The Messenger of God ﷺ died while his armor, which he used to fight in, was pawned with a Jewish man for a measure of barley, which he had taken as food for his family."],[20137,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was invited to the funeral of a man from the Ansar. When the bier was placed down, the Prophet of God ﷺ stepped forward to pray over him, then turned and said: “Does your companion owe a debt?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of God, two dinars.” He said: “Pray over your companion.” Abu Qatadah said: “We will pay it on his behalf, O Prophet of God.” So he prayed over him."],[20138,"\"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ used to create a mixture of musk and saffron, and they would apply it to the lower parts of their hairline before becoming forbidden. Afterwards, they would continue to be forbidden in the same way.\""],[20139,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Ibn Umm Maktūm or Bilāl gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Bilāl or Ibn Umm Maktūm gives the call.” It was only that one of them would give the call, and the other would then ascend. We would take him by the hand and say: as you are, until we took the pre-dawn meal."],[20140,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession regarding it, so enter upon her and ask her. He said: We entered upon her, and she was a large woman, and she said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession regarding it.\""],[20141,"'Abd Allah b. Maslamah al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; my father narrated to me from Hisham b. 'Urwah, from his father, from Asma' bint Abi Bakr, who said: My mother came to me while she was a polytheist during the period of the Quraysh truce, when they made a treaty with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and for its duration. I sought a ruling from the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come to me, and she is desirous [of my kindness]. Should I maintain ties with her?\" He said, \"Yes, maintain ties with your mother.\""],[20142,"I heard Asma' bint Abi Bakr say: My mother came from Makkah to Madinah during the Quraysh truce, and she was a polytheist. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come to me, and she is desirous [of my kindness]. Should I maintain ties with her?\" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to her, \"Maintain ties with her.\""],[20143,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come to me, and she is desirous [of my kindness] and fearful. Should I maintain ties with her?\" He said, \"Maintain ties with her.\""],[20144,"My mother came to me while she was a desirous polytheist. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come while she is a desirous polytheist. Should I maintain ties with her?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Maintain ties with her.\""],[20145,"He heard Asma' bint Abi Bakr say: My mother came to me while she was desirous [of my kindness], during the period of the Quraysh [treaty]. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should I maintain ties with her?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[20146,"\"I prepared a traveling provision for the Prophet ﷺ in the house of Abu Bakr when he wanted to emigrate to Madinah.\" She said: We could not find anything with which to tie his provision bag or his water skin. I said to Abu Bakr, \"By Allah, I find nothing to tie it with except my waist wrapper.\" He said, \"Split it into two, tie the water skin with one, and the provision bag with the other.\" She did so, and for that reason she was called Dhat al-Nitaqayn (She of the Two Waist Wrappers)."],[20147,"Asma' [said]: \"When I gave birth to 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr, he was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he wiped over him and named him 'Abd Allah. Then later, when he was seven or eight years old, he came to pledge allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ—al-Zubayr had ordered him to do that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled when he saw him approaching and accepted his pledge.\""],[20148,"\"We ate horse meat during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[20149,"\"We slaughtered a horse during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ate it.\""],[20150,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so the Messenger of God ﷺ stood to pray. He made a long standing, then a long bowing, then raised his head, then prostrated, then stood for a long time, then raised his head, then prostrated, then stood but not as long as the previous standing, then bowed but not as long as the previous bowing, then raised his head and prostrated, then addressed the people and said: “There is nothing I had not been shown except that I have now seen it, even Paradise and Hellfire.” Then he said: “It has been revealed to me that you will be tested in your graves with a trial close to the trial of the false messiah.”"],[20151,"“Will you finish with this body and give us permission to bury it?” He said: “We still have need of it.” She said to her two clients: “Take me by the hand. I testify that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘There will emerge from Thaqif a liar and a destroyer. So see which of the two you are.’” He said: “O God, a destroyer, not a liar.”"],[20152,"“The Prophet ﷺ granted al-Zubayr a parcel of palm trees.”"],[20153,"Zaid bin Amr bin Nufail used to stand by the Kāba during the times of ignorance and press his back against it, saying, \"O people of Quraysh, I do not find anyone on this earth who follows the religion of Ibrahim except me.\" He had abandoned worshiping idols and eating what was sacrificed to them. He used to set free the captive animals that were brought for slaughtering. Amr bin Zaid bin Nufail said..."],[20154,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about Waraqah b. Nawfal, and he said: “He will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone.”"],[20155,"She used to give on behalf of her household, free and slave alike, at the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, two mudds of wheat or one sa' of dates, using the mudd by which they measured their staples."],[20156,"From Asma' bint Abi Bakr: “They used to give zakat al-fitr at the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ using the mudd by which the household measured its staples, and all the people of Madinah did that.”"],[20157,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “No one is more jealous than God.”"],[20158,"She heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Nothing is more jealous than God, Blessed and Exalted.”"],[20159,"That his mother Aisha bint Abu Bakr told him that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say from the pulpit, \"There is nothing more unjust than Allah.\""],[20160,"She heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Nothing is more jealous than God.”"],[20161,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"No one is more able to be angry than Allah.\""],[20162,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say on the pulpit: “No one is more jealous than God. That is why He forbade indecencies, both open and hidden.”"],[20163,"When she prepared tharid, she would cover it until its steam subsided, then she said: “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘It is greater in blessing.’”"],[20164,"My mother came to me during the time of Quraysh while she was still a polytheist. They made a pact with the Prophet ﷺ during their time. I asked the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"O Messenger of Allah, my mother came to me while she still desires the polytheistic ways. Should I maintain ties with her?\" He replied, \"Yes, maintain ties with your mother.\""],[20165,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed, the believer sits in his grave when those who witnessed his burial turn away from him. It is said to him: 'A man called Muhammad—who is he?' If he was a believer, he says: 'He is the servant of God and His Messenger.' It is said to him: 'Sleep; may your eyes sleep.' And if he was not a believer, he says: 'By God, I do not know. I heard people saying something, so I said it, and they plunged in, so I plunged in.' It is said to him: 'Sleep; may your eyes never sleep.'\""],[20166,"From his grandmother—I do not know whether it was Asma' bt. Abi Bakr or Su'da bt. 'Awf—that the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon Duba'a bt. al-Zubayr b. 'Abd al-Muttalib and said: \"What prevents you, O aunt, from performing Hajj?\" She said: \"I am a sick woman, and I fear being detained.\" He said: \"Enter ihram and stipulate: 'My place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.'\""],[20167,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ mention the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary and say: \"A hundred riders can shade themselves in the shade of one of its branches\"—or he said: \"And a hundred riders can travel in the shade of one of its branches. In it are couches of gold, and its fruits are like large jars.\""],[20168,"\"When the Messenger of God ﷺ set out and Abu Bakr set out with him, Abu Bakr carried with him five thousand dirhams or six thousand dirhams and departed with them.\" She said: \"My grandfather Abu Quhafa entered upon us, and he had lost his sight. He said: 'By God, I think he has afflicted you by taking his wealth with him.' She said: 'I said: Not at all, O father. He has left us abundant good.' She said: 'I took some stones and placed them in a niche in the house where my father used to put his wealth. Then I placed a cloth over them. Then I took his hand and said: Put your hand on this wealth.' She said: 'He put his hand and said: There is no harm if he left you this wealth. Then he raised his hand and said: If he left you this, he has done well, and in this you have sufficiency.' She said: 'By God, he did not leave us anything, but I wanted to calm the old man with that.'\""],[20169,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ stopped at Dhu Tuwa, Abu Quhafa said to a daughter of his from his youngest children: \"O my little daughter, show me Abu Qubays.\" She said—and he had lost his sight—\"so I brought him up to it.\" He said: \"O my daughter, what do you see?\" She said: \"I see a gathered black mass.\" He said: \"That is the cavalry.\" She said: \"And I see a man moving among that black mass, coming and going.\" He said: \"That, O my daughter, is the commander who directs the cavalry. Hurry me to my house.\" She said: \"The cavalry met him before he reached it.\" She said: \"On the girl's neck was a necklace of silver, and a man met her and snatched it from her neck. When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered Makkah and entered the mosque, Abu Bakr brought his father, leading him. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw him, he said: 'Why did you not leave the old man in his house until I came to him?' Abu Bakr said: 'O Messenger of God, he is more deserving of walking to you.' He seated him before him, then wiped his chest and said to him: 'Submit (become Muslim).' His head was like a white-flowered plant. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Change this whiteness of his hair.' Then Abu Bakr stood and took his sister by the hand and said: 'I adjure you by God and by Islam to return my sister's necklace.' No one answered him. He said: 'O my little sister, count your necklace as a loss, for by God, trustworthiness among people today is scarce.'\""],[20170,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Abu Quhafa: \"Submit (become Muslim), and you will be safe.\""],[20171,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do not count, lest it be counted against you.\""],[20172,"Ibn Abbas spoke the truth: \"We set out with the Messenger of God ﷺ as pilgrims, but we turned it into an Umrah and dissolved the entire state of consecration, until incense burners wafted between the men and the women.\""],[20173,"Ibn Abbas spoke the truth: \"We arrived as pilgrims, and the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered us to come out of consecration, so we came out of it completely, until incense burners wafted between the men and the women.\""],[20174,"\"O Messenger of God, I have nothing except what al-Zubayr brings into my house. May I spend from it?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Spend, and do not withhold, lest it be withheld from you.\""],[20175,"I said: \"O Messenger of God, I have no wealth except what al-Zubayr brings into my house.\" He said: \"O Asma, give and donate, and do not withhold, lest it be withheld from you.\""],[20176,"I said: \"O Messenger of God, by God, I have nothing except from what al-Zubayr brings into my house, and so I give from it?\" He said: \"Do not withhold, lest it be withheld from you.\""],[20177,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do not withhold, lest it be withheld from you.\""],[20178,"I said: \"O Messenger of God, I have nothing except what al-Zubayr brings into his house. May I give from it?\" He said: \"Give, and do not withhold, lest it be withheld from you.\""],[20179,"\"I used to serve al-Zubayr, and he had a horse which I tended. There was no service harder for me than tending the horse: I used to gather grass for it and care for it. Then I obtained a servant when captives came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he gave me a servant, who relieved me of tending the horse and removed that burden from me.\""],[20180,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I will be at my Hawd (cistern) until I see who among you comes to me. Some people will be turned away from me, and I will say: 'O Lord, my community, my community!' It will be said: 'Do you know what they did after you? By God, they kept turning back on their heels.'\" Ibn Abi Mulaikah used to say: \"O God, we seek refuge with You from turning back on our heels or changing our religion.\""],[20181,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the eclipse prayer. He stood and prolonged the standing, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, then raised his head, prostrated and prolonged the prostration, then raised his head, prostrated and prolonged the prostration, then finished. He said: \"Paradise was brought so close to me that if I had stretched out for it, I would have brought you a bunch of its bunches. And Hellfire was brought so close to me that I said: 'O Lord, and I am with them?' Then I saw a beautiful woman being scratched by a cat. I said: 'What is the matter with this one?' They said: 'She imprisoned it until it died of hunger: she neither fed it nor let it go to eat.'\" Nafi' said: \"I think he said: 'from the herbage or the plants of the earth.'\""],[20182,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: A beggar comes to me and I give him charity from the house of al-Zubayr without his permission? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Give a little, and do not withhold, lest it be withheld from you.”"],[20183,"I said: O Messenger of God, what of the wealth of al-Zubayr is lawful for me? He said: “Fresh dates,” meaning food."],[20184,"Say to her: al-Hajjaj says to you: Set aside whatever of your own wealth from the wealth of ʿAbd Allah b. al-Zubayr. She said: Would he do that to the son of Asmaʾ’? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “From this quarter of Thaqif shall come two men, one of whom is a liar and the other a destroyer.” As for the liar, we have already known him; and I think the destroyer is none but him. So I returned to him and informed him, and he did not dislike that."],[20185,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: “Whoever among you believes in God and the Last Day, let her not raise her head until we have raised our heads,” lest they see the private parts of the men because their waist-wraps were short; at that time they used to wear this striped cloak."],[20186,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O assembly of women, whoever among you believes in God and the Last Day, let no woman raise her head until the men have raised their heads.” That was because their waist-wraps were short, for fear that their private parts might become exposed."],[20187,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O assembly of believing women, let no woman raise her head before the imam raises his head,” because of the tightness of the men’s garments."],[20188,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying to the women on the pulpit, \"Whoever among you believes in Allah and the Last Day, let her not raise her head until the men raise their heads.\" She said, \"Because there was mutual hostility between them, so they would wear clothes that would cover their bodies and uncover their private parts.\""],[20189,"From Abu ʿUbayd Allah or ʿAbd Allah, the freedman of Asmaʾ bt. Abi Bakr, that she brought out to him a jubbah of Tayalisa fabric made of silk brocade and said: “This is the jubbah of the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he passed away, it was with ʿAʾishah; when ʿAʾishah passed away, I took it, and it is with me. She used to wash it for the sick, seeking healing through it.”"],[20190,"We came with Asmaʾ to Mina at night, and she said: “We used to do that with one better than you,” meaning the Prophet ﷺ."],[20191,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ used to wear this in war.”"],[20192,"Asmaʾ came with some slave girls of hers, and her sight had gone. She said: Where is al-Hajjaj? We said: He is not here. She said: Tell him to order these bones for us, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbidding mutilation. We said: When he comes, we will tell him. She said: When he comes, inform him that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There shall come forth in Thaqif a liar and a destroyer.”"],[20193,"No, by God, he was not a hypocrite, and he used to fast constantly and stand in prayer constantly. He said: Be quiet, for you are an old woman who has become senile. She said: I have not become senile since I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “From Thaqif will emerge a liar and a destroyer.” As for the liar, we have already seen him – she meant al-Mukhtar – and as for the destroyer, it is you. Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah added, so al-Hajjaj said in his version: the destroyer of the hypocrites."],[20194,"“I was once on a piece of land that the Prophet of God ﷺ had allotted to Abu Salama and al-Zubayr from the land of al-Nadir. Al-Zubayr had gone out with the Messenger of God ﷺ. We had a Jewish neighbor who slaughtered a sheep and cooked it. I smelled its aroma, and the smell of meat affected me as nothing had ever affected me before, while I was pregnant with a daughter of mine called Khadija. I could not bear it, so I went and entered upon his wife to borrow some fire from her, in the hope that she might feed me, though I had no need of fire. When I smelled its aroma and saw it, my desire increased, so I put it out. Then I came a second time to borrow fire for the same reason, then a third time. When I saw that, I sat down weeping and calling upon God. Then the Jewish woman’s husband came and said: Did anyone enter upon you? She said: No, except the Arab woman who came to borrow fire. He said: Then I will never eat of it unless you send some of it to her. So she sent me a qadha, and there was nothing on earth more pleasing to me than that morsel. Ibn Bukayr said: “Al-qadha (the bowl) is araqa (a portion of meat).”"],[20195,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: “Do not hoard, lest God withhold from you.”"],[20196,"She visited her sister Aisha while al-Zubayr was away, and the Prophet ﷺ entered and smelled perfume. He said: “What is wrong with a woman that she should not perfume herself when her husband is absent?”"],[20197,"“I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbidding mutilation.”"],[20198,"“I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbidding mutilation.”"],[20199,"The Prophet ﷺ used to come to us in Makkah twice every day. Then one day he came to us at noon. I said, \"O father, this is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said, \"May my father and mother be sacrificed for him. Nothing has brought him at this hour except a matter.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Do you realize that Allah has granted me permission to emigrate?\" Abu Bakr said, \"Then companionship, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Companionship.\" Abu Bakr said, \"I have two riding camels which I have been feeding for such and such a time in anticipation of this day. Take one of them.\" He said, \"For its price, O Abu Bakr.\" He said, \"For its price, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, if you wish.\" She said, \"We prepared provisions for them, then she tore her waist-wrap and tied it with part of it. They set out and stayed in the cave on Mount Thawr. When they reached it, Abu Bakr entered the cave before him and did not leave any hole in it without inserting his finger into it, fearing that a poisonous creature might be in it. Quraysh went out when they missed the two of them, seeking them, and they placed a reward of one hundred camels for the Prophet ﷺ. They went out wandering in the mountains of Makkah until they reached the mountain where the two of them were. Abu Bakr said to a man he saw facing the cave, \"O Messenger of Allah, he can see us.\" He said, \"No, indeed, angels are covering us with their wings.\" That man sat down and urinated facing the cave. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"If he could see us, he would not have done this.\" They stayed for three nights, while 'Amir b. Fuhayrah, the freed slave of Abu Bakr, pastured Abu Bakr's flock for them, then set out from them in the last part of the night and arrived among the shepherds in their grazing grounds at morning. He would go out with them and walk in a bowed manner, then when it became dark he would return with the flock to the two of them, so that the shepherds thought he was with them. Meanwhile 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr would remain in Makkah during the day gathering news, then come to the two of them when it became dark and inform them, then set out from them in the last part of the night and reach Makkah as if he had spent the night there. Then they left the cave and took the coastal route. Abu Bakr would walk in front of him, and when he feared an attack from behind, he would walk behind him. His journey continued like that. Abu Bakr was a well-known man among the people. When someone met him, he would say to Abu Bakr, \"Who is this with you?\" He would say, \"A guide who guides me,\" meaning guidance in religion, while the other man thought he meant a trail guide. When they reached the houses of Qudayd, which was on their coastal route, a man came to the gathering of Banu Mudlij and said, \"I have seen two riders heading toward the coast, and I think one of them is the man of Quraysh whom they are seeking.\" Suraqah b. Malik said, \"Those two riders are from those we sent out in search of him. Comfort the people.\" Then he called his slave girl and whispered to her, ordering her to bring out his horse and to lower his spear but not to stand it up until he came to his resting place at such and such a spot. Then he came to her, mounted his horse, and went out in pursuit of them. Suraqah said, \"I drew near to them until I could hear the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then I spurred the horse and it stumbled on its nose. I took out divining arrows from my quiver and cast them: should I harm him or not? 'Do not harm him' came out. My soul refused until I followed him and caught up with him at a similar spot. The horse stumbled again and I took out his hand once more and cast the arrows: should I harm him or not? 'Do not harm him' came out. My soul refused until, when I was at a similar spot, I feared that something like what had befallen me would befall me again. So I called out to him and said, 'I see that you will have a great affair. Stop so that I may speak with you.' The Prophet ﷺ stopped. He asked him to write for him a guarantee of safety. He ordered him to write for him, and he wrote for him.\" Suraqah said, \"On the day of Hunayn, I came with the document and took it out and called out, 'I am Suraqah.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'A day of faithfulness.'\" Suraqah said, \"I never likened his leg in its stirrups except to the heart of a palm tree. I mentioned something to ask him, saying, 'O Messenger of Allah, I am a man with livestock. The watering troughs are filled with water, and the animals drink, and some water remains in the troughs, and then stray camels come to it. Is there any reward for me in that?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Yes, in every living being with a warm liver there is reward.'\""],[20200,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about menstrual blood that gets on a garment. He said, \"She should scrape it off with water, then sprinkle it, and pray in it.\""],[20201,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik, from Hisham b. 'Urwah, from Fatimah bt. al-Mundhir, from Asma' bt. Abi Bakr, that she said: A woman asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about one of us if blood from menstruation gets on her garment? What should she do?\" He said, \"If blood from menstruation gets on one of your garments, let her scrape it off, then sprinkle it with water, then pray.\""],[20202,"That she asked the Prophet ﷺ about menstrual blood that gets on a garment. He said, \"Rub it off, then scrape it with water, then sprinkle it.\""],[20203,"That she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about menstrual blood that gets on a garment. He said, \"Rub it off, then scrape it with water, then sprinkle it.\""],[20204,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a garment that gets blood from menstruation on it. He said, \"Let her rub it off, then scrape it with water, then pray in it.\""],[20205,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, one of us gets menstrual blood on her garment. What should she do with it?\" He said, \"She should rub it off, then scrape it with water.\""],[20206,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a garment that gets blood from menstruation on it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Let her rub it off, then scrape it, then sprinkle it, then pray in it.\""],[20207,"A woman asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying, \"One of us gets menstrual blood on her garment.\" He said, \"Let her rub it off, then scrape it, then sprinkle it with water, then pray in it.\""],[20208,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about menstrual blood that gets on one of our garments. He said, \"Take it and rub it off, then scrape it, and sprinkle the rest of your garment.\""],[20209,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about menstrual blood that gets on a garment. He said, \"Rub it off, then scrape it with water, then sprinkle it and pray in it.\""],[20210,"A woman asked the Prophet ﷺ: \"One of us gets menstrual blood on her garment.\" He said, \"Let her rub it off, then scrape it with water, then pray in it.\""],[20211,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us menstruates in her garment and sees the blood. He said: \"When one of you sees that in her garment, let her scratch it off with water, then sprinkle it, and pray in it.\""],[20212,"\"We slaughtered a horse during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we ate its meat.\""],[20213,"\"We had a horse during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so we slaughtered it and ate its meat.\""],[20214,"\"We had a horse during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so we slaughtered it and ate it.\""],[20215,"\"We slaughtered a horse during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were in Madinah, and we ate it.\""],[20216,"\"We slaughtered a horse during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we ate it.\""],[20217,"\"We slaughtered a horse during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we ate it.\""],[20218,"\"We ate horse meat during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[20219,"\"We had a horse during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so we slaughtered it and ate it.\""],[20220,"A woman from the Ansar came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have married one of our young girls, and she was ill, so her hair became torn; shall we add hair extensions to her? He said: \"May Allah curse the one who adds hair extensions and the one who has them added.\""],[20221,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he was asked about joining hair, and he cursed the one who adds and the one who has it added."],[20222,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated from Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad Ad-Darawardi from Hisham bin 'Urwah from Fatimah bint Al-Mundhir from Asma bint Abi Bakr that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"Indeed, my daughter is newlywed and she has been afflicted with measles, causing her hair to come out in patches. Should I use hair extensions?\" He ﷺ said, \"May Allah curse the one who gets hair extensions and the one who gives the extensions.\""],[20223,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, my daughter is a bride, and she has been afflicted by this sore, so her hair has become torn; shall I add a hairpiece for her? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah curse the one who adds hair extensions and the one who has them added.\""],[20224,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Prophet of God, my daughter is a bride and she has been stricken with measles, so her hair has fallen out. May I join hair extensions to it?” He said, “God has cursed the one who attaches hair extensions and the one who has them attached.”"],[20225,"“The Prophet ﷺ cursed the one who attaches hair extensions and the one who has them attached.” [Chapter]"],[20226,"The sun was eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so I entered upon A’ishah in her chamber while the Prophet ﷺ was praying with the people. I said, “O A’ishah, what is wrong with the people?” She said, “Glory be to God,” and she gestured with her hand. I said, “A sign?” She said, “Glory be to God,” and she gestured with her head, meaning yes. Abu al-Nu‘man also nodded with his head."],[20227,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us from Malik. And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Abd al-Hakam narrated to us: Malik b. Anas and Mufaddal b. Fadalah narrated to us from Hisham b. ‘Urwah, from Fatimah bt. al-Mundhir, from Asma’ bt. Abi Bakr, who said: I came to A’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, when the sun was eclipsed, and the people were standing in prayer, and she too was standing. I said, “What is wrong with the people?” She gestured with her hand toward the sky and said, “Glory be to God.” I said, “A sign?” She gestured, meaning yes. She said: I stood until I nearly fainted, and I began pouring water over my head. The Messenger of God ﷺ praised God and then said, “There is nothing that I had not seen before except that I have seen it in this station of mine, even Paradise and Hellfire. It has been revealed to me that you will be tested in the graves with a trial like or close to the trial of the Dajjal” — I do not know which of these she said. “One of you will be approached and asked, ‘What knowledge do you have of this man?’ As for the believer or the one who is certain — I do not know which she said — he will say, ‘Muhammad is the Messenger of God ﷺ. He came to us with clear proofs and guidance, and we responded, believed, and followed.’ Then it will be said to him, ‘Sleep righteously; we already knew that you were a believer.’ As for the hypocrite or the doubter — I do not know which Asma’ said — he will say, ‘I do not know; I heard people saying something, so I said it.’”"],[20228,"She said: The sun was eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so I entered the mosque while the Messenger of God ﷺ was praying with the people. I said to A’ishah, “What is wrong with the people?” She said, “Glory be to God,” and she nodded her head toward the sky. I said, “A sign?” She nodded her head, meaning yes. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood and prolonged the standing until dizziness came over me. I approached the water-skin, opened its mouth, and began pouring water over my head. The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed until the sun cleared, and some women of the Ansar made noise, so I silenced them. I said, “O A’ishah, what did the Messenger of God ﷺ do?” She said, “He praised God and extolled Him, then said: ‘Now then, there is nothing that I had not seen except that I have seen it in this station of mine, even Paradise and Hellfire. It has been revealed to me that you will be tested in your graves with a trial close to or like the trial of the Dajjal. One of you will be approached in his grave and asked, “What do you say about this man who was among you?” As for the believer, he will say, “He is Muhammad, the Messenger of God. He came to us with clear proofs and guidance, and we responded and followed.” Then it will be said to him, “We already knew that you used to say that, so sleep righteously.” As for the hypocrite or the doubter, he will say, “I do not know.” Then it will be said to him, “May you never know,” and his grave will be constricted for him.’”"],[20229,"I came to A’ishah and the people were standing and she was praying. I said, “What is wrong with the people?” She gestured with her hand toward the sky and said, “Glory be to God.” I said, “A sign?” She gestured with her head, meaning yes. She said: I stood until faintness nearly overcame me, and I began pouring water over my head. She said: When the Prophet ﷺ finished, he praised God ﷻ and extolled Him, and said, “There is nothing that I had not seen except that I have seen it in this station of mine, even Paradise and Hellfire. It has been revealed to me that you will be tested in the graves with a trial like or close to — I do not know which Asma’ said — the trial of the Messiah the Dajjal. One of you will be approached and asked, ‘What knowledge do you have of this man?’ The believer or the one who is certain — I do not know which Asma’ said — will say, ‘He is Muhammad, the Messenger of God. He came to us with clear proofs and guidance, and we responded and followed.’ Then it will be said, ‘We already knew that you were a believer in him,’ saying it three times. As for the hypocrite or the doubter — I do not know which Asma’ said — he will say, ‘I heard people saying something, so I said it.’”"],[20230,"I came to A’ishah and the people were standing and she was praying. I said, “What is wrong with the people?” She gestured with her hand toward the sky and said, “Glory be to God.” I said, “A sign?” She gestured with her head, meaning yes. I stood until faintness nearly overcame me, and I began pouring water over my head. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ praised God and extolled Him as He deserves, and said, “There is nothing that I was shown except that I saw it in this station of mine, even Paradise and Hellfire. It has been revealed to me that you will be tested in the graves with a trial like or close to — I do not know which Asma’ said — the trial of the Messiah the Dajjal. One of you will be approached and asked, ‘What knowledge do you have of this man?’ As for the believer, he will say, ‘Muhammad is the Messenger of God ﷺ. He came to us with clear proofs and guidance, and we responded and followed.’ Then it will be said, ‘Sleep righteously, for we already knew that you believed in God.’ As for the hypocrite or the doubter — I do not know which she said — he will say, ‘I do not know; I heard people saying something, so I said it.’”"],[20231,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us: ‘Abd al-‘Aziz b. Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us from Hisham b. ‘Urwah, from Fatimah bt. al-Mundhir, from Asma’ bt. Abi Bakr: “The Prophet ﷺ commanded them to free slaves when the sun was eclipsed.”"],[20232,"“The Prophet ﷺ commanded the freeing of slaves at the eclipse of the sun.”"],[20233,"“We used to be commanded to free slaves at the eclipse of the sun.”"],[20234,"From ‘Urwah and Fatimah bt. al-Mundhir that they said: Asma’ bt. Abi Bakr set out when she emigrated while she was pregnant with ‘Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr. She arrived at Quba’ and gave birth to ‘Abd Allah there. Then when she had given birth, she went out to the Messenger of God ﷺ so that he could chew a date for him. “The Messenger of God ﷺ took him from her and placed him in his lap. Then he called for a date.” A’ishah said: We waited for a while looking for it before we found it. “He chewed it and then placed it in his mouth.” The first thing that entered his stomach was the saliva of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Asma’ said: “Then he wiped him, prayed over him, and named him ‘Abd Allah. Then later, when he was seven or eight years old, he came to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ. Al-Zubayr had ordered him to do that. The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled when he saw him coming toward him, and then he accepted his pledge.” [Chapter]"],[20235,"A woman asked the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I have a neighboring wife — meaning a co-wife — and she disliked saying co-wife. Is there any sin on me if I pretend to have been given what I have not been given?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The one who pretends to have been given what he has not been given is like the one who wears two garments of falsehood.”"],[20236,"O Messenger of Allah, I have a husband, and I have a neighbor woman. Is there any sin upon me if I pretend to have been given by my husband what he has not given me? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “The one who pretends to have been given what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood.”"],[20237,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a co-wife. Is there any sin upon me if I pretend to have received from my husband what he does not give me? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who pretends to have been given what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood.”"],[20238,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The one who pretends to have been given what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood.”"],[20239,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who pretends to have been given what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood.”"],[20240,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The one who pretends to have been given what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood.”"],[20241,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who pretends to have been given what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood.” A chapter."],[20242,"\"When a woman in her menstrual period was brought to her, she would order water to be poured on her and she would say, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Cool her down with water, for it is from the heat of Hellfire.'"],[20243,"When a woman who was feverish was brought to her, she would call for water and pour it between her and her sides, and she would say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to cool it with water, and he said: “It is from the heat of Hell.”"],[20244,"A feverish woman would be brought to her, and she would call for water and pour it on her side, and she would say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Cool it with water,” and he said: “It is from the heat of Hell.”"],[20245,"When a woman who was feverish was brought to Asma’, she would pray for her, take water, and pour it between her and her sides, and she said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to cool it with water.”"],[20246,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us from Malik. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ‘Abdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us: Malik narrated to us from Hisham b. ‘Urwah, from Fatimah bt. al-Mundhir, that Asma’ bt. Abi Bakr, when a woman who was feverish was brought to her, she would pray for her, take water, and pour it between her and her sides, and she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water.”"],[20247,"Asma’ bt. Abi Bakr would be brought a feverish woman who was ill, she would pray for her, take water, and pour it between her and her sides, and she said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her to cool it with water.”"],[20248,"A feverish woman would be brought to her, and she would ask for water and pour it over her, and she would say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to cool it with water.”"],[20249,"\"When a menstruating woman was brought to her, she would order water to be poured over her and said, 'The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said: 'Indeed, fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it down with water.'\""],[20250,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “Spend, O Asmā’, and give small gifts like this and like this and like this, and do not count, lest God count against you.”"],[20251,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Give generously and spend and give small gifts, and do not count, lest He count against you, and do not withhold, lest He withhold from you.”"],[20252,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “Spend and give small gifts, and do not count, lest it be counted against you.” [Chapter]"],[20253,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ in a dream after his death, and I saw him saying: “Has the Qur’an been altered, O Asmā’?” I said: “It is so, by my father and mother—the altered and the upright.” He repeated that to me several times, each time I saying: “By my father and mother—the altered and the upright.” Then he said to me: “How are your sons?” I said: “O Messenger of God, they are seized with a severe seizure.” I saw him look toward one of his wives, as if she were Ḥafṣah bint ʿUmar, and he said: “Give her a cure for her two sons. As for death, I do not cure from it.” I saw her give me a black seed like black cumin or like leek seed, red earth, and a string of pearls. She said: “So we, whenever anyone among the children of Asmā’ in all the tribes falls ill, a bowl is taken for him and filled with water, then red earth, leek seed, black cumin, and a string of pearls are put in it, then that water is poured over him.”"],[20254,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ in a dream after his death, and I saw him saying: “Has the Qur’an been altered, O Asmā’?” I said: “It is so, by my father and mother—the altered and the upright.” He repeated that to me several times, each time I saying: “By my father and mother—the altered and the upright.” Then he said to me: “How are your sons?” I said: “O Messenger of God, they are seized with a severe seizure.” I saw him look toward one of his wives, as if she were Ḥafṣah bint ʿUmar, and he said: “Give her a cure for her two sons. As for death, I do not cure from it.” I saw her give me a black seed like black cumin or like leek seed, red earth, and a string of pearls. She said: “So we, whenever anyone among the children of Asmā’ in all the tribes falls ill, a bowl is taken for him and filled with water, then red earth, leek seed, black cumin, and a string of pearls are put in it, then that water is poured over him.”"],[20255,"My mother came to me while she was a polytheist, and I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for permission to maintain ties with her. He said: “Maintain ties with her.”"],[20256,"My mother came to me while she was a polytheist during the time of Quraysh and the treaty they had made with the Messenger of God ﷺ. I said: “O Messenger of God, my mother has come to me, and she is desirous [of my kindness]; shall I maintain ties with her?” He said: “Yes, maintain ties with your mother.”"],[20257,"My mother came to me during the time of Quraysh, and she was a polytheist. I asked the Prophet ﷺ: “Shall I maintain ties with her?” He said: “Yes.” [Chapter]"],[20258,"When ʿAbdullāh b. al-Zubayr was born, he was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he wiped him and prayed over him and named him ʿAbdullāh. Then he came later, when he was seven or eight years old, to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ; al-Zubayr had ordered him to do that. The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled when he saw him approaching, and he accepted his pledge. [Chapter]"],[20259,"“We broke our fast on a cloudy day at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then the sun appeared.” I (one of the narrators) said to Hisham: \"Were they commanded to make up for that day?\" He said: \"It had to be made up.\" (According to Hisham's opinion). (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1674)"],[20260,"“We broke the fast during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ on a cloudy day, then the sun appeared.” It was said to Hishām: “Were they ordered to make it up?” He said: “It is unavoidable.”"],[20261,"I heard a woman asking the Messenger of God ﷺ. She said: “O Messenger of God, I married off my daughter, and she was afflicted by this sore—smallpox or measles—and her hair fell out. She has now recovered, and her husband is urging us regarding her, but there is no hair on her head. Shall we put something on her head to beautify her with it?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “God has cursed the woman who attaches hair extensions and the one who asks for it.”"],[20262,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ while a woman was asking him. She said: “O Messenger of God, I married off my daughter, and she was afflicted by this sore—smallpox or measles—and her hair fell out. Then she recovered, and her husband is urging us regarding her, but there is no hair on her head. Shall we put something on her head to beautify her with it?” He said: “God has cursed the woman who attaches hair extensions and the one who asks for it.”"],[20263,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed the woman who attaches hair extensions and the one who asks for it."],[20264,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a woman asked him about menstrual blood that gets on her clothes. He said, \"Wash it with water, then sprinkle the rest of your garment, and pray in it.\""],[20265,"We used to pay Zakat al-Fitr during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with the mudd of the food we ate."],[20266,"The Prophet ﷺ was alarmed on the day the sun eclipsed. He took a cloak and put it on until he caught a chill. He stood with the people for a very long standing: he would stand, then bow, then rise. If someone came after he had risen, he would not have known that he had bowed anything, nor would he have thought to himself that he had bowed, because of the length of the standing. I began looking at the woman who was older than me and the woman who was sicker than me, standing, and I said, \"I am more entitled to endure the long standing.\""],[20267,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever has a sacrificial animal with him, let him remain in ihram. Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him exit ihram.\" I did not have a sacrificial animal, so I exited ihram. Al-Zubayr had one, so he did not exit ihram. I put on my regular clothes and came and sat beside al-Zubayr. He said, \"Get away from me.\" I said, \"Do you fear that I will pounce on you?\""],[20268,"We went out with the Prophet ﷺ pronouncing talbiyah for Hajj. He said to us, \"Whoever has a sacrificial animal with him, let him remain in ihram. Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him shave his head.\""],[20269,"On the authority of Asma' bt. Abi Bakr: \"They arrived with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Makkah.\""],[20270,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I married off my daughter, and she became ill and her hair fell out. Her husband keeps coming to me about it. May I attach hair extensions to her hair?\" He cursed the woman who attaches hair extensions and the one who asks for it."],[20271,"On the authority of Urwah b. al-Zubayr regarding the naming of those who emigrated to Abyssinia: Ja'far b. Abi Talib, with his wife Asma' bt. Umays al-Khath'amiyyah. She bore for him in Abyssinia: Abd Allah b. Ja'far, Awn b. Ja'far, and Muhammad b. Ja'far."],[20272,"We entered upon Abu Bakr ؓ during his illness. We saw a fair-skinned woman with tattooed hands, shooing away from him. She was Asma' bt. Umays."],[20273,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me words to say at times of distress: \"There is no god but Allah, my Lord; I associate nothing with Him.\""],[20274,"I was present at the wedding procession of Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When morning came, the Prophet ﷺ came and knocked on the door. Umm Ayman arose, went to him, and opened the door for him. He said, \"O Umm Ayman, call my brother for me.\" She said, \"Your brother is he, that is, a Yamani word, and you marry your daughter to him?\" He said, \"O Umm Ayman, call him for me.\" The women heard the Prophet's ﷺ voice, so they moved aside and sat in a corner. Then Ali came, and he supplicated for him and sprinkled some water on him. Then he said, \"Call Fatimah for me.\" She came, sweating or blushing from shyness. He said to her, \"Be quiet, for I have married you to the most beloved of my household to me.\" He supplicated for her, asked for water, and sprinkled it on her. Then he left and saw a dark figure and said, \"Who is this?\" She said, \"Asma'.\" He said, \"Daughter of Umays?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Were you at the wedding procession of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to honor it?\" I said, \"Yes.\" Then he supplicated for me."],[20275,"From Ikrimah and Abu Yazid al-Madini, or one of them (Abd al-Razzaq was uncertain), that Asma' bint Umays said: When Fatimah was sent to Ali b. Abi Talib, we found nothing in his house except spread sand, a pillow stuffed with something, a water jar, and a mug. The Prophet ﷺ sent word to Ali: \"Do not initiate anything,\" or he said, \"Do not approach your wife until I come to you.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ came and said, \"Is my brother there?\" Umm Ayman, who was the mother of Usamah b. Zayd, a Habashi woman and a righteous woman, said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this is your brother and you have married your daughter to him.\" The Prophet ﷺ had established brotherhood among his companions and had made Ali his own brother. He said, \"That is so, O Umm Ayman.\" She said: Then the Prophet ﷺ asked for a vessel containing water and said over it whatever Allah willed him to say. Then he wiped Ali's chest and face with it. Then he called Fatimah, and she came to him, stumbling in her cloak from shyness. He sprinkled some of that water on her and said to her whatever Allah willed him to say. Then he said to her, \"I have not failed you; I have married you to the most beloved of my family to me.\" Then he saw a dark figure behind the curtain or behind the door and said, \"Who is this?\" She said, \"Asma'.\" He said, \"Asma' bint Umays?\" She said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Did you come as a favor to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his daughter?\" She said, \"Yes. On the night a young woman is married, she must have a woman near her in case a need arises, she can tell her about it.\" She said: Then he supplicated for me with a supplication that is indeed the most reliable of my deeds in my view. Then he said to Ali, \"Take your wife.\" Then he left and departed. She said: He kept supplicating for both of them until he disappeared into his chamber."],[20276,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik, from Abd al-Rahman b. al-Qasim, from his father, from Asma' bint Umays: She gave birth to Muhammad b. Abi Bakr at al-Bayda'. Abu Bakr mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"Tell her to perform ghusl and then enter ihram.\""],[20277,"The Prophet ﷺ said to her, \"O daughter of Umays, there is no ghusl, no Friday prayer, no shaving, and no trimming required of you, except that one of you may take for herself or for one who is a mahram some of the ends of her hair from the front of her head on the Day of Sacrifice when she performs Hajj.\""],[20278,"When Ja'far was killed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed me, saying, \"Observe mourning for three days, then do whatever you wish.\""],[20279,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh has been suffering from istihadah for such-and-such a time and has not prayed.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Glory be to Allah! This is from Satan. Let her sit in a tub, and when she sees a yellowish tinge above the water, let her perform one ghusl for Zuhr and Asr, and one ghusl for Maghrib and Isha, and perform wudu in between.\""],[20280,"The first time the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell ill was in the house of Maymunah. His illness became severe until he lost consciousness. She said: His wives consulted one another about giving him medicine, so they gave it to him. When he regained consciousness, he said, \"What is this? Did women come from here?\" And he pointed with his hand toward the land of Abyssinia. Asma' bint Umays was among them. They said, \"We suspected you had pleurisy, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"That is a disease with which Allah would not afflict me. Let no one remain in the house without being given medicine except the paternal uncle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,\" meaning Abbas. He said: Maymunah was given medicine that day while she was fasting, because of the oath of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[20281,"Kilab b. Tamim, a freedman of one of the Banu Layth, said: While he was sitting with Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, the messenger of Nafi' b. Jubayr b. Mut'im came to him, saying, \"Your maternal aunt sends you greetings and asks, 'What is the hadith you narrated to me from Asma' bint Umays?'\" Sa'id said, \"Tell him that Asma' informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Whoever patiently endures the hardship and severity of Madinah, I will be a witness or intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[20282,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the evil eye afflicts the sons of Ja'far quickly; should I seek ruqyah for them?\" He said, \"Yes, seek ruqyah for them, for if I were to say that anything could outpace the divine decree, I would say that the evil eye outpaces it.\""],[20283,"She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered one day upon A'ishah bint Abi Bakr while her sister Asma' was with her, wearing flowing garments with wide sleeves. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw her, he stood up and left. A'ishah said to her, \"Move aside, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw something in you that he disliked.\" She moved aside, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered. A'ishah asked him why he had left. He said, \"Did you not see her appearance? It is not for a Muslim woman to show anything but this.\" He took his sleeves and covered the backs of his hands so that only his fingers showed, then placed his palms on his temples so that only his face showed."],[20284,"She said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"The evil eye afflicts the sons of Ja'far; should I seek ruqyah for them?\" He said, \"Yes, for if anything could outpace the divine decree, the evil eye would outpace it.\""],[20285,"When Ja'far and his companions were killed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me while I had kneaded their dough, washed my sons, oiled them, and cleaned them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Bring me the sons of Ja'far.\" I brought them to him, and he smelled them and his eyes shed tears. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, what makes you weep? Has something reached you about Ja'far and his companions?\" He said, \"Yes, they were killed today.\" I stood up crying, and the women gathered around me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to his family and said, \"Do not neglect the family of Ja'far; prepare food for them, for they are occupied with the affair of their companion.\""],[20286,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr at al-Sahba', then sent Ali on an errand. He returned after the Prophet ﷺ had prayed Asr. The Prophet ﷺ placed his head in Ali's lap and slept, and Ali did not move him until the sun had set. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Allah, Your servant Ali held himself back for the sake of his Prophet, so return the sun for him.\" She said, \"The sun rose for him until it was above the mountains and the earth. Ali got up, performed wudu, prayed Asr, and then the sun set. That was at al-Sahba'.\""],[20287,"\"Your grandmother Fatimah was given in marriage to your grandfather Ali ؓ . The filling of her bed and her pillow was nothing but palm fiber. Ali held a wedding feast for Fatimah, and his wedding feast at that time was no better than it was: he pledged his armor to a Jew for a measure of barley.\""],[20288,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali, \"You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, but there is no prophet after me.\""],[20289,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to Ali, \"You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa.\""],[20290,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to Ali, \"You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me.\""],[20291,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to Ali, \"You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me.\""],[20292,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali, \"You are to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me.\""],[20293,"I heard Fatimah bt. al-Husayn say: Asma' bt. 'Umays narrated to me that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"O 'Ali, you are to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me.\""],[20294,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was receiving revelation while his head was in 'Ali's lap, and he had not prayed 'Asr until the sun had set. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Allah, 'Ali was engaged in obedience to You and obedience to Your Messenger, so return the sun for him.\" Asma' said, \"I saw it set, and I saw it rise after it had set.\" The wording is from the hadith of 'Uthman."],[20295,"Abu al-'Uyuf Sa'b or Su'ayb al-'Anazi narrated to me, saying: I heard Asma' bt. 'Umays say, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with these two ears of mine say, \"Whoever is afflicted by worry, grief, illness, or hardship, and says, 'Allah is my Lord, He has no partner,' that will be removed from him.\""],[20296,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"What do you use as a laxative?\" I said, \"Shubrum (euphorbia).\" He said, \"That is hot, hot.\" I said, \"Then I used senna as a laxative.\" He said, \"If anything could cure death, it would be senna.\""],[20297,"Asma' bt. Yazid b. al-Sakan, the cousin of Mu'adh b. Jabal, killed nine Byzantines on the day of al-Yarmuk with the pole of her tent."],[20298,"The Prophet ﷺ was in my house and he mentioned the Dajjal (false messiah). He said, \"Between his hands are three years, during which the sky will withhold one-third of its rain, and the earth will withhold one-third of its crops. In the second year, the sky will withhold two-thirds of its rain, and the earth will withhold two-thirds of its crops. In the third year, the sky will withhold all of its rain, and the earth will withhold all of its crops, causing the animals to perish, and no beast with fangs or hooves will remain except that it will die. Indeed, the greatest trial of all is when he comes to the Bedouin and says, 'Do you not believe that I am your lord, and I can bring your camel back to life?' The Bedouin will say, 'Yes.' Then, Satan will appear in the form of the camel, at its most beautiful and at its best times. Similarly, a man will come who lost his father and brother, and the Dajjal will say, 'Do you not believe that I can bring them back to life?' He will say, 'Yes.' Then, Satan will appear in the form of his father and brother.\" Asma' said, \"Then, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out for a need and when he returned, the people were in a state of concern and worry due to what he had mentioned. He took hold of the door and said, 'What is the matter?' I (Asma') said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you have frightened us with the mentioning of the Dajjal.' He said, 'If he comes out while I am still alive, I will be his opponent and I will be the defender of every believing Muslim. If he comes out after I have died, then every Muslim will become their own defender.' Asma' said, 'I said, 'By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we knead our dough and cannot bake it until we become hungry. How will it be for the believers on that day?' He said, 'They will be sufficed by what the inhabitants of the heavens are sufficed with, in terms of glorifying and sanctifying Allah.'\""],[20299,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among a gathering of his Companions when they mentioned the Dajjal. He said: \"Before the Hour there will be years of drought: the first year the sky will withhold a third of its rain and the earth a third of its vegetation; the second year the sky will withhold two thirds of its rain and the earth two thirds of its vegetation; the third year the sky will withhold all its rain and the earth all its vegetation, until no animal with a hoof or a cloven hoof remains.\" Then he went out for a need, then returned while they were weeping. He took hold of both sides of the door and said: \"What is the matter with you?\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, one of us kneads his dough and cannot wait for it to rise.\" He said: \"If he appears while I am among you, I will contend with him on your behalf; otherwise, Allah is my successor over every believer.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what will suffice the believer on that day?\" He said: \"What suffices the angels: glorification (tasbih), praise (tahmid), declaring Allah's oneness (tahlil), and magnification (takbir).\""],[20300,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me with a group of his Companions and mentioned the Dajjal. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Before his emergence there will be three years—or a year—when the sky withholds a third of its rain and the earth withholds a third of its vegetation; the second year the sky withholds two thirds of its rain and the earth withholds two thirds of its vegetation; the third year the sky withholds all that is in it and the earth all that is in it, and every creature with molars and cloven hooves will perish. Among the worst of his trials is that he will say to a Bedouin: 'If I revive your camels for you, with huge udders and tall humps, will you know that I am your Lord?' He will say yes, and the devil will appear to him in that form.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out for some need, and I prepared water for his ablution. The people sobbed until their voices grew loud. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of the door and said: \"What is this?\" We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you have terrified their hearts with the Dajjal.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If the Dajjal emerges while I am alive, I will contend with him on your behalf; and if I die, Allah is my successor over every believer.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what will suffice the believers on that day?\" He said: \"What suffices the inhabitants of heaven: glorification (tasbih) and sanctification (taqdis).\""],[20301,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a house when he said: \"When it is before the emergence of the Dajjal, the sky will withhold a third of its rain for three years and the earth will withhold a third of its vegetation. In the second year the sky will withhold two thirds of its rain and the earth two thirds of its vegetation. In the third year the sky will withhold all its rain and the earth all its vegetation.\" Then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of al-Awza'i."],[20302,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you pray over the deceased, recite the Opening of the Book (al-Fatihah).\""],[20303,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , both men and women, and he said, \"Perhaps a man may speak of something that happens between him and his wife, or a woman may speak of something that happens between her and her husband.\" So the people started to laugh and I said, \"By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, they definitely do it, and the women definitely do it too.\" He said, \"Do not do that, for it is like a male devil meeting a female devil on the road, and he covers her while the people are watching.\""],[20304,"The sleeves of the shirt of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached below the wrists."],[20305,"I was among the women from whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the pledge. She said: \"I was a young woman, bold in questioning him, so I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, stretch out your hand so that I may shake it.' He said: 'I do not shake hands with women, but I take from them what Allah has taken from them.'\" She said: \"He looked at a maternal aunt of mine who had two bracelets of gold on her hand. He took something from the ground and threw it at her and said: 'Would it please you for Allah to give you two bracelets of the fire of Hell?' She said: 'I seek refuge with Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'If you have sought refuge with Allah, then throw these two off of you.' She struggled with it and I helped her with that, and she threw them away. I do not know even now who went off with them.\""],[20306,"While she was among a group of women, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by them, greeted them, and then said: \"Beware of the ingratitude of those who are given blessings.\" She said: \"What is the ingratitude of those who are given blessings, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Perhaps one of you remains unmarried for a long time, or becomes an old maid in her parents' house. Then perhaps Allah provides her with a husband, then provides her with a child from him, then she becomes angry and denies his favors, saying: 'By Allah, I have never seen any good from you.'\""],[20307,"That the Prophet ﷺ sent an expedition to the outskirts of Mudar. They mentioned that they camped in a rocky land, and in the morning there was a man in a tent with sheep in his courtyard. They came and stood before him and said, “Protect us,” so he protected them with a sheep. They cooked from it, then he brought it out to them, and they found it insufficient. Then he said, “Nothing remains among my sheep with meat except a pregnant ewe or a ram.” So they sniffed and took a sheep from them. When they brought it out and they were burning in a hot day with no shade with them, they said, “His little flock in his tent,” and they said, “We are more entitled to the shade than these sheep.” So they came to him and said, “Bring out your sheep so we can seek shade.” He said, “If you bring them out, they will perish and cast their young, and I am a man who has believed in Allah and His Messenger, and I have prayed and given zakah.” So they brought out his sheep, and it was not long but an hour of the day before they bleated and cast their young. So he set off quickly until he came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him the news. The Prophet ﷺ became very angry, then said, “Sit until the people return.” When they returned, he gathered between them and him, and they successively lied to him, lie after lie. So the Prophet ﷺ was relieved, but when the Bedouin saw that, he said, “By Allah, Allah knows that I am truthful and they are liars, and perhaps Allah will inform you, O Messenger of Allah.” So it occurred to the Prophet ﷺ that he was truthful. Then he called them one by one, adjuring each man of them, and no man among them adjured except as the Bedouin said. So the Prophet ﷺ stood and said, “What carries you to follow one another in lying as moths follow one another into the fire? Lying is written against the son of Adam except for three traits: a man who lies to his wife to please her, a man who lies in the deceit of war, and a man who lies between two Muslim men to reconcile them.”"],[20308,"That she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “All lying is written against the son of Adam except in three cases: a man who lies in reconciling between people, or lies to his wife, or lies in the deceit of war.”"],[20309,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and addressed the people, saying: “O people, what carries you to follow one another in lying?” Zuhayr said: I think he said: “as moths follow one another into the fire. All lying is written against the son of Adam except for three traits: a man who lies to his wife to please her, or a man who lies between two Muslim men to reconcile them, or a man who lies in the deceit of war.” And the wording is that of the hadith of Ahmad b. Yunus."],[20310,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O people, what carries you to follow one another in lying as moths follow one another into the fire? All lying is written against the son of Adam except for three: a man who lies to his wife to please her, a man who lies between two people to reconcile them, and a man who lies in the deceit of war.”"],[20311,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: “O people, shall I not inform you of the best among you?” They said, “Yes.” He said, “Those who, when they are seen, Allah is remembered. Shall I not inform you of the worst among you?” They said, “Yes.” He said, “Your worst are those who spread malicious gossip, corrupting between loved ones, seeking hardship for the innocent.”"],[20312,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the women near the side of the mosque, and I was among them. He heard their voices and said, \"O group of women, surely you are the majority of the fuel of Hell.\" So, I called the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and was bold in my speech, and I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, why?\" He said, \"Because you, when you are given something, do not express gratitude, and when you are afflicted with a calamity, you do not have patience. And when you are withheld something, you complain and badmouth.\" So, I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is 'Kufran al-muna'meen'?\" He replied, \"The woman who is with her husband and has borne for him two or three children, yet she says, 'I have never seen any good from you.'\""],[20313,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Whoever drinks alcohol, Allah will not accept his repentance for forty days. If he dies in this state, he dies as a disbeliever. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. If he repeats it, it is certain that Allah will make him drink the pus of the people of hell.\" I asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the pus of the people of hell?\" He replied, \"It is the discharge of the people of hell.\""],[20314,"That she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was among his companions saying: “I warn you against the Masih and caution you about him. Every prophet warned his people, and he is among you, O Ummah. I will describe to you from his characteristics what the prophets before me did not describe to their peoples. Before his emergence there will be five years of drought until every hoofed animal perishes.” A man called out to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, how will the believers live?” He said, “By what the angels live on.” Then he will emerge and he is one-eyed, and Allah is not one-eyed. Between his eyes is written ‘kafir’ that every believer, literate or illiterate, will read. Most of his followers will be Jews, women, and Bedouins. They will see the sky raining while it does not rain, and the earth producing vegetation while it does not produce. He will say to the Bedouins, “What do you want from me? Have I not sent the sky upon you abundantly, and brought your livestock to life with raised udders, protruding flanks, and flowing milk?” Devils will be sent with him in the form of fathers, brothers, and acquaintances who have died. One of them will come to his father, brother, or relative and say, “Are you not so-and-so? Do you not know me? He is your Lord, so follow him.” He will remain forty years: a year like a month, a month like a week, a week like a day, a day like an hour, and an hour like the burning of a palm branch in the fire. He will reach every watering place except the two mosques. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to perform ablution and heard the people’s crying and sobbing, so he returned to them and stood among them and said, “Rejoice, for if he emerges while I am among you, Allah and His Messenger will suffice you, and if he emerges after me, Allah is my successor over every Muslim.”"],[20315,"I entered with my maternal aunt upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we had two bracelets of gold. He said, “Do you two pay its zakah?” We said, “No.” He said, “Would you two like Allah to make you wear two bracelets of fire? Pay its zakah.”"],[20316,"When Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet ﷺ , died, the eyes of the Prophet ﷺ shed tears. It was said to him, \"You are the most deserving person who knows the rights of Allah.\" He said, \"The eyes shed tears, and the heart feels sadness, but we do not say anything that displeases the Lord. If it were not for the fact that He is the truthful promise and the gathering appointment, and that the later follows the former, we would be more saddened than this. Verily, O Ibrahim, we are saddened by your loss.\""],[20317,"When Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet ﷺ, passed away, the comforter said to him, \"Either Abu Bakr or Umar, you know better who truly knew Allah.\" The comforter then said, \"The eye sheds tears and the heart grieves, but we do not say anything that angers the Lord. If it were not for the fact that He is truthful in His promise and the meeting is inevitable, and that the following life is a continuation of the first one, we would have found you, O Ibrahim, in a better state than we did, and indeed, we are saddened by your departure.\""],[20318,"I am the one who adorned Aisha for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When I presented her to him and brought her to him, I seated her at his right. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a cup of milk, and he drank, then handed it to Aisha. She lowered her head and was shy, so I said to her, “Take it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” She took it and drank. Then he said, “Pass it to your companion.” She said, “O Messenger of Allah, drink yourself, then pass it to me.” So he drank, then passed it to me. I began to seek the places where the lips of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had touched, and there were women near us or with us. He said, “Pass it to your companions.” They said, “We do not desire it” or “We do not want it.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Do not combine lying and hunger.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw on one of us a bracelet of gold and said, “O this woman, would you like Allah to make you wear in its place a bracelet of fire?” So we removed it and threw it away, and we do not know where it is to this hour. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “It is enough for one of you to take beads of silver.” Perhaps he said, “a bracelet of silver, then take some saffron and taste it, then smear it on it, and it will be as if it is gold.”"],[20319,"That she was with the Prophet ﷺ when a bowl of milk was brought. He drank from it and then said, “Give it to them,” referring to women with him. They said, “We do not desire it.” He said, “Do not combine lying and hunger.”"],[20320,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was among women and greeted us, then said, “Beware of ingratitude to those who have been good to you.” I said, “What is ingratitude to those who have been good to you?” He said, “Perhaps one of you remains unmarried between her parents for a long time and grows old, then Allah provides her a husband and provides her from him wealth and children, then she becomes angry once and denies it, saying, ‘I have never seen any good from you.’”"],[20321,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her while she was among women, and we said, “We have pledged allegiance, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “I do not shake hands with you, but I take from you what Allah took from them.”"],[20322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke to us one day about the Dajjal. A woman stood up and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I knead dough for my family, and I do not think it will rise before my soul departs.” He said, “If he emerges while I am among you, I will be his opponent, and if he emerges after me, Allah is my successor over every Muslim.”"],[20323,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “There was no prophet except that he warned his nation against the Dajjal, and indeed I warn you of him.”"],[20324,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The greatest name of Allah is mentioned in these two verses: 'Alif, Lam, Meem. Allah! There is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence' and 'Your God is one God.'\""],[20325,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated that 'Isa bin Yunus narrated from 'Ubaidullah bin Abi Ziyad, who narrated from Shahru bin Hawshab, who narrated from Asmaa bint Yazid. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The greatest name of Allah is in these two verses: 'And your God is one God' (Quran 2:163) and 'Alif Lam Meem. Allah! There is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence' (Quran 2:255).\""],[20326,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever defends the flesh of his brother in his absence, it is incumbent upon Allah to protect him from the Fire.”"],[20327,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever defends the honor of his brother in his absence, it is incumbent upon Allah, Exalted is He, to free him from the Fire.”"],[20328,"\"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , passed away on the day his shield was held as collateral by a Jewish man for a measure of barley.\""],[20329,"I heard Asmā’ bt. Yazīd say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque one day while a group of women were sitting. He gestured with his right hand in greeting, smiled at them, and said: “Beware of ingratitude toward those who bestow favors.” A woman said: “I seek refuge in Allah, O Messenger of Allah, from ingratitude for Allah’s favors.” He said: “Indeed, one of you remains long without a husband, then Allah provides her a husband, and she gains a child and delight of the eye. Then she becomes angry one time and swears by Allah: ‘I have never seen any good from him ever.’ That is part of ingratitude for Allah’s favors; that is part of ingratitude for Allah’s favors; that is part of ingratitude for Allah’s favors.”"],[20330,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite: “Woe to your mother, Quraysh, for your familiarity with the winter and summer journey.”"],[20331,"Indeed I was holding the rein of al-‘Aḍbā’, the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when al-Mā’idah descended upon him, and it nearly broke the camel’s neck from its weight."],[20332,"Al-An‘ām descended upon the Prophet ﷺ all at once, while I was holding the rein of the Prophet’s she-camel ﷺ; indeed, from its weight it nearly broke the camel’s bone."],[20333,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me while I was wearing rings of gold and a bracelet of gold. He said: “Would it please you that Allah seal you with a ring of Fire and bracelet you with a bracelet of Fire?” So I abandoned them. And he said: “Is one of you unable to make a ring of silver and smear upon it some saffron, ambergris, and wars?”"],[20334,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ one day when a drink was brought. He drank, then gave it to the people and they drank. The vessel passed by a man among the people, and he said: “I am fasting.” Some of the people said: “He does not break his fast; he fasts every day.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “He has neither fasted nor broken his fast—the one who fasts perpetually.”"],[20335,"A drink was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was passed around among the people, among them a man who was fasting. It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, he fasts the whole time.” He said: “He has not fasted—the one who fasts perpetually.”"],[20336,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, I and a daughter of my paternal aunt, to pledge allegiance to him, and he said: “I do not shake hands with women.”"],[20337,"She was among the women from whom the Messenger of God ﷺ took the pledge, and with her was her maternal aunt, who wore gold rings and two gold bracelets. He kept turning his gaze away from her until, when he had finished, he said: “What is this? Would it please you for God to adorn you with ornaments of fire?” She said: I seek refuge in God from the Fire. So she removed her rings and threw them down before her, and she struggled with her bracelets but could not remove them, so she went to him and snapped them off, then threw them somewhere—we do not know what he did with them. She said: I said, “O Messenger of God, we women must adorn ourselves for our husbands; will you permit us two gold earrings?” He refused, saying: “It is enough for one of you to take two silver earrings, then take two threads dyed with saffron and rub them between her fingers until they turn yellow, and it will look like gold.”"],[20338,"The Prophet ﷺ said about the ʿaqīqah: “For a boy, two sheep; for a girl, one sheep.”"],[20339,"She heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Do not kill your children secretly. By the One in whose hand is my soul, the practice of coitus interruptus will catch up with a rider on his horse until it throws him down.”"],[20340,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Do not kill your children secretly, for the one who carries out coitus interruptus will catch up with a rider and hurl him from the back of his horse.”"],[20341,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was sitting with some friends, and he said, \"Beware of the curse of the one who is grateful.\" I was the boldest among them to ask him, so I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the curse of the one who is grateful?\" He replied, \"Perhaps one of you will have a long life with her parents, then Allah will bless her with a husband and children. Then she gets angry and disbelieves, saying, 'By Allah, I have never seen any good from you.'\""],[20342,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever leaves behind two dinars leaves behind two cauterizing brands.”"],[20343,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: “Let your tears cease and your grief depart, for your son is the first one at whom God laughed and for whom the Throne shook.”"],[20344,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever builds a mosque for God, God will build for him a house in Paradise.”"],[20345,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Any woman who adorns herself with a necklace of gold will have the like of it placed around her neck from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20346,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ among a group of women to give him allegiance. He stipulated upon us what is in the Qur’an: “that you do not steal, do not commit adultery, do not kill your children, and do not bring slander that you fabricate.” Then he said to us: “In what you are able and can bear.” We said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than ourselves. We said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not shake hands with us? He said: “I do not shake hands with women. My word to one woman is like my word to a hundred women.”"],[20347,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik (ḥ). And Abū Yazīd al-Qarāṭīsī narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh b. ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us (ḥ). And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us. They both said: Mālik b. Anas narrated to us from Muḥammad b. al-Munkadir from Umaymah bt. Ruqayqah, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among a group of women to give him allegiance. We said: We give you allegiance, O Messenger of Allah, that we will not associate anything with Allah, will not steal, will not commit adultery, will not kill our children, will not bring slander that we fabricate between our hands and feet, and will not disobey you in what is good. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In what you are able and can bear.” We said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than ourselves. Come, let us give you allegiance, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “I do not shake hands with women. My word to a hundred women is like my word to one woman, or the like of my word to one woman.”"],[20348,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ regarding women, and he said, \"Take the pledge not to associate anything with Allah, not to steal, and not to commit adultery.\" Then he said, \"To the best of your ability and within your means.\" We said, \"May Allah and His Messenger be kinder to us than ourselves.\" We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, give us your pledge.\" He said, \"I do not shake hands with women. My statement to a hundred women is the same as my statement to one woman.\""],[20349,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ among a group of women. He said: “You give allegiance that you will not associate anything with Allah, will not steal, and will not commit adultery” — the verse. Then he was silent, then said: “In what you are able and can bear.” They said: Allah and His Messenger know better and are more merciful to us than ourselves. We said: O Messenger of Allah, accept our allegiance. He said: “I do not shake hands with women. My word to a hundred women is like my word to one woman.”"],[20350,"He heard Umaymah bt. Ruqayqah say that she gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he stipulated upon her what he stipulated upon the believing women. Then he said: “In what you are able.”"],[20351,"She gave allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ, and he stipulated upon her what he stipulated upon the believing women in the Book of Allah. Then he said: “In what you are able, O daughter of Ruqayqah.”"],[20352,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ among a group of women. We said: We give you allegiance, O Messenger of Allah, that we will not associate anything with Allah, will not steal, will not commit adultery, will not bring slander that we fabricate between our hands and feet, and will not disobey you in what is good. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In what you are able and can bear.” We said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us. So accept our allegiance, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “I do not shake hands with women. My word to a hundred is like my word to one.”"],[20353,"Ḥukaymah bt. Umaymah bt. Ruqayqah narrated to me from her mother, who said: The Prophet ﷺ used to urinate in a wooden vessel, then place it under his bed. He urinated in it, then came and wanted it, and found that the vessel had nothing in it. He said to a woman called Barakah, who served Umm Ḥabībah and had been brought by her from the land of Abyssinia: “Where is the urine that was in the vessel?” She said: I drank it. He said: “You have shielded yourself from the Fire with a barrier.”"],[20354,"From Umaymah, the freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, she said: I was pouring water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during his ablution when a man entered and said: Counsel me. He said: “Do not associate anything with Allah, even if you are cut into pieces or burned with fire. Do not disobey your parents, even if they command you to abandon your family and your worldly possessions, then abandon them. Do not drink wine, for it is the root of every evil. Do not deliberately abandon prayer, for whoever does that has the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger removed from him. Do not flee on the day of battle, for whoever does that returns with wrath from Allah, and his abode is Hell — an evil destination. Do not increase the boundaries of your land, for whoever does that will carry it on his neck on the Day of Resurrection from the extent of seven earths. Spend on your family from your means, and do not lift your staff from them, and make them fear Allah.”"],[20355,"I heard my aunt, who had performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bilāl gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Bilāl or Ibn Umm Maktūm gives the call.” One would ascend and the other would descend. We would cling to him, as you are, until we took the pre-dawn meal."],[20356,"She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, my son ʿAbdullāh b. Salamah — and he had been a participant in Badr — was killed on the day of Uḥud. I would like to move him so that I can find comfort in his nearness. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted her. She placed him alongside al-Mijdhar b. Ziyād on a camel of hers, in a cloak. She passed by the two of them, and people were amazed at them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at them and said: “Their deeds made them equal.” ʿAbdullāh was a large, heavy man, while al-Mijdhar was lean of flesh. He is the one who says [the poem]."],[20357,"\"Busrah bint Safwan asked the Prophet ﷺ about a woman who hits with her hand and it causes her private part to bleed. He said, 'Perform ablution, O Busrah.'\""],[20358,"He and Marwan discussed ablution due to touching the private part. Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan narrated to me that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanding ablution due to touching the private part. It was as if Urwah did not accept his narration as marfu'. So Marwan sent a guard to her, and he returned and informed them that she had heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanding ablution due to touching the private part."],[20359,"He heard Marwan saying: Busrah bint Safwan informed me; she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'Whoever touches his private part should perform ablution.'"],[20360,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'A man should perform ablution due to touching the penis.'"],[20361,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'Whoever touches his penis should perform ablution.'"],[20362,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'Whoever touches his private part should perform ablution.'"],[20363,"He said: Ablution is required due to touching the penis. Urwah denied that, so Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan informed me of it. So he sent to Busrah, and she said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned what ablution is required from, and he mentioned touching the penis.'"],[20364,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When one of you touches his penis, he should perform ablution.'"],[20365,"That ablution is required due to touching the penis when a man reaches it with his hand. I denied that and said: No ablution is required from touching it. Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioning what ablution is required from, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Ablution is required from touching the penis.' Urwah said: 'I kept arguing with Marwan about that until he called a man from his guard and sent him to Busrah bint Safwan, and he asked her about what she had narrated to him regarding that. Busrah sent back the same as what Marwan had narrated to me from her.'"],[20366,"That ablution is required due to touching the penis when a man reaches it with his hand. I denied that and said: No ablution is required for the one who touches it. Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioning what ablution is required from, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'And ablution is required from touching the penis.' Urwah said: 'I kept disputing with Marwan until he called a man from his guard and sent him to Busrah to ask her about what she had narrated regarding that. Busrah sent to him the same as what he had narrated to me from her.'"],[20367,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever touches his penis should perform ablution.'"],[20368,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever touches his penis should perform ablution.'"],[20369,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik; and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Malik informed us; and Bakr b. Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed us, from 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr b. Muhammad b. 'Amr b. Hazm that he heard Urwah b. al-Zubayr saying: I entered upon Marwan b. al-Hakam, and he mentioned what ablution is required from. Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan informed me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever touches his penis should perform ablution.'"],[20370,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever touches his penis must perform wudu.'"],[20371,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'A man performs wudu from touching the penis.'"],[20372,"It was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what requires wudu, and he said: 'And whoever touches the penis must perform wudu.'"],[20373,"Marwan discussed with me the touching of the penis, and I said: 'No wudu is required for it.' He said: 'Busrah bt. Safwan narrates something about it.' So he sent a messenger to her, and he mentioned that she narrated to him that the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever touches his private part must perform wudu.'"],[20374,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever touches his penis must perform wudu.'"],[20375,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever touches his penis must perform wudu.'"],[20376,"I heard Urwah say: Marwan sent for Busrah and asked her about this hadith, and she narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When one of you touches his penis, he must perform wudu.'"],[20377,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever touches his private part must not pray until he performs wudu.'"],[20378,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"If one of you feels something he should perform ablution.\""],[20379,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When one of you touches his private part, he must perform wudu.' He said: 'I objected to him, so he sent for her, and she narrated it to him from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was present.'"],[20380,"About touching the penis, and he saw no harm in it. Then Marwan sent one of his guards to Busrah bt. Safwan, and he said: 'She narrated to me that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"When a man touches his private part with his hand, he must not pray until he performs wudu.\" ' So he returned and said: 'She said yes.' After that, my father used to say: 'Whoever touches his groin or his testicles must perform wudu.'"],[20381,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When one of you touches his penis, he must perform wudu.'"],[20382,"Whoever touches his private part must perform wudu. Urwah objected to that, so he said: 'O policeman, go to Busrah bt. Safwan and ask her, for she said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Whoever touches his penis must perform wudu.\" '"],[20383,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If one of you touches his penis, or his testicles, or his groin, let him perform ablution.”"],[20384,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever touches his penis, or his testicles, or his groin, let him perform ablution as he does for prayer.”"],[20385,"…about touching the penis, and I did not see any obligation on him to repeat the ablution. So Marwan summoned one of his guards and sent him to Busrah bint Safwan. He asked her about that, and she informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If one of you touches his penis, let him repeat the ablution.”"],[20386,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his penis or his testicles, let him perform ablution.”"],[20387,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his penis, let him perform ablution as he does for prayer.”"],[20388,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his private part, ablution becomes obligatory upon him.”"],[20389,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his groin, or his testicles, or his penis, let him not pray until he performs ablution.”"],[20390,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his penis, let him perform ablution.” Urwah said: Then I asked Busrah, and she confirmed it."],[20391,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If one of you touches his penis, let him perform ablution.”"],[20392,"Hisham heard the hadith of his father about touching the penis. Yahya said: Then I asked Hisham, and he said: My father informed me."],[20393,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “If one of you touches his penis, let him perform ablution.”"],[20394,"From Busrah bint Safwan al-Kinaniyyah—and she was Marwan’s maternal aunt—she said: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying: O Messenger of God, is ablution required for any of us if she touches her private part? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his private part, whether among men or women, ablution is required upon him.”"],[20395,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"O these people, when you hear of an army being swallowed up nearby, then the Hour has drawn near.\""],[20396,"And I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"O people, when you hear of a sinking here nearby, then the Hour has drawn near.\""],[20397,"that I should take charge of this affair. She used to say, \"O Abdul-Malik, I see in you qualities that make you worthy to take charge of this community. If you are appointed to it, beware of bloodshed, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'A man will be turned away from the gate of Paradise, even though he is able to look at it, because of a cupping-glassful of blood that he sheds from a Muslim without right.'\""],[20398,"The Prophet ﷺ had a wooden bowl in which he would urinate and would place it under his bed. He got up and looked for it but could not find it, so he asked, \"Where is the bowl?\" They said, \"Barrah, the servant of Umm Salamah, who came with her from the land of Abyssinia, drank it.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"She has protected herself from the Fire with a barrier.\""],[20399,"She said: My father asked permission of the Prophet ﷺ to enter between him and his shirt, and he permitted him. So he entered between him and his shirt from behind him, and he began to embrace him and wipe his chest against the Prophet's ﷺ back. He said, \"O Messenger of God, what is it that it is not lawful to withhold?\" He said, \"Water.\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, what is it that it is not lawful to withhold?\" He said, \"Salt.\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, what is it that it is not lawful to withhold?\" He said, \"If you do good, it is better for you.\" And his statement ended with water and salt. She said: That man would not withhold any amount of water, even if it was little."],[20400,"I heard Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr say: Buthayna bt. al-Dahhak, the sister of Thabit, and she is the one whom Muhammad b. Maslama proposed to."],[20401,"In three of the sunnah, meat was given as charity to Ali, so I gifted it to Aisha, and she kept it until the Messenger of God ﷺ entered. He said, \"What is this meat?\" She said, \"Meat that was given as charity to Barirah, and she gifted it to us.\" He said, \"For Barirah it is charity, and for us it is a gift.\" She said, \"And I had a contract of emancipation for nine uqiyyahs.\" Aisha said, \"If they wish, I will count them a single count.\" I said, \"They say: unless they stipulate the wala' for themselves.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Stipulate and stipulate, for the wala' belongs to the one who manumits.\" She said, \"And I was manumitted, and I had the choice.\""],[20402,"I looked at the Messenger of God ﷺ while I was in an upper room of mine between Safa and Marwah, and he was saying, \"God has prescribed the sa'y for you, so perform the sa'y.\""],[20403,"From his grandmother, the mother of his father, Tuwaylah bt. Aslam, who was among the women who gave allegiance. She said: We were at our place of prayer among the Banu Harithah when Abbad b. Bishr b. Qayzi said: The Messenger of God ﷺ has turned to face the Sacred House, or the Kaaba. So the men moved to the place of the women, and the women to the place of the men, and they prayed the remaining two prostrations toward the Kaaba."],[20404,"I heard Abdullah b. Abd al-Hakam b. Abi Ziyad say: Salih, the freed slave of al-Taw'amah, and she is the daughter of Umayyah b. Khalaf."],[20405,"The name of Bashir was Zahm, and the Messenger of God ﷺ named him Bashir."],[20406,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ go out to prayer shaking his head and beard from the traces of henna."],[20407,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik; ḥ (turning to another chain) and Abū Yazīd al-Qarāṭīsī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us; ḥ (turning to another chain) and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us; they both said: Mālik reported to us, from Abū al-Aswad Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Nawfal, from ʿUrwah b. al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah, from Judāmah bt. Wahb al-Asadiyyah, who said: She informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I had intended to forbid al-ghīlah (sexual intercourse with a nursing mother) until I recalled that the Persians and Romans do that and it does not harm their children.\""],[20408,"I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among some people while he was saying: \"I had intended to forbid al-ghīlah (sexual intercourse with a nursing mother), but I looked into the Persians and Romans, and found that they have intercourse with their nursing mothers, yet it does not harm their children at all.\" Then they asked him about ʿazl (coitus interruptus), and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"That is the hidden waʾd (burying alive), and it is: 'When the buried girl is asked' (Qur'an 81:8).\""],[20409,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I wanted to forbid al-ghiyāl (sexual intercourse with nursing mothers), but I found that the Persians and Romans have intercourse with their nursing mothers, and it does not harm them at all.\""],[20410,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"Give charity, even from your jewelry, for you are the majority of the people of the Fire.\" So Zaynab came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my husband is in need; is it permissible for me to give back to him?\" He said: \"Yes, you will have two rewards.\""],[20411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed the name of ʿĀṣiyah and said: \"You are Jamīlah.\""],[20412,"My father took me to the Prophet ﷺ after I had responded to my father's camels. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah for the blessing of my daughter.\" The Prophet ﷺ sat me in his room, placed his hand on my head, and prayed for me with blessings."],[20413,"I was with Umm Salamah, the Mother of the Believers, during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"O my mother, have I conveyed to you?\" She said: A young son of hers said, \"O mother, why is he calling his mother?\" She said: I said, \"O my son, he means his community (ummah),\" and he was saying: \"Verily, your honors, your wealth, and your blood are inviolable to you, like the inviolability of this day of yours, in this land of yours, in this month of yours.\""],[20414,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The best generation is my generation.\""],[20415,"Jamīlah bt. Ubayy b. Salūl came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I do not find fault with Thābit b. Qays in character or religion, but I cannot stand him out of dislike, and I hate to commit disbelief within Islam.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Will you return to him his garden?\" She said, \"Yes.\" So the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to take from her what he had given her as dowry, and not to increase."],[20416,"Jamīlah bt. Ubayy b. Salūl came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I do not find fault with Thābit in character or religion, but I hate disbelief within Islam.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Will you return to him his garden?\" She said, \"Yes.\" So she returned it to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ separated them. [Note:] Jamīlah bt. Thābit b. Abī al-Aflaḥ al-Anṣārī, the wife of ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb."],[20417,"Ḥalīmah bt. Abī Dhuʾayb al-Saʿdiyyah of Saʿd b. Bakr b. Hawāzin—and she is the mother of the Prophet ﷺ who suckled him and weaned him—narrated to me; she narrated, saying: A barren, drought-stricken year befell us and left us with nothing, so we went out among a group of women from Banū Saʿd b. Bakr to Makkah seeking suckling infants. When we arrived in Makkah, there was not a woman among us but the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was offered to her, and she would refuse him and dislike him. That was because he had no father, and the wet-nurses only hoped for good from the fathers. A woman would say, \"What shall I do with this one? What can his mother do for me?\" So they disliked him. She said: He was offered to me, and I refused him. No woman of my people remained but found a suckling infant. When they were about to depart for their lands, I feared returning without a suckling baby, so I said to my husband, \"Perhaps I should take that orphan boy; it would be better than returning without a suckling infant.\" So I went to his mother and took him, and brought him to my dwelling. I had a son whom I was nursing, and he would stay awake much of the night from hunger, unable to sleep. When I put the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to my breasts, they turned to him with whatever milk he wished, until he drank his fill, and his brother drank his fill, and slept. My husband got up in the middle of the night to an old she-camel of ours, by Allah, to see if it would yield a drop of milk. She said: His hand fell upon her udder and found it full of milk, ready to be milked. So he came to me and said, \"O daughter of Wahb, by Allah, I think this soul is blessed.\" Then he told me the news of the old she-camel, and I told him the news of what I had seen from my breasts that night. We went out riding a she-donkey of ours that had previously been too weak to catch up with the other donkeys. When we were upon it heading toward our lands, it would go ahead of the people until they would shout at me, \"Woe to you, O daughter of Abū Dhuʾayb! You have left us behind. This she-donkey of yours has something special about it.\" She said: We arrived with him in the lands of Banū Saʿd b. Bakr, and we knew nothing but blessing. Indeed, our shepherd would go out with our sheep and graze them, and our people would send out their sheep. When it was near night, they returned, and our sheep would come back full of milk, while not a single sheep among theirs yielded a drop. They would say to their shepherds, \"Woe to you! Graze where the shepherd of the daughter of Abū Dhuʾayb grazes.\" She said: It remained like that with us. Then one day he was behind our houses among some young lambs of ours, playing with his brother, when his brother came running and said, \"That Qurayshī brother of mine has been killed!\" So we hurried to him, his father and I, and met him with a pale face. We began to embrace him, sometimes I and sometimes his father, saying to him, \"What is the matter with you, O my son?\" He would say, \"I do not know. Two men came to me, threw me down, split open my belly, and began stirring it.\" His father turned to me and said, \"I think this boy has been afflicted. Take him to his family quickly before the matter gets worse for us.\" She said: I had no goal until I brought him to Makkah to his mother, and I said to her, \"O foster mother, I have weaned my son and he has recovered from the ailment, so keep him.\" She said, \"What is the matter with you, are you abandoning him? You used to ask me to leave him with you—it is as if you fear Satan for him.\" First, let me tell you about myself and about him: When I gave birth to him, I saw that a light came out of me that illuminated the palaces of Buṣrā in the land of Syria."],[20418,"I heard Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr say: \"Shuraḥbīl b. Ḥasanah—Ḥasanah was his mother, and she was among those who emigrated to Abyssinia.\""],[20419,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Perform the Fajr prayer when it is bright, for that is greater in reward.”"],[20420,"Habiba bt. Sahl was married to Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas al-Ansari, and she disliked him, for he was an ugly man. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I see him, and were it not for fear of Allah, I would spit in his face.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Will you return to him his garden that he gave you as a dower?” She said: “Yes.” He sent for him, and she returned to him his garden, and he separated the two of them. That was the first khulʿ in Islam."],[20421,"From Ḥiqqah bt. ʿAmr—and she had prayed facing the two qiblahs with the Prophet ﷺ—that when she intended to enter iḥrām, she would place her cloak in her lap, wear whatever of her clothes she wished, including the dyed yellow garment, and then pronounce the talbiyah."],[20422,"Ibn Ishaq said: \"Hamnah bint Jahsh was among the women of Banu Asad who emigrated, from the women he mentioned.\""],[20423,"\"I saw with my own eyes Hamnah bint Jahsh on the day of Uhud giving water to the thirsty and treating the wounded.\""],[20424,"\"I suffered from prolonged menstrual bleeding (istihada) for seven years, and I complained about that to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'That is not menstruation, but rather it is a vein, so perform ghusl.' So she would perform ghusl at the time of every prayer, and she would perform ghusl in a large basin, and one could see the yellowish tinge of blood in the basin.\""],[20425,"\"I used to have a long, heavy menstrual period, so I went to the Prophet ﷺ to seek his advice and inform him about it. I found him in my sister Zainab's house, so I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have a need.' He said, 'What is it? May Allah facilitate it for you.' I said, 'I have a long, heavy menstrual period that prevents me from praying and fasting. What should I do?' He said, 'Use a piece of cloth called a qursuf, as it takes away the blood.' I said, 'It is more than that.' He said, 'Then use a tampon.' I said, 'It is more than that.' He said, 'Then wear a cloth.' She said, 'It is more than that, O Messenger of Allah. It only stops during the hajj ministration.' He said, 'I will tell you two options; whichever one you choose and do, you will be exempted from the other. If you can handle both of them, then you know your situation best.' He said, 'This is a rukhsah (dispensation) from among the dispensations of Satan.' He said, 'You will menstruate for six or seven days, according to the knowledge of Allah, then take a bath. When you see that you have become pure and are certain about it, then pray twenty-four nights and days, or three and twenty nights and days, and fast. This will be sufficient for you.' He said, 'Do this every month, like how women menstruate and become pure according to their menstrual and purification times. If you are able to delay the Dhuhr (noon) prayer and hasten the Asr (afternoon) prayer, then take a bath for both of them. If you are able to delay the Maghrib (sunset) prayer and hasten the Isha (evening) prayer, then take a bath for both of them. Combine between the prayers and take a bath with the Fajr (dawn) prayer. Do the same during fasting if you are able to do so.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'And it is most amazing that you use a tampon.' Meaning, seek forgiveness.\""],[20426,"\"I suffered from an irregular menstruation, so I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Use a loincloth and insert cotton.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, it is more severe than that; I gush forth blood profusely.' He said: 'Use that internally and secure it, and consider your menstruation according to God's knowledge as six or seven days each month. Then perform ghusl, fast, and pray for twenty-three or twenty-four days. Delay the noon prayer and advance the afternoon prayer, and perform ghusl once for both, and perform ghusl for the dawn prayer. This is the more beloved of the two matters to me.'\""],[20427,"\"I used to suffer from severe, heavy prolonged menstrual bleeding, so I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ to seek his ruling and ask him. I found him in the house of my sister Zaynab bint Jahsh. I said: 'O Messenger of God, I have a need to discuss with you.' He said: 'What is it, O you?' I said: 'O Messenger of God, it is a matter about which—by God—there is no escape, and I am shy about it.' He said: 'What is it, O you?' I said: 'O Messenger of God, I suffer from severe, heavy prolonged menstrual bleeding. What do you think about it? It has prevented me from praying and fasting.' He said to her: 'I prescribe for you cotton, for it will take away the blood.' I said: 'It is more than that.' He said: 'Indeed, I will command you with two matters; whichever of them you do, it will suffice you in place of the other. If you are able to do both, you know best. This is only a strike from the strikes of Satan. So pray and fast for twenty-four nights and their days, for that will suffice you; and do likewise every month, just as women menstruate and become pure according to the time of their menstruation and purity. If you are able to delay the noon prayer and hasten the afternoon prayer, and perform ghusl once for both, then pray the noon and afternoon prayers together, then delay the sunset prayer and hasten the night prayer and combine the two prayers, then do so. And perform ghusl with the dawn prayer, and pray accordingly; do so, and pray and fast if you are able to do that.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'And this is more pleasing to me.'\""],[20428,"\"From his grandmother.\""],[20429,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik. And Abu Yazid Yusuf b. Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us; Abdullah b. Abd al-Hakam narrated to us. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us; Abdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us. They said: Ibn Anas informed us from Zayd b. Aslam from Ibn Bujayd from his grandmother that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not turn away a beggar, even if with a burnt hoof.\""],[20430,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: \"Do not turn away a beggar, even if with a burnt hoof.\""],[20431,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Do not repel the one who asks, even with a burnt hoof.\""],[20432,"\"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Do not turn away a beggar, even if with a burnt hoof.'\""],[20433,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us; Abdullah b. Yusuf informed us: Malik narrated to us from Zayd b. Aslam from Amr b. Mu'adh al-Ash-hali from his grandmother that she said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O believing women, let not one of you disdain to give to her neighbor, even if it be a burnt trotter of a sheep.\""],[20434,"\"I said: 'O Messenger of God, a poor man stands at my door until I feel ashamed, but I find nothing to give him.' He said: 'Put in his hand, even if a burnt hoof.'\""],[20435,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, a beggar comes to me and I have nothing to give him.\" He said, \"Do not turn him away empty-handed even if it is with a date.\""],[20436,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O believing women, let not one of you disdain to give to her neighbor, even if it be the burnt foot of a sheep.\""],[20437,"Al-Hawlaa bt. Tuwayt passed by her while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with her. She said: “This al-Hawlaa—they claim that she does not sleep at night.” He said: “Take on of deeds what you can bear, for by Allah, Allah does not tire until you tire.”"],[20438,"Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas struck her a blow whose severity she did not know. She came to the Prophet ﷺ in the darkness before dawn and mentioned to him what had happened to her. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Take back from her [what you gave].” She said: “Indeed what he gave me is with me just as it was.” He said: “Then take back from her.” So he took back from her, and she stayed with her family."],[20439,"From Habiba bt. Sahl, a woman whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had intended to marry, but Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas proposed to her and married her. Thabit b. Qays had harshness in his character, so he struck her. She came at dawn to the door of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said: “Who is this?” She said: “I am Habiba, O Messenger of Allah. Neither I nor Thabit.” Thabit came following her, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Did you strike her?” He said: “Yes, I struck her.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Take back from her [what you gave].” She said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have everything he gave me.” He said: “So he took back from her, and she sat in her house.”"],[20440,"Abu Bakr asked permission of the Prophet ﷺ, when he saw his lightness, to go to Bint Kharija, and he granted him permission—in a long hadith."],[20441,"I was sitting in Aisha’s house when the Prophet ﷺ entered and said: “There are no two Muslims who have three small children die, who have not reached the age of sin, but Allah will admit them to Paradise by the virtue of His mercy toward them.”"],[20442,"She was with Aisha when the Prophet ﷺ came and entered upon her. He said: “There are no two Muslims who have three children die, who have not reached the age of sin, but they will be brought on the Day of Resurrection until they are made to stand at the gate of Paradise. It will be said to them: ‘Enter Paradise.’ They will say: ‘Until our parents enter.’ It will be said to them: ‘Enter Paradise, you and your parents.’”"],[20443,"I saw myself among women of Quraysh in the house of Abu Husayn while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was between al-Safa and al-Marwa. She said: I heard him when he reached the place of saʿy saying: “Perform saʿy, for Allah has prescribed saʿy upon you.”"],[20444,"From Bint Tajra, one of the women of Banu ʿAbd al-Dar, she said: I entered the house of the family of Abu Husayn with women of Quraysh. The Prophet ﷺ looked at me while he was performing saʿy between al-Safa and al-Marwa. I saw him running in the middle of the valley, and his lower garment was twisting around from the intensity of the saʿy until I said: I can see his knees. And I heard him saying: “Perform saʿy, for Allah has prescribed saʿy upon you.”"],[20445,"\"And indeed, I was among the women of Quraysh in the house of Abu Hussein, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was walking between Safa and Marwa, and I heard him saying, 'Hurry up, for the act of walking between Safa and Marwa has been prescribed for you.' She said, 'And truly, his garment was swirling around him due to the intensity of his walking.'\""],[20446,"I looked at the Prophet ﷺ while he was circumambulating between al-Safa and al-Marwa, and I was among women of Quraysh. He was performing saʿy at the rear of the people, saying: “Perform saʿy, for Allah has prescribed saʿy upon you.” I looked at him, and he was performing saʿy, and his lower garment was twisting around from the intensity of the saʿy."],[20447,"I heard ʿAbd Allah b. Nabih from his grandmother Safiyya bt. Shayba from Habiba bt. Abi Tajra, who said: I looked out from an opening between al-Safa and al-Marwa and looked down upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He was performing saʿy between al-Safa and al-Marwa and saying to his companions: “Perform saʿy, for Allah has prescribed saʿy upon you. If you could have seen him from the intensity of the saʿy, his lower garment was turning around his belly and thighs until I saw the whiteness of his thighs.”"],[20448,"Her husband said to her, \"Look, O mother of Muhammad, what are you talking about? Indeed, speaking about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ without certainty is a severe offense.\" She said, \"Woe to me, what benefit do I have in speaking to them about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ if it does not benefit them, and I would be lying about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The dunya (world) is green and sweet, so whoever takes wealth with a good intention will be blessed with it. And many are those who try to deceive in the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger for their own selfish desires, and they will have the fire on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[20449,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed this wealth is green and sweet; so whoever acquires it by its right will be blessed for him in it, and many a one who plunges into whatever his soul desires of the wealth of Allah and His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20450,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Hamzah, and they mentioned worldly matters. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed the world is green and sweet; so whoever takes it by its right, Allah will bless him in it, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger in whatever his soul craves — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20451,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Hamzah were discussing the world, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed the world is sweet and green; so whoever takes its surplus is blessed, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the day he meets Him.”"],[20452,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he and Hamzah were mentioning the world, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed the world is green; whoever takes it by its right will be blessed for him in it, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the day he meets his Lord.”"],[20453,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was discussing the world with Hamzah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed the world is sweet and green; so whoever takes its surplus is blessed for him in it, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20454,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed the world is green and sweet; so whoever takes it by its right, Allah blesses him in it, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20455,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed this wealth is sweet and green; so whoever takes it by its right is blessed for him in it, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20456,"The Prophet ﷺ came to Hamzah, and Khawlah, the wife of Hamzah, was there, and they discussed the world. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed the world is sweet and green; so whoever takes it by its right, Allah blesses it for him, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20457,"Hamzah and the Prophet ﷺ were discussing the world, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed the world is green and sweet; so whoever takes it by its right is blessed for him in it, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20458,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me, and I made for him a kharīzah (a dish of meat and flour), and I presented it to him. He placed his hand in it and found it hot, so he withdrew it and said: “O Khawlah, we cannot endure heat or cold. O Khawlah, Allah has granted me al-Kawthar, and it is a river in Paradise. No creatures are more beloved to me to come to it than your people. O Khawlah, many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger in whatever his soul craves — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20459,"From Khawlah bt. Qays b. Quhd, who was the wife of Hamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, and he was killed leaving her. She came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ to visit him. She said: “O Prophet of Allah, I have been wanting to meet you and ask you about something that was mentioned to me, that you mention that you have a ḥawḍ (basin) between such and such.” He said to her: “Yes, and the people most beloved to me — or the people most beloved to me — to come to it are your people.” She said: “I brought him some ʿaṣīdah (porridge) in a bowl, and when he placed his hand in it, it burned him, and he said: ‘Ḥass!’ Then he said: ‘The son of Adam, if heat afflicts him, says “ḥass”, and if cold afflicts him, says “ḥass.”’”"],[20460,"“Yes, and the most beloved of those who come to me are your people.” This is how Abū Khālid narrated it from Khawlah bt. Ḥakīm, and the correct version is the ḥadīth of Ḥammād b. Zayd."],[20461,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God has not sanctified a nation whose weak do not take their right from their strong without being impeded.” Then he said: “If a debtor departs from his creditor in this matter while he is pleased with him, the beasts of the earth and the fish of the water send blessings upon him. But if a debtor departs while he is displeased, then oppression is recorded against him each day and night, each Friday, and each month.”"],[20462,"There was a basket of dates for a man from the Banu Sa'ida, and the Prophet ﷺ commanded a man from the Ansar to distribute it. He distributed the dates, but the man refused to accept them. The Prophet ﷺ asked him, \"Are you rejecting the command of the Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"Yes, for who is more deserving of justice than the Messenger of Allah?\" Upon hearing this, the eyes of the Prophet ﷺ filled with tears and he said, \"He spoke the truth, for who is more deserving of justice than me, the Messenger of Allah? By the sanctity of Allah, a nation will not be honored if the weak do not receive their rights from the strong, and the strong do not protect them.\" Then he said, \"O Khawla, fulfill his rights and give it to him, for there is no enemy who comes out of his enemy's presence satisfied, except that the beasts of the land and the fish of the sea pray for him, and there is no enemy who oppresses his enemy, except that Allah writes a sin against him for every day and night.\""],[20463,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Shall I inform you of what expiates sins? Performing ablution thoroughly despite difficulties, taking many steps to the prayers, and waiting for the next prayer after the previous prayer.”"],[20464,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Shall I inform you of the expiations of sins?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Performing ablution thoroughly despite difficulties, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for the next prayer after the previous prayer.”"],[20465,"He heard her say: “My hand and the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ differed over a single vessel.”"],[20466,"“My hand and the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ differed over a single vessel during ablution.”"],[20467,"I heard Umm Subayyah al-Juhaniyyah say: “My hand alternated with the Prophet’s ﷺ in ablution from a single vessel.”"],[20468,"I heard Umm Subayyah say: “My hand and the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ differed in ablution from a single vessel.”"],[20469,"Sometimes I contended with the Prophet ﷺ over the vessel, performing ablution, I and he, from a single vessel."],[20470,"“My hand and the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ differed over a single vessel during ablution.”"],[20471,"She was among those who gave themselves to the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[20472,"Khawlah bt. Hakim was among those who gave themselves to the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[20473,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever alights at a place and says, ‘I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from the evil of what He has created,’ nothing will harm him until he departs from that place.”"],[20474,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When one of you alights at a place, let him say: ‘I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,’ for nothing will harm him until he departs from it.”"],[20475,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever alights at a place and says: ‘I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,’ nothing will harm him in that place until he departs.”"],[20476,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If one of you enters a house and says, 'I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,' nothing from that house will harm him until he leaves.\""],[20477,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik. Ḥ. And Abū Yazīd al-Qarāṭīsī narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh b. ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us. Ḥ. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us. They both said: Mālik informed us, that it reached him from Yaʿqūb b. ʿAbdullāh b. al-Ashajj, from Busr b. Saʿīd, the mawlā of the Ḥaḍramīs, from Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ, from Khawlah bt. Ḥakīm, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever alights at a place and says: ‘I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,’ nothing will harm him in that place until he departs from it.”"],[20478,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever alights at a place and says: ‘I seek refuge in all the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,’ nothing will harm him in that place until he moves on from it.”"],[20479,"The Prophet ﷺ came out one day holding one of his daughter's children, saying: “By Allah, you make people stingy, cowardly, and ignorant, and you are among the sweet basil of Allah, and the last place where the Lord of the worlds set foot was Wajj.” Ibn Abī ʿUmar added in his narration: Sufyān said: The last expedition the Prophet ﷺ undertook was to al-Ṭāʾif. And the poet said: “I will surely seek you out with the tread of the one who moves about.”"],[20480,"Khawlah bt. Ḥakīm asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: “O Messenger of Allah, a woman sees in her dream what a man sees.” He said: “If she sees that, she should perform ghusl.”"],[20481,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a ruling about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees: Is ghusl obligatory upon her? He said: “Yes, if she sees the fluid.”"],[20482,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: “Nothing is required of her, just as a man, if he does not ejaculate, is not required to perform ghusl until he ejaculates.”"],[20483,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: “Nothing is required of her, just as a man, if he does not ejaculate, nothing is required of him.”"],[20484,"The righteous woman Khawlah bt. Ḥakīm claimed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Children are a cause of grief, cowardice, ignorance, and stinginess, and the last place where Allah, may He be exalted, set foot was Wajj.”"],[20485,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, I menstruate and I have only one garment.” He said: “Wash it and pray in it.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, the trace of blood remains in it.” He said: “It will not harm you.”"],[20486,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, will you have a ḥawḍ?” He said: “Yes, and the people I most love to come to it are your people.” Thus narrated Abū Khālid al-Aḥmar, and the people said it is from Khawlah bt. Qays."],[20487,"From Khawlah bint al-Ṣāmit—her husband was ill, and he called her, but she delayed. He said to her, 'If I approach you or have intercourse with you, then you are to me like my mother's back.' She went to the Prophet ﷺ and complained about that to him, but he did not reply to her with anything, as nothing had reached him about it. Then she came to him another time, and the Prophet ﷺ came and said, 'Free a slave.' He said, 'I do not have one.' He said, 'Fast two consecutive months.' He said, 'I am not able.' He said, 'Then feed sixty poor people, thirty sāʿs.' He said, 'I do not possess that unless you help me.' So the Prophet ﷺ helped him with fifteen sāʿs, and the people helped him until it reached the amount. He said, 'By Allah, there is no one more in need of it than me and my household.' He said, 'Take it, you and your household.' Abu al-Qāsim said: Thus said Khawlah bint al-Ṣāmit, and she is Khawlah bint Thaʿlabah, the wife of Aws b. al-Ṣāmit."],[20488,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah does not sanctify a nation whose weak cannot take their right from their strong without stammering.' And he said: 'Whoever leaves his debtor while pleased with him, the beasts of the earth and the fish of the seas pray for him. And whoever leaves his debtor while angry with him, it is written against him every day and night, every week and month, that he has wronged.'"],[20489,"About her mother, who was a servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , it was narrated that a scorpion entered the house and went under the bed and died. The Prophet ﷺ stayed for a few days without receiving revelation. He said, \"O Khawla, what happened in the house of the Messenger of Allah? Gabriel does not come to me. Did something happen in the house of the Messenger of Allah?\" I said, \"By Allah, a day has not passed upon us that is better than our day.\" He then put on his shoes and went out. I said, \"If I prepare the house and sweep it, I will sweep under the bed.\" So I took the broom and went under the bed, and there was something heavy. I kept sweeping until I took it out, and it was a dead scorpion. I took it with my hand and threw it behind the house. Then the Messenger of Allah came hearing his beard quivering, and whenever he received revelation, his beard would quiver. He said, \"O Khawla, cover me.\" So Allah revealed: \"By the morning brightness, and by the night when it covers (the earth), your Lord has neither forsaken you nor hated you.\""],[20490,"Khālidah bint Anas, the mother of the Banū Ḥazm al-Sāʿidiyyah, came to the Prophet ﷺ and presented incantations to him, and he ordered them."],[20491,"From her maternal aunt Khulaydah bint Qaʿnab, who was among the women who came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him. She said: A woman came to him wearing a gold bracelet, and he refused to accept her pledge. She left the crowd, threw away the bracelet, then came and he accepted her pledge. She went out to look for the bracelet, and when she went to look for it, it had been taken away."],[20492,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “The best thing to be placed in the Balance on the Day of Resurrection is good character.”"],[20493,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The world is sweet and green, and there will be men who wade into the wealth of God and His Messenger without right. For them is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20494,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us, saying: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what suffices you? For there is no woman who adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it.”"],[20495,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us, saying: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what suffices you? For there is none among you, a woman who adorns herself with gold and displays it, except that she will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20496,"The Prophet ﷺ addressed us, saying: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what suffices you? Indeed, there is none among you who adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20497,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us, praised God, and extolled Him. Then he said: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what you may adorn yourselves with? Indeed, there is no woman who adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it.”"],[20498,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us, saying: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what you may adorn yourselves with? Indeed, there is none among you, a woman who adorns herself with gold, except that she will be punished for it.”"],[20499,"She heard the Messenger of God ﷺ delivering a sermon and saying: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what you may adorn yourselves with? There is none among you, a woman who wears gold and displays it, except that she will be punished with it.”"],[20500,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us, saying: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what you may adorn yourselves with? Indeed, there is no woman who adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it.”"],[20501,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us, praised God, and extolled Him. Then he said: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what you may adorn yourselves with? Indeed, there is no woman who adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it.”"],[20502,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ when he had a fever, and the fever had become severe upon him. I said: “You, O Messenger of God, the fever has become severe upon you. If only you would call upon God, He would remove it from you.” He said: “The people most severely tried are the prophets, then those next to them.” She said: A waterskin had been suspended for him on a tree, and he lay down beneath it, with water dripping onto his heart."],[20503,"We entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ among the women of the Emigrants to visit him, and he was feverish. He ordered a waterskin containing water, and it was suspended on a tree. He made the water drip onto his heart due to the severity of what he felt. We said: “O Messenger of God, if only you would call upon God, He would remove what is upon you.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The people most severely tried are the prophets, then those next to them, then those next to them.”"],[20504,"She entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he ordered a waterskin, which was suspended on a tree. Then he lay down beneath it, and it began dripping onto his heart. I said: “Call upon God, and He will remove it from you.” He said: “Indeed, the people most severely tried are the prophets, then those next to them.”"],[20505,"I visited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among some women, and he had hung up a waterskin that was dripping on him due to the severity of the fever. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you would supplicate, its severity would leave you.' He said, 'The people most severely tried are the prophets, then the righteous, then the next best and the next best.'"],[20506,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ when he had a fever. He ordered a waterskin, and it was hung on a tree; then he lay down beneath it, and the water began to drip on his heart. I said to him, 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you would supplicate to Allah and He would remove it from you.' He said, 'Among the people most severely tried are the prophets, then those who follow them, then those who follow them.'"],[20507,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was suffering from fever, and he had hung up a waterskin that was dripping on his heart. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is this?' He said, 'We, the company of prophets, have affliction multiplied upon us.'"],[20508,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no good in a gathering of women except at a funeral, for when they gather, they say and say.'"],[20509,"One day he came in to me and spoke to me about something while he was somewhat vexed, so I answered him back, and he said, 'You are to me like my mother's back.' Then he went out and sat down; then he called his people, then he returned to me and wanted me for himself, but I refused him. He struggled with me and I struggled with him, and I overcame him as a woman overcomes a weak man. I said, 'No, by the One in Whose hand is the soul of Khuwaylah, you will not reach her until Allah judges between me and you.' So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining to him about what I had encountered from him. He said, 'Your husband and your cousin; fear Allah.' Then Allah revealed: {Allah has heard the statement of she who disputes with you concerning her husband and complains to Allah} until it reached the expiation. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Order him to free a slave.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, he has no slave to free.' He said, 'Then let him fast two consecutive months.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, he is an old man; by Allah, he is not able to fast.' He said, 'Then let him feed sixty poor people.' I said, 'By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he does not have anything to feed.' He said, 'Rather, we will help him with a basket of dates—and the basket is a large measure that holds thirty sāʿs.' I said, 'And I will help him with another basket.' He said, 'You have done well; order him to give it in charity.'"],[20510,"She was a servant of the Prophet ﷺ called Khaḍrah."],[20511,"Her father married her off while she was a previously married woman, and she disliked that. She went to the Prophet ﷺ, and he rejected the marriage."],[20512,"My father married me off while I was unwilling, and I was a virgin. I complained about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'Do not marry her off while she is unwilling.'"],[20513,"Her father married her off while she was a matron, and she was unwilling, so the Prophet ﷺ “rejected her marriage.”"],[20514,"Her case was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he ordered a man, and her father married her to a man from Banu Amr b. Awf; and she longed for Abu Lubabah."],[20515,"Khansa’ bt. Khidam was married by her father while she was unwilling, so she came to the Prophet ﷺ, “and he rejected her marriage.”"],[20516,"The Prophet ﷺ met her coming from the bathhouse and said, “From where are you coming, O Umm al-Darda’?” She said, “From the bathhouse, O Messenger of God.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Any woman who puts down her garments in other than her own house has torn the veil between her and God.”"],[20517,"I heard Umm al-Darda’ say, “I came out of the bathhouse and the Messenger of God ﷺ met me and said, ‘From where, O Umm al-Darda’?’ I said, ‘From the bathhouse.’ He said, ‘By the One in Whose hand is my soul, no woman puts down her garments in other than the house of one of her mothers except that she is a tearer of every veil between her and the Most Merciful, Blessed and Exalted.’”"],[20518,"“Did you hear anything from the Prophet ﷺ?” She said, “Yes. I entered upon him while he was sitting in the gathering, and I heard him say, ‘The first thing to be placed in the Balance is good character.’”"],[20519,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever guards a post on any of the coasts of the Muslims for three days, a year’s garrison duty is fulfilled on his behalf.”"],[20520,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “God created disease and remedy, so treat yourselves, but do not treat with what is forbidden.”"],[20521,"I said, “O Messenger of God, does rage harm?” He said, “Yes, as leaf-stripping harms trees.”"],[20522,"“Supplicate God for good for us, for the Prophet ﷺ used to say, ‘The supplication of the wronged for his brother in his absence is answered; at his head is an angel who says ameen to his supplication; whenever he supplicates for good for him, he says, “Ameen, and for you the like.”’” He said, “Then I went out to the market and met Abu al-Darda’, and he narrated to me from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it.”"],[20523,"The Messenger of God ﷺ met her one day and said, “From where have you come, O Umm al-Darda’?” She said, “From the bathhouse.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, “No woman removes her garments in other than her own house except that she has torn the veil between her and God.”"],[20524,"She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with jewelry and said, “I have given this as charity.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “It is not permissible for a woman to do anything with her wealth except with her husband’s permission. Have you asked Ka'b’s permission?” She said, “Yes.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Ka'b and asked, “Have you permitted Khayrah to give her jewelry as charity?” He said, “Yes.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted it from her. [She was] al-Kharqā’, the black woman who used to remove harmful things from the mosque of the Prophet ﷺ."],[20525,"Durrah bint Abī Lahab was married to al-Ḥārith b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Nawfal, and she bore him ʿUqbah, al-Walīd, and Abū Muslim. Then she came to the Prophet ﷺ in Madinah, and the people spoke much about her parents. She went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, did the disbelievers beget anyone other than me?” The Prophet ﷺ said to her, “And what of that?” She said, “The people of Madinah have hurt me regarding my parents.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, “When you pray ẓuhr, pray where I can see you.” The Prophet ﷺ prayed ẓuhr, then turned toward her and faced the people, saying: “O people, do you have lineage while I have no lineage?” ʿUmar jumped up and said, “May Allah be angry with whoever angers you.” He said, “This is my cousin, so let no one say anything to her but good.”"],[20526,"From the husband of Durrah bint Abī Lahab, from her: She said, “I was with ʿĀ’ishah when a man was brought to the Prophet ﷺ who had called out to him while he was on the pulpit, saying, ‘O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is best?’ She said: The man came and was seized, and he said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, I have no sin; so-and-so ordered me.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘The best of people is the most pious of them, the most commanding of good, the most forbidding of evil, and the most upholding of kinship ties.’”"],[20527,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by us and asked for water. I went to a jug and gave him water to drink. A man wearing two green garments asked him, and he said, “Worship Allah, associating nothing with Him, establish prayer, and give zakāh.” Then he said, “The best of my ummah is my generation, then those who follow them.” Shuʿbah erred in the chain of this hadith."],[20528,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon us when I married the daughter of Abū Lahab and said, “Is there any entertainment?”"],[20529,"There were women sitting with her from the family of Zuraiq. You are the daughter of Abu Lahab, who says, \"May the hands of Abu Lahab perish, and may he himself perish. His wealth and what he earned will never suffice him.\" What will your migration benefit you? So the pearl of the Prophet ﷺ came to her and she complained to him about what had been said to her. He calmed her down and said, \"Sit down.\" Then he prayed Dhuhr with the people and sat on the pulpit for an hour, then he said, \"O people, why am I being harmed in my family? By Allah, my intercession will reach those who deserve it, whether they are alive or dead, and it will reach every soul and tribe on the Day of Judgment.\""],[20530,"Years of drought befell Quraysh, which dried up the udders and emaciated the bones. While I was lying down overcome by grief or troubled, suddenly a caller cried out with a hoarse voice, saying: “O assembly of Quraysh, this Prophet who has been sent—his days have overshadowed you, and this is the time of his rising stars. So hasten to life and fertility! Look for a man among you who is of middle rank, great in stature, large in body, white with radiance, with thick eyelashes, smooth cheeks, and a prominent nose. He has a mark that he suppresses, and a practice that guides to him. Let him and his children set out, and let one man from every clan descend to him. Let them sprinkle water, touch perfume, and touch the corner [of the Kaʿbah]. Then let them climb Abū Qubays, then let the man supplicate and the people say āmīn. Then you will be rained upon as much as you wish.” By Allah, I woke up terrified, my skin trembling and my mind bewildered. I related my vision and lay in the mountain passes of Makkah. By the sanctity and the sacred sanctuary, there remained no one in the valley but that he said, “This is Shaybah al-Ḥamd.” The leaders of Quraysh came to him, and one man from every clan descended to him. They sprinkled, touched, and touched the corner, then climbed Abū Qubays and lined up around him, their pace not slackening until they stood on the summit of the mountain. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib stood, and with him was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a boy who had reached puberty or nearly so. He raised his hand and said: “O Allah, Remover of hardship and Reliever of distress, You are the One who teaches without being taught, and the One who is asked without being withheld from. These are Your male and female servants at the courtyards of Your sanctuary, complaining to You of their year, which has destroyed the camel and the hoofed animal. O Allah, send upon us abundant, fruitful rain.” By the Lord of the Kaʿbah, they did not leave until the sky poured forth its water and the valley overflowed with its torrents. I heard the elders and nobles of Quraysh—ʿAbd Allāh b. Judʿān, Ḥarb b. Umayyah, and Hishām b. al-Mughīrah—saying to ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, “Congratulations to you, O father of the valley, for through you the people of the valley have lived.” And concerning that, Ruqayqah bint Abī Ṣayfī says…"],[20531,"When the Prophet ﷺ came seeking support in al-Ṭā’if, he entered upon me, and I brought him a drink of sawīq. He said, “O Ruqayqah, do not worship their idol and do not pray to it.” She said, “Then they will kill me.” He said, “If they say that to you, say: My Lord is the Lord of this idol. And if you see it, turn your back to it.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left me."],[20532,"Rāʾiṭah, the sister of ʿAbdullāh al-Thaqafiyyah, was married to Ibn Masʿūd. She was a skillful woman who made things and sold from her craft. She said to Ibn Masʿūd: 'You and your child have kept me too busy to spend in the path of Allah, so I am unable to spend in the path of Allah.' He said: 'I would not like you to do that if you had no reward in it.' So I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Spend on them, for you have the reward of whatever you spend on them.'"],[20533,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrating about the wife of Thābit b. Qays b. Shammās al-Anṣārī that there occurred something between her and her husband, and he was a man of harshness. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and spoke with him, and he sent for Thābit b. Qays. They spoke in his presence as Allah willed, then he accepted a ransom from her and she ransomed herself from him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her to observe an ʿiddah of one menstrual period."],[20534,"I brought the Prophet ﷺ a basket of fresh dates and hairy cucumbers. He gave me a handful of jewelry, or gold."],[20535,"“We used to go on military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We would give water to the people, serve them, and bring the dead and wounded back to Madinah.”"],[20536,"From her mother Ruzaynah, the freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Hafsah, the Mother of the Believers, visited Aishah, the Mother of the Believers, one day. Sawdah entered upon them wearing a garment of Yemeni cloth and a head covering, and on the inner corners of her eyes were two dots like lentils of aloe and saffron. ‘Alilah said, “I lived to see women adorning themselves with it for their husbands.” Hafsah said to Aishah, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ will enter upon us and find us plain, while she among us is glowing. I will ruin her adornment today.” Aishah said, “Fear Allah, O Hafsah.” Sawdah said, “What are you saying?” She was hard of hearing. She said, “The one-eyed man has come out.” Sawdah said, “The one-eyed man has come out?” She said, “Yes.” She said, “Where shall I hide?” She said, “Go to the tent.” It was a tent made of palm branches where they cooked pots, and in it were spider webs. She went and entered it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon them while they were laughing, unable to speak to him from laughter. He said, “Why the laughter?” They gestured with their hands toward the tent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the tent and found Sawdah trembling. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, “What is the matter with you?” She said, “O Messenger of Allah, the one-eyed man has come out.” He said, “He has not come out, and he will never come out.” Then he entered, took her by the hand, and began brushing dust and spider webs off her."],[20537,"Shaybah bint Al-Aswad, the niece of my mother, told me that my grandmother, Rawdah, said to me, \"I used to be a companion to a woman in the city. When the Prophet ﷺ migrated from Makkah to Madinah, my guardian, Rawdah, told me to stand at the door of our house and inform her when this man passes by.\" She continued, \"So I stood and the Prophet ﷺ came with a group of his companions. I held onto a corner of his cloak and he smiled at me. Shaybah said, \"I think he wiped his hand on my head.\" I asked my guardian, \"O guardian, this is the man who has come.\" So my guardian and those who were with her in the house came out. Islam was presented to them, and they embraced Islam.\" Shaybah added, \"Rawdah was with me in the house in Bani Sulaym. Whenever the neighbors purchased a slave, servant, garment, or food, they would say to her, 'O Rawdah, place your hand on it.' And everything she touched would be blessed.\""],[20538,"I was with my mother Rā’iṭah bint Sufyān, a woman of Khuzāʿah, while the Prophet ﷺ was taking the pledge from the women, saying: “I take your pledge that you will not associate anything with Allah, will not steal, will not commit adultery, will not kill your children, will not bring a slander you fabricate between your hands and feet, and will not disobey me in what is right.” They lowered their heads. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Say: Yes, in what we are able to do.” So we said, “Yes, in what we are able to do.” I said as they said, and my mother said, “Say yes, say yes.”"],[20539,"Al-Rubayyiʿ bint al-Naḍr slapped a girl of the Anṣār and broke her front tooth. They came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking retaliation. Anas b. al-Naḍr said, “O Messenger of Allah, will the tooth of al-Rubayyiʿ be broken?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Anas, the Book of Allah [requires] retaliation.” The people forgave. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Among Allah’s servants are those who, if they swore by Allah, He would fulfill it; among them is Anas b. al-Naḍr.”"],[20540,"\"Indeed, Rubayyah bintu al-Nadhir came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my son Harithah was martyred on the Day of Badr. If he is in Paradise, I will have patience and seek reward. If not, I will weep and grieve.' The Prophet ﷺ replied, 'O mother of Harithah, it is gardens within Paradise, and he has surely attained the highest part of Firdaus.'\""],[20541,"She said to ʿAbd Allāh one day, “You and your children have distracted me, and I cannot give any charity with you.” He said, “Would you not like to have two rewards?” They asked the Prophet ﷺ about that, and he said, “You have the reward of what you spend on them.”"],[20542,"He said, “I would not like you to do that unless you have a reward in it.” So she and he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman with a craft by which I earn, and I have nothing, nor does my husband or my child. They distract me, so I cannot give charity.” He said, “You have a reward in that for what you spend on them.”"],[20543,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from Hishām b. ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿUbayd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUtbah, from Rā’iṭah, the wife of ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd. She was a skilled craftswoman, and Ibn Masʿūd had no wealth, and she used to spend on him and his children from the proceeds of her craft. She said, “By Allah, you and your children have distracted me from charity, so I cannot give any charity with you.” He said, “I would not like you to do that unless you have a reward in it.” So she and he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “You have a reward in that.”"],[20544,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: 'I am a woman of craftsmanship by which I seek [livelihood], but neither I, nor my husband, nor my children have anything; they preoccupy me so that I do not give charity.' He said: 'You will have a reward for that, whatever you spend on them.'"],[20545,"I obtained a khulʿ from my husband, then I came to ʿUmar and asked him: 'What ʿiddah is incumbent upon me?' He said: 'There is no ʿiddah upon you unless it is a recent matter, in which case you should wait until you menstruate once.' She said: 'Indeed, in that matter, the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is followed concerning Maryam al-Maghāliyyah, who was married to Thābit b. Qays b. Shammās and obtained a khulʿ from him.'"],[20546,"Regarding the ablution of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , she said, \"Yes, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to us and visit us, and he would perform ablution with this container and with a similar container, which was about a Mudd in size. She said, \"He would first wash his hands, then he would rinse his mouth and nose, then he would wash his face three times, then he would wash his hands three times, then he would wipe his head twice, and he would wipe both the outward and inward parts of his ears, and then he would wash his feet three times, three times.\""],[20547,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, and I poured water for him. He rinsed his mouth, snuffed water, and washed his face three times, each three times, his forearms three times, each three times, and wiped his head twice, starting from the back before the front, and wiped the back of his ears, and inserted his fingers into the holes of his ears, and washed his feet three times, each three times."],[20548,"The Prophet ﷺ used to come to us, and we would bring him a water vessel of ours containing water, taking a mudd and a half or two-thirds of the Madinan mudd. I would pour for him, and he would wash his hands three times, rinse his mouth and snuff water, wash his face three times, wipe his head once, and wipe his ears, their outer and inner parts, and purify his feet."],[20549,"Regarding the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He used to perform ablution at her house, so I came to her and asked her, and she brought out a vessel, about a mudd and a quarter by the Hashimi measure. She said: 'I used to bring out his ablution water in this. He would begin by pouring onto his right hand and washing it three times before putting it into the vessel, then rinse his mouth and snuff water three times, wash his face three times, wash his right hand three times and his left hand three times, then wipe his head from front to back.' Sufyān described how he wiped his head until he reached its beginning. This is the wording of Ibn Abī ʿUmar's ḥadīth. Ibn Abī ʿUmar added in his narration: Sufyān said: 'Ibn ʿAjlān added to me, from Ibn ʿAqīl, who said: al-Rabīʿ said: Then he wiped his temples and cheeks, then returned them to the middle of his head, then extended them to the back of his neck, then wiped his ears, then washed his feet.'"],[20550,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped the front of his ears and their back."],[20551,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped his head with the leftover water that was on his hand, starting from the back of his head, then drawing it to the front, then drawing it back to the back."],[20552,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution washing each part three times."],[20553,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to us frequently. She said: 'He came to us, and we placed for him the water vessel. He performed ablution: he washed his palms three times, then rinsed his mouth and snuffed water once, washed his face three times and his forearms three times, wiped with what remained of his ablution water twice, starting from the back, then returned his hands to his forelock, and washed his feet three times, each three times.'"],[20554,"I assisted the Prophet ﷺ in ablution. I brought him a water vessel that held a mudd or a mudd and a third. He said: 'Pour.' He performed ablution, wiping the front of his head and the outer and inner parts of his ears."],[20555,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us, performed ablution, wiped the front of his head, and wiped the outer and inner parts of his ears."],[20556,"I heard al-Rubayyiʿ bt. Muʿawwidh b. ʿAfrāʾ say: The Messenger of God ﷺ used to come to us. I would pour ablution water for him, and he would perform ablution at our place using a water vessel of ours, containing a mudd and a half, and a mudd and a third. I would pour water over his palms three times, then I would set it down for him, and he would rinse his mouth, inhale water, wash his face three times, his hands three times, wipe his head and his ears, then wash his feet three times, three times."],[20557,"About the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ, she said: Yes, the Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution in a vessel like this one, indicating with her hand toward a small water skin that holds a mudd and a third, according to the first (report), as I believe. He rinsed his mouth, inhaled water, washed his face and hands three times, then wiped the front of his head and the back of his head, and wiped his ears along with the back of his head, and washed his feet."],[20558,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to come to us. She narrated to us that he said: “Pour ablution water.” So I poured for him into a water vessel, which is a small water skin that holds a mudd and a third, or a mudd and a quarter of water. He said: “Pour over my hand.” He washed his palms three times, then said: “Place it down.” She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ then performed ablution while I was watching. He washed his face three times, rinsed his mouth and inhaled water once, washed his right hand three times, washed his left hand three times, wiped his head twice, beginning with the back of his head then the front of it, and wiped both his ears, their outer and inner sides, washed his right foot three times, and washed his left foot three times."],[20559,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to come to us. I would take a water vessel of ours holding a mudd and a half, or a mudd and a third, and pour water over him. He would wash his hands three times, rinse his mouth, inhale water, wash his face three times, wipe his head twice, then wash his feet three times, three times."],[20560,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution at her place. He wiped his head, wiping his entire head from above the hair, every side of the hair’s direction, without disturbing the hair from its state."],[20561,"She saw the Messenger of God ﷺ performing ablution. She said: He wiped his head, the front of it and the back of it, and his temples and his ears once."],[20562,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ fill his hands with water, then pour it, then wipe his head, its front and back, then return to the middle of his head and wipe, and he brought his hands to his head and wiped his ears, their insides and outsides, and he took hold of the lobes of his ears."],[20563,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her and called for ablution water. A vessel was brought that could hold a mudd and a third, or a mudd and a half, of the Prophet’s mudd ﷺ. He performed ablution: he washed his face, then washed his hand, wiped his head, and wiped the back of his head until reaching its middle, in each wipe."],[20564,"I heard al-Rubayyiʿ bt. Muʿawwidh b. ʿAfrāʾ say: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ perform ablution. He took fresh water for his head, moving his hands back and forth over it."],[20565,"We were in Madinah on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ, and the young girls were beating the duff and singing. Al-Rabīʿ entered upon us, and we mentioned that to her. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me on the morning of my wedding, while I had two young girls singing and lamenting my fathers who were killed at Badr, and they were saying: ..."],[20566,"I said to al-Rubayyi‘ bt. Mu‘awwidh b. ‘Afra’: Describe for me the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said, “If you had seen him, you would have seen the sun rising.”"],[20567,"Mu‘awwidh b. ‘Afra’ sent me with a basket of fresh dates, upon which were small cucumbers with fuzz, to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to love cucumbers. Some good ones had just arrived from Bahrain, so he filled his hand with them and gave them to me."],[20568,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and entered upon me on the morning my marriage was consummated. He sat on my bed, and some young servant girls began playing a tambourine and lamenting those of my forefathers who were killed at Badr, until one of them said..."],[20569,"On the morning of the day of Ashura, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent word to the villages of the Ansar around Madinah: “Whoever began the day fasting should complete his fast, and whoever began the day not fasting should fast the rest of his day.” So we used to fast it, and we would have our young children fast as well. We would make them a toy of wool and take it to the garden, and if one of them cried for food, we would give him that until it was time to break the fast."],[20570,"\"We used to accompany the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in battles, not fighting, but providing water to the soldiers and treating the wounded.\""],[20571,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — and if I had wished, because of my closeness to him, I could have kissed the seal between his shoulders — saying about Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh on the day he died: “The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for him.”"],[20572,"Did you hear your mother mention anything about fasting on Ashura? She said, \"Yes, I heard my mother Ruqayyah say that the Messenger of Allah, may ﷺ , used to give great importance to it. He would even call his grandchildren and the grandchildren of Fatimah, who were still breastfeeding, on that day. He would put his spittle in their mouths and tell their mothers, 'Do not breastfeed them until nightfall.' His spittle would suffice them.\""],[20573,"On the day of Qurayzah and al-Nadir, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came with Safiyyah bt. Huyayy, holding her by the arm. When she saw the captives, she said, “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah.” So he released her arm from his hand, freed her, proposed to her, and married her, giving her as her dowry Ruzaynah."],[20574,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when a woman came to him with a son of hers and said, “O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah for blessing in him, for three of my children have died.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Since you embraced Islam?” She said, “Yes.” He said, “That is a strong protection.” A man said, “Listen, O Rahma, to what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is saying.”"],[20575,"Zaynab bt. Abi Salamah asked him, “What have you named your daughter?” He said, “I named her Barrah.” She said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade this name. You have named her Barrah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do not praise yourselves; Allah knows best who among you are truly righteous.” They said, “What should we name her?” He said, “Name her Zaynab.”"],[20576,"“My name was Barrah, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named her Zaynab.”"],[20577,"She entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was bathing. He took a handful of water and threw it in my face, saying, “Get back, O little foolish one.”"],[20578,"He entered upon Zaynab bt. Abi Salamah, and she narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with Umm Salamah, and he came in to her with al-Hasan and al-Husayn and Fatimah. He placed al-Hasan on one side and al-Husayn on the other side and Fatimah in his lap, then he said: “The mercy of Allah and His blessings be upon you, O people of the household. Indeed, He is Praiseworthy, Glorious.” I and Umm Salamah were sitting, so Umm Salamah wept. He looked at her and said: “What makes you weep?” She said: O Messenger of Allah, you have singled out these and left me and my daughter. He said: “You and your daughter are of the people of the household.”"],[20579,"My mother said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, he would wash, saying: “Go and enter.” She said: So I entered, and he sprinkled water on my face, then said: “Return.” Al-‘Attaf said: My mother said: “I saw the face of Zaynab when she was a very old woman, and nothing of her face had diminished.”"],[20580,"Kulayb b. Wa’il narrated to us: The stepdaughter of the Prophet ﷺ narrated to me—I think she was Zaynab—she said: “The Prophet of Allah ﷺ forbade gourds and hantam jars.” He said: And I think it included “naqir.”"],[20581,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “When you go out to the ‘isha prayer, do not touch perfume.”"],[20582,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you women attends the ‘isha prayer, she should not touch perfume.”"],[20583,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “When one of you women attends the mosque, she should not touch perfume.”"],[20584,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you women attends the mosque, she should not touch perfume.”"],[20585,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you women attends the mosque, she should not touch perfume.”"],[20586,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whichever of you women goes out to the mosque should not touch perfume.”"],[20587,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us and said: “Whichever of you women attends the ‘isha prayer should not touch perfume.”"],[20588,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Give charity, even from your jewelry.” Zaynab said to ‘Abd Allah: Would it suffice for me to make my charity for you and for the orphaned sons of my brother? ‘Abd Allah was light of hand. ‘Abd Allah said: Ask the Prophet ﷺ about that. Zaynab said: So I went to the Prophet ﷺ, and there was a woman from the Ansar. Zaynab said to her: She has come to ask about the same thing I came to ask about. Bilal came out to us, and we said to him: Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and do not tell him who we are: Would it suffice for me to make my charity for my husband and the orphaned sons of my brother? Bilal went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: Which of the Zaynabs? He said: The wife of ‘Abd Allah b. Mas‘ud and a woman from the Ansar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Tell her that she has two rewards: the reward of charity and the reward of kinship.”"],[20589,"Bilal came out, and we said to him: Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Would it suffice for us, of spending, to spend on our husbands and those our laps have sheltered? He entered and asked him, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “Two rewards: the reward of charity and the reward of kinship.”"],[20590,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there any reward for me if I give charity to the children of Abdullah from other than me? He said: \"You will have two portions of the reward.\""],[20591,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while we were in the mosque and said: \"O assembly of women, give charity,\" and he mentioned the hadith."],[20592,"O Abu Abdur-Rahman, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to me while I was among a group of women from the Ansar and said: \"Give charity, even if from your jewelry.\" So ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whether my spending on you and on my brother's children will suffice for me as charity, otherwise I will spend it in the path of Allah. He said: I feel shy to ask him, so you ask him. So I went to the door of the Prophet ﷺ and there was a woman from the Ansar whose need was my need. Bilal came to us, and we said: O Bilal, convey our greetings and the mercy of Allah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and tell him that we have our husbands and the children of our brothers; if our spending on our husbands and the children of our brothers will suffice for us, otherwise we will spend in the path of Allah. Bilal entered and told him, and he said: Convey to them greeting and the mercy of Allah, and inform them that their spending on their husbands and the children of their sisters is doubled - a double for maintaining ties and a double for charity."],[20593,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Charity given to a relative is multiplied twice in reward.\""],[20594,"\"The Prophet ﷺ gave her fifty wasqs of dates at Khaybar and twenty wasqs of barley in Madinah.\""],[20595,"Zaynab bint Qays bin Makhrama wrote to me, saying, \"When she arrived, she left me 10,000 and she was among those who prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ facing both Qiblas.\""],[20596,"She said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father died and left a slave girl, and she gave birth to a boy, and we suspected her. He said: \"Bring him to me.\" When they brought him to him, he looked at him and said: \"The inheritance is his. As for you, veil yourself from him.\""],[20597,"From Zainab bt. Nubayt b. Jabir, wife of Anas b. Malik, she said: Abu Umamah entrusted my mother and my maternal aunt to the Prophet ﷺ, and a gold and pearl ornament called ri'ath was brought to him. She said: \"He adorned them with the ri'ath.\""],[20598,"From his grandfather Abdullah b. Hisham, who had met the Prophet ﷺ; his mother Zainab bt. Humaid took him to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, he is young. \"So he wiped his head and supplicated for him.\""],[20599,"Sahlah bt. Suhayl b. Amr came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, lives with us in our house, and he has reached what men reach and knows what men know. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Breastfeed him, and you will become unlawful to him.\""],[20600,"The wife of Hudhayfah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, enters upon me while I am not wearing my outer garment, and I feel something in myself. He said: \"Breastfeed him, and what you feel will go away from you.\""],[20601,"\"The Prophet ﷺ commanded Sahlah bt. Suhayl to breastfeed Salim to remove what was in the heart of Abu Hudhayfah.\""],[20602,"Sahlah bt. Suhayl came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I see something in the face of Abu Hudhayfah regarding Salim. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Breastfeed him.\" She said: He is an adult. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled and said: \"Do I not know that he is a man?\" She said: So she did so, then came to him and said: By the One who honored you as He honored you, I no longer see anything in the face of Abu Hudhayfah."],[20603,"On the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that Abu Hudhayfa b. Utba b. Rabi'a b. Abd Shams, who was among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, adopted Salim as a son just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ adopted Zayd b. Haritha. Anyone who adopted a man in the pre-Islamic era, the people would call him (the adopted son) by his (adoptive father's) name and he would inherit from his legacy, until Allah revealed concerning that: {Call them by their fathers' names; that is more just in the sight of Allah. But if you do not know their fathers, then they are your brothers in religion and your clients.} So they were returned to their fathers. Whoever had no known father was a client. Aisha said: And Sahla bt. Suhayl b. Amr al-Qurashi, then al-Amiri, was married to Abu Hudhayfa b. Utba b. Rabi'a. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Allah revealed that, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to consider Salim a son, and he used to stay with me and with Abu Hudhayfa in one house, and he would see me while I am in a state of undress, and Allah has revealed about them what you know. So what do you think about his situation, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"Breastfeed him.\" So she breastfed him five sucklings, and he became forbidden by them, and he took the status of her son through breastfeeding."],[20604,"She said: O Messenger of Allah, Salim, the client of Hudhayfa, enters upon me and he has a beard. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Breastfeed him.\" I said: How can I breastfeed him when he has a beard? He said: \"Breastfeed him.\" So she breastfed him, and he used to enter upon her."],[20605,"She said: O Messenger of Allah, should one of us perform ghusl if she has a wet dream? He said: \"Yes, if she sees the fluid.\""],[20606,"On the authority of Salma, the freedwoman of Abu Rafi', the servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me some words that I can say without becoming excessive (in my supplications).\" He said: \"Say: 'Allahu Akbar' ten times. Allah will say, 'This is for Me.' And say: 'Subhan Allah' ten times. Allah will say, 'This is for Me.' And say: 'Allahumma ighfirli' (O Allah, forgive me) and you will find that you have done (repentance).' Say it ten times and Allah will say, 'You have repented.'\""],[20607,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The believing sisters.” Then he mentioned the hadith."],[20608,"Set him free."],[20609,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ to give him my oath of allegiance, and he said: “Go and dye yourself with henna, then come back so that I may accept your allegiance.”"],[20610,"Umar passed by Talha after the death of the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was dejected. He said to him, \"What is the matter with you? Has the leadership of your paternal cousin upset you?\" He said, \"No, but I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'I know a phrase which, if a person says it at the time of his death, it will be a light in his record, and his body and soul will find relief from it at death.' I did not ask him about it until he died.\" Umar said, \"I know it. It is the phrase he wanted his uncle to say. If he knew of anything more saving than it, he would have commanded him with it.\""],[20611,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Dubāʿah bt. al-Zubayr b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib and said to her, “O aunt, perform Hajj.” She said, “I am a heavy woman and I fear being held back.” He said, “Perform Hajj and stipulate that my place of release is wherever I am held back.”"],[20612,"I heard Sarrā’ bt. Nabhān al-Ghanawiyyah say: Nusayb, our slave, asked the Prophet ﷺ about snakes—which of them should be killed? She said: I heard him say, “Kill those of them that appear, the large and the small, the black and the white, for whoever among my Ummah kills one, it will be a ransom for him from the Fire; and whoever is killed by one, he is a martyr.”"],[20613,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Among the signs of the Hour is that the people of the mosque will push one another forward and not find anyone to lead them in prayer.”"],[20614,"I saw Samrāʾ bt. Nahīk, and she had met the Prophet ﷺ. She wore a thick garment and a thick head covering, and in her hand was a whip. She disciplined people, enjoined good, and forbade evil."],[20615,"I heard my grandmother Sahla bt. Asim b. Adi al-Ansariyya say: I was born at Hunayn on the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Hunayn. He named me Sahla and said: \"May Allah make your affairs easy.\" He allotted a share for me, and Abd al-Rahman b. Awf married me on the day I was born."],[20616,"You have rushed. Observe the waiting period of the longer of the two terms: four months and ten days. So I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me. He said: \"And why is that?\" I informed him of the matter. He said: \"If you find a righteous husband, then marry.\""],[20617,"My husband died while with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage; he was Sa'd b. Khawla. I remained after him for two months, then I gave birth to what was in my womb. Abu al-Sanabil b. Ba'kak, a brother of Banu Abd al-Dar, passed by and entered upon my in-laws. He had wanted me for himself, and I had prepared for marriage and adorned myself. He said: What is the matter with you, O Subay'a? I said: I want to marry. He said: No, by Allah, it is four months and ten days. So I put on my clothes and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the house of Umm Salama, and asked him. He said: \"You are lawful, so marry.\""],[20618,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever among you is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for no one dies there except that I will be an intercessor or witness for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[20619,"Ask Subay'a al-Aslamiyya how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed her when her husband died. She said: \"He gave me the ruling that when I give birth, I may marry.\""],[20620,"That he enter upon Subay'a bt. al-Harith al-Aslamiyya and ask her about her hadith and what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her when she miscarried. Umar b. Abd Allah wrote to Abd Allah b. Utba informing him that Subay'a told him that she was married to Sa'd b. Khawla, who was from Banu Amir and was among those who witnessed Badr. He died leaving her during the Farewell Pilgrimage while she was pregnant. She gave birth after his death. When she recovered from her postpartum bleeding, she adorned herself for suitors. Abu al-Sanabil b. Ba'kak, a man from Banu Abd al-Dar, entered upon her and said: Why do I see you adorned? Perhaps you want to marry. By Allah, you are not to marry until four months and ten days pass over you. Subay'a said: When he said that to me, I gathered my clothes upon me until evening, then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about that. He gave me the ruling that I was lawful on the day I gave birth, and ordered me to marry if I wished."],[20621,"Marwan sent Abd Allah b. Utba to Subay'a bt. al-Harith to ask her about what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for her. She informed him that she was married to Sa'd b. Khawla, who died leaving her during the Farewell Pilgrimage and was a Badri. She gave birth before four months and ten days had passed since his death. Abu al-Sanabil b. Ba'kak met her when she had recovered from her postpartum bleeding and had applied kohl. He said: Perhaps you want to marry. It is four months and ten days from your husband's death. She said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned to him what Abu al-Sanabil said. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You are lawful when you gave birth.\""],[20622,"On the authority of his mother, Salma bt. Qays, who was one of the aunts of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She had prayed with him facing both qiblas and was one of the women of Banu Adi b. al-Najjar. She said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him among a group of women from the Ansar. When he stipulated for us that we should not associate anything with Allah, not steal, not commit adultery, not kill our children, not bring a slander we fabricate between our hands and feet, and not disobey him in what is right, he said: \"And do not deceive your husbands.\" She said: So we pledged allegiance to him. Then we left, and I said to one of the women: Go back and ask the Messenger of Allah what he prohibited us regarding our husbands' wealth. She asked him, and he said: \"That she takes his wealth and gives it to someone else.\""],[20623,"On the authority of Umm al-Mundhir al-Ansariyya, who was one of the aunts of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me, and with him was Ali, who was recovering from an illness. In the house there was a hanging cluster of dates. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate from it while standing, and Ali was with him. He said: \"Do not eat from that, for it does not suit you.\" Then he sat down, and I made for him chard and barley. He said: \"Eat from this, for it is better for you.\""],[20624,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to dislike taking from the top of the food."],[20625,"From his grandmother Salmā, who served the Prophet ﷺ, she said: When one of us had a headache, the Prophet ﷺ would say, “Go and have cupping done,” and if he had a pain in his leg, he would say, “Go and dye it with henna.”"],[20626,"The Prophet ﷺ never got a sore or a thorn but that he placed henna on it."],[20627,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “A house with no dates has no food.”"],[20628,"From his mother, who served the Prophet ﷺ, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “A house with no dates, its family goes hungry.”"],[20629,"I visited al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī, ʿAbd Allāh b. Jaʿfar, and ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbbās, and they said, “Describe for us some food that the Prophet ﷺ used to enjoy eating.” She said, “O my sons, you would not desire it today.” So she got up, took some barley, ground it, sifted it, made it into a loaf, seasoned it with oil, sprinkled pepper over it, and brought it to them, saying, “The Prophet ﷺ used to love this.”"],[20630,"The Prophet ﷺ sent Abū Rāfiʿ to the Banū Umayya b. Zayd to kill the dogs, and he sent another man to kill the dogs."],[20631,"His grandmother Salmā, the freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, told her that she had prepared a meat stew for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and served it. He ate, with some of his Companions, and a little of it remained. A Bedouin passed by the Prophet ﷺ, so the Prophet ﷺ called him, and the Bedouin took all of it with his hand. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Put it down.” Then he said, “Say the name of Allah, and eat from the nearest part of it, and you will be satisfied.” He ate until he was full, and some of it remained."],[20632,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a sheep to Abū Rāfiʿ, and that was on the day of the trench, as far as I know. Abū Rāfiʿ roasted it and put it in a basket, then set off with it. The Prophet ﷺ met him returning from the trench and said to him, “O Abū Rāfiʿ, hand me the foreleg.” So I handed it to him. Then he said, “O Abū Rāfiʿ, hand me the foreleg.” So I handed it to him. Then he said, “O Abū Rāfiʿ, hand me the foreleg.” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, does a sheep have more than two forelegs?” He said, “If you had kept silent, you would have handed me whatever I asked for.”"],[20633,"She said: I was with the Prophet ﷺ in the markets when he said, “A man from the people of Paradise will appear to you.” Then I heard a rustling sound, and it was ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ."],[20634,"Salmā, the wife of Abū Rāfiʿ, came complaining about her husband Abū Rāfiʿ. She said, “O Messenger of Allah, he beats me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “What is the matter with you and her?” He said, “She annoys me.” He said to her, “How do you annoy him?” She said, “O Messenger of Allah, he passed wind and then stood to pray. I said, ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever passes wind should repeat his ablution.”’” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled and said, “Do not beat her.”"],[20635,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to Abu Ammar and Umm Ammar, “Be patient, O family of Yasir, for your appointment is Paradise.”"],[20636,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him, and he said, \"Go and perform ablution, then come back so I can pledge allegiance to you.\""],[20637,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the Shaytan has not met 'Umar since he embraced Islam except that he fell upon his face.\""],[20638,"I was present at the death of Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Whenever I and my sister cried out, and the women cried out, he did not forbid us. But when he died, he forbade us from wailing. He carried him to the edge of the grave, with al-Abbas at his side. Al-Fadl b. Abbas and Usamah b. Zayd went down into his grave. I was weeping at his grave, and the sun eclipsed. The people said, 'This is because of his death.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It does not eclipse for the death of anyone or for his life.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a gap in the grave and ordered that it be filled. It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, will it benefit him?' He said: 'Indeed, it benefits him and does not harm him, but it harms the eye of the living.' He died on Tuesday, ten nights having passed from Rabi' al-Awwal in the year ten."],[20639,"The son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was attended. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and every time I and my sister cried out, he forbade us from wailing. Al-Fadl b. al-Abbas washed him, along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and al-Abbas. He was placed on a bier and then carried. I saw him sitting at the edge of the grave, with al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib at his side. Al-Fadl b. Abbas and Usama b. Zayd descended into his grave. I was crying aloud at the grave, and no one forbade me. The sun was eclipsed that day, and the people said it was because of the death of Ibrahim. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The sun is not eclipsed for the death or life of anyone.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ noticed a gap in the bricks and commanded that it be filled, saying: 'When a servant does a deed, Allah loves that he perfects it.' He died on Tuesday, four nights having passed of Rabi' al-Awwal, in the year ten."],[20640,"Sarra' bt. Nabhan—who was a lady of standing in pre-Islamic times—told me: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"Do you know which day this is?\" She said: It was the day you call the Day of Rūs. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \"This is the middle of the Days of Tashrīq.\" He said: \"Do you know which land this is?\" They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \"This is al-Mashʿar al-Ḥarām.\" Then he said: \"I do not know; perhaps I will not meet you after this. Verily your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to you like the sanctity of this day of yours in this land of yours, until you meet your Lord and He asks you about your deeds. Let those of you who are nearest convey to those farthest. Have I conveyed?\" When he came to Madinah, he remained only a short while until he died."],[20641,"The neighborhood dug in the house of Kilāb and discovered a treasure from the ʿĀd people. Kilāb said, 'It is our house,' while the neighborhood said, 'We dug it up.' They brought the dispute to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ruled in favor of the neighborhood and took the fifth from them. With our share of that, we bought a hundred camels, and we brought them to the neighborhood. The zakāh collector wanted to collect zakāh from us, but we refused and went to the Prophet ﷺ about that. He said, 'If you have mixed them with others, then no, otherwise there is nothing due from you this year.' He also said, 'When the zakāh collector departs from a people while he is pleased with them ؓ, and when he departs while he is angry with them, Allah is angry with them.'"],[20642,"I asked his wife just now, 'By Allah, will you be sold, O Sallama, on account of the debt?' I said, 'If Allah has decreed that against me, I will seek reward.' So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him my story. He said, 'Who is in charge of the estate of al-Hubab?' They said, 'His brother Abu al-Yusr b. ʿAmr.' He was summoned, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Set her free. When you hear of slaves that have come to us, come to me and I will compensate you for her.' So they set her free. Slaves then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he summoned Abu al-Yusr and said, 'Take from these slaves a boy for your brother's son.' He went and took a weak, sickly boy and left the strong, robust ones. I said, 'What prevented you from taking one of the strong ones?' He said, 'By Allah, I feared for my brother's son.' It was not long before he died. Ibn Ishaq said: I narrated this hadith to Rabiʿa b. ʿAbd al-Rahman, and he said, 'By Allah, ʿUmar only freed them because of this hadith.'"],[20643,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me in the early days of Islam while I was tending sheep. He said, “O Salāma, what do you testify?” I said, “I testify that there is no god but God and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of God.” He smiled, laughing."],[20644,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “In Thaqīf there is a liar and a destroyer.”"],[20645,"From Salāma bt. al-Ḥurr, sister of Kharsha bt. al-Ḥurr, she said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “A time will come upon people when they will stand for an hour and not find an imam to lead them in prayer.”"],[20646,"I was present when Fatimah was in labor and experiencing pain. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and asked, \"How is she?\" We said, \"She is struggling.\" He said, \"When she gives birth, do not precede me in doing anything.\" She gave birth, and I wrapped the baby in a yellow cloth and cleaned him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and asked, \"How is she?\" I said, \"She has given birth, O Messenger of Allah, and I wrapped the baby in a cloth and cleaned him.\" He said, \"You have disobeyed me.\" I said, \"I seek refuge in Allah from the disobedience of Allah and His Messenger.\" I cleaned and wrapped the baby, and I could not find anything better than that. He said, \"Bring him to me.\" So I removed the yellow cloth and wrapped him in a white cloth, and he blew into him and dressed him in his own garments. Then Ali came and asked, \"What did you name him, O Ali?\" He said, \"I named him Ja'far, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No, but his name is Hasan, and after him will be Husayn, and you, O Ali, are the father of goodness.\""],[20647,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed for rain on Friday in the mosque, raised his hands, and said, “Seek forgiveness from your Lord; indeed He is ever Forgiving,” and he turned his cloak."],[20648,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed Abū Jahm b. Ḥudhayfa over the spoils of war, and he struck a man with his bow, causing a wound that exposed the bone. The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled for it a compensation of fifteen camels."],[20649,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ one day to ask him something, and he began to make excuses to me while I was blaming him. Then the time for the noon prayer came, and I left. My daughter, who was married to Shuraḥbīl b. Ḥasana, came to me, and I found Shuraḥbīl in the house. I began to blame him, and he said, “O girl, do not blame me, for I had a garment that the Messenger of God ﷺ borrowed.” I said, “May my father and mother be sacrificed for him. I have been blaming him since today, not knowing his situation.”"],[20650,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me while I was sitting with Ḥafṣa bt. ʿUmar. He said, “Why don't you teach this one the incantation for namla as you taught her writing?”"],[20651,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man asked him, “Which deeds are best?” He said, “Faith in God, striving in the path of God, and an accepted pilgrimage.”"],[20652,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I want to strive in the path of God.” He said, “Shall I not direct you to a striving with no hardship in it?” The man said, “Yes.” He said, “Pilgrimage to the House.”"],[20653,"She heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “The best deeds are faith in God, striving in the path of God, and an accepted pilgrimage.”"],[20654,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked which deeds are most virtuous, and he said: “Faith in God, striving in the cause of God, and an accepted Hajj.”"],[20655,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ to ask him for something, and he began to make excuses to me while I was reproaching him. Then the prayer time arrived, so I left and went in to see my daughter, who was married to Shurahbil b. Hasanah. I found Shurahbil in the house and said, “The prayer time has come and you are still in the house!” I began to reproach him, but he said, “O maternal aunt, do not blame me, for we had a garment that the Prophet ﷺ borrowed.” I said, “May my father and mother be sacrificed for him! I have been reproaching him since today when this is his situation, and I did not realize it.” Shurahbil said, “It was nothing but a worn-out cloak that we had patched.”"],[20656,"She used to perform a ruqyah incantation of hers from the pre-Islamic era (jahiliyyah), and when Islam came she said, “I will not perform it until I ask the Messenger of God ﷺ for permission.” So I went to him and sought his counsel, and he said, “Perform the ruqyah as long as it contains no shirk (associating partners with God).”"],[20657,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her while a woman called al-Shifaʾ was with her, performing ruqyah for namlah (a skin ailment). The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: “Teach it to Hafsah.”"],[20658,"The Prophet ﷺ said to his grandmother al-Shifaʾ: “Teach Hafsah your ruqyah.”"],[20659,"“We saw women among the qawaʿid (older women past childbearing age) praying the obligatory prayers with the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[20660,"“We saw the qawaʿid women praying with the Prophet ﷺ in the mosque.”"],[20661,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ laying the foundations of the Mosque of Qubaʾ. Sometimes I saw him carrying a huge stone and pressing it against his belly. We would come to take it from him, but he would say, “Leave it and carry another one.” And Jibril ﷺ was directing him toward the Kaʿbah."],[20662,"I looked at the Messenger of God ﷺ when he arrived and alighted and laid the foundations of this mosque, the Mosque of Qubaʾ. I saw him taking a stone or a rock until the stone pressed against him, and I saw the whiteness of the dust on his belly and navel. A man from among his companions would come and say, “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God, give it to me and let me spare you.” He would say, “No, take a stone like it,” until he had laid its foundations. And he said, “Jibril ﷺ is the one directing it toward the Kaʿbah.” She said: It was said that it was the mosque most accurately oriented toward the qiblah."],[20663,"“The Prophet ﷺ proposed to a woman from Kalb, and he sent ʿAʾishah to look at her.” Shaymaʾ bt. al-Harith b. ʿAbd al-ʿUzza b. Rifaʿah, the foster sister of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[20664,"“The Prophet ﷺ brought the women into one of the fortresses of Madinah on the Day of the Trench.” Hassan b. Thabit was a brave man, so he brought him in with the women and locked the door. A Jew came and sat at the gate of the fortress. Safiyyah bt. ʿAbd al-Muttalib said, “Go down, Hassan, to this infidel and kill him.” He said, “I would not put myself at risk for this infidel.” So she wrapped herself with a cloak, took a stone pestle, went down to him, and cut off his head."],[20665,"Safiyyah bt. ʿAbd al-Muttalib did not cover her head in front of the Messenger of God ﷺ nor in front of ten of the first Muhajirun: Hamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib, her brother; Jaʿfar and ʿAli, the two sons of Abu Talib, the sons of her brother; al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwam, her son; ʿUthman b. ʿAffan, the son of her sister's daughter—his mother was Arwa bt. Kurayz, and her mother was al-Baydaʾ Umm Hakim bt. ʿAbd al-Muttalib; Abu Salamah b. ʿAbd al-Asad and Abu Sabrah b. Abi Ruhm, the two sons of her sister Barrah bt. ʿAbd al-Muttalib; and the mother of Tulayb b. Numayr b. Wahb b. ʿAbd Qusayy, Arwa bt. ʿAbd al-Muttalib; and the mother of ʿAbd Allah and Abu Ahmad the blind poet—his name was ʿAbd b. Jahsh b. Riʾab b. Yaʿmur b. Hubayrah b. Murrah b. Ghanm b. Dudan b. Asad b. Khuzaymah—Umaymah bt. ʿAbd al-Muttalib. Safiyyah died during the caliphate of ʿUmar b. al-Khattab."],[20666,"Safiyyah bint 'Abd al-Muttalib mourning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"],[20667,"When the Prophet ﷺ passed away, Safiyyah went out with her cloak shining as she said"],[20668,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me, and I offered him a shoulder blade I had been scraping; he ate it, then stood for prayer.\""],[20669,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out for Uhud, he placed his women in a fortress called Fari', and placed with them Hassan b. Thabit.\" Hassan would watch for the Prophet ﷺ; if he pressed against the polytheists, he pressed with him in the fortress, and if he returned, he returned behind him. She said: Some people from the Jews came, and one of them climbed the fortress until he looked down upon us. I said to Hassan, 'Get up and kill him.' He said, 'That is not in me; if that were in me, I would have been with the Prophet ﷺ.' Safiyyah struck his head until she cut it off. When she cut it off, she said, 'O Hassan, get up and throw his head at them, for they are below the fortress.' He said, 'By Allah, that is not in me.' She said: So I took his head and threw it at them. They said, 'By Allah, we knew that Muhammad would not leave his family unguarded with no one with them,' and they dispersed and went away. She said: Sa'd b. Mu'adh passed by before, and upon him was a trace of yellow perfume, as if he had been a new groom before that, and he was saying"],[20670,"When the people were at ease on the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated on a camel, touching the Stone with a staff in his hand, then entered the Ka'bah while I watched. He saw a group of idols, stood up, broke them, and threw them away while I watched."],[20671,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wet a cloth while he was in the Ka'bah, then began striking the images that were in it.\""],[20672,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated in the year of the conquest, when he entered Makkah, on his mount around the House, touching the corner with his staff."],[20673,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Perform the sa'y, for the sa'y has been prescribed for you.\""],[20674,"I came to Safiyyah bint Shaybah, an elderly woman, and said to her, \"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ marry while he was in ihram?\" She said, \"No, and he married her while they were both out of ihram.\""],[20675,"\"Safiyyah bint 'Umar b. al-Khattab was with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Khaybar.\""],[20676,"She used to say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on Saturday and said, \"If one of you finds nothing but a green twig, let him break his fast with it.\""],[20677,"She used to say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on Saturday.\""],[20678,"that she heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Do not fast on Saturday except in what is obligatory upon you, and if one of you finds nothing but the bark of a tree, let him chew it.\""],[20679,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Do not fast on Saturday except in what its fasting is obligatory upon you, and if one finds nothing but the bark of a tree or a grape vine, let him chew it.\""],[20680,"She heard the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , saying, \"Do not fast on Saturday unless it is a day that has been prescribed for you. And if one of you does not find anything except a piece of wood or the bark of a tree, let him chew on it.\""],[20681,"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'Do not fast on Saturdays unless it is an obligatory fast prescribed by Allah upon you.'\""],[20682,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for whoever dies in Madinah, I will be a witness or an intercessor for him.\" This is how Salih b. Abi al-Akhdar narrated it, and he was contradicted in its chain of transmission."],[20683,"From Sumaytah, a woman from Banu Layth b. Bakr who was in the care of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: I heard her telling Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd that she heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Whoever among you is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for he will die as a martyr and intercession will be made for him.\""],[20684,"From an orphan woman who was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for whoever dies in Madinah, I will be a witness or an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[20685,"From al-Dariyyah, a woman from Banu 'Abd al-Dar who was in the care of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for whoever dies in it, I will be a witness or an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[20686,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to Duba'ah: \"Perform Hajj and make a condition: 'My place of leaving ihram is wherever You detain me.'\""],[20687,"that Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr b. 'Abd al-Muttalib came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I want to perform Hajj; should I make a condition?\" He said: \"Yes.\" She said: \"How should I say it?\" He said: \"Say: Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, my place of leaving ihram is wherever You detain me on earth.\""],[20688,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to Duba'ah: \"Perform Hajj and make a condition: 'My place of leaving ihram is wherever You detain me.'\""],[20689,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to Duba'ah: \"Perform Hajj and make a condition: say: 'O Allah, my place of leaving ihram is wherever You detain me.'\""],[20690,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to Duba'ah: \"Make a condition: 'My place of leaving ihram is wherever You detain me.'\""],[20691,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to Duba'ah: \"Perform Hajj and make a condition: say: 'O Allah, indeed my place of leaving ihram is wherever You detain me.'\""],[20692,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Dubāʿah bint al-Zubayr b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib while she was ill. She said, \"I intend to perform Hajj, but I am ill.\" He said: \"Perform Hajj and stipulate a condition. Say: O Allah, my place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.\""],[20693,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Dubāʿah bint al-Zubayr b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib: \"Do you intend to perform Hajj?\" She said, \"I am ill.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"Perform Hajj and stipulate a condition, and say: O Allah, my place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.\""],[20694,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Dubāʿah bint al-Zubayr b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, who was married to al-Miqdād b. al-Aswad, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said to her: \"Perhaps you intend to perform Hajj?\" She said, \"By Allah, I find myself only in pain.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"Perform Hajj and stipulate a condition. Say: O Allah, my place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.\""],[20695,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to a merchant, \"Perform Hajj and make a condition that my place of confinement is where you have detained me.\""],[20696,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her to stipulate a condition in her ihram."],[20697,"She saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat a shoulder, then stand for prayer without performing wudu."],[20698,"She (Aisha) lifted some meat for the Prophet ﷺ, he took a bite from it, then he prayed without performing ablution."],[20699,"From Zaynab bint Nubayṭ, from Dubāʿah bint al-Zubayr, that the Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"Perform Hajj and stipulate a condition.\""],[20700,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded her to enter ihram. She said, \"I am ill.\" He said to her: \"Stipulate a condition that my place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.\" When Ibn ʿAbbās heard this hadith, he said: \"Praise be to Allah. I would have done it, but I had not heard anything about it.\""],[20701,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was complaining of illness, and I mentioned Hajj to him. He said: \"Perform Hajj and stipulate a condition: O Allah, my place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.\""],[20702,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me while I was ill and said: \"Do you not intend to perform Hajj this year?\" She said, \"I am sick, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Perform Hajj and say: My place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.\""],[20703,"She had a sheep in her house. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to her: \"Feed us from your sheep.\" She said to the messenger, \"Nothing remains with us except the neck, and I am ashamed to send it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" The messenger returned to him and informed him. He said: \"Go back to her and tell her: Send it, for it is the guide of the sheep, the closest part of the sheep to good, and the farthest from harm.\""],[20704,"My mother ʿAmrah bint Rawāḥah said to him: \"Come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and have him witness it.\" He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, saying: \"I have given my son al-Nuʿmān a gift, and ʿAmrah asked me to have you witness that.\" He said: \"Do you have any other children besides him?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said: \"Have you given all of them the like of what you gave al-Nuʿmān?\" He said, \"No.\" Some of these hadith narrators said: \"This is injustice,\" and others said: \"This is coercion. Have someone other than me witness this.\" Mughīrah said: \"Would it not please you that they be equal to you in dutifulness and kindness?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then have someone other than me witness this.\" Mujālid mentioned in his hadith: \"They have a right over you that you treat them justly, just as you have a right over them that they be dutiful to you.\""],[20705,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Going out is obligatory upon every possessor of a waist-wrapper.\""],[20706,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Going forth is obligatory upon every one who wears a loincloth.”"],[20707,"She prepared for the Prophet ﷺ a shelter in the form of palm branches, swept it and perfumed it, and slaughtered a sheep for him, from which he ate. Then he performed ablution and prayed the noon prayer (zuhr). Then she offered him some of its meat, and he ate and prayed the afternoon prayer (asr) without performing ablution."],[20708,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: “This world is sweet and green. Whoever obtains something from it lawfully, that is the one for whom it is blessed. And how many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger will have the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20709,"She entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, she and her sisters, to pledge allegiance to him; they were five. They found him eating dried meat. He chewed a piece of dried meat for them, then handed me the piece, and each one of them chewed a morsel of it. Then they met Allah without finding any bad breath in their mouths."],[20710,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him, and he took from her the pledge: “That you will not commit adultery, nor steal, nor bring a child that you falsely attribute to your husband, whether openly or secretly.” She said: “As for the open attribution, I know it. As for the hidden attribution, O Messenger of Allah, I do not know it. And it has occurred to me that it is harming the child, so I will never harm a child, ever.” He said: “And she never harmed a child of hers until she died.” The wording is that of the hadith of Ibn Abi Fudayk."],[20711,"Concerning the truth of her vision and Quraysh's denial of it, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ inflicted defeat on them at Badr."],[20712,"She was called Azzah, and she was among the early women. She said: Abu Bakr addressed us and said: 'Do not pray on pack-saddles.'"],[20713,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"When an elderly man and an elderly woman commit adultery, stone them to death immediately for the pleasure they have enjoyed.\""],[20714,"Her father went out with his zakat of two saʿs of dates and with his daughter ʿAmrah until he came to the Prophet ﷺ. He poured out the two saʿs, then said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have a need to present to you.” He said: “And what is it?” He said: “That you supplicate for blessing for me and for her, and that you wipe her head, for I have no child other than her.” She said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on me.” She said: “I swear by Allah, it was as though the coolness of the palm of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was upon my liver ever after.”"],[20715,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This world is sweet and green. Whoever takes from it with its due right, Allah blesses him in it. And many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger will have the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, the day he meets Him.”"],[20716,"I came with my mother Burayrah bt. al-Harith al-ʿAtwariyyah among some women of the Muhajirun, and we pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ while he had pitched a tent for him in al-Abtah. He took from us the pledge that we would not associate anything with Allah, [and the rest of] the verse. When we affirmed and stretched out our hands to pledge to him, he said: “I do not touch the hands of women.” Then he sought forgiveness for us, and that was our pledge."],[20717,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed ʿUthman b. Mazʿun on his cheek after he had died, and it is not known that he kissed anyone other than him."],[20718,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is too great for Allah to take the two precious things of a Muslim and then admit him to the Fire” – meaning his two eyes."],[20719,"I was with my mother Raʾitah bt. Sufyan, a woman of Khuzaʿah, while the Prophet ﷺ was taking allegiance from the women, saying: “I take your allegiance upon your not associating anything with Allah, not stealing, not committing adultery, not killing your children, not bringing slander that you fabricate between your hands and feet, and not disobeying me in what is right.” She said: They lowered their heads. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Say: Yes, in what we are able to do.” So they said: “Yes, in what we are able to do.” I was saying as they said, and my mother was saying: “Say: Yes,” and I would say: “Yes.”"],[20720,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the evil of the two blind ones.” It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, what are the two blind ones?” He said: “The torrent and the fierce camel.”"],[20721,"I saw a rider appear on Abu Qubays and shout: 'O treacherous ones, O wicked ones, go forth for three things.' Then he took a rock from Abu Qubays and threw it at the washtub, and the rock split. There did not remain a single house among the houses of Quraysh but that a piece of it entered it, except the houses of Banu Zuhrah. Al-Abbas said: 'This is indeed a vision. Conceal it and do not mention it.' Al-Abbas went and met al-Walid b. Utbah b. Rabi'ah and mentioned it to him. Al-Walid mentioned it to his father, and the report spread. Al-Abbas said: 'I went out in the morning circumambulating the Ka'bah while Abu Jahl was among a group of Quraysh talking about Atikah's vision. When Abu Jahl saw me he said: O Abu al-Fadl, when you finish your circumambulation, come to us. When I finished, I came and sat with them. Abu Jahl said: O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, is it not enough that your men prophesy until your women prophesy? Atikah claimed in her vision that he said: go forth for three things. We will wait for these three. If what she says is true, it will come to pass, and if the three pass without any of that happening, we will write against you a record that you are the most lying household among the Arabs.' Al-Abbas said: 'By Allah, my only response was to deny that and reject that she had seen anything.' Al-Abbas said: 'When evening came, a woman from among the daughters of Abd al-Muttalib came to me and said: Are you content that this wicked one attacks your men and then attacks your women while you listen and offer no objection? By Allah, if Hamzah had been present, he would not have said what he said. I said: By Allah, he did it and I offered no objection. By Allah, I will confront him, and if he returns to it I will suffice you.' Al-Abbas said: 'I went out on the third day after Atikah's vision, angry that I had missed something I wished to catch. By Allah, I was walking toward him—he was a light man with a sharp face, sharp tongue, and sharp eyes—when he came out toward the gate of the mosque hurrying. I said to myself: What is with him, may Allah curse him? Is all this fear of me that I might revile him? Then it turned out he had heard what I had not heard: he heard the voice of Damdam b. Zur'ah b. Amr al-Ghifari shouting in the valley, having cut the nose of his camel, turned his saddle, and torn his shirt, saying: O Quraysh, Muhammad has set out with his companions. I think you will not catch them. Help, help!' Al-Abbas said: 'Then what came of the matter distracted me from him and distracted him from me.'"],[20722,"Atikah bt. Abd al-Muttalib, the paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was living with her brother al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib. She saw a vision shortly before Badr and was alarmed. She sent to her brother Abbas that night when she was alarmed and woke from her sleep, saying: I saw a vision and fear destruction for your people. He said: What did you see? She said: I will not tell you until you promise me that you will not mention it, for if they hear it they will harm us and make us hear what we dislike. Abbas promised her. She said: I saw a rider coming on his mount from the upper part of Makkah, shouting at the top of his voice: O treacherous ones, O wicked ones, go forth in two or three nights. Then he entered the mosque on his mount and shouted three shouts in the mosque. Men, women, and children gathered around him and the people were terrified by him with the greatest terror. Then I saw him on the back of the Ka'bah on his mount, and he shouted three shouts: O treacherous ones, O wicked ones, go forth in two or three nights, until he made the people between the two mountains of Makkah hear. Then he went to a great rock, pulled it from its base, and sent it upon the people of Makkah. The rock came with a rumble until when it was at the foot of the mountain, it shattered. I do not know of any house or dwelling in Makkah but that a piece of that rock entered it. I feared that evil would befall your people. Abbas was alarmed by it and left her. At the end of that night he met al-Walid b. Utbah b. Rabi'ah, who was a close friend of al-Abbas. He told him Atikah's vision and ordered him not to mention it to anyone. Al-Walid mentioned it to his father, Utbah mentioned it to his brother Shaybah, and the report circulated until it reached Abu Jahl b. Hisham and spread widely. When morning came, Abbas went out to circumambulate the House. He found Abu Jahl, Utbah b. Rabi'ah, Shaybah b. Rabi'ah, Umayyah b. Khalaf, Zam'ah b. al-Aswad, and Abu al-Bakhtari among a group talking. When they saw Abbas circumambulating the House, Abu Jahl called out: O Abu al-Fadl, when you finish your circumambulation, come to us. When he finished, he came and sat. Abu Jahl said: O Abu al-Fadl, what vision did Atikah see? He said: She saw nothing. He said: Indeed. Is it not enough for you, O Banu Hashim, with the lies of men, that you have come to us with the lies of women? We and you were like two racehorses, competing for glory for a long time. When the knees drew level, you said: Among us is a prophet. Nothing remains but for you to say: Among us is a prophetess. I do not know among Quraysh a household more lying in men or more lying in women than you. They harmed him that day with the severest harm. Abu Jahl said: Atikah claimed that the rider said: go forth in two or three nights. If these three pass, your lying will become clear to Quraysh, and we will write a document and hang it on the Ka'bah that you are the most lying household among the Arabs, man and woman. Is it not enough for you, O Banu Qusayy, that you took the hijabah, the council, the watering, the provision, and the support, until you came to us claiming a prophet from among you? They harmed him that day with the severest harm. Abbas said to him: Gently, O you who dyes his anus, will you stop? Lying is in you and your household. Those present said to him: O Abu al-Fadl, you were not ignorant or senile. Abbas met severe harm from Atikah for spreading her report. When it was the evening of the third night of the nights in which Atikah saw the vision, the rider whom Abu Sufyan had sent, Damdam b. Amr al-Ghifari, came to them and said: O Banu Ghalib, go forth. Muhammad and his companions have set out to intercept Abu Sufyan, so protect your caravan. Quraysh were terrified with the greatest terror and feared Atikah's vision, and they went forth on every difficult and tractable mount."],[20723,"A'ishah said: 'Atikah bt. Zayd was married to Abdullah b. Abi Bakr al-Siddiq.'"],[20724,"She said, \"I sent a slaughtered sheep to the Prophet ﷺ, but he rejected it and said, 'Send a sheep that does not produce milk.'\""],[20725,"From Umm Ma'bad: a clothing allowance and something from the produce of Yemen and tar for her camels used to come to her. Uthman passed by her and she said: 'Where is my clothing allowance and where is the produce of Yemen that used to come to me?' He said: It is yours, O Umm Ma'bad, with her. He followed her until he gave it to her."],[20726,"Abu Bakr addressed us and prohibited us, or he prohibited, praying on pack-saddles."],[20727,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to al-Ghumaysa': 'No, until he tastes your sweetness and you taste his sweetness.'"],[20728,"From Ali b. Husayn regarding His saying: {and a believing woman if she gives herself to the Prophet} — that it was Umm Sharik al-Azdiyyah who gave herself to the Prophet ﷺ."],[20729,"When Fatimah bt. Asad b. Hashim, the mother of Ali b. Abi Talib, died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her and sat at her head and said: 'May Allah have mercy on you, O my mother. You were my mother after my mother. You fed me while you went hungry, and clothed me while you went unclothed, and denied yourself good things and gave them to me, seeking thereby the face of Allah and the Hereafter.' Then he ordered that she be washed three times. When the water with the camphor was brought, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ poured it with his hand. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ removed his shirt and clothed her in it, and shrouded her with a garment over it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Usamah b. Zayd, Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, Umar b. al-Khattab, and a black slave to dig, and they dug her grave. When they reached the lahd, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dug it with his hand and removed its earth with his hand. When he finished, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and lay down in it, then said: 'O Allah, who gives life and causes death, and He is living and does not die, forgive my mother Fatimah bt. Asad, prompt her with her proof, and widen her entrance, by the right of Your Prophet and the prophets before me, for You are the most merciful of the merciful.' He said the takbir over her four times, and he, al-Abbas, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ placed her in the lahd."],[20730,"Fatimah bt. Muhammad used to suffice him for the inside, and Fatimah bt. Asad used to suffice him for the outside, meaning the Prophet ﷺ."],[20731,"I said to my mother, Fatimah bt. Asad b. Hashim: 'Suffice Fatimah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for carrying water and going for needs, and she will suffice you for the service of the inside: grinding and kneading.'"],[20732,"A client of mine died and left his daughter, so the Messenger of God ﷺ divided his wealth between me and his daughter, giving me half and her half."],[20733,"A slave of ours who had a contract of manumission died—she had freed him—and he left his daughter. The Messenger of God ﷺ divided his inheritance, giving his daughter half and Umm al-Fadl the remaining half."],[20734,"She freed a slave of hers, then he died and left his daughter and his mistress, the daughter of Hamzah. His daughter inherited half, and the daughter of Hamzah inherited half."],[20735,"The daughter of Hamzah freed a slave boy, and he died leaving a daughter, so he divided it between the two of them."],[20736,"The daughter of Hamzah's client died leaving his daughter and the daughter of Hamzah, so the Messenger of God ﷺ divided the wealth between them in two halves."],[20737,"The daughter of Hamzah freed a slave boy, and he died leaving a daughter, so the Prophet ﷺ gave the daughter of Hamzah half and his daughter half."],[20738,"The daughter of Hamzah freed a slave boy, and he died leaving a daughter. The daughter of Hamzah took half and his daughter took half during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[20739,"He said: \"Do you know what the daughter of Hamzah is to me? She is my sister through my mother. She freed a man, and he died, so his inheritance was divided between her and her.\" I said: \"During the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" He said: \"During the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[20740,"A daughter of Hamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib freed a slave boy of hers, and he died during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ leaving a daughter, so the two of them divided the wealth between them in two halves."],[20741,"The daughter of Hamzah freed a slave boy of hers during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he died leaving a daughter. So the Prophet ﷺ gave the daughter of Hamzah half and gave his daughter half."],[20742,"A client of the daughter of Hamzah died leaving his daughter and the daughter of Hamzah, so the Prophet ﷺ gave his daughter half and the daughter of Hamzah half."],[20743,"A daughter of Hamzah, who was a sister of ʿAbd Allah b. Shaddad b. al-Had through his mother, her client died leaving his daughter and the daughter of Hamzah, so the Messenger of God ﷺ divided the wealth into two halves."],[20744,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gifted me a striped silk garment and told me, “Make it into veils among the Fatimahs.” So I tore from it three veils: a veil for Fatimah bt. Asad, a veil for Fatimah bt. Muhammad ﷺ, and a veil for Fatimah bt. Hamza."],[20745,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who has prolonged vaginal bleeding and do not become pure. Should I abandon the prayer?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “That is only a vein, not menstruation. When menstruation begins, abandon the prayer, and when it ends, wash the blood from yourself, then pray.”"],[20746,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh used to have prolonged vaginal bleeding, so she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, “It is only a vein, not menstruation. When menstruation begins, leave the prayer, and when it ends, perform ghusl and pray.”"],[20747,"that Fatimah b. Abu Hubaysh said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have irregular bleeding, shall I abandon the prayer?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"That is only from a vein and it is not menstruation. When the menstruation begins, then abandon the prayer, and when it ends, wash off the blood and pray.\""],[20748,"Fatimah bt. Hubaysh came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I have prolonged vaginal bleeding. Should I abandon the prayer?” He said, “When menstruation begins, leave it for its usual duration, then wash away the blood and pray.”"],[20749,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh sought the Prophet’s ﷺ legal opinion and said, “I have prolonged vaginal bleeding and do not become pure. Should I abandon the prayer?” He said, “That is a vein, not menstruation. When menstruation begins, abandon the prayer, and when it ends, wash the blood from yourself and perform wudu, for it is only a vein, not menstruation.”"],[20750,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I have prolonged vaginal bleeding and do not become pure. Should I abandon the prayer?” He said, “That is only a vein, not menstruation. When menstruation begins, abandon the prayer, and when it ends, wash the blood from yourself and pray.”"],[20751,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “I am a woman who has prolonged vaginal bleeding and do not become pure. Should I abandon the prayer?” He said, “That is only a vein, not menstruation. When menstruation begins, abandon the prayer, and when it ends, wash away the traces of blood from yourself and pray.”"],[20752,"“O Messenger of Allah, I have prolonged vaginal bleeding and the blood does not stop from me.” He said, “Abandon the prayer during the days of your menstruation. When the days of your menstruation pass, perform ghusl and perform wudu for every prayer.”"],[20753,"Abdullah b. Maslama al-Qa’nabi narrated to us, my father Maslama b. Qa’nab narrated to me, from Hisham b. Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, that Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have prolonged vaginal bleeding and do not become pure. Should I abandon the prayer?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “That is only a vein, not menstruation. When menstruation begins, abandon the prayer, and when it ends, wash the blood from yourself and pray.”"],[20754,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I have prolonged vaginal bleeding and I see blood.” He ordered her to sit out the days of her menstrual cycles. When her time of purity came, she performed ghusl, then performed wudu for every prayer. He said, “It is only a vein from you.”"],[20755,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh al-Asadiyya came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking his legal opinion. She was a woman who had prolonged vaginal bleeding and said, “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I do not become pure. Should I abandon the prayer because of this?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “That is only a vein, not menstruation. When it begins, abandon the prayer, and when it ends, wash the blood from yourself, then pray.”"],[20756,"“O Messenger of Allah, I have prolonged vaginal bleeding and do not become pure. Should I then abandon the prayer?” He said, “That is not menstruation; it is only a vein. When menstruation begins, abandon the prayer, and when it departs” or he said “ends,” “perform ghusl to wash away the blood and pray.”"],[20757,"From Fatimah bt. Qays, of Banu Asad of Quraysh, that she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned to her that she was suffering from prolonged menstrual bleeding. Fatimah claimed that he said: \"That is only a vein. When the menstrual period comes, then abandon the prayer; and when it departs, then wash away the trace of blood from yourself, then pray.\""],[20758,"I reached into a pot of ours and burned my hand. My mother took me to a man sitting in the cemetery and said to him, \"O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"At your service, and at your command.\" Then she brought me close to him. He began to blow gently and speak words I did not know what they were. My mother asked afterwards what he used to say. She said he used to say: \"Remove the affliction, Lord of the people. Heal, for You are the Healer; there is no healer except You.\""],[20759,"\"Abu Hudhayfah b. Utbah went with her and her sister Hind to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" When he stipulated conditions upon them, Hind said, \"Or do you know of any of these faults and blemishes among the women of your people?\" Abu Hudhayfah said, \"Pledge allegiance to him, for thus are the conditions stipulated.\""],[20760,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not assign her any lodging or maintenance.\""],[20761,"To return to her dwelling, and he asked her what prompted her to move before her waiting period ended. She sent to inform him that her maternal aunt Fatimah bint Qays had given her the ruling that the Messenger of God ﷺ had ruled for her when Abu ʿAmr b. Hafs al-Makhzumi divorced her—she was to go out, or move. Marwan sent Qabisah b. Dhu'ayb to Fatimah bint Qays to ask her about that, and she informed him that she had been the wife of Abu ʿAmr b. Hafs al-Makhzumi. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ had appointed ʿAli over part of Yemen, and her husband went out with him. He sent her a divorce that remained for her, and he instructed ʿAyyash b. Abi Rabiʿah and al-Harith b. Hisham to spend on her. They said, \"By God, she has no maintenance unless she is pregnant.\" She asked his permission to move, and he permitted her. She said, \"Where shall I move, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"To Ibn Umm Maktum,\" and he was blind; she could put down her garments with him and he would not see her. She remained there until her waiting period ended, and the Prophet ﷺ married her to Usamah b. Zayd. Qabisah returned to Marwan and informed him of that, and Marwan said, \"I have not heard this tradition except from a woman; we shall adhere to the established practice that we found the people upon.\" Fatimah said when that reached her, \"Between me and you is the Book of God. God said, 'Divorce them at their waiting periods' up to His saying, 'You do not know; perhaps God will bring about something after that.'\" She said, \"What matter will be brought about after the three divorces? It is only the man's taking back his wife. So how can you say she has no maintenance if she is not pregnant? How can a woman be detained without maintenance?\""],[20762,"\"Because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to do that.\" Then she related her story and said, \"I argue against you with the Book of Allah. Allah says in His Book: {When you divorce women, divorce them at their 'iddah, and keep count of the 'iddah, and fear Allah, your Lord. Do not turn them out of their houses, nor shall they leave, unless they commit a clear immorality.} {You do not know; perhaps Allah will bring about after that a matter.} The confinement was not for the sake of revocation. Then He said: {When they have reached their term} the third, {then retain them with kindness or release them with kindness.} By Allah, Allah did not mention after the third any confinement after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to do that.\" He said: So I returned to Marwan and informed him, and he said, \"The statement of a woman, the statement of a woman.\" Then he ordered regarding the woman, and she was returned to her house until her 'iddah was completed.\""],[20763,"She said: I entered upon Fatimah bt. Qays, and her husband had divorced her three times. She said, \"He gave me as mut'ah three sa's of barley and three sa's of dates.\" She said, \"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to stay with Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is blind and will not see me when I remove my head covering.\" He said, \"When you become lawful, do not act before me.\" When I became lawful, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Did anyone mention you?\" I said, \"Yes, Mu'awiyah and Abu Jahm.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"As for Abu Jahm, he is harsh in character with his wives, and as for Mu'awiyah, he has no wealth. But marry Usamah.\" I said, \"Usamah?\" out of disdain for the matter of Usamah. Then I said, \"Hearing and obedience to Allah and His Messenger.\" So he married me to Usamah. \"And Allah honored me through Ibn Zayd, and Allah elevated me through Ibn Zayd, and Allah benefited me through Ibn Zayd.\""],[20764,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not grant her lodging or maintenance.\""],[20765,"I entered upon Fatimah bint Qays and asked her about her divorce. She mentioned that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You have no dwelling nor maintenance.\" She said, a caller for the congregational prayer announced and ascended the minbar, and said, \"Tameem Al-Dari informed me,\" and he mentioned the hadith of Al-Jassasah in its entirety."],[20766,"The Prophet ﷺ visited a woman of the Ansar while she was in pain. He said to her: 'How do you find yourself?' She said: Fine, except that Umm Mildam has afflicted me—meaning the fever. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Be patient, for it removes the filth of the son of Adam as the bellows removes the filth of iron.'"],[20767,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a drink on the day of the conquest of Makkah. He drank from it, then handed it to me, and I drank, and I was fasting. I said, “O Messenger of God, I drank while I was fasting.” He said, “Were you making up something for yourself?” I said, “No.” He said, “Then it does not harm you.”"],[20768,"From his grandmother Umm Hani' bt. Abi Talib: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “God favored Quraysh with seven qualities that were not given to anyone before them, nor will they be given to anyone after them. God favored Quraysh in that I am from them, for prophethood is among them; the guardianship of the Kaaba is among them; the provision of water to pilgrims is among them; He aided them against the elephant; they worshiped God for ten years during which no one else worshiped Him; and God revealed a surah of the Quran concerning them that was not revealed concerning anyone else.”"],[20769,"That she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was judging between people, and he continued judging between them until the day had risen. Then he stood and prayed the forenoon prayer, eight rak'ahs."],[20770,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me on the day of the conquest. I said, 'Will you not excuse me from 'Ali?' He said, 'What is the matter with him?' I said, 'A man came to me and sought my protection, and 'Ali said, \"Get away from me, or I will run you through with the spear,\" and he struck me on the front of my head.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Ali would not strike you.'"],[20771,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed in Makkah two rak'ahs and four, and did not repeat it."],[20772,"Umm Hani' came with two men, and 'Ali wanted to kill them. She went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said, 'We have granted protection to those whom Umm Hani' has protected.'"],[20773,"He ate a shoulder, then prayed and did not perform ablution — meaning the Prophet ﷺ."],[20774,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed overnight in my house on the night he was taken on the Night Journey. I missed him during the night, and sleep was withheld from me for fear that some of Quraysh had waylaid him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Jibril came to me, took me by the hand, and brought me out. There, at the house, was a riding beast, smaller than a mule and larger than a donkey. He mounted me upon it, then departed until he brought me to Jerusalem. He showed me Ibrahim, whose physical appearance resembled mine and mine resembled his. He showed me Musa, dark-skinned, tall, with lank hair; I likened him to the men of Azd Shanu'ah. He showed me 'Isa son of Maryam, of medium height, fair with a reddish tinge; I likened him to 'Urwah b. Mas'ud al-Thaqafi. He showed me the Dajjal, his right eye obliterated; I likened him to Qatan b. 'Abd al-'Uzza. I wanted to go out to Quraysh and tell them what I had seen, but she took hold of his garment and said, \"I remind you of Allah: you will go to a people who will reject you and deny your words, and I fear they will assault you.\" She said: He pulled his garment from my hand, then went out to them. He came to them while they were sitting and told them what he had told me. Jubayr b. Mut'im stood up and said, \"O Muhammad, if I were the young man I used to be, you would not have uttered this while you are among us!\" A man from the people said, \"O Muhammad, did you pass by camels of ours in such-and-such a place?\" He said, \"Yes, by Allah, I found them; they had lost a camel of theirs and were searching for it.\" He said, \"Did you pass by the camels of Banu so-and-so?\" He said, \"Yes, in such-and-such a place; a red she-camel of theirs had broken down, and I found them with a wooden bowl of water, and I drank what was in it.\" They said, \"Tell us their number and how many herdsmen were among them.\" He said, \"I was too preoccupied to note their number.\" Then he left. The camels were brought, and he counted them and learned how many herdsmen were among them. Then he came to Quraysh and said, \"You asked me about the camels of Banu so-and-so: they are such-and-such, and among their herdsmen are so-and-so and so-and-so. You asked me about the camels of Banu so-and-so: they are such-and-such, and among their herdsmen are Ibn Abi Quhafah and so-and-so and so-and-so. They will reach you in the morning at the mountain pass.\" So they went early to the pass to see if he had spoken the truth. They met the camels and asked, \"Did a camel of yours go astray?\" They said, \"Yes.\" They asked the other group, \"Did a red she-camel of yours break down?\" They said, \"Yes.\" They said, \"Did you have a wooden bowl?\" Abu Bakr said, \"By Allah, I placed it there, and no one drank from it or poured it on the ground.\" Abu Bakr confirmed him and believed in him, and from that day he was called al-Siddiq."],[20775,"Umm Hani' bint Abi Talib went out displaying her adornment, her two earrings showing. 'Umar b. al-Khattab said to her, 'Know that Muhammad will not avail you anything.' So she came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is the matter with people who claim that my intercession will not reach my household? Indeed, my intercession will reach Ha and Hukm' — Ha and Hukm are two tribes."],[20776,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who has become heavy; teach me something I can say while I am sitting.' He said, 'Say Allahu Akbar one hundred times, for it is better for you than one hundred adorned, accepted camels. Say Subhan Allah one hundred times, for it is better for you than one hundred saddled, bridled horses that you would ride in Allah's cause. Say Alhamdu lillah one hundred times, for it is better for you than one hundred slaves from Banu Isma'il whom you would set free. Say La ilaha illa Allah one hundred times; it leaves no sin and no deed outpaces them.'"],[20777,"She said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Duha in my house on the Day of the Conquest, eight rak'ahs.'"],[20778,"The Prophet entered and said, \"Why do I not see any blessings with you?\" So I said, \"Which blessings do you want?\" He said, \"Indeed, Allah has sent down three blessings: sheep, palm trees, and fire.\""],[20779,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me on the day of the conquest of Makkah, covered with dust. He ordered a bowl, and I can almost see the traces of dough in it. I poured water into it, and he ordered a garment to be placed between me and him as a screen. Then he stood and poured water over himself, then he stood and prayed Duha eight rak'ahs. Mujahid said: I narrated this hadith to Ibn 'Abbas, and he said, 'That is the Ishraq prayer.'"],[20780,"that she said: O Messenger of God, I have grown old and weak, so teach me a supplication by which I may attain [reward]. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O Umm Hāniʾ, if you glorify God one hundred times, it is better than one hundred slaves you would set free. And if you praise God one hundred times, it is better than one hundred horses you would mount in the way of God. And if you declare God’s oneness one hundred times, no deed will outstrip it, and no sin will remain with it.”"],[20781,"that she asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: Will we visit one another when we die, and will some of us see others? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The souls will be birds that cling to trees, until when the Day of Resurrection comes, every soul will enter its body.”"],[20782,"Qaylah bint Makhramah, when she had taken her place in bed after the late evening prayer, would say: In the name of Allah, and upon Allah I rely. I have laid my side down for my Lord, and I ask His forgiveness for my sin. She would say this repeatedly, then she would say: I seek refuge in Allah and in His perfect words, which neither a righteous person nor a wicked person can overstep, from the evil of what descends from the heaven and what ascends into it, from the evil of what descends into the earth and the evil of what comes out from it, from the evil of the trials of the day and the evil of those that come by night, except one that comes with good. I believe in Allah and hold fast to Him. Praise be to Allah, to whose power every thing has submitted; praise be to Allah, before whose might every thing has humbled itself; praise be to Allah, before whose greatness every thing has lowered itself; and praise be to Allah, before whose dominion every thing has bowed in humility. O Allah, I ask You by the bonds of might from Your Throne, by the utmost mercy from Your Book, by Your highest majesty, by Your greatest Name, and by Your perfect words, which neither a righteous person nor a wicked person can overstep, that You look upon us with a merciful look, leaving no sin of ours except that You forgive it, no poverty except that You mend it, no enemy except that You destroy him, no unclothed person except that You clothe him, no debt except that You settle it, and no matter in which there is benefit for us in this world and the Hereafter except that You grant it to us, O Most Merciful of the merciful. I believe in Allah and hold fast to Him. Then she would say: Glory be to Allah thirty-three times, Allah is greater thirty-three times, and praise be to Allah thirty-four times. Then she would say: O my daughter, this is the chief concluding practice: the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him seeking a servant from him, and he said: \"Shall I not direct you to something better than a servant?\" She said, \"Yes.\" So he instructed her to say these hundred at the time of lying down after the late evening prayer."],[20783,"A Jew and a learned man (habr) came to the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"You associate partners with Allah and you set up rivals. You say, 'No, by the Ka'bah,' and you say, 'What Allah wills and you will.'\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to say, \"No, by the Lord of the Ka'bah,\" and to say, \"What Allah wills, then you will.\""],[20784,"That she was in Syria wearing garments made of khazz (a type of silk-blend fabric) and then she would wrap a lower garment (izar). It was said to her, \"Does this not suffice you instead of the lower garment?\" She said, \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ commanding the wearing of the lower garment.\""],[20785,"\"I brought you from the land of Abyssinia until when I was a night or two away from Madinah, I cooked something for you. The firewood ran out, so I went out to look for some. I reached for the pot and it tipped over onto your forearm.\" Then she came with him to Madinah and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, this is Muhammad b. Hatib, and he is the first to be named after you.\" He wiped his hand over your head and prayed for blessing for you, and he spat lightly into your mouth. Then he began to spit lightly on your hand and say: \"Remove the affliction, Lord of the people, and heal, for You are the Healer; there is no healing except Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness.\" I did not get up with you from his presence until your hand was healed."],[20786,"My father was brought slain on the day of Uhud, and his sister Fatimah began to weep over him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not weep over him, for the angels kept shading him with their wings until he was lifted up.\""],[20787,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not assign me any lodging or maintenance.\""],[20788,"Fatimah bt. Qays said, \"O Messenger of God, my husband has divorced me and I fear that he may break in upon me.\" So he ordered her to move."],[20789,"That she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked his legal opinion about her going out of her house. She claimed that he ordered her to move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man. Marwan refused but to suspect the hadith of Fatimah concerning the divorced woman's going out of her house."],[20790,"\"That she was married to Abu Amr b. Hafs b. al-Mughirah, who divorced her with three pronouncements of divorce. She came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked his legal opinion about her going out of her house, and he ordered her to move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum.\""],[20791,"\"And that she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked his legal opinion about her going out of her house, and he ordered her to move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man.\""],[20792,"And that she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and sought his ruling about leaving her house, so he ordered her to move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum the blind."],[20793,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us from Malik; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us saying: ʿAbdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us: Malik narrated to us from ʿAbdullah b. Yazid, the freedman of al-Aswad b. Sufyan, from Abu Salamah b. ʿAbd al-Rahman, from Fatimah bint Qays: Abu ʿAmr b. Hafs divorced her irrevocably while he was absent. He sent his agent with barley, and she objected to it. He said, \"By God, you have no claim on us for anything.\" She went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said, \"You have no maintenance,\" and ordered her to observe her waiting period in the house of Umm Sharik. Then he said, \"That is a woman whom my companions visit. Observe your waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a blind man; you can put down your garments. When you are free, come to me.\" When I was free, I mentioned to him that Muʿawiyah b. Abi Sufyan and Abu Jahm b. Hudhayfah had proposed to me. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"As for Abu Jahm, he does not put down his staff from his shoulder; and as for Muʿawiyah, he is destitute with no wealth. Marry Usamah b. Zayd.\" She said, \"I disliked him, but then he said, 'Marry Usamah b. Zayd,' and God put good in him, and I was pleased with him.\""],[20794,"My husband divorced me, and he used to provide me with food that was bad. I was a woman who had no one, so I said, \"By God, if I am entitled to maintenance, I will seek it.\" I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said, \"You have no maintenance and no residence. Observe your waiting period at Ibn Umm Maktum's, for he is blind. When you are free, inform me.\" When I was free, I informed him, and he said, \"Who proposed to you?\" I said, \"Muʿawiyah and another man.\" He said, \"As for Muʿawiyah, he is a young man of the young men of Quraysh, with nothing in his hand—or he has nothing—and as for the other, he is a man of evil. Marry Usamah b. Zayd.\" I disliked him, but he said, \"Marry him,\" so I married him."],[20795,"That he should spend on her, so she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and informed him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"You have no maintenance, so go and move to Ibn Umm Maktum and stay with him, for he is a blind man; you can put down your garments with him.\""],[20796,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAziz b. Muhammad narrated to us from Muhammad b. ʿAmr from Abu Salamah from Fatimah bint Qays: She was married to a man from Banu Makhzum, and he divorced her irrevocably. She sent to his family seeking maintenance, and they said, \"You have no maintenance from us.\" That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, \"You have no maintenance from them, and you must observe the waiting period. Move to Umm Sharik.\" Then he said, \"Umm Sharik receives visits from her brothers among the Emigrants. No, rather move to Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a blind man; if you put down your garments, he will not see anything. And do not miss us with regard to yourself.\" When she became free, she mentioned that Muʿawiyah b. Abi Sufyan and Abu Jahm had proposed to her. He said, \"As for Muʿawiyah, he has no wealth; and as for Abu Jahm, he does not put down his staff from his shoulder. Where are you with regard to Usamah?\" Her family seemed to dislike that, but she said, \"By God, I will not marry except what the Messenger of God ﷺ told me,\" so she married him."],[20797,"She was married to a man from Banu Makhzum, and he divorced her irrevocably. She sent to his family seeking maintenance, and they said, \"You have no maintenance from us.\" That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, \"You have no maintenance from them, and you must observe the waiting period. Move to Umm Sharik.\" Then he said, \"Umm Sharik receives visits from her brothers among the first Emigrants. Move to Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a blind man; if you put down your garments, he will not see anything. So do not miss us with regard to yourself.\" When she became free, men proposed to her, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Where are you with regard to Usamah?\" Her family seemed to dislike that, but she said, \"By God, I will not marry except the one whom the Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned,\" so she married him."],[20798,"I was with a man from Banu Makhzum, and he divorced me irrevocably. I sent to his family seeking maintenance, and they said, \"You have no maintenance from us.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"You have no maintenance from them, and you must observe the waiting period. Move to Umm Sharik, and do not miss us with regard to yourself.\" Then he said, \"Umm Sharik receives visits from her brothers among the first Emigrants, but move to Ibn Umm Maktum, for he has lost his sight; if you put down something, he will not see anything.\""],[20799,"Her husband Hafs b. al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi divorced her three times during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, then he went to Yemen. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"She has no maintenance, and she must observe the waiting period.\" He sent a messenger to her saying, \"Do not get ahead of me with regard to yourself,\" and ordered her to move to Umm Sharik. Then he sent to her: \"Umm Sharik is visited by the first Emigrants; move to Ibn Umm Maktum.\" When her waiting period ended, the Messenger of God ﷺ married her to Usamah b. Zayd b. Harithah."],[20800,"Her husband divorced her during the time of the Prophet Muhammad, may ﷺ . He used to provide for her, but when she saw that he had stopped providing for her, she said, \"By Allah, I will speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . If I have a provision, I will take what is sufficient for me, and if I do not have a provision, I will not take anything.\" So I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and he said, \"You will not have a place to live nor will you receive any provision.\""],[20801,"The Messenger of God ﷺ delayed the last evening prayer one night, then he came out and said, \"Only a conversation that Tamim al-Dari was relating to me held me back, about a man who was on an island among the islands of the sea. There he saw a woman dragging her hair. He said, 'What are you?' She said, 'I am the Jassasah. Are you surprised at me?' He said, 'Yes. Go to that palace.' So I went to it, and there was a man dragging his hair, chained in fetters, leaping between the sky and the earth. He said to him, 'What are you?' He said, 'I am the Dajjal. Has the Prophet of the unlettered people appeared?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Did they obey him or disobey him?' He said, 'No, rather they obeyed him.' He said, 'That is better for them. Have the waters receded?'\""],[20802,"The Prophet ﷺ sat for the last evening prayer until the people slept, then he came out and said, \"A conversation that Tamim al-Dari related to me held me back, about a man who was on an island. There he saw a woman dragging her hair. He said, 'What are you?' She said, 'I am the Jassasah. Are you surprised at me? Go to that palace.' So he went, and there was a man dragging his hair, chained in fetters. I said, 'Who are you?' He said, 'I am the Dajjal.' He said, 'Has their messenger appeared among the unlettered people?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Did they obey him or disobey him?' I said, 'Rather they obeyed him.' He said, 'That is better for them.'\""],[20803,"That you might be pregnant, so she came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned her situation to him. The Prophet ﷺ said to her, \"You have no maintenance.\" She asked his permission to move, and he permitted her. She said, \"Where to, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"To Ibn Umm Maktum,\" and he was blind; she could put down her garments with him and he would not see her. When her waiting period ended with him, the Messenger of God ﷺ married her to Usamah b. Zayd. Marwan sent Qabisah b. Dhu'ayb to her to ask about that, and she narrated it to him. Qabisah came to Marwan and informed him, and Marwan said, \"I have not heard this tradition except from a woman.\""],[20804,"That he divorced her three times and went out on one of the military expeditions, and he ordered an agent of his to give her some maintenance, but she deemed it little. So she went to one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ entered while she was with her. She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this is Fatimah bt. Qays. So-and-so divorced her and sent her some maintenance, but she returned it, and he claimed that it was something he gave as a favor.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"He told the truth.\" Then he said to her, \"Move to Umm Maktum and observe your 'iddah with her.\" Then he said, \"No, Umm Maktum is a woman who has many visitors, but move to 'Abdullah b. Umm Maktum, for he is blind.\" So she moved to him and observed her 'iddah with him until her 'iddah ended. Then Abu Jahm and Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan proposed to her, and she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to consult him about them. He said, \"As for Abu Jahm, I fear for you his staff's looseness, and as for Mu'awiyah, he is a man who is devoid of wealth.\" So she married Usamah b. Zayd after that."],[20805,"My husband Abu Hafs b. al-Mughirah sent me my divorce three times with 'Ayyash b. Abi Rabi'ah, and he sent me five sa's of barley and five sa's of dates. I said, \"Is there no maintenance for me except this?\" So I gathered my clothes and went to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"How many times did he divorce you?\" I said, \"Three.\" He said, \"He has spoken the truth. You have no maintenance, and observe your 'iddah in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, where you may put aside your clothes.\""],[20806,"\"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not grant me lodging or maintenance.\""],[20807,"\"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not grant me lodging or maintenance.\""],[20808,"My husband divorced me three times, and I came to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"You have no maintenance and no lodging.\""],[20809,"From 'Amir al-Sha'bi: Fatimah bt. Qays narrated to me, and she had been married to Abu Hafs b. 'Amr or 'Amr b. Hafs. She came to the Prophet ﷺ regarding maintenance and lodging. He said to her, \"Listen, O daughter of Qays,\" and he gestured with his hand, extending it over part of his face as if shielding himself from her and as if saying, \"Be quiet. Maintenance is only for a woman from her husband as long as he has the right to take her back. So she has no maintenance and no lodging. Go to so-and-so,\" or he said, \"Umm Sharik, and observe your 'iddah with her.\" Then he said, \"No, that is a woman to whom people gather,\" or he said, \"at whose place people converse. Observe your 'iddah in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum.\""],[20810,"The people of Madinah disagreed with us regarding the lodging and maintenance of a divorced woman. They said to me, \"Between us and you is the hadith of Fatimah bt. Qays.\" So I went to her and entered upon her and asked her. She said, \"My husband divorced me, and his brother told me, 'You have no lodging and no maintenance.' So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'O daughter of Qays, lodging and maintenance are only as long as your husband has the right to take you back.'\""],[20811,"That she asked the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"My husband divorced me and did not assign me maintenance or lodging.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to her, \"Your husband will not take you back. Lodging and maintenance are only for the one whose husband may take her back.\""],[20812,"I entered upon Fatimah bt. Qays in Madinah and asked her about the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said, \"My husband divorced me irrevocably, and I brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding lodging and maintenance. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not grant me lodging or maintenance, and he commanded me to observe my 'iddah in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum.\""],[20813,"We entered upon Fatimah bt. Qays and asked her about a woman irrevocably divorced three times: where should she observe her waiting period? She said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted me, after my husband had divorced me, to observe my waiting period in my family's home.\""],[20814,"\"My husband divorced me three times, and I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; he did not grant me housing or maintenance.\""],[20815,"Fatimah bt. Qays was given an irrevocable divorce by her husband, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You have no right to maintenance or housing.\""],[20816,"\"My husband divorced me three times, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not grant me housing or maintenance.\""],[20817,"\"He divorced me three times while he was setting out for Yemen, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ affirmed that. I sent to my husband's family asking them for my maintenance, and they wanted to turn me out of my dwelling. So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum.'\""],[20818,"I met Fatimah bt. Qays at al-Harrah and asked her how her affair had been. She said: \"My husband Abu 'Amr divorced me before he departed for Yemen, and he appointed 'Ayyash b. Abi Rabi'ah as his agent and gave me some maintenance. I brought the matter before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'You are entitled to neither maintenance nor housing from them.'\""],[20819,"I heard al-Sha'bi say: Fatimah bt. Qays narrated to me that she came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, my husband has divorced me three times, and I sought housing and maintenance.\" He said: \"One or two pronouncements of divorce mean you inherit from him and he inherits from you; with three you do not inherit from him and he does not inherit from you, and you have no right to housing or maintenance. Stay with Ibn Umm Maktum.\""],[20820,"\"I was married to a man of the Banu Makhzum, and he divorced me three times. He said: 'You are entitled to no maintenance from me.' So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, my husband has divorced me, and I asked him for maintenance, and he said: \"You have no right to housing or maintenance with me.\"' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You are entitled to housing and maintenance.' He sent for him, and he said: 'I divorced her three times.' He said: 'Then observe your waiting period in the house of Umm Sharik.' Then he said: 'Umm Sharik is a woman who receives many visitors, so rather observe your waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a blind man.'\""],[20821,"\"My husband divorced me three times during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I came to the Prophet ﷺ asking him about housing and maintenance, and he did not grant me housing or maintenance.\""],[20822,"\"Abu 'Amr b. Hafs sent me word of my divorce while he was setting out with an army to Yemen. I asked his heirs for maintenance and housing, and they said: 'He sent us nothing about that, nor did he instruct us concerning it.' So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu 'Amr b. Hafs sent me word of my divorce, and I asked for housing and maintenance, and his heirs said: \"He sent us nothing about that.\"' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Housing and maintenance are only for a woman whose husband has the right to take her back. If she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband, then she has no right to maintenance or housing.'\""],[20823,"\"I married Hafs b. al-Mughirah, and he was one of the best young men of Quraysh. When I became widowed, 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf proposed to me along with a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to me on behalf of his freedman Usamah b. Zayd. I had been told that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever loves me should love Usamah.' So when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke to me, I said: 'My affair is in your hands; marry me to whomever you wish.' He said: 'Move to Umm Sharik' — and Umm Sharik was a wealthy woman who spent generously in the way of Allah and received many guests. I said: 'I will do so.' He said: 'Do not do so, for Umm Sharik is a woman with many guests, and I dislike that your headcovering should fall off or your garment be uncovered from your shins so that people see something of you that you dislike. Instead, move to your cousin 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr b. Umm Maktum' — and he was a man of Banu Fihr, the Fihr of Quraysh, from the same clan as her. So I moved to him.\""],[20824,"\"I asked Fatimah bt. Qays how her affair had been. She said: 'My husband divorced me three times all at once, and I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: My in-laws claim that I am entitled to neither housing nor maintenance.' He said: 'They have spoken the truth. Go and observe your waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum' — and he was blind. She said: 'After my waiting period ended, Abu al-Jahm b. Hudhayfah proposed to her, and after him Mu'awiyah. She consulted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"As for Abu al-Jahm, he is a beater of women, and as for Mu'awiyah, he is a poor man with no property. But why not Usamah?\" I said: \"Should I marry Usamah?\" He said: \"Yes, marry Usamah.\"'\""],[20825,"That her husband divorced her thrice, and the Prophet ﷺ did not grant her accommodation or maintenance."],[20826,"That her husband divorced her thrice, and the Messenger of God ﷺ did not grant her accommodation or maintenance. He said: Her husband was Abu Hafs b. Amr b. al-Mughira."],[20827,"My husband divorced me thrice during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'No accommodation and no maintenance.'"],[20828,"My husband divorced me thrice, and I wanted maintenance. I went to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'Move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, your paternal cousin, and observe your waiting period with him.'"],[20829,"That her husband divorced her, and she went to the Prophet ﷺ who commanded her to observe her waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum."],[20830,"I went with a man until we entered upon Fatimah bt. Qays, the sister of al-Dahhak b. Qays. We said, 'O Fatimah, narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ.' She said, 'Yes.' She fed us fresh dates and gave us drink, then said: 'One day the Messenger of God ﷺ came out and sat on the pulpit, and the people sought refuge with him and gathered around him. He said, \"O people, only a piece of news has made me sit.\" She said: It was a time other than his usual sitting time. Tamim al-Dari came to me today during the midday heat and told me that some paternal cousins of his were thrown by their ship onto an island in the sea, which they did not recognize. They went out walking on it and met something they did not know whether it was a man or a woman because of the hair covering it. They said, \"Who are you?\" It said, \"I am al-Jassasa.\" They said, \"Tell us.\" It said, \"I will not tell you, nor will I ask you. If you want news, go to that monastery,\" and it pointed to a monastery on the island not far away. We went walking until we entered, and there was a man bound with large, heavy iron, leaning his back against the foot of a mountain. He said, \"Who are you?\" We said, \"People from the Arabs.\" He said, \"What has the unlettered Prophet ﷺ done, the one who is awaited?\" We said, \"He has come forth.\" He said, \"What has the date palms between Uman and Baysan done?\" We said, \"They are as they are, bearing fruit and being eaten.\" He said, \"What has the spring of Zughar done?\" We said, \"It is as it was.\" He said, \"What has the lake of Tiberias done?\" We said, \"It is full.\" He struck the sole of his foot with his hand and said, \"If I were to come out of this place of mine, I would not leave any spot on earth without treading on it, except Makkah and Taybah.\" Then he sighed and moved through the mountain, then fell; then he moved again, farther than that, then fell; then he moved a third time and went into the mountain, then fell. We said, \"What is wrong with him? May God not bless him.\" It seemed that the Messenger of God ﷺ was pleased by his mention of Makkah and Taybah. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Taybah — twice — the Dajjal will not enter it. There is no mountain pass there but an angel with a drawn sword is upon it, and likewise from the direction of Yemen.\" Then he pointed with his hand: \"And the sleeve of his shirt —\" He made the gesture close to thirty times towards the direction of Iraq, and that is close to thirty times.'"],[20831,"I heard the caller of the Messenger of God ﷺ announcing that prayer was to be held in congregation. I went out with a group of women from the Ansar until we came to the mosque, and the Messenger of God ﷺ led us in the noon prayer. Then he ascended the pulpit and turned his face to us, smiling. Then he said, 'By God, I have not gathered you for desire or fear, but for a report that Tamim al-Dari told me. He came to me, accepted Islam, and pledged allegiance. He told me that he sailed with thirty men from Lakhm and Judham, two tribes of the Arabs from the people of Yemen. They encountered the sea when it was raging, and the waves tossed them for a month. Then it cast them near sunset onto an island of the islands of the sea. There we were met by a shaggy creature whose front could not be distinguished from its back. We said, \"What are you, O creature?\" God permitted it, and it spoke to us with a sharp, fluent tongue, saying, \"I am al-Jassasa.\" We said, \"And what is al-Jassasa?\" It said, \"Away from me! Go to that monastery at the far end of the island, for in it is a man who is longing for news of you.\" He said: We went to the monastery, and there was a man the largest we had ever seen and the best in body. His right eye was obliterated, as if it were a piece of phlegm on a plastered wall. His hands were chained to his neck, and his legs were bound with shackles from his knees to his feet. We said to him, \"What are you, O man?\" He said, \"As for my news, you have attained it. But tell me about your news: what brought you to this island? No human being has reached this island since I came out to it.\" We told him. He said, \"Tell me about the lake of Tiberias: what has happened to it?\" We said, \"About which of its affairs do you ask?\" He said, \"Has its water dried up? Have wonders appeared in it?\" We said, \"No.\" He said, \"Indeed, it will happen.\" Then he was silent for a long time. Then he said, \"Tell me about the spring of Zughar: what has happened to it?\" We said, \"About which of its affairs do you ask?\" He said, \"Do its people cultivate with it?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Indeed, its water will sink away.\" Then he was silent for a long time. Then he said, \"Tell me about the date palms of Baysan: what has happened to them?\" We said, \"About which of their affairs do you ask?\" He said, \"Do they bear fruit?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Indeed, they will not bear fruit.\" Then he was silent for a long time. Then he said, \"Tell me about the unlettered Prophet: what has happened?\" We said, \"About which of his affairs do you ask?\" He said, \"Has he appeared yet?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"What did the Arabs do with him?\" We said, \"Some of them fought him, and some of them believed him.\" He said, \"Indeed, whoever believed him, that is better for him.\" We said, \"Tell us your news, O man.\" He said, \"Do you not know me?\" We said, \"If we knew you, we would not ask you.\" He said, \"I am the Dajjal. It is near that I will be permitted to come out. When I come out, I will tread the islands of the Arabs, all of them, except Makkah and Taybah. Every time I want them, an angel meets me with a drawn sword and repels me from them.\" Abu al-Ashhab said: Amir said: Fatimah bt. Qays said: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ raising his hands until we saw the whiteness of his armpits. Then he said, \"Shall I not tell you that this is Taybah?\" three times. Then he said, \"Shall I not tell you that he is in the sea of Syria?\" three times. Then he fainted for a while, then recovered, then it was relieved from him, and he said, \"Rather, he is in the sea of Iraq. When he comes out, he will come out from a town called Isfahan, from a village of its villages called Ristaqabad. Those who come out in his vanguard will be seventy thousand, wearing the sijan. With him are two rivers: a river of water and a river of fire. Whoever of you reaches that and is told, 'Enter the water,' let him not enter it, for it is fire. And when he is told, 'Enter the fire,' let him enter it, for it is water.'"],[20832,"Ibn Amir said: 'Narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ without attributing it to anyone other than yourself.' She said, 'If you wish, I will do so.' He said to her, 'Yes, narrate to me.' She said, 'I heard the call of the caller of the Messenger of God ﷺ announcing that prayer was to be held in congregation. I went out to the mosque and prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I was in the row of women that was next to the backs of the men. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished his prayer, he sat on the pulpit, smiling. He said, \"Let every person remain in his prayer place.\" Then he said, \"Do you know why I have gathered you?\" They said, \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"By God, I have not gathered you for desire or fear, but I gathered you because Tamim al-Dari was a Christian man. He came, pledged allegiance, and accepted Islam, and he told me a report that agreed with what I used to tell you about the Messiah of the Dajjal. He told me that he sailed in a seafaring ship with thirty men from Lakhm and Judham, and the waves played with them for a month in the sea. Then they were cast onto an island in the sea at the setting of the sun. They sat in the ship's boat and entered the island, and they were met by a shaggy creature, very hairy, whose front could not be distinguished from its back because of the abundance of hair. They said, \"Woe to you! What are you?\" It said, \"I am al-Jassasa.\" They said, \"What is al-Jassasa?\" It said, \"O people, go to this man in the monastery, for he is longing for news of you.\" He said, 'When it named a man to us, we were alarmed that it might be a she-devil. We went quickly until we entered the monastery, and in it was the largest human being we had ever seen in creation and the most tightly bound, with his hands gathered to his neck and from his knees to his ankles with iron. We said, \"Woe to you! What are you?\" He said, \"You have attained my news, so tell me what you are.\" They said, \"People from the Arabs. We sailed in a seafaring ship and encountered the sea when it was raging, and the waves played with us for a month. Then they cast us onto this island of yours. We sat in its boat and entered the island, and we met a shaggy creature, very hairy, whose front we could not distinguish from its back because of the abundance of hair. We said, \"Woe to you! What are you?\" It said, \"I am al-Jassasa.\" We said, \"What is al-Jassasa?\" It said, \"Go to this man, for he is longing for news of you.\" So we came to you quickly, and we were alarmed by it and did not feel safe that it might be a she-devil.\" He said, \"Tell me about the date palms of Baysan.\" We said, \"About which of their affairs do you ask?\" He said, \"I ask you about its palms: do they bear fruit?\" We said to him, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Indeed, it is near that they will not bear fruit.\" He said, \"Tell me about the lake of Tiberias.\" We said, \"About which of its affairs do you ask?\" He said, \"Is there water in it?\" We said, \"It has much water.\" He said, \"Tell me about the spring of Zughar.\" They said, \"About which of its affairs do you ask?\" He said, \"Is there water in the spring, and do its people cultivate with the spring water?\" We said, \"Yes, and it has much water, and its people cultivate with its water.\" He said, \"Tell me about the unlettered Prophet: what has happened?\" They said, \"He came out from Makkah and settled in Yathrib.\" He said, \"Did the Arabs fight him?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"What did he do with them?\" We told him that he prevailed over the Arabs near him and they obeyed him. He said to them, \"Has that happened?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Indeed, that is better for them, that they should do that and obey him. I am going to tell you about myself: I am the Messiah, and it is near that I will be permitted to come out. I will come out and travel through the earth, and I will not leave any town but that I will descend upon it in forty nights, except Makkah and Taybah, for they are forbidden to me. Every time I want to enter one of them, an angel meets me with a drawn sword, repelling me from it. And on every mountain pass there are angels guarding them.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ struck the pulpit with his staff and said, \"This is Taybah, this is Taybah, this is Taybah, meaning al-Madinah. Did I not tell you that?\" The people said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"What pleased me about the report of Tamim al-Dari is that it agreed with what I used to tell you about him, and about al-Madinah and Makkah. Indeed, he is in the sea of Syria or the sea of Yemen. Nay, rather from the direction of the east. He is from the direction of the east. He is from the direction of the east. He is from the direction of the east.\" And he pointed with his hand to the east. She said, 'I memorized this from the Messenger of God ﷺ.'"],[20833,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ called out, 'Prayer in congregation!' at an hour when he did not usually call it. The people went out to the mosque, and the Prophet ﷺ came, ascended the pulpit, then said, 'I warn you of the Dajjal,' three times. 'He did not exist in the past, and he will be among you, O community. Tamim al-Dari told me that he sailed on the sea of Syria with a group from Lakhm and Judham, and the wind cast them onto an island of its islands. There they were met by a dark creature dragging its hair. They said, \"What are you?\" It said, \"I am al-Jassasa.\" They said, \"Tell us.\" It said, \"I am not going to tell you, nor did I ask you. But go to a man in this monastery, for he is longing for news of you.\" They went to him, and there was a man with an obliterated eye, bound to a pillar in iron. He said, \"What are you?\" They said, \"We are the Arabs.\" He said, \"What have the Arabs done?\" We said, \"An unlettered Prophet has been sent to them, calling them to God.\" He said, \"What have the people done?\" They said, \"Some people followed him, and some people abandoned him.\" He said, \"Indeed, if they follow him and believe him, it is better for them, if only they knew.\" Then he said, \"What have the Arabs done? What is their clothing?\" We said, \"Wool and cotton, which their women spin.\" He struck his hand on his thigh and said, \"Alas!\" Then he said, \"What have the date palms of Baysan done?\" We said, \"They are strong, and we find them every year.\" He struck his hand on his thigh and said, \"Alas!\" Then he said, \"What has the spring of Zughar done?\" We said, \"Its water is abundant, flowing, giving drink to whoever comes to it.\" He struck his hand on his thigh and said, \"Alas!\" Then he said, \"If God were to release me from my bonds, there would remain no watering place but that I would enter it, except Makkah and Taybah, for I have no entry to them.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"That is Makkah, and this is Taybah. God has made it sacred just as Ibrahim made Makkah sacred. Indeed, there is no mountain pass or lane but that an angel stands over it with a drawn sword, defending it from the Dajjal until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[20834,"While the people were in al-Madinah with no alarm, the Messenger of God ﷺ came out, prayed the noon prayer, then turned walking until he ascended the pulpit. The people were alarmed by that. When he saw that in their faces, he said, 'O people, I did not come out for a matter to alarm you, but a matter came to me that made me happy, and I wanted to inform you of the joy of your Prophet. Tamim al-Dari told me that some paternal cousins of his went to sea, and their ship brought them to an island they did not recognize. They went out walking, and there was a being with so much hair that they did not know whether it was male or female. They said, \"Who are you?\" It said, \"I am al-Jassasa.\" They said, \"Tell us.\" It said, \"Go to the monastery, for in it is a man who is longing for you to speak to him.\" They entered the monastery, and there was a bound man groaning severely. He said, \"Who are you?\" They said, \"From the people of Palestine, from the island of the Arabs.\" He said, \"Has their Prophet come out yet?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"What has he done?\" They said, \"Some people pledged allegiance to him, and some people parted from him. He fought those of his companions who had pledged allegiance to him until the people of stone and mud gave him submission.\" He said, \"What has the lake of Tiberias done?\" They said, \"It is full, its sides overflowing.\" He said, \"What has the spring of Zughar done?\" They said, \"Its sides are overflowing.\" He said, \"What have the date palms between Uman and Baysan done?\" They said, \"They are bearing fruit.\" He said, \"If I were to escape from these bonds of mine, I would tread the earth, except Taybah.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"It is Taybah,\" twice. \"Al-Madinah. There is no road or narrow place or wide place, easy or difficult in it, but that an angel stands over it with a drawn sword. If he wanted to enter it, he would strike his face with the sword.\" Amir said: I met Muharrar b. Abi Hurayrah and narrated this to him. He said, 'Did she add anything to it?' I said, 'No.' He said, 'She spoke the truth. I bear witness that Abu Hurayrah narrated to me and added to it.' He said: Then he said, 'The sea of Syria — what is it? The sea of Iraq — what is it?' Then he pointed with his hand towards the east twenty times. Then I met Abdullah b. Abi Bakr and narrated this to him. He said, 'Did she add anything to it for you?' I said, 'No.' He said, 'She spoke the truth. I bear witness that Aisha narrated to me, but she said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"And in al-Madinah: what is in it?\"'"],[20835,"Amir al-Shabi narrated to me: Fatimah bt. Qays narrated to me, saying: One day the Messenger of God ﷺ came out, prayed the midday prayer, then sat. The people were alarmed. He said, 'O people, I have not stood in this place of mine for alarm, but Tamim al-Dari came to me and told me a report that prevented me from taking the midday nap, along with joy and comfort of the eye. I wanted to give you the good news of the joy of your Prophet. He told me that a group of his paternal cousins went to sea, and a storm struck them and drove them to an island. They sat in the ship's boat until they came out to the island, and there was a shaggy thing, very hairy, and they did not know whether it was a man or a woman. They greeted it, and it returned their greeting. They said, \"Will you not tell us?\" It said, \"I am not going to tell you, nor ask you. But this monastery, which you have seen, in it is someone who is longing for news of you, to tell you and to ask you.\" We said, \"What are you?\" It said, \"I am al-Jassasa.\" They went until they came to the monastery, and there was a man bound in iron, tightly bound, showing grief, complaining much. They greeted him, and he returned their greeting and said, \"Who are you?\" We said, \"From the Arabs.\" He said, \"What have the Arabs done? Has their Prophet come out yet?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"What have they done?\" We said, \"Good. They believed in him, followed him, and accepted him.\" He said, \"That is better for them.\" They said, \"He had enemies, and God made him victorious over them.\" He said, \"Do the Arabs have one god, one word, and one religion?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"What has the spring of Zughar done?\" They said, \"It is overflowing. Its people drink their fill from it and water their crops from it.\" He said, \"What have the date palms between Uman and Baysan done?\" They said, \"They yield their fruit every year.\" He said, \"What has the lake of Tiberias done?\" They said, \"It is full.\" He sighed, then sighed again, then swore, \"If I were to come out of this place of mine, I would not leave any land of God's land without treading on it, except Taybah. I have no authority over it.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"This is among what made me happy,\" he said it three times. \"Taybah is al-Madinah. God has made my two sanctuaries forbidden to the Dajjal.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ swore, \"By the One besides whom there is no god, there is no narrow road or wide road, no easy path or mountain in it, but that an angel stands over it with a drawn sword until the Day of Resurrection. The Dajjal cannot enter it against its people.\" He said: Al-Shabi said: I met al-Muharrar b. Abi Hurayrah and narrated to him the hadith of Fatimah. He said, 'I bear witness that my father narrated to me just as Fatimah narrated to you, except that he said, \"He is in the east.\"' Then I met al-Qasim b. Muhammad, and he said, 'I bear witness that Aisha narrated to me just as Fatimah narrated to you, except that she said, \"The two sanctuaries are forbidden to him: Makkah and al-Madinah.\"' The wording is from the hadith of Yahya b. Said, and the others are similar."],[20836,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said, 'O people, Tamim al-Dari told me that some people from his tribe were at sea in a ship of theirs, and it broke apart. Some of them rode on a plank from the ship and came out to an island in the sea. There they were met by a disheveled black woman with hideous hair. They said, \"What are you?\" She said, \"I am al-Jassasa. Are you amazed at me?\" They said, \"Yes.\" She said, \"Enter the palace.\" They entered, and there was an old man bound with chains. He asked them who they were, and they told him. He said, \"What has the spring of Zughar done? What has the lake and the date palms of Baysan done?\" They told him. He said, \"By the One by whom oaths are sworn, there will remain no land but that I will tread it with my foot, except Taybah.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"And this is Taybah.\""],[20837,"While I was sitting in the mosque, the Messenger of God ﷺ came out and sat on the pulpit, and the people gathered around him. She said: I called out to listen, and I heard him saying: O people, I have not gathered you because of any news that came to me from your enemy, but Tamim al-Dari told me that cousins of his rode the sea, and a wind struck them so that they did not know whether they went east or west. So they anchored at an island and went out walking in it, and behold, they came upon a beast dragging its hair. They said: What is this? It said: I am al-Jassasah. They said: What is the news? It said: The news is with the master of the monastery. So they went to the monastery, and behold, they came upon the Dajjal, recognizing him, bound in iron. He said: Who are you? They said: From the community of Muhammad ﷺ. He said: Has he been sent? They said: Yes. He said: What did Buhayrat al-Tabariyyah do? So they informed him about it. He said: What did the date palms of Baysan do? So they informed him about it. He said: What did the spring of Zughar do? So they informed him about it. Then he pointed to his two legs and said: Do you see these two legs of mine? There will remain no land of God's land except that I will tread them with these two, except what is of Makkah and Taybah—and he is in the sea between the east and the west, and he is closer to the east—and their wording is one."],[20838,"Abu 'Umar ad-Darir and Abu 'Umar al-Hawdi said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, I am Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from 'Amir ash-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays al-Fihriyah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came one day hastening until he ascended the pulpit and the call to prayer was made for the people to pray in congregation. So he delivered a sermon and said: \"I did not call you out of desire or fear, but Tamim ad-Dari informed me that a group from the people of Palestine embarked on a sea voyage, and the wind cast them onto an island from among the islands of the sea. There, they found a creature with long hair, the likes of which they had never seen before. They asked, 'Who are you?' It said, 'I am the Spy.' They asked, 'Inform us about ourselves.' It said, 'I am not the one who informs you or who can be informed by you. But in this monastery, there is a man who can inform you and you can ask him out of longing.' So they entered the monastery and found a man shackled with iron. They asked, 'Who are you?' He said, 'Who are you?' They said, 'We are Arabs.' He asked, 'Has the Prophet appeared among you?' They said, 'Yes.' He asked, 'Have the Arabs followed him?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Is it better for them that they have done so?' They said, 'Yes.' He asked, 'Has it appeared in Persia?' They said, 'No.' He said, 'Indeed, it will appear among them.' Then he asked, 'What did the one-eyed do?' They said, 'He caused much harm.' He asked, 'What happened to the Lake of Tabariyah?' They said, 'It dried up, leaving behind a meadow.' He asked, 'What happened to the date palm of Bayhan?' They said, 'It has fed its early fruits and leapt as though it would escape from its restraints.' Then he said to them, 'I am the Dajjal. I am going to emerge and will not leave any land except Makkah and Madinah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Give glad tidings, for the Muslims have been given good news. This is the land of Taibah (Madinah), it will not be entered by the Dajjal.'\""],[20839,"It was announced in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'The prayer is to be gathered.' So we went out and sat behind the men's shoulders. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ ascended the pulpit, praised God and extolled Him, then said: Indeed, your brother Tamim al-Dari told me about cousins of his who rode the sea, and the wind carried them away until it forced them to an island among the islands of the sea. So they went out asking about the way, and they met a creature of God's creation the like of which they had never seen before, greater than it; it had nothing on it of what the children of Adam weave, and hair covered it. He said: So we asked it about the way, and it said: If you want to ask about the way, someone who will tell you and who yearns for your talk—then go to this monastery. We said: Tell us, what are you? It said: I am al-Dassasah. So we knew that it was a woman. Then we went to the monastery and entered it, and behold, there was a creature greater than which we had never seen, filled with iron between its collarbones and its ankles, with its eye wiped away. So we asked him about the way, and he said: I will not talk to you until you talk to me about what I ask you. We said: Ask about whatever seems good to you. He said: Tell me about the Prophet of the Arabs—has he come out yet? We said: Yes. He said: To what does he call? So we told him. He said: How quick are the people to what he calls them to? We said: They are quick. He said: That is better for them. He said: Tell me about Buhayrat al-Tabariyyah—what did it do? We said: It overflows. He said: Tell me about the spring of Zughar? We said: It overflows. He said: Ask about whatever seems good to you. He said: We said to him: What are you? He said: I am the Dajjal. By the One in whose hand is my soul, there will remain no land of God's land except that I will tread it with these two feet of mine, except Taybah. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'This is Taybah'—meaning Madinah."],[20840,"I entered Madinah and sat near the pulpit. Then a man came and sat with me and said: Can you direct me to a man who will narrate to me from the Messenger of God ﷺ? So he took me to Fatimah bint Qays, and she said: The Messenger of God ﷺ stood on the pulpit, and the people heard that he stood on the pulpit, so the people came hastening. I was among those who came to him, and I heard him saying: Tamim al-Dari told me that cousins of his rode in a ship of theirs at sea as merchants, and the wind drove them to an island. So they went out, or those of them who went out—did they see anyone?—until they were met by someone whom hair covered so that it was not clear whether that one was male or female. They said: The news! He said: The news is with the master of this monastery, and I am al-Jassas. So they came to the monastery, and behold, there was a man heavily laden with iron. He asked them: From whom are you? So they told him. He said: What has the Prophet of the Arabs done? Has he come out yet? They said: Yes. He said: Do the lowly follow him or the nobles of the people? They said: The foolish follow him. He said: Are they increasing or decreasing? They said: They are increasing. He said: Does anyone return from among those who came to him? They said: No. He said: That is better for them. What did Buhayrat al-Tabariyyah do—does it have water? They said: Yes. He said: What did the date palms of Baysan do—do they bear fruit? They said: Yes. He said: What did the spring of Zughar do—does it have water? They said: Yes. He said: Indeed, if I were permitted, I would tread all this land with this foot of mine, except Taybah. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'And this is Taybah; on every pass of it is an angel with his sword drawn toward Iraq—it is not toward Iraq, it is not.'"],[20841,"We entered upon Fatimah bint Qays, and she offered us fresh dates and gave us a satisfying drink of barley sattu. She said: It was announced among the people that the prayer is to be gathered. So I went among the women who went, and I was in the first row of the women, next to the last row of the men. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: Cousins of Tamim al-Dari rode at sea, and their ship cast them onto an island among the islands of the sea. There they saw a beast whose hair covered it. When the people looked at it, it said: I am al-Jassasah, and in that monastery there is one who longs to see you. So the people went and found a human being shackled in iron, and they were trading with him. It was as if their coming pleased him. He asked them: Has your companion come out yet? They said: Yes. He said: Buhayrat al-Tabariyyah—what did it do? We said: It has plenty of water. He said: What did the date palms of Baysan do? We said: They have borne fruit. He said: And the spring of Zughar? We said: It has plenty of water. He said: Indeed, if I were to come out, I would tread all lands except Makkah and Taybah. She said: It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of God ﷺ raising his hand: 'This is Taybah,' pointing toward Madinah."],[20842,"I entered upon Fatimah bint Qays, and she brought dates near to me. I said: This is good. She said: Who are you? I said: Amir. She said: al-Sha'bi? I said: Yes. I said: Narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. She said: One day he stood on the pulpit and the people gathered. He said: O people, no news has come to me from your enemy, but Tamim al-Dari told me that a group of his people rode the sea, and the wind blew violently and forced them to an island. So they disembarked, and behold, they came upon a beast dragging its hair. We said: Who are you? It said: I am al-Jassasah and al-Dassasah. It said: Go to that monastery, for there is the news. And behold, there was a nearby monastery. They said: So we went, and behold, the Dajjal. He said: Who are you? They said: From the community of Muhammad ﷺ. He rejoiced and said: Has Muhammad ﷺ been sent? Then he asked them about the spring of Zughar and Tabariyyah and about the date palms of Baysan. Then he lifted one of his legs, and behold, they were fettered. He said: If this one were released, I would tread the land with it, except Makkah and Madinah."],[20843,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: 'Indeed in your wealth there is a right besides the zakah.'"],[20844,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade wearing gold and stringing it. A woman threw away a gold bracelet, and it remained in the mosque for days; no one took it."],[20845,"The Messenger of God ﷺ proposed to me, and I excused myself to him, and he accepted my excuse."],[20846,"I used to pass by this verse and not know what it is?—His saying {in the evening and the ishraq}—until Umm Hani' bint Abi Talib told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon her and called for water for ablution in a large bowl, and it is as if I am looking at the trace of dough in it. So he performed ablution, then stood and prayed the Duha prayer. He said: 'O Umm Hani', this is the prayer of ishraq.'"],[20847,"The Messenger of God ﷺ one day prayed the supererogatory Duha prayer, eight rak'ahs, saying the salam after every two rak'ahs."],[20848,"The Prophet ﷺ, in the year of the conquest, performed ghusl, draped himself with a cloth, and prayed eight rak'ahs."],[20849,"Umm Hani' bt. Abi Talib narrated to me that she granted protection to a man from the polytheists on the day of the conquest. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said, “We grant protection to the one you have protected, and we give safety to the one you have given safety.”"],[20850,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her, and a vessel was brought, and he drank. She said, “O Messenger of God, I was fasting, but I disliked to refuse your leftover drink.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “If it was a makeup fast of Ramadan, then make it up on another day; if it was voluntary, then make it up, and if you wish, you need not make it up.”"],[20851,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a drink was brought. He drank from it, then handed it to me, and I drank from it. I said, “O Messenger of God, I have committed a sin, so ask forgiveness for me.” He said, “And what is that?” I said, “I was fasting and I broke my fast.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Was it a makeup fast you were making up?” She said, “No.” He said, “Then it does not harm you.”"],[20852,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a drink was brought and he drank from it, then he handed it to me and I drank from it. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I only see myself in a state of impurity.\" He asked, \"What is that?\" I said, \"I was fasting and I disliked returning your hand, so I drank.\" He said, \"Were you making up a missed fast?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then it does not harm you.\""],[20853,"From Umm Hani' bt. Abi Talib, who is his grandmother. She said, “I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, ‘O Messenger of God, I used to pray a prayer but I became too weak to perform it. Guide me to a deed I can do while seated that God will reward me for.’ He said, ‘O Umm Hani', when you reach the morning, glorify God one hundred times, declare His oneness one hundred times, praise Him one hundred times, and magnify Him one hundred times. One hundred glorifications are like one hundred camels, one hundred magnifications are like one hundred camels that you offer, and one hundred declarations of His oneness leave no sin before or after them.’”"],[20854,"She entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of the conquest of Makkah. He brought me a drink, drank from it, and gave her to drink. She said, “I was fasting, but I disliked to refuse your drink.” He said, “Were you making up a fast?” I said, “No.” He said, “It does not harm you.”"],[20855,"“I would hear the voice of the Messenger of God ﷺ while I was on my wooden couch—meaning his recitation during the night prayer.” Abu al-‘Ala', from whom Mis'ar narrated this hadith, is Hilal b. Khabbab."],[20856,"I hear the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I am on my bed praying."],[20857,"“I would hear the recitation of the Prophet ﷺ, repeating it in the depths of the night while I was reclining on my wooden couch.”"],[20858,"From Badham Abu Salih, the client of Umm Hani', that Umm Hani' said, “I asked the Prophet ﷺ about this verse, ‘And you commit abomination in your assemblies.’ He said, ‘They used to sit by the roadside and throw stones at the wayfarer and mock them.’”"],[20859,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about His saying, “And you commit abomination in your assemblies.” He said, “They used to throw stones at those who passed by them on the road and mock him.”"],[20860,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me on the day of the conquest of Makkah, performed a ritual bath, then prayed eight rak‘ahs. He did not pray them before that day nor after it.”"],[20861,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought water when he conquered Makkah, and they screened him, so he bathed, then prayed eight rak'ahs—no one ever saw him pray them afterwards."],[20862,"The Prophet ﷺ proposed to me, but I was not lawful for him because I had not emigrated. Then it was revealed: {And the daughters of your paternal uncles, the daughters of your paternal aunts, the daughters of your maternal uncles, and the daughters of your maternal aunts who emigrated with you}."],[20863,"\"I never saw the belly of the Messenger of God ﷺ without recalling sheets of paper stacked one upon another.\""],[20864,"The Messenger of God ﷺ proposed to me, and I made an excuse to him, so he excused me. Then God revealed: {Indeed, We have made lawful to you your wives} up to His saying {and the daughters of your maternal aunts who emigrated with you}. For I was not lawful to him because I had not emigrated with him—I was among the freed ones."],[20865,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me one day, and I said: O Messenger of God, I have grown old, so direct me to an action I can do while sitting. He said: \"Glorify God one hundred times with tasbih—it equals freeing one hundred slaves from the descendants of Ishmael. Praise God one hundred times with tahmid—it equals one hundred saddled and bridled horses you charge upon in the path of God. Magnify God one hundred times with takbir—it equals one hundred accepted sacrificial camels. Declare God's oneness one hundred times with tahlil—it fills what is between the heaven and the earth, and no one's deed is raised as better than it unless he brings the like of what you have brought.\""],[20866,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me on the day of the conquest, bathed, and prayed eight rak'ahs while veiled in a single garment. I said: O Messenger of God, I have granted protection to my two brothers-in-law, and the son of my mother—meaning 'Ali—claims he will kill them. He said: \"O Umm Hani', we have granted protection to whomever you have protected.\""],[20867,"She came to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of the conquest and said: O Messenger of God, I have granted protection to my brother-in-law, and the son of my mother—meaning 'Ali—claims he will kill him. He said: \"O Umm Hani', we have granted protection to whomever you have protected.\" Then she poured water for him and screened him, so he bathed. Then he changed into a garment, placing its two ends over his shoulders, and prayed the noon prayer as four rak'ahs."],[20868,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of the conquest and said: O Messenger of God, I have granted protection to my brother-in-law, and the son of my mother—meaning 'Ali—claims he will kill him. He said: \"We have granted protection to whomever you have protected, O Umm Hani'.\" Muhammad said: \"I have seen Abu Murrah.\""],[20869,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed in her house in the year of the conquest. She said: I entered upon him and said: O Messenger of God, I have granted protection to two men whom 'Ali b. Abi Talib claims he will kill—my brothers-in-law—and he will violate my protection. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"We have granted protection to whomever you have protected.\" Then he prayed the forenoon prayer as eight rak'ahs in a single garment, with its two ends crossed."],[20870,"He said: \"Will you grant protection to the polytheists?\" I said: By God, you will not kill them until you start with me before them. Then he left, and I said: Lock the door behind him. I went to the Prophet ﷺ at the foot of the mountain pass, but I did not find him. I found Fatimah, and she was harsher on me than her husband, saying: \"Why do you grant protection to the polytheists?\" Until the Messenger of God ﷺ appeared wearing a single garment and said: \"Welcome to Fakhitah, Umm Hani'.\" I said: What I have met from the son of my mother! I granted protection to two men, my brothers-in-law from the polytheists, and he pounced on them to kill them. He said: \"He had no right to do that. We have granted protection to whomever you have protected and given safety to whomever you have given safety.\""],[20871,"...to kill them. So I went to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"We have granted protection to whomever you have protected and given safety to whomever you have given safety.\" Then he ordered Fatimah, and she poured water for his bath and screened him, so he bathed. Then he stood and prayed the forenoon prayer as eight rak'ahs in a single garment, with its two ends crossed. I never saw him pray that before or after."],[20872,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the conquest, but I did not find him, so I waited for him until he entered. I said: The son of my mother—meaning 'Ali b. Abi Talib—entered upon me and wanted to kill my two brothers-in-law, the sons of Hubayrah. I said: I have granted them protection. He said: \"That is not for you—will you grant protection to the polytheists?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"We have granted protection to whomever you have protected.\" Then he said: \"O Fatimah, pour water for me,\" so he bathed. Then he prayed eight rak'ahs in a single garment, with its two ends crossed."],[20873,"that the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her on the day of the conquest, performed ghusl, then prayed Duha as eight rakʿahs in a single garment, having crossed its two ends. She said: “O Messenger of God, I have given protection to my two brothers-in-law, the sons of Hubayrah, and the son of my mother claims that he will kill them.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “We have granted protection to whom Umm Haniʾ has granted protection.”"],[20874,"Umm Haniʾ bt. Abi Talib said: I went to the Prophet ﷺ in the year of the conquest and found him performing ghusl while Fatimah was screening him with a garment. I greeted him, and he said: “Who is this?” I said: “I am Umm Haniʾ bt. Abi Talib.” He said: “Welcome to Umm Haniʾ.” When he finished his ghusl, he stood and prayed eight rakʿahs wrapped in a single garment. When he finished, I said: “O Messenger of God, the son of my mother claims that he will kill a man whom I have granted protection—so-and-so, the son of Hubayrah.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “We have granted protection to the one you have granted protection, O Umm Haniʾ.” Umm Haniʾ said: And that was in the forenoon."],[20875,"Umm Haniʾ said: I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of the conquest and found him performing ghusl while his daughter Fatimah was screening him with a garment. I greeted him—and that was in the forenoon. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Who is this?” I said: “Umm Haniʾ bt. Abi Talib.” He said: “Welcome to Umm Haniʾ.” When he finished his ghusl, he prayed eight rakʿahs wrapped in a single garment, then he finished. I said: “O Messenger of God, the son of my mother claims that he will kill so-and-so, the son of Hubayrah, a man whom I have granted protection.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “We have granted protection to whom Umm Haniʾ has granted protection.” Al-Dabari reported it thus from ʿAbd al-Razzaq, from Malik, from Maymun b. Maysarah, and he erred in it. The correct version is what al-Qaʿnabi and others narrated from Malik, from Musa b. Maysarah."],[20876,"When it was the day of the conquest, two men from Banu Makhzum fled to her and she granted them protection. ʿAli entered upon me and said: “I will surely kill them.” When I heard him say that, I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was in upper Makkah. When he saw me, he welcomed me and said: “What brings you, O Umm Haniʾ?” I said: “O Prophet of God, I had granted safety to two men from my brothers-in-law, and ʿAli wanted to kill them.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “We have granted protection to the one you have granted protection.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ rose to perform his ghusl, and Fatimah screened him. Then he took his garment, wrapped himself in it, and prayed eight rakʿahs as the Duha prayer."],[20877,"When the Prophet ﷺ conquered Makkah, two men from my in-laws of Banu Makhzum fled to me, and I hid them in my house. My brother ʿAli entered and said: “I will surely kill them.” So I locked the door on them, then I went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said: “We have granted protection to the one you have granted protection, and we have granted safety to the one you have granted safety.”"],[20878,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ encamped in upper Makkah, two men from my in-laws of Banu Makhzum came to me, and she was married to Hubayrah b. Abi Wahb. She said: ʿAli b. Abi Talib entered upon me and said: “I will surely kill them.” So I locked my door on them, then I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ in upper Makkah and found him performing ghusl in a large basin that had traces of dough, while his daughter Fatimah was screening him with a garment. When he finished his ghusl, he took his garment, wrapped it around himself, then prayed eight rakʿahs in the forenoon. Then he turned to me and said: “Welcome, O Umm Haniʾ, what brings you?” I informed him of the matter of the two men and the matter of ʿAli. He said: “We have granted protection to the one you have granted protection.”"],[20879,"She brought two men from Banu Makhzum on the day the Messenger of God ﷺ conquered Makkah. ʿAli entered upon her and said: “What is this, O Umm Haniʾ? I will surely kill them.” She said: So I locked the door on them, then I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and found him performing ghusl while his daughter Fatimah was screening him with a garment. He performed ghusl, then took the garment and wrapped himself in it, then prayed Duha as eight rakʿahs. Then he said: “What is the matter with you, O Umm Haniʾ?” I said: “I have granted protection to two men from my in-laws, and ʿAli came wanting to kill them.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “We have granted safety to the one you have granted safety, and we have granted protection to the one you have granted protection.”"],[20880,"I heard Umm Haniʾ bt. Abi Talib—who was ʿAli’s full sister on both her father’s and mother’s side—say: “The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me on the day of the conquest, performed ghusl, then prayed eight rakʿahs.”"],[20881,"that the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her on the day of the conquest and prayed Duha as eight rakʿahs in a single garment."],[20882,"that the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the conquest had a screen set up for him, and he performed ghusl in the forenoon and prayed eight rakʿahs. She did not know whether its standing, bowing, or prostration was longer."],[20883,"that the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed voluntary prayer on a journey. I found no one to inform me until Umm Haniʾ bt. Abi Talib informed me that he stood on the day of the conquest, ordered a screen, and it was set up for him. He performed ghusl, then prayed eight rakʿahs of voluntary prayer."],[20884,"that the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the Duha prayer, until I heard Umm Haniʾ say: “The Messenger of God ﷺ came after the day had risen on the day of the conquest, ordered a garment, and a screen was set up for him. He performed ghusl, then stood and prayed eight rakʿahs. I do not know whether his standing, bowing, or prostration in them was longer—all of that was close in length. I did not see him pray them before or after.”"],[20885,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the forenoon prayer. I did not find anyone to tell me except Umm Hani' bt. Abi Talib, who informed me: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ came after the day had risen on the day of the conquest, and he ordered a garment, so it was screened over him, and he performed ghusl. Then he stood and prayed eight rak'ahs. I do not know whether his standing was longer than his bowing or his prostration—all of that was comparable. I did not see him pray it before nor after.\""],[20886,"Regarding the Dhuha prayer, did the Prophet ﷺ pray it? I have not seen anyone claiming to have seen him do so except Umm Hani, as she claimed, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Fatimah while she was with her on the day of Jummah, the day of the conquest of Makkah. He washed his face with water and then prayed eight rak'at that we had not seen him pray before or after.\""],[20887,"I met the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and asked them about the forenoon prayer, but I did not find anyone to tell me about it until I came to Umm Hani' bt. Abi Talib and asked her. She said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to Fatimah's house in Makkah on a Friday. He called for a scoop of water, poured it, then performed ghusl while Fatimah screened him. Then he prayed eight rak'ahs, not praying before them nor after them.\""],[20888,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the forenoon prayer in upper Makkah, eight rak'ahs."],[20889,"That when the Prophet ﷺ conquered Makkah, I and Fatimah entered upon him. Fatimah screened him, and he performed ghusl, then prayed the forenoon prayer, eight rak'ahs."],[20890,"On the day of the conquest, the Messenger of God ﷺ entered my house. He ordered water, and it was poured into a large bowl. Then he ordered a garment, and it was screened. Then he performed ghusl, then sprinkled water in a corner of the house, then prayed eight rak'ahs. Their standing, bowing, prostration, and sitting were equal, close in length to each other."],[20891,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the forenoon prayer. So I went out and met Ibn 'Abbas and said, 'Come with me to Umm Hani'.' We entered upon her, and I said, 'Tell your cousin about the Prophet's ﷺ forenoon prayer.' She told him, and he said, 'We interpret this verse as the Duha prayer, and it is the forenoon prayer.'"],[20892,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, Fatimah came and sat on the left of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Umm Hani' on his right. A vessel containing a drink was brought, and he drank from it, then he handed it to Umm Hani' and she drank from it. Then she said, 'O Messenger of God, I have broken my fast, for I was fasting.' He said, 'Were you making up something?' I said, 'No.' He said, 'Then it does not harm you if it was voluntary.'"],[20893,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stopped at upper Makkah on the day of the conquest. I went to him, and Abu Dharr came with a large wooden bowl containing water. She said, 'I surely saw in it traces of dough.' Abu Dharr screened him, and he performed ghusl. Then the Prophet ﷺ screened Abu Dharr, and he performed ghusl. Then he prayed eight rak'ahs, and that was in the forenoon."],[20894,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Keep sheep, for in them is blessing.'"],[20895,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Keep sheep, for in them is blessing.'"],[20896,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to her: 'Acquire some sheep.' I said, 'No.' He said, 'Acquire them, for in them is blessing.'"],[20897,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of the conquest while he was in a tent of his. I found that he had bathed with water that was in a bowl, in which I could see traces of dough, and I found him praying the forenoon prayer."],[20898,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the conquest of Makkah, and he had screened himself with a garment while bathing in a bowl containing traces of dough. When he finished his bath, he prayed the forenoon prayer."],[20899,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was bathing, having been screened with a garment. When he finished his bath, he prayed the forenoon prayer."],[20900,"He entered upon Umm Hani' bt. Abi Talib and asked her about the entry of the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of the conquest. She said, 'He entered at mid-morning, and we poured water for him in a bowl of ours; I could see traces of dough in it.' Yusuf said, 'I do not know which she told me: did he perform ablution or bathe? Then he prayed four rak'ahs in this mosque—meaning a prayer area in her house.'"],[20901,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ with four braids."],[20902,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us in Makkah with four braids."],[20903,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ with four braids."],[20904,"The Prophet ﷺ bathed, he and Maymunah, from a single vessel—a bowl containing traces of dough."],[20905,"\"On the day of the conquest of Mecca, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and was offered a sheet by Umm Hani, Umm Sulaim, and Umm Anas, the mother of Anas ibn Malik, to perform the ritual purification. Then he entered the house of Umm Hani and performed four units of the Duha prayer.\""],[20906,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of God ﷺ called for water, and Umm Hani' and Umm Salamah screened him. He bathed and prayed the forenoon prayer, eight rak'ahs."],[20907,"That Umm Hani bint Abi Talib informed him that Ali ibn Abi Talib entered upon her during the conquest of Mecca and found two men from the family of her husband who had sought refuge with her. He intended to kill them, but when I saw that, I closed my door on them and went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , who was at the highest point of Mecca. When he saw me, he greeted me and said, \"What brings you, Umm Hani?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, two men from the family of my husband sought refuge with me, and Ali found them with me and claimed that he was going to kill them, so I came to you about it.\" He said, \"We have given protection to whomever you have given protection, and we have granted security to whomever you have granted security.\" Then I poured water for him to perform ablution, and he washed, and Fatima, his daughter, covered him with a garment. When he finished washing, he took the water and poured it out, then he stood up and prayed eight prostrations, and that was the forenoon prayer."],[20908,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her on the Day of the Conquest and prayed Duha four rak'ahs."],[20909,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The foremost are four: I am the foremost of the Arabs, Salman is the foremost of Persia, Suhayb is the foremost of the Byzantines, and Bilal is the foremost of the Abyssinians.'"],[20910,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her on the Day of the Conquest and prayed Duha six rak'ahs."],[20911,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ praying Duha — except Umm Hani', for she mentioned that on the day of the conquest of Makkah he performed ghusl in her house and prayed eight rak'ahs. I never saw him pray a lighter prayer, but he completed its bowing and prostration."],[20912,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to me, and I said, 'It is not that I have no desire for you, O Messenger of Allah, but I would not like to marry while my children are young.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Why? The best women who have ridden camels are the women of Quraysh — the most tender to a child in his infancy and the most protective of a husband with regard to what he possesses.'"],[20913,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me and said, 'Do you have anything?' I said, 'No, except dry pieces of bread and vinegar.' He said, 'No household is poor that has vinegar as a condiment.'"],[20914,"The Prophet ﷺ was given a sleeveless garment as a gift. He sent it to Ali, who started wearing it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali, \"I would not be pleased with something that I am not pleased with for myself. I did not give it to you for you to wear it, but I dressed you in it so that it may serve as a distinction between the Fatimah lines.\""],[20915,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “I gave to my maternal aunt Fākhitah bt. ʿAmr a servant boy, and I commanded her not to make him a butcher, nor a goldsmith, nor a cupper.”"],[20916,"that her husband went out in pursuit of runaway slaves until when he was at the edge of al-Qudūm, which is a mountain, he caught up with them and they killed him. So she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned to him that her husband had been killed and that he had left her in a dwelling that was not his, and she asked permission to move. He gave her permission. She departed, and when she was at the door of the room, he ordered that she be called back. He told her to repeat her account to him, and she did. Then he ordered her not to leave her husband’s house until the prescribed period reaches its term.”"],[20917,"from Furayʿah bt. Mālik, sister of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, she informed her that she was married to a man of the Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj. He went out in pursuit of runaway slaves of his and caught up with them at the edge of al-Qudūm, and they attacked him and killed him. So I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “Until the prescribed period reaches its term.”"],[20918,"that her husband went out in pursuit of a servant boy of his and was killed at the edge of al-Qudūm. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked his permission to move to her family. He gave her permission, but when she turned away, he called her and said: “Stay in your house until the prescribed period reaches its term.”"],[20919,"that Furayʿah bt. Mālik, sister of Abū Saʿīd, whose husband was killed at the edge of al-Qudūm, asked the Prophet ﷺ permission to go to her family in Madinah. He gave her permission, then said: “No, until the prescribed period reaches its term.”"],[20920,"that Furayʿah bt. Mālik, sister of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, informed her that her husband went out until when he was six miles from Madinah at the edge of a mountain called al-Qudūm, thieves attacked him and killed him. Furayʿah was among the Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj in a dwelling that did not belong to her husband; it was only a residence. Their brothers came, among them Abū Saʿīd, and said: We have no surplus to give you and keep you, and nothing suits us except that we be together, and we fear loneliness for you, so ask the Prophet ﷺ. She came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked his permission to be with them. He said: “Do so if you wish.” She turned away, and when she was in the room, he said: “Come back, repeat what you said.” She repeated it, and he said: “Stay in your dwelling until the prescribed period reaches its term.”"],[20921,"from Furayʿah bt. Mālik, sister of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, that her husband went out in pursuit of runaway slaves of his and was killed at the edges of al-Qudūm. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned to him her situation and mentioned moving to her brothers. The Prophet ﷺ gave her permission. When she turned away, he called her and said: “Stay in your house until the prescribed period reaches its term: four months and ten days.”"],[20922,"that she was with her husband in one of the villages of Madinah, and he pursued runaway slaves and they killed him. I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned to him the loneliness and that she was in a house that was not hers, and that she asked permission to go to his brothers in Madinah. He gave her permission, then called her and said: “Stay in your house in which the news of his death came to you until the prescribed period reaches its term.”"],[20923,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said that her husband had been killed at al-Qudūm and that she had family. He ordered her to move, but when she turned away, he called her and said: “Stay in your house until the prescribed period reaches its term: four months and ten days.”"],[20924,"My husband set out seeking runaway slaves until when he was at the edge of al-Qudūm, they caught up with him and killed him. I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: My husband was killed at the edge of al-Qudūm, and my husband left me neither a dwelling nor wealth, and I want to move to my brothers so that it would be better for our affairs. She said: He gave me permission. I went out, and when I was in part of the room, the Prophet ﷺ called me and said: “Stay in the house in which the news of your husband’s death came to you until the prescribed period reaches its term.”"],[20925,"From al-Furay'ah bint Malik, the sister of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that her husband Bakkar hired some 'uluj (non-Arab laborers) to work for him, and they killed him. She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I said, 'I am not in a dwelling that belongs to him, nor does any provision from him come to me, so I will move to my family and my orphans and take care of them.' He said, \"Do so.\" Then it occurred to him otherwise, and he said, \"Observe your waiting period where the news reached you.\""],[20926,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik. (H) And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us; 'Abdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us; Malik informed us; from Sa'd b. Ishaq b. Ka'b b. 'Ujrah; from his paternal aunt Zaynab bint Ka'b; from Furay'ah bint Malik, that her husband was struck down at the edge of al-Qudum, so she sought permission from the Prophet ﷺ to go to her family. Then he said, \"No, not until the prescribed term reaches its end.\""],[20927,"My husband went out in search of some 'uluj (laborers) of ours, and he caught up with them at the edge of al-Qudum, and they killed him. News of his death came to me while I was in a house far from the houses of my family. So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked his permission to go to my family, and he gave me permission. Then he said, \"No, not until the prescribed term reaches its end.\""],[20928,"That her husband went out in search of some 'uluj (laborers) belonging to him, until when he was at the edge of al-Qudum, they killed him. The news reached her while she was in a house far from her family, so he gave her permission. Then when she was in the room, he called her back and said, \"Stay where the news came to you until the prescribed term reaches its end.\""],[20929,"\"That she saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat bread and meat and then pray without performing ablution.\""],[20930,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, so we brought him a foreleg of a sheep, and he ate. When the prayer time came, he rinsed his mouth, then stood and prayed without performing ablution.\""],[20931,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ visited them, ate the shoulder of a sheep, then prayed without performing ablution.\""],[20932,"Chapter of Qaf."],[20933,"Chapter of Qaf."],[20934,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and prayed part of the prayer with him. When he finished the prayer, I stood up, and he looked at me—and she was a tall woman—and said, \"If the son of this woman was fighting from behind the barrier.\" She said, \"By Allah, it was indeed so, O Messenger of Allah, but he died.\" She said, \"Write a document for me,\" and I had three daughters with me. So he wrote: From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Qaylah and the three women: \"They shall not be wronged in any right, nor shall they be compelled into marriage. Every believer or Muslim is a guardian and helper for them. If they do well, let them not do evil.\""],[20935,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Marwah, having come out of ihram from an 'umrah. I sat by him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who buys and sells. Sometimes I want to sell a commodity and I ask for it a price higher than what I intend to sell it for, then I reduce it until I sell it for what I intend. And when I want to buy a commodity, I offer for it less than what I intend to take it for, then I increase until I take it for what I intend.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do not do that, O Qaylah. When you want to sell a commodity, ask for it the price you intend to sell it for, whether you are given it or refused. And when you want to buy a commodity, offer for it the price you intend to take it for, whether you are given it or refused.\""],[20936,"A learned man (habr) from among the learned men came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Muhammad, what an excellent people you are, were it not that you associate partners with Allah.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"And what is that?\" He said, \"You say when you swear: 'By the Ka'bah.'\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ paused for a while, then said, 'Whoever swears, let him swear by the Lord of the Ka'bah.' Then he said, 'O Muhammad, what an excellent people you are, were it not that you set up rivals to Allah.'\" He said, \"Glory be to Allah! And what is that?\" He said, \"You say to a man, 'What Allah wills and you will.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ paused, then said, \"He has spoken. So whoever says, 'What Allah wills,' let him put between them, 'then you will.'\""],[20937,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me while I had a water-skin hanging, so he drank from the mouth of the water-skin while standing. I then cut off the mouth of the water-skin, seeking blessing through that."],[20938,"I said, “O Messenger of God, I buried alive four of my sons in the Jāhiliyyah?” He said, “Free four slaves.” She said, “So I freed your father Saʿīd, his two sons Maysarah and Jubayr, and the mother of Maysarah.” She said: And the Messenger of God ﷺ said to us, “The blood of a fair-skinned woman is purer in the sight of God than the blood of a black-skinned woman.”"],[20939,"ʿAkkāf b. Wadāʿah came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, “O ʿAkkāf, do you have a wife?” He replied, “O Messenger of God, I will not leave until you marry me to whomever you wish.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I have married you, in the name of God and with blessing, to Karīmah bt. Kulthūm al-Ḥimyarīyah.”"],[20940,"Kulaybah – or Kulthūm – bt. Burthun al-ʿAnbarīyah called me and said, “O my son, this man took my zarbiyyah (ornamental carpet) which I used to wear.” So I met the man and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ, and I said, “O Messenger of God, this man took my mother’s zarbiyyah.” He said, “Return to him his mother’s zarbiyyah.”"],[20941,"Lubābah bt. al-Ḥārith b. Ḥazn b. Bujayr b. Rībah b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Hilāl b. ʿĀmir b. Ṣaʿṣaʿah b. Muʿāwiyah."],[20942,"The Prophet ﷺ broke his fast at ʿArafah; she brought him milk and he drank."],[20943,"The Messenger of God ﷺ broke his fast at ʿArafah, and Umm al-Faḍl sent him milk, so he drank at ʿArafah."],[20944,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought milk at ʿArafah and he drank while he was delivering the sermon."],[20945,"I brought Umm Ḥabībah bt. al-ʿAbbās to the Prophet ﷺ when she was a little girl, and I placed her in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ. She urinated, so I struck her on the back, then picked her up. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Stop.” Then he called for a cup of water and poured it over the place where she had urinated, then said, “Pour water over the place of urination.”"],[20946,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite Surah Al-Mursalat during Maghrib prayer."],[20947,"that Umm Al-Fadl bint Al-Harith heard him reciting \"By those sent forth in succession\" and she said, \"O my son, you reminded me of your recitation of this Surah, for it is the last thing I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting in the Maghrib prayer.\""],[20948,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pray Maghrib, and he recited therein “By those sent forth in succession” (al-Mursalāt). That was the last prayer he prayed; he did not pray after it."],[20949,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting in the Maghrib prayer with the Mu'assalat verses, which are well-known."],[20950,"“(She was) Lubabah” that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting ‘By the winds sent forth one after another...’[Al-Mursalat (77)] in the Maghrib. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 831)"],[20951,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting the Mu'awwidhat (Surahs of seeking refuge from evil) in Maghrib prayer."],[20952,"His mother, Umm al-Faḍl bt. al-Ḥārith, informed him that she heard the Messenger of God ﷺ recite in Maghrib “By those sent forth in succession,” and then he did not pray until God Almighty took his soul."],[20953,"Umm al-Faḍl heard me while I was reciting “By those sent forth in succession,” and she said, “O my son, this is the last sūrah I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ recite in the Maghrib prayer.”"],[20954,"While I was sitting at the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was ill, I wept. He said: “What makes you weep?” I said: I fear for you, and we do not know what we will face from the people after you. He said: “You are the ones who will be deemed weak after me.”"],[20955,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ, “I saw in a dream as if a part of you was in my house.” He said, “Good. Fatimah will give birth to a boy and you will nurse him in your house.” Then she gave birth to Hasan, and he was in my house. I brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he urinated on him. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, throw away this garment so that I may wash it.” He said, “The urine of females is washed, and the urine of a male is not washed.”"],[20956,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon al-Abbas while he was ill and wishing for death. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O uncle, do not wish for death, for if you are a good-doer, then being delayed will increase you in good upon your good, and if you are an evildoer, then being delayed so that you may seek pardon for your evil is better for you. So do not wish for death.”"],[20957,"“I was a woman who went out with the Prophet ﷺ tending to the wounded.”"],[20958,"He is called Dawud; Umm Habibah bt. Abi Sufyan gave birth to him. From Layla bt. Qanif al-Thaqafiyyah, she said: “I was among those who washed Umm Kulthum, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The first thing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us was the waist-wrapper, then the shift, then the head-cover, then the outer sheet, then she was wrapped in the final garment.”"],[20959,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Maghrib with us in his house, wearing a single garment wrapped around him. He did not pray any prayer after it until he was taken ﷺ."],[20960,"O Messenger of Allah, I had a wife and I married another woman in addition to her, and the first one claimed that she had breastfed the younger one. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “One suckling or two sucklings do not create a marriage prohibition.”"],[20961,"A woman was divorced by her husband, then he married another woman, and his wife claimed that she had breastfed her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “One suckling or two sucklings do not create a marriage prohibition.”"],[20962,"O Messenger of Allah, I married a woman while I already had another wife, and she claimed that she had breastfed the younger one. He said: “One suckling or two sucklings do not create a marriage prohibition.”"],[20963,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about a single suckling: does it create a marriage prohibition? He said: “No.”"],[20964,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “One suckling or two sucklings do not create a marriage prohibition, nor do one or two breastfeedings.”"],[20965,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “One or two breastfeedings, or one or two sucklings, do not create a marriage prohibition.”"],[20966,"May Allah bless His Messenger. He recited in the Maghrib prayer “By those sent forth in succession” (al-Mursalat). He did not lead us in Isha until Allah, Exalted is He, took him."],[20967,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us from Malik. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ‘Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us: Malik informed us from Abu al-Nadr, the freedman of ‘Umar b. ‘Ubayd Allah b. Ma‘mar, from ‘Umayr, the freedman of Ibn ‘Abbas, from Umm al-Fadl bt. al-Harith, that some people differed in her presence on the day of ‘Arafah about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Some said he was fasting, and others said he was not fasting. So she sent him a bowl of milk while he was standing on his camel, and he drank it at ‘Arafah."],[20968,"They were uncertain about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at ‘Arafah. Umm al-Fadl said: “I will resolve that for you.” So she sent him a large cup of milk and he drank from it."],[20969,"He heard Umm al-Fadl saying, \"People had doubts about fasting on the Day of Arafah, while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I sent him a container of milk and he drank it while he was in Arafah.\""],[20970,"The people were uncertain about the Prophet's ﷺ fasting on the day of ‘Arafah. I said: “I will resolve that for you.” So I sent him a vessel containing milk, and he drank."],[20971,"Umm al-Fadl came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “I saw part of your body in my house.” He said, “Good is what you saw. Fatimah will give birth to a boy and you will nurse him with the milk of Qutham.” She said, “So she brought him, carrying him, to the Prophet ﷺ. Then she took him and placed him in his lap, and he urinated. So I slapped him with her hand, and he said, ‘You have hurt my son, may Allah have mercy on you.’ She said, ‘Give me your waist-wrapper so that we may wash it.’ He said, ‘The urine of a girl is washed, and the urine of a boy is sprinkled.’”"],[20972,"Umm al-Fadl said, “O Messenger of Allah, I saw as if part of your body was in my house.” He said, “Good. Fatimah will give birth and you will nurse him.” Then she gave birth to Hasan or Husayn, and she nursed him. Then she brought him to the Prophet ﷺ one day and placed him in his lap, and he urinated, so she struck his shoulder. The Prophet ﷺ said, “You have hurt my son, may Allah have mercy on you.””"],[20973,"Al-Hasan b. Ali urinated in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ, so I said, “Give me your garment and wear another.” He said, “The urine of a female is washed, and the urine of a male is sprinkled.”"],[20974,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I saw in a dream a distressing vision.” He said, “And what is it?” She said, “May Allah keep you righteous; it is severe.” He said, “What is it?” She said, “I saw as if a piece of your body was cut off and then placed in my lap.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Good have you seen. Fatimah will give birth, if Allah wills, to a boy who will be in your lap.” Then Fatimah gave birth to Hasan, and he was in her lap. I entered with him upon the Prophet ﷺ and placed him, and he urinated on him. I went to take him, and he said, “Leave my son, for my son is not impure.” Then he called for water and poured it on him."],[20975,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: He stood one night in Makkah during the night and said, “O Allah, have I conveyed?” three times. Then Umar b. al-Khattab stood up and said, “O Allah, yes. You have striven, advised, and exerted yourself.” In the morning he said, “Faith shall certainly prevail until it drives disbelief back to its homelands, and they shall certainly cross the seas with Islam. And there shall come upon people a time when they learn the Quran, and they learn it and recite it, then they say, ‘We have recited and we have learned, so who is better than us?’ Is there any harm in those?” They said, “No, O Messenger of Allah. And who are those?” He said, “Those are the fuel of the Fire.”"],[20976,"“Where to, O Umm Abdullah?” I said, “You have harmed us in our religion, so we go in Allah’s land where we will not be harmed in the worship of Allah.” He said, “May Allah accompany you.” Then he left, and my husband Amir b. Rabi’ah came to me, and I told him about the softness I saw in Umar. He said, “Do you hope that he will become Muslim?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “By Allah, he will not become Muslim until the donkey of al-Khattab becomes Muslim.”"],[20977,"Among the women who witnessed the Aqabah were Lubaysah and her sister, the two daughters of Ka’b b. Amr b. Awf, and she is Umm Umarah whose son Musaylimah seized."],[20978,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her, and she called for food for him. He invited her to eat with him, and she said, “I am fasting.” He said, “When a fasting person eats in their house, the angels invoke blessings for them until they finish their eating and complete it.”"],[20979,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came in to see me, and I brought him some fruit or food. Some of the people withdrew and did not eat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What is the matter with them?\" I said, \"They are fasting.\" He said, \"No fasting person has people who are not fasting eat in his presence except that the angels send blessings upon them until evening.\""],[20980,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I see that everything is only for men; I do not see women being mentioned with anything.\" Then it was revealed: {Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women} (Quran 33:35)."],[20981,"A woman called Umm 'Umara came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the Quran is only revealed concerning men.\" Then Allah revealed this verse: {Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women}."],[20982,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I see that everything is only for men.\" Then Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, revealed: {Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women} - the verse."],[20983,"From Maymunah - not Maymunah the wife of the Prophet ﷺ - that she said, \"O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about Bayt al-Maqdis.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is the land of gathering and resurrection. Go to it and pray in it, for a prayer in it is like a thousand prayers.\" She said, \"What do you think about someone who is unable to undertake the journey to go there?\" He said, \"If he cannot do that, then let him send oil to it to be used as fuel for its lamps. Whoever sends a gift to it is like one who prayed in it.\""],[20984,"From Maymunah, the freed slave of the Prophet ﷺ, that she said, \"O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about Bayt al-Maqdis.\" He said, \"It is the land of gathering and resurrection. Go to it and pray in it, for a prayer in it is like a thousand prayers.\" She said, \"What do you think if we are unable to undertake the journey to it or to go to it?\" He said, \"Then send to it oil to be used as fuel for its lamps, for whoever sends a gift to it is like one who prayed in it.\""],[20985,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who kissed his wife while they were both fasting. He said, \"They have broken their fast.\""],[20986,"Narrated by Maymunah bint Sa'd, the freed slave woman of the Prophet ﷺ , that the Prophet ﷺ was asked about the child born out of wedlock, and he said, \"There is no goodness in them. Two sandals that I use in fighting are dearer to me than freeing a child born out of wedlock.\""],[20987,"She said, \"Give us a ruling, O Messenger of Allah, about a man who forgot to pray until the sun rose or set. What is its expiation?\" He said, \"When he remembers it, let him pray it and perform his prayer well, and let him perform ablution and perform his ablution well. That is its expiation.\""],[20988,"She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about fasting.\" He said, \"Three days from every month. Whoever is able to fast them, then indeed each day expiates ten bad deeds, and it cleanses from sin as water cleanses a garment.\""],[20989,"She said, \"Give us a ruling, O Messenger of Allah, about stolen property.\" He said, \"Whoever consumes it while knowing that it is stolen has shared in the sin of its thief.\""],[20990,"\"Indeed, it is a veil from the Fire for the one who performs it well, seeking thereby the face of Allah, may He be glorified and exalted.\""],[20991,"She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about the dog.\" He said, \"It is a leftover of the Jahiliyyah, and Allah has made us free from need of it.\""],[20992,"She said: Give us a ruling, O Messenger of God, about the ghusl from janābah. He said: Wet the roots of the hair and clean the skin, for the likeness of those who do not perform the ghusl well is like a tree that water strikes, yet its leaves do not sprout and its roots are not watered. So fear God and perform the ghusl well, for it is among the trust you have been charged with and the secrets you have been entrusted with. She said: I said: How much water suffices for the head, O Messenger of God? He said: Three handfuls."],[20993,"I said: O Messenger of God, may one of us eat while he is junub? He said: He should not eat until he performs wuḍūʾ. She said: I said: O Messenger of God, may the junub sleep? He said: I do not like that he sleep while he is junub until he performs wuḍūʾ and does his wuḍūʾ well, for I fear that he may die and Jibrīl ﷺ will not attend him."],[20994,"She said: Give us a ruling, O Messenger of God, about the Friday prayer. He said: In it there is an hour in which the servant does not call upon his Lord but that He answers him. I said: Which hour is it, O Messenger of God? He said: That is when the imam stands."],[20995,"She said: Give us a ruling, O Messenger of God, about a man who erred in his prayer and does not know how much he prayed. He said: He should depart, then stand in his prayer until he knows how much he prayed, for that is only whispering that comes to him and makes him forget his prayer."],[20996,"She said: Give us a ruling, O Messenger of God, from what is the punishment of the grave? He said: From the trace of urine. So whoever is afflicted by urine, let him wash it, and if he finds no water, let him wipe it with pure dust."],[20997,"She said: Give us a ruling, O Messenger of God, about one who did not go on campaign but gave his wealth so that others campaign with it: does he have a reward, or the one who set out? He said: He has the reward of his wealth, and the one who set out has the reward of what he counted upon from that."],[20998,"From Maymūnah bt. Saʿd, who was a servant of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: The likeness of a woman who walks proudly in adornment in other than her own people is like the darkness of the Day of Resurrection: she has no light."],[20999,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: No woman goes out in a display of perfume, and men look at her, but that she remains in God's displeasure until she returns to her house."],[21000,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, and his toe that is next to the big toe was longer than the big toe, meaning of the foot."],[21001,"\"I stooped for the Messenger of God ﷺ until he climbed a wall on the night he fled from the polytheists.\""],[21002,"I complained of a pain in my throat, so I came to her, and she put for me cow's ghee. She said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Its milk is a cure, its ghee is a remedy, and its meat is a disease.'\""],[21003,"that it should be recent from you, so you seek to be clear of it by one menstrual period. Al-Rubayyi' said, \"ʿUthman took that only from the saying of the Prophet ﷺ to Maryam al-Maghaliyyah, the wife of Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas, and I obtained divorce from him by khulʿ.\""],[21004,"From Maymūnah bt. ʿAsīb, the freedwoman of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that a woman from Ḥarīsh came to the Messenger of God ﷺ on a camel and called out: O ʿĀʾishah, help me with a supplication from the Messenger of God ﷺ that will calm me or reassure me. He said to her: Place your right hand on your heart and say: In the name of God. O God, heal me with Your healing, and cure me with Your cure, and enrich me with Your bounty from all besides You, and ward off from me Your harm. Rabīʿah said: I supplicated with it and found it good. Al-Muntajiʿ said: I think Rabīʿah said in this hadith that the woman was jealous."],[21005,"She heard her father asking the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: I vowed that I would certainly slaughter at Buwānah. He said: Is there an idol or a tyrant worshipped there? He said: No. He said: Fulfill your vow where you vowed."],[21006,"Her father met the Prophet ﷺ while she was riding behind him, and he asked him, saying: I vowed to slaughter at Buwānah. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: Is there an idol there? He said to him: No. He said: Then fulfill your vow where you vowed."],[21007,"He hears of me and does not see me but that he loves me. I said, \"And how do you know that, O Abu Hurayrah?\" He said, \"My mother was a polytheist woman, and I used to call her to Islam, but she refused me. One day I called her, and she made me hear about the Messenger of God ﷺ what I disliked. So I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ weeping and said, 'O Messenger of God, I used to call my mother to Islam, but she refused me, and I called her and she made me hear about you what I disliked. So supplicate to God to guide the mother of Abu Hurayrah.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'O God, guide the mother of Abu Hurayrah.' He said, 'I went out running to give her the good news of the supplication of the Messenger of God ﷺ. When I came to the door, it was closed, and I heard the splashing of water and she heard the sound of my feet. She said, \"O Abu Hurayrah, stay where you are,\" and she opened the door, put on her shift, and hurried to her veil. Then she said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.\" So I returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ weeping from joy as I had wept from sorrow, and I said, \"O Messenger of God, God has answered your supplication for my mother. So supplicate to God to make me and my mother beloved to His believing servants and to make them beloved to us.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'O God, make Your servant and Your female servant beloved to Your believing servants, and make them beloved to the two of them.'\""],[21008,"About his grandmother Maria, who was a servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , she said, \"I have never seen a hand softer than that of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .\""],[21009,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to Nuʿma bt. Jaʿfar, \"Why do I see the bodies of the sons of Jaʿfar emaciated? Do they have a need?\" She said, \"No, but the evil eye is quick to affect them. Should I perform ruqyah on them?\" He said, \"Yes.\" She presented some words to him that were acceptable, and he said, \"Perform ruqyah on them with it.\""],[21010,"We prayed Zuhr or ʿAsr in the mosque of Banu Harithah, and we faced the mosque of Jerusalem (Iliya), and we prayed two rakʿahs. Then someone came to inform us that the Messenger of God ﷺ had turned to face the Sacred House. So the men moved to the place of the women, and the women moved to the place of the men, and we prayed the remaining two prostrations while facing the Sacred House. A man from Banu Harithah told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Those are men who believed in the unseen.'"],[21011,"I was with ʿAʾishah, and she had slaughtered a sheep of hers. The Messenger of God ﷺ entered with a small staff in his hand, which he threw down, then he went to the mosque and prayed two rakʿahs in it, then he went to his bed and lay down on it. Then he said, \"Is there any breakfast?\" We brought him a large bowl containing barley bread, and in it was a piece, and a piece of the stomach, and in it was the foreleg. She said, \"He took a piece of the stomach, and while he was chewing it, she said, 'We slaughtered a sheep today, and we did not keep anything except this.' She said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"No, rather all of it was kept except this.\"'\""],[21012,"\"We washed the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ. He ordered us to wash her with lote-tree leaves three times, or if not, five times, or if not, more than that. We considered that more than that would be seven times.\""],[21013,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from wearing gold and from silver-plating vessels. The women spoke to him about wearing gold, but he refused us, and he permitted us to silver-plate vessels."],[21014,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent ʿAlī on a military expedition. I saw him raising his hands and saying: \"O Allah, do not cause me to die until You show me ʿAlī.\""],[21015,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered Madinah, he gathered the women in a house, then he sent ʿUmar b. al-Khattab to us. He stood at the door and greeted, then said, \"I am the messenger of the Messenger of God ﷺ to you, to take your pledge that you will not steal, commit adultery, kill your children, bring a slander you fabricate between your hands and feet, or disobey him in what is right.\" She said, \"We brought out our hands from outside the door, and he brought out his hand, and we pledged to him.\" She said, \"He ordered us to go out on the two ʿĪds, the unmarried women and the menstruating women, and he forbade us from going out for a funeral or attending Friday prayer.\" I said to her, \"What is 'not disobey him'?\" She said, \"Wailing.\""],[21016,"Zaynab, the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, died. He said, \"Wash her three times, or five times, or more than that if you see fit, and wash her with water and lote-tree leaves, and put in the last washing some camphor. When you finish, inform me.\" When we finished, we informed him, and he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said, \"Wrap her in it as a shroud.\" She said, \"We made her hair into three braids and placed them behind her.\" She said, \"The waist-wrapper is a small lower garment.\""],[21017,"\"We pledged to the Messenger of God ﷺ. She came to Basra seeking a son of hers, but she did not find him.\" She narrated to us, and he mentioned something like the hadith of Maʿmar."],[21018,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us from Malik. And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: ʿAbdullah b. ʿAbd al-Hakam narrated to us. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ʿAbdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us. They said: Malik b. Anas informed us, from Ayyub b. Abi Tamimah, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Umm ʿAtiyyah al-Ansariyyah, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon us when his daughter died and said, \"Wash her three times, or five times, or more than that if you see fit, with water and lote-tree leaves, and put in the last washing camphor or some camphor. When you finish, inform me.\" She said, \"When we finished, we informed him, and he gave us his waist-wrapper and said, 'Wrap her in it as a shroud,' meaning his lower garment.\""],[21019,"A daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ died, so we gathered at her place and we entered upon her. The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon us and said, “Wash her three times, or five times, or more than that if you see fit, with water and sidr, and add in the last washing camphor or some camphor. When you have finished, inform me.” When we finished, we informed him, and he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said, “Use it as her innermost shroud.”"],[21020,"One of the daughters of the Messenger of God ﷺ died. The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and said, “Wash her three times, or five times, or more if you see fit, with water and sidr, and add in the last washing camphor or some camphor. When you have finished, inform me.” When we finished, we informed him, and he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said, “Use it as her innermost shroud.”"],[21021,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon us while we were washing his daughter and said, “Wash her three times, or five times, or more than that if you see fit, with water and sidr, and add in the last washing camphor or some camphor. When you have finished, inform me.” When we finished, we informed him, and he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said, “Use it as her innermost shroud.”"],[21022,"She said: A daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ died. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Wash her with water and sidr three times, or five times, or more than that if you see fit, and put some camphor in the last of them. When you have finished, inform me.” We informed him, and he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said, “Use it as her innermost shroud.”"],[21023,"One of the daughters of the Prophet ﷺ died, and he ordered us to wash her with water and sidr. He said, “Wash her three times, or five times, or more than that if you see fit, and put camphor or some camphor in the last of them. When you have finished, inform me.” When we informed him, he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said, “Use it as her innermost shroud.”"],[21024,"One of the daughters of the Prophet ﷺ died. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Wash her with water and sidr, and wash her an odd number of times: three or five, and if you see fit to add more, then add more, and let that be an odd number. Put camphor or some camphor in the last washing.” Then he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said, “Use it as her innermost shroud.”"],[21025,"One of the daughters of the Prophet ﷺ died, and he ordered us to wash her three times, or five times, or more than that if we saw fit, and to put some camphor and sidr in the last washing."],[21026,"A daughter of the Prophet ﷺ died. He said, “Wash her three times, or five times, or more than that if you see fit, with water and sidr, and put some camphor in the last washing. When you have finished, inform me.” When we finished, we informed him, and he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said, “Use it as her innermost shroud.”"],[21027,"A daughter of the Prophet ﷺ died. He said, “Wash her with water and sidr three times, or five times, or more than that if you see fit, and put some camphor in the last of them. When you have finished, inform me.” She said: We informed him, and he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said, “Use it as her innermost shroud.” Ayyub said: And she said, “Wash her three, or five, or seven times, and make three plaits for her.”"],[21028,"A daughter of the Prophet ﷺ died. He entered upon us while we were washing her and said, “Wash her three times or five times. When you have finished, inform me.” When we finished, we informed him, and he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said, “Use it as her innermost shroud.”"],[21029,"I went on several military expeditions with the Prophet ﷺ. We used to attend to the wounded and treat the injured. I said, “O Messenger of God, one of us goes out with the people on the day of Fitr and the day of Sacrifice.” She said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Bring out the young women, the secluded maidens, and the menstruating women, so that they may witness the good and the supplication of the Muslims.” I said, “O Messenger of God, what if one of us does not have a garment?” He said, “Let her sister clothe her from her garment.”"],[21030,"She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to bring out the young women and the secluded maidens. It was said, “And the menstruating women?” He said, “Yes, they may witness the good and the supplication of the Muslims.” We said, “O Messenger of God, one of us may not have a garment.” He said, “Let her sister clothe her with part of her garment.”"],[21031,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to “bring out on the day of Eid the adolescent girls and those in seclusion.” It was said, “And the menstruating women?” He said, “They should witness the good and the supplication of the Muslims.” A woman said, “O Messenger of Allah, if one of us does not have a garment, what should she do?” He said, “Her companion should let her wear part of her garment.”"],[21032,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bring out the virgins, adolescent girls, those in seclusion, and menstruating women on the two Eids. As for the menstruating women, they would keep away from the prayer area but witness the good and the supplication of the Muslims. One of them said, “If one of them does not have a jilbab?” He said, “Let her sister lend her one of her jilbabs.”"],[21033,"He commanded us to go out on the two Eids, and we would bring out the menstruating women, adolescent girls, and those in seclusion. As for the menstruating women, they would witness the gathering of the Muslims and their supplication, and they would keep away from their prayer."],[21034,"We used to be commanded to go out on the two Eids—those in seclusion and the menstruating women. As for the menstruating women, they would witness the prayer area of the Muslims."],[21035,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to bring out the adolescent girls, those in seclusion, and the menstruating women on the day of Eid. As for the menstruating women, they would witness the prayer area of the Muslims."],[21036,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded us to bring out on the two Eids those in seclusion and the menstruating women, so that they witness with the Muslims their supplication and their prayer, but the menstruating women should keep away from the prayer."],[21037,"She said, and she mentioned the pledge to the Prophet ﷺ: “None of us fulfilled it except Umm Sulaym, Umm Kulthum, and the wife of Mu’adh b. Abi Sabrah.”"],[21038,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took from the women, among what he took, that they would not wail. None of them fulfilled it except so-and-so, so-and-so, and Umm so-and-so."],[21039,"About following funeral processions, and it was not made binding upon us."],[21040,"About following funeral processions, and it was not made binding upon us."],[21041,"About following funeral processions, and it was not made binding upon us."],[21042,"About following funeral processions, and it was not made binding upon us."],[21043,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to observe mourning for more than three days except for a husband.”"],[21044,"That we should not wear during the mourning period dyed garments except ʿaṣb (a kind of striped garment), and we were commanded not to mourn over a deceased one — or she said over a dead person — for more than three days except for a husband, and we were commanded not to touch perfume except the least of it for purification: kust (costus) and aẓfār (a kind of perfume)."],[21045,"That we should observe mourning over a deceased person for more than three nights except for a husband."],[21046,"“We did not consider yellowish or dusky discharge to be anything (i.e., menstruation).”"],[21047,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Verily, Allah does not accept the prayer of someone whose nose does not touch the ground.\""],[21048,"“I went on seven military campaigns with the Prophet ﷺ, staying behind in their camp to look after their riding animals, prepare food for them, tend to the wounded, and treat the sick.”"],[21049,"“I went on seven military campaigns with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, staying behind in their camp, preparing food for them, treating the wounded, and caring for the sick.”"],[21050,"Umm ʿAṭiyyah al-Anṣāriyyah came to us in Basra and said — may my father and mother be ransomed for him, meaning the Prophet ﷺ — “He commanded us to bring out on the two Eids the young unmarried women, the secluded virgins, and the menstruating women. As for the menstruating women, they would keep away from the prayer place but witness the good and the supplication of the Muslims.”"],[21051,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ — may my father and mother be ransomed for him — commanded us to bring them out on the day of Fiṭr (breaking the fast) and the day of Naḥr (sacrifice): the young unmarried women, the secluded virgins, and the menstruating women. She said: As for the menstruating women, they keep away from the prayer place but witness the good and the supplication of the Muslims. She said: We said, “What do you think if one of them does not have a jilbāb (outer garment)?” He said, “Let her sister clothe her with one of her jilbābs.” Hishām said: I heard Muḥammad mention it from Umm ʿAṭiyyah, but I have better memory of Ḥafṣah’s ḥadīth."],[21052,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to bring out on the day of Fiṭr the young unmarried women, the secluded virgins, and the menstruating women. As for the menstruating women, they keep away from the prayer but witness the good and the supplication of the Muslims. Then a woman said, “O Messenger of Allah, what if one of us does not have a jilbāb?” He said, “Let her sister clothe her with her jilbāb.”"],[21053,"“We used to be commanded to go out on the two Eids, including the secluded young women and the virgin. She said: The menstruating women would also go out and stand behind the people, saying takbīr with the people.”"],[21054,"I heard this from the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , regarding women who do not have a jilbab (outer garment): Do they witness the celebration? She said: Yes, by my father. Whenever she spoke about the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , she would say: By my father, I heard the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , saying, \"Allow the unmarried women and those who menstruate to attend the Eid prayer and the supplication of the Muslims, but let them stay away from the prayer area.\""],[21055,"From Umm ʿAṭiyyah: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to go out on the day of the two Eids, even the young girls and unmarried women. Ḥafṣah said: A woman said to Umm ʿAṭiyyah, “And the menstruating women?” She said, “And the menstruating women go out, keeping away from the prayer place, and remember Allah.”"],[21056,"“He took a pledge from us at the time of the oath of allegiance that we would not wail. None of them fulfilled it except five: Umm Sulaym, Umm al-ʿAlāʾ, the daughter of Abī Sabrah, Umm Muʿādh the daughter of Abī Sabrah, and another woman.”"],[21057,"We gave allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He recited to us that we should not associate anything with God, and he forbade us from wailing. A woman among us withdrew her hand and said, 'O Messenger of God, so-and-so helped me (in mourning), and I want to repay her.' He said nothing to her. She went away, then came back and said, 'No woman among us fulfilled it except Umm Sulaym, Umm al-'Ala', the daughter of Abu Sabrah, and the wife of Mu'adh.'"],[21058,"Among what the Messenger of God ﷺ took from us at the pledge of allegiance was that we should not wail."],[21059,"We gave allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and among what he commanded us of good was that we should not wail. A woman said, 'O Messenger of God, the family of so-and-so helped me (in mourning), so I will not give you allegiance until I help them.' She said, 'So I helped them, then I gave him allegiance.' She said, 'No woman among us fulfilled it except me and Umm Sulaym.'"],[21060,"From Umm 'Atiyyah regarding His saying {and they will not disobey you in what is right}, she said: Part of it is wailing. I said to the Prophet ﷺ when we gave allegiance to him that we would not disobey him in what is right: 'O Messenger of God, except the family of so-and-so.'"],[21061,"That we should mourn for a deceased person beyond three days, not applying perfume, not applying kohl, and not wearing a dyed garment except a garment of 'asb (a Yemeni cloth). She said: He permitted them when they bathe after purification to use qust and azfar (types of incense)."],[21062,"\"The deceased wife does not mourn except for her husband, she does not put on henna, perfume, or wear colored clothing except for a garment made of cotton.\" Hisham narrates from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, from the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ something similar to this."],[21063,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'No one should mourn for a deceased person beyond three days except a woman, for she mourns for her husband four months and ten days. She should not wear a dyed garment except a garment of 'asb, nor apply kohl, nor apply perfume except at the time of her purification, when she may apply qust and azfar.'"],[21064,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'A woman should not mourn beyond three days except for her husband, for she mourns four months and ten days. She should not wear a dyed garment except a washed garment, nor apply kohl, nor dye with henna, nor touch perfume except when she has purified from her menstruation, after that with qust or azfar.'"],[21065,"About following funeral processions, and it was not made obligatory upon us."],[21066,"About following funeral processions, and it was not made obligatory upon us."],[21067,"About following funeral processions, and it was not made obligatory upon us."],[21068,"About following funeral processions, and he did not make it obligatory upon us."],[21069,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon 'A'ishah and said, 'Do you have anything?' She said, 'No, except something that Nusaybah, who is Umm 'Atiyyah, sent to us from the sheep that was sent to her as sadaqah (charity).' He said, 'It has reached its proper place.'"],[21070,"The Prophet ﷺ said to ʿĀʾishah: “Do you have anything to feed me?” She said: “No, except from the sheep that Nusaybah sent to me from the zakāh.” He said: “Bring it, for it has reached its destination.”"],[21071,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me a sheep from the zakāh, and ʿĀʾishah sent me some of it. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to ʿĀʾishah, he said: “Do you have anything?” She said: “No, except that Nusaybah sent us from the sheep that I sent to her.” He said: “It has reached its destination.”"],[21072,"From Umm ʿAṭiyyah al-Anṣāriyyah, who had pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ, she said: “We used not to consider the yellowish or brownish discharge after the ritual bath as anything.”"],[21073,"“We used not to consider the yellowish or brownish discharge after purification as anything.”"],[21074,"“We used not to consider the yellowish or brownish discharge as anything.”"],[21075,"One of the daughters of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ came to us and said: “Wash her with lote leaves, and wash her an odd number of times — three, or five, or more than that if you see fit — and put camphor in the last washing. When you finish, inform me.” She said: “When we finished, we informed him, and he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said: ‘Shroud her in it.’” She said: “We braided her hair into three braids, her forelock and two side braids, then we placed them behind her.”"],[21076,"From Umm ʿAṭiyyah al-Anṣāriyyah: One of the daughters of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Wash her with water and lote leaves, and wash her an odd number of times, three or five or more if you see fit, and put camphor or some camphor in the last washing. When you finish, inform me.” We informed him, and he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said: “Shroud her in it.” She said: “So we braided her hair into three braids, her forelock and two side braids, and placed them behind her.”"],[21077,"“We washed the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ and parted her hair into three braids.”"],[21078,"I heard Ḥafṣah bint Sīrīn say: Umm ʿAṭiyyah told us that they made the hair of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ into three braids. I said: “Did she undo it, wash it, and then make it into three braids?” She said: “Yes.”"],[21079,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding washing his daughter: “Begin with her right side and the places of ablution from her.”"],[21080,"From Umm al-Hudhayl, who is Ḥafṣah bint Sīrīn, from Umm ʿAṭiyyah, she said: “When we washed the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ, he said to us while we were washing her: ‘Begin with her right side and the places of ablution.’”"],[21081,"Umm ʿAṭiyyah told us: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us not to withhold the māʿūn.” I said: “What is the māʿūn?” She said: “What people lend to one another.”"],[21082,"I heard Umm ʿAṭiyyah say: \"We used to go out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to treat the wounded and bury the slain.\""],[21083,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to instruct us to guard our private parts and our tongues, and he said: \"They bring you in [to ruin] and do not bring you out.\""],[21084,"When the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: \"Wash her an odd number of times, three or five, and put camphor in the last [wash], or something of camphor. When you have washed her, inform me.\" So we informed him. She said: He threw his waist-wrapper to us and said: \"Wrap her with it.\""],[21085,"A daughter of the Prophet ﷺ died. The Prophet ﷺ entered and said: \"Wash her an odd number of times, three or five, or as you see fit, and make it odd.\" So we washed her. Then he entered and threw his waist-wrapper to us and said: \"Wrap her with it beneath her shroud, and put camphor in the last [wash].\""],[21086,"I was among the women who escorted one of the Prophet's ﷺ daughters to her husband. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: \"When she performs ghusl, pour water over her head three times.\" Yaḥyā said: I said to Sharīk: \"From janābah?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[21087,"He said to her: \"Who was this person with you?\" She said: \"There was no one with me, and I did not wake up until you woke me.\" He said: \"Join your family.\" People talked about her. Her father said to her: \"My little daughter, people have spoken a lot about you. So tell me your story. If the man has spoken truthfully against you, you sent someone to kill him, so the slander would be cut off from you. But if he was lying, you would have taken him to one of the soothsayers of Yemen for judgment.\" She swore to him by what they used to swear by that he was indeed lying against her. Then he said to al-Fākih: \"O man, you have accused my daughter of a grave matter. So take me to one of the soothsayers of Yemen for judgment.\" So ʿUtbah went out with a group from Banū ʿAbd Manāf, and al-Fākih went out with a group from Banū Makhzūm, and Hind went out with them along with some women. When they approached the land, and they said: \"We will go to the soothsayer,\" Hind's condition changed and her face changed. Her father said to her: \"I see what is upon you of changed condition, and that is only because of something hateful to you. Would that this had been before people witnessed our journey!\" She said: \"No, by Allah, my father, it is not because of something hateful. But I know that you are coming to a human being who errs and is right, and I do not feel safe that he will name me with a mark that will be a disgrace upon me among the Arabs.\" He said: \"I will test him before he looks into your affair.\" He whistled to his horse until it lowered [its head], then he took a grain of wheat and inserted it into its urethra and tied a strap over it. When they arrived in the morning, [the soothsayer] honored them and slaughtered for them. When they sat down, ʿUtbah said to him: \"We have come to you about a matter, and I have hidden something for you to test you with. So look at what it is.\" He said: \"A she-camel in a ...?\" He said: \"I want something clearer than this.\" He said: \"A grain of wheat in the urethra of a horse.\" He said: \"You are right. Look into the affair of these women.\" He began to approach one of them, strike her shoulder, and say: \"Rise,\" until he approached Hind, struck her shoulder, and said: \"Rise, you are neither unchaste nor an adulteress, and you will give birth to a boy who will be called Muʿāwiyah.\" Then al-Fākih rose to her and took her hand, but she pulled her hand away from his and said: \"Away with you! By Allah, I will be keen for that [child] to be from other than you.\" Then Abū Sufyān married her, and she gave birth to Muʿāwiyah."],[21088,"Hind came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, there was no household on the face of the earth more beloved to me to be humiliated by Allah than your household, and today there is no household on the face of the earth more beloved to me to be honored by Allah than your household.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"And also, by the One in Whose hand is my soul.\" Maʿmar said: meaning they will surely increase. Then she said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Abū Sufyān is a stingy man. Is there any sin upon me if I take from his wealth to support his dependents without his permission?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no harm upon you to spend on them with what is reasonable.\""],[21089,"Hind came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, there was no household on the face of the earth more beloved to me to be humiliated by Allah than your household, and today there is no household on the face of the earth more beloved to me to be honored by Allah than your household.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"And also, by the One in Whose hand is my soul.\" Maʿmar said: meaning they will surely increase. Then she said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Abū Sufyān is a stingy man. Is there any sin upon me if I take from his wealth to support his dependents without his permission?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no harm upon you to spend on them with what is reasonable.\""],[21090,"Hind came to the Prophet and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, there was no one on the face of the earth whom I loved more than your own people. But today, there is no people on earth whom I love more than your own people.\" The Prophet said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, this is a sign of true faith.\" Then she said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a stingy man. Is it permissible for me to spend on his family from his wealth without his permission?\" The Prophet said, \"There is no harm if you spend on them according to what is reasonable.\""],[21091,"ʿAbdullāh b. Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: My father narrated to me from Hishām b. ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah, who said: Hind, the mother of Muʿāwiyah, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"Abū Sufyān is a miserly man and he does not give me what suffices me and my child except what I take from him without his knowledge. Is there any sin upon me in that?\" The Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"Take what suffices you and your children, with what is reasonable.\""],[21092,"Hind, the mother of Muʿāwiyah, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Abū Sufyān is a miserly man and he does not give my children except what I take from him without his knowledge. Is there anything upon me in that?\" The Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"Take what suffices you and your children, with what is reasonable.\""],[21093,"'Hind came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a stingy man and he does not give me enough for me and my child, except for what I take from his wealth without him realizing.' He said: Take what is sufficient for you and your child, on a reasonable basis.' \" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2293)"],[21094,"Hind, the mother of Mu'awiyah, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a stingy man, and he does not give me and my children enough except what I take from him without his knowledge. Is there any blame on me in that?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Take what suffices you and your children in a reasonable manner.\""],[21095,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a miserly man. Should we feed our slaves from his wealth?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[21096,"Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ? She said, \"Yes, I heard him say, 'The first thing to be weighed in the Balance is good character.'\""],[21097,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, there is no woman who removes her clothes in other than her husband's house or her mothers' houses except that she has torn every veil between her and the Most Merciful ﷻ.\""],[21098,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, \"O Muslim women, you should adhere to glorification (tasbih), declaring God's oneness (tahlil), and sanctification (taqdis). Count them on your fingertips, for they will be made to speak and will be questioned, and they will not be heedless, lest you forget the mercy.\" Abu Kurayb attributed Hani b. 'Uthman, saying: al-Juhani."],[21099,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanding women to attend to glorification, declaring God's oneness, and sanctification, and to count them on their fingertips, saying, \"They will be questioned and made to speak.\" Ibn Dawud said, \"It has reached me that al-Thawri asked Hani about this hadith.\""],[21100,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Muslim, the nephew of al-Zuhri, narrated to us, from his uncle Ibn Shihab, from Humayd b. 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, from his mother Umm Kulthum bt. 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about \"Say: He is Allah, the One\" (Qul huwa Allahu ahad), and he said, \"It is a third of the Quran or equal to it.\""],[21101,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He is not a liar who reconciles between people, saying good or conveying good.\""],[21102,"From his mother Umm Kulthum bt. 'Uqbah, one of the first emigrant women, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"He is not a liar who reconciles between people, saying good or conveying good.\""],[21103,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, saying, \"He is not a liar who reconciles between people.\""],[21104,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"He is not a liar who reconciles between people, saying good or conveying good.\""],[21105,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"He is not a liar who reconciles between people, conveying good or saying good.\""],[21106,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"The liar is not the one who reconciles between people, conveying good or saying it.\""],[21107,"He informed him that his mother, Umm Kulthūm bt. ʿUqbah, who was among the female companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ and among the first female emigrants who gave allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “He is not a liar who reconciles between people and conveys good or says good.”"],[21108,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “A liar is not the one who says something to reconcile between people.”"],[21109,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “He is not a liar who reconciles between people, who says good or conveys good.”"],[21110,"They gave allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ. She informed him that she heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “He is not a liar who reconciles between people and says good or conveys good.”"],[21111,"I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ permit lying in anything except in three cases. The Messenger of God ﷺ would not count it as lying: a man who reconciles between people, adding to the speech while intending reconciliation; a man who speaks in war; and a man who talks to his wife, and a woman who talks to her husband.”"],[21112,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ permit lying except in three cases. The Messenger of God ﷺ would say, “I do not count it as lying: a man who reconciles between people, a man who speaks in war, and a man who talks to his wife and a woman who talks to her husband.”"],[21113,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “He is not a liar who reconciles between people and says good or conveys good.”"],[21114,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “He is not a liar who reconciles between people and says good or conveys good.”"],[21115,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “He is not a liar who reconciles between people and says good or conveys good.”"],[21116,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “He is not a liar who says good or conveys good.”"],[21117,"That she heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"He who makes peace between the people by inventing good information or saying good things, is not a liar.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2692)"],[21118,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “He is not a liar who reconciles between people and conveys good or says good.”"],[21119,"She heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “He is not a liar who reconciles between two people.”"],[21120,"From Umm Kulthum bt. ʿUqba b. Abī Muʿayṭ, and she was the wife of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf, and she had prayed in the direction of both qiblas with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He is not a liar who makes peace between people and says good or conveys good.”"],[21121,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The best charity is that given to a hostile relative.”"],[21122,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: Which deeds are best? He said: “Faith in Allah, then prayer at the beginning of its time.”"],[21123,"“I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dye his hair until he died.”"],[21124,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at Umm Habibah bt. al-‘Abbas as she toddled in front of him, and he said ﷺ: “If this one reaches [maturity] while I am alive, I will marry her.” He was taken before she reached [maturity], so al-Aswad b. ‘Abd al-Asad married her, and she bore him Rizq b. al-Aswad and Lubabah bt. al-Aswad, whom she named after her mother, Umm al-Fadl."],[21125,"From Umm 'Uthman bt. Sufyan, the mother of Shaybah's child, who had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ called Shaybah, and he opened the House. When he entered, he bowed and placed his sides."],[21126,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me, and with him was ʿAli, who was convalescing. She said: We had hanging clusters of grapes. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up to eat, and ʿAli stood up to eat. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Gently, for you are convalescing.” She said: So ʿAli sat down, and the Prophet ﷺ ate from them. Then I served them chard and barley. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Eat from this.”"],[21127,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ in the house of Hafsah, and he was saying, “No man who was present at Badr and al-Hudaybiyyah will enter the Fire.” Hafsah said, “O Messenger of God, God says: {And there is none of you but will come to it; this is, upon your Lord, a decree that must be accomplished.}” He said, “Then what?” She said, {Then We will save those who feared God and leave the wrongdoers therein on their knees.}"],[21128,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I not tell you about the best of people, a man?” They said, “Yes indeed.” He pointed with his hand toward the east and said: “A man holding the reins of his horse in the path of Allah, waiting to raid or be raided upon. Shall I not tell you about the best of people after him, a man?” They said, “Yes indeed.” He pointed with his hand toward the Hijaz and said: “A man among his sheep, who establishes the prayer, gives the zakah, knows what is due to Allah from his wealth, and has withdrawn from people.”"],[21129,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to take a midday nap at my place. I would spread a leather mat for him, and he would nap on it and sweat. I would mix musk with his sweat. Muhammad b. Sirin said, 'I asked Umm Sulaym for some of that musk, and she gave me some. When Muhammad died, he was embalmed with that musk, and Muhammad liked to embalm the deceased with musk.'"],[21130,"Umm Sulaym was with Abu Talha al-Ansari on the day of Hunayn, and she had a dagger. Abu Talha said to her, 'What is this with you, O Umm Sulaym?' She said, 'A dagger I have taken; if any of the polytheists comes near me, I will rip his belly with it.' Abu Talha said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you not hear what Umm Sulaym says? She says such and such.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, some of the freed captives who came after us fled with you, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Umm Sulaym, Allah has sufficed and done well.'"],[21131,"She said to Safiyyah, \"Are you the one who will cause us to fail? Indeed, you are holding us back.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What is that?\" 'A'ishah said, \"Safiyyah has menstruated.\" He said, \"It was said that she has already performed the Ifadah.\" He said, \"Then no, in that case.\" He said, \"So they returned to Ibn 'Abbas and said, 'We found the hadith as she narrated it to us.'\""],[21132,"When the Prophet ﷺ went on the expedition to Badr, I said, “O Messenger of God, permit me to go on a raid with you to treat your wounded and nurse your sick, so that perhaps God may grant me martyrdom.” He said, “Stay in your house, for God will grant you martyrdom.” She was called “the martyr,” and she had recited the Qur’an. She asked the Prophet ﷺ for permission to make a place in her house to pray, and he permitted her."],[21133,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “O Abū Ayyūb, the divorce of Umm Ayyūb is a sin.”"],[21134,"That the Prophet ﷺ stopped at her place. She said, “We made him food containing some of these herbs.” Sufyān said, “Leeks and other things.” He disliked it and said to his companions, “Eat, for I am not like one of you; I fear I would offend my companion [the angel].”"],[21135,"That she asked the Prophet ﷺ, “Will we visit each other when we die, and will we see one another?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “The soul will be a bird that hangs on the trees, until on the Day of Resurrection every soul enters its body.”"],[21136,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No zakah is due on newly acquired wealth until a year passes over it.”"],[21137,"She went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Khaybar, as the sixth of six women. News of that reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he sent for her and said, “With whose permission did you women set out?” I saw anger in him. We said, “O Messenger of Allah, we set out with medicine to treat the wounded, we hand arrows, serve sawiq, spin hair, and help in the cause of Allah.” He said to us, “Stay put.” When Allah granted him victory over Khaybar, he allotted us a share just as he allotted the men. I asked, “What was that?” She said, “Dates.”"],[21138,"The Prophet ﷺ came to Saʿd b. ʿUbāda, greeted him, but he did not respond and remained silent. She said: Saʿd regretted it and said to me: Go to the Messenger of God ﷺ and tell him that we remained silent hoping that he would give us more. She said: Then he came and greeted at the door; I heard his voice but did not see him. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'What are you?' She said: 'I am Umm Mildam.' He said: 'You? Then no welcome to you and no greetings.'"],[21139,"She brought a small skin of ghee to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered Bilāl, who squeezed it and then returned it to her. She went back and found it full, so she came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Has something been revealed concerning me, O Messenger of God? He said: 'And what is that, O Umm Mālik?' She said: Why did you return my gift to me? He called Bilāl and asked him about that. He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I squeezed it until I felt embarrassed. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Congratulations to you, O Umm Mālik; this is a blessing whose reward God has hastened.' Then he taught her to say after every prayer: 'Glory be to God' ten times, 'Praise be to God' ten times, and 'God is greatest' ten times."],[21140,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do not soak dates and raisins together; soak each of them separately."],[21141,"I witnessed Aminah when she gave birth to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When labor struck her, I looked at the stars as they hung low until I said: They will surely fall upon me. When she gave birth, a light came out of her that illuminated the house we were in and the dwelling, so that there was nothing I looked at except light."],[21142,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, our husbands prevent us from praying with you, and we love to pray with you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Your prayer in your houses is better than your prayer in your rooms, and your prayer in your rooms is better than your prayer in your courtyards, and your prayer in your courtyards is better than your prayer in congregation.'"],[21143,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned a tribulation and said: 'The best of you in it, and the best of people in it, is a man who withdraws with his wealth, worships Allah, and gives His due, and a man who takes hold of his horse's head, frightening the enemy and they frighten him.'"],[21144,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was stoning Jamrat al-‘Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice from the bottom of the valley, and he was saying: “O people, do not kill one another. Stone with pebbles like those used for khazf.” He threw seven [pebbles], then left without stopping. Behind him was a man shielding him from the people. I said: “Who is this?” They said: “Al-Fadl b. ‘Abbas.”"],[21145,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the meat of domestic donkeys. He said: “Does it not graze on pasture and eat trees?” The man said: “Yes.” He said: “Then eat of its meat.”"],[21146,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “Hasten the iftar and delay the suhur.”"],[21147,"I brought a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet’s wives refused to accept it, saying, “We do not accept gifts.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said, “Take the gift of Umm Sunbula, for she is from our desert people and we are from her settled people.” And he gave her the valley of such-and-such. Then Abdullah b. Hasan b. Hasan b. Ali b. Abi Talib bought it from her. He said: He gave her a small herd. Amr b. Qayzi said: I saw some of them. Abu Kurayb said: I said to Zayd b. al-Hubab, “Who gave it to her?” He replied, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[21148,"\"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a young boy who wet himself, so he commanded to clean him up. Then, a young girl was brought to him who had menstruated, so he commanded to wash her.\""],[21149,"“Perhaps I used to contend with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ over ablution water from a single vessel.”"],[21150,"Abd al-Munim Abu Said al-Harrani al-Iswari narrated to us, from al-Salt b. Dinar, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from a woman among them called Umm Afif, who said: “We gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he took allegiance from the women, and he enjoined upon them that they should not converse with a man except a mahram, and he commanded us to recite the Fatiha of the Book over our dead.”"],[21151,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a large bowl of tharid was brought. The Messenger of God ﷺ ate, and I ate with him, and Dhul-Yadayn ate with us. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ took a bone with meat on it and handed it to me. He said, \"What is the matter with you?\" I said, \"I was fasting, then I forgot.\" Dhul-Yadayn said, \"Now, after you have eaten your fill?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"No harm upon you. It is only a provision that God has brought to you, so complete your fast.\""],[21152,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he ordered for me some barley porridge and clothed me with a cloak."],[21153,"The naqir is the hollowed-out base of palm trunks, that which the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade."],[21154,"Her father took her to the Prophet ﷺ, and he wiped his hand over her and blessed her. She said, \"She became a devout, righteous woman.\""],[21155,"The Messenger of God ﷺ looked out one evening and said, \"O people, are you not ashamed?\" They said, \"Of what, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"You gather what you do not eat, build what you do not inhabit, and hope for what you do not attain. Are you not ashamed of that?\""],[21156,"She went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked him to provide them with a servant. The Messenger of God ﷺ had just arrived from a journey and had acquired some slaves. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The orphans of the people of Badr have preceded you.\""],[21157,"I saw Budayl b. Warqa' on a camel following the people and proclaiming, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ orders you not to fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking.\""],[21158,"From her mother, Umm Sinan al-Aslamiyyah, one of the women who gave the pledge, she said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I have come to you with shyness, and I did not come to you until I was compelled by need.” He said, “If you were self-sufficient, it would be better for you.”"],[21159,"“He waited for Umm ‘Abd until she prayed over ‘Utbah.”"],[21160,"I entered upon Abu Musa while he was in his final illness. His wife was about to weep or intended to, so Abu Musa said to her, “Have you not heard what the Messenger of God ﷺ said?” She said, “Yes,” and fell silent. When Abu Musa died, Yazid said: I met his wife and said to her, “Abu Musa’s saying: ‘Have you not heard what the Messenger of God ﷺ said,’ then you fell silent.” She said, “Yes, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘He is not one of us who shaves, wails, or tears.’”"],[21161,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden.”"],[21162,"From Umm Qays bt. Mihsan—and she was among the first of the emigrant women who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she was the sister of 'Ukkashah bt. Mihsan—that she brought a son of hers who had not reached the age of eating food to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he urinated in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and sprinkled it over the urine, and did not wash it."],[21163,"Um Qais said to me, \"If you could see me and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ holding hands in a path from the streets of Madinah, where there is no house, until we reached the graveyard of Gharkad. He said to me, 'O Um Qais!' I said, 'Here I am, at your service, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'You will see this graveyard from which Allah will resurrect seventy thousand people on the Day of Resurrection, resembling the full moon on a night of the full moon. They will enter Paradise without any reckoning.' Ukashah stood up and said, 'Am I included in them, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Yes, you are.' Then another man stood up and said, 'Am I included in them, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Ukashah has beaten you to it.'\""],[21164,"From Abu al-Hasan, the mawla of Umm Qays bt. Mihsan, from Umm Qays, that she said: My son died, and I grieved over him. I said to the one washing him, \"Do not wash my son with cold water, lest you kill him.\" 'Ukkashah b. Mihsan went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him of her words. He smiled and said, \"What she said—may her life be long.\" We do not know of any woman who lived as long as she did."],[21165,"My father went out on a military expedition during the time of the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to look after us and milk a goat of ours. He would milk it into a large bowl and it would fill up. When Khabbab returned, he milked it, and its milking returned to its former amount."],[21166,"When the Prophet ﷺ consummated his marriage with Umm Salama, he said: “I had sent a gift to the Negus, and I do not think it will fail to return to us, for I believe the Negus has died. I sent him a robe and some ounces of musk. When it returns to us, O Umm Salama, it is yours.” She said: It happened as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. The Negus died and the gift returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he sent an ounce of musk to each of his wives, and he sent the robe and the remaining musk to Umm Salama."],[21167,"From Umm Farwa, who had given allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: Which deeds are best? He said: “Prayer at the beginning of its time.”"],[21168,"From Umm Farwa, the grandmother of his father, who was among those who gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The most beloved of deeds to Allah is hastening the prayer to the beginning of its time.”"],[21169,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The most beloved of deeds to Allah, may He be exalted, is prayer at the beginning of its time.”"],[21170,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, while I was listening: Which deeds are best? He said: “Prayer at the beginning of its time.”"],[21171,"I asked Umm Rūmān, who is the mother of ʿĀʾisha, the Mother of the Believers, about the affair of ʿĀʾisha when what was said to her was said, and Allah sent down her vindication. She said: The mother of Misṭaḥ said: May Allah do to Misṭaḥ and did. ʿĀʾisha said: Why? She said: Because he was among those who spread the talk. ʿĀʾisha said: And what talk of his? She informed her. She said: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abū Bakr hear it? She said: Yes. She fell down unconscious, and she did not recover except with a violent fever. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said: What is wrong with her? She said: We said: A fever has seized her. He said: Perhaps it is because of the talk that is being circulated. She said: She sat up and said: By Allah, if I swear, you will not believe me, and if I offer an excuse, you will not excuse me. My example and yours is like Yaʿqūb and his sons. And Allah is the one sought for help against what you describe. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left, and Allah, may He be exalted, sent down what He sent down. He came to her and informed her, and she said: By the praise of Allah, not by the praise of anyone."],[21172,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and ate a shoulder cut. Then Bilāl came and called him to prayer, and he prayed without performing ablution.”"],[21173,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “entered upon her sister Ḍubāʿa bt. al-Zubayr and tore off some meat from a shoulder cut, then stood and prayed without performing ablution.”"],[21174,"She “handed the Prophet ﷺ a shoulder cut of meat, and he ate from it, then prayed.”"],[21175,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me, so I brought a shoulder of meat close to him, and he ate from it, then he stood and prayed."],[21176,"She used to prepare food for the Prophet ﷺ and send it to him, and sometimes he would come to her and eat at her place. She claimed that one day he came to her, and she brought him a shoulder of meat, and she began to slice it for him. She claimed that he ate and prayed without performing wudu."],[21177,"From Umm Ayman, and she was among those who gave allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ."],[21178,"Umm Ayman is the mother of Usamah."],[21179,"Umm Ayman, the mother of Usamah b. Zayd, was from Abyssinia. She was a servant of Abdullah b. Abd al-Muttalib, and she used to nurse the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was small. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed her, then gave her in marriage to Zayd b. Harithah. She died five months after the Prophet ﷺ. Thus said al-Zuhri, and it is narrated in this hadith that she lived after the death of Umar b. al-Khattab."],[21180,"Umm Ayman said on the day Umar was killed: \"Today Islam has been weakened.\""],[21181,"When Umm Ayman arrived from the land of Abyssinia, she pointed to the nest."],[21182,"She sifted flour and made it into a loaf for the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"What is this?\" She said, \"Food that we make here, and I wanted to make a loaf of it for you.\" He said, \"Return it to it, then knead it.\""],[21183,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Hand me the small mat from the mosque.\" She said, \"I am menstruating.\" He said, \"Your menstruation is not in your hand.\""],[21184,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Hand me the small mat.\" I said, \"I am menstruating.\" He said, \"Is it in your hand?\""],[21185,"Umm Ayman wept over the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so they said to her, \"Do you weep over the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he is among the people of Paradise?\" She said, \"I only weep over the news of heaven; it used to come to us.\""],[21186,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, Umm Ayman, who was the mother of Usama b. Zayd, cried. It was asked, \"What makes you cry?\" She replied, \"The news from heaven has been cut off from us.\""],[21187,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The thief is not to have his hand cut off except for a shield.\" And it was valued during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at a dinar or ten dirhams."],[21188,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The black person is only [such] by his stomach and his private parts.”"],[21189,"From Nubayh al-‘Anazi, from Umm Ayman, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up at night to a clay pot in a corner of the house and urinated in it. I got up at night, thirsty, and drank what was in it without realizing. When the Prophet ﷺ rose in the morning, he said: “O Umm Ayman, get up and pour out what is in that clay pot.” I said: “By Allah, I have drunk what was in it.” She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars showed, then said: “Indeed, you will never suffer from pain in your stomach.”"],[21190,"If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw this, he would love it. He mentioned his love for what Umm Ayman gave birth to, and she was the nurse of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[21191,"That the Prophet ﷺ married his daughter Fatimah to ‘Ali b. Abi Talib and ordered him not to enter upon his wife until he came. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and he mentioned the hadith."],[21192,"From Umm ‘Ayyash, who was a servant of the Prophet ﷺ: He sent her with his daughter to ‘Uthman b. ‘Affan."],[21193,"\"I used to help the Messenger of Allah perform ablution, when I was standing and he was sitting.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 392)"],[21194,"Ruqayyah gave birth to a boy for ‘Uthman, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him ‘Abdullah and gave ‘Uthman the kunya Abu ‘Abdullah."],[21195,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “I did not marry Umm Kulthum to ‘Uthman except by revelation from heaven.”"],[21196,"I was among the women who prepared the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ [for burial], and he said: “Pour three times on her head during the washing from major impurity.”"],[21197,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought some garments, among them a small striped cloak. He said: “Who do you think should be given this?” The people fell silent, so he said: “Bring me Umm Khalid.” I was brought, carried, and he took the cloak in his hand and put it on me, saying: “Wear it out and make it worn; wear it out and make it worn.” She said: There was a green or yellow decoration on it, and he said: “O Umm Khalid, this is sanah, sanah” — in Abyssinian it means “beautiful.”"],[21198,"The Prophet ﷺ clothed me in a striped cloak with decorations, and he began wiping over it and saying: “Saniyyah, sanih” — in Abyssinian it means “good.”"],[21199,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking refuge from the punishment of the grave."],[21200,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave, for the punishment of the grave is true.\" Musa b. 'Uqbah said, \"I did not hear anyone say 'I heard the Prophet ﷺ' except Umm Khalid.\""],[21201,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave."],[21202,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and looked at the seal of prophethood between his shoulders."],[21203,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking refuge from the punishment of the grave."],[21204,"She entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Who is this?\" They said, \"Umm Khalid bt. al-Aswad b. 'Abd Yaghuth.\" He said, \"Praise be to Allah who brings forth the living from the dead,\" meaning the believer from the disbeliever."],[21205,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Umm Khalid and said, \"Who is this?\" They said, \"She is one of your paternal aunts.\" He said, \"Indeed, my paternal aunts on this earth are amazing.\" They said, \"Umm Khalid, the daughter of Al-Aswad ibn 'Abd Yaghuth.\" He said, \"Glory be to the One who brings the living from the dead.\""],[21206,"She heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"People will certainly flee from the Dajjal into the mountains.\" Umm Sharik said, \"O Messenger of Allah, where will the Arabs be on that day?\" He said, \"They will be few.\""],[21207,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her to kill geckos."],[21208,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded the killing of geckos."],[21209,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite the Fatihah of the Book over funeral processions."],[21210,"She saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walking briskly between al-Safa and al-Marwah, saying, \"The bat-ha' is not to be crossed except with a fast pace.\""],[21211,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whoever sponsors an orphan, whether his own or from other people, I and he will be in Paradise like these two.”"],[21212,"From the Prophet ﷺ: Her name is Salma bint Qays. Ibn Numayr said: Yunus b. Bukayr narrated that to us from Ibn Ishaq: “And she prayed toward both qiblahs with the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[21213,"O Umm ʿAta, the Messenger of God ﷺ has forbidden the Muslims to eat from their sacrificial animals beyond three days, so do not eat it. I said, “May my father be your ransom, what do we do with what is gifted to us?” He said, “As for what is gifted to you, then it is your affair.”"],[21214,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Umm Mubashshir in a palm grove and said, “Who planted these palms, a Muslim or an unbeliever?” She said, “Rather, a Muslim.” He said, “No Muslim plants a tree or sows a crop and then a beast, bird, or human eats from it, except that it is charity for him.”"],[21215,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me and said, “Who planted this, a Muslim or an unbeliever?” I said, “A Muslim.” He said, “No Muslim plants a tree and then a human, beast, or bird eats from it, except that it is charity for him.”"],[21216,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me while I was in a palm grove and said, “A Muslim planted this or an unbeliever?” I said, “No, rather a Muslim.” He said, “No Muslim plants a tree or sows a crop and then a bird, wild animal, beast, or human eats from it, except that it is charity for him.”"],[21217,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me while I was in a palm grove of mine and said, “Who planted these palms, a Muslim or an unbeliever?” I said, “No, rather a Muslim.” He said, “No Muslim plants a tree and then a bird, human, wild animal, or beast eats from it, except that it is charity for him.”"],[21218,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me while I was in a palm grove of mine and said, “Is this yours?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Who planted it, a Muslim or an unbeliever?” I said, “A Muslim.” He said, “No Muslim plants a tree or sows a crop and then a bird, human, wild animal, or anything eats from it, except that it is charity for him.”"],[21219,"Hatib's servant came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “By God, Hatib will not enter Paradise.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “You have lied; indeed, he was present at Badr and al-Hudaybiyyah.”"],[21220,"The Prophet ﷺ proposed to the daughter of al-Bara b. Maʿrur, and she said, “I stipulated for my husband that I would not marry after him.” He said, “That is not proper.”"],[21221,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was in one of the walled gardens of Banu al-Najjar in which there were graves of those who had died in the pre-Islamic era. He went out and I heard him say: “Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, is there punishment in the grave?” He said: “Yes, indeed they are punished in their graves with a punishment that the beasts hear.”"],[21222,"She heard the Prophet ﷺ say, in the presence of Hafsah: “No one from the people of the tree who pledged allegiance beneath it will enter the Fire, if Allah wills.” She said, “Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah,” and he rebuked her. Then Hafsah recited: {And there is none of you except he will come to it} [Maryam: 71]. The Prophet ﷺ said: {Then We will save those who feared Allah and leave the wrongdoers in it on their knees} [Maryam: 72]."],[21223,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “O Umm Mubashshir, whoever has three children who die in infancy, Allah will admit her to Paradise by the virtue of His mercy toward them.” Umm Mubashshir was cooking a dish and said, “Or two?” He said: “Or two.”"],[21224,"“O Abu Abd al-Rahman, if you meet my son, convey to him my greetings of peace.” He said, “May Allah forgive you, O Umm Bishr; we are lower than that.” She said, “O Abu Abd al-Rahman, have you not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Indeed the souls of the believers are in the crops of green birds, perched upon the trees of Paradise’?” He said, “Yes indeed.” She said, “Then that is it.”"],[21225,"Abu Talhah proposed to Um Sulaim before accepting Islam, and she said, \"Indeed, I desire you, and there is no one like you, but you are a disbeliever and I am a Muslim woman. If you accept Islam, that will be my dowry and I will not ask you for anything else.\" And Abu Talhah married her."],[21226,"Abu Talhah married Umm Sulaym, and the dower between them was Islam. Umm Sulaym accepted Islam before Abu Talhah. He proposed to her, and she said: “I have become a Muslim; if you become a Muslim, I will marry you.” So he became a Muslim, and the dower between them was Islam."],[21227,"Abu Talhah came to Umm Sulaym—she was the mother of Anas, and Abu Talhah was his stepfather—and said, “Do you have anything, O Umm Sulaym? I passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was teaching the people of the Suffah Surah al-Nisa’, and he had tied a stone over his stomach from hunger.” She said, “I had some barley which I ground. Then she sent me to the markets—and the markets were their walled gardens—so I brought them some firewood, and she made a flat loaf from it.” Then he said, “Do you have any condiment?” She said, “I had a small skin of ghee, but I do not know whether anything remains in it.” So she brought it to him and he squeezed it. He said, “Squeezing by two is more effective than squeezing by one.” So they squeezed it together and extracted about the size of a date. She greased the flat loaf, then he called me and said, “O Anas, do you know the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “I left him with his companions in the Suffah teaching them. Invite him, but do not invite anyone else with him. Be careful not to embarrass me.” So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he saw me he said, “Perhaps your father sent you to us?” I said, “Yes.” Then he said to the people, “Go,” and they went. That day they were eighty men. He held my hand, and when I drew near the house, I pulled my hand from his. Abu Talhah began looking for me in the house and throwing stones at me, saying, “You have embarrassed me before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Then he went out to him and told him the news. He said, “It will not harm you.” Then he ordered them and they sat down. Then he entered and we brought him the flat loaf. He said, “Is there any condiment?” Umm Sulaym said, “O Messenger of Allah, we had a small skin, and Abu Talhah and I squeezed it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Bring it, for squeezing by three is more effective than squeezing by two.” So it was brought, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ squeezed it, and they extracted from it the size of a date. They wiped the flat loaf with it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped it with his hand. Then he invoked blessing over it, then said, “Call ten for me.” So I called ten, and they ate from it until they were full to satiety. They kept entering ten by ten until all were full. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down and we sat with him, and we ate until there was leftover."],[21228,"I recognized in the speech of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hunger. He said, “Do you have anything?” She said, “Yes.” She brought out flat loaves of barley, then brought out a headcover of hers and wrapped the bread in it, then sent me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I went and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque with people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “Did Abu Talhah send you?” I said, “Yes.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to those with him, “Get up.” So he set off, and I went ahead of them until I came to Abu Talhah and told him. Abu Talhah said, “O Umm Sulaym, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has come with the people, and we do not have enough food to satisfy them.” She said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” Abu Talhah went out until we reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah came forward with Abu Talhah until they entered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Bring what you have, O Umm Sulaym.” She brought that bread, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered it to be crumbled. Umm Sulaym squeezed a small skin of ghee and used it as a condiment. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said over it whatever Allah willed him to say, then said, “Give permission to ten.” He gave them permission, and they ate until they were full, then left. Then he said, “Give permission to ten,” and they ate until they were full, then left. Then he said, “Give permission to ten,” and they ate until they were full, then left. Then he said, “Give permission to ten,” and they ate until they were full, then left. Then he said, “Give permission to ten,” and all the people ate until they were full. The people were seventy or eighty."],[21229,"Abu Talhah said, “O Umm Sulaym, prepare something for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” She ground some barley and prepared it. Then Abu Talhah called me and said, “Go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and say, ‘My father invites you,’ and keep it secret.” Anas said: I went while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in the mosque. When he saw me he said, “O Anas.” I said, “At your service, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Did your father invite me?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Get up.” Then he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not pass by any gathering except that he said, “Get up.” I went out quickly until I came to Abu Talhah and said, “Here is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he has come with the people.” Abu Talhah said, “Did I not order you to be alone with him?” I said, “When he asked me, ‘Did your father invite me?’ I said, ‘Yes’; I did not lie to him.” Abu Talhah met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the door of the house and said, “O Messenger of Allah, it is only a little something we wanted to reserve for you.” He said, “Enter.” So he entered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: Umm Sulaym had a small skin of ghee which she was squeezing, and it had dried or almost dried. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Umm Sulaym, hand it to me so that I may squeeze it better than you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it in his hand and did thus with the ghee. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on the top of the tharid and said, “O Abu Talhah, admit ten.” So ten entered and ate until they were full. He kept admitting ten by ten, and they ate until they were satiated, until between seventy and eighty entered. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the household ate, and they had leftovers which they gave as a gift to their neighbors."],[21230,"He heard Anas b. Malik say: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day and found him sitting with his companions, talking to them, and he had tied a stone over his stomach. I said to one of his companions, “Why has the Messenger of Allah ﷺ tied his stomach?” He said, “From hunger.” So I went to Abu Talhah, who was the husband of Umm Sulaym bt. Milhan, and said, “O father, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ tie his stomach with a band. I asked one of his companions, and he said, ‘From hunger.’” Abu Talhah went in to my mother and said, “Is there anything?” She said, “I have pieces of bread and some dates. If the Prophet ﷺ comes alone, we can satisfy him; but if someone comes with him, it will be too little for them.” Abu Talhah said, “Go, O Anas, and stand near the Messenger of Allah. When he gets up, invite him after his companions and those with him have dispersed. When he stands at the threshold of his door, say, ‘My father invites you.’” I did that. When I said, “My father invites you,” he said to his companions, “O these, come.” Then he took my hand and squeezed it, and came with his companions until they drew near our house. Then he released my hand, and I entered feeling sad because of the large number who came with him. I said, “O father, I said to the Messenger of Allah what you told me, and he called his companions and has come with them.” Abu Talhah went out to them and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I only sent Anas to invite you alone, and I do not have enough to satisfy those I see.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Enter, for Allah ﷻ will satisfy them with what you have.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered with me and said, “Gather whatever you have and bring it near.” Those with him sat at the doorstep. I brought what we had of bread and dates, and we placed it on our mat. He invoked blessing over it, then said, “Admit eight to me.” I admitted eight, and he placed his palm over the food and said, “Eat and mention the name of Allah.” They ate from between his fingers until they were full. Then he ordered me, and I admitted eight more while the first group left. They entered and ate until they were full. Then he ordered me, and I admitted eight more. He continued like that until eighty men entered, all eating until full. Then he called me and my mother and Abu Talhah and said, “Eat.” We ate until we were full. Then he lifted his hand and said, “O Umm Sulaym, where is this compared to your food when you presented it?” She said, “May my father and mother be ransomed for you! Had I not seen them eating, I would have said that nothing of our food had decreased.”"],[21231,"Umm Sulaym bt. Milhan was married to Abu Talhah. She prepared a khazirah. Then Abu Talhah said to me, “Go, my son, and invite the Messenger of Allah.” I went and invited him. I came to him while he was among the people, and I said, “My father invites you.” He said to the people, “Go.” When I saw that he said to the people, I went ahead of them until I came to Abu Talhah and said, “O father, here is the Messenger of Allah with the people.” Abu Talhah stood at the door until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, then said, “O Messenger of Allah, it was only a little something.” He said, “Bring it, for Allah will put blessing in it.” So he brought it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ put his hands in it and invoked blessing over it, until eighty men ate from it."],[21232,"When Abu Talhah saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hungry, he came to Umm Sulaym and said, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hungry. Do you have anything?” She said, “We have about two mudds of barley flour.” He said, “Knead it and bake it; perhaps we can invite the Prophet ﷺ to eat from it.” She kneaded it and baked it, and it came out as one flat loaf. He said to me, “Invite the Messenger of Allah.” So I went to the Prophet ﷺ while there were people with him—I think he said about eighty-some. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, Abu Talhah invites you.” He said to his companions, “Answer Abu Talhah’s invitation.” I came back quickly and told him that he and his companions were coming. He said, “By Allah, the Messenger of Allah knows better what is in my house than I do.” Abu Talhah went out to meet him and said, “By Allah, we have nothing but one flat loaf. I saw you hungry, so I ordered Umm Sulaym to make a flat loaf for you.” He called for the flat loaf and for a large bowl, placed it in it, and said, “Is there any ghee?” Abu Talhah said, “There was something in the small skin.” He said: So he brought it, and the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Talhah squeezed it until some came out. The Prophet ﷺ wiped his forefinger with it, then wiped the flat loaf, then said, “In the name of Allah.” The flat loaf swelled, and he continued doing that while the flat loaf swelled until I saw the flat loaf in the bowl turning liquid. Then he said, “Call ten of my companions for me.” I called ten for him, and the Prophet ﷺ placed the flat loaf and said, “Eat, in the name of Allah.” They ate from around the flat loaf until they were full. He kept calling ten by ten, and they ate that flat loaf until eighty-some men ate from around the flat loaf until they were full. He said: And indeed the middle of the flat loaf, where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had placed his hand, remained as it was."],[21233,"Prepare for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ food specifically for himself that he may eat from it. Then Abu Talha sent me to the Prophet ﷺ. I came to him and said, 'Abu Talha has sent me to you.' He said to the people, 'Arise.' Abu Talha met us and said, 'O Prophet of Allah, I only prepared food for you yourself specifically.' He said, 'Never mind, proceed with us.' The people went with him, and he brought the food, which he had made only for the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand and invoked the name of Allah over it, then said, 'Give permission to ten.' So I gave them permission, and they entered. He said, 'Eat, in the name of Allah.' They ate until they were full, then they rose. The Prophet ﷺ placed his hand as he had done the first time and invoked the name, then said, 'Give permission to ten.' He said, 'Until he had done that with eighty men. Then the Prophet ﷺ and the household ate, and they left leftovers.'"],[21234,"Prepare for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ food for himself specifically that he may eat from it. Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Amr b. Qusayt and Sa'id b. Hafs exactly."],[21235,"Abu Talha, who was his paternal uncle and his mother's husband, brought two mudds of barley. He ordered them to be prepared. Then he said to me, 'Go and invite the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for us.' I invited him, and he said to the people, 'Arise.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and I walked ahead of him until I entered upon Abu Talha. He said, 'What have you done, or what did you make?' I said, 'I have invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to the people, \"Arise.\"' He said, 'Did you not know what we have?' I said, 'Yes, but I could not say anything to the Messenger of Allah.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached the door, he called ten at a time. He spoke as Allah willed, then said to the people, 'Eat.' They ate until they were full, then they left. He called another ten, until eighty men ate from it, and there remained enough for the household to eat their fill."],[21236,"He informed him that he heard Anas b. Malik say: Abu Talha came one day and found the Prophet ﷺ standing, teaching the people of the Suffah, with a small rock on his stomach to hold it up from hunger. He returned to Umm Sulaym and said, 'I have seen something regarding the Messenger of Allah that angered me. Do you have anything?' She said, 'Yes, a little barley.' He said to me, 'Prepare it.' I prepared it. Then he said to me, 'Go and invite the Prophet of Allah, and let no one know about you.' Anas said, 'When the Prophet ﷺ saw me, he said, \"Did Abu Talha send you?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Arise.\" Seventy men arose with him. I came to Abu Talha and informed him. He said, \"O Prophet of Allah, it is only a little something we made for you. By Allah, we do not have enough to satisfy them.\" He said, \"Bring what you have.\" I brought it to him. Umm Sulaym had a small skin of clarified butter, and she kept squeezing it to season the food with it. Then he placed his hand and said, \"Come, ten at a time.\" They began to eat, none of them refraining from another, until they were full and left leftovers, until Umm Sulaym gave some to her neighbors.'"],[21237,"His mother Umm Sulaym took two mudds of barley and ground it, and made from it a porridge. She squeezed a small skin of clarified butter that she had. Then she sent me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I came to him while he was among his companions and invited him. He said, 'And those with me?' I went to my mother and said, 'He says, \"And those with me?\"' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came with his companions. Abu Talha went out to him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, it is only something Umm Sulaym made for you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled, entered, and the food was brought. He said, 'Admit ten to me.' They entered and ate until they were full. Then he said, 'Admit ten,' until he counted forty. Then the Prophet ﷺ ate, then he stood up. I began to look to see whether anything had decreased from it."],[21238,"Umm Sulaym made a porridge from barley that she had and ground it. He said, 'She sent me to him to invite him. I came to him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Umm Sulaym has made a porridge of barley for you.\" He said, \"I and those with me?\" He said, \"I returned to her and informed her.\" Abu Talha came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, it is only a mudd or less than a mudd that Umm Sulaym made for you.\" He said, \"I and those with me?\" The Prophet ﷺ and those with him arose and entered the house. He said to me, \"O Anas, admit ten to me.\" Ten entered and ate until they were full. Then he said, \"Admit ten.\" Ten entered and ate until they were full. Then he said, \"Admit ten to me.\" I said to Anas, \"How many were they?\" He said, \"Thirty or forty.\" They ate until they were full. Then the Prophet ﷺ ate, and we ate until we were full. He said, \"It was as if nothing had decreased from it.\" In the hadith of Abu Talha: \"a little barley that Umm Sulaym prepared, and she squeezed onto it a small skin that contained clarified butter.\""],[21239,"Umm Sulaym gave birth to a boy. He fell ill, his illness worsened, then he died while Abu Talha was with the Prophet ﷺ. Abu Talha left him after praying Maghrib. Umm Sulaym had wrapped him up and placed him in a corner of her house. Abu Talha went toward him. She said, 'I adjure you by my right not to approach him, for he has not been better since he fell ill than he is tonight.' She brought his evening meal close, and he broke his fast. Then she took perfume and put it on herself, then she drew near to Abu Talha and he had relations with her. She said, 'O Abu Talha, suppose you saw neighbors who lent their neighbors something on loan, until they thought they had given it to them permanently. When they asked for it back, they felt resentment.' He said, 'They did badly.' She said, 'Allah lent you so-and-so, then He took him back from you, and He is more entitled to him.' He went to the Prophet ﷺ in the morning and told him the news. He said, 'O Allah, bless them in their night.' She conceived Abdullah b. Abi Talha and gave birth to him at the end of the night. She said, 'Do not disturb him until morning.' When morning came, she washed him and wrapped him, then called Anas and said, 'My son, take your brother to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Anas said, 'I went carrying him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing in a waist-wrapper with a spade in his hand. He said, \"O Anas, what is this with you?\" I said, \"My brother, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Hand him to me.\" I handed him to him. He called for dates, chewed them, then placed them in his mouth. The infant smacked his lips, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled and said, \"The Ansar love dates.\"'"],[21240,"She said to her family, 'Do not tell Abu Talha of my son's death until I am the one who tells him.' He came, and she brought near his dinner and drink. He ate and drank. Then she adorned herself for him better than she had ever done before. When he was full and had quenched his thirst, he lay with her. When she knew that he was full, had quenched his thirst, and had satisfied his need from her, she said, 'O Abu Talha, suppose the people of a household lent their loan to another household, and then asked for their loan back, would they have the right to withhold their loan?' He said, 'No.' She said, 'Then expect reward for your son.' She said, 'He became angry and said, \"You left me until I became defiled, then you tell me of my son's death.\" He went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, did you not see what Umm Sulaym did, such and such?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"May Allah bless you both in the remainder of your night.\" He said, 'That night she conceived.' He said, 'She and Abu Talha were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When they approached Madinah, labor pains seized her. Abu Talha stayed behind with her, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went on.' He said, 'Abu Talha said, \"O Lord, You know that it pleased me to go out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he went out and to enter with him when he entered. Here she is detained as You see.\"' He said, 'Umm Sulaym said, \"O Abu Talha, I no longer feel what I felt. Go with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He went until he arrived with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Labor pains struck her, and she gave birth to a boy. My mother said to me, \"O Anas, do not let him taste anything until you take him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the morning.\"' He said, 'I spent that night watching over him, bent over him while he cried, until morning. I took him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found a branding iron in his hand. When he saw the infant with me, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Perhaps Umm Sulaym has given birth?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He put down the branding iron and sat. I brought the infant and placed him in his lap. He called for some pressed dates from Madinah, chewed them in his mouth until they dissolved, then placed them in the infant's mouth. The infant smacked his lips. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Look at the Ansar's love of dates.\" Then he wiped his face and named him Abdullah.'"],[21241,"The Prophet ﷺ came and said, 'It is hot with us.' He sweated. Umm Sulaym came with a bottle and began to wipe the sweat into it. The Prophet ﷺ woke up and said, 'O Umm Sulaym, what are you doing?' She said, 'This is your sweat; we put it in our perfume, and it is the best of perfumes.'"],[21242,"Umm Sulaym asked the Prophet ﷺ to pray in her house so that they could take it as a place of prayer. He came to her on a mat of hers, or theirs, and she sprinkled it with water. He prayed on it, and they prayed with him."],[21243,"I had a sheep, so I collected its ghee into a small skin container and sent it with Zaynab. I said, \"O Zaynab, convey this container of ghee to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so he may use it as a condiment.\" Zaynab came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this is ghee that Umm Sulaym has sent to you.\" He said, \"Empty her container for her.\" So the container was emptied and returned to her. She came back while Umm Sulaym was not in the house, and I hung the container on a peg. Then Umm Sulaym came and saw the container full, dripping with ghee. She said, \"O Zaynab, did I not order you to convey this container to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so he may use it as a condiment?\" She said, \"I did. If you do not believe me, come with me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So Umm Sulaym and Zaynab went with her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she said, \"I sent you with her a container of ghee.\" He said, \"She brought it.\" I said, \"By the One Who sent you with guidance and the religion of truth, it is full of ghee, dripping with it.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Are you amazed, O Umm Sulaym, that Allah has fed you?\""],[21244,"A camel driver who was driving with her among some women along with the Prophet ﷺ, named Anjasha, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Gently, O Anjasha, drive the crystal vessels slowly.\""],[21245,"I was in one of the rooms of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ while he was there, when a man came to him and complained of need. He said, \"Be patient, for by Allah, there has been nothing in the household of Muhammad for seven days, and no fire has been lit under a cooking pot of theirs for three days. By Allah, if I were to ask Allah to make all the mountains of Tihama gold, He would do it.\""],[21246,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray on a khumra (small palm-fiber mat).\""],[21247,"The Prophet ﷺ used to come to her and take a midday nap at her place. She would spread for him a leather mat and he would nap on it. He perspired a lot, so she would collect his sweat and put it into perfume and bottles. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What is this?\" She said, \"Your sweat; we put it in perfume.\" And the Prophet ﷺ used to pray on the khumra."],[21248,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray in her house on a khumra.\""],[21249,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray on a khumra.\""],[21250,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited them one day and prayed for me until I did not care if he added to it. I said to him, \"I have a family member who is especially dear to me, and I would love for you to pray specifically for him because of that special place he holds with me.\" He said, \"Who is he?\" I said, \"Anas, your servant, may my father and mother be your ransom.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed until I did not care if he did not add to it. Among what he prayed was: \"And grant him wealth and children.\" Anas said, \"I do not know anyone who attained the ease and comfort of life like what I attained. Indeed, I have buried with these two hands of mine one hundred of my children—I do not say miscarriages nor grandchildren.\""],[21251,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"used to take us with him on military expeditions, women of the Ansar, and we would give water to the sick and treat the wounded.\""],[21252,"My mother said, \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Please invoke Allah on behalf of your servant.\" He said, \"O Allah! Increase his wealth and children, and bestow Your Blessing on whatever You give him.\" a time of distress. (Using translation from Bukhārī 6344)"],[21253,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: H And Abu Zur'a 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Adam narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us: H And al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: 'Uthman b. Abi Shayba narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us, from Layth, from 'Abd al-Malik b. Abi Bashir, from Hafsa bt. Sirin, from Umm Sulaym, the mother of Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When a woman dies and they want to wash her, let them begin with her belly and wipe it gently. If she is not pregnant, then if she is pregnant, do not move her. If you want to wash her, begin with her lower half. Place a concealing garment over her private area. Then take a piece of cotton and wash her, and do it well. Then insert your hand under the garment and wipe her with cotton three times, wiping her well before performing her ablution. Then perform her ablution with water containing lote-tree leaves, and let a woman pour the water while standing, taking charge of nothing else, until she is cleansed with the lote-tree leaves while you are washing. Let the woman most entitled to her among her relatives undertake her washing, otherwise a pious woman. If she is young or weak, let a pious Muslim woman undertake it. When you finish washing her lower half with a clean washing using water and lote-tree leaves, perform her ablution as for prayer. This is the explanation of her ablution. Then wash her after that three times with water and lote-tree leaves, beginning with her head before anything else, and rinse the washing from the lote-tree leaves with water. Do not comb her hair with a comb. If something occurs from her after the three washings, make it five. If something occurs in the fifth, make it seven. All of that should be an odd number, with water and lote-tree leaves. If it is in the fifth or the third, add some camphor and some lote-tree leaves. Then put that in a new jar. Then sit her up and pour it over her, beginning with her head until you reach her feet. When you finish with her, place a clean garment over her. Then insert your hand from behind the garment and remove it from her. Then stuff her lower area with cotton as much as you can, and stuff the cotton with some of her perfume. Then take a long washed strip of cloth and tie it on her buttocks as a belt is tied. Then tie it between her thighs and press her thighs together. Then throw the end of the strip from her buttocks to near her knees. This is the matter of her lower area. Then perfume her and shroud her, and fold her hair into three braids—a forelock and two braids—and do not make her resemble men. Let her shroud be in five garments, one of which is the waist-wrapper with which you wrap her thighs. Do not remove anything from her hair with depilatory paste or anything else. Whatever falls from her hair, wash it, then stick it back into her head hair. Perfume her head hair and perfume it well. Do not wash her with heated water. Cover her and what you shroud her with with seven sprinklings if you wish, and make everything from them in odd numbers. If you prefer to cover her in her bier, make that an odd number as well. This is the matter of her shroud and her head. If she is drooping or constricted or similar, take a single piece of cloth and soak it in water, and make it follow every part of her, but do not move her, for I fear that something may escape from her that cannot be returned.\""],[21254,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"There are no two Muslims who lose three children who have not reached the age of accountability except that Allah will admit them to Paradise by the abundance of His mercy to them.\" I said, \"And two?\" He said, \"And two.\""],[21255,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There are no two Muslims who lose three of their children who have not reached the age of accountability except that Allah will admit them both to Paradise by the abundance of His mercy to them.\""],[21256,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her while she had a hanging waterskin, so he went to it and drank from its mouth. Then she went to the mouth of the waterskin and cut it off."],[21257,"I brought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a roasted shoulder, and he ate from it. Then he stood to pray and did not perform ablution."],[21258,"That she came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in the house of Umm Salamah, and with him was a group of people who were sitting. So I sat until they left. Then I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I will never refrain from asking about a matter that gives me understanding in my religion and draws me closer to Allah. What do you think, O Messenger of Allah, about a woman who sees in a dream what a man sees? Should she perform ghusl?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When she sees the fluid, she should perform ghusl.\" Umm Salamah said, \"May your hands be dusty, O Umm Sulaim! You have exposed the women.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Rather, may your hands be dusty. Were it not for that, the child would not resemble its mother.\""],[21259,"I entered upon 'A'ishah and said, \"Where is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" She said, \"He is in the house, receiving revelation.\" Then I remained as long as Allah willed that I remain. Then I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"O 'A'ishah, this is Jibril ﷺ conveying peace to you.\""],[21260,"\"And what is wrong with them?\" I said, \"They were lent a loan, and when it was demanded back from them, they became distressed.\" He said, \"What a bad thing they did.\" I said, \"This is your son.\" He said, \"Then surely you will not overcome me in patience tonight.\" When morning came, he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He said, \"O Allah, bless them in their night. For after that I saw for her in the mosque seven children, all of whom had memorized the Quran.\""],[21261,"That she sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after she menstruated or gave birth after having performed the Ifadah on the Day of Sacrifice. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted her, so she departed."],[21262,"That she said, \"O Messenger of Allah, advise me.\" He said, \"Abandon sins, for that is the best emigration. Guard the obligatory duties, for that is the best jihad. And increase in the remembrance of Allah, for you will not come to Allah with anything more beloved to Him than abundant remembrance of Him.\""],[21263,"That she said, \"I reached the elderly women while they were praying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[21264,"The grave of Umm Haram bint Milhan is in Cyprus, and they say, \"This is the grave of the righteous woman.\""],[21265,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I entered Paradise and heard a rustling sound, so I said, 'What is this?' They said, 'This is Rumaysa' bint Milhan.'\""],[21266,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I entered Paradise and heard before me a rustling sound, and behold, it was Ghumaysa' bint Milhan.\""],[21267,"That the Prophet ﷺ said one day in her house, then he woke up and he was laughing. She said, “O Messenger of God, what makes you laugh?” He said, “I marveled at a people from my community who ride the sea like kings upon couches.” She said, “O Messenger of God, supplicate God to make me among them.” He said, “You are among them.” Then he slept and woke up laughing, and he said to me the like of that two or three times, and I said, “O Messenger of God, supplicate God to make me among them,” and he said, “You are among the first ones.” He said, “Then ʿUbāda b. al-Ṣāmit married her, and he took her out on a military expedition. When she returned, a mount was brought near for her to ride, and she fell and her neck broke."],[21268,"I was sleeping near the Prophet ﷺ, and I was not far from him. He woke up glorifying God, so I asked him, and he said, “People from my community were shown to me riding the green sea like kings upon couches.” I said, “O Messenger of God, supplicate God to make me among them,” and he supplicated God, may He be exalted."],[21269,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was taking an afternoon nap in my house, he woke up laughing. I said, “May my father be your ransom, what makes you laugh?” He said, “People from my community were shown to me riding the back of this sea like kings upon couches.” I said, “Supplicate God to make me among them,” and he said, “O God, make her among them.” Then he slept again and woke up laughing. I said, “May my father and mother be your ransom, what makes you laugh?” He said, “People from my community were shown to me riding the back of this sea like kings upon couches.” I said, “Supplicate God to make me among them,” and he said, “You are among the first ones.” So she went on a military expedition with her husband ʿUbāda b. al-Ṣāmit, and when she returned, a gray mule of hers kicked her, and she died."],[21270,"The Prophet ﷺ reclined at the daughter of Milḥān’s and dozed off. He woke up laughing, and I said, “O Messenger of God, why do you laugh?” He said, “Because of a people from my community who ride and raid this green sea; their likeness is like kings upon couches.” I said, “O Messenger of God, supplicate God to make me among them,” and he said, “You are among them.” She then married ʿUbāda b. al-Ṣāmit and went out with Ibn Qurṭa. When she mounted, her mount threw her and broke her neck, and she died, then she was buried."],[21271,"That she heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “The first army from my community to raid this sea have already made [it] obligatory.” Umm Ḥarām said, “O Messenger of God, am I among them?” He said, “You are among them.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The first army from my community to raid the city of Caesar will be forgiven.” Umm Ḥarām said, “O Messenger of God, am I among them?” He said, “No.”"],[21272,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned sea raiders and said, “For the one who is afflicted with seasickness, the reward of a martyr; and for the one who drowns, the reward of two martyrs.” I said, “O Messenger of God, supplicate God to make me among them.” He said, “O God, make her among them.” So she rode the sea, and when she came out she mounted a riding beast, fell, and died."],[21273,"From a woman who was with the Messenger of God ﷺ one day while he was sleeping. He woke up laughing, and she said, “O Messenger of God, perhaps you laugh at my head?” He said, “No, a people from my community were shown to me riding the sea as raiders in the path of God; their likeness is like kings upon couches.” She said, “Then he slept and woke up laughing,” and she said, “What makes you laugh, O Messenger of God?” He said, “A people were shown to me riding the sea as raiders in the path of God, then they return with little booty, forgiven.” I said, “O Messenger of God, supplicate God to make me among them,” and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “O God, make her among them.”"],[21274,"From Umm Waraqa bt. ʿAbd Allah b. al-Ḥārith al-Anṣārī. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to visit her and call her “the martyr,” and she had collected the Qur’an. When the Messenger of God ﷺ went on the expedition to Badr, she said to him, “Will you permit me to go out with you to treat your wounded and nurse your sick, so that perhaps God may grant me martyrdom?” He said, “God will grant you martyrdom.” The Messenger of God ﷺ had commanded her to lead her household in prayer. She had a muezzin, and she led her household in prayer until a slave girl and a slave boy of hers, whom she had set to be freed after her death, attacked her and killed her during the caliphate of ʿUmar. It was said to him, “Umm Waraqa has been killed by her slave boy and slave girl.” He stood among the people and said, “Umm Waraqa was attacked by her slave boy and slave girl, and they killed her. They fled, and they were brought, and he crucified them. They were the first two crucified in Madinah.” ʿUmar said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ spoke the truth; he used to say, ‘Let us go visit the martyr.’”"],[21275,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a military expedition with captives. My sister and I went and entered upon Fatimah, then we went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him to give us a share, mentioning our needs. He said, “The orphans of the people of Badr have beaten you to it.”"],[21276,"“We gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Among what he took upon us was that we should dye with full immersion, comb with honey, and not leave our hands bare of dye.”"],[21277,"I heard my paternal aunt say: I saw Umm Layla dyeing for her a garment, a head-cover, and a wrap once every month, and she would dye her body and her feet with a full immersion. She said, “Upon this we gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” She said: And I saw her with two bracelets of gold on her arm. They used to think that it was from the war spoils. Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla used to dye for her."],[21278,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us: if any one of us is able to have two bracelets of silver on her arm, then if she cannot, she should adorn her arms even with a strap. And he said: “Do not imitate men.”"],[21279,"Uthman b. Maz'un died, and the Prophet ﷺ entered upon him. I said, “May Allah have mercy on you, Abu al-Sa'ib. My testimony for you is that Allah has honored you.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “What makes you know that Allah has honored him?” I said, “I do not know.” He said, “As for him, certainty has come to him from his Lord. By Allah, I am the Messenger of Allah, and I do not know what will be done with me or with you.” I said, “By Allah, I will never praise anyone after him.” She said: Then I saw in a dream an eye of Uthman flowing with water, and I asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “That is his deeds.”"],[21280,"From Umm al-Ala', who was a woman among their women who had given allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ. She said: Uthman b. Maz'un died, and we placed him in his garments. The Prophet ﷺ came, and I said, “May Allah have mercy on you, Abu al-Sa'ib. My testimony for you is that Allah has honored you.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “What makes you know that? As for him, certainty has come to him. By Allah, I hope good for him, and I do not know what Allah will do with him.” I said, “By Allah, I will never praise anyone after him ever.” His words silenced me. When I slept, I saw an eye flowing with water for Uthman b. Maz'un. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “That is his deeds.”"],[21281,"When the Muslims came to Madinah, they drew lots for dwellings. One would stay with another. Among them was Uthman b. Maz'un, who stayed with a woman from the Ansar. He fell ill, and the Prophet ﷺ kept visiting him. It happened that he died, and the woman said, “My testimony for you, Abu al-Sa'ib, is that Allah has honored you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, “What makes you know that?”"],[21282,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her during her illness and said, “Rejoice, O Umm al-Ala', for the illness of a Muslim removes his sins just as fire removes the dross of iron.”"],[21283,"“I memorized Qaf. By the Glorious Quran from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he used to recite it on Friday on the pulpit.”"],[21284,"We and the family of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained for a month with nothing for us or them except a single oven in which we baked. “I memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ Qaf, from what he used to recite from it on the pulpit on Friday.”"],[21285,"I memorized from the Prophet ﷺ Qāf in the Fajr prayer."],[21286,"We stayed two years, or a year and part of a year, while our oven and the oven of the Messenger of God ﷺ were one. And I did not memorize Qāf wal-Qurʾān al-Majīd except from the tongue of the Messenger of God ﷺ, who used to recite it to the people every Friday when he delivered the sermon."],[21287,"Our oven and the oven of the Messenger of God ﷺ were one for two years, or a year and part of a year. And I did not take Qāf wal-Qurʾān al-Majīd except from the Messenger of God ﷺ; he used to recite it every Friday when he addressed the people."],[21288,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'I saw my Lord in a dream in the form of a young man with abundant hair, in green garments, wearing two sandals of gold, and on his face a covering of gold.'"],[21289,"Umm al-Tufayl said to Ubayy b. Kaʿb: Will you not inform ʿUmar of what the Messenger of God ﷺ said regarding Subayʿa bt. al-Ḥārith when she gave birth a few days after her husband's death, and so the Messenger of God ﷺ married her to a man?"],[21290,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us and asked permission several times, but no one responded, so he left. Saʿd said: Go to the Messenger of God, convey peace to him, and tell him that we remained silent only because we hoped he would give us more. So I went to him, and while I was sitting with him, something came and asked permission at the door. He said: 'Who are you?' She said: 'I am Umm Mildam.' He said: 'No welcome and no greetings.'"],[21291,"The Prophet ﷺ came and asked permission, but Saʿd remained silent. Then he came again, and Saʿd remained silent, so the Prophet ﷺ left. She said: Saʿd sent me to him to say: Nothing prevented us from granting you permission except that we wanted you to give us more. She said: Then I heard a voice at the door asking permission, but I saw nothing. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Who are you?' She said: 'I am Umm Mildam.' He said: 'No welcome and no greetings. Will you go to the people of Qubāʾ?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then go to them.'"],[21292,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon ʿUthmān b. Maẓʿūn while he was dying, and the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered a cloth, and he was covered with it. ʿUthmān was staying with a woman of the Anṣār called Umm Muʿādh. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ remained over him for a long time, with his companions with him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ withdrew and wept, and when he wept, the household wept. He said: 'May God have mercy on you, Abū al-Sāʾib.' Al-Sāʾib had witnessed Badr with him. He said: Umm Muʿādh said: Congratulations to you, Abū Sāʾib, Paradise. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'And what makes you know, O Umm Muʿādh? As for him, certainty has come to him, and we know nothing but good.' She said: No, by God, I will never say it to anyone after him."],[21293,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbidding the two mixtures: dates and unripe dates, and fresh dates. He said: Drink each of them separately."],[21294,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ with a bone with meat on it. He gnawed it while he was in the mosque of Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal, then he stood and prayed without performing ablution."],[21295,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my eyes overpower me and prevent me from performing the night prayers (Al-Isha)?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Hurry up, O Umm Anas, when the night fills the belly of every valley, the time for prayer has come. So, pray, and there is no sin on you.\""],[21296,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'May Allah place you in the highest company of Paradise, and me with you.' And I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, teach me a righteous deed that I may do.' He said: 'Establish the prayer, for it is the best jihad. Abandon sins, for that is the best hijrah. And remember Allah much, for it is the most beloved of deeds to Allah with which you will meet Him.'"],[21297,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The best of people in tribulation is a man who withdraws with his wealth, worships his Lord, and gives His due, and a man who takes hold of his horse's head in the path of Allah, frightening them and they frighten him.'"],[21298,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, 'Which people are best in tribulation?' He said, 'A man who takes hold of his horse's head, having frightened the enemy and they frightened him.' A man said to Tawus, 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, which enemy?' He said, 'The polytheists.'"],[21299,"She extracted some clarified butter of hers and put it in a leather container, then gifted it to the Prophet ﷺ. He accepted it, took what was in it, and prayed for blessing for her. They returned it to her while it was full of clarified butter. She thought that the Prophet ﷺ had not accepted it, so she came to the Prophet ﷺ crying out. He said, 'Tell her the story.' So she ate from it for the remainder of the Prophet's ﷺ life, the rule of Abu Bakr, the rule of 'Umar, and the rule of 'Uthman, until there was what there was between 'Ali and Mu'awiyah."],[21300,"Marwan's messenger whom he sent to Umm Ma'qil informed me. He said: She said, 'I said, O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who has grown old and fallen ill. Is there a deed that will suffice me for my Hajj?' He said: 'An 'Umrah in Ramadan suffices you.'"],[21301,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , \"What is an equivalent to Hajj?\" He said, \"Performing Umrah in Ramadan is equivalent to Hajj.\""],[21302,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Ma'qil has perished, and we had a camel. Abu Ma'qil bequeathed it in the path of Allah.' He said, 'Why did you not go out on it, meaning for Hajj?'"],[21303,"\"I was among those who traveled with Marwan ibn Al-Hakam to visit Umm Maqil, and I was among those who entered her company with him when this incident happened.\""],[21304,"\"To perform Hajj with the Prophet ﷺ , but she was not prepared for it, so she asked the Prophet ﷺ what should she do instead? He said, 'Perform Umrah in Ramadan.'\""],[21305,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'I prepared for Hajj, but an obstacle came to me.' The Prophet ﷺ said to her: 'Perform 'Umrah in Ramadan, for an 'Umrah in it is like a Hajj.'"],[21306,"Abu Ma'qil died and left a camel that he had designated in the path of Allah. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Ma'qil has perished and left a camel that he designated for the cause, and I owe a Hajj?' He said: 'O Umm Ma'qil, perform Hajj on your camel, for Hajj is from the path of Allah.'"],[21307,"I intended to perform Hajj, but my camel went astray. I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, \"Perform ʿumrah in the month of Ramadan, for an ʿumrah in the month of Ramadan is equivalent to a Hajj.\""],[21308,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, I have vowed to perform Hajj, but I have a lean camel.\" He said, \"Perform ʿumrah in Ramadan, for an ʿumrah in Ramadan is like a Hajj.\""],[21309,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, I want to perform Hajj, but my camel is lean.\" He said, \"Perform ʿumrah in Ramadan, for an ʿumrah in Ramadan is like a Hajj.\""],[21310,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Perform ʿumrah in Ramadan, for it is equivalent to a Hajj.\""],[21311,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me while I was in a tent of mine made of tanned leather. He said to me, \"How fine it is, as long as there is no dead animal hide in it.\" So I began to tear it."],[21312,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me while I was in a tent. He said, \"What an excellent tent, as long as there is no dead animal hide in it.\""],[21313,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ delivering a sermon at Mina, wrapped in his garment, and the muscle of his upper arm was trembling as he said, \"O people, fear God, and listen and obey, even if a mutilated Abyssinian slave is placed in authority over you. Listen and obey as long as he upholds the Book of God, Exalted is He, among you.\""],[21314,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage, while he was on his saddle and mount, and Husayn was in my lap. He had tucked his garment under his armpit and was saying, \"O people, fear God, and listen and obey whoever is in authority over you, even if he is a mutilated Abyssinian slave. Listen and obey as long as he upholds the Book of God among you.\""],[21315,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and I heard him reminding them and commanding them. Among what I heard him say was, \"If a mutilated Abyssinian slave is appointed over you and he upholds the Book of God among you, then listen to him and obey.\""],[21316,"I performed the Farewell Pilgrimage with the Messenger of God ﷺ. I saw Bilal and Usamah, with Bilal leading his mount by the nose-rein and the other holding up his garment as a shade from the heat, until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah. Then he departed, having placed his garment under his right armpit over his left shoulder. I saw beneath the joint of his right shoulder something like a seal or a gathering. He stood for the people and spoke at length. Among what he said was, \"If a black Abyssinian slave is placed in authority over you, leading you by the Book of God, then listen and obey.\""],[21317,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ on the evening of ʿArafah, standing on a camel, gesturing with his cloak like this, and he exposed his right upper arm. She said, \"I heard him saying, 'O people, listen and obey, even if a mutilated Abyssinian slave is placed in authority over you and he upholds the Book of God among you.'\""],[21318,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ, wearing his striped Yemeni cloak, wrapped in it, saying, \"If a mutilated Abyssinian slave is placed in authority over you, then listen to him as long as he upholds the Book of God, Exalted is He, among you.\""],[21319,"She used to pray behind the Prophet ﷺ in a row of women, and she heard him recite: {All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, Master of the Day of Judgment} until he reached {nor of those who go astray}, then he said: Amin, so loudly that I heard him while I was in the row of women. And he used to say takbir when he prostrated and when he raised [his head]."],[21320,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Listen and obey, even if a slave is placed in authority over you who leads you by the Book of Allah.” And I heard him say: “O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.” He said it three times. They said: “And those who shorten [their hair]?” He said after the third time: “And those who shorten [their hair].”"],[21321,"The Prophet ﷺ came while the people were crowding around him at the jamrah or the jamarat, and he said: “O people, do not destroy yourselves. Stone the jamarat with pebbles like those used for khazf.”"],[21322,"She saw the Prophet ﷺ at the jamrah saying: “Do not kill one another. Stone with pebbles like those used for khazf.”"],[21323,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stone Jamrat al-‘Aqabah from the bottom of the valley on the Day of Sacrifice while he was riding a mount. Then he left, and a woman from Khath‘am followed him, and she had a young son with her who was afflicted. She said: “O Messenger of Allah, this is my son and the remnant of my family, and he is afflicted and cannot speak.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bring me some water.” He washed his hands and rinsed his mouth, then gave it to her and said: “Give him to drink from it and pour some of it over him, and seek healing from Allah for him.” She said: I later met the woman and said: “If only you would give me some of it.” She said: “It is only for this afflicted one.” She said: I met the woman the following year and asked her about the boy, and she said: “He recovered and gained an intellect unlike the intellects of people.”"],[21324,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Day of Sacrifice at Jamrat al-‘Aqabah while he was riding his mule, and a man was behind him shielding him from the people. I asked about the man and was told: “This is al-Fadl b. al-‘Abbas.” The people crowded around him, and he said: “O people, do not kill one another. When you stone the jamarat, stone with pebbles like those used for khazf.” Then he went into the interior of the valley, faced the jamrah, and stoned it from the bottom of the valley with seven pebbles, saying takbir with each pebble. Then he left."],[21325,"A Jewish woman used to visit ‘A’ishah and converse with her. When she got up, she would say: “May Allah protect you from the punishment of the grave.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, ‘A’ishah informed him of that. He said: “She lied. That is only for the People of the Book.” Then the sun was eclipsed, and he said: “I seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave.” Then he said takbir, stood up, and prolonged the standing; then he bowed and prolonged the bowing; then he raised his head, stood up, and prolonged the standing; then he bowed and prolonged the bowing, but less than the first bowing; then he performed two rak‘ahs and two prostrations, standing in them as long as his standing and bowing as long as his bowing."],[21326,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the reward of the rich from the poor?” He said: “Sincere advice and supplication.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, we dislike refusing a kindness.” He said: “How ugly it is! If a trotter were gifted to me, I would accept it, and if I were invited to a foreleg, I would respond.”"],[21327,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Exchange gifts, for a gift increases love and removes the ill-feelings of the heart.”"],[21328,"Hubabah bt. ‘Ajlan narrated to us: My mother Hafsah narrated to me, from Safiyyah bt. Jarir, from Umm Hakim bt. Wada‘, who said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The supplication of a parent reaches the veil.”"],[21329,"It is called \"Umm Bilal.\" Her father was with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Hudaybiyah. She said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Sacrifice the trunk of the sheep, as it is permissible.\""],[21330,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the aqiqah, and he said, “For a boy, two sheep of equal age, and for a girl, one sheep.”"],[21331,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “For the aqiqah: for a boy two sheep, and for a girl one sheep.”"],[21332,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the Aqeeqah. He said, for a baby boy, two sheep as a reward, and for a baby girl, one sheep. I asked, what are the rewards? He said, they are equal."],[21333,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “For a boy, two sheep of equal age, and for a girl, one sheep.”"],[21334,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the aqiqah, and he said, “For a boy, two sheep of equal age, and for a girl, one sheep.”"],[21335,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “For the aqiqah: for a boy two sheep of equal age, and for a girl one sheep.”"],[21336,"She heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “For a boy two sheep, and for a girl one sheep.”"],[21337,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the aqiqah, and he said, “For a boy two sheep, and for a girl one sheep, and it will not harm you whether they are male or female.”"],[21338,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the aqiqah, and he said, “For a boy two sheep, and for a girl one sheep, and it will not harm you whether they are male or female.”"],[21339,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Make the birds rest on their perches.\""],[21340,"My maternal aunt Umm Hufayd gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ some clarified butter, dried curd, and a dab lizard. He ate from the clarified butter and the dried curd and left the dab lizard out of distaste. Had it been forbidden, it would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[21341,"I used to give water to a group of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, among them Zayd b. Thabit and Mu'adh b. Jabal."],[21342,"As for the dubba', it is the gourd which the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade."],[21343,"O my son, one who makes forbidden what God has made lawful is like one who makes lawful what God has made forbidden."],[21344,"The hantam is a jar that is found in the land of the non-Arabs. This is what the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade."],[21345,"“O Prophet of God, what equals Hajj with you?” He said, “An ‘Umrah in Ramadan.”"],[21346,"“Umar ؓ allocated for the women of the emigrants in thousand thousand; among them was Umm ‘Abd.”"],[21347,"She sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ a bowl of milk at the time of his breaking the fast while he was fasting, and that was during the length of the day and intense heat. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent back to her: “How did you get this milk?” She said, “From a sheep of mine.” He sent back to her messenger: “How did you get this sheep?” She said, “I bought it with my own money.” So he took it from her. When it was the next day, Umm ‘Abd Allah came to him and said, “O Messenger of God, I sent you the milk as a gift for you because of the length of the day and intense heat, and you sent the messenger back about it.” He said to her, “With that the messengers were commanded: that we eat only what is pure and do only what is righteous.”"],[21348,"When Abu Musa became gravely ill, his wife cried out. He said, “Do you not know what the Messenger of God ﷺ said?” She said, “Yes,” then fell silent. It was said to her afterwards, “What did the Messenger of God ﷺ say?” She said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘God has cursed whoever shaves, tears, or wails.’”"],[21349,"Umm Kabshah, a woman from ‘Udhrah of Quda‘ah, said: “O Messenger of God, permit me to go out with such-and-such an army.” He said, “No.” I said, “O Messenger of God, I do not intend to fight; I only intend to treat the wounded and the sick, or give water to the sick.” He said, “Were it not that it would become a sunnah and it would be said, ‘So-and-so went out,’ I would have permitted you. But sit.”"],[21350,"\"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding mixing two things, so I asked, 'And what are they?' He said, 'Dates and raisins.' And she was the mother of Mugheeth ibn Abi Abdur Rahman, and she had prayed towards both Qiblas during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .' \""],[21351,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ grew old and put on weight, he leaned on her."],[21352,"Umm Qays bt. Mihsan, who was one of the first emigrant women who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, informed me that she brought her son to the Messenger of God ﷺ, who had not reached the age of eating food, and she had pressed his uvula because of a throat ailment. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Why do you press your children’s throats with these? Use this Indian wood—meaning costus—for it contains seven cures, one of which is pleurisy.” ‘Ubayd Allah said: Umm Qays informed me that her son urinated in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ, so the Messenger of God ﷺ called for water and poured it over the urine, but did not wash it."],[21353,"Umm Qays bt. Mihsan entered with a son of hers who had not yet eaten food, and he urinated on the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he called for water and sprinkled it on him."],[21354,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik (h) and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us: Malik informed us (h) and 'Ali b. al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us: Isma'il b. Abi Uways narrated to us: Malik narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Utbah, from Umm Qays bt. Mihsan, that she brought a small son of hers who had not yet eaten food to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she seated him in his lap, and he urinated on his garment. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and sprinkled it, and did not wash it."],[21355,"That she came to the Prophet ﷺ with a small son of hers who had not yet eaten food. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ seated him in his lap, and he urinated on him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and sprinkled it on it, and did not wash it."],[21356,"That she brought a small son of hers who had not yet eaten food to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ seated him in his lap, and he urinated on him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and sprinkled it, and did not wash it."],[21357,"That she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a small son of hers upon whom she had hung amulets for 'udhrah (throat inflammation). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Why do you treat your children with these amulets? Use this Indian wood—meaning costus—for it contains seven cures, among them pleurisy.\" 'Ubayd Allah said: And Umm Qays informed me that her son urinated in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and poured it over the urine, and did not wash it."],[21358,"\"We entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with me was a son of mine who had not yet eaten food. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed him in his lap, and he urinated on his garment. He called for water and sprinkled it on it, and did not wash it.\""],[21359,"We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Use this Indian wood—meaning costus—for it contains seven cures, among them pleurisy.\""],[21360,"\"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a son of mine who had not yet eaten food. He placed him in his lap, and he urinated on the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He called for water and sprinkled it on his garment, and did not wash it.\""],[21361,"That she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about menstrual blood that gets on a garment. He said, \"Wash it with water and sidr (lote-tree leaves), and scrub it with a rib (of a palm leaf).\""],[21362,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya b. Sa'id, from Bushayr b. Yasar, that Husayn b. Mihsan informed him that his paternal aunt entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day, and he said, \"Do you have a husband?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"How are you toward him?\" She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I do not fall short except in what I am unable to do.\" He said, \"Look to how you are toward him, for he is your paradise and your hell.\""],[21363,"That she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a need, and he fulfilled her need. Then he said, \"Do you have a husband?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"How are you toward him?\" She said, \"I do not fall short except in what I am unable to do.\" He said, \"Look to how you are toward him, for he is your paradise and your hell.\""],[21364,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said, \"Do you have a husband?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"How are you toward him?\" She said, \"I do not fall short except what I am unable to do.\" He said, \"Know that he is your Paradise and your Hell.\""],[21365,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Al-Hajjaj b. Safwan narrated to us from Usayd b. Abi Usayd al-Barrad, from a woman among those who gave the pledge. She said: Among what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took upon us was: \"That we not disobey him in what is right, that we not scratch a face, not let down hair, not tear a collar, and not call for woe.\""],[21366,"We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we have paths to the mosque that are foul.\" He said, \"Are there not beyond them paths cleaner than them?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then this for this.\""],[21367,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we have a path that is bad during rain.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Is there not besides it a good path?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then that for that.\""],[21368,"From Zaynab bt. Nubayt b. Jabir, from her mother or her maternal aunt, daughters of Abu Umamah. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entrusted to me his daughters—meaning Abu Umamah As'ad b. Zurarah. They said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ adorned us with gold earrings.\""],[21369,"she said, the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ recited the Āyah of Stoning to us: \"al-shaykhu wa-al-shaykhah idhā zanayā fārjumūhumā al-battata bimā qaḍayā min al-ladhhah (The [married] man and a woman, if they commit adultery, then absolutely stone them for what they spent in [seeking] pleasure.)\" (Using translation from Ḥākim 8070)"],[21370,"I was one day with Zaynab, the wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while we were dyeing clothes with red ochre. While we were doing that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appeared before us. When he saw the red ochre, he turned back. When Zaynab saw that, she knew that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked what she had done. So she took water and washed her clothes and hid all redness. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned, looked, saw nothing, and entered."],[21371,"I witnessed Aminah when she gave birth to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When labor struck her, I looked at the stars descending until I said, \"They will surely fall upon me.\" When she gave birth to him, a light came out from her that illuminated the house we were in and the dwelling. There was nothing I looked at except light."],[21372,"From an orphan woman who was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Thaqif, that she narrated to Safiyyah bt. Abi 'Ubayd that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever among you is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for whoever dies there, I will be a witness or intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[21373,"When Muhammad b. Talhah was born, I brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"What did they name him?\" We said, \"Muhammad.\" He said, \"This is my name and his kunyah is Abu al-Qasim.\""]]);
